window.EXAM_DATA=window.EXAM_DATA||{};window.EXAM_DATA["dop-c02"]=[{"id":1,"question_en":"A company has a mobile application that makes HTTP API calls to an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The ALB routes requests to an AWS Lambda function. Many different versions of the application are in use at any given time, including versions that are in testing by a subset of users. The version of the application is defined in the user-agent header that is sent with all requests to the API. After a series of recent changes to the API, the company has observed issues with the application. The company needs to gather a metric for each API operation by response code for each version of the application that is in use. A DevOps engineer has modified the Lambda function to extract the API operation name, version information from the user-agent header and response code. Which additional set of actions should the DevOps engineer take to gather the required metrics?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款移动应用程序，该程序通过 HTTP API 调用应用负载均衡器（ALB）。ALB 将请求路 由到 AWS Lambda 函数。在任何给定时间，都有许多不同版本的应用程序在使用，其中包括由部分用户 进行测试的版本。应用程序的版本在发送给 API 的所有请求的用户代理标头中定义。 在对 API 进行了一系列近期更改之后，该公司发现应用程序出现了问题。公司需要为每个版本的应 用程序中每个 API 操作按响应代码收集一个指标。一位 DevOps 工程师修改了 Lambda 函数，以从用 户代理标头中提取 API 操作名称、版本信息和响应代码。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪一组额外的操作来收集所需的指标？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the Lambda function to write the API operation name, response code, and version number as a log line to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure a CloudWatch Logs metric filter that increments a metric for each API operation name. Specify response code and application version as dimensions for the metric.","B":"Modify the Lambda function to write the API operation name, response code, and version number as a log line to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure a CloudWatch Logs Insights query to populate CloudWatch metrics from the log lines. Specify response code and application version as dimensions for the metric.","C":"Configure the ALB access logs to write to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Modify the Lambda function to respond to the ALB with the API operation name, response code, and version number as response metadata. Configure a CloudWatch Logs metric filter that increments a metric for each API operation name. Specify response code and application version as dimensions for the metric.","D":"Configure AWS X-Ray integration on the Lambda function. Modify the Lambda function to create an X- Ray subsegment with the API operation name, response code, and version number. Configure X-Ray insights to extract an aggregated metric for each API operation name and to publish the metric to Amazon CloudWatch. Specify response code and application version as dimensions for the metric."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 Lambda 函数，将 API 操作名称、响应代码和版本号作为一条日志行写入 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。配置一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，为每个 API 操作名称递增一个指标。将响应 代码和应用程序版本指定为该指标的维度。","B":"修改 Lambda 函数，将 API 操作名称、响应代码和版本号作为一条日志行写入 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。配置 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询，从日志行中填充 CloudWatch 指标。将响应代码 和应用程序版本指定为指标的维度。","C":"将应用负载均衡器（ALB）的访问日志配置为写入 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。修改 Lambda 函数，使其以 API 操作名称、响应代码和版本号作为响应元数据来响应 ALB。配置 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，为每个 API 操作名称递增一个指标。将响应代码和应用程序版本指定为该指标 的维度。","D":"在 Lambda 函数上配置 AWS X-Ray 集成。修改 Lambda 函数以使用 API 操作名称、响应代码和版本 号创建 X-Ray 子段。配置 X-Ray 洞察以提取每个 API 操作名称的聚合指标，并将该指标发布到 Amazon CloudWatch。将响应代码和应用程序版本指定为指标的维度。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The Lambda function already extracts the API operation name, version (from the user-agent header), and response code. The native, documented way to turn these into a per-operation metric broken down by response code and version is to write them as a structured (JSON or space-delimited) log line to CloudWatch Logs and attach a CloudWatch Logs metric filter. The docs state a metric filter 'increments the metric's count by a specified numerical value' each time a matching log event is found, and that for JSON/space-delimited patterns 'You can create JSON and space-delimited metric filters with up to three dimensions' extracted from log fields. Publishing response code and application version as two of the allowed three dimensions on a per-operation metric exactly satisfies the requirement, which is why option A is correct.","explanation_zh":"Lambda function 已從 user-agent header 中擷取出 API operation name、版本資訊與 response code。要把這些資料轉成『依 response code 與版本細分的每個 API operation 指標』，AWS 原生且有文件支援的做法是：把它們以結構化(JSON 或空白分隔)的 log line 寫入 CloudWatch Logs，再設定 CloudWatch Logs metric filter。文件指出 metric filter 在每次比對到符合的 log event 時就會將指標計數依指定數值遞增；對於 JSON/空白分隔的 pattern，可從 log 欄位擷取並發佈最多三個 dimensions。將 response code 與 application version 作為其中兩個 dimension 附加到每個 operation 的指標上，正好符合需求，因此選項 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights is an interactive ad hoc query/analysis engine. AWS docs explicitly contrast the two: 'Metric filters differ from CloudWatch Logs Insights queries in that a specified numerical value is added to a metric filter each time a matching log is found.' Logs Insights does not continuously 'populate CloudWatch metrics' nor emit custom metrics with dimensions; the described mechanism does not exist.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 是互動式的臨時查詢/分析引擎。AWS 文件明確將兩者區分：『metric filter 與 Logs Insights 查詢不同，metric filter 在每次比對到符合 log 時就為指標加值』。Logs Insights 不會持續『產生 CloudWatch 指標』，也不會發佈帶 dimensions 的自訂指標；題目描述的機制並不存在。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ALB access logs are delivered to Amazon S3, not to a CloudWatch Logs log group, and they record network/HTTP-level fields rather than Lambda-computed application data. A Lambda behind an ALB cannot inject custom 'response metadata' (application operation name, user-agent version, application response code) into ALB access logs, so a metric filter over those logs cannot produce the required dimensioned metrics.","why_zh":"ALB access logs 是送到 Amazon S3，而非 CloudWatch Logs log group，且記錄的是網路/HTTP 層級欄位，並非 Lambda 計算出的應用層資料。ALB 後的 Lambda 無法把自訂的『response metadata』(應用 operation name、user-agent 版本、應用回應碼) 注入 ALB access logs，因此對這些 log 套用 metric filter 無法產生所需的帶 dimension 指標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"X-Ray subsegments support annotations/metadata, but X-Ray Insights detects anomalies/incidents in traces (e.g., anomalous services, latency spikes) and emits incident notifications via EventBridge. It does not 'extract an aggregated metric for each API operation name' and publish a custom CloudWatch metric with user-defined dimensions such as response code and application version. That capability is fabricated and adds unnecessary overhead.","why_zh":"X-Ray subsegment 可帶 annotation/metadata，但 X-Ray Insights 是偵測追蹤資料中的異常/事件(例如異常服務、延遲飆升)，並透過 EventBridge 發出事件通知。它不會『為每個 API operation name 擷取彙整指標』並以 response code、application version 等自訂 dimensions 發佈自訂 CloudWatch 指標；該功能屬虛構且增加不必要的維運負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntaxForMetricFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CountOccurrencesExample.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/ExtractBytesExample.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-logs-metricfilter-dimension.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/aws-xray.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":2,"question_en":"A company provides an application to customers. The application has an Amazon API Gateway REST API that invokes an AWS Lambda function. On initialization, the Lambda function loads a large amount of data from an Amazon DynamoDB table. The data load process results in long cold-start times of 8-10 seconds. The DynamoDB table has DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) configured. Customers report that the application intermittently takes a long time to respond to requests. The application receives thousands of requests throughout the day. In the middle of the day, the application experiences 10 times more requests than at any other time of the day. Near the end of the day, the application's request volume decreases to 10% of its normal total. A DevOps engineer needs to reduce the latency of the Lambda function at all times of the day. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司向客户提供一款应用程序。该应用程序有一个通过亚马逊 API 网关的 REST API 调用 AWS Lambda 函数的接口。在初始化时，Lambda 函数会从一个亚马逊 DynamoDB 表中加载大量数据。数据 加载过程导致冷启动时间长达 8 到 10 秒。DynamoDB 表已配置了 DynamoDB 加速器（DAX）。 客户报告称，该应用程序间歇性地对请求作出响应的时间过长。该应用程序全天会收到数千个请求。 在一天的中间时段，其收到的请求量是一天中其他任何时段的 10 倍。临近一天结束时，该应用程序 的请求量会降至正常总量的 10%。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要在一天中的任何时候都降低 Lambda 函数的延迟。哪种解决方案能 满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure provisioned concurrency on the Lambda function with a concurrency value of 1. Delete the DAX cluster for the DynamoDB table.","B":"Configure reserved concurrency on the Lambda function with a concurrency value of 0.","C":"Configure provisioned concurrency on the Lambda function. Configure AWS Application Auto Scaling on the Lambda function with provisioned concurrency values set to a minimum of 1 and a maximum of 100.","D":"Configure reserved concurrency on the Lambda function. Configure AWS Application Auto Scaling on the API Gateway API with a reserved concurrency maximum value of 100."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Lambda 函数的预配置并发设置为 1。删除 DynamoDB 表的 DAX 集群。","B":"在 Lambda 函数上配置预留并发量，将并发量值设为 0。","C":"在 Lambda 函数上配置预置并发。在 Lambda 函数上配置 AWS 应用程序自动扩展，将预置并发值设 置为最小值 1 和最大值 100。","D":"在 Lambda 函数上配置预留并发量。在 API Gateway API 上配置 AWS 应用程序自动扩展，预留并发 量的最大值设为 100。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The 8-10 second latency comes from the Lambda function loading a large amount of DynamoDB data during the Init phase, which only occurs on a cold start. Provisioned concurrency pre-initializes execution environments so they are ready to respond immediately with double-digit-millisecond response times; AWS docs state a function using provisioned concurrency does not exhibit cold start behavior because the environment is prepared ahead of invocation. Because traffic is highly variable (10x at the mid-day peak, dropping to 10% near end of day), a single fixed value cannot keep latency low at all times: too low brings back cold starts at peak, too high over-provisions otherwise. AWS docs explicitly recommend using Application Auto Scaling target tracking to automate provisioned concurrency for workloads without predictable traffic patterns, and the documented CLI example registers the scalable target with exactly --min-capacity 1 --max-capacity 100, matching option C. DAX accelerates DynamoDB reads, not the Lambda Init-phase load, so it should not be deleted.","explanation_zh":"8-10 秒的延遲來自 Lambda function 在 Init 階段從 DynamoDB 載入大量資料，而這只在 cold start 時發生。Provisioned concurrency 會預先初始化執行環境，使其能立即以雙位數毫秒的回應時間提供服務；AWS 文件指出使用 provisioned concurrency 的 function 不會出現 cold start，因為環境已在叫用前準備好。由於流量變化極大（中午尖峰是平時的 10 倍，傍晚降到 10%），單一固定值無法在所有時段維持低延遲：值太低尖峰時 cold start 會回來，值太高其餘時段又過度配置。AWS 文件明確建議對沒有可預測流量模式的工作負載使用 Application Auto Scaling target tracking 來自動化 provisioned concurrency，且文件中的 CLI 範例註冊 scalable target 時正好使用 --min-capacity 1 --max-capacity 100，與選項 C 完全吻合。DAX 加速的是 DynamoDB 讀取，而非 Lambda Init 階段的載入，因此不應刪除。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A single fixed provisioned concurrency of 1 cannot absorb the 10x mid-day spike, so cold starts and high latency return at peak. Deleting the DAX cluster also harms DynamoDB read performance; DAX is unrelated to the Lambda Init-phase cold start, so removing it provides no latency benefit and is counterproductive.","why_zh":"固定為 1 的 provisioned concurrency 無法吸收中午 10 倍的尖峰，尖峰時 cold start 與高延遲會回來。刪除 DAX cluster 還會損害 DynamoDB 讀取效能；DAX 與 Lambda Init 階段的 cold start 無關，移除它毫無延遲上的好處且適得其反。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Reserved concurrency is a max/min cap on concurrent instances and does not pre-initialize environments, so it never reduces cold starts. Worse, AWS docs state that setting reserved concurrency to 0 intentionally throttles the function and stops it from processing any events entirely, which breaks the application.","why_zh":"Reserved concurrency 是對並發實例數的上/下限，並不會預先初始化環境，因此完全無法降低 cold start。更糟的是，AWS 文件指出將 reserved concurrency 設為 0 等於刻意限流，會讓 function 完全停止處理任何事件，直接讓應用程式中斷。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Reserved concurrency does not pre-warm execution environments and therefore does not eliminate the cold-start latency. In addition, API Gateway is not an Application Auto Scaling scalable target and 'reserved concurrency on the API Gateway API' is not a valid configuration, so the option is technically invalid.","why_zh":"Reserved concurrency 不會預先暖機執行環境，因此無法消除 cold start 延遲。此外，API Gateway 不是 Application Auto Scaling 的 scalable target，「在 API Gateway API 上設定 reserved concurrency」並非有效設定，因此此選項在技術上不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/provisioned-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/application/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-lambda.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":3,"question_en":"A company is adopting AWS CodeDeploy to automate its application deployments for a Java-Apache Tomcat application with an Apache Webserver. The development team started with a proof of concept, created a deployment group for a developer environment, and performed functional tests within the application. After completion, the team will create additional deployment groups for staging and production. The current log level is configured within the Apache settings, but the team wants to change this configuration dynamically when the deployment occurs, so that they can set different log level configurations depending on the deployment group without having a different application revision for each group. How can these requirements be met with the LEAST management overhead and without requiring different script versions for each deployment group?","question_zh":"一家公司正在采用 AWS CodeDeploy 来实现其 Java - Apache Tomcat 应用程序（搭配 Apache Web 服务器） 的自动化部署。开发团队首先进行了概念验证，为开发环境创建了一个部署组，并在应用程序内部进行 了功能测试。完成后，团队将为预发布和生产环境创建更多的部署组。 当前的日志级别是在 Apache 设置中配置的，但团队希望在部署时动态更改此配置，以便他们可以根据 部署组设置不同的日志级别配置，而无需为每个组都使用不同的应用程序版本。 如何以最小的管理开销满足这些要求，同时又无需为每个部署组准备不同的脚本版本？","options_en":{"A":"Tag the Amazon EC2 instances depending on the deployment group. Then place a script into the application revision that calls the metadata service and the EC2 API to identify which deployment group the instance is part of. Use this information to configure the log level settings. Reference the script as part of the AfterInstall lifecycle hook in the appspec.yml file.","B":"Create a script that uses the CodeDeploy environment variable DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ NAME to identify which deployment group the instance is part of. Use this information to configure the log level settings. Reference this script as part of the BeforeInstall lifecycle hook in the appspec.yml file.","C":"Create a CodeDeploy custom environment variable for each environment. Then place a script into the application revision that checks this environment variable to identify which deployment group the instance is part of. Use this information to configure the log level settings. Reference this script as part of the ValidateService lifecycle hook in the appspec.yml file.","D":"Create a script that uses the CodeDeploy environment variable DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID to identify which deployment group the instance is part of to configure the log level settings. Reference this script as part of the Install lifecycle hook in the appspec.yml file."},"options_zh":{"A":"根据部署组对 Amazon EC2 实例进行标记。然后在应用程序修订版中放入一个脚本，该脚本调用元数 据服务和 EC2 API 以确定实例所属的部署组。使用此信息来配置日志级别设置。在 appspec.yml 文件 的 AfterInstall 生命周期挂钩中引用该脚本。","B":"创建一个脚本，该脚本使用 CodeDeploy 环境变量 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 来确定实例所属 的部署组。利用此信息来配置日志级别设置。在 appspec.yml 文件的 BeforeInstall 生命周期挂钩中 引用此脚本。","C":"为每个环境创建一个 CodeDeploy 自定义环境变量。然后在应用程序修订版中放入一个脚本，该脚本 检查此环境变量以确定实例属于哪个部署组。使用此信息来配置日志级别设置。在 appspec.yml 文 件的 ValidateService 生命周期挂钩中引用此脚本。","D":"创建一个脚本，该脚本使用 CodeDeploy 环境变量 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID 来识别实例所属的部署 组，以配置日志级别设置。在 appspec.yml 文件的 Install 生命周期挂钩中引用此脚本。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeDeploy automatically exposes built-in environment variables to every EC2/On-Premises lifecycle hook script, including DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME, DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID, APPLICATION_NAME, DEPLOYMENT_ID, and LIFECYCLE_EVENT. A single script in one application revision can branch on DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME to set per-environment Apache log levels, so no per-group revision and no per-group script version are needed, giving the lowest management overhead. The AWS 'AppSpec hooks section' doc gives this exact scenario verbatim: a script that runs 'sed -i -e s/LogLevel warn/LogLevel debug/g /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf' when DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME equals Staging, and states it 'must be invoked during the BeforeInstall deployment lifecycle event.' BeforeInstall is the documented hook for preinstall configuration changes such as editing httpd.conf before the new files are installed, which makes option B both technically correct and the documented best practice.","explanation_zh":"CodeDeploy 會自動將內建環境變數提供給每個 EC2/On-Premises lifecycle hook 腳本，包括 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME、DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID、APPLICATION_NAME、DEPLOYMENT_ID 與 LIFECYCLE_EVENT。單一 application revision 內的單一腳本可依 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 分支來設定各環境的 Apache log level，因此不需要為每個 deployment group 建立不同 revision，也不需要不同腳本版本，管理負擔最低。AWS 'AppSpec hooks section' 文件正好逐字提供此情境的範例：當 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 等於 Staging 時執行 'sed -i -e s/LogLevel warn/LogLevel debug/g /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf' 的腳本，並明確說明此腳本必須在 BeforeInstall lifecycle event 執行。BeforeInstall 是文件指定用於安裝前設定變更（例如在安裝新檔案前修改 httpd.conf）的 hook，因此選項 B 在技術上正確且為文件記載的最佳實務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Tagging EC2 instances and calling the metadata/EC2 API to derive the deployment group is far more management overhead than simply reading the built-in DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME variable that CodeDeploy already injects into every hook. It also adds IAM permissions and API-call complexity for no benefit, and AfterInstall would change config only after the files are already installed.","why_zh":"為 EC2 instance 加標籤並呼叫 metadata/EC2 API 來判斷 deployment group，比直接讀取 CodeDeploy 已自動注入每個 hook 的內建 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 變數負擔大得多，還需額外 IAM 權限與 API 呼叫，毫無好處；且 AfterInstall 是在檔案安裝之後才修改設定。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating CodeDeploy custom environment variables per environment is unnecessary because DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME is already built in, adding setup overhead. Worse, ValidateService is documented as 'the last deployment lifecycle event... used to verify the deployment was completed successfully,' not to configure the application before install, so it is the wrong hook for changing log config.","why_zh":"為每個環境建立 CodeDeploy 自訂環境變數沒有必要，因為 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 已是內建，反而增加設定負擔。更糟的是文件明確指出 ValidateService 是『最後一個 lifecycle event，用於驗證部署是否成功完成』，並非在安裝前設定應用程式，因此是修改 log 設定的錯誤 hook。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The AWS doc states the Install event 'is reserved for the CodeDeploy agent and cannot be used to run scripts' (the agent copies revision files from the temporary location to the destination), so referencing a script under the Install hook is invalid. DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID is a real built-in variable but is a less readable identifier than DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME; the fatal flaw is the unusable Install hook.","why_zh":"AWS 文件指出 Install 事件『保留給 CodeDeploy agent，不能用來執行腳本』（由 agent 將 revision 檔案從暫存位置複製到目的地），因此在 Install hook 下引用腳本是無效的。DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID 確實是內建變數，但比 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 不易閱讀；致命缺陷是 Install hook 根本無法執行腳本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":4,"question_en":"A company requires its developers to tag all Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes in an account to indicate a desired backup frequency. This requirement Includes EBS volumes that do not require backups. The company uses custom tags named Backup_Frequency that have values of none, daily, or weekly that correspond to the desired backup frequency. An audit finds that developers are occasionally not tagging the EBS volumes. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that all EBS volumes always have the Backup_Frequency tag so that the company can perform backups at least weekly unless a different value is specified. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司要求其开发人员为账户中的所有亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷添加标签，以表明所 需的备份频率。此要求包括那些不需要备份的 EBS 卷。该公司使用名为“Backup_Frequency”的自 定义标签，其值为“none”（无）、“daily”（每日）或“weekly”（每周），分别对应所需的备份 频率。一次审计发现，开发人员偶尔会忘记为 EBS 卷添加标签。 DevOps 工程师需要确保所有 EBS 卷始终具有“Backup_Frequency”标签，以便公司至少每周执行一次 备份，除非指定了不同的值。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up AWS Config in the account. Create a custom rule that returns a compliance failure for all Amazon EC2 resources that do not have a Backup_Frequency tag applied. Configure a remediation action that uses a custom AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to apply the Backup_Frequency tag with a value of weekly.","B":"Set up AWS Config in the account. Use a managed rule that returns a compliance failure for EC2::Volume resources that do not have a Backup_Frequency tag applied. Configure a remediation action that uses a custom AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to apply the Backup_Frequency tag with a value of weekly.","C":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail in the account. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EBS CreateVolume events. Configure a custom AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to apply the Backup_Frequency tag with a value of weekly. Specify the runbook as the target of the rule.","D":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail in the account. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EBS CreateVolume events or EBS ModifyVolume events. Configure a custom AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to apply the Backup_Frequency tag with a value of weekly. Specify the runbook as the target of the rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"在账户中设置 AWS Config。创建一条自定义规则，对于所有未应用“Backup_Frequency”标签的 Amazon EC2 资源返回合规性失败。配置一个修复操作，使用自定义的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册来应用“Backup_Frequency”标签，其值为“每周”。","B":"在账户中设置 AWS Config。使用一个托管规则，对于未应用“Backup_Frequency”标签的 EC2:: Volume 资源返回合规性失败。配置一个修复操作，使用自定义的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册来应用“Backup_Frequency”标签，其值为“weekly”。","C":"在账户中启用 AWS CloudTrail。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 EBS 作出反应。 创建卷事件。配置一个自定义的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，将“Backup_Frequency” 标签的值设置为“weekly”。将该运行手册指定为规则的目标。","D":"在账户中启用 AWS CloudTrail。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 EBS CreateVolume 事件或 EBS ModifyVolume 事件做出反应。配置一个自定义的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，将 Backup_Frequency 标签的值设置为 weekly。将该运行手册指定为规则的目标。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is that all EBS volumes ALWAYS carry the Backup_Frequency tag, defaulting to weekly when none is specified. The AWS Config managed rule required-tags (identifier REQUIRED_TAGS) explicitly lists AWS::EC2::Volume among its supported resource types and uses a 'Configuration changes' trigger, so it continuously evaluates every volume and flags any that lack the tag - both at creation and if the tag is later removed (because tag removal is itself a recorded configuration change). The required-tags doc page also states verbatim that the AWS-managed AWS-SetRequiredTags automation document does NOT work as remediation for this rule and that you must create your own custom Systems Manager Automation document - which is exactly what option B specifies (a custom runbook applying Backup_Frequency=weekly). Because the rule only flags volumes missing the tag, developers who already specified none/daily/weekly keep their chosen value, while untagged volumes get the safe weekly default. Options C and D are event-driven on CreateVolume (and ModifyVolume for D), firing only at creation/attribute-change time, so they never re-tag a volume whose tag was later deleted; per the EC2 API reference, ModifyVolume changes size, type, and IOPS (not tags), so D's addition closes no gap. Option A needlessly defines a custom rule scoped to all EC2 resources when the purpose-built managed rule already exists and supports volumes.","explanation_zh":"需求是所有 EBS 磁碟區「永遠」都要帶有 Backup_Frequency 標籤，未指定時預設為 weekly。AWS Config 受管規則 required-tags（識別碼 REQUIRED_TAGS）的支援資源類型清單中明確包含 AWS::EC2::Volume，並採用「組態變更（Configuration changes）」觸發，因此會持續評估每個磁碟區並標記任何缺少標籤者，包含建立時未加標籤，以及標籤之後被移除的情形（因為移除標籤本身就是一筆會被記錄的組態變更）。required-tags 文件頁面亦逐字載明：AWS 受管的 AWS-SetRequiredTags 自動化文件無法作為此規則的修復動作，必須自行建立自訂的 Systems Manager Automation 文件，這正是選項 B 所述（自訂 runbook 套用 Backup_Frequency=weekly）。由於規則只標記缺少標籤的磁碟區，已自行指定 none/daily/weekly 的開發者會保留其選擇的值，未加標籤者則套用安全的 weekly 預設值。選項 C、D 以 CreateVolume（D 另含 ModifyVolume）事件驅動，僅在建立或屬性變更時觸發，無法為之後被刪除標籤的磁碟區重新加標；依 EC2 API 參考，ModifyVolume 變更的是大小、類型與 IOPS（而非標籤），故 D 的新增並未補上任何缺口。選項 A 在已有專用受管規則且支援磁碟區的情況下，多此一舉地定義範圍涵蓋所有 EC2 資源的自訂規則。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses an unnecessary custom AWS Config rule scoped to ALL EC2 resources (instances, security groups, ENIs, etc.) when the purpose-built managed rule required-tags already exists and explicitly supports AWS::EC2::Volume. Wrong scope and far more custom effort than needed.","why_zh":"在已有專用受管規則 required-tags 且明確支援 AWS::EC2::Volume 的情況下，使用範圍涵蓋所有 EC2 資源（執行個體、安全群組、ENI 等）的自訂 AWS Config 規則，範圍錯誤且自訂工作量遠高於所需。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EventBridge reacting only to CreateVolume events tags volumes at creation only; it does not re-apply the tag if a developer later removes it, so it fails the 'all EBS volumes always have the tag' requirement.","why_zh":"EventBridge 僅對 CreateVolume 事件反應，只在建立時加標籤；若開發者之後移除標籤不會重新套用，無法滿足『所有 EBS 磁碟區永遠都要有標籤』的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Adding ModifyVolume does not help: per the EC2 API reference, ModifyVolume changes size, type, and IOPS, not tags (tag removal is done via DeleteTags). So this still only triggers at creation/attribute-change and never re-tags volumes whose tag was deleted, failing the 'always' requirement.","why_zh":"加入 ModifyVolume 無濟於事：依 EC2 API 參考，ModifyVolume 變更的是大小、類型與 IOPS 而非標籤（移除標籤是透過 DeleteTags）。因此仍只在建立或屬性變更時觸發，無法為被刪標籤的磁碟區重新加標，不符『永遠』要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/required-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/APIReference/API_ModifyVolume.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":5,"question_en":"A company is using an Amazon Aurora cluster as the data store for its application. The Aurora cluster is configured with a single DB instance. The application performs read and write operations on the database by using the cluster's instance endpoint. The company has scheduled an update to be applied to the cluster during an upcoming maintenance window. The cluster must remain available with the least possible interruption during the maintenance window. What should a DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其应用程序的数据存储设置为亚马逊 Aurora 集群。该 Aurora 集群配置了一个单一的数据库 实例。应用程序通过使用集群的实例端点对数据库执行读写操作。 该公司已安排在即将到来的维护窗口期间对集群进行更新。在维护窗口期间，集群必须保持可用状态， 且中断时间应尽可能短。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add a reader instance to the Aurora cluster. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster endpoint for write operations. Update the Aurora cluster's reader endpoint for reads.","B":"Add a reader instance to the Aurora cluster. Create a custom ANY endpoint for the cluster. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster's custom ANY endpoint for read and write operations.","C":"Turn on the Multi-AZ option on the Aurora cluster. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster endpoint for write operations. Update the Aurora cluster’s reader endpoint for reads.","D":"Turn on the Multi-AZ option on the Aurora cluster. Create a custom ANY endpoint for the cluster. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster's custom ANY endpoint for read and write operations"},"options_zh":{"A":"向 Aurora 集群添加一个读取器实例。更新应用程序，使其在写入操作时使用 Aurora 集群端点。更新 Aurora 集群的读取器端点以用于读取操作。","B":"向 Aurora 集群添加一个读取器实例。为该集群创建一个自定义的 ANY 端点。更新应用程序，使其使用 Aurora 集群的自定义 ANY 端点来执行读写操作。","C":"在 Aurora 集群上启用多可用区选项。更新应用程序，使其在写入操作时使用 Aurora 集群端点。更新 Aurora 集群的只读端点以用于读取操作。","D":"在 Aurora 集群上启用多可用区选项。为该集群创建自定义的 ANY 端点。更新应用程序，使其使用 Aurora 集群的自定义 ANY 端点来执行读写操作。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The cluster has a single DB instance, so a maintenance/failure event forces Aurora to recreate the primary instance, which the AWS HA docs say typically takes less than 10 minutes (read and write operations fail during that window). Converting the cluster to Multi-AZ by adding a reader (Aurora Replica) in a different AZ gives Aurora a promotion target, and the docs state that promoting an Aurora Replica is 'much faster than creating a new primary instance' — service is typically restored in less than 60 seconds and often less than 30 seconds, which is the least possible interruption. The cluster (writer) endpoint always represents the current primary instance and provides automatic failover support, so the application should keep using the cluster endpoint for writes and the reader endpoint for reads. Option A matches both the correct mechanism (add a reader in another AZ) and the correct endpoint usage, so it is the right answer.","explanation_zh":"此叢集只有單一 DB instance，因此維護或故障事件會迫使 Aurora 重新建立 primary instance，AWS 高可用文件指出這通常需時少於 10 分鐘（期間讀寫操作會失敗）。在另一個 AZ 新增 reader（Aurora Replica）以將叢集轉為 Multi-AZ，會提供可供 Aurora 提升的目標，文件指出提升 Aurora Replica「遠快於重新建立新 primary instance」——服務通常於少於 60 秒、且常少於 30 秒內恢復，達到最小中斷。cluster（writer）endpoint 永遠代表目前的 primary instance 並提供自動 failover 支援，因此應用程式應繼續以 cluster endpoint 進行寫入、以 reader endpoint 進行讀取。選項 A 同時符合正確的機制（在另一個 AZ 新增 reader）與正確的 endpoint 用法，因此是正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adding a reader is correct, but using a custom ANY endpoint for both reads and writes is broken. AWS docs state Aurora directs connections on an ANY-type endpoint to any associated DB instance with equal probability, so writes/DDL can land on a read-only reader instance and fail. The cluster endpoint, not a custom ANY endpoint, is the construct that always tracks the writer.","why_zh":"新增 reader 是正確的，但對讀取與寫入都使用 custom ANY endpoint 是錯的。AWS 文件指出 Aurora 會以相同機率將 ANY 型 endpoint 的連線導向任一相關 DB instance，因此寫入/DDL 可能落到唯讀的 reader instance 而失敗。永遠追蹤 writer 的是 cluster endpoint，而非 custom ANY endpoint。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The endpoint usage (cluster for writes, reader for reads) is correct, but provisioned Aurora has no simple 'Turn on Multi-AZ' toggle the way Amazon RDS does. AWS docs say you convert an existing Aurora cluster to Multi-AZ by adding a new reader DB instance in a different AZ — exactly what option A does, not what C describes.","why_zh":"endpoint 用法（cluster 寫、reader 讀）正確，但 provisioned Aurora 並不像 Amazon RDS 那樣有簡單的「開啟 Multi-AZ」開關。AWS 文件指出，將既有 Aurora 叢集轉為 Multi-AZ 的方式是在不同 AZ 新增 reader DB instance——正是選項 A 的做法，而非 C 所述。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines two errors: provisioned Aurora has no 'Turn on Multi-AZ' option (you add a reader in another AZ instead), and a custom ANY endpoint cannot be relied on for writes because connections are distributed to any instance with equal probability, including read-only replicas.","why_zh":"結合兩個錯誤：provisioned Aurora 沒有「開啟 Multi-AZ」選項（而是在另一個 AZ 新增 reader），且 custom ANY endpoint 不能用於寫入，因為連線會以相同機率分散到任一 instance，包含唯讀 replica。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Concepts.AuroraHighAvailability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Overview.Endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Endpoints.Cluster.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Endpoints.Custom.Considerations.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":6,"question_en":"A company must encrypt all AMIs that the company shares across accounts. A DevOps engineer has access to a source account where an unencrypted custom AMI has been built. The DevOps engineer also has access to a target account where an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group will launch EC2 instances from the AMI. The DevOps engineer must share the AMI with the target account. The company has created an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key in the source account. Which additional steps should the DevOps engineer perform to meet the requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"公司必须对其跨账户共享的所有 AMI 进行加密。一位 DevOps 工程师能够访问源账户，在该账户中已构建 了一个未加密的自定义 AMI。该 DevOps 工程师还能够访问目标账户，在该账户中，Amazon EC2 自动扩展 组将从该 AMI 启动 EC2 实例。DevOps 工程师必须将 AMI 与目标账户共享。 该公司已在源账户中创建了一个 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥。 为了满足要求，DevOps 工程师还应执行哪些额外步骤？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"In the source account, copy the unencrypted AMI to an encrypted AMI. Specify the KMS key in the copy action.","B":"In the source account, copy the unencrypted AMI to an encrypted AMI. Specify the default Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) encryption key in the copy action.","C":"In the source account, create a KMS grant that delegates permissions to the Auto Scaling group service-linked role in the target account.","D":"In the source account, modify the key policy to give the target account permissions to create a grant. In the target account, create a KMS grant that delegates permissions to the Auto Scaling group service- linked role.","E":"In the source account, share the unencrypted AMI with the target account.","F":"In the source account, share the encrypted AMI with the target account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在源账户中，将未加密的 AMI 复制为加密的 AMI。在复制操作中指定 KMS 密钥。","B":"在源账户中，将未加密的 AMI 复制为加密的 AMI。在复制操作中指定默认的 Amazon 弹性块存储 （Amazon EBS）加密密钥。","C":"在源账户中，创建一个 KMS 授予，将权限委托给目标账户中的 Auto Scaling 组服务相关角色。","D":"在源账户中，修改密钥策略以授予目标账户创建授权的权限。在目标账户中，创建一个 KMS 授权，将权 限委托给 Auto Scaling 组服务相关角色。","E":"在源账户中，与目标账户共享未加密的 AMI。","F":"在源账户中，与目标账户共享加密的 AMI。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The goal is to share an AMI encrypted with a customer managed KMS key cross-account and let an Auto Scaling group in the target account launch from it. You cannot encrypt an AMI in place, so you copy the unencrypted AMI to an encrypted AMI and specify the source-account customer managed key in the CopyImage action; AWS documents exactly this 'Copy an unencrypted source AMI to an encrypted target AMI' scenario (A). You cannot use the default AWS managed EBS key because AMIs backed by snapshots encrypted with the default AWS managed key cannot be shared across accounts (eliminates B). For the target account's Auto Scaling group to launch instances with EBS volumes encrypted by a CMK that lives in a different account, AWS requires the two-step cross-account flow in 'Required AWS KMS key policy for use with encrypted volumes', Example 2: first the source account (the key owner) modifies the key policy to let the target account root call kms:CreateGrant, then from the target account you create a KMS grant whose grantee principal is the AWSServiceRoleForAutoScaling service-linked role (D). Finally you must share the encrypted AMI (not the unencrypted original) with the target account using modify-image-attribute (F).","explanation_zh":"目標是用 customer managed KMS key 加密 AMI 並跨帳號分享，讓目標帳號的 Auto Scaling group 從中啟動執行個體。AMI 無法原地加密，因此需將未加密 AMI 複製為加密 AMI，並在 CopyImage 動作中指定來源帳號的 customer managed key；AWS 文件正是記載此『Copy an unencrypted source AMI to an encrypted target AMI』情境（A）。不能用預設 AWS managed EBS key，因為以預設 AWS managed key 加密快照所支援的 AMI 無法跨帳號分享（排除 B）。要讓目標帳號的 Auto Scaling group 以位於另一帳號的 CMK 加密 EBS 磁碟區啟動執行個體，AWS 在『Required AWS KMS key policy for use with encrypted volumes』Example 2 規定了兩步驟跨帳號流程：先由來源帳號（key 擁有者）修改 key policy 允許目標帳號 root 呼叫 kms:CreateGrant，再從目標帳號建立 KMS grant，其 grantee principal 為 AWSServiceRoleForAutoScaling service-linked role（D）。最後必須以 modify-image-attribute 將加密後的 AMI（而非未加密的原始 AMI）分享給目標帳號（F）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Specifying the default EBS encryption key (the AWS managed key aws/ebs) is wrong: the AMI sharing documentation states explicitly that you cannot share AMIs backed by snapshots encrypted with the default AWS managed key. A customer managed key is required for cross-account sharing.","why_zh":"指定預設 EBS 加密金鑰（AWS 受管金鑰 aws/ebs）是錯的：AMI 分享文件明確指出，以預設 AWS managed key 加密快照所支援的 AMI 無法跨帳號分享。跨帳號分享必須使用 customer managed key。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The grant must be created FROM the target account (where the Auto Scaling group lives), not from the source account. Per Example 2, the source account only modifies the key policy to permit the target account root to call kms:CreateGrant; the target account then issues the grant to the AWSServiceRoleForAutoScaling service-linked role.","why_zh":"grant 必須由目標帳號（Auto Scaling group 所在帳號）建立，而非來源帳號。依 Example 2，來源帳號僅修改 key policy 允許目標帳號 root 呼叫 kms:CreateGrant；接著由目標帳號對 AWSServiceRoleForAutoScaling service-linked role 建立 grant。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Sharing the unencrypted AMI directly violates the explicit requirement that all AMIs shared across accounts must be encrypted; you must share the encrypted copy instead (F).","why_zh":"直接分享未加密 AMI 違反了所有跨帳號分享的 AMI 都必須加密的明確需求；應改為分享加密後的副本（F）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/key-policy-requirements-EBS-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/how-ami-copy-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/sharingamis-explicit.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":7,"question_en":"A company uses AWS CodePipeline pipelines to automate releases of its application A typical pipeline consists of three stages build, test, and deployment. The company has been using a separate AWS CodeBuild project to run scripts for each stage. However, the company now wants to use AWS CodeDeploy to handle the deployment stage of the pipelines. The company has packaged the application as an RPM package and must deploy the application to a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances are in an EC2 Auto Scaling group and are launched from a common AMI. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer perform to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 管道来自动化其应用程序的发布。典型的管道包含三个阶段：构建、测 试和部署。该公司此前一直使用单独的 AWS CodeBuild 项目来运行每个阶段的脚本。然而，该公司现 在希望使用 AWS CodeDeploy 来处理管道的部署阶段。 该公司已将应用程序打包为 RPM 软件包，并且必须将该应用程序部署到一组亚马逊 EC2 实例上。这些 EC2 实例位于一个 EC2 自动扩展组中，并且是从一个通用的 AMI 启动的。 DevOps 工程师应执行哪些步骤组合才能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new version of the common AMI with the CodeDeploy agent installed. Update the IAM role of the EC2 instances to allow access to CodeDeploy.","B":"Create a new version of the common AMI with the CodeDeploy agent installed. Create an AppSpec file that contains application deployment scripts and grants access to CodeDeploy.","C":"Create an application in CodeDeploy. Configure an in-place deployment type. Specify the Auto Scaling group as the deployment target. Add a step to the CodePipeline pipeline to use EC2 Image Builder to create a new AMI. Configure CodeDeploy to deploy the newly created AMI.","D":"Create an application in CodeDeploy. Configure an in-place deployment type. Specify the Auto Scaling group as the deployment target. Update the CodePipeline pipeline to use the CodeDeploy action to deploy the application.","E":"Create an application in CodeDeploy. Configure an in-place deployment type. Specify the EC2 instances that are launched from the common AMI as the deployment target. Update the CodePipeline pipeline to use the CodeDeploy action to deploy the application."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个安装了 CodeDeploy 代理的新通用 AMI 版本。更新 EC2 实例的 IAM 角色，以允许其访问 CodeDeploy。","B":"创建一个安装了 CodeDeploy 代理的新版本通用 AMI。创建一个包含应用程序部署脚本并授予 CodeDeploy 访问权限的 AppSpec 文件。","C":"在 CodeDeploy 中创建一个应用程序。配置为原地部署类型。指定 Auto Scaling 组作为部署目标。在 CodePipeline 管道中添加一个步骤，使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建新的 AMI。配置 CodeDeploy 以部署新 创建的 AMI。","D":"在 CodeDeploy 中创建一个应用程序。配置原地部署类型。指定 Auto Scaling 组作为部署目标。更新 CodePipeline 管道以使用 CodeDeploy 操作来部署应用程序。","E":"在 CodeDeploy 中创建一个应用程序。配置原地部署类型。指定从通用 AMI 启动的 EC2 实例作为部署目 标。更新 CodePipeline 管道以使用 CodeDeploy 操作来部署应用程序。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two prerequisites are required to use CodeDeploy for the deployment stage when targeting an EC2 Auto Scaling group of instances launched from a common AMI. (A) The CodeDeploy agent must run on every instance; because the instances boot from a shared AMI in an ASG, the documented method is to bake the agent into a new version of that AMI ('Using a custom AMI with CodeDeploy and Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling'), and the EC2 instance IAM role/instance profile must grant access to S3/CodeDeploy so the agent can poll for and download revisions (step 1 of 'Deploying CodeDeploy applications to Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling groups' is to create an IAM instance profile that lets the instances work with S3). (D) You create a CodeDeploy application, choose the in-place deployment type, and specify the Auto Scaling group name as the deployment target, then add the CodeDeploy action to the CodePipeline deployment stage. Targeting the ASG (not individual instances) is essential because CodeDeploy installs Auto Scaling launch lifecycle hooks so that instances added by future scale-out events automatically receive the latest deployed revision. CodeDeploy deploys application revisions (the RPM/files described by appspec.yml), not AMIs, so no EC2 Image Builder step is needed.","explanation_zh":"若要使用 CodeDeploy 對由共用 AMI 啟動、位於 EC2 Auto Scaling group 中的 instances 執行部署階段，需要兩項前置作業。（A）每台 instance 上都必須運行 CodeDeploy agent；由於這些 instances 從共用 AMI 在 ASG 中啟動，官方文件建議的做法是將 agent 預先烘焙進新版的該 AMI（'Using a custom AMI with CodeDeploy and Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling'），且 EC2 instance 的 IAM role / instance profile 必須授予存取 S3/CodeDeploy 的權限，agent 才能輪詢並下載 revision（'Deploying CodeDeploy applications to Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling groups' 的第 1 步即為建立讓 instances 能與 S3 協作的 IAM instance profile）。（D）建立 CodeDeploy application，選擇 in-place 部署類型，將 Auto Scaling group 名稱指定為部署目標，再於 CodePipeline 的部署階段加入 CodeDeploy action。以 ASG（而非個別 instances）為目標至關重要，因為 CodeDeploy 會安裝 Auto Scaling launch lifecycle hook，使未來 scale-out 事件新增的 instances 自動收到最新部署的 revision。CodeDeploy 部署的是 application revision（由 appspec.yml 描述的 RPM/檔案），而非 AMI，因此不需要 EC2 Image Builder 步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Baking the agent into the AMI is fine, but the AppSpec file does not 'grant access to CodeDeploy.' Access is granted through IAM roles/instance profiles; appspec.yml only declares what files to install and which lifecycle event hooks to run. The IAM instance profile (covered by A) is the actual missing prerequisite, so this option's second clause is technically false.","why_zh":"將 agent 烘焙進 AMI 沒問題，但 AppSpec 檔案並不會『授予存取 CodeDeploy 的權限』。權限是透過 IAM role / instance profile 授予；appspec.yml 僅宣告要安裝哪些檔案以及執行哪些 lifecycle event hook。實際缺少的前置作業是 IAM instance profile（由 A 涵蓋），因此本選項的第二個子句在技術上是錯誤的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeDeploy deploys application revisions (the RPM and files defined by appspec.yml), not AMIs. Adding an EC2 Image Builder step to build a new AMI and have CodeDeploy 'deploy the AMI' is the wrong mechanism for CodeDeploy and adds unnecessary operational overhead; replacing instances via a new AMI is an Auto Scaling/instance-refresh pattern, not a CodeDeploy revision deployment.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 部署的是 application revision（RPM 及 appspec.yml 定義的檔案），而非 AMI。加入 EC2 Image Builder 步驟建立新 AMI 並讓 CodeDeploy『部署該 AMI』對 CodeDeploy 而言是錯誤的機制，也帶來不必要的維運負擔；透過新 AMI 替換 instances 屬於 Auto Scaling / instance refresh 模式，而非 CodeDeploy 的 revision 部署。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Targeting the individual EC2 instances launched from the common AMI instead of the Auto Scaling group breaks the ASG integration. The deployment group must reference the Auto Scaling group name so CodeDeploy can install the launch lifecycle hook that auto-deploys to newly scaled-out instances; tag/instance targeting leaves future instances without the application.","why_zh":"以從共用 AMI 啟動的個別 EC2 instances 為目標，而非 Auto Scaling group，會破壞 ASG 整合。deployment group 必須引用 Auto Scaling group 名稱，CodeDeploy 才能安裝 launch lifecycle hook 以自動部署到新擴展出的 instances；以 tag/instance 為目標會使未來新增的 instances 缺少應用程式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/tutorials-auto-scaling-group.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/getting-started-create-iam-instance-profile.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":8,"question_en":"A company’s security team requires that all external Application Load Balancers (ALBs) and Amazon API Gateway APIs are associated with AWS WAF web ACLs. The company has hundreds of AWS accounts, all of which are included in a single organization in AWS Organizations. The company has configured AWS Config for the organization. During an audit, the company finds some externally facing ALBs that are not associated with AWS WAF web ACLs. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer take to prevent future violations? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司安全团队要求所有面向外部的应用程序负载均衡器（ALB）和 Amazon API Gateway API 都要与 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）相关联。该公司拥有数百个 AWS 账户，所有这些账户都包含在 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织内。该公司已为该组织配置了 AWS Config。在一次审计中，该公司发现了一些 面向外部的 ALB 未与 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表相关联。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪两种步骤组合来防止未来出现违规行为？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Delegate AWS Firewall Manager to a security account.","B":"Delegate Amazon GuardDuty to a security account.","C":"Create an AWS Firewall Manager policy to attach AWS WAF web ACLs to any newly created ALBs and API Gateway APIs.","D":"Create an Amazon GuardDuty policy to attach AWS WAF web ACLs to any newly created ALBs and API Gateway APIs.","E":"Configure an AWS Config managed rule to attach AWS WAF web ACLs to any newly created ALBs and API Gateway APIs."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AWS Firewall Manager 委托给一个安全账户。","B":"将 Amazon GuardDuty 委托给安全账户。","C":"创建一个 AWS Firewall Manager 策略，将 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）附加到任何新创 建的应用负载均衡器（ALB）和 API 网关 API 上。","D":"创建一个 Amazon GuardDuty 策略，将 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（ACL）附加到任何新创建的应 用负载均衡器（ALB）和 API 网关 API 上。","E":"配置 AWS Config 管理规则，将 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）附加到任何新创建的应用 负载均衡器（ALB）和 API 网关 API 上。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Firewall Manager is the purpose-built service for centrally and continuously enforcing AWS WAF web ACL associations across hundreds of accounts in an AWS Organization, which is exactly what 'prevent future violations' requires. Firewall Manager must run from a delegated administrator account: per the docs, 'only an organization's management account can create Firewall Manager administrator accounts,' so it designates a member (security) account as the Firewall Manager administrator (A) as the required prerequisite. You then create an AWS WAF Firewall Manager policy (C): the docs state Firewall Manager 'creates and manages web ACLs for in-scope resources,' automatically associating them, continuously remediating newly created or noncompliant resources, and even overriding a customer-attached web ACL. In-scope AWS WAF policy resource types include Application Load Balancers and Amazon API Gateway stages. By contrast, the AWS Config managed rule alb-waf-enabled only checks association and marks resources NON_COMPLIANT (detective only) and cannot attach web ACLs, and GuardDuty is a threat-detection service with no WAF-association capability and no such policy, so B, D, and E do not proactively prevent violations.","explanation_zh":"AWS Firewall Manager 是專為在 AWS Organizations 中跨數百個帳戶集中且持續強制套用 AWS WAF web ACL 關聯而設計的服務，正符合題目「防止未來違規」的需求。Firewall Manager 必須由委派管理員帳戶執行：文件指出「只有組織的 management account 才能建立 Firewall Manager 管理員帳戶」，由它指定某個成員（安全）帳戶作為 Firewall Manager 管理員（A），這是必要的前置步驟。接著建立 AWS WAF Firewall Manager 政策（C）：文件說明 Firewall Manager 會「為範圍內資源建立並管理 web ACL」，自動進行關聯並持續對新建立或不合規的資源進行修復，甚至會覆寫客戶手動關聯的 web ACL。AWS WAF 政策的範圍內資源類型包含 Application Load Balancers 與 Amazon API Gateway 階段。相對地，AWS Config 受管規則 alb-waf-enabled 只會檢查關聯並將資源標記為 NON_COMPLIANT（僅偵測），無法附加 web ACL；GuardDuty 則是威脅偵測服務，沒有 WAF 關聯能力，也不存在此類政策，因此 B、D、E 都無法主動防止違規。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that analyzes logs for malicious activity; it has no capability to associate AWS WAF web ACLs with ALBs or API Gateway, so delegating it does nothing for this requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是分析日誌以偵測惡意活動的威脅偵測服務，無法將 AWS WAF web ACL 關聯到 ALB 或 API Gateway，因此委派它對此需求毫無幫助。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no 'GuardDuty policy' that attaches AWS WAF web ACLs. GuardDuty does not create, manage, or associate web ACLs; this option describes a non-existent capability. WAF association policies are a Firewall Manager function.","why_zh":"並不存在會附加 AWS WAF web ACL 的「GuardDuty 政策」。GuardDuty 不會建立、管理或關聯 web ACL；此選項描述的是不存在的功能。WAF 關聯政策是 Firewall Manager 的功能。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"The AWS Config managed rule alb-waf-enabled only evaluates whether WAF is enabled and marks resources NON_COMPLIANT; Config managed rules are detective and cannot attach/associate web ACLs. They detect violations rather than proactively prevent them, and any remediation would require separate SSM Automation, not the rule itself.","why_zh":"AWS Config 受管規則 alb-waf-enabled 只會評估是否啟用 WAF 並將資源標記為 NON_COMPLIANT；Config 受管規則屬偵測性質，無法附加/關聯 web ACL，只能偵測違規而非主動防止，任何修復都需另行透過 SSM Automation 完成，而非規則本身。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/fms-creating-administrators.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/how-fms-manages-web-acls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/getting-started-fms-waf.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/alb-waf-enabled.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":9,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) keys and manual key rotation to meet regulatory compliance requirements. The security team wants to be notified when any keys have not been rotated after 90 days. Which solution will accomplish this?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥和手动密钥轮换来满足监管合规要求。安全团队希望 在任何密钥 90 天未轮换时收到通知。 哪种解决方案能实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS KMS to publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when keys are more than 90 days old.","B":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge event to launch an AWS Lambda function to call the AWS Trusted Advisor API and publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","C":"Develop an AWS Config custom rule that publishes to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when keys are more than 90 days old.","D":"Configure AWS Security Hub to publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when keys are more than 90 days old."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS KMS，使其在密钥超过 90 天时向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发布通知。","B":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件以启动一个 AWS Lambda 函数来调用 AWS Trusted Advisor API 并发 布到一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。","C":"创建一个 AWS Config 自定义规则，当密钥超过 90 天时向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发 布通知。","D":"配置 AWS 安全中心，使其在密钥超过 90 天时向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发布通知。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The company performs MANUAL KMS key rotation, which means replacing an existing KMS key with a brand-new key (with different cryptographic material) rather than letting KMS automatically rotate the backing key material. No native KMS feature, Trusted Advisor check, or Security Hub control evaluates whether a manually rotated key is older than 90 days and then notifies. The correct approach is an AWS Config CUSTOM rule (a periodic Lambda or Guard rule). AWS Config records AWS::KMS::Key as a supported resource type, so a custom rule can evaluate each key's creation date/age, flag keys older than 90 days as NON_COMPLIANT, and AWS Config natively sends a notification to an Amazon SNS topic when a resource's compliance status changes. The only AWS managed Config rule for KMS rotation (cmk-backing-key-rotation-enabled) merely checks whether AUTOMATIC rotation is enabled, which does not apply to manual rotation, so a custom rule is required.","explanation_zh":"此公司執行的是 MANUAL（手動）KMS key rotation，意即用一把全新的 KMS key（具有不同的密碼學金鑰材料）來取代既有的 key，而非讓 KMS 自動輪替底層金鑰材料。KMS 本身、Trusted Advisor 檢查項或 Security Hub 控制項都沒有原生功能可評估「手動輪替的 key 是否已超過 90 天」並發出通知。正確做法是使用 AWS Config 的 CUSTOM rule（定期觸發的 Lambda 或 Guard 規則）。AWS Config 將 AWS::KMS::Key 列為支援的 resource type，因此 custom rule 可評估每把 key 的建立日期/存在天數，將超過 90 天的 key 標記為 NON_COMPLIANT；當資源的 compliance 狀態改變時，AWS Config 原生會向 Amazon SNS topic 發送通知。唯一與 KMS 輪替相關的 AWS managed Config rule（cmk-backing-key-rotation-enabled）只檢查是否啟用 AUTOMATIC rotation，對手動輪替並不適用，因此必須使用 custom rule。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS KMS has no native feature to evaluate a key's age and publish to SNS when keys are more than 90 days old. KMS emits CloudTrail events and can integrate with EventBridge for rotation events, but it does not natively track a 90-day age threshold or push notifications based on key age. The capability is fabricated.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 沒有原生功能可評估 key 的存在天數並在超過 90 天時發布到 SNS。KMS 會產生 CloudTrail 事件並可透過 EventBridge 整合輪替事件，但不會原生追蹤 90 天的存在天數門檻或依 key 年齡推送通知，此能力為杜撰。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor has no check that evaluates KMS key age or manual-rotation status against a 90-day threshold. Its security checks cover items like exposed IAM access keys, MFA on root, S3 bucket permissions, and security groups, not custom KMS key-age compliance, so the Lambda calling the Trusted Advisor API would have no relevant data to act on.","why_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 沒有任何檢查項可依 90 天門檻評估 KMS key 的存在天數或手動輪替狀態。其安全檢查涵蓋如外洩的 IAM access key、root MFA、S3 bucket 權限與 security group 等，並不包含自訂的 KMS key 年齡合規檢查，因此呼叫 Trusted Advisor API 的 Lambda 取不到相關資料。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Security Hub does not have a control that flags manually rotated KMS keys older than 90 days. Its KMS-related control (KMS.4) only checks whether AUTOMATIC key rotation is enabled, which is irrelevant to manual rotation. Security Hub also does not publish to SNS based on its own custom logic; routing findings to SNS is done via EventBridge, and there is no such 90-day-age finding to begin with.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 沒有可標記「手動輪替且超過 90 天」KMS key 的控制項。其與 KMS 相關的控制項（KMS.4）僅檢查是否啟用 AUTOMATIC key rotation，與手動輪替無關。Security Hub 也不會依自身自訂邏輯直接發布到 SNS；將 findings 路由到 SNS 需透過 EventBridge，且根本不存在這種以 90 天年齡為基礎的 finding。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/rotate-keys-manually.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/resource-config-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/cmk-backing-key-rotation-enabled.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":10,"question_en":"A security review has identified that an AWS CodeBuild project is downloading a database population script from an Amazon S3 bucket using an unauthenticated request. The security team does not allow unauthenticated requests to S3 buckets for this project. How can this issue be corrected in the MOST secure manner?","question_zh":"安全审查发现，一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目正在使用未认证的请求从 Amazon S3 存储桶下载数据库填充 脚本。安全团队不允许此项目对 S3 存储桶发出未认证的请求。 如何以最安全的方式纠正这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Add the bucket name to the AllowedBuckets section of the CodeBuild project settings. Update the build spec to use the AWS CLI to download the database population script.","B":"Modify the S3 bucket settings to enable HTTPS basic authentication and specify a token. Update the build spec to use cURL to pass the token and download the database population script.","C":"Remove unauthenticated access from the S3 bucket with a bucket policy. Modify the service role for the CodeBuild project to include Amazon S3 access. Use the AWS CLI to download the database population script.","D":"Remove unauthenticated access from the S3 bucket with a bucket policy. Use the AWS CLI to download the database population script using an IAM access key and a secret access key."},"options_zh":{"A":"将存储桶名称添加到 CodeBuild 项目设置的“AllowedBuckets”部分。更新构建规范以使用 AWS CLI 下 载数据库填充脚本。","B":"修改 S3 存储桶设置以启用 HTTPS 基本身份验证并指定一个令牌。更新构建规范以使用 cURL 传递令 牌并下载数据库填充脚本。","C":"使用存储桶策略从 S3 存储桶中移除未认证访问权限。修改 CodeBuild 项目的服务角色以包含对 Amazon S3 的访问权限。使用 AWS CLI 下载数据库填充脚本。","D":"使用存储桶策略从 S3 存储桶中移除未认证访问权限。使用 AWS 命令行界面（AWS CLI），通 过 IAM 访问密钥和秘密访问密钥下载数据库填充脚本。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeBuild interacts with other AWS services through its IAM service role, which supplies temporary credentials that the AWS CLI automatically uses to make SigV4-signed (authenticated) requests. The most secure fix has two parts: (1) remove anonymous/unauthenticated read access from the S3 bucket with a bucket policy, since all S3 resources are private by default and a bucket policy is the tool to control who can read objects; and (2) grant the CodeBuild service role s3:GetObject (Amazon S3 access) so the build can authenticate using the role's temporary credentials. The build spec then uses the AWS CLI, which signs requests with those role credentials. This matches the AWS IAM best practice 'Require workloads to use temporary credentials with IAM roles to access AWS,' which states there is no need to distribute long-lived credentials to workloads running on AWS. Option C does exactly this. Option D also removes anonymous access, but it embeds long-term IAM access keys and a secret access key, which AWS explicitly discourages and is therefore less secure than reusing the existing service role.","explanation_zh":"CodeBuild 透過其 IAM service role 與其他 AWS 服務互動，該 role 提供臨時憑證 (temporary credentials)，而 AWS CLI 會自動使用這些憑證發出經過 SigV4 簽署的 (已驗證) 請求。最安全的修正分為兩部分：(1) 使用 bucket policy 移除 S3 bucket 的匿名／未驗證讀取存取，因為所有 S3 資源預設皆為私有，而 bucket policy 正是控制誰可讀取物件的工具；(2) 為 CodeBuild service role 授予 s3:GetObject (Amazon S3 存取權)，讓建置程序能以 role 的臨時憑證進行驗證。build spec 接著使用 AWS CLI，AWS CLI 會以這些 role 憑證簽署請求。這符合 AWS IAM 最佳實務「Require workloads to use temporary credentials with IAM roles to access AWS」，其明確指出在 AWS 上執行的工作負載無需散布長期憑證。選項 C 正是如此做。選項 D 雖然也移除了匿名存取，但卻嵌入長期 IAM access key 與 secret access key，這是 AWS 明確不建議的做法，因此比重用既有 service role 更不安全。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no 'AllowedBuckets' section in CodeBuild project settings; CodeBuild controls S3 access through its IAM service role, not a project-level bucket allowlist. The feature is fabricated, and nothing here makes the request authenticated, so it does not solve the security finding.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 專案設定中並沒有「AllowedBuckets」區段；CodeBuild 透過其 IAM service role 控制 S3 存取，而非專案層級的 bucket 允許清單。此功能屬虛構，且沒有任何機制讓請求變成已驗證，因此無法解決此安全問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon S3 does not support 'HTTPS basic authentication' with a token. S3 authenticates requests using AWS Signature Version 4 with IAM credentials. Passing a token via cURL is not a valid S3 authentication method, so this option describes a nonexistent feature and is not secure.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 不支援使用 token 的「HTTPS basic authentication」。S3 是以 AWS Signature Version 4 搭配 IAM 憑證驗證請求。透過 cURL 傳遞 token 並非有效的 S3 驗證方式，因此此選項描述一個不存在的功能，且並不安全。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This correctly removes anonymous access, but it authenticates with a long-term IAM access key and secret access key, which requires storing static credentials in the build. AWS IAM best practices direct workloads on AWS to use IAM role temporary credentials instead of distributing long-lived keys, so D is functional but less secure than reusing the CodeBuild service role in option C. The question asks for the MOST secure approach.","why_zh":"此選項正確地移除了匿名存取，但卻以長期 IAM access key 與 secret access key 進行驗證，這需要在建置中儲存靜態憑證。AWS IAM 最佳實務指出在 AWS 上的工作負載應使用 IAM role 的臨時憑證，而非散布長期金鑰，因此 D 雖可運作，但比選項 C 重用 CodeBuild service role 更不安全。題目要求「最安全」的做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/setting-up-service-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":11,"question_en":"An ecommerce company has chosen AWS to host its new platform. The company's DevOps team has started building an AWS Control Tower landing zone. The DevOps team has set the identity store within AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to external identity provider (IdP) and has configured SAML 2.0. The DevOps team wants a robust permission model that applies the principle of least privilege. The model must allow the team to build and manage only the team's own resources. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家电子商务公司已选择 AWS 来托管其新平台。该公司的 DevOps 团队已开始构建 AWS 控制塔着陆区。 DevOps 团队已将身份存储设置为 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）中的外部身份提供程序（IdP）， 并已配置 SAML 2.0。 DevOps 团队希望采用一种强大的权限模型，遵循最小权限原则。该模型必须允许团队仅构建和管理团队自 身的资源。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create IAM policies that include the required permissions. Include the aws:PrincipalTag condition key.","B":"Create permission sets. Attach an inline policy that includes the required permissions and uses the aws:PrincipalTag condition key to scope the permissions.","C":"Create a group in the IdP. Place users in the group. Assign the group to accounts and the permission sets in IAM Identity Center.","D":"Create a group in the IdP. Place users in the group. Assign the group to OUs and IAM policies.","E":"Enable attributes for access control in IAM Identity Center. Apply tags to users. Map the tags as key- value pairs.","F":"Enable attributes for access control in IAM Identity Center. Map attributes from the IdP as key-value pairs."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建包含所需权限的 IAM 策略。包含 aws:PrincipalTag 条件键。","B":"创建权限集。附加一个内联策略，其中包含所需的权限并使用 AWS：用于限定权限范围的 PrincipalTag 条件键。","C":"在身份提供方（IdP）中创建一个组。将用户放入该组。在 IAM 身份中心中将该组分配给账户 和权限集。","D":"在身份提供方（IdP）中创建一个组。将用户放入该组。将该组分配给组织单位（OU）和 IAM 策略。","E":"在 IAM 身份中心启用用于访问控制的属性。为用户应用标签。将标签映射为键值对。","F":"在 IAM 身份中心启用用于访问控制的属性。将来自身份提供方的属性映射为键值对。"},"answer":["B","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical IAM Identity Center attribute-based access control (ABAC) pattern with an external SAML 2.0 IdP. (B) In IAM Identity Center, permissions are delivered through permission sets, which contain IAM policies (managed or inline) that Identity Center deploys as IAM roles in each assigned account. To enforce least privilege so the team manages only its own resources, the permission set's inline policy uses the aws:PrincipalTag condition key (e.g., \"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\") to scope access to resources tagged for that team. (C) Access is granted by assigning a group (AWS recommends groups over individual users) to AWS accounts together with one or more permission sets on the AWS accounts page; you cannot assign to OUs and you do not attach raw IAM policies in the assignment, which eliminates D. (F) Because the identity source is an external IdP using SAML 2.0, you enable Attributes for access control and source the attributes from the IdP (passed through SAML assertions or mapped from synchronized IdP attributes); Identity Center then passes them as session tags referenced by aws:PrincipalTag. The decisive contrast is E vs F: both begin with 'Enable attributes for access control,' but E ('Apply tags to users') describes the Identity Store / IAM Identity Center-as-identity-source flow where you manually set user attributes, which does not match an external SAML IdP, whereas F ('Map attributes from the IdP') correctly reflects sourcing attributes from the external IdP.","explanation_zh":"這是搭配外部 SAML 2.0 IdP 的 IAM Identity Center 屬性型存取控制 (ABAC) 標準模式。(B) 在 IAM Identity Center 中，權限是透過 permission sets 交付；permission set 包含 IAM 政策（受管或內嵌），Identity Center 會在每個被指派的帳戶中部署為 IAM 角色。為落實最小權限、讓團隊只管理自己的資源，permission set 的內嵌政策會使用 aws:PrincipalTag 條件鍵（例如 \"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\"），把存取範圍限縮到標記給該團隊的資源。(C) 存取是在 AWS accounts 頁面把群組（AWS 建議用群組而非個別使用者）指派給 AWS 帳戶並搭配一或多個 permission sets 來授予；無法指派給 OU，指派時也不會附加原始 IAM 政策，因此排除 D。(F) 由於身分來源是使用 SAML 2.0 的外部 IdP，你需啟用 Attributes for access control，並從 IdP 取得屬性（透過 SAML 斷言傳遞，或對應已同步的 IdP 屬性）；Identity Center 接著會把它們以 session tags 傳遞，供 aws:PrincipalTag 引用。關鍵對比在於 E 與 F：兩者都以「Enable attributes for access control」開頭，但 E（對使用者套用標籤）描述的是 Identity Store／IAM Identity Center 作為身分來源的流程，需手動設定使用者屬性，與外部 SAML IdP 情境不符；F（對應來自 IdP 的屬性）才正確反映從外部 IdP 取得屬性。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM Identity Center grants access through permission sets, not standalone IAM identity policies. While the aws:PrincipalTag condition key idea is correct, creating plain IAM policies is the wrong delivery mechanism for an IAM Identity Center landing zone; the policy belongs inside a permission set (B).","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 是透過 permission sets 授權，而非獨立的 IAM 身分政策。雖然使用 aws:PrincipalTag 條件鍵的概念正確，但在 IAM Identity Center landing zone 中建立純 IAM policy 是錯誤的交付機制；該政策應放在 permission set 內（即 B）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"In IAM Identity Center you assign groups/users to AWS accounts paired with permission sets, not to OUs, and you do not attach raw IAM policies to assignments. OU-level targeting and IAM-policy attachment are not how IAM Identity Center assignments work, so this step is technically invalid.","why_zh":"在 IAM Identity Center 中是將 group/user 指派到搭配 permission set 的 AWS accounts，而非指派到 OU，也不會將原生 IAM policy 掛在指派上。以 OU 為對象、掛載 IAM policy 並非 IAM Identity Center 的指派運作方式，故此步驟技術上無效。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"'Apply tags to users' and mapping those tags applies when IAM Identity Center (or its Identity Store) is the identity source and you set user attributes manually. With an external SAML 2.0 IdP, attributes are sourced from the IdP and passed via SAML assertions, so you map IdP attributes (F), not user-applied tags. F is the precise external-IdP choice.","why_zh":"「Apply tags to users」（為使用者套用標籤）並對應這些標籤，適用於以 IAM Identity Center（或其 Identity Store）作為身分來源、手動設定使用者屬性的情境。使用外部 SAML 2.0 IdP 時，屬性來自 IdP 並透過 SAML 斷言傳遞，因此應對應 IdP 屬性（F），而非由使用者套用的標籤。F 才是針對外部 IdP 的精確選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/attributesforaccesscontrol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/permissionsetsconcept.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/assignusers.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":12,"question_en":"An ecommerce company is receiving reports that its order history page is experiencing delays in reflecting the processing status of orders. The order processing system consists of an AWS Lambda function that uses reserved concurrency. The Lambda function processes order messages from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue and inserts processed orders into an Amazon DynamoDB table. The DynamoDB table has auto scaling enabled for read and write capacity. Which actions should a DevOps engineer take to resolve this delay? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家电子商务公司收到报告称，其订单历史页面在反映订单处理状态时出现延迟。该公司的订单处 理系统由一个使用预留并发量的 AWS Lambda 函数组成。该 Lambda 函数从 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列中处理订单消息，并将处理后的订单插入到一个启用了读写容量自动扩 展的 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些行动来解决此延误？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Check the ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage metric for the SQS queue. Increase the Lambda function concurrency limit.","B":"Check the ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage metric for the SQS queue Configure a redrive policy on the SQS queue.","C":"Check the NumberOfMessagesSent metric for the SQS queue. Increase the SQS queue visibility timeout.","D":"Check the WriteThrottleEvents metric for the DynamoDB table. Increase the maximum write capacity units (WCUs) for the table's scaling policy.","E":"Check the Throttles metric for the Lambda function. Increase the Lambda function timeout."},"options_zh":{"A":"检查 SQS 队列的“ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage”指标。提高 Lambda 函数的并发限制。","B":"检查 SQS 队列的“ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage”指标。为 SQS 队列配置重传策略。","C":"检查 SQS 队列的“已发送消息数”指标。增加 SQS 队列的可见性超时时间。","D":"检查 DynamoDB 表的 WriteThrottleEvents 指标。增加表的自动扩展策略的最大写入容量单位 （WCUs）。","E":"检查 Lambda 函数的节流指标。增加 Lambda 函数的超时时间。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The delay has two independent causes — a queue-side throughput bottleneck and a database-side throttling bottleneck — so two distinct fixes are required. (A) The Lambda function uses reserved concurrency, which AWS documents as acting 'as both a lower and upper bound', preventing the function from scaling beyond that limit. When messages arrive faster than the capped concurrency can drain them, the Lambda event-source-mapping troubleshooting guide states the symptom is backpressure with 'the age of the oldest message growing linearly' (the ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage metric), and a listed resolution is to raise the function's concurrency. (D) Even with Auto Scaling enabled, the DynamoDB provisioned-throughput documentation explicitly states 'Throttling can occur regardless of whether Auto Scaling is enabled... it does not respond instantly and it is constrained by the maximum capacity limits you configure.' Because the Lambda inserts (writes) processed orders, you detect this with the WriteThrottleEvents metric ('Watch for requests that exceed the provisioned WCU') and remediate sustained traffic that hits the ceiling by raising the maximum WCU in the scaling policy. Together A and D clear both bottlenecks delaying order-status updates.","explanation_zh":"延遲有兩個獨立成因——佇列端的吞吐量瓶頸與資料庫端的節流瓶頸——因此需要兩個不同的修正。(A) 此 Lambda 使用 reserved concurrency，AWS 文件說明其「同時作為下限與上限」，會阻止函式擴展超過該上限。當訊息湧入速度快於受上限限制的並行度所能消化的速度時，Lambda event source mapping 疑難排解指南指出症狀為 backpressure，亦即「最舊訊息的存留時間呈線性成長」（即 ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage 指標），其列出的解法之一即為提高函式的並行度上限。(D) 即使已啟用 Auto Scaling，DynamoDB provisioned throughput 文件明確指出「節流不論是否啟用 Auto Scaling 都可能發生……它不會即時反應，且受限於你設定的最大容量上限。」由於 Lambda 將處理後的訂單寫入資料表，你可用 WriteThrottleEvents 指標偵測（『監看超過已佈建 WCU 的請求』），並透過提高 scaling policy 的最大 WCU 來緩解持續觸頂的流量。A 與 D 一併清除兩個導致訂單狀態更新延遲的瓶頸。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage is the correct diagnostic metric, but a redrive policy only sends repeatedly failed messages to a dead-letter queue. It handles poison/failing messages, not a throughput backlog, so it adds no processing capacity and does not relieve the backpressure causing the delay.","why_zh":"ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage 是正確的診斷指標，但 redrive policy 只會把反覆失敗的訊息送往 dead-letter queue，處理的是毒丸/失敗訊息而非吞吐量積壓，並不會增加處理能力，也無法紓解造成延遲的 backpressure。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"NumberOfMessagesSent measures the producer's send rate, not the consumer backlog, so it does not diagnose the delay. Worse, increasing the visibility timeout keeps in-flight messages invisible longer, which does not add throughput and can make the delay appear worse rather than resolving it.","why_zh":"NumberOfMessagesSent 衡量的是生產者送出速率，而非消費端積壓，無法診斷延遲。更糟的是，增加 visibility timeout 會讓處理中的訊息隱形更久，既不增加吞吐量，反而可能加重延遲表現而非解決問題。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Throttles is a valid Lambda metric, but the proposed fix is wrong: throttling stems from hitting the reserved-concurrency cap, not from short durations. Increasing the function timeout makes each invocation hold a concurrency slot longer, reducing effective throughput and worsening both throttling and the backlog.","why_zh":"Throttles 是合理的 Lambda 指標，但所提修正錯誤：節流源自觸及 reserved concurrency 上限，而非執行時間過短。增加函式 timeout 會讓每次調用占用並行槽更久，降低有效吞吐量，反而加重節流與積壓。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/troubleshooting-event-source-mapping.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/throttling-provisioned-capacity-exceeded-mitigation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/TroubleshootingThrottling-cloudwatch.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":13,"question_en":"A company has a single AWS account that runs hundreds of Amazon EC2 instances in a single AWS Region. New EC2 instances are launched and terminated each hour in the account. The account also includes existing EC2 instances that have been running for longer than a week. The company's security policy requires all running EC2 instances to use an EC2 instance profile. If an EC2 instance does not have an instance profile attached, the EC2 instance must use a default instance profile that has no IAM permissions assigned. A DevOps engineer reviews the account and discovers EC2 instances that are running without an instance profile. During the review, the DevOps engineer also observes that new EC2 instances are being launched without an instance profile. Which solution will ensure that an instance profile is attached to all existing and future EC2 instances in the Region?","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 AWS 账户中运行着数百个位于单个 AWS 区域的亚马逊 EC2 实例。该账户每 小时都会启动和终止新的 EC2 实例，同时还包含运行时间超过一周的现有 EC2 实例。 该公司的安全策略要求所有正在运行的 EC2 实例都使用 EC2 实例配置文件。如果某个 EC2 实例未 附加实例配置文件，则该 EC2 实例必须使用默认的实例配置文件，且该默认配置文件未分配任何 IAM 权限。 一位 DevOps 工程师审查了账户，发现有 EC2 实例在没有实例配置文件的情况下运行。在审查过程 中，该 DevOps 工程师还注意到新启动的 EC2 实例也没有配置实例配置文件。 哪种解决方案能确保将实例配置文件附加到该区域内的所有现有和未来的 EC2 实例？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EC2 RunInstances API calls. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","B":"Configure the ec2-instance-profile-attached AWS Config managed rule with a trigger type of configuration changes. Configure an automatic remediation action that invokes an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","C":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EC2 StartInstances API calls. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances","D":"Configure the iam-role-managed-policy-check AWS Config managed rule with a trigger type of configuration changes. Configure an automatic remediation action that invokes an AWS Lambda function to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 EC2 的 RunInstances API 调用做出反应。将该规则 配置为调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例上。","B":"配置带有配置更改触发类型的“ec2 实例配置文件附加”AWS Config 管理规则。配置一个 自动修复操作，调用 AWS Systems。 用于将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例的经理自动化运行手册。","C":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 EC2 的 StartInstances API 调用做出反应。将该规则配置为 调用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例上。","D":"配置 AWS Config 管理规则 iam-role-managed-policy-check，触发类型为配置更改。配置自动修复操 作，调用 AWS Lambda 函数将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to attach an instance profile to ALL existing AND future EC2 instances. AWS Config's managed rule ec2-instance-profile-attached (identifier EC2_INSTANCE_PROFILE_ATTACHED) evaluates resource type AWS::EC2::Instance and is NON_COMPLIANT when no IAM profile is attached; its documented trigger type is exactly 'Configuration changes'. Because AWS Config records and evaluates the full inventory of EC2 instances, the long-running existing instances and every newly launched instance are all evaluated. Pairing the rule with an automatic remediation action that runs an SSM Automation runbook fixes the violations: the AWS Config docs state that enabling auto remediation 'initiates the remediation process for all noncompliant resources for that specific rule,' which covers the existing noncompliant instances, while the configuration-change trigger evaluates and remediates each new instance as it is created. Option B is the only choice that uses the correct rule, correct resource type, and a mechanism that reaches both the existing and future populations.","explanation_zh":"需求是要為「所有現有與未來」的 EC2 instances 附加 instance profile。AWS Config 的 managed rule ec2-instance-profile-attached（識別碼 EC2_INSTANCE_PROFILE_ATTACHED）評估資源類型 AWS::EC2::Instance，當沒有附加 IAM profile 時判定為 NON_COMPLIANT；其文件記載的 trigger type 正好是「Configuration changes」。由於 AWS Config 會記錄並評估完整的 EC2 instance 清單，因此既能涵蓋長期運行的現有 instances，也能涵蓋每個新啟動的 instance。將此 rule 搭配自動修復動作（automatic remediation action）執行 SSM Automation runbook，即可修正違規：AWS Config 文件明確指出啟用 auto remediation 會「對該 rule 的所有 noncompliant 資源啟動修復流程」，涵蓋現有不合規的 instances；而 configuration-change 觸發則會在每個新 instance 建立時加以評估並修復。選項 B 是唯一使用正確 rule、正確資源類型，並能同時觸及現有與未來兩類 instances 的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An EventBridge rule reacting to the RunInstances API only catches NEW instance launches and does nothing for the existing instances that have already been running for over a week, so it fails the 'all existing' part of the requirement.","why_zh":"對 RunInstances API 反應的 EventBridge rule 只能捕捉「新啟動」的 instance，對已運行超過一週的現有 instances 完全無作為，因此無法滿足「所有現有」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An EventBridge rule on StartInstances fires only when a stopped instance is started; it does not catch newly launched (RunInstances) instances nor already-running existing instances, so neither future launches nor existing running instances are reliably covered.","why_zh":"針對 StartInstances 的 EventBridge rule 僅在已停止的 instance 被重新啟動時觸發；它無法捕捉新啟動（屬於 RunInstances）的 instance，也無法處理已在運行的現有 instances，因此未來啟動與現有運行中的 instances 都無法可靠涵蓋。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The iam-role-managed-policy-check rule (IAM_ROLE_MANAGED_POLICY_CHECK) evaluates AWS::IAM::Role resources to verify that specified managed policies are attached to a role. It has nothing to do with whether an EC2 instance has an instance profile attached, so it cannot detect or remediate the actual non-compliance.","why_zh":"iam-role-managed-policy-check rule（IAM_ROLE_MANAGED_POLICY_CHECK）評估的是 AWS::IAM::Role 資源，確認指定的 managed policies 是否附加到 role，與 EC2 instance 是否附加 instance profile 完全無關，因此無法偵測或修復實際的不合規狀況。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/ec2-instance-profile-attached.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/iam-role-managed-policy-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":14,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building a continuous deployment pipeline for a serverless application that uses AWS Lambda functions. The company wants to reduce the customer impact of an unsuccessful deployment. The company also wants to monitor for issues. Which deploy stage configuration will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一个使用 AWS Lambda 函数的无服务器应用程序构建持续部署流水线。该公 司希望将不成功的部署对客户造成的影响降到最低。同时，该公司还希望对问题进行监控。 哪种部署阶段配置能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) template to define the serverless application. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the Lambda functions with the Canary10Percent15Minutes Deployment Preference Type. Use Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor the health of the functions.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation to publish a new stack update, and include Amazon CloudWatch alarms on all resources. Set up an AWS CodePipeline approval action for a developer to verify and approve the AWS CloudFormation change set.","C":"Use AWS CloudFormation to publish a new version on every stack update, and include Amazon CloudWatch alarms on all resources. Use the RoutingConfig property of the AWS::Lambda::Alias resource to update the traffic routing during the stack update.","D":"Use AWS CodeBuild to add sample event payloads for testing to the Lambda functions. Publish a new version of the functions, and include Amazon CloudWatch alarms. Update the production alias to point to the new version. Configure rollbacks to occur when an alarm is in the ALARM state."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 无服务器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）模板来定义无服务器应用程序。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 以“金丝雀 10% 15 分钟”部署偏好类型部署 Lambda 函数。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控函数 的运行状况。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 发布新的堆栈更新，并在所有资源上设置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。为开发 人员设置一个 AWS CodePipeline 批准操作，以验证并批准 AWS CloudFormation 更改集。","C":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 在每次堆栈更新时发布新版本，并在所有资源上包含 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。使用 AWS::Lambda::Alias 资源的 RoutingConfig 属性在堆栈更新期间更新流量 路由。","D":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 为 Lambda 函数添加用于测试的示例事件负载。发布函数的新版本，并包含 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。将生产别名更新为指向新版本。配置在警报处于 ALARM 状态时执行回滚。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are to reduce customer impact of an unsuccessful deployment (gradual traffic shifting with automatic rollback) and to monitor for issues (CloudWatch alarms). AWS SAM has built-in CodeDeploy integration for gradual Lambda deployments: by adding AutoPublishAlias and a DeploymentPreference containing a Type and Alarms, SAM automatically creates a CodeDeploy resource that publishes a new version, creates/updates an alias, and gradually shifts traffic. Canary10Percent15Minutes is an officially listed Deployment Preference Type that shifts 10% of traffic to the new version and the remaining 90% after 15 minutes, limiting blast radius. The Alarms property tells CodeDeploy to automatically roll back the deployment when a CloudWatch alarm enters the ALARM state, satisfying both the monitoring and the safe-deployment requirements. This is the AWS-prescribed safe-deployment pattern for serverless Lambda, so A is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是降低部署失敗對客戶的影響（漸進式流量轉移並自動回滾），以及監控問題（CloudWatch alarms）。AWS SAM 內建與 CodeDeploy 整合以提供 Lambda 漸進式部署：在範本中加入 AutoPublishAlias 以及包含 Type 與 Alarms 的 DeploymentPreference 後，SAM 會自動建立一個 CodeDeploy 資源，發佈新版本、建立或更新 alias，並逐步轉移流量。Canary10Percent15Minutes 是官方列出的 Deployment Preference Type，會先將 10% 流量導向新版本，15 分鐘後再轉移剩餘 90%，藉此限制影響範圍。Alarms 屬性會讓 CodeDeploy 在 CloudWatch alarm 進入 ALARM 狀態時自動回滾部署，同時滿足監控與安全部署的需求。這正是 AWS 為 serverless Lambda 規定的安全部署模式，因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A plain CloudFormation stack update is an all-at-once cutover, so a faulty change immediately affects 100% of customers. A manual CodePipeline approval action only gates the change set before deployment; it provides no gradual traffic shifting and the alarms are not wired into any automatic rollback, so it does not reduce customer impact of an unsuccessful deployment.","why_zh":"單純的 CloudFormation stack update 是一次性全量切換，有問題的變更會立即影響 100% 客戶。手動 CodePipeline approval action 只是在部署前對 change set 設關卡，並未提供漸進式流量轉移，且 alarms 未串接任何自動回滾，因此無法降低部署失敗對客戶的影響。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Setting the RoutingConfig (VersionWeight) on AWS::Lambda::Alias gives a static, manually defined weight applied during the stack update; it is not an automated time-based canary, and CloudFormation does not automatically roll back the alias weighting based on those CloudWatch alarms the way CodeDeploy does. The alarms are merely included on resources, not part of an orchestrated alarm-driven rollback, so it is a clunky approximation rather than the prescribed safe-deployment mechanism.","why_zh":"在 AWS::Lambda::Alias 上設定 RoutingConfig（VersionWeight）只是在 stack update 時套用靜態、手動定義的權重，並非自動的時間式 canary，且 CloudFormation 不會像 CodeDeploy 那樣依據這些 CloudWatch alarms 自動回滾別名權重。alarms 只是被包含在資源上，並非協調式 alarm 回滾的一部分，因此是笨拙的近似做法，而非標準的安全部署機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Updating the production alias to point directly to the new version is a 100% all-at-once cutover, immediately exposing all customers to the new code, so it does not reduce customer impact. Rolling back only after an alarm fires happens after full exposure, and the CodeBuild sample-payload testing plus hand-built alias-flip/rollback do not provide the native, time-incremented canary shifting the requirement calls for.","why_zh":"將 production alias 直接指向新版本是 100% 一次性全量切換，會立即將所有客戶暴露於新程式碼，無法降低客戶影響。僅在 alarm 觸發後才回滾是在全量暴露之後才動作，且 CodeBuild 的範例 payload 測試加上手動的 alias 切換/回滾並未提供需求所要求的原生、按時間漸進的 canary 轉移。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/automating-updates-to-serverless-apps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/sam-property-function-deploymentpreference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/tutorial-lambda-sam-template.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuring-alias-routing.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":15,"question_en":"To run an application, a DevOps engineer launches an Amazon EC2 instance with public IP addresses in a public subnet. A user data script obtains the application artifacts and installs them on the instances upon launch. A change to the security classification of the application now requires the instances to run with no access to the internet. While the instances launch successfully and show as healthy, the application does not seem to be installed. Which of the following should successfully install the application while complying with the new rule?","question_zh":"要运行应用程序，DevOps 工程师会在公共子网中启动具有公共 IP 地址的 Amazon EC2 实例。用户数据脚本 在实例启动时获取应用程序构件并将其安装在实例上。现在，由于应用程序的安全分类发生变化，要求这些 实例在运行时不能访问互联网。虽然实例成功启动并显示为正常运行，但应用程序似乎并未安装。 以下哪一项在符合新规则的情况下应能成功安装该应用程序？","options_en":{"A":"Launch the instances in a public subnet with Elastic IP addresses attached. Once the application is installed and running, run a script to disassociate the Elastic IP addresses afterwards.","B":"Set up a NAT gateway. Deploy the EC2 instances to a private subnet. Update the private subnet's route table to use the NAT gateway as the default route.","C":"Publish the application artifacts to an Amazon S3 bucket and create a VPC endpoint for S3. Assign an IAM instance profile to the EC2 instances so they can read the application artifacts from the S3 bucket.","D":"Create a security group for the application instances and allow only outbound traffic to the artifact repository. Remove the security group rule once the install is complete."},"options_zh":{"A":"在带有弹性 IP 地址的公共子网中启动实例。应用程序安装并运行后，运行一个脚本将弹性 IP 地址解 除关联。","B":"设置一个 NAT 网关。将 EC2 实例部署到私有子网。更新私有子网的路由表，将 NAT 网关设置为默 认路由。","C":"将应用程序构件发布到 Amazon S3 存储桶，并为 S3 创建一个 VPC 端点。为 EC2 实例分配一个 IAM 实 例配置文件，以便它们可以从 S3 存储桶读取应用程序构件。","D":"为应用程序实例创建一个安全组，并仅允许向工件存储库发送出站流量。安装完成后删除该安全组 规则。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The new security classification requires the instances to have NO access to the internet, yet the user data script must still be able to fetch and install the application artifacts. A gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3 satisfies both constraints. The AWS documentation states explicitly that with a gateway endpoint 'you can access Amazon S3 from your VPC, without requiring an internet gateway or NAT device for your VPC' - the traffic stays on the AWS network and never touches the internet. By publishing the artifacts to an S3 bucket, creating an S3 gateway endpoint (and adding it as a route table target), and attaching an IAM instance profile that grants s3:GetObject, the instances can privately download and install the artifacts with zero internet exposure. This is the only option that both installs the application and fully complies with the no-internet rule.","explanation_zh":"新的安全分類要求這些 instance 完全沒有 internet 存取權，但 user data script 仍必須能取得並安裝應用程式 artifacts。Amazon S3 的 gateway VPC endpoint 同時滿足這兩個條件。AWS 文件明確指出，使用 gateway endpoint 時「可在不需要 internet gateway 或 NAT device 的情況下從 VPC 存取 Amazon S3」，流量保留在 AWS 網路內，完全不會經過 internet。將 artifacts 發布到 S3 bucket、建立 S3 gateway endpoint（並將其加入 route table 作為目標），再為 instance 附加授予 s3:GetObject 的 IAM instance profile，instance 即可在零 internet 暴露的情況下私密地下載並安裝 artifacts。這是唯一既能安裝應用程式又完全符合無 internet 規則的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Elastic IP addresses in a public subnet require an internet gateway and give the instances direct internet access during installation, which violates the no-internet requirement. Disassociating the EIPs afterward does not undo the internet access already used, and it is operationally fragile - relying on a timing race to detach the EIPs.","why_zh":"public subnet 中的 Elastic IP 需要 internet gateway，並在安裝期間讓 instance 擁有直接的 internet 存取，違反無 internet 要求。事後解除 EIP 關聯並無法改變已使用 internet 存取的事實，且此做法很脆弱，依賴時序競態來卸除 EIP。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A public NAT gateway is explicitly designed to enable instances in a private subnet to send outbound traffic to the internet. The AWS docs describe its primary use case as 'Access the internet from a private subnet,' so adding it as the default route grants internet access and directly violates the 'no access to the internet' requirement.","why_zh":"public NAT gateway 的設計目的正是讓 private subnet 中的 instance 將出站流量傳送至 internet。AWS 文件將其主要用途描述為「從 private subnet 存取 internet」，因此將其設為預設路由會授予 internet 存取權，直接違反「無 internet 存取」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A security group only filters traffic; it does not provide a network path to a repository that lives on the internet. Reaching an internet-hosted artifact repository still requires an internet gateway or NAT (and thus internet access, violating the rule), and without that route the instances cannot connect at all. This neither complies with the rule nor reliably installs the application.","why_zh":"security group 只能過濾流量，並不會為位於 internet 上的 repository 提供網路路徑。要存取 internet 上的 artifact repository 仍需要 internet gateway 或 NAT（因此屬於 internet 存取，違反規則），而在沒有該路由的情況下 instance 根本無法連線。這既不符合規則，也無法可靠地安裝應用程式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/gateway-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nat-gateway-scenarios.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat-gateway.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":16,"question_en":"A development team is using AWS CodeCommit to version control application code and AWS CodePipeline to orchestrate software deployments. The team has decided to use a remote main branch as the trigger for the pipeline to integrate code changes. A developer has pushed code changes to the CodeCommit repository, but noticed that the pipeline had no reaction, even after 10 minutes. Which of the following actions should be taken to troubleshoot this issue?","question_zh":"一个开发团队正在使用 AWS CodeCommit 来对应用程序代码进行版本控制，并使用 AWS CodePipeline 来编 排软件部署。该团队决定使用远程主分支作为触发管道以集成代码更改的触发器。一名开发人员已将代码更 改推送到 CodeCommit 存储库，但注意到即使过了 10 分钟，管道也没有任何反应。 为解决此问题，应采取以下哪项措施？","options_en":{"A":"Check that an Amazon EventBridge rule has been created for the main branch to trigger the pipeline.","B":"Check that the CodePipeline service role has permission to access the CodeCommit repository.","C":"Check that the developer’s IAM role has permission to push to the CodeCommit repository.","D":"Check to see if the pipeline failed to start because of CodeCommit errors in Amazon CloudWatch Logs."},"options_zh":{"A":"检查是否为主分支创建了 Amazon EventBridge 规则以触发管道。","B":"检查 CodePipeline 服务角色是否具有访问 CodeCommit 代码库的权限。","C":"检查开发人员的 IAM 角色是否有权向 CodeCommit 存储库推送内容。","D":"检查一下是否 管道启动失败，原因是 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中出现了 CodeCommit 错误。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For a CodeCommit source action, CodePipeline uses an Amazon EventBridge rule as the default and recommended change-detection mechanism (created by the console wizard). When code is pushed to the monitored branch, that rule fires and starts the pipeline. The AWS troubleshooting topic 'Pipelines with an Amazon S3, Amazon ECR, or CodeCommit source no longer start automatically' states that when the event rule is not created/updated, 'the pipeline no longer starts automatically' - precisely the 'no reaction' symptom here, and it specifically lists Repository name + Branch name as the CodeCommit trigger identifiers. So verifying that an EventBridge rule exists and is scoped to the main branch (Option A) is the correct first troubleshooting step. The decisive qualifier is the symptom: the pipeline never started at all, which points to the change-detection trigger rather than a permissions failure that would let the pipeline start and then surface a visible error.","explanation_zh":"對於 CodeCommit source action，CodePipeline 預設且建議使用 Amazon EventBridge rule 作為變更偵測機制（由 console 精靈建立）。當程式碼推送到受監控的分支時，該 rule 會觸發並啟動 pipeline。AWS 疑難排解主題『Pipelines with an Amazon S3, Amazon ECR, or CodeCommit source no longer start automatically』指出，當 event rule 未被建立或更新時，『the pipeline no longer starts automatically（pipeline 不再自動啟動）』，正是本題『毫無反應』的症狀，且該主題明確列出 Repository name + Branch name 為 CodeCommit 的觸發識別碼。因此檢查是否存在且指向 main 分支的 EventBridge rule（選項 A）是正確的第一個排錯步驟。決定性的判斷依據是症狀：pipeline 完全沒有啟動，這指向變更偵測觸發機制，而非會讓 pipeline 啟動後才顯示可見錯誤的權限問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A missing CodePipeline service-role permission for CodeCommit produces a different, documented symptom: the pipeline DOES start (the trigger fires) and the source action then FAILS with 'Could not access the CodeCommit repository... Make sure that the pipeline IAM role has sufficient permissions to access the repository.' The question states there was no reaction at all, so this is not the cause.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 服務角色缺少 CodeCommit 權限會產生另一種有文件記載的症狀：pipeline 仍會啟動（觸發成功），但 source action 隨後失敗並顯示『Could not access the CodeCommit repository... Make sure that the pipeline IAM role has sufficient permissions to access the repository.』題目說 pipeline 完全沒反應，故此非主因。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The scenario states the developer already successfully pushed code. If the developer's IAM role lacked push permission, the git push itself would have failed and the code would never have landed in the repository. This option is contradicted by the facts of the scenario.","why_zh":"題目已說明開發者成功推送了程式碼。若開發者的 IAM 角色缺少推送權限，git push 本身就會失敗，程式碼根本不會進入儲存庫。此選項與題目情境矛盾。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodePipeline does not emit a 'pipeline failed to start because of CodeCommit errors' diagnostic to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The change-detection path is EventBridge; a missing or misconfigured rule simply produces no event and therefore no pipeline execution at all - there is no CloudWatch Logs start-failure entry to find. This is a fabricated troubleshooting path.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 不會將『因 CodeCommit 錯誤導致 pipeline 無法啟動』這類診斷寫入 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。變更偵測路徑是 EventBridge；rule 遺失或設定錯誤只會導致沒有事件、因而完全沒有 pipeline 執行，根本不會有 CloudWatch Logs 的啟動失敗記錄可查。此為虛構的排錯路徑。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/change-detection-methods.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/triggering.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":17,"question_en":"A company's developers use Amazon EC2 instances as remote workstations. The company is concerned that users can create or modify EC2 security groups to allow unrestricted inbound access. A DevOps engineer needs to develop a solution to detect when users create unrestricted security group rules. The solution must detect changes to security group rules in near real time, remove unrestricted rules, and send email notifications to the security team. The DevOps engineer has created an AWS Lambda function that checks for security group ID from input, removes rules that grant unrestricted access, and sends notifications through Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"该公司开发人员使用亚马逊 EC2 实例作为远程工作站。公司担心用户能够创建或修改 EC2 安全组，从而允 许不受限制的入站访问。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要开发一种解决方案，用于检测用户创建无限制的安全组规则的情况。该解决方案必 须能够近乎实时地检测安全组规则的变更，移除无限制的规则，并向安全团队发送电子邮件通知。该 DevOps 工程师已创建了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会从输入中获取安全组 ID，移除授予无限制访问权 限的规则，并通过亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）发送通知。 为了满足要求，开发运维工程师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Lambda function to be invoked by the SNS topic. Create an AWS CloudTrail subscription for the SNS topic. Configure a subscription filter for security group modification events.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to invoke the Lambda function. Define a schedule pattern that runs the Lambda function every hour.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge event rule that has the default event bus as the source. Define the rule’s event pattern to match EC2 security group creation and modification events. Configure the rule to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge custom event bus that subscribes to events from all AWS services. Configure the Lambda function to be invoked by the custom event bus."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Lambda 函数配置为由 SNS 主题调用。为 SNS 主题创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 订阅。为安全组修改事件 配置订阅筛选器。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则以调用 Lambda 函数。定义一个每小时运行一次 Lambda 函 数的计划模式。","C":"创建一个以默认事件总线作为源的 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则。定义规则的事件模式以匹配 EC2 安全 组的创建和修改事件。配置规则以调用 Lambda 函数。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 自定义事件总线，使其订阅来自所有 AWS 服务的事件。配置 Lambda 函数，使其由自定义事件总线触发。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"EC2 security group changes are made through public AWS API calls such as AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress, AuthorizeSecurityGroupEgress, and RevokeSecurityGroupIngress. AWS CloudTrail records these calls and delivers them to the default EventBridge event bus as events with detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' (the EventBridge docs use an EC2 API call as the canonical example, and state these events are delivered to the default event bus only). Creating an EventBridge rule on the default event bus whose event pattern matches EC2 security group creation/modification events invokes the existing Lambda function as a native target the instant a change occurs, satisfying the near-real-time requirement and passing the event detail (including the security group ID) so the Lambda can revoke the unrestricted rules and publish to SNS. This is the standard event-driven remediation pattern for security group changes.","explanation_zh":"EC2 security group 的變更是透過公開的 AWS API 呼叫完成，例如 AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress、AuthorizeSecurityGroupEgress 與 RevokeSecurityGroupIngress。AWS CloudTrail 會記錄這些呼叫，並以 detail-type 為「AWS API Call via CloudTrail」的事件傳送到 default EventBridge event bus（EventBridge 文件以 EC2 API 呼叫作為標準範例，並明確指出這類事件只會送到 default event bus）。在 default event bus 上建立一條 EventBridge rule，並設定 event pattern 比對 EC2 security group 的建立/修改事件，即可在變更發生的當下將既有 Lambda function 作為原生 target 觸發，滿足近即時需求，並把事件細節（含 security group ID）傳入 Lambda，讓它移除不受限制的規則並發佈到 SNS。這正是針對 security group 變更的標準事件驅動修復模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This is backwards and not a real feature. There is no 'CloudTrail subscription for an SNS topic' with a 'subscription filter for security group modification events.' CloudTrail can publish an SNS notification when it delivers a new log file, but it cannot filter per event type, and having SNS invoke the Lambda provides no security group ID as input. This flow does not detect changes correctly in near real time.","why_zh":"此選項方向相反且非真實功能。並不存在「為 SNS topic 建立 CloudTrail subscription」搭配「security group 修改事件的 subscription filter」。CloudTrail 只能在遞送新 log 檔時發 SNS 通知，無法依事件類型過濾，且由 SNS 觸發 Lambda 也無法提供 security group ID。此流程無法正確近即時偵測變更。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A scheduled EventBridge rule that runs the Lambda every hour is periodic polling, not near-real-time detection, so it directly violates the explicit near-real-time requirement. A scheduled invocation also does not carry the specific security group ID from a change event that the Lambda needs as input.","why_zh":"每小時執行一次 Lambda 的排程 EventBridge rule 屬於週期性輪詢，並非近即時偵測，直接違反明確的近即時需求。排程觸發也不會帶入 Lambda 所需的特定 security group ID（來自變更事件）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom event buses do not natively subscribe to events from all AWS services. CloudTrail-delivered events ('AWS API Call via CloudTrail') and AWS service events are delivered to the default event bus only; to process them on a custom bus you must create a rule on the default bus that forwards them. As described, this setup would not receive the EC2 security group change events.","why_zh":"Custom event bus 無法原生「訂閱所有 AWS 服務的事件」。CloudTrail 傳遞的事件（「AWS API Call via CloudTrail」）與 AWS 服務事件只會送到 default event bus；要在 custom bus 上處理，必須在 default bus 建立 rule 來轉發。如題所述，此設定收不到 EC2 security group 變更事件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-create-pattern.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":18,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is creating an AWS CloudFormation template to deploy a web service. The web service will run on Amazon EC2 instances in a private subnet behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The DevOps engineer must ensure that the service can accept requests from clients that have IPv6 addresses. What should the DevOps engineer do with the CloudFormation template so that IPv6 clients can access the web service?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板以部署一个网络服务。该网络服务将在位于应 用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的私有子网中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。DevOps 工程师必须确保该服务能够 接受来自具有 IPv6 地址的客户端的请求。 DevOps 工程师应该如何处理 CloudFormation 模板，以便 IPv6 客户端能够访问该网络服务？","options_en":{"A":"Add an IPv6 CIDR block to the VPC and the private subnet for the EC2 instances. Create route table entries for the IPv6 network, use EC2 instance types that support IPv6, and assign IPv6 addresses to each EC2 instance.","B":"Assign each EC2 instance an IPv6 Elastic IP address. Create a target group, and add the EC2 instances as targets. Create a listener on port 443 of the ALB, and associate the target group with the ALB.","C":"Replace the ALB with a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Add an IPv6 CIDR block to the VPC and subnets for the NLB, and assign the NLB an IPv6 Elastic IP address.","D":"Add an IPv6 CIDR block to the VPC and subnets for the ALB. Create a listener on port 443, and specify the dualstack IP address type on the ALB. Create a target group, and add the EC2 instances as targets. Associate the target group with the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"向 VPC 和用于 EC2 实例的私有子网添加 IPv6 CIDR 块。为 IPv6 网络创建路由表条目，使用支持 IPv6 的 EC2 实例类型，并为这些实例分配 IPv6 地址。 每个 EC2 实例。","B":"为每个 EC2 实例分配一个 IPv6 弹性 IP 地址。创建一个目标组，并将 EC2 实例添加为目标。在 ALB 的 443 端口上创建一个监听器，并将目标组与 ALB 关联。","C":"用网络负载均衡器（NLB）替换 ALB。为 VPC 和 NLB 的子网添加一个 IPv6 CIDR 块，并为 NLB 分配一个 IPv6 弹性 IP 地址。","D":"向 VPC 和 ALB 的子网添加 IPv6 CIDR 块。在端口 443 上创建一个监听器，并在 ALB 上指定双栈 IP 地址 类型。创建一个目标组，并将 EC2 实例添加为目标。将目标组与 ALB 关联。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"To let IPv6 clients reach a web service behind an Application Load Balancer, you make the ALB dualstack. Per AWS docs, you can configure an ALB so clients communicate using IPv4 only or using both IPv4 and IPv6 (dualstack); the dualstack endpoint resolves to both A and AAAA DNS records, so IPv6 clients connect over IPv6 while IPv4 clients still use IPv4. The dualstack type requires the VPC and the load balancer's subnets to have associated IPv6 CIDR blocks (and the subnet route tables, security groups, and network ACLs must allow IPv6 traffic). Critically, the load balancer communicates with its targets based on the target group's IP address type, so the EC2 instances can remain IPv4-only in the private subnet; you just register them in a target group and associate it with the port 443 listener. Option D captures exactly this design: add an IPv6 CIDR to the VPC and ALB subnets, create the port 443 listener, set the ALB IP address type to dualstack, create a target group with the EC2 instances, and associate it with the ALB.","explanation_zh":"要讓 IPv6 用戶端透過 Application Load Balancer 存取 web 服務，需將 ALB 設為 dualstack。根據 AWS 文件，可將 ALB 設定為僅以 IPv4 與用戶端通訊，或同時以 IPv4 與 IPv6（dualstack）通訊；dualstack 端點會解析為 A 與 AAAA DNS 記錄，使 IPv6 用戶端能以 IPv6 連線，IPv4 用戶端仍使用 IPv4。dualstack 類型要求 VPC 與 ALB 所在的 subnet 都關聯 IPv6 CIDR block（且 subnet 的 route table、security group 與 network ACL 須允許 IPv6 流量）。關鍵在於：ALB 與其 target 的通訊是依 target group 的 IP address type，因此私有子網內的 EC2 instance 可維持僅 IPv4；只需把它們註冊到 target group 並關聯到 443 埠的 listener 即可。選項 D 正是此設計：為 VPC 與 ALB 的 subnet 加上 IPv6 CIDR、建立 443 listener、將 ALB 的 IP address type 設為 dualstack、建立含 EC2 的 target group 並關聯到 ALB。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Assigning IPv6 to the EC2 instances and adding IPv6 routing to the private subnet does not make external IPv6 clients able to reach the service, because clients connect to the ALB (via its DNS name), not to the instances directly. The ALB itself must be dualstack to accept IPv6 from clients; making the private backend IPv6 is unnecessary and never creates an IPv6 client-facing entry point.","why_zh":"為 EC2 instance 指派 IPv6 並為私有子網加入 IPv6 路由，無法讓外部 IPv6 用戶端存取服務，因為用戶端是連到 ALB（透過其 DNS 名稱），而非直接連到 instance。必須讓 ALB 本身為 dualstack 才能接受用戶端的 IPv6；讓私有後端使用 IPv6 並非必要，也從未建立面向用戶端的 IPv6 入口。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no such thing as an 'IPv6 Elastic IP address'; Elastic IP addresses are IPv4-only. ALBs also do not use Elastic IPs (they use service-managed addresses), and this option never enables dualstack/IPv6 on the ALB, so IPv6 clients still cannot connect. It is technically invalid.","why_zh":"並不存在「IPv6 Elastic IP」；Elastic IP 僅支援 IPv4。ALB 也不使用 Elastic IP（它使用服務代管位址），且此選項從未在 ALB 上啟用 dualstack/IPv6，因此 IPv6 用戶端仍無法連線。在技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Replacing the ALB with an NLB is an unnecessary architectural change, and NLBs do not use 'IPv6 Elastic IP addresses' (Elastic IPs are IPv4-only). The requirement is simply to accept IPv6 client requests, which the existing ALB can do natively via the dualstack IP address type without swapping load balancer types.","why_zh":"把 ALB 換成 NLB 是不必要的架構變更，且 NLB 不使用「IPv6 Elastic IP」（Elastic IP 僅 IPv4）。需求只是接受 IPv6 用戶端請求，現有的 ALB 透過 dualstack IP address type 即可原生達成，無需更換負載平衡器類型。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-ip-address-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/application-load-balancers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/userguide/how-elastic-load-balancing-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-elasticloadbalancingv2-loadbalancer.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":19,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations and AWS Control Tower to manage all the company's AWS accounts. The company uses the Enterprise Support plan. A DevOps engineer is using Account Factory for Terraform (AFT) to provision new accounts. When new accounts are provisioned, the DevOps engineer notices that the support plan for the new accounts is set to the Basic Support plan. The DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to provision the new accounts with the Enterprise Support plan. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 组织和 AWS 控制塔来管理公司所有的 AWS 账户。该公司采用企业支持计划。 一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 Terraform 账户工厂（AFT）来创建新账户。在创建新账户时，该 DevOps 工程 师注意到新账户的支持计划被设置为基本支持计划。该 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，以便为新账 户配置企业支持计划。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS Config conformance pack to deploy the account-part-of-organizations AWS Config rule and to automatically remediate any noncompliant accounts.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function to create a ticket for AWS Support to add the account to the Enterprise Support plan. Grant the Lambda function the support:ResolveCase permission.","C":"Add an additional value to the control_tower_parameters input to set the AWSEnterpriseSupport parameter as the organization's management account number.","D":"Set the aft_feature_enterprise_support feature flag to True in the AFT deployment input configuration. Redeploy AFT and apply the changes."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Config 合规性包部署“账户属于组织”AWS Config 规则，并自动修复任何不符合要求的账 户。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为 AWS 支持服务创建工单，将账户添加到企业支持计划中。 授予该 Lambda 函数 support:ResolveCase 权限。","C":"在 control_tower_parameters 输入中添加一个额外的值，将 AWSEnterpriseSupport 参数设置为组织 的管理账户编号。","D":"在 AFT 部署输入配置中将 aft_feature_enterprise_support 特性标志设置为 True。重新部署 AFT 并应用更 改。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Control Tower Account Factory for Terraform (AFT) ships with optional feature flags that you set in the AFT deployment input configuration (the terraform-aws-control_tower_account_factory module). The official 'Enable feature options' page documents an 'AWS Enterprise Support plan' feature: 'When this option is enabled, the AFT pipeline turns on the AWS Enterprise Support plan for accounts provisioned by AFT... AFT provides automated enrollment into the enterprise support level... The provisioning process opens a support ticket for the account, requesting it to be added to the AWS Enterprise Support plan. To enable the Enterprise Support option, set the following feature flag to True in your AFT deployment input configuration: aft_feature_enterprise_support.' This is exactly the native, supported mechanism for the described scenario (new AFT accounts defaulting to Basic Support). The documented prerequisite ('you must enroll the payer account into the Enterprise Support plan') is satisfied because the company already uses the Enterprise Support plan. After changing the flag you redeploy AFT to apply the change, matching option D verbatim.","explanation_zh":"AWS Control Tower Account Factory for Terraform (AFT) 在 AFT deployment input configuration（即 terraform-aws-control_tower_account_factory 模組）中提供可選的 feature flags。官方「Enable feature options」頁面記載了「AWS Enterprise Support plan」這個功能：啟用後，AFT pipeline 會為 AFT 所佈建的帳戶開啟 AWS Enterprise Support plan，AFT 會自動將帳戶登記到 enterprise support 等級，佈建流程會開立一張 support ticket 要求把該帳戶加入 AWS Enterprise Support plan。要啟用此選項，需在 AFT deployment input configuration 中將 feature flag aft_feature_enterprise_support 設為 True。這正是題目情境（AFT 新帳戶預設為 Basic Support）的原生支援解法。文件中要求的先決條件（payer account 必須已加入 Enterprise Support plan）已被滿足，因為該公司本身就使用 Enterprise Support plan。修改 flag 後重新部署 AFT 以套用變更，完全符合選項 D。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no 'account-part-of-organizations' AWS Config rule that manages support plans, and AWS Config conformance packs evaluate/remediate resource configuration, not AWS Support plan enrollment. Support plan level is a billing/account-level setting not represented as a Config-evaluable resource, so this cannot set Enterprise Support.","why_zh":"不存在能管理支援方案的 'account-part-of-organizations' AWS Config 規則，且 AWS Config conformance pack 是評估/修復資源組態，而非 AWS Support 方案的登記。支援方案等級屬於帳單/帳戶層級設定，無法用 Config 規則評估或修復，因此無法設定 Enterprise Support。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building a custom Lambda to open support cases reinvents functionality AFT already provides natively, adding unnecessary operational overhead. Worse, support:ResolveCase only closes/resolves a case; it does not create a case or change the support plan. The correct API would be support:CreateCase, so the permission is wrong and the approach is not the AWS-recommended solution.","why_zh":"自建 Lambda 開立支援案件等於重造 AFT 已內建的功能，增加不必要的運維負擔。更糟的是 support:ResolveCase 只能關閉/解決案件，無法建立案件或變更支援方案；正確 API 應為 support:CreateCase，因此權限錯誤，且非 AWS 建議的做法。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"control_tower_parameters drives Control Tower setup inputs, and there is no 'AWSEnterpriseSupport' parameter; setting a management account number as a support parameter is fabricated. Enterprise Support enrollment for AFT accounts is controlled by the aft_feature_enterprise_support feature flag, not by control_tower_parameters.","why_zh":"control_tower_parameters 提供 Control Tower 設定輸入，且不存在 'AWSEnterpriseSupport' 這個參數；把管理帳戶號碼當成支援參數是虛構的。AFT 帳戶的 Enterprise Support 登記由 aft_feature_enterprise_support feature flag 控制，而非 control_tower_parameters。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/aft-feature-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/aft-overview.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":20,"question_en":"A company's DevOps engineer uses AWS Systems Manager to perform maintenance tasks during maintenance windows. The company has a few Amazon EC2 instances that require a restart after notifications from AWS Health. The DevOps engineer needs to implement an automated solution to remediate these notifications. The DevOps engineer creates an Amazon EventBridge rule. How should the DevOps engineer configure the EventBridge rule to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS 系统管理器在维护窗口期间执行维护任务。该公司有几台 Amazon EC2 实例，在收到 AWS 健康通知后需要重启。DevOps 工程师需要实施一个自动化解决方 案来解决这些通知。DevOps 工程师创建了一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置 EventBridge 规则以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an event source of AWS Health, a service of EC2, and an event type that indicates instance maintenance. Target a Systems Manager document to restart the EC2 instance.","B":"Configure an event source of Systems Manager and an event type that indicates a maintenance window. Target a Systems Manager document to restart the EC2 instance.","C":"Configure an event source of AWS Health, a service of EC2, and an event type that indicates instance maintenance. Target a newly created AWS Lambda function that registers an automation task to restart the EC2 instance during a maintenance window.","D":"Configure an event source of EC2 and an event type that indicates instance maintenance. Target a newly created AWS Lambda function that registers an automation task to restart the EC2 instance during a maintenance window."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Health（EC2 的一项服务）作为事件源，并指定表示实例维护的事件类型。将目标设置为 Systems Manager 文档以重启 EC2 实例。","B":"配置一个 Systems Manager 事件源以及表示维护窗口的事件类型。将 Systems Manager 文档作为目 标以重启 EC2 实例。","C":"配置 AWS Health（EC2 的一项服务）作为事件源，并指定表示实例维护的事件类型。将目标设置为新创 建的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数在维护窗口期间注册自动化任务以重启 EC2 实例。","D":"配置一个 EC2 事件源和一种表示实例维护的事件类型。将目标指向新创建的 AWS Lambda 函数，该 函数在维护窗口期间注册一个自动化任务以重启 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The remediation must be triggered by an AWS Health notification, so the EventBridge event source must be AWS Health (source: aws.health). AWS's own documented runbook 'Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health' specifies exactly this configuration: in the EventBridge rule choose Service name = Health, Specific service = EC2, and an event-type category of scheduledChange (the instance retirement/maintenance event code). The rule's target is set directly to an SSM Automation document (AWS-RestartEC2Instance) using an existing role; no intermediate Lambda function is required. Option A captures this pattern precisely (AWS Health source, EC2 service, instance-maintenance event type, SSM document target) and has the lowest operational overhead. A documented prerequisite is that the instances must be managed by Systems Manager.","explanation_zh":"此自動修復必須由 AWS Health 通知觸發，因此 EventBridge 的事件來源必須是 AWS Health（source: aws.health）。AWS 官方文件「Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health」明確說明了正確設定：在 EventBridge 規則中選擇 Service name = Health、Specific service = EC2，並使用 scheduledChange 事件類型類別（即 instance retirement/maintenance 的事件代碼）。規則的 target 直接設定為 SSM Automation document（AWS-RestartEC2Instance）並使用 existing role，不需要任何中介的 Lambda function。選項 A 精準符合此模式（AWS Health 來源、EC2 service、instance-maintenance 事件類型、SSM document target），且營運負擔最低。文件中的前提是這些 EC2 instance 必須由 Systems Manager 管理。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Wrong event source. The trigger is an AWS Health notification, not a Systems Manager maintenance-window event. An event source of Systems Manager with a maintenance-window event type does not capture AWS Health scheduledChange notifications, so the rule would never fire on the Health event.","why_zh":"事件來源錯誤。觸發來源是 AWS Health 通知，而非 Systems Manager 維護視窗事件。以 Systems Manager 並搭配 maintenance window 事件類型作為事件來源無法擷取 AWS Health 的 scheduledChange 通知，規則永遠不會因 Health 事件被觸發。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Correct event source but unnecessary architecture. AWS documents targeting the SSM Automation document (AWS-RestartEC2Instance) directly from the EventBridge rule. Inserting a Lambda function to register the automation adds development and operational overhead with no benefit, making A the better, lower-overhead answer.","why_zh":"事件來源正確但架構多餘。AWS 文件是讓 EventBridge 規則直接以 SSM Automation document（AWS-RestartEC2Instance）為 target。額外加入一個 Lambda function 去註冊 automation 會增加開發與營運負擔且無益處，因此 A 是更佳、負擔更低的答案。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Wrong event source. The notification originates from AWS Health (source: aws.health), not from a native EC2 service event. Using EC2 as the source would miss the AWS Health scheduledChange/maintenance notifications, and it also adds an unnecessary Lambda function.","why_zh":"事件來源錯誤。通知來自 AWS Health（source: aws.health），而非原生 EC2 服務事件。以 EC2 作為來源會漏接 AWS Health 的 scheduledChange/maintenance 通知，且同樣多了一個不必要的 Lambda function。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/automating-instance-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/cloudwatch-events-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/aws-health-events-eventbridge-schema.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":21,"question_en":"A company has containerized all of its in-house quality control applications. The company is running Jenkins on Amazon EC2 instances, which require patching and upgrading. The compliance officer has requested a DevOps engineer begin encrypting build artifacts since they contain company intellectual property. What should the DevOps engineer do to accomplish this in the MOST maintainable manner?","question_zh":"一家公司已将其所有内部质量控制应用程序进行了容器化处理。该公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行 Jenkins，这些实例需要打补丁和升级。合规官要求一名 DevOps 工程师开始对构建工件进行加密， 因为这些工件包含公司的知识产权。 为了以最易于维护的方式实现这一目标，开发运维工程师应该怎么做？","options_en":{"A":"Automate patching and upgrading using AWS Systems Manager on EC2 instances and encrypt Amazon EBS volumes by default.","B":"Deploy Jenkins to an Amazon ECS cluster and copy build artifacts to an Amazon S3 bucket with default encryption enabled.","C":"Leverage AWS CodePipeline with a build action and encrypt the artifacts using AWS Secrets Manager.","D":"Use AWS CodeBuild with artifact encryption to replace the Jenkins instance running on EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 对 EC2 实例进行自动补丁安装和升级，并默认加密 Amazon EBS 卷。","B":"将 Jenkins 部署到 Amazon ECS 集群，并将构建工件复制到启用默认加密的 Amazon S3 存储桶 中。","C":"利用 AWS CodePipeline 中的构建操作，并使用 AWS Secrets Manager 对构建工件进行加密。","D":"使用带有工件加密功能的 AWS CodeBuild 来替代在 EC2 实例上运行的 Jenkins 实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario has two pain points to solve at once with the MOST maintainable approach: a self-managed Jenkins fleet on EC2 that 'requires patching and upgrading,' and a compliance requirement to encrypt build artifacts. AWS CodeBuild is a fully managed build service that, per the AWS docs, 'eliminates the need to set up, patch, update, and manage your own build servers' and scales automatically, so replacing Jenkins/EC2 with CodeBuild removes the patching/upgrading burden entirely. CodeBuild also natively encrypts its build output artifacts: by default it uses the AWS managed KMS key for Amazon S3, and you can optionally supply a customer managed key, satisfying the compliance officer with no bolt-on components. Because the applications are already containerized and CodeBuild runs containerized build environments, the migration is a clean fit. Option D is therefore the only choice that addresses BOTH pain points while minimizing ongoing operational maintenance.","explanation_zh":"本題要以「最易維護 (MOST maintainable)」的方式同時解決兩個痛點：EC2 上自管的 Jenkins 機群「需要修補與升級」，以及合規上必須加密建置產物的需求。AWS CodeBuild 是全託管的建置服務，依 AWS 文件可「免除設定、修補、更新與管理自有建置伺服器的需求」並自動擴展，因此以 CodeBuild 取代 Jenkins/EC2 即可完全消除修補與升級負擔。CodeBuild 也原生加密其建置輸出產物：預設使用 Amazon S3 的 AWS 受管 KMS key，亦可選用客戶受管 key，無須額外元件即可滿足合規官需求。由於應用程式已容器化、CodeBuild 本身即以容器化建置環境執行，遷移相當契合。因此 D 是唯一能同時解決兩個痛點、且將持續營運維護降到最低的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Automating patching with Systems Manager and enabling EBS default encryption keeps the self-managed Jenkins-on-EC2 fleet alive, so you still own the server lifecycle, OS/Jenkins upgrades, and scaling. EBS default encryption only protects the underlying volume, not the build artifacts as a deliverable, and it does not eliminate the build-server maintenance burden the question wants removed.","why_zh":"用 Systems Manager 自動修補並啟用 EBS 預設加密，仍保留自管的 Jenkins/EC2 機群，因此你依舊要負責伺服器生命週期、OS/Jenkins 升級與擴展。EBS 預設加密只保護底層磁碟區，並非針對建置產物本身，也無法消除題目想去除的建置伺服器維運負擔。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Moving Jenkins to an ECS cluster still means you maintain Jenkins itself (plugins, configuration, controller/agent images and upgrades) and, on the EC2 launch type, the container instances too. S3 default encryption would protect the artifacts, but you still carry Jenkins maintenance, so this has more moving parts and is less maintainable than fully replacing Jenkins with a managed build service.","why_zh":"把 Jenkins 搬到 ECS 叢集仍需自行維護 Jenkins 本身（外掛、設定、controller/agent 映像與升級），若採 EC2 啟動類型還要管理容器執行個體。S3 預設加密雖能保護產物，但你仍背負 Jenkins 維護，元件更多、維護性不如以全託管建置服務完全取代 Jenkins。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Secrets Manager stores and rotates secrets such as credentials, API keys, and OAuth tokens; it is not a service for encrypting build artifacts, so 'encrypt the artifacts using Secrets Manager' is a technical misuse. CodePipeline is only an orchestrator and still needs an underlying build provider, so this option also fails to remove the Jenkins patching/upgrading problem.","why_zh":"AWS Secrets Manager 用於儲存與輪替憑證、API 金鑰、OAuth token 等機密，並非用來加密建置產物的服務，因此「用 Secrets Manager 加密產物」屬技術誤用。CodePipeline 僅為編排服務，仍需底層的建置供應者，故此選項也無法去除 Jenkins 的修補/升級問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/setting-up-kms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":22,"question_en":"An IT team has built an AWS CloudFormation template so others in the company can quickly and reliably deploy and terminate an application. The template creates an Amazon EC2 instance with a user data script to install the application and an Amazon S3 bucket that the application uses to serve static webpages while it is running. All resources should be removed when the CloudFormation stack is deleted. However, the team observes that CloudFormation reports an error during stack deletion, and the S3 bucket created by the stack is not deleted. How can the team resolve the error in the MOST efficient manner to ensure that all resources are deleted without errors?","question_zh":"一个 IT 团队构建了一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，以便公司内的其他人能够快速且可靠地部署和终 止应用程序。该模板创建了一个带有用户数据脚本的 Amazon EC2 实例，用于安装应用程序，还创建了 一个 Amazon S3 存储桶，应用程序在运行时用于提供静态网页。 在删除 CloudFormation 堆栈时，所有资源都应被移除。然而，团队发现 CloudFormation 在删除堆栈期 间报告错误，并且由该堆栈创建的 S3 存储桶未被删除。 团队如何以最高效的方式解决错误，以确保所有资源都能无误地被删除？","options_en":{"A":"Add a DelelionPolicy attribute to the S3 bucket resource, with the value Delete forcing the bucket to be removed when the stack is deleted.","B":"Add a custom resource with an AWS Lambda function with the DependsOn attribute specifying the S3 bucket, and an IAM role. Write the Lambda function to delete all objects from the bucket when RequestType is Delete.","C":"Identify the resource that was not deleted. Manually empty the S3 bucket and then delete it.","D":"Replace the EC2 and S3 bucket resources with a single AWS OpsWorks Stacks resource. Define a custom recipe for the stack to create and delete the EC2 instance and the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"向 S3 存储桶资源添加一个 DeletionPolicy 属性，其值为 Delete，这样在删除堆栈时会强制删除该存 储桶。","B":"添加一个自定义资源，该资源包含一个 AWS Lambda 函数，使用 DependsOn 属性指定 S3 存储桶和 一个 IAM 角色。编写 Lambda 函数，当 RequestType 为 Delete 时，从存储桶中删除所有对象。","C":"确定未被删除的资源。手动清空 S3 存储桶，然后将其删除。","D":"用单个 AWS OpsWorks Stacks 资源替换 EC2 和 S3 存储桶资源。为堆栈定义一个自定义配方，以 创建和删除 EC2 实例和 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application serves static webpages out of the S3 bucket, so the bucket holds objects when the stack is deleted. CloudFormation cannot delete a non-empty S3 bucket: the DeletionPolicy reference explicitly states 'For Amazon S3 buckets, you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed,' which is exactly the deletion error the team sees. The most efficient, repeatable, fully template-based fix is a Lambda-backed custom resource (with an IAM execution role) that empties the bucket when RequestType is Delete. Custom resources support Create, Update, and Delete operations, and CloudFormation waits for the custom resource's response before continuing the stack operation. The DependsOn attribute documentation confirms the deletion ordering rule: when resource A depends on resource B, 'Resource A is deleted before resource B.' So putting DependsOn the S3 bucket on the custom resource forces the Lambda to run (RequestType=Delete) and empty the bucket BEFORE CloudFormation deletes the bucket itself. This keeps the entire deploy/terminate lifecycle inside the template so others can run it reliably without any manual steps.","explanation_zh":"應用程式從 S3 bucket 提供靜態網頁，因此刪除堆疊時 bucket 內含有物件。CloudFormation 無法刪除非空的 S3 bucket：DeletionPolicy 參考文件明確指出『對於 Amazon S3 buckets，必須先刪除 bucket 內所有物件才能成功刪除』，這正是團隊看到的刪除錯誤。最有效率、可重複且完全寫在範本內的解法，是使用由 Lambda 支援的 custom resource（搭配 IAM 執行角色），當 RequestType 為 Delete 時清空 bucket。Custom resource 支援 Create、Update、Delete 操作，且 CloudFormation 會等待 custom resource 回應後才繼續堆疊操作。DependsOn 屬性文件確認了刪除順序規則：當資源 A 相依於資源 B 時，『資源 A 會在資源 B 之前被刪除』。因此對 custom resource 加上 DependsOn 指向該 S3 bucket，會強制 Lambda 先執行（RequestType=Delete）並清空 bucket，CloudFormation 才會接著刪除該 bucket。如此整個部署/終止生命週期都在範本內，讓其他人能可靠地執行而無需任何手動步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DeletionPolicy: Delete is already the default behavior and does NOT empty a bucket. The DeletionPolicy reference explicitly states that for S3 buckets you must delete all objects for deletion to succeed, so a non-empty bucket still fails exactly as observed. The option's claim that Delete 'forces' removal of a non-empty bucket is technically false (and it even misspells the attribute as 'DelelionPolicy').","why_zh":"DeletionPolicy: Delete 本來就是預設行為，並不會清空 bucket。DeletionPolicy 參考文件明確指出 S3 bucket 必須刪除所有物件才能成功刪除，因此非空 bucket 仍會如所觀察到的失敗。此選項聲稱 Delete 會『強制』移除非空 bucket 在技術上是錯的（且還把屬性拼成 'DelelionPolicy'）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Manually emptying and deleting the bucket is a one-time fix and contradicts the stated goal that others must be able to quickly and reliably deploy AND terminate the stack without errors. It is not automated or repeatable, so it is not the most efficient solution.","why_zh":"手動清空並刪除 bucket 只是一次性修補，與『讓其他人能快速且可靠地部署與終止堆疊且無錯誤』的目標相違。它無法自動化或重複執行，因此不是最有效率的解法。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Replacing EC2 and S3 with a single OpsWorks Stacks resource is a massive over-engineered rewrite, not the 'most efficient' change, and OpsWorks Stacks is a legacy service slated for end of life. It also would not natively solve emptying a non-empty bucket any more simply than a custom resource.","why_zh":"把 EC2 與 S3 改成單一 OpsWorks Stacks 資源是大規模、過度設計的重寫，並非『最有效率』的變更，且 OpsWorks Stacks 已是即將終止服務的舊版服務。它也無法比 custom resource 更簡單地原生解決清空非空 bucket 的問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-attribute-deletionpolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-attribute-dependson.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/troubleshooting.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":23,"question_en":"A company has an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that is configured with an Amazon S3 bucket in the eu- west-1 Region. The pipeline deploys an AWS Lambda application to the same Region. The pipeline consists of an AWS CodeBuild project build action and an AWS CloudFormation deploy action. The CodeBuild project uses the aws cloudformation package AWS CLI command to build an artifact that contains the Lambda function code’s .zip file and the CloudFormation template. The CloudFormation deploy action references the CloudFormation template from the output artifact of the CodeBuild project’s build action. The company wants to also deploy the Lambda application to the us-east-1 Region by using the pipeline in eu-west-1. A DevOps engineer has already updated the CodeBuild project to use the aws cloudformation package command to produce an additional output artifact for us-east-1. Which combination of additional steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道配置了位于 euwest-1 区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶。 该管道将一个 AWS Lambda 应用程序部署到同一区域。该管道由一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目构建操 作和一个 AWS CloudFormation 部署操作组成。 CodeBuild 项目使用 AWS CLI 命令 `aws cloudformation package` 来构建一个包含 Lambda 函数代码的 `.zip` 文件和 CloudFormation 模板的工件。CloudFormation 部署操作从 CodeBuild 项目构建操作的输出工件中引 用 CloudFormation 模板。 该公司还希望利用位于 eu-west-1 区域的管道将 Lambda 应用程序部署到 us-east-1 区域。一位 DevOps 工程师 已更新 CodeBuild 项目，使用 aws cloudformation package 命令为 us-east-1 区域生成额外的输出工件。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些额外步骤的组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Modify the CloudFormation template to include a parameter for the Lambda function code’s zip file location. Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to pass in the us-east-1 artifact location as a parameter override.","B":"Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to use the CloudFormation template from the us-east-1 output artifact.","C":"Create an S3 bucket in us-east-1. Configure the S3 bucket policy to allow CodePipeline to have read and write access.","D":"Create an S3 bucket in us-east-1. Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the S3 bucket in eu-west-1 to the S3 bucket in us-east-1.","E":"Modify the pipeline to include the S3 bucket for us-east-1 as an artifact store. Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to use the CloudFormation template from the us-east-1 output artifact."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 CloudFormation 模板，添加一个用于 Lambda 函数代码压缩文件位置的参数。在管道中为 us-east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。配置新的部署操作，将 us-east-1 的工件位置作为参数覆盖 传入。","B":"在管道中为 us-east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。将新的部署操作配置为使用来自 us- east-1 输出工件的 CloudFormation 模板。","C":"在 us-east-1 区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。配置 S3 存储桶策略，允许 CodePipeline 具有读写访问权限。","D":"在 us-east-1 区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。配置从 eu-west-1 区域的 S3 存储桶到 us-east-1 区域的 S3 存储桶的 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。","E":"修改管道，将 us-east-1 的 S3 存储桶作为工件存储包含进来。在管道中为 us-east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。配置新的部署操作，使其使用来自 us-east-1 输出工件的 CloudFormation 模 板。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Adding a CloudFormation deploy action that executes in us-east-1 makes it a CodePipeline cross-Region action. AWS documentation states that for a cross-Region action you must have one artifact bucket in the pipeline Region (eu-west-1) and one artifact bucket in every Region where an action runs (us-east-1). When the pipeline is managed via the CLI, CloudFormation, or an SDK (as here), CodePipeline does NOT auto-provision that bucket; you must create it yourself and then register it in the pipeline's artifactStores map (the docs are explicit: 'If you create a cross-region action in your pipeline, you must use artifactStores' and 'there must be an artifact store for the pipeline Region and for each cross-region action'). Therefore you must (C) create the us-east-1 S3 bucket and grant CodePipeline read/write access to it, and (E) add the us-east-1 bucket to the pipeline as an artifact store while creating the new CloudFormation deploy action that consumes the us-east-1 output artifact (whose template the engineer already produced with 'aws cloudformation package', so the Lambda .zip location is already baked in and references a us-east-1 location). CodePipeline automatically copies the input artifacts from eu-west-1 into the us-east-1 bucket, so no manual replication is needed. C supplies the physical per-Region bucket; E wires it into the pipeline and adds the deploy action, making them the complete, minimal pair.","explanation_zh":"新增一個在 us-east-1 執行的 CloudFormation deploy action,等於建立了 CodePipeline 的 cross-Region action。AWS 官方文件指出:cross-Region action 需要在 pipeline 所在 Region(eu-west-1)有一個 artifact bucket,並且在每一個會執行 action 的 Region(us-east-1)也各有一個 artifact bucket。當使用 CLI、CloudFormation 或 SDK 管理 pipeline(如本題情境)時,CodePipeline 不會自動建立該 bucket,你必須自行建立並把它登錄到 pipeline 的 artifactStores map(文件明確寫道:'If you create a cross-region action in your pipeline, you must use artifactStores',以及 'there must be an artifact store for the pipeline Region and for each cross-region action')。因此必須 (C) 在 us-east-1 建立 S3 bucket 並授予 CodePipeline 讀寫權限,以及 (E) 把 us-east-1 bucket 加入 pipeline 作為 artifact store,同時新增使用 us-east-1 output artifact 的 CloudFormation deploy action(工程師已用 'aws cloudformation package' 產生該模板,Lambda .zip 位置已內嵌且指向 us-east-1 位置)。CodePipeline 會自動把 input artifacts 從 eu-west-1 複製到 us-east-1 bucket,因此不需要手動複製。C 提供實體的 per-Region bucket;E 將其接入 pipeline 並建立 deploy action,兩者組成完整且最精簡的答案組合。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Parameterizing the .zip location and passing a parameter override is an alternative packaging pattern that contradicts the stated premise: the engineer already ran 'aws cloudformation package' for us-east-1, which rewrites the template to hard-code the us-east-1 .zip S3 location, so no parameter override is needed. Crucially, A still does not provide the mandatory us-east-1 artifact store that a cross-Region action requires, so it cannot complete the set.","why_zh":"把 .zip 位置參數化並用 parameter override 是另一種封裝方式,與題目前提矛盾:工程師已對 us-east-1 執行 'aws cloudformation package',模板中已硬寫入 us-east-1 的 .zip S3 位置,因此不需要 parameter override。最關鍵的是,A 仍未提供 cross-Region action 必備的 us-east-1 artifact store,因此無法構成完整答案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creating the deploy action that uses the us-east-1 template is correct but incomplete: it omits registering the required us-east-1 artifact store (the docs require artifactStores for any cross-region action). Option E is a strict superset of B (it adds the artifact store as well), so B is redundant and inferior to E.","why_zh":"建立使用 us-east-1 模板的 deploy action 雖正確但不完整:它遺漏了登錄必要的 us-east-1 artifact store(文件規定任何 cross-region action 都必須使用 artifactStores)。選項 E 是 B 的嚴格超集(同時也加入 artifact store),因此 B 相對於 E 多餘且較差。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Cross-Region Replication is unnecessary and does not meet the requirement. CodePipeline itself copies the cross-Region action's input artifacts from the pipeline Region into the action's Region; CRR is asynchronous and eventually consistent, and it does not register a bucket as an artifact store, so it cannot drive the cross-Region deploy action.","why_zh":"S3 Cross-Region Replication 並非必要,也無法滿足需求。CodePipeline 本身會把 cross-Region action 的 input artifacts 從 pipeline Region 複製到 action 所在 Region;CRR 為非同步且最終一致,且不會把 bucket 登錄為 artifact store,因此無法驅動 cross-Region deploy action。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-create-cross-region.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codepipeline-pipeline-artifactstoremap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/reference-pipeline-structure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/continuous-delivery-codepipeline-cfn-artifacts.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":24,"question_en":"A company runs an application on one Amazon EC2 instance. Application metadata is stored in Amazon S3 and must be retrieved if the instance is restarted. The instance must restart or relaunch automatically if the instance becomes unresponsive. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在一台亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行应用程序。应用程序的元数据存储在亚马逊 S3 中，如果实例重启， 必须能够获取这些元数据。如果实例无响应，必须自动重启或重新启动。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for the StatusCheckFailed metric. Use the recover action to stop and start the instance. Use an S3 event notification to push the metadata to the instance when the instance is back up and running.","B":"Configure AWS OpsWorks, and use the auto healing feature to stop and start the instance. Use a lifecycle event in OpsWorks to pull the metadata from Amazon S3 and update it on the instance.","C":"Use EC2 Auto Recovery to automatically stop and start the instance in case of a failure. Use an S3 event notification to push the metadata to the instance when the instance is back up and running.","D":"Use AWS CloudFormation to create an EC2 instance that includes the UserData property for the EC2 resource. Add a command in UserData to retrieve the application metadata from Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"为“StatusCheckFailed”指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。使用恢复操作来停止并重新启动实例。 使用 S3 事件通知在实例重新启动并运行时将元数据推送到实例。","B":"配置 AWS OpsWorks，并使用自动恢复功能停止和启动实例。在 OpsWorks 中使用生命周期事件从 Amazon S3 拉取元数据并在实例上进行更新。","C":"使用 EC2 自动恢复功能，在实例出现故障时自动停止并重新启动实例。使用 S3 事件通知，在实例恢 复运行时将元数据推送到实例。","D":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 创建一个包含 EC2 资源的 UserData 属性的 EC2 实例。在 UserData 中添加一 条命令，从 Amazon S3 获取应用程序元数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must BOTH be met: (1) the instance must automatically restart or relaunch when it becomes unresponsive, and (2) the application metadata in S3 must be retrieved after the instance comes back. Only option B satisfies both with valid mechanisms. AWS OpsWorks Stacks auto healing detects an unresponsive instance (the OpsWorks agent stops sending its heartbeat) and automatically restarts or replaces it, meeting requirement 1. When the instance returns, OpsWorks runs lifecycle events (Setup, Configure, Deploy) whose Chef recipes can PULL the metadata from Amazon S3 and apply it on the instance, meeting requirement 2. Options A and C both rely on an 'S3 event notification to push the metadata to the instance,' which is impossible: per the S3 Event Notifications documentation, S3 can only send notifications to Amazon SNS, Amazon SQS, AWS Lambda, or Amazon EventBridge — never directly to an EC2 instance — and there is no S3 event that fires 'when the instance is back up.' Option D's CloudFormation UserData runs only at first launch and provides no automatic restart-on-failure mechanism, so it fails requirement 1 entirely. Therefore B is the only technically valid solution.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個必須同時滿足的需求:(1) 當執行個體無回應時自動重啟或重新啟動;(2) 執行個體恢復後從 S3 取回應用程式 metadata。只有選項 B 能以有效機制同時滿足這兩點。AWS OpsWorks Stacks 的 auto healing(自動修復)會偵測無回應的執行個體(OpsWorks agent 停止傳送 heartbeat),並自動重啟或替換該執行個體,滿足需求一。執行個體恢復後,OpsWorks 會觸發 lifecycle events(Setup、Configure、Deploy),其 Chef recipe 可以從 Amazon S3 主動拉取(pull) metadata 並套用到執行個體上,滿足需求二。選項 A 與 C 都依賴 S3 event notification 將 metadata『推送(push)』到 EC2 執行個體,這在技術上不可能:依據 S3 Event Notifications 文件,S3 只能將通知發送到 Amazon SNS、Amazon SQS、AWS Lambda 或 Amazon EventBridge,絕不能直接送到 EC2 執行個體,而且也沒有『執行個體恢復時』觸發的 S3 事件。選項 D 的 CloudFormation UserData 只在首次啟動時執行,且完全不提供故障時的自動重啟,因此完全不滿足需求一。所以 B 是唯一技術上可行的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The fatal flaw is that an S3 event notification cannot 'push metadata to the instance' — S3 notifications only target SNS, SQS, Lambda, or EventBridge, never an EC2 instance, and no S3 event fires when an instance comes back up. Separately, the CloudWatch 'recover' action does not 'stop and start'; it moves the instance to new hardware. The metadata requirement is unmet.","why_zh":"致命缺陷在於 S3 event notification 無法『將 metadata push 到實例』——S3 通知只能以 SNS、SQS、Lambda 或 EventBridge 為目標,絕不能直接送到 EC2 執行個體,且沒有在執行個體恢復時觸發的 S3 事件。另外 CloudWatch 的 recover 動作並非『stop and start』,而是將執行個體移到新硬體。metadata 需求未被滿足。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Shares A's broken mechanism: S3 event notifications cannot push metadata directly to an EC2 instance (destinations limited to SNS/SQS/Lambda/EventBridge), so the metadata-retrieval requirement is not met. Also, EC2 auto recovery recovers the instance onto new hardware rather than literally 'stop and start.'","why_zh":"與 A 同樣有錯誤機制:S3 事件通知無法直接把 metadata 推送到 EC2 執行個體(目的地僅限 SNS/SQS/Lambda/EventBridge),因此無法滿足取回 metadata 的需求。此外 EC2 auto recovery 是把執行個體恢復到新硬體,而非字面上的『stop and start』。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFormation UserData fetches metadata from S3 only at the instance's first launch (boot), and CloudFormation provides no mechanism to automatically restart or relaunch an instance when it becomes unresponsive, so it fails the auto-recovery requirement entirely.","why_zh":"CloudFormation UserData 只在執行個體首次啟動(開機)時從 S3 取回 metadata,而 CloudFormation 不提供任何在執行個體無回應時自動重啟或重新啟動的機制,因此完全無法滿足自動復原需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/notification-how-to-event-types-and-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/cloudwatch-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/UsingAlarmActions.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":25,"question_en":"A company has multiple AWS accounts. The company uses AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign- On) that is integrated with AWS Toolkit for Microsoft Azure DevOps. The attributes for access control feature is enabled in IAM Identity Center. The attribute mapping list contains two entries. The department key is mapped to ${path:enterprise.department}. The costCenter key is mapped to ${path:enterprise.costCenter}. All existing Amazon EC2 instances have a department tag that corresponds to three company departments (d1, d2, d3). A DevOps engineer must create policies based on the matching attributes. The policies must minimize administrative effort and must grant each Azure AD user access to only the EC2 instances that are tagged with the user’s respective department name. Which condition key should the DevOps engineer include in the custom permissions policies to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司拥有多个 AWS 账户。该公司使用与 Microsoft Azure DevOps 的 AWS 工具包集成的 AWS IAM 身份 中心（AWS 单点登录）。IAM 身份中心的访问控制属性功能已启用。 属性映射列表包含两个条目。部门键映射到 ${path:enterprise.department}。成本中心键映射到 $ {path:enterprise.costCenter}。 所有现有的亚马逊 EC2 实例都有一个部门标签，对应于公司的三个部门（d1、d2、d3）。一位 DevOps 工 程师必须基于匹配的属性创建策略。这些策略必须将管理工作的量减至最少，并且必须仅授予每个 Azure AD 用户访问其所在部门名称标记的 EC2 实例的权限。 DevOps 工程师应在自定义权限策略中包含哪个条件键才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"","B":"","C":"","D":""},"options_zh":{},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical IAM Identity Center attribute-based access control (ABAC) scenario. AWS docs confirm: when ABAC ('Attributes for access control') is enabled and attribute mappings are configured (department -> ${path:enterprise.department}), IAM Identity Center passes the authenticated user's attribute value into IAM as a SESSION TAG, and you reference that session tag in permission policies with the aws:PrincipalTag/tag-key condition key, where tag-key must match the mapped key name exactly. The official EC2 example is identical in form: \"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\". Here the EC2 instances carry a 'department' tag (d1/d2/d3) and access must be granted by the user's department, so the policy compares the resource department tag against the user's department session tag using aws:PrincipalTag/department. This single dynamic permission set minimizes administrative effort: no per-department policies are needed; adding users/instances only requires correct tagging. The correct condition key is aws:PrincipalTag/department, which in the canonical published version of this question is option C. NOTE: the option text supplied in this dump is blank for all four letters; the C mapping relies on the standard published option ordering (A: aws:PrincipalTag/costCenter, B: ec2:ResourceTag/costCenter, C: aws:PrincipalTag/department, D: ec2:ResourceTag/department), hence medium confidence on the letter even though the underlying technical answer (aws:PrincipalTag/department) is certain.","explanation_zh":"這是 IAM Identity Center 屬性型存取控制 (ABAC) 的標準情境。AWS 文件確認：當啟用 ABAC（Attributes for access control）並設定屬性對應（department -> ${path:enterprise.department}）時，IAM Identity Center 會將已驗證使用者的屬性值以 SESSION TAG（工作階段標籤）形式傳入 IAM；在權限政策中以 aws:PrincipalTag/tag-key 條件鍵參照該工作階段標籤，tag-key 必須與對應的 key 名稱完全一致。官方 EC2 範例形式完全相同：\"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\"。此題中 EC2 執行個體帶有 department 標籤（d1/d2/d3），且需依使用者的 department 授予存取，因此政策用 aws:PrincipalTag/department 將資源的 department 標籤與使用者的 department 工作階段標籤比對。此單一動態 permission set 可最小化管理工作：不需為每個部門建立政策，新增使用者或執行個體只需正確標記。正確條件鍵為 aws:PrincipalTag/department，在本題標準公開版本中對應選項 C。注意：本 dump 提供的四個選項文字皆為空白；C 的對應是依標準公開選項排序推定（A: aws:PrincipalTag/costCenter、B: ec2:ResourceTag/costCenter、C: aws:PrincipalTag/department、D: ec2:ResourceTag/department），故對「字母」給予 medium 信心，但底層技術答案（aws:PrincipalTag/department）為確定。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A costCenter-based principal tag (aws:PrincipalTag/costCenter) does not satisfy the requirement. EC2 instances are tagged by department (d1/d2/d3) and access must be granted by department, not cost center, so matching the costCenter session tag would not align users to their department's instances.","why_zh":"以 costCenter 為基礎的 principal tag（aws:PrincipalTag/costCenter）不符需求。EC2 執行個體以 department（d1/d2/d3）標記，且存取需依 department 授予而非 cost center，因此用 costCenter 工作階段標籤比對無法將使用者對應到其部門的執行個體。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"ec2:ResourceTag/costCenter is a resource-side key on the wrong attribute. It describes the resource's cost center, not the user's department, and a resource tag key alone is not the condition key that carries the federated user's attribute; the user attribute is exposed via aws:PrincipalTag and must be the value compared against the resource's department tag.","why_zh":"ec2:ResourceTag/costCenter 是錯誤屬性上的資源端鍵。它描述資源的 cost center 而非使用者的 department，且資源標籤鍵本身並非承載聯合身分使用者屬性的條件鍵；使用者屬性是透過 aws:PrincipalTag 呈現，必須以該值與資源的 department 標籤比對。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ec2:ResourceTag/department describes the EC2 instance's department tag, not the user's attribute. While the policy does reference this resource tag, the condition KEY that injects the user's department value (the thing the question asks for) is aws:PrincipalTag/department; ResourceTag is the left side of the comparison, the PrincipalTag is the dynamic user attribute being supplied.","why_zh":"ec2:ResourceTag/department 描述 EC2 執行個體的 department 標籤，而非使用者屬性。雖然政策確實會參照此資源標籤，但注入使用者 department 值的條件鍵（即本題詢問者）是 aws:PrincipalTag/department；ResourceTag 是比較式的左側，PrincipalTag 才是被提供的動態使用者屬性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/attributesforaccesscontrol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_ec2-start-stop-match-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":26,"question_en":"A company hosts a security auditing application in an AWS account. The auditing application uses an IAM role to access other AWS accounts. All the accounts are in the same organization in AWS Organizations. A recent security audit revealed that users in the audited AWS accounts could modify or delete the auditing application's IAM role. The company needs to prevent any modification to the auditing application's IAM role by any entity other than a trusted administrator IAM role. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 账户中托管了一个安全审计应用程序。该审计应用程序使用一个 IAM 角色来访问其他 AWS 账户。所有账户都在 AWS Organizations 中的同一个组织内。 最近的一次安全审计发现，被审计的 AWS 账户中的用户能够修改或删除审计记录。 应用程序的 IAM 角色。该公司需要防止除受信任的管理员 IAM 角色之外的任何实体对审计应用程序 的 IAM 角色进行任何修改。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that includes a Deny statement for changes to the auditing application's IAM role. Include a condition that allows the trusted administrator IAM role to make changes. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","B":"Create an SCP that includes an Allow statement for changes to the auditing application's IAM role by the trusted administrator IAM role. Include a Deny statement for changes by all other IAM principals. Attach the SCP to the IAM service in each AWS account where the auditing application has an IAM role.","C":"Create an IAM permissions boundary that includes a Deny statement for changes to the auditing application's IAM role. Include a condition that allows the trusted administrator IAM role to make changes. Attach the permissions boundary to the audited AWS accounts.","D":"Create an IAM permissions boundary that includes a Deny statement for changes to the auditing application’s IAM role. Include a condition that allows the trusted administrator IAM role to make changes. Attach the permissions boundary to the auditing application's IAM role in the AWS accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），其中包含拒绝更改审计应用程序的 IAM 角色的语句。添加一个条 件，允许受信任的管理员 IAM 角色进行更改。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","B":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），其中包含允许受信任管理员 IAM 角色对审计应用程序的 IAM 角 色进行更改的“允许”语句，以及拒绝所有其他 IAM 实体进行更改的“拒绝”语句。将该 SCP 附加到每个拥有审计应用程序 IAM 角色的 AWS 账户中的 IAM 服务。","C":"创建一个包含拒绝更改审计应用程序 IAM 角色语句的 IAM 权限边界。包含一个允许受信任的 管理员 IAM 角色进行更改的条件。将权限边界附加到被审计的 AWS 账户。","D":"创建一个包含拒绝更改审计应用程序 IAM 角色语句的 IAM 权限边界。包含一个允许受信任的管理 员 IAM 角色进行更改的条件。将权限边界附加到 AWS 账户中审计应用程序的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to centrally prevent any principal in the member accounts, other than a trusted administrator role, from modifying or deleting the auditing application's IAM role. A Service Control Policy (SCP) is the correct mechanism: SCPs set maximum-permission guardrails for IAM users and roles in member accounts and support the recommended deny-list strategy. A Deny statement on the role's modify/delete actions (e.g. iam:DeleteRole, iam:UpdateRole, iam:UpdateAssumeRolePolicy, iam:AttachRolePolicy, iam:PutRolePolicy) scoped to the role's ARN, plus a condition that exempts the trusted admin (ArnNotLike/ArnNotEquals on aws:PrincipalARN), blocks everyone else. AWS publishes a near-identical real example in Control Tower control CT.IAM.PV.1, which uses exactly this SCP shape to disallow modification of a managed IAM role. SCPs can be attached to the organization root, where the guardrail applies to all member accounts, and a Deny at any level in the path applies to every account beneath it. Permissions boundaries (C and D) are the wrong tool because a boundary only caps the maximum permissions of the entity it is attached to and never governs what OTHER principals may do TO that entity, and a boundary cannot be attached to an account at all.","explanation_zh":"需求是要集中性地阻止成員帳戶中除受信任的管理員角色之外的任何主體修改或刪除稽核應用程式的 IAM role。正確的機制是 Service Control Policy (SCP)：SCP 為成員帳戶中的 IAM users 與 roles 設定最大權限護欄，並支援建議的「拒絕清單 (deny list)」策略。以 Deny 陳述式針對該 role 的修改/刪除動作（例如 iam:DeleteRole、iam:UpdateRole、iam:UpdateAssumeRolePolicy、iam:AttachRolePolicy、iam:PutRolePolicy），將 Resource 限定為該 role 的 ARN，再加上一個條件以放行受信任的管理員（對 aws:PrincipalARN 使用 ArnNotLike/ArnNotEquals），即可封鎖其他所有人。AWS 在 Control Tower 控制項 CT.IAM.PV.1 中發布了幾乎相同的真實範例，正是用這種 SCP 形式來禁止修改受管的 IAM role。SCP 可附加到組織 root，使護欄套用到所有成員帳戶；路徑上任何層級的 Deny 都會套用到其下的每個帳戶。Permissions boundaries（C 與 D）是錯誤工具，因為 boundary 只限制其所附加實體本身的最大權限，從不規範「其他主體」可以對「該實體」做什麼，而且 boundary 根本無法附加到帳戶。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"SCPs cannot be attached to 'the IAM service in each AWS account'; they attach only to the organization root, an OU, or an account. SCPs also never grant permissions, so the described Allow-plus-Deny structure plus the invalid attachment target make this option technically impossible (the recommended approach is a deny list relying on the default FullAWSAccess).","why_zh":"SCP 無法附加到「每個帳戶中的 IAM 服務」；它只能附加到組織 root、OU 或帳戶。SCP 也從不授予權限，因此所述的 Allow 加 Deny 結構與無效的附加目標使此選項在技術上不可行（建議方式是依賴預設 FullAWSAccess 的拒絕清單）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A permissions boundary is an IAM feature attached to an IAM entity (user or role), not to an account, so it cannot be 'attached to the audited AWS accounts'. A boundary also only caps the attached entity's own permissions and does not control what other principals can do to the auditing role.","why_zh":"Permissions boundary 是附加到 IAM 實體（user 或 role）的 IAM 功能，而非附加到帳戶，因此無法「附加到受稽核的 AWS 帳戶」。boundary 也僅限制所附加實體本身的權限，無法控制其他主體對稽核 role 能做什麼。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Attaching a permissions boundary to the auditing role only limits what that role itself can do; it does NOT prevent other IAM principals from calling iam:DeleteRole/UpdateRole on it. Boundaries govern the holder's outbound permissions, not inbound modification by others, so it fails the requirement.","why_zh":"將 permissions boundary 附加到稽核 role 只會限制該 role 本身能做什麼；它「不會」阻止其他 IAM 主體對其呼叫 iam:DeleteRole/UpdateRole。boundary 規範的是持有者的對外權限，而非他人對其的修改，因此無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/ct-iam-pv-1.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":27,"question_en":"A company has an on-premises application that is written in Go. A DevOps engineer must move the application to AWS. The company's development team wants to enable blue/green deployments and perform A/B testing. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个用 Go 语言编写的本地应用程序。一位 DevOps 工程师必须将该应用程序迁移到 AWS。公司的开发团队希望启用蓝/绿部署并进行 A/B 测试。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application on an Amazon EC2 instance, and create an AMI of the instance. Use the AMI to create an automatic scaling launch configuration that is used in an Auto Scaling group. Use Elastic Load Balancing to distribute traffic. When changes are made to the application, a new AMI will be created, which will initiate an EC2 instance refresh.","B":"Use Amazon Lightsail to deploy the application. Store the application in a zipped format in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use this zipped version to deploy new versions of the application to Lightsail. Use Lightsail deployment options to manage the deployment.","C":"Use AWS CodeArtifact to store the application code. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the application to a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. Use Elastic Load Balancing to distribute the traffic to the EC2 instances. When making changes to the application, upload a new version to CodeArtifact and create a new CodeDeploy deployment.","D":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to host the application. Store a zipped version of the application in Amazon S3. Use that location to deploy new versions of the application. Use Elastic Beanstalk to manage the deployment options."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon EC2 实例上部署应用程序，并创建该实例的 AMI。使用该 AMI 创建自动扩展启动配置， 该配置用于自动扩展组。使用弹性负载均衡来分配流量。当对应用程序进行更改时，将创建新的 AMI，从而启动 EC2 实例刷新。","B":"使用 Amazon Lightsail 部署应用程序。将应用程序以压缩格式存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用此 压缩版本将应用程序的新版本部署到 Lightsail。使用 Lightsail 部署选项来管理部署。","C":"使用 AWS CodeArtifact 存储应用程序代码。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序部署到一组 Amazon EC2 实例。使用弹性负载均衡将流量分发到 EC2 实例。在对应用程序进行更改时，将新版本上传到 CodeArtifact 并创建新的 CodeDeploy 部署。","D":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 来托管应用程序。将应用程序的压缩版本存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用该位 置来部署应用程序的新版本。使用 Elastic Beanstalk 来管理部署选项。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk natively supports the Go platform, so the on-premises Go application can be rehosted with minimal operational overhead: package it as a source bundle, upload the zipped version to Amazon S3, and deploy it as a new application version. Elastic Beanstalk provides built-in blue/green deployments by launching a separate clone environment with the new version and swapping the environment CNAMEs to redirect traffic instantly (and to swap back for fast rollback). For A/B testing it offers the Traffic splitting deployment policy on load-balanced environments using an Application Load Balancer; it launches a full set of new instances and forwards a specified percentage of incoming client traffic to the new version for an evaluation period (canary / A-B testing), per the May 18, 2020 release. This single managed service satisfies every requirement (Go support, blue/green, A/B traffic-splitting) without manually assembling EC2, Auto Scaling, ELB, and deployment orchestration.","explanation_zh":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk 原生支援 Go 平台，因此可以將內部部署的 Go 應用程式以最小的營運負擔重新託管：將其打包為 source bundle，把壓縮版本上傳至 Amazon S3，再部署為新的應用程式版本。Elastic Beanstalk 提供內建的 blue/green 部署，方式是另外建立一個帶有新版本的複製環境，再交換環境的 CNAME 以立即將流量導向新版本（並可換回以快速回滾）。對於 A/B 測試，Elastic Beanstalk 在使用 Application Load Balancer 的負載平衡環境上提供 Traffic splitting 部署原則；它會啟動一整組新執行個體，並在評估期間將指定百分比的進入用戶端流量轉送到新版本（金絲雀／A-B 測試），此功能於 2020 年 5 月 18 日發布。這個單一的受管服務一次滿足所有需求（Go 支援、blue/green、A/B 流量分流），無需手動組合 EC2、Auto Scaling、ELB 與部署協作。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Baking an AMI, launch configuration, Auto Scaling group, ELB, and triggering an EC2 instance refresh performs a rolling in-place instance replacement, not a true blue/green deployment, and provides no native A/B traffic-splitting capability. It also carries far higher operational overhead than a managed platform and uses the deprecated launch configuration concept.","why_zh":"烘焙 AMI、launch configuration、Auto Scaling group、ELB 並觸發 EC2 instance refresh 屬於滾動式就地執行個體替換，並非真正的 blue/green 部署，也沒有原生的 A/B 流量分流能力；其營運負擔遠高於受管平台，且使用了已淘汰的 launch configuration。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Lightsail is a simplified VPS service aimed at simple workloads; it does not offer managed blue/green deployments or A/B traffic-splitting as built-in deployment options, so it cannot meet the A/B testing and blue/green requirements.","why_zh":"Amazon Lightsail 是針對簡單工作負載的簡化 VPS 服務，沒有內建的受管 blue/green 部署或 A/B 流量分流部署選項，因此無法滿足 A/B 測試與 blue/green 的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS CodeArtifact is a software package/dependency repository (npm, Maven, PyPI, NuGet, etc.), not a deployment-artifact (application revision) store consumed by CodeDeploy. CodeDeploy pulls application revisions from Amazon S3 or GitHub, not from CodeArtifact, so this architecture is misconfigured. Although CodeDeploy itself can perform blue/green deployments, the stated CodeArtifact usage is incorrect.","why_zh":"AWS CodeArtifact 是軟體套件／相依性儲存庫（npm、Maven、PyPI、NuGet 等），並非供 CodeDeploy 使用的部署成品（應用程式修訂版）儲存庫。CodeDeploy 從 Amazon S3 或 GitHub 取得應用程式修訂版，而非 CodeArtifact，因此此架構配置錯誤。雖然 CodeDeploy 本身可執行 blue/green 部署，但題目中描述的 CodeArtifact 用法不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/create_deploy_go.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.CNAMESwap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.rolling-version-deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.deploy-existing-version.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/relnotes/release-2020-05-18-ts-deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/welcome.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":28,"question_en":"A developer is maintaining a fleet of 50 Amazon EC2 Linux servers. The servers are part of an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group, and also use Elastic Load Balancing for load balancing. Occasionally, some application servers are being terminated after failing ELB HTTP health checks. The developer would like to perform a root cause analysis on the issue, but before being able to access application logs, the server is terminated. How can log collection be automated?","question_zh":"一位开发人员正在维护一个由 50 台亚马逊 EC2 Linux 服务器组成的集群。这些服务器属于一个亚马 逊 EC2 自动扩展组，并且还使用弹性负载均衡来进行负载均衡。 有时，一些应用服务器在未能通过 ELB HTTP 健康检查后会被终止。开发人员希望对这一问题进行 根本原因分析，但在能够访问应用日志之前，服务器已被终止。 如何实现日志收集的自动化？","options_en":{"A":"Use Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to put instances in a Pending:Wait state. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for EC2 Instance Terminate Successful and trigger an AWS Lambda function that invokes an SSM Run Command script to collect logs, push them to Amazon S3, and complete the lifecycle action once logs are collected.","B":"Use Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to put instances in a Terminating:Wait state. Create an AWS Config rule for EC2 Instance-terminate Lifecycle Action and trigger a step function that invokes a script to collect logs, push them to Amazon S3, and complete the lifecycle action once logs are collected.","C":"Use Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to put instances in a Terminating:Wait state. Create an Amazon CloudWatch subscription filter for EC2 Instance Terminate Successful and trigger a CloudWatch agent that invokes a script to collect logs, push them to Amazon S3, and complete the lifecycle action once logs are collected.","D":"Use Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to put instances in a Terminating:Wait state. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for EC2 Instance-terminate Lifecycle Action and trigger an AWS Lambda function that invokes an SSM Run Command script to collect logs, push them to Amazon S3, and complete the lifecycle action once logs are collected."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩将实例置于“待处理：等待”状态。为“EC2 实例终止成功”创 建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，并触发一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 SSM 运行命令 脚本以收集日志，将它们推送到 Amazon S3，并在收集日志后完成生命周期操作。","B":"使用 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩将实例置于“Terminating:Wait”状态。创建一个针对 EC2 实例终止 生命周期操作的 AWS Config 规则，并触发一个步骤函数，该函数调用一个脚本以收集日志，将 它们推送到 Amazon S3，并在收集完日志后完成生命周期操作。","C":"使用 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩将实例置于“终止：等待”状态。为 EC2 实例终止成功的事件创建 一个 Amazon CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，并触发 CloudWatch 代理，该代理会调用一个脚本收集日志， 将它们推送到 Amazon S3，然后在收集完日志后完成生命周期操作。","D":"使用 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩将实例置于“终止：等待”状态。创建一个针对 EC2 实例终止生命周 期操作的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，并触发一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 SSM 运行命令脚 本以收集日志，将它们推送到 Amazon S3，并在收集完日志后完成生命周期操作。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"To capture logs before an Auto Scaling group fully terminates an instance, you add a termination lifecycle hook. When it fires, EC2 Auto Scaling moves the instance to the Terminating:Wait state and emits the EventBridge event with detail-type 'EC2 Instance-terminate Lifecycle Action' (source aws.autoscaling), giving you a window (one hour by default) before termination completes. An EventBridge rule matching that event invokes a Lambda function that uses SSM Run Command to collect the logs, push them to Amazon S3, and then call CompleteLifecycleAction so termination can proceed. Option D is the only choice with all four elements correct: the Terminating:Wait state, the real lifecycle-action event, the right service to react to it (EventBridge, not AWS Config or a CloudWatch subscription filter), and a correctly ordered callback. The 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful' event used by A and C is a post-termination 'successful scaling event' that fires after the instance is already gone, so it is useless for pre-termination log collection.","explanation_zh":"要在 Auto Scaling group 完全終止執行個體之前擷取日誌，需新增終止 (termination) lifecycle hook。當它觸發時，EC2 Auto Scaling 會將執行個體移入 Terminating:Wait 狀態，並透過 EventBridge 發出 detail-type 為 'EC2 Instance-terminate Lifecycle Action'（source 為 aws.autoscaling）的事件，提供一段等待時間（預設一小時）讓終止暫停。比對該事件的 EventBridge rule 觸發一個 Lambda function，由它呼叫 SSM Run Command 收集日誌、推送到 Amazon S3，最後呼叫 CompleteLifecycleAction 讓終止繼續進行。選項 D 是唯一四個要素全部正確的答案：Terminating:Wait 狀態、真正的 lifecycle-action 事件、正確的反應服務（EventBridge，而非 AWS Config 或 CloudWatch subscription filter），以及順序正確的回呼。A 與 C 使用的 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful' 是終止之後才發出的『成功擴縮事件』，執行個體早已消失，無法用於終止前的日誌收集。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Two errors: Pending:Wait is a launch (scale-out) wait state, not a termination state, and 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful' is a post-termination success event that fires after the instance is already gone, too late to collect logs. Using a CloudWatch alarm to react to that event is also the wrong trigger model.","why_zh":"兩處錯誤：Pending:Wait 是啟動（scale-out）等待狀態而非終止狀態；且 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful' 是終止後才發出的成功事件，此時執行個體早已不存在，無法收集日誌。以 CloudWatch alarm 反應該事件的方式也屬錯誤的觸發模型。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The Terminating:Wait state is correct, but AWS Config rules evaluate resource-configuration compliance over time; they do not trigger on Auto Scaling lifecycle-action events. The lifecycle action is delivered through Amazon EventBridge, not AWS Config, so this trigger mechanism cannot reliably capture logs during the wait window.","why_zh":"Terminating:Wait 狀態正確，但 AWS Config rule 是用來持續評估資源組態合規性，並不會因 Auto Scaling lifecycle-action 事件而觸發。該 lifecycle 動作是透過 Amazon EventBridge 傳遞而非 AWS Config，因此此觸發機制無法在等待期間可靠地擷取日誌。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A CloudWatch Logs subscription filter routes log-stream data, not Auto Scaling lifecycle events, so it cannot match a lifecycle-action event; and a CloudWatch agent cannot be 'triggered' by a subscription filter to run a script. It also keys on 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful', the post-termination event that is too late for log collection.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 作用於日誌串流資料，而非 Auto Scaling lifecycle 事件，因此無法比對 lifecycle-action 事件；CloudWatch agent 也無法由 subscription filter『觸發』執行腳本。同時它引用 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful'，這是終止後事件，對收集日誌而言為時已晚。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-event-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/lifecycle-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/tutorial-lifecycle-hook-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-autoscaling.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":29,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations. The organization includes workload accounts that contain enterprise applications. The company centrally manages users from an operations account. No users can be created in the workload accounts. The company recently added an operations team and must provide the operations team members with administrator access to each workload account. Which combination of actions will provide this access? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有一个组织架构。该组织架构包含有企业应用程序的工作负载账户。公司从 运营账户集中管理用户。工作负载账户中不能创建用户。该公司最近新增了一个运营团队，必须为运 营团队成员提供对每个工作负载账户的管理员访问权限。 哪些操作组合将提供此访问权限？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a SysAdmin role in the operations account. Attach the AdministratorAccess policy to the role. Modify the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action from the workload accounts.","B":"Create a SysAdmin role in each workload account. Attach the AdministratorAccess policy to the role. Modify the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action from the operations account.","C":"Create an Amazon Cognito identity pool in the operations account. Attach the SysAdmin role as an authenticated role.","D":"In the operations account, create an IAM user for each operations team member.","E":"In the operations account, create an IAM user group that is named SysAdmins. Add an IAM policy that allows the sts:AssumeRole action for the SysAdmin role in each workload account. Add all operations team members to the group.","F":"Create an Amazon Cognito user pool in the operations account. Create an Amazon Cognito user for each operations team member."},"options_zh":{"A":"在运营账户中创建一个系统管理员角色。将管理员访问策略附加到该角色。修改信任关系，允许工 作负载账户执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。","B":"在每个工作负载账户中创建一个系统管理员角色。将 AdministratorAccess 策略附加到该角色。修改 信任关系，允许操作账户执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。","C":"在运营账户中创建一个 Amazon Cognito 身份池。将 SysAdmin 角色作为已认证角色进行关联。","D":"在操作账户中，为每个操作团队成员创建一个 IAM 用户。","E":"在操作账户中，创建一个名为 SysAdmins 的 IAM 用户组。添加一个 IAM 策略，允许该组成员执行每 个工作负载账户中的 SysAdmin 角色的 sts:AssumeRole 操作。将所有操作团队成员添加到该组。","F":"在运营账户中创建一个 Amazon Cognito 用户池。为每个运营团队成员创建一个 Amazon Cognito 用 户。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical IAM cross-account role-delegation pattern from the AWS tutorial 'Delegate access across AWS accounts using IAM roles.' In that pattern the trusting (Destination) account is the account being accessed, so it creates the role with the needed permissions and a trust policy that names the trusted (Originating) account; users in the trusted account are then given sts:AssumeRole permission. Mapping to this scenario: (B) create a SysAdmin role in EACH workload account, attach AdministratorAccess, and set the trust relationship to allow sts:AssumeRole from the operations account - the privileged role must live in the account being administered (the trusting account). (D) because users are centrally managed only in the operations account and cannot be created in the workload accounts, create an IAM user for each operations team member in the operations account. (E) create a SysAdmins IAM user group in the operations account whose policy allows sts:AssumeRole on the SysAdmin role in each workload account, and add all team members to it - this grants the trusted-side permission to assume the cross-account role and follows the best practice of granting permissions through groups. Together B+D+E deliver administrator access to every workload account without creating any users in those accounts.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS 教學文件「Delegate access across AWS accounts using IAM roles」所描述的標準 IAM 跨帳戶角色委派模式。在此模式中,被存取的帳戶即受信任 (trusting / Destination) 帳戶,由它建立具備所需權限的角色,並在信任政策中指定信任 (trusted / Originating) 帳戶;接著該受信任帳戶中的使用者才被授予 sts:AssumeRole 權限。對應本題情境:(B) 在「每一個」workload 帳戶中建立 SysAdmin 角色、附加 AdministratorAccess 政策,並設定信任關係以允許來自 operations 帳戶的 sts:AssumeRole - 具特權的角色必須位於被管理的帳戶 (即 trusting 帳戶)。(D) 由於使用者僅集中於 operations 帳戶管理且無法在 workload 帳戶建立,故在 operations 帳戶為每位運維團隊成員建立一個 IAM user。(E) 在 operations 帳戶建立名為 SysAdmins 的 IAM user group,其政策允許對各 workload 帳戶的 SysAdmin 角色執行 sts:AssumeRole,並將所有成員加入該群組 - 這賦予受信任端承擔跨帳戶角色的權限,同時符合透過群組授權的最佳實務。B+D+E 三者結合即可在不於 workload 帳戶建立任何使用者的前提下,提供對每個 workload 帳戶的管理員存取。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creates the SysAdmin role with AdministratorAccess in the operations account, which inverts the trust direction. The privileged role must be created in each workload account (the trusting account that is accessed), with a trust policy that points to the operations account - not a role in the operations account that trusts the workload accounts. As written it would let workload accounts assume into operations, the opposite of what is required, and grants no access to the workload accounts.","why_zh":"在 operations 帳戶建立帶有 AdministratorAccess 的 SysAdmin 角色,使信任方向顛倒。具特權的角色必須建立於各 workload 帳戶 (被存取的 trusting 帳戶),且其信任政策應指向 operations 帳戶,而非在 operations 帳戶建立並信任 workload 帳戶的角色。如此設定反而會讓 workload 帳戶假設進 operations,與需求相反,且無法授予對 workload 帳戶的存取。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Cognito identity pools provide temporary AWS credentials to end users of web and mobile applications via federation; they are not the mechanism for delegating administrator access to internal operations staff across AWS Organizations accounts. The documented cross-account console/CLI role-switching pattern relies on IAM roles and sts:AssumeRole, not Cognito.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito identity pool 是透過聯合身分為 Web/行動應用程式的終端使用者提供臨時 AWS 憑證,並非用來在 AWS Organizations 帳戶間為內部運維人員委派管理員存取的機制。文件所述的跨帳戶 console/CLI 角色切換採用 IAM 角色與 sts:AssumeRole,而非 Cognito。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Amazon Cognito user pools are a user directory for application sign-up/sign-in (authentication for app end users), not a means of managing IAM principals that assume cross-account AWS roles or of granting administrator access to workload accounts. It does not implement the sts:AssumeRole cross-account delegation required here.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito user pool 是供應用程式註冊/登入使用的使用者目錄 (為應用終端使用者做驗證),並非用於管理假設跨帳戶 AWS 角色的 IAM 主體,也無法賦予對 workload 帳戶的管理員存取,無法實作本題所需的 sts:AssumeRole 跨帳戶委派。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies-cross-account-resource-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create_for-user.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":30,"question_en":"A company has multiple accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company's SecOps team needs to receive an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notification if any account in the organization turns off the Block Public Access feature on an Amazon S3 bucket. A DevOps engineer must implement this change without affecting the operation of any AWS accounts. The implementation must ensure that individual member accounts in the organization cannot turn off the notification. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有多个账户。该公司的安全运维团队需要在组织中的任何账户关闭 Amazon S3 存储桶的“阻止公共访问”功能时收到 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）的通知。一位 DevOps 工程师必须在不影响任何 AWS 账户运行的情况下实施此变更。该实施必须确保组织中的各个 成员账户无法关闭此通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Designate an account to be the delegated Amazon GuardDuty administrator account. Turn on GuardDuty for all accounts across the organization. In the GuardDuty administrator account, create an SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team's email address to the SNS topic. In the same account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses an event pattern for GuardDuty findings and a target of the SNS topic.","B":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that creates an SNS topic and subscribes the SecOps team’s email address to the SNS topic. In the template, include an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses an event pattern of CloudTrail activity for s3:PutBucketPublicAccessBlock and a target of the SNS topic. Deploy the stack to every account in the organization by using CloudFormation StackSets.","C":"Turn on AWS Config across the organization. In the delegated administrator account, create an SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team's email address to the SNS topic. Deploy a conformance pack that uses the s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited AWS Config managed rule in each account and uses an AWS Systems Manager document to publish an event to the SNS topic to notify the SecOps team.","D":"Turn on Amazon Inspector across the organization. In the Amazon Inspector delegated administrator account, create an SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team’s email address to the SNS topic. In the same account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses an event pattern for public network exposure of the S3 bucket and publishes an event to the SNS topic to notify the SecOps team."},"options_zh":{"A":"指定一个账户作为委托的 Amazon GuardDuty 管理员账户。为组织内的所有账户开启 GuardDuty 服务。在 GuardDuty 管理员账户中，创建一个 SNS 主题。将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该 SNS 主题。在 同一个账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则使用 GuardDuty 发现结果的事件模式，并将 SNS 主题作为目标。","B":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于创建一个 SNS 主题，并将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地址订阅到 该 SNS 主题。在模板中，包含一个使用 CloudTrail 活动事件模式（针对 s3:PutBucketPublicAccessBlock） 的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，其目标为 SNS 主题。通过使用 CloudFormation StackSets 将该堆栈部署到 组织中的每个账户。","C":"在整个组织内启用 AWS Config。在委托管理员账户中创建一个 SNS 主题。将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地 址订阅到该 SNS 主题。在每个账户中部署一个一致性包，该包使用 AWS Config 管理规则 s3-bucket- level-public-access-prohibited，并使用 AWS Systems Manager 文档向 SNS 主题发布事件以通知 SecOps 团 队。","D":"在整个组织内启用 Amazon Inspector。在 Amazon Inspector 委托管理员账户中，创建一个 SNS 主题。将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该 SNS 主题。在同一个账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规 则，该规则使用 S3 存储桶公共网络暴露的事件模式，并将事件发布到 SNS 主题以通知 SecOps 团队。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Amazon GuardDuty has a purpose-built finding type for exactly this event: Policy:S3/BucketBlockPublicAccessDisabled - 'An IAM entity invoked an API used to disable S3 Block Public Access on a bucket' (with Policy:S3/AccountBlockPublicAccessDisabled at the account level), sourced from CloudTrail management events. Designating a delegated GuardDuty administrator and auto-enabling GuardDuty for ALL accounts (including new ones) means member accounts have no control over the detection. The SNS topic, the email subscription, and the EventBridge rule all live in the GuardDuty administrator account, which receives finding events for every member account in a multi-account organization, so individual member accounts cannot turn off the notification. The pipeline is notify-only (EventBridge to SNS), so it does not affect account operations. Option C is the strongest distractor and the dump answer, but it is technically weaker: the named rule s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited evaluates whether a bucket is effectively publicly accessible, not whether the Block Public Access toggle was turned off (the rule that watches the BPA setting itself is s3-account-level-public-access-blocks), so disabling BPA on a bucket with no public policy would leave it COMPLIANT and produce no notification; additionally, using a Config remediation action (an SSM Automation document, designed to change/fix resources) merely to publish an SNS message is a contrived misuse - the idiomatic notify path is EventBridge on a compliance-change event, not a remediation runbook.","explanation_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 有一個專為此事件設計的 finding 類型：Policy:S3/BucketBlockPublicAccessDisabled，原文為「An IAM entity invoked an API used to disable S3 Block Public Access on a bucket」（帳戶層級則為 Policy:S3/AccountBlockPublicAccessDisabled），資料來源為 CloudTrail management events。指定委派的 GuardDuty administrator 並對 ALL 帳戶（含新加入帳戶）自動啟用 GuardDuty，使成員帳戶無法控制偵測機制。SNS topic、email 訂閱與 EventBridge rule 全都建立在 GuardDuty administrator 帳戶內，而該帳戶在多帳戶組織中會收到每個成員帳戶的 finding 事件，因此個別成員帳戶無法關閉通知。整條管線僅為通知用途（EventBridge 到 SNS），不影響帳戶運作。選項 C 是最強干擾項，也是題庫給的答案，但技術上較弱：所指的規則 s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited 評估的是 bucket 是否實際對外公開，而非 Block Public Access 開關是否被關閉（真正監看 BPA 設定的規則是 s3-account-level-public-access-blocks）；因此若在沒有公開政策的 bucket 上關閉 BPA，該規則仍維持 COMPLIANT 而不會發出通知。此外，用 Config remediation action（即用來變更/修復資源的 SSM Automation document）僅僅去發送 SNS 訊息屬於非慣用的誤用，慣用的通知路徑是針對 compliance-change 事件的 EventBridge，而非 remediation runbook。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The SNS topic, EventBridge rule, and email subscription are deployed into each member account via CloudFormation StackSets, so the notification resources are owned by the member account. A sufficiently privileged member-account administrator can delete or disable the local EventBridge rule or SNS subscription, turning off the notification. StackSets (even service-managed) does not make those member-account resources immutable against local admins, so this fails the requirement that members cannot turn off the notification.","why_zh":"SNS topic、EventBridge rule 與 email 訂閱透過 CloudFormation StackSets 部署到每個成員帳戶內，這些通知資源由成員帳戶擁有。具足夠權限的成員帳戶管理員可刪除或停用本地 EventBridge rule 或 SNS 訂閱而關閉通知。即使是 service-managed StackSets，也不會使這些成員帳戶資源對本地管理員不可變更，故未滿足成員無法關閉通知的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Two technical weaknesses make this inferior to A. First, the chosen managed rule s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited checks whether a bucket is effectively publicly accessible, not whether the Block Public Access setting was turned off; turning BPA off on a bucket that has no public policy/ACL leaves it COMPLIANT, so SecOps would not be notified for the exact event the question describes (the setting-watching rule is s3-account-level-public-access-blocks). Second, a Config remediation action is an SSM Automation document meant to modify/fix noncompliant resources; repurposing it only to publish an SNS message is contrived versus the standard EventBridge-on-compliance-change notification path. The governance/non-modifiable claim is true for org conformance packs, but the detection-and-notify mechanism itself is the weaker fit.","why_zh":"兩個技術弱點使其不如 A。第一，所選受管規則 s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited 檢查的是 bucket 是否實際對外公開，而非 Block Public Access 設定是否被關閉；在沒有公開 policy/ACL 的 bucket 上關閉 BPA 會維持 COMPLIANT，因此對題目描述的確切事件不會通知 SecOps（監看設定本身的規則是 s3-account-level-public-access-blocks）。第二，Config remediation action 是用來修改/修復不合規資源的 SSM Automation document，將其重新用途化為僅發送 SNS 訊息，相較於標準的 EventBridge compliance-change 通知路徑顯得牽強。組織 conformance pack 不可被成員修改的治理說法確實成立，但其偵測與通知機制本身較不貼合需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector scans EC2 instances, ECR container images, and Lambda functions for software vulnerabilities and network reachability; it does not monitor S3 bucket Block Public Access configuration. There is no Inspector 'public network exposure of the S3 bucket' finding, so it cannot detect BPA being turned off and cannot meet the requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 掃描 EC2 執行個體、ECR 容器映像與 Lambda 函式的軟體弱點與網路可達性，並不監控 S3 bucket 的 Block Public Access 設定。Inspector 沒有所謂「S3 bucket 公開網路暴露」的 finding，因此無法偵測 BPA 被關閉，也無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/set-guardduty-auto-enable-preferences.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-account-level-public-access-blocks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-pack-organization-apis.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":31,"question_en":"A company has migrated its container-based applications to Amazon EKS and want to establish automated email notifications. The notifications sent to each email address are for specific activities related to EKS components. The solution will include Amazon SNS topics and an AWS Lambda function to evaluate incoming log events and publish messages to the correct SNS topic. Which logging solution will support these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已将其基于容器的应用程序迁移到了亚马逊 EKS，并希望建立自动化的电子邮件通知机制。发送到 每个电子邮件地址的通知是针对与 EKS 组件相关的特定活动。该解决方案将包括亚马逊 SNS 主题和一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于评估传入的日志事件并向正确的 SNS 主题发布消息。 哪种日志记录解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon CloudWatch Logs to log the EKS components. Create a CloudWatch subscription filter for each component with Lambda as the subscription feed destination.","B":"Enable Amazon CloudWatch Logs to log the EKS components. Create CloudWatch Logs Insights queries linked to Amazon EventBridge events that invoke Lambda.","C":"Enable Amazon S3 logging for the EKS components. Configure an Amazon CloudWatch subscription filter for each component with Lambda as the subscription feed destination.","D":"Enable Amazon S3 logging for the EKS components. Configure S3 PUT Object event notifications with AWS Lambda as the destination."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 来记录 EKS 组件。为每个组件创建一个 CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，并将 Lambda 作为订阅源的目的地。","B":"启用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 来记录 EKS 组件。创建与 Amazon EventBridge 事件关联的 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询，这些事件会调用 Lambda。","C":"为 EKS 组件启用 Amazon S3 日志记录。为每个组件配置一个 Amazon CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，将 Lambda 作为订阅源的目的地。","D":"为 EKS 组件启用 Amazon S3 日志记录。将 S3 PUT 对象事件通知配置为以 AWS Lambda 作为目标。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon EKS control plane logging sends audit and diagnostic logs from the Kubernetes control plane directly to CloudWatch Logs. Each enabled log type (api, audit, authenticator, controllerManager, scheduler) corresponds to a control plane component and is delivered as a separate log stream within a log group for the cluster. The EKS doc explicitly states you can use CloudWatch subscription filters to do real-time analysis on these logs or forward them to other services, and the CloudWatch Logs subscription filter doc lists AWS Lambda as a supported destination. Therefore creating a per-component subscription filter that invokes a Lambda function lets the function evaluate each incoming log event in real time and publish to the correct SNS topic for the matching email subscribers, satisfying the requirement. Option A is correct.","explanation_zh":"Amazon EKS control plane logging 會把 Kubernetes 控制平面的稽核與診斷日誌直接送到 CloudWatch Logs。每個啟用的日誌類型 (api、audit、authenticator、controllerManager、scheduler) 對應一個控制平面元件，並以個別的 log stream 形式送進該叢集的 log group。EKS 文件明確說明可使用 CloudWatch subscription filters 對這些日誌進行即時分析或轉發到其他服務，而 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 文件也列出 AWS Lambda 為支援的目的地。因此為每個元件建立一個 subscription filter 並以 Lambda 作為訂閱目的地，Lambda 即可即時評估每筆傳入的 log event，並發布到對應的 SNS topic 給相符的 email 訂閱者，符合需求。選項 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights is an interactive, on-demand query tool for ad hoc analysis; you cannot 'link' a Logs Insights query to EventBridge events to invoke Lambda as a continuous, per-log-event evaluation pipeline. This is not a supported real-time forwarding pattern.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 是互動式、隨選的查詢工具，用於臨時分析；無法把 Logs Insights 查詢「連結」到 EventBridge 事件以觸發 Lambda 來持續逐筆評估日誌。這不是支援的即時轉發模式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EKS control plane logging delivers to CloudWatch Logs, not to S3 directly, so 'enable Amazon S3 logging for the EKS components' is not a native EKS capability. It also incoherently applies a CloudWatch subscription filter, which operates on a CloudWatch Logs log group, to S3 logging.","why_zh":"EKS control plane logging 是送到 CloudWatch Logs，而非直接送到 S3，所以「為 EKS 元件啟用 Amazon S3 logging」不是 EKS 原生能力。它還矛盾地把作用於 CloudWatch Logs log group 的 subscription filter 套用在 S3 logging 上。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EKS does not natively export control plane component logs to S3; control plane logging targets CloudWatch Logs. Even if logs landed in S3, S3 PUT Object event notifications fire per object/batch, not per individual log event, so they cannot evaluate each log event for real-time routing to the correct SNS topic.","why_zh":"EKS 不會原生地把控制平面元件日誌匯出到 S3；控制平面日誌的目的地是 CloudWatch Logs。即使日誌落到 S3，S3 PUT Object 事件通知是以物件/批次層級觸發，而非逐筆 log event，因此無法即時評估每筆 log event 以路由到正確的 SNS topic。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/control-plane-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":32,"question_en":"A company is implementing an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster to run its workload. The company architecture will run multiple ECS services on the cluster. The architecture includes an Application Load Balancer on the front end and uses multiple target groups to route traffic. A DevOps engineer must collect application and access logs. The DevOps engineer then needs to send the logs to an Amazon S3 bucket for near-real-time analysis. Which combination of steps must the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在部署亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）集群以运行其工作负载。该公司的架构将在集 群上运行多个 ECS 服务。架构前端包含一个应用负载均衡器，并使用多个目标组来路由流量。 DevOps 工程师必须收集应用程序和访问日志。然后，该工程师需要将这些日志发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶， 以便进行近乎实时的分析。 DevOps 工程师必须采取哪些步骤组合才能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Download the Amazon CloudWatch Logs container instance from AWS. Configure this instance as a task. Update the application service definitions to include the logging task.","B":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch Logs agent on the ECS instances. Change the logging driver in the ECS task definition to awslogs.","C":"Use Amazon EventBridge to schedule an AWS Lambda function that will run every 60 seconds and will run the Amazon CloudWatch Logs create-export-task command. Then point the output to the logging S3 bucket.","D":"Activate access logging on the ALB. Then point the ALB directly to the logging S3 bucket.","E":"Activate access logging on the target groups that the ECS services use. Then send the logs directly to the logging S3 bucket.","F":"Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that has a destination of the logging S3 bucket. Then create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs subscription filter for Kinesis Data Firehose."},"options_zh":{"A":"从 AWS 下载 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 容器实例。将此实例配置为任务。更新应用程序服务定义以包 含日志记录任务。","B":"在 ECS 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 代理。更改日志驱动程序在 ECS 任务定义到 awslogs。","C":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 安排一个每 60 秒运行一次的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数将运行 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 的 create-export-task 命令。然后将输出指向日志 S3 存储桶。","D":"在应用负载均衡器（ALB）上启用访问日志记录。然后将 ALB 直接指向日志记录的 S3 存储桶。","E":"在 ECS 服务所使用的目标组上启用访问日志记录功能。然后将日志直接发送到日志记录 S3 存储桶。","F":"创建一个将日志 S3 存储桶作为目的地的 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流。然后为 Kinesis Data Firehose 创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 订阅筛选器。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The task is to collect both ECS application logs and ALB access logs and land them in S3 for near-real-time analysis. (B) Setting the awslogs log driver in the ECS task definition logConfiguration ships container STDOUT/STDERR to CloudWatch Logs, the documented way to centralize ECS application logs and the prerequisite for the near-real-time S3 path. (D) Access logging is an attribute of the Application Load Balancer itself; when enabled it writes access logs directly to a specified S3 bucket, satisfying the access-log requirement. (F) Creating a Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream with an S3 destination and attaching a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to it is AWS's documented near-real-time pipeline from CloudWatch Logs to S3 - the CloudWatch Logs S3-export docs explicitly recommend subscriptions over create-export-task for near-real-time, continuous delivery. Together, D handles access logs and B->F handles application logs, both reaching S3 near-real-time.","explanation_zh":"需求是同時收集 ECS 應用程式日誌與 ALB 存取日誌，並送到 S3 進行近即時分析。(B) 在 ECS task definition 的 logConfiguration 設定 awslogs log driver，可將容器的 STDOUT/STDERR 傳送至 CloudWatch Logs，這是集中化 ECS 應用程式日誌的官方做法，也是近即時送入 S3 路徑的前置條件。(D) 存取日誌（access logging）是 Application Load Balancer 本身的屬性；啟用後會直接將存取日誌寫入指定的 S3 bucket，滿足存取日誌需求。(F) 建立以 S3 為目的地的 Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream，並對其建立 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter，是 AWS 官方文件記載的「CloudWatch Logs 到 S3 的近即時管線」；CloudWatch Logs 的 S3 匯出文件明確建議近即時與持續傳遞應使用 subscriptions 而非 create-export-task。綜合來看，D 處理存取日誌，B->F 處理應用程式日誌，兩者都能近即時抵達 S3。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no downloadable 'CloudWatch Logs container instance' artifact that you configure as a task and attach to service definitions; this is a fabricated mechanism. ECS application logs are shipped via the awslogs (or FireLens/awsfirelens) log driver, not a separate logging task image.","why_zh":"不存在可下載並設定為 task、再掛到 service 定義上的「CloudWatch Logs container instance」；這是杜撰的機制。ECS 應用程式日誌是透過 awslogs（或 FireLens/awsfirelens）log driver 傳送，而非另起一個 logging task 映像。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs create-export-task is a batch export: data can take up to 12 hours to become available, and the docs explicitly advise against using it for continuous/near-real-time delivery, recommending subscriptions instead. Scheduling it every 60 seconds is unworkable (one active export task per account) and is not near-real-time.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs create-export-task 是批次匯出：資料最多可能需 12 小時才可匯出，且文件明確不建議用於持續/近即時傳遞，而建議改用 subscriptions。每 60 秒排程執行不可行（每帳戶僅能有一個進行中的匯出任務），也不是近即時。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Access logging is an attribute of the load balancer, not of target groups. Target groups do not emit access logs, so 'activate access logging on the target groups' is not a real configuration; the correct option is D (enable it on the ALB).","why_zh":"存取日誌是負載平衡器（load balancer）的屬性，而非 target group 的屬性。Target group 不會產生存取日誌，因此「在 target group 啟用 access logging」並非真實設定；正確選項是 D（在 ALB 上啟用）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/using_awslogs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/specify-log-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-access-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/enable-access-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/writing-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/S3Export.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":33,"question_en":"A company that uses electronic health records is running a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances with an Amazon Linux operating system. As part of patient privacy requirements, the company must ensure continuous compliance for patches for operating system and applications running on the EC2 instances. How can the deployments of the operating system and application patches be automated using a default and custom repository?","question_zh":"一家使用电子健康记录的公司正在运行一批搭载亚马逊 Linux 操作系统的亚马逊 EC2 实例。作为患者隐 私要求的一部分，该公司必须确保其 EC2 实例上运行的操作系统和应用程序的补丁能够持续合规。 如何使用默认和自定义存储库来自动部署操作系统和应用程序补丁？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager to create a new patch baseline including the custom repository. Run the AWS-RunPatchBaseline document using the run command to verify and install patches.","B":"Use AWS Direct Connect to integrate the corporate repository and deploy the patches using Amazon CloudWatch scheduled events, then use the CloudWatch dashboard to create reports.","C":"Use yum-config-manager to add the custom repository under /etc/yum.repos.d and run yum- config-manager-enable to activate the repository.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager to create a new patch baseline including the corporate repository. Run the AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline document using the run command to verify and install patches."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 创建一个新的补丁基准，包括自定义存储库。使用 run 命令运行 AWS- RunPatchBaseline 文档以验证并安装补丁。","B":"使用 AWS Direct Connect 集成企业存储库，并通过 Amazon CloudWatch 定期事件部署补丁，然后使 用 CloudWatch 控制面板创建报告。","C":"使用 yum-config-manager 在 /etc/yum.repos.d 下添加自定义存储库，并运行 yum-config-manager -- enable 来激活该存储库。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 创建一个新的补丁基准，包括企业存储库。使用 run 命令运行 AWS- AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline 文档以验证并安装补丁。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager automates OS and application patching for EC2 fleets and continuously tracks patch compliance, which satisfies the continuous-compliance requirement. To patch from a source other than the node's default repositories (such as a corporate/custom repo) while still using the defaults, you specify alternative patch source repositories when you CREATE A CUSTOM PATCH BASELINE; the AWS docs note that to keep applying default-repo updates you also list the default repositories in the alternative source configuration, so both default and custom repositories are used. You then run patching by executing the AWS-RunPatchBaseline SSM document via Run Command, which scans (verifies) and installs both operating-system and application patches on Amazon Linux/Linux nodes and reports compliance back to Patch Manager. This matches option A exactly. Option D is wrong because AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline is the name of a PREDEFINED PATCH BASELINE resource, not a runnable SSM document; the recommended runnable patch documents are AWS-RunPatchBaseline, AWS-RunPatchBaselineAssociation, AWS-RunPatchBaselineWithHooks, AWS-ConfigureWindowsUpdate, and AWS-InstallWindowsUpdates, so you cannot 'run' AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline via Run Command.","explanation_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager 可自動化 EC2 機群的作業系統與應用程式修補，並持續追蹤修補合規狀態，符合題目所要求的持續合規。若要從節點預設儲存庫以外的來源（例如企業/自訂 repo）進行修補，同時仍套用預設儲存庫，您需在「建立自訂 patch baseline」時指定替代的修補來源儲存庫；AWS 文件指出，若要持續套用預設 repo 的更新，必須在替代來源設定中一併列出預設儲存庫，如此預設與自訂儲存庫皆會被使用。接著透過 Run Command 執行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline SSM document 來進行修補，它會掃描（驗證）並安裝 Amazon Linux/Linux 節點上的作業系統與應用程式修補，並將合規結果回報給 Patch Manager。這完全對應選項 A。選項 D 錯誤，因為 AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline 是「預先定義的 patch baseline」資源名稱，並非可執行的 SSM document；建議用於修補的可執行 document 為 AWS-RunPatchBaseline、AWS-RunPatchBaselineAssociation、AWS-RunPatchBaselineWithHooks、AWS-ConfigureWindowsUpdate 與 AWS-InstallWindowsUpdates，因此無法以 Run Command 執行 AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Direct Connect is a dedicated network connectivity service, not a patch-distribution or automation mechanism, and CloudWatch scheduled events plus a dashboard do not scan, install, or report OS/application patch compliance. This ignores the purpose-built Patch Manager and cannot deliver continuous patch compliance.","why_zh":"AWS Direct Connect 是專用網路連線服務，並非修補散佈或自動化機制；CloudWatch 排程事件加儀表板無法掃描、安裝或回報作業系統/應用程式的修補合規。此選項忽略專為修補設計的 Patch Manager，也無法達成持續修補合規。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Manually editing /etc/yum.repos.d and running yum-config-manager on each instance is a per-node manual step, not centralized AWS automation, and provides no fleet-wide baseline approval rules or continuous compliance tracking/reporting. It bypasses Systems Manager Patch Manager entirely.","why_zh":"在每台執行個體手動編輯 /etc/yum.repos.d 並執行 yum-config-manager 屬於逐台手動操作，並非集中式 AWS 自動化，且無法跨機群提供 baseline 核准規則或持續合規追蹤/回報，完全略過 Systems Manager Patch Manager。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline is a predefined patch baseline resource (it resolves to a patchbaseline/pb-... ARN), not an SSM Run Command document you can 'run.' The runnable patching document that scans and installs patches is AWS-RunPatchBaseline. So although the custom-baseline idea is partly right, the execution action described is technically invalid.","why_zh":"AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline 是「預先定義的 patch baseline」資源（會對應到 patchbaseline/pb-... ARN），並非可被「執行」的 SSM Run Command document。可掃描並安裝修補的可執行 document 是 AWS-RunPatchBaseline。因此即使自訂 baseline 的概念部分正確，此處描述的執行動作在技術上並不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-alternative-source-repository.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-aws-runpatchbaseline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-ssm-documents.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-predefined-and-custom-patch-baselines.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":34,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CodePipeline to automate its release pipeline. AWS CodeDeploy is being used in the pipeline to deploy an application to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) using the blue/ green deployment model. The company wants to implement scripts to test the green version of the application before shifting traffic. These scripts will complete in 5 minutes or less. If errors are discovered during these tests, the application must be rolled back. Which strategy will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 来自动化其发布流程。在该流程中，AWS CodeDeploy 用于将应用 程序部署到 Amazon Elastic Container Service （Amazon ECS），采用蓝/绿部署模式。该公司希望在切换 流量之前实施脚本对绿色版本的应用程序进行测试，这些脚本将在 5 分钟内完成。如果在这些测试中发 现错误，必须回滚应用程序。 哪种策略能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add a stage to the CodePipeline pipeline between the source and deploy stages. Use AWS CodeBuild to create a runtime environment and build commands in the buildspec file to invoke test scripts. If errors are found, use the aws deploy stop-deployment command to stop the deployment.","B":"Add a stage to the CodePipeline pipeline between the source and deploy stages. Use this stage to invoke an AWS Lambda function that will run the test scripts. If errors are found, use the aws deploy stop-deployment command to stop the deployment.","C":"Add a hooks section to the CodeDeploy AppSpec file. Use the AfterAllowTestTraffic lifecycle event to invoke an AWS Lambda function to run the test scripts. If errors are found, exit the Lambda function with an error to initiate rollback.","D":"Add a hooks section to the CodeDeploy AppSpec file. Use the AfterAllowTraffic lifecycle event to invoke the test scripts. If errors are found, use the aws deploy stop-deployment CLI command to stop the deployment."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CodePipeline 管道的源代码和部署阶段之间添加一个阶段。使用 AWS CodeBuild 创建运行时环境， 并在 buildspec 文件中编写构建命令以调用测试脚本。如果发现错误，请使用 aws deploy stop- deployment 命令停止部署。","B":"在 CodePipeline 管道的源代码和部署阶段之间添加一个阶段。使用此阶段调用一个 AWS Lambda 函 数来运行测试脚本。如果发现错误，请使用 aws deploy stop-deployment 命令停止部署。","C":"在 CodeDeploy AppSpec 文件中添加一个钩子部分。使用 AfterAllowTestTraffic 生命周期事件来调用 一个 AWS Lambda 函数以运行测试脚本。如果发现错误，让 Lambda 函数以错误退出，从而启动 回滚。","D":"在 CodeDeploy AppSpec 文件中添加一个钩子部分。使用 AfterAllowTraffic 生命周期事件来调用测试 脚本。如果发现错误，请使用 aws deploy stop-deployment CLI 命令停止部署。 部署。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For a CodeDeploy ECS blue/green deployment, the AppSpec 'hooks' section is the native mechanism to validate the green (replacement) task set before production traffic is shifted. The AfterAllowTestTraffic lifecycle event runs after the test listener serves traffic to the replacement task set but before production traffic is shifted, which exactly matches the requirement to test the green version first. ECS deployment hooks invoke a Lambda function, and AWS documentation explicitly states that the results of a hook function at this point can trigger a rollback. The Lambda reports Succeeded or Failed via putLifecycleEventHookExecutionStatus; a Failed result (exiting the function with an error) causes CodeDeploy to roll back automatically. The 5-minute test scripts are well within the 1-hour hook timeout, so option C meets every requirement.","explanation_zh":"對於 CodeDeploy ECS blue/green 部署，AppSpec 的 'hooks' 區段是在切換正式流量前驗證 green（replacement）task set 的原生機制。AfterAllowTestTraffic 生命週期事件會在 test listener 將流量送往 replacement task set 之後、但在正式流量切換之前執行，正好符合「先測試 green 版本」的需求。ECS 部署 hooks 會呼叫 AWS Lambda function，且 AWS 文件明確指出此事件的 hook function 結果可觸發 rollback。Lambda 透過 putLifecycleEventHookExecutionStatus 回報 Succeeded 或 Failed；回報 Failed（以錯誤結束 function）會讓 CodeDeploy 自動 rollback。5 分鐘的測試指令碼遠低於 1 小時的 hook 逾時上限，因此選項 C 完全滿足所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Placing a CodeBuild test stage between the source and deploy stages runs the tests before the green task set is even deployed, so there is no green version to validate yet. Also, aws deploy stop-deployment merely halts a deployment; at this point in the pipeline the CodeDeploy deployment has not started, and stop-deployment is not the documented rollback mechanism.","why_zh":"在 source 與 deploy 階段之間放一個 CodeBuild 測試階段，會在 green task set 尚未部署前就執行測試，根本沒有 green 版本可驗證。此外 aws deploy stop-deployment 只是停止部署，而此時 pipeline 中 CodeDeploy 部署尚未開始，stop-deployment 也不是文件所載的 rollback 機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same timing flaw as A: a Lambda test stage between source and deploy executes before the green task set is created, so it cannot test the running green application before traffic shift. stop-deployment also does not roll back to the prior version, and there is no in-progress deployment to stop at this stage.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的時序缺陷：在 source 與 deploy 之間的 Lambda 測試階段會在 green task set 建立前執行，因此無法在流量切換前測試正在運行的 green 應用程式。stop-deployment 也不會回滾到舊版本，且此階段並無進行中的部署可停止。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The AfterAllowTraffic lifecycle event runs after production traffic has already been shifted to the green task set, so real users would hit the new version before testing completes, violating 'test before shifting traffic.' It also relies on the aws deploy stop-deployment CLI command rather than the hook's Succeeded/Failed result, which is not the documented rollback mechanism for ECS hooks.","why_zh":"AfterAllowTraffic 生命週期事件是在正式流量已切換到 green task set 之後才執行，真實使用者在測試完成前就已存取新版本，違反「在切換流量前測試」的要求。它還依賴 aws deploy stop-deployment CLI 指令，而非 hook 的 Succeeded/Failed 結果，這並非 ECS hooks 文件所載的 rollback 機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/tutorial-ecs-deployment-with-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-steps-ecs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":35,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Storage Gateway in file gateway mode in front of an Amazon S3 bucket that is used by multiple resources. In the morning when business begins, users do not see the objects processed by a third party the previous evening. When a DevOps engineer looks directly at the S3 bucket, the data is there, but it is missing in Storage Gateway. Which solution ensures that all the updated third-party files are available in the morning?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 存储网关的文件网关模式置于一个由多个资源使用的 Amazon S3 存储桶之前。每天早上 业务开始时，用户看不到前一天晚上由第三方处理的对象。当一名 DevOps 工程师直接查看 S3 存储桶时， 数据在那里，但在存储网关中却不见了。 哪种解决方案能确保所有更新的第三方文件在早上都可用？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a nightly Amazon EventBridge event to invoke an AWS Lambda function to run the RefreshCache command for Storage Gateway.","B":"Instruct the third party to put data into the S3 bucket using AWS Transfer for SFTP.","C":"Modify Storage Gateway to run in volume gateway mode.","D":"Use S3 Same-Region Replication to replicate any changes made directly in the S3 bucket to Storage Gateway."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个每晚触发的 Amazon EventBridge 事件，以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来运行 Storage Gateway 的刷新缓存命令。","B":"指示第三方使用 AWS Transfer for SFTP 将数据放入 S3 存储桶。","C":"将存储网关修改为卷网关模式运行。","D":"使用 S3 同区域复制功能，将直接在 S3 存储桶中所做的任何更改复制到存储网关。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An S3 File Gateway (file gateway mode) maintains a cached inventory of the objects in its backing S3 bucket so it can serve NFS/SMB clients with low latency. When a third party writes objects directly into the S3 bucket (outside the file-share workflow between the gateway and S3), the gateway's cached inventory is not automatically aware of them, so users do not see the new files even though they exist in S3. The RefreshCache API finds objects that were added, removed, or replaced in the bucket since the gateway last listed it and updates the cached inventory accordingly. AWS documentation explicitly describes configuring an automated cache refresh schedule by having a scheduled Amazon EventBridge/CloudWatch rule invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls RefreshCache, which is exactly the recommended pattern when bucket contents are updated directly outside the gateway. A nightly EventBridge-scheduled Lambda running RefreshCache therefore ensures the third party's evening uploads are reflected in the gateway by morning.","explanation_zh":"S3 File Gateway (file gateway mode) 會為其後端 S3 bucket 維護一份物件的快取清單 (cached inventory)，以低延遲地為 NFS/SMB 用戶端提供服務。當第三方直接將物件寫入 S3 bucket (繞過 gateway 與 S3 之間的 file-share 工作流程) 時，gateway 的快取清單不會自動得知這些物件，因此即使檔案已存在於 S3，使用者仍看不到。RefreshCache API 會找出自 gateway 上次列出 bucket 以來新增、移除或替換的物件，並據此更新快取清單。AWS 官方文件明確說明可透過排程的 Amazon EventBridge/CloudWatch rule 來觸發 AWS Lambda function 呼叫 RefreshCache，以設定自動快取重新整理排程，這正是當 bucket 內容在 gateway 之外被直接更新時的建議做法。因此，使用 EventBridge 每晚排程觸發執行 RefreshCache 的 Lambda，即可確保第三方傍晚上傳的檔案在隔天早上能在 gateway 中呈現。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Switching the third party to AWS Transfer for SFTP still results in objects being written directly into the S3 bucket, bypassing the gateway's NFS/SMB workflow. The gateway's cached inventory would remain stale, so the new files would still not appear to gateway users. It changes the upload mechanism but does not refresh the cache.","why_zh":"改用 AWS Transfer for SFTP 仍然是將物件直接寫入 S3 bucket，繞過 gateway 的 NFS/SMB 工作流程。gateway 的快取清單仍會過時，新檔案對 gateway 使用者依然不會出現。它只改變上傳機制，並未重新整理快取。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Volume Gateway presents iSCSI block storage backed by S3 (stored/cached volumes), not a file interface that maps S3 bucket objects to readable files. It is a different gateway type with a different data model, would break the existing file-based access pattern, and still would not surface objects written directly into the S3 bucket as files.","why_zh":"Volume Gateway 提供的是由 S3 支援的 iSCSI 區塊儲存 (stored/cached volumes)，而非將 S3 bucket 物件對應為可讀檔案的檔案介面。它是不同的 gateway 類型、採用不同的資料模型，會破壞既有的以檔案為基礎的存取方式，也無法把直接寫入 S3 bucket 的物件以檔案形式呈現。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Same-Region Replication replicates objects between two S3 buckets; a File Gateway is not an S3 replication destination. You cannot 'replicate changes into Storage Gateway' via SRR, and it would not refresh the gateway's cached inventory, so the files would remain invisible to gateway users. This is not a valid mechanism for the problem.","why_zh":"S3 Same-Region Replication 是在兩個 S3 bucket 之間複製物件；File Gateway 並非 S3 複寫目的地。無法透過 SRR 將變更「複寫到 Storage Gateway」，它也不會重新整理 gateway 的快取清單，因此檔案仍對 gateway 使用者不可見。這並不是解決此問題的有效機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/refresh-cache.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/APIReference/API_RefreshCache.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":36,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to back up sensitive Amazon S3 objects that are stored within an S3 bucket with a private bucket policy using S3 cross-Region replication functionality. The objects need to be copied to a target bucket in a different AWS Region and account. Which combination of actions should be performed to enable this replication? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要使用 S3 跨区域复制功能，将存储在具有私有存储桶策略的 S3 存储桶中的敏感对 象进行备份。这些对象需要复制到不同 AWS 区域和账户中的目标存储桶。 应执行哪些操作组合才能启用此复制？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a replication IAM role in the source account","B":"Create a replication IAM role in the target account.","C":"Add statements to the source bucket policy allowing the replication IAM role to replicate objects.","D":"Add statements to the target bucket policy allowing the replication IAM role to replicate objects.","E":"Create a replication rule in the source bucket to enable the replication.","F":"Create a replication rule in the target bucket to enable the replication."},"options_zh":{"A":"在源账户中创建一个复制 IAM 角色","B":"在目标账户中创建一个用于复制的 IAM 角色。","C":"向源存储桶策略添加语句，允许复制 IAM 角色复制对象。","D":"向目标存储桶策略添加语句，允许复制 IAM 角色复制对象。","E":"在源存储桶中创建一个复制规则以启用复制功能。","F":"在目标存储桶中创建一个复制规则以启用复制。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For S3 cross-Region, cross-account replication, AWS docs prescribe exactly three actions. (A) The IAM role that Amazon S3 assumes to read and replicate objects is created in the SOURCE account and referenced in the source bucket's replication configuration; the cross-account walkthrough explicitly uses the source-account profile (acctA) to create this role. (E) Replication rules are always added to the SOURCE bucket ('When you configure replication, you add replication rules to the source bucket') to define what gets replicated and the destination. (D) Because the destination bucket is owned by a different account, the destination/target bucket owner must add a bucket policy on the TARGET bucket granting the source account's replication IAM role permission to perform s3:ReplicateObject and s3:ReplicateDelete (plus s3:GetBucketVersioning / s3:PutBucketVersioning). The 'private bucket policy' on the source is a red herring: the source bucket needs no replication-specific bucket-policy statements because the IAM role itself carries the read/list permissions.","explanation_zh":"對於 S3 跨區域且跨帳戶的 replication，AWS 文件明確規定三個動作。(A) Amazon S3 用來讀取並複寫物件而擔任 (assume) 的 IAM role 建立於「來源 (source) 帳戶」，並在來源 bucket 的 replication configuration 中被引用；跨帳戶逐步教學明確使用來源帳戶設定檔 (acctA) 來建立此 role。(E) Replication rule 一律加在「來源 bucket」上（「When you configure replication, you add replication rules to the source bucket」），用以定義要複寫哪些物件及目的地。(D) 由於目的 bucket 屬於不同帳戶，目的/目標 bucket 擁有者必須在「目標 (target) bucket」上加入 bucket policy，授予來源帳戶的 replication IAM role 執行 s3:ReplicateObject 與 s3:ReplicateDelete（以及 s3:GetBucketVersioning / s3:PutBucketVersioning）的權限。題目中對來源「private bucket policy」的描述是干擾項：來源 bucket 不需要任何 replication 專屬的 bucket policy 陳述句，因為 IAM role 本身已帶有讀取/列出權限。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The replication IAM role must be created in the SOURCE account (Amazon S3 in the source account assumes it to read source objects and write replicas), not in the target account. The cross-account walkthrough uses the acctA (source) profile to create the role.","why_zh":"Replication IAM role 必須建立在「來源帳戶」（來源帳戶的 Amazon S3 擔任此 role 以讀取來源物件並寫入複本），而非目標帳戶。跨帳戶教學使用 acctA（來源）設定檔來建立 role。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"No replication-specific statements are needed on the SOURCE bucket policy. Amazon S3's read/list/replicate permissions come from the IAM role's permissions policy, not from a source bucket policy. The cross-account grant is required only on the destination bucket.","why_zh":"「來源」bucket policy 不需要任何 replication 專屬陳述句。Amazon S3 的讀取/列出/複寫權限來自 IAM role 的權限政策，而非來源 bucket policy。跨帳戶授權僅需加在目的 bucket 上。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Replication rules are configured on the SOURCE bucket only, never on the target/destination bucket. The destination bucket only needs a bucket policy granting cross-account access, not a replication rule.","why_zh":"Replication rule 只設定在「來源」bucket，絕不設在目標/目的 bucket。目的 bucket 只需要一個授予跨帳戶存取的 bucket policy，而非 replication rule。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-walkthrough-2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/setting-repl-config-perm-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-walkthrough1.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":37,"question_en":"A company has multiple member accounts that are part of an organization in AWS Organizations. The security team needs to review every Amazon EC2 security group and their inbound and outbound rules. The security team wants to programmatically retrieve this information from the member accounts using an AWS Lambda function in the management account of the organization. Which combination of access changes will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中拥有多个成员账户，这些账户属于同一个组织。安全团队需要审查每个 Amazon EC2 安全组及其入站和出站规则。安全团队希望使用组织管理账户中的 AWS Lambda 函数从成员 账户中以编程方式检索此信息。 哪些访问更改的组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a trust relationship that allows users in the member accounts to assume the management account IAM role.","B":"Create a trust relationship that allows users in the management account to assume the IAM roles of the member accounts.","C":"Create an IAM role in each member account that has access to the AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess managed policy.","D":"Create an IAM role in each member account to allow the sts:AssumeRole action against the management account IAM role's ARN.","E":"Create an IAM role in the management account that allows the sts:AssumeRole action against the member account IAM role's ARN.","F":"Create an IAM role in the management account that has access to the AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess managed policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一种信任关系，使成员账户中的用户能够承担管理账户的 IAM 角色。","B":"建立一种信任关系，使管理账户中的用户能够承担目标账户中的 IAM 角色。 会员账户。","C":"在每个成员账户中创建一个具有访问 AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess 管理策略权限的 IAM 角色。","D":"在每个成员账户中创建一个 IAM 角色，以允许针对管理账户 IAM 角色的 ARN 执行 sts: AssumeRole 操作。","E":"在管理账户中创建一个 IAM 角色，该角色允许对成员账户 IAM 角色的 ARN 执行 sts: AssumeRole 操作。","F":"在管理账户中创建一个具有访问 AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess 管理策略权限的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"This is the canonical cross-account IAM role delegation pattern described in the AWS 'Originating / Destination' tutorial. The EC2 security groups live in the member accounts, so each member account is the Destination (trusting/resource) account and the management account that runs the Lambda function is the Originating (trusted/calling) account. Three changes are required. (C) In each member account, create an IAM role and attach AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess, because the DescribeSecurityGroups permissions must reside where the EC2 resources actually are. (B) That member-account role needs a trust policy that names the management account as a trusted entity, so management-account principals are allowed to assume it. (E) In the management account, create the Lambda execution role with an identity-based policy granting sts:AssumeRole on the member-account role ARNs; AssumeRole succeeds only when BOTH the target role's trust policy permits the caller AND the calling principal has an sts:AssumeRole permission. The AWS delegation tutorial shows exactly this split: the Destination account creates the role with a permissions policy plus a trust policy naming the Originating account, and the Originating-account principal gets an inline Allow of sts:AssumeRole on the Destination role ARN.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS 官方「Originating / Destination」教學所描述的標準跨帳戶 IAM role 委派模式。EC2 security groups 位於 member accounts，因此每個 member account 是 Destination（受信任、擁有資源/trusting）帳戶，而執行 Lambda function 的 management account 是 Originating（被信任的呼叫端/trusted）帳戶。需要三項變更。(C) 在每個 member account 建立 IAM role 並附加 AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess，因為 DescribeSecurityGroups 權限必須位於 EC2 資源實際所在的帳戶。(B) 該 member-account role 需要 trust policy，將 management account 指定為受信任實體，才能允許 management account 的 principal 去 assume 它。(E) 在 management account 建立 Lambda execution role，並以 identity-based policy 授予對 member-account role ARN 的 sts:AssumeRole 權限；AssumeRole 必須同時滿足目標 role 的 trust policy 允許呼叫者，以及呼叫端 principal 擁有 sts:AssumeRole 權限，兩者缺一不可。AWS 委派教學正是這樣分工：Destination 帳戶建立帶有 permissions policy 與指定 Originating 帳戶之 trust policy 的 role，而 Originating 帳戶的 principal 取得對 Destination role ARN 的 Allow sts:AssumeRole。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Direction is reversed. This would let member-account users assume a role in the management account, but the Lambda runs IN the management account and must reach INTO the member accounts. The trust relationship must let the management account assume the member-account role, not the other way around.","why_zh":"方向相反。此選項讓 member-account 使用者去 assume management account 的 role，但 Lambda 是在 management account 執行，必須反向進入 member accounts。trust relationship 應允許 management account assume member-account 的 role，而非相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Backwards and redundant. The sts:AssumeRole identity-based permission belongs on the calling principal in the management (Originating) account, targeting the member-account role ARN. The member account is the resource side and does not need permission to call AssumeRole against the management account.","why_zh":"方向錯誤且多餘。sts:AssumeRole 的 identity-based 權限應放在 management（Originating）帳戶的呼叫 principal 上，並以 member-account role ARN 為目標。member account 是資源端，不需要取得對 management account 呼叫 AssumeRole 的權限。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"An EC2 read-only role in the management account only grants visibility into the management account's own EC2 resources. It cannot read security groups in the member accounts, which is the actual requirement. The read permissions must live in each member account (option C).","why_zh":"在 management account 建立 EC2 唯讀 role 只能看見 management account 自身的 EC2 資源，無法讀取 member accounts 的 security groups，而後者才是真正需求。讀取權限必須位於各 member account（即選項 C）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies-cross-account-resource-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_update-role-trust-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-intro-execution-role.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":38,"question_en":"A space exploration company receives telemetry data from multiple satellites. Small packets of data are received through Amazon API Gateway and are placed directly into an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue. A custom application is subscribed to the queue and transforms the data into a standard format. Because of inconsistencies in the data that the satellites produce, the application is occasionally unable to transform the data. In these cases, the messages remain in the SQS queue. A DevOps engineer must develop a solution that retains the failed messages and makes them available to scientists for review and future processing. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家太空探索公司从多颗卫星接收遥测数据。通过亚马逊 API 网关接收到的小数据包直接放入亚马逊 简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）标准队列中。一个自定义应用程序订阅该队列，并将数据转换为标准格 式。 由于卫星生成的数据存在不一致的情况，应用程序有时无法转换这些数据。在这种情况下，消息会留 在 SQS 队列中。DevOps 工程师必须开发一个解决方案，将失败的消息保留下来，并提供给科学家进行 审查和未来的处理。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Lambda to poll the SQS queue and invoke a Lambda function to check whether the queue messages are valid. If validation fails, send a copy of the data that is not valid to an Amazon S3 bucket so that the scientists can review and correct the data. When the data is corrected, amend the message in the SQS queue by using a replay Lambda function with the corrected data.","B":"Convert the SQS standard queue to an SQS FIFO queue. Configure AWS Lambda to poll the SQS queue every 10 minutes by using an Amazon EventBridge schedule. Invoke the Lambda function to identify any messages with a SentTimestamp value that is older than 5 minutes, push the data to the same location as the application's output location, and remove the messages from the queue.","C":"Create an SQS dead-letter queue. Modify the existing queue by including a redrive policy that sets the Maximum Receives setting to 1 and sets the dead-letter queue ARN to the ARN of the newly created queue. Instruct the scientists to use the dead-letter queue to review the data that is not valid. Reprocess this data at a later time.","D":"Configure API Gateway to send messages to different SQS virtual queues that are named for each of the satellites. Update the application to use a new virtual queue for any data that it cannot transform, and send the message to the new virtual queue. Instruct the scientists to use the virtual queue to review the data that is not valid. Reprocess this data at a later time."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Lambda 以轮询 SQS 队列，并调用一个 Lambda 函数来检查队列消息是否有效。如果验证 失败，将无效的数据副本发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶，以便科学家进行审查和更正。当数据更正后， 使用带有更正数据的重放 Lambda 函数修改 SQS 队列中的消息。","B":"将 SQS 标准队列转换为 SQS FIFO 队列。使用 Amazon EventBridge 计划配置 AWS Lambda 每 10 分钟轮询一次 SQS 队列。调用 Lambda 函数以识别任何 SentTimestamp 值超过 5 分钟的消息，将 数据推送到与应用程序输出位置相同的位置，并从队列中删除这些消息。","C":"创建一个 SQS 死信队列。修改现有队列，添加重定向策略，将“最大接收次数”设置为 1，并将死 信队列的 ARN 设置为新创建队列的 ARN。指示科学家使用死信队列来审查无效的数据。稍后重 新处理这些数据。","D":"配置 API 网关，使其将消息发送到以每颗卫星命名的不同 SQS 虚拟队列。更新应用程序，使其对 于无法转换的任何数据使用新的虚拟队列，并将消息发送到该新虚拟队列。指示科学家使用该虚 拟队列来审查无效的数据。稍后重新处理这些数据。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SQS dead-letter queues (DLQs) are the AWS-native, purpose-built feature for retaining messages a consumer cannot process so they can be isolated for later review and reprocessing. You first create a new queue, then add a redrive policy to the source queue that names the DLQ ARN and sets maxReceiveCount (the console's 'Maximum Receives'). When the custom transform repeatedly fails on malformed telemetry, the message is received but never deleted; once the receive count exceeds maxReceiveCount, SQS automatically moves it to the DLQ, where scientists can inspect the bad data and later redrive it. The AWS docs explicitly state that setting maxReceiveCount to a low value such as 1 moves a message to the DLQ after a single failed attempt, and that DLQs exist precisely to isolate unconsumed messages for diagnosis and redrive. This is configuration-only with no custom code. The other options either invent a non-existent ability to edit an SQS message in place (A), are technically impossible/incorrect (B: you cannot convert a standard queue to FIFO in place, and selecting by SentTimestamp would also discard valid messages), or misuse the client-side Temporary Queue Client 'virtual queues' that API Gateway cannot natively target (D).","explanation_zh":"Amazon SQS dead-letter queue (DLQ) 是 AWS 原生、專門用來保留消費者無法處理之訊息的功能，將其隔離以供日後檢視與重新處理。做法是先建立一個新佇列，再於來源佇列加上 redrive policy，指定該 DLQ 的 ARN 並設定 maxReceiveCount（主控台中的 'Maximum Receives'）。當自訂轉換程式對格式錯誤的遙測資料反覆失敗時，訊息會被接收但不會被刪除；一旦接收次數超過 maxReceiveCount，SQS 會自動將其移至 DLQ，科學家可在此檢視壞資料並日後 redrive 重新處理。AWS 文件明確指出將 maxReceiveCount 設為像 1 這樣的低值，會在單次失敗後即把訊息移到 DLQ，且 DLQ 的存在正是為了隔離未消費訊息以利診斷與 redrive。此方案僅需設定、無需自訂程式碼。其他選項不是杜撰了原地編輯 SQS 訊息的能力（A），就是技術上不可行/錯誤（B：無法原地將 standard queue 轉成 FIFO，且以 SentTimestamp 篩選會連有效訊息一併丟棄），或誤用了 API Gateway 無法原生指向的用戶端 Temporary Queue Client『virtual queues』（D）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This rebuilds DLQ behavior with a custom Lambda poller, an S3 bucket, and a replay Lambda — far more code and operational overhead than the native DLQ feature. It is also technically muddled: SQS messages are immutable, so you cannot 'amend the message in the SQS queue' in place, and polling SQS with a Lambda to validate reinvents what an event source mapping plus a DLQ already do natively.","why_zh":"此方案用自訂 Lambda 輪詢器、S3 儲存桶與 replay Lambda 重新打造 DLQ 行為，程式碼與營運負擔遠高於原生 DLQ。技術上也含糊：SQS 訊息不可變，無法就地『修改 SQS 佇列中的訊息』，而用 Lambda 輪詢 SQS 驗證等於重新發明事件來源映射加 DLQ 已原生提供的功能。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"You cannot convert an existing standard queue into a FIFO queue in place; FIFO requires creating a new queue. Worse, it selects messages purely by SentTimestamp age rather than by transform failure, so it would move every message older than 5 minutes — including valid, still-processable ones — to the output location. It does not distinguish failed messages at all.","why_zh":"無法原地將現有 standard queue 轉成 FIFO queue；FIFO 需新建佇列。更糟的是它僅以 SentTimestamp 的時間篩選訊息，而非依轉換失敗，會把所有超過 5 分鐘的訊息（含仍可處理的有效訊息）都移到輸出位置，完全無法辨別失敗訊息。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SQS 'virtual queues' are a client-side construct of the awslabs Amazon SQS Temporary Queue Client (a Java library for request-response messaging over a single host queue), not a server-side feature that API Gateway can route to, and not a mechanism for capturing transform failures. It misuses an unrelated library feature and provides none of the durable, native failed-message retention/redrive a DLQ does.","why_zh":"SQS『virtual queues』是 awslabs Amazon SQS Temporary Queue Client（用於在單一主機佇列上做請求-回應的 Java 函式庫）的用戶端構造，並非 API Gateway 可路由的伺服器端功能，也不是捕捉轉換失敗的機制。此方案誤用了不相關的函式庫功能，無法提供 DLQ 那種持久、原生的失敗訊息保留/redrive。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-dead-letter-queues.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-configure-dead-letter-queue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-temporary-queues.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":39,"question_en":"A company wants to use AWS CloudFormation for infrastructure deployment. The company has strict tagging and resource requirements and wants to limit the deployment to two Regions. Developers will need to deploy multiple versions of the same application. Which solution ensures resources are deployed in accordance with company policy?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用 AWS CloudFormation 进行基础设施部署。该公司有严格的标签和资源要求，并希望 将部署限制在两个区域。开发人员需要部署同一应用程序的多个版本。 哪种解决方案能确保资源的部署符合公司政策？","options_en":{"A":"Create AWS Trusted Advisor checks to find and remediate unapproved CloudFormation StackSets.","B":"Create a CloudFormation drift detection operation to find and remediate unapproved CloudFormation StackSets.","C":"Create CloudFormation StackSets with approved CloudFormation templates.","D":"Create AWS Service Catalog products with approved CloudFormation templates."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 AWS Trusted Advisor 检查，以查找并修复未经批准的 CloudFormation StackSets。","B":"创建一个 CloudFormation 漂移检测操作，以查找并修复未经批准的 CloudFormation 资源。 堆栈集","C":"使用经批准的 CloudFormation 模板创建 CloudFormation 栈集。","D":"使用经批准的 CloudFormation 模板创建 AWS 服务目录产品。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Service Catalog is purpose-built for this scenario. Administrators create products by importing approved CloudFormation templates ('standardized and pre-approved templates'), so only sanctioned infrastructure can be launched. Governance controls enforce company policy: TagOptions and template/launch constraints enforce strict tagging and resource requirements that propagate to provisioned resources, and a Stack Set constraint lets admins specify exactly which Regions a product deploys to ('In Region settings, choose the geographic regions to deploy products'), satisfying the 'limit to two Regions' requirement. Service Catalog also provides built-in versioning: 'Service Catalog allows you to manage multiple versions of the products in your catalog,' and each new version is automatically distributed to entitled users who choose which version to launch, satisfying 'deploy multiple versions of the same application.' This single service simultaneously meets every requirement, which the other options cannot.","explanation_zh":"AWS Service Catalog 正是為此情境設計。管理員透過匯入已核准的 CloudFormation 範本（『標準化且預先核准的範本』）來建立 product，因此只能啟動經核准的基礎設施。治理控制可強制執行公司政策：TagOptions 與 template/launch constraints 可強制套用嚴格的標記與資源需求並傳播至佈建的資源，而 Stack Set constraint 讓管理員精確指定 product 部署到哪些 Region（『在 Region settings 選擇要部署 product 的地理區域』），滿足『限制兩個 Region』的需求。Service Catalog 也內建版本管理：『Service Catalog 允許你管理目錄中 product 的多個版本』，每個新版本會自動發布給有權限的使用者，由使用者自行選擇要啟動哪個版本，滿足『部署同一應用程式的多個版本』。此單一服務同時滿足所有需求，其他選項皆無法做到。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor has no check for 'unapproved CloudFormation StackSets' and cannot remediate them. Trusted Advisor provides best-practice checks (cost optimization, security, fault tolerance, service limits, performance), not governance enforcement of CloudFormation deployments. This is a reactive, non-existent control and addresses none of tagging, resource limits, region restriction, or versioning.","why_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 並沒有針對『未核准的 CloudFormation StackSets』的檢查，也無法修復它們。Trusted Advisor 提供最佳實務檢查（成本最佳化、安全、容錯、服務配額、效能），而非對 CloudFormation 部署的治理強制。這是一個反應式且不存在的控制，無法處理標記、資源限制、Region 限制或版本管理。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFormation drift detection finds differences between a stack's actual resource configuration and its template; it does not detect or remediate 'unapproved StackSets,' and it has no automatic remediation engine. It is a reactive, detective control, not a preventive governance mechanism, and addresses none of the policy requirements (approved templates, tagging, resource limits, regions, versions).","why_zh":"CloudFormation drift detection 用於找出 stack 實際資源組態與其範本之間的差異；它無法偵測或修復『未核准的 StackSets』，也沒有自動修復引擎。它是反應式的偵測控制，而非預防性的治理機制，且無法滿足任何政策需求（已核准範本、標記、資源限制、Region、版本）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudFormation StackSets deploy a stack across multiple accounts/Regions in a single operation, but they provide no self-service product catalog, no built-in version management for developers to launch multiple application versions, and no constraint-based enforcement of tagging/resource governance (a StackSet simply deploys whatever template is supplied). It addresses the multi-region piece but fails the 'multiple versions of the same application' and 'strict tagging/resource requirements' governance needs that Service Catalog provides (Service Catalog can itself use a Stack Set constraint to reach the two Regions).","why_zh":"CloudFormation StackSets 可在單一操作中跨多個帳戶/Region 部署 stack，但它不提供自助式 product catalog、不提供讓開發者啟動多個應用程式版本的內建版本管理，也不以 constraint 強制執行標記/資源治理（StackSet 只會部署所提供的範本）。它能處理多 Region 部分，但無法滿足『同一應用程式的多個版本』與『嚴格標記/資源需求』的治理需求，而 Service Catalog 能提供這些（Service Catalog 本身可使用 Stack Set constraint 部署到那兩個 Region）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/what-is_concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/constraints-stackset.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/managing-versions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/constraints-launch.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":40,"question_en":"A company requires that its internally facing web application be highly available. The architecture is made up of one Amazon EC2 web server instance and one NAT instance that provides outbound internet access for updates and accessing public data. Which combination of architecture adjustments should the company implement to achieve high availability? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司要求其内部使用的网络应用程序具有高可用性。其架构由一台亚马逊 EC2 网络服务器实例和 一台提供互联网出站访问以进行更新和访问公共数据的 NAT 实例组成。 公司应实施哪两种架构调整组合来实现高可用性？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add the NAT instance to an EC2 Auto Scaling group that spans multiple Availability Zones. Update the route tables.","B":"Create additional EC2 instances spanning multiple Availability Zones. Add an Application Load Balancer to split the load between them.","C":"Configure an Application Load Balancer in front of the EC2 instance. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to recover the EC2 instance upon host failure.","D":"Replace the NAT instance with a NAT gateway in each Availability Zone. Update the route tables.","E":"Replace the NAT instance with a NAT gateway that spans multiple Availability Zones. Update the route tables."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 NAT 实例添加到跨越多个可用区的 EC2 自动扩展组中。更新路由表。","B":"创建跨越多个可用区的额外 EC2 实例。添加一个应用负载均衡器在它们之间分配负载。","C":"在 EC2 实例前配置应用负载均衡器。配置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，在主机出现故障时恢复 EC2 实例。","D":"在每个可用区中用 NAT 网关替换 NAT 实例。更新路由表。","E":"用一个跨越多个可用区的 NAT 网关替换 NAT 实例。更新路由表。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The architecture has two single points of failure: one EC2 web server and one NAT instance. To make the web tier highly available, option B adds multiple EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones behind an Application Load Balancer, so traffic is distributed and the application survives an instance or AZ failure. To make outbound internet access highly available, option D replaces the single NAT instance with a NAT gateway in each Availability Zone and updates the route tables so each AZ's resources egress through their local NAT gateway. AWS documentation states 'Each NAT gateway is created in a specific Availability Zone and implemented with redundancy in that zone' and explicitly recommends 'create a NAT gateway in each Availability Zone' for a zone-independent, highly available design; it also recommends replacing a NAT instance with a NAT gateway. A single NAT gateway is zonal and does not span multiple AZs, so option E is technically inaccurate, and option C leaves a single EC2 instance (CloudWatch recover only restarts it in the same AZ), which is not multi-AZ HA.","explanation_zh":"此架構有兩個單點故障：一個 EC2 web 伺服器和一個 NAT instance。要讓 web 層高可用，選項 B 在多個 Availability Zone 部署多個 EC2 instance 並置於 Application Load Balancer 之後，可分散流量並在 instance 或 AZ 故障時繼續運作。要讓對外網路存取高可用，選項 D 以每個 Availability Zone 各一個 NAT gateway 取代單一 NAT instance，並更新 route table 讓各 AZ 的資源透過該 AZ 本地的 NAT gateway 出網。AWS 文件指出『每個 NAT gateway 建立在特定 Availability Zone 且在該 zone 內實作備援』，並明確建議『在每個 Availability Zone 建立一個 NAT gateway』以達成 zone-independent 的高可用設計，同時建議以 NAT gateway 取代 NAT instance。單一 NAT gateway 屬 zonal 不會跨多個 AZ，因此選項 E 在技術上不正確；選項 C 仍只有一個 EC2 instance（CloudWatch recover 僅在相同 AZ 重啟），並非跨多 AZ 的高可用。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS explicitly recommends replacing NAT instances with NAT gateways because gateways provide better availability with no administrative effort. Running a NAT instance in an Auto Scaling group across AZs does not automatically update VPC route tables on failover (it requires custom scripting/Lambda), so it is high-overhead and not the AWS-recommended HA pattern.","why_zh":"AWS 明確建議以 NAT gateway 取代 NAT instance，因為 gateway 提供更佳可用性且無需維運。將 NAT instance 放進跨 AZ 的 Auto Scaling group 在故障切換時無法自動更新 VPC route table（需自訂腳本/Lambda），屬高維運負擔且非 AWS 建議的 HA 模式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Putting an ALB in front of a single EC2 instance and using a CloudWatch recover alarm still leaves one instance as a single point of failure. Instance recovery (StatusCheckFailed_System) restarts the instance in the same Availability Zone on new hardware and does not provide multi-AZ high availability.","why_zh":"在單一 EC2 instance 前放 ALB 並用 CloudWatch recover 警報，仍只有一個 instance 為單點故障。Instance recovery（StatusCheckFailed_System）在相同 Availability Zone 以新硬體重啟 instance，並非跨多 AZ 的高可用。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A NAT gateway is created in a single specified Availability Zone and is implemented with redundancy only within that zone; it does not span multiple AZs. AWS guidance is to create one NAT gateway per AZ, so this option misdescribes how NAT gateways work.","why_zh":"NAT gateway 建立於單一指定的 Availability Zone，且僅在該 zone 內具備備援，並不會跨多個 AZ。AWS 的指引是每個 AZ 建立一個 NAT gateway，因此此選項錯誤描述了 NAT gateway 的運作方式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nat-gateway-basics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat-comparison.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/cloudwatch-recovery.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":41,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building a multistage pipeline with AWS CodePipeline to build, verify, stage, test, and deploy an application. A manual approval stage is required between the test stage and the deploy stage. The development team uses a custom chat tool with webhook support that requires near-real-time notifications. How should the DevOps engineer configure status updates for pipeline activity and approval requests to post to the chat tool?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 构建一个多阶段流水线，用于构建、验证、暂存、 测试和部署应用程序。在测试阶段和部署阶段之间需要一个手动审批阶段。开发团队使用一个具有 Webhook 支持的自定义聊天工具，该工具需要近乎实时的通知。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置管道活动和审批请求的状态更新，以便将其发布到聊天工具？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs subscription that filters on CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change. Publish subscription events to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the chat webhook URL to the SNS topic, and complete the subscription validation.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by AWS CloudTrail events. When a CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change event is detected, send the event details to the chat webhook URL.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that filters on CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change. Publish the events to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Create an AWS Lambda function that sends event details to the chat webhook URL. Subscribe the function to the SNS topic.","D":"Modify the pipeline code to send the event details to the chat webhook URL at the end of each stage. Parameterize the URL so that each pipeline can send to a different URL based on the pipeline environment."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 订阅，筛选条件为 CodePipeline 管道执行状态更改。将订阅事 件发布到 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题。将聊天网络钩子 URL 订阅 到 SNS 主题，并完成订阅验证。","B":"创建一个由 AWS CloudTrail 事件触发的 AWS Lambda 函数。当检测到 CodePipeline 管道执行状 态更改事件时，将事件详情发送至聊天网络钩子 URL。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，筛选 CodePipeline 管道执行状态更改事件。将事件发布到 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将事件详情发送到 聊天网络钩子 URL。将该函数订阅到 SNS 主题。","D":"修改管道代码，在每个阶段结束时将事件详情发送到聊天网络钩子 URL。对 URL 进行参数化， 以便每个管道都能根据管道环境发送到不同的 URL。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodePipeline sends 'CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change' events directly to Amazon EventBridge (source: aws.codepipeline) as a near-real-time stream, so an EventBridge rule is the correct, native trigger. EventBridge routes those events to targets such as Amazon SNS and AWS Lambda. Because a custom chat webhook cannot be a direct SNS subscriber (an HTTP/HTTPS subscription must answer the SNS SubscriptionConfirmation handshake, and SNS would deliver its own envelope rather than the JSON the chat tool expects), an AWS Lambda function subscribed to the SNS topic transforms the event into the webhook's expected payload and POSTs it over HTTPS. This decoupled EventBridge -> SNS -> Lambda -> webhook pattern handles both general pipeline activity and approval requests with low operational overhead and near-real-time delivery, which is exactly option C.","explanation_zh":"CodePipeline 會將「CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change」事件以近即時方式直接傳送到 Amazon EventBridge（source 為 aws.codepipeline），因此以 EventBridge rule 作為觸發來源才是原生且正確的做法。EventBridge 可將事件路由到 Amazon SNS、AWS Lambda 等目標。由於自訂聊天工具的 webhook 無法直接成為 SNS 訂閱者（HTTP/HTTPS 訂閱必須回應 SNS 的 SubscriptionConfirmation 確認握手，且 SNS 會送出自己的訊息封裝格式，而非聊天工具預期的 JSON），因此需要一個訂閱該 SNS topic 的 AWS Lambda 函式，將事件轉換為 webhook 預期的格式並透過 HTTPS POST 出去。此解耦的 EventBridge -> SNS -> Lambda -> webhook 模式能以低營運負擔、近即時方式同時處理一般管線活動與核准請求，正是選項 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no CloudWatch Logs subscription that filters on 'CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change'; that is an EventBridge service detail-type. CloudWatch Logs subscription filters operate on log events in a log group, not on CodePipeline state-change events. Also, subscribing the raw chat webhook URL directly to SNS fails because the webhook will not complete the SNS HTTP/HTTPS subscription-confirmation handshake and would receive the SNS envelope, not the chat tool's expected format.","why_zh":"並不存在可針對「CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change」過濾的 CloudWatch Logs 訂閱；那是 EventBridge 的服務 detail-type。CloudWatch Logs 訂閱篩選器作用於 log group 中的日誌事件，而非 CodePipeline 的狀態變更事件。此外，將聊天 webhook URL 直接訂閱到 SNS 會失敗，因為 webhook 無法完成 SNS 的 HTTP/HTTPS 訂閱確認握手，且只會收到 SNS 封裝格式而非聊天工具預期的格式。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The 'Pipeline Execution State Change' detail-type is emitted directly by CodePipeline to EventBridge; CloudTrail carries API-call events and its delivery is best-effort and not near-real-time. Lambda is also not directly invoked by CloudTrail. This uses the wrong, slower detection mechanism for a near-real-time requirement.","why_zh":"「Pipeline Execution State Change」detail-type 是由 CodePipeline 直接送到 EventBridge；CloudTrail 承載的是 API 呼叫事件，其傳遞屬於 best-effort 且非近即時。Lambda 也無法由 CloudTrail 直接調用。對於近即時需求而言，此做法採用了錯誤且較慢的偵測機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Embedding notification code in the pipeline to POST at the end of each stage is high operational overhead and brittle; it couples notification logic to every pipeline definition and does not cleanly capture the manual-approval-request notification, which is a CodePipeline-managed approval event (delivered via SNS) rather than something custom stage-end code emits. AWS favors decoupled, event-driven notifications over hardcoded webhook calls.","why_zh":"在管線中內嵌通知程式碼，於每個階段結束時 POST，營運負擔高且脆弱；它將通知邏輯耦合到每個管線定義，也無法乾淨地捕捉手動核准請求通知，因為核准事件是由 CodePipeline 託管（透過 SNS 傳遞），並非自訂的階段結束程式碼所發出。AWS 偏好解耦、事件驅動的通知，而非硬編碼 webhook 呼叫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/detect-state-changes-cloudwatch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codepipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/SendMessageToHttp.confirm.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/http-subscription-confirmation-json.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":42,"question_en":"A company's application development team uses Linux-based Amazon EC2 instances as bastion hosts. Inbound SSH access to the bastion hosts is restricted to specific IP addresses, as defined in the associated security groups. The company's security team wants to receive a notification if the security group rules are modified to allow SSH access from any IP address. What should a DevOps engineer do to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"该公司的应用程序开发团队使用基于 Linux 的 Amazon EC2 实例作为堡垒主机。堡垒主机的入站 SSH 访问仅限于特定的 IP 地址，这些地址在关联的安全组中定义。该公司的安全团队希望在安全组规则被 修改为允许从任何 IP 地址进行 SSH 访问时收到通知。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with a source of aws.cloudtrail and the event name AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress. Define an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the target.","B":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty and check the findings for security groups in AWS Security Hub. Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule with a custom pattern that matches GuardDuty events with an output of NON_COMPLIANT. Define an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the target.","C":"Create an AWS Config rule by using the restricted-ssh managed rule to check whether security groups disallow unrestricted incoming SSH traffic. Configure automatic remediation to publish a message to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","D":"Enable Amazon Inspector. Include the Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures-1.1 rules package to check the security groups that are associated with the bastion hosts. Configure Amazon Inspector to publish a message to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，其来源为 aws.cloudtrail，事件名称为 AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngre ss。将 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题定义为目标。","B":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 并在 AWS Security Hub 中检查安全组的发现结果。配置一个带有自定义模式 的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该模式匹配输出为“不符合”的 GuardDuty 事件。将 Amazon 简单通 知服务（Amazon SNS）主题定义为目标。","C":"使用受限 SSH 管理规则创建一个 AWS Config 规则，以检查安全组是否禁止不受限制的入站 SSH 流量。 配置自动修复功能，将消息发布到 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。","D":"启用 Amazon Inspector。包含通用漏洞和暴露 - 1.1 规则包以检查与堡垒主机关联的安全组。配置 Amazon Inspector 向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发布消息。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to be notified when a security group rule is changed to allow SSH (port 22) from any IP address (0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0). AWS Config provides the managed rule restricted-ssh (rule identifier INCOMING_SSH_DISABLED), which is COMPLIANT only when the incoming SSH CIDR is restricted (other than 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0) and NON_COMPLIANT otherwise; its trigger type is Configuration changes and Periodic, so it re-evaluates whenever the security group is modified. AWS Config auto-remediation runs an SSM Automation document, and the AWS-managed runbook AWS-PublishSNSNotification publishes a message to an SNS topic, so configuring automatic remediation to publish to SNS is a fully supported, standard pattern that delivers the notification. Option A is the closest alternative but is too coarse as written: an EventBridge pattern of just eventName AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress matches every ingress-rule addition regardless of port or CIDR (and the source for a CloudTrail-recorded EC2 API call is aws.ec2, not aws.cloudtrail), so it would over-notify and would not specifically detect SSH-from-any-IP. Therefore C is the genuinely correct answer.","explanation_zh":"需求是當 security group 規則被修改為允許從任何 IP (0.0.0.0/0 或 ::/0) 進行 SSH (port 22) 存取時收到通知。AWS Config 提供受管規則 restricted-ssh (規則識別碼 INCOMING_SSH_DISABLED),只有當入站 SSH 的 CIDR 受限制 (非 0.0.0.0/0 或 ::/0) 時才為 COMPLIANT,否則為 NON_COMPLIANT;其觸發類型為 Configuration changes 與 Periodic,因此只要 security group 被修改就會重新評估。AWS Config 的 auto-remediation 會執行 SSM Automation document,而 AWS 受管 runbook AWS-PublishSNSNotification 會將訊息發佈到 SNS topic,因此設定自動修復以發佈到 SNS 是完全受支援的標準模式,可送達通知。選項 A 是最接近的替代方案,但寫法過於粗略:僅以 eventName AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress 的 EventBridge 模式會比對到每一次入站規則新增,不論 port 或 CIDR (而且 CloudTrail 記錄的 EC2 API 呼叫其 source 是 aws.ec2,而非 aws.cloudtrail),因此會過度通知,也無法明確偵測 SSH-from-any-IP。所以 C 才是真正正確的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An EventBridge pattern with only source aws.cloudtrail and eventName AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress matches every ingress-rule addition regardless of port or source CIDR, so it does not specifically detect SSH from any IP and would fire on unrelated changes. The source for a CloudTrail-recorded EC2 API call is also aws.ec2, not aws.cloudtrail, so the pattern as written is technically off as well.","why_zh":"僅以 source aws.cloudtrail 和 eventName AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress 的 EventBridge 模式會比對到每一次入站規則新增,不論 port 或來源 CIDR,因此無法明確偵測 SSH-from-any-IP,且會對不相關的變更觸發。此外,CloudTrail 記錄的 EC2 API 呼叫其 source 是 aws.ec2 而非 aws.cloudtrail,所以此寫法在技術上也不正確。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty detects threats from logs (VPC Flow Logs, DNS, CloudTrail) and does not evaluate security group configuration compliance; it has no finding for 'SG allows SSH from any IP'. NON_COMPLIANT is AWS Config/Security Hub control terminology, not a GuardDuty finding output, so this pipeline would never match the intended event.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是從日誌 (VPC Flow Logs、DNS、CloudTrail) 偵測威脅,並不會評估 security group 設定的合規性,也沒有針對「SG 允許從任何 IP 進行 SSH」的 finding。NON_COMPLIANT 是 AWS Config/Security Hub 控制項的用語,並非 GuardDuty 的 finding 輸出,因此此流程永遠不會比對到目標事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector assesses EC2/ECR/Lambda for software vulnerabilities (CVEs) and network reachability; it does not monitor security group rule modifications. The 'Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures' rules package is from the deprecated Inspector Classic and addresses host CVEs, not changes to SG ingress rules, so it cannot satisfy the requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是評估 EC2/ECR/Lambda 的軟體弱點 (CVE) 與網路可達性,它不會監控 security group 規則的修改。「Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures」規則套件來自已淘汰的 Inspector Classic,針對的是主機 CVE,而非 SG 入站規則的變更,因此無法滿足此需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/restricted-ssh.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-publishsnsnotification.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-create-pattern.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":43,"question_en":"A DevOps team manages an API running on-premises that serves as a backend for an Amazon API Gateway endpoint. Customers have been complaining about high response latencies, which the development team has verified using the API Gateway latency metrics in Amazon CloudWatch. To identify the cause, the team needs to collect relevant data without introducing additional latency. Which actions should be taken to accomplish this? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队管理着一个在本地运行的 API，该 API 作为 Amazon API Gateway 端点的后端。客户一 直在抱怨响应延迟过高，开发团队已通过 Amazon CloudWatch 中的 API Gateway 延迟指标进行了验证。 为了找出原因，该团队需要收集相关数据，同时又不能引入额外的延迟。 应采取哪些行动来完成此任务？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Install the CloudWatch agent server side and configure the agent to upload relevant logs to CloudWatch.","B":"Enable AWS X-Ray tracing in API Gateway, modify the application to capture request segments, and upload those segments to X-Ray during each request.","C":"Enable AWS X-Ray tracing in API Gateway, modify the application to capture request segments, and use the X-Ray daemon to upload segments to X-Ray.","D":"Modify the on-premises application to send log information back to API Gateway with each request.","E":"Modify the on-premises application to calculate and upload statistical data relevant to the API service requests to CloudWatch metrics."},"options_zh":{"A":"在服务器端安装 CloudWatch 代理，并配置代理将相关日志上传到 CloudWatch。","B":"在 API 网关中启用 AWS X-Ray 跟踪，修改应用程序以捕获请求段，并在每次请求期间将这些段上 传到 X-Ray。","C":"在 API 网关中启用 AWS X-Ray 跟踪，修改应用程序以捕获请求段，并使用 X-Ray 守护进程将段上 传到 X-Ray。","D":"修改本地应用程序，使其在每次请求时都将日志信息发送回 API 网关。","E":"修改本地应用程序，使其能够计算与 API 服务请求相关的统计信息，并将其上传到 CloudWatch 指标。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is collecting diagnostic data 'without introducing additional latency'. Option C is correct: enabling X-Ray active tracing on the API Gateway stage gives an end-to-end view of request latency including the on-premises backend (AWS docs: 'Because X-Ray gives you an end-to-end view of an entire request, you can analyze latencies in your APIs and their backend services'), and using the X-Ray daemon means the instrumented application emits segments to the local daemon over UDP port 2000 in a fire-and-forget manner. The daemon 'listens for traffic on UDP port 2000, gathers raw segment data, and relays it to the AWS X-Ray API' asynchronously and can be run on-premises, so no latency is added to the request path. Option A is also correct: the CloudWatch agent collects logs from on-premises servers and ships them to CloudWatch Logs out-of-band, providing additional server-side diagnostic data without affecting request latency. Together they let the team correlate API Gateway latency with backend behavior and pinpoint the source. Option B is the trap because uploading segments to X-Ray 'during each request' means synchronous API calls in the request path, which adds latency and is exactly what the daemon is designed to avoid.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是收集診斷資料時『不可引入額外延遲』。選項 C 正確：在 API Gateway 階段啟用 X-Ray active tracing 可獲得包含地端後端在內的端對端請求延遲視圖（AWS 文件：『Because X-Ray gives you an end-to-end view of an entire request, you can analyze latencies in your APIs and their backend services』），而使用 X-Ray daemon 表示經過 instrumentation 的應用程式透過 UDP port 2000 以 fire-and-forget 方式把 segment 送給本機 daemon。daemon 會『listens for traffic on UDP port 2000, gathers raw segment data, and relays it to the AWS X-Ray API』，以非同步方式上傳且可在地端執行，因此不會對請求路徑增加延遲。選項 A 也正確：CloudWatch agent 可從地端伺服器收集 logs 並以 out-of-band 方式送到 CloudWatch Logs，提供額外的伺服器端診斷資料而不影響請求延遲。兩者結合可讓團隊將 API Gateway 延遲與後端行為關聯起來並找出根因。選項 B 是陷阱，因為在『during each request』時上傳 segment 到 X-Ray 代表在請求路徑中執行同步 API 呼叫，會增加延遲，而這正是 daemon 被設計用來避免的問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uploading segments to X-Ray 'during each request' performs synchronous PutTraceSegments API calls inside the request path, which adds latency. The X-Ray daemon (Option C) exists precisely to decouple segment transmission via local UDP so it happens asynchronously and out-of-band, contradicting the 'without introducing additional latency' requirement.","why_zh":"在『during each request』時上傳 segment 到 X-Ray 會在請求路徑中執行同步的 PutTraceSegments API 呼叫，因而增加延遲。X-Ray daemon（選項 C）的存在正是為了透過本機 UDP 將 segment 傳輸解耦，使其以非同步、out-of-band 的方式進行，因此此選項違反『不增加額外延遲』的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Sending log information back to API Gateway with each request bloats the response payload and adds processing inside the request path, increasing latency. API Gateway is not a logging or diagnostic store, so this provides no useful place to collect or analyze the data and is not a supported mechanism.","why_zh":"在每個請求中把 log 資訊回傳給 API Gateway 會使回應 payload 變大並在請求路徑中增加處理，導致延遲上升。API Gateway 並非 logging 或診斷儲存系統，因此無法提供有用的收集或分析資料之處，且並非支援的機制。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Having the application calculate and upload statistical data to CloudWatch metrics during request processing introduces synchronous PutMetricData calls in the request path, adding latency. CloudWatch already exposes API Gateway latency metrics; app-computed aggregate statistics would not pinpoint where backend latency originates the way per-request X-Ray traces do.","why_zh":"讓應用程式在處理請求時計算並上傳統計資料到 CloudWatch metrics，會在請求路徑中引入同步的 PutMetricData 呼叫而增加延遲。CloudWatch 已提供 API Gateway 延遲 metrics；應用程式自行計算的彙總統計無法像逐請求的 X-Ray trace 那樣定位後端延遲的來源。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/xray-daemon.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-xray.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/xray-services-apigateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":44,"question_en":"A company has an application that is using a MySQL-compatible Amazon Aurora Multi-AZ DB cluster as the database. A cross-Region read replica has been created for disaster recovery purposes. A DevOps engineer wants to automate the promotion of the replica so it becomes the primary database instance in the event of a failure. Which solution will accomplish this?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，该程序使用与 MySQL 兼容的 Amazon Aurora 多可用区数据库集群作为数据 库。为了实现灾难恢复，已创建了一个跨区域读取副本。一位 DevOps 工程师希望在出现故障时自动 将该副本提升为主数据库实例。 哪种解决方案能实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a latency-based Amazon Route 53 CNAME with health checks so it points to both the primary and replica endpoints. Subscribe an Amazon SNS topic to Amazon RDS failure notifications from AWS CloudTrail and use that topic to invoke an AWS Lambda function that will promote the replica instance as the primary.","B":"Create an Aurora custom endpoint to point to the primary database instance. Configure the application to use this endpoint. Configure AWS CloudTrail to run an AWS Lambda function to promote the replica instance and modify the custom endpoint to point to the newly promoted instance.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to modify the application's AWS CloudFormation template to promote the replica, apply the template to update the stack, and point the application to the newly promoted instance. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to invoke this Lambda function after the failure event occurs.","D":"Store the Aurora endpoint in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Create an Amazon EventBridge event that detects the database failure and runs an AWS Lambda function to promote the replica instance and update the endpoint URL stored in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Code the application to reload the endpoint from Parameter Store if a database connection fails."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个基于延迟的 Amazon Route 53 CNAME 并设置健康检查，使其指向主实例和副本实例 的端点。订阅 AWS CloudTrail 发出的 Amazon RDS 故障通知的 Amazon SNS 主题，并使用该 主题调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将副本实例提升为主实例。","B":"创建一个 Aurora 自定义端点以指向主数据库实例。将应用程序配置为使用此端点。配置 AWS CloudTrail 以运行一个 AWS Lambda 函数来提升副本实例，并修改自定义端点以指向新提升的实 例。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于修改应用程序的 AWS CloudFormation 模板以提升副本，应用 该模板以更新堆栈，并将应用程序指向新提升的实例。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，在 故障事件发生后调用此 Lambda 函数。","D":"将 Aurora 端点存储在 AWS 系统管理器参数存储中。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件，用于检 测数据库故障，并运行一个 AWS Lambda 函数来提升副本实例并更新存储在 AWS 系统管理器参 数存储中的端点 URL。编写应用程序代码，使其在数据库连接失败时从参数存储中重新加载端 点。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS prescribes this exact DR procedure for an Aurora MySQL cross-Region read replica: monitor the source DB cluster for failures, then (1) promote the read replica, (2) direct database traffic to the promoted DB cluster, and (3) create a replacement replica. Option D implements every step with documented building blocks. Amazon RDS sends service events (including RDS DB Cluster Event and RDS DB Instance Event) directly to Amazon EventBridge, so an EventBridge rule can detect the database failure and invoke an AWS Lambda function as a target. The Lambda promotes the replica via the PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster API (promote-read-replica-db-cluster CLI) and updates the endpoint in Systems Manager Parameter Store; the application then reloads the endpoint when its connection fails, satisfying the 'direct traffic to the promoted cluster' step. This is a complete, supported, fully automated solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS 對 Aurora MySQL 跨區域 read replica 的災難復原程序明確規定：監控來源 DB cluster 是否故障，然後 (1) 提升 read replica、(2) 將資料庫流量導向被提升的 DB cluster、(3) 建立替代 replica。選項 D 以官方文件中的元件實作了每一個步驟。Amazon RDS 會將服務事件（包含 RDS DB Cluster Event 與 RDS DB Instance Event）直接傳送到 Amazon EventBridge，因此 EventBridge rule 可偵測資料庫故障並以 AWS Lambda function 作為 target 觸發之。該 Lambda 透過 PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster API（promote-read-replica-db-cluster CLI）提升 replica，並更新 Systems Manager Parameter Store 中的 endpoint；當應用程式連線失敗時即重新讀取 endpoint，符合「將流量導向被提升的 cluster」這一步。這是一個完整、受支援且全自動化的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Technically incoherent. A latency-based Route 53 CNAME pointing at both the primary and the cross-Region replica is not failover routing and would not correctly redirect after promotion (the replica is not writable until promoted). Moreover, RDS failure notifications are not obtained by 'subscribing an SNS topic to RDS failure notifications from AWS CloudTrail' — CloudTrail logs API activity and does not emit RDS infrastructure-failure event notifications to SNS; RDS event delivery is via RDS event subscriptions/EventBridge.","why_zh":"技術上不通。latency-based Route 53 CNAME 同時指向 primary 與跨區域 replica 並非 failover routing，提升後也無法正確重導流量（replica 在提升前無法寫入）。更關鍵的是，RDS 故障通知並非透過「將 SNS topic 訂閱到來自 AWS CloudTrail 的 RDS 故障通知」取得 — CloudTrail 記錄 API 活動，不會向 SNS 發出 RDS 基礎設施故障事件通知；RDS 事件是經由 RDS event subscription / EventBridge 傳遞。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An Aurora custom endpoint groups instances within a single DB cluster for load balancing and cannot span a cross-Region replica that lives in a separate cluster, so it cannot be repointed to the newly promoted standalone cluster. Also, AWS CloudTrail does not 'run a Lambda function' or detect failures — CloudTrail only records API calls; the detection/invocation mechanism is invalid.","why_zh":"Aurora custom endpoint 是在單一 DB cluster 內將執行個體分組以做負載平衡，無法涵蓋位於另一個 cluster 的跨區域 replica，因此無法重新指向新提升的獨立 cluster。此外 AWS CloudTrail 並不會「執行 Lambda function」或偵測故障 — CloudTrail 只記錄 API 呼叫；其偵測/觸發機制無效。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Promotion is a runtime data-recovery operation, not a CloudFormation template property change; there is no CloudFormation promote action and rewriting/applying a CFN template to promote a cross-Region replica is unsupported, slow, and fragile compared with calling the PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster API directly. The approach is convoluted and not an actual promotion mechanism.","why_zh":"提升是執行時的資料復原操作，並非 CloudFormation template 的屬性變更；CloudFormation 並無對應的 promote 動作，改寫並套用 CFN template 來提升跨區域 replica 不受支援，相較於直接呼叫 PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster API 既緩慢又脆弱。此作法迂迴且不是真正的提升機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/AuroraMySQL.Replication.CrossRegion.Promote.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-rds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-cloud-watch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/APIReference/API_PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":45,"question_en":"A company hosts its staging website using an Amazon EC2 instance backed with Amazon EBS storage. The company wants to recover quickly with minimal data losses in the event of network connectivity issues or power failures on the EC2 instance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用由亚马逊 EBS 存储支持的亚马逊 EC2 实例来托管其预发布网站。该公司希望在出现网 络连接问题或 EC2 实例断电的情况下能够快速恢复，并将数据丢失降至最低。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add the instance to an EC2 Auto Scaling group with the minimum, maximum, and desired capacity set to 1.","B":"Add the instance to an EC2 Auto Scaling group with a lifecycle hook to detach the EBS volume when the EC2 instance shuts down or terminates.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for the StatusCheckFailed_System metric and select the EC2 action to recover the instance.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for the StatusCheckFailed_Instance metric and select the EC2 action to reboot the instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"将该实例添加到一个 EC2 自动扩展组中，将最小容量、最大容量和期望容量均设置为 1。","B":"将实例添加到具有生命周期挂钩的 EC2 自动扩展组中，以便在 EC2 实例关闭或终止时分离 EBS 卷。","C":"为“StatusCheckFailed_System”指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，并选择 EC2 操作以恢 复实例。","D":"为“StatusCheckFailed_Instance”指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，并选择 EC2 操作以重 启实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario explicitly names network connectivity issues and power failures on the EC2 instance. AWS documentation lists exactly these as examples that cause a System status check to fail: 'Loss of network connectivity' and 'Loss of system power' (plus host hardware/software issues), and a failed system status check increments the StatusCheckFailed_System CloudWatch metric. CloudWatch action based recovery works with the StatusCheckFailed_System metric, and when triggered with the EC2 recover action it migrates the instance to a new healthy host while retaining its instance ID, private/Elastic IP, and its EBS volumes. Because the instance is EBS-backed, persistent data on EBS is preserved (only RAM contents are lost), giving fast recovery with minimal data loss. Option C is therefore correct.","explanation_zh":"題目明確指出 EC2 instance 發生網路連線問題與電源故障。AWS 文件正好把這些列為導致 System status check 失敗的範例：'Loss of network connectivity'（網路連線中斷）與 'Loss of system power'（系統電源中斷），以及實體主機的硬體/軟體問題；當 system status check 失敗時會遞增 StatusCheckFailed_System 這個 CloudWatch 指標。CloudWatch action based recovery 是搭配 StatusCheckFailed_System 指標運作，當以 EC2 recover 動作觸發時，會將 instance 遷移到新的健康主機，同時保留其 instance ID、private/Elastic IP 以及 EBS volumes。由於此 instance 為 EBS-backed，EBS 上的持久資料會被保留（僅遺失 RAM 內容），因此能快速復原且資料遺失最少。故選 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An Auto Scaling group with min/max/desired all set to 1 replaces (terminates and relaunches) an unhealthy instance rather than recovering the running one. A replacement loses the original instance ID and typically destroys the staging website's data on the root EBS volume, so it causes data loss instead of minimal data loss, and is heavier than a recovery alarm.","why_zh":"將 Auto Scaling group 的最小/最大/期望容量都設為 1，會在 instance 不健康時替換（終止並重新啟動）它，而非復原正在執行的 instance。替換會失去原本的 instance ID，且通常會銷毀 staging 網站在根 EBS volume 上的資料，造成資料損失而非最小資料損失，設定也比復原警示繁重。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A lifecycle hook that detaches the EBS volume on shutdown/termination does not detect or remediate host-level power or network failures and does not recover instance availability; it only manages volume detachment during scale-in. It adds operational complexity without restoring the instance.","why_zh":"在關機/終止時卸離 EBS volume 的 lifecycle hook，並不會偵測或修復主機層級的電源或網路故障，也無法復原 instance 的可用性；它只是在縮減時管理 volume 卸離。這增加操作複雜度卻無法還原 instance。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"StatusCheckFailed_Instance reflects Instance status checks, which detect in-guest issues such as incorrect networking/startup config, exhausted memory, corrupted file system, or incompatible kernel — not host power or network failures. Additionally the chosen 'reboot' action keeps the instance on the same impaired physical host, so it cannot resolve a loss of system power or host network connectivity.","why_zh":"StatusCheckFailed_Instance 對應 Instance status checks，偵測的是 instance 內部問題，例如錯誤的網路/啟動設定、記憶體耗盡、檔案系統損毀或不相容的 kernel，而非主機電源或網路故障。此外所選的 'reboot' 動作會讓 instance 留在同一台受損的實體主機上，無法解決系統電源中斷或主機網路連線中斷。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/monitoring-system-instance-status-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-instance-recover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/cloudwatch-recovery.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":46,"question_en":"A company wants to use AWS development tools to replace its current bash deployment scripts. The company currently deploys a LAMP application to a group of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). During the deployments, the company unit tests the committed application, stops and starts services, unregisters and re-registers instances with the load balancer, and updates file permissions. The company wants to maintain the same deployment functionality through the shift to using AWS services. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用 AWS 开发工具来取代其当前的 bash 部署脚本。该公司目前将一个 LAMP 应用程 序部署到一组位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上。在部署过程中，该公司会对 提交的应用程序进行单元测试，停止和启动服务，从负载均衡器中注销并重新注册实例，并更新文件 权限。该公司希望在转向使用 AWS 服务的过程中保持相同的部署功能。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CodeBuild to test the application. Use bash scripts invoked by AWS CodeDeploy's appspec.yml file to restart services, and deregister and register instances with the ALB. Use the appspec.yml file to update file permissions without a custom script.","B":"Use AWS CodePipeline to move the application from the AWS CodeCommit repository to AWS CodeDeploy. Use CodeDeploy's deployment group to test the application, unregister and re-register instances with the ALB. and restart services. Use the appspec.yml file to update file permissions without a custom script.","C":"Use AWS CodePipeline to move the application source code from the AWS CodeCommit repository to AWS CodeDeploy. Use CodeDeploy to test the application. Use CodeDeploy's appspec.yml file to restart services and update permissions without a custom script. Use AWS CodeBuild to unregister and re-register instances with the ALB.","D":"Use AWS CodePipeline to trigger AWS CodeBuild to test the application. Use bash scripts invoked by AWS CodeDeploy's appspec.yml file to restart services. Unregister and re-register the instances in the AWS CodeDeploy deployment group with the ALB. Update the appspec.yml file to update file permissions without a custom script."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 对应用程序进行测试。使用由 AWS CodeDeploy 的 appspec.yml 文件 调用的 bash 脚本重启服务，并从应用负载均衡器（ALB）中注销和注册实例。使用 appspec.yml 文件更新文件权限，无需自定义脚本。","B":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 将应用程序从 AWS CodeCommit 存储库迁移到 AWS CodeDeploy。使用 CodeDeploy 的部署组来测试应用程序，从应用负载均衡器（ALB）中注销并重新注册实例， 并重新启动服务。使用 appspec.yml 文件更新文件权限，而无需自定义脚本。","C":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 将应用程序源代码从 AWS CodeCommit 存储库移动到 AWS CodeDeploy。使用 CodeDeploy 测试应用程序。使用 CodeDeploy 的 appspec.yml 文件重启服务并更新权限，无需自定义脚 本。使用 AWS CodeBuild 从应用负载均衡器（ALB）注销并重新注册实例。","D":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 触发 AWS CodeBuild 对应用程序进行测试。使用由 AWS CodeDeploy 的 appspec. yml 文件调用的 bash 脚本重启服务。在 AWS CodeDeploy 部署组中注销并重新注册实例与 ALB 的关联。 更新 appspec.yml 文件以更改文件权限，无需自定义脚本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Map each of the four deployment tasks to the correct AWS service or mechanism. (1) Unit testing the committed application is a build/test concern handled by AWS CodeBuild, which runs the test commands in its buildspec build phases; neither CodeDeploy nor a CodeDeploy deployment group runs unit tests on committed source. (2) Stopping and starting services is done by bash scripts invoked from the CodeDeploy appspec.yml ApplicationStop and ApplicationStart EC2/On-Premises lifecycle hooks. (3) Deregistering and re-registering instances with the ALB is performed automatically by the CodeDeploy deployment group when an Elastic Load Balancing load balancer is associated with it: the AWS docs state that during an in-place deployment, 'instances in a deployment group are deregistered from the load balancer, updated with the latest application revision, and then reregistered with the load balancer as part of the same deployment group after the deployment is successful' (via the reserved BlockTraffic/AllowTraffic events). (4) Updating file permissions is done natively by the appspec.yml 'permissions' section (EC2/On-Premises only), which sets owner, group, and mode with no custom script. Option D assigns all four tasks correctly: CodePipeline triggers CodeBuild to test, appspec.yml bash scripts restart services, the CodeDeploy deployment group handles ALB deregister/register, and the appspec.yml permissions section updates file permissions.","explanation_zh":"把四項部署任務分別對應到正確的 AWS 服務或機制。(1) 對已提交的應用程式做單元測試屬於 build/test 範疇，由 AWS CodeBuild 在其 buildspec 的 build 階段執行測試指令；CodeDeploy 或 CodeDeploy deployment group 都不會對提交的原始碼跑單元測試。(2) 停止與啟動服務是由 CodeDeploy appspec.yml 的 ApplicationStop 與 ApplicationStart EC2/On-Premises 生命週期 hook 所呼叫的 bash 指令稿完成。(3) 與 ALB 取消註冊及重新註冊執行個體，是在 deployment group 關聯了 Elastic Load Balancing 負載平衡器時由 CodeDeploy deployment group 自動執行：AWS 文件指出在 in-place deployment 期間，deployment group 中的執行個體會從負載平衡器取消註冊、更新為最新的應用程式修訂版，並在部署成功後重新註冊回同一個 deployment group 的負載平衡器（透過保留的 BlockTraffic/AllowTraffic 事件）。(4) 更新檔案權限由 appspec.yml 的 'permissions' 區段原生完成（僅限 EC2/On-Premises），可設定 owner、group 與 mode，無需自訂指令稿。選項 D 把全部四項任務對應到正確機制：CodePipeline 觸發 CodeBuild 測試、appspec.yml 的 bash 指令稿重啟服務、CodeDeploy deployment group 處理 ALB 取消/重新註冊、appspec.yml permissions 區段更新檔案權限。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"It correctly uses CodeBuild to test, but it claims bash scripts invoked by appspec.yml must deregister and register instances with the ALB. When an ALB is associated with the deployment group, CodeDeploy performs that deregister/register automatically as part of the deployment group via the reserved BlockTraffic/AllowTraffic events (custom scripts are only an optional alternative). The option also omits the CodePipeline orchestration the company wants, making it a poorer fit than D.","why_zh":"它正確地用 CodeBuild 測試，但宣稱必須用 appspec.yml 呼叫的 bash 指令稿來與 ALB 取消/重新註冊執行個體。當 ALB 關聯到 deployment group 時，CodeDeploy 會透過保留的 BlockTraffic/AllowTraffic 事件作為 deployment group 的一部分自動完成取消/重新註冊（自訂指令稿只是可選的替代方案）。此選項也省略了公司想要的 CodePipeline 流程編排，比 D 不理想。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It states the CodeDeploy deployment group tests the application. A deployment group is only configuration (Auto Scaling groups, ALB association, deployment config) and does not run unit tests on committed source code; testing is a build-phase task for AWS CodeBuild. This misassignment makes B incorrect.","why_zh":"它說由 CodeDeploy deployment group 來測試應用程式。deployment group 僅是設定（Auto Scaling 群組、ALB 關聯、部署設定），並不會對提交的原始碼執行單元測試；測試是 AWS CodeBuild 的 build 階段任務。此錯誤對應使 B 不正確。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It contains two errors: it says CodeDeploy tests the application (CodeDeploy does not run unit tests on source code; that is CodeBuild's role) and it says CodeBuild unregisters and re-registers instances with the ALB. CodeBuild is a build/test service and does not manage ALB target registration during a deployment; that is handled natively by the CodeDeploy deployment group.","why_zh":"它有兩處錯誤：它說由 CodeDeploy 測試應用程式（CodeDeploy 不會對原始碼跑單元測試，那是 CodeBuild 的工作），又說由 CodeBuild 與 ALB 取消/重新註冊執行個體。CodeBuild 是 build/test 服務，不負責部署期間的 ALB target 註冊；那是由 CodeDeploy deployment group 原生處理。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-elastic-load-balancing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":47,"question_en":"A company runs an application with an Amazon EC2 and on-premises configuration. A DevOps engineer needs to standardize patching across both environments. Company policy dictates that patching only happens during non-business hours. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司运行着一个采用亚马逊 EC2 和本地配置的应用程序。一位 DevOps 工程师需要在两个环境中统一 打补丁的标准。公司政策规定，打补丁只能在非工作时间进行。 哪些操作组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add the physical machines into AWS Systems Manager using Systems Manager Hybrid Activations.","B":"Attach an IAM role to the EC2 instances, allowing them to be managed by AWS Systems Manager.","C":"Create IAM access keys for the on-premises machines to interact with AWS Systems Manager.","D":"Run an AWS Systems Manager Automation document to patch the systems every hour","E":"Use Amazon EventBridge scheduled events to schedule a patch window.","F":"Use AWS Systems Manager Maintenance Windows to schedule a patch window."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 混合激活功能将物理机添加到 AWS Systems Manager 中。","B":"附加一个 IAM 角 色 连接到 EC2 实例，使它们能够通过 AWS Systems Manager 进行管理。","C":"为本地机器创建 IAM 访问密钥，以便其与 AWS 系统管理器进行交互。","D":"每小时运行一次 AWS Systems Manager Automation 文档以修补系统","E":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 定期事件来安排补丁更新窗口。","F":"使用 AWS 系统管理器维护窗口来安排补丁更新窗口。"},"answer":["A","B","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Standardizing patching across EC2 and on-premises machines with AWS Systems Manager requires registering both environments and scheduling patching for non-business hours. (A) Non-EC2 / on-premises machines become Systems Manager managed nodes through a Hybrid Activation: you run create-activation to obtain an Activation Code and Activation ID, then install SSM Agent with them. (B) EC2 instances need an IAM instance profile/role attached so SSM Agent can communicate with and be managed by Systems Manager. (F) Maintenance Windows defines a schedule (cron/rate with a time zone and active periods) for potentially disruptive actions like patching, so patching runs only during the specified non-business hours, and it targets both EC2 and hybrid managed nodes. C is the trap: hybrid activations exist precisely so on-premises machines do NOT use long-lived IAM access keys; the activation code/ID plus an ssm.amazonaws.com service role provide secure access. D fails the policy because patching every hour would run during business hours. E (EventBridge scheduled events) is not the purpose-built Systems Manager mechanism for patch windows; Maintenance Windows is.","explanation_zh":"要使用 AWS Systems Manager 在 EC2 與地端機器之間統一修補，需要先把兩種環境都註冊為受管節點，並把修補排程在非營業時段。(A) 非 EC2／地端機器透過 Hybrid Activation 成為 Systems Manager managed node：執行 create-activation 取得 Activation Code 與 Activation ID，再用它們安裝 SSM Agent。(B) EC2 執行個體需附加 IAM instance profile/role，SSM Agent 才能與 Systems Manager 通訊並被其管理。(F) Maintenance Windows 可定義排程（cron/rate，含時區與作用期間）來執行像修補這類可能造成中斷的動作，因此修補只會在指定的非營業時段執行，且能同時針對 EC2 與 hybrid managed node。C 是陷阱：Hybrid Activations 的存在正是為了讓地端機器「不需」使用長期 IAM access keys；安全存取由 activation code/ID 加上 ssm.amazonaws.com service role 提供。D 不符合政策，因為每小時修補會落在營業時段。E（EventBridge scheduled events）並非 Systems Manager 專為修補視窗設計的機制，Maintenance Windows 才是。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Hybrid Activations are designed specifically to avoid long-lived IAM access keys on on-premises machines; secure access is provided by the activation code/ID plus an ssm.amazonaws.com service role, not IAM access keys. Distributing static access keys to each server would be insecure and is not the documented method (option A is the correct registration path).","why_zh":"Hybrid Activations 的設計正是要避免在地端機器上使用長期 IAM access keys；安全存取由 activation code/ID 加上 ssm.amazonaws.com service role 提供，而非 IAM access keys。在每台伺服器放靜態金鑰既不安全也非官方做法（選項 A 才是正確的註冊方式）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running an Automation document to patch every hour would patch during business hours, directly violating the policy that patching happens only during non-business hours; a fixed hourly interval is not how scheduled patch windows are implemented.","why_zh":"每小時執行 Automation document 進行修補會在營業時段進行修補，直接違反只能在非營業時段修補的政策；固定每小時執行並非排程修補視窗的實作方式。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Although EventBridge can trigger actions on a schedule, the native, documented Systems Manager mechanism for scheduling disruptive patch windows (with duration, time zone, targets, and registered patch tasks such as AWS-RunPatchBaseline) is Maintenance Windows. Option F is the purpose-built correct fit; E is the weaker distractor against F.","why_zh":"雖然 EventBridge 可依排程觸發動作，但 Systems Manager 原生且官方文件中用於排程具干擾性修補視窗（含持續時間、時區、目標與註冊的 AWS-RunPatchBaseline 等修補任務）的機制是 Maintenance Windows。選項 F 才是專為此設計的正確選項，E 是相對較弱的干擾項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-hybrid-multicloud.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-setting-up-nodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/maintenance-windows.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/maintenance-window-tutorial-patching.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/sysman-patch-scheduletasks.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":48,"question_en":"A company has chosen AWS to host a new application. The company needs to implement a multi-account strategy. A DevOps engineer creates a new AWS account and an organization in AWS Organizations. The DevOps engineer also creates the OU structure for the organization and sets up a landing zone by using AWS Control Tower. The DevOps engineer must implement a solution that automatically deploys resources for new accounts that users create through AWS Control Tower Account Factory. When a user creates a new account, the solution must apply AWS CloudFormation templates and SCPs that are customized for the OU or the account to automatically deploy all the resources that are attached to the account. All the OUs are enrolled in AWS Control Tower. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST automated way?","question_zh":"一家公司已选择 AWS 来托管新的应用程序。该公司需要实施多账户策略。一位 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 新的 AWS 账户和一个 AWS Organizations 组织。该 DevOps 工程师还为该组织创建了组织单元（OU）结构， 并使用 AWS Control Tower 设置了着陆区。 DevOps 工程师必须实现一个解决方案，该方案能够自动为用户通过 AWS Control Tower 账户工厂创建的新 账户部署资源。当用户创建新账户时，该解决方案必须应用针对组织单元（OU）或账户定制的 AWS CloudFormation 模板和 SCP，以自动部署与该账户关联的所有资源。所有组织单元均已注册到 AWS Control Tower。 哪种解决方案能以最自动化的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Service Catalog with AWS Control Tower. Create portfolios and products in AWS Service Catalog. Grant granular permissions to provision these resources. Deploy SCPs by using the AWS CLI and JSON documents.","B":"Deploy CloudFormation stack sets by using the required templates. Enable automatic deployment. Deploy stack instances to the required accounts. Deploy a CloudFormation stack set to the organization’s management account to deploy SCPs.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to detect the CreateManagedAccount event. Configure AWS Service Catalog as the target to deploy resources to any new accounts. Deploy SCPs by using the AWS CLI and JSON documents.","D":"Deploy the Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) solution. Use an AWS CodeCommit repository as the source. In the repository, create a custom package that includes the CloudFormation templates and the SCP JSON documents."},"options_zh":{"A":"结合 AWS Control Tower 使用 AWS 服务目录。在 AWS 服务目录中创建组合和产品。授予精细的权限以 配置这些资源。使用 AWS CLI 和 JSON 文档部署 SCP。","B":"使用所需的模板部署 CloudFormation 堆栈集。启用自动部署。将堆栈实例部署到所需的账户。将 CloudFormation 堆栈集部署到组织的管理账户以部署 SCP。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以检测 CreateManagedAccount 事件。将 AWS 服务目录配置为目 标，以便向任何新账户部署资源。使用 AWS CLI 和 JSON 文档部署 SCP。","D":"部署 AWS Control Tower 自定义解决方案（CfCT）。使用 AWS CodeCommit 存储库作为源。在该存储 库中，创建一个自定义包，其中包含 CloudFormation。 模板和 SCP JSON 文档。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical use case for Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT). The CfCT overview documentation states almost verbatim that customizations are implemented with AWS CloudFormation templates and service control policies (SCPs), that CfCT is integrated with AWS Control Tower lifecycle events, and that 'when a new account is created through account factory, all resources attached to the account are deployed automatically,' with the ability to deploy custom templates and policies to individual accounts and OUs. CfCT uses an AWS CodeCommit repository (or an Amazon S3 bucket) as the configuration source, where a custom package and manifest.yaml define which CloudFormation templates and SCP JSON documents apply to which accounts and OUs. Because both resource deployment and SCP application are triggered automatically by Account Factory lifecycle events with no manual per-account action, option D is the MOST automated solution that satisfies every requirement (CloudFormation + SCPs, customized per OU/account, on Account Factory account creation).","explanation_zh":"這是 Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) 的標準使用情境。CfCT 概觀文件幾乎逐字說明：customizations 以 AWS CloudFormation 範本與 service control policies (SCPs) 實作，CfCT 與 AWS Control Tower lifecycle events 整合，且「當透過 account factory 建立新帳戶時，所有附加至該帳戶的資源會自動部署」，並可將自訂範本與政策部署至個別帳戶與 OUs。CfCT 使用 AWS CodeCommit 儲存庫（或 Amazon S3 儲存貯體）作為設定來源，其中的 custom package 與 manifest.yaml 定義哪些 CloudFormation 範本與 SCP JSON 文件套用至哪些帳戶與 OUs。由於資源部署與 SCP 套用都由 Account Factory lifecycle events 自動觸發，無需逐帳戶手動操作，因此選項 D 是滿足所有需求（CloudFormation + SCPs、依 OU/帳戶自訂、在 Account Factory 建立帳戶時觸發）且最自動化的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Service Catalog requires users to provision products from a portfolio; granting granular provisioning permissions does not auto-deploy resources when Account Factory creates an account. Deploying SCPs via the AWS CLI and JSON documents is a manual step, so this is far less automated than the lifecycle-event-driven CfCT.","why_zh":"AWS Service Catalog 需要使用者從 portfolio 佈建產品，授予細粒度佈建權限並不會在 Account Factory 建立帳戶時自動部署資源。以 AWS CLI 與 JSON 文件部署 SCPs 是手動步驟，因此自動化程度遠低於由 lifecycle event 驅動的 CfCT。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFormation StackSets auto-deployment triggers on AWS Organizations OU membership rather than the native Control Tower Account Factory customization path, and centrally managing per-OU/per-account SCPs is not what StackSets is designed for (even though an AWS::Organizations::Policy resource exists, that is a management-account-only construct and not the integrated pattern here). CfCT is the purpose-built, lifecycle-integrated solution that bundles both CloudFormation templates and SCP application, so it is more automated and better aligned with the requirement.","why_zh":"CloudFormation StackSets 的自動部署是依 AWS Organizations 的 OU 成員資格觸發，而非原生的 Control Tower Account Factory 自訂路徑，且集中管理依 OU/帳戶的 SCPs 並非 StackSets 的設計用途（雖然存在 AWS::Organizations::Policy 資源，但那是僅限管理帳戶的構件，並非此處的整合模式）。CfCT 是專為此打造、與 lifecycle 整合的解決方案，同時封裝 CloudFormation 範本與 SCP 套用，因此更自動化且更符合需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Although CreateManagedAccount is a real Control Tower lifecycle event, AWS Service Catalog is not a directly supported EventBridge target for auto-provisioning resources into a brand-new account, and deploying SCPs via the AWS CLI remains manual. This is a brittle, partially manual design compared with CfCT, which already provides the lifecycle integration natively.","why_zh":"雖然 CreateManagedAccount 是真實的 Control Tower lifecycle event，但 AWS Service Catalog 並非直接支援的 EventBridge 目標來自動將資源佈建至全新帳戶，且以 AWS CLI 部署 SCPs 仍是手動。相較於原生提供 lifecycle 整合的 CfCT，這是脆弱且部分手動的設計。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/cfct-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/automate-customizations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/the-manifest-file.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":49,"question_en":"An online retail company based in the United States plans to expand its operations to Europe and Asia in the next six months. Its product currently runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The instances run in an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. All data is stored in an Amazon Aurora database instance. When the product is deployed in multiple regions, the company wants a single product catalog across all regions, but for compliance purposes, its customer information and purchases must be kept in each region. How should the company meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of application changes?","question_zh":"一家总部位于美国的在线零售公司计划在未来六个月内将其业务拓展至欧洲和亚洲。该公司目前的产品 运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器之后。这些实例在多个可用区的亚马逊 EC2 自动扩展组中运行。所有数据都存储在亚马逊 Aurora 数据库实例中。 当产品部署在多个地区时，该公司希望在所有地区拥有一个统一的产品目录，但出于合规性考虑，其客 户信息和购买记录必须保存在各自所在的地区。 公司应如何以最少的应用程序变更来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Redshift for the product catalog and Amazon DynamoDB tables for the customer information and purchases.","B":"Use Amazon DynamoDB global tables for the product catalog and regional tables for the customer information and purchases.","C":"Use Aurora with read replicas for the product catalog and additional local Aurora instances in each region for the customer information and purchases.","D":"Use Aurora for the product catalog and Amazon DynamoDB global tables for the customer information and purchases."},"options_zh":{"A":"产品目录使用亚马逊 Redshift，客户信息和购买记录使用亚马逊 DynamoDB 表。","B":"对于产品目录使用亚马逊 DynamoDB 全球表，对于客户信息和购买记录使用区域表。","C":"对于产品目录，使用带有只读副本的 Aurora，对于每个区域的客户信息和购买记录，则使用额外 的本地 Aurora 实例。","D":"使用 Aurora 作为产品目录，使用亚马逊 DynamoDB 全球表来存储客户信息和购买记录。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application already runs entirely on Amazon Aurora (a relational engine), and the deciding qualifier is LEAST amount of application changes. Option C keeps everything relational: a single product catalog served globally via Aurora cross-Region read replicas (one writer in the primary Region, read-only replicas in Europe and Asia), plus separate local Aurora instances in each Region for customer information and purchases so that regulated data never leaves its Region (data residency/compliance). Because the relational data model and SQL access layer are unchanged, the code barely changes. Aurora MySQL supports up to five cross-Region read replicas (Aurora global database is the managed alternative, and the only cross-Region option for Aurora PostgreSQL), so a read-mostly catalog replicated across Regions is fully supported. Option B (DynamoDB global tables + regional tables) maps the global-vs-regional split correctly but would force a full migration of the Aurora relational schema and all query/data-access code to a NoSQL key-value model, which is the MOST application change, not the least.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式目前完全運行在 Amazon Aurora（關聯式引擎）上，而決定性條件是「最少的應用程式變更（LEAST application changes）」。選項 C 全部維持關聯式架構：產品目錄透過 Aurora cross-Region read replicas 在全球提供單一目錄（主要 Region 一個 writer，歐洲與亞洲各有唯讀 replica），並在每個 Region 各自設置本地的 Aurora 執行個體存放客戶資訊與購買紀錄，使受規範的資料不會離開所屬 Region（資料落地/合規）。由於關聯式資料模型與 SQL 存取層不變，程式碼幾乎無需改動。Aurora MySQL 最多支援五個 cross-Region read replicas（Aurora global database 是受管的替代方案，也是 Aurora PostgreSQL 唯一的跨 Region 選項），因此以讀取為主的目錄跨 Region 複寫完全可行。選項 B（DynamoDB global tables + regional tables）雖然正確對應了全域與區域的切分，但會迫使將 Aurora 關聯式 schema 與所有查詢/資料存取程式碼整體遷移到 NoSQL key-value 模型，這是最大的應用程式變更，而非最少。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Redshift is an OLAP data warehouse, not an operational transactional store for a live product catalog, and it has no native multi-active cross-Region replication for serving the catalog. Moving customer/purchase data to DynamoDB also abandons the existing Aurora relational app, requiring extensive rewrites and not addressing per-Region residency well — far from the least change.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift 是 OLAP 資料倉儲，不適合作為線上產品目錄的交易型資料存放，也沒有原生的多主動跨 Region 複寫來服務目錄。同時把客戶/購買資料改用 DynamoDB 也等於放棄現有 Aurora 關聯式應用，需要大量改寫，且未妥善處理各 Region 的資料落地，遠非最少變更。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Global tables for the catalog and regional DynamoDB tables for customer data correctly model the global-vs-regional requirement, but the existing app is built on relational Aurora. Re-platforming all data and access code from SQL to a NoSQL key-value model is the MOST application change, directly violating the LEAST-changes qualifier.","why_zh":"用 global tables 放目錄、各 Region DynamoDB tables 放客戶資料，雖然正確對應全域與區域需求，但現有應用建構於關聯式 Aurora。把所有資料與存取程式碼從 SQL 改寫成 NoSQL key-value 模型是最大的應用程式變更，直接違反「最少變更」的限定條件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This inverts the requirement. DynamoDB global tables replicate data across all Regions, so using them for customer information and purchases would spread that data globally — exactly what compliance forbids (it must stay per-Region). Meanwhile a single Aurora cluster does not serve a globally distributed catalog well. The global/regional mapping is backwards.","why_zh":"此選項把需求顛倒了。DynamoDB global tables 會把資料跨所有 Region 複寫，因此用於客戶資訊與購買紀錄會讓這些資料散布到全球，正是合規所禁止的（必須保留在各自 Region）。同時單一 Aurora cluster 也不適合服務全球分散的目錄。全域/區域的對應關係完全相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/aurora-replication-options/cross-region-aurora-replicas.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":50,"question_en":"A company is implementing a well-architected design for its globally accessible API stack. The design needs to ensure both high reliability and fast response times for users located in North America and Europe. The API stack contains the following three tiers: Amazon API Gateway AWS Lambda Amazon DynamoDB Which solution will meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在为其全球可访问的 API 堆栈实施架构良好的设计。该设计需要确保位于北美和欧洲的 用户都能获得高可靠性和快速响应时间。 该 API 堆栈包含以下三个层级： 亚马逊 API 网关 AWS Lambda 亚马逊 DynamoDB 哪种解决方案能满足要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon Route 53 to point to API Gateway APIs in North America and Europe using health checks. Configure the APIs to forward requests to a Lambda function in that Region. Configure the Lambda functions to retrieve and update the data in a DynamoDB table in the same Region as the Lambda function.","B":"Configure Amazon Route 53 to point to API Gateway APIs in North America and Europe using latency- based routing and health checks. Configure the APIs to forward requests to a Lambda function in that Region. Configure the Lambda functions to retrieve and update the data in a DynamoDB global table.","C":"Configure Amazon Route 53 to point to API Gateway in North America, create a disaster recovery API in Europe, and configure both APIs to forward requests to the Lambda functions in that Region. Retrieve the data from a DynamoDB global table. Deploy a Lambda function to check the North America API health every 5 minutes. In the event of a failure, update Route 53 to point to the disaster recovery API.","D":"Configure Amazon Route 53 to point to API Gateway API in North America using latency-based routing. Configure the API to forward requests to the Lambda function in the Region nearest to the user. Configure the Lambda function to retrieve and update the data in a DynamoDB table."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用健康检查将 Amazon Route 53 配置为指向北美和欧洲的 API Gateway API。将这些 API 配置为将 请求转发到该区域内的 Lambda 函数。将 Lambda 函数配置为从与该 Lambda 函数位于同一区域的 DynamoDB 表中检索和更新数据。","B":"使用基于延迟的路由和健康检查配置 Amazon Route 53，使其指向北美和欧洲的 API Gateway API。配 置这些 API 将请求转发到该区域的 Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数从 DynamoDB 全局表中检索和 更新数据。","C":"配置亚马逊 Route 53 指向北美的 API 网关，在欧洲创建一个灾难恢复 API，并将这两个 API 配置为 将请求转发到该区域的 Lambda 函数。从 DynamoDB 全球表中检索数据。部署一个 Lambda 函数， 每 5 分钟检查一次北美 API 的运行状况。如果出现故障，更新 Route 53 使其指向灾难恢复 API。","D":"使用基于延迟的路由配置 Amazon Route 53 指向北美的 API Gateway API。配置 API 将请求转发至 距离最近区域的 Lambda 函数。 用户。配置 Lambda 函数以从 DynamoDB 表中检索和更新数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The design must deliver BOTH fast response times and high reliability for users in North America and Europe across an API Gateway -> Lambda -> DynamoDB stack. Option B uses Route 53 latency-based routing to send each user to the Region that provides the lowest latency (fast response times), and pairs it with health checks so Route 53 stops resolving to an unhealthy Region (high reliability) at the API tier. It backs this with a DynamoDB global table, which AWS documents as a multi-active, multi-Region feature that 'provides easy to use data replication and fast local read and write performance' and where 'any global table replica can serve reads and writes,' giving each Region's Lambda local data access and a low/zero-RPO failover path. Together, latency-based routing + health checks + global table is the well-architected active-active pattern that satisfies both qualifiers at every tier. The decisive distinction is that only Option B provides BOTH per-user latency optimization AND multi-Region replicated, highly available data; every other option drops one or both.","explanation_zh":"此設計必須同時為北美與歐洲使用者提供「快速回應」與「高可靠性」，且涵蓋 API Gateway -> Lambda -> DynamoDB 三層。選項 B 使用 Route 53 latency-based routing 將每位使用者導向延遲最低的 Region（快速回應），並搭配 health checks，讓 Route 53 在某 Region 不健康時停止解析至該 Region（API 層的高可靠性）。資料層則使用 DynamoDB global table；AWS 文件指出 global table 是 multi-active、multi-Region 功能，提供「易於使用的資料複寫與快速的在地讀寫效能」，且「任一 global table 副本皆可服務讀寫」，使各 Region 的 Lambda 能就近存取資料並具備低或零 RPO 的故障移轉路徑。latency-based routing + health checks + global table 共同構成 well-architected 的 active-active 架構，在每一層都滿足兩項需求。關鍵差異在於：只有選項 B 同時提供「依使用者的延遲最佳化」與「跨 Region 複寫且高可用的資料」，其他選項皆缺其一或兩者。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses health checks but NO latency-based routing, so there is no mechanism to direct each user to the lowest-latency Region (fails 'fast response times' at the DNS tier). It also uses a separate standalone DynamoDB table per Region with no replication, so North America and Europe hold divergent, unsynchronized data rather than a unified, highly available global dataset.","why_zh":"雖有 health checks 但沒有 latency-based routing，缺乏將每位使用者導向延遲最低 Region 的機制（在 DNS 層未滿足『快速回應時間』）。此外各 Region 使用獨立未複寫的 DynamoDB table，導致北美與歐洲資料各自分歧、無法同步，而非統一且高可用的全球資料集。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An active-passive DR design with a single active Region (North America), so European users hit North America in normal operation and do not get fast response times. The custom Lambda polling health every 5 minutes plus manually updating Route 53 adds high operational overhead and gives much slower, more fragile failover than native Route 53 health checks. Not well-architected.","why_zh":"這是 active-passive 災難復原設計，僅有單一作用中 Region（北美），正常運作下歐洲使用者會連到北美而無法獲得快速回應。每 5 分鐘自訂 Lambda 輪詢健康狀態再手動更新 Route 53 帶來高營運負擔，且故障移轉遠比原生 Route 53 health checks 緩慢且脆弱，不符合 Well-Architected。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Latency-based routing pointing to only a single API in North America is meaningless (latency routing needs multiple regional records). It also claims the API forwards to a Lambda 'in the Region nearest to the user', which is not how API Gateway/Lambda works—an API invokes Lambda in its own Region. It uses a single non-global DynamoDB table, so it is neither multi-Region nor reliable, and provides no fast response for Europe.","why_zh":"latency-based routing 只指向北美單一 API 毫無意義（延遲路由需要多個 Region 記錄）。它還宣稱 API 會轉發到『離使用者最近 Region』的 Lambda，這並非 API Gateway/Lambda 的運作方式——API 只會呼叫同 Region 的 Lambda。並且使用單一非全球的 DynamoDB table，既非多 Region 也不可靠，且無法為歐洲提供快速回應。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":51,"question_en":"A rapidly growing company wants to scale for developer demand for AWS development environments. Development environments are created manually in the AWS Management Console. The networking team uses AWS CloudFormation to manage the networking infrastructure, exporting stack output values for the Amazon VPC and all subnets. The development environments have common standards, such as Application Load Balancers, Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling groups, security groups, and Amazon DynamoDB tables. To keep up with demand, the DevOps engineer wants to automate the creation of development environments. Because the infrastructure required to support the application is expected to grow, there must be a way to easily update the deployed infrastructure. CloudFormation will be used to create a template for the development environments. Which approach will meet these requirements and quickly provide consistent AWS environments for developers?","question_zh":"一家发展迅速的公司希望扩大其 AWS 开发环境以满足开发人员的需求。开发环境目前是在 AWS 管理 控制台中手动创建的。网络团队使用 AWS CloudFormation 来管理网络基础设施，并导出 Amazon VPC 及所有子网的堆栈输出值。开发环境具有通用标准，例如应用负载均衡器、Amazon EC2 自动扩展组、 安全组和 Amazon DynamoDB 表。 为了满足需求，DevOps 工程师希望实现开发环境创建的自动化。由于支持应用程序所需的基础设 施预计会不断扩展，因此必须有一种简便的方式来更新已部署的基础设施。将使用 CloudFormation 来为开发环境创建模板。 哪种方法能满足这些要求，并能迅速为开发人员提供一致的 AWS 环境？","options_en":{"A":"Use Fn::ImportValue intrinsic functions in the Resources section of the template to retrieve Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and subnet values. Use CloudFormation StackSets for the development environments, using the Count input parameter to indicate the number of environments needed. Use the UpdateStackSet command to update existing development environments.","B":"Use nested stacks to define common infrastructure components. To access the exported values, use TemplateURL to reference the networking team’s template. To retrieve Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and subnet values, use Fn::ImportValue intrinsic functions in the Parameters section of the root template. Use the CreateChangeSet and ExecuteChangeSet commands to update existing development environments.","C":"Use nested stacks to define common infrastructure components. Use Fn::ImportValue intrinsic functions with the resources of the nested stack to retrieve Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and subnet values. Use the CreateChangeSet and ExecuteChangeSet commands to update existing development environments.","D":"Use Fn::ImportValue intrinsic functions in the Parameters section of the root template to retrieve Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and subnet values. Define the development resources in the order they need to be created in the CloudFormation nested stacks. Use the CreateChangeSet and ExecuteChangeSet commands to update existing development environments."},"options_zh":{"A":"在模板的“资源”部分使用 Fn::ImportValue 内置函数来获取虚拟私有云（VPC）和子网的值。使用 CloudFormation StackSets 来创建开发环境，通过“Count”输入参数来指定所需的环境数量。使用 UpdateStackSet 命令来更新现有的开发环境。","B":"使用嵌套堆栈来定义常见的基础架构组件。要访问导出的值，请使用 TemplateURL 引用网络团队 的模板。要在根模板的参数部分获取虚拟私有云（VPC）和子网的值，请使用 Fn::ImportValue 内 置函数。使用 CreateChangeSet 和 ExecuteChangeSet 命令来更新现有的开发环境。","C":"使用嵌套堆栈来定义常见的基础设施组件。使用 Fn::ImportValue 内置函数以及嵌套堆栈中的资 源来获取虚拟私有云（VPC）和子网的值。使用 CreateChangeSet 和 ExecuteChangeSet 命令来 更新现有的开发环境。","D":"在根模板的参数部分使用 Fn::ImportValue 内置函数来获取虚拟私有云（VPC）和子网的值。按照 创建顺序在 CloudFormation 嵌套堆栈中定义开发资源。使用 CreateChangeSet 和 ExecuteChangeSet 命令来更新现有的开发环境。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The scenario needs reusable common components (ALBs, Auto Scaling groups, security groups, DynamoDB tables) shared across many identical dev environments, consumption of the networking team's exported VPC/subnet outputs, and an easy way to update deployed infrastructure as it grows. Nested stacks are AWS's recommended way to package repeatedly-used resource configurations into dedicated reusable templates referenced via AWS::CloudFormation::Stack. Fn::ImportValue consumes another stack's exported Outputs (same account and Region), and the canonical AWS example shows it placed inside a resource property (for example SubnetId: Fn::ImportValue ...), i.e. with the resources of the (nested) stack. Change sets for nested stacks let you preview and then apply updates across the entire stack hierarchy via CreateChangeSet/ExecuteChangeSet, satisfying the 'easily update' requirement. Option C is the only choice that gets all three pieces right. The decisive flaw in B and D is that they place Fn::ImportValue in the Parameters section, where only static attributes (Type, Default, AllowedValues, etc.) are valid and intrinsic functions are not resolved; A invents a non-existent StackSets 'Count' input parameter and uses StackSets (cross-account/Region orchestration) instead of nested stacks.","explanation_zh":"此情境需要在多個相同的開發環境間共用可重用的共通元件 (Application Load Balancers、EC2 Auto Scaling groups、security groups、DynamoDB tables)、取用 networking 團隊匯出的 VPC/subnet outputs，並能隨著基礎設施成長輕鬆更新已部署的資源。Nested stacks 是 AWS 建議用來把重複使用的資源組態封裝成專屬可重用範本 (透過 AWS::CloudFormation::Stack 引用) 的方式。Fn::ImportValue 用來取用另一個 stack 匯出的 Outputs (限同一 account 與 Region)，且 AWS 官方範例顯示它應放在資源屬性中 (例如 SubnetId: Fn::ImportValue ...)，也就是放在 (nested) stack 的 resources 內。Change sets for nested stacks 可透過 CreateChangeSet/ExecuteChangeSet 預覽並套用整個 stack 階層的更新，滿足『輕鬆更新』需求。Option C 是唯一三個要件都正確的選項。B 與 D 的決定性錯誤在於把 Fn::ImportValue 放在 Parameters section，而該 section 只接受靜態屬性 (Type、Default、AllowedValues 等)，intrinsic functions 不會在此被解析；A 則杜撰了不存在的 StackSets 'Count' 輸入參數，且改用 StackSets (跨 account/Region 編排) 而非 nested stacks。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"StackSets has no 'Count' input parameter; StackSets is designed to deploy a stack across multiple accounts/Regions, not to spin up N copies in one account via a count. It also abandons the requested nested-stack reuse model. While UpdateStackSet is real, the invented Count premise makes the option invalid, and Fn::ImportValue is limited to the same account and Region.","why_zh":"StackSets 沒有 'Count' 輸入參數；StackSets 是用來跨多個 account/Region 部署 stack，而非以計數方式在單一 account 建立 N 份副本，且放棄了題目要求的 nested-stack 重用模型。雖然 UpdateStackSet 確實存在，但杜撰的 Count 前提使此選項無效，且 Fn::ImportValue 僅限同一 account 與 Region。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Places Fn::ImportValue in the Parameters section, where intrinsic functions are not evaluated (only static attributes like Type/Default/AllowedValues are valid). It also misframes TemplateURL as a way to 'access exported values'; TemplateURL points to a child template to nest as its own stack, not a mechanism to read another stack's exported outputs.","why_zh":"把 Fn::ImportValue 放在 Parameters section，而該處不會解析 intrinsic functions (僅接受 Type/Default/AllowedValues 等靜態屬性)。並錯誤地把 TemplateURL 描述為『取用匯出值』的方式；TemplateURL 指向要當成 nested stack 部署的子範本，並非讀取另一個 stack 已匯出 outputs 的機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as B: Fn::ImportValue is not valid in the Parameters section of the root template because that section does not resolve intrinsic functions. CloudFormation also resolves resource creation order automatically via dependency references (Ref/GetAtt) and DependsOn, so manually 'defining resources in the order they need to be created' is unnecessary and is not how nested-stack ordering is expressed.","why_zh":"與 B 相同的致命缺陷：Fn::ImportValue 不能用於 root template 的 Parameters section，因該處不解析 intrinsic functions。CloudFormation 也會透過相依參照 (Ref/GetAtt) 與 DependsOn 自動決定資源建立順序，故手動『依建立順序定義資源』既非必要，也非 nested-stack 排序的表達方式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/intrinsic-function-reference-importvalue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/parameters-section-structure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-nested-stacks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/change-sets-for-nested-stacks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-stack-exports.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":52,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage multiple accounts. Information security policies require that all unencrypted Amazon EBS volumes be marked as non-compliant. A DevOps engineer needs to automatically deploy the solution and ensure that this compliance check is always present. Which solution will accomplish this?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理多个账户。信息安全政策要求将所有未加密的 Amazon EBS 卷标记为不符合规定。一位 DevOps 工程师需要自动部署解决方案，并确保始终执行此合规性检查。 哪种解决方案能实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that defines an AWS Inspector rule to check whether EBS encryption is enabled. Save the template to an Amazon S3 bucket that has been shared with all accounts within the company. Update the account creation script pointing to the CloudFormation template in Amazon S3.","B":"Create an AWS Config organizational rule to check whether EBS encryption is enabled and deploy the rule using the AWS CLI. Create and apply an SCP to prohibit stopping and deleting AWS Config across the organization.","C":"Create an SCP in Organizations. Set the policy to prevent the launch of Amazon EC2 instances without encryption on the EBS volumes using a conditional expression. Apply the SCP to all AWS accounts. Use Amazon Athena to analyze the AWS CloudTrail output, looking for events that deny an ec2:RunInstances action.","D":"Deploy an IAM role to all accounts from a single trusted account. Build a pipeline with AWS CodePipeline with a stage in AWS Lambda to assume the IAM role, and list all EBS volumes in the account. Publish a report to Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，定义一个 AWS Inspector 规则以检查 EBS 加密是否已启用。 将该模板保存到已与公司内所有账户共享的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。更新账户创建脚本，使其指 向 Amazon S3 中的 CloudFormation 模板。","B":"使用 AWS CLI 创建一条 AWS Config 组织规则，以检查 EBS 加密是否已启用，并部署该规则。创建 并应用一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止停止和删除 AWS Config 资源。 该组织。","C":"在组织中创建一个服务控制策略（SCP）。使用条件表达式设置策略，以防止在未对 EBS 卷进行加密 的情况下启动 Amazon EC2 实例。将该 SCP 应用于所有 AWS 账户。使用 Amazon Athena 分析 AWS CloudTrail 输出，查找拒绝 ec2:RunInstances 操作的事件。","D":"从一个受信任的账户向所有账户部署一个 IAM 角色。使用 AWS CodePipeline 构建一个管道，在 AWS Lambda 中设置一个阶段以承担该 IAM 角色，并列出该账户中的所有 EBS 卷。将报告发 布到 Amazon S3。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is detective: mark all unencrypted EBS volumes as NON_COMPLIANT across an AWS Organizations multi-account environment, deploy it automatically, and ensure the check is always present. AWS Config provides the managed rule 'encrypted-volumes' (identifier ENCRYPTED_VOLUMES) which checks attached AWS::EC2::Volume resources and reports NON_COMPLIANT when a volume is unencrypted, exactly matching the requirement wording. AWS Config organization rules are created with PutOrganizationConfigRule and, per AWS docs, can only be created via the API or CLI (the console is not supported), which is why option B specifies the AWS CLI; they deploy the rule across all member accounts, auto-deploy to any new account that joins (and remove it when an account leaves), and let the management/delegated administrator account enforce governance so member accounts cannot modify the rule. Applying an SCP that prohibits stopping/deleting AWS Config (e.g., config:StopConfigurationRecorder, config:DeleteConfigurationRecorder) prevents member accounts from disabling the recorder, satisfying the 'always present' requirement. Option B is the only choice that delivers detective compliance marking, organization-wide automatic deployment, and persistence.","explanation_zh":"需求屬於偵測型 (detective)：在 AWS Organizations 多帳戶環境中，將所有未加密的 EBS volume 標記為 NON_COMPLIANT，自動部署，並確保此合規檢查始終存在。AWS Config 提供受管規則 'encrypted-volumes'（識別碼 ENCRYPTED_VOLUMES），會檢查已掛載的 AWS::EC2::Volume 資源，volume 未加密時回報 NON_COMPLIANT，與需求字面完全相符。AWS Config 的 organization rule 透過 PutOrganizationConfigRule 建立，依官方文件只能透過 API 或 CLI 建立（不支援主控台），這正是選項 B 指定使用 AWS CLI 的原因；它會將規則部署到所有成員帳戶、對新加入的帳戶自動部署（帳戶離開時自動移除），並讓管理帳戶/委派管理員帳戶強制治理，使成員帳戶無法修改規則。再套用一個禁止停止/刪除 AWS Config（例如 config:StopConfigurationRecorder、config:DeleteConfigurationRecorder）的 SCP，可防止成員帳戶停用 recorder，滿足『始終存在』的要求。選項 B 是唯一同時達成偵測型合規標記、組織範圍自動部署與持久性的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability and network-reachability assessment service; it has no 'rule' that evaluates whether EBS encryption is enabled and produces a NON_COMPLIANT compliance marking - that capability belongs to AWS Config, not Inspector. Distributing a CloudFormation template via S3 and an account-creation script is also brittle and does not guarantee the check is 'always present' (nothing prevents deletion or skipping it).","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是漏洞與網路可達性評估服務，並沒有判斷 EBS 加密是否啟用並產生 NON_COMPLIANT 合規標記的『規則』——該能力屬於 AWS Config，而非 Inspector。透過 S3 散佈 CloudFormation 範本並依賴帳戶建立腳本既脆弱，也無法保證檢查『始終存在』（無法防止刪除或略過）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP with a conditional expression is preventive: it blocks launching EC2 with unencrypted volumes, but it does not 'mark unencrypted EBS volumes as non-compliant' (no compliance reporting) and cannot flag pre-existing unencrypted volumes. Using Athena over CloudTrail to find denied ec2:RunInstances events audits blocked launch attempts, not the compliance state of existing volumes, so it fails the stated detective requirement and adds high operational overhead.","why_zh":"帶條件運算式的 SCP 屬於預防型：它阻擋啟動帶有未加密 volume 的 EC2，但不會『將未加密的 EBS volume 標記為 non-compliant』（沒有合規回報），也無法標記既有的未加密 volume。用 Athena 分析 CloudTrail 尋找被拒絕的 ec2:RunInstances 事件，是稽核被擋下的啟動嘗試，而非既有 volume 的合規狀態，因此不符合偵測型需求且營運負擔高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A custom CodePipeline + Lambda solution that assumes a role, lists EBS volumes, and publishes a report to S3 is a hand-built, point-in-time inventory job. It does not produce a managed continuous NON_COMPLIANT compliance state, does not automatically apply to new accounts, is not guaranteed to be 'always present', and reinvents functionality AWS Config provides natively - over-engineered and fragile.","why_zh":"自建的 CodePipeline + Lambda 方案（assume role、列出 EBS volume、寫報告到 S3）是手工、時間點式的盤點作業。它不會產生受管的持續性 NON_COMPLIANT 合規狀態，不會自動套用到新帳戶，也無法保證『始終存在』，且重新發明了 AWS Config 原生提供的功能——過度設計且脆弱。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/encrypted-volumes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/config-rule-multi-account-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/APIReference/API_PutOrganizationConfigRule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":53,"question_en":"A company is performing vulnerability scanning for all Amazon EC2 instances across many accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. Each account's VPCs are attached to a shared transit gateway. The VPCs send traffic to the internet through a central egress VPC. The company has enabled Amazon Inspector in a delegated administrator account and has enabled scanning for all member accounts. A DevOps engineer discovers that some EC2 instances are listed in the \"not scanning\" tab in Amazon Inspector. Which combination of actions should the DevOps engineer take to resolve this issue? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在对多个账户中的所有亚马逊 EC2 实例执行漏洞扫描。这些账户位于 AWS 组织中的一个组 织内。每个账户的 VPC 都连接到一个共享的中转网关。VPC 通过一个中央出口 VPC 访问互联网。该公 司已在委托管理员账户中启用了 Amazon Inspector，并为所有成员账户启用了扫描功能。 一位 DevOps 工程师发现，亚马逊 Inspector 中的“未扫描”选项卡里列出了部分 EC2 实例。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些行动组合来解决此问题？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Verify that AWS Systems Manager Agent is installed and is running on the EC2 instances that Amazon Inspector is not scanning.","B":"Associate the target EC2 instances with security groups that allow outbound communication on port 443 to the AWS Systems Manager service endpoint.","C":"Grant inspector:StartAssessmentRun permissions to the IAM role that the DevOps engineer is using.","D":"Configure EC2 Instance Connect for the EC2 instances that Amazon Inspector is not scanning.","E":"Associate the target EC2 instances with instance profiles that grant permissions to communicate with AWS Systems Manager.","F":"Create a managed-instance activation. Use the Activation Code and the Activation ID to register the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"确认 AWS 系统管理器代理已安装并正在运行在亚马逊 Inspector 未扫描的 EC2 实例上。","B":"将目标 EC2 实例与允许通过端口 443 向 AWS Systems Manager 服务端点进行出站通信的安全组相 关联。","C":"授予检查员：启动评估运行权限给开发运维工程师正在使用的 IAM 角色。","D":"为 Amazon Inspector 不扫描的 EC2 实例配置 EC2 实例连接。","E":"将目标 EC2 实例与授予其与 AWS Systems Manager 通信权限的实例配置文件相关联。","F":"创建托管实例激活。使用激活码和激活 ID 注册 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A","B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Inspector's Enhanced EC2 (VM) Scanning installs and runs the scanner via AWS Systems Manager (SSM). For an instance to be scanned (and not appear in the 'not scanning' tab), the official requirements are: (1) the SSM Agent is installed and running on the instance (Option A); (2) the instance has an IAM instance profile that allows SSM to manage it (Option E); and (3) the instance has network connectivity to the SSM service endpoints, which requires SSM Agent to reach the SSM/ssmmessages endpoints over HTTPS port 443 outbound (Option B). These three requirements are explicitly listed on the Inspector 'Enabling Inspector VM Scanner / Requirements' page and the SSM Agent troubleshooting page (port 443 to ssm/ssmmessages). Together they directly resolve why instances show as 'not scanning'.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 Enhanced EC2 (VM) Scanning 透過 AWS Systems Manager (SSM) 安裝並執行掃描器。要讓執行個體能被掃描（不出現在 'not scanning' 分頁），官方需求為：(1) 執行個體上已安裝並執行 SSM Agent（選項 A）；(2) 執行個體具有允許 SSM 管理它的 IAM instance profile（選項 E）；(3) 執行個體可連線到 SSM service endpoints，亦即 SSM Agent 需透過 HTTPS port 443 對外連到 ssm/ssmmessages endpoints（選項 B）。這三項需求明確列於 Inspector 'Enabling Inspector VM Scanner / Requirements' 頁面及 SSM Agent 疑難排解頁面（port 443 連到 ssm/ssmmessages），共同解決執行個體顯示為 'not scanning' 的問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"inspector:StartAssessmentRun is an Inspector Classic (v1) API and is unrelated to Inspector v2 continuous VM scanning. The 'not scanning' status is caused by SSM eligibility on the instances, not by the engineer's IAM permission to start an assessment run. The DevOps engineer's permissions do not affect whether an instance is scannable.","why_zh":"inspector:StartAssessmentRun 屬於 Inspector Classic (v1) API，與 Inspector v2 的持續性 VM 掃描無關。'not scanning' 狀態是由執行個體的 SSM 適格性造成，而非工程師啟動評估的 IAM 權限；工程師的權限不影響執行個體是否可被掃描。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EC2 Instance Connect provides SSH browser access to instances; it has nothing to do with Inspector scanning, which relies on SSM Agent connectivity to AWS endpoints, not interactive SSH sessions.","why_zh":"EC2 Instance Connect 提供瀏覽器 SSH 連線存取，與 Inspector 掃描無關。Inspector 掃描依賴 SSM Agent 連線到 AWS endpoints，而非互動式 SSH 工作階段。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Managed-instance (hybrid) activation using an Activation Code and Activation ID is the registration method for non-EC2 / on-premises servers and VMs. EC2 instances must NOT be registered this way; they use an attached IAM instance profile (Option E) instead. Using hybrid activation on EC2 is incorrect and unsupported for this use case.","why_zh":"使用 Activation Code 與 Activation ID 的 managed-instance（hybrid）activation 是用於非 EC2／地端伺服器與 VM 的註冊方式。EC2 執行個體不應以此方式註冊，而應改用附加的 IAM instance profile（選項 E）。對 EC2 使用 hybrid activation 在此情境屬錯誤且不受支援。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/inspector-vm-scanner-enabling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-ssm-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/setup-instance-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":54,"question_en":"A development team uses AWS CodeCommit for version control for applications. The development team uses AWS CodePipeline, AWS CodeBuild. and AWS CodeDeploy for CI/CD infrastructure. In CodeCommit, the development team recently merged pull requests that did not pass long-running tests in the code base. The development team needed to perform rollbacks to branches in the codebase, resulting in lost time and wasted effort. A DevOps engineer must automate testing of pull requests in CodeCommit to ensure that reviewers more easily see the results of automated tests as part of the pull request review. What should the DevOps engineer do to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"开发团队使用 AWS CodeCommit 对应用程序进行版本控制。该团队使用 AWS CodePipeline、AWS CodeBuild 和 AWS CodeDeploy 构建持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）基础设施。在 CodeCommit 中，开发 团队最近合并了一些未通过代码库中长期运行测试的拉取请求。开发团队需要对代码库中的分支执行回 滚操作，导致浪费了时间和精力。 DevOps 工程师必须在 CodeCommit 中实现对拉取请求的自动化测试，以便审阅者在审查拉取请求时能 更轻松地查看自动化测试的结果。 开发运维工程师应该怎么做才能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to the pullRequestStatusChanged event. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes a CodePipeline pipeline with a CodeBuild action that runs the tests for the application. Program the Lambda function to post the CodeBuild badge as a comment on the pull request so that developers will see the badge in their code review.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to the pullRequestCreated event. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes a CodePipeline pipeline with a CodeBuild action that runs the tests for the application. Program the Lambda function to post the CodeBuild test results as a comment on the pull request when the test results are complete.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to pullRequestCreated and pullRequestSourceBranchUpdated events. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes a CodePipeline pipeline with a CodeBuild action that runs the tests for the application. Program the Lambda function to post the CodeBuild badge as a comment on the pull request so that developers will see the badge in their code review.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to the pullRequestStatusChanged event. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes a CodePipeline pipeline with a CodeBuild action that runs the tests for the application. Program the Lambda function to post the CodeBuild test results as a comment on the pull request when the test results are complete."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 pullRequestStatusChanged 事件做出响应。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用具有 CodeBuild 操作的 CodePipeline 管道，以运行应用程序的测试。编写 Lambda 函数，使其将 CodeBuild 徽章作为评论发布在拉取请求上，以便开发人员在代码审查时能看 到该徽章。","B":"创建一个亚马逊账 户 对“pullRequestCreated”事件作出响应的 EventBridge 规则。创建一个 AWS 一个 Lambda 函数，用于调用具有 CodeBuild 操作的 CodePipeline 管道，该操作会运行应用程序 的测试。编写该 Lambda 函数，使其在测试结果完成后将 CodeBuild 测试结果作为评论发布到拉 取请求中。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 pullRequestCreated 和 pullRequestSourceBranchUpdated 事件做出响应。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用具有 CodeBuild 操作的 CodePipeline 管 道，以运行应用程序的测试。编写 Lambda 函数，使其将 CodeBuild 徽章作为评论发布到拉取请求 中，以便开发人员在代码审查时能看到该徽章。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 pullRequestStatusChanged 事件做出响应。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用具有 CodeBuild 操作的 CodePipeline 管道，以运行应用程序的测 试。编写 Lambda 函数，使其在测试结果完成后将 CodeBuild 测试结果作为评论发布到拉取请求 中。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The recurring problem is that code which failed long-running tests kept getting merged, including commits pushed to a pull request AFTER it was opened, forcing rollbacks. To prevent this, the tests must run both when a PR is first created and every time the source branch receives new commits. Per the CodeCommit EventBridge events reference, pullRequestCreated fires once at PR creation, and pullRequestSourceBranchUpdated fires when 'one or more commits' are added to the source branch of an open PR. Only option C subscribes to BOTH events, giving full coverage so later commits are re-tested before merge. pullRequestStatusChanged (A and D) is the wrong trigger: the doc example shows it firing on a status transition such as Open to Closed, so it does not run tests on creation or on new commits before review/merge. Option B triggers only on pullRequestCreated, so commits pushed after the PR is opened are never re-tested, leaving the exact described failure mode open. C's CodeBuild build badge (PASSING/FAILING/IN_PROGRESS/UNKNOWN for the most recent branch build) is an AWS-documented way to surface automated build/test status in the source repository, so reviewers can see pass/fail as part of the review. Because the primary business problem is untested code being merged, correct event coverage is the load-bearing, non-negotiable factor, making C the best single answer.","explanation_zh":"反覆出現的問題是未通過長時間測試的程式碼一直被合併，且包含在 pull request 開啟之後才推送的 commit，導致必須回滾。要避免這種情況，測試必須在 PR 建立時、以及每次 source branch 收到新 commit 時都執行。根據 CodeCommit 的 EventBridge events 參考文件，pullRequestCreated 只在 PR 建立時觸發一次，而 pullRequestSourceBranchUpdated 會在開啟中的 PR 其 source branch 被加入「一個或多個 commit」時觸發。只有選項 C 同時訂閱這兩個事件，提供完整覆蓋，使後續 commit 在合併前都被重新測試。pullRequestStatusChanged（A 與 D）是錯誤的觸發器：文件範例顯示它在狀態轉換（例如 Open 變為 Closed）時觸發，因此不會在建立時或新 commit 時於審查/合併前執行測試。選項 B 只在 pullRequestCreated 時觸發，因此 PR 開啟之後推送的 commit 永遠不會被重新測試，正好留下題目所述的失敗情境。C 使用的 CodeBuild build badge（顯示最近一次分支建置的 PASSING/FAILING/IN_PROGRESS/UNKNOWN）是 AWS 文件記載、用於在 source repository 中呈現自動化建置/測試狀態的方式，讓審查者能在審查中看到通過或失敗。由於主要的業務問題是未測試的程式碼被合併，正確的事件覆蓋是關鍵且不可妥協的因素，因此 C 是最佳的單一答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Reacts only to pullRequestStatusChanged, which the CodeCommit events doc shows firing on status transitions such as Open to Closed/Merged. It would not run tests when a PR is created or when new commits are added, so failing code would not be caught before review or merge.","why_zh":"只回應 pullRequestStatusChanged，CodeCommit 事件文件顯示它在狀態轉換（如 Open 變為 Closed/Merged）時觸發。它不會在 PR 建立時或加入新 commit 時執行測試，因此無法在審查或合併前攔截失敗的程式碼。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Triggers only on pullRequestCreated, so commits pushed to the source branch after the PR is opened are never re-tested. This leaves the exact described failure mode (later commits that fail tests getting merged) unaddressed, even though posting actual test results is otherwise a good approach.","why_zh":"只在 pullRequestCreated 時觸發，因此 PR 開啟後推送到 source branch 的 commit 永遠不會被重新測試。雖然張貼實際測試結果是不錯的做法，但這仍未解決題目所述的失敗情境（之後加入且未通過測試的 commit 被合併）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses pullRequestStatusChanged as the trigger, which fires on status transitions (e.g., Open to Closed) rather than at creation or on new commits. Tests would run at the wrong time and not before review/merge, so it fails to prevent merging code that did not pass tests, despite posting test results.","why_zh":"使用 pullRequestStatusChanged 作為觸發器，它在狀態轉換（例如 Open 變為 Closed）時觸發，而非在建立或新 commit 時。測試會在錯誤的時間執行，且不在審查/合併之前，因此即使有張貼測試結果，仍無法避免合併未通過測試的程式碼。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/monitoring-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codecommit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/badge-statuses.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/publish-badges.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/v1/reference/codecommit/post-comment-for-pull-request.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":55,"question_en":"A company has deployed an application in a production VPC in a single AWS account. The application is popular and is experiencing heavy usage. The company’s security team wants to add additional security, such as AWS WAF, to the application deployment. However, the application's product manager is concerned about cost and does not want to approve the change unless the security team can prove that additional security is necessary. The security team believes that some of the application's demand might come from users that have IP addresses that are on a deny list. The security team provides the deny list to a DevOps engineer. If any of the IP addresses on the deny list access the application, the security team wants to receive automated notification in near real time so that the security team can document that the application needs additional security. The DevOps engineer creates a VPC flow log for the production VPC. Which set of additional steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements MOST cost- effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司在其单个 AWS 账户中的生产 VPC 中部署了一个应用程序。该应用程序很受欢迎，使用量 很大。公司的安全团队希望为应用程序部署添加额外的安全措施，例如 AWS WAF。然而，该应用程 序的产品经理担心成本问题，除非安全团队能够证明额外的安全措施是必要的，否则不会批准这一 变更。 安全团队认为，该应用程序的部分请求可能来自被列入拒绝访问列表的用户。安全团队将拒绝访问列 表提供给了一位 DevOps 工程师。如果拒绝访问列表中的任何 IP 地址访问该应用程序，安全团队希望 在近乎实时的情况下收到自动通知，以便安全团队能够记录该应用程序需要额外的安全措施。DevOps 工程师为生产 VPC 创建了 VPC 流日志。 为了以最经济高效的方式满足这些要求，DevOps 工程师应采取哪一组额外步骤？","options_en":{"A":"Create a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Configure the VPC flow log to capture accepted traffic and to send the data to the log group. Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric filter for IP addresses on the deny list. Create a CloudWatch alarm with the metric filter as input. Set the period to 5 minutes and the datapoints to alarm to 1. Use an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send alarm notices to the security team.","B":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket for log files. Configure the VPC flow log to capture all traffic and to send the data to the S3 bucket. Configure Amazon Athena to return all log files in the S3 bucket for IP addresses on the deny list. Configure Amazon QuickSight to accept data from Athena and to publish the data as a dashboard that the security team can access. Create a threshold alert of 1 for successful access. Configure the alert to automatically notify the security team as frequently as possible when the alert threshold is met.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket for log files. Configure the VPC flow log to capture accepted traffic and to send the data to the S3 bucket. Configure an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster and domain for the log files. Create an AWS Lambda function to retrieve the logs from the S3 bucket, format the logs, and load the logs into the OpenSearch Service cluster. Schedule the Lambda function to run every 5 minutes. Configure an alert and condition in OpenSearch Service to send alerts to the security team through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when access from the IP addresses on the deny list is detected.","D":"Create a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to hold query results. Configure the VPC flow log to capture all traffic and to send the data to the log group. Deploy an Amazon Athena CloudWatch connector in AWS Lambda. Connect the connector to the log group. Configure Athena to periodically query for all accepted traffic from the IP addresses on the deny list and to store the results in the S3 bucket. Configure an S3 event notification to automatically notify the security team through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when new objects are added to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个日志组。配置 VPC 流日志以捕获已接受的流量，并将数据 发送到该日志组。为拒绝列表中的 IP 地址创建一个 CloudWatch 指标过滤器。使用该指标过滤器 作为输入创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。将周期设置为 5 分钟，将触发警报的数据点设置为 1。使用 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题向安全团队发送警报通知。","B":"创建一个用于日志文件的 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 VPC 流日志以捕获所有流量，并将数据发送到 该 S3 存储桶。配置 Amazon Athena 以返回 S3 存储桶中所有列入拒绝列表的 IP 地址的日志文件。 配置 Amazon QuickSight 以接受来自 Athena 的数据，并将数据发布为安全团队可访问的仪表板。 设置成功访问的阈值警报为 1。配置警报，使其在达到警报阈值时尽可能频繁地自动通知安全团 队。","C":"创建一个用于日志文件的 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 VPC 流日志以捕获已接受的流量，并将数据发 送到 S3 存储桶。配置一个用于日志文件的 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群和域。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于从 S3 存储桶中检索日志，格式化日志，并将日志加载到 OpenSearch Service 集 群中。安排该 Lambda 函数每 5 分钟运行一次。在 OpenSearch Service 中配置警报和条件，当检测 到来自拒绝列表中的 IP 地址的访问时，通过 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题向安全团队发送警报。","D":"在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个日志组。创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶来保存查询结果。配置 VPC 流日志以捕获所有流量，并将数据发送到日志组。在 AWS Lambda 中部署一个 Amazon Athena CloudWatch 连接器。将连接器连接到日志组。配置 Athena 定期查询拒绝列表中 IP 地址的 所有已接受流量，并将结果存储在 S3 存储桶中。配置 S3 事件通知，当有新对象添加到 S3 存储桶 时，通过 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题自动通知安全团队。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is near-real-time, automated notification when deny-list IPs access the application, done MOST cost-effectively. Option A is exactly the pattern AWS documents in 'Process flow log records in CloudWatch Logs': publish VPC flow logs to a CloudWatch Logs log group, create a metric filter that matches the target traffic pattern (the AWS example matches REJECT SSH; here it matches the deny-list IPs in the source field), create a CloudWatch alarm on that metric, and notify via an SNS topic. Metric filters convert log data into metrics as the logs arrive, and a 5-minute period with datapoints-to-alarm of 1 fires on a single matching event, giving near-real-time alerting. Capturing accepted traffic is correct because, with no WAF yet, deny-list users actually reach the application, so the team must prove that access on accepted traffic. This solution is fully serverless and uses only a CloudWatch Logs metric filter, a CloudWatch alarm, and an SNS topic, making it the cheapest of the four options. The other options layer on Athena, QuickSight, or an always-on OpenSearch cluster, which add cost and reduce timeliness.","explanation_zh":"需求是當拒絕清單上的 IP 存取應用程式時，以最具成本效益的方式提供近即時的自動通知。選項 A 正是 AWS 文件「Process flow log records in CloudWatch Logs」所記載的模式：將 VPC flow logs 發佈到 CloudWatch Logs log group，建立比對目標流量模式的 metric filter（AWS 範例比對 REJECT SSH，本題比對 source 欄位中拒絕清單的 IP），對該 metric 建立 CloudWatch alarm，並透過 SNS topic 通知。Metric filter 會在日誌送達時即時將日誌資料轉為 metric，搭配週期 5 分鐘、datapoints to alarm 設為 1，可在單一符合事件時近即時告警。擷取已接受 (accepted) 流量是正確的，因為目前尚未有 WAF，拒絕清單的使用者確實會抵達應用程式，因此團隊必須證明這些已接受流量上的存取行為。此方案完全 serverless，只用到 CloudWatch Logs metric filter、CloudWatch alarm 與 SNS topic，是四個選項中最便宜的。其他選項加上了 Athena、QuickSight 或常駐的 OpenSearch 叢集，既增加成本又降低即時性。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Athena + QuickSight is a batch analytics / BI dashboard pipeline, not near-real-time alerting. QuickSight threshold alerts are not designed for near-real-time security notifications, and QuickSight is an expensive BI service requiring user subscriptions. This is neither timely nor cost-effective.","why_zh":"Athena + QuickSight 是批次分析/BI 儀表板管線，並非近即時告警。QuickSight 閾值警示並非為近即時安全通知設計，且 QuickSight 是需要使用者訂閱的昂貴 BI 服務。既不即時也不具成本效益。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster runs 24/7 and is the most expensive option here; adding a Lambda that runs every 5 minutes to pull logs from S3, format them, and load them into the cluster adds operational overhead and latency. This contradicts the MOST cost-effective requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon OpenSearch Service 叢集需 24/7 持續運行，是此處最昂貴的選項；再加上每 5 分鐘從 S3 拉取、格式化並載入日誌的 Lambda，增加維運負擔與延遲。這違背最具成本效益的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using the Athena CloudWatch (federated query) connector via Lambda, periodic Athena queries, an S3 results bucket, and S3 event notifications is far more complex and costly than a native metric filter. Periodic Athena queries are batch, not near real time, and capturing all traffic increases ingestion cost.","why_zh":"透過 Lambda 使用 Athena CloudWatch（聯合查詢）連接器、定期 Athena 查詢、S3 結果儲存桶與 S3 事件通知，遠比原生 metric filter 更複雜且昂貴。定期 Athena 查詢屬批次處理，並非近即時，且擷取所有流量會增加擷取成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/process-records-cwl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs-cwl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":56,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer has automated a web service deployment by using AWS CodePipeline with the following steps: 1. An AWS CodeBuild project compiles the deployment artifact and runs unit tests. 2. An AWS CodeDeploy deployment group deploys the web service to Amazon EC2 instances in the staging environment. 3. A CodeDeploy deployment group deploys the web service to EC2 instances in the production environment. The quality assurance (QA) team requests permission to inspect the build artifact before the deployment to the production environment occurs. The QA team wants to run an internal penetration testing tool to conduct manual tests. The tool will be invoked by a REST API call. Which combination of actions should the DevOps engineer take to fulfill this request? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师通过使用 AWS CodePipeline 自动化了一个 Web 服务的部署，具体步骤如下： 1. 一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目会编译部署工件并运行单元测试。 2. AWS CodeDeploy 部署组将 Web 服务部署到预生产环境中的 Amazon EC2 实例上。 3. 一个 CodeDeploy 部署组将网络服务部署到生产环境中的 EC2 实例上。 质量保证（QA）团队请求在部署到生产环境之前检查构建工件。QA 团队希望运行一个内部渗透测试工 具来进行手动测试。该工具将通过 REST API 调用进行调用。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪两种组合操作来满足此请求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Insert a manual approval action between the test actions and deployment actions of the pipeline.","B":"Modify the buildspec.yml file for the compilation stage to require manual approval before completion.","C":"Update the CodeDeploy deployment groups so that they require manual approval to proceed.","D":"Update the pipeline to directly call the REST API for the penetration testing tool.","E":"Update the pipeline to invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls the REST API for the penetration testing tool."},"options_zh":{"A":"在流水线的测试操作和部署操作之间插入一个手动审批操作。","B":"修改用于编译阶段的 buildspec.yml 文件，使其在完成前需要人工审批。","C":"更新 CodeDeploy 部署组，使其在继续执行前需要手动审批。","D":"更新管道，使其直接调用渗透测试工具的 REST API。","E":"更新管道以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会调用渗透测试工具的 REST API。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must be met: pause the pipeline before production so the QA team can inspect the build artifact, and trigger an external penetration-testing tool via a REST API call. A manual approval action (A) is the exact CodePipeline construct for this; AWS docs state you use manual approvals when 'you want someone to perform manual quality assurance testing on the latest version of an application, or to confirm the integrity of a build artifact, before it is released.' Placed between the staging actions and the production deploy action, it stops execution until an authorized IAM approver approves. CodePipeline's built-in action categories are only Source, Build, Test, Deploy, Approval, and Invoke, so there is no native action that directly calls an arbitrary external REST API; the documented pattern is a Lambda invoke action (E), since the docs say Lambda lets you 'perform almost any task' and explicitly list 'To add integration with third-party products to your pipeline' as a use case. The Lambda function calls the pen-testing tool's REST API. Together, the approval gate plus the Lambda-invoked REST call satisfy both requirements.","explanation_zh":"需滿足兩項需求：在進入 production 前暫停 pipeline，讓 QA 團隊檢查 build artifact；以及透過 REST API 觸發外部滲透測試工具。Manual approval action (A) 正是 CodePipeline 為此設計的機制；AWS 文件指出，當你希望有人『對應用程式最新版本執行手動品質保證測試，或在發行前確認 build artifact 的完整性』時即可使用 manual approval。把它放在 staging 動作與 production 部署動作之間，會讓執行暫停直到授權的 IAM 核准者核准。CodePipeline 的內建 action 類別僅有 Source、Build、Test、Deploy、Approval 與 Invoke，故沒有可直接呼叫任意外部 REST API 的原生 action；文件記載的標準做法是使用 Lambda invoke action (E)，因為文件說明 Lambda 可『執行幾乎任何任務』，並明列『為 pipeline 加入與第三方產品的整合』作為用途。由 Lambda function 呼叫滲透測試工具的 REST API。核准關卡加上由 Lambda 觸發的 REST 呼叫，正好滿足兩項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeBuild's buildspec.yml has no manual-approval mechanism. Buildspec only defines build phases (install, pre_build, build, post_build) and commands; pausing for human approval is a pipeline-level construct (manual approval action), not a build-phase feature. It is also at the wrong place (compilation stage, not before production), and it does not invoke the pen-testing REST API.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 的 buildspec.yml 沒有手動核准機制。Buildspec 僅定義 build 階段（install、pre_build、build、post_build）與指令；等待人工核准是 pipeline 層級的 manual approval action，而非 build 階段功能。位置也不對（在編譯階段，而非 production 前），且不會呼叫滲透測試的 REST API。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeDeploy deployment groups have no 'require manual approval to proceed' setting. Deployment group settings cover deployment type, target instances/tags, traffic shifting, CloudWatch alarms, load balancers, and Auto Scaling groups. Human approval gating is provided by CodePipeline manual approval actions, not by a deployment group property, and this option does nothing to invoke the pen-testing tool.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy deployment group 沒有『需手動核准才能繼續』的設定。Deployment group 設定涵蓋部署類型、目標執行個體/標籤、流量轉移、CloudWatch 警示、負載平衡器與 Auto Scaling group。人工核准關卡由 CodePipeline 的 manual approval action 提供，而非 deployment group 屬性，且此選項也無法觸發滲透測試工具。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodePipeline has no native action type that directly calls an arbitrary external REST API. Built-in action categories are only Source, Build, Test, Deploy, Approval, and Invoke. To call a third-party REST API you must wrap it in a Lambda invoke action (E) or a custom action with a job worker, so a 'direct' call from the pipeline is not possible.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 沒有可直接呼叫任意外部 REST API 的原生 action type。內建 action 類別僅有 Source、Build、Test、Deploy、Approval 與 Invoke。要呼叫第三方 REST API 必須用 Lambda invoke action (E) 或自訂 action 搭配 job worker 包裝，故無法從 pipeline『直接』呼叫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-invoke-lambda-function.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-edit.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":57,"question_en":"A company is hosting a web application in an AWS Region. For disaster recovery purposes, a second region is being used as a standby. Disaster recovery requirements state that session data must be replicated between regions in near-real time and 1% of requests should route to the secondary region to continuously verify system functionality. Additionally, if there is a disruption in service in the main region, traffic should be automatically routed to the secondary region, and the secondary region must be able to scale up to handle all traffic. How should a DevOps engineer meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 区域中托管一个网络应用程序。出于灾难恢复的目的，另一个区域被用作备用区 域。灾难恢复要求规定会话数据必须在近实时状态下在两个区域之间进行复制，并且 1% 的请求应路 由到备用区域以持续验证系统功能。此外，如果主区域的服务出现中断，流量应自动路由到备用区域， 并且备用区域必须能够扩展以处理所有流量。 DevOps 工程师应如何满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In both regions, deploy the application on AWS Elastic Beanstalk and use Amazon DynamoDB global tables for session data. Use an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy with health checks to distribute the traffic across the regions.","B":"In both regions, launch the application in Auto Scaling groups and use DynamoDB for session data. Use a Route 53 failover routing policy with health checks to distribute the traffic across the regions.","C":"In both regions, deploy the application in AWS Lambda, exposed by Amazon API Gateway, and use Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL with cross-region replication for session data. Deploy the web application with client-side logic to call the API Gateway directly.","D":"In both regions, launch the application in Auto Scaling groups and use DynamoDB global tables for session data. Enable an Amazon CloudFront weighted distribution across regions. Point the Amazon Route 53 DNS record at the CloudFront distribution."},"options_zh":{"A":"在两个区域中，均在 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 上部署应用程序，并使用 Amazon DynamoDB 全球表来 存储会话数据。使用带有健康检查的 Amazon Route 53 加权路由策略在两个区域之间分配流量。","B":"在两个区域中，以自动扩展组的形式启动应用程序，并使用 DynamoDB 存储会话数据。采用带有 健康检查的 Route 53 故障转移路由策略，在两个区域之间分配流量。","C":"在两个区域中，将应用程序部署在 AWS Lambda 中，通过 Amazon API Gateway 进行公开，并使用 具有跨区域复制功能的 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 来存储会话数据。将包含客户端逻辑的 Web 应用程序部署为直接调用 API Gateway。","D":"在两个区域中，以自动扩展组的形式启动应用程序，并使用 DynamoDB 全球表来存储会话数据。 在各区域启用 Amazon CloudFront 加权分发。将 Amazon Route 53 DNS 记录指向 CloudFront 分发。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"All four requirements are satisfied only by A. (1) Near-real-time cross-region session replication requires DynamoDB global tables (multi-active, asynchronous near-real-time replication); plain regional DynamoDB in option B does not replicate across regions. (2) Routing exactly 1% of requests to the secondary region requires a Route 53 weighted routing policy (e.g., weights 99/1) — a failover routing policy (B) sends 0% to the standby until the primary fails and cannot do a percentage split, and CloudFront has no 'weighted distribution across regions' feature (D); CloudFront origin groups only do primary-to-secondary failover, not percentage weighting. (3) Automatic failover is achieved by attaching health checks to the weighted records: AWS docs state you configure active-active failover using any routing policy other than failover, and Route 53 stops returning unhealthy records. (4) The secondary region must scale to full traffic — Elastic Beanstalk runs on Auto Scaling groups, so it can scale up. Thus A uniquely covers replication, the 1% split, automatic health-check failover, and scaling.","explanation_zh":"只有 A 同時滿足四項需求。(1) 跨區域近即時的 session 複寫需要 DynamoDB global tables（multi-active、非同步近即時複寫）；選項 B 的單一區域 DynamoDB 不會跨區複寫。(2) 將恰好 1% 流量導向次要區域需要 Route 53 weighted routing policy（例如權重 99/1）——failover routing policy（B）在主要區域故障前對備援送出 0%，無法做百分比分流；CloudFront 也沒有所謂『跨區域 weighted distribution』功能（D），CloudFront origin groups 只能做主要對次要的故障切換，不能依百分比分流。(3) 自動故障切換靠在 weighted records 上附加 health checks 達成：AWS 文件指出可用 failover 以外的任何 routing policy 設定 active-active failover，Route 53 會停止回傳不健康的記錄。(4) 次要區域需能擴展到承載全部流量——Elastic Beanstalk 底層使用 Auto Scaling groups，可向上擴展。因此 A 是唯一同時涵蓋複寫、1% 分流、health-check 自動切換與擴展的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Two failures: regional (non-global) DynamoDB does not replicate session data across regions, and a Route 53 failover routing policy sends 100% to primary / 0% to secondary until failover, so it cannot route 1% of requests for continuous verification.","why_zh":"兩處錯誤：區域型（非 global）DynamoDB 不會跨區複寫 session；且 Route 53 failover routing policy 在切換前對主要送 100%、對次要送 0%，無法導 1% 流量做持續驗證。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"RDS for PostgreSQL cross-region replication is asynchronous (not the near-real-time multi-active session store implied) and writes only go to the primary, breaking active-active session use; more critically the design specifies no mechanism to split 1% of traffic or to fail over between regions.","why_zh":"RDS for PostgreSQL 跨區複寫為非同步（非題目要求的近即時 multi-active session 儲存），且寫入只在主庫，破壞 active-active 的 session 使用；更關鍵是此設計完全沒有描述如何分流 1% 或在區域間故障切換。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses a non-existent feature: CloudFront has no 'weighted distribution across regions'. CloudFront origin groups provide only primary-to-secondary origin failover, not percentage-weighted (1%) traffic distribution, so the continuous-verification requirement cannot be met.","why_zh":"使用不存在的功能：CloudFront 沒有『跨區域 weighted distribution』。CloudFront origin groups 只提供主要對次要的來源故障切換，無法做百分比（1%）加權分流，因此無法滿足持續驗證的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-weighted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":58,"question_en":"A company runs an application on Amazon EC2 instances. The company uses a series of AWS CloudFormation stacks to define the application resources. A developer performs updates by building and testing the application on a laptop and then uploading the build output and CloudFormation stack templates to Amazon S3. The developer's peers review the changes before the developer performs the CloudFormation stack update and installs a new version of the application onto the EC2 instances. The deployment process is prone to errors and is time-consuming when the developer updates each EC2 instance with the new application. The company wants to automate as much of the application deployment process as possible while retaining a final manual approval step before the modification of the application or resources. The company already has moved the source code for the application and the CloudFormation templates to AWS CodeCommit. The company also has created an AWS CodeBuild project to build and test the application. Which combination of steps will meet the company’s requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行应用程序。该公司使用一系列 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来定义应用 程序资源。开发人员在笔记本电脑上构建和测试应用程序，然后将构建输出和 CloudFormation 堆栈模板 上传到亚马逊 S3。开发人员的同事会先审查这些更改，之后开发人员才会执行 CloudFormation 堆栈更新， 并在 EC2 实例上安装应用程序的新版本。 当开发人员使用新应用程序更新每个 EC2 实例时，部署过程容易出错且耗时。该公司希望尽可能多地实 现应用程序部署过程的自动化，同时在修改应用程序或资源之前保留最终的手动审批步骤。 该公司已将应用程序的源代码和 CloudFormation 模板迁移到 AWS CodeCommit。该公司还创建了一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建和测试该应用程序。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足公司的要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an application group and a deployment group in AWS CodeDeploy. Install the CodeDeploy agent on the EC2 instances.","B":"Create an application revision and a deployment group in AWS CodeDeploy. Create an environment in CodeDeploy. Register the EC2 instances to the CodeDeploy environment.","C":"Use AWS CodePipeline to invoke the CodeBuild job, run the CloudFormation update, and pause for a manual approval step. After approval, start the AWS CodeDeploy deployment.","D":"Use AWS CodePipeline to invoke the CodeBuild job, create CloudFormation change sets for each of the application stacks, and pause for a manual approval step. After approval, run the CloudFormation change sets and start the AWS CodeDeploy deployment.","E":"Use AWS CodePipeline to invoke the CodeBuild job, create CloudFormation change sets for each of the application stacks, and pause for a manual approval step. After approval, start the AWS CodeDeploy deployment."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CodeDeploy 中创建一个应用组和一个部署组。在 EC2 实例上安装 CodeDeploy 代理。","B":"在 AWS CodeDeploy 中创建应用修订版和部署组。在 CodeDeploy 中创建环境。将 EC2 实例注册到 CodeDeploy 环境。","C":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 调用 CodeBuild 任务，运行 CloudFormation 更新，并暂停以等待人工审批步 骤。审批通过后，启动 AWS CodeDeploy 部署。","D":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 调用 CodeBuild 任务，为每个应用程序堆栈创建 CloudFormation 更改集，并 暂停以等待手动审批步骤。审批通过后，运行 CloudFormation 更改集并启动 AWS CodeDeploy 部署。","E":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 调用 CodeBuild 作业，为每个应用程序堆栈创建 CloudFormation 更改集，并 暂停以等待手动审批步骤。审批通过后，启动 AWS CodeDeploy 部署。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The company needs CodePipeline to orchestrate build (CodeBuild), CloudFormation stack updates, a final manual approval before any modification, and CodeDeploy to push the app to EC2. Option D is correct because CodePipeline first creates CloudFormation change sets (CHANGE_SET_REPLACE), which only preview changes without altering the stack, then pauses for manual approval, and only after approval executes the change sets (CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE) and starts the CodeDeploy deployment. This satisfies 'final manual approval before modification of the application or resources' and still actually applies the stack changes. Option A is the correct CodeDeploy setup: a deployment group plus the CodeDeploy agent installed on the EC2 instances is exactly what an EC2/On-Premises deployment requires. Although A says 'application group' instead of the precise term 'application', it pairs the correct 'deployment group' with the required agent install, whereas the other CodeDeploy option invents an 'environment' concept that does not exist in CodeDeploy.","explanation_zh":"此情境需要 CodePipeline 來協調建置 (CodeBuild)、CloudFormation 堆疊更新、在任何變更前的最終手動核准,以及用 CodeDeploy 將應用程式部署到 EC2。選項 D 正確,因為 CodePipeline 先建立 CloudFormation change set (CHANGE_SET_REPLACE),這只是預覽變更而不會改動堆疊,接著暫停等待手動核准,核准後才執行 change set (CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE) 並啟動 CodeDeploy 部署。這同時滿足『在修改應用程式或資源前進行最終手動核准』,又確實套用了堆疊變更。選項 A 是正確的 CodeDeploy 設定:deployment group 加上在 EC2 執行個體安裝 CodeDeploy agent,正是 EC2/On-Premises 部署所需。雖然 A 用了『application group』而非精確的『application』,但它把正確的『deployment group』與必要的 agent 安裝配在一起;另一個 CodeDeploy 選項則杜撰了 CodeDeploy 並不存在的『environment』概念。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeDeploy has no 'environment' concept and you do not 'register EC2 instances to a CodeDeploy environment'. CodeDeploy primary components are application, deployment group, deployment configuration, and revision; instances are matched to a deployment group via EC2 tags or Auto Scaling groups, not a registered environment. Also it omits installing the CodeDeploy agent.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 沒有『environment』概念,也不會『將 EC2 執行個體註冊到 CodeDeploy environment』。CodeDeploy 的主要元件是 application、deployment group、deployment configuration 與 revision;執行個體是透過 EC2 標籤或 Auto Scaling group 對應到 deployment group,而非註冊到 environment,且此選項也漏掉安裝 CodeDeploy agent。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It runs the CloudFormation update FIRST and then pauses for approval, which modifies the stack resources before the manual approval. This directly violates the requirement to keep a final manual approval step before any modification of the application or resources.","why_zh":"它先執行 CloudFormation 更新,然後才暫停等待核准,這會在手動核准之前就修改堆疊資源,直接違反『在任何應用程式或資源修改前保留最終手動核准步驟』的要求。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"It creates the change sets and approves, but after approval only starts the CodeDeploy deployment and never executes the CloudFormation change sets (CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE). The stack resource changes would therefore never be applied, leaving the infrastructure updates incomplete.","why_zh":"它建立了 change set 並核准,但核准後只啟動 CodeDeploy 部署,卻從未執行 CloudFormation change set (CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE)。因此堆疊資源變更永遠不會被套用,導致基礎設施更新不完整。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CloudFormation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/primary-components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/codedeploy-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-updating-stacks-changesets-execute.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":59,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages a web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The instances run in an EC2 Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. The engineer needs to implement a deployment strategy that: Launches a second fleet of instances with the same capacity as the original fleet. Maintains the original fleet unchanged while the second fleet is launched. Transitions traffic to the second fleet when the second fleet is fully deployed. Terminates the original fleet automatically 1 hour after transition. Which solution will satisfy these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师负责管理一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的网络应用程序，这些实例位于应用负载均 衡器（ALB）之后。这些实例在多个可用区的 EC2 自动扩展组中运行。该工程师需要实施一种部署策略， 该策略： 启动与原实例舰队容量相同的第二支实例舰队。 在维持原有舰队不变的情况下，第二支舰队也已启航。 当第二舰队完全部署完毕时，将交通转至第二舰队。 在转换后 1 小时自动终止原舰队。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS CloudFormation template with a retention policy for the ALB set to 1 hour. Update the Amazon Route 53 record to reflect the new ALB.","B":"Use two AWS Elastic Beanstalk environments to perform a blue/green deployment from the original environment to the new one. Create an application version lifecycle policy to terminate the original environment in 1 hour.","C":"Use AWS CodeDeploy with a deployment group configured with a blue/green deployment configuration Select the option Terminate the original instances in the deployment group with a waiting period of 1 hour.","D":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk with the configuration set to Immutable. Create an .ebextension using the Resources key that sets the deletion policy of the ALB to 1 hour, and deploy the application."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用带有保留策略的 AWS CloudFormation 模板，将 ALB 的保留时间设置为 1 小时。更新 Amazon Route 53 记录以反映新的 ALB。","B":"使用两个 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 环境执行从原始环境到新环境的蓝/绿部署。创建一个应用版本生命 周期策略，在 1 小时后终止原始环境。","C":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 并配置具有蓝/绿部署配置的部署组 选择“在部署组中终止原始实例并设置 1 小 时等待期”这一选项。","D":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 并将配置设置为不可变。使用 Resources 键创建一个 .ebextension，将 ALB 的删除策略设置为 1 小时，然后部署应用程序。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is a textbook EC2/On-Premises blue/green deployment with AWS CodeDeploy. Choosing 'Automatically copy Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group' launches a replacement (green) fleet with the same number of healthy instances as the original (blue) fleet, while the original fleet keeps running unchanged. When the replacement instances are provisioned, healthy, and registered with the ALB target group, CodeDeploy reroutes traffic from blue to green. The 'Original instances' setting 'Terminate the original instances in the deployment group' (BlueInstanceTerminationOption Action=TERMINATE) terminates the deregistered original instances after a wait period you specify (TerminationWaitTimeInMinutes), which can be set to 60 minutes = 1 hour. All four requirements map directly onto native CodeDeploy options, so C is correct.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS CodeDeploy 經典的 EC2/On-Premises 藍綠部署情境。選擇「Automatically copy Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group」會以與原始（藍色）車隊相同數量的健康執行個體建立替換（綠色）車隊，同時原始車隊維持不變繼續運行。當替換執行個體佈建完成、通過健康檢查並註冊到 ALB target group 後，CodeDeploy 會把流量從藍色切換到綠色。在「Original instances」設定中選擇「Terminate the original instances in the deployment group」（即 BlueInstanceTerminationOption 的 Action=TERMINATE），會在你指定的等待期間（TerminationWaitTimeInMinutes，可設為 60 分鐘 = 1 小時）之後終止已取消註冊的原始執行個體。四項需求都對應到 CodeDeploy 的原生選項，因此 C 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation DeletionPolicy values are Retain, Delete, Snapshot, and RetainExceptOnCreate — there is no time-based '1 hour retention policy' for an ALB. CloudFormation cannot launch a parallel same-capacity fleet, hold both, reroute traffic, then auto-terminate the old fleet after exactly 1 hour. This is invented behavior.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 的 DeletionPolicy 只有 Retain、Delete、Snapshot、RetainExceptOnCreate，並沒有針對 ALB 的「1 小時時間性保留政策」。CloudFormation 無法自動啟動同容量的平行車隊、同時保留兩者、切換流量後再於恰好 1 小時後自動終止舊車隊，此為杜撰的行為。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Beanstalk blue/green (CNAME swap) does meet the swap behavior, but an 'application version lifecycle policy' controls retention of application versions (source bundles in S3), not the termination of an environment. There is no Beanstalk feature that terminates the original environment automatically 1 hour after the swap.","why_zh":"Beanstalk 藍綠部署（CNAME 交換）確實符合切換行為，但「application version lifecycle policy」管理的是應用程式版本（S3 中的原始程式套件）的保留，而非終止環境。Beanstalk 並沒有可在交換後 1 小時自動終止原始環境的功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Beanstalk Immutable updates do NOT keep the original fleet running for a swap — they launch a temporary second ASG, and once new instances are healthy they are moved into the original ASG and the temporary group is removed; it is not a blue/green traffic transition with a 1-hour delayed teardown. Also, an .ebextension cannot set a time-based 'deletion policy of the ALB to 1 hour'; DeletionPolicy is not time-based.","why_zh":"Beanstalk Immutable 更新並不會為了切換而保留原始車隊運行——它會啟動一個暫時的第二 ASG，待新執行個體健康後將其移入原始 ASG 並移除暫時群組；這不是帶有 1 小時延遲拆除的藍綠流量切換。此外，.ebextension 無法將「ALB 的 deletion policy 設為 1 小時」，DeletionPolicy 並非時間性設定。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-create-blue-green.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codedeploy-deploymentgroup-blueinstanceterminationoption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/environmentmgmt-updates-immutable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.CNAMESwap.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":60,"question_en":"A video-sharing company stores its videos in Amazon S3. The company has observed a sudden increase in video access requests, but the company does not know which videos are most popular. The company needs to identify the general access pattern for the video files. This pattern includes the number of users who access a certain file on a given day, as well as the number of pull requests for certain files. How can the company meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of effort?","question_zh":"一家视频分享公司将其视频存储在亚马逊 S3 上。该公司注意到视频访问请求突然增多，但并不清楚哪些视 频最受欢迎。该公司需要确定视频文件的一般访问模式。这种模式包括在给定的一天内访问特定文件的用 户数量以及对某些文件的拉取请求数量。 公司怎样才能以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Activate S3 server access logging. Import the access logs into an Amazon Aurora database. Use an Aurora SQL query to analyze the access patterns.","B":"Activate S3 server access logging. Use Amazon Athena to create an external table with the log files. Use Athena to create a SQL query to analyze the access patterns.","C":"Invoke an AWS Lambda function for every S3 object access event. Configure the Lambda function to write the file access information, such as user. S3 bucket, and file key, to an Amazon Aurora database. Use an Aurora SQL query to analyze the access patterns.","D":"Record an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log message for every S3 object access event. Configure a CloudWatch Logs log stream to write the file access information, such as user, S3 bucket, and file key, to an Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL application. Perform a sliding window analysis."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 S3 服务器访问日志记录。将访问日志导入到 Amazon Aurora 数据库中。使用 Aurora SQL 查询来 分析访问模式。","B":"启用 S3 服务器访问日志记录。使用 Amazon Athena 创建一个包含日志文件的外部表。使用 Athena 创 建一个 SQL 查询来分析访问模式。","C":"对于每个 S3 对象访问事件，调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数，将文件访问信息（例如 用户、S3 存储桶和文件键）写入 Amazon Aurora 数据库。使用 Aurora SQL 查询来分析访问模式。","D":"对每个 S3 对象访问事件记录一条 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志消息。配置一个 CloudWatch Logs 日志 流，将文件访问信息（例如用户、S3 存储桶和文件键）写入 Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL 应 用程序。执行滑动窗口分析。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"S3 server access logging records detailed information about every request made to the bucket (requester, bucket, object key, operation such as GET/REST.GET.OBJECT, request datetime, etc.) and delivers those logs as objects into an S3 bucket. AWS's own documentation 'Using Amazon S3 server access logs to identify requests' explicitly recommends using Amazon Athena to create an EXTERNAL TABLE over the access-log files and run SQL queries to analyze them, including identifying object access requests. This is fully serverless and requires no data movement or custom code: turn on logging, create one external table, and query in place. This directly answers 'which videos are most popular,' 'number of users who access a file on a given day,' and 'number of pull (GET) requests for certain files,' and does so with the LEAST amount of effort. The qualifier LEAST effort decides between B and the alternatives that involve standing up databases or writing Lambda/streaming pipelines.","explanation_zh":"S3 server access logging 會記錄對儲存貯體的每個請求的詳細資訊（requester、bucket、物件 key、操作如 GET/REST.GET.OBJECT、請求時間等），並將這些日誌以物件形式投遞到 S3 儲存貯體中。AWS 官方文件「Using Amazon S3 server access logs to identify requests」明確建議使用 Amazon Athena 對存取日誌檔案建立 EXTERNAL TABLE 並執行 SQL 查詢來分析，包括辨識物件存取請求。此方法完全 serverless，不需搬移資料或撰寫自訂程式碼：只要開啟 logging、建立一個外部資料表，即可就地查詢。這正好回答「哪些影片最熱門」、「某天有多少使用者存取某檔案」以及「特定檔案的 pull (GET) 請求數量」，並以最少的工作量達成。題目限定詞 LEAST effort 決定了在 B 與其他需要架設資料庫或撰寫 Lambda/串流管線的選項之間的取捨。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Server access logging is correct, but importing logs into an Amazon Aurora database adds significant operational overhead: provisioning/managing a relational database and building an ingestion/ETL process to load log files. Athena queries the logs in place with no database to manage, so A is far more effort than B.","why_zh":"Server access logging 部分正確，但將日誌匯入 Amazon Aurora 資料庫會增加大量營運負擔：需要佈建/管理關聯式資料庫並建立載入日誌檔案的擷取/ETL 流程。Athena 可就地查詢日誌且無需管理資料庫，因此 A 比 B 費力得多。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Invoking a Lambda function for every object access and writing records to Aurora requires custom code, an event pipeline, and a managed database. Note S3 event notifications mainly fire on object create/delete, not on read/GET access, so this cannot reliably capture 'pull requests.' Highest effort and technically weak for read tracking.","why_zh":"對每次物件存取觸發 Lambda 並寫入 Aurora 需要自訂程式碼、事件管線與受管資料庫。注意 S3 事件通知主要在物件建立/刪除時觸發，而非讀取/GET 存取，因此無法可靠擷取「pull requests」。工作量最高且對讀取追蹤技術上不足。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Recording a CloudWatch Logs message per object access and streaming to Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL with sliding-window analysis is a complex real-time pipeline. S3 does not natively emit a log message per read event to CloudWatch Logs, so this requires custom instrumentation and is the opposite of least effort for analyzing historical access patterns.","why_zh":"為每次物件存取記錄 CloudWatch Logs 訊息並串流到 Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL 進行滑動視窗分析，是複雜的即時管線。S3 並不會原生地對每個讀取事件向 CloudWatch Logs 發送日誌訊息，因此需要自訂檢測，與分析歷史存取模式所需的最少工作量背道而馳。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-s3-access-logs-to-identify-requests.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/ServerLogs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/enable-server-access-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/what-is.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":61,"question_en":"A development team wants to use AWS CloudFormation stacks to deploy an application. However, the developer IAM role does not have the required permissions to provision the resources that are specified in the AWS CloudFormation template. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution that allows the developers to deploy the stacks. The solution must follow the principle of least privilege. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个开发团队希望使用 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来部署应用程序。然而，开发人员的 IAM 角色没有在 AWS CloudFormation 模板中指定的资源所需的权限。一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，使开发 人员能够部署这些堆栈。该解决方案必须遵循最小权限原则。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM policy that allows the developers to provision the required resources. Attach the policy to the developer IAM role.","B":"Create an IAM policy that allows full access to AWS CloudFormation. Attach the policy to the developer IAM role.","C":"Create an AWS CloudFormation service role that has the required permissions. Grant the developer IAM role a cloudformation:* action. Use the new service role during stack deployments.","D":"Create an AWS CloudFormation service role that has the required permissions. Grant the developer IAM role the iam:PassRole permission. Use the new service role during stack deployments."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 IAM 策略，允许开发人员配置所需的资源。将该策略附加到开发人员的 IAM 角色上。","B":"创建一个允许对 AWS CloudFormation 进行完全访问的 IAM 策略。将该策略附加到开发人员的 IAM 角色。","C":"创建一个具有所需权限的 AWS CloudFormation 服务角色。授予开发人员 IAM 角色 cloudformation:* 操 作权限。在堆栈部署期间使用新的服务角色。","D":"创建一个具有所需权限的 AWS CloudFormation 服务角色。授予开发人员 IAM 角色 iam:PassRole 权限。 在堆栈部署期间使用新的服务角色。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A CloudFormation service role is an IAM role that CloudFormation assumes to create/update/delete stack resources on the principal's behalf. When a service role is specified, CloudFormation uses the service role's credentials for resource operations, so the developer's own IAM role does NOT need permissions to provision the resources. This is exactly the AWS-documented least-privilege pattern: build a service role scoped to only the required actions (working backward from the template), and grant the developer principal the iam:PassRole permission so it can pass that service role to CloudFormation. AWS Prescriptive Guidance states: 'To use a service role to create CloudFormation stacks, IAM principals must have permissions to pass the service role to CloudFormation, and the trust policy of the service role must allow CloudFormation to assume the role.' Option D captures this precisely, satisfying least privilege.","explanation_zh":"CloudFormation service role 是一個 IAM 角色,CloudFormation 會代表使用者承擔(assume)該角色來建立、更新或刪除堆疊資源。當指定 service role 時,CloudFormation 會使用該 service role 的憑證來執行資源操作,因此開發人員自己的 IAM 角色不需要佈建這些資源的權限。這正是 AWS 文件記載的最小權限模式:建立一個僅限必要動作(從範本反推)的 service role,並授予開發人員 principal iam:PassRole 權限,使其能將該 service role 傳遞給 CloudFormation。AWS Prescriptive Guidance 明確指出:要使用 service role 建立 CloudFormation 堆疊,IAM principal 必須具有將 service role 傳遞給 CloudFormation 的權限,且 service role 的信任政策必須允許 CloudFormation 承擔該角色。選項 D 精確符合此模式並滿足最小權限原則。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Granting the developer role all the resource-provisioning permissions directly violates least privilege; the explicit goal is that developers should NOT hold those broad provisioning permissions, and it bypasses the standardization benefit of CloudFormation service roles.","why_zh":"直接授予開發人員角色所有資源佈建權限違反最小權限原則;明確目標是開發人員不應持有這些廣泛的佈建權限,且此做法繞過了 CloudFormation service role 的標準化好處。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Full CloudFormation access is overly broad (not least privilege), and by default CloudFormation uses the calling principal's own credentials for stack operations, so the developer would still need the underlying resource permissions. It does not actually solve the missing-permissions problem.","why_zh":"完整的 CloudFormation 存取權過於寬鬆(非最小權限),且預設情況下 CloudFormation 會使用呼叫者本身的憑證執行堆疊操作,因此開發人員仍需具備底層資源權限,並未真正解決缺少權限的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Using a service role is correct, but granting cloudformation:* is overly broad and not least privilege. More importantly, passing a service role to CloudFormation requires iam:PassRole, not cloudformation:* ; cloudformation:* alone does not authorize passing the role.","why_zh":"使用 service role 方向正確,但授予 cloudformation:* 過於寬鬆,不符合最小權限。更重要的是,將 service role 傳遞給 CloudFormation 需要 iam:PassRole,而非 cloudformation:*;單靠 cloudformation:* 無法授權傳遞該角色。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-iam-servicerole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/least-privilege-cloudformation/service-roles-for-cloudformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_passrole.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":62,"question_en":"A production account has a requirement that any Amazon EC2 instance that has been logged in to manually must be terminated within 24 hours. All applications in the production account are using Auto Scaling groups with the Amazon CloudWatch Logs agent configured. How can this process be automated?","question_zh":"生产账户有一项要求，即任何手动登录过的 Amazon EC2 实例必须在 24 小时内终止。生产账户中的所 有应用程序都在使用配置了 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 代理的自动扩展组。 这个过程如何实现自动化？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Logs subscription to an AWS Step Functions application. Configure an AWS Lambda function to add a tag to the EC2 instance that produced the login event and mark the instance to be decommissioned. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke a second Lambda function once a day that will terminate all instances with this tag.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that will be invoked by the login event. Send the notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that the operations team is subscribed to, and have them terminate the EC2 instance within 24 hours.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that will be invoked by the login event. Configure the alarm to send to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Use a group of worker instances to process messages from the queue, which then schedules an Amazon EventBridge rule to be invoked.","D":"Create a CloudWatch Logs subscription to an AWS Lambda function. Configure the function to add a tag to the EC2 instance that produced the login event and mark the instance to be decommissioned. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke a daily Lambda function that terminates all instances with this tag."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 订阅到 AWS Step Functions 应用程序。配置一个 AWS Lambda 函数，为 产生登录事件的 EC2 实例添加一个标签，并将该实例标记为即将退役。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每天调用一个 Lambda 函数，终止所有带有此标签的实例。","B":"创建一个由登录事件触发的 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。将通知发送到运营团队订阅的 Amazon 简单 通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，并要求他们在 24 小时内终止该 EC2 实例。","C":"创建一个由登录事件触发的 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。将警报配置为发送到 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列。使用一组工作实例来处理队列中的消息，然后安排 Amazon EventBridge 规则被调用。","D":"创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 订阅到 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该函数，为产生登录事件的 EC2 实例 添加一个标签，并将该实例标记为待退役。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每天调用一个 Lambda 函数来终止所有带有此标签的实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to automatically tag and terminate any EC2 instance that has a manual login event (captured by the CloudWatch Logs agent) within 24 hours. CloudWatch Logs subscriptions deliver a real-time feed of matching log events directly to AWS Lambda, which is the correct mechanism to react to a specific login event. Option D wires a CloudWatch Logs subscription to a Lambda that tags the offending instance for decommissioning, then an EventBridge scheduled (daily) rule invokes a second Lambda that terminates all tagged instances - fully automated and using only documented, supported destinations. Per the docs, valid subscription-filter destinations are Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Data Firehose, and OpenSearch; Step Functions is NOT a supported subscription destination, so Option A is technically invalid as written.","explanation_zh":"需求是要在 24 小時內自動標記並終止任何發生手動登入事件 (由 CloudWatch Logs agent 擷取) 的 EC2 instance。CloudWatch Logs subscriptions 會把符合條件的 log 事件即時 (real-time) 傳遞給 AWS Lambda,這正是針對特定登入事件做出反應的正確機制。選項 D 將 CloudWatch Logs subscription 連到一個 Lambda,由它替違規的 instance 加上待除役的 tag,再用 EventBridge 排程 (每日) 規則觸發第二個 Lambda 去終止所有帶該 tag 的 instance,完全自動化且只使用官方支援的目的地。依文件,subscription filter 的有效目的地只有 Kinesis Data Streams、Lambda、Data Firehose 與 OpenSearch;Step Functions 並非支援的 subscription 目的地,因此選項 A 在技術上不成立。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudWatch Logs subscription cannot target AWS Step Functions. The only documented subscription-filter destinations are Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Data Firehose, and OpenSearch. The design is technically impossible as written, and Step Functions adds needless complexity over the direct Lambda approach in D.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription 無法以 AWS Step Functions 作為目的地。官方文件支援的 subscription filter 目的地只有 Kinesis Data Streams、Lambda、Data Firehose 與 OpenSearch。此設計在技術上無法實現,且相較於 D 直接用 Lambda,Step Functions 還多了不必要的複雜度。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch alarms are triggered by metric thresholds, not directly 'invoked by a login event' - a metric filter would be required first. More importantly, it relies on the operations team manually terminating instances, which is not automation and is error-prone for the 24-hour SLA.","why_zh":"CloudWatch alarm 是由 metric 門檻觸發,而非直接被『登入事件觸發』,需先有 metric filter。更關鍵的是它仰賴維運團隊手動終止 instance,這並非自動化,對 24 小時的時限而言容易出錯。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Alarms are not 'invoked by a login event' directly, and routing through SQS plus a fleet of worker instances that then schedule EventBridge rules is convoluted and high-overhead. The worker instances themselves would be running and could be logged into, and dynamically scheduling EventBridge rules per event is unnecessary.","why_zh":"Alarm 並非直接『被登入事件觸發』,而透過 SQS 再加一群 worker instance 去排程 EventBridge 規則既迂迴又高負擔。這些 worker instance 本身在運行也可能被登入,且為每個事件動態排程 EventBridge 規則並無必要。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/Subscriptions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Alarm-On-Logs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":63,"question_en":"A company has enabled all features for its organization in AWS Organizations. The organization contains 10 AWS accounts. The company has turned on AWS CloudTrail in all the accounts. The company expects the number of AWS accounts in the organization to increase to 500 during the next year. The company plans to use multiple OUs for these accounts. The company has enabled AWS Config in each existing AWS account in the organization. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that enables AWS Config automatically for all future AWS accounts that are created in the organization. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中为其组织启用了所有功能。该组织包含 10 个 AWS 账户。该公司已在 所有账户中启用了 AWS CloudTrail。该公司预计在接下来的一年里，组织中的 AWS 账户数量将增加到 500 个。该公司计划为这些账户使用多个组织单元（OU）。 该公司已在组织内的每个现有 AWS 账户中启用了 AWS Config。一位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解 决方案，以便在组织中创建的所有未来 AWS 账户中自动启用 AWS Config。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the organization's management account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to a CreateAccount API call. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that enables trusted access to AWS Config for the organization.","B":"In the organization's management account, create an AWS CloudFormation stack set to enable AWS Config. Configure the stack set to deploy automatically when an account is created through Organizations.","C":"In the organization's management account, create an SCP that allows the appropriate AWS Config API calls to enable AWS Config. Apply the SCP to the root-level OU.","D":"In the organization's management account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to a CreateAccount API call. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to enable AWS Config for the account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 CreateAccount API 调用做出 响应。配置该规则以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，为组织启用对 AWS Config 的可信访问。","B":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 栈集以启用 AWS Config。将栈集配置为在通 过 Organizations 创建账户时自动部署。","C":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许进行适当的 AWS Config API 调用以启 用 AWS Config。将该 SCP 应用于根级别的组织单位（OU）。","D":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 CreateAccount API 调用做出反应。 配置该规则以调用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，为该账户启用 AWS Config。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The native, documented way to automatically enable AWS Config for all future accounts in an organization is a service-managed CloudFormation StackSet with automatic deployment turned on. AWS docs state that with service-managed permissions you can 'turn on automatic deployments to accounts that you add to your organization in the future,' and that 'CloudFormation can automatically deploy additional stacks to new AWS Organizations accounts when they're added to your target organization or organizational units (OUs).' The StackSet template can create the AWS::Config::ConfigurationRecorder and DeliveryChannel resources so each new account starts recording with no manual action. Because the company plans multiple OUs and growth to 500 accounts, targeting the org/root with auto-deployment scales cleanly. Option B is correct.","explanation_zh":"在 AWS Organizations 中為所有未來帳戶自動啟用 AWS Config 的原生且有文件支援的做法,是使用採用 service-managed 權限並開啟自動部署 (automatic deployment) 的 CloudFormation StackSet。AWS 文件明確指出,在 service-managed 權限模型下可以「對未來加入組織的帳戶開啟自動部署」,且「當帳戶被加入目標 organization 或 OU 時,CloudFormation 會自動部署堆疊」。StackSet 範本可建立 AWS::Config::ConfigurationRecorder 與 DeliveryChannel 等資源,使每個新帳戶無需人工操作即開始記錄。由於公司規劃多個 OU 並將擴增至 500 個帳戶,以 root/OU 為目標並開啟自動部署能乾淨地擴展。因此選 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Enabling 'trusted access to AWS Config for the organization' only unlocks org-level capabilities (aggregators, organization Config rules/conformance packs). It does NOT create the configuration recorder/delivery channel inside each member account, so AWS Config recording would not actually be enabled in new accounts.","why_zh":"啟用「AWS Config 的組織信任存取」僅解鎖組織層級功能 (aggregator、organization Config rules/conformance packs),並不會在每個成員帳戶內建立 configuration recorder/delivery channel,因此新帳戶實際上不會啟用 Config 記錄。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP is a permission guardrail that allows or denies API actions; it never proactively invokes APIs or turns on a service. Allowing Config API calls does not cause Config to be enabled in any account.","why_zh":"SCP 只是權限護欄,用於允許或拒絕 API 動作,本身不會主動呼叫 API 或啟用服務。允許 Config API 呼叫並不會讓任何帳戶實際啟用 Config。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EventBridge rule on CreateAccount invoking an SSM Automation runbook is a custom, higher-operational-overhead build versus the purpose-built StackSet auto-deployment feature, and it relies on cross-account role assumption and the asynchronous CreateAccount/CreateAccountResult flow. It is not the AWS-recommended native solution that B provides.","why_zh":"以 EventBridge 監聽 CreateAccount 並呼叫 SSM Automation runbook 屬於自訂、運維負擔較高的方案,且需仰賴跨帳戶角色擔任與非同步的 CreateAccount/CreateAccountResult 流程;相較於 B 所提供的專用 StackSet 自動部署功能,這並非 AWS 推薦的原生作法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-manage-auto-deployment.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":64,"question_en":"A company has many applications. Different teams in the company developed the applications by using multiple languages and frameworks. The applications run on premises and on different servers with different operating systems. Each team has its own release protocol and process. The company wants to reduce the complexity of the release and maintenance of these applications. The company is migrating its technology stacks, including these applications, to AWS. The company wants centralized control of source code, a consistent and automatic delivery pipeline, and as few maintenance tasks as possible on the underlying infrastructure. What should a DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有众多应用程序。公司内不同团队使用多种语言和框架开发了这些应用程序。这些应用程 序在本地和不同操作系统下的不同服务器上运行。每个团队都有自己的发布协议和流程。该公司希望 降低这些应用程序发布和维护的复杂性。 该公司正在将其技术栈（包括这些应用程序）迁移到 AWS。该公司希望实现源代码的集中管理、一致且 自动化的交付流程，并尽可能减少底层基础设施的维护任务。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create one AWS CodeCommit repository for all applications. Put each application's code in a different branch. Merge the branches, and use AWS CodeBuild to build the applications. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the applications to one centralized application server.","B":"Create one AWS CodeCommit repository for each of the applications. Use AWS CodeBuild to build the applications one at a time. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the applications to one centralized application server.","C":"Create one AWS CodeCommit repository for each of the applications. Use AWS CodeBuild to build the applications one at a time and to create one AMI for each server. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to automatically provision and decommission Amazon EC2 fleets by using these AMIs.","D":"Create one AWS CodeCommit repository for each of the applications. Use AWS CodeBuild to build one Docker image for each application in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the applications to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on infrastructure that AWS Fargate manages."},"options_zh":{"A":"为所有应用程序创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。将每个应用程序的代码放在不同的分支中。合并这 些分支，并使用 AWS CodeBuild 构建应用程序。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序部署到一个集中的 应用服务器上。","B":"为每个应用程序创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。使用 AWS CodeBuild 依次构建这些应用程序。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序部署到一个集中的应用服务器上。","C":"为每个应用程序创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库。使用 AWS CodeBuild 依次构建应用程序，并为每台 服务器创建一个 AMI。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 通过这些 AMI 自动配置和停用 Amazon EC2 集群。","D":"为每个应用程序创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。使用 AWS CodeBuild 在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 中为每个应用程序构建一个 Docker 镜像。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序 部署到由 AWS Fargate 管理的 Amazon Elastic Container Service （Amazon ECS） 上。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is 'as few maintenance tasks as possible on the underlying infrastructure,' combined with the need to support many applications written in different languages/frameworks on different operating systems through a single, consistent, automated delivery pipeline. Packaging each application as a Docker image normalizes the heterogeneity of languages, frameworks, and OSs into a uniform deployable artifact. Building one image per app with CodeBuild and storing it in Amazon ECR, then deploying to Amazon ECS on AWS Fargate, removes the need to provision, configure, patch, or scale servers/EC2 clusters because Fargate is serverless container compute (per the ECS docs: 'run containers without having to manage servers or clusters of Amazon EC2 instances'). One CodeCommit repo per application provides centralized source control, and CodeBuild + CodeDeploy give a repeatable automatic pipeline. This is the only option that simultaneously delivers centralization, automation, multi-language support, and minimal infrastructure maintenance.","explanation_zh":"決定性條件是『盡可能減少底層基礎設施的維護工作』，同時需要透過單一、一致、自動化的交付管線，支援以不同語言/框架、執行於不同作業系統上的眾多應用程式。將每個應用程式封裝為 Docker image，可把語言、框架與作業系統的異質性統一為一致的可部署成品。使用 CodeBuild 為每個應用建置一個 image 並存放於 Amazon ECR，再部署到 Amazon ECS on AWS Fargate，即可免除佈建、設定、修補或擴展伺服器/EC2 叢集的需求，因為 Fargate 是無伺服器的容器運算（ECS 文件指出：『run containers without having to manage servers or clusters of Amazon EC2 instances』）。每個應用一個 CodeCommit repo 提供集中式原始碼控管，CodeBuild + CodeDeploy 則提供可重複的自動化管線。這是唯一同時達成集中化、自動化、多語言支援與最少基礎設施維護的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Putting all apps in branches of one repo and merging them is an anti-pattern that mixes unrelated codebases and creates merge conflicts; deploying many different language/framework apps to 'one centralized application server' (EC2) keeps OS/runtime patching and server maintenance, contradicting the 'as few maintenance tasks as possible on the underlying infrastructure' requirement and is not consistent or automatic.","why_zh":"把所有應用放在同一 repo 的不同分支再合併是反模式，會混雜不相關的程式碼並造成合併衝突；將多種語言/框架的應用部署到『單一集中式應用伺服器』(EC2) 仍需修補作業系統/執行環境並維護伺服器，違反『盡可能減少底層基礎設施維護』的要求，且既不一致也非自動化。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Although one repo per app is correct, deploying multiple heterogeneous-language applications to a single centralized EC2 application server still requires managing, patching, and scaling that server (high infrastructure maintenance) and risks runtime/dependency conflicts between different frameworks on one host.","why_zh":"雖然每個應用一個 repo 是正確的，但將多種不同語言的應用部署到單一集中式 EC2 應用伺服器，仍需管理、修補與擴展該伺服器（基礎設施維護負擔高），且不同框架共處於同一主機可能造成執行環境/相依性衝突。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Baking one AMI per server and using CloudFormation StackSets to provision EC2 fleets means you still own and must patch/maintain the EC2 operating systems and AMIs, which is significant ongoing infrastructure maintenance; StackSets is primarily for deploying stacks across multiple accounts/Regions, not an app delivery pipeline, so it does not minimize maintenance.","why_zh":"為每台伺服器建立 AMI 並用 CloudFormation StackSets 佈建 EC2 機群，代表你仍擁有並必須修補/維護 EC2 作業系統與 AMI，這是相當可觀的持續性基礎設施維護；StackSets 主要用於跨多個帳戶/區域部署堆疊，並非應用交付管線，因此無法將維護降到最低。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/AWS_Fargate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/tutorial-ecs-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/ecs-cd-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/deployment-type-blue-green.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":65,"question_en":"A company's application is currently deployed to a single AWS Region. Recently, the company opened a new office on a different continent. The users in the new office are experiencing high latency. The company's application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and uses Amazon DynamoDB as the database layer. The instances run in an EC2 Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. A DevOps engineer is tasked with minimizing application response times and improving availability for users in both Regions. Which combination of actions should be taken to address the latency issues? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"该公司当前的应用程序部署在单个 AWS 区域。最近，该公司在另一个大洲开设了新的办事处。新办事处 的用户正遭遇高延迟问题。该公司的应用程序运行在多个可用区的 EC2 自动扩展组中的实例上，并通过应 用负载均衡器（ALB）提供服务，使用 Amazon DynamoDB 作为数据库层。一位 DevOps 工程师的任务是 减少应用程序的响应时间，并提高两个区域用户的可用性。 应采取哪些行动组合来解决延迟问题？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new DynamoDB table in the new Region with cross-Region replication enabled.","B":"Create new ALB and Auto Scaling group global resources and configure the new ALB to direct traffic to the new Auto Scaling group.","C":"Create new ALB and Auto Scaling group resources in the new Region and configure the new ALB to direct traffic to the new Auto Scaling group.","D":"Create Amazon Route 53 records, health checks, and latency-based routing policies to route to the ALB.","E":"Create Amazon Route 53 aliases, health checks, and failover routing policies to route to the ALB.","F":"Convert the DynamoDB table to a global table."},"options_zh":{"A":"在新区域创建一个启用了跨区域复制功能的新 DynamoDB 表。","B":"创建新的应用负载均衡器（ALB）和自动扩展组全局资源，并配置新的 ALB 将流量定向到新的自动扩展 组。","C":"在新区域创建新的应用负载均衡器（ALB）和自动扩展组资源，并配置新的 ALB 将流量导向新的自动 扩展组。","D":"创建 Amazon Route 53 记录、健康检查以及基于延迟的路由策略，以将流量路由到应用负载均衡器 （ALB）。","E":"创建 Amazon Route 53 别名、健康检查和故障转移路由策略以将流量路由到应用负载均衡器（ALB）。","F":"将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。"},"answer":["C","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The goal is an active-active multi-Region deployment that both minimizes response time and improves availability for users on both continents, which requires addressing all three tiers. C handles the compute tier: ALBs and EC2 Auto Scaling groups are Regional resources, so you must create a new ALB and Auto Scaling group in the new Region pointing the ALB at the new ASG. D handles DNS: Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing with health checks sends each user to the Region that provides the lowest latency, which is exactly the AWS-documented use case ('If your application is hosted in multiple AWS Regions, you can improve performance for your users by serving their requests from the AWS Region that provides the lowest latency'). F handles the data tier: converting the DynamoDB table to a global table gives multi-active, multi-Region replication with fast local read and write performance and high availability, with no application changes required.","explanation_zh":"目標是建立 active-active 多 Region 部署，同時降低回應延遲並提升兩地使用者的可用性，必須同時處理三個層級。C 處理運算層：ALB 與 EC2 Auto Scaling group 都是 Regional 資源，因此必須在新 Region 建立新的 ALB 與 Auto Scaling group，並讓新 ALB 指向新 ASG。D 處理 DNS 層：Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing 搭配 health checks，會把每位使用者導向延遲最低的 Region，這正是 AWS 文件記載的用途（『若應用程式部署在多個 AWS Region，可由提供最低延遲的 Region 服務請求以提升效能』）。F 處理資料層：將 DynamoDB table 轉換為 global table，提供 multi-active、多 Region 複寫，具備快速的本地讀寫效能與高可用性，且不需更改應用程式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DynamoDB does not have a 'cross-Region replication' option you enable on a separately-created table; the supported multi-Region mechanism is converting the table to a global table (option F). Creating a separate, manually-replicated table is technically inaccurate and would not provide multi-active local writes.","why_zh":"DynamoDB 並沒有在另外建立的 table 上啟用『cross-Region replication』的選項；官方支援的多 Region 機制是把 table 轉換為 global table（選項 F）。建立另一個手動複寫的 table 在技術上不正確，也無法提供 multi-active 的本地寫入。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"ALBs and EC2 Auto Scaling groups are Regional, not global, resources. There is no 'global ALB' or 'global Auto Scaling group,' so this option is technically impossible.","why_zh":"ALB 與 EC2 Auto Scaling group 是 Regional 資源，而非 global 資源。不存在『global ALB』或『global Auto Scaling group』，因此此選項技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Failover routing is active-passive: it sends all traffic to the primary Region and only switches to the secondary on failure. It does not minimize latency for users in both Regions, which is the stated objective; latency-based routing (D) does.","why_zh":"Failover routing 是 active-passive：將所有流量導向主 Region，僅在故障時才切換到次要 Region。它無法為兩地使用者降低延遲（這是題目目標），而 latency-based routing（D）可以。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/introduction.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":66,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to apply a core set of security controls to an existing set of AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. Individual teams will administer individual accounts by using the AdministratorAccess AWS managed policy. For all accounts. AWS CloudTrail and AWS Config must be turned on in all available AWS Regions. Individual account administrators must not be able to edit or delete any of the baseline resources. However, individual account administrators must be able to edit or delete their own CloudTrail trails and AWS Config rules. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要将一组核心的安全控制措施应用于现有的 AWS 账户。这些账户位于 AWS 组织中 的一个组织内。各个团队将通过使用“AdministratorAccess”AWS 管理策略来管理各自的账户。对于所有账 户，必须在所有可用的 AWS 区域中启用 AWS CloudTrail 和 AWS Config。各个账户管理员不得编辑或删除 任何基准资源，但必须能够编辑或删除其自身的 CloudTrail 跟踪和 AWS Config 规则。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that defines the standard account resources. Deploy the template to all accounts from the organization's management account by using CloudFormation StackSets. Set the stack policy to deny Update:Delete actions.","B":"Enable AWS Control Tower. Enroll the existing accounts in AWS Control Tower. Grant the individual account administrators access to CloudTrail and AWS Config.","C":"Designate an AWS Config management account. Create AWS Config recorders in all accounts by using AWS CloudFormation StackSets. Deploy AWS Config rules to the organization by using the AWS Config management account. Create a CloudTrail organization trail in the organization’s management account. Deny modification or deletion of the AWS Config recorders by using an SCP.","D":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that defines the standard account resources. Deploy the template to all accounts from the organization's management account by using CloudFormation StackSets Create an SCP that prevents updates or deletions to CloudTrail resources or AWS Config resources unless the principal is an administrator of the organization's management account."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于定义标准账户资源。通过 CloudFormation StackSets 从组织 的管理账户将该模板部署到所有账户。将堆栈策略设置为拒绝更新和删除操作。","B":"启用 AWS 控制塔。将现有账户注册到 AWS 控制塔。授予各个账户管理员对 CloudTrail 和 AWS Config 的访问权限。","C":"指定一个 AWS Config 管理账户。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在所有账户中创建 AWS Config 记录器。通过 AWS Config 管理账户将 AWS Config 规则部署到组织中。在组织的管理账户中创建 CloudTrail 组织跟踪。使用服务控制策略（SCP）禁止修改或删除 AWS Config 记录器。","D":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，定义标准账户资源。通过使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从组 织的管理账户将该模板部署到所有账户。创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），除非主体是组织管理 账户的管理员，否则禁止对 CloudTrail 资源或 AWS Config 资源进行更新或删除操作。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The decisive requirement is the nested condition: account admins (who hold AdministratorAccess) must NOT be able to edit or delete the centrally deployed BASELINE resources, yet they MUST still be able to edit/delete their OWN CloudTrail trails and AWS Config rules. Option C achieves exactly this: organization-level Config rules deployed from the Config management account are, per the AWS Config docs, 'not modifiable by your organization's member accounts,' and a CloudTrail organization trail created in the management account produces member-account copies that only the management/delegated-admin can manage. These two mechanisms protect the baseline without touching the member admins' ability to create and manage their own (non-organization) trails and rules. The single narrowly-scoped SCP only denies modification/deletion of the AWS Config recorders, so it does not block admins from managing their own resources. StackSets ensures recorders exist in all accounts/Regions. Together this satisfies all three requirements with low operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"決定性需求是巢狀條件：擁有 AdministratorAccess 的帳戶管理員「不可」編輯或刪除集中佈署的 baseline 資源，但仍「必須」能編輯/刪除「自己的」CloudTrail trail 與 AWS Config 規則。選項 C 正好達成：由 Config 管理帳戶佈署的 organization Config rules，依 AWS Config 文件說明『member accounts 無法修改』；由管理帳戶建立的 CloudTrail organization trail 在成員帳戶產生的複本僅能由管理/委派管理帳戶管理。這兩種機制保護了 baseline，卻不影響成員管理員建立與管理自己的 trail 與規則。唯一且範圍精準的 SCP 只拒絕對 AWS Config recorder 的修改/刪除，因此不會阻擋管理員管理自己的資源。StackSets 確保所有帳戶/區域都有 recorder。整體以低營運負擔滿足全部三項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudFormation stack policy 'applies only during stack updates' and 'doesn't provide access controls like an IAM policy; use it only as a fail-safe mechanism to prevent accidental updates.' An account admin with AdministratorAccess can still directly call cloudtrail:DeleteTrail or config:DeleteConfigRule via the service API, bypassing CloudFormation. So a stack policy with Deny Update:Delete does not actually protect the baseline resources from a determined member admin.","why_zh":"CloudFormation stack policy『僅在 stack 更新期間生效』且『並非如 IAM 般的存取控制，只作為防止意外更新的保險機制』。具 AdministratorAccess 的帳戶管理員仍可直接呼叫 cloudtrail:DeleteTrail 或 config:DeleteConfigRule 服務 API，繞過 CloudFormation。因此 Deny Update:Delete 的 stack policy 無法真正保護 baseline 資源。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Enabling AWS Control Tower and enrolling existing accounts is a heavyweight, opinionated landing-zone deployment that is not the most operationally efficient way to apply just a core set of controls to an existing set of accounts. It imposes enrollment prerequisites and an OU/guardrail model, and 'grant the individual account administrators access to CloudTrail and AWS Config' does not cleanly address the requirement that admins must be blocked from the baseline yet still manage their own resources.","why_zh":"啟用 AWS Control Tower 並把既有帳戶納管，是一套笨重且高度定型的 landing zone 佈署，對於只是要對既有帳戶套用一組核心控制而言並非最有效率。它強制納管前置條件與 OU/guardrail 模型，且『授予各帳戶管理員存取 CloudTrail 與 AWS Config』並未明確解決『阻擋 baseline 但仍能管理自身資源』的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer and the classic trap. The SCP denies ALL CloudTrail and AWS Config update/delete actions for every member-account principal (only management-account admins are exempt, since SCPs don't affect the management account). That blanket deny also blocks member admins from editing or deleting their OWN trails and Config rules, directly violating the requirement that they must be able to do so. The deny is too broad.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案，也是典型陷阱。該 SCP 對所有成員帳戶 principal 拒絕全部 CloudTrail 與 AWS Config 的 update/delete 動作（因 SCP 不影響管理帳戶，故僅管理帳戶管理員例外）。此一律拒絕也會阻擋成員管理員編輯或刪除『自己的』trail 與 Config 規則，直接違反『他們必須能這麼做』的需求。拒絕範圍過廣。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/protect-stack-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/config-rule-multi-account-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/creating-trail-organization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":67,"question_en":"A company has its AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. AWS Config is manually configured in each AWS account. The company needs to implement a solution to centrally configure AWS Config for all accounts in the organization The solution also must record resource changes to a central account. Which combination of actions should a DevOps engineer perform to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司的 AWS 账户在 AWS Organizations 中的组织内。AWS Config 在每个 AWS 账户中都是手动配 置的。该公司需要实施一个解决方案，以便在组织内的所有账户中集中配置 AWS Config。该解决方案 还必须将资源更改记录到一个中央账户中。 DevOps 工程师应执行哪些操作组合才能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure a delegated administrator account for AWS Config. Enable trusted access for AWS Config in the organization.","B":"Configure a delegated administrator account for AWS Config. Create a service-linked role for AWS Config in the organization’s management account.","C":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template to create an AWS Config aggregator. Configure a CloudFormation stack set to deploy the template to all accounts in the organization.","D":"Create an AWS Config organization aggregator in the organization's management account. Configure data collection from all AWS accounts in the organization and from all AWS Regions.","E":"Create an AWS Config organization aggregator in the delegated administrator account. Configure data collection from all AWS accounts in the organization and from all AWS Regions."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 AWS Config 配置一个委托管理员账户。在组织中为 AWS Config 启用受信任访问权限。","B":"为 AWS Config 配置委托管理员账户。在组织的管理账户中为 AWS Config 创建服务相关角色。","C":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板以创建 AWS Config 聚合器。配置一个 CloudFormation 堆栈集，将该模板部署到组织中的所有账户。","D":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个 AWS Config 组织聚合器。配置从组织中的所有 AWS 账户以及所有 AWS 区域收集数据。","E":"在委托管理员账户中创建一个 AWS Config 组织聚合器。配置从组织中的所有 AWS 账户以及所有 AWS 区域收集数据。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The solution needs two things: central configuration of AWS Config across the organization, and central recording/collection of resource configuration data into one account. Option A delivers central configuration: you enable trusted access for AWS Config in the organization and register a member account as a delegated administrator (service principals config.amazonaws.com and config-multiaccountsetup.amazonaws.com), which lets that account manage Config rules/conformance packs and aggregation organization-wide. Option E delivers central recording: an AWS Config organization aggregator collects configuration and compliance data from all accounts and all Regions into a single (aggregator) account. Because a delegated administrator was set up in A, the aggregator belongs in the delegated administrator account (not the management account), which aligns with the AWS Security Reference Architecture guidance to keep the management account minimal and delegate security tooling. Note: an aggregator gives a read-only, replicated view of source-account data, and authorization is not required when aggregating accounts that are part of AWS Organizations, so A + E is a clean, consistent design.","explanation_zh":"此方案需要兩件事：在整個組織中集中設定 AWS Config，以及將資源組態資料集中記錄/收集到單一帳戶。選項 A 提供集中設定：在組織中為 AWS Config 啟用 trusted access，並將一個成員帳戶註冊為 delegated administrator（服務主體為 config.amazonaws.com 與 config-multiaccountsetup.amazonaws.com），使該帳戶能在組織範圍內管理 Config rules/conformance packs 與資料彙總。選項 E 提供集中記錄：AWS Config organization aggregator 會將所有帳戶與所有 Region 的組態與合規資料彙集到單一（aggregator）帳戶。由於 A 已設定 delegated administrator，aggregator 應建立於 delegated administrator 帳戶（而非 management 帳戶），這符合 AWS Security Reference Architecture 將 management 帳戶保持精簡、把安全工具委派出去的最佳實務。補充：aggregator 提供來源帳戶資料的唯讀複製視圖，且彙總 AWS Organizations 內的帳戶時不需要 authorization，因此 A + E 是乾淨且一致的設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The AWSServiceRoleForConfig service-linked role is created automatically by AWS Config when trusted access is enabled; you do not manually create it in the management account, and creating an SLR there does not record resource changes to a central account.","why_zh":"AWSServiceRoleForConfig 服務連結角色會在啟用 trusted access 時由 AWS Config 自動建立，無需在 management 帳戶手動建立，且在該處建立 SLR 也無法將資源變更記錄到中央帳戶。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An aggregator is a single central resource, not something deployed to every account. Using a StackSet to deploy an aggregator template to all accounts is the wrong model and does not centrally configure Config or provide a single central record.","why_zh":"aggregator 是單一的中央資源，並非要部署到每個帳戶。用 StackSet 將 aggregator 範本部署到所有帳戶是錯誤模型，既無法集中設定 Config，也無法提供單一中央記錄。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically an organization aggregator can live in the management account, but since the design uses a delegated administrator (Option A), the aggregator should reside in the delegated administrator account per AWS best practice (SRA recommends keeping the management account minimal). E is the consistent pairing with A; D is not.","why_zh":"技術上 organization aggregator 可建立於 management 帳戶，但既然方案採用 delegated administrator（選項 A），依 AWS 最佳實務（SRA 建議 management 帳戶保持精簡），aggregator 應位於 delegated administrator 帳戶。E 才是與 A 一致的搭配，D 則否。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/aggregated-register-delegated-administrator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/aggregate-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/security-reference-architecture/org-management.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":68,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate its content sharing web application hosted on Amazon EC2 to a serverless architecture. The company currently deploys changes to its application by creating a new Auto Scaling group of EC2 instances and a new Elastic Load Balancer, and then shifting the traffic away using an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy. For its new serverless application, the company is planning to use Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda. The company will need to update its deployment processes to work with the new application. It will also need to retain the ability to test new features on a small number of users before rolling the features out to the entire user base. Which deployment strategy will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望将其托管在亚马逊 EC2 上的内容共享网络应用程序迁移到无服务器架构。该公司目前 通过创建新的 EC2 实例自动扩展组和新的弹性负载均衡器来部署应用程序的更改，然后使用亚马逊 Route 53 加权路由策略将流量转移过去。 该公司计划为其新的无服务器应用程序使用亚马逊 API 网关和 AWS Lambda。公司需要更新其部署 流程以适应新应用。此外，公司还需要保留先在少量用户中测试新功能，然后再向全体用户推广的功 能。 哪种部署策略能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CDK to deploy API Gateway and Lambda functions. When code needs to be changed, update the AWS CloudFormation stack and deploy the new version of the APIs and Lambda functions. Use a Route 53 failover routing policy for the canary release strategy.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation to deploy API Gateway and Lambda functions using Lambda function versions. When code needs to be changed, update the CloudFormation stack with the new Lambda code and update the API versions using a canary release strategy. Promote the new version when testing is complete.","C":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to deploy API Gateway and Lambda functions. When code needs to be changed, deploy a new version of the API and Lambda functions. Shift traffic gradually using an Elastic Beanstalk blue/green deployment.","D":"Use AWS OpsWorks to deploy API Gateway in the service layer and Lambda functions in a custom layer. When code needs to be changed, use OpsWorks to perform a blue/green deployment and shift traffic gradually."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CDK 部署 API Gateway 和 Lambda 函数。当代码需要更改时，更新 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈并部署 API 和 Lambda 函数的新版本。对于金丝雀发布策略，使用 Route 53 故障转移路由策略。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 API Gateway 和 Lambda 函数，使用 Lambda 函数版本。当代码需 要更改时，使用新的 Lambda 更新 CloudFormation 堆栈。 使用金丝雀发布策略来编写和更新 API 版本。测试完成后推广新版本。","C":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 部署 API Gateway 和 Lambda 函数。当代码需要更改时，部署 API 和 Lambda 函数的新版本。使用 Elastic Beanstalk 蓝/绿部署逐步转移流量。","D":"使用 AWS OpsWorks 在服务层部署 API 网关，并在自定义层部署 Lambda 函数。当代码需要更 改时，使用 OpsWorks 执行蓝/绿部署，并逐步转移流量。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to deploy serverless API Gateway + Lambda and retain the ability to test new features on a small subset of users before full rollout (a canary release). API Gateway natively supports canary release deployments: you add canarySettings to a stage that route a configurable small percentage of traffic at random to a new deployment (new Lambda version), while the base/production version serves the rest. After test metrics pass, you promote the canary to production. These canarySettings are fully expressible in CloudFormation via AWS::ApiGateway::Deployment CanarySetting, and Lambda function versions let you ship immutable new code. Option B matches this exactly: deploy via CloudFormation, update the stack with new Lambda code, use the API canary release to split traffic, then promote. This is the AWS-recommended canary strategy for serverless and replaces the EC2-era Route 53 weighted ASG/ELB pattern.","explanation_zh":"需求是部署 serverless 的 API Gateway + Lambda，並保留在全面推出前先讓少量使用者測試新功能的能力（即 canary release）。API Gateway 原生支援 canary release 部署：在 stage 上加入 canarySettings，將可設定的一小部分流量隨機導向新的 deployment（新的 Lambda 版本），其餘流量仍由 base/production 版本處理。測試指標通過後，再把 canary 提升（promote）為 production。這些 canarySettings 可透過 CloudFormation 的 AWS::ApiGateway::Deployment CanarySetting 完整定義，而 Lambda function versions 則用於發佈不可變的新程式碼。選項 B 完全符合：以 CloudFormation 部署、用新 Lambda 程式碼更新 stack、利用 API canary release 分流，最後 promote。這是 AWS 對 serverless 推薦的 canary 策略，取代了 EC2 時代以 Route 53 weighted 搭配 ASG/ELB 的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Route 53 failover routing is an active-passive, health-check-driven failover mechanism, not a canary/percentage traffic split. It cannot send a small fraction of users to a new version for testing; only weighted (or canary at the API layer) does that. So the stated routing policy does not implement a canary release.","why_zh":"Route 53 failover routing 是 active-passive、由 health check 觸發的容錯機制，並非 canary/百分比流量分割。它無法把一小部分使用者導向新版本進行測試；只有 weighted（或 API 層的 canary）才能做到。因此該路由策略無法實作 canary release。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Elastic Beanstalk does not deploy API Gateway or Lambda functions; it provisions and manages web application platforms on EC2/containers. It is not a valid deployment service for a serverless API Gateway + Lambda architecture.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk 不會部署 API Gateway 或 Lambda 函式；它是用來在 EC2/容器上佈建與管理 web 應用平台。對於 serverless 的 API Gateway + Lambda 架構而言，它不是有效的部署服務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"OpsWorks is a Chef/Puppet-based configuration management service for EC2 instances. It does not deploy API Gateway or Lambda, and there is no service/custom layer that hosts these serverless services or performs blue/green for them.","why_zh":"OpsWorks 是針對 EC2 執行個體、以 Chef/Puppet 為基礎的組態管理服務。它不會部署 API Gateway 或 Lambda，也沒有所謂的 service/custom layer 可承載這些 serverless 服務或為其執行 blue/green。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/canary-release.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-apigateway-deployment-canarysetting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/how-to-deploy-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-failover.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":69,"question_en":"A development team uses AWS CodeCommit, AWS CodePipeline, and AWS CodeBuild to develop and deploy an application. Changes to the code are submitted by pull requests. The development team reviews and merges the pull requests, and then the pipeline builds and tests the application. Over time, the number of pull requests has increased. The pipeline is frequently blocked because of failing tests. To prevent this blockage, the development team wants to run the unit and integration tests on each pull request before it is merged. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个开发团队使用 AWS CodeCommit、AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 来开发和部署应用程序。 代码变更通过拉取请求提交。开发团队审核并合并拉取请求，然后管道会构建和测试应用程序。 随着时间的推移，拉取请求的数量不断增加。由于测试失败，流水线经常被阻塞。为防止这种情况 发生，开发团队希望在每个拉取请求合并之前运行单元测试和集成测试。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CodeBuild project to run the unit and integration tests. Create a CodeCommit approval rule template. Configure the template to require the successful invocation of the CodeBuild project. Attach the approval rule to the project's CodeCommit repository.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match pullRequestCreated events from CodeCommit Create a CodeBuild project to run the unit and integration tests. Configure the CodeBuild project as a target of the EventBridge rule that includes a custom event payload with the CodeCommit repository and branch information from the event.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match pullRequestCreated events from CodeCommit. Modify the existing CodePipeline pipeline to not run the deploy steps if the build is started from a pull request. Configure the EventBridge rule to run the pipeline with a custom payload that contains the CodeCommit repository and branch information from the event.","D":"Create a CodeBuild project to run the unit and integration tests. Create a CodeCommit notification rule that matches when a pull request is created or updated. Configure the notification rule to invoke the CodeBuild project."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 CodeBuild 项目来运行单元测试和集成测试。创建一个 CodeCommit 批准规则模板。配 置模板以要求成功调用 CodeBuild 项目。将批准规则附加到项目的 CodeCommit 存储库。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以匹配来自 CodeCommit 的 pullRequestCreated 事件。创建一 个 CodeBuild 项目来运行单元测试和集成测试。将 CodeBuild 项目配置为 EventBridge 规则的目 标，该规则包含一个自定义事件负载，其中包含来自事件的 CodeCommit 存储库和分支信息。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以匹配来自 CodeCommit 的 pullRequestCreated 事件。修改 现有的 CodePipeline 管道，使其在从拉取请求启动构建时跳过部署步骤。配置 EventBridge 规则， 使用包含事件中 CodeCommit 存储库和分支信息的自定义负载来运行管道。","D":"创建一个 CodeBuild 项目来运行单元测试和集成测试。创建一个 CodeCommit 通知规则，用于匹 配创建或更新拉取请求的情况。配置通知规则以调用 CodeBuild 项目。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The team needs to automatically run unit and integration tests on every CodeCommit pull request before it is merged, decoupled from the deploy pipeline. CodeCommit emits a pullRequestCreated event to Amazon EventBridge, and EventBridge directly supports CodeBuild projects as a target. So you create an EventBridge rule matching pullRequestCreated events and set a CodeBuild project (running the unit/integration tests) as the target. Because CodeBuild needs to build the pull request's source code, the rule passes a custom event payload (constant input / input transformer) carrying the CodeCommit repository and branch (source reference) information from the event, which CodeBuild uses as a source version override. This is exactly Option B and matches the documented EventBridge-to-CodeBuild target pattern.","explanation_zh":"團隊需要在每個 CodeCommit pull request 合併之前自動執行單元與整合測試，並與部署 pipeline 解耦。CodeCommit 會將 pullRequestCreated 事件送往 Amazon EventBridge，而 EventBridge 原生支援以 CodeBuild project 作為 target。因此建立一個比對 pullRequestCreated 事件的 EventBridge rule，並將執行單元/整合測試的 CodeBuild project 設為 target。由於 CodeBuild 需要建置該 pull request 的原始碼，rule 透過自訂事件 payload（constant input / input transformer）帶入事件中的 CodeCommit repository 與 branch（來源參考）資訊，供 CodeBuild 作為 source version override 使用。這正是選項 B，符合官方文件記載的 EventBridge 至 CodeBuild target 模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodeCommit approval rule templates only define the number of required approvals and an optional pool of IAM users/roles whose approvals count. They cannot require the successful invocation of a CodeBuild project as a merge condition, so this approach cannot enforce test execution before merge.","why_zh":"CodeCommit approval rule template 只能定義所需的核准數量以及可選的 IAM 使用者/角色核准池，無法將 CodeBuild project 的成功執行設為合併條件，因此無法在合併前強制執行測試。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This reuses the existing deploy pipeline, which is the very thing being blocked by failing tests. The goal is to test PRs independently before merge so the pipeline stops getting blocked; running the same pipeline (even skipping deploy) is more complex and does not cleanly meet the requirement to pre-merge test each PR. EventBridge can target CodePipeline but cannot inject an arbitrary branch/source override into an existing pipeline the way a CodeBuild target can.","why_zh":"此方案重用既有的部署 pipeline，而該 pipeline 正是因測試失敗而被卡住的對象。目標是在合併前獨立測試 PR 以避免 pipeline 被阻塞；重新執行同一條 pipeline（即使跳過 deploy）更複雜，也無法乾淨地滿足在每個 PR 合併前測試的需求。EventBridge 可以 target CodePipeline，但無法像 CodeBuild target 那樣對既有 pipeline 注入任意的 branch/source override。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeStar/Developer Tools notification rules can only target Amazon SNS topics and AWS Chatbot clients (Slack, Microsoft Teams, Amazon Chime). A notification rule cannot directly invoke a CodeBuild project, so this configuration is not supported.","why_zh":"CodeStar/Developer Tools 的 notification rule 只能 target Amazon SNS topic 與 AWS Chatbot client（Slack、Microsoft Teams、Amazon Chime）。notification rule 無法直接呼叫 CodeBuild project，因此此設定不被支援。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/monitoring-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-targets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/approval-rule-templates.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dtconsole/latest/userguide/notifications-chatbot.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":70,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The application requires frequent restarts. The application logs contain error messages when a restart is required. The application logs are published to a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. An Amazon CloudWatch alarm notifies an application engineer through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when the logs contain a large number of restart-related error messages. The application engineer manually restarts the application on the instances after the application engineer receives a notification from the SNS topic. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to automate the application restart on the instances without restarting the instances. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient manner?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例集群上的应用程序。该应用程序需要频繁重启。当需要重 启时，应用程序日志中会包含错误消息。应用程序日志会发布到亚马逊 CloudWatch Logs 中的一个 日志组。 当日志中包含大量与重启相关的错误消息时，Amazon CloudWatch 警报会通过 Amazon 简单通知服 务（Amazon SNS）主题通知应用程序工程师。应用程序工程师在收到 SNS 主题的通知后，会手动 在实例上重启应用程序。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，以在不重启实例的情况下实现应用程序的自动重启。 哪种解决方案能在操作效率最高的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that runs a script to restart the application on the instances. Configure the SNS topic to invoke the runbook.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function that restarts the application on the instances. Configure the Lambda function as an event destination of the SNS topic.","C":"Configure an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that runs a script to restart the application on the instances. Create an AWS Lambda function to invoke the runbook. Configure the Lambda function as an event destination of the SNS topic.","D":"Configure an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that runs a script to restart the application on the instances. Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts when the CloudWatch alarm enters ALARM state. Specify the runbook as a target of the rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 AWS 系统管理器自动化运行手册，使其运行一个脚本以在实例上重启应用程序。配置 SNS 主题以调用该运行手册。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于重启实例上的应用程序。将该 Lambda 函数配置为 SNS 主题的事件 目标。","C":"配置一个 AWS 系统管理器自动化运行手册，运行一个脚本以在实例上重启应用程序。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来调用该运行手册。将 Lambda 函数配置为 SNS 主题的事件目标。","D":"配置一个 AWS 系统管理器自动化运行手册，运行一个脚本以在实例上重启应用程序。配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，当 CloudWatch 警报进入“告警”状态时触发该规则。将运行手册指定为 规则的目标。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST operationally efficient. CloudWatch sends alarm state-change events directly to Amazon EventBridge, and EventBridge's available target list explicitly includes 'Systems Manager Automation'. So an EventBridge rule that matches the alarm entering ALARM state can invoke the SSM Automation runbook directly, with no custom code. The runbook can use the aws:runCommand action to restart the application process on the instances without rebooting the instances. This native, code-free integration has the fewest moving parts, so it is the most operationally efficient. Option A is technically impossible because Amazon SNS subscription protocols are limited to HTTP/HTTPS, Email/Email-JSON, SQS, Lambda, platform application, SMS, and Firehose; SNS cannot directly invoke an SSM Automation runbook. Options B and C add custom Lambda code that must be written and maintained, increasing operational overhead unnecessarily.","explanation_zh":"限定條件是「最高運維效率 (MOST operationally efficient)」。CloudWatch 會將告警的狀態變更事件直接送往 Amazon EventBridge，而 EventBridge 的可用目標清單明確包含 'Systems Manager Automation'。因此，一條在告警進入 ALARM 狀態時觸發的 EventBridge rule 可以直接調用 SSM Automation runbook，完全不需要自訂程式碼。該 runbook 可使用 aws:runCommand 動作在執行個體上重啟應用程式行程，而不需重啟執行個體。這種原生、免程式碼的整合元件最少，因此運維效率最高。選項 A 技術上不可行，因為 Amazon SNS 訂閱協定僅限 HTTP/HTTPS、Email/Email-JSON、SQS、Lambda、platform application、SMS 與 Firehose；SNS 無法直接調用 SSM Automation runbook。選項 B 與 C 則加入了需編寫與維護的自訂 Lambda 程式碼，徒增運維負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon SNS cannot directly invoke an SSM Automation runbook. SNS subscription protocols are limited to HTTP/HTTPS, Email, SQS, Lambda, platform application, SMS, and Firehose. There is no SNS protocol or 'invoke runbook' action, so this is technically impossible.","why_zh":"Amazon SNS 無法直接調用 SSM Automation runbook。SNS 訂閱協定僅限 HTTP/HTTPS、Email、SQS、Lambda、platform application、SMS 與 Firehose，沒有可調用 runbook 的協定或動作，技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"While Lambda is a valid SNS subscriber, writing custom Lambda code to restart the app adds maintenance overhead, and the Lambda would still need to reach into the EC2 instances (typically via SSM Run Command/Automation) to restart the process. More code and more moving parts than the native EventBridge-to-Automation path, so not the most operationally efficient.","why_zh":"Lambda 雖是合法的 SNS 訂閱者，但需編寫自訂 Lambda 程式碼來重啟應用，增加維護負擔，且該 Lambda 仍須透過（通常是 SSM Run Command/Automation）連入 EC2 執行個體才能重啟行程。相較於原生的 EventBridge 直接觸發 Automation，元件與程式碼更多，運維效率較低。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This works (Lambda subscribes to SNS and invokes the runbook), but it inserts an unnecessary Lambda layer that must be coded and maintained. EventBridge can target Systems Manager Automation directly off the alarm state change, so the Lambda is redundant overhead, making this less operationally efficient than D.","why_zh":"此方案可行（Lambda 訂閱 SNS 並調用 runbook），但插入了一層多餘且需編寫維護的 Lambda。EventBridge 可在告警狀態變更時直接以 Systems Manager Automation 為目標，因此該 Lambda 屬多餘負擔，運維效率不如 D。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-targets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-create-subscribe-endpoint-to-topic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-cloudwatch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/alarm-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-automation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":71,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer at a company is supporting an AWS environment in which all users use AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). The company wants to immediately disable credentials of any new IAM user and wants the security team to receive a notification. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"某公司的 DevOps 工程师正在维护一个 AWS 环境，该环境中所有用户均使用 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）。该公司希望立即禁用任何新 IAM 用户的凭证，并希望安全团队收到通知。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to an IAM CreateUser API call in AWS CloudTrail.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to an IAM GetLoginProfile API call in AWS CloudTrail.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is a target of the EventBridge rule. Configure the Lambda function to disable any access keys and delete the login profiles that are associated with the IAM user.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is a target of the EventBridge rule. Configure the Lambda function to delete the login profiles that are associated with the IAM user.","E":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that is a target of the EventBridge rule. Subscribe the security team's group email address to the topic.","F":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue that is a target of the Lambda function. Subscribe the security team's group email address to the queue."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CloudTrail 中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 IAM CreateUser API 调用做出响应。","B":"在 AWS CloudTrail 中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 IAM 的 GetLoginProfile API 调用做出响应。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，使其成为 EventBridge 规则的目标。配置该 Lambda 函数以禁用任何访问密 钥并删除与 IAM 用户关联的登录配置文件。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，使其成为 EventBridge 规则的目标。配置该 Lambda 函数以删除与 IAM 用户关联的登录配置文件。","E":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，使其成为 EventBridge 规则的目标。将安全团队的 组电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。","F":"创建一个亚马逊简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）队列，将其设为 Lambda 函数的目标。将安全团队 的组电子邮件地址订阅到该队列。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to immediately disable the credentials of any NEW IAM user and notify the security team. (A) An EventBridge rule reacting to the IAM CreateUser API call delivered via CloudTrail is the correct trigger, because CreateUser is the event that signals a new IAM user. (C) The Lambda target must disable any access keys AND delete the login profile. This is decisive: AWS documentation for DeleteLoginProfile explicitly states that deleting the login profile only blocks console sign-in and 'does not prevent the user from running any AWS CLI, PowerShell, or API calls using AWS access keys that might still be attached to the user account.' To fully disable a user's credentials you must address both the programmatic credentials (access keys) and the console credentials (login profile). (E) An SNS topic as the EventBridge target, with the security team's email subscribed, delivers the notification. SNS supports email subscriptions natively. This combination of A, C, E fully satisfies both requirements.","explanation_zh":"需求是立即停用任何「新」IAM 使用者的憑證並通知安全團隊。(A) 透過 CloudTrail 傳遞的 IAM CreateUser API 呼叫建立 EventBridge 規則是正確的觸發來源，因為 CreateUser 才是代表建立新 IAM 使用者的事件。(C) Lambda 目標必須同時停用所有 access keys 並刪除 login profile，這是決定性關鍵：AWS DeleteLoginProfile 文件明確說明刪除 login profile 只會封鎖主控台登入，「並不會阻止使用者透過仍附加在帳號上的 access keys 執行任何 AWS CLI、PowerShell 或 API 呼叫」。要完整停用憑證，必須同時處理程式化憑證（access keys）與主控台憑證（login profile）。(E) 以 SNS topic 作為 EventBridge 目標並讓安全團隊的 email 訂閱，即可送出通知，SNS 原生支援 email 訂閱。A、C、E 的組合完整滿足兩項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"GetLoginProfile is a read-only API that retrieves an existing user's password info; it does not signal creation of a new IAM user. The correct trigger for a newly created user is CreateUser, not GetLoginProfile.","why_zh":"GetLoginProfile 是唯讀 API，用於擷取既有使用者的密碼資訊，並非建立新 IAM 使用者的訊號。新使用者的正確觸發事件是 CreateUser，而非 GetLoginProfile。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Deleting only the login profile is incomplete. Per AWS docs, DeleteLoginProfile only blocks console sign-in and does NOT stop programmatic access via access keys. The new user could still have active access keys, so this fails to fully 'disable credentials.' Option C (which also disables access keys) strictly supersedes D.","why_zh":"只刪除 login profile 並不完整。依 AWS 文件，DeleteLoginProfile 只封鎖主控台登入，並不會停止透過 access keys 的程式化存取。新使用者仍可能有有效的 access keys，因此無法完整「停用憑證」。同時停用 access keys 的選項 C 完全優於 D。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"You cannot subscribe an email address to an Amazon SQS queue; only Amazon SNS supports email endpoint subscriptions. SQS is a polling-based message queue with no email delivery. The notification path must use SNS (option E).","why_zh":"無法將 email 訂閱到 Amazon SQS 佇列，只有 Amazon SNS 支援 email 端點訂閱。SQS 是以輪詢為基礎的訊息佇列，沒有 email 傳遞功能。通知路徑必須使用 SNS（選項 E）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/iam_example_iam_DeleteLoginProfile_section.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_access-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-email-notifications.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":72,"question_en":"A company wants to set up a continuous delivery pipeline. The company stores application code in a private GitHub repository. The company needs to deploy the application components to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), Amazon EC2, and AWS Lambda. The pipeline must support manual approval actions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司想要建立一个持续交付流水线。该公司将应用程序代码存储在私有 GitHub 代码库中。该公司需 要将应用程序组件部署到亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）、亚马逊 EC2 和 AWS Lambda 上。该流 水线必须支持人工审批操作。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CodePipeline with Amazon ECS, Amazon EC2, and Lambda as deploy providers.","B":"Use AWS CodePipeline with AWS CodeDeploy as the deploy provider.","C":"Use AWS CodePipeline with AWS Elastic Beanstalk as the deploy provider.","D":"Use AWS CodeDeploy with GitHub integration to deploy the application."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 与 Amazon ECS、Amazon EC2 和 Lambda 作为部署提供程序。","B":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 并将 AWS CodeDeploy 作为部署提供程序。","C":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 并将 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 作为部署提供商。","D":"使用与 GitHub 集成的 AWS CodeDeploy 部署应用程序。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CodePipeline provides the continuous delivery pipeline (with a GitHub source via a connection and built-in Manual approval action type). The deploy requirement spans three different compute targets: Amazon ECS, Amazon EC2, and AWS Lambda. AWS CodeDeploy is the single deployment service that natively automates application deployments across all three compute platforms (EC2/On-Premises, AWS Lambda, and Amazon ECS), as stated on the CodeDeploy 'What is CodeDeploy?' page. Therefore using CodePipeline with CodeDeploy as the deploy provider lets one consistent deploy provider handle ECS, EC2, and Lambda while CodePipeline supplies the GitHub source integration and manual approval actions. This is the standard, fully supported answer.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodePipeline 提供持續交付管線（可透過 connection 使用 GitHub 來源，並內建 Manual approval 動作類型）。部署需求橫跨三種不同的運算目標：Amazon ECS、Amazon EC2 與 AWS Lambda。AWS CodeDeploy 是唯一能原生自動化部署到全部三種運算平台（EC2/On-Premises、AWS Lambda、Amazon ECS）的部署服務，這在 CodeDeploy 的「What is CodeDeploy?」頁面有明確說明。因此使用 CodePipeline 搭配 CodeDeploy 作為 deploy provider，可由單一一致的部署提供者處理 ECS、EC2 與 Lambda，而 CodePipeline 則提供 GitHub 來源整合與手動核准動作。這是標準且完全受支援的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Although CodePipeline does have native EC2, ECS, and Lambda deploy action types, framing the solution as using three separate native deploy providers is not the intended/standard answer; the question wants a single deploy provider that covers all three targets, which is CodeDeploy. Option A also misnames these as a unified 'deploy provider' approach and is less aligned with AWS exam guidance than CodeDeploy.","why_zh":"雖然 CodePipeline 確實有原生的 EC2、ECS 與 Lambda deploy action 類型，但把方案描述成使用三個獨立的原生 deploy provider 並非預期/標準答案；題目要的是能涵蓋全部三種目標的單一 deploy provider，也就是 CodeDeploy。選項 A 也較不符合 AWS 考試指引。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk is a PaaS for deploying web applications onto managed EC2 environments; it is not a deploy provider for arbitrary Amazon ECS services or AWS Lambda functions, so it cannot meet the requirement to deploy to all three targets.","why_zh":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk 是用於將 Web 應用部署到受管 EC2 環境的 PaaS，並非可部署任意 Amazon ECS 服務或 AWS Lambda 函式的 deploy provider，因此無法滿足同時部署到三種目標的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeDeploy with GitHub integration alone is just the deployment engine; it does not provide pipeline orchestration or built-in manual approval actions. Manual approval is a CodePipeline action type, so CodePipeline is required, not standalone CodeDeploy.","why_zh":"僅用 CodeDeploy 搭配 GitHub 整合只是部署引擎本身，並不提供管線編排或內建的手動核准動作。Manual approval 是 CodePipeline 的動作類型，因此需要 CodePipeline，而非單獨使用 CodeDeploy。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodestarConnectionSource.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":73,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. When the application starts up, the application needs to process data from an Amazon S3 bucket before the application can start to serve requests. The size of the data that is stored in the S3 bucket is growing. When the Auto Scaling group adds new instances, the application now takes several minutes to download and process the data before the application can serve requests. The company must reduce the time that elapses before new EC2 instances are ready to serve requests. Which solution is the MOST cost-effective way to reduce the application startup time?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的应用程序，这些实例位于一个自动扩展组中。当应用程 序启动时，它需要先处理来自亚马逊 S3 存储桶的数据，然后才能开始响应请求。 存储在 S3 存储桶中的数据量正在增加。当自动扩展组添加新实例时，应用程序现在需要花费数分 钟来下载和处理数据，才能开始响应请求。该公司必须缩短新 EC2 实例准备好响应请求所需的时间。 哪种解决方案是降低应用程序启动时间的最具成本效益的方法？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a warm pool for the Auto Scaling group with warmed EC2 instances in the Stopped state. Configure an autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group. Modify the application to complete the lifecycle hook when the application is ready to serve requests.","B":"Increase the maximum instance count of the Auto Scaling group. Configure an autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group. Modify the application to complete the lifecycle hook when the application is ready to serve requests.","C":"Configure a warm pool for the Auto Scaling group with warmed EC2 instances in the Running state. Configure an autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group. Modify the application to complete the lifecycle hook when the application is ready to serve requests.","D":"Increase the maximum instance count of the Auto Scaling group. Configure an autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group. Modify the application to complete the lifecycle hook and to place the new instance in the Standby state when the application is ready to serve requests."},"options_zh":{"A":"为自动扩展组配置一个包含处于停止状态的预热 EC2 实例的预热池。在自动扩展组上配置一个自 动扩展：EC2 实例启动生命周期挂钩。修改应用程序，使其在准备好处理请求时完成生命周期挂 钩。","B":"增加自动扩展组的最大实例数。在自动扩展组上配置一个生命周期挂钩 autoscaling:EC2_ INSTANCE_LAUNCHING。修改应用程序，使其在准备好处理请求时完成生命周期挂钩。","C":"为自动扩展组配置一个包含处于运行状态的预热 EC2 实例的暖池。在自动扩展组上配置一个 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING 生命周期挂钩。修改应用程序，使其在准备好处理请 求时完成生命周期挂钩。","D":"增加自动扩展组的最大实例数。在自动扩展组上配置一个生命周期挂钩 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_ LAUNCHING。修改应用程序以完成生命周期挂钩，并在应用程序准备好处理请求时将新实例置 于备用状态。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application has a long boot time because it must download and process growing S3 data before serving requests. This is the canonical use case for an EC2 Auto Scaling warm pool, which keeps pre-initialized instances alongside the group so they can warm-start quickly during scale-out. The lifecycle hook (autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING) holds the instance in a wait state while the application finishes the S3 download/processing; the app completes the hook only when ready, so the prepared instance (with processed data already on its EBS volume) is then stopped and parked in the warm pool. The qualifier is MOST cost-effective, which decides between A (Stopped) and C (Running): AWS docs state that keeping warm-pool instances in the Stopped state minimizes cost (you pay only for EBS volumes and any Elastic IPs), whereas keeping them Running is 'highly discouraged to avoid incurring unnecessary charges.' Therefore A is correct.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式啟動時間長，因為它必須先下載並處理不斷增長的 S3 資料才能開始服務請求。這正是 EC2 Auto Scaling warm pool 的典型使用情境：warm pool 在 Auto Scaling group 旁維護預先初始化的執行個體，在 scale-out 時可快速 warm-start。生命週期掛鉤 (autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING) 會讓執行個體進入等待狀態，直到應用程式完成 S3 下載與處理後才完成掛鉤，這樣處理好的執行個體（資料已存在於 EBS 磁碟區）便會被停止並停放在 warm pool 中。題目限定詞是 MOST cost-effective，這決定 A (Stopped) 與 C (Running) 何者正確：AWS 文件指出將 warm pool 執行個體保持在 Stopped 狀態可將成本降到最低（只需支付 EBS 磁碟區與 Elastic IP 費用），而保持 Running 則『強烈不建議，以避免產生不必要的費用』。因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Increasing the maximum instance count does nothing to reduce per-instance startup time; new instances still must download and process the S3 data from scratch. The lifecycle hook only delays the instance from going InService, it does not pre-warm anything. No warm pool means no improvement to readiness latency.","why_zh":"提高最大執行個體數量無法縮短單一執行個體的啟動時間；新執行個體仍須從頭下載並處理 S3 資料。生命週期掛鉤僅延後執行個體進入 InService，並不會預先暖機。沒有 warm pool 就無法改善就緒延遲。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A warm pool in the Running state does technically reduce startup latency, but it is NOT the most cost-effective option. AWS docs explicitly say keeping warm-pool instances Running is 'highly discouraged to avoid incurring unnecessary charges' because you pay full instance cost. Stopped state (A) achieves the same latency benefit at far lower cost.","why_zh":"Running 狀態的 warm pool 技術上確實能降低啟動延遲，但並非最具成本效益的選項。AWS 文件明確指出將 warm pool 執行個體保持 Running『強烈不建議，以避免產生不必要的費用』，因為需支付完整執行個體費用。Stopped 狀態 (A) 能以遠低的成本達到相同的延遲改善。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Increasing max instance count provides no pre-warming benefit (same problem as B). Additionally, placing the instance in Standby state takes it out of service so it does not serve requests and does not count toward serving traffic, which is the opposite of the goal. Standby is for maintenance, not for accelerating readiness.","why_zh":"提高最大執行個體數量無預先暖機效益（與 B 相同問題）。此外，將執行個體置於 Standby 狀態會使其離開服務、不處理請求，與目標相反。Standby 用於維護，並非加速就緒。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-warm-pools.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/create-warm-pool.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/warm-pool-instance-lifecycle.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/lifecycle-hooks.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":74,"question_en":"A company is using an AWS CodeBuild project to build and package an application. The packages are copied to a shared Amazon S3 bucket before being deployed across multiple AWS accounts. The buildspec.yml file contains the following: The DevOps engineer has noticed that anybody with an AWS account is able to download the artifacts. What steps should the DevOps engineer take to stop this?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建和打包应用程序。这些包在部署到多个 AWS 账户之 前会被复制到一个共享的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 buildspec.yml 文件包含以下内容： DevOps 工程师注意到，任何拥有 AWS 账户的人都能够下载这些工件。 DevOps 工程师应该采取哪些措施来阻止这种情况？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the post_build command to use --acl public-read and configure a bucket policy that grants read access to the relevant AWS accounts only.","B":"Configure a default ACL for the S3 bucket that defines the set of authenticated users as the relevant AWS accounts only and grants read-only access.","C":"Create an S3 bucket policy that grants read access to the relevant AWS accounts and denies read access to the principal “*”.","D":"Modify the post_build command to remove --acl authenticated-read and configure a bucket policy that allows read access to the relevant AWS accounts only."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 post_build 命令以使用 --acl public-read，并配置一个仅授予相关 AWS 账户读取权限的存储桶 策略。","B":"为 S3 存储桶配置默认访问控制列表（ACL），将经过身份验证的用户定义为仅相关 AWS 账户， 并授予只读访问权限。","C":"创建一个 S3 存储桶策略，授予相关 AWS 账户读取权限，并拒绝“*”主体的读取权限。","D":"修改 post_build 命令以移除 --acl authenticated-read，并配置一个仅允许相关 AWS 账户读取访问权限的存 储桶策略。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The symptom 'anybody with an AWS account can download the artifacts' is the exact signature of the S3 'authenticated-read' canned ACL. Per the S3 ACL overview, the authenticated-read canned ACL grants READ to the AuthenticatedUsers predefined group, which 'represents all AWS accounts' and 'allows any AWS authenticated user in the world' to access the resource. Therefore the buildspec post_build must be running 'aws s3 cp ... --acl authenticated-read'. The fix is to remove that over-broad ACL grant and instead scope access with a bucket policy that allows read only to the relevant AWS accounts, which is also AWS's recommended pattern (use policies, keep ACLs disabled). That is exactly option D. Option C is the trap: an explicit Deny on Principal '*' overrides any Allow (explicit deny always trumps allow), so it would also deny the relevant accounts you intend to allow, and it leaves the offending ACL in place rather than removing the root cause.","explanation_zh":"症狀「任何擁有 AWS 帳戶的人都能下載成品」正是 S3 'authenticated-read' canned ACL 的典型特徵。根據 S3 ACL overview 文件，authenticated-read canned ACL 會把 READ 權限授予 AuthenticatedUsers 預定義群組，而該群組『代表所有 AWS 帳戶』，會『允許世界上任何已驗證的 AWS 使用者』存取資源。因此 buildspec 的 post_build 必定執行了 'aws s3 cp ... --acl authenticated-read'。正確修法是移除這個過於寬鬆的 ACL 授權，改用 bucket policy 只允許相關 AWS 帳戶讀取，這也是 AWS 建議的做法（用 policy、停用 ACL）。這正是選項 D。選項 C 是陷阱：對 Principal '*' 的明確 Deny 會覆蓋任何 Allow（explicit deny 永遠勝過 allow），因此會連你想允許的相關帳戶都一併拒絕，且未移除真正的根因 ACL。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"--acl public-read maps to the AllUsers group, which grants access to ANYONE in the world (even anonymous/unauthenticated). This makes the exposure worse, not better, and a bucket policy Allow cannot retract the open ACL grant.","why_zh":"--acl public-read 對應 AllUsers 群組，會授權給世界上任何人（甚至匿名未驗證者）。這只會讓暴露更嚴重，而 bucket policy 的 Allow 也無法收回已經放開的 ACL 授權。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"You cannot use the AuthenticatedUsers ACL group to mean 'only the relevant accounts'; that predefined group always means ALL AWS accounts. Defining a 'default ACL' this way does not exist and would not restrict access; ACLs are also discouraged in favor of policies.","why_zh":"無法用 AuthenticatedUsers ACL 群組來表示『只有相關帳戶』；該預定義群組永遠代表所有 AWS 帳戶。這樣的『預設 ACL』設定並不存在，也無法限制存取；而且 AWS 建議改用 policy 而非 ACL。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An explicit Deny on Principal '*' overrides every Allow (explicit deny always wins), so the relevant accounts you Allow would also be denied, breaking the legitimate cross-account deployment. It also leaves the root-cause authenticated-read ACL in place.","why_zh":"對 Principal '*' 的明確 Deny 會覆蓋所有 Allow（明確拒絕永遠勝出），因此你 Allow 的相關帳戶也會被拒絕，破壞合法的跨帳戶部署。同時也未移除真正根因的 authenticated-read ACL。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/acl-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic_AccessPolicyLanguage_Interplay.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":75,"question_en":"A company has developed a serverless web application that is hosted on AWS. The application consists of Amazon S3. Amazon API Gateway, several AWS Lambda functions, and an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. The company is using AWS CodeCommit to store the source code. The source code is a combination of AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) templates and Python code. A security audit and penetration test reveal that user names and passwords for authentication to the database are hardcoded within CodeCommit repositories. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution to automatically detect and prevent hardcoded secrets. What is the MOST secure solution that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一个无服务器的网络应用程序，该应用程序托管在 AWS 上。此应用程序由 Amazon S3、 Amazon API Gateway、若干 AWS Lambda 函数以及一个 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库组成。该公司使用 AWS CodeCommit 来存储源代码。源代码由 AWS 无服务器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）模板和 Python 代码 组合而成。 安全审计和渗透测试显示，用于数据库身份验证的用户名和密码被硬编码在 CodeCommit 存储库中。 DevOps 工程师必须实施解决方案，以自动检测并防止硬编码的机密信息。 满足这些要求的最安全的解决方案是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon CodeGuru Profiler. Decorate the handler function with @with_lambda_profiler(). Manually review the recommendation report. Write the secret to AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as a secure string. Update the SAM templates and the Python code to pull the secret from Parameter Store.","B":"Associate the CodeCommit repository with Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer. Manually check the code review for any recommendations. Choose the option to protect the secret. Update the SAM templates and the Python code to pull the secret from AWS Secrets Manager.","C":"Enable Amazon CodeGuru Profiler. Decorate the handler function with @with_lambda_profiler(). Manually review the recommendation report. Choose the option to protect the secret. Update the SAM templates and the Python code to pull the secret from AWS Secrets Manager.","D":"Associate the CodeCommit repository with Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer. Manually check the code review for any recommendations. Write the secret to AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as a string. Update the SAM templates and the Python code to pull the secret from Parameter Store."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 Amazon CodeGuru Profiler。使用 @with_lambda_profiler（） 装饰处理函数。手动审查建议报告。 将密钥作为安全字符串写入 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储。更新 SAM 模板和 Python 代码以从参 数存储中提取密钥。","B":"将 CodeCommit 存储库与 Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 关联。手动检查代码审查中的任何建议。选择保 护机密的选项。更新 SAM 模板和 Python 代码以从 AWS Secrets Manager 中获取机密。","C":"启用 Amazon CodeGuru Profiler。使用 @with_lambda_profiler（） 装饰处理函数。手动审查建议报告。选 择保护密钥的选项。更新 SAM 模板和 Python 代码，从 AWS Secrets Manager 中获取密钥。","D":"将 CodeCommit 存储库与 Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 关联。手动检查代码审查中的任何建议。将密 钥作为字符串写入 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储。更新 SAM 模板和 Python 代码以从参数存储中 获取密钥。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to automatically detect and prevent hardcoded secrets in a Java/Python source repository (AWS SAM templates + Python) stored in CodeCommit, and to do so as securely as possible. Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer is the AWS service whose secrets detector automatically scans Java and Python repositories (including CodeCommit) for hardcoded passwords, database connection strings, user names, and more. When it finds an unprotected secret it generates a recommendation with a 'Protect your credential' option that opens the AWS Secrets Manager console so you can migrate the secret. Secrets Manager is the most secure target because it provides encryption, fine-grained access control, audit logging, and automatic rotation of credentials (ideal for the RDS for MySQL password). Option B associates the CodeCommit repo with CodeGuru Reviewer, uses the protect-the-secret recommendation, and pulls the secret from Secrets Manager, which exactly matches the AWS documented workflow and is the MOST secure choice.","explanation_zh":"需求是自動偵測並防止存放在 CodeCommit 的 Java/Python 原始碼（AWS SAM 範本 + Python）中硬編碼的機密，並以最安全的方式達成。Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 的 secrets detector 會自動掃描 Java 與 Python 儲存庫（包含 CodeCommit），找出硬編碼的密碼、資料庫連線字串、使用者名稱等。當偵測到未受保護的機密時，會產生建議並提供「Protect your credential」選項，直接開啟 AWS Secrets Manager 主控台以遷移該機密。Secrets Manager 是最安全的目標，因為它提供加密、細緻的存取控制、稽核紀錄，以及自動輪替憑證（非常適合 RDS for MySQL 密碼）。選項 B 將 CodeCommit 儲存庫與 CodeGuru Reviewer 關聯、使用保護機密的建議，並從 Secrets Manager 取得機密，完全符合 AWS 官方文件流程，是最安全的選擇。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon CodeGuru Profiler with @with_lambda_profiler() is for runtime CPU/performance and heap profiling of Lambda functions, not for detecting hardcoded secrets in source code. Parameter Store SecureString is encrypted but is less feature-rich (no built-in automatic rotation) and this option uses the wrong detection service.","why_zh":"Amazon CodeGuru Profiler 與 @with_lambda_profiler() 是用於 Lambda 函式的執行期 CPU/效能與堆積分析，並非偵測原始碼中的硬編碼機密。Parameter Store SecureString 雖加密但功能較少（無內建自動輪替），且此選項使用了錯誤的偵測服務。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same fundamental error as A: CodeGuru Profiler does not detect secrets. The 'Protect your credential' option and Secrets Manager integration belong to CodeGuru Reviewer, not Profiler, so the workflow described is technically impossible.","why_zh":"與 A 有相同的根本錯誤：CodeGuru Profiler 不會偵測機密。「Protect your credential」選項與 Secrets Manager 整合屬於 CodeGuru Reviewer 而非 Profiler，因此所述流程在技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeGuru Reviewer is the correct detection service, but storing the credential in Parameter Store as a plaintext 'string' (not even a SecureString) is the least secure storage option and ignores the documented 'Protect your credential' -> Secrets Manager workflow. The question asks for the MOST secure solution.","why_zh":"CodeGuru Reviewer 是正確的偵測服務，但將憑證以純文字「string」（甚至不是 SecureString）存入 Parameter Store 是最不安全的儲存方式，並忽略了官方文件的「Protect your credential」->Secrets Manager 流程。題目要求最安全的解決方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeguru/latest/reviewer-ug/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeguru/latest/reviewer-ug/recommendations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeguru/latest/profiler-ug/what-is-codeguru-profiler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":76,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon S3 buckets to store important documents. The company discovers that some S3 buckets are not encrypted. Currently, the company’s IAM users can create new S3 buckets without encryption. The company is implementing a new requirement that all S3 buckets must be encrypted. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution to ensure that server-side encryption is enabled on all existing S3 buckets and all new S3 buckets. The encryption must be enabled on new S3 buckets as soon as the S3 buckets are created. The default encryption type must be 256-bit Advanced Encryption Standard (AES-256). Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊 S3 存储桶来存储重要文件。该公司发现有些 S3 存储桶未加密。目前，该公司的 IAM 用户可以创建未加密的新 S3 存储桶。该公司正在实施一项新要求，即所有 S3 存储桶都必须加密。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一项解决方案，以确保所有现有的 S3 存储桶以及所有新创建的 S3 存储桶都启用服 务器端加密。新创建的 S3 存储桶必须在创建时立即启用加密。默认加密类型必须为 256 位高级加密标准 （AES-256）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked periodically by an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule. Program the Lambda function to scan all current S3 buckets for encryption status and to set AES- 256 as the default encryption for any S3 bucket that does not have an encryption configuration.","B":"Set up and activate the s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled AWS Config managed rule. Configure the rule to use the AWS-EnableS3BucketEncryption AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook as the remediation action. Manually run the re-evaluation process to ensure that existing S3 buckets are compliant.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by an Amazon EventBridge event rule. Define the rule with an event pattern that matches the creation of new S3 buckets. Program the Lambda function to parse the EventBridge event, check the configuration of the S3 buckets from the event, and set AES- 256 as the default encryption.","D":"Configure an IAM policy that denies the s3:CreateBucket action if the s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption condition key has a value that is not AES-256. Create an IAM group for all the company’s IAM users. Associate the IAM policy with the IAM group."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数由 Amazon EventBridge 定期调度规则周期性调用。编写该 Lambda 函数，使其扫描所有当前的 S3 存储桶以检查加密状态，并将任何未配置加密的 S3 存储桶的默认加密 方式设置为 AES-256。","B":"设置并激活 s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled AWS Config 管理规则。将规则配置为使用 AWS- EnableS3BucketEncryption AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册作为修复操作。手动运行重新 评估流程，以确保现有 S3 存储桶符合要求。","C":"创建一个由 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则触发的 AWS Lambda 函数。定义该规则 使用与创建新的 S3 存储桶相匹配的事件模式。编写 Lambda 函数来解析 EventBridge 事件，从事 件中检查 S3 存储桶的配置，并将 AES-256 设置为默认加密方式。","D":"配置一个 IAM 策略，如果 s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption 条件键的值不是 AES-256，则拒绝 s3: CreateBucket 操作。为公司所有的 IAM 用户创建一个 IAM 组。将 IAM 策略与 IAM 组关联。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Option B is correct. The AWS Config managed rule s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled checks whether each S3 bucket has default encryption (AES-256 or KMS) and is NON_COMPLIANT if not. Its trigger type is 'Configuration changes', so it evaluates new buckets as soon as they are created and resources can be re-evaluated for the existing fleet. Attaching the AWS-EnableS3BucketEncryption SSM Automation runbook as the remediation action sets default encryption with SSEAlgorithm defaulting to AES256, fixing both existing and new noncompliant buckets near-immediately. This covers all three requirements: existing buckets, new buckets at creation time, and AES-256. The dump's suggested answer D is technically wrong: s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption is an OBJECT-operation condition key used with s3:PutObject to require encryption on uploads; it is not a condition key for s3:CreateBucket, so the Deny would not enforce bucket-level default encryption, and it does nothing for already-existing unencrypted buckets nor does it ever set default encryption.","explanation_zh":"正確答案為 B。AWS Config 受管規則 s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled 會檢查每個 S3 bucket 是否已啟用預設加密（AES-256 或 KMS），若未啟用則標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。其觸發類型為「Configuration changes」，因此新建立的 bucket 一經建立即會被評估，且可對既有 bucket 重新評估。將 AWS-EnableS3BucketEncryption SSM Automation runbook 設為補救動作，SSEAlgorithm 預設為 AES256，可近乎即時修復既有與新建的不合規 bucket。此方案同時滿足三項需求：既有 bucket、建立時即加密的新 bucket、以及 AES-256。題庫建議答案 D 在技術上是錯誤的：s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption 是用於 s3:PutObject 的「物件操作」條件鍵，用於要求上傳物件加密，並非 s3:CreateBucket 的條件鍵，因此該 Deny 無法強制 bucket 層級的預設加密，也無法處理既有未加密的 bucket，更不會設定預設加密。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A periodic EventBridge schedule only scans existing buckets on an interval and does not enable encryption on new buckets 'as soon as' they are created; there is a delay until the next scheduled run, violating the immediacy requirement. It is also more operational overhead than the managed Config rule + runbook.","why_zh":"週期性 EventBridge 排程僅按間隔掃描既有 bucket，無法在新 bucket「一建立即」啟用加密；直到下一次排程執行前都有延遲，違反即時性要求。相較受管 Config 規則加 runbook，營運負擔也更高。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An EventBridge rule on bucket creation handles only NEW buckets and does nothing for the existing unencrypted buckets, which is an explicit requirement. It also requires custom Lambda code (more overhead) versus the managed solution.","why_zh":"針對 bucket 建立的 EventBridge 規則只處理「新」bucket，對既有未加密的 bucket 毫無作用，而那是明確需求之一。同時需自寫 Lambda 程式（負擔更高），不如受管方案。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption is an object-operation (s3:PutObject) condition key, not a valid condition key for s3:CreateBucket, so the Deny does not enforce bucket default encryption. It also never remediates existing unencrypted buckets and never sets AES-256 default encryption on any bucket.","why_zh":"s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption 是物件操作（s3:PutObject）的條件鍵，並非 s3:CreateBucket 的有效條件鍵，故該 Deny 無法強制 bucket 預設加密。它也完全不會修復既有未加密的 bucket，更不會為任何 bucket 設定 AES-256 預設加密。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-enableS3bucketencryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/amazon-s3-policy-keys.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":77,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is architecting a continuous development strategy for a company’s software as a service (SaaS) web application running on AWS. For application and security reasons, users subscribing to this application are distributed across multiple Application Load Balancers (ALBs), each of which has a dedicated Auto Scaling group and fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The application does not require a build stage, and when it is committed to AWS CodeCommit, the application must trigger a simultaneous deployment to all ALBs, Auto Scaling groups, and EC2 fleets. Which architecture will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of configuration?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一家公司运行在 AWS 上的软件即服务（SaaS）网络应用程序设计持续开发 策略。出于应用程序和安全方面的考虑，订阅该应用程序的用户分布在多个应用负载均衡器（ALB）上， 每个 ALB 都有一个专用的自动扩展组和一组亚马逊 EC2 实例。该应用程序无需构建阶段，当提交到 AWS CodeCommit 时，必须同时触发对所有 ALB、自动扩展组和 EC2 实例群的部署。 哪种架构能够以最少的配置满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline that deploys the application in parallel using unique AWS CodeDeploy applications and deployment groups created for each ALB-Auto Scaling group pair.","B":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline that deploys the application using a single AWS CodeDeploy application and single deployment group.","C":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline that deploys the application in parallel using a single AWS CodeDeploy application and unique deployment group for each ALB-Auto Scaling group pair.","D":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline for each ALB-Auto Scaling group pair that deploys the application using an AWS CodeDeploy application and deployment group created for the same ALB- Auto Scaling group pair."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个单一的 AWS CodePipeline 管道，使用为每个 ALB - Auto Scaling 组对创建的独特的 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序和部署组并行部署应用程序。","B":"创建一个单一的 AWS CodePipeline 管道，使用一个单一的 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序和 一个单一的部署组来部署应用程序。","C":"创建一个单一的 AWS CodePipeline 管道，使用单个 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序并为每个 ALB - Auto Scaling 组对创建独特的部署组来并行部署应用程序。","D":"为每个 ALB - 自动扩展组对创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，使用为同一 ALB - 自动扩展组对创 建的 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序和部署组来部署应用程序。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A CodeDeploy application is a container for one or more deployment groups, and each EC2/On-Premises deployment group defines a specific set of target instances via Auto Scaling group(s) plus an associated load balancer/target group. Because every ALB-Auto Scaling group pair is a distinct ASG fronted by a distinct ALB, you need one deployment group per pair. Within a single CodePipeline stage, multiple deploy actions assigned the same runOrder execute in parallel, so a single pipeline with one Source stage and one Deploy stage containing N parallel CodeDeploy actions triggers a simultaneous deployment to all pairs when the CodeCommit commit fires the source action. Option C achieves this with the minimum building blocks: one pipeline, one CodeDeploy application, and one deployment group per pair. This is fewer resources than Option A (which needlessly creates a separate CodeDeploy application per pair) and far fewer than Option D (one whole pipeline per pair).","explanation_zh":"CodeDeploy application 是一個或多個 deployment group 的容器，而每個 EC2/On-Premises deployment group 透過 Auto Scaling group 以及關聯的 load balancer/target group 定義一組特定的目標執行個體。由於每個 ALB-Auto Scaling group 組合都是獨立的 ASG 搭配獨立的 ALB，因此每個組合都需要一個獨立的 deployment group。在單一 CodePipeline stage 中，被指定相同 runOrder 的多個 deploy action 會平行執行，因此只要一條 pipeline（一個 Source stage 加上一個含 N 個平行 CodeDeploy action 的 Deploy stage），在 CodeCommit 提交觸發 source action 時即可同時部署到所有組合。選項 C 以最少的元件達成：一條 pipeline、一個 CodeDeploy application、每個組合一個 deployment group。這比選項 A（多餘地為每個組合建立獨立的 CodeDeploy application）資源更少，更遠少於選項 D（每個組合一整條 pipeline）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Works functionally (one pipeline, parallel actions, one deployment group per pair) but creates a separate CodeDeploy application for every ALB-ASG pair, which is unnecessary configuration; a single application can hold all the deployment groups, so A is not the LEAST configuration.","why_zh":"功能上可行（一條 pipeline、平行 action、每組一個 deployment group），但為每個 ALB-ASG 組合各建立一個獨立的 CodeDeploy application 屬於多餘的設定；單一 application 即可容納所有 deployment group，因此 A 並非最少設定。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A single deployment group cannot serve as the deployment target for multiple distinct ASGs each fronted by its own ALB; a deployment group's instance targeting and load balancer association are part of its definition, so one group cannot cleanly map to many separate ALB-ASG pairs. It fails the requirement to deploy to all pairs.","why_zh":"單一 deployment group 無法作為多個各自有獨立 ALB 的不同 ASG 的部署目標；deployment group 的執行個體目標與 load balancer 關聯屬於其定義的一部分，因此一個 group 無法乾淨地對應到多個獨立的 ALB-ASG 組合，無法滿足部署到所有組合的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating one entire pipeline per ALB-ASG pair works but is the MOST configuration: N pipelines, N source actions and N CodeCommit triggers. The question explicitly asks for the LEAST configuration, so D is wrong.","why_zh":"為每個 ALB-ASG 組合各建立一整條 pipeline 雖可行，但是設定量最多：N 條 pipeline、N 個 source action 與 N 個 CodeCommit 觸發。題目明確要求最少設定，因此 D 錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/reference-pipeline-structure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-create-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/primary-components.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":78,"question_en":"A company is hosting a static website from an Amazon S3 bucket. The website is available to customers at example.com. The company uses an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy with a TTL of 1 day. The company has decided to replace the existing static website with a dynamic web application. The dynamic web application uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. On the day of production launch to customers, the company creates an additional Route 53 weighted DNS record entry that points to the ALB with a weight of 255 and a TTL of 1 hour. Two days later, a DevOps engineer notices that the previous static website is displayed sometimes when customers navigate to example.com. How can the DevOps engineer ensure that the company serves only dynamic content for example.com?","question_zh":"一家公司正在通过 Amazon S3 存储桶托管一个静态网站，该网站可通过 example.com 访问。该公司使用 了 Amazon Route 53 的加权路由策略，其 TTL 为 1 天。该公司决定用一个动态网络应用程序取代现有的 静态网站。该动态网络应用程序在一组 Amazon EC2 实例前使用了应用负载均衡器（ALB）。 在向客户推出产品的当天，该公司创建了一个额外的 Route 53 加权 DNS 记录条目，该条目指向 ALB， 权重为 255，TTL 为 1 小时。两天后，一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，当客户访问 example.com 时，有时 会显示之前的静态网站。 DevOps 工程师如何确保公司只为 example.com 提供动态内容？","options_en":{"A":"Delete all objects, including previous versions, from the S3 bucket that contains the static website content.","B":"Update the weighted DNS record entry that points to the S3 bucket. Apply a weight of 0. Specify the domain reset option to propagate changes immediately.","C":"Configure webpage redirect requests on the S3 bucket with a hostname that redirects to the ALB.","D":"Remove the weighted DNS record entry that points to the S3 bucket from the example.com hosted zone. Wait for DNS propagation to become complete."},"options_zh":{"A":"从包含静态网站内容的 S3 存储桶中删除所有对象，包括其先前版本。","B":"更新指向 S3 存储桶的加权 DNS 记录条目。将权重设置为 0。选择立即传播更改的域名重置选项。","C":"在 S3 存储桶上配置网页重定向请求，使用可重定向到应用负载均衡器（ALB）的主机名。","D":"从 example.com 托管区域中删除指向 S3 存储桶的加权 DNS 记录条目。等待 DNS 传播完成。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The old static website still appears intermittently because the original weighted DNS record pointing to the S3 bucket still exists in the example.com hosted zone with a non-zero weight. With weighted routing, Route 53 distributes queries across all records in the group proportionally to their weights, so as long as the S3 record retains a non-zero weight it keeps receiving a share of queries. To serve only dynamic content, the engineer must remove the S3 weighted record from the hosted zone so the ALB record is the only answer Route 53 returns. Because resolvers cache the old answer, you then wait for DNS propagation (the S3 record's 1-day TTL) to complete; two days had already passed for new launch, but the active record was still being served, so removal plus waiting for any cached entries to expire fully fixes it. The AWS weighted routing doc notes you 'can change the weight for that record to 0' to stop traffic, but the option that does this (B) invents a non-existent 'domain reset option to propagate changes immediately,' which is not a Route 53 feature, making D the only valid and complete answer.","explanation_zh":"舊的靜態網站仍偶爾出現，是因為指向 S3 bucket 的原始 weighted DNS 記錄仍存在於 example.com 的 hosted zone 中，且權重不為零。weighted routing 會依各記錄的權重比例把查詢分散到群組中的所有記錄，因此只要 S3 記錄保留非零權重，它就會持續接收一部分查詢。要只提供動態內容，工程師必須從 hosted zone 移除該 S3 weighted 記錄，使 ALB 記錄成為 Route 53 唯一回傳的答案。由於 resolver 會快取舊答案，接著需等待 DNS 傳播完成（S3 記錄的 1 天 TTL）；雖然啟用後已過兩天，但該記錄仍被主動提供回應，所以移除記錄並等待任何快取項目過期才能徹底解決。AWS weighted routing 文件確實指出可把記錄權重改為 0 來停止流量，但採用此做法的選項 B 卻虛構了不存在的『domain reset option to propagate changes immediately』，Route 53 並無此功能，因此 D 是唯一正確且完整的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deleting the S3 objects does not change DNS routing. Route 53 would still send a proportion of queries to the S3 website endpoint, where customers would now hit errors instead of dynamic content, so it does not ensure only dynamic content is served.","why_zh":"刪除 S3 物件不會改變 DNS 路由。Route 53 仍會把一部分查詢送到 S3 網站端點，此時客戶會看到錯誤而非動態內容，因此無法確保只提供動態內容。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Setting weight 0 would technically stop traffic to the S3 record, but Route 53 has no 'domain reset option to propagate changes immediately.' That feature is fabricated; DNS changes still depend on TTL expiry and cannot be force-propagated, so this option is invalid.","why_zh":"把權重設為 0 在技術上確實能停止流向 S3 記錄的流量，但 Route 53 並無『domain reset option to propagate changes immediately』。此功能屬虛構；DNS 變更仍取決於 TTL 過期且無法強制傳播，因此此選項無效。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Configuring an S3 website redirect to the ALB is an unnecessary, convoluted workaround. It still leaves the S3 weighted DNS record in place and adds a redirect hop instead of cleanly removing the source of the problem at the DNS layer.","why_zh":"在 S3 設定網站重新導向到 ALB 是不必要且迂迴的做法。它仍保留 S3 的 weighted DNS 記錄，並增加一次重新導向，而非在 DNS 層乾淨地移除問題根源。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-weighted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/migrate-dns-domain-in-use.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":79,"question_en":"A company is implementing AWS CodePipeline to automate its testing process. The company wants to be notified when the execution state fails and used the following custom event pattern in Amazon EventBridge: Which type of events will match this event pattern?","question_zh":"一家公司正在实施 AWS CodePipeline 来自动化其测试流程。该公司希望在执行状态失败时收到通知，并在 Amazon EventBridge 中使用了以下自定义事件模式： 哪种类型的事件会匹配此事件模式？","options_en":{"A":"Failed deploy and build actions across all the pipelines","B":"All rejected or failed approval actions across all the pipelines","C":"All the events across all pipelines","D":"Approval actions across all the pipelines"},"options_zh":{"A":"所有管道中的部署和构建操作均失败","B":"所有流水线中所有被拒绝或审批未通过的操作","C":"所有管道中的所有事件","D":"所有流水线中的审批操作"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The four options are verbatim copies of the descriptive captions AWS uses for its sample CodePipeline EventBridge event patterns in the 'Monitoring CodePipeline events' documentation. The pattern in this question filters on detail-type 'CodePipeline Action Execution State Change' with detail.state = ['FAILED'] and detail.type.category = ['Approval']. AWS documents this exact pattern with the caption: 'Use this sample event pattern to capture all rejected or failed approval actions across all the pipelines.' Critically, for approval actions the FAILED state means the action was either rejected by the reviewer or failed due to incorrect configuration, so a state=FAILED + category=Approval filter captures rejected OR failed approvals. This matches option B exactly.","explanation_zh":"四個選項逐字對應 AWS 'Monitoring CodePipeline events' 文件中各範例 EventBridge event pattern 的描述文字。本題的 pattern 篩選 detail-type 為 'CodePipeline Action Execution State Change'，且 detail.state = ['FAILED']、detail.type.category = ['Approval']。AWS 文件對此 pattern 的描述正是：'Use this sample event pattern to capture all rejected or failed approval actions across all the pipelines.' 關鍵在於：對 approval action 而言，FAILED 狀態代表該動作被審核者拒絕（rejected）或因設定錯誤而失敗，因此 state=FAILED + category=Approval 即可捕捉被拒絕或失敗的審核動作，完全對應選項 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This describes the separate AWS sample pattern that filters state=['FAILED'] with type.category=['Deploy','Build'] — failed deploy and build actions, not approval actions.","why_zh":"這對應另一個 AWS 範例 pattern：state=['FAILED'] 搭配 type.category=['Deploy','Build']，即失敗的 deploy 與 build 動作，而非 approval 動作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"'All the events across all pipelines' corresponds to the AWS sample pattern listing all three detail-types (Pipeline/Stage/Action Execution State Change), not a FAILED + Approval-category action filter.","why_zh":"'所有 pipeline 的所有事件' 對應的是列出三種 detail-type（Pipeline/Stage/Action Execution State Change）的範例 pattern，而非 FAILED + Approval category 的動作篩選。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"'Approval actions across all the pipelines' (without the FAILED qualifier) would be a pattern filtering only type.category=['Approval'] with no state restriction, which would match approvals in any state (STARTED, SUCCEEDED, FAILED). The pattern here restricts state to FAILED, so it captures rejected/failed approvals specifically, not all approval actions.","why_zh":"'所有 pipeline 的審核動作'（無 FAILED 限定）對應的是只篩選 type.category=['Approval'] 而不限定 state 的 pattern，會比對任何狀態（STARTED、SUCCEEDED、FAILED）的審核。本題 pattern 限定 state 為 FAILED，因此專門捕捉被拒絕/失敗的審核，而非所有審核動作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/detect-state-changes-cloudwatch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codepipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":80,"question_en":"An application running on a set of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group requires a configuration file to operate. The instances are created and maintained with AWS CloudFormation. A DevOps engineer wants the instances to have the latest configuration file when launched, and wants changes to the configuration file to be reflected on all the instances with a minimal delay when the CloudFormation template is updated. Company policy requires that application configuration files be maintained along with AWS infrastructure configuration files in source control. Which solution will accomplish this?","question_zh":"在一组由 AWS CloudFormation 创建和维护的 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行的应用程序 需要一个配置文件才能运行。一位 DevOps 工程师希望实例在启动时拥有最新的配置文件，并且希望 在更新 CloudFormation 模板时，配置文件的更改能以最小的延迟反映到所有实例上。公司政策要求将 应用程序配置文件与 AWS 基础设施配置文件一起保存在源代码控制中。 哪种解决方案能实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"In the CloudFormation template, add an AWS Config rule. Place the configuration file content in the rule’s InputParameters property, and set the Scope property to the EC2 Auto Scaling group. Add an AWS Systems Manager Resource Data Sync resource to the template to poll for updates to the configuration.","B":"In the CloudFormation template, add an EC2 launch template resource. Place the configuration file content in the launch template. Configure the cfn-init script to run when the instance is launched, and configure the cfn-hup script to poll for updates to the configuration.","C":"In the CloudFormation template, add an EC2 launch template resource. Place the configuration file content in the launch template. Add an AWS Systems Manager Resource Data Sync resource to the template to poll for updates to the configuration.","D":"In the CloudFormation template, add CloudFormation init metadata. Place the configuration file content in the metadata. Configure the cfn-init script to run when the instance is launched, and configure the cfn-hup script to poll for updates to the configuration."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFormation 模板中添加一个 AWS Config 规则。将配置文件内容放入规则的 InputParameters 属 性中，并将 Scope 属性设置为 EC2 自动扩展组。添加一个 将 AWS Systems Manager 资源数据同步资源添加到模板中，以轮询配置更新。","B":"在 CloudFormation 模板中，添加一个 EC2 启动模板资源。将配置文件的内容放入启动模板中。配 置 cfn-init 脚本在实例启动时运行，并配置 cfn-hup 脚本轮询配置的更新。","C":"在 CloudFormation 模板中，添加一个 EC2 启动模板资源。将配置文件的内容放入启动模板中。在 模板中添加一个 AWS Systems Manager 资源数据同步资源，以轮询配置的更新。","D":"在 CloudFormation 模板中添加 CloudFormation 初始化元数据。将配置文件的内容放入元数据中。配 置 cfn-init 脚本在实例启动时运行，并配置 cfn-hup 脚本轮询配置的更新。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical CloudFormation pattern for delivering and refreshing a configuration file on Auto Scaling instances. You place the file content in AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata (which lives in the template, satisfying the source-control requirement). cfn-init runs at instance launch to write the latest file, and the cfn-hup daemon detects changes in the resource metadata and runs user-specified actions when a change is detected, allowing configuration updates on running instances through the UpdateStack API (default poll interval 15 minutes, configurable lower), so an updated template propagates to all instances with minimal delay. Option B is wrong because AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata must be attached to a resource's Metadata block (the launch template or instance resource) and read by cfn-init; cfn-init/cfn-hup read the AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key, not arbitrary 'configuration file content placed in the launch template' user data. Resource Data Sync (A, C) only aggregates Inventory/OpsData/Compliance data into S3 and never pushes config files to instances, and an AWS Config rule (A) only evaluates compliance.","explanation_zh":"這是 CloudFormation 在 Auto Scaling 執行個體上派送並更新設定檔的標準模式。將檔案內容放入 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata（存在於範本中，符合納入原始碼控管的要求）。cfn-init 在執行個體啟動時執行以寫入最新檔案；cfn-hup daemon 會偵測資源 metadata 的變更，並在偵測到變更時執行使用者指定的動作，透過 UpdateStack API 對執行中的執行個體套用設定更新（預設輪詢間隔 15 分鐘，可調更短），因此更新範本後能以最小延遲傳播到所有執行個體。選項 B 錯誤，因為 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata 必須附加在資源的 Metadata 區塊（執行個體或 launch template 資源）並由 cfn-init 讀取；cfn-init/cfn-hup 讀取的是 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key，而非單純放在 launch template 內的『設定檔內容』。Resource Data Sync（A、C）只會將 Inventory/OpsData/Compliance 資料彙整到 S3，從不會將設定檔推送到執行個體；AWS Config rule（A）只做合規評估。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config rules evaluate resource compliance and do not deliver configuration files to EC2 instances; InputParameters are evaluation inputs, not file content. Resource Data Sync only aggregates Inventory/OpsData/Compliance data into S3. Neither component refreshes a config file on instances.","why_zh":"AWS Config rule 只評估資源合規，不會將設定檔派送到 EC2 執行個體；InputParameters 是評估輸入而非檔案內容。Resource Data Sync 只將 Inventory/OpsData/Compliance 資料彙整到 S3。兩者都無法更新執行個體上的設定檔。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"cfn-init and cfn-hup read the AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key, not free-form 'configuration file content placed in the launch template'. The Init metadata mechanism is the documented way; placing file content directly in the launch template (e.g., user data) is not how cfn-init/cfn-hup detect and apply metadata changes.","why_zh":"cfn-init 與 cfn-hup 讀取的是 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key，而非『放在 launch template 內的設定檔內容』。Init metadata 機制才是官方記載的方法；直接把檔案內容放進 launch template（如 user data）並非 cfn-init/cfn-hup 偵測並套用 metadata 變更的方式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Resource Data Sync syncs Inventory/OpsData/Compliance data to an S3 bucket; it cannot poll for or push configuration-file updates to instances. There is no cfn-hup or update-detection mechanism here, so changes would never reach running instances.","why_zh":"Resource Data Sync 將 Inventory/OpsData/Compliance 資料同步到 S3；無法輪詢或將設定檔更新推送到執行個體。此處沒有 cfn-hup 或變更偵測機制，因此變更永遠不會傳到執行中的執行個體。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-hup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-init.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-init.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/inventory-create-resource-data-sync.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":81,"question_en":"A company manages an application that stores logs in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The company wants to archive the logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. Logs are rarely accessed after 90 days and must be retained for 10 years. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司管理着一个将日志存储在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中的应用程序。该公司希望将日志归档到 Amazon S3 存储桶中。90 天后，这些日志很少被访问，但必须保留 10 年。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤的组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to use AWS Glue to transfer all logs to an S3 bucket.","B":"Configure a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to stream all logs to an S3 bucket.","C":"Configure a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to stream all logs to an S3 bucket.","D":"Configure the S3 bucket lifecycle policy to transition logs to S3 Glacier after 90 days and to expire logs after 3,650 days.","E":"Configure the S3 bucket lifecycle policy to transition logs to Reduced Redundancy after 90 days and to expire logs after 3,650 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 CloudWatch 日志订阅筛选器，使用 AWS Glue 将所有日志传输到 S3 存储桶。","B":"配置 CloudWatch 日志订阅筛选器，使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 将所有日志流式传输到 S3 存储桶。","C":"配置 CloudWatch 日志订阅筛选器，将所有日志流式传输到 S3 存储桶。","D":"配置 S3 存储桶生命周期策略，将日志在 90 天后转存至 S3 Glacier，并在 3650 天后过期。","E":"配置 S3 存储桶生命周期策略，将日志在 90 天后转为低冗余存储，并在 3650 天后过期。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filters can deliver log data only to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service - they cannot write directly to Amazon S3 and cannot target AWS Glue. To continuously archive all logs to S3, the supported pattern is a subscription filter that streams to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, which natively delivers to an S3 bucket (B). For retention and cost optimization, an S3 Lifecycle policy transitions objects to S3 Glacier after 90 days (logs are rarely accessed after 90 days) and expires them after 3,650 days = 10 years (D). S3 Lifecycle's supported transition targets are S3 Standard-IA, Intelligent-Tiering, One Zone-IA, Glacier Instant/Flexible Retrieval, and Glacier Deep Archive - Reduced Redundancy Storage is a deprecated class and is not a valid lifecycle transition target, so E is invalid.","explanation_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能將日誌傳送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service，無法直接寫入 Amazon S3，也無法以 AWS Glue 作為目的地。要持續將所有日誌歸檔到 S3，受支援的做法是使用 subscription filter 串流到 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose，再由 Firehose 原生交付到 S3 bucket（B）。在保留與成本最佳化方面，S3 Lifecycle 政策在 90 天後將物件轉換到 S3 Glacier（日誌在 90 天後鮮少存取），並在 3,650 天（即 10 年）後使其到期（D）。S3 Lifecycle 支援的轉換目標為 S3 Standard-IA、Intelligent-Tiering、One Zone-IA、Glacier Instant/Flexible Retrieval 以及 Glacier Deep Archive，Reduced Redundancy Storage 是已棄用的儲存類別，並非有效的 lifecycle 轉換目標，因此 E 無效。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Glue is not a valid CloudWatch Logs subscription filter destination; subscription filters only support Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Data Firehose, and OpenSearch Service.","why_zh":"AWS Glue 不是有效的 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 目的地；subscription filter 只支援 Kinesis Data Streams、Lambda、Data Firehose 與 OpenSearch Service。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A subscription filter cannot stream directly to an S3 bucket; S3 is not one of the supported subscription filter destinations, so an intermediary like Firehose is required.","why_zh":"subscription filter 無法直接串流到 S3 bucket；S3 並非受支援的目的地，必須透過 Firehose 之類的中介服務。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Reduced Redundancy Storage (RRS) is a deprecated, not-recommended storage class and is not a valid S3 Lifecycle transition target; valid targets are Standard-IA, Intelligent-Tiering, One Zone-IA, and the Glacier classes.","why_zh":"Reduced Redundancy Storage (RRS) 是已棄用且不建議使用的儲存類別，不是有效的 S3 Lifecycle 轉換目標；有效目標為 Standard-IA、Intelligent-Tiering、One Zone-IA 及各 Glacier 類別。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/writing-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-transition-general-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-expire-general-considerations.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":82,"question_en":"A company is developing a new application. The application uses AWS Lambda functions for its compute tier. The company must use a canary deployment for any changes to the Lambda functions. Automated rollback must occur if any failures are reported. The company’s DevOps team needs to create the infrastructure as code (IaC) and the CI/CD pipeline for this solution. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一款新的应用程序。该应用程序的计算层使用 AWS Lambda 函数。对于 Lambda 函数的任何变更，公司必须采用金丝雀部署。如果出现任何故障报告，必须自动回滚。 该公司的 DevOps 团队需要为该解决方案创建基础设施即代码（IaC）和持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD） 流水线。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template for the application. Define each Lambda function in the template by using the AWS::Lambda::Function resource type. In the template, include a version for the Lambda function by using the AWS::Lambda::Version resource type. Declare the CodeSha256 property. Configure an AWS::Lambda::Alias resource that references the latest version of the Lambda function.","B":"Create an AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) template for the application. Define each Lambda function in the template by using the AWS::Serverless::Function resource type. For each function, include configurations for the AutoPublishAlias property and the DeploymentPreference property. Configure the deployment configuration type to LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes.","C":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline. Use the CodeCommit repository in a new source stage that starts the pipeline. Create an AWS CodeBuild project to deploy the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) template. Upload the template and source code to the CodeCommit repository. In the CodeCommit repository, create a buildspec.yml file that includes the commands to build and deploy the SAM application.","D":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline. Use the CodeCommit repository in a new source stage that starts the pipeline. Create an AWS CodeDeploy deployment group that is configured for canary deployments with a DeploymentPreference type of Canary10Percent10Minutes. Upload the AWS CloudFormation template and source code to the CodeCommit repository. In the CodeCommit repository, create an appspec.yml file that includes the commands to deploy the CloudFormation template.","E":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch composite alarm for all the Lambda functions. Configure an evaluation period and dimensions for Lambda. Configure the alarm to enter the ALARM state if any errors are detected or if there is insufficient data.","F":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for each Lambda function. Configure the alarms to enter the ALARM state if any errors are detected. Configure an evaluation period, dimensions for each Lambda function and version, and the namespace as AWS/Lambda on the Errors metric."},"options_zh":{"A":"为应用程序创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板。使用 AWS::Lambda::Function 资源类型在模板中 定义每个 Lambda 函数。在模板中，使用 AWS::Lambda::Version 资源类型为 Lambda 函数包含一 个版本。声明 CodeSha256 属性。配置一个引用 Lambda 函数最新版本的 AWS::Lambda::Alias 资 源。","B":"为应用程序创建一个 AWS 无服务器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）模板。使用 AWS::Serverless:: Function 资源类型在模板中定义每个 Lambda 函数。对于每个函数，包含 AutoPublishAlias 属性 和 DeploymentPreference 属性的配置。将部署配置类型设置为 LambdaCanary10Percent10Minute s。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。使用 CodeCommit 在新的源代码阶段创建一个代码库以启动流水线。创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来部署 AWS 无服务 器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）模板。将模板和源代码上传到 CodeCommit 代码库。在 CodeCommit 代 码库中，创建一个包含构建和部署 SAM 应用程序命令的 buildspec.yml 文件。","D":"创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。在新的源阶段使用 CodeCommit 代码库来启动管道。创建一个配置为金丝雀部署且部署偏好类型为 Canary10Percent10M inutes 的 AWS CodeDeploy 部署组。将 AWS CloudFormation 模板和源代码上传到 CodeCommit 代码 库。在 CodeCommit 代码库中，创建一个包含部署 CloudFormation 模板所需命令的 appspec.yml 文件。","E":"为所有 Lambda 函数创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 复合警报。为 Lambda 配置评估周期和维度。如果检 测到任何错误或数据不足，配置警报进入“警报”状态。","F":"为每个 Lambda 函数创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。将警报配置为在检测到任何错误时进入“警 报”状态。为每个 Lambda 函数及其版本配置评估周期、维度，并将命名空间配置为 AWS/Lambda， 针对“错误”指标进行设置。"},"answer":["B","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Automated Lambda canary deployments with automatic rollback are natively provided by AWS SAM. Option B is the core mechanism: AWS::Serverless::Function with AutoPublishAlias (publishes a new version and points an alias at it) plus DeploymentPreference, which auto-generates a CodeDeploy resource that shifts traffic in canary increments and rolls back automatically when a referenced CloudWatch alarm fires. (Note: the precise SAM Type identifier is Canary10Percent10Minutes, not LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes — the Lambda prefix belongs to the underlying CodeDeployDefault.* config name — but B is still the only option describing the correct SAM canary+rollback design.) Option C is the matching CI/CD pipeline for a SAM app: CodeCommit source triggers CodePipeline, and a CodeBuild project runs sam build/sam deploy driven by a buildspec.yml. Option F supplies the rollback trigger: a per-function CloudWatch metric alarm on the AWS/Lambda namespace Errors metric with dimensions for each function/version, which is exactly what SAM's DeploymentPreference.Alarms list expects (the SAM docs reference two such per-alias/per-version error alarms).","explanation_zh":"Lambda 的自動化 canary 部署與自動 rollback 由 AWS SAM 原生提供。選項 B 是核心機制：AWS::Serverless::Function 搭配 AutoPublishAlias（發佈新版本並讓 alias 指向它）加上 DeploymentPreference，後者會自動產生一個 CodeDeploy 資源，以 canary 增量方式轉移流量，並在所參照的 CloudWatch alarm 觸發時自動 rollback。（注意：SAM 的 Type 正確識別字是 Canary10Percent10Minutes，而非 LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes；Lambda 前綴屬於底層 CodeDeployDefault.* 設定名稱。但 B 仍是唯一描述正確 SAM canary + rollback 設計的選項。）選項 C 是對應 SAM 應用的 CI/CD pipeline：CodeCommit source 觸發 CodePipeline，CodeBuild project 透過 buildspec.yml 執行 sam build / sam deploy。選項 F 提供 rollback 觸發器：針對每個 function 在 AWS/Lambda namespace 的 Errors metric、含 function/version dimensions 的 CloudWatch metric alarm，正是 SAM DeploymentPreference.Alarms 清單所需（SAM 文件範例參照了 alias 與 version 兩個 error alarm）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Raw CloudFormation with AWS::Lambda::Version and an alias pointing at the latest version provides no canary traffic shifting and no automated rollback. A static alias does not implement gradual deployment, so this fails both core requirements.","why_zh":"純 CloudFormation 使用 AWS::Lambda::Version 並讓 alias 指向最新版本，不提供 canary 流量轉移，也沒有自動 rollback。靜態 alias 無法實作漸進式部署，因此無法滿足兩個核心需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This pairs a plain CloudFormation template with a CodeDeploy deployment group plus appspec.yml to 'deploy the CloudFormation template,' which is not how Lambda canary deployments work. DeploymentPreference/Canary10Percent10Minutes is a SAM construct (and CodeDeployDefault config), not a CodeDeploy deployment-group setting you wire to a CFN template this way; CodeDeploy does not deploy CFN templates via appspec for Lambda canaries.","why_zh":"此選項把純 CloudFormation template 與 CodeDeploy deployment group 加 appspec.yml 配對來「部署 CloudFormation template」，這並非 Lambda canary 部署的運作方式。DeploymentPreference / Canary10Percent10Minutes 是 SAM 的構件（與 CodeDeployDefault 設定），不是以這種方式接到 CFN template 的 CodeDeploy deployment-group 設定；CodeDeploy 不會透過 appspec 為 Lambda canary 部署 CFN template。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A composite alarm determines its state from rule expressions over OTHER alarms; it has no evaluation period or metric dimensions of its own, so 'configure dimensions for Lambda' on a composite alarm is incorrect. Triggering on insufficient-data would also cause spurious rollbacks. SAM/CodeDeploy rollback uses per-function metric alarms (as in F), not a composite alarm.","why_zh":"composite alarm 的狀態來自對「其他 alarm」的 rule expression；它本身沒有 evaluation period 或 metric dimensions，因此在 composite alarm 上「設定 Lambda 的 dimensions」是錯誤的。以 insufficient-data 觸發也會造成誤判 rollback。SAM/CodeDeploy 的 rollback 使用每個 function 的 metric alarm（如 F），而非 composite alarm。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/automating-updates-to-serverless-apps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/sam-property-function-deploymentpreference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/alarm-combining.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/monitoring-functions-metrics.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":83,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is deploying a new version of a company’s application in an AWS CodeDeploy deployment group associated with its Amazon EC2 instances. After some time, the deployment fails. The engineer realizes that all the events associated with the specific deployment ID are in a Skipped status, and code was not deployed in the instances associated with the deployment group. What are valid reasons for this failure? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在将公司应用程序的新版本部署到与亚马逊 EC2 实例相关联的 AWS CodeDeploy 部署组中。过了一段时间，部署失败了。工程师发现与特定部署 ID 相关的所有事件都处于“已跳过” 状态，并且代码未部署到与部署组相关联的实例中。 导致此失败的合理原因是什么？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"The networking configuration does not allow the EC2 instances to reach the internet via a NAT gateway or internet gateway, and the CodeDeploy endpoint cannot be reached.","B":"The IAM user who triggered the application deployment does not have permission to interact with the CodeDeploy endpoint.","C":"The target EC2 instances were not properly registered with the CodeDeploy endpoint.","D":"An instance profile with proper permissions was not attached to the target EC2 instances.","E":"The appspec.yml file was not included in the application revision."},"options_zh":{"A":"网络配置不允许 EC2 实例通过 NAT 网关或互联网网关访问互联网，因此无法连接到 CodeDeploy 端点。","B":"触发应用程序部署的 IAM 用户无权与 CodeDeploy 端点进行交互。","C":"目标 EC2 实例未正确注册到 CodeDeploy 端点。","D":"目标 EC2 实例未附加具有适当权限的实例配置文件。","E":"应用程序修订中未包含 appspec.yml 文件。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When all lifecycle events for an EC2/on-premises CodeDeploy deployment show Skipped and no code is deployed, the AWS troubleshooting guide 'Troubleshooting all lifecycle events skipped errors' lists the exact root causes. Two of them map directly to the options: (1) the instance cannot reach the CodeDeploy or Amazon S3 public endpoint over port 443 - AWS says to assign a public IP with an internet gateway, or use a NAT gateway for instances in a private subnet, and allow outbound 443 (matches option A); and (2) the instance does not have an IAM instance profile attached, or has one without the required permissions (matches option D). The CodeDeploy agent on the instance polls the CodeDeploy endpoint; if it cannot connect (networking) or lacks credentials (instance profile), the agent never receives or processes the commands, so the host-agent lifecycle events are all Skipped and nothing is installed.","explanation_zh":"當 EC2/On-Premises CodeDeploy 部署的所有 lifecycle events 都顯示 Skipped 且沒有任何程式碼被部署時，AWS 的疑難排解文件「Troubleshooting all lifecycle events skipped errors」列出了確切的根本原因。其中兩項直接對應到選項：(1) instance 無法透過 port 443 連到 CodeDeploy 或 Amazon S3 的 public endpoint，AWS 建議指派 public IP 並使用 internet gateway，或對私有子網中的 instance 使用 NAT gateway，並允許 outbound 443（對應選項 A）；(2) instance 沒有附加 IAM instance profile，或附加的 profile 缺少必要權限（對應選項 D）。Instance 上的 CodeDeploy agent 會輪詢 CodeDeploy endpoint；若無法連線（網路）或缺少憑證（instance profile），agent 永遠收不到或無法處理命令，因此所有 host-agent lifecycle events 都被 Skipped，且不會安裝任何內容。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Permissions of the IAM user who triggers the deployment are evaluated at CreateDeployment API call time. If that principal lacked codedeploy:CreateDeployment permission, the deployment would never be created (an AccessDenied error), not produce a deployment with all instance lifecycle events in Skipped status. This is not in the documented causes for skipped lifecycle events.","why_zh":"觸發部署的 IAM user 權限是在 CreateDeployment API 呼叫時評估。若該 principal 缺少 codedeploy:CreateDeployment 權限，部署根本不會被建立（會收到 AccessDenied 錯誤），而不會產生一個所有 instance lifecycle events 都是 Skipped 的部署。這不在文件記載的 skipped 原因中。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EC2 instances are not 'registered' with a CodeDeploy endpoint; registration (register-on-premises-instance) applies only to on-premises instances. EC2 instances are matched to a deployment group via tags or Auto Scaling. If no instances matched the deployment group you would get a 'no instances were found' error, not all events Skipped.","why_zh":"EC2 instance 並不會向 CodeDeploy endpoint「註冊」；註冊（register-on-premises-instance）僅適用於 on-premises instance。EC2 instance 是透過 tag 或 Auto Scaling 對應到 deployment group。若沒有 instance 符合 deployment group，會收到「no instances were found」錯誤，而非所有 events 都 Skipped。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A missing appspec.yml causes failure during/after DownloadBundle when the agent tries to read the AppSpec, surfacing an AppSpec/validation error - not all lifecycle events showing Skipped before anything is downloaded. The all-events-skipped symptom points to the agent being unable to connect or authenticate, which is upstream of reading the AppSpec.","why_zh":"缺少 appspec.yml 會在 DownloadBundle 階段或之後、agent 嘗試讀取 AppSpec 時失敗，呈現 AppSpec/驗證錯誤，而不是在下載任何內容前所有 lifecycle events 都顯示 Skipped。所有 events 都 Skipped 的症狀指向 agent 無法連線或驗證，這發生在讀取 AppSpec 之前。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-deployments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-general.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/instances-ec2-configure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/codedeploy-agent.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":84,"question_en":"A company has a guideline that every Amazon EC2 instance must be launched from an AMI that the company’s security team produces. Every month, the security team sends an email message with the latest approved AMIs to all the development teams. The development teams use AWS CloudFormation to deploy their applications. When developers launch a new service, they have to search their email for the latest AMIs that the security department sent. A DevOps engineer wants to automate the process that the security team uses to provide the AMI IDs to the development teams. What is the MOST scalable solution that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司有一项规定，即所有亚马逊 EC2 实例都必须从公司安全团队制作的 AMI 启动。每个月，安全 团队都会向所有开发团队发送一封电子邮件，附上最新批准的 AMI 列表。 开发团队使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署其应用程序。当开发人员推出新服务时，他们必须在电子邮件中 查找安全团队发送的最新 AMI。一位 DevOps 工程师希望将安全团队向开发团队提供 AMI ID 的流程自动 化。 满足这些要求的最具可扩展性的解决方案是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Direct the security team to use CloudFormation to create new versions of the AMIs and to list the AMI ARNs in an encrypted Amazon S3 object as part of the stack’s Outputs section. Instruct the developers to use a cross-stack reference to load the encrypted S3 object and obtain the most recent AMI ARNs.","B":"Direct the security team to use a CloudFormation stack to create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that builds new AMIs and places the latest AMI ARNs in an encrypted Amazon S3 object as part of the pipeline output. Instruct the developers to use a cross-stack reference within their own CloudFormation template to obtain the S3 object location and the most recent AMI ARNs.","C":"Direct the security team to use Amazon EC2 Image Builder to create new AMIs and to place the AMI ARNs as parameters in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Instruct the developers to specify a parameter of type SSM in their CloudFormation stack to obtain the most recent AMI ARNs from Parameter Store.","D":"Direct the security team to use Amazon EC2 Image Builder to create new AMIs and to create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic so that every development team can receive notifications. When the development teams receive a notification, instruct them to write an AWS Lambda function that will update their CloudFormation stack with the most recent AMI ARNs."},"options_zh":{"A":"指示安全团队使用 CloudFormation 创建 AMI 的新版本，并在堆栈的“输出”部分将 AMI 的 ARN 列表 以加密的 Amazon S3 对象形式列出。告知开发人员使用跨堆栈引用加载加密的 S3 对象并获取最新的 AMI ARN。","B":"指挥安保工作 团队使用 CloudFormation 堆栈创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道 构建新的 AMI 并将最新的 AMI ARN 放入加密的 Amazon S3 对象中，作为管道输出的一部分。指示 开发人员在其自己的 CloudFormation 模板中使用跨栈引用以获取 S3 对象的位置和最新的 AMI ARN。","C":"指示安全团队使用亚马逊 EC2 Image Builder 创建新的 AMI，并将 AMI 的 ARN 作为参数放置在 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储中。告知开发人员在其 CloudFormation 堆栈中指定类型为 SSM 的 参数，以便从参数存储中获取最新的 AMI ARN。","D":"指示安全团队使用亚马逊 EC2 镜像构建器创建新的 AMI，并创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，以便每个开发团队都能收到通知。当开发团队收到通知时，指导他们编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用最新的 AMI 资源名称更新其 CloudFormation 堆栈。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The canonical AWS pattern for distributing approved AMI IDs is to publish the AMI ID to AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store and have consumers reference it. EC2 Image Builder automates the creation of hardened/golden AMIs and can update a Parameter Store parameter with the output AMI ID. CloudFormation natively supports the SSM parameter type 'AWS::SSM::Parameter::Value<AWS::EC2::Image::Id>', which resolves the latest value from Parameter Store at stack create/update time. This means developers never have to search email; they simply point a parameter at a well-known Parameter Store key (for example /golden-ami) and CloudFormation always launches from the latest approved AMI. The EC2 user guide explicitly describes this exact scenario: 'every month... you create a new version of your AMI... you can create a Systems Manager parameter that points to the correct AMI ID... Your users don't have to know about the periodic updates.' This is fully managed, requires no custom code, and scales to any number of development teams, making it the MOST scalable solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS 分發核准 AMI ID 的標準模式是把 AMI ID 發佈到 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store，再由消費端引用。EC2 Image Builder 能自動建立強化過的 golden AMI，並可將輸出的 AMI ID 寫入 Parameter Store 參數。CloudFormation 原生支援 SSM 參數型別 'AWS::SSM::Parameter::Value<AWS::EC2::Image::Id>'，會在建立或更新堆疊時自動從 Parameter Store 解析出最新值。如此開發人員不需再翻找電子郵件，只要把參數指向一個固定的 Parameter Store key（例如 /golden-ami），CloudFormation 就一律以最新核准的 AMI 啟動。EC2 使用者指南明確描述此情境：『每個月建立新版 AMI…可建立指向正確 AMI ID 的 Systems Manager 參數…使用者不需知道定期更新』。此方案全託管、無須自訂程式碼，且可擴展到任意數量的開發團隊，因此是最具擴展性的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation does not 'create new versions of AMIs' as a native capability; AMI baking requires Image Builder or custom automation. Storing ARNs in an encrypted S3 object and loading it via a cross-stack reference is invalid: cross-stack references (Fn::ImportValue) import exported stack Outputs, not the contents of an S3 object, and they cannot read encrypted file contents. This is convoluted and not the supported mechanism.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 本身無法『建立新版 AMI』，AMI 烘焙需要 Image Builder 或自訂自動化。把 ARN 存到加密 S3 物件再用 cross-stack reference 載入是錯的：cross-stack reference（Fn::ImportValue）匯入的是匯出的堆疊 Outputs，而非 S3 物件內容，也無法讀取加密檔案內容，做法繞遠且非受支援機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A CodePipeline that builds AMIs and writes ARNs to an encrypted S3 object is far more operational overhead than the native Parameter Store integration, and cross-stack references still cannot load an S3 object's contents or an S3 location to obtain AMI ARNs. The mechanism described is not how cross-stack references work, so it does not meet the requirement scalably. (Note this option also contains injected spam text.)","why_zh":"用 CodePipeline 烘焙 AMI 並把 ARN 寫進加密 S3 物件，比原生 Parameter Store 整合的維運負擔大很多，且 cross-stack reference 仍無法載入 S3 物件內容或 S3 位置來取得 AMI ARN。所述機制並非 cross-stack reference 的運作方式，因此無法可擴展地滿足需求。（此選項另含被植入的垃圾文字。）"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using SNS to notify teams and then requiring each team to write a Lambda function to update their own CloudFormation stack is the opposite of scalable: it pushes custom code and manual notification handling onto every development team. It reintroduces the same per-team manual burden the question wants to eliminate and adds maintenance of many Lambda functions.","why_zh":"用 SNS 通知各團隊、再要求每個團隊各自撰寫 Lambda 去更新自己的 CloudFormation 堆疊，與可擴展性背道而馳：把自訂程式碼與手動通知處理推給每個開發團隊，重新引入題目想消除的每團隊手動負擔，還要維護大量 Lambda 函式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/using-systems-manager-parameter-to-find-AMI.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/cloudformation-supplied-parameter-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/what-is-image-builder.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-parameter-store.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":85,"question_en":"An application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). A DevOps engineer is using AWS CodeDeploy to release a new version. The deployment fails during the AllowTraffic lifecycle event, but a cause for the failure is not indicated in the deployment logs. What would cause this?","question_zh":"一个应用程序在应用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行。一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 发布新版本。在 AllowTraffic 生命周期事件期间部署失败，但部署日志中未指明失败 原因。 这会是什么原因造成的？","options_en":{"A":"The appspec.yml file contains an invalid script that runs in the AllowTraffic lifecycle hook.","B":"The user who initiated the deployment does not have the necessary permissions to interact with the ALB.","C":"The health checks specified for the ALB target group are misconfigured.","D":"The CodeDeploy agent was not installed in the EC2 instances that are part of the ALB target group."},"options_zh":{"A":"appspec.yml 文件中包含一个在 AllowTraffic 生命周期挂钩中运行的无效脚本。","B":"发起部署的用户没有与应用负载均衡器（ALB）进行交互所需的权限。","C":"针对 ALB 目标组指定的健康检查配置有误。","D":"作为应用负载均衡器目标组一部分的 EC2 实例上未安装 CodeDeploy 代理。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The AWS CodeDeploy troubleshooting documentation contains a section titled almost verbatim to this question: 'Troubleshooting a failed AllowTraffic lifecycle event with no error reported in the deployment logs.' It states that when a blue/green deployment fails during the AllowTraffic lifecycle event but the deployment logs do not indicate the cause, the failure is typically due to incorrectly configured health checks in Elastic Load Balancing for the Classic Load Balancer, Application Load Balancer, or Network Load Balancer used to manage traffic for the deployment group. The remediation is to review and correct the load balancer (target group) health check configuration. During AllowTraffic, CodeDeploy registers the new instances with the ALB target group and waits for them to pass health checks before shifting traffic; if the health checks are misconfigured, the targets never become healthy and the event silently fails with no script-level log entry. This is option C.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeDeploy 的疑難排解文件中有一個章節標題幾乎與本題逐字相同：『Troubleshooting a failed AllowTraffic lifecycle event with no error reported in the deployment logs』。文件指出，當 blue/green 部署在 AllowTraffic 生命週期事件失敗、但部署日誌未顯示失敗原因時，此失敗通常是因為用來管理部署群組流量的 Elastic Load Balancing（Classic Load Balancer、Application Load Balancer 或 Network Load Balancer）的健康檢查設定錯誤。解決方式是檢視並修正 load balancer（target group）的健康檢查設定。在 AllowTraffic 期間，CodeDeploy 會將新執行個體註冊到 ALB target group，並等待其通過健康檢查才轉移流量；若健康檢查設定錯誤，目標永遠不會變成 healthy，該事件便會在沒有 script 層級日誌的情況下靜默失敗。因此答案是 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AllowTraffic is not a user-script hook on the EC2/On-Premises platform. The valid AppSpec hooks are ApplicationStop, BeforeInstall, AfterInstall, ApplicationStart, ValidateService, BeforeBlockTraffic, AfterBlockTraffic, BeforeAllowTraffic, and AfterAllowTraffic. AllowTraffic itself is an internal CodeDeploy/ELB action with no appspec hook, so no custom script runs there. Moreover, a failing script would write an explicit error to the deployment logs, contradicting the 'no cause indicated' premise.","why_zh":"AllowTraffic 在 EC2/On-Premises 平台上並非使用者腳本 hook。有效的 AppSpec hooks 為 ApplicationStop、BeforeInstall、AfterInstall、ApplicationStart、ValidateService、BeforeBlockTraffic、AfterBlockTraffic、BeforeAllowTraffic 與 AfterAllowTraffic。AllowTraffic 本身是 CodeDeploy/ELB 的內部動作，沒有對應的 appspec hook，因此不會在此執行自訂腳本。此外，腳本失敗會在部署日誌寫入明確錯誤，與『日誌未顯示原因』的前提矛盾。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The user/operator does not directly interact with the ALB during deployment; CodeDeploy uses its service role to register targets and manage traffic. A permissions problem would surface as an explicit IAM/AccessDenied error, not a silent failure with no logged cause. This is not the documented cause for a silent AllowTraffic failure.","why_zh":"在部署過程中，使用者/操作者並不直接與 ALB 互動；CodeDeploy 是透過其 service role 來註冊目標並管理流量。權限問題會以明確的 IAM/AccessDenied 錯誤呈現，而非沒有記錄原因的靜默失敗。這並非文件記載的 AllowTraffic 靜默失敗原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"If the CodeDeploy agent were not installed, the deployment would fail much earlier (e.g., the instance would not be registered or the DownloadBundle/install phases would fail) and would produce a clear error, not fail specifically at AllowTraffic with no logged cause. The agent is required well before the AllowTraffic stage is reached.","why_zh":"若未安裝 CodeDeploy agent，部署會在更早階段失敗（例如執行個體無法註冊、或 DownloadBundle/安裝階段失敗）並產生明確錯誤，而不會恰好在 AllowTraffic 階段以無記錄原因的方式失敗。在到達 AllowTraffic 階段之前就已需要 agent 運作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-deployments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/target-group-health-checks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":86,"question_en":"A company has 20 service teams. Each service team is responsible for its own microservice. Each service team uses a separate AWS account for its microservice and a VPC with the 192.168.0.0/22 CIDR block. The company manages the AWS accounts with AWS Organizations. Each service team hosts its microservice on multiple Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The microservices communicate with each other across the public internet. The company’s security team has issued a new guideline that all communication between microservices must use HTTPS over private network connections and cannot traverse the public internet. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that fulfills these obligations and minimizes the number of changes for each service team. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有 20 个服务团队。每个服务团队负责自己的微服务。每个服务团队为其微服务使用单独的 AWS 账户，并使用具有 192.168.0.0/22 CIDR 块的 VPC。该公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理这些 AWS 账户。 每个服务团队都在多个亚马逊 EC2 实例上托管其微服务，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器之后。微服务 之间通过公共互联网进行通信。公司的安全团队发布了一项新指南，规定所有微服务之间的通信必须通 过专用网络连接使用 HTTPS，且不能通过公共互联网传输。 一位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一种解决方案，以履行这些职责，并将每个服务团队所需进行的变更数量 降至最低。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account in AWS Organizations. Create a VPC in this account, and use AWS Resource Access Manager to share the private subnets of this VPC with the organization. Instruct the service teams to launch a new Network Load Balancer (NLB) and EC2 instances that use the shared private subnets. Use the NLB DNS names for communication between microservices.","B":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each of the microservice VPCs. Use AWS PrivateLink to create VPC endpoints in each AWS account for the NLBs. Create subscriptions to each VPC endpoint in each of the other AWS accounts. Use the VPC endpoint DNS names for communication between microservices.","C":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each of the microservice VPCs. Create VPC peering connections between each of the microservice VPCs. Update the route tables for each VPC to use the peering links. Use the NLB DNS names for communication between microservices.","D":"Create a new AWS account in AWS Organizations. Create a transit gateway in this account, and use AWS Resource Access Manager to share the transit gateway with the organization. In each of the microservice VPCs, create a transit gateway attachment to the shared transit gateway. Update the route tables of each VPC to use the transit gateway. Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each of the microservice VPCs. Use the NLB DNS names for communication between microservices."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS 组织中创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在该账户中创建一个 VPC，并使用 AWS 资源访问管理器 将此 VPC 的私有子网与组织共享。指示服务团队在共享的私有子网中启动新的网络负载均衡器 （NLB）和 EC2 实例。使用 NLB 的 DNS 名称在微服务之间进行通信。","B":"在每个微服务的虚拟私有云（VPC）中创建一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）。使用 AWS PrivateLink 在 每个 AWS 账户中为 NLB 创建 VPC 端点。在其他每个 AWS 账户中为每个 VPC 端点创建订阅。使 用 VPC 端点的 DNS 名称在微服务之间进行通信。","C":"在每个微服务的虚拟私有云（VPC）中创建一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）。创建 VPC 对等连接 在每个微服务的虚拟私有云（VPC）之间建立连接。更新每个 VPC 的路由表以使用对等链接。使用网 络负载均衡器（NLB）的 DNS 名称在微服务之间进行通信。","D":"在 AWS 组织中创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在该账户中创建一个传输网关，并使用 AWS 资源访问管理器 将传输网关与组织共享。在每个微服务 VPC 中，创建一个到共享传输网关的传输网关连接。更新每个 VPC 的路由表以使用传输网关。在每个微服务 VPC 中创建一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）。使用 NLB 的 DNS 名称在微服务之间进行通信。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The decisive constraint is that all 20 microservice VPCs use the SAME CIDR block (192.168.0.0/22), so their IP ranges overlap. AWS PrivateLink (option B) is the only choice that works with overlapping CIDRs: each provider exposes its service via a Network Load Balancer behind a VPC endpoint service, and consumers reach it through an interface VPC endpoint that has its own ENI/private IP inside the consumer's own VPC. Because traffic terminates on an endpoint ENI rather than being IP-routed between VPCs, overlapping CIDRs are irrelevant, traffic stays on the AWS private network (never the public internet), and NLB/PrivateLink carries TLS so HTTPS is satisfied. It also minimizes per-team change: each team adds an NLB and creates endpoints. VPC peering (C) explicitly cannot have overlapping CIDR blocks and is non-transitive, and Transit Gateway (D) likewise requires non-overlapping IP ranges to route (AWS Well-Architected REL02-BP05), so both are technically broken here. Option A (RAM-shared VPC) forces every team to relaunch EC2 and NLBs into new shared subnets, which is the maximum amount of change, contradicting the requirement to minimize changes. The word 'subscriptions' in B is loose phrasing for endpoint connections, but the architecture is uniquely correct.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限制是 20 個 microservice VPC 全部使用相同的 CIDR (192.168.0.0/22)，因此 IP 範圍重疊。AWS PrivateLink (選項 B) 是唯一能在 CIDR 重疊情況下運作的方案：每個 provider 透過 Network Load Balancer 背後的 VPC endpoint service 公開服務，consumer 則透過 interface VPC endpoint 連線，該 endpoint 在 consumer 自己的 VPC 內有獨立的 ENI/私有 IP。由於流量終結在 endpoint ENI 上，而不是在 VPC 之間進行 IP 路由，因此 CIDR 重疊不影響運作，流量保持在 AWS 私有網路 (從不經過公網)，且 NLB/PrivateLink 可承載 TLS，滿足 HTTPS 要求。這也最大限度減少每個團隊的變更：每隊只需新增 NLB 並建立 endpoints。VPC peering (C) 明確不允許重疊 CIDR 且不支援傳遞路由；Transit Gateway (D) 同樣需要不重疊的 IP 範圍才能路由 (AWS Well-Architected REL02-BP05)，因此兩者在此情境下技術上都行不通。選項 A (RAM 共享 VPC) 強迫每個團隊將 EC2 與 NLB 重新部署到新的共享子網，變更量最大，違反最小化變更的要求。B 中的「subscriptions」用詞不精確 (實為 endpoint connections)，但其架構是唯一正確的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A RAM-shared central VPC requires every one of the 20 teams to relaunch their EC2 instances and NLBs into the new shared private subnets, which is the maximum possible change and directly contradicts 'minimize the number of changes for each service team'. It also collapses team isolation.","why_zh":"RAM 共享的中央 VPC 要求 20 個團隊全部把 EC2 與 NLB 重新部署到新的共享私有子網，變更量最大，直接違反『最小化每個團隊的變更』，且破壞團隊隔離。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"VPC peering explicitly does NOT support overlapping CIDR blocks (the accepter VPC cannot have a CIDR that overlaps the requester), and all 20 VPCs share 192.168.0.0/22. Peering is also non-transitive, requiring a near-full mesh (~190 connections). Technically impossible here.","why_zh":"VPC peering 明確不支援重疊的 CIDR (接受方 VPC 不能與請求方 CIDR 重疊)，而 20 個 VPC 全用 192.168.0.0/22。Peering 也不支援傳遞路由，需要近乎全網狀 (約 190 條連線)。此處技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Transit Gateway routes by destination IP and requires non-overlapping CIDR ranges (AWS Well-Architected REL02-BP05). With 20 identical 192.168.0.0/22 VPCs, the TGW route tables cannot distinguish destinations, so routing breaks.","why_zh":"Transit Gateway 依目的地 IP 路由，需要不重疊的 CIDR 範圍 (AWS Well-Architected REL02-BP05)。20 個相同的 192.168.0.0/22 VPC 會使 TGW 路由表無法區分目的地，路由失效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/peering/vpc-peering-basics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/peering/create-vpc-peering-connection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2024-06-27/framework/rel_planning_network_topology_non_overlap_ip.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":87,"question_en":"An Amazon EC2 instance is running in a VPC and needs to download an object from a restricted Amazon S3 bucket. When the DevOps engineer tries to download the object, an AccessDenied error is received. What are the possible causes for this error? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一个亚马逊 EC2 实例正在虚拟私有云（VPC）中运行，需要从一个受限制的亚马逊 S3 存储桶下载一个对 象。当开发运维工程师尝试下载该对象时，收到了“访问被拒绝”的错误。 此错误可能由哪些原因导致？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"The S3 bucket default encryption is enabled.","B":"There is an error in the S3 bucket policy.","C":"The object has been moved to S3 Glacier.","D":"There is an error in the IAM role configuration.","E":"S3 Versioning is enabled."},"options_zh":{"A":"S3 存储桶的默认加密已启用。","B":"S3 存储桶策略存在错误。","C":"该对象已移至 S3 Glacier。","D":"IAM 角色配置有误。","E":"已启用 S3 版本控制。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An EC2 instance downloads from S3 using the IAM role attached via its instance profile, and access is also gated by the bucket's resource-based policy. The AWS 403 troubleshooting guide lists \"Bucket policies and IAM policies\" as the primary causes of AccessDenied: an incorrect bucket policy (missing Allow or an explicit Deny for s3:GetObject) or a misconfigured IAM role (no s3:GetObject permission, so an implicit deny) both produce AccessDenied. Because IAM implicitly denies by default, the policy must explicitly allow the action; otherwise access is denied. The other options do not produce AccessDenied: an object archived to S3 Glacier returns an InvalidObjectState error (you must RestoreObject first), not AccessDenied; S3 Versioning is transparent to a normal GET of the current version; and S3 default encryption (SSE-S3) is transparent on download and does not by itself deny access.","explanation_zh":"EC2 執行個體透過附加在 instance profile 上的 IAM role 來下載 S3 物件，而存取同時也受 bucket 的資源型政策 (bucket policy) 控管。AWS 的 403 疑難排解文件將「Bucket policies 與 IAM policies」列為 AccessDenied 的主要成因：bucket policy 設定錯誤（缺少 Allow 或對 s3:GetObject 有明確 Deny），或 IAM role 設定錯誤（未授予 s3:GetObject，形成隱含拒絕），兩者都會造成 AccessDenied。由於 IAM 預設隱含拒絕，政策必須明確 Allow 該動作，否則即被拒絕。其餘選項不會產生 AccessDenied：物件被歸檔至 S3 Glacier 時會回傳 InvalidObjectState 錯誤（需先 RestoreObject），而非 AccessDenied；S3 Versioning 對讀取目前版本的一般 GET 是透明的；S3 預設加密 (SSE-S3) 在下載時是透明的，本身不會拒絕存取。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 default encryption (SSE-S3) is transparent on download and does not by itself cause AccessDenied. Only a missing KMS key grant under SSE-KMS could, but plain 'default encryption enabled' as stated does not deny access.","why_zh":"S3 預設加密 (SSE-S3) 在下載時是透明的，本身不會造成 AccessDenied。只有 SSE-KMS 下缺少 KMS 金鑰授權才可能，但題目所述的單純『啟用預設加密』不會拒絕存取。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An object in S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval / Deep Archive returns InvalidObjectState ('operation not valid for object storage class') and requires RestoreObject first; it does not return AccessDenied.","why_zh":"位於 S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval / Deep Archive 的物件會回傳 InvalidObjectState（『此儲存類別不支援該操作』），需先執行 RestoreObject，並不會回傳 AccessDenied。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"S3 Versioning is transparent to a normal GetObject of the current version and does not cause AccessDenied.","why_zh":"S3 Versioning 對讀取目前版本的一般 GetObject 是透明的，不會造成 AccessDenied。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/troubleshoot-403-errors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/security_iam_troubleshoot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/botocore/latest/reference/services/s3/client/exceptions/InvalidObjectState.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/archival-storage.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":88,"question_en":"A company wants to use a grid system for a proprietary enterprise in-memory data store on top of AWS. This system can run in multiple server nodes in any Linux-based distribution. The system must be able to reconfigure the entire cluster every time a node is added or removed. When adding or removing nodes, an /etc/cluster/nodes.config file must be updated, listing the IP addresses of the current node members of that cluster. The company wants to automate the task of adding new nodes to a cluster. What can a DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望在 AWS 之上为专有的企业内存数据存储使用网格系统。该系统能够在任何基于 Linux 的发 行版的多个服务器节点上运行。每当添加或移除节点时，该系统必须能够重新配置整个集群。在添加或移 除节点时，必须更新 /etc/cluster/nodes.config 文件，列出该集群当前节点成员的 IP 地址。 该公司希望实现向集群添加新节点这一任务的自动化。 DevOps 工程师能做些什么来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS OpsWorks Stacks to layer the server nodes of that cluster. Create a Chef recipe that populates the content of the /etc/cluster/nodes.config file and restarts the service by using the current members of the layer. Assign that recipe to the Configure lifecycle event.","B":"Put the file nodes.config in version control. Create an AWS CodeDeploy deployment configuration and deployment group based on an Amazon EC2 tag value for the cluster nodes. When adding a new node to the cluster, update the file with all tagged instances, and make a commit in version control. Deploy the new file and restart the services.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket and upload a version of the /etc/cluster/nodes.config file. Create a crontab script that will poll for that S3 file and download it frequently. Use a process manager, such as Monit or systemd, to restart the cluster services when it detects that the new file was modified. When adding a node to the cluster, edit the file’s most recent members. Upload the new file to the S3 bucket.","D":"Create a user data script that lists all members of the current security group of the cluster and automatically updates the /etc/cluster/nodes.config file whenever a new instance is added to the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS OpsWorks Stacks 对该集群的服务器节点进行分层。创建一个 Chef 配置文件，用于填充 /etc/ cluster/nodes.config 文件的内容，并使用当前层的成员重启服务。将该配置文件分配给“配置”生命 周期事件。","B":"将文件 nodes.config 纳入版本控制。根据集群节点的 Amazon EC2 标签值创建 AWS CodeDeploy 部署配置 和部署组。向集群添加新节点时，使用所有已标记的实例更新该文件，并在版本控制中提交更改。部署 新文件并重启服务。","C":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶，并上传一份 /etc/cluster/nodes.config 文件的版本。创建一个 crontab 脚本， 用于定期轮询该 S3 文件并频繁下载。使用诸如 Monit 或 systemd 之类的进程管理器，在检测到新文件 被修改时重启集群服务。当向集群添加节点时，编辑该文件中的最新成员。将新文件上传到 S3 存储桶。","D":"创建一个用户数据脚本，列出集群当前安全组中的所有成员，并在向集群添加新实例时自动更新 / etc/cluster/nodes.config 文件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS OpsWorks Stacks supports five lifecycle events: Setup, Configure, Deploy, Undeploy, and Shutdown. The Configure event is the decisive feature here: OpsWorks Stacks triggers the Configure event on EVERY instance in the stack whenever any instance enters or leaves the online state (i.e., a node is started, stopped, or auto-healed). This exactly matches the requirement to 'reconfigure the entire cluster every time a node is added or removed.' A custom Chef recipe assigned to the Configure event has access to the current online layer/stack members through the OpsWorks stack configuration and deployment JSON (node attributes), so it can regenerate /etc/cluster/nodes.config with the IP addresses of the current members and restart the service. This is fully automated and event-driven with no polling, no manual file edits, and no commits. The grid system runs on any Linux distribution, which OpsWorks Stacks (Chef-based) supports.","explanation_zh":"AWS OpsWorks Stacks 支援五個 lifecycle 事件：Setup、Configure、Deploy、Undeploy 與 Shutdown。此題的關鍵在於 Configure 事件：每當 stack 中任一 instance 進入或離開 online 狀態（即節點被啟動、停止或 auto-heal）時，OpsWorks Stacks 會在 stack 內的「每一個」instance 上觸發 Configure 事件。這正好對應題目要求「每次新增或移除節點時重新設定整個叢集」。指派到 Configure 事件的 custom Chef recipe 可透過 OpsWorks 的 stack configuration 與 deployment JSON（node attributes）取得目前 online 的 layer/stack 成員，因而能以目前成員的 IP 重新產生 /etc/cluster/nodes.config 並重啟服務。整個流程完全自動化、由事件驅動，無需輪詢、手動編輯檔案或 commit。該 grid 系統可在任何 Linux 發行版上執行，而 OpsWorks Stacks（以 Chef 為基礎）支援此需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeDeploy is not event-driven on cluster membership changes. It requires a human to manually edit nodes.config with all tagged instances and commit to version control before each deployment, which defeats the requirement to 'automate the task of adding new nodes.' It is manual and reactive, not automatic on node add/remove.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 不會因叢集成員變動而自動觸發。每次部署前都需人工手動編輯 nodes.config（列出所有具標籤的 instance）並 commit 到版本控制，違反「自動化新增節點」的需求；屬於手動且被動的做法。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Relies on a manual step (editing the file with current members and uploading to S3) plus frequent cron polling, which adds latency and operational overhead. Membership changes are not detected automatically; an operator must compute and upload the member list each time, so it does not truly automate node addition.","why_zh":"依賴手動步驟（人工編輯成員清單並上傳到 S3）加上頻繁的 cron 輪詢，造成延遲與營運負擔。成員變動不會自動偵測，每次都需人工計算並上傳清單，因此並未真正自動化節點新增。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Security group membership is not a list of instance members; security groups define inbound/outbound rules, not the set of instances belonging to a cluster. A user data script also runs only once at instance launch, so it cannot continuously reconfigure existing nodes when other nodes are added or removed. This approach is technically unworkable for maintaining live cluster membership.","why_zh":"Security group 並不是「instance 成員清單」；它定義的是入站/出站規則，而非屬於叢集的 instance 集合。此外 user data script 只在 instance 啟動時執行一次，無法在其他節點新增或移除時持續重新設定現有節點，因此在維護即時叢集成員上技術上不可行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-ruby/v2/api/Aws/OpsWorks/Types/Layer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opsworks/latest/userguide/workingcookbook-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opsworks/latest/userguide/workingcookbook-events-configure.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":89,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is working on a data archival project that requires the migration of on-premises data to an Amazon S3 bucket. The DevOps engineer develops a script that incrementally archives on-premises data that is older than 1 month to Amazon S3. Data that is transferred to Amazon S3 is deleted from the on-premises location. The script uses the S3 PutObject operation. During a code review, the DevOps engineer notices that the script does not verify whether the data was successfully copied to Amazon S3. The DevOps engineer must update the script to ensure that data is not corrupted during transmission. The script must use MD5 checksums to verify data integrity before the on- premises data is deleted. Which solutions for the script will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在从事一个数据归档项目，该项目需要将本地的数据迁移到 Amazon S3 存储桶。该 DevOps 工程师开发了一个脚本，用于将本地超过 1 个月的数据逐步归档到 Amazon S3。转移到 Amazon S3 的数据会从本地位置删除。该脚本使用 S3 的 PutObject 操作。 在代码审查期间，DevOps 工程师发现该脚本没有验证数据是否已成功复制到亚马逊 S3。DevOps 工程师必 须更新脚本，以确保在传输过程中数据不会损坏。在删除本地数据之前，脚本必须使用 MD5 校验和来验证 数据的完整性。 哪些脚本解决方案能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Check the returned response for the VersionId. Compare the returned VersionId against the MD5 checksum.","B":"Include the MD5 checksum within the Content-MD5 parameter. Check the operation call’s return status to find out if an error was returned.","C":"Include the checksum digest within the tagging parameter as a URL query parameter.","D":"Check the returned response for the ETag. Compare the returned ETag against the MD5 checksum.","E":"Include the checksum digest within the Metadata parameter as a name-value pair. After upload, use the S3 HeadObject operation to retrieve metadata from the object."},"options_zh":{"A":"检查返回的响应中的 VersionId。将返回的 VersionId 与 MD5 校验和进行比较。","B":"在 Content-MD5 参数中包含 MD5 校验和。检查操作调用的返回状态，以确定是否返回了错误。","C":"将校验和摘要作为 URL 查询参数包含在标记参数内。","D":"检查返回响应中的 ETag。将返回的 ETag 与 MD5 校验和进行比较。","E":"在元数据参数中以名称 - 值对的形式包含校验和摘要。上传完成后，使用 S3 HeadObject 操作从对象中 检索元数据。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS S3 documents exactly two MD5-based methods to verify upload integrity, and they map directly to B and D. (B) Per the PutObject API and the 'Using Content-MD5 when uploading objects' section: you supply the precomputed MD5 digest in the Content-MD5 header; S3 recalculates the MD5 of the received object and, if it does not match the provided value, returns an error (e.g., BadDigest). The script checks the operation's return status for that error before deleting the on-premises copy. (D) Per 'Using Content-MD5 and the ETag to verify uploaded objects': for objects created by PutObject that are plaintext or SSE-S3 encrypted and not uploaded as multipart, the ETag IS the MD5 digest of the object data, so the script can compare the returned ETag against its locally computed MD5 checksum. The PutObject page states both options verbatim: use Content-MD5 (S3 returns an error on mismatch) OR compare the returned ETag to the calculated MD5. The question requires MD5 checksums to verify integrity before deletion, and only B and D use MD5 to actually validate the transmitted bytes.","explanation_zh":"AWS S3 文件明確記載兩種以 MD5 驗證上傳完整性的方法，正好對應 B 與 D。(B) 依 PutObject API 及『Using Content-MD5 when uploading objects』章節：在 Content-MD5 標頭提供預先計算的 MD5 摘要，S3 會重新計算收到物件的 MD5，若與提供值不符即回傳錯誤（如 BadDigest）。腳本在刪除地端資料前檢查該操作的回傳狀態是否有錯誤即可。(D) 依『Using Content-MD5 and the ETag to verify uploaded objects』：對於以 PutObject 建立、且為明文或 SSE-S3 加密、非 multipart 上傳的物件，其 ETag 即為物件資料的 MD5 摘要，因此腳本可將回傳的 ETag 與本地計算的 MD5 進行比對。PutObject 頁面逐字列出此兩種方式：使用 Content-MD5（不符時 S3 回傳錯誤）或比對回傳的 ETag 與計算出的 MD5。題目要求以 MD5 驗證完整性後再刪除，只有 B 與 D 真正以 MD5 驗證所傳輸的位元組。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"VersionId is a unique identifier S3 assigns to an object version when versioning is enabled; it is not a hash of the object content. Comparing a VersionId against an MD5 checksum is meaningless and does not validate data integrity.","why_zh":"VersionId 是啟用版本控制時 S3 為物件版本指派的唯一識別碼，並非物件內容的雜湊值。將 VersionId 與 MD5 校驗碼比對毫無意義，無法驗證資料完整性。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Object tagging stores key-value metadata and does not trigger any server-side integrity check. S3 never compares a tag value against the object's content, so placing a checksum digest in the tagging parameter does not verify that the transmitted data is uncorrupted.","why_zh":"物件標籤儲存的是鍵值中繼資料，不會觸發任何伺服器端完整性檢查。S3 不會將標籤值與物件內容比對，因此把校驗摘要放入 tagging 參數無法驗證傳輸資料是否未損毀。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Storing the checksum in user-defined Metadata and then retrieving it with HeadObject only echoes back the value you originally supplied; S3 does not recompute the object's MD5 or compare it to your metadata. This detects nothing about transmission corruption, unlike Content-MD5 where S3 actually validates the received bytes.","why_zh":"把校驗碼存入使用者自訂 Metadata 再用 HeadObject 取回，只會回傳你原本存入的值；S3 不會重新計算物件 MD5 也不會與中繼資料比對。這完全偵測不到傳輸損毀，與 Content-MD5（S3 會實際驗證收到的位元組）不同。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/checking-object-integrity-upload.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_PutObject.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":90,"question_en":"A company deploys updates to its Amazon API Gateway API several times a week by using an AWS CodePipeline pipeline. As part of the update process, the company exports the JavaScript SDK for the API from the API Gateway console and uploads the SDK to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company has configured an Amazon CloudFront distribution that uses the S3 bucket as an origin. Web clients then download the SDK by using the CloudFront distribution’s endpoint. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to make the new SDK available automatically during new API deployments. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司每周数次通过使用 AWS CodePipeline 管道对其 Amazon API Gateway API 进行部署更新。作为更新流 程的一部分，该公司从 API Gateway 控制台导出 API 的 JavaScript SDK，并将 SDK 上传到 Amazon S3 存储 桶。 该公司已配置了一个使用 S3 存储桶作为源的 Amazon CloudFront 分发。然后，Web 客户端通过使用 CloudFront 分发的端点来下载 SDK。一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，以便在新的 API 部署期 间自动提供新的 SDK。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CodePipeline action immediately after the deployment stage of the API. Configure the action to invoke an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to download the SDK from API Gateway, upload the SDK to the S3 bucket, and create a CloudFront invalidation for the SDK path.","B":"Create a CodePipeline action immediately after the deployment stage of the API. Configure the action to use the CodePipeline integration with API Gateway to export the SDK to Amazon S3. Create another action that uses the CodePipeline integration with Amazon S3 to invalidate the cache for the SDK path.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to UpdateStage events from aws.apigateway. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to download the SDK from API Gateway, upload the SDK to the S3 bucket, and call the CloudFront API to create an invalidation for the SDK path.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to CreateDeployment events from aws.apigateway. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to download the SDK from API Gateway, upload the SDK to the S3 bucket, and call the S3 API to invalidate the cache for the SDK path."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 API 部署阶段之后立即创建一个 CodePipeline 操作。配置该操作 要调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数从 API 下载 SDK。 网关，请将 SDK 上传至 S3 存储桶，并为 SDK 路径创建 CloudFront 无效化操作。","B":"在 API 部署阶段之后立即创建一个 CodePipeline 操作。配置该操作以使用 CodePipeline 与 API Gateway 的 集成将 SDK 导出到 Amazon S3。创建另一个操作，使用 CodePipeline 与 Amazon S3 的集成来使 SDK 路 径的缓存失效。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对来自 aws.apigateway 的 UpdateStage 事件做出反应。配置该规 则以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，从 API Gateway 下载 SDK，将 SDK 上传到 S3 存储桶，并调用 CloudFront API 为 SDK 路径创建一个无效化操作。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对来自 aws.apigateway 的 CreateDeployment 事件做出反应。配 置该规则以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，从 API Gateway 下载 SDK，将 SDK 上传到 S3 存储桶，并调 用 S3 API 使 SDK 路径的缓存失效。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Only option A uses components that all genuinely exist and are wired correctly. CodePipeline supports an Invoke action that calls AWS Lambda, so adding a Lambda invoke action immediately after the API deploy stage is valid. The Lambda then performs three real, supported API operations: download the SDK from API Gateway (GetSdk), upload it to the S3 bucket (PutObject), and create a CloudFront invalidation (CloudFront CreateInvalidation) for the SDK path. Crucially, cache invalidation must be done through the CloudFront CreateInvalidation API; there is no S3 API to invalidate a CloudFront cache, which kills option D. CodePipeline also has no native action that exports an SDK from API Gateway and no native S3 cache-invalidation action (the valid Deploy/Invoke provider list contains neither), which kills option B. Coupling the refresh to the pipeline that performs deployments guarantees the new SDK is published with each release.","explanation_zh":"只有選項 A 的所有元件都真實存在且正確串接。CodePipeline 支援 Invoke 動作呼叫 AWS Lambda，因此在 API deploy 階段之後加入 Lambda invoke 動作是合法的。該 Lambda 接著執行三個真實且受支援的 API 操作：從 API Gateway 下載 SDK（GetSdk）、上傳到 S3 儲存桶（PutObject）、並為 SDK 路徑建立 CloudFront invalidation（CloudFront CreateInvalidation）。關鍵在於：快取失效必須透過 CloudFront 的 CreateInvalidation API 完成，沒有任何 S3 API 可以使 CloudFront 快取失效，這直接排除選項 D。此外 CodePipeline 並沒有原生動作可以從 API Gateway 匯出 SDK，也沒有原生的 S3 快取失效動作（合法的 Deploy/Invoke provider 清單中兩者皆無），這排除了選項 B。將更新綁定在執行部署的 pipeline 上，可確保每次發布都會同步發佈新的 SDK。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodePipeline has no native integration that exports an API Gateway SDK, and no native S3 action that invalidates a cache. The valid action-provider list (Source/Build/Test/Deploy/Approval/Invoke) contains no such providers, so this configuration is not buildable.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 沒有可匯出 API Gateway SDK 的原生整合，也沒有可使快取失效的原生 S3 動作。合法的 action provider 清單（Source/Build/Test/Deploy/Approval/Invoke）中並無此類 provider，因此此設定無法建立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The CloudFront invalidation step is correct, but the trigger is wrong: a stage deployment driven by CodePipeline issues a CreateDeployment call, not necessarily UpdateStage, so an UpdateStage rule would not reliably fire on each new API deployment. (Such management calls also reach EventBridge only as 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' events keyed on eventName, not as a native UpdateStage detail-type.)","why_zh":"CloudFront invalidation 步驟是正確的，但觸發條件錯誤：由 CodePipeline 驅動的階段部署會發出 CreateDeployment 呼叫，而非必然是 UpdateStage，因此 UpdateStage 規則無法在每次新部署時可靠觸發。（這類管理呼叫也僅以「AWS API Call via CloudTrail」事件、以 eventName 比對抵達 EventBridge，而非原生的 UpdateStage detail-type。）"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CreateDeployment is the right event to key on, but invalidating a CloudFront cache cannot be done with 'the S3 API'. Cache invalidation is a CloudFront operation (CreateInvalidation); there is no S3 API that invalidates a CloudFront distribution's cache, so this solution cannot work as written.","why_zh":"CreateDeployment 是正確的觸發事件，但使 CloudFront 快取失效不能用「S3 API」完成。快取失效是 CloudFront 的操作（CreateInvalidation）；沒有任何 S3 API 可使 CloudFront 發佈的快取失效，因此此方案依其敘述無法運作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-valid-providers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-Lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/Invalidation_Requests.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-apigateway.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":91,"question_en":"A company has developed an AWS Lambda function that handles orders received through an API. The company is using AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the Lambda function as the final stage of a CI/CD pipeline. A DevOps engineer has noticed there are intermittent failures of the ordering API for a few seconds after deployment. After some investigation, the DevOps engineer believes the failures are due to database changes not having fully propagated before the Lambda function is invoked. How should the DevOps engineer overcome this?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于处理通过 API 接收的订单。该公司正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将 Lambda 函数作为 CI/CD 管道的最后阶段进行部署。 一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，在部署后，订单 API 会出现间歇性的故障，每次持续几秒钟。经过一番调查， 该 DevOps 工程师认为故障是由于在调用 Lambda 函数之前，数据库的更改尚未完全传播所致。 DevOps 工程师应如何克服这一难题？","options_en":{"A":"Add a BeforeAllowTraffic hook to the AppSpec file that tests and waits for any necessary database changes before traffic can flow to the new version of the Lambda function.","B":"Add an AfterAllowTraffic hook to the AppSpec file that forces traffic to wait for any pending database changes before allowing the new version of the Lambda function to respond.","C":"Add a BeforeInstall hook to the AppSpec file that tests and waits for any necessary database changes before deploying the new version of the Lambda function.","D":"Add a ValidateService hook to the AppSpec file that inspects incoming traffic and rejects the payload if dependent services, such as the database, are not yet ready."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AppSpec 文件中添加一个 BeforeAllowTraffic 钩子，用于测试并等待任何必要的数据库更改完 成，然后再允许流量流向新版本的 Lambda 函数。","B":"在 AppSpec 文件中添加一个 AfterAllowTraffic 钩子，强制流量在允许新版本的 Lambda 函数响应之 前等待任何未完成的数据库更改。","C":"在 AppSpec 文件中添加一个 BeforeInstall 钩子，用于测试并等待任何必要的数据库更改，然后再部 署 Lambda 函数的新版本。","D":"在 AppSpec 文件中添加一个 ValidateService 钩子，用于检查传入的流量，如果依赖的服务（如数据 库）尚未准备好，则拒绝负载。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For an AWS Lambda deployment, CodeDeploy supports exactly two AppSpec lifecycle event hooks: BeforeAllowTraffic and AfterAllowTraffic. BeforeAllowTraffic runs tasks before any traffic is shifted to the newly deployed Lambda function version, so it is the correct place to test for and wait on dependent database changes to fully propagate before the new version begins serving requests. If the hook function returns Failed (or does not call putLifecycleEventHookExecutionStatus within an hour), the deployment is stopped/rolled back, ensuring traffic only flows once the database is ready. AfterAllowTraffic runs after traffic has already been shifted, which is too late to prevent the intermittent failures. The qualifier here is fewest changes that correctly prevents pre-readiness traffic, and only the BeforeAllowTraffic gate satisfies that.","explanation_zh":"對於 AWS Lambda 部署，CodeDeploy 的 AppSpec 僅支援兩個生命週期事件 hook：BeforeAllowTraffic 與 AfterAllowTraffic。BeforeAllowTraffic 會在流量切換到新部署的 Lambda 函數版本之前執行任務，因此這正是用來測試並等待相依的資料庫變更完全傳播後才讓新版本開始處理請求的正確位置。若 hook 函數回傳 Failed（或一小時內未呼叫 putLifecycleEventHookExecutionStatus），部署會停止/回復，確保只有在資料庫就緒後流量才會流入。AfterAllowTraffic 在流量已切換之後才執行，無法防止部署後幾秒鐘的間歇性失敗。本題的判定關鍵是用最少的變更正確阻止尚未就緒時的流量，唯有 BeforeAllowTraffic 閘門符合此需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AfterAllowTraffic runs only after all traffic has already been shifted to the new Lambda version, so it cannot make traffic wait for pending database changes; the intermittent failures would still occur during the window it is meant to prevent.","why_zh":"AfterAllowTraffic 只在所有流量已切換到新 Lambda 版本之後才執行，因此無法讓流量等待尚未完成的資料庫變更；它本應阻止的時間窗內仍會發生間歇性失敗。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"BeforeInstall is not a valid hook for a Lambda (serverless) deployment. It exists only for ECS and EC2/on-premises deployments; specifying it in a Lambda AppSpec would be invalid.","why_zh":"BeforeInstall 並非 Lambda（無伺服器）部署的有效 hook，僅存在於 ECS 與 EC2/on-premises 部署；在 Lambda AppSpec 中指定它是無效的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ValidateService is not a CodeDeploy Lambda hook (it is an EC2/on-premises hook), and CodeDeploy hooks do not inspect or reject individual request payloads in real time; they validate the deployment, not live API traffic.","why_zh":"ValidateService 並非 CodeDeploy 的 Lambda hook（它是 EC2/on-premises 的 hook），且 CodeDeploy hook 不會即時檢查或拒絕個別請求的 payload；它們驗證的是部署本身，而非即時的 API 流量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-example.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":92,"question_en":"A company uses a single AWS account to test applications on Amazon EC2 instances. The company has turned on AWS Config in the AWS account and has activated the restricted-ssh AWS Config managed rule. The company needs an automated monitoring solution that will provide a customized notification in real time if any security group in the account is not compliant with the restricted-ssh rule. The customized notification must contain the name and ID of the noncompliant security group. A DevOps engineer creates an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in the account and subscribes the appropriate personnel to the topic. What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用单个 AWS 账户在 Amazon EC2 实例上测试应用程序。该公司已在该 AWS 账户中启用 AWS Config，并激活了受限 SSH 的 AWS Config 管理规则。 该公司需要一个自动化监控解决方案，如果账户中的任何安全组不符合受限 SSH 规则，该方案应能实时 提供定制通知。定制通知必须包含不符合规则的安全组的名称和 ID。 一位 DevOps 工程师在账户中创建了一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，并将相关人员订阅 到该主题。 为了满足这些要求，DevOps 工程师接下来应该怎么做？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches an AWS Config evaluation result of NON_COMPLIANT for the restricted-ssh rule. Configure an input transformer for the EventBridge rule. Configure the EventBridge rule to publish a notification to the SNS topic.","B":"Configure AWS Config to send all evaluation results for the restricted-ssh rule to the SNS topic. Configure a filter policy on the SNS topic to send only notifications that contain the text of NON_COMPLIANT in the notification to subscribers.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches an AWS Config evaluation result of NON_COMPLIANT for the restricted-ssh rule. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke AWS Systems Manager Run Command on the SNS topic to customize a notification and to publish the notification to the SNS topic.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches all AWS Config evaluation results of NON_COMPLIANT. Configure an input transformer for the restricted-ssh rule. Configure the EventBridge rule to publish a notification to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其与针对 restricted-ssh 规则的 AWS Config 评估结果为“不合规” 相匹配。为 EventBridge 规则配置输入转换器。配置 EventBridge 规则以向 SNS 主题发布通知。","B":"配置 AWS Config 将受限 SSH 规则的所有评估结果发送到 SNS 主题。在 SNS 主题上配置一个过 滤策略，仅向订阅者发送通知中包含“NON_COMPLIANT”文本的通知。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则与 AWS Config 对受限 SSH 规则的评估结果为“不合规”相 匹配。配置 EventBridge 规则，使其在 SNS 主题上调用 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 来自定义 通知，并将通知发布到 SNS 主题。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，匹配所有 AWS Config 评估结果为“不合规”的情况。为 受限 SSH 规则配置输入转换器。配置 EventBridge 规则以向 SNS 主题发布通知。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config sends a 'Config Rules Compliance Change' event directly to Amazon EventBridge (source: aws.config). The event detail contains configRuleName (restricted-ssh), newEvaluationResult.complianceType (NON_COMPLIANT), resourceType, and resourceId (the security group ID), so an EventBridge rule can both filter on the restricted-ssh rule being NON_COMPLIANT and extract the security group identifiers. An EventBridge input transformer is the AWS-documented way to customize the text sent to a target (SNS) by mapping JSON paths from the event into a custom input template, which lets the engineer include the security group name and ID in the notification before publishing to the SNS topic in real time. This is exactly option A.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 會將 'Config Rules Compliance Change' 事件直接送到 Amazon EventBridge（source: aws.config）。事件的 detail 內含 configRuleName（restricted-ssh）、newEvaluationResult.complianceType（NON_COMPLIANT）、resourceType 與 resourceId（即 security group ID），因此 EventBridge rule 可同時針對 restricted-ssh 規則為 NON_COMPLIANT 進行比對，並擷取 security group 的識別資訊。EventBridge input transformer 是 AWS 官方文件記載用來自訂送往目標（SNS）文字的機制，它透過 JSON path 將事件值對應到自訂的 input template，讓工程師能在即時發布到 SNS topic 前，把 security group 名稱與 ID 放入通知內容。這正是選項 A。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An SNS filter policy filters on message attributes, not arbitrary body text, and AWS Config does not set per-evaluation filterable attributes for NON_COMPLIANT. More importantly, a filter policy can only suppress messages; it cannot customize the notification to include the security group name and ID in a custom format.","why_zh":"SNS filter policy 是依 message attributes 過濾，而非任意的訊息本文文字，且 AWS Config 並未為 NON_COMPLIANT 設定可供過濾的逐筆屬性。更關鍵的是 filter policy 只能抑制訊息，無法自訂通知以加入 security group 名稱與 ID。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager Run Command executes commands on managed nodes/EC2 instances, not 'on an SNS topic.' You cannot target an SNS topic with Run Command, so this configuration is invalid and cannot produce or publish a notification.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Run Command 是在受管節點/EC2 執行個體上執行指令，並非『在 SNS topic 上』執行。Run Command 無法以 SNS topic 為目標，因此此設定無效，無法產生或發布通知。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Matching all NON_COMPLIANT evaluation results is not scoped to the restricted-ssh rule in the event pattern, and an input transformer only transforms text; it cannot perform filtering or scope the rule. Notifications would therefore fire for every Config rule, not just restricted-ssh. The scoping is placed in the wrong component.","why_zh":"比對所有 NON_COMPLIANT 結果並未在 event pattern 中限定為 restricted-ssh 規則，而 input transformer 只能轉換文字，無法進行過濾或限定規則。如此一來每個 Config 規則都會觸發通知，而非只有 restricted-ssh。限定條件被放在錯誤的元件上。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-input-transformer-tutorial.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-transform-target-input.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/example-config-rule-compliance-notification.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":93,"question_en":"A company requires an RPO of 2 hours and an RTO of 10 minutes for its data and application at all times. An application uses a MySQL database and Amazon EC2 web servers. The development team needs a strategy for failover and disaster recovery. Which combination of deployment strategies will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司要求其数据和应用程序在任何时候的恢复点目标（RPO）为 2 小时，恢复时间目标（RTO）为 10 分钟。 该应用程序使用 MySQL 数据库和亚马逊 EC2 网络服务器。开发团队需要制定故障转移和灾难恢复 策略。 哪种部署策略组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Aurora cluster in one Availability Zone across multiple Regions as the data store. Use Aurora’s automatic recovery capabilities in the event of a disaster.","B":"Create an Amazon Aurora global database in two Regions as the data store. In the event of a failure, promote the secondary Region as the primary for the application.","C":"Create an Amazon Aurora multi-master cluster across multiple Regions as the data store. Use a Network Load Balancer to balance the database traffic in different Regions.","D":"Set up the application in two Regions and use Amazon Route 53 failover-based routing that points to the Application Load Balancers in both Regions. Use health checks to determine the availability in a given Region. Use Auto Scaling groups in each Region to adjust capacity based on demand.","E":"Set up the application in two Regions and use a multi-Region Auto Scaling group behind Application Load Balancers to manage the capacity based on demand. In the event of a disaster, adjust the Auto Scaling group’s desired instance count to increase baseline capacity in the failover Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在多个区域中的一个可用区创建 Amazon Aurora 集群作为数据存储。在发生灾难时，利用 Aurora 的自动恢复功能。","B":"在两个区域创建一个 Amazon Aurora 全球数据库作为数据存储。在出现故障时，将备用区域提升 为应用程序的主区域。","C":"在多个区域创建 Amazon Aurora 多主集群作为数据存储。使用网络负载均衡器来平衡不同区 域的数据库流量。","D":"在两个区域设置应用程序，并使用基于 Amazon Route 53 故障转移的路由，该路由指向两个区域 中的应用负载均衡器。使用健康检查来确定给定区域的可用性。在每个区域使用自动扩展组根 据需求调整容量。","E":"在两个区域设置应用程序，并在应用程序负载均衡器后面使用多区域自动扩展组来根据需求管理 容量。在发生灾难时，调整自动扩展组的期望实例数以增加故障转移区域的基线容量。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements (RPO 2 hours, RTO 10 minutes) apply to both the data tier and the application tier, so the two correct answers split across those tiers. For data, an Amazon Aurora global database (Option B) replicates from the primary Region to a secondary Region with sub-second lag, giving an RPO typically measured in seconds and an RTO of minutes when the secondary cluster is promoted to primary; this comfortably meets RPO 2h / RTO 10m. For the application, deploying EC2 web servers behind ALBs in two Regions with Route 53 failover-based routing and health checks (Option D) provides active-passive cross-Region failover: Route 53 detects the unhealthy primary Region via health checks and shifts DNS to the standby Region, while Auto Scaling groups already running in each Region scale capacity, satisfying the 10-minute RTO. Options A, C, and E describe configurations that do not exist or cannot work (a single AZ cannot span Regions; Aurora multi-master is single-Region only and an NLB cannot balance cross-Region DB writes; there is no multi-Region Auto Scaling group and an ALB cannot front instances across Regions).","explanation_zh":"需求 (RPO 2 小時、RTO 10 分鐘) 同時涵蓋資料層與應用層，因此兩個正確答案分別對應這兩層。資料層方面，Amazon Aurora global database (選項 B) 以通常低於一秒的延遲將主要 Region 複寫到次要 Region，RPO 通常以秒計、將次要叢集提升為主要時 RTO 為數分鐘，輕鬆滿足 RPO 2h / RTO 10m。應用層方面，將 EC2 web 伺服器部署於兩個 Region 的 ALB 之後，搭配 Route 53 failover 路由與 health checks (選項 D)，提供 active-passive 跨 Region 容錯：Route 53 透過 health checks 偵測主要 Region 不健康後，將 DNS 切換到待命 Region，而各 Region 既有的 Auto Scaling group 自動調整容量，滿足 10 分鐘 RTO。選項 A、C、E 所述的設定不存在或無法運作 (單一 AZ 無法跨 Region；Aurora multi-master 僅限單一 Region 且 NLB 無法平衡跨 Region 的資料庫寫入；不存在跨 Region 的 Auto Scaling group，ALB 也無法將跨 Region 的執行個體作為目標)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A single Availability Zone cannot span multiple Regions, so the description is self-contradictory. Relying on intra-AZ automatic recovery gives no multi-Region (or even multi-AZ) resilience and fails the regional DR requirement.","why_zh":"單一 Availability Zone 無法橫跨多個 Region，描述本身自相矛盾。僅依賴 AZ 內的自動復原無法提供跨 Region (甚至跨 AZ) 的韌性，無法滿足 Region 層級的 DR 需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Aurora multi-master is a single-Region feature (and has been deprecated/removed); it cannot span Regions. A Network Load Balancer also cannot balance cross-Region database write traffic, so this architecture is technically invalid.","why_zh":"Aurora multi-master 是單一 Region 的功能 (且已被棄用/移除)，無法跨 Region。Network Load Balancer 也無法平衡跨 Region 的資料庫寫入流量，因此此架構技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"There is no 'multi-Region Auto Scaling group'; ASGs are Regional and an ALB can only target instances within its own Region. Manually adjusting desired capacity after a disaster also provides no automated DNS/traffic failover, so it cannot meet a 10-minute RTO.","why_zh":"並不存在「跨 Region 的 Auto Scaling group」；ASG 是 Region 範圍，ALB 只能將自身 Region 內的執行個體作為目標。災難後手動調整 desired capacity 也無法提供自動的 DNS/流量容錯，因此無法滿足 10 分鐘 RTO。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-configuring.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":94,"question_en":"A business has an application that consists of five independent AWS Lambda functions. The DevOps engineer has built a CI/CD pipeline using AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild that builds, tests, packages, and deploys each Lambda function in sequence. The pipeline uses an Amazon EventBridge rule to ensure the pipeline starts as quickly as possible after a change is made to the application source code. After working with the pipeline for a few months, the DevOps engineer has noticed the pipeline takes too long to complete. What should the DevOps engineer implement to BEST improve the speed of the pipeline?","question_zh":"一家企业有一个应用程序，该程序由五个独立的 AWS Lambda 函数组成。 该 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 构建了一个 CI/CD 管道，依次构建、测 试、打包和部署每个 Lambda 函数。该管道使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则来确保在对应用程序源代码 进行更改后，管道能尽快启动。 在使用该流水线几个月后，DevOps 工程师注意到流水线完成所需的时间太长。 DevOps 工程师应实施什么措施才能最大程度地提高流水线的速度？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the CodeBuild projects within the pipeline to use a compute type with more available network throughput.","B":"Create a custom CodeBuild execution environment that includes a symmetric multiprocessing configuration to run the builds in parallel.","C":"Modify the CodePipeline configuration to run actions for each Lambda function in parallel by specifying the same runOrder.","D":"Modify each CodeBuild project to run within a VPC and use dedicated instances to increase throughput."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改流水线中的 CodeBuild 项目，使其使用具有更高可用网络吞吐量的计算类型。","B":"创建一个自定义的 CodeBuild 执行环境，其中包含对称多处理配置，以便并行运行构建任 务。","C":"通过指定相同的运行顺序，修改 CodePipeline 配置，以并行运行每个 Lambda 函数的操作。","D":"将每个 CodeBuild 项目修改为在 VPC 内运行，并使用专用实例来提高吞吐量。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The five Lambda functions are independent, but the pipeline builds, tests, packages, and deploys each one in sequence, which is the root cause of the slowness. In CodePipeline, the runOrder field controls execution order within a stage: actions with the same runOrder integer run in parallel, while increasing integers run serially. By assigning the same runOrder to each Lambda function's action, all five run concurrently instead of one after another, so the total pipeline time drops to roughly the time of the slowest single function rather than the sum of all five. Because the functions have no dependencies on each other, parallelization is safe and directly removes the serialization bottleneck, making this the BEST option to improve speed.","explanation_zh":"五個 Lambda 函式彼此獨立，但目前 pipeline 是依序對每個函式進行 build、test、package、deploy，這正是速度緩慢的根本原因。在 CodePipeline 中，runOrder 欄位控制 stage 內動作的執行順序：runOrder 整數相同的動作會平行執行，整數遞增則會串行執行。將每個 Lambda 函式的動作設定為相同的 runOrder，五個函式就能同時執行而非一個接一個，整體 pipeline 時間會縮短到約等於最慢單一函式的時間，而非五個的總和。由於這些函式彼此沒有相依性，平行化是安全的，並直接消除了串行瓶頸，因此這是改善速度的最佳選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Lambda deployment packages are small, so network throughput is not the bottleneck. A higher-network compute type does nothing to address the actual problem, which is that the five independent functions are processed one after another.","why_zh":"Lambda 部署套件很小，網路吞吐量並非瓶頸。提供更高網路吞吐的 compute type 完全無法解決真正的問題，也就是五個獨立函式被依序逐一處理。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A custom CodeBuild environment with 'symmetric multiprocessing' to run builds in parallel inside one build is not a real CodeBuild feature and does not change the pipeline's stage/action sequencing. The bottleneck is the serial pipeline flow across functions, not single-build CPU parallelism.","why_zh":"以『對稱多處理 (SMP)』自訂 CodeBuild 環境在單一 build 內平行執行並非真實的 CodeBuild 功能，且無法改變 pipeline 的 stage/action 順序。瓶頸在於跨函式的串行流程，而非單一 build 的 CPU 平行度。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeBuild does not run on customer 'dedicated instances,' and placing builds in a VPC generally adds ENI/startup latency rather than increasing throughput. It also does nothing to parallelize the serially executed functions.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 並非執行在客戶的『專用執行個體』上，而將 build 放進 VPC 通常會增加 ENI/啟動延遲而非提升吞吐量。它同樣無法讓串行執行的函式平行化。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-requirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/reference-pipeline-structure.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":95,"question_en":"A company uses AWS CloudFormation stacks to deploy updates to its application. The stacks consist of different resources. The resources include AWS Auto Scaling groups, Amazon EC2 instances, Application Load Balancers (ALBs), and other resources that are necessary to launch and maintain independent stacks. Changes to application resources outside of CloudFormation stack updates are not allowed. The company recently attempted to update the application stack by using the AWS CLI. The stack failed to update and produced the following error message: “ERROR: both the deployment and the CloudFormation stack rollback failed. The deployment failed because the following resource(s) failed to update: [AutoScalingGroup].” The stack remains in a status of UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED. Which solution will resolve this issue?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来部署其应用程序的更新。这些堆栈包含不同的资源，其中包 括 AWS 自动扩展组、Amazon EC2 实例、应用负载均衡器（ALB）以及其他用于启动和维护独立堆 栈所必需的资源。不允许在 CloudFormation 堆栈更新之外对应用程序资源进行更改。 该公司最近尝试使用 AWS 命令行界面更新应用程序堆栈，但更新失败，并产生了以下错误消息： “错误：部署和 CloudFormation 堆栈回滚均失败。部署失败是因为以下资源更新失败： “自动缩放组。” 该堆栈仍处于“更新回滚失败”的状态。 哪种解决方案能解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Update the subnet mappings that are configured for the ALBs. Run the aws cloudformation update- stack-set AWS CLI command.","B":"Update the IAM role by providing the necessary permissions to update the stack. Run the aws cloudformation continue-update-rollback AWS CLI command.","C":"Submit a request for a quota increase for the number of EC2 instances for the account. Run the aws cloudformation cancel-update-stack AWS CLI command.","D":"Delete the Auto Scaling group resource. Run the aws cloudformation rollback-stack AWS CLI command."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新为应用负载均衡器（ALB）配置的子网映射。运行 aws cloudformation updatestack-set AWS CLI 命令。","B":"通过提供更新堆栈所需的权限来更新 IAM 角色。运行 aws cloudformation continue-update-rollback AWS CLI 命令。","C":"为账户提交增加 EC2 实例数量配额的请求。运行 aws cloudformation cancel-update-stack AWS CLI 命令。","D":"删除自动扩展组资源。运行 aws cloudformation rollback-stack AWS CLI 命令。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The stack is in UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED because the rollback could not complete. The error names the AutoScalingGroup resource that failed to update. AWS's official troubleshooting guidance for 'Update rollback failed' lists 'Insufficient permissions' as a cause and says to check that you have sufficient IAM permissions to modify the resources, and then continue the update rollback. The recovery action for any UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED cause is the continue-update-rollback operation (CLI: aws cloudformation continue-update-rollback), which moves the stack from UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED to UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE. Option B performs exactly the required two steps: grant the missing IAM permissions, then run continue-update-rollback. This also respects the constraint that no out-of-band changes to resources are allowed, since the fix is performed through CloudFormation.","explanation_zh":"該 stack 處於 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 狀態，因為 rollback 無法完成，錯誤訊息指出是 AutoScalingGroup 資源更新失敗。AWS 官方對「Update rollback failed」的疑難排解說明列出「Insufficient permissions（權限不足）」為原因之一，並指示先確認擁有足夠的 IAM 權限可修改資源，然後再繼續 update rollback。針對任何 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 的修復動作都是 continue-update-rollback 操作（CLI: aws cloudformation continue-update-rollback），它會將 stack 從 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 推進到 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE。選項 B 正是執行所需的兩個步驟：補足缺少的 IAM 權限，再執行 continue-update-rollback，同時符合不得在 CloudFormation 之外手動變更資源的限制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Updating ALB subnet mappings is unrelated to the AutoScalingGroup update failure, and update-stack-set is for CloudFormation StackSets (multi-account/region), not a single failed stack. It does not recover a stack from UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED.","why_zh":"更新 ALB 的 subnet mappings 與 AutoScalingGroup 更新失敗無關，且 update-stack-set 是用於 CloudFormation StackSets（跨帳號/區域），並非單一失敗的 stack，無法將 stack 從 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 復原。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A quota increase only matters if the failure was a 'Limitation error', but the error here points to an update failure on the ASG, and the troubleshooting doc still says to continue the rollback. cancel-update-stack only works while a stack is UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS; it cannot act on an UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED stack.","why_zh":"提升配額僅在失敗為「Limitation error」時才相關，但此處錯誤指向 ASG 的更新失敗，且文件仍指示要繼續 rollback。cancel-update-stack 只能在 stack 處於 UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS 時使用，無法作用於 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 的 stack。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Deleting the Auto Scaling group is an out-of-band change, which the scenario explicitly forbids and which AWS warns can put the stack in an unrecoverable state. rollback-stack triggers a rollback for CREATE_FAILED/UPDATE_FAILED stacks (typically with disabled rollback); it is not the operation that recovers a stack already in UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED.","why_zh":"刪除 Auto Scaling group 屬於在 CloudFormation 之外的手動變更，情境明確禁止，AWS 也警告這可能使 stack 進入無法復原狀態。rollback-stack 是針對 CREATE_FAILED/UPDATE_FAILED 的 stack（通常配合停用 rollback）觸發回復，並非用來復原已處於 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 的 stack。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-updating-stacks-continueupdaterollback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/cloudformation/continue-update-rollback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/APIReference/API_ContinueUpdateRollback.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":96,"question_en":"A company is deploying a new application that uses Amazon EC2 instances. The company needs a solution to query application logs and AWS account API activity. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在部署一个使用亚马逊 EC2 实例的新应用程序。该公司需要一个解决方案来查询应用程 序日志和 AWS 账户的 API 活动。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to send logs from the EC2 instances to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Configure AWS CloudTrail to deliver the API logs to Amazon S3. Use CloudWatch to query both sets of logs.","B":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to send logs from the EC2 instances to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Configure AWS CloudTrail to deliver the API logs to CloudWatch Logs. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to query both sets of logs.","C":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to send logs from the EC2 instances to Amazon Kinesis. Configure AWS CloudTrail to deliver the API logs to Kinesis. Use Kinesis to load the data into Amazon Redshift. Use Amazon Redshift to query both sets of logs.","D":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to send logs from the EC2 instances to Amazon S3. Use AWS CloudTrail to deliver the API logs to Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena to query both sets of logs in Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理将 EC2 实例的日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。配置 AWS CloudTrail 将 API 日志交付到 Amazon S3。使用 CloudWatch 查询这两组日志。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理将 EC2 实例的日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。配置 AWS CloudTrail 将 API 日志传递到 CloudWatch Logs。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询这两组日志。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理将 EC2 实例的日志发送到 Amazon Kinesis。配置 AWS CloudTrail 将 API 日 志传递到 Kinesis。使用 Kinesis 将数据加载到 Amazon Redshift 中。使用 Amazon Redshift 查询这两组日 志。","D":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理将 EC2 实例的日志发送到 Amazon S3。使用 AWS CloudTrail 将 API 日 志交付到 Amazon S3。使用 Amazon Athena 查询 Amazon S3 中的这两组日志。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a single solution to query both EC2 application logs and AWS account API activity. Option B is correct because both log sets are consolidated into CloudWatch Logs and queried with one tool. The Amazon CloudWatch agent natively sends application/system logs from EC2 instances to CloudWatch Logs, and AWS CloudTrail has a native feature to deliver management, data, and Insights events (the API activity) directly to a CloudWatch Logs log group. CloudWatch Logs Insights then interactively searches and analyzes data across log groups, and it natively auto-discovers fields from AWS services including AWS CloudTrail, so it can query both the application logs and the CloudTrail API logs. This is the least-overhead working design because it relies on built-in integrations and a single query engine over a single store.","explanation_zh":"需求是用單一方案同時查詢 EC2 應用程式日誌與 AWS 帳戶 API 活動。選項 B 正確，因為兩組日誌都集中到 CloudWatch Logs，並以單一工具查詢。Amazon CloudWatch agent 原生將 EC2 的應用程式/系統日誌送到 CloudWatch Logs；AWS CloudTrail 具備原生功能，可將 management、data 與 Insights 事件（即 API 活動）直接送到 CloudWatch Logs 的 log group。接著 CloudWatch Logs Insights 可跨 log group 互動式搜尋與分析，並原生自動辨識包含 AWS CloudTrail 在內的 AWS 服務欄位，因此能同時查詢應用程式日誌與 CloudTrail API 日誌。這是營運負擔最低且可行的設計，因為使用內建整合與單一查詢引擎、單一存放區。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail logs are delivered to S3 while app logs are in CloudWatch Logs. CloudWatch/Logs Insights cannot natively query data sitting in S3, so you cannot query both sets with CloudWatch.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 日誌送到 S3，應用程式日誌在 CloudWatch Logs。CloudWatch/Logs Insights 無法原生查詢存於 S3 的資料，因此無法用 CloudWatch 同時查詢兩組日誌。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The CloudWatch agent's destination is CloudWatch Logs, not Kinesis. Building a Kinesis to Redshift pipeline to query logs is heavily over-engineered with high operational overhead and is not the agent's native behavior.","why_zh":"CloudWatch agent 的目的地是 CloudWatch Logs，而非 Kinesis。建置 Kinesis 到 Redshift 的管線來查詢日誌過度設計、營運負擔高，且非 agent 原生行為。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The CloudWatch agent does not deliver logs directly to Amazon S3; its log destination is CloudWatch Logs. So the premise of sending EC2 logs to S3 via the CloudWatch agent (to then query with Athena) is technically invalid.","why_zh":"CloudWatch agent 不會直接將日誌送到 Amazon S3，其日誌目的地是 CloudWatch Logs。因此用 CloudWatch agent 把 EC2 日誌送到 S3（再以 Athena 查詢）的前提在技術上不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/send-cloudtrail-events-to-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/QuickStartEC2Instance.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":97,"question_en":"A company wants to ensure that their EC2 instances are secure. They want to be notified if any new vulnerabilities are discovered on their instances, and they also want an audit trail of all login activities on the instances. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望确保其 EC2 实例的安全。他们希望在实例上发现任何新的漏洞时能收到通知，并且还希望 对实例上的所有登录活动进行审计跟踪。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager to detect vulnerabilities on the EC2 instances. Install the Amazon Kinesis Agent to capture system logs and deliver them to Amazon S3.","B":"Use AWS Systems Manager to detect vulnerabilities on the EC2 instances. Install the Systems Manager Agent to capture system logs and view login activity in the CloudTrail console.","C":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch to detect vulnerabilities on the EC2 instances. Install the AWS Config daemon to capture system logs and view them in the AWS Config console.","D":"Configure Amazon Inspector to detect vulnerabilities on the EC2 instances. Install the Amazon CloudWatch Agent to capture system logs and record them via Amazon CloudWatch Logs."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 检测 EC2 实例上的漏洞。安装 Amazon Kinesis Agent 以捕获系统日志并将其 交付到 Amazon S3。","B":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 检测 EC2 实例上的漏洞。安装 Systems Manager 代理以捕获系统日志， 并在 CloudTrail 控制台中查看登录活动。","C":"配置 Amazon CloudWatch 以检测 EC2 实例上的漏洞。安装 AWS Config 守护进程以捕获系统日志，并在 AWS Config 控制台中查看这些日志。","D":"配置 Amazon Inspector 以检测 EC2 实例上的漏洞。安装 Amazon 使用 CloudWatch 代理来捕获系统日志，并通过 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 进行记录。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements: be notified of new EC2 vulnerabilities, and keep an audit trail of all login (OS-level) activity. Amazon Inspector is AWS's vulnerability management service that automatically and continuously scans EC2 instances for software vulnerabilities and produces findings (which can trigger notifications via EventBridge/SNS) - this satisfies the vulnerability requirement. The Amazon CloudWatch Agent collects OS-level system logs (such as /var/log/secure or /var/log/auth.log that record SSH/console login activity) and delivers them to Amazon CloudWatch Logs, providing the login audit trail. Option D pairs the correct service for each requirement.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個需求：當 EC2 出現新弱點時收到通知，以及保留所有登入（作業系統層級）活動的稽核軌跡。Amazon Inspector 是 AWS 的弱點管理服務，會自動且持續掃描 EC2 執行個體的軟體弱點並產生 findings（可透過 EventBridge/SNS 觸發通知），滿足弱點偵測需求。Amazon CloudWatch Agent 會收集作業系統層級的系統日誌（例如記錄 SSH/主控台登入活動的 /var/log/secure 或 /var/log/auth.log），並送至 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，提供登入稽核軌跡。選項 D 為每個需求搭配了正確的服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager is not a vulnerability detection service (Patch Manager only reports missing patches/compliance, not CVE vulnerability findings - that is Amazon Inspector's role). Routing system logs through the Kinesis Agent to S3 is a non-standard, convoluted pattern for a login audit trail.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager 並非弱點偵測服務（Patch Manager 僅回報缺少的修補程式/合規狀態，而非 CVE 弱點 findings，那是 Amazon Inspector 的職責）。透過 Kinesis Agent 將系統日誌送到 S3 是非標準且繁瑣的登入稽核做法。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Systems Manager does not perform vulnerability detection. More decisively, CloudTrail records AWS API activity (console/CLI/SDK calls), NOT OS-level SSH/console login activity on the instance, so you cannot view instance login activity in the CloudTrail console.","why_zh":"Systems Manager 不執行弱點偵測。更關鍵的是，CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API 活動（主控台/CLI/SDK 呼叫），而非執行個體上作業系統層級的 SSH/主控台登入活動，因此無法在 CloudTrail 主控台檢視執行個體登入活動。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon CloudWatch does not detect vulnerabilities. AWS Config tracks resource configuration changes, not system logs, and there is no 'AWS Config daemon' for capturing OS logs.","why_zh":"Amazon CloudWatch 不偵測弱點。AWS Config 追蹤的是資源組態變更，而非系統日誌，且並不存在用於擷取作業系統日誌的『AWS Config daemon』。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/what-is-inspector.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Agent-on-EC2-Instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-user-guide.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":98,"question_en":"A company is running an application on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. Recently, an issue occurred that prevented EC2 instances from launching successfully, and it took several hours for the support team to discover the issue. The support team wants to be notified by email whenever an EC2 instance does not start successfully. Which action will accomplish this?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例的自动扩展组中运行应用程序。最近出现了一个问题，导致 EC2 实例无法成 功启动，支持团队花了好几个小时才发现问题所在。支持团队希望每当 EC2 实例启动失败时都能通过电 子邮件收到通知。 哪项行动能达成此目标？","options_en":{"A":"Add a health check to the Auto Scaling group to invoke an AWS Lambda function whenever an instance status is impaired.","B":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to send a notification to an Amazon SNS topic whenever a failed instance launch occurs.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that invokes an AWS Lambda function when a failed AttachInstances Auto Scaling API call is made.","D":"Create a status check alarm on Amazon EC2 to send a notification to an Amazon SNS topic whenever a status check fail occurs."},"options_zh":{"A":"向自动扩展组添加一个健康检查，以便在实例状态受损时调用 AWS Lambda 函数。","B":"将自动扩展组配置为在实例启动失败时向 Amazon SNS 主题发送通知。","C":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，当调用 AttachInstances Auto Scaling API 失败时，该警 报会触发一个 AWS Lambda 函数。","D":"在 Amazon EC2 上创建状态检查警报，以便在状态检查失败时向 Amazon SNS 主题发送通知。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling natively supports Amazon SNS notifications for instance lifecycle events. The supported notification types are autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH (successful launch), autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH_ERROR (failed instance launch), autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATE, and autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATE_ERROR. By configuring the Auto Scaling group to send EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH_ERROR notifications to an SNS topic with an email subscription, the support team is automatically emailed whenever an EC2 instance fails to launch. This is the purpose-built, lowest-overhead mechanism for the exact scenario described, so option B is correct.","explanation_zh":"Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 原生支援透過 Amazon SNS 發送執行個體生命週期事件通知。支援的通知類型包含 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH（成功啟動）、autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH_ERROR（啟動失敗）、autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATE 與 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATE_ERROR。將 Auto Scaling group 設定為在發生 EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH_ERROR 時將通知傳送到具有 email 訂閱的 SNS topic，support 團隊即可在 EC2 執行個體啟動失敗時自動收到 email。這是針對此情境最直接、營運負擔最低的內建機制，因此 B 為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Auto Scaling health checks detect already-running instances that become impaired (e.g., failing EC2 status checks or ELB health checks); they do not fire when an instance fails to launch in the first place. Health checks also do not directly invoke Lambda. This does not address launch failures.","why_zh":"Auto Scaling 健康檢查偵測的是已在執行但變為受損的執行個體（例如 EC2 狀態檢查或 ELB 健康檢查失敗），無法在執行個體一開始就啟動失敗時觸發，且健康檢查也無法直接呼叫 Lambda，因此無法解決啟動失敗問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AttachInstances attaches existing EC2 instances to an Auto Scaling group; it is unrelated to the group launching new instances during scaling. A CloudWatch alarm on a failed AttachInstances API call would not detect normal scale-out launch failures, and CloudWatch alarms watch metrics, not arbitrary failed API calls.","why_zh":"AttachInstances 是將既有 EC2 執行個體附加到 Auto Scaling group，與群組在擴展時啟動新執行個體無關。針對失敗的 AttachInstances API 呼叫設定的 CloudWatch 警報無法偵測一般的 scale-out 啟動失敗，且 CloudWatch 警報是監控指標而非任意失敗的 API 呼叫。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EC2 status check alarms only monitor instances that have already launched and are running (instance/system status checks). They cannot detect a launch that never succeeded, because a status check requires a running instance to evaluate. This misses the failed-launch scenario entirely.","why_zh":"EC2 狀態檢查警報僅監控已啟動並執行中的執行個體（執行個體/系統狀態檢查），無法偵測從未成功的啟動，因為狀態檢查需要有執行中的執行個體才能評估，因此完全無法涵蓋啟動失敗的情境。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-sns-notifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ts-as-instancelaunchfailure.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":99,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations to centrally manage its AWS accounts. The company has turned on AWS Config in each member account by using AWS CloudFormation StackSets. The company has configured trusted access in Organizations for AWS Config and has configured a member account as a delegated administrator account for AWS Config. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a new security policy. The policy must require all current and future AWS member accounts to use a common baseline of AWS Config rules that contain remediation actions that are managed from a central account. Non-administrator users who can access member accounts must not be able to modify this common baseline of AWS Config rules that are deployed into each member account. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS Organizations 来集中管理其 AWS 账户。该公司通过使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在每个成员账户中启用了 AWS Config。该公司已在 Organizations 中为 AWS Config 配置了受 信任访问，并将一个成员账户配置为 AWS Config 的委托管理员账户。 DevOps 工程师需要实施一项新的安全策略。该策略必须要求所有当前和未来的 AWS 成员账户使用由 中央账户管理的包含修复操作的通用 AWS Config 规则基线。能够访问成员账户的非管理员用户不得 修改部署到每个成员账户的通用 AWS Config 规则基线。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudFormation template that contains the AWS Config rules and remediation actions. Deploy the template from the Organizations management account by using CloudFormation StackSets.","B":"Create an AWS Config conformance pack that contains the AWS Config rules and remediation actions. Deploy the pack from the Organizations management account by using CloudFormation StackSets.","C":"Create a CloudFormation template that contains the AWS Config rules and remediation actions. Deploy the template from the delegated administrator account by using AWS Config.","D":"Create an AWS Config conformance pack that contains the AWS Config rules and remediation actions. Deploy the pack from the delegated administrator account by using AWS Config."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个包含 AWS Config 规则和修复操作的 CloudFormation 模板。通过使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从组织管理账户部署该模板。","B":"创建一个包含 AWS Config 规则和修复操作的 AWS Config 合规性包。通过使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从组织管理账户部署该包。","C":"创建一个包含 AWS Config 规则和修复操作的 CloudFormation 模板。通过 AWS Config 从委托管理员账 户部署该模板。","D":"创建一个包含 AWS Config 规则和修复操作的 AWS Config 合规性包。通过 AWS Config 从委托管理员 账户部署该包。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An AWS Config organization conformance pack is purpose-built for this scenario. The AWS Config docs state you can use it to deploy a common set of AWS Config rules and remediation actions across all accounts, that it automatically applies to accounts that later join the organization (current and future members), and critically that it lets the management account enforce governance by ensuring the underlying Config rules and remediation actions are not modifiable by member accounts. Organization conformance packs are deployed natively through AWS Config (PutOrganizationConformancePack), and the question already establishes a registered delegated administrator account, which is the supported account from which to deploy. Option D therefore satisfies the common baseline, the include-future-accounts requirement, and the non-modifiable-by-member-users requirement.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 的 organization conformance pack 正是為此情境設計。AWS Config 文件指出，可用它在所有帳戶部署一組共同的 AWS Config rules 與 remediation actions，且當新帳戶加入組織時會自動套用（涵蓋現有與未來成員帳戶），最關鍵的是它讓 management account 透過確保底層的 Config rules 與 remediation actions「無法被成員帳戶修改」來強制治理。Organization conformance pack 是透過 AWS Config 原生機制（PutOrganizationConformancePack）部署，而題目已設定好註冊的 delegated administrator account，這正是支援的部署來源帳戶。因此選項 D 同時滿足共同基線、涵蓋未來帳戶、以及成員帳戶使用者無法修改三項要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation StackSets deploys CFN stacks containing account-level AWS Config rule resources into each member account; those rules are ordinary local rules that account administrators/users can modify or delete, so it fails the non-modifiable-by-member-users governance requirement. It also bypasses the delegated administrator model already established.","why_zh":"CloudFormation StackSets 會把含有帳戶層級 AWS Config rule 資源的 CFN 堆疊部署到每個成員帳戶；這些是一般本地 rules，成員帳戶的管理者/使用者可修改或刪除，因此無法滿足成員帳戶不可修改的治理要求，也繞過了題目已設定的 delegated administrator 模型。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Conflates two mechanisms: organization conformance packs are not deployed via CloudFormation StackSets. Deploying a regular conformance pack through StackSets would create independent account-level packs that member admins can modify, failing the governance lock; and the question already designates a delegated administrator as the deployment point rather than the management account.","why_zh":"混淆了兩種機制：organization conformance pack 不是透過 CloudFormation StackSets 部署。透過 StackSets 部署一般 conformance pack 會在各帳戶建立獨立的帳戶層級 pack，成員管理者可修改，無法達成治理鎖定；且題目已指定 delegated administrator 為部署點，而非 management account。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot deploy a CloudFormation template by using AWS Config; the mechanism is mismatched. Even setting that aside, CFN-deployed Config rules in a member account are local resources that can be modified there, so it does not provide the centrally enforced, non-modifiable baseline.","why_zh":"無法用 AWS Config 來部署 CloudFormation template，機制不相符。即使忽略此點，透過 CFN 部署到成員帳戶的 Config rules 是本地資源，可在當地被修改，無法提供集中強制且不可修改的基線。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-pack-organization-apis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-packs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/APIReference/API_PutOrganizationConformancePack.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/aggregated-register-delegated-administrator.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":100,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages a large commercial website that runs on Amazon EC2. The website uses Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to collect and process web logs. The DevOps engineer manages the Kinesis consumer application, which also runs on Amazon EC2. Sudden increases of data cause the Kinesis consumer application to fall behind, and the Kinesis data streams drop records before the records can be processed. The DevOps engineer must implement a solution to improve stream handling. Which solution meets these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师负责管理一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 上的大型商业网站。该网站使用亚马逊 Kinesis 数据流来收集和处理网络日志。这位 DevOps 工程师还负责管理同样运行在亚马逊 EC2 上的 Kinesis 消费者应用程序。 数据量的突然增加导致 Kinesis 消费者应用程序处理滞后，Kinesis 数据流在记录被处理之前就丢弃 了这些记录。DevOps 工程师必须实施解决方案以改进流处理。 哪种解决方案在满足这些要求的同时具有最高的运营效率？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the Kinesis consumer application to store the logs durably in Amazon S3. Use Amazon EMR to process the data directly on Amazon S3 to derive customer insights. Store the results in Amazon S3.","B":"Horizontally scale the Kinesis consumer application by adding more EC2 instances based on the Amazon CloudWatch GetRecords.IteratorAgeMilliseconds metric. Increase the retention period of the Kinesis data streams.","C":"Convert the Kinesis consumer application to run as an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Kinesis data streams as the event source for the Lambda function to process the data streams.","D":"Increase the number of shards in the Kinesis data streams to increase the overall throughput so that the consumer application processes the data faster."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 Kinesis 消费者应用程序，将日志持久存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon EMR 直接在 Amazon S3 上处理数据以获取客户洞察。将结果存储在 Amazon S3 中。","B":"根据 Amazon CloudWatch 的 GetRecords.IteratorAgeMilliseconds 指标，通过添加更多 EC2 实例来水 平扩展 Kinesis 消费者应用程序。增加 Kinesis 数据流的保留期。","C":"将 Kinesis 消费者应用程序转换为作为 AWS Lambda 函数运行。将 Kinesis 数据流配置为 Lambda 函 数的事件源，以处理数据流。","D":"增加 Kinesis 数据流中的分片数量以提高整体吞吐量，从而使消费者应用程序更快地处理数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST operational efficiency. The root problem is that a self-managed KCL consumer fleet on EC2 cannot keep up with sudden traffic spikes, so records expire from the stream before being processed. Converting the consumer to an AWS Lambda function with the Kinesis data stream configured as the event source is the most operationally efficient fix: the Lambda event source mapping is fully managed by Lambda, polls each shard automatically, and keeps processing batches until the function catches up with the stream, scaling concurrency per shard with no servers to provision, patch, autoscale, or KCL lease tables to manage. Option B keeps the entire EC2 fleet plus a CloudWatch-driven scaling pipeline that the engineer must build and operate, and increasing retention is only a stopgap that buys time rather than fixing the throughput shortfall, so it is far less operationally efficient. The AWS troubleshooting guidance even points to scaling parallelism/resources, but Lambda accomplishes that automatically, which is why C wins on the operational-efficiency axis.","explanation_zh":"題目限定詞是 MOST operational efficiency（最高營運效率）。問題根因是在 EC2 上自管的 KCL consumer 機隊無法跟上突發流量，導致記錄在被處理前就因保留期到期而遺失。將 consumer 改寫為 AWS Lambda 函式並把 Kinesis data stream 設為事件來源（event source）是營運效率最高的解法：Lambda event source mapping 完全由 Lambda 服務代管，會自動輪詢每個 shard，持續處理批次直到追上 stream，並依每個 shard 自動擴展並行度，無需佈建、修補或自行設定 Auto Scaling 的伺服器，也不必管理 KCL lease table。選項 B 仍保留整個 EC2 機隊以及需要工程師自行建置與維運的 CloudWatch 驅動擴展流程，而增加 retention 只是爭取時間的權宜之計、並未解決吞吐量不足，營運效率明顯較低。AWS 疑難排解文件雖建議擴增並行度/資源，但 Lambda 會自動完成這件事，因此在營運效率軸上 C 勝出。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Re-architecting to dump logs to S3 and run EMR for batch analytics changes the processing model entirely, still relies on the failing EC2 consumer to write to S3, and adds an EMR cluster to operate. It is a heavy, high-overhead redesign, not the most operationally efficient stream-handling fix.","why_zh":"改成把日誌寫到 S3 再用 EMR 做批次分析，會完全改變處理模型，仍依賴正在出問題的 EC2 consumer 寫入 S3，還要額外維運 EMR 叢集，是高負擔的重構，並非營運效率最高的串流處理修正。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it preserves the EC2 fleet and forces the engineer to build and operate a CloudWatch IteratorAgeMilliseconds-driven autoscaling pipeline plus KCL lease management; increasing retention is only a stopgap that delays data loss rather than fixing throughput. It works technically but has much higher operational overhead than serverless Lambda.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案，但它保留 EC2 機隊，並強迫工程師自行建置與維運以 CloudWatch IteratorAgeMilliseconds 驅動的 Auto Scaling 流程及 KCL lease 管理；增加 retention 只是延後資料遺失的權宜之計，並未解決吞吐量問題。技術上可行，但營運負擔遠高於 serverless 的 Lambda。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Adding shards raises stream capacity and read parallelism, but the bottleneck described is the consumer falling behind, not the stream's ingest throughput; more shards do not make a slow self-managed EC2 consumer process faster on their own, and you still operate the EC2 fleet. It is a partial, less efficient fix that also raises cost.","why_zh":"增加 shard 可提升 stream 容量與讀取並行度，但題述瓶頸是 consumer 跟不上，而非 stream 的擷取吞吐量；單純增加 shard 並不會讓緩慢的自管 EC2 consumer 處理更快，且仍需維運 EC2 機隊。這是片面且效率較低的修正，同時也提高成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-kinesis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-eventsourcemapping.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/troubleshooting-consumers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-kinesis-create.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":101,"question_en":"A company recently created a new AWS Control Tower landing zone in a new organization in AWS Organizations. The landing zone must be able to demonstrate compliance with the Center for Internet Security (CIS) Benchmarks for AWS Foundations. The company’s security team wants to use AWS Security Hub to view compliance across all accounts. Only the security team can be allowed to view aggregated Security Hub findings. In addition, specific users must be able to view findings from their own accounts within the organization. All accounts must be enrolled in Security Hub after the accounts are created. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements in the MOST automated way? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近在 AWS 组织中为一个新的组织创建了一个新的 AWS 控制塔着陆区。该着陆区必须 能够证明符合 AWS 基础设施的互联网安全中心（CIS）基准。 该公司的安全团队希望使用 AWS 安全中心来查看所有账户的合规情况。只有安全团队能够查看安全中心 的汇总发现结果。此外，特定用户必须能够查看其所在组织内自身账户的发现结果。所有账户在创建后 都必须加入安全中心。 哪种步骤组合将以最自动化的方式满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Turn on trusted access for Security Hub in the organization’s management account. Create a new security account by using AWS Control Tower. Configure the new security account as the delegated administrator account for Security Hub. In the new security account, provide Security Hub with the CIS Benchmarks for AWS Foundations standards.","B":"Turn on trusted access for Security Hub in the organization’s management account. From the management account, provide Security Hub with the CIS Benchmarks for AWS Foundations standards.","C":"Create an AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) permission set that includes the required permissions. Use the CreateAccountAssignment API operation to associate the security team users with the permission set and with the delegated security account.","D":"Create an SCP that explicitly denies any user who is not on the security team from accessing Security Hub.","E":"In Security Hub, turn on automatic enablement.","F":"In the organization’s management account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to the CreateManagedAccount event. Create an AWS Lambda function that uses the Security Hub CreateMembers API operation to add new accounts to Security Hub. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中为 Security Hub 开启受信任访问。使用 AWS Control Tower 创建一个新的安全账 户。将新安全账户配置为 Security Hub 的委托管理员账户。在新安全账户中，为 Security Hub 提供 AWS 基础设施 CIS 基准标准。","B":"在组织的管理账户中为 Security Hub 启用受信任访问。从管理账户向 Security Hub 提供 AWS 基础设施 CIS 基准标准。","C":"创建一个包含所需权限的 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）权限集。使用 CreateAccountAssig nment API 操作将安全团队用户与权限集以及委托的安全账户相关联。","D":"创建一个安全策略配置（SCP），明确禁止任何不在安全团队的用户访问安全中心。","E":"在 Security Hub 中，开启自动启用功能。","F":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 CreateManagedAccount 事件作出反 应。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数使用 Security Hub 的 CreateMembers API 操作将新账户添 加到 Security Hub 中。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is the MOST automated way. (A) Following AWS best practice, you turn on trusted access for Security Hub and designate a separate, Control Tower-provisioned security account as the delegated administrator (AWS explicitly recommends NOT using the management account because billing users differ from security users), then enable the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark standard there; this gives the security team a single aggregation point for all-account findings. (C) IAM Identity Center's CreateAccountAssignment API assigns a principal (user/group) to a permission set for a specified AWS account, automatically provisioning the access; associating the security team with a permission set scoped to the delegated security account grants them aggregated-view access, while the same mechanism grants specific users access to their own member accounts. (E) Turning on Security Hub automatic enablement natively adds every new organization account as a member and enables Security Hub (and the default standards including CIS) when the account is created, satisfying the auto-enrollment requirement with no custom code. This beats (F), which would build and maintain an EventBridge rule plus a Lambda calling CreateMembers, far more operational overhead for the same outcome, and beats (B), which makes the management account the admin against AWS guidance.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是「最自動化的方式 (MOST automated)」。(A) 依照 AWS 最佳實務，開啟 Security Hub 的 trusted access，並指定一個由 Control Tower 建立的獨立 security account 作為 delegated administrator（AWS 明確建議不要使用 management account，因為負責帳務的使用者與負責安全的使用者通常不同），並在該帳號啟用 CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark 標準；如此安全團隊即擁有單一的跨帳號 findings 彙整點。(C) IAM Identity Center 的 CreateAccountAssignment API 會將 principal（user 或 group）指派到特定 AWS 帳號的 permission set，並自動佈建存取權；把安全團隊指派到對應 delegated security account 的 permission set，即可授予彙整檢視權限，相同機制也可讓特定使用者存取自己的 member account。(E) 開啟 Security Hub 的 automatic enablement 為原生功能，可在新組織帳號建立時自動將其加入為 member 並啟用 Security Hub（含預設標準如 CIS），無須自訂程式即滿足自動納管需求。此優於 (F)（需自建並維護 EventBridge rule 加 Lambda 呼叫 CreateMembers，營運負擔更高），也優於 (B)（讓 management account 當管理者，違反 AWS 指引）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Making the organization management account the Security Hub administrator violates AWS best practice (docs recommend a separate account because billing/management users differ from security users) and does not satisfy 'only the security team can view aggregated findings.' Also, Security Hub cannot be enabled automatically for the management account.","why_zh":"讓組織 management account 擔任 Security Hub 管理者違反 AWS 最佳實務（文件建議使用獨立帳號，因帳務/管理使用者與安全使用者不同），且無法滿足「僅安全團隊可檢視彙整 findings」；此外 Security Hub 無法為 management account 自動啟用。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An SCP applies to accounts and root/OU scopes, not to a notion of 'users on the security team,' so it cannot cleanly restrict aggregated-view access to the security team nor grant per-account viewing. It is also not the automated enrollment/access mechanism the requirements need.","why_zh":"SCP 作用於帳號與 root/OU 範圍，而非「安全團隊成員」概念，無法乾淨地將彙整檢視限制給安全團隊，也無法授予各自帳號檢視權；亦非需求所需的自動納管/存取機制。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Building an EventBridge rule on CreateManagedAccount plus a Lambda that calls the Security Hub CreateMembers API is functional but introduces significant custom code and maintenance overhead. The native automatic enablement feature (E) achieves the same auto-enrollment outcome with zero custom code, so F loses on the 'MOST automated' qualifier.","why_zh":"建立針對 CreateManagedAccount 的 EventBridge rule 加上呼叫 Security Hub CreateMembers API 的 Lambda 雖可運作，但引入大量自訂程式與維運負擔。原生的 automatic enablement（E）可零自訂程式達成相同的自動納管結果，故在「最自動化」限定詞下 F 落敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/designate-orgs-admin-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/accounts-orgs-auto-enable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/APIReference/API_CreateAccountAssignment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/assignusers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-controltower.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":102,"question_en":"A company runs applications in AWS accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The applications use Amazon EC2 instances and Amazon S3. The company wants to detect potentially compromised EC2 instances, suspicious network activity, and unusual API activity in its existing AWS accounts and in any AWS accounts that the company creates in the future. When the company detects one of these events, the company wants to use an existing Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send a notification to its operational support team for investigation and remediation. Which solution will meet these requirements in accordance with AWS best practices?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中的多个 AWS 账户中运行应用程序。这些应用程序使用亚马逊 EC2 实例和 亚马逊 S3。 该公司希望检测其现有 AWS 账户以及未来创建的任何 AWS 账户中可能受到攻击的 EC2 实例、可疑的网 络活动和异常的 API 活动。当公司检测到此类事件时，希望使用现有的亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题向其运营支持团队发送通知，以便进行调查和修复。 哪种解决方案符合 AWS 最佳实践并满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the organization’s management account, configure an AWS account as the Amazon GuardDuty administrator account. In the GuardDuty administrator account, add the company’s existing AWS accounts to GuardDuty as members. In the GuardDuty administrator account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule with an event pattern to match GuardDuty events and to forward matching events to the SNS topic.","B":"In the organization’s management account, configure Amazon GuardDuty to add newly created AWS accounts by invitation and to send invitations to the existing AWS accounts. Create an AWS CloudFormation stack set that accepts the GuardDuty invitation and creates an Amazon EventBridge rule. Configure the rule with an event pattern to match GuardDuty events and to forward matching events to the SNS topic. Configure the CloudFormation stack set to deploy into all AWS accounts in the organization.","C":"In the organization’s management account, create an AWS CloudTrail organization trail. Activate the organization trail in all AWS accounts in the organization. Create an SCP that enables VPC Flow Logs in each account in the organization. Configure AWS Security Hub for the organization. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with an event pattern to match Security Hub events and to forward matching events to the SNS topic.","D":"In the organization’s management account, configure an AWS account as the AWS CloudTrail administrator account. In the CloudTrail administrator account, create a CloudTrail organization trail. Add the company’s existing AWS accounts to the organization trail. Create an SCP that enables VPC Flow Logs in each account in the organization. Configure AWS Security Hub for the organization. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with an event pattern to match Security Hub events and to forward matching events to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中，将一个 AWS 账户配置为 Amazon GuardDuty 管理员账户。在 GuardDuty 管理 员账户中，将公司现有的 AWS 账户添加为 GuardDuty 成员。在 GuardDuty 管理员账户中，创建一 个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则包含一个事件模式，用于匹配 GuardDuty 事件并将匹配的事 件转发到 SNS 主题。","B":"在组织的管理账户中，配置 Amazon GuardDuty 以通过邀请添加新创建的 AWS 账户，并向现有 AWS 账户发送邀请。创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集，用于接受 GuardDuty 邀请并创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则的事件模式以匹配 GuardDuty 事件，并将匹配的事件转发到 SNS 主题。配置 CloudFormation 堆栈集以部署到组织中的所有 AWS 账户。","C":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 组织跟踪。在组织中的所有 AWS 账户中激活组织跟 踪。创建一个 SCP，以在组织中的每个账户中启用 VPC 流日志。为组织配置 AWS 安全中心。创建 一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则具有与安全中心事件匹配的事件模式，并将匹配的事件转发 到 SNS 主题。","D":"在组织的管理账户中，将一个 AWS 账户配置为 AWS CloudTrail 管理员账户。在 CloudTrail 管理员账 户中，创建一个 CloudTrail 组织跟踪。将公司的现有 AWS 账户添加到组织跟踪中。创建一个 SCP， 以在组织中的每个账户中启用 VPC 流日志。为组织配置 AWS 安全中心。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则具有与安全中心事件匹配的事件模式，并将匹配的事件转发到 SNS 主题。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The three detection needs map directly to Amazon GuardDuty: compromised EC2 instances, suspicious network activity (from VPC Flow Logs), and unusual API activity (from CloudTrail management events). GuardDuty automatically consumes CloudTrail, VPC Flow Logs, and DNS logs as foundational data sources with no extra configuration, so there is no need to create organization trails, enable VPC Flow Logs via SCPs, or aggregate with Security Hub. Best practice for an organization is to designate a delegated GuardDuty administrator account from the management account (security operations should not live in the management account), add the existing accounts as members via the AWS Organizations integration, and use auto-enable for new accounts so future accounts are covered automatically. GuardDuty publishes findings natively to Amazon EventBridge, so an EventBridge rule in the administrator account matching GuardDuty events and forwarding to the existing SNS topic completes the notification path. Option A implements exactly this pattern.","explanation_zh":"三項偵測需求直接對應到 Amazon GuardDuty：受侵害的 EC2 instances、可疑網路活動（來自 VPC Flow Logs）、異常 API 活動（來自 CloudTrail management events）。GuardDuty 會自動將 CloudTrail、VPC Flow Logs 與 DNS logs 作為基礎資料來源使用，無需額外設定，因此不需要建立 organization trail、用 SCP 啟用 VPC Flow Logs，也不需要用 Security Hub 彙整。組織層級的最佳實務是從 management account 指派一個委派的 GuardDuty administrator account（安全營運不應放在 management account），透過 AWS Organizations 整合把現有帳戶加入為 member，並開啟 auto-enable 讓未來新建帳戶自動納管。GuardDuty 原生會將 findings 發佈到 Amazon EventBridge，因此在 administrator account 建立比對 GuardDuty 事件並轉發到既有 SNS topic 的 EventBridge rule 即完成通知流程。選項 A 正是此模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Invitation-based membership is the legacy method; AWS best practice for an organization is the delegated-administrator plus auto-enable model via AWS Organizations integration. Using a CloudFormation stack set to accept invitations and deploy per-account EventBridge rules is unnecessarily complex and not the recommended pattern.","why_zh":"邀請式 (invitation) 加入成員是舊式方法；組織的 AWS 最佳實務是透過 AWS Organizations 整合採用委派管理員加 auto-enable 模式。用 CloudFormation stack set 去接受邀請並逐帳戶部署 EventBridge rule 過於複雜，並非建議做法。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This manually reconstructs GuardDuty's capabilities. A CloudTrail organization trail plus VPC Flow Logs only collect raw logs and do not generate threat findings for compromised EC2 or anomalies. Security Hub aggregates findings from other services rather than producing these detections itself. Also, an SCP cannot enable VPC Flow Logs; SCPs are permission guardrails, not a feature-enablement mechanism. This is far more operational overhead.","why_zh":"此選項是手動重建 GuardDuty 的能力。CloudTrail organization trail 加 VPC Flow Logs 只是收集原始日誌，並不會產生受侵害 EC2 或異常的威脅 findings。Security Hub 是彙整其他服務的 findings，而非自行產生這些偵測。此外 SCP 無法啟用 VPC Flow Logs；SCP 是權限護欄而非啟用功能的機制。整體營運負擔大很多。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same flaws as C plus an invalid construct: there is no 'CloudTrail administrator account' delegated-admin concept used this way for the stated purpose, and an SCP still cannot enable VPC Flow Logs. CloudTrail logs and Security Hub do not by themselves detect compromised EC2 instances or network/API anomalies the way GuardDuty does, and the approach carries excessive operational overhead.","why_zh":"與 C 相同的缺陷，再加上無效的構件：本情境下並沒有這樣使用的『CloudTrail administrator account』委派管理概念，且 SCP 仍無法啟用 VPC Flow Logs。CloudTrail 日誌與 Security Hub 本身不會像 GuardDuty 那樣偵測受侵害 EC2 或網路/API 異常，且此方法營運負擔過高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_data-sources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/maintaining-guardduty-organization-delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/set-guardduty-auto-enable-preferences.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/delegated-admin-designate.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":103,"question_en":"A company’s DevOps engineer is working in a multi-account environment. The company uses AWS Transit Gateway to route all outbound traffic through a network operations account. In the network operations account, all account traffic passes through a firewall appliance for inspection before the traffic goes to an internet gateway. The firewall appliance sends logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and includes event severities of CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW, and INFO. The security team wants to receive an alert if any CRITICAL events occur. What should the DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师在多账户环境中工作。该公司使用 AWS 转发网关将所有出站流量通过网络运 营账户进行路由。在网络运营账户中，所有账户流量在到达互联网网关之前都要通过防火墙设备进行检 查。 防火墙设备会将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，并包含 CRITICAL（严重）、HIGH（高）、 MEDIUM（中）、LOW（低）和 INFO（信息）这几种事件严重级别。安全团队希望在出现任何严重事 件时收到警报。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics canary to monitor the firewall state. If the firewall reaches a CRITICAL state or logs a CRITICAL event, use a CloudWatch alarm to publish a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the security team’s email address to the topic.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric filter by using a search for CRITICAL events. Publish a custom metric for the finding. Use a CloudWatch alarm based on the custom metric to publish a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the security team’s email address to the topic.","C":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty in the network operations account. Configure GuardDuty to monitor flow logs. Create an Amazon EventBridge event rule that is invoked by GuardDuty events that are CRITICAL. Define an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as a target. Subscribe the security team’s email address to the topic.","D":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to apply consistent policies across all accounts. Create an Amazon EventBridge event rule that is invoked by Firewall Manager events that are CRITICAL. Define an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as a target. Subscribe the security team’s email address to the topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics 健康检查来监控防火墙的状态。如果防火墙达到 CRITICAL （危急）状态或记录了 CRITICAL（危急）事件，使用 CloudWatch 警报向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题发布通知。将安全团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。","B":"通过搜索“CRITICAL”事件创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 指标筛选器。为该发现发布一个自定义指 标。基于自定义指标使用 CloudWatch 警报向 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题发布通知。将安全团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。","C":"在网络运营账户中启用亚马逊 GuardDuty。配置 GuardDuty 以监控流量。 日志。创建一个由 GuardDuty 发出的 CRITICAL 级别事件触发的 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则。将 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题定义为目标。将安全团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。","D":"使用 AWS 防火墙管理器在所有账户中应用一致的策略。创建一个由防火墙管理器发出的 CRITICAL 级别事件触发的 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则。将 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题定 义为目标。将安全团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The firewall appliance already ships logs (including CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/INFO event severities) to CloudWatch Logs. The canonical AWS pattern to alert on a specific term or pattern inside log data is a CloudWatch Logs metric filter that matches the term (here, CRITICAL) and increments a custom metric, combined with a CloudWatch alarm on that metric that publishes to an Amazon SNS topic, with the security team's email subscribed. This is exactly the 'Alarming on logs' / 'Creating metrics from log events using filters' workflow documented by AWS. Option B implements this end to end and is the correct answer.","explanation_zh":"防火牆設備已將日誌（包含 CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/INFO 嚴重性事件）傳送到 CloudWatch Logs。要針對日誌資料中特定字詞或模式發出告警，AWS 的標準做法是建立 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 比對該字詞（此處為 CRITICAL）並將其轉為自訂 metric，再以 CloudWatch alarm 監控該 metric，於觸發時發佈到 Amazon SNS topic，並讓安全團隊的電子郵件訂閱該 topic。這正是 AWS 文件中「Alarming on logs」/「Creating metrics from log events using filters」的流程。選項 B 完整實作此流程，為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudWatch Synthetics canaries are scripted (Node.js/Python) checks that monitor endpoint/application availability and latency by simulating user requests; they cannot read CloudWatch Logs content or monitor a 'firewall state', so they cannot detect CRITICAL log events.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Synthetics canary 是以腳本模擬使用者請求來監控端點/應用程式可用性與延遲，無法讀取 CloudWatch Logs 內容或監控『防火牆狀態』，因此無法偵測 CRITICAL 日誌事件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"GuardDuty only analyzes AWS foundational data sources (CloudTrail management/data events, VPC Flow Logs, Route 53 DNS query logs) and select integrations; it does not ingest or analyze a third-party firewall appliance's CloudWatch Logs, so it cannot raise findings from the appliance's CRITICAL log events.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 僅分析 AWS 基礎資料來源（CloudTrail 管理/資料事件、VPC Flow Logs、Route 53 DNS 查詢日誌）及部分整合，並不讀取或分析第三方防火牆設備寫入 CloudWatch Logs 的內容，因此無法從設備的 CRITICAL 日誌事件產生發現。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Firewall Manager centrally administers WAF rules, Shield Advanced, Network Firewall, and security-group policies across accounts; it does not parse the severity of a firewall appliance's log events, and there is no 'Firewall Manager CRITICAL event' to drive the EventBridge rule.","why_zh":"AWS Firewall Manager 是跨帳戶集中管理 WAF 規則、Shield Advanced、Network Firewall 及安全群組政策，並不解析防火牆設備日誌事件的嚴重性，也沒有可驅動 EventBridge 規則的『Firewall Manager CRITICAL 事件』。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Alarm-On-Logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SearchDataFilterPattern.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_data-sources.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":104,"question_en":"A company is divided into teams. Each team has an AWS account, and all the accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. Each team must retain full administrative rights to its AWS account. Each team also must be allowed to access only AWS services that the company approves for use. AWS services must gain approval through a request and approval process. How should a DevOps engineer configure the accounts to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司被划分为多个团队。每个团队都有一个 AWS 账户，所有账户都在 AWS 组织中的一个组织内。 每个团队必须对其 AWS 账户保留完全的管理权限。每个团队还必须仅被允许访问公司批准使用的 AWS 服务。AWS 服务必须通过请求和审批流程获得批准。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置账户以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to provision IAM policies in each account to deny access to restricted AWS services. In each account, configure AWS Config rules that ensure that the policies are attached to IAM principals in the account.","B":"Use AWS Control Tower to provision the accounts into OUs within the organization. Configure AWS Control Tower to enable AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). Configure IAM Identity Center to provide administrative access. Include deny policies on user roles for restricted AWS services.","C":"Place all the accounts under a new top-level OU within the organization. Create an SCP that denies access to restricted AWS services. Attach the SCP to the OU.","D":"Create an SCP that allows access to only approved AWS services. Attach the SCP to the root OU of the organization. Remove the FullAWSAccess SCP from the root OU of the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在每个账户中配置 IAM 策略，以拒绝访问受限的 AWS 服务。在每 个账户中，配置 AWS Config 规则以确保这些策略已附加到账户中的 IAM 实体。","B":"使用 AWS Control Tower 将账户配置到组织内的组织单位（OU）中。配置 AWS Control Tower 以启用 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）。配置 IAM 身份中心以提供管理访问权限。在用户角色上为 受限的 AWS 服务包含拒绝策略。","C":"将所有账户置于组织内的新顶级组织单位（OU）下。创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），拒绝访问受限 的 AWS 服务。将该 SCP 附加到该 OU。","D":"创建一个仅允许访问已批准的 AWS 服务的 SCP（服务控制策略）。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根组织单 元。从组织的根组织单元移除 FullAWSAccess SCP。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive requirement is that AWS services must gain approval through a request-and-approval process, which means the default posture must be deny and only explicitly approved services may be used (an allowlist/whitelist model). Option D implements exactly this: an SCP that allows only approved services is attached to the root, and the AWS-managed FullAWSAccess SCP is removed so that anything not explicitly allowed (including any newly released AWS service) is denied by default. To approve a new service, an administrator updates the SCP, satisfying the request-and-approval workflow. SCPs are guardrails that do not grant permissions, so each team still keeps full administrative rights to its own account within the approved-service boundary via its own IAM. Option C is a denylist, which leaves all non-listed services (and every future AWS service) automatically accessible, failing the approval-gated requirement.","explanation_zh":"決定性需求是「AWS 服務必須透過申請與核准流程才能使用」，這代表預設必須為拒絕，只有明確核准的服務才可使用（即 allowlist/白名單模式）。選項 D 正是如此：在 root 附加一個只允許已核准服務的 SCP，並移除 AWS 受管的 FullAWSAccess SCP，使得任何未明確允許的項目（包含未來新推出的 AWS 服務）預設都被拒絕。要核准新服務，管理員需更新 SCP，符合申請與核准流程。SCP 是護欄，本身不授予權限，因此各團隊仍在已核准服務範圍內透過自己帳號的 IAM 保有完整管理權限。選項 C 是 denylist，會讓所有未列出的服務（以及未來每個 AWS 新服務）自動可用，無法滿足需經核准的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation StackSets pushing IAM deny policies plus AWS Config rules is high-overhead and unreliable: IAM policies can be detached or overridden by the team's full admin rights, Config only detects drift after the fact, and it is a denylist (everything not denied is allowed), so it does not enforce an approval-gated allowlist or guarantee restriction.","why_zh":"用 CloudFormation StackSets 佈署 IAM 拒絕政策加上 AWS Config 規則，運維負擔高且不可靠：擁有完整管理權的團隊可分離或覆寫 IAM 政策，Config 只能事後偵測偏移，且屬於 denylist（未拒絕者皆允許），無法落實需核准的白名單或保證限制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Control Tower with IAM Identity Center and deny policies on user roles forces a centralized SSO access model and a denylist on roles; teams would lose full direct administrative control of their own accounts, and role-level deny lists allow any non-denied/new service by default, so it does not implement an approval-gated allowlist.","why_zh":"用 Control Tower 搭配 IAM Identity Center 並在使用者角色上加拒絕政策，會強制集中式 SSO 存取模型且在角色上採 denylist；團隊將失去對自身帳號的完整直接管理權，而角色層的拒絕清單預設仍允許任何未拒絕／新服務，無法實作需核准的白名單。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A deny SCP for restricted services is a denylist: FullAWSAccess remains, so every service not explicitly denied (including future AWS services) is automatically usable. This contradicts the requirement that services must be approved through a request-and-approval process before use.","why_zh":"對受限服務使用拒絕型 SCP 屬於 denylist：FullAWSAccess 仍保留，因此任何未明確拒絕的服務（含未來 AWS 新服務）都自動可用，違反「服務須經申請與核准流程才能使用」的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":105,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer used an AWS CloudFormation custom resource to set up AD Connector. The AWS Lambda function ran and created AD Connector, but CloudFormation is not transitioning from CREATE_IN_PROGRESS to CREATE_COMPLETE. Which action should the engineer take to resolve this issue?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS CloudFormation 自定义资源来设置 AD 连接器。AWS Lambda 函数运行并 创建了 AD 连接器，但 CloudFormation 未从“CREATE_IN_PROGRESS”（创建中）状态过渡到 “CREATE_COMPLETE”（创建完成）状态。 工程师应该采取哪项行动来解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Ensure the Lambda function code has exited successfully.","B":"Ensure the Lambda function code returns a response to the pre-signed URL.","C":"Ensure the Lambda function IAM role has cloudformation:UpdateStack permissions for the stack ARN.","D":"Ensure the Lambda function IAM role has ds:ConnectDirectory permissions for the AWS account."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保 Lambda 函数代码已成功退出。","B":"确保 Lambda 函数代码向预签名的 URL 返回响应。","C":"确保 Lambda 函数的 IAM 角色具有针对该堆栈 ARN 的 cloudformation:UpdateStack 权限。","D":"确保 Lambda 函数的 IAM 角色对于 AWS 账户具有 ds:ConnectDirectory 权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A CloudFormation custom resource backed by Lambda works by CloudFormation invoking the function asynchronously with an event containing a 'ResponseURL' (a pre-signed Amazon S3 URL). CloudFormation then waits for the function to upload a SUCCESS or FAILED response to that pre-signed URL before transitioning the resource. In this scenario the AD Connector was actually created, which proves the function's API calls and IAM permissions worked. The reason the stack is stuck in CREATE_IN_PROGRESS is the classic symptom of the function never sending its response to the pre-signed callback URL, so CloudFormation keeps waiting until the multi-hour timeout. The fix is to ensure the Lambda code returns a response (e.g., via the cfn-response helper) to the pre-signed ResponseURL.","explanation_zh":"由 Lambda 支援的 CloudFormation custom resource 運作方式為:CloudFormation 以非同步方式叫用該 function,事件中包含一個 'ResponseURL'(預先簽署的 Amazon S3 URL)。CloudFormation 接著會等待 function 將 SUCCESS 或 FAILED 回應上傳到該 pre-signed URL,才會讓資源狀態轉換。在此情境中,AD Connector 已實際建立成功,證明 function 的 API 呼叫與 IAM 權限都正常運作。Stack 卡在 CREATE_IN_PROGRESS 的典型原因,就是 function 從未將回應送到 pre-signed callback URL,導致 CloudFormation 持續等待直到數小時的逾時。解法是確保 Lambda 程式碼會將回應(例如透過 cfn-response 輔助模組)送回 pre-signed ResponseURL。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Lambda function exiting successfully is not what signals CloudFormation. Because the invocation is asynchronous, CloudFormation never sees the function's return value or exit status; it only proceeds when a SUCCESS/FAILED response is written to the pre-signed ResponseURL. A function can exit cleanly yet still leave the stack hung if it never sent that response.","why_zh":"Lambda function 正常結束並非觸發 CloudFormation 的訊號。由於叫用是非同步的,CloudFormation 看不到 function 的回傳值或結束狀態;只有當 SUCCESS/FAILED 回應被寫入 pre-signed ResponseURL 時才會繼續。即使 function 乾淨地結束,只要沒送出回應,stack 仍會卡住。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"cloudformation:UpdateStack is irrelevant here. A custom resource Lambda does not call back into the CloudFormation API to advance the stack; it signals completion only by uploading a response to the pre-signed S3 URL. Granting UpdateStack would do nothing to release a stuck CREATE_IN_PROGRESS.","why_zh":"cloudformation:UpdateStack 在此無關。Custom resource 的 Lambda 不會回呼 CloudFormation API 來推進 stack;它只透過將回應上傳到 pre-signed S3 URL 來表示完成。授予 UpdateStack 對解開卡住的 CREATE_IN_PROGRESS 毫無作用。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ds:ConnectDirectory is the permission needed to create the AD Connector, but the question states the AD Connector was successfully created. That proves the IAM permissions were already sufficient, so adding them again would not resolve the hang.","why_zh":"ds:ConnectDirectory 是建立 AD Connector 所需的權限,但題目已說明 AD Connector 成功建立了。這證明 IAM 權限原本就足夠,因此再加上該權限無法解決卡住的問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-cloudformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/crpg-ref-responses.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":106,"question_en":"A company uses AWS CodeCommit for source code control. Developers apply their changes to various feature branches and create pull requests to move those changes to the main branch when the changes are ready for production. The developers should not be able to push changes directly to the main branch. The company applied the AWSCodeCommitPowerUser managed policy to the developers’ IAM role, and now these developers can push changes to the main branch directly on every repository in the AWS account. What should the company do to restrict the developers’ ability to push changes to the main branch directly?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodeCommit 进行源代码控制。开发人员将他们的更改应用到不同的功能分支，并在 更改完成后创建拉取请求，将这些更改合并到主分支。 已准备好投入生产。 开发人员不应能够直接向主分支推送更改。该公司将 AWSCodeCommitPowerUser 管理策略应用于开发 人员的 IAM 角色，现在这些开发人员可以在 AWS 账户中的每个代码库直接向主分支推送更改。 公司应该采取什么措施来限制开发人员直接向主分支推送更改？","options_en":{"A":"Create an additional policy to include a Deny rule for the GitPush and PutFile actions. Include a restriction for the specific repositories in the policy statement with a condition that references the main branch.","B":"Remove the IAM policy, and add an AWSCodeCommitReadOnly managed policy. Add an Allow rule for the GitPush and PutFile actions for the specific repositories in the policy statement with a condition that references the main branch.","C":"Modify the IAM policy. Include a Deny rule for the GitPush and PutFile actions for the specific repositories in the policy statement with a condition that references the main branch.","D":"Create an additional policy to include an Allow rule for the GitPush and PutFile actions. Include a restriction for the specific repositories in the policy statement with a condition that references the feature branches."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一项额外的策略，为 GitPush 和 PutFile 操作添加拒绝规则。在策略声明中包含针对特定存储库 的限制条件，并引用主分支。","B":"删除 IAM 策略，并添加 AWSCodeCommitReadOnly 管理策略。在策略语句中为特定代码库添加允许 规则，允许 GitPush 和 PutFile 操作，并添加一个条件，引用主分支。","C":"修改 IAM 策略。在策略语句中为特定的代码库添加一条拒绝规则，拒绝执行 GitPush 和 PutFile 操作，并添加一个条件，该条件引用主分支。","D":"创建一项额外的策略，为 GitPush 和 PutFile 操作添加一条允许规则。在策略声明中包含针对特 定存储库的限制条件，并引用功能分支。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS documents that to prevent specific users from pushing or merging to a branch, you create a conditional IAM policy with an explicit Deny on actions such as codecommit:GitPush and codecommit:PutFile (plus merge/delete actions), scoped to the specific repository ARN in Resource, with a Condition on codecommit:References pointing at the branch (e.g., refs/heads/main). Because AWSCodeCommitPowerUser is an AWS managed policy, it cannot be edited, so the Deny must live in a separate additional policy attached to the developers' group or role alongside PowerUser. Option A is exactly this: an additional policy containing a Deny for GitPush and PutFile, restricted to specific repositories, conditioned on the main branch. This is the only option that both uses Deny (the requirement is to restrict/prevent pushes) and respects that the managed policy cannot be modified.","explanation_zh":"AWS 官方文件說明，若要阻止特定使用者直接推送或合併到某分支，應建立一個條件式 IAM 政策，對 codecommit:GitPush 與 codecommit:PutFile（以及 merge/delete 等動作）使用明確的 Deny，Resource 限定為特定 repository ARN，並透過 codecommit:References 條件鎖定分支（例如 refs/heads/main）。由於 AWSCodeCommitPowerUser 是 AWS 受管政策（AWS managed policy），無法被編輯修改，因此 Deny 規則必須放在另一個額外的政策中，與 PowerUser 一起附加到開發者的 group 或 role。選項 A 正是如此：建立額外政策，對 GitPush 與 PutFile 設定 Deny，限定特定 repository，並以 main 分支為條件。這是唯一同時使用 Deny（需求是限制/阻止推送）且尊重受管政策不可修改的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Switching to AWSCodeCommitReadOnly removes all write access (developers could no longer push to feature branches), and explicitly Allowing GitPush/PutFile on the main branch does the opposite of the requirement, which is to block direct pushes to main.","why_zh":"改用 AWSCodeCommitReadOnly 會移除所有寫入權限（開發者連 feature 分支都無法推送），而對 main 分支明確 Allow GitPush/PutFile 與需求（阻止直接推送 main）完全相反。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWSCodeCommitPowerUser is an AWS managed policy, which customers cannot modify or edit. The restriction must be in a separate (additional) policy, so 'Modify the IAM policy' is not possible.","why_zh":"AWSCodeCommitPowerUser 是 AWS 受管政策，客戶無法修改或編輯。限制必須放在獨立的額外政策中，因此「修改該 IAM 政策」做不到。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An Allow rule for feature branches accomplishes nothing here: developers already retain push access to main via the PowerUser Allow, so adding another Allow for feature branches does not deny pushes to main. Only an explicit Deny conditioned on main removes that access.","why_zh":"對 feature 分支設定 Allow 規則在此毫無作用：開發者已透過 PowerUser 的 Allow 保有對 main 的推送權限，再對 feature 分支加 Allow 並不會拒絕對 main 的推送。只有以 main 為條件的明確 Deny 才能移除該權限。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-conditional-branch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/customer-managed-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AWSCodeCommitPowerUser.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/security-iam-awsmanpol.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":107,"question_en":"A company manages a web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The EC2 instances run in an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. The application uses an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance to store the data. The company has configured Amazon Route 53 with an alias record that points to the ALB. A new company guideline requires a geographically isolated disaster recovery (DR) site with an RTO of 4 hours and an RPO of 15 minutes. Which DR strategy will meet these requirements with the LEAST change to the application stack?","question_zh":"一家公司管理着一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的网络应用程序，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB） 之后，并且分布在多个可用区的自动扩展组中。该应用程序使用亚马逊 RDS 的 MySQL 数据库实例来 存储数据。该公司已在亚马逊 Route 53 中配置了一个别名记录，该记录指向 ALB。 新公司准则要求设立一个地理位置上与主站点隔离的灾难恢复（DR）站点，其恢复时间目标（RTO） 为 4 小时，恢复点目标（RPO）为 15 分钟。 哪种灾难恢复策略能够在对应用堆栈改动最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Launch a replica environment of everything except Amazon RDS in a different Availability Zone. Create an RDS read replica in the new Availability Zone, and configure the new stack to point to the local RDS DB instance. Add the new stack to the Route 53 record set by using a health check to configure a failover routing policy.","B":"Launch a replica environment of everything except Amazon RDS in a different AWS Region. Create an RDS read replica in the new Region, and configure the new stack to point to the local RDS DB instance. Add the new stack to the Route 53 record set by using a health check to configure a latency routing policy.","C":"Launch a replica environment of everything except Amazon RDS in a different AWS Region. In the event of an outage, copy and restore the latest RDS snapshot from the primary Region to the DR Region. Adjust the Route 53 record set to point to the ALB in the DR Region.","D":"Launch a replica environment of everything except Amazon RDS in a different AWS Region. Create an RDS read replica in the new Region, and configure the new environment to point to the local RDS DB instance. Add the new stack to the Route 53 record set by using a health check to configure a failover routing policy. In the event of an outage, promote the read replica to primary."},"options_zh":{"A":"在不同的可用区中启动除 Amazon RDS 之外的所有内容的副本环境。在新的可用区中创建 RDS 读取 副本，并将新堆栈配置为指向本地 RDS 数据库实例。使用健康检查将新堆栈添加到 Route 53 记录 集，以配置故障转移路由策略。","B":"在不同的 AWS 区域中启动除 Amazon RDS 之外的所有内容的副本环境。在新区域中创建 RDS 读取 副本，并将新堆栈配置为指向本地 RDS 数据库实例。通过使用健康检查配置延迟路由策略，将新 堆栈添加到 Route 53 记录集。","C":"在不同的 AWS 区域中启动除 Amazon RDS 之外所有内容的副本环境。在出现故障时，将主区域 中的最新 RDS 快照复制并恢复到 DR 区域。调整 Route 53 记录集以指向 DR 区域中的 ALB。","D":"在不同的 AWS 区域中启动除 Amazon RDS 之外的所有内容的副本环境。在新区域中创建 RDS 读取 副本，并将新环境配置为指向本地 RDS 数据库实例。使用健康检查将新堆栈添加到 Route 53 记录 集，以配置故障转移路由策略。在出现故障时，将读取副本提升为主副本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a geographically isolated DR site (a different AWS Region, not just another AZ) with RPO 15 min and RTO 4 hours, using the least change to the stack. A cross-Region RDS for MySQL read replica continuously replicates asynchronously, keeping the DR database within seconds-to-minutes of the primary, comfortably meeting a 15-minute RPO. Amazon RDS docs explicitly list 'promote a read replica to a standalone instance as a disaster recovery solution if the primary DB instance fails' as a supported use case, and promotion completes in minutes, easily meeting a 4-hour RTO. Route 53 active/passive DR uses a FAILOVER routing policy with health checks so the passive DR Region only receives traffic after the primary becomes unhealthy. Option D replicates the same stack to another Region and only changes DNS/promotes on failover, which is the least invasive change that satisfies all constraints.","explanation_zh":"需求是地理隔離的 DR 站點（必須是不同的 AWS Region，而非僅是另一個 AZ），RPO 15 分鐘、RTO 4 小時，且對應用程式堆疊變更最少。跨 Region 的 RDS for MySQL read replica 會持續以非同步方式複寫，使 DR 資料庫與主庫僅相差數秒至數分鐘，可輕鬆滿足 15 分鐘的 RPO。Amazon RDS 文件明確將「在主資料庫故障時將 read replica 提升為獨立執行個體作為災難復原方案」列為支援用途，且提升只需數分鐘，可滿足 4 小時的 RTO。Route 53 的主動／被動 DR 使用 FAILOVER 路由策略搭配 health check，使被動 DR Region 僅在主站不健康時才接收流量。選項 D 將相同堆疊複製到另一個 Region，只在故障切換時變更 DNS 並提升 replica，是滿足所有條件且變更最少的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses a different Availability Zone, not a different Region. The requirement explicitly demands a geographically isolated DR site, and a same-Region AZ provides no protection against a regional disaster.","why_zh":"使用不同的 Availability Zone 而非不同的 Region。需求明確要求地理隔離的 DR 站點，同一 Region 內的 AZ 無法防護整個 Region 層級的災難。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Latency routing policy is designed to send users to the lowest-latency active endpoint for performance, not for active/passive DR failover; it could route live traffic to the read-only DR replica. It also never promotes the read replica, so the DR database stays read-only and cannot serve writes.","why_zh":"Latency 路由策略是為了將使用者導向延遲最低的作用中端點以提升效能，而非用於主動／被動的 DR 故障切換，甚至可能將正式流量導向唯讀的 DR replica。它也未提升 read replica，導致 DR 資料庫保持唯讀、無法承接寫入。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Copy-and-restore of the latest RDS snapshot is a backup-and-restore approach; automated RDS snapshots are typically daily, so RPO would far exceed 15 minutes, and restoring a snapshot in the DR Region during an outage is slow and the most manual effort, risking the 4-hour RTO.","why_zh":"複製並還原最新 RDS 快照屬於 backup-and-restore 方式；RDS 自動快照通常為每日一次，RPO 將遠超過 15 分鐘，而在故障時於 DR Region 還原快照既緩慢又需最多手動作業，可能無法達成 4 小時 RTO。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.XRgn.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/disaster-recovery-workloads-on-aws/disaster-recovery-options-in-the-cloud.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":108,"question_en":"A large enterprise is deploying a web application on AWS. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The instances run in an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. The application stores data in an Amazon RDS for Oracle DB instance and Amazon DynamoDB. There are separate environments for development, testing, and production. What is the MOST secure and flexible way to obtain password credentials during deployment?","question_zh":"一家大型企业正在 AWS 上部署一个网络应用程序。该应用程序在应用负载均衡器后面的亚马逊 EC2 实例上 运行。这些实例在多个可用区的自动扩展组中运行。应用程序的数据存储在亚马逊 RDS for Oracle 数据库实 例和亚马逊 DynamoDB 中。开发、测试和生产环境是分开的。 在部署过程中，获取密码凭证最安全且最灵活的方式是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Retrieve an access key from an AWS Systems Manager SecureString parameter to access AWS services. Retrieve the database credentials from a Systems Manager SecureString parameter.","B":"Launch the EC2 instances with an EC2 IAM role to access AWS services. Retrieve the database credentials from AWS Secrets Manager.","C":"Retrieve an access key from an AWS Systems Manager plaintext parameter to access AWS services. Retrieve the database credentials from a Systems Manager SecureString parameter.","D":"Launch the EC2 instances with an EC2 IAM role to access AWS services. Store the database passwords in an encrypted config file with the application artifacts."},"options_zh":{"A":"从 AWS 系统管理器的 SecureString 参数中获取访问密钥以访问 AWS 服务。从系统管理器的 SecureString 参数中获取数据库凭据。","B":"使用具有访问 AWS 服务权限的 EC2 IAM 角色启动 EC2 实例。从 AWS Secrets Manager 中获取数 据库凭证。","C":"从 AWS 系统管理器的明文参数中检索访问密钥以访问 AWS 服务。从系统管理器的 SecureString 参 数中检索数据库凭据。","D":"使用具有访问 AWS 服务权限的 EC2 IAM 角色启动 EC2 实例。将数据库密码存储在与应用程序 工件一起的加密配置文件中。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS best practice for workloads running on EC2 is to use an IAM role attached to the instance (via an instance profile). AWS automatically delivers temporary, auto-rotating credentials to the instance, so there is no need to distribute long-lived IAM user access keys. This is the most secure way for the application to call AWS services such as DynamoDB. For the database (RDS for Oracle) password, AWS Secrets Manager is purpose-built to store, retrieve, and automatically rotate database credentials at runtime, eliminating hard-coded secrets and making it easy to maintain separate secrets per environment (dev/test/prod). Option B uniquely combines both best practices: IAM role for AWS service access and Secrets Manager for database credentials, which is the MOST secure and flexible approach.","explanation_zh":"對於在 EC2 上執行的工作負載，AWS 最佳做法是透過 instance profile 將 IAM role 附加到執行個體。AWS 會自動將暫時且會自動輪替的憑證交付給執行個體，因此不需要散布長期有效的 IAM user access key。這是讓應用程式存取 AWS 服務（例如 DynamoDB）最安全的方式。至於資料庫（RDS for Oracle）密碼，AWS Secrets Manager 專為在執行階段儲存、擷取並自動輪替資料庫憑證而設計，可消除硬編碼的祕密，並可輕鬆為每個環境（dev/test/prod）維護獨立的祕密。選項 B 同時結合這兩項最佳做法：以 IAM role 存取 AWS 服務，以 Secrets Manager 管理資料庫憑證，是最安全且最具彈性的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using an SSM SecureString to hold an access key still relies on a long-lived IAM user access key, which AWS explicitly recommends against for workloads on EC2. IAM roles delivering temporary credentials are far more secure, and SSM SecureString lacks native automatic rotation for DB credentials.","why_zh":"用 SSM SecureString 保存 access key 仍依賴長期有效的 IAM user access key，AWS 明確建議 EC2 上的工作負載不要這樣做。提供暫時憑證的 IAM role 安全得多，且 SSM SecureString 對資料庫憑證沒有原生自動輪替功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Storing an access key in an SSM plaintext (String) parameter is the least secure option: the long-lived credential is unencrypted and still violates the IAM-role best practice. Worse than A.","why_zh":"將 access key 存放在 SSM 純文字（String）參數是最不安全的做法：長期憑證未加密，且同樣違反使用 IAM role 的最佳做法。比 A 更糟。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The IAM role part is correct, but storing database passwords in an encrypted config file bundled with the application artifacts hard-codes the secret, makes rotation difficult, and is less secure and less flexible than Secrets Manager, which AWS recommends for DB credentials and supports automatic rotation and per-environment secrets.","why_zh":"IAM role 部分正確，但把資料庫密碼存在與應用程式構件一起打包的加密設定檔等於硬編碼祕密，輪替困難，且不如 Secrets Manager 安全與彈性；AWS 建議資料庫憑證使用 Secrets Manager，並支援自動輪替與各環境獨立祕密。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotating-secrets.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":109,"question_en":"The security team depends on AWS CloudTrail to detect sensitive security issues in the company’s AWS account. The DevOps engineer needs a solution to auto-remediate CloudTrail being turned off in an AWS account. What solution ensures the LEAST amount of downtime for the CloudTrail log deliveries?","question_zh":"安全团队依靠 AWS CloudTrail 来检测公司 AWS 账户中的敏感安全问题。DevOps 工程师需要一个解决方 案来自动修复 AWS 账户中 CloudTrail 被关闭的情况。 哪种解决方案能确保 CloudTrail 日志交付的停机时间最短？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for the CloudTrail StopLogging event. Create an AWS Lambda function that uses the AWS SDK to call StartLogging on the ARN of the resource in which StopLogging was called. Add the Lambda function ARN as a target to the EventBridge rule.","B":"Deploy the AWS-managed CloudTrail-enabled AWS Config rule, set with a periodic interval of 1 hour. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for AWS Config rules compliance change. Create an AWS Lambda function that uses the AWS SDK to call StartLogging on the ARN of the resource in which StopLogging was called. Add the Lambda function ARN as a target to the EventBridge rule.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for a scheduled event every 5 minutes. Create an AWS Lambda function that uses the AWS SDK to call StartLogging on a CloudTrail trail in the AWS account. Add the Lambda function ARN as a target to the EventBridge rule.","D":"Launch a t2.nano instance with a script running every 5 minutes that uses the AWS SDK to query CloudTrail in the current account. If the CloudTrail trail is disabled, have the script re-enable the trail."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 CloudTrail 的 StopLogging 事件创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。创建一个使用 AWS SDK 调用 StartLogging 的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数针对的是调用 StopLogging 的资源的 ARN。将 Lambda 函数 的 ARN 作为目标添加到 EventBridge 规则中。","B":"部署由 AWS 管理的启用 CloudTrail 的 AWS Config 规则，并将其设置为每 1 小时执行一次。为 AWS Config 规则合规性变更创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。创建一个使用 AWS SDK 调用 StartLogging 的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数针对调用了 StopLogging 的资源的 ARN。将 Lambda 函数 的 ARN 作为目标添加到 EventBridge 规则中。","C":"创建一个每 5 分钟触发一次的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。创建一个使用 AWS SDK 调用 AWS 账户中 CloudTrail 跟踪的 StartLogging 操作的 AWS Lambda 函数。将 Lambda 函数的 ARN 作为目标添加到 EventBridge 规则中。","D":"启动一个 t2.nano 实例，运行一个每 5 分钟执行一次的脚本，该脚本使用 AWS SDK 查询当前账户中的 CloudTrail 跟踪。如果 CloudTrail 跟踪已禁用，让脚本重新启用该跟踪。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is LEAST amount of downtime for CloudTrail log deliveries. Option A is event-driven: CloudTrail delivers the StopLogging API call to the default EventBridge event bus as an 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' event in near real time, an EventBridge rule matches it, and a Lambda function immediately calls StartLogging on the exact resource ARN from the event, so logging is restored within seconds. Option B relies on the AWS managed Config rule cloudtrail-enabled (CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED), which has a Periodic trigger type only; with a 1-hour interval, detection (and therefore remediation) can lag up to an hour, producing far more downtime, and a Config compliance-change event does not carry the StopLogging resource ARN the Lambda is described as using. Options C and D both poll on a 5-minute schedule, leaving up to five minutes of downtime, are not event-driven, and (C) hardcode a single trail or (D) add the operational overhead of running and patching an EC2 instance. Therefore A minimizes downtime and is the correct answer.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是「CloudTrail 日誌傳遞的停機時間最短」。選項 A 是事件驅動：CloudTrail 會將 StopLogging API 呼叫近乎即時地以 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' 事件傳送到預設的 EventBridge event bus，EventBridge rule 比對到後立即觸發 Lambda，對事件中該資源的確切 ARN 呼叫 StartLogging，因此可在數秒內恢復記錄。選項 B 依賴 AWS 受管 Config rule cloudtrail-enabled (CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED)，其 Trigger type 僅為 Periodic；以 1 小時間隔評估時，偵測（進而補救）可能延遲長達一小時，停機時間遠大於 A，且 Config compliance-change 事件並不會帶有該 Lambda 所述使用的 StopLogging 資源 ARN。選項 C 與 D 皆以 5 分鐘排程輪詢，最多會有 5 分鐘停機、非事件驅動，且 C 寫死單一 trail、D 還增加運行與修補 EC2 執行個體的營運負擔。因此 A 能將停機時間降到最低，為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The cloudtrail-enabled managed Config rule (CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED) is Periodic trigger type only; a 1-hour interval means remediation can lag up to an hour, far more downtime than event-driven A. A Config compliance-change event also does not contain the StopLogging resource ARN the Lambda is said to use.","why_zh":"cloudtrail-enabled 受管 Config rule (CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED) 僅有 Periodic 觸發類型；1 小時間隔代表補救可能延遲長達一小時，停機時間遠超過事件驅動的 A。且 Config compliance-change 事件並不含 Lambda 所述的 StopLogging 資源 ARN。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A 5-minute scheduled poll leaves up to 5 minutes of downtime and is not event-driven; it also hardcodes a single named trail rather than acting on whichever trail was stopped.","why_zh":"5 分鐘排程輪詢最多會有 5 分鐘停機且非事件驅動；同時寫死單一 trail，而非針對被停用的那個 trail 作業。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running a t2.nano EC2 instance polling every 5 minutes adds the highest operational overhead (instance management, patching) and still allows up to 5 minutes of downtime; it is the least cloud-native option.","why_zh":"運行 t2.nano EC2 執行個體每 5 分鐘輪詢，營運負擔最高（執行個體管理、修補），且仍最多有 5 分鐘停機，是最不符合雲端原生的方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/cloudtrail-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-turning-off-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/code-library/latest/ug/cloudtrail_example_cloudtrail_StopLogging_section.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":110,"question_en":"A company uses AWS CodeArtifact to centrally store Python packages. The CodeArtifact repository is configured with the following repository policy: A development team is building a new project in an account that is in an organization in AWS Organizations. The development team wants to use a Python library that has already been stored in the CodeArtifact repository in the organization. The development team uses AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild to build the new application. The CodeBuild job that the development team uses to build the application is configured to run in a VPC. Because of compliance requirements, the VPC has no internet connectivity. The development team creates the VPC endpoints for CodeArtifact and updates the CodeBuild buildspec.yaml file. However, the development team cannot download the Python library from the repository. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer take so that the development team can use CodeArtifact? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodeArtifact 来集中存储 Python 包。CodeArtifact 存储库配置了以下存储库策略： 一个开发团队正在 AWS 组织中的一个账户内构建一个新项目。该开发团队希望使用已存储 在组织的 CodeArtifact 存储库中的 Python 库。开发团队使用 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 来构建新应用程序。开发团队用于构建应用程序的 CodeBuild 作业配置为在 VPC 中运行。由于合规性要求，该 VPC 没有互联网连接。 开发团队为 CodeArtifact 创建了 VPC 端点，并更新了 CodeBuild 的 buildspec.yaml 文 件。然而，开发团队无法从存储库下载 Python 库。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤的组合，才能让开发团队使用 CodeArtifact？（选择两 项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint. Update the route tables for the subnets that are running the CodeBuild job.","B":"Update the repository policy’s Principal statement to include the ARN of the role that the CodeBuild project uses.","C":"Share the CodeArtifact repository with the organization by using AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM).","D":"Update the role that the CodeBuild project uses so that the role has sufficient permissions to use the CodeArtifact repository.","E":"Specify the account that hosts the repository as the delegated administrator for CodeArtifact in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon S3 网关端点。更新运行 CodeBuild 作业的子网的路由表。","B":"将存储库策略的 Principal 语句更新为包含 CodeBuild 项目所使用角色的 ARN。","C":"使用 AWS 资源访问管理器（AWS RAM）与组织共享 CodeArtifact 存储库。","D":"更新 CodeBuild 项目所使用的角色，以便该角色拥有使用 CodeArtifact 存储库的足够权限。","E":"指定托管存储库的账户作为组织中 CodeArtifact 的委托管理员。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"CodeArtifact cross-account access requires BOTH a resource-based policy on the repository that names the consumer principal AND an identity-based policy on the consumer's IAM role. The CodeBuild role lives in a different account, so the repository policy's Principal must include that role's ARN (B), and the CodeBuild role must itself have CodeArtifact permissions such as GetAuthorizationToken, GetRepositoryEndpoint, and ReadFromRepository (D). The decisive qualifier is that the package is a Python library: the CodeArtifact docs explicitly state 'An Amazon S3 endpoint is not needed when using Python or Swift package formats,' so the S3 gateway endpoint in option A is not the missing step for this Python scenario, which eliminates the dump's [A,D] answer. CodeArtifact does not use AWS RAM for sharing (C is invalid), and a delegated administrator (E) governs org-wide domain/policy management, not a consumer account's ability to download a package. Therefore the correct combination is B and D.","explanation_zh":"CodeArtifact 的跨帳戶存取同時需要兩件事：repository 上的 resource-based policy 必須指名 consumer 端的 principal，以及 consumer 端 IAM role 上的 identity-based policy。CodeBuild role 位於不同帳戶，因此 repository policy 的 Principal 必須包含該 role 的 ARN（B），而 CodeBuild role 本身也必須擁有 CodeArtifact 權限，例如 GetAuthorizationToken、GetRepositoryEndpoint 與 ReadFromRepository（D）。關鍵限定條件在於這是 Python library：CodeArtifact 文件明確指出『使用 Python 或 Swift package 格式時不需要 Amazon S3 endpoint』，所以選項 A 的 S3 gateway endpoint 並非此 Python 情境的缺失步驟，這也排除了 dump 的 [A,D] 答案。CodeArtifact 不使用 AWS RAM 來分享（C 無效），而 delegated administrator（E）是治理組織層級的 domain/policy 管理，並非 consumer 帳戶下載 package 的必要條件。因此正確組合為 B 與 D。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The CodeArtifact docs state an Amazon S3 endpoint is not needed for Python or Swift package formats. Since this is a Python library, the S3 gateway endpoint is not the missing step, so A does not resolve this scenario.","why_zh":"CodeArtifact 文件指出使用 Python 或 Swift package 格式時不需要 Amazon S3 endpoint。因為這是 Python library，S3 gateway endpoint 並非缺失步驟，所以 A 無法解決此情境。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeArtifact does not support sharing repositories via AWS Resource Access Manager. Cross-account sharing is done with repository and domain resource policies, not RAM.","why_zh":"CodeArtifact 不支援透過 AWS Resource Access Manager 分享 repository。跨帳戶分享是透過 repository 與 domain 的 resource policy，而非 RAM。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A delegated administrator for CodeArtifact governs organization-wide domain and policy management; it is not required for a consumer account's CodeBuild role to download a package from a shared repository.","why_zh":"CodeArtifact 的 delegated administrator 用於治理組織層級的 domain 與 policy 管理，並非 consumer 帳戶的 CodeBuild role 從已分享 repository 下載 package 的必要條件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/create-s3-gateway-endpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/create-vpc-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repo-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/security_iam_service-with-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/security_iam_troubleshoot.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":111,"question_en":"A company uses a series of individual Amazon CloudFormation templates to deploy its multi-Region applications. These templates must be deployed in a specific order. The company is making more changes to the templates than previously expected and wants to deploy new templates more efficiently. Additionally, the data engineering team must be notified of all changes to the templates. What should the company do to accomplish these goals?","question_zh":"一家公司使用一系列单独的亚马逊 CloudFormation 模板来部署其多区域应用程序。这些模板必须按照特 定顺序进行部署。该公司对模板所做的更改比预期的要多，并希望更高效地部署新模板。此外，数据工 程团队必须收到所有模板更改的通知。 公司应采取什么措施来实现这些目标？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to deploy the CloudFormation templates in the required order. Use stack policies to alert the data engineering team.","B":"Host the CloudFormation templates in Amazon S3. Use Amazon S3 events to directly trigger CloudFormation updates and Amazon SNS notifications.","C":"Implement CloudFormation StackSets and use drift detection to trigger update alerts to the data engineering team.","D":"Leverage CloudFormation nested stacks and stack sets for deployments. Use Amazon SNS to notify the data engineering team."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，按所需顺序部署 CloudFormation 模板。使用堆栈策略向数据工程团 队发出警报。","B":"将 CloudFormation 模板托管在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon S3 事件直接触发 CloudFormation 更新，并使用 Amazon SNS 发送通知。","C":"实施 CloudFormation 栈集，并使用漂移检测向数据工程团队触发更新警报。","D":"利用 CloudFormation 嵌套堆栈和堆栈集进行部署。使用 Amazon SNS 通知数据工程团队。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: deploy individual templates in a specific order, deploy multi-Region applications, do it more efficiently, and notify the data engineering team of all changes. Nested stacks (the AWS::CloudFormation::Stack resource, with DependsOn) let you compose the individual templates into a single root-stack deployment that enforces ordering and is deployed as one unit, which is more efficient than orchestrating templates manually. StackSets natively deploy stacks across multiple Regions in a single operation. Amazon SNS is the standard CloudFormation notification mechanism: the NotificationARNs you set on CreateStack/UpdateStack cause CloudFormation to publish stack event notifications to SNS topics, so the data engineering team can subscribe and be alerted on every change. Option D uses native CloudFormation features for all four requirements, which is why it is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是：依特定順序部署多個個別範本、部署多 Region 應用程式、更有效率地部署，並在所有變更時通知 data engineering 團隊。Nested stacks（AWS::CloudFormation::Stack 資源，搭配 DependsOn）可將多個個別範本組合成單一 root stack 部署，強制執行順序並以單一單位部署，比手動編排範本更有效率。StackSets 原生支援以單一操作跨多個 Region 部署 stacks。Amazon SNS 是 CloudFormation 的標準通知機制：在 CreateStack/UpdateStack 設定的 NotificationARNs 會讓 CloudFormation 將 stack 事件通知發佈到 SNS topic，data engineering 團隊可訂閱並在每次變更時收到提醒。選項 D 對四個需求皆使用 CloudFormation 原生功能，因此正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A custom Lambda to enforce ordering is unnecessary reinvention since nested stacks/DependsOn do this natively. More importantly, stack policies do NOT alert anyone; they protect resources from unintended updates, so they cannot notify the data engineering team.","why_zh":"用自訂 Lambda 強制順序是多餘的重造，因為 nested stacks/DependsOn 原生即可達成。更關鍵的是 stack policies 並不會通知任何人；它們是用來保護資源不被意外更新，無法通知 data engineering 團隊。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 events cannot directly trigger CloudFormation stack updates; there is no native S3-to-CloudFormation-update integration (it would need Lambda/EventBridge glue). It also ignores the ordering and multi-Region requirements.","why_zh":"S3 events 無法直接觸發 CloudFormation stack 更新；沒有原生的 S3 到 CloudFormation 更新整合（需透過 Lambda/EventBridge 串接）。它也忽略了順序與多 Region 需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Drift detection finds divergence between deployed resources and their template state; it does not detect or alert on changes made to the templates themselves. StackSets alone also does not enforce ordering among the individual templates.","why_zh":"Drift detection 偵測的是已部署資源與其範本狀態之間的差異；它無法偵測或對範本本身的變更發出提醒。單用 StackSets 也無法在多個個別範本之間強制執行部署順序。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-nested-stacks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/what-is-cfnstacksets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":112,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer has implemented a CI/CD pipeline to deploy an AWS CloudFormation template that provisions a web application. The web application consists of an Application Load Balancer (ALB), a target group, a launch template that uses an Amazon Linux 2 AMI, an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances, a security group, and an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. The launch template includes user data that specifies a script to install and start the application. The initial deployment of the application was successful. The DevOps engineer made changes to update the version of the application with the user data. The CI/CD pipeline has deployed a new version of the template. However, the health checks on the ALB are now failing. The health checks have marked all targets as unhealthy. During investigation, the DevOps engineer notices that the CloudFormation stack has a status of UPDATE_COMPLETE. However, when the DevOps engineer connects to one of the EC2 instances and checks /var/log/messages, the DevOps engineer notices that the Apache web server failed to start successfully because of a configuration error. How can the DevOps engineer ensure that the CloudFormation deployment will fail if the user data fails to successfully finish running?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师已实现了一条 CI/CD 管道，用于部署一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，该模板可配置 一个网络应用程序。该网络应用程序由一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）、一个目标组、一个使用 Amazon Linux 2 AMI 的启动模板、一个 Amazon EC2 实例的自动扩展组、一个安全组以及一个 Amazon RDS MySQL 数据库组成。启动模板包含用户数据，其中指定了用于安装和启动应用程序的脚本。 应用程序的初始部署成功了。开发运维工程师对应用程序进行了更新，以包含用户数据。持续集成/持 续部署（CI/CD）流水线已部署了模板的新版本。然而，应用负载均衡器（ALB）的健康检查现在失败 了。健康检查已将所有目标标记为不健康。 在调查过程中，DevOps 工程师注意到 CloudFormation 堆栈的状态为 UPDATE_COMPLETE。然而，当 DevOps 工程师连接到其中一个 EC2 实例并检查 /var/log/messages 时，发现由于配置错误，Apache 网 络服务器未能成功启动。 DevOps 工程师如何确保如果用户数据未能成功运行完毕，CloudFormation 部署就会失败？","options_en":{"A":"Use the cfn-signal helper script to signal success or failure to CloudFormation. Use the WaitOnResourceSignals update policy within the CloudFormation template. Set an appropriate timeout for the update policy.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for the UnhealthyHostCount metric. Include an appropriate alarm threshold for the target group. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the target to signal success or failure to CloudFormation.","C":"Create a lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group by using the AWS::AutoScaling::LifecycleHook resource. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the target to signal success or failure to CloudFormation. Set an appropriate timeout on the lifecycle hook.","D":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to stream the cloud-init logs. Create a subscription filter that includes an AWS Lambda function with an appropriate invocation timeout. Configure the Lambda function to use the SignalResource API operation to signal success or failure to CloudFormation."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 cfn-signal 辅助脚本向 CloudFormation 发送成功或失败的信号。在 CloudFormation 模板中使用 WaitOnResourceSignals 更新策略。为更新策略设置适当的超时时间。","B":"为 UnhealthyHostCount 指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。为目标组设置适当的警报阈值。 创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题作为 CloudFormation 的目标，以发送成功 或失败的信号。 CAutoScaling::LifecycleHook 资源在自动扩展组上创建生命周期挂钩。创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题作为目标，向 CloudFormation 发送成功或失败的信号。为生命周期挂钩设 置适当的超时时间。","D":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理来流式传输 cloud-init 日志。创建一个订阅筛选器，其中包含一个 具有适当调用超时设置的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以使用 SignalResource API 操 作向 CloudFormation 发送成功或失败的信号。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario is a stack UPDATE: the user data lives in the launch template, and changing it changes the LaunchTemplate version, which triggers an AutoScalingRollingUpdate. The cfn-signal helper script signals CloudFormation success or failure from the instance, and it is designed to be used with a CreationPolicy attribute OR an UpdatePolicy attribute that has WaitOnResourceSignals set to true for EC2 Auto Scaling groups. When WaitOnResourceSignals is set, CloudFormation suspends the rolling update until each replaced instance signals success or until the configured timeout (PauseTime) expires; if user data fails to start Apache it can signal failure (or simply not signal before timeout), so the rolling update fails and the stack rolls back instead of reaching UPDATE_COMPLETE. This is exactly the mechanism that prevents CloudFormation from reporting success when user data has not finished correctly. Because this is an update (not initial create), the UpdatePolicy/WaitOnResourceSignals path is the correct one rather than CreationPolicy.","explanation_zh":"本情境是堆疊 UPDATE：user data 位於 launch template 中，修改 user data 會改變 LaunchTemplate 版本，進而觸發 AutoScalingRollingUpdate。cfn-signal 輔助指令稿會從執行個體向 CloudFormation 回報成功或失敗，且其設計就是搭配 CreationPolicy，或搭配將 WaitOnResourceSignals 設為 true 的 UpdatePolicy（用於 EC2 Auto Scaling group）。當設定 WaitOnResourceSignals 時，CloudFormation 會暫停 rolling update，直到每個被替換的執行個體回報成功，或直到逾時（PauseTime）為止；若 user data 啟動 Apache 失敗，即可回報 failure（或單純在逾時前不回報），rolling update 便會失敗並回滾，而不會到達 UPDATE_COMPLETE。這正是避免 user data 未正確完成時 CloudFormation 仍回報成功的機制。由於這是 update 而非初次 create，因此應使用 UpdatePolicy/WaitOnResourceSignals 路徑，而非 CreationPolicy。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A CloudWatch alarm on UnhealthyHostCount with an SNS topic does not signal success or failure back to CloudFormation. SNS cannot complete a CloudFormation resource signal, and an alarm firing after the stack already reaches UPDATE_COMPLETE does not cause the deployment to fail or roll back. This is a detection/notification mechanism, not a deployment gate.","why_zh":"在 UnhealthyHostCount 上設定 CloudWatch 警示並搭配 SNS topic，無法向 CloudFormation 回報成功或失敗。SNS 無法完成 CloudFormation 的資源 signal，且在堆疊已達 UPDATE_COMPLETE 之後才觸發的警示也不會使部署失敗或回滾。這只是偵測/通知機制，並非部署的把關門檻。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An AWS::AutoScaling::LifecycleHook with an SNS target governs instance launch/terminate transitions and can delay or abandon an instance, but it does not signal CloudFormation about user-data application health, and SNS cannot signal CloudFormation. A lifecycle hook completing (or timing out and abandoning) does not directly fail the stack update based on whether Apache started; it is not the documented mechanism for gating user-data success.","why_zh":"搭配 SNS 目標的 AWS::AutoScaling::LifecycleHook 用於控管執行個體啟動/終止轉換，可延遲或放棄某個執行個體，但它不會就 user data 的應用程式健康狀態向 CloudFormation 回報，且 SNS 無法對 CloudFormation 發出 signal。lifecycle hook 完成（或逾時放棄）並不會依 Apache 是否啟動而直接使堆疊更新失敗；這並非用來把關 user data 成功與否的官方機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Streaming cloud-init logs to CloudWatch and parsing them with a subscription-filter Lambda that calls SignalResource is convoluted and fragile (it relies on log pattern matching). While SignalResource is the underlying API, AWS provides cfn-signal plus WaitOnResourceSignals as the supported, far simpler pattern. This option adds unnecessary components and is not the idiomatic or reliable solution.","why_zh":"將 cloud-init 日誌串流至 CloudWatch，再用 subscription filter 的 Lambda 解析並呼叫 SignalResource，做法繁瑣且脆弱（仰賴日誌字串比對）。雖然 SignalResource 是底層 API，但 AWS 提供 cfn-signal 搭配 WaitOnResourceSignals 作為受支援且簡單許多的模式。此選項加入不必要的元件，並非慣用或可靠的解法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-signal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-attribute-updatepolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-attribute-creationpolicy.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":113,"question_en":"A company has a data ingestion application that runs across multiple AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company needs to monitor the application and consolidate access to the application. Currently, the company is running the application on Amazon EC2 instances from several Auto Scaling groups. The EC2 instances have no access to the internet because the data is sensitive. Engineers have deployed the necessary VPC endpoints. The EC2 instances run a custom AMI that is built specifically for the application. To maintain and troubleshoot the application, system administrators need the ability to log in to the EC2 instances. This access must be automated and controlled centrally. The company’s security team must receive a notification whenever the instances are accessed. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款跨多个 AWS 账户运行的数据摄取应用程序。这些账户位于 AWS 组织中的一个组 织内。该公司需要监控该应用程序并集中访问权限。目前，该公司在来自多个自动扩展组的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行该应用程序。由于数据敏感，这些 EC2 实例无法访问互联网。工程师已部署了必要 的 VPC 端点。EC2 实例运行的是专门为该应用程序构建的自定义 AMI。 为了维护和排查应用程序故障，系统管理员需要能够登录到 EC2 实例。这种访问权限必须实现自动 化并进行集中控制。每当实例被访问时，公司的安全团队都必须收到通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to send notifications to the security team whenever a user logs in to an EC2 instance. Use EC2 Instance Connect to log in to the instances. Deploy Auto Scaling groups by using AWS CloudFormation. Use the cfn-init helper script to deploy appropriate VPC routes for external access. Rebuild the custom AMI so that the custom AMI includes AWS Systems Manager Agent.","B":"Deploy a NAT gateway and a bastion host that has internet access. Create a security group that allows incoming traffic on all the EC2 instances from the bastion host. Install AWS Systems Manager Agent on all the EC2 instances. Use Auto Scaling group lifecycle hooks for monitoring and auditing access. Use Systems Manager Session Manager to log in to the instances. Send logs to a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Export data to Amazon S3 for auditing. Send notifications to the security team by using S3 event notifications.","C":"Use EC2 Image Builder to rebuild the custom AMI. Include the most recent version of AWS Systems Manager Agent in the image. Configure the Auto Scaling group to attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore role to all the EC2 instances. Use Systems Manager Session Manager to log in to the instances. Enable logging of session details to Amazon S3. Create an S3 event notification for new file uploads to send a message to the security team through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager Automation to build Systems Manager Agent into the custom AMI. Configure AWS Config to attach an SCP to the root organization account to allow the EC2 instances to connect to Systems Manager. Use Systems Manager Session Manager to log in to the instances. Enable logging of session details to Amazon S3. Create an S3 event notification for new file uploads to send a message to the security team through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便每当用户登录到 EC2 实例时向安全团队发送通知。使用 EC2 实例连接登录到实例。通过 AWS CloudFormation 部署自动扩展组。使用 cfn-init 辅助脚本部 署适当的 VPC 路由以实现外部访问。重新构建自定义 AMI，使其包含 AWS Systems Manager Agent。","B":"部署一个网络地址转换（NAT）网关和一个具有互联网访问权限的堡垒主机。创建一个安全组，允 许来自堡垒主机的所有入站流量访问所有 EC2 实例。在所有 EC2 实例上安装 AWS 系统管理器代 理。使用自动扩展组生命周期挂钩进行监控和访问审计。使用系统管理器会话管理器登录实例。 将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中的日志组。将数据导出到 Amazon S3 以进行审计。使用 S3 事件通知向安全团队发送通知。","C":"使用 EC2 Image Builder 重新构建自定义 AMI。在映像中包含 AWS Systems Manager Agent 的最新 版本。配置自动缩放组，将 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 角色附加到所有 EC2 实例。使用 Systems Manager Session Manager 登录到实例。启用会话详细信息的日志记录到 Amazon S3。为 新文件上传创建 S3 事件通知，通过 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题向安全团队发 送消息。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 将 Systems Manager Agent 构建到自定义 AMI 中。配置 AWS Config 以将 SCP 附加到根组织账户，从而允许 EC2 实例连接到 Systems Manager。使用 Systems Manager Session Manager 登录到实例。启用会话详细信息的日志记录到 Amazon S3。为 新文件上传创建 S3 事件通知，通过 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题向安全团队发送 消息。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"All requirements point to Systems Manager Session Manager: centrally controlled, automated, auditable login with no inbound ports and no need for a bastion or internet (Session Manager works over the already-deployed VPC interface endpoints for ssm/ssmmessages/ec2messages). Option C is the only fully correct path: EC2 Image Builder rebuilds the custom AMI (Image Builder includes the latest SSM Agent in its pipelines by default), the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore role attached to the instances grants exactly the permissions Session Manager needs, Session Manager logs session details to S3, and an S3 event notification on new object uploads triggers an SNS topic to alert the security team. This satisfies the no-internet constraint and the central, automated, notified access requirements.","explanation_zh":"所有需求都指向 Systems Manager Session Manager：集中控管、自動化、可稽核的登入，無需開放入站連接埠，也不需要 bastion 或網際網路（Session Manager 可透過已部署的 VPC interface endpoint，即 ssm/ssmmessages/ec2messages 運作）。選項 C 是唯一完全正確的方案：EC2 Image Builder 重建自訂 AMI（Image Builder 的 pipeline 預設包含最新版 SSM Agent），附加到執行個體的 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 角色提供 Session Manager 所需的精確權限，Session Manager 將工作階段細節記錄到 S3，並透過 S3 物件上傳事件通知觸發 SNS 主題通知安全團隊。這滿足無網際網路存取的限制以及集中、自動化、可通知的存取需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using cfn-init to deploy VPC routes for external (internet) access directly contradicts the requirement that instances have no internet access. EventBridge also has no native event for an OS-level user logging in to an EC2 instance, so notifications would not work as described. EC2 Instance Connect over a private network without a public path is also awkward here.","why_zh":"用 cfn-init 部署 VPC 路由以提供外部（網際網路）存取，直接違反執行個體無網際網路存取的需求。EventBridge 也沒有針對使用者作業系統層級登入 EC2 的原生事件，因此通知無法如描述般運作。在沒有公開路徑的私有網路上使用 EC2 Instance Connect 也不合適。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Deploying a NAT gateway and a bastion host with internet access violates the explicit no-internet requirement for the sensitive data instances. Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks are for instance launch/terminate transitions, not for monitoring or auditing interactive login access. This reintroduces exactly the bastion/SSH overhead Session Manager is meant to eliminate.","why_zh":"部署具網際網路存取的 NAT gateway 與 bastion host，違反了敏感資料執行個體不可連網的明確需求。Auto Scaling lifecycle hook 用於執行個體啟動／終止的轉換階段，並非用來監控或稽核互動式登入存取。這正好重新引入了 Session Manager 旨在消除的 bastion／SSH 維運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config cannot attach SCPs — SCPs are managed by AWS Organizations, and Config only evaluates resource configuration compliance. Moreover, SCPs are permission guardrails (maximum allowed) and never grant permissions, so an SCP cannot 'allow EC2 instances to connect to Systems Manager'; that requires an IAM instance role such as AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore. Using SSM Automation to bake the agent into the AMI is also not the appropriate AMI-build mechanism.","why_zh":"AWS Config 無法附加 SCP——SCP 由 AWS Organizations 管理，而 Config 僅評估資源組態合規性。此外，SCP 是權限護欄（最大允許範圍），永遠不會授予權限，因此 SCP 無法『允許 EC2 執行個體連線到 Systems Manager』；那需要像 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 這樣的 IAM 執行個體角色。使用 SSM Automation 將代理程式內建到 AMI 也不是適當的 AMI 建置機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/setup-instance-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-logging-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/ib-tutorials.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":114,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon S3 to store proprietary information. The development team creates buckets for new projects on a daily basis. The security team wants to ensure that all existing and future buckets have encryption, logging, and versioning enabled. Additionally, no buckets should ever be publicly read or write accessible. What should a DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 S3 存储专有信息。开发团队每天都会为新项目创建存储桶。安全团队希望确保 所有现有和未来的存储桶都启用加密、日志记录和版本控制功能。此外，任何存储桶都不应公开可读 或可写。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS CloudTrail and configure automatic remediation using AWS Lambda.","B":"Enable AWS Config rules and configure automatic remediation using AWS Systems Manager documents.","C":"Enable AWS Trusted Advisor and configure automatic remediation using Amazon EventBridge.","D":"Enable AWS Systems Manager and configure automatic remediation using Systems Manager documents."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 AWS CloudTrail 并使用 AWS Lambda 配置自动修复。","B":"启用 AWS Config 规则，并使用 AWS Systems Manager 文档配置自动修复。","C":"启用 AWS 可信顾问，并使用 Amazon EventBridge 配置自动修复。","D":"启用 AWS 系统管理器，并使用系统管理器文档配置自动修复。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config is the purpose-built service for continuously evaluating resource configurations against desired state for both existing and future resources. AWS provides managed Config rules that directly cover every requirement: s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled (encryption), s3-bucket-logging-enabled (logging), s3-bucket-versioning-enabled (versioning), and s3-bucket-public-read-prohibited / s3-bucket-public-write-prohibited (no public read/write). Config rules support automatic remediation, and per the AWS Config developer guide the remediation actions are defined as AWS Systems Manager (SSM) Automation documents, which Config invokes on noncompliant resources. Because Config continuously discovers and evaluates resources, newly created buckets (created daily) are automatically assessed and remediated, satisfying both the existing and future requirement. This is exactly option B.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 是專門用來持續評估資源組態是否符合期望狀態的服務，且同時涵蓋現有與未來建立的資源。AWS 提供的 managed Config rules 正好對應所有需求：s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled（加密）、s3-bucket-logging-enabled（記錄）、s3-bucket-versioning-enabled（版本控制），以及 s3-bucket-public-read-prohibited / s3-bucket-public-write-prohibited（禁止公開讀寫）。Config rules 支援自動修復，且依據 AWS Config 開發者指南，修復動作是以 AWS Systems Manager（SSM）Automation documents 定義，由 Config 對不合規資源觸發執行。由於 Config 會持續探索並評估資源，每日新建立的 bucket 會被自動評估並修復，因此同時滿足現有與未來的需求，這正是選項 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail only records API activity (an audit log); it does not evaluate resource compliance state or determine whether a bucket has encryption/logging/versioning enabled. While Lambda could remediate, CloudTrail is not the detective control for ongoing configuration compliance, and it does not natively trigger per-resource remediation against desired configuration.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 只記錄 API 活動（稽核日誌），不會評估資源的合規狀態，也無法判斷 bucket 是否已啟用加密／記錄／版本控制。雖然 Lambda 可做修復，但 CloudTrail 並非用於持續組態合規的偵測控制，且無法原生地針對每個資源依期望組態觸發修復。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Trusted Advisor provides periodic best-practice checks across cost, security, etc., but it is not a continuous configuration compliance engine with managed rules for all four S3 requirements, and it does not integrate with EventBridge to drive auto-remediation in the structured rule+SSM-document way Config does. It is not the AWS-recommended detective control for enforcing specific resource configurations.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 提供成本、安全等面向的定期最佳實務檢查，但並非具備涵蓋全部四項 S3 需求的 managed rules 的持續組態合規引擎，也無法像 Config（規則＋SSM 文件）那樣以結構化方式透過 EventBridge 驅動自動修復。它不是 AWS 建議用來強制執行特定資源組態的偵測控制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Systems Manager (and its Automation documents) is the remediation/execution engine, not the compliance detection engine. SSM does not by itself continuously evaluate S3 buckets against encryption/logging/versioning/public-access rules; that detection is AWS Config's role. SSM documents are the remediation mechanism that Config invokes, so SSM alone is incomplete without Config to detect noncompliance.","why_zh":"Systems Manager（及其 Automation documents）是修復／執行引擎，而非合規偵測引擎。SSM 本身不會持續對 S3 bucket 評估加密／記錄／版本控制／公開存取規則；該偵測屬於 AWS Config 的職責。SSM 文件是 Config 觸發的修復機制，因此缺少 Config 偵測不合規，單靠 SSM 並不完整。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-account-level-public-access-blocks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":115,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is researching the least expensive way to implement an image batch processing cluster on AWS. The application cannot run in Docker containers and must run on Amazon EC2. The batch job stores checkpoint data on an NFS volume and can tolerate interruptions. Configuring the cluster software from a generic EC2 Linux image takes 30 minutes. What is the MOST cost-effective solution?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在研究在 AWS 上以最低成本实现图像批处理集群的方法。该应用程序无法在 Docker 容器中运行，必须在 Amazon EC2 上运行。批处理作业将检查点数据存储在 NFS 卷上，并且能够容忍中断。 从通用的 EC2 Linux 镜像配置集群软件需要 30 分钟。 哪种方案的成本效益最高？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon EFS for checkpoint data. To complete the job, use an EC2 Auto Scaling group and an On-Demand pricing model to provision EC2 instances temporarily.","B":"Use GlusterFS on EC2 instances for checkpoint data. To run the batch job, configure EC2 instances manually. When the job completes, shut down the instances manually.","C":"Use Amazon EFS for checkpoint data. Use EC2 Fleet to launch EC2 Spot Instances, and utilize user data to configure the EC2 Linux instance on startup.","D":"Use Amazon EFS for checkpoint data. Use EC2 Fleet to launch EC2 Spot Instances. Create a custom AMI for the cluster and use the latest AMI when creating instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon EFS 来存储检查点数据。要完成任务，请使用 EC2 自动扩展组和按需定价模式临时配置 EC2 实例。","B":"在 EC2 实例上使用 GlusterFS 来存储检查点数据。要运行批处理作业，请手动配置 EC2 实例。作业完 成后，请手动关闭实例。","C":"使用 Amazon EFS 存储检查点数据。使用 EC2 集群启动 EC2 竞价型实例，并利用用户数据在启动时配 置 EC2 Linux 实例。","D":"使用 Amazon EFS 存储检查点数据。使用 EC2 集群启动 EC2 竞价型实例。为集群创建自定义 AMI，并 在创建实例时使用最新 AMI。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The job tolerates interruptions and the goal is MOST cost-effective, so Spot Instances (up to 90% cheaper than On-Demand) are correct, eliminating the On-Demand option A. For the NFS checkpoint volume, Amazon EFS is a fully managed NFS service that is cheaper and lower-overhead than self-managing GlusterFS on additional EC2 instances, eliminating B. The deciding detail is that configuring the cluster software from a generic Linux image takes 30 minutes. With Spot Instances, instances are frequently interrupted and relaunched, so option C (configure via user data on every startup) would repeatedly waste 30 minutes of paid compute per launch before any useful work begins. Option D bakes the configuration into a custom AMI so each instance is ready almost immediately, avoiding the repeated 30-minute provisioning cost. AWS documentation confirms a custom AMI improves provisioning time when a lot of software must be installed, making D the most cost-effective combination of Spot + EFS + custom AMI.","explanation_zh":"此工作可容忍中斷，且目標是「最具成本效益」，因此應使用 Spot Instances（比 On-Demand 便宜最多 90%），故排除使用 On-Demand 的選項 A。對於 NFS checkpoint 磁碟區，Amazon EFS 是全代管的 NFS 服務，比在額外 EC2 instances 上自行維運 GlusterFS 更便宜且維運負擔更低，故排除 B。關鍵在於從通用 Linux image 設定 cluster 軟體需時 30 分鐘。使用 Spot Instances 時，instances 會頻繁被中斷並重新啟動，因此選項 C（每次啟動皆透過 user data 設定）會在每次啟動時重複浪費 30 分鐘的付費運算時間才能開始有用的工作。選項 D 將設定預先烘焙進 custom AMI，使每個 instance 幾乎可立即就緒，避免重複的 30 分鐘佈建成本。AWS 文件確認當需要安裝大量軟體時，custom AMI 可改善佈建時間，因此 Spot + EFS + custom AMI 的組合 D 最具成本效益。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"On-Demand pricing is far more expensive than Spot for an interruption-tolerant batch job, so it is not the MOST cost-effective even though EFS is the right storage choice.","why_zh":"對於可容忍中斷的批次工作而言，On-Demand 計價遠比 Spot 昂貴，因此即使 EFS 是正確的儲存選擇，它也不是最具成本效益的方案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Self-managed GlusterFS on EC2 adds persistent always-on instance costs and significant operational overhead versus managed EFS, and manual configuration/shutdown is neither cost-optimal nor scalable.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上自行維運 GlusterFS 相較於代管的 EFS，會增加持續常駐的 instance 成本與大量維運負擔，而手動設定/關機既非成本最佳化也不具擴展性。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Using user data to configure each instance on startup means every Spot launch and frequent Spot replacement repeats the 30-minute configuration, wasting paid compute time and making it less cost-effective than a pre-baked custom AMI.","why_zh":"在啟動時用 user data 設定每個 instance，代表每次 Spot 啟動及頻繁的 Spot 替換都會重複 30 分鐘的設定，浪費付費運算時間，因此比預先烘焙的 custom AMI 更不具成本效益。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.customenv.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/batch/latest/userguide/bestpractice6.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/cost-optimization-leveraging-ec2-spot-instances/when-to-use-spot-instances.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/AMIs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":116,"question_en":"A company recently migrated its legacy application from on-premises to AWS. The application is hosted on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer, which is behind Amazon API Gateway. The company wants to ensure users experience minimal disruptions during any deployment of a new version of the application. The company also wants to ensure it can quickly roll back updates if there is an issue. Which solution will meet these requirements with MINIMAL changes to the application?","question_zh":"一家公司最近将其遗留应用程序从本地迁移到了 AWS。该应用程序托管在位于应用负载均衡器后面的亚马 逊 EC2 实例上，而应用负载均衡器又位于亚马逊 API 网关之后。该公司希望在部署应用程序新版本期间， 用户能感受到尽可能小的干扰。同时，该公司还希望在出现问题时能够迅速回滚更新。 哪种解决方案只需对应用程序进行最小的改动就能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Introduce changes as a separate environment parallel to the existing one. Configure API Gateway to use a canary release deployment to send a small subset of user traffic to the new environment.","B":"Introduce changes as a separate environment parallel to the existing one. Update the application’s DNS alias records to point to the new environment.","C":"Introduce changes as a separate target group behind the existing Application Load Balancer. Configure API Gateway to route user traffic to the new target group in steps.","D":"Introduce changes as a separate target group behind the existing Application Load Balancer. Configure API Gateway to route all traffic to the Application Load Balancer, which then sends the traffic to the new target group."},"options_zh":{"A":"作为现有环境的并行环境引入变更。配置 API 网关使用金丝雀发布部署，将一小部分用户流量发送到 新环境。","B":"作为现有环境的并行环境引入变更。更新应用程序的 DNS 别名记录，使其指向新环境。","C":"在现有的应用负载均衡器之后，将变更作为单独的目标组引入。逐步配置 API 网关，将用户流量路由到 新的目标组。","D":"在现有的应用负载均衡器后面将变更作为单独的目标组引入。配置 API 网关将所有流量路由到应用负载均 衡器，然后由其将流量发送到新的目标组。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The architecture is API Gateway -> ALB -> EC2. The requirements are minimal user disruption during a deployment, quick rollback, and minimal application changes. API Gateway natively supports a canary release deployment, where total traffic on a stage is randomly split between the production release and a canary release by a configurable percentTraffic (0.0-100.0). The canary uses stageVariableOverrides, which can override the HTTP integration endpoint, so canary traffic can be directed to a separate parallel environment (a new ALB/backend) while production stays on the existing one. This sends only a small subset of users to the new version (minimal disruption) and lets you instantly roll back by discarding/turning off the canary, with no application code changes. Option A describes exactly this native feature, so it is the best fit for all three qualifiers, especially 'minimal changes' and 'quickly roll back'.","explanation_zh":"架構為 API Gateway -> ALB -> EC2。需求是部署新版本時對使用者干擾最小、能快速回復 (rollback)，且對應用程式的變更最少。API Gateway 原生支援 canary release deployment：同一個 stage 上的總流量會依可設定的 percentTraffic (0.0-100.0) 隨機分流給 production release 與 canary release。Canary 使用 stageVariableOverrides，可覆寫 HTTP integration 的後端端點，因此可將 canary 流量導向一個獨立的平行環境 (新的 ALB/後端)，production 流量仍維持在既有環境。這樣只有一小部分使用者會被導到新版本 (干擾最小)，並可藉由停用/捨棄 canary 立即回復，且不需修改應用程式碼。選項 A 正是描述此原生功能，最符合三個限定條件，特別是「變更最少」與「快速回復」。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Updating DNS alias records to point to the new parallel environment is an all-at-once cutover, not sending a small subset of traffic, so it does not minimize disruption. DNS TTL caching also makes rollback slow rather than quick, failing the fast-rollback requirement.","why_zh":"更新 DNS alias 紀錄指向新平行環境屬於一次性全量切換，而非只導入一小部分流量，無法將干擾降到最低。DNS TTL 快取也使回復變慢而非快速，不符合快速回復需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"API Gateway cannot route to a specific ALB target group or weight traffic between target groups 'in steps'. API Gateway integrates with the ALB endpoint (listener), and target-group selection/weighting is an ALB-level concern, not something API Gateway controls. The described mechanism is technically inaccurate.","why_zh":"API Gateway 無法路由到特定的 ALB target group，也無法在 target group 之間「逐步」加權分流。API Gateway 整合的是 ALB 端點 (listener)，target group 的選擇/加權屬於 ALB 層級而非 API Gateway 控制範圍，所述機制在技術上不正確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Routing ALL traffic to the ALB which forwards everything to the new target group is a hard cutover, not a gradual rollout, so it does not minimize disruption. It also describes no built-in weighting or rollback mechanism, failing the quick-rollback requirement.","why_zh":"將所有流量導到 ALB 再全部轉發到新的 target group，是硬切換而非漸進式上線，無法將干擾降到最低。它也未描述任何內建的加權或回復機制，不符合快速回復需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/canary-release.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/create-canary-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/how-to-deploy-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-stages.stage-variables.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":117,"question_en":"A company is storing 100 GB of log data in .csv format in an Amazon S3 bucket. SQL developers want to query this data and generate graphs to visualize it. The SQL developers also need an efficient, automated way to store metadata from the .csv file. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of effort? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中以 .csv 格式存储 100GB 的日志数据。SQL 开发人员希望查询这些数据并 生成图表来可视化它。SQL 开发人员还需要一种高效、自动化的办法来存储来自 .csv 文件的元数据。 哪三种步骤的组合能以最少的努力满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Filter the data through AWS X-Ray to visualize the data.","B":"Filter the data through Amazon QuickSight to visualize the data.","C":"Query the data with Amazon Athena.","D":"Query the data with Amazon Redshift.","E":"Use the AWS Glue Data Catalog as the persistent metadata store.","F":"Use Amazon DynamoDB as the persistent metadata store."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过 AWS X-Ray 过滤数据以可视化数据。","B":"通过 Amazon QuickSight 过滤数据以可视化呈现数据。","C":"使用 Amazon Athena 查询数据。","D":"使用 Amazon Redshift 查询数据。","E":"使用 AWS Glue 数据目录作为持久的元数据存储。","F":"使用亚马逊 DynamoDB 作为持久化的元数据存储。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST amount of effort for SQL developers to query 100 GB of CSV in S3, visualize it, and automatically store metadata. The canonical serverless pattern is: (C) Amazon Athena queries CSV directly in S3 using standard SQL with no clusters to provision; (E) the AWS Glue Data Catalog is the built-in persistent metadata store (Hive-compatible metastore) that Athena uses natively as AwsDataCatalog, and a Glue crawler can automatically infer and store the CSV schema/metadata; and (B) Amazon QuickSight connects natively to Athena to build graphs and dashboards with minimal effort. This combination is fully serverless and requires no infrastructure management, satisfying least effort.","explanation_zh":"本題限定詞為「最少工作量」，讓 SQL 開發者查詢 S3 中 100 GB 的 CSV、視覺化並自動儲存 metadata。標準的無伺服器分析模式為：(C) Amazon Athena 以標準 SQL 直接查詢 S3 中的 CSV，無需佈建叢集；(E) AWS Glue Data Catalog 為內建的持久性 metadata 儲存（Hive 相容 metastore），Athena 原生以 AwsDataCatalog 使用它，且 Glue crawler 可自動推斷並儲存 CSV 的 schema/metadata；(B) Amazon QuickSight 原生連接 Athena，可輕鬆建立圖表與儀表板。此組合完全無伺服器、無需管理基礎設施，符合最少工作量要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS X-Ray is a distributed tracing service for analyzing and debugging application request flows; it does not visualize arbitrary CSV/business data and cannot produce data graphs.","why_zh":"AWS X-Ray 是分散式追蹤服務，用於分析與除錯應用程式請求流程，無法視覺化任意 CSV/業務資料，也無法產生資料圖表。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Redshift would require provisioning a cluster and loading/COPYing the data into it, which is far more operational effort than Athena querying S3 in place; it violates the LEAST effort qualifier.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift 需佈建叢集並將資料 COPY 載入其中，相較 Athena 直接就地查詢 S3 工作量大得多，違反「最少工作量」限定詞。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Amazon DynamoDB is a NoSQL key-value/document database, not a schema/metadata store for Athena; Athena uses the Glue Data Catalog, and using DynamoDB would require custom code to manage metadata.","why_zh":"Amazon DynamoDB 是 NoSQL 鍵值/文件資料庫，並非 Athena 的 schema/metadata 儲存；Athena 使用 Glue Data Catalog，改用 DynamoDB 需自行撰寫程式管理 metadata。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/gdc-register-query-the-data-source.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/schema-csv.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/add-crawler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/analyze-and-visualize-nested-json-data-with-amazon-athena-and-amazon-quicksight.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/emr/latest/ReleaseGuide/emr-hive-metastore-glue.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":118,"question_en":"A company deploys its corporate infrastructure on AWS across multiple AWS Regions and Availability Zones. The infrastructure is deployed on Amazon EC2 instances and connects with AWS IoT Greengrass devices. The company deploys additional resources on on-premises servers that are located in the corporate headquarters. The company wants to reduce the overhead involved in maintaining and updating its resources. The company’s DevOps team plans to use AWS Systems Manager to implement automated management and application of patches. The DevOps team confirms that Systems Manager is available in the Regions that the resources are deployed in. Systems Manager also is available in a Region near the corporate headquarters. Which combination of steps must the DevOps team take to implement automated patch and configuration management across the company’s EC2 instances, IoT devices, and on-premises infrastructure? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在多个 AWS 区域和可用区内部署了其企业基础设施，这些基础设施部署在亚马逊 EC2 实例上， 并与 AWS IoT Greengrass 设备相连接。该公司还在位于企业总部的本地服务器上部署了额外的资源。 该公司希望减少维护和更新资源所产生的管理费用。公司的 DevOps 团队计划使用 AWS Systems Manager 来实现补丁的自动化管理和应用。DevOps 团队确认 Systems Manager 在部署资源的区域可用。Systems Manager 在靠近公司总部的区域也提供服务。 DevOps 团队必须采取哪些步骤组合才能在公司的 EC2 实例、物联网设备和本地基础设施上实现自动化的 补丁和配置管理？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Apply tags to all the EC2 instances, AWS IoT Greengrass devices, and on-premises servers. Use Systems Manager Session Manager to push patches to all the tagged devices.","B":"Use Systems Manager Run Command to schedule patching for the EC2 instances, AWS IoT Greengrass devices, and on-premises servers.","C":"Use Systems Manager Patch Manager to schedule patching for the EC2 instances, AWS IoT Greengrass devices, and on-premises servers as a Systems Manager maintenance window task.","D":"Configure Amazon EventBridge to monitor Systems Manager Patch Manager for updates to patch baselines. Associate Systems Manager Run Command with the event to initiate a patch action for all EC2 instances, AWS IoT Greengrass devices, and on-premises servers.","E":"Create an IAM instance profile for Systems Manager. Attach the instance profile to all the EC2 instances in the AWS account. For the AWS IoT Greengrass devices and on-premises servers, create an IAM service role for Systems Manager.","F":"Generate a managed-instance activation. Use the Activation Code and Activation ID to install Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent) on each server in the on-premises environment. Update the AWS IoT Greengrass IAM token exchange role. Use the role to deploy SSM Agent on all the IoT devices."},"options_zh":{"A":"对所有 EC2 实例、AWS IoT Greengrass 设备和本地服务器应用标签。使用系统管理器会话管理器 将补丁推送到所有已标记的设备。","B":"使用系统管理器运行命令为 EC2 实例、AWS IoT 核绿格设备和本地服务器安排补丁更新。","C":"使用系统管理器补丁管理器安排对 EC2 实例、AWS IoT Greengrass 设备和本地服务器的补丁安装， 将其作为系统管理器维护窗口任务。","D":"配置 Amazon EventBridge 以监控 Systems Manager Patch Manager 中补丁基线的更新。将 Systems Manager Run Command 与该事件关联，以对所有 EC2 实例、AWS IoT Greengrass 设备和本地服务 器启动补丁操作。","E":"为 Systems Manager 创建一个 IAM 实例配置文件。将该实例配置文件附加到 AWS 账户中的所有 EC2 实例。对于 AWS IoT Greengrass 设备和本地服务器，请为 Systems Manager 创建一个 IAM 服务角色。","F":"生成托管实例激活码。使用激活码和激活 ID 在本地环境中的每台服务器上安装 Systems Manager 代理 （SSM 代理）。更新 AWS IoT Greengrass IAM 令牌交换角色。使用该角色在所有 IoT 设备上部署 SSM 代理。"},"answer":["C","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"To manage EC2, AWS IoT Greengrass (edge) devices, and on-premises servers with Systems Manager, you must (1) set up the correct IAM permissions, (2) register/install SSM Agent so each resource becomes a managed node, and (3) schedule patching. Option E is correct because EC2 instances use an IAM instance profile attached to the instance, while non-EC2 resources (Greengrass edge devices and on-premises servers) use an IAM service role for Systems Manager; this exact split is documented for hybrid setup and for the Greengrass SSM Agent component (Step 2: Create an IAM service role for Systems Manager). Option F is correct because on-premises servers are registered with a hybrid (managed-instance) activation whose Activation Code and Activation ID are used when installing SSM Agent, while Greengrass core devices require updating the Greengrass token exchange role (adding ssm:RegisterManagedInstance, ssm:AddTagsToResource, iam:PassRole) and then deploying the SSM Agent Greengrass component. Option C is correct because once all three resource types are registered managed nodes, Patch Manager schedules and applies patches via a maintenance window task running AWS-RunPatchBaseline. The decisive qualifier is that automated patch/configuration management requires registering every device as a managed node first (IAM + activation/agent) and then using Patch Manager (not Session Manager, Run Command alone, or an EventBridge-triggered Run Command) to drive scheduled patching.","explanation_zh":"要用 Systems Manager 管理 EC2、AWS IoT Greengrass（邊緣）裝置與地端伺服器，必須 (1) 設定正確的 IAM 權限、(2) 註冊並安裝 SSM Agent 讓每個資源成為 managed node、(3) 排程修補。選項 E 正確，因為 EC2 instance 使用附加在執行個體上的 IAM instance profile，而非 EC2 資源（Greengrass 邊緣裝置與地端伺服器）則使用 Systems Manager 的 IAM service role；hybrid 設定與 Greengrass SSM Agent component 文件（Step 2: Create an IAM service role for Systems Manager）明確記載此區分。選項 F 正確，因為地端伺服器透過 hybrid（managed-instance）activation 註冊，安裝 SSM Agent 時使用其 Activation Code 與 Activation ID；Greengrass core device 則需更新 Greengrass token exchange role（新增 ssm:RegisterManagedInstance、ssm:AddTagsToResource、iam:PassRole），再部署 SSM Agent Greengrass component。選項 C 正確，因為三類資源都註冊為 managed node 後，Patch Manager 透過 maintenance window task 執行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline 來排程並套用修補。關鍵判別點在於：自動化修補/組態管理需先把每個裝置註冊為 managed node（IAM + activation/agent），再用 Patch Manager（而非 Session Manager、單獨的 Run Command 或 EventBridge 觸發的 Run Command）來驅動排程修補。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Session Manager provides interactive shell/port-forwarding sessions, not patch distribution; it cannot 'push patches.' Tagging resources also does not register edge/on-premises devices as managed nodes, so this step fails the core requirement.","why_zh":"Session Manager 提供互動式 shell／連接埠轉送工作階段，並非用來派送修補，無法『push patches』。僅打標籤也無法把邊緣／地端裝置註冊為 managed node，因此不符合核心需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Run Command can run a command on registered nodes but is not the native mechanism to schedule patching; AWS uses Patch Manager with maintenance windows (or patch policies) for that. Run Command also cannot reach devices that have not been registered first.","why_zh":"Run Command 可在已註冊節點上執行指令，但並非原生的修補排程機制；AWS 以 Patch Manager 搭配 maintenance window（或 patch policy）來排程修補。Run Command 也無法觸及尚未註冊的裝置。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Triggering Run Command from EventBridge whenever a patch baseline changes is a convoluted, non-recommended pattern and does not establish scheduled patching across managed nodes; Patch Manager maintenance windows are the documented approach. It also still presumes devices are already registered.","why_zh":"每當 patch baseline 變更就由 EventBridge 觸發 Run Command 是迂迴且非建議的做法，也無法在 managed node 上建立排程修補；文件建議的方式是 Patch Manager maintenance window。此選項同樣預設裝置已註冊。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/greengrass/v2/developerguide/install-systems-manager-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/greengrass/v2/developerguide/systems-manager-agent-component.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-hybrid-multicloud.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/sysman-patch-scheduletasks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/maintenance-window-tutorial-patching.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":119,"question_en":"A company is testing a web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The instances run in an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. The company uses a blue/green deployment process with immutable instances when deploying new software. During testing, users are being automatically logged out of the application at random times. Testers also report that, when a new version of the application is deployed, all users are logged out. The development team needs a solution to ensure users remain logged in across scaling events and application deployments. What is the MOST operationally efficient way to ensure users remain logged in?","question_zh":"一家公司正在测试一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的网络应用程序，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器之后。 这些实例在多个可用区的自动扩展组中运行。该公司在部署新软件时采用蓝/绿部署流程，并使用不可 变实例。 在测试期间，用户会在随机时间被自动从应用程序中注销。测试人员还发现 报告称，当应用程序的新版本部署时，所有用户都会被登出。开发团队需要一个解决方案，以确保用 户在扩展事件和应用程序部署期间保持登录状态。 确保用户保持登录状态的最高效操作方式是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Enable smart sessions on the load balancer and modify the application to check for an existing session.","B":"Enable session sharing on the load balancer and modify the application to read from the session store.","C":"Store user session information in an Amazon S3 bucket and modify the application to read session information from the bucket.","D":"Modify the application to store user session information in an Amazon ElastiCache cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在负载均衡器上启用智能会话，并修改应用程序以检查是否存在会话。","B":"在负载均衡器上启用会话共享，并修改应用程序以从会话存储中读取。","C":"将用户会话信息存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并修改应用程序以从该存储桶读取会话信息。","D":"修改 将用户会话信息存储在 Amazon ElastiCache 集群中的应用程序。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Users are logged out at random times (scale-in terminates the instance holding their in-memory session) and on every deployment (immutable blue/green replaces all instances). The fix is to make the web tier stateless by offloading session state to a shared, durable, multi-AZ data store, so any instance can serve any request. AWS Well-Architected REL05-BP06 explicitly recommends offloading session state to Amazon ElastiCache or Amazon DynamoDB, and its Figure 7 literally shows 'session state is offloaded to Amazon ElastiCache.' Option D (store session info in an ElastiCache cluster) is exactly this pattern and the MOST operationally efficient durable solution. Sticky sessions would not help because pinning a user to one target still loses the session when that target is deregistered during scale-in or replaced during an immutable deployment.","explanation_zh":"使用者在隨機時間被登出（scale-in 終止了持有其記憶體內 session 的執行個體），且每次部署都被登出（immutable blue/green 會替換所有執行個體）。解法是讓 web tier 變成 stateless，把 session 狀態卸載到共享、持久、多 AZ 的資料儲存中，使任一執行個體都能處理任一請求。AWS Well-Architected REL05-BP06 明確建議將 session 狀態卸載到 Amazon ElastiCache 或 Amazon DynamoDB，其 Figure 7 直接顯示「session state is offloaded to Amazon ElastiCache」。選項 D（將 session 資訊存在 ElastiCache cluster）正是此模式，也是最具營運效率的持久解法。Sticky sessions 無法解決問題，因為將使用者綁定到單一 target，在 scale-in 取消註冊該 target 或 immutable 部署替換它時，session 仍會遺失。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no 'smart sessions' feature on an Application Load Balancer. Even ALB sticky sessions only pin a client to a specific target via a cookie; when that target is terminated during scale-in or replaced during an immutable deployment, the locally stored session is lost. This does not keep users logged in.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 並無『smart sessions』功能。即使是 ALB sticky sessions 也只是用 cookie 把用戶綁到特定 target；當該 target 在 scale-in 被終止或在 immutable 部署中被替換時，本機儲存的 session 仍會遺失，無法讓使用者保持登入。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"ALB has no 'session sharing' feature; the load balancer cannot share or replicate application session data across instances. Session sharing must be implemented at the application layer by reading/writing to an external store such as ElastiCache or DynamoDB, which is what D describes.","why_zh":"ALB 沒有『session sharing』功能；負載平衡器無法在執行個體間共享或複製應用程式 session 資料。Session 共享必須在應用層透過讀寫外部儲存（如 ElastiCache 或 DynamoDB）實作，這正是 D 所描述的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon S3 is object storage, not a low-latency session store. Reading/writing session state to S3 on every request adds high latency and is not the AWS-recommended pattern for ephemeral session data; ElastiCache (in-memory, sub-millisecond) is the documented choice for session state.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 是物件儲存，並非低延遲的 session 儲存。每個請求都讀寫 S3 會帶來高延遲，且非 AWS 建議的暫時性 session 資料模式；ElastiCache（記憶體內、次毫秒）才是文件建議的 session 狀態選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2023-10-03/framework/rel_mitigate_interaction_failure_stateless.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/best-practices-wordpress/stateless-web-tier.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonElastiCache/latest/dg/elasticache-use-cases.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/load-balancer-stickiness/welcome.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":120,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to configure a blue/green deployment for an existing three-tier application. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances and uses an Amazon RDS database. The EC2 instances run behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and are in an Auto Scaling group. The DevOps engineer has created a launch template and an Auto Scaling group for the blue environment. The DevOps engineer also has created a launch template and an Auto Scaling group for the green environment. Each Auto Scaling group deploys to a matching blue or green target group. The target group also specifies which software, blue or green, gets loaded on the EC2 instances. The ALB can be configured to send traffic to the blue environment’s target group or the green environment’s target group. An Amazon Route 53 record for www.example.com points to the ALB. The deployment must move traffic all at once between the software on the blue environment’s EC2 instances to the newly deployed software on the green environment’s EC2 instances. What should the DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要为现有的三层应用程序配置蓝/绿部署。该应用程序在 Amazon EC2 实例上运 行，并使用 Amazon RDS 数据库。EC2 实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后，并处于自动扩展组中。 DevOps 工程师为蓝色环境创建了一个启动模板和一个自动扩展组。DevOps 工程师还为绿色环境创建 了一个启动模板和一个自动扩展组。每个自动扩展组都会部署到相应的蓝色或绿色目标组。目标组还 指定了在 EC2 实例上加载哪个软件，是蓝色的还是绿色的。应用负载均衡器（ALB）可以配置为将流 量发送到蓝色环境的目标组或绿色环境的目标组。Amazon Route 53 中为 www.example.com 设置的记录 指向该应用负载均衡器。 部署操作必须一次性将流量从蓝色环境的 EC2 实例上的软件转移到新部署的绿色环境的 EC2 实 例上的软件。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Start a rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new software on the green environment’s EC2 instances. When the rolling restart is complete, use an AWS CLI command to update the ALB to send traffic to the green environment’s target group.","B":"Use an AWS CLI command to update the ALB to send traffic to the green environment’s target group. Then start a rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new software on the green environment’s EC2 instances.","C":"Update the launch template to deploy the green environment’s software on the blue environment’s EC2 instances. Keep the target groups and Auto Scaling groups unchanged in both environments. Perform a rolling restart of the blue environment’s EC2 instances.","D":"Start a rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new software on the green environment’s EC2 instances. When the rolling restart is complete, update the Route 53 DNS to point to the green environment’s endpoint on the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"对绿色环境的自动扩展组启动滚动重启，以便在绿色环境的 EC2 实例上部署新软件。滚动重启完 成后，使用 AWS CLI 命令更新应用负载均衡器（ALB），使其将流量发送到绿色环境的目标组。","B":"使用 AWS CLI 命令将应用负载均衡器（ALB）更新为将流量发送到绿色环境的目标组。然后对绿 色环境的自动扩展组执行滚动重启，以便在绿色环境的 EC2 实例上部署新软件。","C":"更新启动模板，以便在蓝色环境的 EC2 实例上部署绿色环境的软件。保持两个环境中的目标组和自 动扩展组不变。对蓝色环境的 EC2 实例执行滚动重启。","D":"开始对绿色环境的自动扩展组进行滚动重启，以便在绿色环境的 EC2 实例上部署新软件。滚动重 启完成后，更新 Route 53 DNS 以指向 ALB 上绿色环境的端点。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Correct blue/green cutover order: first deploy the new software to the green environment by refreshing/rolling-restarting the green Auto Scaling group so the green EC2 instances launch with the new software and register healthy in the green target group; only then flip the ALB to send traffic to the green target group. The ALB cutover is performed by modifying the listener's default action to forward to the green target group (e.g., via the AWS CLI elbv2 modify-listener command). Because the listener default action is changed in a single operation, all traffic moves from blue to green at once, which satisfies the 'all at once' requirement. The Route 53 record stays pointing at the same single ALB DNS name, which is consistent with the described architecture where the ALB (not DNS) selects the target group.","explanation_zh":"正確的 blue/green 切換順序為：先透過 rolling restart 重新整理 green Auto Scaling group，使 green EC2 instances 以新軟體啟動並在 green target group 中註冊為健康狀態；待完成後，再將 ALB 切換到 green target group。ALB 的切換是透過修改 listener 的 default action（預設規則）forward 到 green target group（例如使用 AWS CLI 的 elbv2 modify-listener）一次性完成，因此所有流量會一次性（all at once）從 blue 轉到 green，符合需求。Route 53 紀錄仍指向同一個 ALB 的 DNS 名稱，符合題目中由 ALB（而非 DNS）選擇 target group 的架構。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Reverses the order: it flips the ALB to the green target group before the new software is deployed, so production traffic hits green instances that are still running the old software or are mid-restart and unhealthy, causing errors/downtime.","why_zh":"順序顛倒：在新軟體尚未部署前就把 ALB 切到 green target group，導致正式流量打到仍跑舊軟體或正在重啟、不健康的 green 執行個體，造成錯誤或停機。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Defeats the blue/green pattern entirely: it overwrites the blue instances in place with green software, keeps both environments unchanged, and uses a rolling restart (gradual, not all-at-once). There is no isolated green environment to roll back to, and rolling does not move traffic all at once.","why_zh":"完全違背 blue/green 模式：把 green 軟體就地覆寫到 blue 執行個體上，且使用 rolling restart（漸進式而非一次性）。沒有獨立的 green 環境可供回復，rolling 也不是一次性切換流量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A single ALB has only one DNS name; there is no separate 'green endpoint on the ALB' for Route 53 to point to, and the architecture states the ALB (the listener/target group) selects blue vs green. DNS-based cutover also does not move traffic 'all at once' because of DNS TTL/client caching.","why_zh":"單一 ALB 只有一個 DNS 名稱，並不存在可供 Route 53 指向的『ALB 上的 green 端點』，且題目說明是由 ALB（listener/target group）選擇 blue 或 green。基於 DNS 的切換也因 TTL/用戶端快取而無法做到一次性切換流量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-listeners.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/elbv2/modify-listener.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-target-groups.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":121,"question_en":"A company is building a new pipeline by using AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild in a build account. The pipeline consists of two stages. The first stage is a CodeBuild job to build and package an AWS Lambda function. The second stage consists of deployment actions that operate on two different AWS accounts: a development environment account and a production environment account. The deployment stages use the AWS CloudFormation action that CodePipeline invokes to deploy the infrastructure that the Lambda function requires. A DevOps engineer creates the CodePipeline pipeline and configures the pipeline to encrypt build artifacts by using the AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) AWS managed key for Amazon S3 (the aws/s3 key). The artifacts are stored in an S3 bucket. When the pipeline runs, the CloudFormation actions fail with an access denied error. Which combination of actions must the DevOps engineer perform to resolve this error? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 在一个构建账户中构建新的管道。该管道包含 两个阶段。第一阶段是一个 CodeBuild 任务，用于构建和打包一个 AWS Lambda 函数。第二阶段包含 在两个不同的 AWS 账户上执行的部署操作：开发环境账户和生产环境账户。部署阶段使用 CodePipeline 调用的 AWS CloudFormation 操作来部署基础设施。 Lambda 函数需要。 一位 DevOps 工程师创建了 CodePipeline 管道，并配置该管道使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）为 Amazon S3 管理的密钥（aws/s3 密钥）对构建工件进行加密。这些工件存储在 S3 存储桶中。当管道运行 时，CloudFormation 操作会因访问被拒绝而失败。 开发运维工程师必须执行哪两项操作才能解决此错误？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 bucket in each AWS account for the artifacts. Allow the pipeline to write to the S3 buckets. Create a CodePipeline S3 action to copy the artifacts to the S3 bucket in each AWS account. Update the CloudFormation actions to reference the artifacts S3 bucket in the production account.","B":"Create a customer managed KMS key. Configure the KMS key policy to allow the IAM roles used by the CloudFormation action to perform decrypt operations. Modify the pipeline to use the customer managed KMS key to encrypt artifacts.","C":"Create an AWS managed KMS key. Configure the KMS key policy to allow the development account and the production account to perform decrypt operations. Modify the pipeline to use the KMS key to encrypt artifacts.","D":"In the development account and in the production account, create an IAM role for CodePipeline. Configure the roles with permissions to perform CloudFormation operations and with permissions to retrieve and decrypt objects from the artifacts S3 bucket. In the CodePipeline account, configure the CodePipeline CloudFormation action to use the roles.","E":"In the development account and in the production account, create an IAM role for CodePipeline. Configure the roles with permissions to perform CloudFormation operations and with permissions to retrieve and decrypt objects from the artifacts S3 bucket. In the CodePipeline account, modify the artifacts S3 bucket policy to allow the roles access. Configure the CodePipeline CloudFormation action to use the roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建一个 S3 存储桶用于存放构建产物。允许管道向这些 S3 存储桶写入内容。创 建一个 CodePipeline S3 操作，将构建产物复制到每个 AWS 账户中的 S3 存储桶。更新 CloudFormation 操作以引用生产账户中的构建产物 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建一个客户管理的 KMS 密钥。配置 KMS 密钥策略，允许 CloudFormation 操作所使用的 IAM 角 色执行解密操作。修改管道以使用客户管理的 KMS 密钥对工件进行加密。","C":"创建一个由 AWS 管理的 KMS 密钥。配置 KMS 密钥策略，允许开发账户和生产账户执行解密操作。 修改管道以使用 KMS 密钥对工件进行加密。","D":"在开发账户和生产账户中，为 CodePipeline 创建一个 IAM 角色。配置这些角色，使其具有执行 CloudFormation 操作的权限以及从制品 S3 存储桶中检索和解密对象的权限。在 CodePipeline 账 户中，配置 CodePipeline 的 CloudFormation 操作以使用这些角色。","E":"在开发账户和生产账户中，为 CodePipeline 创建一个 IAM 角色。配置这些角色，使其具有执行 CloudFormation 操作的权限以及从制品 S3 存储桶中检索和解密对象的权限。在 CodePipeline 账户中， 修改制品 S3 存储桶策略以允许这些角色访问。配置 CodePipeline 的 CloudFormation 操作以使用这 些角色。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Cross-account CodePipeline deployment requires two things that together resolve the access-denied error. First (B), the pipeline must encrypt artifacts with a customer managed KMS key whose key policy grants the cross-account IAM roles (used by the CloudFormation actions in the dev and prod accounts) decrypt permissions. The AWS managed aws/s3 key cannot be used for cross-account access because its key policy is not editable, so the other accounts can never be granted kms:Decrypt on it. The AWS cross-account walkthrough explicitly states you must create or use a customer managed key and grant its usage to AccountB. Second (E), in each target account you create an IAM role with permissions to perform CloudFormation operations and to retrieve and decrypt the artifacts, the pipeline (AccountA) artifacts S3 bucket policy must be modified to grant those roles access, and the CloudFormation action is configured with that role's ARN (roleArn). Cross-account S3 access requires BOTH an identity policy on the assuming role AND a resource-based bucket policy granting the other account, which is why E (which adds the bucket policy step) is correct and D (which omits it) is incomplete. The decisive qualifier is completeness: D fails because without the bucket policy the assumed role still cannot read the artifacts in the pipeline account's bucket.","explanation_zh":"跨帳戶 CodePipeline 部署需要兩件事共同解決 access denied 錯誤。第一 (B)，pipeline 必須使用 customer managed KMS key 加密 artifacts，且該金鑰的 key policy 要授予 dev 與 prod 帳戶中 CloudFormation action 所使用的跨帳戶 IAM role 解密權限。AWS managed aws/s3 key 無法用於跨帳戶存取，因為其 key policy 不可編輯，其他帳戶永遠無法被授予 kms:Decrypt。AWS 官方跨帳戶教學明確指出必須建立或使用 customer managed key 並將使用權授予 AccountB。第二 (E)，在每個目標帳戶建立具有執行 CloudFormation 操作以及擷取並解密 artifacts 權限的 IAM role，pipeline 帳戶 (AccountA) 的 artifacts S3 bucket policy 必須修改以授權這些 role 存取，且 CloudFormation action 需以該 role 的 ARN (roleArn) 設定。跨帳戶 S3 存取同時需要被擔任 role 的身分政策以及授權對方帳戶的 resource-based bucket policy，因此包含 bucket policy 步驟的 E 才正確，而省略此步驟的 D 不完整。決定性的關鍵字是完整性：D 失敗是因為缺少 bucket policy，被擔任的 role 仍無法讀取 pipeline 帳戶 bucket 中的 artifacts。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Copying artifacts into a separate S3 bucket in each account is not the AWS-documented cross-account pattern and does not address the KMS access-denied root cause. The CloudFormation actions fail because of KMS decrypt and cross-account role/bucket permissions, not because the artifacts live in the pipeline account; duplicating buckets adds overhead and still requires the role/key/bucket-policy fixes.","why_zh":"將 artifacts 複製到每個帳戶的獨立 S3 bucket 並非 AWS 官方文件的跨帳戶模式，也未解決 KMS access denied 的根因。CloudFormation action 失敗是因為 KMS 解密與跨帳戶 role/bucket 權限，而非 artifacts 位於 pipeline 帳戶；複製 bucket 增加額外負擔且仍需修正 role/key/bucket policy。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot create an AWS managed KMS key, nor edit its key policy, so granting the dev and prod accounts decrypt operations on an AWS managed key is impossible. AWS managed keys are created and controlled by the owning AWS service; cross-account sharing requires a customer managed key (as in B).","why_zh":"你無法建立 AWS managed KMS key，也無法編輯其 key policy，因此無法在 AWS managed key 上授予 dev 與 prod 帳戶解密操作。AWS managed key 由擁有的 AWS 服務建立與控制；跨帳戶共享需使用 customer managed key（即 B）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is nearly correct but omits modifying the artifacts S3 bucket policy in the pipeline account. Cross-account access to an S3 bucket requires a resource-based bucket policy granting the other account in addition to the role's identity policy; without it the assumed role still gets access denied retrieving the artifacts. E is the complete version of D.","why_zh":"此選項幾乎正確，但省略了修改 pipeline 帳戶中 artifacts S3 bucket policy。跨帳戶存取 S3 bucket 除了 role 的身分政策外，還需要授權對方帳戶的 resource-based bucket policy；缺少時被擔任的 role 仍會在擷取 artifacts 時 access denied。E 是 D 的完整版本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/pipelines-create-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codepipeline-pipeline-encryptionkey.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":122,"question_en":"A company is using an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The company’s development team wants to use AWS Lambda functions to meet resiliency requirements and is rewriting all applications to work with Lambda functions that are deployed in a VPC. The development team is using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) as shared storage in Account A in the organization. The company wants to continue to use Amazon EFS with Lambda. Company policy requires all serverless projects to be deployed in Account B. A DevOps engineer needs to reconfigure an existing EFS file system to allow Lambda functions to access the data through an existing EFS access point. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 组织中的一个组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司的开发团队希望使用 AWS Lambda 函数来满足弹性要求，并正在将所有应用程序重写为与部署在 VPC 中的 Lambda 函数配合使用。 开发团队在组织中的账户 A 中使用 Amazon Elastic File System（Amazon EFS）作为共享存储。 该公司希望继续在 Lambda 中使用亚马逊 EFS。公司政策要求所有无服务器项目都部署在账户 B 中。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要重新配置现有的 EFS 文件系统，以便 Lambda 函数能够通过现有的 EFS 访问点 访问数据。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the EFS file system policy to provide Account B with access to mount and write to the EFS file system in Account A.","B":"Create SCPs to set permission guardrails with fine-grained control for Amazon EFS.","C":"Create a new EFS file system in Account B. Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to keep data from Account A and Account B synchronized.","D":"Update the Lambda execution roles with permission to access the VPC and the EFS file system.","E":"Create a VPC peering connection to connect Account A to Account B.","F":"Configure the Lambda functions in Account B to assume an existing IAM role in Account A."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 EFS 文件系统策略，为账户 B 提供访问账户 A 中 EFS 文件系统并进行挂载和写入的权限。","B":"创建 SCP 以对 Amazon EFS 设置具有细粒度控制的权限防护栏。","C":"在账户 B 中创建一个新的 EFS 文件系统。使用 AWS 数据库迁移服务（AWS DMS）保持账户 A 和账户 B 中的数据同步。","D":"更新 Lambda 执行角色，使其具有访问 VPC 和 EFS 文件系统的权限。","E":"创建一个 VPC 对等连接，将账户 A 与账户 B 连接起来。","F":"在账户 B 中配置 Lambda 函数以承担账户 A 中现有的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The EFS file system lives in Account A and Lambda must run in Account B, so three things are needed. (A) The EFS file system policy is a resource-based policy; it can name a principal (the Lambda execution role/account) and grant elasticfilesystem:ClientMount and ClientWrite so Account B can mount and write to the file system in Account A. (D) The Lambda execution role must carry the elasticfilesystem permissions (ClientMount/ClientWrite) AND the VPC connection permissions (AWSLambdaVPCAccessExecutionRole) - Lambda's own docs require both to attach the function to a VPC and reach EFS over NFS port 2049. (E) EFS is mounted over the local network inside a VPC; because the file system is in a different VPC/account, the function's VPC must be peered to the file system's VPC. AWS's 'Giving Lambda functions access to a resource in an Amazon VPC in another account' guide and the EFS-for-Lambda pricing note ('Lambda charges for data transfer between VPCs ... if your function's VPC is peered to another VPC with a file system') both confirm VPC peering is the cross-account/cross-VPC mechanism.","explanation_zh":"EFS file system 位於 Account A，而 Lambda 必須在 Account B 執行，因此需要三項設定。(A) EFS file system policy 是 resource-based policy，可指定 principal（Lambda execution role/帳號）並授予 elasticfilesystem:ClientMount 與 ClientWrite，讓 Account B 能掛載並寫入 Account A 的 file system。(D) Lambda execution role 必須同時具備 elasticfilesystem 權限（ClientMount/ClientWrite）以及 VPC 連線權限（AWSLambdaVPCAccessExecutionRole）；Lambda 官方文件要求兩者都要有，才能將函式連接到 VPC 並透過 NFS port 2049 存取 EFS。(E) EFS 是在 VPC 內透過本地網路掛載；由於 file system 位於不同 VPC/帳號，函式所在的 VPC 必須與 file system 的 VPC 建立 VPC peering。AWS 的「Giving Lambda functions access to a resource in an Amazon VPC in another account」指南，以及 EFS-for-Lambda 的定價說明（『Lambda charges for data transfer between VPCs ... if your function's VPC is peered to another VPC with a file system』）都證實 VPC peering 是跨帳號/跨 VPC 的存取機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"SCPs only set permission guardrails (maximum boundaries) across the organization; they never grant access. Restricting EFS via SCPs does nothing to enable cross-account mount/write and is not a required step here.","why_zh":"SCP 只能設定組織層級的權限護欄（上限邊界），永遠不會『授予』存取權。用 SCP 限制 EFS 對於啟用跨帳號掛載/寫入毫無幫助，並非此情境所需的步驟。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The requirement is to keep using and reconfigure the EXISTING EFS file system, not to duplicate it. AWS DMS migrates databases, not POSIX file systems, so it cannot synchronize EFS data; this contradicts the stated goal.","why_zh":"需求是繼續使用並重新設定『既有』的 EFS file system，而非複製一份。AWS DMS 用於遷移資料庫而非 POSIX 檔案系統，無法同步 EFS 資料，與題目目標相違背。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"EFS access is not granted by assuming a role in Account A. Access is controlled by the network path (mount target reachable via VPC peering), the EFS file system policy, and the function's execution role permissions - not by cross-account role assumption from the Lambda function.","why_zh":"EFS 存取並非透過在 Account A 扮演（assume）角色取得。存取由網路路徑（透過 VPC peering 可達的 mount target）、EFS file system policy 以及函式的 execution role 權限控制，而非由 Lambda 函式跨帳號 assume role。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-filesystem-efs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/security_iam_resource-based-policy-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/manage-fs-access-vpc-peering.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":123,"question_en":"A media company has several thousand Amazon EC2 instances in an AWS account. The company is using Slack and a shared email inbox for team communications and important updates. A DevOps engineer needs to send all AWS-scheduled EC2 maintenance notifications to the Slack channel and the shared inbox. The solution must include the instances’ Name and Owner tags. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家媒体公司在其 AWS 账户中拥有数千个 Amazon EC2 实例。该公司使用 Slack 和一个共享的电子邮件 收件箱来进行团队沟通和重要更新。一位 DevOps 工程师需要将所有 AWS 安排的 EC2 维护通知发送到 Slack 频道和共享收件箱。解决方案必须包含实例的“名称”和“所有者”标签。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Integrate AWS Trusted Advisor with AWS Config. Configure a custom AWS Config rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to publish notifications to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe a Slack channel endpoint and the shared inbox to the topic.","B":"Use Amazon EventBridge to monitor for AWS Health events. Configure the maintenance events to target an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe an AWS Lambda function to the SNS topic to send notifications to the Slack channel and the shared inbox.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that sends EC2 maintenance notifications to the Slack channel and the shared inbox. Monitor EC2 health events by using Amazon CloudWatch metrics. Configure a CloudWatch alarm that invokes the Lambda function when a maintenance notification is received.","D":"Configure AWS Support integration with AWS CloudTrail. Create a CloudTrail lookup event to invoke an AWS Lambda function to pass EC2 maintenance notifications to Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). Configure Amazon SNS to target the Slack channel and the shared inbox."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AWS Trusted Advisor 与 AWS Config 集成。配置自定义的 AWS Config 规则，以调用 AWS Lambda 函 数向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题发布通知。将 Slack 通道端点和共享收件箱 订阅到该主题。","B":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 监控 AWS Health 事件。将维护事件配置为指向 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题。订阅 SNS 主题以将通知发送到 Slack 频道和共享收件箱。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 EC2 维护通知发送到 Slack 频道和共享收件箱。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 指标监控 EC2 健康事件。配置一个 CloudWatch 警报，当收到维护通知时调用 Lambda 函 数。","D":"配置 AWS 支持与 AWS CloudTrail 的集成。创建 CloudTrail 查找事件以调用 AWS Lambda 函数，将 EC2 维护通知传递给 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）。配置 Amazon SNS 以将通知发送至 Slack 频道和共享收件箱。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS-scheduled EC2 maintenance (retirements, reboots, system maintenance) is surfaced as AWS Health events. The official AWS Health documentation states you use Amazon EventBridge to detect and react to AWS Health events (source aws.health) and explicitly gives the example: 'you can use a Lambda function to pass a notification to a Slack channel when an AWS Health event occurs,' with Amazon SNS topics being a supported EventBridge target. So EventBridge rules match the maintenance events, target an SNS topic, and a Lambda subscriber formats and delivers the message to both the Slack channel and the shared email inbox. The instances' Name and Owner tags requirement is met because EC2 lets you customize scheduled event notifications to include tags (register-instance-event-notification-attributes), and the AWS Health event schema includes affected entities/resources. This is exactly option B.","explanation_zh":"AWS 排程的 EC2 維護（instance retirement、重啟、系統維護）會以 AWS Health 事件形式發布。官方 AWS Health 文件指出可使用 Amazon EventBridge 偵測並回應 AWS Health 事件（source 為 aws.health），並明確舉例『可使用 Lambda function 在 AWS Health 事件發生時將通知傳送到 Slack 頻道』，且 Amazon SNS topic 為支援的 EventBridge target。因此由 EventBridge rule 比對維護事件、target 指向 SNS topic，再由訂閱該 topic 的 Lambda 格式化並送到 Slack 頻道與共用信箱。Name 與 Owner tag 的需求亦可滿足，因為 EC2 允許自訂排程事件通知以包含 tag（register-instance-event-notification-attributes），且 AWS Health 事件 schema 也含受影響資源資訊。這正是選項 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor and AWS Config evaluate configuration/best-practice compliance, not AWS-scheduled EC2 maintenance. A custom Config rule is triggered by configuration changes, not by upcoming maintenance/retirement events, so it cannot detect scheduled EC2 maintenance notifications.","why_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 與 AWS Config 是評估組態與最佳實務合規，並非 AWS 排程的 EC2 維護。自訂 Config rule 由組態變更觸發，無法偵測即將到來的維護/退役事件，因此無法擷取排程 EC2 維護通知。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no CloudWatch metric that represents AWS-scheduled EC2 maintenance notifications, and CloudWatch alarms act on metric thresholds, not on maintenance/health events. EC2 status-check metrics are not the same as scheduled maintenance, so an alarm cannot reliably fire when a maintenance notification is received.","why_zh":"並不存在代表 AWS 排程 EC2 維護通知的 CloudWatch 指標，且 CloudWatch alarm 是針對指標門檻動作，並非針對維護/health 事件。EC2 狀態檢查指標與排程維護不同，因此 alarm 無法在收到維護通知時可靠觸發。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail records API activity for auditing; a CloudTrail 'lookup event' is a manual/historical query, not an event-driven trigger that invokes Lambda on maintenance events. There is no 'AWS Support integration with CloudTrail' mechanism that delivers scheduled EC2 maintenance notifications.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄 API 活動以供稽核；CloudTrail 的 lookup event 是手動/歷史查詢，並非在維護事件發生時呼叫 Lambda 的事件驅動觸發器。也不存在所謂『AWS Support 與 CloudTrail 整合』來傳遞排程 EC2 維護通知的機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/cloudwatch-events-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/customizing_scheduled_event_notifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/aws-health-events-eventbridge-schema.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":124,"question_en":"An AWS CodePipeline pipeline has implemented a code release process. The pipeline is integrated with AWS CodeDeploy to deploy versions of an application to multiple Amazon EC2 instances for each CodePipeline stage. During a recent deployment, the pipeline failed due to a CodeDeploy issue. The DevOps team wants to improve monitoring and notifications during deployment to decrease resolution times. What should the DevOps engineer do to create notifications when issues are discovered?","question_zh":"一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道已实现代码发布流程。该管道与 AWS CodeDeploy 集成，以便在每个 CodePipeline 阶段将应用程序的版本部署到多个 Amazon EC2 实例上。 在最近的一次部署中，由于 CodeDeploy 出现问题，管道部署失败。DevOps 团队希望改进部署期间的监 控和通知，以缩短问题解决时间。 当发现问题时，开发运维工程师应该怎么做才能创建通知？","options_en":{"A":"Implement Amazon CloudWatch Logs for CodePipeline and CodeDeploy, create an AWS Config rule to evaluate code deployment issues, and create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify stakeholders of deployment issues.","B":"Implement Amazon EventBridge for CodePipeline and CodeDeploy, create an AWS Lambda function to evaluate code deployment issues, and create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify stakeholders of deployment issues.","C":"Implement AWS CloudTrail to record CodePipeline and CodeDeploy API call information, create an AWS Lambda function to evaluate code deployment issues, and create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify stakeholders of deployment issues.","D":"Implement Amazon EventBridge for CodePipeline and CodeDeploy, create an Amazon Inspector assessment target to evaluate code deployment issues, and create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify stakeholders of deployment issues."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 CodePipeline 和 CodeDeploy 实施 Amazon CloudWatch 日志，创建一个 AWS Config 规则来评估代码部 署问题，并创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题，以通知相关方部署问题。","B":"在 CodePipeline 和 CodeDeploy 中实现 Amazon EventBridge，创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来评估代码部署 问题，并创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，以通知相关方部署问题。","C":"实施 AWS CloudTrail 来记录 CodePipeline 和 CodeDeploy 的 API 调用信息，创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数 来评估代码部署问题，并创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题来通知相关 方部署问题。","D":"为 CodePipeline 和 CodeDeploy 实施 Amazon EventBridge，创建 Amazon Inspector 评估目标以评估代 码部署问题，并创建 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题以通知相关方部署问题。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Both CodePipeline and CodeDeploy emit state-change events (including deployment/stage/action failures) directly to Amazon EventBridge, which is the AWS-recommended near-real-time eventing mechanism for these services. EventBridge rules can target AWS Lambda (to evaluate/filter the event and determine the nature of the deployment issue) and Amazon SNS (to notify stakeholders). The CodeDeploy 'Logging and monitoring' guide explicitly lists Lambda functions and SNS topics as valid event targets and gives the exact use case 'Use a Lambda function to pass a notification... whenever deployments fail.' The CodePipeline 'Monitoring CodePipeline events' guide states EventBridge 'routes that data to targets such as AWS Lambda and Amazon Simple Notification Service.' Option B is the only choice that combines the correct event source (EventBridge), a valid evaluation mechanism (Lambda), and the correct notification target (SNS).","explanation_zh":"CodePipeline 與 CodeDeploy 都會將狀態變更事件（包含部署/階段/動作失敗）直接送往 Amazon EventBridge，這是 AWS 建議用於這兩個服務的近即時事件機制。EventBridge 規則可以將事件導向 AWS Lambda（用以評估與過濾事件、判斷部署問題的性質）以及 Amazon SNS（通知相關人員）。CodeDeploy 的「Logging and monitoring」文件明確列出 Lambda function 與 SNS topic 為有效的事件目標，並給出確切用例：「使用 Lambda function 在部署失敗時傳送通知」。CodePipeline 的「Monitoring CodePipeline events」文件指出 EventBridge 會「將資料導向諸如 AWS Lambda 與 Amazon SNS 等目標」。選項 B 是唯一同時結合正確事件來源（EventBridge）、有效評估機制（Lambda）與正確通知目標（SNS）的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config evaluates resource configuration compliance, not real-time CodeDeploy/CodePipeline deployment state changes or failures. There is no AWS Config rule that detects a failed deployment event, so this cannot drive deployment-failure notifications.","why_zh":"AWS Config 評估的是資源組態合規性，而非即時的 CodeDeploy/CodePipeline 部署狀態變更或失敗。沒有任何 AWS Config rule 能偵測部署失敗事件，因此無法用於部署失敗通知。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudTrail records API calls for auditing and is not designed for near-real-time deployment-failure alerting; it has delivery latency and captures management API activity rather than service state-change events. EventBridge is the AWS-preferred mechanism for reacting to deployment state changes.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄 API 呼叫以供稽核，並非設計用於近即時的部署失敗告警；它有傳遞延遲且擷取的是管理 API 活動，而非服務狀態變更事件。EventBridge 才是 AWS 建議用來回應部署狀態變更的機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability/security assessment service for workloads (EC2, ECR, Lambda); an Inspector assessment target cannot evaluate CodeDeploy/CodePipeline deployment failures. It is the wrong tool for parsing and reacting to deployment events.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是針對工作負載（EC2、ECR、Lambda）的弱點/安全評估服務；Inspector assessment target 無法評估 CodeDeploy/CodePipeline 的部署失敗。它並非用來解析與回應部署事件的正確工具。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/detect-state-changes-cloudwatch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/incident-response.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codedeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codepipeline.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":125,"question_en":"A global company manages multiple AWS accounts by using AWS Control Tower. The company hosts internal applications and public applications. Each application team in the company has its own AWS account for application hosting. The accounts are consolidated in an organization in AWS Organizations. One of the AWS Control Tower member accounts serves as a centralized DevOps account with CI/CD pipelines that application teams use to deploy applications to their respective target AWS accounts. An IAM role for deployment exists in the centralized DevOps account. An application team is attempting to deploy its application to an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster in an application AWS account. An IAM role for deployment exists in the application AWS account. The deployment is through an AWS CodeBuild project that is set up in the centralized DevOps account. The CodeBuild project uses an IAM service role for CodeBuild. The deployment is failing with an Unauthorized error during attempts to connect to the cross-account EKS cluster from CodeBuild. Which solution will resolve this error?","question_zh":"一家全球性公司通过使用 AWS 控制塔来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司托管内部应用程序和公共应用 程序。 公司内的每个应用团队都有自己的 AWS 账户用于应用托管。这些账户在 AWS Organizations 中整合到一 个组织中。AWS Control Tower 成员账户中的一个账户作为集中式的 DevOps 账户，拥有应用团队用于将 应用部署到各自目标 AWS 账户的 CI/CD 管道。集中式的 DevOps 账户中存在一个用于部署的 IAM 角色。 一个应用程序团队正试图将其应用程序部署到应用程序 AWS 账户中的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service （Amazon EKS）集群。应用程序 AWS 账户中存在用于部署的 IAM 角色。部署是通过设置在集中式 DevOps 账户中的 AWS CodeBuild 项目进行的。CodeBuild 项目使用 CodeBuild 的 IAM 服务角色。在从 CodeBuild 连接到跨账户 EKS 集群时，部署因未经授权的错误而失败。 哪种解决方案能解决这个错误？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the application account’s deployment IAM role to have a trust relationship with the centralized DevOps account. Configure the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action. Configure the application account’s deployment IAM role to have the required access to the EKS cluster. Configure the EKS cluster aws-auth ConfigMap to map the role to the appropriate system permissions.","B":"Configure the centralized DevOps account’s deployment IAM role to have a trust relationship with the application account. Configure the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action. Configure the centralized DevOps account’s deployment IAM role to allow the required access to CodeBuild.","C":"Configure the centralized DevOps account’s deployment IAM role to have a trust relationship with the application account. Configure the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML action. Configure the centralized DevOps account’s deployment IAM role to allow the required access to CodeBuild.","D":"Configure the application account’s deployment IAM role to have a trust relationship with the AWS Control Tower management account. Configure the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action. Configure the application account’s deployment IAM role to have the required access to the EKS cluster. Configure the EKS cluster aws-auth ConfigMap to map the role to the appropriate system permissions."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置应用程序账户的部署 IAM 角色与集中式 DevOps 账户建立信任关系。配置该信任关系以允 许执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。配置应用程序账户的部署 IAM 角色以获取对 EKS 集群的必要访 问权限。配置 EKS 集群的 aws-auth ConfigMap 以将该角色映射到适当的系统权限。","B":"配置集中式 DevOps 账户的部署 IAM 角色与应用账户建立信任关系。配置该信任关系以允许执行 sts: AssumeRole 操作。配置集中式 DevOps 账户的部署 IAM 角色以允许对 CodeBuild 进行所需访问。","C":"配置集中式 DevOps 账户的部署 IAM 角色，使其与应用账户建立信任关系。配置该信任关系以允许 执行 sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML 操作。配置集中式 DevOps 账户的部署 IAM 角色，使其能够访问 CodeBuild 所需的权限。","D":"配置应用程序账户的部署 IAM 角色与 AWS Control Tower 管理账户建立信任关系。配置信任关系以允 许执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。配置应用程序账户的部署 IAM 角色以获取对 EKS 集群的必要访问权 限。配置 EKS 集群的 aws-auth ConfigMap 以将该角色映射到适当的系统权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeBuild runs in the centralized DevOps account and must reach an EKS cluster in the application account. The correct cross-account pattern is for CodeBuild (DevOps account) to assume a deployment role that lives in the application account where the cluster resides. For that to work, the application-account role's trust policy must allow the DevOps account principal to call sts:AssumeRole, and the role must hold the IAM permissions needed for the EKS API (for example eks:DescribeCluster). The decisive clue is the 'Unauthorized' error: this is a Kubernetes RBAC authorization failure surfaced by the AWS IAM Authenticator, meaning the IAM principal authenticated to the cluster but is not mapped to any Kubernetes group. Resolving it requires mapping that application-account role in the cluster's aws-auth ConfigMap (or an access entry) to the appropriate system permissions. Option A is the only choice that both points the trust the correct direction (application-account role trusts the DevOps account) and adds the aws-auth ConfigMap mapping that clears the Unauthorized error.","explanation_zh":"CodeBuild 執行於集中式 DevOps 帳戶，必須存取位於應用程式帳戶中的 EKS 叢集。正確的跨帳戶模式是讓 CodeBuild（DevOps 帳戶）assume 一個存在於叢集所在的應用程式帳戶的部署角色。為此，該應用程式帳戶角色的信任政策必須允許 DevOps 帳戶主體執行 sts:AssumeRole，且該角色須具備呼叫 EKS API 所需的 IAM 權限（例如 eks:DescribeCluster）。關鍵線索是 'Unauthorized' 錯誤：這是由 AWS IAM Authenticator 回報的 Kubernetes RBAC 授權失敗，代表該 IAM 主體已通過叢集驗證，但未對應到任何 Kubernetes group。要解決就必須在叢集的 aws-auth ConfigMap（或 access entry）中將該應用程式帳戶角色對應到適當的 system 權限。選項 A 是唯一同時把信任方向設定正確（應用程式帳戶角色信任 DevOps 帳戶）並加入 aws-auth ConfigMap 對應以清除 Unauthorized 錯誤的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Trust direction is reversed (the DevOps role trusts the application account, but CodeBuild in DevOps needs to assume INTO the application account) and it never maps any role in the EKS aws-auth ConfigMap, so the Kubernetes Unauthorized error would persist.","why_zh":"信任方向相反（DevOps 角色信任應用程式帳戶，但位於 DevOps 的 CodeBuild 需要 assume 進入應用程式帳戶），且完全沒有在 EKS aws-auth ConfigMap 中對應任何角色，因此 Kubernetes 的 Unauthorized 錯誤仍會存在。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same reversed trust direction as B, and it uses sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML which is for SAML identity federation that does not apply here; it also omits the aws-auth ConfigMap mapping.","why_zh":"信任方向與 B 一樣相反，且使用 sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML（用於 SAML 身分聯合，與此情境無關），同樣未處理 aws-auth ConfigMap 對應。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It maps the ConfigMap correctly but trusts the wrong account: it has the application-account role trust the Control Tower management account, whereas CodeBuild actually runs in the centralized DevOps member account, so the AssumeRole call would still fail.","why_zh":"ConfigMap 對應正確，但信任了錯誤的帳戶：讓應用程式帳戶角色信任 Control Tower 管理帳戶，而 CodeBuild 實際上是執行於集中式 DevOps 成員帳戶，因此 AssumeRole 呼叫仍會失敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/security-iam-troubleshoot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/auth-configmap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/grant-k8s-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_common-scenarios_aws-accounts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":126,"question_en":"A highly regulated company has a policy that DevOps engineers should not log in to their Amazon EC2 instances except in emergencies. If a DevOps engineer does log in, the security team must be notified within 15 minutes of the occurrence. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家受到严格监管的公司规定，DevOps 工程师除非在紧急情况下，否则不得登录其亚马逊 EC2 实例。 如果 DevOps 工程师确实登录了，安全团队必须在事件发生后的 15 分钟内得到通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Install the Amazon Inspector agent on each EC2 instance. Subscribe to Amazon EventBridge notifications. Invoke an AWS Lambda function to check if a message is about user logins. If it is, send a notification to the security team using Amazon SNS.","B":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on each EC2 instance. Configure the agent to push all logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and set up a CloudWatch metric filter that searches for user logins. If a login is found, send a notification to the security team using Amazon SNS.","C":"Set up AWS CloudTrail with Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Subscribe CloudWatch Logs to Amazon Kinesis. Attach AWS Lambda to Kinesis to parse and determine if a log contains a user login. If it does, send a notification to the security team using Amazon SNS.","D":"Set up a script on each Amazon EC2 instance to push all logs to Amazon S3. Set up an S3 event to invoke an AWS Lambda function, which invokes an Amazon Athena query to run. The Athena query checks for logins and sends the output to the security team using Amazon SNS."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon Inspector 代理。订阅 Amazon EventBridge 通知。调用 AWS Lambda 函 数检查消息是否与用户登录有关。如果是，则使用 Amazon SNS 向安全团队发送通知。","B":"在每个 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理。配置代理将所有日志推送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，并设置一个 CloudWatch 指标过滤器以搜索用户登录信息。如果发现登录信息，则使用 Amazon SNS 向安全团队发送通知。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 设置 AWS CloudTrail。将 CloudWatch Logs 订阅到 Amazon Kinesis。将 AWS Lambda 附加到 Kinesis 以解析日志并确定其是否包含用户登录信息。如果包含，则使用 Amazon SNS 向安全团队发送通知。","D":"在每个 Amazon EC2 实例上设置一个脚本，将所有日志推送到 Amazon S3。设置一个 S3 事件以调 用 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 Amazon Athena 查询来运行。Athena 查询检查登录情况，并使 用 Amazon SNS 将输出发送给安全团队。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is to detect OS-level interactive user logins (SSH/RDP) on EC2 instances and alert the security team within 15 minutes. The CloudWatch agent is installed on each instance and streams the OS authentication logs (Linux /var/log/secure or /var/log/auth.log, Windows Security event log) to CloudWatch Logs. A CloudWatch Logs metric filter scans log data as it arrives for login patterns (for example 'session opened' or 'Accepted password') and increments a metric; a CloudWatch alarm on that metric then publishes to an Amazon SNS topic to notify the security team. This is the documented 'Alarming on logs' pattern (metric filter to alarm to SNS notification), and alarm evaluation periods of 1-5 minutes comfortably meet the 15-minute SLA. The other options rely on services that do not capture OS-level logins (Inspector, CloudTrail) or use high-latency batch architectures (Athena over S3).","explanation_zh":"需求是偵測 EC2 instance 上的 OS 層級互動式使用者登入 (SSH/RDP)，並在 15 分鐘內通知安全團隊。CloudWatch agent 安裝在每台 instance 上，將 OS 驗證日誌 (Linux 的 /var/log/secure 或 /var/log/auth.log、Windows 的 Security event log) 串流到 CloudWatch Logs。CloudWatch Logs metric filter 在日誌進入時即時掃描登入模式 (例如 'session opened' 或 'Accepted password') 並遞增一個 metric；接著針對該 metric 的 CloudWatch alarm 發佈到 Amazon SNS topic 來通知安全團隊。這正是官方文件中的 'Alarming on logs' 模式 (metric filter 到 alarm 再到 SNS 通知)，而 alarm 的評估週期 (1-5 分鐘) 可輕鬆滿足 15 分鐘的 SLA。其他選項所依賴的服務無法擷取 OS 層級登入 (Inspector、CloudTrail)，或採用高延遲的批次架構 (Athena over S3)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability/security assessment service (CVE scanning, configuration and network reachability analysis). Its agent does not capture or emit OS-level interactive login events, so there is no 'user login' message in EventBridge for Lambda to inspect. It conflates services.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是漏洞/安全評估服務 (CVE 掃描、組態與網路可達性分析)。其 agent 不會擷取或發出 OS 層級的互動式登入事件，因此 EventBridge 中根本不存在可供 Lambda 檢查的 'user login' 訊息，屬於服務概念混淆。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail records AWS API/management-plane and data events, not OS-level interactive SSH/RDP logins inside the instance operating system. An SSH/RDP session generates no CloudTrail event, so parsing CloudTrail via Kinesis and Lambda would never see the login. The pipeline is also needlessly complex and higher latency.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API/管理層與資料事件，而非 instance 作業系統內的 OS 層級互動式 SSH/RDP 登入。SSH/RDP 連線不會產生 CloudTrail 事件，因此經由 Kinesis 與 Lambda 解析 CloudTrail 永遠看不到登入，且該管線過於複雜且延遲較高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Athena is an ad-hoc interactive query service over S3, not a real-time alerting mechanism. A batch script pushing logs to S3, then triggering an Athena query per object on S3 events, is fragile, high-latency, and operationally heavy, and cannot reliably guarantee notification within the 15-minute window.","why_zh":"Athena 是針對 S3 的臨時互動式查詢服務，並非即時告警機制。以批次腳本將日誌推送到 S3、再由 S3 事件對每個物件觸發 Athena 查詢的做法既脆弱、高延遲又營運負擔重，無法可靠地保證在 15 分鐘內通知。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Alarm-On-Logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Agent-on-EC2-Instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/logging-management-events-with-cloudtrail.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":127,"question_en":"A company updated the AWS CloudFormation template for a critical business application. The stack update process failed due to an error in the updated template, and AWS CloudFormation automatically began the stack rollback process. Later, a DevOps engineer discovered that the application was still unavailable and that the stack was in the UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED state. Which combination of actions should the DevOps engineer perform so that the stack rollback can complete successfully? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司更新了关键业务应用程序的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。由于更新后的模板存在错误，堆栈更 新过程失败，AWS CloudFormation 自动开始执行堆栈回滚操作。后来，一位 DevOps 工程师发现应用程 序仍不可用，且堆栈处于 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 状态。 DevOps 工程师应执行哪两种操作组合才能使堆栈回滚成功完成？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Attach the AWSCloudFormationFullAccess IAM policy to the AWS CloudFormation role.","B":"Automatically recover the stack resources by using AWS CloudFormation drift detection.","C":"Issue a ContinueUpdateRollback command from the AWS CloudFormation console or the AWS CLI.","D":"Manually adjust the resources to match the expectations of the stack.","E":"Update the existing AWS CloudFormation stack by using the original template."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AWSCloudFormationFullAccess IAM 策略附加到 AWS CloudFormation 角色。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 漂移检测自动恢复堆栈资源。","C":"从 AWS CloudFormation 控制台或 AWS CLI 发布 ContinueUpdateRollback 命令。","D":"手动调整资源以符合堆栈的预期。","E":"使用原始模板更新现有的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A stack in UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED state cannot be updated, but it can be returned to UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE so the application becomes available again. Per the official AWS guidance for 'Continue rolling back an update', in most cases you must first manually fix the error that caused the rollback to fail so the actual resources match what CloudFormation expects (D), and then issue the ContinueUpdateRollback command from the console or AWS CLI to complete the rollback (C). The two steps work together: fixing the resource mismatch removes the cause of the failure, and ContinueUpdateRollback then drives the stack from UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED to UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE. After that the engineer can attempt the stack update again. This matches the documented remediation procedure exactly.","explanation_zh":"處於 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 狀態的 stack 無法被更新，但可以被帶回 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE 狀態，讓應用程式恢復可用。根據 AWS 官方「Continue rolling back an update」文件，多數情況下你必須先手動修正導致 rollback 失敗的錯誤，讓實際資源與 CloudFormation 預期一致（D），然後從 console 或 AWS CLI 發出 ContinueUpdateRollback 指令以完成 rollback（C）。兩個步驟相輔相成：修正資源不一致可消除失敗原因，ContinueUpdateRollback 接著將 stack 從 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 推進到 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE，之後工程師即可再次嘗試更新 stack。這完全符合文件記載的補救程序。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Granting AWSCloudFormationFullAccess to the CloudFormation role does not address the UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED condition. The role needs permissions on the underlying resource services (EC2, RDS, etc.), not CloudFormation's own API, and the failure here is caused by a resource state mismatch from the bad template, not a CloudFormation permission gap.","why_zh":"將 AWSCloudFormationFullAccess 授予 CloudFormation role 無法解決 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED。該 role 需要的是底層資源服務（EC2、RDS 等）的權限，而非 CloudFormation 自身 API 權限，且此處失敗是由錯誤範本造成的資源狀態不一致，並非 CloudFormation 權限不足。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Drift detection only reports differences between the stack template and actual resource configuration; it is a read-only diagnostic and cannot automatically recover or modify resources to resolve a failed rollback.","why_zh":"Drift detection 只會回報 stack 範本與實際資源設定的差異，屬於唯讀診斷工具，無法自動復原或修改資源來解決失敗的 rollback。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A stack in UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED state cannot be updated at all, so re-submitting the original template would be rejected. The stack must first reach UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE via ContinueUpdateRollback before any further update can be performed.","why_zh":"處於 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 狀態的 stack 根本無法被更新，因此重新提交原始範本會被拒絕。必須先透過 ContinueUpdateRollback 讓 stack 進入 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE，才能執行後續更新。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-updating-stacks-continueupdaterollback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/APIReference/API_ContinueUpdateRollback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/troubleshooting.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":128,"question_en":"A development team manually builds an artifact locally and then places it in an Amazon S3 bucket. The application has a local cache that must be cleared when a deployment occurs. The team runs a command to do this, downloads the artifact from Amazon S3, and unzips the artifact to complete the deployment. A DevOps team wants to migrate to a CI/CD process and build in checks to stop and roll back the deployment when a failure occurs. This requires the team to track the progression of the deployment. Which combination of actions will accomplish this? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"开发团队在本地手动构建一个工件，然后将其放入 Amazon S3 存储桶中。应用程序有一个本地缓存，在部 署时必须清除。团队运行一个命令来完成此操作，从 Amazon S3 下载工件，并解压工件以完成部署。 一个 DevOps 团队希望迁移到持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流程，并在部署失败时设置检查以停止并 回滚部署。这需要团队跟踪部署的进展情况。 哪些行动组合能够达成此目标？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Allow developers to check the code into a code repository. Using Amazon EventBridge, on every pull into the main branch, invoke an AWS Lambda function to build the artifact and store it in Amazon S3.","B":"Create a custom script to clear the cache. Specify the script in the BeforeInstall lifecycle hook in the AppSpec file.","C":"Create user data for each Amazon EC2 instance that contains the clear cache script. Once deployed, test the application. If it is not successful, deploy it again.","D":"Set up AWS CodePipeline to deploy the application. Allow developers to check the code into a code repository as a source for the pipeline.","E":"Use AWS CodeBuild to build the artifact and place it in Amazon S3. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the artifact to Amazon EC2 instances.","F":"Use AWS Systems Manager to fetch the artifact from Amazon S3 and deploy it to all the instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"允许开发人员将代码提交到代码库。使用 Amazon EventBridge，在每次将代码拉取到主分支时，调用一 个 AWS Lambda 函数来构建工件并将其存储在 Amazon S3 中。","B":"创建一个自定义脚本以清除缓存。在 AppSpec 文件的 BeforeInstall 生命周期钩子中指定该脚本。","C":"为每个包含清除缓存脚本的 Amazon EC2 实例创建用户数据。部署完成后，测试应用程序。如果测试不 成功，请重新部署。","D":"设置 AWS CodePipeline 以部署应用程序。允许开发人员将代码检入代码库作为管道的源代码。","E":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 构建工件并将其放置在 Amazon S3 中。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将工件部署到 Amazon EC2 实例上。","F":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 从 Amazon S3 获取工件并将其部署到所有实例。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario needs a managed CI/CD pipeline that builds an artifact to S3, deploys it to EC2, clears the application cache when a deployment occurs, and stops/rolls back on failure while tracking the progression of the deployment. D establishes AWS CodePipeline with the code repository as the pipeline source; CodePipeline orchestrates the Source/Build/Deploy stages and natively tracks the progression of every pipeline execution, satisfying the CI/CD and progression-tracking requirements. E uses AWS CodeBuild (a managed build service) to produce the artifact and place it in S3, replacing the manual local build, and AWS CodeDeploy to deploy that artifact to the EC2 instances; CodeDeploy supports automatic rollback that redeploys the last known good revision when a deployment fails, satisfying the stop-and-roll-back requirement. B addresses 'clear the cache when a deployment occurs' by running a custom clear-cache script in the BeforeInstall lifecycle hook of the AppSpec file; AWS docs state the EC2/On-Premises BeforeInstall event is a scriptable preinstall hook (for tasks such as decrypting files or backing up the current version) that runs before the new revision is installed. Together B+D+E cover managed build to S3, deploy with automatic rollback, native progression tracking, and per-deployment cache clearing using AWS-native managed services.","explanation_zh":"情境需要一個受管的 CI/CD 流程：建置成品並放到 S3、部署到 EC2、在部署發生時清除應用程式快取、失敗時停止並回復，同時追蹤部署進度。D 建立 AWS CodePipeline 並以程式碼儲存庫作為 pipeline 來源；CodePipeline 協調 Source/Build/Deploy 各階段，並原生追蹤每次 pipeline 執行的進度，滿足 CI/CD 與進度追蹤需求。E 使用受管建置服務 AWS CodeBuild 產生成品並放到 S3（取代手動本機建置），再用 AWS CodeDeploy 將成品部署到 EC2 執行個體；CodeDeploy 支援自動回復（automatic rollback），在部署失敗時重新部署上一個已知良好版本，滿足停止與回復的需求。B 透過在 AppSpec 檔案的 BeforeInstall 生命週期掛勾執行自訂清除快取腳本，解決『部署發生時清除快取』；AWS 文件指出 EC2/On-Premises 的 BeforeInstall 事件是可寫入腳本的安裝前掛勾（用於解密檔案或備份目前版本等任務），會在安裝新版本之前執行。B+D+E 結合即涵蓋受管建置到 S3、含自動回復的部署、原生進度追蹤，以及每次部署的清除快取，全部使用 AWS 原生受管服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Triggering a Lambda function via EventBridge on every pull into main to build the artifact is a fragile custom build path. Lambda is not a managed build service, has runtime/size limits, and on its own provides no deployment progression tracking, no stop/rollback, and no deployment orchestration. AWS CodeBuild (option E) is the native managed build service for this job.","why_zh":"以 EventBridge 在每次合併到 main 時觸發 Lambda 來建置成品是脆弱的自訂建置方式。Lambda 並非受管建置服務，有執行時間與大小限制，本身也無法提供部署進度追蹤、停止/回復或部署協調。AWS CodeBuild（選項 E）才是此工作的原生受管建置服務。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EC2 user data only runs at instance launch, not on each deployment, so it cannot reliably clear the cache 'when a deployment occurs.' Manually testing and 'deploy it again' on failure is not automated stop/rollback and provides no progression tracking, the opposite of the managed CI/CD process the team wants.","why_zh":"EC2 user data 僅在執行個體啟動時執行，而非每次部署，因此無法在『部署發生時』可靠地清除快取。手動測試並在失敗時『再部署一次』不是自動化的停止/回復，也無法追蹤進度，與團隊想要的受管 CI/CD 流程相反。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Using AWS Systems Manager to fetch the artifact and deploy to all instances is a competing deploy mechanism that overlaps with CodeDeploy (option E). It lacks CodeDeploy's lifecycle-hook-based automatic rollback and the integrated CodePipeline deployment progression tracking the scenario demands, and is redundant with E.","why_zh":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 取得成品並部署到所有執行個體，是與 CodeDeploy（選項 E）重疊的競爭部署機制。它缺少 CodeDeploy 基於生命週期掛勾的自動回復，以及情境所需的整合 CodePipeline 部署進度追蹤，且與 E 重複。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-rollback-and-redeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/welcome.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":129,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is working on a project that is hosted on Amazon Linux and has failed a security review. The DevOps manager has been asked to review the company buildspec.yaml file for an AWS CodeBuild project and provide recommendations. The buildspec.yaml file is configured as follows: What changes should be recommended to comply with AWS security best practices? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在处理一个托管在亚马逊 Linux 上的项目，该项目未能通过安全审查。DevOps 经理被要求审查公司 AWS CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec.yaml 文件，并提出建议。该 buildspec.yaml 文件 的配置如下： 为了符合 AWS 安全最佳实践，应推荐哪些变更？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add a post-build command to remove the temporary files from the container before termination to ensure they cannot be seen by other CodeBuild users.","B":"Update the CodeBuild project role with the necessary permissions and then remove the AWS credentials from the environment variable.","C":"Store the DB_PASSWORD as a SecureString value in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store and then remove the DB_PASSWORD from the environment variables.","D":"Move the environment variables to the ‘db-deploy-bucket’ Amazon S3 bucket, add a prebuild stage to download, then export the variables.","E":"Use AWS Systems Manager run command versus scp and ssh commands directly to the instance.","F":"Scramble the environment variables using XOR followed by Base64, add a section to install, and then run XOR and Base64 to the build phase."},"options_zh":{"A":"添加一个构建后命令，在容器终止前删除临时文件，以确保其他 CodeBuild 用户无法看到这些文 件。","B":"使用必要的权限更新 CodeBuild 项目角色，然后从环境变量中移除 AWS 凭证。","C":"将 DB_PASSWORD 作为 SecureString 值存储在 AWS 系统管理器参数存储中，然后从环境变量中移除 DB_PASSWORD。","D":"将环境变量移至“db-deploy-bucket” Amazon S3 存储桶，添加一个预构建阶段以下载这些变量，然 后导出它们。","E":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 的运行命令，而非直接向实例发送 scp 和 ssh 命令。","F":"使用异或运算对环境变量进行打乱，然后进行 Base64 编码，在安装部分添加相关内容，接着在构建 阶段运行异或运算和 Base64 编码。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The buildspec has three concrete security flaws, and B, C, and E each remediate one. (B) The file embeds long-term AWS access keys as environment variables. IAM security best practices and the Well-Architected Framework require workloads on AWS compute (including CodeBuild) to use temporary credentials delivered automatically through an IAM role, not long-lived IAM user keys; therefore you grant the needed permissions to the CodeBuild project (service) role and remove the static credentials. (C) The DB_PASSWORD is a PLAINTEXT environment variable. The CodeBuild EnvironmentVariable API doc states AWS 'strongly discourage the use of PLAINTEXT environment variables to store sensitive values' because they are visible in the console and CLI, and recommends Systems Manager Parameter Store (SecureString / type PARAMETER_STORE) or Secrets Manager, referenced at runtime. (E) The project deploys to the Amazon Linux instance with direct scp/ssh. Systems Manager Session Manager / Run Command is the recommended secure alternative: centralized IAM-based access control, TLS encryption, full session/command logging, and no open inbound SSH ports, bastion hosts, or managed SSH keys. The remaining options are weaker or anti-patterns: A is moot because CodeBuild build containers are ephemeral and isolated per build; D keeps secrets in plaintext and merely relocates the exposure; F is reversible encoding (XOR + Base64), not encryption, and AWS never endorses it over Parameter Store/Secrets Manager/KMS.","explanation_zh":"此 buildspec 有三個明確的安全缺陷，B、C、E 分別修補其一。(B) 檔案以環境變數內嵌長期 AWS access key。IAM 安全最佳實務與 Well-Architected Framework 要求在 AWS 運算服務（含 CodeBuild）上的工作負載使用透過 IAM role 自動派發的臨時憑證，而非長期 IAM user 金鑰；因此應將所需權限授予 CodeBuild 專案（service）role，並移除靜態憑證。(C) DB_PASSWORD 是 PLAINTEXT 環境變數。CodeBuild EnvironmentVariable API 文件明確表示 AWS「強烈不建議使用 PLAINTEXT 環境變數儲存敏感值」，因為在 console 與 CLI 會以明文顯示，並建議改存於 Systems Manager Parameter Store（SecureString / 類型 PARAMETER_STORE）或 Secrets Manager，於執行期再引用。(E) 專案以直接 scp/ssh 部署到 Amazon Linux 執行個體。Systems Manager Session Manager / Run Command 是建議的安全替代方案：提供集中式 IAM 存取控制、TLS 加密、完整的 session/command 記錄，並免除開放 SSH 入站埠、bastion host 與管理 SSH 金鑰的需求。其餘選項較弱或屬反模式：A 無意義，因為 CodeBuild build 容器短暫且每次建置隔離；D 仍以明文保存秘密，只是搬移暴露點；F 屬可逆編碼（XOR + Base64）而非加密，AWS 從不建議以此取代 Parameter Store/Secrets Manager/KMS。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodeBuild build containers are ephemeral and isolated per build; they are destroyed after the build and are not shared with other CodeBuild users, so deleting temporary files in a post-build step addresses no real cross-user exposure and is not an AWS-recognized best practice here.","why_zh":"CodeBuild build 容器為短暫且每次建置隔離，建置後即銷毀且不與其他 CodeBuild 使用者共用，因此在 post-build 刪除暫存檔並未解決任何實際的跨使用者暴露，亦非此情境的 AWS 最佳實務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Moving the credentials/password into an S3 object and re-exporting them keeps the secrets in plaintext and merely relocates the exposure; it lacks the encryption-at-rest and runtime substitution of Parameter Store SecureString or Secrets Manager, so it is inferior to C and not the recommended pattern.","why_zh":"把憑證/密碼搬到 S3 物件再 export，仍以明文保存秘密、只是搬移暴露點；缺乏 Parameter Store SecureString 或 Secrets Manager 的靜態加密與執行期替換，因此遜於 C，並非建議做法。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"XOR plus Base64 is obfuscation/encoding, not encryption; it is trivially reversible and the deobfuscation script lives in the same build, so it provides no real protection. AWS recommends Parameter Store SecureString, Secrets Manager, and KMS for sensitive values, never home-grown scrambling, making this a security anti-pattern.","why_zh":"XOR 加 Base64 屬混淆/編碼而非加密，可被輕易還原，且解混淆指令也留在同一建置中，毫無實質保護。AWS 對敏感值建議使用 Parameter Store SecureString、Secrets Manager 與 KMS，絕不建議自製打亂，故屬安全反模式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/APIReference/API_EnvironmentVariable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2024-06-27/framework/sec_identities_unique.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-parameter-store.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":130,"question_en":"A company has a legacy application. A DevOps engineer needs to automate the process of building the deployable artifact for the legacy application. The solution must store the deployable artifact in an existing Amazon S3 bucket for future deployments to reference. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款遗留应用程序。一位 DevOps 工程师需要将为该遗留应用程序构建可部署工件的过程 实现自动化。解决方案必须将可部署工件存储在现有的 Amazon S3 存储桶中，以便未来部署时引用。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a custom Docker image that contains all the dependencies for the legacy application. Store the custom Docker image in a new Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Configure a new AWS CodeBuild project to use the custom Docker image to build the deployable artifact and to save the artifact to the S3 bucket.","B":"Launch a new Amazon EC2 instance. Install all the dependencies for the legacy application on the EC2 instance. Use the EC2 instance to build the deployable artifact and to save the artifact to the S3 bucket.","C":"Create a custom EC2 Image Builder image. Install all the dependencies for the legacy application on the image. Launch a new Amazon EC2 instance from the image. Use the new EC2 instance to build the deployable artifact and to save the artifact to the S3 bucket.","D":"Create an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster with an AWS Fargate profile that runs in multiple Availability Zones. Create a custom Docker image that contains all the dependencies for the legacy application. Store the custom Docker image in a new Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Use the custom Docker image inside the EKS cluster to build the deployable artifact and to save the artifact to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个自定义的 Docker 镜像，其中包含旧版应用程序的所有依赖项。将自定义的 Docker 镜像存储 在新的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。配置一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目，使用自定义的 Docker 镜像来构建可部署的工件，并将工件保存到 S3 存储桶中。","B":"启动一个新的亚马逊 EC2 实例。在 EC2 实例上安装遗留应用程序的所有依赖项。使用 EC2 实例构建可 部署的工件，并将工件保存到 S3 存储桶。","C":"创建一个自定义的 EC2 Image Builder 镜像。在该镜像上安装旧版应用程序的所有依赖项。从该镜像 启动一个新的 Amazon EC2 实例。使用新的 EC2 实例构建可部署的工件，并将工件保存到 S3 存储 桶中。","D":"创建一个带有在多个可用区运行的 AWS Fargate 配置文件的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service （Amazon EKS） 集群。创建一个自定义 Docker 镜像，其中包含遗留应用程序的所有依赖项。将自 定义 Docker 镜像存储在新的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。在 EKS 集群中使用自定义 Docker 镜像构建可部署的工件，并将工件保存到 S3 存储桶中。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CodeBuild is a fully managed build service that 'compiles your source code, runs unit tests, and produces artifacts that are ready to deploy' and 'eliminates the need to provision, manage, and scale your own build servers' (no setup, patching, or updating of build servers). The legacy application's dependencies can be packaged into a custom Docker image stored in Amazon ECR, and a CodeBuild project can use that custom image as its build environment to produce the deployable artifact. CodeBuild natively writes build output to Amazon S3 by setting the project/buildspec artifacts type to S3, satisfying the requirement to store the artifact in the existing bucket for future deployments. Because there are no servers or clusters to provision, patch, or manage, this is the MOST operationally efficient option. Options B and C both require managing EC2 build servers, and option D stands up an entire EKS/Fargate cluster just to run a build, which is gross over-engineering.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeBuild 是一個全受管的建置服務，它會「編譯原始碼、執行單元測試並產生可直接部署的成品」，並且「免除佈建、管理及擴展自有建置伺服器的需要」（不需設定、修補、更新或管理建置伺服器）。可以把這個 legacy 應用程式的所有相依套件打包成自訂 Docker image 並儲存在 Amazon ECR，再讓 CodeBuild 專案以該自訂 image 作為建置環境來產生可部署成品。CodeBuild 透過將專案/buildspec 的 artifacts 類型設為 S3，即可原生地把建置輸出寫入既有的 Amazon S3 儲存貯體，滿足保存成品供日後部署參考的需求。由於沒有任何伺服器或叢集需要佈建、修補或管理，這是「營運上最有效率」的選項。選項 B 與 C 都需要自行管理 EC2 建置伺服器；選項 D 為了跑一次建置卻架設整個 EKS/Fargate 叢集，屬於過度設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Manually launching an EC2 instance, installing dependencies, and using it to build and upload the artifact is high operational overhead: you must provision, patch, scale, secure, and keep the instance running, and the process is largely manual rather than automated. CodeBuild removes all of this.","why_zh":"手動啟動 EC2 執行個體、安裝相依套件，再用它建置並上傳 artifact，操作負擔極高：需自行佈建、修補、擴展、保護並維持執行個體運作，流程偏手動而非自動化。CodeBuild 可免除這一切。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EC2 Image Builder produces a golden AMI/container image, but you still must launch and manage an EC2 instance to actually run the build, plus maintain the image pipeline. Image Builder is for creating and maintaining images, not for running on-demand artifact builds, so this carries more ongoing instance-management overhead than CodeBuild.","why_zh":"EC2 Image Builder 用於產生黃金 AMI／容器映像，但仍需啟動並管理 EC2 執行個體才能實際執行建置，還要維護映像建置管線。Image Builder 的用途是建立與維護映像，並非執行隨需的 artifact 建置，因此相較 CodeBuild 會帶來更多持續的執行個體管理負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EKS cluster with a Fargate profile across multiple Availability Zones is massively over-engineered for a simple build task. Managing a Kubernetes cluster (control plane, Fargate profiles, scheduling, networking) adds substantial operational complexity and cost compared to a single managed CodeBuild project.","why_zh":"跨多個可用區、搭配 Fargate 設定檔的 EKS 叢集，對於單純的建置工作而言過度設計。管理 Kubernetes 叢集（控制平面、Fargate 設定檔、排程、網路）相較於單一受管的 CodeBuild 專案，會增加大量操作複雜度與成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/sample-docker-custom-image.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codebuild-project-artifacts.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":131,"question_en":"A company builds a container image in an AWS CodeBuild project by running Docker commands. After the container image is built, the CodeBuild project uploads the container image to an Amazon S3 bucket. The CodeBuild project has an IAM service role that has permissions to access the S3 bucket. A DevOps engineer needs to replace the S3 bucket with an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository to store the container images. The DevOps engineer creates an ECR private image repository in the same AWS Region of the CodeBuild project. The DevOps engineer adjusts the IAM service role with the permissions that are necessary to work with the new ECR repository. The DevOps engineer also places new repository information into the docker build command and the docker push command that are used in the buildspec.yml file. When the CodeBuild project runs a build job, the job fails when the job tries to access the ECR repository. Which solution will resolve the issue of failed access to the ECR repository?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS CodeBuild 项目中通过运行 Docker 命令来构建容器镜像。容器镜像构建完成后， CodeBuild 项目会将其上传至 Amazon S3 存储桶。CodeBuild 项目具有一个 IAM 服务角色，该角色拥有 访问 S3 存储桶的权限。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要将 S3 存储桶替换为 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储 库来存储容器镜像。该 DevOps 工程师在与 CodeBuild 项目相同的 AWS 区域中创建了一个 ECR 私有 镜像存储库。该 DevOps 工程师还调整了 IAM 服务角色，赋予其与新 ECR 存储库交互所需的权限。 此外，该 DevOps 工程师还将新的存储库信息放入 buildspec.yml 文件中使用的 docker build 命令和 docker push 命令中。 当 CodeBuild 项目运行构建任务时，如果该任务尝试访问 ECR 存储库，则任务会失败。 哪种解决方案可以解决无法访问 ECR 仓库的问题？","options_en":{"A":"Update the buildspec.yml file to log in to the ECR repository by using the aws ecr get-login-password AWS CLI command to obtain an authentication token. Update the docker login command to use the authentication token to access the ECR repository.","B":"Add an environment variable of type SECRETS_MANAGER to the CodeBuild project. In the environment variable, include the ARN of the CodeBuild project's IAM service role. Update the buildspec.yml file to use the new environment variable to log in with the docker login command to access the ECR repository.","C":"Update the ECR repository to be a public image repository. Add an ECR repository policy that allows the IAM service role to have access.","D":"Update the buildspec.yml file to use the AWS CLI to assume the IAM service role for ECR operations. Add an ECR repository policy that allows the IAM service role to have access."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 buildspec.yml 文件，通过使用 aws ecr get-login-password AWS CLI 命令获取身份验证令牌来 登录到 ECR 仓库。更新 docker login 命令以使用身份验证令牌访问 ECR 仓库。","B":"在 CodeBuild 项目中添加一个类型为 SECRETS_MANAGER 的环境变量。在该环境变量中包 含 CodeBuild 项目的 IAM 服务角色的 ARN。更新 buildspec.yml 文件，使用新的环境变量通 过 docker login 命令登录以访问 ECR 仓库。","C":"将 ECR 代码库更新为公共镜像代码库。添加一个 ECR 代码库策略，允许 IAM 服务角色进行访问。","D":"更新 buildspec.yml 文件，使用 AWS CLI 假定 IAM 服务角色以执行 ECR 操作。添加一个 ECR 存 储库策略，允许 IAM 服务角色进行访问。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The Docker CLI does not support native IAM authentication, so granting the CodeBuild IAM service role ECR permissions and updating the docker build/push commands is not sufficient. Before Docker can push to an ECR private repository, the client must authenticate using an authorization token. The 'aws ecr get-login-password' AWS CLI command retrieves and decodes a 12-hour token (with username 'AWS') that is piped into 'docker login --password-stdin' against the registry URI (aws_account_id.dkr.ecr.region.amazonaws.com). This is exactly the pre_build step shown in AWS's official 'Publish Docker image to Amazon ECR' CodeBuild sample buildspec.yml. The engineer omitted this login step, which is why the build fails when it tries to access the ECR repository, and option A adds precisely that missing step.","explanation_zh":"Docker CLI 不支援原生的 IAM 驗證，因此只給 CodeBuild 的 IAM service role 加上 ECR 權限並更新 docker build/push 指令是不夠的。Docker 在推送至 ECR private repository 之前，必須先使用授權權杖進行驗證。'aws ecr get-login-password' AWS CLI 指令會擷取並解碼一個有效 12 小時的權杖（使用者名稱為 'AWS'），再以管線傳給 'docker login --password-stdin' 並指定 registry URI（aws_account_id.dkr.ecr.region.amazonaws.com）。這正是 AWS 官方 'Publish Docker image to Amazon ECR' CodeBuild 範例 buildspec.yml 中 pre_build 階段的步驟。工程師遺漏了這個登入步驟，導致建置工作在存取 ECR repository 時失敗，而選項 A 正好補上這個缺少的步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A SECRETS_MANAGER environment variable references a secret stored in AWS Secrets Manager, not an IAM role ARN, and an IAM role ARN is not a valid docker login credential. This does not perform the required ECR authorization-token authentication.","why_zh":"SECRETS_MANAGER 類型的環境變數參照的是儲存在 AWS Secrets Manager 中的 secret，而非 IAM role ARN；IAM role ARN 也不是有效的 docker login 憑證，無法完成 ECR 所需的授權權杖驗證。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Making the repository public is unnecessary, less secure, contradicts the private-repository requirement, and does not address the real problem. A private repository works once Docker authenticates via get-login-password; the failure is a missing login step, not the repository's access scope.","why_zh":"將 repository 改為 public 不必要、較不安全，且違背使用 private repository 的需求，也未解決真正問題。私有 repository 只要透過 get-login-password 完成 Docker 驗證即可運作；失敗原因是缺少登入步驟，而非 repository 的存取範圍。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeBuild already runs under its IAM service role, so re-assuming that same role via the CLI provides no new credentials and still does not authenticate the Docker CLI to ECR. The repository policy is also not the gap, since the service role already has the necessary permissions; only the docker login step is missing.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 本來就以其 IAM service role 執行，透過 CLI 再次 assume 同一個 role 不會取得新憑證，也無法讓 Docker CLI 對 ECR 完成驗證。repository policy 也不是缺口，因為 service role 已具備所需權限；真正缺少的只有 docker login 步驟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/registry_auth.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/docker-push-ecr-image.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/sample-docker-docker-hub.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":132,"question_en":"A company manually provisions IAM access for its employees. The company wants to replace the manual process with an automated process. The company has an existing Active Directory system configured with an external SAML 2.0 identity provider (IdP). The company wants employees to use their existing corporate credentials to access AWS. The groups from the existing Active Directory system must be available for permission management in AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). A DevOps engineer has completed the initial configuration of AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) in the company’s AWS account. What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司目前为员工手动配置 IAM（身份和访问管理）权限。该公司希望用自动化流程取代手动流程。 该公司已配置了一个现有的 Active Directory 系统，并与外部 SAML 2.0 身份提供商（IdP）进行了集成。 该公司希望员工使用现有的企业凭证访问 AWS。现有 Active Directory 系统中的组必须能在 AWS 身 份和访问管理（IAM）中用于权限管理。一位 DevOps 工程师已在公司的 AWS 账户中完成了 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）的初始配置。 为了满足要求，开发运维工程师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an external IdP as an identity source. Configure automatic provisioning of users and groups by using the SCIM protocol.","B":"Configure AWS Directory Service as an identity source. Configure automatic provisioning of users and groups by using the SAML protocol.","C":"Configure an AD Connector as an identity source. Configure automatic provisioning of users and groups by using the SCIM protocol.","D":"Configure an external IdP as an identity source Configure automatic provisioning of users and groups by using the SAML protocol."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置外部身份提供程序作为身份源。使用 SCIM 协议配置用户和组的自动配置。","B":"将 AWS 目录服务配置为身份源。使用 SAML 协议配置用户和组的自动配置。","C":"配置 AD 连接器作为身份源。使用 SCIM 协议配置用户和组的自动配置。","D":"配置外部身份提供程序作为身份源 通过使用 SAML 协议配置用户和组的自动配置。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The company already has an existing external SAML 2.0 IdP (fronting Active Directory) and wants employees to sign in with their existing corporate credentials, with AD groups made available for permission management in IAM Identity Center. In IAM Identity Center, the correct identity source for an existing external SAML IdP (such as Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, or an AD-backed federation) is 'External identity provider'. AWS docs state that with an external IdP you connect via SAML 2.0 for authentication, but 'The SAML protocol does not provide a way to query the IdP to learn about users and groups,' so users and groups must be provisioned separately. Automatic provisioning of users and groups into IAM Identity Center is done using the SCIM v2.0 protocol, which is exactly what makes the AD groups available for permission management. Therefore the next step is option A: configure an external IdP as the identity source and configure automatic provisioning of users and groups using SCIM.","explanation_zh":"公司已擁有現有的外部 SAML 2.0 IdP（前端銜接 Active Directory），希望員工以既有企業憑證登入，並讓 AD 群組可在 IAM Identity Center 中用於權限管理。在 IAM Identity Center 中，對於既有的外部 SAML IdP（例如 Okta、Microsoft Entra ID 或以 AD 為後端的聯合驗證），正確的身分來源是 External identity provider。AWS 文件指出，使用外部 IdP 時透過 SAML 2.0 進行身分驗證，但「SAML 通訊協定不提供向 IdP 查詢使用者與群組的方法」，因此必須另行佈建使用者與群組。將使用者與群組自動佈建（同步）到 IAM Identity Center 是透過 SCIM v2.0 通訊協定完成，這正是讓 AD 群組可用於權限管理的機制。因此下一步是選項 A：將 external IdP 設定為身分來源，並使用 SCIM 設定使用者與群組的自動佈建。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The company uses an existing external SAML 2.0 IdP, not AWS Directory Service, so AWS Directory Service is the wrong identity source. Also, SAML is an authentication protocol and cannot provision users/groups; provisioning into IAM Identity Center uses SCIM.","why_zh":"公司使用的是現有的外部 SAML 2.0 IdP，而非 AWS Directory Service，因此身分來源選錯。此外，SAML 是身分驗證通訊協定，無法佈建使用者/群組；佈建到 IAM Identity Center 須使用 SCIM。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AD Connector is for connecting a self-managed Active Directory under the 'Active Directory' identity source, but the company explicitly wants to use its existing external SAML 2.0 IdP and corporate credentials. The AD/AD Connector identity source synchronizes via the directory connection, not via a SCIM endpoint, so the protocol pairing is also incorrect.","why_zh":"AD Connector 用於在「Active Directory」身分來源下連接自管的 Active Directory，但公司明確希望使用其現有的外部 SAML 2.0 IdP 與企業憑證。AD/AD Connector 身分來源是透過目錄連線同步，而非透過 SCIM 端點，因此通訊協定搭配也不正確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"External IdP is the correct identity source, but SAML cannot provision users and groups. AWS docs explicitly state 'The SAML protocol does not provide a way to query the IdP to learn about users and groups,' so automatic provisioning of users/groups must use SCIM, not SAML.","why_zh":"External IdP 是正確的身分來源，但 SAML 無法佈建使用者與群組。AWS 文件明確指出「SAML 通訊協定不提供向 IdP 查詢使用者與群組的方法」，因此使用者/群組的自動佈建必須使用 SCIM，而非 SAML。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/provision-automatically.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/scim-profile-saml.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":133,"question_en":"A company is using AWS to run digital workloads. Each application team in the company has its own AWS account for application hosting. The accounts are consolidated in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company wants to enforce security standards across the entire organization. To avoid noncompliance because of security misconfiguration, the company has enforced the use of AWS CloudFormation. A production support team can modify resources in the production environment by using the AWS Management Console to troubleshoot and resolve application-related issues. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution to identify in near real time any AWS service misconfiguration that results in noncompliance. The solution must automatically remediate the issue within 15 minutes of identification. The solution also must track noncompliant resources and events in a centralized dashboard with accurate timestamps. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 运行数字工作负载。该公司内的每个应用程序团队都有自己的 AWS 账户用于应 用程序托管。这些账户在 AWS 组织中进行了整合。 该公司希望在整个组织内推行安全标准。为避免因安全配置不当而导致的不合规情况，公司强制使用 AWS CloudFormation。生产支持团队可以通过使用 AWS 管理控制台来修改生产环境中的资源，以解决 与应用程序相关的故障并进行修复。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一种解决方案，以便近乎实时地识别出任何导致不合规的 AWS 服务配置错误。 该解决方案必须在识别出问题后的 15 分钟内自动修复该问题。此外，该解决方案还必须在一个集中的仪 表板中跟踪不合规的资源和事件，并附上准确的时间戳。 哪种解决方案 哪种方案能以最低的开发成本满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use CloudFormation drift detection to identify noncompliant resources. Use drift detection events from CloudFormation to invoke an AWS Lambda function for remediation. Configure the Lambda function to publish logs to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard to use the log group for tracking.","B":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail in the AWS accounts. Analyze CloudTrail logs by using Amazon Athena to identify noncompliant resources. Use AWS Step Functions to track query results on Athena for drift detection and to invoke an AWS Lambda function for remediation. For tracking, set up an Amazon QuickSight dashboard that uses Athena as the data source.","C":"Turn on the configuration recorder in AWS Config in all the AWS accounts to identify noncompliant resources. Enable AWS Security Hub with the --no-enable-default-standards option in all the AWS accounts. Set up AWS Config managed rules and custom rules. Set up automatic remediation by using AWS Config conformance packs. For tracking, set up a dashboard on Security Hub in a designated Security Hub administrator account.","D":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail in the AWS accounts. Analyze CloudTrail logs by using Amazon CloudWatch Logs to identify noncompliant resources. Use CloudWatch Logs filters for drift detection. Use Amazon EventBridge to invoke the Lambda function for remediation. Stream filtered CloudWatch logs to Amazon OpenSearch Service. Set up a dashboard on OpenSearch Service for tracking."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 CloudFormation 漂移检测来识别不合规的资源。使用 CloudFormation 的漂移检测事件来调用 AWS Lambda 函数进行修复。配置 Lambda 函数将日志发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。配 置 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板以使用该日志组进行跟踪。","B":"在 AWS 账户中启用 AWS CloudTrail。使用 Amazon Athena 分析 CloudTrail 日志以识别不符合规定 的资源。使用 AWS Step Functions 跟踪 Athena 上的查询结果以进行漂移检测，并调用 AWS Lambda 函数进行修复。为跟踪目的，设置一个使用 Athena 作为数据源的 Amazon QuickSight 仪 表板。","C":"在所有 AWS 账户中开启 AWS Config 中的配置记录器以识别不合规资源。在所有 AWS 账户中使用 -- no-enable-default-standards 选项启用 AWS Security Hub。设置 AWS Config 管理规则和自定义规则。 通过使用 AWS Config 合规性包设置自动修复。为跟踪目的，在指定的 Security Hub 管理员账户中设 置 Security Hub 仪表板。","D":"在 AWS 账户中启用 AWS CloudTrail。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 分析 CloudTrail 日志以识别不合 规的资源。使用 CloudWatch Logs 过滤器进行漂移检测。使用 Amazon EventBridge 调用 Lambda 函 数进行修复。将过滤后的 CloudWatch 日志流式传输到 Amazon OpenSearch Service。在 OpenSearch Service 上设置仪表板以进行跟踪。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config's configuration recorder continuously records configuration changes to resources (including manual console changes made by the production support team) and evaluates them against Config rules in near real time, satisfying the near-real-time misconfiguration detection requirement. AWS Config conformance packs are a single deployable entity that bundles Config managed and custom rules together with remediation actions, and can be deployed across an organization in AWS Organizations; remediation runs automatically via AWS Systems Manager Automation documents, which can complete well within the 15-minute window. AWS Config immediately sends its rule evaluations to AWS Security Hub, which transforms them into findings and aggregates them across all accounts into a centralized dashboard in a delegated Security Hub administrator account with accurate ASFF timestamps. Because every component is a managed service that requires only configuration (no custom detection pipelines, orchestration, or dashboard code), this meets all requirements with the LEAST development overhead. The other options require building custom detection logic, orchestration, Lambda remediation code, and custom dashboards.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 的 configuration recorder 會持續記錄資源的組態變更（包含 production support 團隊透過 console 手動所做的變更），並近乎即時地依據 Config rules 進行評估，符合「近乎即時偵測錯誤組態」的需求。AWS Config conformance packs 是一個可單一部署的實體，把 Config managed 與 custom rules 連同 remediation actions 綁在一起，並可跨 AWS Organizations 整個組織部署；remediation 透過 AWS Systems Manager Automation documents 自動執行，可在 15 分鐘內完成。AWS Config 會立即把其 rule evaluations 送到 AWS Security Hub，由 Security Hub 轉換成 findings，並在指定的 Security Hub administrator account 中跨所有帳號彙整為集中式儀表板，帶有正確的 ASFF 時間戳記。由於每個元件都是只需設定的 managed service（不需自建偵測流程、編排或儀表板程式碼），因此以最少的開發負擔滿足所有需求。其他選項都需要自建偵測邏輯、編排、Lambda remediation 程式碼以及自訂儀表板。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation drift detection is an on-demand operation you must explicitly initiate (console/CLI/API); it is not continuous or near real time, and there is no native 'drift detection event' emitted automatically when a resource changes. Making it near real time would require building a custom EventBridge scheduler plus Lambda to repeatedly call DetectStackDrift, and it only covers resources managed within CloudFormation stacks (unsupported types are marked NOT_CHECKED), not arbitrary service misconfigurations. The Lambda remediation plus log-based CloudWatch dashboard further increase development overhead.","why_zh":"CloudFormation drift detection 是必須明確發起的隨需操作（console/CLI/API），並非持續或近乎即時，也不會在資源變更時自動發出原生的「drift detection event」。要使其近乎即時就得自建 EventBridge 排程加 Lambda 反覆呼叫 DetectStackDrift，且它只涵蓋 CloudFormation stack 內管理的資源（不支援的類型會被標為 NOT_CHECKED），而非任意的服務錯誤組態。再加上 Lambda remediation 與以 log 為基礎的 CloudWatch 儀表板，開發負擔更高。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Analyzing CloudTrail logs via Athena is batch/query-based, not a near-real-time compliance evaluation. Using Athena 'for drift detection', Step Functions to track query results, Lambda for remediation, and a QuickSight dashboard requires extensive custom development (queries, state machines, remediation code, BI pipeline) and is not how AWS performs continuous compliance evaluation, so it is the opposite of LEAST development overhead.","why_zh":"透過 Athena 分析 CloudTrail logs 是批次/查詢式，並非近乎即時的合規評估。用 Athena 做 drift detection、Step Functions 追蹤查詢結果、Lambda remediation 與 QuickSight 儀表板，需要大量自訂開發（查詢、狀態機、修復程式碼、BI 管線），且非 AWS 進行持續合規評估的方式，與「最少開發負擔」相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Routing CloudTrail to CloudWatch Logs and using metric/subscription filters for 'drift detection' is custom logic that inspects API events rather than continuously evaluating resource compliance state. Combining EventBridge, a custom Lambda for remediation, streaming filtered logs to Amazon OpenSearch Service, and building an OpenSearch dashboard is the most build-heavy option and far higher development overhead than the managed Config plus Security Hub approach.","why_zh":"把 CloudTrail 送到 CloudWatch Logs 並用 metric/subscription filters 做 drift detection 是自訂邏輯，檢視的是 API 事件而非持續評估資源合規狀態。再結合 EventBridge、自訂 Lambda remediation、把過濾後的 log 串流到 Amazon OpenSearch Service 並自建 OpenSearch 儀表板，是最需自建的選項，開發負擔遠高於 managed 的 Config 加 Security Hub 方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-packs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/WhatIsConfig.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setting-up-aws-config-rules-with-console-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/designate-orgs-admin-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/detect-drift-stack.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":134,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The organization root has an OU that is named Environments. The Environments OU has two child OUs that are named Development and Production, respectively. The Environments OU and the child OUs have the default FullAWSAccess policy in place. A DevOps engineer plans to remove the FullAWSAccess policy from the Development OU and replace the policy with a policy that allows all actions on Amazon EC2 resources. What will be the outcome of this policy replacement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。组织根目录下有一个名为“Environments”的组 织单元（OU）。该“Environments”组织单元有两个子组织单元，分别名为“Development”和 “Production”。 环境组织单位（OU）及其子组织单位默认启用了“FullAWSAccess”策略。一位 DevOps 工程师计划从开 发组织单位移除“FullAWSAccess”策略，并用一个允许对亚马逊 EC2 资源执行所有操作的策略来替代。 这项政策的更替将会带来怎样的结果？","options_en":{"A":"All users in the Development OU will be allowed all API actions on all resources.","B":"All users in the Development OU will be allowed all API actions on EC2 resources. All other API actions will be denied.","C":"All users in the Development OU will be denied all API actions on all resources.","D":"All users in the Development OU will be denied all API actions on EC2 resources. All other API actions will be allowed."},"options_zh":{"A":"开发组织单位中的所有用户都将被允许对所有资源执行所有 API 操作。","B":"开发组织单位中的所有用户都将被允许对 EC2 资源执行所有 API 操作。其他所有 API 操作都将被拒绝。","C":"开发组织单位中的所有用户将被禁止对所有资源执行所有 API 操作。","D":"开发组织单位中的所有用户将被禁止对 EC2 资源执行所有 API 操作。其他所有 API 操作将被允许。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Service control policies (SCPs) use a deny-by-default allowlist model. AWS docs state that for a permission to be allowed for an account, there must be an explicit Allow statement at every level in the direct path from the root through each OU down to the account; any permission not explicitly allowed at every level is denied. In this scenario the Root still has FullAWSAccess and the Environments OU still has FullAWSAccess, so both allow all actions. The Development OU's FullAWSAccess is replaced by a policy that allows only ec2:* . For EC2 actions there is an Allow at all three levels (Root, Environments, Development), so EC2 is permitted by the guardrail. For any non-EC2 action, the Development OU no longer contains an explicit Allow, so even though the parent levels allow it, it is denied by the implicit deny-by-default. The net SCP guardrail outcome is therefore: all EC2 API actions allowed and all other API actions denied, which is option B. (Note: SCPs only set the maximum permission boundary and do not themselves grant access; actual access still requires matching IAM identity-based permissions, but B is the only option that correctly describes the resulting guardrail.)","explanation_zh":"Service control policies (SCPs) 採用預設拒絕 (deny-by-default) 的允許清單模型。AWS 文件指出：要讓某帳戶獲得某項權限，必須在從 root 經過直接路徑上每個 OU 一直到該帳戶的每一個層級都有明確的 Allow 陳述式；任何未在每一層級都被明確允許的權限即被拒絕。在此情境中，Root 仍保有 FullAWSAccess、Environments OU 仍保有 FullAWSAccess，兩者皆允許所有動作。Development OU 的 FullAWSAccess 被替換成只允許 ec2:* 的政策。對於 EC2 動作，三個層級 (Root、Environments、Development) 都有 Allow，因此 EC2 在護欄 (guardrail) 內被允許。對於任何非 EC2 動作，Development OU 已不再包含明確的 Allow，即使父層級允許，也會因隱含的 deny-by-default 而被拒絕。因此 SCP 護欄的最終結果為：允許所有 EC2 API 動作、拒絕所有其他 API 動作，即選項 B。(注意：SCP 只設定權限上限，本身不授予存取權；實際存取仍需相符的 IAM 身分型權限，但 B 是唯一正確描述護欄結果的選項。)","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This would be true only if FullAWSAccess remained at the Development level. Once it is replaced with an ec2:*-only policy, non-EC2 actions lose their explicit Allow at the Development level and are denied by deny-by-default, so not all actions on all resources remain allowed.","why_zh":"只有在 Development 層仍保有 FullAWSAccess 時才成立。一旦被替換成僅允許 ec2:* 的政策，非 EC2 動作在 Development 層失去明確 Allow，會被 deny-by-default 拒絕，因此並非所有資源的所有動作都仍被允許。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"All actions would be denied only if no Allow remained at the Development level (e.g., FullAWSAccess removed with no replacement). Here the replacement policy still allows ec2:* , so EC2 actions are permitted, not everything denied.","why_zh":"只有在 Development 層完全沒有任何 Allow (例如移除 FullAWSAccess 且無替代) 時才會拒絕所有動作。此處替代政策仍允許 ec2:* ，因此 EC2 動作被允許，並非全部被拒絕。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This inverts the result. SCPs are not deny lists by default; the ec2:* Allow makes EC2 the allowed set, while everything else (lacking an explicit Allow at the Development level) is denied. EC2 is allowed and other actions are denied, the opposite of this option.","why_zh":"此選項把結果顛倒。SCP 預設不是拒絕清單；ec2:* 的 Allow 使 EC2 成為被允許的集合，而其餘動作 (在 Development 層缺少明確 Allow) 被拒絕。EC2 被允許、其他動作被拒絕，與本選項相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":135,"question_en":"A company is examining its disaster recovery capability and wants the ability to switch over its daily operations to a secondary AWS Region. The company uses AWS CodeCommit as a source control tool in the primary Region. A DevOps engineer must provide the capability for the company to develop code in the secondary Region. If the company needs to use the secondary Region, developers can add an additional remote URL to their local Git configuration. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在评估其灾难恢复能力，并希望能够在主 AWS 区域出现故障时将其日常运营切换到备用 AWS 区域。该公司在主区域使用 AWS CodeCommit 作为源代码控制工具。 DevOps 工程师必须为公司提供在辅助区域开发代码的能力。如果公司需要使用辅助区域，开发人员可以在 其本地 Git 配置中添加一个额外的远程 URL。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CodeCommit repository in the secondary Region. Create an AWS CodeBuild project to perform a Git mirror operation of the primary Region's CodeCommit repository to the secondary Region's CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes the CodeBuild project. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to merge events in the primary Region's CodeCommit repository. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket in the secondary Region. Create an AWS Fargate task to perform a Git mirror operation of the primary Region's CodeCommit repository and copy the result to the S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function that initiates the Fargate task. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to merge events in the CodeCommit repository. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function.","C":"Create an AWS CodeArtifact repository in the secondary Region. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses the primary Region’s CodeCommit repository for the source action. Create a cross- Region stage in the pipeline that packages the CodeCommit repository contents and stores the contents in the CodeArtifact repository when a pull request is merged into the CodeCommit repository.","D":"Create an AWS Cloud9 environment and a CodeCommit repository in the secondary Region. Configure the primary Region's CodeCommit repository as a remote repository in the AWS Cloud9 environment. Connect the secondary Region's CodeCommit repository to the AWS Cloud9 environment."},"options_zh":{"A":"在辅助区域创建一个 CodeCommit 存储库。创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目，用于将主区域的 CodeCommit 存储库镜像到辅助区域的 CodeCommit 存储库。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来调用 CodeBuild 项目。创 建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以响应主区域 CodeCommit 存储库中的合并事件。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"在辅助区域创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。创建一个 AWS Fargate 任务，用于执行主区域 CodeCommit 存 储库的 Git 镜像操作，并将结果复制到 S3 存储桶。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来启动 Fargate 任务。 创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以响应 CodeCommit 存储库中的合并事件。配置 EventBridge 规 则以调用 Lambda 函数。","C":"在辅助区域创建一个 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道将主区域的 CodeCommit 存储库用作源操作。在管道中创建一个跨区域阶段，当 CodeCommit 存储库中的拉取请求 被合并时，该阶段会将 CodeCommit 存储库的内容进行打包并将其存储在 CodeArtifact 存储库中。","D":"在辅助区域创建一个 AWS Cloud9 环境和一个 CodeCommit 代码库。将主区域的 CodeCommit 代码库配置 为 AWS Cloud9 环境中的远程代码库。将辅助区域的 CodeCommit 代码库连接到 AWS Cloud9 环境。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a usable CodeCommit repository in the secondary Region, kept in sync from the primary Region, that developers can add as an additional Git remote URL during a DR failover. Option A is the only choice that delivers a real Git endpoint plus automated replication: it creates a CodeCommit repository in the secondary Region (a Git endpoint developers can clone/push/pull as documented in the CodeCommit connect/migrate guides), and uses CodeBuild to run a Git mirror operation (git clone --mirror followed by git push --mirror) to copy the primary repository into the secondary repository. CodeCommit sends events directly to EventBridge, including 'CodeCommit Pull Request State Change' and 'CodeCommit Repository State Change', so an EventBridge rule can react to merge events and invoke the Lambda function that starts the CodeBuild mirror job, keeping the secondary repository current automatically. This combines the standard Git migration/mirror pattern with CodeCommit's native EventBridge integration, satisfying every requirement in the scenario.","explanation_zh":"需求是在次要 Region 建立一個可用且持續與主要 Region 同步的 CodeCommit 儲存庫，讓開發者能在 DR 切換時將其加入為額外的 Git remote URL。選項 A 是唯一同時提供真正 Git 端點與自動化複製的方案：它在次要 Region 建立 CodeCommit 儲存庫（依官方 CodeCommit connect/migrate 文件，這是開發者可 clone/push/pull 的 Git 端點），並使用 CodeBuild 執行 Git mirror 操作（git clone --mirror 後接 git push --mirror）將主要儲存庫複製到次要儲存庫。CodeCommit 會直接將事件送至 EventBridge，包含 'CodeCommit Pull Request State Change' 與 'CodeCommit Repository State Change'，因此 EventBridge 規則可在合併事件發生時調用 Lambda 來啟動 CodeBuild mirror 工作，自動保持次要儲存庫同步。這結合了標準的 Git 遷移/mirror 模式與 CodeCommit 原生的 EventBridge 整合，滿足情境中的所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Mirrors the repository into an Amazon S3 bucket, which is object storage, not a Git remote. Developers cannot add an S3 bucket as a Git remote URL to clone, push, or pull code, so it fails the core requirement of developing code in the secondary Region.","why_zh":"將儲存庫鏡像到 Amazon S3 儲存桶，那是物件儲存而非 Git remote。開發者無法將 S3 儲存桶當作 Git remote URL 來 clone/push/pull，因此無法滿足在次要 Region 開發程式碼的核心需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS CodeArtifact is a package/artifact repository (npm, Maven, PyPI, NuGet, etc.), not a Git source-control repository. You cannot clone or push code to it as a Git remote, so developers cannot use it to develop code as a CodeCommit substitute.","why_zh":"AWS CodeArtifact 是套件/構件儲存庫（npm、Maven、PyPI、NuGet 等），並非 Git 原始碼控制儲存庫。無法以 Git remote 方式 clone 或 push 程式碼，因此開發者無法用它取代 CodeCommit 來開發程式碼。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Cloud9 environment with a manually configured remote is a one-time, single-user development setup, not automated continuous replication of merges. It does not keep the secondary-Region CodeCommit repository synchronized on each merge and does not provide the resilient, automated DR sync the scenario requires; the developers' own machines (not a single Cloud9 IDE) are what need the additional remote URL.","why_zh":"Cloud9 環境加上手動設定的 remote 只是一次性、單一使用者的開發設定，而非自動且持續的合併複製。它無法在每次合併時保持次要 Region CodeCommit 儲存庫同步，也無法提供情境所需具韌性、自動化的 DR 同步；真正需要加入額外 remote URL 的是開發者自己的機器，而非單一 Cloud9 IDE。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codecommit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/monitoring-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-migrate-repository-existing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-connect.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":136,"question_en":"A DevOps team is merging code revisions for an application that uses an Amazon RDS Multi-AZ DB cluster for its production database. The DevOps team uses continuous integration to periodically verify that the application works. The DevOps team needs to test the changes before the changes are deployed to the production database. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队正在合并一个应用程序的代码修订版本，该应用程序的生产数据库使用的是亚马逊 RDS 多可用区数据库集群。DevOps 团队使用持续集成来定期验证应用程序是否正常运行。在将更改部署到生产 数据库之前，DevOps 团队需要对这些更改进行测试。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a buildspec file in AWS CodeBuild to restore the DB cluster from a snapshot of the production database, run integration tests, and drop the restored database after verification.","B":"Deploy the application to production. Configure an audit log of data control language (DCL) operations to capture database activities to perform if verification fails.","C":"Create a snapshot of the DB cluster before deploying the application. Use the Update requires:Replacement property on the DB instance in AWS CloudFormation to deploy the application and apply the changes.","D":"Ensure that the DB cluster is a Multi-AZ deployment. Deploy the application with the updates. Fail over to the standby instance if verification fails."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CodeBuild 中使用构建规范文件从生产数据库的快照恢复数据库集群，运行集成测试，并在 验证后删除恢复的数据库。","B":"将应用程序部署到生产环境。配置数据控制语言（DCL）操作的审计日志，以捕获验证失败时要执行的 数据库活动。","C":"在部署应用程序之前，为数据库集群创建一个快照。在 AWS CloudFormation 中使用 DB 实例的“更新 要求：替换”属性来部署应用程序并应用更改。","D":"确保数据库集群采用多可用区部署。使用更新内容部署应用程序。如果验证失败，则故障转移到备用实 例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to test the application changes BEFORE they reach the production database, with no risk to live production data. Restoring an RDS DB cluster from a snapshot of production always provisions a brand-new, isolated DB instance/cluster: the AWS docs state \"You can't restore from a DB snapshot to an existing DB instance; you create a new DB instance when you restore the snapshot.\" Running integration tests via an AWS CodeBuild buildspec against this throwaway copy validates the code against production-equivalent data, and dropping it afterward keeps cost and footprint minimal. This is the canonical CI pattern for safe pre-production database testing. The other options all apply untested changes directly to the live production cluster (B and C) or rely on Multi-AZ failover, which only provides high availability and does not isolate or roll back schema/data changes because all replicas share the same data via semisynchronous replication (D).","explanation_zh":"需求是在變更觸及正式資料庫之前先進行測試，且不能對線上正式資料造成任何風險。從正式環境的快照 (snapshot) 還原 RDS DB cluster 一定會佈建一個全新、隔離的 DB instance/cluster：AWS 文件明確指出「You can't restore from a DB snapshot to an existing DB instance; you create a new DB instance when you restore the snapshot.」透過 AWS CodeBuild buildspec 對這個可丟棄的副本執行整合測試，能以與正式環境相同的資料驗證程式碼，測試後再刪除可將成本與資源佔用降到最低。這是 CI 流程中安全進行上線前資料庫測試的標準做法。其他選項不是把未經測試的變更直接套用到線上正式 cluster（B、C），就是依賴 Multi-AZ 容錯移轉，而後者只提供高可用性，無法隔離或回復結構描述/資料變更，因為所有副本透過半同步複寫共用相同資料（D）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"This deploys the untested changes directly to production first, which is exactly what the requirement forbids. A DCL (data control language) audit log only records grant/revoke permission operations; it is not a testing or rollback mechanism and provides no way to verify the application before deployment.","why_zh":"此選項直接把未經測試的變更先部署到正式環境，恰恰違反了需求。DCL（資料控制語言）稽核紀錄只記錄授權/撤銷權限的操作，並非測試或回復機制，無法在部署前驗證應用程式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Taking a snapshot before deploying only provides a rollback point; the untested changes are still applied directly to the production DB cluster. Worse, Update requires:Replacement on the DB instance forces CloudFormation to delete and recreate the production instance, causing data loss and downtime instead of isolated testing.","why_zh":"在部署前先建立快照只是提供回復點，變更仍直接套用到正式 DB cluster。更糟的是，對 DB instance 使用 Update requires:Replacement 會迫使 CloudFormation 刪除並重建正式實例，導致資料遺失與停機，而非在隔離環境中測試。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Multi-AZ DB cluster has a writer and two reader instances that share the same data via semisynchronous replication; the readers are not a separate test environment. Deploying updates writes them to all replicas, so failing over to a standby does NOT revert a bad schema or data change. Failover delivers high availability, not change isolation or rollback.","why_zh":"Multi-AZ DB cluster 由一個寫入實例與兩個讀取實例組成，透過半同步複寫共用相同資料，讀取實例並非獨立的測試環境。部署更新會寫入所有副本，因此切換到備援實例並不能回復錯誤的結構描述或資料變更。容錯移轉提供的是高可用性，而非變更隔離或回復。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_RestoreFromSnapshot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/multi-az-db-clusters-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/multi-az-db-clusters-concepts-failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":137,"question_en":"A company manages a multi-tenant environment in its VPC and has configured Amazon GuardDuty for the corresponding AWS account. The company sends all GuardDuty findings to AWS Security Hub. Traffic from suspicious sources is generating a large number of findings. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to automatically deny traffic across the entire VPC when GuardDuty discovers a new suspicious source. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在其虚拟私有云（VPC）中管理一个多租户环境，并为相应的 AWS 账户配置了 Amazon GuardDuty。 该公司将所有 GuardDuty 发现结果发送至 AWS 安全中心。 来自可疑来源的流量正在生成大量发现结果。DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，在 GuardDuty 发现新 的可疑来源时，自动拒绝整个 VPC 的流量。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a GuardDuty threat list. Configure GuardDuty to reference the list. Create an AWS Lambda function that will update the threat list. Configure the Lambda function to run in response to new Security Hub findings that come from GuardDuty.","B":"Configure an AWS WAF web ACL that includes a custom rule group. Create an AWS Lambda function that will create a block rule in the custom rule group. Configure the Lambda function to run in response to new Security Hub findings that come from GuardDuty.","C":"Configure a firewall in AWS Network Firewall. Create an AWS Lambda function that will create a Drop action rule in the firewall policy. Configure the Lambda function to run in response to new Security Hub findings that come from GuardDuty.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that will create a GuardDuty suppression rule. Configure the Lambda function to run in response to new Security Hub findings that come from GuardDuty."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 GuardDuty 威胁列表。配置 GuardDuty 引用该列表。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来更新威 胁列表。配置该 Lambda 函数在收到来自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub 找到结果时运行。","B":"配置一个包含自定义规则组的 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表 （web ACL）。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数， 该函数将在自定义规则组中创建一条阻止规则。配置该 Lambda 函数，使其在收到来自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub 找到的漏洞时运行。","C":"在 AWS Network Firewall 中配置防火墙。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会在防火墙策略中创建一 条丢弃操作规则。将 Lambda 函数配置为在收到来自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub 找到的漏洞时运行。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于创建 GuardDuty 抑制规则。将该 Lambda 函数配置为在收到来自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub 找到结果时运行。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is to actively DENY (block) network traffic across the ENTIRE VPC when GuardDuty discovers a new suspicious source. AWS Network Firewall is a stateful, managed network firewall for a VPC that filters traffic at the VPC perimeter (internet gateway, NAT gateway, VPN, Direct Connect). With route tables sending VPC traffic through the firewall endpoints, a Drop-action rule in the firewall policy actively blocks the suspicious source's traffic for the whole VPC. A Lambda function, triggered via EventBridge on new GuardDuty-sourced Security Hub findings, can programmatically add that Drop rule, satisfying both the 'deny traffic' and 'entire VPC' requirements. Network Firewall is the only option here that provides a network-level (L3/L4) enforcement primitive covering all VPC traffic; the dump's suggested answer and the first analyst's verdict of C are correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是當 GuardDuty 偵測到新的可疑來源時，主動在整個 VPC 範圍內拒絕（封鎖）網路流量。AWS Network Firewall 是 VPC 的具狀態（stateful）受管網路防火牆，可在 VPC 邊界（internet gateway、NAT gateway、VPN、Direct Connect）過濾流量。透過路由表將 VPC 流量導向 firewall endpoint，再於 firewall policy 中加入 Drop action 規則，即可在整個 VPC 範圍內主動封鎖該可疑來源的流量。由 EventBridge 在收到來自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub findings 時觸發 Lambda function，即可自動新增該 Drop 規則，同時滿足『拒絕流量』與『整個 VPC』兩項要求。Network Firewall 是本題唯一提供涵蓋全部 VPC 流量之網路層（L3/L4）強制執行機制的選項；dump 建議答案與第一位分析師的判定 C 皆正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A GuardDuty threat (entity/IP) list does NOT block traffic. Per AWS docs, when GuardDuty detects activity involving entries on a threat list it only GENERATES findings to alert you. It is a detection enhancement, not an enforcement control, so it would actually create MORE findings rather than deny the traffic.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 威脅清單（entity/IP list）並不會封鎖流量。依 AWS 文件，當 GuardDuty 偵測到涉及威脅清單項目的活動時，僅會『產生 findings』來提醒你。這是偵測強化功能，並非執行/阻擋控制，反而會產生更多 findings，無法拒絕流量。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS WAF only protects specific Layer 7, HTTP-facing resources (CloudFront, Application Load Balancer, API Gateway, AppSync, Cognito, App Runner, Verified Access, Amplify) via web ACL association and inspects HTTP(S) requests. It cannot deny arbitrary network traffic 'across the entire VPC' and does not sit on general VPC network paths.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 僅能透過 web ACL 關聯保護特定的第七層、面向 HTTP 的資源（CloudFront、Application Load Balancer、API Gateway、AppSync、Cognito、App Runner、Verified Access、Amplify），並檢查 HTTP(S) 請求。它無法拒絕『整個 VPC』的一般網路流量，也不位於 VPC 一般網路路徑上。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A GuardDuty suppression rule only auto-ARCHIVES matching findings to reduce noise/false positives; suppressed findings are not even sent to Security Hub, S3, Detective, or EventBridge. It only hides findings and performs no traffic blocking, directly contradicting the goal of denying traffic.","why_zh":"GuardDuty suppression rule 只會自動將符合條件的新 findings『封存（archive）』以降低雜訊／誤判；被抑制的 findings 甚至不會送往 Security Hub、S3、Detective 或 EventBridge。它僅隱藏 findings，完全不執行任何流量封鎖，與『拒絕流量』的目標背道而馳。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/what-is-aws-network-firewall.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/firewall-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/suricata-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/findings_suppression-rule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_upload-lists.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/how-aws-waf-works-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":138,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Secrets Manager to store a set of sensitive API keys that an AWS Lambda function uses. When the Lambda function is invoked the Lambda function retrieves the API keys and makes an API call to an external service. The Secrets Manager secret is encrypted with the default AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key. A DevOps engineer needs to update the infrastructure to ensure that only the Lambda function’s execution role can access the values in Secrets Manager. The solution must apply the principle of least privilege. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Secrets Manager 来存储一组敏感的 API 密钥，这些密钥由一个 AWS Lambda 函数使用。 当调用 Lambda 函数时，该函数会检索这些 API 密钥，并向外部服务发起 API 调用。Secrets Manager 密钥使 用默认的 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥进行加密。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要更新基础设施，以确保只有 Lambda 函数的执行角色能够访问 Secrets Manager 中的 值。解决方案必须遵循最小权限原则。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the default KMS key for Secrets Manager to allow only the Lambda function’s execution role to decrypt","B":"Create a KMS customer managed key that trusts Secrets Manager and allows the Lambda function's execution role to decrypt. Update Secrets Manager to use the new customer managed key","C":"Create a KMS customer managed key that trusts Secrets Manager and allows the account's root principal to decrypt. Update Secrets Manager to use the new customer managed key","D":"Ensure that the Lambda function’s execution role has the KMS permissions scoped on the resource level. Configure the permissions so that the KMS key can encrypt the Secrets Manager secret","E":"Remove all KMS permissions from the Lambda function’s execution role"},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Secrets Manager 的默认 KMS 密钥更新为仅允许 Lambda 函数的执行角色进行解密","B":"创建一个受信任 Secrets Manager 并允许 Lambda 函数执行角色进行解密的 KMS 客户管理密钥。更新 Secrets Manager 以使用新的客户管理密钥。","C":"创建一个信任 Secrets Manager 并允许账户根用户进行解密的 KMS 客户管理密钥。更新 Secrets Manager 以使用新的客户管理密钥。","D":"确保 Lambda 函数的执行角色在资源级别具有 KMS 权限。配置权限，以便 KMS 密钥能够加密 Secrets Manager 密钥。","E":"从 Lambda 函数的执行角色中移除所有 KMS 权限"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The secret is currently encrypted with the AWS managed key aws/secretsmanager (the default key). Restricting decryption to ONLY the Lambda execution role with least privilege requires two complementary steps because AWS KMS uses a dual-control model: 'Unless the key policy explicitly allows it, you cannot use IAM policies to allow access to a KMS key.' (1) Option B: create a customer managed KMS key whose key policy trusts Secrets Manager (kms:ViaService = secretsmanager.<region>.amazonaws.com) and grants kms:Decrypt only to the Lambda execution role, then re-point the secret to this CMK. This is mandatory because, per AWS docs, the AWS managed key policy 'is established by the service. You cannot change the key policy'; its default policy grants kms:Encrypt/kms:Decrypt to Principal AWS '*' for any account principal that calls via Secrets Manager, so it can never be narrowed to a single role. Only a customer managed key gives the customer exclusive control of the key policy. (2) Option D: the Lambda execution role must also have the matching KMS permissions scoped at the resource level (the specific CMK ARN) so it can actually use the key when GetSecretValue triggers the KMS Decrypt of the data key. Both the key policy (B) and the principal's resource-scoped IAM permission (D) are required, and scoping to the key ARN enforces least privilege. This matches the dump's suggested answer.","explanation_zh":"目前該 secret 是使用 AWS 受管金鑰 aws/secretsmanager（預設金鑰）加密。要在最小權限下將解密限制為「只有」該 Lambda 執行角色，需要兩個互補步驟，因為 AWS KMS 採雙重控管模型：『Unless the key policy explicitly allows it, you cannot use IAM policies to allow access to a KMS key.』(1) 選項 B：建立一把 customer managed KMS key，其 key policy 信任 Secrets Manager（kms:ViaService = secretsmanager.<region>.amazonaws.com），且僅授予 Lambda 執行角色 kms:Decrypt，再將 secret 改用這把 CMK。此為必要，因為依 AWS 文件，AWS 受管金鑰政策『is established by the service. You cannot change the key policy』；其預設政策對 Principal AWS '*'（任何透過 Secrets Manager 呼叫的帳戶主體）授予 kms:Encrypt/kms:Decrypt，無法縮小到單一角色。只有 customer managed key 才能讓客戶完全掌控 key policy。(2) 選項 D：Lambda 執行角色也必須具備對應的 KMS 權限，並把範圍鎖定在資源層級（特定 CMK ARN），這樣 GetSecretValue 觸發 KMS 對 data key 進行 Decrypt 時才能實際使用該金鑰。key policy（B）與主體之資源範圍 IAM 權限（D）兩者皆需，並以金鑰 ARN 範圍落實最小權限。此結論與題庫建議答案一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Impossible. The default key for Secrets Manager is the AWS managed key aws/secretsmanager; its key policy is established by the service and cannot be modified by the customer ('You cannot change the key policy'). It cannot be edited to allow only the Lambda role, so it can never be narrowed for least privilege.","why_zh":"不可行。Secrets Manager 的預設金鑰是 AWS 受管金鑰 aws/secretsmanager，其 key policy 由服務設定且客戶無法修改（『You cannot change the key policy』），無法改成只允許 Lambda 角色，因此無法縮小達成最小權限。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Violates least privilege. Granting kms:Decrypt to the account root principal delegates control to IAM for the entire account, so any principal granted KMS access via an IAM policy could decrypt the secret, not just the Lambda role.","why_zh":"違反最小權限。將 kms:Decrypt 授予帳戶 root 主體等於把控制權交給整個帳戶的 IAM，任何透過 IAM 政策取得 KMS 權限的主體都能解密，而不只是 Lambda 角色。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Breaks functionality. Removing all KMS permissions from the Lambda role prevents the role from decrypting the data key, so GetSecretValue fails with AccessDenied and the function cannot retrieve the API keys. This is the opposite of granting the scoped permission required in Option D.","why_zh":"會破壞功能。移除 Lambda 角色的所有 KMS 權限後，角色無法解密 data key，GetSecretValue 會 AccessDenied 失敗，函式將無法取得 API keys。這與選項 D 所需的資源範圍授權完全相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/security-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/auth-and-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/least-privilege.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":139,"question_en":"A company's DevOps engineer is creating an AWS Lambda function to process notifications from an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. The Lambda function will process the notification messages and will write the contents of the notification messages to an Amazon RDS Multi-AZ DB instance. During testing, a database administrator accidentally shut down the DB instance. While the database was down the company lost several of the SNS notification messages that were delivered during that time. The DevOps engineer needs to prevent the loss of notification messages in the future. Which solutions will meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师正在创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于处理来自 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题的通知。该 Lambda 函数将处理通知消息，并将通知消息的内容写入 Amazon RDS 多可用区数据库实例。 在测试期间，一名数据库管理员意外关闭了数据库实例。在数据库停机期间，公司丢失了当时送达的几条 SNS 通知消息。 DevOps 工程师需要防止未来出现通知消息丢失的情况。 哪些解决方案能满足这一要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Replace the RDS Multi-AZ DB instance with an Amazon DynamoDB table.","B":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as a destination of the Lambda function.","C":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) dead-letter queue for the SNS topic.","D":"Subscribe an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue to the SNS topic. Configure the Lambda function to process messages from the SQS queue.","E":"Replace the SNS topic with an Amazon EventBridge event bus. Configure an EventBridge rule on the new event bus to invoke the Lambda function for each event."},"options_zh":{"A":"用 Amazon DynamoDB 表替换 RDS 多可用区数据库实例。","B":"将 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列配置为 Lambda 函数的目标。","C":"为 SNS 主题配置一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）死信队列。","D":"将 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列订阅到 SNS 主题。配置 Lambda 函数以处理来自 SQS 队列的消息。","E":"将 SNS 主题替换为 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。在新的事件总线上配置 EventBridge 规则，以便为每 个事件调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SNS delivered each notification to a Lambda function as an asynchronous invocation. While RDS was down, the function kept failing; once the SNS subscription retries and Lambda's own async retries exhausted with nowhere to capture the failures, the messages were discarded. The SNS docs state plainly that when retries are exhausted 'Amazon SNS discards the message - unless a dead-letter queue is attached to the subscription,' and the Lambda async docs state 'When an event expires or fails all processing attempts, Lambda discards it.' (C) Attaching an Amazon SQS dead-letter queue to the SNS subscription holds messages that cannot be delivered to the endpoint after retries so they are retained for reprocessing instead of discarded - the canonical SNS durability fix. (D) Subscribing an SQS queue to the SNS topic and having Lambda poll that queue inserts a durable buffer (SQS retains messages, up to 14 days); if Lambda fails because RDS is down, the SQS event source mapping leaves the messages in the queue (they become visible again after the visibility timeout) until they are processed successfully, preventing loss. Both directly satisfy 'prevent the loss of notification messages.'","explanation_zh":"SNS 將每筆通知以非同步呼叫的方式送至 Lambda。在 RDS 停機期間，function 持續失敗；當 SNS 訂閱重試與 Lambda 自身的非同步重試都耗盡且沒有任何地方可保存失敗訊息時，訊息就被丟棄。SNS 官方文件明確指出，重試耗盡後『Amazon SNS 會丟棄訊息 — 除非該訂閱附加了 dead-letter queue』，而 Lambda 非同步文件也指出『當事件過期或所有處理嘗試都失敗時，Lambda 會丟棄它』。(C) 在 SNS 訂閱上附加 Amazon SQS dead-letter queue，可保留重試後仍無法投遞至端點的訊息以供重新處理，而非被丟棄，這是 SNS 持久性的標準修正方式。(D) 將 SQS queue 訂閱至 SNS topic，並讓 Lambda 輪詢該 queue，等於插入一個持久緩衝（SQS 訊息最長保留 14 天）；若 Lambda 因 RDS 停機而失敗，SQS event source mapping 會將訊息留在 queue 中（在 visibility timeout 後重新可見），直到成功處理為止，因而避免遺失。兩者都能直接滿足『避免通知訊息遺失』的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Replacing RDS with DynamoDB only swaps the data store; it does nothing to make the SNS->Lambda delivery durable. If the target store were unavailable or throttling, messages would still be discarded after SNS/Lambda retries exhaust, so loss is not prevented.","why_zh":"把 RDS 換成 DynamoDB 只是更換資料庫，並未讓 SNS->Lambda 的投遞變得持久；若目標資料庫不可用或受限流，訊息在 SNS/Lambda 重試耗盡後仍會被丟棄，因此無法防止遺失。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Lambda 'destination' is an async on-success/on-failure record target that only fires after Lambda's own retries are exhausted, and the option does not even specify on-failure. It protects neither the in-flight SNS delivery nor the data, and is the weaker, non-canonical choice versus an SNS subscription dead-letter queue (C). The documented AWS pattern for SNS notification durability is the subscription DLQ, not a Lambda destination.","why_zh":"Lambda 的『destination』是非同步 on-success/on-failure 的記錄目標，只會在 Lambda 自身重試耗盡後觸發，且此選項甚至未指明 on-failure。它既無法保護進行中的 SNS 投遞，也無法保護資料，相較於 SNS 訂閱 dead-letter queue(C) 較弱且非標準做法。AWS 文件針對 SNS 通知持久性建議的是訂閱層級 DLQ，而非 Lambda destination。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Replacing SNS with an EventBridge bus that invokes Lambda is still an asynchronous invocation with the same retry-then-discard behavior. EventBridge expires events after their maximum age (24h by default) and, with no DLQ configured on the rule/target, still loses them. As worded the option adds no DLQ or buffer, so it does not inherently prevent loss.","why_zh":"將 SNS 換成 EventBridge event bus 再呼叫 Lambda，仍是非同步呼叫，具有相同的『重試後丟棄』行為；EventBridge 在事件超過最大保留時間（預設 24 小時）後會過期，且若 rule/target 未設定 DLQ，事件仍會遺失。依此選項的敘述並未加入任何 DLQ 或緩衝，因此本質上無法防止遺失。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-dead-letter-queues.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-configure-dead-letter-queue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/subscribe-sqs-queue-to-sns-topic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-error-handling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-retain-records.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":140,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The company uses an AWS CodePipeline pipeline to deploy the application into multiple AWS Regions. The pipeline is configured with a stage for each Region. Each stage contains an AWS CloudFormation action for each Region. When the pipeline deploys the application to a Region, the company wants to confirm that the application is in a healthy state before the pipeline moves on to the next Region. Amazon Route 53 record sets are configured for the application in each Region. A DevOps engineer creates a Route 53 health check that is based on an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for each Region where the application is deployed. What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的应用程序。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 管道将应用程序部署 到多个 AWS 区域。该管道针对每个区域都配置了一个阶段。每个阶段都包含针对每个区域的 AWS CloudFormation 操作。 当管道将应用程序部署到某个区域时，公司希望在管道继续推进到下一个区域之前确认应用程序处于健康 状态。在每个区域都为应用程序配置了 Amazon Route 53 记录集。一位 DevOps 工程师为应用程序部署的每 个区域创建了一个基于 Amazon CloudWatch 警报的 Route 53 健康检查。 为了满足要求，开发运维工程师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Step Functions workflow to check the state of the CloudWatch alarm. Configure the Step Functions workflow to exit with an error if the alarm is in the ALARM state. Create a new stage in the pipeline between each Region deployment stage. In each new stage, include an action to invoke the Step Functions workflow.","B":"Configure an AWS CodeDeploy application to deploy a CloudFormation template with automatic rollback. Configure the CloudWatch alarm as the instance health check for the CodeDeploy application. Remove the CloudFormation actions from the pipeline. Create a CodeDeploy action in the pipeline stage for each Region.","C":"Create a new pipeline stage for each Region where the application is deployed. Configure a CloudWatch alarm action for the new stage to check the state of the CloudWatch alarm and to exit with an error if the alarm is in the ALARM state","D":"Configure the CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances to report the application status to the Route 53 health check. Create a new pipeline stage for each Region where the application is deployed. Configure a CloudWatch alarm action to exit with an error if the CloudWatch alarm is in the ALARM state."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Step Functions 工作流来检查 CloudWatch 警报的状态。将 Step Functions 工作流配置为在 警报处于 ALARM 状态时以错误退出。在每个区域部署阶段之间创建一个新的阶段。在每个新阶段中， 包含一个调用 Step Functions 工作流的操作。","B":"配置一个 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序以部署带有自动回滚功能的 CloudFormation 模板。将 CloudWatch 警 报配置为 CodeDeploy 应用程序的实例健康检查。从管道中移除 CloudFormation 操作。在每个区域的管 道阶段中创建一个 CodeDeploy 操作。","C":"为应用部署的每个区域创建一个新的流水线阶段。为新阶段配置 CloudWatch 警报操作，以检查 CloudWatch 警报的状态，如果警报处于“ALARM”状态，则退出并报错。","D":"在 EC2 实例上配置 CloudWatch 代理，将应用程序状态报告给 Route 53 健康检查。为应用程序部署的每 个区域创建一个新的流水线阶段。配置 CloudWatch 警报操作，如果 CloudWatch 警报处于 ALARM 状 态，则退出并报错。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The Step Functions invoke action is a real, documented CodePipeline action (Category: Invoke, Owner: AWS, Provider: StepFunctions). A state machine can call the CloudWatch DescribeAlarms API to check the Route 53-backed health-check alarm and use a Fail state, which causes the invoke action to fail. When a CodePipeline action fails, the stage fails and the pipeline stops without advancing to the next Region stage. By inserting a new stage between each Region's deployment stage that invokes this Step Functions workflow, the pipeline confirms the application is healthy in one Region before deploying to the next. This integrates cleanly with the existing CloudFormation deploy actions and the existing CloudWatch alarm / Route 53 health check without re-architecting the pipeline. Options C and D rely on a non-existent 'CloudWatch alarm action' type; the only valid action categories are Source, Build, Test, Deploy, Approval, and Invoke, and CloudWatchAlarm exists only as a Rule for stage conditions, not as a standalone action you place to 'exit with an error.'","explanation_zh":"Step Functions invoke action 是 CodePipeline 真實存在且有官方文件的動作（Category: Invoke、Owner: AWS、Provider: StepFunctions）。state machine 可呼叫 CloudWatch DescribeAlarms API 檢查由 Route 53 健康檢查支援的 alarm 狀態，並透過 Fail state 使該 invoke action 失敗。當 CodePipeline 的 action 失敗時，該 stage 失敗且 pipeline 會停止，不會前進到下一個 Region stage。在每個 Region 部署 stage 之間插入一個呼叫此 Step Functions workflow 的新 stage，pipeline 便能在前往下一個 Region 前先確認當前 Region 應用程式健康。此做法可與既有的 CloudFormation 部署動作以及既有的 CloudWatch alarm / Route 53 健康檢查無縫整合，無須重構 pipeline。選項 C 與 D 依賴並不存在的『CloudWatch alarm action』動作類型；唯一有效的 action 類別為 Source、Build、Test、Deploy、Approval 與 Invoke，而 CloudWatchAlarm 僅以 stage conditions 的 Rule 形式存在，並非可放入 stage 中『以錯誤結束』的獨立 action。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeDeploy deploys applications to EC2/Lambda/ECS compute, not CloudFormation templates; you cannot have a CodeDeploy application 'deploy a CloudFormation template.' It also misuses 'instance health check' (CodeDeploy deployment health is governed by deployment configurations, not by attaching a CloudWatch alarm as an instance health check) and removing the CloudFormation actions needlessly re-architects a working pipeline. CodeDeploy automatic rollback is per-deployment and does not act as a cross-Region progression gate.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 部署的是 EC2/Lambda/ECS 等運算目標，而非 CloudFormation 範本；CodeDeploy 應用程式無法『部署 CloudFormation 範本』。此選項誤用『instance health check』（CodeDeploy 的部署健康由 deployment configuration 控管，而非把 CloudWatch alarm 當成 instance health check），且移除 CloudFormation 動作會不必要地重構可運作的 pipeline。CodeDeploy 的自動回復屬單次部署層級，無法作為跨 Region 前進的閘門。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no 'CloudWatch alarm action' type in CodePipeline. The valid action categories are Source, Build, Test, Deploy, Approval, and Invoke. CloudWatchAlarm exists only as a Rule for stage conditions (Entry / On Failure / On Success), not as a standalone action you place in a stage to 'exit with an error.'","why_zh":"CodePipeline 並不存在『CloudWatch alarm action』動作類型。有效的動作類別為 Source、Build、Test、Deploy、Approval 與 Invoke。CloudWatchAlarm 僅以 stage conditions（Entry / On Failure / On Success）的 Rule 形式存在，並非可放入 stage 中『以錯誤結束』的獨立 action。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fictional 'CloudWatch alarm action' problem as C. Additionally, the CloudWatch agent reports metrics/logs to CloudWatch; it does not 'report application status to a Route 53 health check.' Route 53 health checks of this type are derived from a CloudWatch alarm, not fed by the agent.","why_zh":"與 C 相同，依賴並不存在的『CloudWatch alarm action』。此外，CloudWatch agent 是將指標/日誌回報至 CloudWatch，並非『將應用程式狀態回報給 Route 53 健康檢查』；此類 Route 53 健康檢查是依據 CloudWatch alarm，而非由 agent 餵入。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-StepFunctions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-valid-providers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/concepts-how-it-works-conditions.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":141,"question_en":"A company plans to use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor its Amazon EC2 instances. The company needs to stop EC2 instances when the average of the NetworkPacketsIn metric is less than 5 for at least 3 hours in a 12-hour time window. The company must evaluate the metric every hour. The EC2 instances must continue to run if there is missing data for the NetworkPacketsIn metric during the evaluation period. A DevOps engineer creates a CloudWatch alarm for the NetworkPacketsIn metric. The DevOps engineer configures a threshold value of 5 and an evaluation period of 1 hour. Which set of additional actions should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划使用亚马逊 CloudWatch 来监控其亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司需要在 12 小时的时间窗口内， 当 NetworkPacketsIn 指标平均值连续 3 小时低于 5 时停止 EC2 实例。该公司必须每小时评估一次该指 标。如果在评估期间 NetworkPacketsIn 指标存在缺失数据，则 EC2 实例必须继续运行。 一位 DevOps 工程师为 NetworkPacketsIn 指标创建了一个 CloudWatch 警报。该 DevOps 工程师将阈值 设为 5，并将评估周期设为 1 小时。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪一系列额外行动来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Datapoints to Alarm value to be 3 out of 12. Configure the alarm to treat missing data as breaching the threshold. Add an AWS Systems Manager action to stop the instance when the alarm enters the ALARM state.","B":"Configure the Datapoints to Alarm value to be 3 out of 12. Configure the alarm to treat missing data as not breaching the threshold. Add an EC2 action to stop the instance when the alarm enters the ALARM state.","C":"Configure the Datapoints to Alarm value to be 9 out of 12. Configure the alarm to treat missing data as breaching the threshold. Add an EC2 action to stop the instance when the alarm enters the ALARM state.","D":"Configure the Datapoints to Alarm value to be 9 out of 12. Configure the alarm to treat missing data as not breaching the threshold. Add an AWS Systems Manager action to stop the instance when the alarm enters the ALARM state."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据点的告警值配置为 12 个中的 3 个。将告警配置为将缺失数据视为超出阈值。添加一个 AWS 系统管理器操作，当告警进入“告警”状态时停止实例。","B":"将数据点的告警值配置为 12 个中的 3 个。配置告警，将缺失数据视为未超出阈值。添加一个 EC2 操作，在告警进入“告警”状态时停止实例。","C":"将数据点的告警值配置为 12 中的 9。将告警配置为将缺失数据视为超出阈值。添加一个 EC2 操作， 在告警进入“告警”状态时停止实例。","D":"将数据点的告警值配置为 12 中的 9。将告警配置为将缺失数据视为未超出阈值。添加一个 AWS 系 统管理器操作，当告警进入“告警”状态时停止实例。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"With a 1-hour period, a 12-hour window equals 12 evaluation periods (N=12), and 'less than 5 for at least 3 hours' maps to 3 breaching datapoints, so Datapoints to Alarm must be 3 out of 12 (an M-of-N alarm that fires when 3 of the most recent 12 datapoints breach). This eliminates the 9-out-of-12 options C and D. The requirement that instances keep running when data is missing means missing datapoints must not drive the alarm to ALARM; treating missing data as notBreaching keeps the alarm in OK (per the CloudWatch missing-data evaluation tables, NOT BREACHING never yields ALARM from missing-only data), whereas treating it as breaching (A and C) would push the alarm to ALARM and stop the instance. Finally, only the native CloudWatch EC2 action directly stops an instance; a Systems Manager alarm action merely creates an OpsItem in OpsCenter and cannot stop an instance, eliminating A and D. Only option B combines 3-of-12 datapoints, notBreaching missing-data treatment, and an EC2 stop action. (Note: AWS actually recommends treating missing data as 'missing' for EC2 stop/terminate alarms, but that option is not offered; among the choices, notBreaching is the one that satisfies 'instances must continue to run' because the alarm goes to OK rather than ALARM.)","explanation_zh":"在 period 設為 1 小時時,12 小時時間窗等於 12 個 evaluation periods(N=12),而「低於 5 達至少 3 小時」對應 3 個違規 datapoints,因此 Datapoints to Alarm 必須是 3 out of 12(即 M-of-N 警報:最近 12 個 datapoints 中有 3 個超過門檻即觸發)。這排除了使用 9 out of 12 的選項 C 與 D。需求「資料遺失時 instance 必須繼續運行」表示遺失的 datapoints 不能把警報推向 ALARM;將 missing data 視為 notBreaching 會讓警報維持 OK 狀態(依 CloudWatch missing-data 評估表,NOT BREACHING 在僅有遺失資料時絕不會產生 ALARM),而視為 breaching(A 與 C)則會把警報推向 ALARM 並停止 instance。最後,只有原生的 CloudWatch EC2 action 能直接停止 instance;Systems Manager 警報 action 只會在 OpsCenter 建立 OpsItem,無法停止 instance,故排除 A 與 D。只有選項 B 同時具備 3-of-12 datapoints、notBreaching 的遺失資料處理,以及 EC2 stop action。(補充:AWS 實際上建議 EC2 stop/terminate 警報將遺失資料視為 'missing',但題目未提供此選項;在現有選項中,notBreaching 是能滿足『instance 必須繼續運行』的選擇,因為警報會進入 OK 而非 ALARM。)","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Treating missing data as breaching would push the alarm to ALARM when NetworkPacketsIn data is missing, stopping the instance and violating the 'must continue to run on missing data' requirement; also a Systems Manager alarm action only creates an OpsItem, it cannot stop the instance.","why_zh":"將遺失資料視為 breaching 會在 NetworkPacketsIn 資料遺失時把警報推向 ALARM 並停止 instance,違反『資料遺失時必須繼續運行』的要求;且 Systems Manager 警報 action 只會建立 OpsItem,無法停止 instance。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"9 out of 12 would require 9 breaching hours, not the required 3 hours; and treating missing data as breaching would stop the instance on missing data, violating the keep-running requirement.","why_zh":"9 out of 12 需要 9 小時違規,而非要求的 3 小時;且將遺失資料視為 breaching 會在資料遺失時停止 instance,違反保持運行的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"9 out of 12 requires 9 breaching hours instead of 3, and a Systems Manager alarm action only creates an OpsItem in OpsCenter rather than stopping the EC2 instance.","why_zh":"9 out of 12 需要 9 小時違規而非 3 小時,且 Systems Manager 警報 action 只會在 OpsCenter 建立 OpsItem,無法停止 EC2 instance。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/alarms-and-missing-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/UsingAlarmActions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/AlarmThatSendsEmail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/OpsCenter-creating-or-editing-existing-alarm-console.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":142,"question_en":"A company manages 500 AWS accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company discovers many unattached Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes in all the accounts. The company wants to automatically tag the unattached EBS volumes for investigation. A DevOps engineer needs to deploy an AWS Lambda function to all the AWS accounts. The Lambda function must run every 30 minutes to tag all the EBS volumes that have been unattached for a period of 7 days or more. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient manner?","question_zh":"一家公司管理着 AWS 组织中的 500 个 AWS 账户。该公司发现所有账户中存在大量未挂载的 Amazon Elastic Block Store（Amazon EBS）卷。该公司希望自动为这些未挂载的 EBS 卷添加标签以便进行调 查。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要将一个 AWS Lambda 函数部署到所有 AWS 账户中。该 Lambda 函数必须每 30 分钟运行一次，为所有已断开连接 7 天或更长时间的 EBS 卷添加标签。 哪种解决方案能在操作效率最高的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a delegated administrator account for the organization. Create an AWS CloudFormation template that contains the Lambda function. Use CloudFormation StackSets to deploy the CloudFormation template from the delegated administrator account to all the member accounts in the organization. Create an Amazon EventBridge event bus in the delegated administrator account to invoke the Lambda function in each member account every 30 minutes.","B":"Create a cross-account IAM role in the organization's member accounts. Attach the AWSLambda_FullAccess policy and the AWSCloudFormationFullAccess policy to the role. Create an AWS CloudFormation template that contains the Lambda function and an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to invoke the Lambda function every 30 minutes. Create a custom script in the organization’s management account that assumes the role and deploys the CloudFormation template to the member accounts.","C":"Configure a delegated administrator account for the organization. Create an AWS CloudFormation template that contains the Lambda function and an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to invoke the Lambda function every 30 minutes. Use CloudFormation StackSets to deploy the CloudFormation template from the delegated administrator account to all the member accounts in the organization","D":"Create a cross-account IAM role in the organization's member accounts. Attach the AmazonS3FullAccess policy and the AWSCodeDeployDeployerAccess policy to the role. Use AWS CodeDeploy to assume the role to deploy the Lambda function from the organization's management account. Configure an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule in the member accounts to invoke the Lambda function every 30 minutes."},"options_zh":{"A":"为组织配置一个委托管理员账户。创建一个包含 Lambda 函数的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从委托管理员账户将 CloudFormation 模板部署到组织中的所有成员账 户。在委托管理员账户中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线，每 30 分钟调用每个成员账户 中的 Lambda 函数。","B":"在组织成员账户中创建一个跨账户 IAM 角色。将 AWSLambda_FullAccess 策略和 AWSCloudFormationFullAccess 策略附加到该角色。创建一个包含 Lambda 函数和每 30 分钟通过 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则调用 Lambda 函数的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。在组织管理账户 中创建一个自定义脚本，该脚本可代入该角色并将 CloudFormation 模板部署到成员账户。","C":"为组织配置一个委托管理员账户。创建一个包含 Lambda 函数和 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则的 AWS CloudFormation 模板，该规则每 30 分钟调用一次 Lambda 函数。使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从委托管理员账户将 CloudFormation 模板部署到组织中的所有成员账户。","D":"在组织成员账户中创建跨账户 IAM 角色。将 AmazonS3FullAccess 策略和 AWSCodeDeployDeplo yerAccess 策略附加到该角色。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 假定该角色，从组织管理账户部署 Lambda 函数。在成员账户中配置 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则，每 30 分钟调用一次 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Option C is the most operationally efficient. CloudFormation StackSets with service-managed permissions can be initiated from a delegated administrator account and deploy a single template to all member accounts of an AWS Organization in one operation without creating IAM roles in each target account (StackSets creates the roles on your behalf, per the StackSets concepts doc). By packaging BOTH the Lambda function AND a local EventBridge scheduled rule (rate of 30 minutes) in that one template, each member account becomes self-contained: its own rule invokes its own local Lambda on schedule, with no cross-account invocation, no per-function resource policies, and no custom scripting. This scales cleanly to 500 accounts. Option A is the trap: it pushes only the Lambda via StackSets and then tries to drive all 500 functions from a single EventBridge event bus in the delegated admin account. EventBridge cross-account integration operates at the event-bus level and, per the cross-account docs, now requires IAM roles for cross-account event-bus targets; fanning a schedule out to 500 Lambda targets in other accounts is far more complex and brittle, defeating operational efficiency.","explanation_zh":"選項 C 最具操作效率。採用 service-managed permissions 的 CloudFormation StackSets 可由 delegated administrator account 發起，以一次操作將單一範本部署到 AWS Organizations 的所有成員帳戶，且不需在每個目標帳戶手動建立 IAM 角色（依 StackSets concepts 文件，StackSets 會代為建立角色）。將 Lambda function 與本地的 EventBridge scheduled rule（每 30 分鐘 rate）一起打包進同一範本後，每個成員帳戶都自成一體：由各自的 rule 觸發各自的本地 Lambda，無需跨帳戶調用、無需在每個函式上設定 resource policy、也無需自訂腳本，能乾淨地擴展到 500 個帳戶。選項 A 是陷阱：它只透過 StackSets 部署 Lambda，再企圖用 delegated admin account 中單一 EventBridge event bus 去驅動全部 500 個函式。EventBridge 跨帳戶整合是在 event bus 層級運作，依跨帳戶文件，現已要求跨帳戶 event bus 目標使用 IAM 角色；將排程扇出到其他帳戶的 500 個 Lambda 目標遠更複雜且脆弱，違背操作效率原則。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deploys only the Lambda via StackSets, then relies on a single EventBridge event bus in the delegated admin account to invoke the Lambda in each of the 500 member accounts every 30 minutes. Scheduled rules and their targets run within their own account; EventBridge cross-account integration is account-to-account event-bus forwarding (and now requires IAM roles for cross-account event-bus targets), so driving 500 cross-account Lambda targets is complex and not operationally efficient. A local scheduled rule bundled in the template (option C) avoids all of this.","why_zh":"只透過 StackSets 部署 Lambda，再依賴 delegated admin account 的單一 EventBridge event bus 每 30 分鐘調用 500 個成員帳戶中的 Lambda。scheduled rule 與其目標在自身帳戶執行；EventBridge 跨帳戶整合是帳戶對帳戶的 event bus 轉發（現要求跨帳戶 event bus 目標使用 IAM 角色），驅動 500 個跨帳戶 Lambda 目標複雜且不具操作效率。將本地 scheduled rule 一併打包進範本（選項 C）可完全避免這些問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses a custom script in the management account that assumes cross-account roles to deploy CloudFormation to each member account, and attaches overly broad AWSLambda_FullAccess and AWSCloudFormationFullAccess policies. Custom multi-account scripting and per-account role management for 500 accounts is exactly what StackSets service-managed permissions eliminate; this is high operational overhead and violates least privilege.","why_zh":"在管理帳戶使用自訂腳本，透過跨帳戶角色逐一部署 CloudFormation 到每個成員帳戶，並附加過於寬鬆的 AWSLambda_FullAccess 與 AWSCloudFormationFullAccess。為 500 個帳戶自訂腳本與逐帳戶管理角色正是 StackSets service-managed permissions 要消除的工作，操作負擔高且違反最小權限。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeDeploy is an application deployment service, not the organization-wide multi-account distribution mechanism; assuming a cross-account role from the management account to deploy a Lambda via CodeDeploy across 500 accounts is not how Lambda is provisioned at organization scale. The attached AmazonS3FullAccess and AWSCodeDeployDeployerAccess policies are mismatched for tagging EBS volumes, making this both technically wrong and inefficient.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 是應用程式部署服務，並非組織層級多帳戶分發機制；透過管理帳戶假設跨帳戶角色用 CodeDeploy 在 500 個帳戶部署 Lambda 並非組織規模下佈建 Lambda 的方式。所附 AmazonS3FullAccess 與 AWSCodeDeployDeployerAccess 與標記 EBS volume 的需求不符，技術上既錯誤又無效率。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/what-is-cfnstacksets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-create-rule-schedule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-cross-account.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":143,"question_en":"A company's production environment uses an AWS CodeDeploy blue/green deployment to deploy an application. The deployment incudes Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling groups that launch instances that run Amazon Linux 2. A working appspec.yml file exists in the code repository and contains the following text: A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that a script downloads and installs a license file onto the instances before the replacement instances start to handle request traffic. The DevOps engineer adds a hooks section to the appspec.yml file. Which hook should the DevOps engineer use to run the script that downloads and installs the license file?","question_zh":"一家公司的生产环境使用 AWS CodeDeploy 蓝/绿部署来部署应用程序。该部署包括使用 Amazon EC2 自动扩展组启动运行 Amazon Linux 2 的实例。 代码库中存在一个有效的 appspec.yml 文件，其中包含以下内容： DevOps 工程师需要确保在替换实例开始处理请求流量之前，脚本能够将许可证文件下载并安装到实例上。 为此，DevOps 工程师在 appspec.yml 文件中添加了一个 hooks 部分。 DevOps 工程师应该使用哪个钩子来运行下载并安装许可证文件的脚本？","options_en":{"A":"AfterBlockTraffic","B":"BeforeBlockTraffic","C":"BeforeInstall","D":"DownloadBundle"},"options_zh":{"A":"堵车之后","B":"阻止区块传播前","C":"安装前","D":"下载包"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is a CodeDeploy EC2/On-Premises blue/green deployment, so the script must run on the REPLACEMENT (new) instances before they begin serving request traffic. In the AppSpec 'Lifecycle event hook availability' table, the 'Blue/green deployment: Replacement instances' column allows only ApplicationStop, DownloadBundle, BeforeInstall, Install, AfterInstall, ApplicationStart, ValidateService, and BeforeAllowTraffic. Of the four options, BeforeInstall (C) is the only scriptable hook that runs on the replacement instances; AWS documents it for preinstall tasks such as decrypting files and creating a backup, which fits downloading and installing a license file before the application is installed and before the instances start to handle traffic. DownloadBundle (D) is reserved for the CodeDeploy agent and 'cannot be used to run scripts,' and the BlockTraffic-related hooks BeforeBlockTraffic (B) and AfterBlockTraffic (A) are not available on replacement instances at all (they run only on the original/terminating instances being deregistered). Therefore BeforeInstall is correct.","explanation_zh":"這是一個 CodeDeploy EC2/On-Premises 的 blue/green 部署，因此腳本必須在「replacement（新）instances」開始處理請求流量之前，於這些新執行個體上執行。在 AppSpec 的「Lifecycle event hook availability」表格中，「Blue/green deployment: Replacement instances」欄位只允許 ApplicationStop、DownloadBundle、BeforeInstall、Install、AfterInstall、ApplicationStart、ValidateService 與 BeforeAllowTraffic。在四個選項中，BeforeInstall（C）是唯一可在 replacement instances 上執行腳本的 hook；AWS 文件說明它用於安裝前（preinstall）任務，例如解密檔案與建立備份，正好適合在應用程式安裝之前、且執行個體開始處理流量之前下載並安裝授權檔。DownloadBundle（D）保留給 CodeDeploy agent，'cannot be used to run scripts'；而 BlockTraffic 相關的 BeforeBlockTraffic（B）與 AfterBlockTraffic（A）在 replacement instances 上完全不可用（只會在被取消註冊的 original/終止執行個體上執行）。因此 BeforeInstall 為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AfterBlockTraffic is not available on blue/green replacement instances (the availability table shows it only on original/terminating instances and rollback-replacement). It runs after instances are deregistered from the load balancer, which applies to instances being torn down, not the new ones coming up to serve traffic.","why_zh":"AfterBlockTraffic 不適用於 blue/green 的 replacement instances（可用性表顯示它只用於 original/終止執行個體與回滾替換情境）。它在執行個體從負載平衡器取消註冊後執行，針對的是被淘汰的執行個體，而非即將上線提供流量的新執行個體。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"BeforeBlockTraffic is also not available on replacement instances; it runs on instances before they are deregistered from a load balancer (original/terminating instances), so it cannot run the license script on the new instances.","why_zh":"BeforeBlockTraffic 同樣不適用於 replacement instances；它在執行個體從負載平衡器取消註冊之前執行（original/終止執行個體），因此無法在新執行個體上執行授權腳本。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DownloadBundle is reserved for the CodeDeploy agent (it copies the revision files to a temporary location) and the AWS docs explicitly state it 'cannot be used to run scripts,' so no license-install script can be attached to it.","why_zh":"DownloadBundle 保留給 CodeDeploy agent（用於將修訂版檔案複製到暫存位置），AWS 文件明確指出它『cannot be used to run scripts』，因此無法附加授權安裝腳本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":144,"question_en":"A company has an application that includes AWS Lambda functions. The Lambda functions run Python code that is stored in an AWS CodeCommit repository. The company has recently experienced failures in the production environment because of an error in the Python code. An engineer has written unit tests for the Lambda functions to help avoid releasing any future defects into the production environment. The company's DevOps team needs to implement a solution to integrate the unit tests into an existing AWS CodePipeline pipeline. The solution must produce reports about the unit tests for the company to view. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个包含 AWS Lambda 函数的应用程序。这些 Lambda 函数运行存储在 AWS CodeCommit 代码 库中的 Python 代码。该公司最近在生产环境中遇到了故障，原因是 Python 代码中存在错误。一位工程师 为这些 Lambda 函数编写了单元测试，以帮助避免将来在生产环境中出现任何缺陷。 该公司的 DevOps 团队需要实施一个解决方案，将单元测试集成到现有的 AWS CodePipeline 管道中。该 解决方案必须生成有关单元测试的报告，以便公司查看。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Associate the CodeCommit repository with Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer. Create a new AWS CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, configure a test stage that uses the new CodeBuild project. Create a buildspec.yml file in the CodeCommit repository. In the buildspec yml file, define the actions to run a CodeGuru review.","B":"Create a new AWS CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, configure a test stage that uses the new CodeBuild project. Create a CodeBuild report group. Create a buildspec.yml file in the CodeCommit repository. In the buildspec.yml file, define the actions to run the unit tests with an output of JUNITXML in the build phase section. Configure the test reports to be uploaded to the new CodeBuild report group.","C":"Create a new AWS CodeArtifact repository. Create a new AWS CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, configure a test stage that uses the new CodeBuild project. Create an appspec.yml file in the original CodeCommit repository. In the appspec.yml file, define the actions to run the unit tests with an output of CUCUMBERJSON in the build phase section. Configure the tests reports to be sent to the new CodeArtifact repository.","D":"Create a new AWS CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, configure a test stage that uses the new CodeBuild project. Create a new Amazon S3 bucket. Create a buildspec.yml file in the CodeCommit repository. In the buildspec yml file, define the actions to run the unit tests with an output of HTML in the phases section. In the reports section, upload the test reports to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CodeCommit 存储库与 Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 关联。创建一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中，配置一个使用新 CodeBuild 项目的测试阶段。在 CodeCommit 存储库中创建一 个 buildspec.yml 文件。在 buildspec.yml 文件中，定义运行 CodeGuru 审查的操作。","B":"创建一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中，配置一个使用新 CodeBuild 项目的测试 阶段。创建一个 CodeBuild 报告组。在其中创建一个 buildspec.yml 文件。 在 CodeCommit 存储库中，在 buildspec.yml 文件中定义在构建阶段运行单元测试的操作，并将输出 设置为 JUNITXML。配置将测试报告上传到新的 CodeBuild 报告组。","C":"创建一个新的 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。创建一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中， 配置一个测试阶段，使用新的 CodeBuild 项目。在原始的 CodeCommit 存储库中创建一个 appspec. yml 文件。在 appspec.yml 文件中，在构建阶段部分定义运行单元测试的操作，并将输出设置为 CUCUMBERJSON。配置将测试报告发送到新的 CodeArtifact 存储库。","D":"创建一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中，配置一个使用新 CodeBuild 项目的测试 阶段。创建一个新的 Amazon S3 存储桶。在 CodeCommit 代码库中创建一个 buildspec.yml 文件。在 buildspec.yml 文件的 phases 部分定义运行单元测试并输出 HTML 格式报告的操作。在 reports 部分， 将测试报告上传到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to execute Python (pytest) unit tests inside an existing CodePipeline and produce viewable reports. AWS CodeBuild has native test reporting: you run the tests in a build phase of buildspec.yml and declare a reports section that points to a CodeBuild report group with a supported file-format. The supported test report formats are Cucumber JSON, JUnit XML, NUnit XML, NUnit3 XML, TestNG XML, and Visual Studio TRX. The official pytest reporting guide shows exactly this pattern: run 'python -m pytest --junitxml=...' and add a reports section with file-format: JUNITXML uploading to a report group, which is then viewable in the CodeBuild console. Option B matches this canonical pattern (CodeBuild project as a CodePipeline test stage, a report group, buildspec.yml, JUNITXML output uploaded to the report group), so it is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是在現有的 CodePipeline 中執行 Python (pytest) 單元測試並產生可檢視的報告。AWS CodeBuild 內建測試報告功能：在 buildspec.yml 的 build 階段執行測試，並宣告 reports 區段指向一個 CodeBuild report group，搭配支援的 file-format。CodeBuild 支援的測試報告格式為 Cucumber JSON、JUnit XML、NUnit XML、NUnit3 XML、TestNG XML 與 Visual Studio TRX。官方 pytest 報告指引正是此模式：執行 'python -m pytest --junitxml=...'，並加入 reports 區段設定 file-format: JUNITXML 上傳至 report group，之後即可在 CodeBuild 主控台檢視。選項 B 完全符合此標準模式（以 CodeBuild project 作為 CodePipeline 的 test stage、建立 report group、使用 buildspec.yml、輸出 JUNITXML 並上傳至 report group），因此正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer performs automated static code analysis and recommendations; it does not execute the engineer's pytest unit tests or produce unit-test reports. A CodeGuru review in a buildspec would not run or report on the new unit tests, so it fails the requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 執行的是自動化靜態程式碼分析與建議，並不會執行工程師撰寫的 pytest 單元測試或產生單元測試報告。在 buildspec 中執行 CodeGuru review 不會運行或報告這些新測試，因此不符合需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Multiple errors: appspec.yml belongs to CodeDeploy (not CodeBuild) and is not where test commands/reports are defined; CodeArtifact is a software package repository, not a destination for test reports (reports go to report groups, optionally exported to S3). The combination does not produce CodeBuild test reports.","why_zh":"多處錯誤：appspec.yml 屬於 CodeDeploy（非 CodeBuild），也不是定義測試指令／報告之處；CodeArtifact 是軟體套件儲存庫，並非測試報告的目的地（報告應送往 report group，必要時匯出至 S3）。此組合無法產生 CodeBuild 測試報告。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"HTML is not a supported CodeBuild test report file-format (only Cucumber JSON, JUnit XML, NUnit XML, NUnit3 XML, TestNG XML, and Visual Studio TRX/TRX XML are supported). Test reports are produced via a report group and the reports section, not by uploading HTML files to an S3 bucket, so this does not yield viewable native CodeBuild test reports.","why_zh":"HTML 不是 CodeBuild 支援的測試報告 file-format（僅支援 Cucumber JSON、JUnit XML、NUnit XML、NUnit3 XML、TestNG XML 與 Visual Studio TRX/TRX XML）。測試報告是透過 report group 與 reports 區段產生，而非把 HTML 檔案上傳到 S3 bucket，因此無法產生可檢視的原生 CodeBuild 測試報告。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/test-reporting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/test-report-pytest.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/report-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":145,"question_en":"A company manages multiple AWS accounts in AWS Organizations. The company’s security policy states that AWS account root user credentials for member accounts must not be used. The company monitors access to the root user credentials. A recent alert shows that the root user in a member account launched an Amazon EC2 instance. A DevOps engineer must create an SCP at the organization's root level that will prevent the root user in member accounts from making any AWS service API calls. Which SCP will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司的安全政策规定，成员账户的 AWS 账户根用户凭 证不得使用。该公司会监控对根用户凭证的访问情况。 最近的一则警报显示，成员账户中的 root 用户启动了一个 Amazon EC2 实例。DevOps 工程师必须 在组织的根级别创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），以防止成员账户中的 root 用户调用任何 AWS 服 务的 API。 哪个 SCP 会符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"","B":"","C":"","D":""},"options_zh":{},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is a single SCP at the organization root that prevents ONLY the member-account root user from making any AWS service API call. SCPs follow a deny-by-default, guardrail model: an Allow-type SCP only widens the maximum-permission boundary and cannot block anything, while an explicit Deny attached anywhere in the path from the root down (including the root) denies that permission for every account beneath it. So the policy must use Effect: Deny, Action: \"*\", Resource: \"*\". To restrict only the root user (and not IAM users or roles), it must carry a Condition that POSITIVELY matches the root principal: StringLike on aws:PrincipalArn equal to arn:aws:iam::*:root. The account root user's ARN is arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT-ID:root, so the wildcard in the account-ID position lets this one root-level SCP cover the root user of every member account, while IAM user/role ARNs (:user/... and :assumed-role/...) do not match and remain unaffected. Option C uses exactly this Deny + StringLike-on-aws:PrincipalArn (arn:aws:iam::*:root) pattern, so it is correct; the dump suggestion agrees. Confidence is medium only because the option text is corrupted in this dump and the verdict relies on the known C mapping for this canonical DOP-C02 item.","explanation_zh":"需求是在組織根（organization root）建立「單一」SCP，僅阻止成員帳戶的 root 使用者進行任何 AWS 服務 API 呼叫。SCP 採用 deny-by-default 的權限護欄模型：Allow 型 SCP 只會放寬最大權限邊界，本身無法封鎖任何動作；而在從根往下的路徑（含根層級）任一層附加的明確 Deny，會對其底下所有帳戶封鎖該權限。因此政策必須為 Effect: Deny、Action: \"*\"、Resource: \"*\"。為了「僅」限制 root 使用者而不影響 IAM 使用者或角色，必須加上「正向」比對 root 主體的條件：StringLike 比對 aws:PrincipalArn 等於 arn:aws:iam::*:root。帳戶 root 使用者的 ARN 為 arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT-ID:root，因此在帳戶 ID 位置使用萬用字元，使這一條根層級 SCP 即可涵蓋所有成員帳戶的 root 使用者；而 IAM 使用者/角色的 ARN（:user/... 與 :assumed-role/...）不會被比中，因此不受影響。選項 C 正是採用 Deny + 對 aws:PrincipalArn 進行 StringLike（arn:aws:iam::*:root）的模式，故為正確答案，與 dump 建議一致。信心設為 medium，僅因本 dump 中選項文字損毀，判定須依賴此標準 DOP-C02 題目已知的 C 對應。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Corrupted placeholder text in this dump (a store name), not a real policy. In the canonical question the non-answer options fail because they either use Effect: Allow (an Allow SCP only widens the permission ceiling and cannot deny the root user any action) or otherwise do not produce an explicit Deny targeting the root principal.","why_zh":"此 dump 中為損毀的佔位文字（店名），並非真實政策。在標準題目中，非答案選項之所以錯誤，是因為它們使用 Effect: Allow（Allow 型 SCP 只放寬權限上限，無法對 root 使用者拒絕任何動作），或未產生針對 root 主體的明確 Deny。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Empty/corrupted in this dump. Canonically the trap option uses StringNotLike on aws:PrincipalArn arn:aws:iam::*:root, which inverts the logic: it denies every principal EXCEPT root, locking out IAM users/roles while leaving the root user completely unrestricted, the opposite of the requirement.","why_zh":"此 dump 中為空白/損毀。標準上此陷阱選項對 aws:PrincipalArn arn:aws:iam::*:root 使用 StringNotLike，邏輯反轉：它封鎖 root 以外的所有主體，鎖死 IAM 使用者/角色，卻完全不限制 root 使用者，與需求恰好相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Empty/corrupted in this dump. Canonically a distractor uses Effect: Allow or a Deny with no condition (or a condition that does not isolate the root principal), so it either blocks nothing or would block all principals (including IAM users/roles), failing 'prevent only the root user from all API calls'.","why_zh":"此 dump 中為空白/損毀。標準上此干擾選項使用 Effect: Allow，或使用沒有條件（或條件未鎖定 root 主體）的 Deny，因此要麼什麼都不封鎖，要麼會封鎖所有主體（含 IAM 使用者/角色），無法滿足「僅阻止 root 使用者進行所有 API 呼叫」。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_principal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/root-user-best-practices.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":146,"question_en":"A company uses AWS and has a VPC that contains critical compute infrastructure with predictable traffic patterns. The company has configured VPC flow logs that are published to a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The company's DevOps team needs to configure a monitoring solution for the VPC flow logs to identify anomalies in network traffic to the VPC over time. If the monitoring solution detects an anomaly, the company needs the ability to initiate a response to the anomaly. How should the DevOps team configure the monitoring solution to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS，并且其 VPC 中包含具有可预测流量模式的关键计算基础设施。该公司已配置 VPC 流日志，将其发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中的一个日志组。 该公司的 DevOps 团队需要为 VPC 流日志配置一个监控解决方案，以便随着时间的推移识别出流向 VPC 的网络流量中的异常情况。如果监控解决方案检测到异常，公司需要具备对异常情况发起响应的能 力。 开发运维团队应如何配置监控解决方案以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Subscribe the log group to the data stream. Configure Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics to detect log anomalies in the data stream. Create an AWS Lambda function to use as the output of the data stream. Configure the Lambda function to write to the default Amazon EventBridge event bus in the event of an anomaly finding.","B":"Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that delivers events to an Amazon S3 bucket. Subscribe the log group to the delivery stream. Configure Amazon Lookout for Metrics to monitor the data in the S3 bucket for anomalies. Create an AWS Lambda function to run in response to Lookout for Metrics anomaly findings. Configure the Lambda function to publish to the default Amazon EventBridge event bus.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to detect anomalies. Configure the Lambda function to publish an event to the default Amazon EventBridge event bus if the Lambda function detects an anomaly. Subscribe the Lambda function to the log group.","D":"Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Subscribe the log group to the data stream. Create an AWS Lambda function to detect log anomalies. Configure the Lambda function to write to the default Amazon EventBridge event bus if the Lambda function detects an anomaly. Set the Lambda function as the processor for the data stream."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。将日志组订阅到该数据流。配置 Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics 以检测 数据流中的日志异常。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数作为数据流的输出。配置 Lambda 函数，在检测到异 常时将其写入默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。","B":"创建一个将事件传递到 Amazon S3 存储桶的 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流。将日志组订阅到该交 付流。配置 Amazon Lookout for Metrics 来监控 S3 存储桶中的数据是否存在异常。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以响应 Lookout for Metrics 的异常发现而运行。配置该 Lambda 函数以发布到默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来检测异常。将 Lambda 函数配置为在检测到异常时向默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线发布事件。将 Lambda 函数订阅到日志组。","D":"创建一个 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。将日志组订阅到该数据流。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来检测日志异 常。如果 Lambda 函数检测到异常，则配置该函数将信息写入默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。将 Lambda 函数设置为数据流的处理器。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement is to detect anomalies in VPC flow log network traffic over time and then initiate a response. A CloudWatch Logs subscription filter can deliver a log group only to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service, so routing the log group to a Kinesis data stream is valid. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics provides the built-in RANDOM_CUT_FOREST function that assigns an anomaly score to streaming records based on numeric values, learning a baseline over time, and the AWS-documented pattern uses an AWS Lambda function as the application output to process those anomaly scores and configure alerts. Option A implements exactly this canonical streaming anomaly-detection pattern (data stream -> Kinesis Data Analytics anomaly detection -> Lambda as output -> publish to the default EventBridge event bus to initiate a response), so it is correct. The dump's answer (B) is wrong because Amazon Lookout for Metrics requires structured, tabular metric data (measures, dimensions, and a timestamp delivered on a regular interval, e.g., CSV/JSONLines in templated S3 paths); the raw base64-encoded, gzip-compressed CloudWatch log JSON that a subscription filter delivers via Firehose is not in that format and cannot be ingested without an omitted transformation/aggregation step.","explanation_zh":"需求是要對 VPC flow logs 的網路流量做隨時間的異常偵測,並在偵測到異常時觸發回應。CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能將 log group 投遞到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service,因此將 log group 訂閱到 Kinesis data stream 是有效作法。Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics 內建 RANDOM_CUT_FOREST 函式,可依數值欄位為串流記錄指派異常分數並隨時間建立基準線;AWS 文件記載的模式正是以 AWS Lambda 作為應用程式輸出來處理這些異常分數並設定告警。選項 A 完整實作了此標準的串流異常偵測架構(data stream -> Kinesis Data Analytics 異常偵測 -> Lambda 作為輸出 -> 發佈到預設 EventBridge event bus 以觸發回應),因此正確。題庫建議答案 B 是錯的,因為 Amazon Lookout for Metrics 需要結構化的表格式 metric 資料(measures、dimensions 與依固定間隔投遞的 timestamp,例如以樣板化 S3 路徑存放的 CSV/JSONLines);subscription filter 經由 Firehose 投遞的原始 base64 編碼、gzip 壓縮的 CloudWatch log JSON 不符此格式,缺少被省略的轉換/彙整步驟便無法被攝取。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Lookout for Metrics ingests structured, aggregated metric data (measures, dimensions, and a timestamp on a fixed interval, e.g., CSV/JSONLines in templated S3 paths). Raw base64/gzip CloudWatch log JSON delivered via Firehose to S3 is not in that format, so it cannot be analyzed without an omitted transformation/aggregation step. The architecture as written does not work. (Lookout for Metrics has also been deprecated by AWS.)","why_zh":"Amazon Lookout for Metrics 需要結構化、已彙整的 metric 資料(measures、dimensions 與依固定間隔的 timestamp,例如以樣板化 S3 路徑存放的 CSV/JSONLines)。經 Firehose 投遞到 S3 的原始 base64/gzip CloudWatch log JSON 不符該格式,缺少被省略的轉換/彙整步驟即無法分析,所述架構無法運作。(Lookout for Metrics 亦已被 AWS 終止服務。)"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Lambda function subscribed to a log group receives only small batches of log events and is stateless; it has no built-in or managed capability to learn a baseline and detect anomalies in traffic over time. This is custom, incomplete, and not the documented anomaly-detection approach.","why_zh":"訂閱 log group 的 Lambda 只會收到少量 log 批次且為無狀態,沒有內建或受管能力去學習基準並隨時間偵測流量異常。屬自訂且不完整,也非文件所述的異常偵測作法。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same core flaw as C: a Lambda set as the processor of the Kinesis data stream handles per-batch records with no managed/ML anomaly detection over time; it would require custom stateful logic the option does not provide, unlike Kinesis Data Analytics RANDOM_CUT_FOREST.","why_zh":"與 C 同樣的核心缺陷:作為 Kinesis data stream 處理器的 Lambda 只逐批處理記錄,沒有隨時間的受管/ML 異常偵測;需要選項未提供的自訂有狀態邏輯,不像 Kinesis Data Analytics 的 RANDOM_CUT_FOREST。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/app-anomaly-detection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/how-it-works-output-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-lookoutmetrics-anomalydetector-s3sourceconfig.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":147,"question_en":"AnyCompany is using AWS Organizations to create and manage multiple AWS accounts. AnyCompany recently acquired a smaller company, Example Corp. During the acquisition process, Example Corp's single AWS account joined AnyCompany's management account through an Organizations invitation. AnyCompany moved the new member account under an OU that is dedicated to Example Corp. AnyCompany's DevOps engineer has an IAM user that assumes a role that is named OrganizationAccountAccessRole to access member accounts. This role is configured with a full access policy. When the DevOps engineer tries to use the AWS Management Console to assume the role in Example Corp's new member account, the DevOps engineer receives the following error message: \"Invalid information in one or more fields. Check your information or contact your administrator.\" Which solution will give the DevOps engineer access to the new member account?","question_zh":"AnyCompany 正在使用 AWS Organizations 来创建和管理多个 AWS 账户。AnyCompany 最近收购了一家 规模较小的公司 Example Corp。在收购过程中，Example Corp 的单个 AWS 账户通过 Organizations 邀请 加入了 AnyCompany 的管理账户。AnyCompany 将新成员账户移至专门用于 Example Corp 的组织单元 （OU）下。 AnyCompany 的 DevOps 工程师有一个 IAM 用户，该用户会切换到名为 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 的角 色以访问成员账户。此角色配置了全访问策略。当该 DevOps 工程师尝试使用 AWS 管理控制台在 Example Corp 的新成员账户中切换到该角色时，收到了以下错误消息：“一个或多个字段中的信息无效。请检查您的 信息或联系管理员。” 哪种解决方案能让 DevOps 工程师访问新成员账户？","options_en":{"A":"In the management account, grant the DevOps engineer's IAM user permission to assume the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role in the new member account.","B":"In the management account, create a new SCP. In the SCP, grant the DevOps engineer's IAM user full access to all resources in the new member account. Attach the SCP to the OU that contains the new member account.","C":"In the new member account, create a new IAM role that is named OrganizationAccountAccessRole. Attach the AdministratorAccess AWS managed policy to the role. In the role's trust policy, grant the management account permission to assume the role.","D":"In the new member account, edit the trust policy for the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role. Grant the management account permission to assume the role."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中，授予 DevOps 工程师的 IAM 用户在新成员账户中承担 OrganizationAccountAccess Role IAM 角色的权限。","B":"在管理账户中，创建一个新的服务控制策略（SCP）。在该 SCP 中，授予 DevOps 工程师的 IAM 用户对 新成员账户中所有资源的完全访问权限。将该 SCP 附加到包含新成员账户的组织单元（OU）上。","C":"在新成员账户中，创建一个名为 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 的新 IAM 角色。将 AdministratorAccess AWS 管理策略附加到该角色。在角色的信任策略中，授予管理账户承担该角色 的权限。","D":"在新成员账户中，编辑 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色的信任策略。授予管理账户承担该 角色的权限。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Example Corp's account joined the organization via an Organizations invitation. Per AWS docs, when you CREATE a member account with Organizations, the OrganizationAccountAccessRole (with administrator permissions and a trust policy for the management account) is created automatically. However, accounts that you INVITE to join do NOT get this role created automatically — you must create it manually. Therefore the role does not exist in Example Corp's account, so the console switch-role attempt cannot resolve it and returns 'Invalid information in one or more fields.' The documented fix is to manually duplicate the role in the member account: create an IAM role (recommended name OrganizationAccountAccessRole), attach the AdministratorAccess AWS managed policy, and configure the trust policy so the management account can assume it — exactly what option C describes.","explanation_zh":"Example Corp 的帳號是透過 Organizations 邀請（invitation）加入組織的。根據 AWS 文件，當你使用 Organizations「建立（create）」成員帳號時，系統會自動建立 OrganizationAccountAccessRole（含管理員權限以及針對 management account 的信任政策）。但你「邀請（invite）」加入的現有帳號並不會自動產生此角色，必須手動建立。因此該角色在 Example Corp 帳號中根本不存在，主控台的 switch-role 無法解析它，才會出現「Invalid information in one or more fields」錯誤。文件記載的修正方式是在成員帳號中手動複製此角色：建立一個 IAM role（建議命名為 OrganizationAccountAccessRole），附加 AdministratorAccess AWS 受管政策，並設定信任政策讓 management account 可以 assume 該角色 — 這正是選項 C 所描述的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Granting the IAM user sts:AssumeRole in the management account addresses the source (assuming) side, but the engineer already assumes OrganizationAccountAccessRole in other member accounts with a full-access policy, so source permission is not the gap. The actual problem is that the target role does not exist in the invited account, so A does not resolve the 'Invalid information' error.","why_zh":"在 management account 授予 IAM 使用者 sts:AssumeRole 處理的是來源（發起方）端，但工程師已能在其他成員帳號 assume OrganizationAccountAccessRole 且擁有 full-access 政策，來源權限並非問題所在。真正的缺口是目標角色在被邀請的帳號中不存在，因此 A 無法解決「Invalid information」錯誤。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SCPs are guardrails that filter the maximum available permissions; they NEVER grant permissions to IAM users or roles, and by default do not even affect the management account. You cannot use an SCP to 'grant full access' to a user, and an SCP cannot create the missing role, so B is technically wrong.","why_zh":"SCP 是防護欄，用來限制可用權限的上限；它從不授予 IAM 使用者或角色任何權限，預設甚至不影響 management account。無法用 SCP「授予」使用者完整存取，SCP 也無法建立缺失的角色，故 B 在技術上是錯的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Editing the trust policy of OrganizationAccountAccessRole presupposes the role already exists, but invited accounts do not automatically get this role created — there is no role to edit. The full role must be created (including attaching AdministratorAccess), not merely re-pointed via a trust policy edit, which is why C is correct and D is inapplicable.","why_zh":"編輯 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 的信任政策前提是角色已存在，但被邀請的帳號不會自動建立此角色 — 根本沒有角色可編輯。必須建立完整的角色（包括附加 AdministratorAccess），而不只是透過編輯信任政策來重新指向，這就是 C 正確而 D 不適用的原因。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_create-cross-account-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access-cross-account-role.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":148,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is designing an application that integrates with a legacy REST API. The application has an AWS Lambda function that reads records from an Amazon Kinesis data stream. The Lambda function sends the records to the legacy REST API. Approximately 10% of the records that the Lambda function sends from the Kinesis data stream have data errors and must be processed manually. The Lambda function event source configuration has an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) dead-letter queue as an on-failure destination. The DevOps engineer has configured the Lambda function to process records in batches and has implemented retries in case of failure. During testing, the DevOps engineer notices that the dead-letter queue contains many records that have no data errors and that already have been processed by the legacy REST API. The DevOps engineer needs to configure the Lambda function's event source options to reduce the number of errorless records that are sent to the dead-letter queue. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在设计一个与遗留的 REST API 集成的应用程序。该应用程序包含一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于从 Amazon Kinesis 数据流中读取记录。Lambda 函数将这些记录发送到遗留的 REST API。 Lambda 函数从 Kinesis 数据流发送的记录中约有 10% 存在数据错误，必须手动处理。Lambda 函数的事 件源配置将 Amazon 简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）死信队列设置为失败时的目的地。DevOps 工程师已 将 Lambda 函数配置为批量处理记录，并在出现故障时实现了重试机制。 在测试期间，DevOps 工程师注意到死信队列中包含许多没有数据错误且已由旧版 REST API 处理过的 记录。DevOps 工程师需要配置 Lambda 函数的事件源选项，以减少发送到死信队列的无错误记录的数 量。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the retry attempts.","B":"Configure the setting to split the batch when an error occurs.","C":"Increase the concurrent batches per shard.","D":"Decrease the maximum age of record."},"options_zh":{"A":"增加重试次数。","B":"将设置配置为在出现错误时拆分批次。","C":"增加每个分片的并发批处理数量。","D":"降低记录的最大年龄。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"By default, a Kinesis event source mapping checkpoints to the highest sequence number of a batch only when the ENTIRE batch succeeds; if any single record causes a function error, Lambda treats the whole batch as a failure, retries the entire batch, and after retries/age are exhausted discards the entire batch to the on-failure destination (the SQS DLQ). That is exactly why the DLQ contains many errorless records already accepted by the legacy REST API: they shared a batch with the ~10% bad records. Turning on BisectBatchOnFunctionError ('split the batch when an error occurs') makes Lambda split a failed batch into two smaller batches and retry each half, recursively isolating the bad records into progressively smaller batches; AWS docs state this 'splits a failed batch into two smaller batches, isolating bad records' and that 'splitting batches doesn't consume the retry quota.' Consequently the halves of good records succeed and get committed, and only the tiny batch that actually contains a bad record is ultimately discarded to the DLQ, dramatically reducing the number of errorless records sent there. This is set directly in the event source mapping options, exactly as the question asks.","explanation_zh":"預設情況下，Kinesis event source mapping 只有在「整批」記錄全部成功時，才會 checkpoint 到該批最高的 sequence number；只要批次中有任何一筆記錄造成 function 錯誤，Lambda 就把整批視為失敗、重試整批，待重試次數或 record 最大壽命耗盡後，便把「整批」丟到 on-failure destination（即 SQS DLQ）。這正是為何 DLQ 裡有大量沒有資料錯誤、且 legacy REST API 已成功處理過的記錄：它們與那約 10% 的壞記錄被分在同一批。開啟 BisectBatchOnFunctionError（即「發生錯誤時分割批次」）後，Lambda 會把失敗的批次一分為二並分別重試，遞迴地把壞記錄隔離到愈來愈小的批次中；AWS 文件明確指出此設定會「將失敗的批次分割成兩個較小的批次，隔離壞記錄」，且「分割批次不會消耗重試配額」。因此，含好記錄的那一半會成功並被 commit，最終只有真正包含壞記錄的極小批次會被丟到 DLQ，大幅減少送到 DLQ 的無錯誤記錄數量。此設定正是在 event source mapping 選項中設定，完全符合題目要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing MaximumRetryAttempts only retries the same failing batch more times. Because the ~10% bad records have genuine, persistent data errors, they can never succeed, so the whole batch (including the errorless, already-processed records) is still ultimately discarded to the DLQ; this only delays the discard and may add latency and duplicate calls to the legacy API.","why_zh":"增加 MaximumRetryAttempts 只是把同一個失敗批次重試更多次。由於約 10% 的壞記錄是真實且持續的資料錯誤、永遠不會成功，整批（含已處理的無錯誤記錄）最終仍會被丟到 DLQ；這只是延後丟棄，且可能增加延遲與對 legacy API 的重複呼叫。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Concurrent batches per shard (ParallelizationFactor) only increases throughput by processing multiple batches per shard in parallel. It changes parallelism, not failure granularity, so a failed batch is still discarded whole (with its good records) to the DLQ. It does nothing to reduce errorless records in the DLQ.","why_zh":"每個 shard 的並行批次數（ParallelizationFactor）只是透過並行處理多個批次來提升吞吐量，改變的是並行度而非失敗的粒度，失敗批次仍會整批（含好記錄）被丟到 DLQ，無法減少 DLQ 中的無錯誤記錄。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Decreasing MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds makes records expire and be discarded to the DLQ sooner once they exceed the age limit. This would increase (or at least not reduce) the volume of records, including errorless ones, sent to the DLQ, which is the opposite of the goal.","why_zh":"降低 MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds 會讓記錄一旦超過年齡上限就更快過期並被丟到 DLQ。這只會增加（或至少不會減少）送入 DLQ 的記錄量（含無錯誤記錄），與目標相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/kinesis-on-failure-destination.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-kinesis-batchfailurereporting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-kinesis-parameters.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":149,"question_en":"A company has microservices running in AWS Lambda that read data from Amazon DynamoDB. The Lambda code is manually deployed by developers after successful testing. The company now needs the tests and deployments be automated and run in the cloud. Additionally, traffic to the new versions of each microservice should be incrementally shifted over time after deployment. What solution meets all the requirements, ensuring the MOST developer velocity?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Lambda 上运行微服务，这些微服务从 Amazon DynamoDB 中读取数据。Lambda 代码 由开发人员在测试成功后手动部署。该公司现在需要将测试和部署自动化，并在云端运行。此外，在部 署后，每个微服务新版本的流量应逐步转移。 哪种解决方案能满足所有要求，确保开发人员的工作效率最高？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodePipeline configuration and set up a post-commit hook to trigger the pipeline after tests have passed. Use AWS CodeDeploy and create a Canary deployment configuration that specifies the percentage of traffic and interval.","B":"Create an AWS CodeBuild configuration that triggers when the test code is pushed. Use AWS CloudFormation to trigger an AWS CodePipeline configuration that deploys the new Lambda versions and specifies the traffic shift percentage and interval.","C":"Create an AWS CodePipeline configuration and set up the source code step to trigger when code is pushed. Set up the build step to use AWS CodeBuild to run the tests. Set up an AWS CodeDeploy configuration to deploy, then select the CodeDeployDefault.LambdaLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes option.","D":"Use the AWS CLI to set up a post-commit hook that uploads the code to an Amazon S3 bucket after tests have passed Set up an S3 event trigger that runs a Lambda function that deploys the new version. Use an interval in the Lambda function to deploy the code over time at the required percentage."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 配置，并设置一个在测试通过后触发管道的提交后钩子。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 并创建一个金丝雀部署配置，指定流量百分比和间隔。","B":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 配置，当测试代码被推送时触发。使用 AWS CloudFormation 触发一个 AWS CodePipeline 配置，以部署新的 Lambda 版本，并指定流量转移百分比和间隔。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 配置，并设置源代码步骤在代码推送时触发。设置构建步骤以使用 AWS CodeBuild 运行测试。设置 AWS CodeDeploy 配置以进行部署，然后选择 CodeDeployDefault.LambdaLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes 选项。","D":"使用 AWS 命令行界面（CLI）设置一个在测试通过后将代码上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶的提交后钩 子。设置一个 S3 事件触发器，该触发器运行一个 Lambda 函数来部署新版本。在 Lambda 函数中 使用间隔，以便在规定的时间段内按要求的百分比逐步部署代码。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option C is the canonical fully-managed CI/CD pattern: a CodePipeline whose Source stage triggers automatically when code is pushed, a Build stage that uses CodeBuild to run the tests in the cloud, and a Deploy stage that uses CodeDeploy. Selecting the predefined deployment configuration CodeDeployDefault.LambdaLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes shifts 10 percent of traffic to the new Lambda version every three minutes until all traffic is shifted, satisfying the requirement to incrementally shift traffic over time after deployment. The AWS CodeDeploy deployment-configurations page confirms this is a real predefined AWS Lambda compute-platform configuration with exactly that behavior. Because everything runs as managed AWS services with a single predefined config and no custom code, it delivers the MOST developer velocity with the least operational overhead. The other answers either rely on client-side Git post-commit hooks (which run on a developer machine, not in the cloud), omit a cloud test stage, invert the orchestration awkwardly, or hand-roll the traffic shifting.","explanation_zh":"選項 C 是標準的全託管 CI/CD 模式：CodePipeline 的 Source 階段在程式碼推送時自動觸發、Build 階段使用 CodeBuild 在雲端執行測試，Deploy 階段使用 CodeDeploy。選擇預先定義的部署設定 CodeDeployDefault.LambdaLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes，會每三分鐘將 10% 的流量轉移到新的 Lambda 版本，直到全部流量轉移完成，符合「部署後隨時間逐步轉移流量」的需求。AWS CodeDeploy 的 deployment configurations 文件確認這是 AWS Lambda compute platform 真實存在且行為完全相符的預先定義設定。由於全部以託管 AWS 服務搭配單一預設設定且無自訂程式碼，提供最高的開發者效率與最少的維運負擔。其他選項分別依賴客戶端 Git post-commit hook（在開發者機器而非雲端執行）、省略雲端測試階段、以彆扭方式反轉編排，或手刻流量轉移邏輯。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Git post-commit hook is a client-side hook that runs on the developer's local machine, not a cloud trigger; CodePipeline triggers natively on source changes via events/webhooks. The wording also describes a 'Canary deployment configuration that specifies the percentage of traffic and interval', but the predefined Lambda canary configs use fixed values (10 percent first, remainder after a set interval) and the design omits a cloud build/test stage, so the 'tests run in the cloud' requirement is not clearly met.","why_zh":"Git post-commit hook 是在開發者本機端執行的客戶端 hook，並非雲端觸發；CodePipeline 原生透過事件/webhook 觸發。其敘述的『可指定流量百分比與間隔的 Canary 部署設定』也不符實際——預先定義的 Lambda canary 設定使用固定值（先 10%，間隔後轉移其餘），且設計省略雲端建置/測試階段，無法明確滿足『測試在雲端執行』的需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It inverts the orchestration: having CodeBuild trigger CloudFormation which then triggers CodePipeline is convoluted and not a native pattern (normally CodePipeline orchestrates CodeBuild and CloudFormation, not the reverse). The pipeline does not natively 'specify the traffic shift percentage and interval' without CodeDeploy, and this added indirection reduces developer velocity rather than maximizing it.","why_zh":"它反轉了編排順序：讓 CodeBuild 觸發 CloudFormation 再觸發 CodePipeline 既迂迴又非原生模式（通常是 CodePipeline 編排 CodeBuild 與 CloudFormation，而非相反）。不透過 CodeDeploy，pipeline 並無法原生『指定流量轉移百分比與間隔』，且這種額外的間接層降低而非最大化開發者效率。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This hand-rolls everything: a CLI client-side post-commit hook, an S3 upload, an S3 event, and a custom Lambda that performs traffic shifting with a manual interval loop. It reinvents managed CodeDeploy traffic-shifting, provides no clear managed test stage, and yields the lowest developer velocity with the highest operational overhead.","why_zh":"這完全手刻：CLI 客戶端 post-commit hook、S3 上傳、S3 事件，以及用手動間隔迴圈執行流量轉移的自訂 Lambda。它重新發明託管 CodeDeploy 的流量轉移、沒有明確的託管測試階段，開發者效率最低且維運負擔最高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/pipelines-triggers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/tutorials-lambda-deploy.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":150,"question_en":"A company is building a web and mobile application that uses a serverless architecture powered by AWS Lambda and Amazon API Gateway. The company wants to fully automate the backend Lambda deployment based on code that is pushed to the appropriate environment branch in an AWS CodeCommit repository. The deployment must have the following: Separate environment pipelines for testing and production Automatic deployment that occurs for test environments only Which steps should be taken to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在构建一个基于 AWS Lambda 和 Amazon API Gateway 的无服务器架构的网络和移动应用程 序。该公司希望根据推送到 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中相应环境分支的代码，完全自动执行后端 Lambda 部署。 部署必须具备以下内容： 为测试和生产环境分别设置独立的环境管道 仅针对测试环境进行的自动部署 应采取哪些步骤来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a new AWS CodePipeline service. Create a CodeCommit repository for each environment. Set up CodePipeline to retrieve the source code from the appropriate repository. Set up the deployment step to deploy the Lambda functions with AWS CloudFormation.","B":"Create two AWS CodePipeline configurations for test and production environments. Configure the production pipeline to have a manual approval step. Create a CodeCommit repository for each environment. Set up each CodePipeline to retrieve the source code from the appropriate repository. Set up the deployment step to deploy the Lambda functions with AWS CloudFormation.","C":"Create two AWS CodePipeline configurations for test and production environments. Configure the production pipeline to have a manual approval step. Create one CodeCommit repository with a branch for each environment. Set up each CodePipeline to retrieve the source code from the appropriate branch in the repository. Set up the deployment step to deploy the Lambda functions with AWS CloudFormation.","D":"Create an AWS CodeBuild configuration for test and production environments. Configure the production pipeline to have a manual approval step. Create one CodeCommit repository with a branch for each environment. Push the Lambda function code to an Amazon S3 bucket. Set up the deployment step to deploy the Lambda functions from the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个新的 AWS CodePipeline 服务。为每个环境创建一个 CodeCommit 代码库。设置 CodePipeline 从相应的代码库获取源代码。设置部署步骤，使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 Lambda 函数。","B":"为测试和生产环境创建两个 AWS CodePipeline 配置。将生产管道配置为包含一个手动审批步骤。为每 个环境创建一个 CodeCommit 代码库。将每个 CodePipeline 设置为从相应的代码库获取源代码。设置 部署步骤，使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 Lambda 函数。","C":"为测试和生产环境创建两个 AWS CodePipeline 配置。将生产管道配置为包含一个手动审批步骤。创 建一个 CodeCommit 代码库，并为每个环境设置一个分支。将每个 CodePipeline 设置为从代码库中 的相应分支获取源代码。设置部署步骤，使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 Lambda 函数。","D":"为测试和生产环境创建 AWS CodeBuild 配置。将生产管道配置为包含手动审批步骤。创建一个 CodeCommit 代码库，为每个环境设置一个分支。将 Lambda 函数代码推送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。设 置部署步骤，从 S3 存储桶部署 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Three requirements must be met: separate test and production pipelines, automatic deployment for the test environment only (production gated), and deployment triggered by code pushed to the appropriate environment BRANCH of a CodeCommit repository. Option C satisfies all three. Two distinct CodePipeline configurations give isolated test and production pipelines. A manual approval action on the production pipeline halts that pipeline until an IAM-authorized person approves, so only the test pipeline deploys automatically while production waits for human approval (per the AWS approvals docs, an approval action stops execution until approved/rejected). A single CodeCommit repository with one branch per environment matches the explicit 'environment branch' wording, and the CodeCommit source action requires both RepositoryName and BranchName and starts the pipeline only when a new commit is made on the configured branch, so each pipeline triggers solely on its own branch. The deploy stage uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy the Lambda functions. The decisive qualifiers are 'pushed to the appropriate environment branch' (one repo, multiple branches) and 'automatic deployment for test only' (manual approval gate on prod), which only C satisfies.","explanation_zh":"需滿足三項需求:測試與生產環境分開的 pipeline、僅測試環境自動部署(生產須有閘控)、以及由推送到 CodeCommit repository 中對應環境「分支(branch)」的程式碼觸發部署。選項 C 全部滿足。兩個獨立的 CodePipeline 設定提供分離的測試與生產 pipeline。生產 pipeline 上的 manual approval action 會暫停該 pipeline,直到具備 IAM 權限者核准,因此只有測試 pipeline 自動部署,生產則等待人工核准(依 AWS approvals 文件,approval action 會停止執行直到被核准或拒絕)。單一 CodeCommit repository 並為每個環境建立一個分支,符合題目明確的「environment branch」措辭;CodeCommit source action 同時必須提供 RepositoryName 與 BranchName,且僅在設定的分支有新 commit 時才啟動 pipeline,因此每個 pipeline 僅由其對應分支觸發。部署階段使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 Lambda 函式。決定性關鍵詞為「pushed to the appropriate environment branch」(單一 repo、多分支)與「僅測試環境自動部署」(生產端 manual approval 閘控),唯有 C 同時滿足。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Configures only one CodePipeline (no separate test/prod pipelines), creates a repository per environment (contradicts the 'environment branch' requirement), and has no manual approval, so production would deploy automatically, violating 'automatic deployment for test only.'","why_zh":"只設定一個 CodePipeline(沒有分離的測試/生產 pipeline),為每個環境建立一個 repository(與「environment branch」需求相違),且沒有 manual approval,生產會自動部署,違反「僅測試環境自動部署」。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Has two pipelines and a production manual approval, but creates a separate CodeCommit repository for each environment instead of one repository with per-environment branches, contradicting the requirement that code is pushed to the appropriate environment branch in a (single) repository.","why_zh":"雖有兩個 pipeline 與生產 manual approval,但為每個環境建立各自的 CodeCommit repository,而非單一 repository 內每環境一分支,與「推送到 repository 中對應環境分支」的需求相違。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses CodeBuild 'configurations' rather than CodePipeline pipelines (CodeBuild is a build service, not a multi-stage deployment pipeline), then references 'the production pipeline' inconsistently since no pipeline was created; pushing Lambda code to S3 and deploying from S3 omits the orchestrated pipeline and CloudFormation-based environment separation the requirements call for.","why_zh":"使用 CodeBuild「設定」而非 CodePipeline pipeline(CodeBuild 是建置服務,並非多階段部署 pipeline),且因未建立 pipeline 卻提到「production pipeline」前後不一致;將 Lambda 程式碼推送到 S3 再從 S3 部署,缺少需求所要求的協調式 pipeline 與 CloudFormation 環境分離結構。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodeCommit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals-action-add.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":151,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer wants to find a solution to migrate an application from on premises to AWS. The application is running on Linux and needs to run on specific versions of Apache Tomcat, HAProxy, and Varnish Cache to function properly. The application's operating system-level parameters require tuning. The solution must include a way to automate the deployment of new application versions. The infrastructure should be scalable and faulty servers should be replaced automatically. Which solution should the DevOps engineer use?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师想要找到一种解决方案，将一个应用程序从本地迁移到 AWS。该应用程序运行在 Linux 系统上，需要在特定版本的 Apache Tomcat、HAProxy 和 Varnish Cache 上运行才能正常工作。 应用程序的操作系统级参数需要进行调整。该解决方案必须包含一种自动部署新应用程序版本的方法。 基础设施应具备可扩展性，并且出现故障的服务器应能自动替换。 DevOps 工程师应该使用哪种解决方案？","options_en":{"A":"Upload the application as a Docker image that contains all the necessary software to Amazon ECR. Create an Amazon ECS cluster using an AWS Fargate launch type and an Auto Scaling group. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses Amazon ECR as a source and Amazon ECS as a deployment provider.","B":"Upload the application code to an AWS CodeCommit repository with a saved configuration file to configure and install the software. Create an AWS Elastic Beanstalk web server tier and a load balanced-type environment that uses the Tomcat solution stack. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses CodeCommit as a source and Elastic Beanstalk as a deployment provider.","C":"Upload the application code to an AWS CodeCommit repository with a set of .ebextensions files to configure and install the software. Create an AWS Elastic Beanstalk worker tier environment that uses the Tomcat solution stack. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses CodeCommit as a source and Elastic Beanstalk as a deployment provider.","D":"Upload the application code to an AWS CodeCommit repository with an appspec.yml file to configure and install the necessary software. Create an AWS CodeDeploy deployment group associated with an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses CodeCommit as a source and CodeDeploy as a deployment provider."},"options_zh":{"A":"将应用程序作为包含所有必要软件的 Docker 镜像上传到 Amazon ECR。使用 AWS Fargate 启动类型和 自动扩展组创建一个 Amazon ECS 集群。创建一个使用 Amazon ECR 作为源和 Amazon ECS 作为部 署提供程序的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。","B":"将应用程序代码上传到 AWS CodeCommit 存储库，并附带一个保存的配置文件以配置和安装软件。创 建一个使用 Tomcat 解决方案堆栈的 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 网络服务器层和负载均衡类型的环境。创 建一个使用 CodeCommit 作为源和 Elastic Beanstalk 作为部署提供商的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。","C":"将应用程序代码上传到 AWS CodeCommit 存储库，并附带一组 .ebextensions 文件以配置和安装软件。 创建一个使用 Tomcat 解决方案堆栈的 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 工作负载环境。创建一个使用 CodeCommit 作为源和 Elastic Beanstalk 作为部署提供商的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。","D":"将应用程序代码上传至带有 appspec.yml 文件的 AWS CodeCommit 存储库，以配置并安装必要的软件。 创建一个与之关联的 AWS CodeDeploy 部署组。 亚马逊 EC2 自动扩展组。创建一个使用 CodeCommit 作为源并使用 CodeDeploy 作为部署提供商的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application requires specific versions of Apache Tomcat, HAProxy, and Varnish Cache AND tuning of OS-level (kernel/sysctl) parameters, so it needs full control of the operating system. Only EC2 instances provide that. Option D uses an EC2 Auto Scaling group (scalability plus automatic replacement of faulty instances), CodeCommit as source, and CodeDeploy with an appspec.yml whose EC2/On-Premises 'hooks' lifecycle events (BeforeInstall/AfterInstall/etc.) run scripts that install the three exact software versions and tune the OS. CodeDeploy is integrated with EC2 Auto Scaling: when new instances launch into the group, CodeDeploy automatically deploys the latest revision to them, so scaled-out and replacement instances are bootstrapped correctly. CodePipeline (CodeCommit -> CodeDeploy) automates deployment of new application versions, satisfying every requirement.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式需要特定版本的 Apache Tomcat、HAProxy 與 Varnish Cache，並且要調整作業系統層級 (kernel/sysctl) 參數，因此需要對作業系統的完整控制權，只有 EC2 執行個體能提供。選項 D 使用 EC2 Auto Scaling group (提供擴展能力並自動替換異常執行個體)、CodeCommit 作為來源，以及搭配 appspec.yml 的 CodeDeploy；其 EC2/On-Premises 'hooks' 生命週期事件 (BeforeInstall/AfterInstall 等) 執行指令碼來安裝這三個確切軟體版本並調整 OS 參數。CodeDeploy 與 EC2 Auto Scaling 整合：當新執行個體加入該群組時，CodeDeploy 會自動將最新版本部署到這些執行個體，確保擴展與替換的執行個體被正確初始化。CodePipeline (CodeCommit -> CodeDeploy) 自動化新版本部署，完全符合所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Fargate is serverless and locks down the host: per AWS docs it 'prevents containers from accessing the underlying host's resources, such as the file system, devices, networking' and restricts Linux capabilities like CAP_SYS_ADMIN, so OS-level/kernel parameter tuning is not possible. The option also pairs Fargate with an 'Auto Scaling group,' but Fargate uses ECS service auto scaling, not an EC2 ASG.","why_zh":"AWS Fargate 為無伺服器架構並鎖定主機：根據 AWS 文件，它『防止容器存取底層主機資源，例如檔案系統、裝置、網路』，並限制 CAP_SYS_ADMIN 等 Linux capabilities，因此無法進行 OS 層級/kernel 參數調整。此選項還將 Fargate 與 'Auto Scaling group' 搭配，但 Fargate 使用 ECS service auto scaling，而非 EC2 ASG。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The Elastic Beanstalk managed Tomcat solution stack fixes the platform software (a managed Tomcat plus an nginx/Apache proxy) and is not built to host specific versions of HAProxy and Varnish Cache as part of the stack; deep OS tuning fights the managed platform. The option also relies on a 'saved configuration file' (environment settings) rather than the install/config scripting needed to deploy the three packages.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk 受管 Tomcat 解決方案堆疊固定了平台軟體 (受管 Tomcat 加上 nginx/Apache 代理)，並非用來在堆疊內託管特定版本的 HAProxy 與 Varnish Cache；深度 OS 調整會與受管平台衝突。此選項還倚賴 'saved configuration file' (環境設定)，而非部署這三個套件所需的安裝/設定指令碼。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Elastic Beanstalk worker tier is for offloading long-running asynchronous background tasks processed via an SQS daemon (per AWS docs), not for a web-facing application served by Tomcat/HAProxy/Varnish. Wrong environment tier, and the same managed-platform software constraints as B apply.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk worker tier 用於將長時間執行的非同步背景任務透過 SQS daemon 處理 (根據 AWS 文件)，而非由 Tomcat/HAProxy/Varnish 對外提供服務的網頁應用程式。屬於錯誤的環境層級，且同樣受 B 的受管平台軟體限制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/fargate-security-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features-managing-env-tiers.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":152,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is using AWS CodeDeploy across a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances in an EC2 Auto Scaling group. The associated CodeDeploy deployment group, which is integrated with EC2 Auto Scaling, is configured to perform in-place deployments with CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime. During an ongoing new deployment, the engineer discovers that, although the overall deployment finished successfully, two out of five instances have the previous application revision deployed. The other three instances have the newest application revision. What is likely causing this issue?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 在一个 EC2 自动扩展组中的多个 Amazon EC2 实例上 进行部署。与 EC2 自动扩展集成的关联 CodeDeploy 部署组配置为使用 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime 进行原地部署。在正在进行的新部署过程中，工程师发现，尽管整个部署成功完成，但五台实例中有 两台部署的是旧的应用程序版本，而另外三台实例部署的是最新的应用程序版本。 这问题可能是什么原因造成的？ 受影响的两个实例未能获取新的部署。","options_en":{"A":"The two affected instances failed to fetch the new deployment.","B":"A failed AfterInstall lifecycle event hook caused the CodeDeploy agent to roll back to the previous version on the affected instances.","C":"The CodeDeploy agent was not installed in two affected instances.","D":"EC2 Auto Scaling launched two new instances while the new deployment had not yet finished, causing the previous version to be deployed on the affected instances."},"options_zh":{"B":"由于 AfterInstall 生命周期事件钩子失败，CodeDeploy 代理在受影响的实例上回滚到了之前的版 本。","C":"两个受影响的实例中未安装 CodeDeploy 代理。","D":"在新部署尚未完成时，EC2 自动扩展启动了两个新实例，导致受影响的实例上部署了旧版本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When a CodeDeploy deployment group is integrated with an EC2 Auto Scaling group, CodeDeploy installs an Auto Scaling launch lifecycle hook that is always enabled and cannot be turned off. The AWS documentation section 'Scale-out events during a deployment' states verbatim: 'If an Auto Scaling scale-out event occurs while a deployment is underway, the new instances will be updated with the application revision that was previously deployed, not the newest application revision. If the deployment succeeds, the old instances and the newly scaled-out instances will be hosting different application revisions.' This exactly matches the scenario: three pre-existing instances received the newest revision via the normal CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime in-place deployment, while two instances that Auto Scaling launched mid-deployment received the previously deployed revision through a launch deployment, and the overall deployment still reported success. Therefore option D is correct. (Note: CodeDeploy normally starts a follow-on deployment to reconcile outdated instances, but that automatic update can be disabled, which is consistent with the persistent mixed-revision state described.)","explanation_zh":"當 CodeDeploy deployment group 與 EC2 Auto Scaling group 整合時,CodeDeploy 會安裝一個 Auto Scaling launch lifecycle hook,此 hook 永遠啟用且無法關閉。AWS 文件的「Scale-out events during a deployment」段落原文寫道:『若在部署進行中發生 Auto Scaling scale-out event,新啟動的執行個體將會被部署「先前已部署的」application revision,而非最新的 application revision。若部署成功,舊執行個體與新增的 scale-out 執行個體將會託管不同的 application revision。』這完全符合題目情境:三台原有執行個體透過正常的 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime in-place deployment 取得最新版本,而兩台在部署進行中由 Auto Scaling 啟動的執行個體則透過 launch deployment 取得先前版本,整體部署仍回報成功。因此選項 D 正確。(註:CodeDeploy 通常會啟動後續部署以更新過時執行個體,但此自動更新可被停用,與題述持續存在的版本不一致狀態一致。)","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"If the two instances had failed to fetch (DownloadBundle) the new revision, those instance-level deployments would fail at that lifecycle event and be marked failed, not left silently running a complete prior revision; with CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime an instance failure typically fails the overall deployment, contradicting the 'finished successfully' premise.","why_zh":"若兩台執行個體無法擷取(DownloadBundle)新版本,該執行個體層級的部署會在該 lifecycle event 失敗並被標記為失敗,而不是悄悄停留在執行完整的舊版本;在 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime 下執行個體失敗通常會使整體部署失敗,與題目「成功完成」的前提矛盾。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A failed AfterInstall hook marks the instance/deployment as failed; CodeDeploy in-place deployments do not silently roll back individual instances to the previous revision on a hook failure. A hook failure would prevent the reported successful completion rather than yield a success with the old revision present.","why_zh":"AfterInstall hook 失敗會將執行個體/部署標記為失敗;CodeDeploy 的 in-place deployment 不會因 hook 失敗而靜默地將個別執行個體回退到先前版本。hook 失敗會使題目所述的成功完成無法達成,而非在保留舊版本的情況下回報部署成功。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"If the CodeDeploy agent were not installed on the two instances, CodeDeploy could not communicate with them, so the launch deployment would time out (Heartbeat Timeout) and fail rather than installing a complete previous revision. The affected instances clearly have a working agent because a full prior revision was deployed to them.","why_zh":"若兩台執行個體未安裝 CodeDeploy agent,CodeDeploy 無法與其通訊,launch deployment 會逾時(Heartbeat Timeout)並失敗,而不會安裝完整的舊版本。受影響的執行個體顯然有正常運作的 agent,因為其上已部署了完整的舊版本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-configure-advanced-options.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":153,"question_en":"A security team is concerned that a developer can unintentionally attach an Elastic IP address to an Amazon EC2 instance in production. No developer should be allowed to attach an Elastic IP address to an instance. The security team must be notified if any production server has an Elastic IP address at any time. How can this task be automated?","question_zh":"安全团队担心开发人员可能会无意中将弹性 IP 地址附加到生产环境中的 Amazon EC2 实例上。任何开发 人员都不应被允许将弹性 IP 地址附加到实例上。如果任何生产服务器在任何时候都附加了弹性 IP 地址， 必须通知安全团队。 如何才能使这项任务实现自动化？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Athena to query AWS CloudTrail logs to check for any associate-address attempts. Create an AWS Lambda function to disassociate the Elastic IP address from the instance, and alert the security team.","B":"Attach an IAM policy to the developers' IAM group to deny associate-address permissions. Create a custom AWS Config rule to check whether an Elastic IP address is associated with any instance tagged as production, and alert the security team.","C":"Ensure that all IAM groups associated with developers do not have associate-address permissions. Create a scheduled AWS Lambda function to check whether an Elastic IP address is associated with any instance tagged as production, and alert the security team if an instance has an Elastic IP address associated with it.","D":"Create an AWS Config rule to check that all production instances have EC2 IAM roles that include deny associate-address permissions. Verify whether there is an Elastic IP address associated with any instance, and alert the security team if an instance has an Elastic IP address associated with it."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Athena 查询 AWS CloudTrail 日志以检查是否存在任何关联地址的尝试。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将弹性 IP 地址从实例中分离，并向安全团队发出警报。","B":"将一个 IAM 策略附加到开发人员的 IAM 组，以拒绝其关联地址的权限。创建一个自定义的 AWS Config 规则，检查弹性 IP 地址是否与任何标记为“生产”的实例相关联，并向安全团队发出警 报。","C":"确保与开发人员关联的所有 IAM 组均无关联地址的权限。创建一个计划的 AWS Lambda 函数，检查 是否有任何标记为生产环境的实例关联了弹性 IP 地址，如果有，则向安全团队发出警报。","D":"创建一个 AWS Config 规则，检查所有生产实例的 EC2 IAM 角色是否包含拒绝关联弹性 IP 地址的权 限。验证是否有任何实例关联了弹性 IP 地址，如果有实例关联了弹性 IP 地址，则向安全团队发出 警报。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: (1) prevent developers from attaching an Elastic IP address, and (2) be notified if any production server has an EIP 'at any time'. Attaching an EIP is the ec2:AssociateAddress (associate-address) action performed by the developer's own IAM identity, so attaching an explicit Deny for associate-address to the developers' IAM group reliably blocks the action (an explicit Deny always overrides any Allow). For the 'at any time' detection, an AWS Config rule with a configuration-change trigger continuously tracks resource configuration changes and evaluates resources as they change, and AWS Config can stream compliance-state changes to an Amazon SNS topic to alert the security team. A CUSTOM Config rule is required here because the AWS managed rule eip-attached checks the opposite condition (it returns NON_COMPLIANT when an EIP's AssociationId is null, i.e., it flags EIPs that are NOT attached), so it cannot detect EIPs that ARE associated with production instances. Option B scopes the custom rule to instances tagged production and alerts the team, satisfying both prevention and continuous detection/alerting.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩個部分:(1) 防止開發人員附加 Elastic IP address;(2) 在任何時候 ('at any time') 若有 production 伺服器擁有 EIP 時通知安全團隊。附加 EIP 是由開發人員自身的 IAM identity 執行的 ec2:AssociateAddress (associate-address) 動作,因此在開發人員的 IAM group 上附加明確的 Deny associate-address 政策可確實阻止此動作 (明確的 Deny 永遠優先於任何 Allow)。對於 'at any time' 的偵測,採用 configuration-change 觸發類型的 AWS Config rule 會持續追蹤資源組態變更並在資源變更時進行評估,且 AWS Config 可將合規狀態變更串流至 Amazon SNS topic 以通知安全團隊。此處必須使用 CUSTOM Config rule,因為 AWS 受管規則 eip-attached 檢查的是相反條件 (當 EIP 的 AssociationId 為 null 時回傳 NON_COMPLIANT,即標示未附加的 EIP),無法偵測已關聯到 production 執行個體的 EIP。選項 B 將自訂規則的範圍限定在標記為 production 的執行個體並通知團隊,同時滿足預防與持續偵測/告警兩項要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Querying CloudTrail logs via Athena is on-demand/batch and historical (CloudTrail delivery is delayed), so it cannot provide continuous 'at any time' detection. It also does nothing to PREVENT a developer from attaching an EIP; it only reacts after the fact by disassociating, whereas the requirement is that no developer should be allowed to attach one in the first place.","why_zh":"透過 Athena 查詢 CloudTrail 日誌屬於隨選/批次且具歷史延遲性質 (CloudTrail 傳遞有延遲),無法提供持續的 'at any time' 偵測。它也完全沒有預防開發人員附加 EIP,僅在事後以解除關聯方式反應,而需求是不應允許任何開發人員附加 EIP。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Merely ensuring groups 'do not have' associate-address permission is weaker than an explicit Deny, because another attached policy or assumed role could still grant the permission. More importantly, a scheduled (periodic) Lambda polls only at intervals, leaving gaps, so it does not satisfy continuous 'at any time' detection the way an AWS Config configuration-change-triggered rule does.","why_zh":"僅確保 group 'does not have' associate-address 權限弱於明確的 Deny,因為其他附加政策或所擔任的角色仍可能授予該權限。更重要的是,排程 (週期性) 的 Lambda 只在固定間隔輪詢,留有偵測空窗,無法像 configuration-change 觸發的 AWS Config rule 那樣滿足持續的 'at any time' 偵測。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This misunderstands the permission model. An IAM role attached to an EC2 instance governs what that instance's own processes can do via the instance profile; it does NOT control whether a developer (a separate IAM identity using their own credentials) can call AssociateAddress against the instance. Therefore a Config rule checking instances for 'deny associate-address' instance roles does not prevent developers from attaching EIPs.","why_zh":"此選項誤解了權限模型。附加到 EC2 instance 的 IAM role 透過 instance profile 控管的是該執行個體自身行程能做什麼,並不控制開發人員 (使用自身憑證的另一個 IAM identity) 是否能對該執行個體呼叫 AssociateAddress。因此檢查執行個體是否具有 'deny associate-address' role 的 Config rule 無法防止開發人員附加 EIP。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/eip-attached.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/notifications-for-AWS-Config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/APIReference/API_AssociateAddress.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":154,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations to create separate AWS accounts for each of its departments. The company needs to automate the following tasks: Update the Linux AMIs with new patches periodically and generate a golden image Install a new version of Chef agents in the golden image, if available Provide the newly generated AMIs to the department's accounts Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST management overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 组织为每个部门创建单独的 AWS 账户。这 公司需要将以下任务自动化： 定期使用新补丁更新 Linux AMI 并生成黄金镜像 如果可用，请在黄金映像中安装新版本的 Chef 代理程序 将新生成的 AMI 提供给部门的账户 哪种解决方案在满足这些要求的同时，管理开销最小？","options_en":{"A":"Write a script to launch an Amazon EC2 instance from the previous golden image. Apply the patch updates. Install the new version of the Chef agent, generate a new golden image, and then modify the AMI permissions to share only the new image with the department's accounts.","B":"Use Amazon EC2 Image Builder to create an image pipeline that consists of the base Linux AMI and components to install the Chef agent. Use AWS Resource Access Manager to share EC2 Image Builder images with the department's accounts.","C":"Use an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to update the Linux AMI by using the previous image. Provide the URL for the script that will update the Chef agent. Use AWS Organizations to replace the previous golden image in the department's accounts.","D":"Use Amazon EC2 Image Builder to create an image pipeline that consists of the base Linux AMI and components to install the Chef agent. Create a parameter in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to store the new AMI ID that can be referenced by the department's accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"编写一个脚本，从之前的黄金镜像启动一个 Amazon EC2 实例。应用补丁更新。安装新版本的 Chef 代理，生成新的黄金镜像，然后修改 AMI 权限，仅与部门账户共享新镜像。","B":"使用 Amazon EC2 Image Builder 创建一个包含基础 Linux AMI 以及用于安装 Chef 代理的组件的映 像管道。使用 AWS 资源访问管理器与部门账户共享 EC2 Image Builder 映像。","C":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册通过使用之前的镜像来更新 Linux AMI。提供用 于更新 Chef 代理的脚本的 URL。使用 AWS Organizations 在部门账户中替换之前的黄金镜像。","D":"使用 Amazon EC2 Image Builder 创建一个包含基础 Linux AMI 以及用于安装 Chef 代理的组件的映像 管道。在 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储中创建一个参数来存储新的 AMI ID，以便部门的账户可 以引用。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"All requirements (periodic Linux patching to a golden image, conditional Chef-agent install, and distribution to department accounts) point to EC2 Image Builder, which runs an image pipeline on a schedule from a base Linux AMI plus components (a patch/update component and a Chef-agent component) with no manual instance management. That eliminates A (fully manual scripting) and C (misuse of an Automation runbook plus a non-existent Organizations 'replace image' capability). Both B and D build correctly with Image Builder, so the decision is how the new AMI is 'provided' to department accounts. AWS docs are explicit that AMIs are NOT Image Builder resources -- they are 'external resources that Image Builder distributes' via distribution configuration; AWS RAM only shares the Image Builder image/component/recipe resources, and a RAM-shared image merely lets consumers 'use it as the base image in their recipes' (granting just imagebuilder:GetImage/ListImages), which would force each department to build its own image. That mismatches the requirement to hand out a ready-to-use golden AMI, so B is wrong. Option D keeps the Image Builder pipeline and uses Systems Manager Parameter Store -- Image Builder natively writes the new AMI ID to an SSM parameter via SsmParameterConfiguration (dataType aws:ec2:image) -- so department accounts always reference the latest golden AMI automatically, the documented lowest-overhead pattern. Therefore D is correct; the dump's suggested answer B mischaracterizes RAM.","explanation_zh":"所有需求（定期為 Linux 打補丁產生 golden image、條件式安裝 Chef agent、並把 AMI 提供給各部門帳號）都指向 EC2 Image Builder：它依排程以基底 Linux AMI 加上 components（一個 patch/update component 與一個 Chef-agent component）執行 image pipeline，無需手動管理執行個體。這排除了 A（全手動腳本）與 C（誤用 Automation runbook，且 AWS Organizations 並無『取代 golden image』的功能）。B 與 D 都正確地以 Image Builder 建置，差別在於如何把新 AMI『提供』給部門帳號。AWS 文件明確指出 AMI 並非 Image Builder 資源，而是『Image Builder 透過 distribution configuration 分發的外部資源』；AWS RAM 只能分享 Image Builder 的 image/component/recipe 資源，而被 RAM 分享的 image 只允許消費者『在自己的 recipe 中作為基底映像使用』（僅授予 imagebuilder:GetImage/ListImages），等於每個部門還要自行建置映像，無法滿足直接交付可用 golden AMI 的需求，故 B 錯誤。D 維持 Image Builder pipeline，並使用 Systems Manager Parameter Store——Image Builder 透過 distribution 設定中的 SsmParameterConfiguration（dataType 為 aws:ec2:image）原生將新 AMI ID 寫入 SSM 參數——讓部門帳號自動參考最新 golden AMI，這是文件記載且管理負擔最低的模式。因此正確答案為 D；題庫建議答案 B 誤解了 RAM。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A custom script that launches an instance, patches it, installs Chef, creates an AMI, and manually modifies AMI launch permissions is the highest-overhead, fully manual approach -- exactly what EC2 Image Builder exists to automate. It fails the 'LEAST management overhead' qualifier.","why_zh":"自訂腳本啟動執行個體、打補丁、安裝 Chef、建立 AMI、再手動修改 AMI launch permissions，是負擔最高的全手動做法，正是 EC2 Image Builder 要取代的工作，違反『管理負擔最低』的限定條件。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Image Builder is correct, but AWS RAM is the wrong sharing primitive: per AWS docs an AMI is an external resource distributed via distribution configuration, not an Image Builder resource. RAM shares the Image Builder image/component/recipe resources, and a RAM-shared image only lets consumers use it as a base image in their own recipes (imagebuilder:GetImage/ListImages). It does not deliver a launchable golden AMI to department accounts and adds per-department build overhead, so it mismatches the 'provide the AMIs' requirement.","why_zh":"Image Builder 正確，但 AWS RAM 是錯誤的分享原語：依 AWS 文件，AMI 是透過 distribution configuration 分發的外部資源，並非 Image Builder 資源。RAM 分享的是 image/component/recipe 資源，被分享的 image 只能讓消費者在自己的 recipe 中當作 base image（imagebuilder:GetImage/ListImages），不會把可啟動的 golden AMI 交付給部門帳號，反而讓每個部門都要自行建置，與『提供 AMI』需求不符。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A hand-built SSM Automation runbook plus a URL-fetched Chef-update script is more bespoke and brittle automation to maintain than an Image Builder pipeline, and 'use AWS Organizations to replace the previous golden image in the department's accounts' is not a real Organizations capability -- Organizations does not push or replace AMIs into member accounts.","why_zh":"自建 SSM Automation runbook 加上以 URL 取得的 Chef 更新腳本，需維護的客製化且脆弱的自動化比 Image Builder pipeline 多；而且『用 AWS Organizations 取代部門帳號中先前的 golden image』並非 Organizations 的真實功能——Organizations 不會把 AMI 推送或取代到成員帳號。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/manage-shared-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/manage-shared-resources-share.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/cross-account-dist.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/how-image-builder-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/tutorial-ssm-parameters-recipe.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/APIReference/API_SsmParameterConfiguration.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":155,"question_en":"A company has a mission-critical application on AWS that uses automatic scaling. The company wants the deployment lifecycle to meet the following parameters: The application must be deployed one instance at a time to ensure the remaining fleet continues to serve traffic. The application is CPU intensive and must be closely monitored. The deployment must automatically roll back if the CPU utilization of the deployment instance exceeds 85%. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上运行着一个关键任务应用程序，该程序使用了自动扩展功能。该公司希望其部署生 命周期满足以下参数： 必须一次部署一个实例，以确保其余的实例群组能够继续处理流量。 该应用程序对 CPU 资源消耗很大，必须密切监控。 如果部署实例的 CPU 利用率超过 85%，则部署必须自动回滚。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation to create an AWS Step Functions state machine and Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to move to one instance at a time into a wait state. Use AWS Systems Manager automation to deploy the update to each instance and move it back into the Auto Scaling group using the heartbeat timeout.","B":"Use AWS CodeDeploy with Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling Configure an alarm tied to the CPU utilization metric. Use the CodeDeployDefault OneAtAtime configuration as a deployment strategy. Configure automatic rollbacks within the deployment group to roll back the deployment if the alarm thresholds are breached.","C":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk for load balancing and AWS Auto Scaling. Configure an alarm tied to the CPU utilization metric. Configure rolling deployments with a fixed batch size of one instance. Enable enhanced health to monitor the status of the deployment and roll back based on the alarm previously created.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager to perform a blue/green deployment with Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling. Configure an alarm tied to the CPU utilization metric. Deploy updates one at a time. Configure automatic rollbacks within the Auto Scaling group to roll back the deployment if the alarm thresholds are breached."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 创建 AWS Step Functions 状态机和 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩，每次将一 个实例移入等待状态。使用 AWS Systems Manager 自动化功能将更新部署到每个实例，并在心跳 超时后将其移回 Auto Scaling 组。","B":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 与 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 结合 配置与 CPU 利用率指标相关的警报。使用 CodeDeployDefault OneAtAtime 配置作为部署策略。在部署组中配置自动回滚，以便在警报阈值被 突破时回滚部署。","C":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 进行负载均衡和 AWS Auto Scaling。配置与 CPU 利用率指标相关的警报。 配置固定批次大小为一个实例的滚动部署。启用增强型健康检查以监控部署状态，并根据之前创 建的警报进行回滚。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 通过 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 执行蓝/绿部署。配置与 CPU 利用率指 标相关的警报。一次部署一个更新。在 Auto Scaling 组内配置自动回滚，如果警报阈值被突破则 回滚部署。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CodeDeploy with Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling natively satisfies all three requirements with the least operational overhead. (1) One instance at a time: the predefined CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime deployment configuration deploys the revision to only one instance at a time, so the rest of the fleet keeps serving traffic. (2) Close monitoring: you associate a CloudWatch alarm on the CPU utilization metric (the alarm can be created for an EC2 instance or an EC2 Auto Scaling group) with the deployment group. (3) Automatic rollback: CodeDeploy supports configuring a deployment group to 'automatically roll back when a deployment fails or when a monitoring threshold you specify is met' - specifically the 'Roll back when alarm thresholds are met' option, which redeploys the last known good revision when the associated alarm (CPU > 85%) activates. This is the purpose-built, lowest-overhead solution and maps exactly to each parameter without custom orchestration.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeDeploy 搭配 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 以最低營運負擔原生滿足全部三項需求。(1) 一次一台：預先定義的 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime 部署設定一次只將修訂版部署到一台執行個體，因此其餘機群可持續提供服務。(2) 密切監控：將針對 CPU utilization 指標建立的 CloudWatch alarm（該 alarm 可針對 EC2 執行個體或 EC2 Auto Scaling group 建立）關聯到 deployment group。(3) 自動回復：CodeDeploy 支援將 deployment group 設定為『當部署失敗或達到您指定的監控門檻時自動回復』，具體即『Roll back when alarm thresholds are met』選項，當關聯的 alarm（CPU > 85%）觸發時會重新部署最後一個已知正常的修訂版。這是專為此情境設計、負擔最低的方案，與每項參數精準對應，無需自訂編排。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Building a custom Step Functions state machine plus Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks and SSM Automation is far higher operational overhead than the purpose-built CodeDeploy. More importantly, it provides no native automatic rollback tied to a CPU alarm; the heartbeat timeout merely governs how long the lifecycle hook holds an instance in a wait state, not CPU-based rollback. The required alarm-driven rollback behavior is not met.","why_zh":"自行建構 Step Functions 狀態機加上 Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks 與 SSM Automation 的營運負擔遠高於專用的 CodeDeploy。更關鍵的是，它不提供與 CPU alarm 連動的原生自動回復；heartbeat timeout 只是控制 lifecycle hook 將執行個體保持在等待狀態的時間，並非以 CPU 為依據的回復機制，無法滿足以 alarm 驅動回復的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Elastic Beanstalk rolling deployments can use a batch size of one, but their rollback is driven by Beanstalk's own enhanced health monitoring (failed health checks per batch), not by an arbitrary user-defined CloudWatch alarm on CPU utilization. Beanstalk does not natively wire 'roll back when this CPU alarm fires' the way CodeDeploy's deployment-group alarm-based automatic rollback does, so the alarm-driven rollback requirement is not cleanly met.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk 滾動式部署可採用批次大小為一，但其回復是由 Beanstalk 自身的 enhanced health 監控（各批次健康檢查失敗）驅動，而非由使用者自訂的 CPU utilization CloudWatch alarm 驅動。Beanstalk 並未像 CodeDeploy 的 deployment-group alarm 自動回復那樣原生支援『當此 CPU alarm 觸發時回復』，因此無法乾淨地滿足以 alarm 驅動回復的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager is not a blue/green deployment service for EC2 Auto Scaling, and 'automatic rollbacks within the Auto Scaling group' based on a CloudWatch alarm is not a real ASG feature - ASGs do not roll back application deployments on alarm. Additionally, blue/green deployment replaces the whole fleet rather than updating one instance at a time, contradicting the stated requirement. The option attributes capabilities to the wrong services.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager 並非用於 EC2 Auto Scaling 的藍綠部署服務，且以 CloudWatch alarm 為依據在 Auto Scaling group 內進行『自動回復』並非真實的 ASG 功能——ASG 不會因 alarm 而回復應用程式部署。此外，藍綠部署是替換整個機群而非一次更新一台，與題目需求矛盾。此選項把功能歸給了錯誤的服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-rollback-and-redeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-configure-advanced-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":156,"question_en":"A company has a single developer writing code for an automated deployment pipeline. The developer is storing source code in an Amazon S3 bucket for each project. The company wants to add more developers to the team but is concerned about code conflicts and lost work. The company also wants to build a test environment to deploy newer versions of code for testing and allow developers to automatically deploy to both environments when code is changed in the repository. What is the MOST efficient way to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一名开发人员为自动化部署流水线编写代码。该开发人员为每个项目将源代码存储在亚马 逊 S3 存储桶中。该公司希望为团队增加更多开发人员，但担心代码冲突和工作丢失。该公司还希望 构建一个测试环境，以便在代码库中代码发生更改时部署较新版本的代码进行测试，并允许开发人员 自动将代码部署到这两个环境。 满足这些要求的最有效方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository for each project, use the main branch for production code, and create a testing branch for code deployed to testing. Use feature branches to develop new features and pull requests to merge code to testing and main branches.","B":"Create another S3 bucket for each project for testing code, and use an AWS Lambda function to promote code changes between testing and production buckets. Enable versioning on all buckets to prevent code conflicts.","C":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository for each project, and use the main branch for production and test code with different deployment pipelines for each environment. Use feature branches to develop new features.","D":"Enable versioning and branching on each S3 bucket, use the main branch for production code, and create a testing branch for code deployed to testing. Have developers use each branch for developing in each environment."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个项目创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库，将主分支用于生产代码，并创建一个测试分支用 于部署到测试环境的代码。使用功能分支开发新功能，并使用拉取请求将代码合并到测试分支和 主分支。","B":"为每个项目创建另一个 S3 存储桶用于测试代码，并使用 AWS Lambda 函数在测试存储桶和生 产存储桶之间推进代码变更。在所有存储桶上启用版本控制以防止代码冲突。","C":"为每个项目创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库，并使用主分支存放生产环境和测试环境的代码， 同时为每个环境设置不同的部署管道。使用功能分支开发新功能。","D":"在每个 S3 存储桶上启用版本控制和分支功能，将主分支用于生产代码，并为部署到测试环境的 代码创建一个测试分支。要求开发人员在每个环境中使用相应的分支进行开发。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: (1) prevent code conflicts and lost work when adding more developers, and (2) maintain separate testing and production environments with automated deployment when code changes. A source/version control service (Git) is the purpose-built tool for collaborative development. AWS CodeCommit is a managed Git service; its documentation states it 'is optimized for team software development. It manages batches of changes across multiple files, which can occur in parallel with changes made by other developers,' and explicitly contrasts it with S3 versioning, which 'supports the recovery of past versions of files, but it's not focused on collaborative file tracking features that software development teams need.' The Well-Architected best practice OPS05-BP01 also recommends a source control system such as CodeCommit precisely to avoid the anti-patterns in the question (lost work, inability to revert a bad change, write-lock conflicts between developers). Option A implements the canonical CodeCommit branching workflow: a main branch for production, a testing branch for test, feature branches for new work, and pull requests to review and merge changes -- exactly the mechanism that prevents conflicts and lost work. The separate main and testing branches map cleanly to two deployment pipelines so code changes trigger automatic deployment to the matching environment. This is the MOST efficient design because it uses native Git collaboration features rather than bolting custom logic onto object storage.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩點：(1) 在增加開發人員時避免程式碼衝突與工作遺失；(2) 維護獨立的測試與正式環境，並在程式碼變更時自動部署。原始碼／版本控制服務 (Git) 才是協同開發的專用工具。AWS CodeCommit 是受管的 Git 服務，其文件明確指出它『針對團隊軟體開發最佳化，可管理跨多個檔案的批次變更，並能與其他開發人員並行的變更同時發生』，並與 S3 versioning 對比：S3 versioning『支援還原檔案的舊版本，但並未聚焦於軟體開發團隊所需的協同檔案追蹤功能』。Well-Architected 最佳實務 OPS05-BP01 也建議使用如 CodeCommit 的原始碼控制系統，正是為了避免題目中描述的反模式 (工作遺失、無法回復錯誤變更、開發人員間的寫入鎖定衝突)。選項 A 實作標準的 CodeCommit 分支工作流程：main 分支用於正式環境、testing 分支用於測試、feature 分支用於開發新功能，並用 pull request 審查與合併變更——這正是防止衝突與工作遺失的機制。獨立的 main 與 testing 分支可清楚對應到兩條部署管線，程式碼變更即觸發對應環境的自動部署。這是最有效率的設計，因為它使用原生 Git 協同功能，而非在物件儲存上加上自訂邏輯。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Using a second S3 bucket plus a Lambda function to promote code and relying on S3 versioning 'to prevent code conflicts' does not work: S3 versioning recovers past object versions but provides no merge, branch, or pull-request capability, and on simultaneous writes it simply 'stores all of those objects' rather than reconciling them, so it cannot prevent concurrent-edit conflicts or lost work in team development. It also builds bespoke promotion logic instead of using a native version control service, increasing operational overhead.","why_zh":"用第二個 S3 bucket 加 Lambda 來推進程式碼，並以 S3 versioning『避免程式碼衝突』行不通：S3 versioning 只能還原舊版物件，無合併、分支或 pull request 能力，且同時寫入時只是『將所有物件都存起來』而非協調合併，無法防止團隊並行編輯的衝突或工作遺失。它還需自建推進邏輯，而非使用原生版本控制服務，增加營運負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Putting both production and test code on a single main branch with two pipelines defeats the purpose of separate environments: there is no isolated testing branch, so test deployments and production deployments draw from the same code state, and merging only via feature branches into one branch gives no place to validate newer versions before they reach production. It is less efficient and riskier than A's main/testing branch separation.","why_zh":"把正式與測試程式碼都放在單一 main 分支再配兩條管線，違背了環境隔離的目的：沒有獨立的 testing 分支，測試部署與正式部署取自同一份程式碼狀態，且僅透過 feature 分支併入單一分支，無處在進入正式環境前驗證較新版本。比 A 的 main/testing 分支隔離更低效且風險更高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon S3 does not have 'branching' as a feature -- S3 only offers object versioning. AWS documentation states S3 versioning is not focused on the collaborative file-tracking features software teams need, so it cannot provide branches, merges, or pull requests. This option describes capabilities that do not exist for S3.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 並沒有『branching (分支)』功能——S3 只提供物件 versioning。AWS 文件指出 S3 versioning 並未聚焦於軟體團隊所需的協同檔案追蹤功能，故無法提供分支、合併或 pull request。此選項描述的是 S3 不存在的功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/pull-requests.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/Versioning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2023-04-10/framework/ops_dev_integ_version_control.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":157,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer notices that all Amazon EC2 instances running behind an Application Load Balancer in an Auto Scaling group are failing to respond to user requests. The EC2 instances are also failing target group HTTP health checks. Upon inspection, the engineer notices the application process was not running in any EC2 instances. There are a significant number of out of memory messages in the system logs. The engineer needs to improve the resilience of the application to cope with a potential application memory leak. Monitoring and notifications should be enabled to alert when there is an issue. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，在一个自动扩展组中，所有运行在应用负载均衡器后面的亚马逊 EC2 实例都无法响应用户的请求。这些 EC2 实例也无法通过目标组的 HTTP 健康检查。 工程师检查后发现，该应用程序在任何 EC2 实例中都没有运行。系统日志中有大量内存不足的错误 信息。工程师需要提高应用程序的弹性，以应对潜在的应用程序内存泄漏问题。应启用监控和通知 功能，以便在出现问题时发出警报。 哪种行动组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Change the Auto Scaling configuration to replace the instances when they fail the load balancer's health checks.","B":"Change the target group health check HealthCheckIntervalSeconds parameter to reduce the interval between health checks.","C":"Change the target group health checks from HTTP to TCP to check if the port where the application is listening is reachable.","D":"Enable the available memory consumption metric within the Amazon CloudWatch dashboard for the entire Auto Scaling group. Create an alarm when the memory utilization is high. Associate an Amazon SNS topic to the alarm to receive notifications when the alarm goes off.","E":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to collect the memory utilization of the EC2 instances in the Auto Scaling group. Create an alarm when the memory utilization is high and associate an Amazon SNS topic to receive a notification."},"options_zh":{"A":"更改自动扩展配置，以便在实例未通过负载均衡器的健康检查时将其替换。","B":"更改目标组的健康检查参数 HealthCheckIntervalSeconds，以缩短健康检查之间的间隔。","C":"将目标组的健康检查从 HTTP 更改为 TCP，以检查应用程序监听的端口是否可达。","D":"在 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板中为整个 Auto Scaling 组启用可用内存使用情况指标。当内存利 用率较高时创建警报。将 Amazon SNS 主题与警报关联，以便在警报触发时接收通知。","E":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理收集自动扩展组中 EC2 实例的内存利用率。当内存利用率较高时 创建警报，并关联一个 Amazon SNS 主题以接收通知。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When the application is killed by an OOM event the EC2 instance keeps running, so the default Auto Scaling health check (EC2 status checks, which only verify the instance is running and the hardware/hypervisor is healthy) still passes, even though the ALB target group HTTP health check fails. (A) The fix is to turn on Elastic Load Balancing health checks for the Auto Scaling group; AWS docs state this check type 'must be turned on' and, once enabled, EC2 Auto Scaling uses the load balancer's results to mark the failing instances Unhealthy and automatically replace them, restoring resilience to the memory leak. (E) Memory utilization is not one of the metrics EC2 publishes by default to CloudWatch; the CloudWatch agent docs say the agent's metrics are 'in addition to the metrics enabled by default,' so memory must be collected with the CloudWatch agent. Installing the agent to publish memory utilization, then creating a high-memory alarm tied to an SNS topic, delivers the required proactive monitoring and notification. A plus E give automatic recovery plus alerting.","explanation_zh":"當應用程式因 OOM 事件被終止時，EC2 執行個體仍持續執行，因此 Auto Scaling 預設的健康檢查（EC2 status checks，僅確認執行個體正在執行且底層硬體/hypervisor 正常）仍會通過，即使 ALB target group 的 HTTP health check 失敗。(A) 解法是為 Auto Scaling group 開啟 Elastic Load Balancing health checks；AWS 文件指出此檢查類型「必須手動開啟」，啟用後 EC2 Auto Scaling 會依據負載平衡器的結果，將故障執行個體標記為 Unhealthy 並自動替換，恢復對記憶體洩漏的韌性。(E) 記憶體使用率並非 EC2 預設發佈到 CloudWatch 的指標；CloudWatch agent 文件說明 agent 收集的指標是「在預設啟用指標之外額外提供」，因此記憶體必須由 CloudWatch agent 收集。安裝 agent 發佈記憶體使用率，再建立高記憶體警示並關聯 SNS topic，即可提供所需的主動監控與通知。A 與 E 合併即提供自動復原與警示。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Reducing HealthCheckIntervalSeconds only makes the ALB detect the failure slightly faster; it does nothing on its own because, without enabling ELB health checks in the ASG (Option A), the failing instances are still never replaced (EC2 status checks keep passing). It also provides no monitoring or notification.","why_zh":"縮短 HealthCheckIntervalSeconds 只會讓 ALB 稍微更快偵測到故障；單獨使用毫無作用，因為若未在 ASG 啟用 ELB health checks（選項 A），故障執行個體仍不會被替換（EC2 status checks 持續通過）。它也未提供任何監控或通知。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Changing the health check from HTTP to TCP weakens it: a TCP check only confirms the port is reachable, so it would pass a broken app that still listens but returns errors, masking problems. After an OOM the process is gone anyway, so this does not improve resilience and provides no monitoring or notification.","why_zh":"將健康檢查從 HTTP 改為 TCP 反而削弱檢查：TCP 檢查只確認連接埠可達，故障但仍在監聽卻回傳錯誤的應用程式會被誤判為健康，掩蓋問題。OOM 後行程已消失，因此這無法提升韌性，也未提供監控或通知。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no built-in 'available memory consumption' metric that you can simply enable from a CloudWatch dashboard for EC2; the CloudWatch agent docs state agent metrics are 'in addition to the metrics enabled by default,' meaning memory requires the agent to be installed first. As written this option skips the agent and is technically not achievable; Option E is the correct memory-monitoring approach.","why_zh":"CloudWatch 中並無可直接從儀表板為 EC2「啟用」的內建「可用記憶體消耗」指標；CloudWatch agent 文件說明 agent 指標是「在預設啟用指標之外額外提供」，意即記憶體必須先安裝 agent 才能取得。按其敘述此選項略過了 agent，技術上無法達成；選項 E 才是正確的記憶體監控做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/health-checks-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/attach-load-balancer-asg.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/autoscaling-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/metrics-collected-by-CloudWatch-agent.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":158,"question_en":"An ecommerce company uses a large number of Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) backed Amazon EC2 instances. To decrease manual work across all the instances, a DevOps engineer is tasked with automating restart actions when EC2 instance retirement events are scheduled. How can this be accomplished?","question_zh":"一家电子商务公司使用大量由亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）支持的亚马逊 EC2 实例。为了减少所 有实例上的手动工作，一位 DevOps 工程师被指派在计划 EC2 实例退役事件时自动执行重启操作。 这该如何实现呢？","options_en":{"A":"Create a scheduled Amazon EventBridge rule to run an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that checks if any EC2 instances are scheduled for retirement once a week. If the instance is scheduled for retirement, the runbook will hibernate the instance.","B":"Enable EC2 Auto Recovery on all of the instances. Create an AWS Config rule to limit the recovery to occur during a maintenance window only.","C":"Reboot all EC2 instances during an approved maintenance window that is outside of standard business hours. Set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms to send a notification in case any instance is failing EC2 instance status checks.","D":"Set up an AWS Health Amazon EventBridge rule to run AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks that stop and start the EC2 instance when a retirement scheduled event occurs."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个计划的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每周运行一次 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手 册，检查是否有任何 EC2 实例计划退役。如果实例计划退役，该运行手册将使实例进入休眠状态。","B":"在所有实例上启用 EC2 自动恢复功能。创建一条 AWS Config 规则，仅允许在维护窗口期间进行恢 复操作。","C":"在标准工作时间之外的经批准的维护窗口期间重新启动所有 EC2 实例。设置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报， 以便在任何实例未通过 EC2 实例状态检查时发送通知。","D":"设置一个 AWS Health Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在计划退役事件发生时运行 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行本，从而停止和启动 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When an EBS-backed EC2 instance is scheduled for retirement, AWS Health emits the AWS_EC2_PERSISTENT_INSTANCE_RETIREMENT_SCHEDULED event type. The AWS Health User Guide page 'Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health' describes this exact scenario: create an EventBridge rule (source aws.health) that detects this event type and targets an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to automatically stop and start the instance, so you don't perform the action manually. A stop/start migrates the instance to a new healthy host, which is precisely what resolves a retirement; the EC2 docs note this 'is not the same as rebooting the instance.' Because the workflow is event-driven, the action fires exactly when retirement is scheduled. This matches option D.","explanation_zh":"當 EBS 支援的 EC2 執行個體被排定退役時，AWS Health 會發出 AWS_EC2_PERSISTENT_INSTANCE_RETIREMENT_SCHEDULED 事件類型。AWS Health User Guide 的『Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health』頁面描述了完全相同的情境：建立一個 EventBridge 規則（source aws.health）偵測此事件類型，並以 AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook 作為目標，自動 stop 與 start 執行個體，因此無需手動執行。stop/start 會將執行個體遷移到新的健康主機，這正是解決退役所需的動作；EC2 文件也指出這『與 reboot 執行個體不同』。由於整個流程是事件驅動，動作會在退役被排定時精準觸發。這正符合選項 D。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A weekly scheduled EventBridge poll is not event-driven and could lag or miss retirements scheduled within the week. More critically, hibernating the instance does not migrate it off the failing host, so it does not resolve the retirement; a stop/start is required to move to a healthy host.","why_zh":"每週排程的 EventBridge 輪詢並非事件驅動，可能延誤或錯過在該週內排定的退役。更關鍵的是，hibernate 執行個體不會將其從故障主機遷移，因此無法解決退役；需要 stop/start 才能移到健康主機。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"EC2 Auto Recovery responds to system status check failures of the underlying host, not to scheduled retirement events, so it does not proactively act when a retirement is scheduled. AWS Config evaluates resource configuration compliance and cannot gate or restrict a recovery action to a maintenance window, so this design does not work as described.","why_zh":"EC2 Auto Recovery 是針對底層主機的系統狀態檢查失敗作出回應，而非針對排定的退役事件，因此不會在退役被排定時主動採取行動。AWS Config 是評估資源組態合規性，無法將復原動作閘控或限制在維護時段，因此此設計無法如所述運作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Rebooting keeps the instance on the same underlying host, so it does NOT migrate the instance off the failing hardware and does not resolve a retirement (AWS docs explicitly state stop/start is 'not the same as rebooting'). It is also a manual maintenance-window task rather than automation, failing the goal of decreasing manual work.","why_zh":"reboot 會讓執行個體留在同一底層主機，因此不會將其從故障硬體遷移，也無法解決退役（AWS 文件明確指出 stop/start『與 reboot 不同』）。此外它是手動的維護時段作業而非自動化，未達成減少手動工作的目標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/automating-instance-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/schedevents_actions_retire.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/instance-retirement.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":159,"question_en":"A company manages AWS accounts for application teams in AWS Control Tower. Individual application teams are responsible for securing their respective AWS accounts. A DevOps engineer needs to enable Amazon GuardDuty for all AWS accounts in which the application teams have not already enabled GuardDuty. The DevOps engineer is using AWS CloudFormation StackSets from the AWS Control Tower management account. How should the DevOps engineer configure the CloudFormation template to prevent failure during the StackSets deployment?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 控制塔中管理应用程序团队的 AWS 账户。各个应用程序团队负责保护其各自的 AWS 账户的安全。 DevOps 工程师需要为应用团队尚未启用 Amazon GuardDuty 的所有 AWS 账户启用该服务。该 DevOps 工程师正在从 AWS 控制塔管理账户使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置 CloudFormation 模板以防止在 StackSets 部署期间出现故障？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudFormation custom resource that invokes an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to conditionally enable GuardDuty if GuardDuty is not already enabled in the accounts.","B":"Use the Conditions section of the CloudFormation template to enable GuardDuty in accounts where GuardDuty is not already enabled.","C":"Use the CloudFormation Fn::GetAtt intrinsic function to check whether GuardDuty is already enabled. If GuardDuty is not already enabled, use the Resources section of the CloudFormation template to enable GuardDuty.","D":"Manually discover the list of AWS account IDs where GuardDuty is not enabled. Use the CloudFormation Fn::ImportValue intrinsic function to import the list of account IDs into the CloudFormation template to skip deployment for the listed AWS accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 CloudFormation 自定义资源，用于调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数，使 其在账户中尚未启用 GuardDuty 时有条件地启用 GuardDuty。","B":"使用 CloudFormation 模板的“条件”部分，在尚未启用 GuardDuty 的账户中启用 GuardDuty。","C":"使用 CloudFormation 的 Fn::GetAtt 内置函数检查 GuardDuty 是否已启用。如果 GuardDuty 尚未启用， 请在 CloudFormation 模板的 Resources 部分启用它。","D":"手动找出未启用 GuardDuty 的 AWS 账户 ID 列表。使用 CloudFormation 的 Fn:: ImportValue 内置函数将账户 ID 列表导入 CloudFormation 模板，以便跳过对所列 AWS 账户的部署。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"GuardDuty needs to be enabled only once per account and Region (one detector), so deploying an AWS::GuardDuty::Detector with Enable=true via StackSets fails in any account where an application team already enabled GuardDuty. AWS Prescriptive Guidance addresses this exact scenario: 'If you attempt to enable GuardDuty through CloudFormation in an account where it's already active, the stack deployment fails,' and its recommended solution is a CloudFormation custom resource backed by a Lambda function that performs a dynamic state check and enables GuardDuty only if it isn't already enabled. The same doc notes you extend the solution across many accounts/Regions with StackSets - matching the Control Tower management-account deployment described here. Only a Lambda-backed custom resource can query runtime per-account API state (ListDetectors/GetDetector) and act idempotently, so A is correct.","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty 每個帳戶每個區域只需啟用一次（單一 detector），因此透過 StackSets 部署 Enable=true 的 AWS::GuardDuty::Detector 時，在已由應用團隊啟用 GuardDuty 的帳戶中會失敗。AWS Prescriptive Guidance 針對此情境明確說明：『若你嘗試在 GuardDuty 已啟用的帳戶中透過 CloudFormation 啟用它，堆疊部署會失敗』，其建議解法正是使用由 Lambda 函式支援的 CloudFormation custom resource，執行動態狀態檢查，僅在尚未啟用時才啟用 GuardDuty。同份文件也指出可用 StackSets 將此解法擴展到多帳戶／多區域，正符合本題在 Control Tower 管理帳戶部署的情境。只有 Lambda 支援的 custom resource 能查詢執行時各帳戶的 API 狀態（ListDetectors/GetDetector）並以冪等方式運作，因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS docs state plainly that 'traditional CloudFormation conditions support only static value comparisons, which makes it difficult to check the current state of services such as GuardDuty.' Conditions are evaluated at deploy time from static inputs (parameters, mappings, pseudo-parameters) and cannot query whether GuardDuty is already enabled in each target account, so they cannot prevent the per-account creation failure.","why_zh":"AWS 文件明確指出『傳統 CloudFormation conditions 僅支援靜態值比較，難以檢查像 GuardDuty 這類服務的當前狀態』。Conditions 在部署時依靜態輸入（參數、mappings、pseudo-parameters）評估，無法查詢各目標帳戶是否已啟用 GuardDuty，因此無法防止各帳戶的建立失敗。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Fn::GetAtt only returns attributes of resources already defined within the same template (e.g., the Detector's Id); it cannot inspect an account's existing GuardDuty state before the resource is created. There is also no Fn::GetAtt-based 'check then create' branching mechanism, so this option does not prevent the failure.","why_zh":"Fn::GetAtt 只回傳同一範本內已定義資源的屬性（例如 Detector 的 Id），無法在建立資源前檢查帳戶現有的 GuardDuty 狀態；也不存在以 Fn::GetAtt 為基礎的『先檢查再建立』分支機制，因此無法防止失敗。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Fn::ImportValue imports exported Output values from other CloudFormation stacks in the same account and Region, not arbitrary cross-account account-ID lists, and a StackSet cannot selectively skip individual target accounts through an imported value. Manual discovery is not idempotent, defeats automation, and breaks as teams enable/disable GuardDuty over time.","why_zh":"Fn::ImportValue 匯入的是同帳戶同區域其他 CloudFormation 堆疊匯出的 Output 值，並非任意跨帳戶的帳戶 ID 清單，StackSet 也無法透過匯入值選擇性略過個別目標帳戶。手動探查不具冪等性、違反自動化，且當團隊隨時間啟用／停用 GuardDuty 時會失效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/enable-amazon-guardduty-conditionally-by-using-aws-cloudformation-templates.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-guardduty-detector.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/what-is-cfnstacksets.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":160,"question_en":"A company has an AWS Control Tower landing zone. The company's DevOps team creates a workload OU. A development OU and a production OU are nested under the workload OU. The company grants users full access to the company's AWS accounts to deploy applications. The DevOps team needs to allow only a specific management IAM role to manage the IAM roles and policies of any AWS accounts in only the production OU. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个 AWS 控制塔着陆区。该公司的 DevOps 团队创建了一个工作负载组织单元。开发 组织单元和生产组织单元嵌套在工作负载组织单元之下。该公司授予用户对公司所有 AWS 账户的完 全访问权限，以便部署应用程序。 DevOps 团队需要仅允许特定的管理 IAM 角色在仅生产组织单位中管理任何 AWS 账户的 IAM 角 色和策略。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that denies full access with a condition to exclude the management IAM role for the organization root.","B":"Ensure that the FullAWSAccess SCP is applied at the organization root.","C":"Create an SCP that allows IAM related actions. Attach the SCP to the development OU.","D":"Create an SCP that denies IAM related actions with a condition to exclude the management IAM role. Attach the SCP to the workload OU.","E":"Create an SCP that denies IAM related actions with a condition to exclude the management IAM role. Attach the SCP to the production OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 SCP（安全策略），在拒绝完全访问权限的同时，将组织根目录的管理 IAM 角色排除在外。","B":"确保在组织根目录应用“FullAWSAccess”服务控制策略（SCP）。","C":"创建一个允许执行与 IAM 相关操作的服务控制策略（SCP）。将该 SCP 附加到开发组织单位（OU）。","D":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），该策略在条件中排除管理 IAM 角色的情况下拒绝与 IAM 相关的操作。 将该 SCP 附加到工作负载组织单位（OU）。","E":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），该策略在条件中排除管理 IAM 角色的情况下拒绝与 IAM 相关的操作。 将该 SCP 附加到生产组织单位（OU）。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SCPs follow a deny-by-default model: a permission is allowed only if there is an explicit Allow at every level from the root down to the account, which is why AWS Organizations (and AWS Control Tower) attaches the AWS-managed FullAWSAccess SCP at every level by default. Because users were granted full access to deploy applications, FullAWSAccess must remain applied at the organization root; if the root-level Allow is missing, all member accounts are blocked from every action (B). To restrict IAM role/policy management to only a specific management role in only the production OU, you create a Deny SCP on IAM-related actions with a condition that excludes the management role (for example, aws:PrincipalArn with ArnNotLike) and attach it to the production OU. A Deny attached at any level applies to every account beneath it, so attaching it at the production OU scopes the restriction to production accounts and leaves the development OU unaffected (E). The AWS Organizations SCP evaluation guide's Scenario 4 mirrors this exact two-level structure (Workloads OU with nested Test and Production sub-OUs), keeping FullAWSAccess at root and the OU while applying a targeted Deny only at the specific sub-OU.","explanation_zh":"SCP 採用預設拒絕 (deny-by-default) 模型：只有當從 organization root 一路到帳戶的「每一層」都有明確的 Allow 時，權限才會被允許，這也是 AWS Organizations（以及 AWS Control Tower）預設在每一層都附加 AWS 受管的 FullAWSAccess SCP 的原因。由於使用者被授予部署應用程式的完整存取權，FullAWSAccess 必須持續套用在 organization root；若 root 層缺少 Allow，所有成員帳戶將被封鎖、無法執行任何動作（B）。要將 IAM 角色／政策管理限制為只有特定 management role、且僅限 production OU，你需要建立一個 Deny IAM 相關動作的 SCP，並加上排除該 management role 的 condition（例如 aws:PrincipalArn 搭配 ArnNotLike），再將其附加到 production OU。Deny 在任一層附加後會套用到其下所有帳戶，因此附加在 production OU 可將限制範圍鎖定在 production 帳戶，而不影響 development OU（E）。AWS Organizations SCP 評估指南的 Scenario 4 正好對應這個兩層結構（Workloads OU 下巢狀 Test 與 Production 子 OU），在 root 與 OU 保留 FullAWSAccess，並只在特定子 OU 附加針對性的 Deny。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An SCP that denies full access at the organization root would block every action for all member accounts (except the excluded role), breaking the requirement that users keep full access to deploy applications. It is also scoped to the whole org/root rather than only the production OU, so it cannot satisfy the 'only the production OU' qualifier.","why_zh":"在 organization root 拒絕 full access 的 SCP 會封鎖所有成員帳戶的所有動作（被排除的角色除外），違反使用者須保留完整部署存取權的需求。它的範圍是整個組織／root，而非僅 production OU，因此無法滿足『只限 production OU』的條件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP never grants permissions; it only sets the maximum permission boundary. An Allow SCP on the development OU does nothing to restrict IAM management, and the requirement targets the production OU, not the development OU, so this step is irrelevant.","why_zh":"SCP 從不授予權限，只設定權限上限。在 development OU 套用 Allow SCP 無法限制 IAM 管理，且需求針對的是 production OU 而非 development OU，因此此步驟與目標無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Attaching the Deny SCP to the workload OU applies the restriction to every account beneath it, which includes both the nested development OU and the production OU. This over-restricts development accounts and violates the 'only the production OU' requirement; the Deny must be attached at the production OU instead.","why_zh":"將 Deny SCP 附加到 workload OU 會將限制套用到其下所有帳戶，包含巢狀的 development OU 與 production OU。這會過度限制 development 帳戶，違反『只限 production OU』的需求；Deny 應改附加在 production OU。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":161,"question_en":"A company hired a penetration tester to simulate an internal security breach. The tester performed port scans on the company's Amazon EC2 instances. The company's security measures did not detect the port scans. The company needs a solution that automatically provides notification when port scans are performed on EC2 instances. The company creates and subscribes to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. What should the company do next to meet the requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司聘请了一名渗透测试人员来模拟内部安全漏洞。该测试人员对公司亚马逊 EC2 实例进行了端口扫 描。公司的安全措施并未检测到这些端口扫描。 该公司需要一种解决方案，当有人对 EC2 实例执行端口扫描时能自动发出通知。该公司创建并订阅了一个 亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。 公司接下来应该怎么做才能满足要求？","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that Amazon GuardDuty is enabled. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for detected EC2 and port scan findings. Connect the alarm to the SNS topic.","B":"Ensure that Amazon Inspector is enabled. Create an Amazon EventBridge event for detected network reachability findings that indicate port scans. Connect the event to the SNS topic.","C":"Ensure that Amazon Inspector is enabled. Create an Amazon EventBridge event for detected CVEs that cause open port vulnerabilities. Connect the event to the SNS topic.","D":"Ensure that AWS CloudTrail is enabled. Create an AWS Lambda function to analyze the CloudTrail logs for unusual amounts of traffic from an IP address range. Connect the Lambda function to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保已启用 Amazon GuardDuty。为检测到的 EC2 和端口扫描发现创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。 将警报连接到 SNS 主题。","B":"确保已启用 Amazon Inspector。为检测到的表明存在端口扫描的网络可达性发现结果创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件。将该事件连接到 SNS 主题。","C":"确保已启用 Amazon Inspector。为导致开放端口漏洞的检测到的 CVE 创建 Amazon EventBridge 事件。 将该事件连接到 SNS 主题。","D":"确保已启用 AWS CloudTrail。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来分析 CloudTrail 日志，查找来自某个 IP 地址 范围的异常流量。将 Lambda 函数连接到 SNS 主题。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Detecting active port scans against EC2 instances is a job for Amazon GuardDuty, which analyzes VPC Flow Logs of real network traffic and has dedicated reconnaissance/impact finding types such as Recon:EC2/Portscan, Recon:EC2/PortProbeUnprotectedPort, and Impact:EC2/PortSweep. Option A is the only choice that uses GuardDuty, the service that actually detects this behavior, and routes the finding to the existing SNS topic for notification. The wording 'CloudWatch alarm' is loose because GuardDuty findings are published to EventBridge (formerly CloudWatch Events), which then delivers to the SNS topic; but A is still the only technically viable option because every other answer relies on a service that cannot detect active port scans. Inspector (B/C) performs static configuration/CVE assessment and explicitly does not send packets, and CloudTrail (D) records API activity rather than packet-level network traffic. Therefore A is correct by both technical merit and elimination.","explanation_zh":"偵測針對 EC2 instances 的主動 port scan 是 Amazon GuardDuty 的工作。GuardDuty 會分析 VPC Flow Logs 中的實際網路流量，並具有專門的偵察／影響類 finding 類型，例如 Recon:EC2/Portscan、Recon:EC2/PortProbeUnprotectedPort 與 Impact:EC2/PortSweep。選項 A 是唯一使用 GuardDuty（真正能偵測此行為的服務）並將 finding 路由到既有 SNS topic 以發出通知的選項。其中『CloudWatch alarm』的措辭較不精確，因為 GuardDuty findings 實際上是發佈到 EventBridge（前身為 CloudWatch Events），再由其傳遞到 SNS topic；但因其他所有選項所依賴的服務都無法偵測主動 port scan，A 仍是唯一技術上可行的答案。Inspector（B/C）執行的是靜態設定／CVE 評估且明確不送出封包，而 CloudTrail（D）記錄的是 API 活動而非封包層級的網路流量。因此 A 在技術正確性與排除法上皆成立。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector Network Reachability analyzes network configurations (security groups, ACLs, IGWs) to identify reachable ports 'without having to install scanners and send packets.' It reports configuration-based reachability, not active port scans performed against the instances by a penetration tester.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 Network Reachability 分析的是網路設定（security groups、ACLs、IGWs）以找出可被存取的 port，且明確是『無需安裝掃描器或送出封包』。它回報的是基於設定的可達性，而非滲透測試人員針對 instance 實際執行的主動 port scan。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector CVE scanning finds known software vulnerabilities and package CVEs, not network reconnaissance activity such as port scans. It does not generate events when an external actor scans ports.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 CVE 掃描尋找的是已知軟體漏洞與套件 CVE，而非像 port scan 這類網路偵察活動。當外部行為者掃描 port 時，它不會產生事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail records AWS API/management-plane activity, not data-plane network traffic. Port scans are packet-level network activity that does not appear in CloudTrail, so a Lambda analyzing CloudTrail logs for 'traffic from an IP range' cannot detect port scans.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API／管理層活動，而非資料層的網路流量。Port scan 屬於封包層級的網路活動，不會出現在 CloudTrail 中，因此用 Lambda 分析 CloudTrail 日誌以偵測『來自某 IP 範圍的流量』無法偵測 port scan。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_data-sources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/v1/userguide/inspector_network-reachability.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":162,"question_en":"A company runs applications in an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. The EKS cluster uses an Application Load Balancer to route traffic to the applications that run in the cluster. A new application that was migrated to the EKS cluster is performing poorly. All the other applications in the EKS cluster maintain appropriate operation. The new application scales out horizontally to the preconfigured maximum number of pods immediately upon deployment, before any user traffic routes to the web application. Which solution will resolve the scaling behavior of the web application in the EKS cluster?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群中运行应用程序。该 EKS 集群使用应用负载 均衡器将流量路由到集群中运行的应用程序。 新迁移到 EKS 集群的应用程序运行状况不佳。EKS 集群中的其他所有应用程序均保持正常运行。新应用 程序在部署后立即水平扩展到预配置的最大 Pod 数量，此时还没有任何用户流量路由到该 Web 应用程序。 哪种解决方案可以解决 EKS 集群中网络应用程序的扩展行为问题？","options_en":{"A":"Implement the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler in the EKS cluster.","B":"Implement the Vertical Pod Autoscaler in the EKS cluster.","C":"Implement the Cluster Autoscaler.","D":"Implement the AWS Load Balancer Controller in the EKS cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 EKS 集群中实现水平 Pod 自动缩放器。","B":"在 EKS 集群中实现垂直 Pod 自动缩放器。","C":"实施集群自动扩展器。","D":"在 EKS 集群中部署 AWS 负载均衡器控制器。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The phrase 'scales out horizontally to the preconfigured maximum number of pods' tells you a Horizontal Pod Autoscaler is already configured for this deployment (it has a min/max replica range). The defect is that it fires to max instantly at idle, before any traffic. HPA scales on CPU utilization expressed as a percentage of each pod's resource request (the EKS HPA walkthrough shows targets like '250%/50%', and replicas increase while the actual percentage exceeds the target). If the migrated application's CPU/memory requests are set too low, even baseline idle consumption (startup, runtime warmup, sidecars) computes to a utilization percentage far above the HPA target, so HPA immediately drives replicas to the maximum. The fix is to right-size the pod resource requests, which is exactly what the Vertical Pod Autoscaler does: per AWS docs it 'automatically adjusts the CPU and memory reservations for your Pods to help right size your applications.' With correct requests, HPA's percentage calculation is accurate and the spurious scale-out stops. AWS best-practice guidance explicitly pairs them: use HPA to control replica count and VPA to adjust per-replica requests and limits. The other apps behave normally because they were already sized correctly, so the fix targets the new app's requests (VPA).","explanation_zh":"「水平擴展到預先設定的最大 Pod 數量」這句話代表此 deployment 已配置了 Horizontal Pod Autoscaler（已設有 min/max replica 範圍）。問題在於它在閒置、尚無流量時就立即衝到最大值。HPA 是以 CPU 使用率（表示為每個 Pod resource request 的百分比）來擴展，EKS 的 HPA 範例會顯示如「250%/50%」的目標值，且只要實際百分比高於目標就會持續增加 replica。若遷移過來的應用程式 CPU/記憶體 requests 設得過低，即使只是閒置時的基礎消耗（啟動、runtime 暖機、sidecar）換算出來的使用率百分比也會遠高於 HPA 目標，於是 HPA 立刻把 replica 推到最大。修正方法是正確調整 Pod 的 resource requests，而這正是 Vertical Pod Autoscaler 的功能：依 AWS 文件，VPA「會自動調整 Pod 的 CPU 與記憶體保留量以協助正確調整應用程式大小」。當 requests 正確後，HPA 的百分比計算就準確，誤觸發的擴展也隨之停止。AWS 最佳實務明確將兩者搭配：用 HPA 控制 replica 數量，用 VPA 調整每個 replica 的 requests 與 limits。其他應用程式運作正常是因為它們本來就已正確配置大小，因此修正方向應針對新應用程式的 requests（即 VPA）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An HPA is already present and is the thing misbehaving (it is what produces the 'preconfigured maximum number of pods' and the immediate scale-out). Implementing HPA does not fix an HPA that is already firing incorrectly; the root cause is mis-sized pod resource requests, which HPA cannot correct.","why_zh":"HPA 已存在，且正是出問題的元件（它造成「預先設定的最大 Pod 數量」與瞬間擴展）。實作 HPA 無法修正一個已在誤觸發的 HPA；根本原因是 Pod resource requests 設定錯誤，而 HPA 本身無法修正這一點。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Cluster Autoscaler adjusts the number of worker nodes (EC2 instances) so unschedulable pods can be placed; it does not control how many pod replicas a deployment runs. The problem here is replica-level (pods scaling to max), not node-level capacity, so Cluster Autoscaler does not address the scaling behavior.","why_zh":"Cluster Autoscaler 調整的是 worker node（EC2 執行個體）數量，以便讓無法排程的 Pod 能被放置；它不控制 deployment 要跑幾個 Pod replica。此處問題在 replica 層級（Pod 擴展到最大值）而非節點容量，因此 Cluster Autoscaler 無法解決此擴展行為。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The AWS Load Balancer Controller provisions and manages the ALB for ingress traffic. The cluster already has a working ALB routing traffic, and the runaway scaling occurs before any user traffic arrives, so it is fully decoupled from the load balancer and unrelated to pod replica scaling.","why_zh":"AWS Load Balancer Controller 負責佈建與管理用於 ingress 流量的 ALB。叢集已有正常運作的 ALB 在路由流量，且失控的擴展發生在任何使用者流量到達之前，因此與負載平衡器完全脫鉤，也與 Pod replica 擴展無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/vertical-pod-autoscaler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/horizontal-pod-autoscaler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/best-practices/cost-opt-compute.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/scaling-amazon-eks-infrastructure/workload-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/autoscaling.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":163,"question_en":"A company has an AWS Control Tower landing zone that manages its organization in AWS Organizations. The company created an OU structure that is based on the company's requirements. The company's DevOps team has established the core accounts for the solution and an account for all centralized AWS CloudFormation and AWS Service Catalog solutions. The company wants to offer a series of customizations that an account can request through AWS Control Tower. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个 AWS 控制塔着陆区，用于管理其在 AWS 组织中的机构。该公司根据自身需求创建了组 织单元（OU）结构。公司的 DevOps 团队为解决方案建立了核心账户，并为所有集中式的 AWS CloudFormation 和 AWS 服务目录解决方案创建了一个账户。 该公司希望提供一系列定制服务，客户可以通过 AWS 控制塔提出请求。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable trusted access for CloudFormation with Organizations by using service-managed permissions.","B":"Create an IAM role that is named AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess. Configure the role with a trust policy that allows the AWSControlTowerAdmin role in the management account to assume the role. Attach the AWSServiceCatalogAdminFullAccess IAM policy to the AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess role.","C":"Create a Service Catalog product for each CloudFormation template.","D":"Create a CloudFormation stack set for each CloudFormation template. Enable automatic deployment for each stack set. Create a CloudFormation stack instance that targets specific OUs.","E":"Deploy the Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) CloudFormation stack.","F":"Create a CloudFormation template that contains the resources for each customization."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过使用服务管理权限，为 CloudFormation 与 Organizations 启用受信任访问。","B":"创建一个名为 AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess 的 IAM 角色。为该角色配置一个信任策略，允许管理 账户中的 AWSControlTowerAdmin 角色承担此角色。将 AWSServiceCatalogAdminFullAccess IAM 策略 附加到 AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess 角色。","C":"为每个 CloudFormation 模板创建一个服务目录产品。","D":"为每个 CloudFormation 模板创建一个 CloudFormation 堆栈集。为每个堆栈集启用自动部署。创建一个 针对特定组织单位的目标 CloudFormation 堆栈实例。","E":"部署 AWS 控制塔自定义配置（CfCT）CloudFormation 堆栈。","F":"创建一个包含每个自定义资源的 CloudFormation 模板。"},"answer":["B","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario describes offering a series of self-service customizations that an account can request through the AWS Control Tower console - this is the Account Factory Customization (AFC) feature, which provisions accounts from AWS Service Catalog products called 'custom blueprints'. The documented one-time setup maps to exactly three steps. (F) Author a CloudFormation template that contains the resources for each customization; this template becomes the account blueprint (the AFC 'Summary of steps to create a blueprint' says to create a CloudFormation template that will become your account blueprint). (C) Create an AWS Service Catalog product from each template - Step 2 of AFC ('Create the AWS Service Catalog product', also called a blueprint product) by uploading the template in the hub account. (B) Step 1 of AFC: create an IAM role named exactly AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess in the hub account, with a trust policy allowing the AWSControlTowerAdmin role in the management account to assume it, and attach the AWSServiceCatalogAdminFullAccess managed policy; Control Tower assumes this role to create the Service Catalog portfolio, add the blueprint product, and share it with the member account during provisioning. The other options describe entirely different mechanisms (CfCT pipeline, StackSets mass deployment, CloudFormation trusted access for service-managed StackSets) that are not the per-account self-service blueprint flow.","explanation_zh":"情境描述的是讓帳戶可以透過 AWS Control Tower 主控台自助請求一系列客製化 - 這正是 Account Factory Customization (AFC) 功能,它使用稱為「custom blueprints」的 AWS Service Catalog 產品來佈建帳戶。官方記載的一次性設定恰好對應三個步驟。(F) 撰寫一個包含每項客製化資源的 CloudFormation 範本,此範本即成為帳戶 blueprint(AFC 的「建立 blueprint 的步驟摘要」說明要建立一個將成為帳戶 blueprint 的 CloudFormation 範本)。(C) 由每個範本建立一個 AWS Service Catalog 產品 - 即 AFC 的 Step 2(「建立 AWS Service Catalog 產品」,又稱 blueprint product),在 hub account 中上傳範本。(B) AFC 的 Step 1:在 hub account 中建立名稱必須為 AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess 的 IAM role,設定信任政策允許 management account 中的 AWSControlTowerAdmin role assume 此角色,並附加 AWSServiceCatalogAdminFullAccess 受管政策;Control Tower 會 assume 此角色以建立 Service Catalog portfolio、加入 blueprint product,並在佈建期間與成員帳戶共享。其餘選項描述的是完全不同的機制(CfCT pipeline、StackSets 大量部署、為 service-managed StackSets 啟用 CloudFormation trusted access),並非逐帳戶自助 blueprint 流程。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Enabling trusted access for CloudFormation with Organizations (service-managed permissions) is required for service-managed StackSets that deploy across the org, not for AFC blueprints. AFC relies on the AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess role plus an AWS Service Catalog product, and does not require enabling CloudFormation trusted access.","why_zh":"為 CloudFormation 與 Organizations 啟用 trusted access(service-managed permissions)是 service-managed StackSets 跨組織部署所需,而非 AFC blueprint 所需。AFC 依賴 AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess role 加上 AWS Service Catalog 產品,不需啟用 CloudFormation trusted access。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a StackSet per template with auto-deployment and stack instances targeting OUs is a push-based mass-deployment mechanism that applies resources to whole OUs automatically. It is not the per-account, on-request self-service model the question requires, which is delivered via Service Catalog blueprints chosen during account creation in Account Factory.","why_zh":"為每個範本建立 StackSet 並啟用自動部署、以 stack instance 鎖定 OU,是一種推送式大量部署機制,會自動將資源套用至整個 OU。這不是題目要求的逐帳戶、依請求的自助模式;後者是在 Account Factory 建立帳戶時透過選擇 Service Catalog blueprint 來提供。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) is a separate solution that uses a CodePipeline-based framework with a manifest file to deploy CloudFormation stacks/SCPs to accounts and OUs after account lifecycle events. It is not the native console-based AFC blueprint flow that lets an account request a customization, and it adds pipeline maintenance the AFC setup explicitly avoids.","why_zh":"Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) 是另一套獨立解決方案,使用以 CodePipeline 為基礎的框架搭配 manifest 檔案,在帳戶生命週期事件後將 CloudFormation stacks/SCP 部署到帳戶與 OU。這不是讓帳戶請求客製化的原生主控台 AFC blueprint 流程,並會增加 AFC 設定明確要避免的 pipeline 維護工作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/afc-setup-steps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/step-1-create-blueprint-access-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/step-2-create-blueprint-product.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/service-catalog.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/methods-of-provisioning.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":164,"question_en":"A company runs a workload on Amazon EC2 instances. The company needs a control that requires the use of Instance Metadata Service Version 2 (IMDSv2) on all EC2 instances in the AWS account. If an EC2 instance does not prevent the use of Instance Metadata Service Version 1 (IMDSv1), the EC2 instance must be terminated. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行工作负载。该公司需要一种控制措施，要求其 AWS 账户中的所有 EC2 实例都必须使用实例元数据服务版本 2（IMDSv2）。如果某个 EC2 实例未禁止使用实例元数据服务版本 1 （IMDSv1），则必须终止该 EC2 实例。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up AWS Config in the account. Use a managed rule to check EC2 instances. Configure the rule to remediate the findings by using AWS Systems Manager Automation to terminate the instance.","B":"Create a permissions boundary that prevents the ec2:RunInstance action if the ec2:MetadataHttpTokens condition key is not set to a value of required. Attach the permissions boundary to the IAM role that was used to launch the instance.","C":"Set up Amazon Inspector in the account. Configure Amazon Inspector to activate deep inspection for EC2 instances. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for an Inspector2 finding. Set an AWS Lambda function as the target to terminate the instance.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for the EC2 instance launch successful event. Send the event to an AWS Lambda function to inspect the EC2 metadata and to terminate the instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"在账户中设置 AWS Config。使用托管规则检查 EC2 实例。配置该规则，通过使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 终止实例来修复发现的问题。","B":"创建一个权限边界，如果 ec2:MetadataHttpTokens 条件键未设置为 required 值，则阻止 ec2: RunInstance 操作。将该权限边界附加到用于启动实例的 IAM 角色上。","C":"在账户中设置 Amazon Inspector。配置 Amazon Inspector 以对 EC2 实例启用深度检查。为 Inspector2 找 到的问题创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将 AWS Lambda 函数设置为目标以终止实例。","D":"为 EC2 实例启动成功的事件创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将该事件发送到一个 AWS Lambda 函 数，以检查 EC2 元数据并终止该实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a detective control across ALL EC2 instances in the account that must terminate any instance still permitting IMDSv1. AWS Config provides the managed rule ec2-imdsv2-check, which evaluates AWS::EC2::Instance resources and marks an instance NON_COMPLIANT when HttpTokens is set to 'optional' (IMDSv1 still allowed). AWS Config auto-remediation associates a Systems Manager Automation document with the rule (via PutRemediationConfigurations) and can pass the non-compliant resource ID; the AWS-managed runbook AWS-TerminateEC2Instance accepts an InstanceId and terminates the instance. This combination satisfies both the 'require IMDSv2 on all instances' detection and the 'terminate the instance' remediation, so A is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是一個涵蓋帳戶中『所有』EC2 執行個體的偵測型控制 (detective control)，並且要終止任何仍允許 IMDSv1 的執行個體。AWS Config 提供受管規則 ec2-imdsv2-check，它會評估 AWS::EC2::Instance 資源，當 HttpTokens 設為 'optional'（即仍允許 IMDSv1）時將執行個體標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。AWS Config 自動修復 (auto-remediation) 會透過 PutRemediationConfigurations 將 Systems Manager Automation 文件關聯到該規則，並可傳入不合規資源的 resource ID；AWS 受管 runbook AWS-TerminateEC2Instance 接受 InstanceId 並終止該執行個體。此組合同時滿足『要求所有執行個體使用 IMDSv2』的偵測與『終止執行個體』的修復需求，因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A permissions boundary using ec2:MetadataHttpTokens on RunInstances is a PREVENTIVE guardrail that blocks launching non-compliant instances; it never terminates an existing instance, so it fails the explicit 'must be terminated' requirement. It also only affects launches made via that one role, not all existing EC2 instances in the account (it references the action as ec2:RunInstance, but the real action is ec2:RunInstances).","why_zh":"在 RunInstances 上使用 ec2:MetadataHttpTokens 的 permissions boundary 屬於『預防型』(preventive) 護欄，會阻擋啟動不合規執行個體，但永遠不會終止既有執行個體，因此無法滿足明確的『必須終止』需求。它也僅影響透過該角色的啟動，而非帳戶中所有既有的 EC2 執行個體（選項寫成 ec2:RunInstance，實際動作為 ec2:RunInstances）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector deep inspection scans EC2 instances for software/package (CVE) vulnerabilities; it does not evaluate IMDS configuration (HttpTokens optional vs required). There is no Inspector2 finding type for IMDSv1 usage, so the EventBridge rule and Lambda termination would never be triggered for this control.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector deep inspection 掃描 EC2 執行個體的軟體/套件 (CVE) 弱點，並不會評估 IMDS 設定（HttpTokens optional 或 required）。沒有針對 IMDSv1 使用的 Inspector2 finding 類型，因此 EventBridge 規則與 Lambda 終止動作永遠不會因此控制被觸發。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EventBridge rule on an instance launch event with a Lambda only inspects newly launched instances at launch time. It does not evaluate ALL existing instances in the account, failing the required scope, and it is a brittle custom build compared with the purpose-built AWS Config managed rule plus SSM remediation that evaluates the entire resource inventory.","why_zh":"在執行個體啟動事件上的 EventBridge 規則加 Lambda，僅在啟動時檢查新啟動的執行個體。它無法評估帳戶中『所有』既有執行個體，不符合需求範圍；相較於專用的 AWS Config 受管規則加 SSM 修復（會評估整個資源清單），這是脆弱的自製方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/ec2-imdsv2-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-terminateec2instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/instance-metadata-transition-to-version-2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/deep-inspection.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":165,"question_en":"A company builds an application that uses an Application Load Balancer in front of Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The application is stateless. The Auto Scaling group uses a custom AMI that is fully prebuilt. The EC2 instances do not have a custom bootstrapping process. The AMI that the Auto Scaling group uses was recently deleted. The Auto Scaling group's scaling activities show failures because the AMI ID does not exist. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司构建了一个应用程序，该程序在 Amazon EC2 实例前使用应用负载均衡器，这些实例位于一个自动 扩展组中。该应用程序是无状态的。自动扩展组使用自定义 AMI。 这是完全预构建好的。EC2 实例没有自定义的引导过程。 自动扩展组使用的 AMI 最近已被删除。由于 AMI ID 不存在，自动扩展组的扩展活动显示失败。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new launch template that uses the new AMI.","B":"Update the Auto Scaling group to use the new launch template.","C":"Reduce the Auto Scaling group's desired capacity to 0.","D":"Increase the Auto Scaling group's desired capacity by 1.","E":"Create a new AMI from a running EC2 instance in the Auto Scaling group.","F":"Create a new AMI by copying the most recent public AMI of the operating system that the EC2 instances use."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个使用新 AMI 的新启动模板。","B":"更新自动扩展组以使用新的启动模板。","C":"将自动扩展组的期望容量减少至 0。","D":"将自动扩展组的期望容量增加 1。","E":"从自动扩展组中的运行中的 EC2 实例创建一个新的 AMI。","F":"通过复制 EC2 实例所使用的操作系统的最新公共 AMI 来创建一个新的 AMI。"},"answer":["A","B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The custom AMI is fully prebuilt and the instances have NO bootstrapping process, so 100% of the customization lives only inside the AMI image. The instances currently running in the Auto Scaling group were launched from the now-deleted AMI, so they are the ONLY surviving copy of that prebuilt configuration. The correct, lossless recovery is: (E) create a new EBS-backed AMI from one of the running instances in the group, which captures the customized root volume exactly; (A) create a new launch template that references the new AMI ID, because a launch template stores the AMI ID and there is no existing template that points at a valid image; and (B) update the Auto Scaling group to use that new launch template so subsequent scaling activities reference a valid AMI and succeed. This restores scaling without losing any custom configuration.","explanation_zh":"此 custom AMI 是完全預先建置的，而且執行個體沒有任何 bootstrapping 流程，因此所有客製化內容只存在於 AMI 映像中。Auto Scaling group 內目前正在執行的執行個體是從現已刪除的 AMI 啟動的，所以它們是該預先建置設定的唯一倖存副本。正確且不遺失資料的復原方式是：(E) 從群組中一個正在執行的執行個體建立新的 EBS-backed AMI，精確擷取已客製化的根磁碟區；(A) 建立新的 launch template 並參照新的 AMI ID，因為 launch template 會儲存 AMI ID，而目前沒有任何指向有效映像的 template；(B) 更新 Auto Scaling group 以使用該新 launch template，使後續的擴展活動參照有效 AMI 並成功。如此可在不遺失任何 custom 設定的情況下恢復擴展功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Reducing desired capacity to 0 would terminate the currently running instances, which are the ONLY remaining source of the prebuilt custom configuration (the AMI is deleted and there is no bootstrapping). This destroys the very data needed to recreate the AMI and would make recovery impossible.","why_zh":"將 desired capacity 降為 0 會終止目前正在執行的執行個體，而這些執行個體是預先建置 custom 設定的唯一剩餘來源（AMI 已刪除且無 bootstrapping）。這會摧毀重建 AMI 所需的資料，使復原無法進行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Increasing desired capacity by 1 only triggers another launch attempt that still references the missing AMI ID, producing the same failure. It does nothing to fix the root cause (the deleted AMI / broken launch template) and is not a required recovery step.","why_zh":"將 desired capacity 增加 1 只會觸發另一次仍參照缺失 AMI ID 的啟動嘗試，造成相同的失敗。它無法解決根本原因（已刪除的 AMI／失效的 launch template），也非必要的復原步驟。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Copying the most recent public OS AMI produces a generic, vanilla image WITHOUT the company's prebuilt application and customizations. Because there is no bootstrapping process to re-apply configuration at launch, instances from this AMI would not run the application correctly.","why_zh":"複製最新的公開 OS AMI 會得到一個通用的原始映像，不含公司預先建置的應用程式與客製化內容。由於沒有 bootstrapping 流程在啟動時重新套用設定，從此 AMI 啟動的執行個體無法正確執行應用程式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/creating-an-ami-ebs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/create-launch-template.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/update-auto-scaling-group.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ts-as-instancelaunchfailure.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":166,"question_en":"A company deploys a web application on Amazon EC2 instances that are behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The company stores the application code in an AWS CodeCommit repository. When code is merged to the main branch, an AWS Lambda function invokes an AWS CodeBuild project. The CodeBuild project packages the code, stores the packaged code in AWS CodeArtifact, and invokes AWS Systems Manager Run Command to deploy the packaged code to the EC2 instances. Previous deployments have resulted in defects, EC2 instances that are not running the latest version of the packaged code, and inconsistencies between instances. Which combination of actions should a DevOps engineer take to implement a more reliable deployment solution? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上部署了一个网络应用程序，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。 该公司将应用程序代码存储在 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中。当代码合并到主分支时，一个 AWS Lambda 函数会调用 AWS CodeBuild 项目。CodeBuild 项目对代码进行打包，将打包后的代码存储在 AWS CodeArtifact 中，并调用 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 将打包后的代码部署到 EC2 实例上。 之前的部署导致了缺陷，EC2 实例未运行打包代码的最新版本，以及各实例之间存在不一致的情况。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪两种行动组合来实现更可靠的部署方案？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline that uses the CodeCommit repository as a source provider. Configure pipeline stages that run the CodeBuild project in parallel to build and test the application. In the pipeline, pass the CodeBuild project output artifact to an AWS CodeDeploy action.","B":"Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline that uses the CodeCommit repository as a source provider. Create separate pipeline stages that run a CodeBuild project to build and then test the application. In the pipeline, pass the CodeBuild project output artifact to an AWS CodeDeploy action.","C":"Create an AWS CodeDeploy application and a deployment group to deploy the packaged code to the EC2 instances. Configure the ALB for the deployment group.","D":"Create individual Lambda functions that use AWS CodeDeploy instead of Systems Manager to run build, test, and deploy actions.","E":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Modify the CodeBuild project to store the packages in the S3 bucket instead of in CodeArtifact. Use deploy actions in CodeDeploy to deploy the artifact to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个管道，将 CodeCommit 存储库用作源提供程序。配置管道阶段，使 CodeBuild 项目并行运行以构建和测试应用程序。在管道中，将 CodeBuild 项目的输出工件传递给 AWS CodeDeploy 操作。","B":"在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个流水线，将 CodeCommit 存储库用作源提供程序。创建单独的流水 线阶段，运行 CodeBuild 项目来构建应用程序，然后对其进行测试。在流水线中，将 CodeBuild 项 目的输出工件传递给 AWS CodeDeploy 操作。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序和一个部署组，将打包的代码部署到 EC2 实例上。为部署组配 置应用负载均衡器（ALB）。","D":"创建单独的 Lambda 函数，使用 AWS CodeDeploy 而不是 Systems Manager 来执行构建、测试和部 署操作。","E":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。修改 CodeBuild 项目，将软件包存储在 S3 存储桶中，而非 CodeArtifact 中。使用 CodeDeploy 中的部署操作将软件包部署到 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The three reported failures map to two root causes: defects reach production because there is no test gate, and instances drift apart / miss the latest revision because SSM Run Command has no deployment orchestration, no per-instance health tracking, no automatic rollback, and no guarantee that every instance receives the same revision. Option B builds a CodePipeline with a CodeCommit source and SEPARATE sequential stages that build and then test the application before passing the output artifact to a CodeDeploy action; the CodeBuild action reference confirms CodeBuild can act as a dedicated Test-category action, so the test stage catches defects before deploy. Option C creates a CodeDeploy application and deployment group and configures the ALB for it; the CodeDeploy docs confirm that EC2/On-Premises in-place deployments perform a controlled rolling update, track application health according to configured rules, support automatic and manual stop/roll back, and integrate with Elastic Load Balancing so the ALB deregisters and re-registers instances to manage traffic during the deployment. Together B and C guarantee every instance ends up on the same latest revision and that bad revisions are caught (test stage) or rolled back. The verdict matches the dump's suggested answer ['B','C'].","explanation_zh":"三個回報的故障對應到兩個根本原因：缺陷流入生產環境是因為沒有測試關卡；而執行個體之間漂移、未取得最新修訂版本，是因為 SSM Run Command 沒有部署編排、沒有逐一執行個體的健康追蹤、沒有自動回滾，也無法保證每個執行個體都收到相同的修訂版本。選項 B 建立以 CodeCommit 為來源的 CodePipeline，並使用「分開且循序」的階段先建置再測試，最後把產出物交給 CodeDeploy 動作；CodeBuild action reference 確認 CodeBuild 可作為專屬的 Test 類別動作，因此測試階段能在部署前攔截缺陷。選項 C 建立 CodeDeploy 應用程式與部署群組並為其設定 ALB；CodeDeploy 文件確認 EC2/On-Premises 就地（in-place）部署會執行受控的滾動更新、依設定規則追蹤應用程式健康狀態、支援自動與手動停止/回滾，並與 Elastic Load Balancing 整合，讓 ALB 在部署期間取消註冊與重新註冊執行個體以管理流量。B 與 C 一起確保每個執行個體最終都執行相同的最新修訂版本，且不良版本能被攔截（測試階段）或回滾。此判定與 dump 建議答案『B』『C』一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Running the build and test CodeBuild projects IN PARALLEL is illogical: tests run against the build output, so they cannot execute before the build completes. Tests must run in a stage that follows the build stage, which is exactly what B specifies.","why_zh":"讓建置與測試的 CodeBuild 專案『平行』執行不合邏輯：測試是針對建置產出物執行的，因此在建置完成前無法執行。測試必須在建置階段之後的階段執行，這正是 B 所描述的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using individual Lambda functions to invoke CodeDeploy for build, test, and deploy keeps the same fragile, hand-rolled Lambda orchestration that caused the original problems. CodeDeploy is a deployment service, not a build or test runner, and CodePipeline is the AWS-native orchestration layer for sequencing these stages.","why_zh":"用個別 Lambda 函式去呼叫 CodeDeploy 來執行建置、測試與部署，仍維持了當初造成問題的脆弱自訂 Lambda 編排。CodeDeploy 是部署服務，並非建置或測試執行器，而 CodePipeline 才是用來排序這些階段的 AWS 原生編排層。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Swapping CodeArtifact for an S3 bucket does not address the root causes (no testing gate and no managed, health-tracked, rollback-capable deployment orchestration). The artifact storage location never caused the defects or instance inconsistency, and E provides no test stage. Although CodeDeploy can pull artifacts from S3, B+C already solve the problem regardless of where the package is stored, so this change is unnecessary.","why_zh":"把 CodeArtifact 換成 S3 儲存貯體並未解決根本原因（沒有測試關卡、缺少受管且具健康追蹤與回滾能力的部署編排）。產出物儲存位置從來不是造成缺陷或執行個體不一致的原因，且 E 也未提供測試階段。雖然 CodeDeploy 可從 S3 取得產出物，但不論套件存放於何處，B+C 已能解決問題，因此此變更並非必要。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-elastic-load-balancing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-create-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodeBuild.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pipeline.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":167,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company's automation account contains a CI/CD pipeline that creates and configures new AWS accounts. The company has a group of internal service teams that provide services to accounts in the organization. The service teams operate out of a set of services accounts. The service teams want to receive an AWS CloudTrail event in their services accounts when the CreateAccount API call creates a new account. How should the company share this CloudTrail event with the service accounts?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司的自动化账户包含一个 CI/ CD 管道，用于创建和配置新的 AWS 账户。 该公司拥有一批内部服务团队，为组织内的账户提供服务。这些服务团队通过一组服务账户开展工作。 服务团队希望在通过 CreateAccount API 调用创建新账户时，在其服务账户中收到 AWS CloudTrail 事件。 公司应如何将此 CloudTrail 事件与服务账户共享？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule in the automation account to send account creation events to the default event bus in the services accounts. Update the default event bus in the services accounts to allow events from the automation account.","B":"Create a custom Amazon EventBridge event bus in the services accounts. Update the custom event bus to allow events from the automation account. Create an EventBridge rule in the services account that directly listens to CloudTrail events from the automation account.","C":"Create a custom Amazon EventBridge event bus in the automation account and the services accounts. Create an EventBridge rule and policy that connects the custom event buses that are in the automation account and the services accounts.","D":"Create a custom Amazon EventBridge event bus in the automation account. Create an EventBridge rule and policy that connects the custom event bus to the default event buses in the services accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"在自动化账户中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，将账户创建事件发送到服务账户中的默认事件 总线。更新服务账户中的默认事件总线，以允许来自自动化账户的事件。","B":"在服务账户中创建一个自定义的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。更新自定义事件总线以允许来自自 动化账户的事件。在服务账户中创建一个 EventBridge 规则，直接监听来自自动化账户的 CloudTrail 事件。","C":"在自动化账户和服务账户中创建自定义的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。创建一个 EventBridge 规则 和策略，将自动化账户和服务账户中的自定义事件总线连接起来。","D":"在自动化账户中创建一个自定义的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。创建一个 EventBridge 规则和策略， 将自定义事件总线连接到服务账户中的默认事件总线。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS docs state that CloudTrail sends 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' events (which is how a CreateAccount call appears) to the DEFAULT EventBridge event bus in the account where the API call occurred (here, the automation account). The canonical cross-account pattern is: on the SENDER (automation) account, create a rule whose target is the receiver account's event bus; on the RECEIVER (services) account, edit the event bus resource-based policy to allow events:PutEvents from the sender account. The docs explicitly note 'The default event bus accepts events from AWS services, other authorized AWS accounts, and PutEvents calls,' and the example cross-account policy grants PutEvents on event-bus/default to the sender account. Option A implements exactly this: an EventBridge rule in the automation account forwards account-creation events to each services account's default event bus, and each services account updates its default bus policy to allow the automation account. No custom bus is required, and the services teams can then write rules on their own default bus to react.","explanation_zh":"AWS 文件指出 CloudTrail 會將 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' 事件 (CreateAccount 呼叫即以此形式呈現) 傳遞到「發生該 API 呼叫之帳戶」(此處為 automation 帳戶) 的「預設」EventBridge event bus。標準的跨帳戶模式是：在「發送端」(automation) 帳戶建立一條 rule，其 target 為接收端帳戶的 event bus；在「接收端」(services) 帳戶編輯 event bus 的 resource-based policy，允許來自發送端帳戶的 events:PutEvents。文件明確說明『default event bus 接受來自 AWS 服務、其他已授權 AWS 帳戶與 PutEvents 呼叫的事件』，且跨帳戶範例 policy 即是在 event-bus/default 上授予發送端帳戶 PutEvents 權限。選項 A 正是如此實作：在 automation 帳戶建立 EventBridge rule，將帳戶建立事件轉發至各 services 帳戶的 default event bus，並由各 services 帳戶更新其 default bus policy 以允許 automation 帳戶。不需要 custom bus，services 團隊接著可在自己的 default bus 上建立 rule 來回應。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A rule cannot directly listen to another account's CloudTrail events. The CreateAccount event lands on the default bus in the account where the API call happened (automation account); the services account must first RECEIVE the forwarded events on its own bus before a rule can match them. This option omits the forwarding rule in the automation account, so events never reach the services account's bus.","why_zh":"rule 無法直接監聽另一個帳戶的 CloudTrail 事件。CreateAccount 事件會落在發生 API 呼叫之帳戶 (automation) 的 default bus 上；services 帳戶必須先在自己的 bus「接收」轉發過來的事件，rule 才能比對。此選項缺少 automation 帳戶端的轉發 rule，事件因此永遠到不了 services 帳戶的 bus。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating custom event buses in both accounts is unnecessary complexity. The CreateAccount CloudTrail event arrives on the automation account's DEFAULT bus, not a custom bus, so a custom bus there receives nothing without an extra forwarding rule. 'A rule and policy that connects' two custom buses is vague and adds hops with no benefit over the standard default-bus forwarding pattern in A.","why_zh":"在兩個帳戶都建立 custom event bus 是不必要的複雜化。CreateAccount 的 CloudTrail 事件會抵達 automation 帳戶的 default bus 而非 custom bus，因此若無額外轉發 rule，該 custom bus 收不到任何東西。『以 rule 與 policy 連接』兩個 custom bus 的說法含糊，且相較選項 A 標準的 default-bus 轉發模式只是徒增環節而無益處。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It introduces a custom bus in the automation account that the CloudTrail event does not flow to (CloudTrail delivers to the default bus), so an extra hop would be needed just to populate that custom bus. It is more complex than Option A while achieving the same result, and the receiver-side permission step is folded into a vague 'policy that connects.'","why_zh":"它在 automation 帳戶引入一個 CloudTrail 事件不會流經的 custom bus (CloudTrail 傳遞至 default bus)，因此光是把事件送進該 custom bus 就需要額外環節。相較選項 A 更複雜卻達成相同結果，且接收端的授權步驟被含糊地塞進『連接的 policy』中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-event-bus-example-policy-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-event-bus-perms.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":168,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building a solution that uses Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queues. The solution also includes an AWS Lambda function and an Amazon DynamoDB table. The Lambda function pulls content from an SQS queue event source and writes the content to the DynamoDB table. The solution must maximize the scalability of Lambda and must prevent successfully processed SQS messages from being processed multiple times. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在构建一个解决方案，该方案使用亚马逊简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）标准队 列。该解决方案还包括一个 AWS Lambda 函数和一个亚马逊 DynamoDB 表。Lambda 函数从 SQS 队列 事件源中提取内容，并将内容写入 DynamoDB 表。 该解决方案必须最大限度地提高 Lambda 的可扩展性，并且必须防止已成功处理的 SQS 消息被多 次处理。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Decrease the batch window to 1 second when configuring the Lambda function's event source mapping.","B":"Decrease the batch size to 1 when configuring the Lambda function's event source mapping.","C":"Include the ReportBatchItemFailures value in the FunctionResponseTypes list in the Lambda function's event source mapping.","D":"Set the queue visibility timeout on the Lambda function's event source mapping to account for invocation throttling of the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"在配置 Lambda 函数的事件源映射时，将批处理窗口缩短至 1 秒。","B":"在配置 Lambda 函数的事件源映射时，将批处理大小减少到 1。","C":"在 Lambda 函数的事件源映射中的 FunctionResponseTypes 列表中包含 ReportBatchItemFailures 值。","D":"将 Lambda 函数事件源映射中的队列可见性超时设置为考虑 Lambda 函数的调用节流情况。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: maximize Lambda scalability AND prevent successfully processed SQS messages from being processed again. By default, when a Lambda invocation errors on any message in a batch, the ENTIRE batch (including messages Lambda already processed successfully) becomes visible in the queue again after the visibility timeout, so those successful messages get reprocessed. Adding ReportBatchItemFailures to the event source mapping's FunctionResponseTypes turns on partial batch responses: the function returns a batchItemFailures list containing only the IDs of the failed messages, so only those reappear while the successful messages are deleted. The AWS docs also state that 'When ReportBatchItemFailures is activated, Lambda doesn't scale down message polling when function invocations fail,' which preserves throughput and scalability. Option C is therefore the only choice that satisfies both requirements simultaneously.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩部分:最大化 Lambda 的可擴展性,以及防止已成功處理的 SQS 訊息被重複處理。預設情況下,當 Lambda 叫用在批次中任一訊息發生錯誤時,整個批次(包括 Lambda 已成功處理的訊息)會在 visibility timeout 後重新變為可見,因此這些成功的訊息會被重複處理。在 event source mapping 的 FunctionResponseTypes 中加入 ReportBatchItemFailures 可啟用 partial batch responses:函式回傳的 batchItemFailures 清單只包含失敗訊息的 ID,因此只有失敗的訊息會重新出現,成功的訊息會被刪除。AWS 文件也指出『當啟用 ReportBatchItemFailures 時,Lambda 在函式叫用失敗時不會縮減訊息輪詢(does not scale down message polling)』,這維持了吞吐量與可擴展性。因此選項 C 是唯一同時滿足兩項需求的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Decreasing the batch window to 1 second only affects how long Lambda waits to gather records before invoking (a latency/batching tuning). It does not stop successfully processed messages in a failed batch from being made visible and reprocessed, nor does it maximize scalability.","why_zh":"將 batch window 降為 1 秒只影響 Lambda 收集記錄後叫用前的等待時間(屬於延遲/批次調校)。它無法阻止失敗批次中已成功處理的訊息重新變為可見並被重複處理,也無法最大化可擴展性。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Setting batch size to 1 means each invocation handles one message, so a failure cannot affect already-successful messages; but it drastically reduces throughput and forces far more invocations and polling per message, directly contradicting the requirement to maximize scalability. It fails the first requirement.","why_zh":"將 batch size 設為 1 代表每次叫用只處理一則訊息,失敗不會影響已成功的訊息;但這會大幅降低吞吐量,並使每則訊息產生更多叫用與輪詢,直接違反『最大化可擴展性』的需求,無法滿足第一項要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Visibility timeout is a property of the SQS queue, not a setting on the Lambda event source mapping, and it only controls how long a message stays hidden after being received. Tuning it for throttling does not prevent successfully processed messages within a failed batch from reappearing and being reprocessed, and it does not improve scalability.","why_zh":"Visibility timeout 是 SQS 佇列的屬性,而非 Lambda event source mapping 上的設定,且它只控制訊息被接收後隱藏多久。為節流(throttling)調整它並無法防止失敗批次中已成功處理的訊息重新出現並被重複處理,也無法提升可擴展性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-errorhandling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_UpdateEventSourceMapping.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":169,"question_en":"A company has a new AWS account that teams will use to deploy various applications. The teams will create many Amazon S3 buckets for application-specific purposes and to store AWS CloudTrail logs. The company has enabled Amazon Macie for the account. A DevOps engineer needs to optimize the Macie costs for the account without compromising the account's functionality. Which solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司新创建了一个 AWS 账户，各团队将使用该账户部署各种应用程序。团队会为特定的应用程序 目的以及存储 AWS CloudTrail 日志创建许多 Amazon S3 存储桶。该公司已为该账户启用 Amazon Macie。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要在不影响账户功能的前提下优化 Macie 的成本。 哪些解决方案能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Exclude S3 buckets that contain CloudTrail logs from automated discovery.","B":"Exclude S3 buckets that have public read access from automated discovery.","C":"Configure scheduled daily discovery jobs for all S3 buckets in the account.","D":"Configure discovery jobs to include S3 objects based on the last modified criterion.","E":"Configure discovery jobs to include S3 objects that are tagged as production only."},"options_zh":{"A":"将包含 CloudTrail 日志的 S3 存储桶排除在自动发现之外。","B":"将具有公共读取访问权限的 S3 存储桶排除在自动发现之外。","C":"为账户中的所有 S3 存储桶配置每日计划的发现任务。","D":"配置发现任务，使其基于“上次修改”标准包含 S3 对象。","E":"配置发现任务，使其仅包含标记为“生产专用”的 S3 对象。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Macie pricing is based partly on the amount of data that Macie analyzes during sensitive data discovery, so cost is optimized by reducing the volume of data inspected without dropping coverage of buckets that could hold sensitive data. (A) The Macie documentation explicitly gives 'AWS CloudTrail event logs' as the canonical example of buckets to exclude from automated sensitive data discovery; CloudTrail logs are structured AWS service logs, not the personal/sensitive data Macie detects, so excluding them cuts analyzed bytes (and cost) while still protecting buckets that matter. (D) Discovery jobs support an S3 object criterion based on the 'Last modified' date, letting Macie analyze only objects created or changed within a window (and periodic jobs already analyze only new or changed objects each run); this directly reduces inspected bytes and cost while still covering all buckets. The wrong choices either increase cost or compromise functionality: B and E skip buckets/objects that could legitimately contain sensitive data, and C runs full daily scans of every bucket, maximizing cost.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Macie 的計費部分取決於敏感資料探索所分析的資料量，因此最佳化成本的方法是減少被檢測的資料量，同時不放棄對可能含有敏感資料之 bucket 的涵蓋。(A) Macie 文件明確以「AWS CloudTrail event logs」作為應從 automated sensitive data discovery 中排除的標準範例；CloudTrail 日誌是結構化的 AWS 服務日誌，並非 Macie 偵測的個人/敏感資料，因此排除它們可減少被分析的位元組（與成本），同時仍保護重要的 bucket。(D) Discovery jobs 支援以「Last modified」日期為基礎的 S3 object criterion，可讓 Macie 僅分析在特定時間範圍內建立或變更的物件（且 periodic jobs 每次執行本就只分析新增或變更的物件）；這直接減少被檢測的位元組與成本，同時仍涵蓋所有 bucket。其餘錯誤選項不是提高成本就是損及功能：B 與 E 會跳過可能合法含有敏感資料的 bucket/物件，而 C 對每個 bucket 進行每日完整掃描，反而使成本最大化。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Public-read access is a security signal, not a cost lever. Excluding public buckets from discovery skips exactly the buckets most likely to expose sensitive data, compromising functionality, and there is no documented per-public-bucket cost benefit.","why_zh":"公開讀取權限是安全訊號而非成本槓桿。把公開 bucket 排除在探索之外，等於略過最可能外洩敏感資料的 bucket，會損及功能，且文件中並無依公開 bucket 計費的成本好處。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This increases cost rather than optimizing it. Running daily discovery jobs on ALL buckets re-inspects huge amounts of data every day (billed per GB) and duplicates what automated discovery already does, the opposite of cost optimization.","why_zh":"這會增加成本而非優化。對所有 bucket 每天執行 discovery jobs 會每天重新檢查大量資料（依 GB 計費），且與 automated discovery 重複，與成本最佳化背道而馳。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Macie object criteria are file name extension, last modified date, prefix, and storage size — there is no object-level tag criterion (tags are a bucket-level criterion). Limiting analysis to production-tagged objects also skips non-production objects/buckets that could still hold sensitive data, compromising functionality.","why_zh":"Macie 的 object criteria 為檔名副檔名、最後修改日期、prefix 與儲存大小，並無物件層級的標籤條件（標籤屬於 bucket 層級條件）。僅分析標記為 production 的物件也會略過仍可能含有敏感資料的非正式環境物件/bucket，損及功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-asdd-account-configure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-jobs-scope.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-jobs-costs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":170,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company recently acquired another company that has standalone AWS accounts. The acquiring company's DevOps team needs to consolidate the administration of the AWS accounts for both companies and retain full administrative control of the accounts. The DevOps team also needs to collect and group findings across all the accounts to implement and maintain a security posture. Which combination of steps should the DevOps team take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司最近收购了另一家拥有独立 AWS 账户的公司。收购 公司的 DevOps 团队需要整合两家公司的 AWS 账户的管理，并保持对这些账户的完全管理控制权。DevOps 团队还需要收集并汇总所有账户中的发现结果，以实施和维护安全态势。 开发运维团队应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Invite the acquired company's AWS accounts to join the organization. Create an SCP that has full administrative privileges. Attach the SCP to the management account.","B":"Invite the acquired company's AWS accounts to join the organization. Create the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role in the invited accounts. Grant permission to the management account to assume the role.","C":"Use AWS Security Hub to collect and group findings across all accounts. Use Security Hub to automatically detect new accounts as the accounts are added to the organization.","D":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to collect and group findings across all accounts. Enable all features for the organization. Designate an account in the organization as the delegated administrator account for Firewall Manager.","E":"Use Amazon Inspector to collect and group findings across all accounts. Designate an account in the organization as the delegated administrator account for Amazon Inspector."},"options_zh":{"A":"邀请被收购公司的 AWS 账户加入组织。创建一个具有完全管理权限的服务控制策略（SCP）。将 该 SCP 附加到管理账户。","B":"邀请被收购公司的 AWS 账户加入组织。在受邀账户中创建 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色。授予管理账户承担该角色的权限。","C":"使用 AWS Security Hub 收集并汇总所有账户中的发现结果。利用 Security Hub 自动检测新账户， 以便在新账户加入组织时能够及时发现。","D":"使用 AWS 防火墙管理器收集并汇总所有账户中的发现结果。为整个组织启用所有功能。在组织中指定 一个账户作为防火墙管理器的委托管理员账户。","E":"使用 Amazon Inspector 收集并汇总所有账户中的发现结果。在组织中指定一个账户作为 Amazon Inspector 的委托管理员账户。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must be met: (1) consolidate administration of the acquired standalone accounts with FULL administrative control, and (2) collect and group security findings across all accounts. Option B is correct: AWS Organizations only auto-creates the OrganizationAccountAccessRole in accounts it CREATES; accounts you INVITE do not automatically get an administrator role. The AWS docs explicitly state you must manually create the role (with the AdministratorAccess managed policy) in the invited accounts and grant the management account permission to assume it via sts:AssumeRole, which yields full administrative control over the acquired accounts. Option C is correct: AWS Security Hub is the purpose-built service to aggregate and group security findings across all member accounts in an organization, and via central configuration / auto-enable it onboards new accounts as they join the organization, directly supporting implementing and maintaining a security posture.","explanation_zh":"本題需同時滿足兩項需求：(1) 整併被收購之獨立帳戶的管理並取得「完整」管理控制權，以及 (2) 跨所有帳戶收集並分組安全 findings。選項 B 正確：AWS Organizations 只會在「由它建立」的成員帳戶中自動建立 OrganizationAccountAccessRole；以「邀請」方式加入的帳戶不會自動取得管理員角色。AWS 文件明確指出，必須在受邀帳戶中手動建立該角色（附加 AdministratorAccess 受管政策），並透過 sts:AssumeRole 授權 management account 來扮演該角色，藉此取得對被收購帳戶的完整管理控制權。選項 C 正確：AWS Security Hub 是專為跨組織所有成員帳戶彙總並分組安全 findings 而設計的服務，並可透過 central configuration / auto-enable 在新帳戶加入組織時自動納管，直接支援建立與維護安全態勢。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SCPs do not GRANT permissions - they only define maximum permission guardrails (boundaries) for member accounts, and a full-access SCP (FullAWSAccess) is already attached by default. Attaching an 'administrative' SCP to the management account accomplishes nothing toward administering the acquired accounts, since the management account is not restricted by SCPs and SCPs cannot confer cross-account admin control.","why_zh":"SCP 不會「授予」權限，僅定義成員帳戶的權限上限（護欄），且預設已附加全存取的 FullAWSAccess SCP。將「管理員」SCP 附加到 management account 對管理被收購帳戶毫無作用，因為 management account 不受 SCP 限制，且 SCP 無法賦予跨帳戶的管理控制權。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Firewall Manager centrally configures and manages firewall protections (AWS WAF, Shield Advanced, VPC security groups, AWS Network Firewall, Route 53 Resolver DNS Firewall) across accounts. It is not a service for collecting and grouping security findings to maintain an overall security posture; that is the role of Security Hub.","why_zh":"AWS Firewall Manager 用於跨帳戶集中設定與管理防火牆保護（AWS WAF、Shield Advanced、VPC security groups、AWS Network Firewall、Route 53 Resolver DNS Firewall），並非用來收集與分組安全 findings 以維護整體安全態勢，後者屬於 Security Hub 的職責。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Amazon Inspector performs automated vulnerability scanning (software CVEs, network reachability, code) for compute workloads. While it supports a delegated administrator for organization-wide scanning, it does not collect and GROUP findings across all security sources to provide a consolidated security posture - it is one finding source that feeds INTO Security Hub. Security Hub is the aggregation/grouping service the question asks for.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 對運算工作負載執行自動化弱點掃描（軟體 CVE、網路可達性、程式碼）。雖然它支援委派管理員進行組織範圍掃描，但它不會跨所有安全來源「收集並分組」findings 以提供整合式安全態勢，它只是匯入 Security Hub 的一個發現來源。題目要求的彙整／分組服務是 Security Hub。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_create-cross-account-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access-cross-account-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/designate-orgs-admin-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/central-configuration-intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/what-is-aws-waf.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":171,"question_en":"A company has an application and a CI/CD pipeline. The CI/CD pipeline consists of an AWS CodePipeline pipeline and an AWS CodeBuild project. The CodeBuild project runs tests against the application as part of the build process and outputs a test report. The company must keep the test reports for 90 days. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款应用程序和一个持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流水线。该 CI/CD 流水线由一个 AWS CodePipeline 流水线和一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目组成。CodeBuild 项目在构建过程中对应用程序进行测试， 并输出测试报告。该公司必须将测试报告保存 90 天。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add a new stage in the CodePipeline pipeline after the stage that contains the CodeBuild project. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the reports. Configure an S3 deploy action type in the new CodePipeline stage with the appropriate path and format for the reports.","B":"Add a report group in the CodeBuild project buildspec file with the appropriate path and format for the reports. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the reports. Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function to copy the reports to the S3 bucket when a build is completed. Create an S3 Lifecycle rule to expire the objects after 90 days.","C":"Add a new stage in the CodePipeline pipeline. Configure a test action type with the appropriate path and format for the reports. Configure the report expiration time to be 90 days in the CodeBuild project buildspec file.","D":"Add a report group in the CodeBuild project buildspec file with the appropriate path and format for the reports. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the reports. Configure the report group as an artifact in the CodeBuild project buildspec file. Configure the S3 bucket as the artifact destination. Set the object expiration to 90 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"在包含 CodeBuild 项目的阶段之后，在 CodePipeline 管道中添加一个新阶段。创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储报告。在新的 CodePipeline 阶段中配置 S3 部署操作类型，并设置报告的适当路径 和格式。","B":"在 CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec 文件中添加一个报告组，指定适当的路径和格式。创建一个 Amazon S3 存 储桶来存储报告。配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在构建完成时调用 AWS Lambda 函数将报告复 制到 S3 存储桶。创建一个 S3 生命周期规则，在 90 天后过期对象。","C":"在 CodePipeline 管道中添加一个新阶段。配置测试操作类型，并设置报告的适当路径和格式。在 CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec 文件中将报告过期时间配置为 90 天。","D":"在 CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec 文件中添加一个报告组，并指定适当的路径和格式。创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储报告。在 CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec 文件中将报告组配置为一个构建工件。将 S3 存储 桶配置为工件的目标位置。设置对象过期时间为 90 天。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A CodeBuild test report expires 30 days after it is created, and this 30-day expiration is NOT configurable. The only AWS-documented way to keep test results longer than 30 days is to export the report group's raw test result data files to an Amazon S3 bucket; exported files do not expire. To then cap retention at 90 days, you must use an S3 Lifecycle rule (the documented S3 mechanism for expiring objects after a set number of days). Option B is a complete, technically valid end-to-end solution: it adds a report group to the buildspec, creates an S3 bucket, uses an EventBridge rule plus a Lambda function to copy the reports to S3 on build completion (CodeBuild emits build state-change events to EventBridge), and applies an S3 Lifecycle rule to expire objects after 90 days. Option D is the closest distractor but is wrong: report-group S3 export is configured via the report group's exportConfig (S3ReportExportConfig) property, not as a buildspec 'artifacts' destination, and 'setting object expiration to 90 days' on S3 requires a Lifecycle rule, which D never specifies.","explanation_zh":"CodeBuild 測試報告會在建立後 30 天到期，且此 30 天到期時間無法設定。AWS 官方文件唯一能讓測試結果保留超過 30 天的方法，是將 report group 的原始測試結果資料檔匯出到 Amazon S3 bucket，匯出的檔案不會到期。若要再把保留期限限制為 90 天，必須使用 S3 Lifecycle rule（文件記載讓物件在指定天數後到期的 S3 機制）。選項 B 是完整且技術上可行的端到端解法：在 buildspec 加入 report group、建立 S3 bucket、用 EventBridge rule 搭配 Lambda 函式在 build 完成時把報告複製到 S3（CodeBuild 會將 build state-change 事件送到 EventBridge），並套用 S3 Lifecycle rule 讓物件在 90 天後到期。選項 D 是最接近的干擾項但錯誤：report group 的 S3 匯出是透過 report group 的 exportConfig（S3ReportExportConfig）屬性設定，而非 buildspec 的 artifacts 目的地；而且在 S3 上「將物件到期設為 90 天」必須靠 Lifecycle rule，而 D 從未提及。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CodePipeline S3 deploy action deploys pipeline output artifacts, not CodeBuild test report-group data, and the option provides no mechanism to enforce 90-day retention. It does nothing to retain reports past the non-configurable 30-day report expiration.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 的 S3 deploy action 是部署 pipeline 的輸出 artifacts，而非 CodeBuild 測試 report group 的資料，且此選項沒有任何強制 90 天保留的機制，無法解決報告在不可設定的 30 天後到期的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no 'report expiration time' setting in the CodeBuild buildspec. Test reports always expire at 30 days and that value cannot be changed, so configuring 90 days in the buildspec is impossible.","why_zh":"CodeBuild buildspec 並沒有「report expiration time」的設定。測試報告固定 30 天到期且無法變更，因此在 buildspec 設定 90 天是不可能的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeBuild report groups are not configured as buildspec 'artifacts'; report S3 export is set via the report group's exportConfig (S3ReportExportConfig) property, while artifacts are a separate build-output concept. Also, 'setting object expiration to 90 days' on S3 requires an S3 Lifecycle rule, which D never specifies, so the retention mechanism is technically invalid.","why_zh":"CodeBuild report group 不能設定為 buildspec 的 artifact；報告的 S3 匯出是透過 report group 的 exportConfig（S3ReportExportConfig）屬性設定，而 artifacts 是另一個 build 輸出概念。此外在 S3 上「將物件到期設為 90 天」必須使用 S3 Lifecycle rule，而 D 並未提及，因此保留機制在技術上無效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/test-reporting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/report-group-export-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/report-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codebuild.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lifecycle-mgmt.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":172,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon API Gateway regional REST API to host its application API. The REST API has a custom domain. The REST API's default endpoint is deactivated. The company's internal teams consume the API. The company wants to use mutual TLS between the API and the internal teams as an additional layer of authentication. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 API 网关的区域 REST API 来托管其应用程序 API。该 REST API 具有自定义域名。 REST API 的默认端点已停用。 该公司内部团队使用该 API。公司希望在 API 与内部团队之间使用双向 TLS 作为额外的身份验证层。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) to create a private certificate authority (CA). Provision a client certificate that is signed by the private CA.","B":"Provision a client certificate that is signed by a public certificate authority (CA). Import the certificate into AWS Certificate Manager (ACM).","C":"Upload the provisioned client certificate to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the API Gateway mutual TLS to use the client certificate that is stored in the S3 bucket as the trust store.","D":"Upload the provisioned client certificate private key to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the API Gateway mutual TLS to use the private key that is stored in the S3 bucket as the trust store.","E":"Upload the root private certificate authority (CA) certificate to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the API Gateway mutual TLS to use the private CA certificate that is stored in the S3 bucket as the trust store."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 证书管理器（ACM）创建一个私有证书颁发机构（CA）。提供一个由私有 CA 签名的客 户端证书。","B":"配置由公共证书颁发机构（CA）签名的客户端证书。将证书导入 AWS 证书管理器（ACM）。","C":"将已配置的客户端证书上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。将 API 网关双向 TLS 配置为使用存储在 S3 存储桶 中的客户端证书作为信任库。","D":"将已配置的客户端证书私钥上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。将 API 网关双向 TLS 配置为使用存储在 S3 存储桶中的私钥作为信任库。","E":"将根私有证书颁发机构 （CA） 证书上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 API 网关双向 TLS 使用存储在 S3 存储桶中的私有 CA 证书作为信任库。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"API Gateway mutual TLS for a REST API requires two distinct artifacts. First, clients must present X.509 client certificates during the TLS handshake, and those certificates must be issued by a certificate authority whose certificate is in the trust store. Option A provides this by provisioning a client certificate signed by a private CA created and managed through AWS Private CA (accessible via ACM), which issues the X.509 certificates the internal teams present. Second, you must build a trust store, a single .pem bundle containing the complete chain of trust (issuing CA up to the root CA), and upload it to an Amazon S3 bucket; the custom domain name is then configured with truststoreUri=s3://bucket/key. Option E provides this by uploading the private CA (root CA) certificate to S3 and configuring it as the trust store. The deciding distinction is that the trust store holds CA certificates (E), never an individual client certificate (C) and never any private key (D), and the client certificate must be issued by a CA whose chain is in that trust store (A).","explanation_zh":"API Gateway 對 REST API 啟用 mutual TLS 需要兩個不同的元件。第一,用戶端在 TLS handshake 時必須出示 X.509 client certificate,而該憑證必須由其 CA 憑證位於 trust store 中的憑證授權單位簽發。Option A 透過 AWS Private CA(可經由 ACM 存取)建立並管理的 private CA 簽發 client certificate,供內部團隊出示使用,符合此需求。第二,你必須建立 trust store,也就是一個包含完整信任鏈(從簽發 CA 一直到 root CA)的單一 .pem 檔,並上傳到 Amazon S3 bucket;接著在 custom domain name 上以 truststoreUri=s3://bucket/key 進行設定。Option E 透過把 private CA(root CA)憑證上傳到 S3 並設定為 trust store,符合此需求。關鍵差異在於:trust store 存放的是 CA 憑證(E),絕不是個別的 client certificate(C),也絕不是任何 private key(D);而 client certificate 必須由其信任鏈位於該 trust store 中的 CA 簽發(A)。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The client certificate is presented directly by the client during the TLS handshake; it is not imported into ACM. ACM holds the server/domain certificate (regionalCertificateArn) and the ownershipVerificationCertificate, not the client certificate. Importing the client cert into ACM plays no role in the mutual TLS client-authentication flow and does nothing to populate the S3 trust store.","why_zh":"Client certificate 是由用戶端在 TLS handshake 時直接出示,並不會匯入 ACM。ACM 存放的是 server/domain 憑證(regionalCertificateArn)與 ownershipVerificationCertificate,而非 client certificate。把 client cert 匯入 ACM 在 mutual TLS 的用戶端驗證流程中沒有作用,也無法填入 S3 trust store。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The trust store must contain CA certificates (the chain of trust from the issuing CA up to the root CA), not an individual client certificate. Uploading the client certificate itself as the trust store does not establish the CA-based validation the scenario requires; API Gateway validates clients by checking the certificate issuer against the CA certs in the trust store.","why_zh":"Trust store 必須包含 CA 憑證(從簽發 CA 一直到 root CA 的信任鏈),而非個別的 client certificate。把 client certificate 本身當作 trust store 上傳,無法建立情境所需的以 CA 為基礎的驗證;API Gateway 是以憑證的簽發者比對 trust store 中的 CA 憑證來驗證用戶端。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A trust store never contains a private key; it is a .pem bundle of public X.509 CA certificates. The client certificate's private key stays with the client (used in the curl --key request) and must never be uploaded to S3 or placed in the trust store.","why_zh":"Trust store 絕不會包含 private key,它是由公開的 X.509 CA 憑證組成的 .pem 檔。Client certificate 的 private key 應留在用戶端(用於 curl --key 請求),絕不可上傳到 S3 或放入 trust store。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/rest-api-mutual-tls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/privateca/latest/userguide/PcaWelcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/privateca/latest/userguide/create-CA.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":173,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory as its identity provider (IdP). The company requires all infrastructure to be defined and deployed by AWS CloudFormation. A DevOps engineer needs to create a fleet of Windows-based Amazon EC2 instances to host an application. The DevOps engineer has created a CloudFormation template that contains an EC2 launch template, IAM role, EC2 security group, and EC2 Auto Scaling group. The DevOps engineer must implement a solution that joins all EC2 instances to the domain of the AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 目录服务中的 Microsoft Active Directory 作为其身份提供商（IdP）。该公司要求所有基 础设施均由 AWS CloudFormation 定义和部署。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要创建一批基于 Windows 的 Amazon EC2 实例来托管一个应用程序。该 DevOps 工程师已创建了一个 CloudFormation 模板，其中包含一个 EC2 启动模板、IAM 角色、EC2 安全组和 EC2 自动扩展组。DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解决方案，将所有 EC2 实例加入到 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 目录的域中。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the CloudFormation template, create an AWS::SSM::Document resource that joins the EC2 instance to the AWS Managed Microsoft AD domain by using the parameters for the existing directory. Update the launch template to include the SSMAssociation property to use the new SSM document. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore and AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess AWS managed policies to the IAM role that the EC2 instances use.","B":"In the CloudFormation template, update the launch template to include specific tags that propagate on launch. Create an AWS::SSM::Association resource to associate the AWS- JoinDirectoryServiceDomain Automation runbook with the EC2 instances that have the specified tags. Define the required parameters to join the AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore and AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess AWS managed policies to the IAM role that the EC2 instances use.","C":"Store the existing AWS Managed Microsoft AD domain connection details in AWS Secrets Manager. In the CloudFormation template, create an AWS::SSM::Association resource to associate the AWS- CreateManagedWindowsInstanceWithApproval Automation runbook with the EC2 Auto Scaling group. Pass the ARNs for the parameters from Secrets Manager to join the domain. Attach the AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess and SecretsManagerReadWrite AWS managed policies to the IAM role that the EC2 instances use.","D":"Store the existing AWS Managed Microsoft AD domain administrator credentials in AWS Secrets Manager. In the CloudFormation template, update the EC2 launch template to include user data. Configure the user data to pull the administrator credentials from Secrets Manager and to join the AWS Managed Microsoft AD domain. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore and SecretsManagerReadWrite AWS managed policies to the IAM role that the EC2 instances use."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFormation 模板中，创建一个 AWS::SSM：：Document 资源，使用现有目录的参数将 EC2 实例加 入到 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 域。更新启动模板以包含 SSMAssociation 属性，以便使用新的 SSM 文 档。将 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 和 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess AWS 管理策略附加到 EC2 实例使用的 IAM 角色。","B":"在 CloudFormation 模板中，更新启动模板以包含在启动时传播的特定标签。创建一个 AWS::SSM:: Association 资源，将 AWS-JoinDirectoryServiceDomain 自动化运行本与具有指定标签的 EC2 实例相关 联。定义加入 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 目录所需的参数。将 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 和 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess AWS 管理策略附加到 EC2 实例使用的 IAM 角色。","C":"将现有的 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 域连接详细信息存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。在 CloudFormation 模板中，创建一个 AWS::SSM：：Association 资源，将 AWS-CreateManagedWindowsInstanceWithAppro val 自动化运行本与 EC2 自动缩放组相关联。将来自 Secrets Manager 的参数的 ARN 传递给域连接。将 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess 和 SecretsManagerReadWrite AWS 管理策略附加到 EC2 实例使用的 IAM 角色。","D":"将现有的 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 域管理员凭证存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。在 CloudFormation 模 板中，更新 EC2 启动模板以包含用户数据。配置用户数据从 Secrets Manager 中提取管理员凭证，并将 实例加入到 AWS 中。 管理 Microsoft AD 域。将 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 和 SecretsManagerReadWrite 这两个 AWS 管理策略附加到 EC2 实例所使用的 IAM 角色上。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The most operationally efficient pattern is an AWS::SSM::Association (a State Manager association) declared in CloudFormation that targets instances by tag and runs an AWS-provided domain-join document, with the documented IAM policies AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore and AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess on the instance role (AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess grants the ds:CreateComputer/DescribeDirectories needed to join the domain). AWS docs for seamless/automated domain join list exactly these two managed policies, which already eliminates C and D (they use SecretsManagerReadWrite and pull credentials manually). State Manager associations are built for dynamic fleets: the AWS::SSM::Association CloudFormation resource explicitly states that for dynamic targets such as an Auto Scaling Group it applies the configuration when new instances are added, and associations can target nodes by tags. So B automatically joins scale-out instances with no custom document and no credential handling. Option A is technically invalid because the SsmAssociations property exists only on AWS::EC2::Instance, not on AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate (LaunchTemplateData has no such property), and it needlessly authors a custom SSM document to recreate AWS's existing domain-join capability. (Note: AWS-JoinDirectoryServiceDomain is strictly a Command document rather than an Automation runbook, but B's mechanism, tag targeting, and IAM policies are all correct, making it the best answer by a wide margin.)","explanation_zh":"最具運維效率的做法是在 CloudFormation 中宣告 AWS::SSM::Association（即 State Manager association），以 tag 為目標並執行 AWS 內建的 domain-join document，同時在 instance role 上掛載文件指定的 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 與 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess 受管政策（AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess 提供加網域所需的 ds:CreateComputer/DescribeDirectories 權限）。AWS 關於 seamless/自動 domain join 的文件正是列出這兩個受管政策，這一點就排除了使用 SecretsManagerReadWrite 並手動拉取憑證的 C 與 D。State Manager association 本就是為動態機群設計：AWS::SSM::Association CloudFormation 資源明確指出，對於 Auto Scaling Group 這類動態目標，會在新 instance 加入群組時套用設定，且 association 可以用 tags 鎖定節點。因此 B 能自動將擴增的 instance 加入網域，不需自訂 document 也不需處理憑證。選項 A 在技術上無效，因為 SsmAssociations 屬性只存在於 AWS::EC2::Instance，而非 AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate（LaunchTemplateData 沒有此屬性），且還用自訂 SSM document 重造 AWS 既有的 domain-join 能力。（註：AWS-JoinDirectoryServiceDomain 嚴格說是 Command document 而非 Automation runbook，但 B 的機制、tag 目標與 IAM 政策皆正確，仍是明顯最佳解。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The SsmAssociations/SSMAssociation property exists only on AWS::EC2::Instance, not on AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate (its LaunchTemplateData has no such property), so updating the launch template this way is invalid. It also authors a custom AWS::SSM::Document to reinvent AWS's existing domain-join capability, which is more work and less suited to a dynamically scaling fleet than a tag-targeted State Manager association. The IAM policies are correct, but the approach is less operationally efficient.","why_zh":"SsmAssociations/SSMAssociation 屬性只存在於 AWS::EC2::Instance，不在 AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate（其 LaunchTemplateData 沒有此屬性），因此以這種方式更新 launch template 無效。它還自行撰寫客製 AWS::SSM::Document 重造 AWS 既有的 domain-join 能力，工作量較大，且對動態擴縮機群不如以 tag 為目標的 State Manager association 合適。IAM 政策雖正確，但整體運維效率較低。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS-CreateManagedWindowsInstanceWithApproval provisions a single new instance behind a manual approval step; it does not join an existing Auto Scaling fleet to the domain and cannot be associated with an Auto Scaling group for domain join. It also attaches SecretsManagerReadWrite (overly broad and unnecessary), omits AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore, and the approval gate reduces operational efficiency.","why_zh":"AWS-CreateManagedWindowsInstanceWithApproval 是在人工審批步驟後佈建單一新 instance；它不會把既有 Auto Scaling 機群加入網域，也無法用於對 Auto Scaling group 做 domain join。它還掛載範圍過大且不必要的 SecretsManagerReadWrite、缺少 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore，且審批關卡降低運維效率。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Pulling domain admin credentials from Secrets Manager via user data to perform a manual domain join is the least operationally efficient and least secure option: it bypasses the AWS managed domain-join mechanism, requires storing/handling privileged credentials, uses SecretsManagerReadWrite (overly broad), and omits the documented AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess.","why_zh":"透過 user data 從 Secrets Manager 取得網域管理員憑證進行手動加網域，是運維效率最低、安全性最差的做法：它繞過 AWS 受管的 domain-join 機制、需儲存與處理特權憑證、使用範圍過大的 SecretsManagerReadWrite，又缺少文件指定的 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/launching_instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/ms_ad_join_instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-ssm-association.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-ec2-launchtemplate-launchtemplatedata.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-ec2-instance-ssmassociation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-about.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":174,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company has a root OU that has a child OU. The root OU has an SCP that allows all actions on all resources. The child OU has an SCP that allows all actions for Amazon DynamoDB and AWS Lambda, and denies all other actions. The company has an AWS account that is named vendor-data in the child OU. A DevOps engineer has an IAM user that is attached to the Administrator Access IAM policy in the vendor-data account. The DevOps engineer attempts to launch an Amazon EC2 instance in the vendor-data account but receives an access denied error. Which change should the DevOps engineer make to launch the EC2 instance in the vendor-data account?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司有一个根组织单元（OU），其下有一个子组 织单元（OU）。根组织单元有一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许对所有资源执行所有操作。子组织单元有一 个服务控制策略，允许对 Amazon DynamoDB 和 AWS Lambda 执行所有操作，并拒绝所有其他操作。 该公司在子组织单位（OU）中有一个名为 vendor-data 的 AWS 账户。一位 DevOps 工程师在 vendor-data 账 户中拥有一个 IAM 用户，该用户已附加了管理员访问权限的 IAM 策略。该 DevOps 工程师尝试在 vendor- data 账户中启动一个 Amazon EC2 实例，但收到了访问被拒绝的错误。 DevOps 工程师应做出哪项更改才能在 vendor-data 账户中启动 EC2 实例？","options_en":{"A":"Attach the AmazonEC2FullAccess IAM policy to the IAM user.","B":"Create a new SCP that allows all actions for Amazon EC2. Attach the SCP to the vendor-data account.","C":"Update the SCP in the child OU to allow all actions for Amazon EC2.","D":"Create a new SCP that allows all actions for Amazon EC2. Attach the SCP to the root OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AmazonEC2FullAccess IAM 策略附加到 IAM 用户。","B":"创建一个新的服务控制策略（SCP），允许对亚马逊 EC2 执行所有操作。将该 SCP 附加到供应商数据账户。","C":"将子组织单位中的 SCP 更新为允许对 Amazon EC2 执行所有操作。","D":"创建一个新的服务控制策略（SCP），允许对亚马逊 EC2 执行所有操作。将该 SCP 附加到根组织单元（OU）。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SCPs are guardrails that set the maximum available permissions; they never grant permissions. For an action to be allowed in a member account, there must be an explicit Allow at EVERY level in the direct path from the root, through each OU, down to the account. The root OU SCP allows all actions (EC2 is permitted there), but the child OU SCP only allows DynamoDB and Lambda and denies everything else, so EC2 is blocked at the child OU level. Because vendor-data sits under the child OU, EC2 is blocked even though the IAM user has AdministratorAccess - AWS docs state explicitly that a permission blocked at any level above the account cannot be used 'even if the account administrator attaches the AdministratorAccess IAM policy with */* permissions to the user.' The fix is to add the missing/explicit Allow for EC2 at the level that is blocking it, i.e., update the child OU SCP to allow EC2 (option C). After that, EC2 is allowed at the root and the child OU, the account inherits the default FullAWSAccess, and the launch succeeds.","explanation_zh":"SCP 是設定「最大可用權限」的護欄（guardrail），本身永遠不會授予權限。要讓某動作在成員帳戶中被允許，必須在從 root 經由每一層 OU 到該帳戶的整條直接路徑上，「每一層」都有明確的 Allow。root OU 的 SCP 允許所有動作（EC2 在該層被允許），但 child OU 的 SCP 只允許 DynamoDB 與 Lambda 並拒絕其他所有動作，所以 EC2 在 child OU 這一層被阻擋。由於 vendor-data 帳戶位於 child OU 之下，即使 IAM user 擁有 AdministratorAccess，EC2 仍被阻擋 — AWS 文件明確指出，若權限在帳戶上方任一層被封鎖，使用者就無法使用，「即使帳戶管理員為該使用者附加具有 */* 權限的 AdministratorAccess IAM 政策也一樣」。正確做法是在「阻擋的那一層」加入 EC2 的明確 Allow，也就是更新 child OU 的 SCP 以允許 EC2 動作（選項 C）。之後 EC2 在 root、child OU 都被允許，帳戶層繼承預設的 FullAWSAccess，啟動 EC2 即可成功。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The IAM user already has AdministratorAccess, which is broader than AmazonEC2FullAccess. The denial is caused by the SCP guardrail, not by insufficient IAM permissions. SCPs cap the maximum permissions, so no amount of IAM permission can grant EC2 when the SCP in the path does not allow it; AWS docs confirm this holds even with AdministratorAccess attached.","why_zh":"該 IAM user 已擁有 AdministratorAccess，範圍比 AmazonEC2FullAccess 還廣。被拒絕的原因是 SCP 護欄，而非 IAM 權限不足。SCP 設定權限上限，因此當路徑上的 SCP 不允許 EC2 時，再多的 IAM 權限也無法授予 EC2；AWS 文件確認即使附加 AdministratorAccess 也是如此。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Attaching an EC2-allow SCP at the vendor-data account level does not help because an Allow is required at EVERY level in the path. The child OU SCP still does not allow EC2 (and explicitly denies all other actions), so EC2 remains blocked above the account.","why_zh":"在 vendor-data 帳戶層級附加允許 EC2 的 SCP 沒有用，因為路徑上「每一層」都必須有 Allow。child OU 的 SCP 仍未允許 EC2（且明確拒絕其他所有動作），所以 EC2 在帳戶上方仍被阻擋。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The root OU SCP already allows all actions, including EC2, so attaching another EC2-allow SCP at the root changes nothing. The blocking level is the child OU, which still does not allow EC2.","why_zh":"root OU 的 SCP 已允許所有動作（含 EC2），因此在 root 再附加一個允許 EC2 的 SCP 毫無作用。阻擋的層級是 child OU，它仍未允許 EC2。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":175,"question_en":"A company's security policies require the use of security hardened AMIs in production environments. A DevOps engineer has used EC2 Image Builder to create a pipeline that builds the AMIs on a recurring schedule. The DevOps engineer needs to update the launch templates of the company's Auto Scaling groups. The Auto Scaling groups must use the newest AMIs during the launch of Amazon EC2 instances. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司的安全政策要求在生产环境中使用经过安全强化的 AMI。一位 DevOps 工程师使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建了一个管道，按照预定的时间表构建 AMI。 DevOps 工程师需要更新公司自动扩展组的启动模板。在启动 Amazon EC2 实例时，自动扩展组必须使用 最新的 AMI。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to receive new AMI events from Image Builder. Target an AWS Systems Manager Run Command document that updates the launch templates of the Auto Scaling groups with the newest AMI ID.","B":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to receive new AMI events from Image Builder. Target an AWS Lambda function that updates the launch templates of the Auto Scaling groups with the newest AMI ID.","C":"Configure the launch template to use a value from AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store for the AMI ID. Configure the Image Builder pipeline to update the Parameter Store value with the newest AMI ID.","D":"Configure the Image Builder distribution settings to update the launch templates with the newest AMI ID. Configure the Auto Scaling groups to use the newest version of the launch template."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以接收来自 Image Builder 的新 AMI 事件。将目标设置为一个 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 文档，该文档会使用最新的 AMI ID 更新 Auto Scaling 组的启动模板。","B":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以接收来自 Image Builder 的新 AMI 事件。将目标指定为一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会使用最新的 AMI ID 更新自动扩展组的启动模板。","C":"将启动模板配置为使用来自 AWS 系统管理器参数存储的 AMI ID 值。将 Image Builder 管道配置为使用最 新的 AMI ID 更新参数存储中的值。","D":"配置 Image Builder 分发设置，以使用最新的 AMI ID 更新启动模板。配置自动扩展组以使用启动模板 的最新版本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST operational efficiency while ensuring newly launched instances always use the newest hardened AMI. Option C points the launch template's ImageId at an SSM Parameter Store reference (resolve:ssm:parameter-name) and has the Image Builder pipeline update that parameter with each new AMI ID. This is a first-class, no-code integration: EC2 Image Builder distribution configurations natively support 'SSM parameter configurations' (ssmParameter) that store the output AMI ID in a Parameter Store parameter during distribution - the docs literally include 'Example: Store the output AMI ID in an SSM parameter'. Because the launch template uses resolve:ssm with no version pinned, EC2 resolves the parameter to its latest value at instance launch time, so the Auto Scaling group always launches the newest AMI. The Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling User Guide states this explicitly: 'With Systems Manager parameters, you can update your Auto Scaling groups to use new AMI IDs without needing to create new launch templates or new versions of launch templates each time an AMI ID changes.' There is no EventBridge rule, no Lambda, no Run Command, no per-build template version churn, and the ASG never needs to be touched. Option D (the dump's suggested answer) is mechanically valid (Image Builder creates a NEW launch template version containing the new AMI), but it generates a new launch template version on every build and binds distribution to specific templates - the exact churn the SSM-parameter approach is documented to avoid - so C is strictly more operationally efficient and is the genuinely correct answer.","explanation_zh":"限定詞是 MOST operational efficiency（最高運維效率），同時確保新啟動的執行個體永遠使用最新的強化 AMI。選項 C 將 launch template 的 ImageId 指向 SSM Parameter Store 參考（resolve:ssm:parameter-name），並由 Image Builder pipeline 在每次產生新 AMI 時更新該參數值。這是原生、零程式碼的整合：EC2 Image Builder distribution configurations 原生支援『SSM parameter configurations』（ssmParameter），可在 distribution 階段將輸出 AMI ID 寫入 Parameter Store 參數（文件中明確列出『Example: Store the output AMI ID in an SSM parameter』）。由於 launch template 使用未指定版本的 resolve:ssm，EC2 會在執行個體啟動時將參數解析為最新值，因此 Auto Scaling group 永遠以最新 AMI 啟動。Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 使用者指南明確指出：『使用 Systems Manager parameters，您可以讓 Auto Scaling groups 採用新的 AMI ID，而無需在每次 AMI ID 變更時建立新的 launch templates 或新的 launch template 版本。』無需 EventBridge 規則、Lambda、Run Command，也不會每次建置產生版本，更不需更動 ASG。選項 D（題庫建議答案）機制上可行（Image Builder 會建立含新 AMI 的『新』launch template 版本），但每次建置都會產生新版本並將 distribution 綁定到特定 template，正是 SSM 參數做法文件所要避免的版本累積；因此 C 在運維效率上嚴格優於 D，是真正正確的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An EventBridge rule plus an SSM Run Command document to rewrite launch templates is heavy, custom automation. Run Command executes commands on managed EC2 instances - it is not the mechanism for editing launch templates, so this requires custom scripting plus event rules and IAM wiring. Far less operationally efficient than C's native SSM parameter, and it still produces new launch template versions.","why_zh":"EventBridge 規則加上 SSM Run Command 文件來改寫 launch templates 屬於繁重的自訂自動化。Run Command 是在受管 EC2 執行個體上執行命令，並非編輯 launch template 的機制，因此需自訂腳本、事件規則與 IAM 設定。相較 C 的原生 SSM 參數運維效率低很多，且仍會產生新的 launch template 版本。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An EventBridge rule targeting a Lambda function that modifies each Auto Scaling group's launch template works, but it requires writing, deploying, and maintaining custom Lambda code plus event rules and IAM permissions, and it creates a new launch template version per build. C achieves the same outcome with native SSM parameter resolution and zero custom code, so it is more operationally efficient.","why_zh":"EventBridge 規則觸發 Lambda 函式去修改每個 Auto Scaling group 的 launch template 雖可行，但需撰寫、部署並維護自訂 Lambda 程式碼、事件規則與 IAM 權限，且每次建置都會產生新的 launch template 版本。C 透過原生 SSM 參數解析即可達成相同結果且無任何自訂程式碼，運維效率更高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Image Builder distribution settings can add the new AMI to a launch template, creating a NEW launch template version, and the ASG can use the latest version. This is mechanically valid but generates per-build version churn and binds the distribution config to specific templates. AWS documents the SSM-parameter approach (C) precisely as the way to update ASGs to new AMIs WITHOUT creating new launch template versions, making C strictly more operationally efficient than D. D is the dump's suggested answer but is not the best choice.","why_zh":"Image Builder distribution settings 可將新 AMI 加入 launch template，建立『新版本』，且 ASG 可使用最新版本。此法機制上可行，但每次建置都會產生版本累積，並將 distribution 設定綁定到特定 template。AWS 文件正是把 SSM 參數做法（C）描述為『無需建立新 launch template 版本』即可讓 ASG 採用新 AMI 的方式，因此 C 在運維效率上嚴格優於 D。D 是題庫建議答案，但並非最佳選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/using-systems-manager-parameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/cr-upd-ami-distribution-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/using-systems-manager-parameter-to-find-AMI.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/dist-using-launch-template.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":176,"question_en":"A company has configured an Amazon S3 event source on an AWS Lambda function. The company needs the Lambda function to run when a new object is created or an existing object is modified in a particular S3 bucket. The Lambda function will use the S3 bucket name and the S3 object key of the incoming event to read the contents of the created or modified S3 object. The Lambda function will parse the contents and save the parsed contents to an Amazon DynamoDB table. The Lambda function's execution role has permissions to read from the S3 bucket and to write to the DynamoDB table. During testing, a DevOps engineer discovers that the Lambda function does not run when objects are added to the S3 bucket or when existing objects are modified. Which solution will resolve this problem?","question_zh":"一家公司已在 AWS Lambda 函数上配置了 Amazon S3 事件源。该公司需要 当在特定的 S3 存储桶中创建新对象或修改现有对象时运行的 Lambda 函数。该 Lambda 函数将使用传 入事件中的 S3 存储桶名称和 S3 对象键来读取所创建或修改的 S3 对象的内容。该 Lambda 函数将解析 内容，并将解析后的内容保存到 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。 Lambda 函数的执行角色具有从 S3 存储桶读取以及向 DynamoDB 表写入的权限。在测试期间，一 位 DevOps 工程师发现，当向 S3 存储桶添加对象或修改现有对象时，Lambda 函数不会运行。 哪种解决方案能解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the memory of the Lambda function to give the function the ability to process large files from the S3 bucket.","B":"Create a resource policy on the Lambda function to grant Amazon S3 the permission to invoke the Lambda function for the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as an OnFailure destination for the Lambda function.","D":"Provision space in the /tmp folder of the Lambda function to give the function the ability to process large files from the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"增加 Lambda 函数的内存，使该函数能够处理来自 S3 存储桶的大文件。","B":"在 Lambda 函数上创建资源策略，授予 Amazon S3 对该 S3 存储桶调用 Lambda 函数的权限。","C":"将一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列配置为 Lambda 函数的 OnFailure 目的地。","D":"在 Lambda 函数的 /tmp 文件夹中预留空间，使该函数能够处理来自 S3 存储桶的大文件。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon S3 invokes a Lambda function asynchronously, but only if the function's resource-based (resource) policy authorizes the S3 service principal to call lambda:InvokeFunction. The official Lambda docs state: 'To invoke your function, Amazon S3 needs permission from the function's resource-based policy. When you configure an Amazon S3 trigger in the Lambda console, the console modifies the resource-based policy... If you configure the notification in Amazon S3, you use the Lambda API to update the policy.' In this scenario the function never runs at all, which is the classic symptom of a missing resource-based policy statement (S3 is silently denied permission to invoke). The execution role mentioned in the question only governs what the function code can do AFTER it is invoked (read S3, write DynamoDB); it does not authorize S3 to invoke the function. The fix is option B: add a resource policy statement (e.g., via lambda add-permission with --principal s3.amazonaws.com, --source-arn the bucket ARN, and --source-account the account ID) granting S3 permission to invoke the function.","explanation_zh":"Amazon S3 會以非同步方式呼叫 (asynchronously invoke) Lambda function，但前提是該 function 的 resource-based policy（資源政策）必須授權 S3 service principal 執行 lambda:InvokeFunction。官方 Lambda 文件明確指出：'To invoke your function, Amazon S3 needs permission from the function's resource-based policy. When you configure an Amazon S3 trigger in the Lambda console, the console modifies the resource-based policy... If you configure the notification in Amazon S3, you use the Lambda API to update the policy.' 本題的徵狀是 function 根本完全沒有被觸發執行，這正是缺少 resource-based policy 陳述式時的典型現象（S3 被默默拒絕呼叫權限）。題目提到的 execution role 只控制 function 程式碼被呼叫之後可以做什麼（讀取 S3、寫入 DynamoDB），並不會授權 S3 去呼叫該 function。正確解法是選項 B：新增一條 resource policy 陳述式（例如使用 lambda add-permission，--principal s3.amazonaws.com、--source-arn 為 bucket ARN、--source-account 為帳號 ID），授權 S3 呼叫該 function。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing memory only affects performance and timeout once the function executes. The symptom is that the function never runs at all, so memory has no effect on invocation.","why_zh":"增加記憶體只在 function 已執行時影響效能或逾時。問題是 function 根本沒被觸發，記憶體與呼叫與否無關。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An OnFailure destination (SQS) only captures the result of asynchronous invocations that actually occurred but failed. If S3 cannot invoke the function in the first place, there is no failed invocation to route to a destination, so this does not resolve the problem.","why_zh":"OnFailure destination（SQS）只會擷取實際發生但失敗的非同步呼叫結果。若 S3 一開始就無法呼叫 function，就沒有失敗的呼叫可路由到 destination，因此無法解決問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Provisioning /tmp ephemeral storage only helps with processing large files after invocation. It does nothing to authorize or trigger the invocation, which is the actual failure.","why_zh":"配置 /tmp 暫時儲存空間只在呼叫後處理大型檔案時有幫助，無法授權或觸發呼叫，而呼叫失敗才是真正的問題所在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/permissions-function-services.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/access-control-resource-based.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":177,"question_en":"A company has deployed a critical application in two AWS Regions. The application uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in both Regions. The company has Amazon Route 53 alias DNS records for both ALBs. The company uses Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller to ensure that the application can fail over between the two Regions. The Route 53 ARC configuration includes a routing control for both Regions. The company uses Route 53 ARC to perform quarterly disaster recovery (DR) tests. During the most recent DR test, a DevOps engineer accidentally turned off both routing controls. The company needs to ensure that at least one routing control is turned on at all times. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已在两个 AWS 区域部署了一个关键应用程序。该应用程序在这两个区域均使用了应用负载 均衡器（ALB）。该公司为这两个 ALB 都设置了 Amazon Route 53 别名 DNS 记录。 该公司使用亚马逊 Route 53 应用程序恢复控制器来确保应用程序能够在两个区域之间进行故障转移。 Route 53 ARC 配置包括针对两个区域的路由控制。该公司使用 Route 53 ARC 每季度进行一次灾难恢 复（DR）测试。 在最近的一次灾难恢复测试中，一名 DevOps 工程师不小心关闭了两个路由控制。公司需要确保 任何时候至少有一个路由控制处于开启状态。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？ 在 Route 53 ARC 中创建一个新的断言安全规则。将该断言安全规则应用于两个路由控制。将规则配置 为 ATLEAST 类型，并设置阈值为 1。","options_en":{"A":"In Route 53 ARC, create a new assertion safety rule. Apply the assertion safety rule to the two routing controls. Configure the rule with the ATLEAST type with a threshold of 1.","B":"In Route 53 ARC, create a new gating safety rule. Apply the assertion safety rule to the two routing controls. Configure the rule with the OR type with a threshold of 1.","C":"In Route 53 ARC, create a new resource set. Configure the resource set with an AWS::Route53::HealthCheck resource type. Specify the ARNs of the two routing controls as the target resource. Create a new readiness check for the resource set.","D":"In Route 53 ARC, create a new resource set. Configure the resource set with an AWS::Route53RecoveryReadiness::DNSTargetResource resource type. Add the domain names of the two Route 53 alias DNS records as the target resource. Create a new readiness check for the resource set."},"options_zh":{"B":"在 Route 53 ARC 中，创建一个新的网关安全规则。将断言安全规则应用于两个路由控制。将规 则配置为“或”类型，并设置阈值为 1。","C":"在 Route 53 ARC 中，创建一个新的资源集。使用 AWS::Route53::HealthCheck 资源类型配置该资源 集。将两个路由控制的 ARN 指定为目标资源。为该资源集创建一个新的就绪检查。","D":"在 Route 53 ARC 中，创建一个新的资源集。使用 AWS::Route53RecoveryReadiness:: DNSTargetResource 资源类型配置该资源集。将两个 Route 53 别名 DNS 记录的域名添加为目标资 源。为该资源集创建一个新的就绪检查。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Route 53 Application Recovery Controller (ARC) safety rules come in two types: assertion rules and gating rules. An assertion rule enforces that the criteria you set is met whenever routing control states change, or the change is rejected. AWS documentation gives this exact scenario as the canonical example: to prevent a fail-open scenario where all routing controls get turned off, you create an assertion rule with type ATLEAST and a threshold of 1, applied to the set of (asserted) routing controls. This guarantees at least one routing control stays On at all times, so the engineer's attempt to turn off both would be blocked. The Create-safety-rule API example shows precisely this: AssertedControls = the two routing control ARNs, RuleConfig = {Threshold: 1, Type: ATLEAST, Inverted: false}. That matches option A exactly.","explanation_zh":"Route 53 Application Recovery Controller (ARC) 的 safety rules 有兩種類型: assertion rules 與 gating rules。Assertion rule 會在 routing control 狀態變更時強制檢查你設定的條件，若不符合就拒絕變更。AWS 官方文件正是以此情境作為標準範例: 為避免 fail-open (全部 routing control 被關閉) 的情況，建立一條 type 為 ATLEAST、threshold 為 1 的 assertion rule，套用到那組 (asserted) routing controls，即可確保任何時刻至少一個 routing control 維持 On。如此一來工程師想同時關閉兩個 routing control 的動作就會被阻擋。Create-safety-rule API 範例正好顯示: AssertedControls = 兩個 routing control 的 ARN，RuleConfig = {Threshold: 1, Type: ATLEAST, Inverted: false}，與選項 A 完全吻合。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Gating rules act as an overall on/off master switch over target routing controls via a separate gating routing control; they do not assert that targets must remain On. The AWS gating-rule example uses OR with threshold 0, not threshold 1, and the option's wording 'Apply the assertion safety rule' inside a gating-rule choice is internally inconsistent.","why_zh":"Gating rules 是透過獨立的 gating routing control 對 target routing controls 施加整體 on/off 開關，並不會強制 target 必須維持 On。AWS gating-rule 範例使用 OR、threshold 0，而非 threshold 1，且該選項在 gating rule 中又寫『套用 assertion safety rule』本身就互相矛盾。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Resource sets and readiness checks belong to ARC's readiness checking feature, which audits whether resources are provisioned and configured to handle failover (quotas, config, capacity). They do not enforce or constrain routing control state changes, so they cannot keep a routing control turned on. Routing control ARNs are also not AWS::Route53::HealthCheck resources.","why_zh":"Resource sets 與 readiness checks 屬於 ARC 的 readiness checking 功能，用來稽核資源是否已備妥可承接 failover (配額、設定、容量)。它們不會強制或限制 routing control 的狀態變更，因此無法讓某個 routing control 保持開啟。Routing control ARN 也不是 AWS::Route53::HealthCheck 資源。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like C, this uses the readiness-check feature (DNSTargetResource resource type), which validates DNS target configuration/readiness rather than governing routing control states. It cannot prevent a DevOps engineer from turning off both routing controls.","why_zh":"與 C 相同，這使用 readiness-check 功能 (DNSTargetResource 資源類型)，僅驗證 DNS target 的設定/就緒程度，而非管控 routing control 狀態，無法阻止工程師同時關閉兩個 routing control。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/r53recovery/latest/dg/routing-control.safety-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/recovery-cluster/latest/api/create-safety-rule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/recovery-cluster/latest/api/safetyrule.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":178,"question_en":"A healthcare services company is concerned about the growing costs of software licensing for an application for monitoring patient wellness. The company wants to create an audit process to ensure that the application is running exclusively on Amazon EC2 Dedicated Hosts. A DevOps engineer must create a workflow to audit the application to ensure compliance. What steps should the engineer take to meet this requirement with the LEAST administrative overhead?","question_zh":"一家医疗保健服务公司对用于监测患者健康状况的应用程序的软件许可费用不断上涨感到担忧。该公 司希望创建一个审计流程以确保 该应用程序仅在亚马逊 EC2 专用主机上运行。一名 DevOps 工程师必须创建一个工作流程来审核该应用程 序，以确保其合规性。 采取哪些步骤 工程师应如何以最低的管理开销来满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager Configuration Compliance. Use calls to the put-compliance-items API action to scan and build a database of noncompliant EC2 instances based on their host placement configuration. Use an Amazon DynamoDB table to store these instance IDs for fast access. Generate a report through Systems Manager by calling the list-compliance-summaries API action.","B":"Use custom Java code running on an EC2 instance. Set up EC2 Auto Scaling for the instance depending on the number of instances to be checked. Send the list of noncompliant EC2 instance IDs to an Amazon SQS queue. Set up another worker instance to process instance IDs from the SQS queue and write them to Amazon DynamoDB. Use an AWS Lambda function to terminate noncompliant instance IDs obtained from the queue, and send them to an Amazon SNS email topic for distribution.","C":"Use AWS Config. Identify all EC2 instances to be audited by enabling Config Recording on all Amazon EC2 resources for the region. Create a custom AWS Config rule that triggers an AWS Lambda function by using the \"config-rule-change -triggered\" blueprint. Modify the Lambda evaluateCompliance() function to verify host placement to return a NON_COMPLIANT result if the instance is not running on an EC2 Dedicated Host. Use the AWS Config report to address noncompliant instances.","D":"Use AWS CloudTrail. Identify all EC2 instances to be audited by analyzing all calls to the EC2 RunCommand API action. Invoke an AWS Lambda function that analyzes the host placement of the instance. Store the EC2 instance ID of noncompliant resources in an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. Generate a report by querying the RDS instance and exporting the query results to a CSV text file."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 配置合规性。通过调用 put-compliance-items API 操作扫描并构建一个基于其 主机放置配置的不合规 EC2 实例数据库。使用 Amazon DynamoDB 表存储这些实例 ID 以实现快速访问。 通过调用 list-compliance-summaries API 操作，利用 Systems Manager 生成报告。","B":"在 EC2 实例上运行自定义 Java 代码。根据要检查的实例数量为该实例设置 EC2 自动扩展。将不符合要 求的 EC2 实例 ID 列表发送到 Amazon SQS 队列。设置另一个工作实例从 SQS 队列处理实例 ID 并将其 写入 Amazon DynamoDB。使用 AWS Lambda 函数终止从队列获取的不符合要求的实例 ID，并将其发 送到 Amazon SNS 电子邮件主题以进行分发。","C":"使用 AWS Config。通过在该区域的所有 Amazon EC2 资源上启用配置记录来识别所有要审核的 EC2 实例。 创建一个自定义的 AWS Config 规则，使用“config-rule-change-triggered”蓝图触发 AWS Lambda 函数。 修改 Lambda 的 evaluateCompliance（） 函数以验证主机放置，如果实例未在 EC2 专用主机上运行，则 返回“不合规”结果。使用 AWS Config 报告来处理不合规的实例。","D":"使用 AWS CloudTrail。通过分析对 EC2 RunCommand API 操作的所有调用，确定所有要审计的 EC2 实例。调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数来分析实例的主机放置情况。将不符合要求的资源的 EC2 实例 ID 存储在 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例中。通过查询 RDS 实例生成报告，并将查询结果导 出为 CSV 文本文件。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a detective audit/compliance workflow to verify EC2 instances run exclusively on Dedicated Hosts, with the LEAST administrative overhead. AWS Config is the purpose-built detective compliance service for this: it natively records the AWS::EC2::Instance resource type (including its placement/tenancy configuration), and you author a custom AWS Config rule backed by a Lambda function (the 'config-rule-change-triggered' blueprint) whose evaluateCompliance() logic inspects host placement and returns NON_COMPLIANT when an instance is not on a Dedicated Host. AWS Config aggregates results into a built-in compliance dashboard/report with no custom data store or polling to build. AWS even ships a managed rule, desired-instance-tenancy (identifier DESIRED_INSTANCE_TENANCY, resource type AWS::EC2::Instance, Configuration-changes trigger), that checks for DEDICATED/HOST tenancy and specific Dedicated Host IDs, confirming Config is the native, low-overhead fit. Option C matches this managed-service, change-triggered, serverless pattern exactly.","explanation_zh":"需求是建立偵測型稽核/合規流程以驗證 EC2 執行個體是否只在 Dedicated Hosts 上運行，且要求最少的管理開銷。AWS Config 正是為此設計的偵測型合規服務：它原生記錄 AWS::EC2::Instance 資源類型（含其 placement/tenancy 設定），你只需建立自訂 AWS Config rule，並以 Lambda 函式（config-rule-change-triggered 範本）實作 evaluateCompliance() 來檢查 host placement，若執行個體不在 Dedicated Host 上即回傳 NON_COMPLIANT。AWS Config 會自動彙整結果成內建合規儀表板/報告，不需自建資料庫或輪詢。事實上 AWS 還提供受管規則 desired-instance-tenancy（識別碼 DESIRED_INSTANCE_TENANCY、資源類型 AWS::EC2::Instance、Configuration changes 觸發），可檢查 DEDICATED/HOST tenancy 與特定 Dedicated Host ID，足見 Config 是原生且低開銷的解法。選項 C 完全符合此受管服務、變更觸發、無伺服器的模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Systems Manager Configuration Compliance tracks only Patch Manager patch compliance, State Manager association compliance, and custom compliance reported by the SSM Agent on managed nodes via put-compliance-items; per the AWS docs it does not inspect EC2 control-plane attributes like host placement/tenancy. You would have to build a custom agent-side scanner and manually plumb data into a separate DynamoDB table, which is far more administrative overhead, and list-compliance-summaries is not a native EC2 host-placement report.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Configuration Compliance 只追蹤 Patch Manager 的 patch 合規、State Manager 關聯合規，以及由 SSM Agent 在受管節點上透過 put-compliance-items 回報的自訂合規；依 AWS 文件，它不會檢查像 host placement/tenancy 這類 EC2 控制平面屬性。你得自建代理端掃描程式並手動把資料寫入額外的 DynamoDB 表，管理開銷大得多，且 list-compliance-summaries 並非原生的 EC2 host placement 報告。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Custom Java code on EC2 with Auto Scaling, SQS, worker instances, DynamoDB, Lambda termination, and SNS is a fully hand-built, high-maintenance pipeline. It also terminates noncompliant instances, which an audit/compliance requirement did not ask for, and represents the maximum administrative overhead, the opposite of the qualifier.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上跑自訂 Java 程式並搭配 Auto Scaling、SQS、worker 執行個體、DynamoDB、Lambda 終止與 SNS，是完全手工打造、維運成本極高的流程。它還會終止不合規執行個體，而稽核/合規需求並未要求此動作，且代表最大的管理開銷，正好與題目限定詞相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail records API events, but auditing host placement by analyzing 'EC2 RunCommand' calls is wrong: there is no such event for instance launches (the launch API is RunInstances, and RunCommand belongs to SSM), and CloudTrail is an event log, not a current-state compliance evaluator. Storing results in RDS for MySQL and exporting CSV manually adds undifferentiated heavy lifting versus Config's built-in compliance reporting.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄 API 事件，但透過分析「EC2 RunCommand」呼叫來稽核 host placement 是錯的：根本沒有這個事件對應執行個體啟動（啟動 API 是 RunInstances，而 RunCommand 屬於 SSM），且 CloudTrail 是事件日誌而非當前狀態的合規評估器。把結果存進 RDS for MySQL 並手動匯出 CSV，相較於 Config 內建的合規報告，增加了大量無差異化的繁重工作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/desired-instance-tenancy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/compliance-about.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":179,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is planning to deploy a Ruby-based application to production. The application needs to interact with an Amazon RDS for MySQL database and should have automatic scaling and high availability. The stored data in the database is critical and should persist regardless of the state of the application stack. The DevOps engineer needs to set up an automated deployment strategy for the application with automatic rollbacks. The solution also must alert the application team when a deployment fails. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师计划将一个基于 Ruby 的应用程序部署到生产环境。该应用程序需要与 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库进行交互，并应具备自动扩展和高可用性。数据库中存储的数据至关重要，无论应用程序堆 栈处于何种状态，这些数据都应得以保留。 DevOps 工程师需要为应用程序设置具有自动回滚功能的自动化部署策略。该解决方案还必须在部 署失败时向应用程序团队发出警报。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application on AWS Elastic Beanstalk. Deploy an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance as part of the Elastic Beanstalk configuration.","B":"Deploy the application on AWS Elastic Beanstalk. Deploy a separate Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance outside of Elastic Beanstalk.","C":"Configure a notification email address that alerts the application team in the AWS Elastic Beanstalk configuration.","D":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to monitor AWS Health events. Use an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as a target to alert the application team.","E":"Use the immutable deployment method to deploy new application versions.","F":"Use the rolling deployment method to deploy new application versions."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 上部署应用程序。作为 Elastic Beanstalk 配置的一部分，部署一个 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例。","B":"在 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 上部署应用程序。在 Elastic Beanstalk 之外单独部署一个 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例。","C":"在 AWS 弹性 Beanstalk 配置中设置一个通知电子邮件地址，以便在出现情况时向应用程序团队发出警 报。","D":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则来监控 AWS Health 事件。使用 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题作为目标，向应用程序团队发出警报。","E":"使用不可变部署方法来部署新的应用程序版本。","F":"使用滚动部署方法来部署新的应用程序版本。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The app needs a Ruby platform with auto scaling and HA (Elastic Beanstalk), an RDS for MySQL whose data persists regardless of the stack, automated deployment with automatic rollback, and failure alerting. B is correct because a separate (external/decoupled) RDS DB instance is independent of the environment lifecycle: AWS docs state you can terminate the environment and keep the database operational, so the critical data persists 'regardless of the state of the application stack.' A is wrong because a coupled RDS instance shares the environment lifecycle. C is correct because Elastic Beanstalk has a native notification feature: you enter an email address and Beanstalk creates an SNS topic that emails you whenever an error occurs or environment/instance health changes (which includes a failed deployment) - the lowest-overhead native alert. E is correct because Immutable is the deployment policy documented as having 'a quick and safe rollback in case the deployment fails'; its failed-deployment rollback process is 'Terminate new instances,' i.e., automatic. F (Rolling) is wrong because its rollback process is 'Manual redeploy,' not automatic. D is wrong: an EventBridge rule on AWS Health events monitors AWS service/account infrastructure health, not application deployment failures, and is redundant given C.","explanation_zh":"需求為 Ruby 平台具自動擴展與高可用（Elastic Beanstalk）、一個資料能不受堆疊狀態影響而保留的 RDS for MySQL、具自動回滾的自動化部署，以及部署失敗通知。B 正確，因為獨立（外部/decoupled）的 RDS DB instance 不受環境生命週期約束：AWS 文件指出你可終止環境並保留資料庫繼續運作，因此關鍵資料能「不論應用堆疊狀態為何」皆保留。A 錯誤，因為 coupled 的 RDS instance 與環境共享生命週期。C 正確，因為 Elastic Beanstalk 內建通知功能：輸入電子郵件後，Beanstalk 會建立 SNS topic，在發生錯誤或環境/執行個體健康變化（含部署失敗）時寄送郵件，是最低營運負擔的原生告警。E 正確，因為 Immutable 是文件中載明「部署失敗時可快速且安全回滾」的部署策略，其失敗回滾流程為「終止新執行個體」，即自動回滾。F（Rolling）錯誤，因為其回滾流程為「手動重新部署」，非自動。D 錯誤：EventBridge 監控 AWS Health events 是針對 AWS 服務/帳戶基礎設施健康，而非應用程式部署失敗，且在有 C 的情況下屬冗餘。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A coupled RDS instance shares the Elastic Beanstalk environment lifecycle, so terminating the environment can destroy the DB; data does not persist regardless of stack state. AWS docs recommend an external/decoupled DB for production.","why_zh":"Coupled 的 RDS instance 與 Elastic Beanstalk 環境共享生命週期，終止環境可能銷毀資料庫，資料無法不受堆疊狀態影響而保留。AWS 文件建議生產環境使用外部/decoupled 資料庫。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EventBridge rules on AWS Health events track AWS service/account infrastructure health, not application deployment success/failure. It is the wrong event source and is redundant given the native email notification in C.","why_zh":"EventBridge 對 AWS Health events 的規則追蹤的是 AWS 服務/帳戶基礎設施健康，而非應用程式部署成功/失敗。事件來源錯誤，且在 C 提供原生郵件通知下屬冗餘。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Rolling deployment's documented rollback process is 'Manual redeploy,' so it does not provide automatic rollback on failure. Immutable (E) provides the automatic, safe rollback the requirement demands.","why_zh":"Rolling 部署在文件中載明的回滾流程為「手動重新部署」，不提供失敗時的自動回滾。Immutable（E）才提供需求所要求的自動且安全的回滾。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.managing.db.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.deploy-existing-version.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.managing.sns.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/environmentmgmt-updates-immutable.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":180,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CodePipeline to deploy an application. According to a new guideline, a member of the company's security team must sign off on any application changes before the changes are deployed into production. The approval must be recorded and retained. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 部署应用程序。根据一项新规定，公司安全团队的一名成员必须在任 何应用程序变更部署到生产环境之前进行审批。该审批必须被记录并保存。 哪种行动组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure CodePipeline to write actions to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","B":"Configure CodePipeline to write actions to an Amazon S3 bucket at the end of each pipeline stage.","C":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail to deliver logs to Amazon S3.","D":"Create a CodePipeline custom action to invoke an AWS Lambda function for approval. Create a policy that gives the security team access to manage CodePipeline custom actions.","E":"Create a CodePipeline manual approval action before the deployment step. Create a policy that grants the security team access to approve manual approval stages."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CodePipeline 配置为将操作写入 Amazon CloudWatch 日志。","B":"配置 CodePipeline，使其在每个管道阶段结束时将操作写入 Amazon S3 存储桶。","C":"创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪以将日志传递到 Amazon S3。","D":"创建一个 CodePipeline 自定义操作以调用 AWS Lambda 函数进行审批。创建一个策略，授予安全团队管 理 CodePipeline 自定义操作的权限。","E":"在部署步骤之前创建一个 CodePipeline 手动审批操作。创建一项策略，授予安全团队批准手动审批阶段的 权限。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The two requirements are (1) a security team member must sign off before a production deployment and (2) the approval must be recorded and retained. Option E satisfies the sign-off: CodePipeline's native manual approval action is added to a stage at the point where you want pipeline execution to stop so that someone with the required IAM permissions can approve or reject; the setup explicitly requires granting IAM approval permissions (the AWSCodePipelineApproverAccess managed policy or a scoped custom policy) to the security team. Option C satisfies the recorded-and-retained requirement: AWS docs state all CodePipeline API actions are logged by CloudTrail, and creating a trail enables continuous delivery of those events to an Amazon S3 bucket for an ongoing, durable record. The approve/reject decision (the PutApprovalResult API call) is therefore captured and retained in S3. Together C and E meet both requirements, confirming the dump's suggested answer.","explanation_zh":"兩項需求是 (1) 部署到生產環境前必須由安全團隊成員簽核，(2) 該簽核必須被記錄並保留。選項 E 滿足簽核需求：CodePipeline 原生的 manual approval action 加在 stage 中希望暫停 pipeline 執行的位置，讓擁有所需 IAM 權限的人核准或拒絕；其設定流程明確要求授予安全團隊 IAM 核准權限（AWSCodePipelineApproverAccess 受管政策或範圍化的自訂政策）。選項 C 滿足記錄與保留需求：AWS 文件指出所有 CodePipeline API 動作都會由 CloudTrail 記錄，而建立 trail 可將這些事件持續遞送到 Amazon S3 bucket，形成持久的記錄。核准/拒絕決定（PutApprovalResult API 呼叫）因此會被捕捉並保留在 S3。C 與 E 一起滿足兩項需求，確認題庫建議答案正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodePipeline has no configuration to 'write actions to CloudWatch Logs.' Pipeline state changes flow to EventBridge, not a logs sink, and this does not capture the approver identity in a durable, retained audit record the way a CloudTrail trail to S3 does.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 沒有「將動作寫入 CloudWatch Logs」的設定。Pipeline 狀態變更是送往 EventBridge，而非日誌儲存，且無法像 CloudTrail trail 寫入 S3 那樣以持久、可保留的稽核記錄捕捉核准者身分。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodePipeline does not write an audit log of actions to S3 at the end of each stage. S3 is used for pipeline artifacts, not action/approval auditing. This is a fabricated feature.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 不會在每個 stage 結束時將動作稽核日誌寫入 S3。S3 用於 pipeline artifacts，而非動作/核准稽核。此為杜撰的功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom actions integrate third-party/custom job workers for build, test, or deploy steps, not approvals. The native manual approval action is the correct sign-off mechanism, and granting access to 'manage CodePipeline custom actions' is not the same as authorizing an approve/reject decision.","why_zh":"Custom actions 用於整合第三方/自訂 job worker 的 build、test 或 deploy 步驟，並非用於核准。原生的 manual approval action 才是正確的簽核機制，而授予「管理 CodePipeline custom actions」的權限不等於授權核准/拒絕決定。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals-iam-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/monitoring-cloudtrail-logs.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":181,"question_en":"A company requires its internal business teams to launch resources through pre-approved AWS CloudFormation templates only. The security team requires automated monitoring when resources drift from their expected state. Which strategy should be used to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司要求其内部业务团队仅通过预先批准的 AWS CloudFormation 模板来部署资源。安全团队要求 在资源偏离预期状态时进行自动监控。 应采用哪种策略来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Allow users to deploy CloudFormation stacks using a CloudFormation service role only. Use CloudFormation drift detection to detect when resources have drifted from their expected state.","B":"Allow users to deploy CloudFormation stacks using a CloudFormation service role only. Use AWS Config rules to detect when resources have drifted from their expected state.","C":"Allow users to deploy CloudFormation stacks using AWS Service Catalog only. Enforce the use of a launch constraint. Use AWS Config rules to detect when resources have drifted from their expected state.","D":"Allow users to deploy CloudFormation stacks using AWS Service Catalog only. Enforce the use of a template constraint. Use Amazon EventBridge notifications to detect when resources have drifted from their expected state."},"options_zh":{"A":"允许用户仅使用 CloudFormation 服务角色部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。使用 CloudFormation 漂移 检测来检测资源是否偏离其预期状态。","B":"允许用户仅使用 CloudFormation 服务角色部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。使用 AWS Config 规则检测资 源是否偏离其预期状态。","C":"允许用户仅通过 AWS 服务目录部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。强制使用启动约束。使用 AWS Config 规 则检测资源是否偏离预期状态。","D":"允许用户仅通过 AWS 服务目录部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。强制使用模板约束。使用 Amazon EventBridge 通知来检测资源是否偏离预期状态。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must both be met: (1) internal teams may launch resources only through pre-approved CloudFormation templates, and (2) automated monitoring of resource drift. AWS Service Catalog is the governance service for distributing pre-approved CloudFormation products. A launch constraint assigns an IAM role that Service Catalog assumes when launching, updating, or terminating the product, so end users do not need their own CloudFormation or resource permissions and therefore can only deploy through the approved products. AWS Config rules continuously and automatically evaluate resource configurations and flag non-compliant (drifted) resources, satisfying the security team's automated-monitoring requirement. Option C combines both correctly.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個必須同時滿足的需求：(1) 內部團隊只能透過預先核准的 CloudFormation 範本啟動資源；(2) 對資源偏移進行自動化監控。AWS Service Catalog 是用於發佈預先核准 CloudFormation 產品的治理服務。launch constraint 會指定一個 IAM 角色，由 Service Catalog 在啟動、更新或終止產品時代為承擔，因此終端使用者不需要自己的 CloudFormation 或資源權限，只能透過核准的產品進行部署。AWS Config rules 會持續且自動地評估資源組態，並標記不合規（偏移）的資源，滿足安全團隊的自動化監控需求。選項 C 正確結合了這兩者。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudFormation service role lets users pass a role to CloudFormation but does not restrict them to pre-approved templates; users can still author and deploy arbitrary templates. CloudFormation drift detection is also not automatic/continuous - it must be triggered manually or on a schedule, so it fails the automated-monitoring requirement.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 服務角色只是讓使用者把角色傳給 CloudFormation，並不會限制他們只能使用預先核准的範本；使用者仍可自行撰寫並部署任意範本。此外 CloudFormation drift detection 不是自動/持續的，必須手動或排程觸發，因此無法滿足自動化監控需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config rules correctly provide automated drift monitoring, but a CloudFormation service role does not enforce pre-approved templates only - it merely supplies permissions to CloudFormation while users can still submit their own templates. Requirement 1 is not met.","why_zh":"AWS Config rules 確實能提供自動化偏移監控，但 CloudFormation 服務角色無法強制只使用預先核准的範本，它只是提供 CloudFormation 所需權限，使用者仍可提交自己的範本，因此未滿足需求 1。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A template constraint only narrows the allowable parameter values within a product (e.g., restricting instance types); it does not control who can deploy or enforce pre-approved-templates-only access - that role belongs to a launch constraint. Also, EventBridge does not detect drift; it only delivers a Drift Detection Status Change event after a drift-detection operation has been run, so it cannot perform automated monitoring on its own.","why_zh":"template constraint 只會縮小產品內可用的參數值（例如限制執行個體類型），並不能控制誰可以部署，也無法強制只使用預先核准範本，那是 launch constraint 的職責。此外 EventBridge 本身不會偵測偏移，它只是在偏移偵測作業執行後傳遞 Drift Detection Status Change 事件，因此無法獨立執行自動化監控。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/constraints-launch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/catalogs_constraints_template-constraints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/event-detail-stack-drift-detection-change.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/detect-drift-stack.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":182,"question_en":"A company has multiple development groups working in a single shared AWS account. The senior manager of the groups wants to be alerted via a third-party API call when the creation of resources approaches the service limits for the account. Which solution will accomplish this with the LEAST amount of development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司有多个开发团队在一个共享的 AWS 账户中工作。这些团队的高级经理希望在账户的服务 资源接近上限时，通过第三方 API 调用收到提醒。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs periodically and targets an AWS Lambda function. Within the Lambda function, evaluate the current state of the AWS environment and compare deployed resource values to resource limits on the account. Notify the senior manager if the account is approaching a service limit.","B":"Deploy an AWS Lambda function that refreshes AWS Trusted Advisor checks, and configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Lambda function periodically. Create another EventBridge rule with an event pattern matching Trusted Advisor events and a target Lambda function. In the target Lambda function, notify the senior manager.","C":"Deploy an AWS Lambda function that refreshes AWS Health Dashboard checks, and configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Lambda function periodically. Create another EventBridge rule with an event pattern matching Health Dashboard events and a target Lambda function. In the target Lambda function, notify the senior manager.","D":"Add an AWS Config custom rule that runs periodically, checks the AWS service limit status, and streams notifications to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Deploy an AWS Lambda function that notifies the senior manager, and subscribe the Lambda function to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个定期运行的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，并将其目标设置为一个 AWS Lambda 函数。在 Lambda 函数中，评估 AWS 环境的当前状态，并将已部署资源的值与账户的服务限制进行比较。如果账户即将 达到服务限制，则通知高级经理。","B":"部署一个 AWS Lambda 函数来刷新 AWS 可信顾问检查，并配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以定期运行 该 Lambda 函数。创建另一个 EventBridge 规则，其事件模式匹配可信顾问事件，并将目标设置为一个 Lambda 函数。在目标 Lambda 函数中，通知高级经理。","C":"部署一个 AWS Lambda 函数来刷新 AWS 健康仪表板检查，并配置一个 创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，定期运行 Lambda 函数。再创建一个 EventBridge 规则，其事件模式 匹配健康仪表板事件，并将目标设置为另一个 Lambda 函数。在该目标 Lambda 函数中，通知高级经理。","D":"添加一个定期运行的 AWS Config 自定义规则，检查 AWS 服务限制状态，并将通知流式传输到 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题。部署一个 AWS Lambda 函数以通知高级经理，并将 该 Lambda 函数订阅到 SNS 主题。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor's 'Service limits' category checks already evaluate account quota utilization and alert at 80% (yellow) and 100% (red) of the limit - precisely 'approaching the service limits.' This means the limit-evaluation logic is built in, so almost no custom code is needed. Trusted Advisor natively emits 'Trusted Advisor Check Item Refresh Notification' events directly to EventBridge (source: aws.trustedadvisor). The solution only needs one Lambda to periodically refresh the checks (a single AWS Support RefreshTrustedAdvisorCheck API call) plus a second EventBridge rule matching the Trusted Advisor event pattern that triggers a small Lambda to make the third-party API call. This is the LEAST development effort because Trusted Advisor performs the resource-vs-limit comparison for you.","explanation_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 的「Service limits」類別檢查已經會評估帳戶配額使用率，並在達到上限的 80%（黃色）與 100%（紅色）時發出警示，正好對應題目所說的「approaching the service limits」。因此上限評估邏輯是內建的，幾乎不需自行撰寫程式。Trusted Advisor 會原生地將「Trusted Advisor Check Item Refresh Notification」事件直接送至 EventBridge（source: aws.trustedadvisor）。此方案只需一個 Lambda 定期刷新檢查（單一 AWS Support RefreshTrustedAdvisorCheck API 呼叫），再加上第二個比對 Trusted Advisor 事件模式的 EventBridge 規則，觸發一個小型 Lambda 進行第三方 API 呼叫。因為由 Trusted Advisor 替你完成資源對配額的比較，所以這是開發工作量最少的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Requires writing and maintaining a large custom Lambda that enumerates every deployed resource across all services and compares each against its limit. This re-implements what Trusted Advisor already provides, making it the MOST development effort, not the least.","why_zh":"需要撰寫並維護龐大的自訂 Lambda，列舉所有服務中已部署的資源並逐一與其上限比較。這等於重新實作 Trusted Advisor 已提供的功能，是開發量最大的選項，而非最少。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Health Dashboard surfaces operational events and scheduled changes affecting your resources; it does not track service-limit/quota utilization or alert when usage approaches limits. It is the wrong service for monitoring quota thresholds.","why_zh":"AWS Health Dashboard 呈現影響資源的營運事件與排程變更，並不追蹤服務上限/配額使用率，也不會在用量接近上限時發出警示。對於監控配額門檻而言是錯誤的服務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config has no native service-limit/quota check; a custom rule would still need custom Lambda code to query quota usage (comparable effort to option A). The description of a Config custom rule that itself 'streams notifications to an SNS topic' also misrepresents how Config rule evaluations work, so it is neither lower-effort nor accurate.","why_zh":"AWS Config 沒有原生的服務上限/配額檢查；自訂規則仍需自訂 Lambda 程式碼查詢配額使用量（工作量與選項 A 相當）。所謂 Config 自訂規則本身會「將通知串流至 SNS 主題」的描述也誤解了 Config 規則評估的運作方式，因此既非工作量較少也不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/user/service-limits.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-trustedadvisor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/user/trustedadvisor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/user/trusted-advisor-check-reference.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":183,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is setting up a container-based architecture. The engineer has decided to use AWS CloudFormation to automatically provision an Amazon ECS cluster and an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group to launch the EC2 container instances. After successfully creating the CloudFormation stack, the engineer noticed that, even though the ECS cluster and the EC2 instances were created successfully and the stack finished the creation, the EC2 instances were associating with a different cluster. How should the DevOps engineer update the CloudFormation template to resolve this issue?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在搭建基于容器的架构。该工程师决定使用 AWS CloudFormation 自动配置一个 Amazon ECS 集群和一个 Amazon EC2 自动扩展组来启动 EC2 容器实例。在成功创建 CloudFormation 堆栈 后，工程师注意到，尽管 ECS 集群和 EC2 实例都已成功创建且堆栈已完成创建，但 EC2 实例却关联到了 另一个集群。 DevOps 工程师应如何更新 CloudFormation 模板以解决此问题？ AECS::Cluster 资源中引用 EC2 实例，并在 AWS::ECS::Service 资源中引用 ECS 集群。 BAutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration 资源的 UserData 属性中引用 ECS 集群。","options_en":{"A":"Reference the EC2 instances in the AWS::ECS::Cluster resource and reference the ECS cluster in the AWS::ECS::Service resource.","B":"Reference the ECS cluster in the AWS::AutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration resource of the UserData property.","C":"Reference the ECS cluster in the AWS::EC2::Instance resource of the UserData property.","D":"Reference the ECS cluster in the AWS::CloudFormation::CustomResource resource to trigger an AWS Lambda function that registers the EC2 instances with the appropriate ECS cluster."},"options_zh":{"C":"在 UserDataEC2::Instance 资源中引用 ECS 集群。 DCloudFormation::CustomResource 资源中引用 ECS 集群，以触发一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 EC2 实例注册 到相应的 ECS 集群中。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An ECS EC2 container instance decides which cluster to join based on the ECS_CLUSTER agent variable in /etc/ecs/ecs.config, which is read when the Amazon ECS container agent starts. AWS documentation states explicitly: 'By default, your container instance launches into your default cluster. To launch into a non-default cluster... paste the following script into the User data field... echo ECS_CLUSTER=your_cluster_name >> /etc/ecs/ecs.config'. This exactly matches the symptom: the instances registered with a different cluster (the 'default' cluster) because ECS_CLUSTER was never written via user data, yet the stack still finished successfully because no resource failed. Because the instances are launched by an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group, the user data is defined in the AWS::AutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration resource's UserData property (the ASG launches the instances itself; there is no standalone AWS::EC2::Instance resource). Therefore option B is the correct fix.","explanation_zh":"ECS 上的 EC2 container instance 是依據 /etc/ecs/ecs.config 中的 ECS_CLUSTER agent 變數來決定要加入哪個 cluster，該檔案會在 Amazon ECS container agent 啟動時被讀取。AWS 文件明確指出：預設情況下 container instance 會加入 default cluster；若要加入非 default 的 cluster，必須在 User data 中寫入 echo ECS_CLUSTER=your_cluster_name >> /etc/ecs/ecs.config。這完全符合題目描述的症狀：因為從未透過 user data 設定 ECS_CLUSTER，instances 註冊到了另一個 cluster（也就是 default cluster），而 stack 仍然建立成功，因為沒有任何資源失敗。由於 instances 是由 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group 啟動，user data 應定義在 AWS::AutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration 資源的 UserData 屬性中（ASG 自行啟動 instances，並沒有獨立的 AWS::EC2::Instance 資源）。因此選項 B 是正確的修正方式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The AWS::ECS::Cluster resource does not reference EC2 instances, and AWS::ECS::Service governs task placement, not container instance cluster registration. Cluster membership is determined by the agent's ECS_CLUSTER variable in user data, so this does not fix the wrong-cluster association.","why_zh":"AWS::ECS::Cluster 資源不會參照 EC2 執行個體，AWS::ECS::Service 管理的是任務放置，而非容器執行個體的 cluster 註冊。Cluster 成員資格由 user data 中代理程式的 ECS_CLUSTER 變數決定，因此無法解決註冊到錯誤 cluster 的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The mechanism (set ECS_CLUSTER in UserData) is correct, but the resource is wrong. Instances launched by an Auto Scaling group are configured through AWS::AutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration (or a launch template), not through a standalone AWS::EC2::Instance resource, which is not part of this architecture.","why_zh":"機制（在 UserData 設定 ECS_CLUSTER）是正確的，但資源用錯了。由 Auto Scaling group 啟動的執行個體是透過 AWS::AutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration（或 launch template）設定，而非透過此架構中並不存在的獨立 AWS::EC2::Instance 資源。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A custom resource with a Lambda function to register instances is unnecessary and overly complex. ECS instances self-register at boot when ECS_CLUSTER is set in user data; there is no need for an out-of-band Lambda registration step, and a custom resource runs once at stack create, not per instance launched by the ASG over time.","why_zh":"使用自訂資源搭配 Lambda 函數來註冊執行個體是不必要且過度複雜的。當 user data 設定了 ECS_CLUSTER 時，ECS 執行個體會在開機時自我註冊；不需要額外的 Lambda 註冊步驟，而且自訂資源只在 stack 建立時執行一次，無法涵蓋 ASG 後續啟動的每一台執行個體。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/bootstrap_container_instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/launch_container_instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/ecs-agent-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-autoscaling-launchconfiguration.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":184,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is implementing governance controls for a company that requires its infrastructure to be housed within the United States. The engineer must restrict which AWS Regions can be used, and ensure an alert is sent as soon as possible if any activity outside the governance policy takes place. The controls should be automatically enabled on any new Region outside the United States (US). Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一家要求其基础设施必须部署在美国境内的公司实施治理控制措施。该工程师 必须限制可使用的 AWS 区域，并确保一旦出现任何违反治理策略的活动，能尽快发出警报。对于任何新 启用的位于美国境外的区域，这些控制措施应自动生效。 哪种行动组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Organizations SCP that denies access to all non-global services in non-US Regions. Attach the policy to the root of the organization.","B":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and enable it for all Regions. Use a CloudWatch Logs metric filter to send an alert on any service activity in non-US Regions.","C":"Use an AWS Lambda function that checks for AWS service activity and deploy it to all Regions. Write an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs the Lambda function every hour, sending an alert if activity is found in a non-US Region.","D":"Use an AWS Lambda function to query Amazon Inspector to look for service activity in non-US Regions and send alerts if any activity is found.","E":"Write an SCP using the aws:RequestedRegion condition key limiting access to US Regions. Apply the policy to all users, groups, and roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Organizations 服务控制策略（SCP），拒绝在非美国区域访问所有非全球服务。将该策 略附加到组织的根节点。","B":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，并在所有区域启用。使用 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，在非美国区域的任何服务活动时发送警报。","C":"使用一个检查 AWS 服务活动的 AWS Lambda 函数，并将其部署到所有区域。编写一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每小时运行一次该 Lambda 函数，如果在非美国区域发现活动，则发送警报。","D":"使用 AWS Lambda 函数查询 Amazon Inspector，查找非美国区域的服务活动，如果发现任何活动则发送警 报。","E":"使用 aws:RequestedRegion 条件键编写一个 SCP，限制对美国区域的访问。将该策略应用于所有用户、组 和角色。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: (1) restrict usage to US Regions in a way that automatically covers any NEW non-US Region, and (2) alert as soon as possible on out-of-policy activity. Option E is the AWS-documented mechanism: an SCP using the aws:RequestedRegion condition key as an allow-list (Deny when aws:RequestedRegion is not one of the approved US Regions). Because it is an allow-list of permitted Regions, it inherently and automatically blocks any future/new non-US Region without any modification, exactly matching 'automatically enabled on any new Region outside the US.' This is the same pattern AWS Control Tower uses for its Region deny control. Option B provides the near-real-time alert: a multi-Region CloudTrail trail sends events to CloudWatch Logs, and CloudWatch Logs metric filters + alarms fire on activity in non-US Regions; per AWS docs a multi-Region trail captures all enabled Regions and automatically creates a copy in any newly enabled (opt-in) Region, so coverage extends to new Regions. Option A is the dump-suggested distractor: framing the SCP as denying 'non-US Regions' implies enumerating non-US Regions, which does NOT automatically cover newly added non-US Regions and is not the aws:RequestedRegion allow-list pattern. Note E's phrase 'apply to all users, groups, and roles' is imprecise (SCPs attach to root/OUs/accounts), but E is still the technically correct region-restriction mechanism, whereas A fails the auto-new-Region requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩部分：(1) 限制只能使用美國 Region，且必須自動涵蓋任何新增的非美國 Region；(2) 對違反政策的活動盡快發出警示。選項 E 是 AWS 官方文件記載的機制：使用 aws:RequestedRegion 條件鍵作為允許清單的 SCP（當 aws:RequestedRegion 不屬於核准的美國 Region 時 Deny）。因為它是允許清單，會自動封鎖任何未來新增的非美國 Region，完全符合「對任何新增的非美國 Region 自動生效」。這正是 AWS Control Tower 的 Region deny control 所用的模式。選項 B 提供近即時警示：多區域 CloudTrail trail 將事件送到 CloudWatch Logs，再用 CloudWatch Logs metric filter + alarm 對非美國 Region 的活動觸發警示；依官方文件，多區域 trail 涵蓋所有已啟用 Region，並會在任何新啟用（opt-in）的 Region 自動建立副本，因此涵蓋新 Region。選項 A 是 dump 建議的誘答：把 SCP 描述為拒絕「非美國 Region」暗示要逐一列舉非美國 Region，無法自動涵蓋新增的非美國 Region，也不是 aws:RequestedRegion 允許清單模式。注意 E 的「apply to all users, groups, and roles」措辭不精確（SCP 是附加到 root/OU/account），但 E 仍是技術上正確的 Region 限制機制，而 A 無法滿足自動涵蓋新 Region 的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Denying access to 'non-US Regions' implies maintaining an explicit list of non-US Regions; that approach does not automatically cover any NEW non-US Region (the stated requirement). The correct, auto-covering pattern is an aws:RequestedRegion allow-list of US Regions (option E), not a deny-list of non-US Regions.","why_zh":"拒絕「非美國 Region」暗示需維護明確的非美國 Region 清單；此法無法自動涵蓋新增的非美國 Region（本題要求）。正確且能自動涵蓋的模式是用 aws:RequestedRegion 列出允許的美國 Region（選項 E），而非列舉非美國 Region 的拒絕清單。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Lambda + EventBridge schedule running every hour is polling, not event-driven; an hourly cron does not meet 'alert as soon as possible.' It also requires deploying and maintaining Lambda in every Region, which is high operational overhead and does not auto-extend to new Regions.","why_zh":"Lambda + EventBridge 每小時排程屬於輪詢而非事件驅動；每小時一次無法達到「盡快警示」。且需在每個 Region 部署與維護 Lambda，營運負擔高，亦無法自動延伸到新 Region。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability/assessment service for workloads (EC2, ECR, Lambda); it does not track or report cross-Region AWS service/API activity. It is the wrong service for detecting governance violations by Region.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是針對工作負載（EC2、ECR、Lambda）的弱點/評估服務，不會追蹤或回報跨 Region 的 AWS 服務/API 活動。用它偵測各 Region 的治理違規屬於服務選用錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/primary-region-deny-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/monitor-cloudtrail-log-files-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-multi-region-trails.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateMetricFilterProcedure.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":185,"question_en":"A company sells products through an ecommerce web application. The company wants a dashboard that shows a pie chart of product transaction details. The company wants to integrate the dashboard with the company's existing Amazon CloudWatch dashboards. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司通过电子商务网络应用程序销售产品。该公司希望有一个仪表板，能够展示产品交易详情的饼图。 该公司还希望将此仪表板与公司现有的亚马逊 CloudWatch 仪表板集成。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the ecommerce application to emit a JSON object to a CloudWatch log group for each processed transaction. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the log group and to visualize the results in a pie chart format. Attach the results to the desired CloudWatch dashboard.","B":"Update the ecommerce application to emit a JSON object to an Amazon S3 bucket for each processed transaction. Use Amazon Athena to query the S3 bucket and to visualize the results in a pie chart format. Export the results from Athena. Attach the results to the desired CloudWatch dashboard.","C":"Update the ecommerce application to use AWS X-Ray for instrumentation. Create a new X-Ray subsegment. Add an annotation for each processed transaction. Use X-Ray traces to query the data and to visualize the results in a pie chart format. Attach the results to the desired CloudWatch dashboard.","D":"Update the ecommerce application to emit a JSON object to a CloudWatch log group for each processed transaction. Create an AWS Lambda function to aggregate and write the results to Amazon DynamoDB. Create a Lambda subscription filter for the log file. Attach the results to the desired CloudWatch dashboard."},"options_zh":{"A":"将电子商务应用程序更新为针对每笔处理完成的交易向 CloudWatch 日志组发送一个 JSON 对象。 使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询该日志组，并以饼图格式可视化结果。将结果附加到所需的 CloudWatch 仪表板。","B":"更新电子商务应用程序，使其为每笔处理完成的交易向 Amazon S3 存储桶发送一个 JSON 对象。使用 Amazon Athena 查询 S3 存储桶，并将结果以饼图格式可视化。从 Athena 导出结果。将结果附加到所需 的 CloudWatch 仪表板。","C":"将电子商务应用程序更新为使用 AWS X-Ray 进行检测。创建一个新的 X-Ray 子段。为每笔处理的交 易添加注释。使用 X-Ray 跟踪来查询数据，并以饼图格式可视化结果。将结果附加到所需的 CloudWatch 仪表板。","D":"更新电子商务应用程序，使其为每笔处理完成的交易向 CloudWatch 日志组发送一个 JSON 对象。创建一 个 AWS Lambda 函数来聚合结果并将其写入 Amazon DynamoDB。为日志文件创建一个 Lambda 订阅 筛选器。将结果附加到所需的 CloudWatch 仪表板。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights natively satisfies every requirement with the least operational effort. The application emits one JSON object per transaction to a log group; Logs Insights automatically discovers JSON fields, and a query that uses stats with an aggregation function (optionally grouped with bin()) can be rendered as a pie chart. AWS docs explicitly state that such results can be viewed as 'a line graph, stacked area graph, pie chart, or bar chart.' Logs Insights also has a built-in 'Add to dashboard' action that attaches the query and the chosen widget type directly to an existing CloudWatch dashboard, and the docs confirm these dashboard queries 'run every time you load the dashboard and every time that the dashboard refreshes' - so the pie chart stays live with no manual export. No extra services, ETL, or custom code are required, which makes this the MOST operationally efficient option.","explanation_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 原生即可滿足所有需求，且維運負擔最低。應用程式每筆交易輸出一個 JSON 物件到 log group；Logs Insights 會自動探索 JSON 欄位，使用 stats 聚合函數（可搭配 bin() 分組）的查詢即可呈現為圓餅圖。AWS 文件明確指出此類結果可以檢視為「折線圖、堆疊面積圖、圓餅圖或長條圖」。Logs Insights 也內建「Add to dashboard」動作，可將查詢與選定的 widget 類型直接掛到既有的 CloudWatch dashboard；文件確認這些 dashboard 查詢「每次載入 dashboard 與每次 dashboard 刷新時都會重新執行」，因此圓餅圖會即時更新且無需手動匯出。不需額外服務、ETL 或自訂程式，因此這是維運效率最高的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Athena over S3 can query the data, but Athena does not render native pie charts and its results cannot be attached directly to a CloudWatch dashboard. The option itself admits you must export the results and then attach them manually, which is extra manual ETL and produces a static, non-refreshing artifact rather than a live dashboard widget.","why_zh":"用 Athena 查詢 S3 可以取得資料，但 Athena 不會產生原生圓餅圖，其結果也無法直接掛到 CloudWatch dashboard。此選項本身就承認必須匯出結果再手動附加，屬於額外的手動 ETL，且產生的是靜態、不會刷新的成品，而非即時的 dashboard widget。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"X-Ray is for distributed tracing, latency analysis, and service maps, not business-transaction aggregation. X-Ray annotations index trace data for filtering, but X-Ray does not produce pie charts of transaction counts and X-Ray traces/service maps cannot be added to a CloudWatch dashboard as a pie-chart widget. Instrumenting every transaction as a trace is an anti-pattern with high overhead.","why_zh":"X-Ray 用於分散式追蹤、延遲分析與服務地圖，而非業務交易聚合。X-Ray annotation 用於索引 trace 資料以供篩選，但 X-Ray 無法以圓餅圖呈現交易筆數，其 trace/服務地圖也不能以圓餅圖 widget 加入 CloudWatch dashboard。把每筆交易都做成 trace 屬反模式且開銷高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Lambda subscription filter that aggregates into DynamoDB is custom-code-heavy ETL, and DynamoDB data still cannot be charted as a pie directly on a CloudWatch dashboard. This is the most operationally complex path and is unnecessary because Logs Insights already visualizes the same log data natively and attaches it to a dashboard.","why_zh":"用 Lambda 訂閱過濾器將資料聚合進 DynamoDB 屬於需大量自訂程式的 ETL，且 DynamoDB 資料仍無法直接在 CloudWatch dashboard 以圓餅圖呈現。這是維運最複雜的路徑，而且完全不必要，因為 Logs Insights 已能原生視覺化相同的 log 資料並掛到 dashboard。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_VisualizationQuery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_Insights-Visualizing-Log-Data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_ExportQueryResults.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":186,"question_en":"A company is launching an application. The application must use only approved AWS services. The account that runs the application was created less than 1 year ago and is assigned to an AWS Organizations OU. The company needs to create a new Organizations account structure. The account structure must have an appropriate SCP that supports the use of only services that are currently active in the AWS account. The company will use AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) Access Analyzer in the solution. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在推出一款应用程序。该应用程序必须仅使用经批准的 AWS 服务。运行该应用程序的账 户创建时间不足 1 年，并且已分配到 AWS Organizations 组织单元（OU）。 该公司需要创建一个新的组织账户结构。该账户结构必须具备适当的 SCP（服务控制策略），以支持仅使用 当前在 AWS 账户中处于活动状态的服务。该公司将在解决方案中使用 AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）访问 分析器。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that allows the services that IAM Access Analyzer identifies. Create an OU for the account. Move the account into the new OU. Attach the new SCP to the new OU. Detach the default FullAWSAccess SCP from the new OU.","B":"Create an SCP that denies the services that IAM Access Analyzer identifies. Create an OU for the account. Move the account into the new OU. Attach the new SCP to the new OU.","C":"Create an SCP that allows the services that IAM Access Analyzer identifies. Attach the new SCP to the organization's root.","D":"Create an SCP that allows the services that IAM Access Analyzer identifies. Create an OU for the account. Move the account into the new OU. Attach the new SCP to the management account. Detach the default FullAWSAccess SCP from the new OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许 IAM 访问分析器识别的服务。为该账户创建一个组织单位 （OU）。将该账户移至新的 OU 中。将新的 SCP 附加到新的 OU。从新的 OU 中分离默认的 FullAWSAccess SCP。","B":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），拒绝 IAM 访问分析器所识别的服务。为该账户创建一个组织单位 （OU）。将该账户移至新的 OU 中。将新的 SCP 附加到新的 OU。","C":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许 IAM 访问分析器识别的服务。将新创建的 SCP 附加到组织的根节 点。","D":"创建一个允许 IAM 访问分析器识别的服务的 SCP。为该账户创建一个组织单位（OU）。将该账户移至 新的 OU 中。将新的 SCP 附加到管理账户。从新的 OU 中分离默认的 FullAWSAccess SCP。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"IAM Access Analyzer policy generation analyzes CloudTrail events to identify the services/actions that have actually been used (i.e., are active) in the account, so the SCP must ALLOW those identified services (allow-list strategy), not deny them. To make an allow-list SCP actually restrictive, you must detach the default FullAWSAccess SCP at the level you are restricting; otherwise FullAWSAccess (which allows all services/actions) keeps the broader allow in effect and the restriction has no impact. AWS best practice is to NOT attach a restrictive SCP to the organization root without testing; instead create an OU, move the account into it, and apply/replace the SCP there so you can validate impact on a single account. Option A does exactly this: allow the Access-Analyzer-identified services, create a new OU, move the account in, attach the allow-list SCP to the OU, and detach FullAWSAccess from that OU. Because root still has FullAWSAccess (all allowed) and the OU now allows only approved services, the effective intersection at the account is exactly the approved/active services, while other accounts are unaffected.","explanation_zh":"IAM Access Analyzer 的政策產生功能會分析 CloudTrail 事件，找出帳戶中實際使用過（即目前作用中）的服務與動作，因此 SCP 必須以「允許清單」(allow-list) 方式 Allow 這些被辨識出的服務，而非 Deny。要讓 allow-list SCP 真正產生限制效果，必須在要限制的層級卸除預設的 FullAWSAccess SCP；否則 FullAWSAccess（允許所有服務與動作）仍然生效，限制就形同虛設。AWS 最佳實務是不要未經測試就把限制性 SCP 直接掛在 organization root；應建立一個 OU，將帳戶移入該 OU，再於該層套用/取代 SCP，以便先在單一帳戶驗證影響。選項 A 正是這個做法：允許 Access Analyzer 辨識出的服務、建立新 OU、將帳戶移入、把 allow-list SCP 掛到該 OU、並從該 OU 卸除 FullAWSAccess。由於 root 仍保有 FullAWSAccess（全部允許），而 OU 只允許核准的服務，帳戶層的有效權限交集剛好就是核准/作用中的服務，且其他帳戶不受影響。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses a Deny list of the services Access Analyzer identifies. This is backwards: Access Analyzer identifies the services that ARE used/active (the approved ones), so denying them would block the very services the application needs while still allowing every other (unapproved) service via the still-attached FullAWSAccess. It fails the requirement to allow only active services.","why_zh":"對 Access Analyzer 辨識出的服務使用 Deny。這完全相反：Access Analyzer 辨識出的是有在使用/作用中的（核准）服務，Deny 它們會擋掉應用程式需要的服務，而其他未核准的服務反而因 FullAWSAccess 仍掛著而被允許，無法達成只允許作用中服務的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Attaches the allow-list SCP to the organization root. AWS strongly recommends NOT attaching a restrictive SCP to the root without testing because it affects every account; it also does not create an isolated OU and does not detach FullAWSAccess, so the restriction would either not take effect (FullAWSAccess still allows all) or risk locking out other accounts. Violates the test-in-an-OU best practice.","why_zh":"把 allow-list SCP 直接掛在 organization root。AWS 強烈建議未經測試不要把限制性 SCP 掛在 root，因為會影響所有帳戶；此選項也未建立隔離的 OU、未卸除 FullAWSAccess，因此限制要嘛不生效（FullAWSAccess 仍允許全部），要嘛可能鎖死其他帳戶，違反「先在 OU 測試」的最佳實務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Attaches the allow-list SCP to the management account, but SCPs do NOT affect users/roles in the management account, so it grants no restriction there. Worse, it detaches FullAWSAccess from the new OU while attaching the allow SCP to the management account (not the OU). With no Allow statement at the OU level, the deny-by-default model blocks ALL actions for the account in that OU, locking it out. Broken on two counts.","why_zh":"把 allow-list SCP 掛到 management account，但 SCP 不會影響 management account 內的使用者/角色，因此在該處毫無限制效果。更糟的是，它從新 OU 卸除 FullAWSAccess，卻把 allow SCP 掛在 management account（而非該 OU）。OU 層級沒有任何 Allow 陳述式時，預設拒絕模型會擋掉該 OU 內帳戶的所有動作，導致帳戶被鎖死。兩處皆錯。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-policy-generation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":187,"question_en":"A company has multiple development teams in different business units that work in a shared single AWS account. All Amazon EC2 resources that are created in the account must include tags that specify who created the resources. The tagging must occur within the first hour of resource creation. A DevOps engineer needs to add tags to the created resources that include the user ID that created the resource and the cost center ID. The DevOps engineer configures an AWS Lambda function with the cost center mappings to tag the resources. The DevOps engineer also sets up AWS CloudTrail in the AWS account. An Amazon S3 bucket stores the CloudTrail event logs. Which solution will meet the tagging requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有多个开发团队分布在不同的业务部门，这些团队在一个共享的单一 AWS 账户中工作。该账户 中创建的所有亚马逊 EC2 资源都必须包含指定创建者的标签。 创建了资源。必须在资源创建后的第一个小时内完成标记。 DevOps 工程师需要为创建的资源添加标签，标签中应包含创建资源的用户 ID 和成本中心 ID。DevOps 工程师配置了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数包含成本中心映射，用于为资源添加标签。DevOps 工程 师还在 AWS 账户中设置了 AWS CloudTrail。Amazon S3 存储桶用于存储 CloudTrail 事件日志。 哪种解决方案能满足标签要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 event notification on the S3 bucket to invoke the Lambda function for s3:ObjectTagging:Put events. Enable bucket versioning on the S3 bucket.","B":"Enable server access logging on the S3 bucket. Create an S3 event notification on the S3 bucket for s3:ObjectTagging:* events.","C":"Create a recurring hourly Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule that invokes the Lambda function. Modify the Lambda function to read the logs from the S3 bucket.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses Amazon EC2 as the event source. Configure the rule to match events delivered by CloudTrail. Configure the rule to target the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 S3 存储桶上创建 S3 事件通知，以便在发生 s3:ObjectTagging:Put 事件时调用 Lambda 函数。在 S3 存储桶上启用版本控制。","B":"在 S3 存储桶上启用服务器访问日志记录。在 S3 存储桶上为 s3:ObjectTagging:* 事件创建 S3 事件通 知。","C":"创建一个每小时重复触发的 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则，以调用 Lambda 函数。修改 Lambda 函数，使其能够从 S3 存储桶读取日志。","D":"创建一个使用 Amazon EC2 作为事件源的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以匹配 CloudTrail 发 送的事件。配置该规则以将目标指向 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to automatically tag newly created EC2 resources with the creating user's ID and a cost center ID within one hour of creation, using a Lambda function that holds the cost-center mappings, with CloudTrail already enabled. AWS CloudTrail records the EC2 API call (e.g., RunInstances) including the userIdentity, and CloudTrail delivers an 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' event (source aws.ec2) to the default EventBridge event bus. An EventBridge rule that uses EC2 as the event source, matches events delivered by CloudTrail, and targets the Lambda function triggers the function in near real time, so the Lambda can read the user ID from the event and apply the tags well within the one-hour window. This is the exact pattern in the official AWS tutorial 'Create an EventBridge rule that reacts to AWS API calls via CloudTrail,' which uses Event source = EC2, Event type = AWS API Call via CloudTrail, target = Lambda. Option D matches this canonical, event-driven design.","explanation_zh":"需求是在 EC2 資源建立後一小時內，自動以建立者的 user ID 與 cost center ID 對其加上標籤，並使用內含 cost center 對應關係的 Lambda 函數，且 CloudTrail 已啟用。AWS CloudTrail 會記錄 EC2 的 API 呼叫（例如 RunInstances），其中包含 userIdentity，並將 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' 事件（source 為 aws.ec2）傳遞到預設 EventBridge 事件匯流排。一條以 EC2 為事件來源、比對由 CloudTrail 傳遞之事件、並以 Lambda 函數為目標的 EventBridge 規則，會近乎即時觸發該函數，使 Lambda 能從事件中讀取 user ID 並在一小時內套用標籤。這正是官方 AWS 教學 'Create an EventBridge rule that reacts to AWS API calls via CloudTrail' 的模式（Event source = EC2、Event type = AWS API Call via CloudTrail、target = Lambda）。選項 D 符合此標準的事件驅動設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"s3:ObjectTagging:Put events fire only when tags are placed on S3 objects, which is unrelated to EC2 resource creation. CloudTrail writes log object files to the bucket, not tags, so this notification would never fire for the relevant action. Bucket versioning is irrelevant to EC2 tagging.","why_zh":"s3:ObjectTagging:Put 事件只有在對 S3 物件設定標籤時才會觸發，與 EC2 資源建立無關。CloudTrail 寫入的是日誌物件檔案而非標籤，因此此通知不會因相關動作而觸發。Bucket versioning 與 EC2 標記無關。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Server access logging and s3:ObjectTagging:* notifications relate to S3 object tagging, not EC2 resource creation. CloudTrail delivering log files to the bucket are PutObject/Create events, not ObjectTagging events, so the Lambda would never be invoked for EC2 creation.","why_zh":"Server access logging 與 s3:ObjectTagging:* 通知都與 S3 物件標籤有關，而非 EC2 資源建立。CloudTrail 將日誌檔案傳送到 bucket 屬於 PutObject/Create 事件，而非 ObjectTagging 事件，因此 Lambda 不會因 EC2 建立而被叫用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An hourly scheduled rule that parses CloudTrail logs from S3 is far more operationally complex and fragile: CloudTrail delivers logs to S3 in batches with delay (often up to ~15 minutes), so polling once per hour risks missing the one-hour SLA and requires custom log parsing and deduplication. The event-driven EventBridge approach in D is the AWS-recommended, simpler, near-real-time pattern.","why_zh":"每小時排程規則去 S3 解析 CloudTrail 日誌，運維上更複雜且脆弱：CloudTrail 以批次方式延遲（通常可達約 15 分鐘）傳送日誌到 S3，因此每小時輪詢一次有錯過一小時 SLA 的風險，並需自訂日誌解析與去重。選項 D 的事件驅動 EventBridge 方式才是 AWS 建議、更簡單且近乎即時的模式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-log-api-call.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-cloudtrail.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":188,"question_en":"A company runs an application for multiple environments in a single AWS account. An AWS CodePipeline pipeline uses a development Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster to test an image for the application from an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. The pipeline promotes the image to a production ECS cluster. The company needs to move the production cluster into a separate AWS account in the same AWS Region. The production cluster must be able to download the images over a private connection. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 AWS 账户中为多个环境运行一个应用程序。一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道使用开发环境 的 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）集群来测试来自 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR）存储库的应用程序镜像。该管道将镜像推广到生产环境的 ECS 集群。 该公司需要将生产集群迁移到同一 AWS 区域内的单独 AWS 账户中。生产集群必须能够通过私有 连接下载镜像。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon ECR VPC endpoints and an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint. In the separate AWS account, create an ECR repository. Set the repository policy to allow the production ECS tasks to pull images from the main AWS account. Configure the production ECS task execution role to have permission to download the image from the ECR repository.","B":"Set a repository policy on the production ECR repository in the main AWS account. Configure the repository policy to allow the production ECS tasks in the separate AWS account to pull images from the main account. Configure the production ECS task execution role to have permission to download the image from the ECR repository.","C":"Configure ECR private image replication in the main AWS account. Activate cross-account replication. Define the destination account ID of the separate AWS account.","D":"Use Amazon ECR VPC endpoints and an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint. Set a repository policy on the production ECR repository in the main AWS account. Configure the repository policy to allow the production ECS tasks in the separate AWS account to pull images from the main account. Configure the production ECS task execution role to have permission to download the image from the ECR repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon ECR VPC 端点和 Amazon S3 网关端点。在单独的 AWS 账户中创建一个 ECR 存储库。 将存储库策略设置为允许生产 ECS 任务从主 AWS 账户拉取镜像。配置生产 ECS 任务执行角色， 使其有权从 ECR 存储库下载镜像。","B":"在主 AWS 账户的生产 ECR 存储库上设置存储库策略。将存储库策略配置为允许单独 AWS 账户中 的生产 ECS 任务从主账户拉取镜像。将生产 ECS 任务执行角色配置为有权从 ECR 存储库下载镜 像。","C":"在主 AWS 账户中配置 ECR 私有镜像复制。激活跨账户复制。定义单独 AWS 账户的目标账户 ID。","D":"使用 Amazon ECR VPC 端点和 Amazon S3 网关端点。在主 AWS 账户的生产 ECR 存储库上设置存储 库策略。将存储库策略配置为允许单独 AWS 账户中的生产 ECS 任务从主账户拉取镜像。配置生产 ECS 任务执行角色，使其有权从 ECR 存储库下载镜像。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question has two distinct requirements: (1) the production ECS cluster in a separate account must be able to pull images from the main account's ECR repository (cross-account access), and (2) the pull must happen over a private connection. Cross-account access to an existing ECR repository is granted by a repository policy on the source (main-account) repository allowing the consuming account's principals to pull, combined with the consuming task execution role having ecr permissions. Private connectivity for ECR image pulls requires an ECR interface VPC endpoint (PrivateLink) AND an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint, because ECR stores the image layers in S3 and the layer download goes to S3. Option D is the only choice that satisfies both requirements: it creates the ECR/S3 endpoints for the private path and sets the cross-account repository policy plus task execution role permissions on the main-account repository. Options B (no endpoints), A (creates a useless empty repo in the wrong account), and C (replication only, no private connectivity) each fail at least one requirement.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個明確需求：(1) 位於獨立帳戶的 production ECS cluster 必須能從主帳戶的 ECR repository 拉取映像（跨帳戶存取）；(2) 拉取必須透過私有連線進行。對既有 ECR repository 的跨帳戶存取，是在來源（主帳戶）repository 上設定 repository policy 允許目標帳戶的 principal 拉取，並讓目標帳戶的 task execution role 具備 ecr 權限。ECR 映像拉取的私有連線需要 ECR interface VPC endpoint（PrivateLink）以及 Amazon S3 gateway endpoint，因為 ECR 將映像層儲存在 S3，層下載會走 S3。Option D 是唯一同時滿足兩項需求的選項：它建立 ECR/S3 endpoints 提供私有路徑，並在主帳戶 repository 上設定跨帳戶 repository policy 與 task execution role 權限。Option B（缺 endpoints）、Option A（在錯誤帳戶建立空的無用 repo）、Option C（僅複製，無私有連線）各自至少缺一項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a new empty ECR repository in the separate account and setting its policy does not grant access to the main account's existing images; the policy is on the wrong (empty) repository and no replication or sharing of the actual images is configured.","why_zh":"在獨立帳戶建立新的空 ECR repository 並設定其 policy，並不會授予存取主帳戶既有映像的權限；policy 設在錯誤的（空的）repository 上，且未設定任何複製或共享實際映像的機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The repository policy plus task execution role correctly enable cross-account pull, but this option omits the ECR VPC endpoints and S3 gateway endpoint, so it fails the explicit 'private connection' requirement.","why_zh":"repository policy 加上 task execution role 確實能啟用跨帳戶拉取，但此選項缺少 ECR VPC endpoints 與 S3 gateway endpoint，因此無法滿足明確的『私有連線』需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Cross-account replication copies images into the separate account, but on its own it provides no private connection for the production cluster's pulls; the requirement to download images over a private connection is unmet.","why_zh":"跨帳戶複製會把映像複製到獨立帳戶，但其本身並未為 production cluster 的拉取提供私有連線；『透過私有連線下載映像』的需求未被滿足。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/vpc-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/repository-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/ECR_on_ECS.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/registry-permissions-create-replication.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":189,"question_en":"A company needs to ensure that flow logs remain configured for all existing and new VPCs in its AWS account. The company uses an AWS CloudFormation stack to manage its VPCs. The company needs a solution that will work for any VPCs that any IAM user creates. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要确保其 AWS 账户中所有现有和新创建的 VPC 都已配置了流量日志。该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来管理其 VPC。该公司需要一个解决方案，能够适用于任何 IAM 用户创建的任何 VPC。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add the AWS::EC2::FlowLog resource to the CloudFormation stack that creates the VPCs.","B":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Add the company's AWS account to the organization. Create an SCP to prevent users from modifying VPC flow logs.","C":"Turn on AWS Config. Create an AWS Config rule to check whether VPC flow logs are turned on. Configure automatic remediation to turn on VPC flow logs.","D":"Create an IAM policy to deny the use of API calls for VPC flow logs. Attach the IAM policy to all IAM users."},"options_zh":{"A":"在创建 VPC 的 CloudFormation 堆栈EC2::FlowLog 资源。","B":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建一个组织。将公司的 AWS 账户添加到该组织中。创建一个服务控制策 略（SCP），以防止用户修改 VPC 流日志。","C":"启用 AWS Config。创建一条 AWS Config 规则以检查 VPC 流日志是否已开启。配置自动修复 以开启 VPC 流日志。","D":"创建一个 IAM 策略以禁止使用 VPC 流日志的 API 调用。将该 IAM 策略附加到所有 IAM 用户。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config provides the managed rule vpc-flow-logs-enabled (VPC_FLOW_LOGS_ENABLED), which checks the AWS::EC2::VPC resource type and is NON_COMPLIANT if flow logs are not enabled for any VPC. AWS Config continuously discovers and evaluates both existing and newly created VPCs regardless of which IAM user, console, CLI, SDK, or CloudFormation stack created them. Coupling the rule with automatic remediation (an SSM Automation document triggered via PutRemediationConfigurations) turns flow logs back on for any noncompliant VPC. This is the only option that guarantees flow logs remain configured for all existing and new VPCs created by any IAM user.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 提供受管規則 vpc-flow-logs-enabled (VPC_FLOW_LOGS_ENABLED)，它檢查 AWS::EC2::VPC 資源類型，若任何 VPC 未啟用 flow logs 即標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。AWS Config 會持續探索並評估既有與新建立的 VPC，不論是哪位 IAM user 或透過 console、CLI、SDK、CloudFormation 建立。搭配 automatic remediation（透過 PutRemediationConfigurations 觸發的 SSM Automation 文件）即可為任何不合規的 VPC 重新開啟 flow logs。這是唯一能保證所有既有與新建立 VPC（無論由哪位 IAM user 建立）都維持 flow logs 設定的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adding AWS::EC2::FlowLog to the CloudFormation stack only covers VPCs created through that specific stack. IAM users can create VPCs via the console, CLI, or SDK outside the stack, and it does not cover existing VPCs not managed by the stack, so it fails the 'any VPCs that any IAM user creates' requirement.","why_zh":"在 CloudFormation stack 中加入 AWS::EC2::FlowLog 只涵蓋透過該 stack 建立的 VPC。IAM user 可透過 console、CLI、SDK 在 stack 之外建立 VPC，且無法涵蓋未由該 stack 管理的既有 VPC，因此無法滿足『任何 IAM user 建立的任何 VPC』需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An SCP preventing users from modifying VPC flow logs is only a preventive guardrail against changes. It does nothing to enable flow logs on existing VPCs or on new VPCs that are created without flow logs, so it does not ensure flow logs remain configured.","why_zh":"SCP 防止使用者修改 VPC flow logs 只是阻止變更的預防性防護，無法為既有 VPC 或新建立但未設定 flow logs 的 VPC 啟用 flow logs，因此無法確保 flow logs 維持設定。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Denying VPC flow log API calls would prevent flow logs from being created or managed at all, which is the opposite of the requirement. It also only applies to the attached IAM users (not roles) and is unmanageable.","why_zh":"拒絕 VPC flow log API 呼叫會完全阻止 flow logs 的建立或管理，與需求相反；且僅套用於所附加的 IAM users（不含 roles），難以維護。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/vpc-flow-logs-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":190,"question_en":"A company's application teams use AWS CodeCommit repositories for their applications. The application teams have repositories in multiple AWS accounts. All accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. Each application team uses AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) configured with an external IdP to assume a developer IAM role. The developer role allows the application teams to use Git to work with the code in the repositories. A security audit reveals that the application teams can modify the main branch in any repository. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that allows the application teams to modify the main branch of only the repositories that they manage. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司的应用团队在其应用中使用 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。这些应用团队在多个 AWS 账户中拥 有代码库。所有账户都在 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织内。 每个应用程序团队都使用与外部身份提供商（IdP）配置的 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）来 承担开发人员 IAM 角色。开发人员角色允许应用程序团队使用 Git 对存储库中的代码进行操作。 一项安全审计显示，应用程序团队可以在任何代码库中修改主分支。一位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解 决方案，使应用程序团队只能修改其管理的代码库的主分支。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the SAML assertion to pass the user's team name. Update the IAM role's trust policy to add an access-team session tag that has the team name.","B":"Create an approval rule template for each team in the Organizations management account. Associate the template with all the repositories. Add the developer role ARN as an approver.","C":"Create an approval rule template for each account. Associate the template with all repositories. Add the \"aws:ResourceTag/access-team\": \"$ ;{aws:PrincipalTag/access-team}\" condition to the approval rule template.","D":"For each CodeCommit repository, add an access-team tag that has the value set to the name of the associated team.","E":"Attach an SCP to the accounts. Include the following statement:","F":"Create an IAM permissions boundary in each account. Include the following statement:"},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 SAML 断言以传递用户的团队名称。更新 IAM 角色的信任策略，添加一个具有团队名称的访问 团队会话标签。","B":"在“组织管理”账户中为每个团队创建一个审批规则模板。将该模板与所有代码库相关联。添加开 发人员角色的 ARN 作为审批人。","C":"为每个账户创建一个审批规则模板。将该模板与所有存储库相关联。在审批规则模板中添加“aws: ResourceTag/access-team”： “$ ;{aws:PrincipalTag/access-team}”条件。","D":"对于每个 CodeCommit 代码库，添加一个 access-team 标签，将其值设置为相关团队的名称。","E":"将 SCP 附加到账户上。包含以下声明：","F":"在每个账户中创建一个 IAM 权限边界。包含以下语句："},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is a classic attribute-based access control (ABAC) guardrail across an AWS Organization. (A) The external IdP passes the user's team name in the SAML assertion, and IAM Identity Center surfaces it as a session tag so it is available as aws:PrincipalTag/access-team during the developer role session. (D) Each CodeCommit repository is tagged with access-team set to the owning team, making aws:ResourceTag/access-team available on the resource. (E) An SCP attached to the member accounts denies the branch-write actions (codecommit:GitPush, the MergeBranches*/MergePullRequest* actions, DeleteBranch, PutFile, etc.) on refs/heads/main (via the codecommit:References condition) whenever aws:ResourceTag/access-team does not equal aws:PrincipalTag/access-team. Because all accounts are in the organization, an SCP is the natural org-wide guardrail that applies to every IAM principal (including the IAM Identity Center permission-set roles) in every member account, so teams can modify main only in repos they own. The principal tag (A) plus resource tag (D) plus the comparing Deny policy (E) is exactly the ABAC 'tags must match' pattern.","explanation_zh":"這是跨 AWS Organization 的典型屬性式存取控制（ABAC）防護。(A) 外部 IdP 在 SAML assertion 中傳遞使用者的 team 名稱，IAM Identity Center 將其作為 session tag 帶入，使其在 developer role 工作階段中以 aws:PrincipalTag/access-team 形式可用。(D) 為每個 CodeCommit repository 加上 access-team 標籤並設為所屬團隊，使資源上可取得 aws:ResourceTag/access-team。(E) 在成員帳戶附加 SCP，透過 codecommit:References 條件鎖定 refs/heads/main，當 aws:ResourceTag/access-team 不等於 aws:PrincipalTag/access-team 時，拒絕分支寫入動作（codecommit:GitPush、MergeBranches*/MergePullRequest* 動作、DeleteBranch、PutFile 等）。由於所有帳戶都在 organization 內，SCP 是天然的全組織防護，會套用到每個成員帳戶中的所有 IAM 主體（包含 IAM Identity Center 權限集角色），讓團隊只能修改自己擁有的 repo 的 main 分支。principal tag (A) 加上 resource tag (D) 再加上比較兩者的 Deny 政策 (E)，正是 ABAC『標籤必須相符』的模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Approval rule templates only require a number of pull-request approvals before a PR can be merged; they do not prevent a developer from directly pushing commits (git push / GitPush) to the main branch, and adding the shared developer role ARN as an approver does not scope writes to repos a team owns. It also creates the template in the management account, but templates are regional/per-account resources that must exist in each account.","why_zh":"Approval rule templates 只是在合併 PR 前要求一定數量的核准；無法阻止開發者直接 push commit（git push / GitPush）到 main 分支，且把共用的 developer role ARN 加為核准者也無法將寫入限縮到團隊擁有的 repo。它也在管理帳戶建立範本，但範本是各帳戶/各區域的資源，須在每個帳戶各自存在。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Approval rule templates do not support IAM policy condition syntax such as \"aws:ResourceTag/access-team\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/access-team}\"; they only define destination branches, the approval pool (IAM ARNs/wildcards), and the number of approvals needed. They govern pull-request merges, not direct branch pushes, so this option is technically invalid.","why_zh":"Approval rule templates 不支援 IAM 政策條件語法（如 \"aws:ResourceTag/access-team\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/access-team}\"）；它們只定義目標分支、核准者集合（IAM ARN/萬用字元）以及所需核准數量。它們管的是 PR 合併而非直接分支 push，因此此選項在技術上無效。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"A permissions boundary only sets the maximum permissions of an entity and must be attached to each individual IAM user/role; it does not automatically apply org-wide and cannot be cleanly attached to the IAM Identity Center permission-set roles that are auto-provisioned into each account. An SCP (E) is the proper organization-level guardrail for this multi-account scenario, making F the weaker, harder-to-operate alternative.","why_zh":"permissions boundary 只設定單一實體的最大權限，且必須附加到每個個別的 IAM user/role；它不會自動套用到整個組織，也無法乾淨地附加到自動佈建到各帳戶的 IAM Identity Center 權限集角色。對此多帳戶情境而言，SCP（E）才是正確的組織層級防護，使 F 成為較弱、較難維運的替代方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-conditional-branch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-attributes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/attributesforaccesscontrol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/introduction_attribute-based-access-control.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/auth-and-access-control-permissions-reference.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":191,"question_en":"A company uses AWS WAF to protect its cloud infrastructure. A DevOps engineer needs to give an operations team the ability to analyze log messages from AWS WAF. The operations team needs to be able to create alarms for specific patterns in the log output. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS WAF 来保护其云基础设施。一位 DevOps 工程师需要赋予运营团队分析 AWS WAF 日志消息的能力。运营团队需要能够针对日志输出中的特定模式创建警报。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure the appropriate AWS WAF web ACL to send log messages to the log group. Instruct the operations team to create CloudWatch metric filters.","B":"Create an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster and appropriate indexes. Configure an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to stream log data to the indexes. Use OpenSearch Dashboards to create filters and widgets.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket for the log output. Configure AWS WAF to send log outputs to the S3 bucket. Instruct the operations team to create AWS Lambda functions that detect each desired log message pattern. Configure the Lambda functions to publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","D":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket for the log output. Configure AWS WAF to send log outputs to the S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to create an external table definition that fits the log message pattern. Instruct the operations team to write SQL queries and to create Amazon CloudWatch metric filters for the Athena queries."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。配置适当的 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）， 将日志消息发送到该日志组。指示运营团队创建 CloudWatch 指标筛选器。","B":"创建一个 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群和相应的索引。配置一个 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流， 将日志数据流式传输到索引中。使用 OpenSearch Dashboards 创建过滤器和小部件。","C":"创建一个用于日志输出的 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 AWS WAF 将日志输出发送到该 S3 存储桶。指示运 营团队创建用于检测每个所需日志消息模式的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以发布到 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。","D":"创建一个用于日志输出的 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 AWS WAF 将日志输出发送到该 S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon Athena 创建一个符合日志消息模式的外部表定义。指示运营团队编写 SQL 查询，并为 Athena 查询创建 Amazon CloudWatch 指标过滤器。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS WAF natively supports three logging destinations: an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group, an Amazon S3 bucket, and Amazon Data Firehose. Sending web ACL logs directly to a CloudWatch Logs log group (the log group name must start with 'aws-waf-logs-') requires no intermediary pipeline. Once logs are in CloudWatch Logs, the operations team can create CloudWatch metric filters that match specific patterns in the log output and then attach CloudWatch alarms (which can notify via SNS). This fully managed, no-custom-code, no-infrastructure approach gives the LEAST operational overhead, which is the deciding qualifier. The AWS-documented pattern for 'alarm on a specific log pattern' is exactly metric filter plus alarm.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 原生支援三種記錄目的地：Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group、Amazon S3 bucket 以及 Amazon Data Firehose。將 web ACL 記錄直接送到 CloudWatch Logs log group（log group 名稱必須以 'aws-waf-logs-' 開頭）不需要任何中介管線。一旦記錄進入 CloudWatch Logs，營運團隊即可建立 CloudWatch metric filter 來比對記錄輸出中的特定模式，再附加 CloudWatch alarm（可透過 SNS 通知）。這種全託管、無需自訂程式碼、無需自建基礎設施的做法營運負擔最低，正是本題的決定性條件。AWS 官方文件針對『依特定記錄模式發出警示』的標準做法就是 metric filter 加 alarm。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Provisioning and managing an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster plus indexes and a Firehose stream is heavy operational overhead (cluster sizing, patching, capacity). OpenSearch Dashboards filters/widgets are for visualization and do not natively create alarms the way the requirement intends.","why_zh":"佈建並維運 Amazon OpenSearch Service 叢集、索引以及 Firehose 串流的營運負擔很重（叢集規模、修補、容量管理）。OpenSearch Dashboards 的 filter/widget 是用於視覺化，並無法以題目要求的方式原生建立警示。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Writing and maintaining a custom AWS Lambda function for each desired log pattern is significant custom-code operational overhead compared with managed CloudWatch metric filters.","why_zh":"為每個所需記錄模式撰寫並維護自訂的 AWS Lambda 函式，相較於託管的 CloudWatch metric filter，是相當高的自訂程式碼營運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is technically incoherent: CloudWatch metric filters operate on CloudWatch Logs log events, not on Athena query results, so you cannot create metric filters 'for the Athena queries'. It also requires manually authoring and running SQL, adding overhead.","why_zh":"此選項在技術上不通：CloudWatch metric filter 作用於 CloudWatch Logs 的記錄事件，而非 Athena 查詢結果，因此無法為 Athena 查詢建立 metric filter。此外還需手動撰寫並執行 SQL，增加營運負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-cw-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-policies-logging-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntaxForMetricFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/process-records-cwl.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":192,"question_en":"A software team is using AWS CodePipeline to automate its Java application release pipeline. The pipeline consists of a source stage, then a build stage, and then a deploy stage. Each stage contains a single action that has a runOrder value of 1. The team wants to integrate unit tests into the existing release pipeline. The team needs a solution that deploys only the code changes that pass all unit tests. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个软件团队正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 来自动化其 Java 应用程序的发布流程。该流程包括源代码阶段、 构建阶段和部署阶段。每个阶段都包含一个 runOrder 值为 1 的单一操作。 团队希望将单元测试整合到现有的发布流程中。团队需要一个解决方案，仅部署通过所有单元测试的代 码更改。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the build stage. Add a test action that has a runOrder value of 1. Use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to run unit tests.","B":"Modify the build stage. Add a test action that has a runOrder value of 2. Use AWS CodeBuild as the action provider to run unit tests.","C":"Modify the deploy stage. Add a test action that has a runOrder value of 1. Use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to run unit tests.","D":"Modify the deploy stage. Add a test action that has a runOrder value of 2. Use AWS CodeBuild as the action provider to run unit tests."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改构建阶段。添加一个运行顺序值为 1 的测试操作。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序来运行 单元测试。","B":"修改构建阶段。添加一个运行顺序值为 2 的测试操作。使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来运行 单元测试。","C":"修改部署阶段。添加一个运行顺序值为 1 的测试操作。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序来运 行单元测试。","D":"修改部署阶段。添加一个运行顺序值为 2 的测试操作。使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来运行 单元测试。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is that code is deployed only if it passes all unit tests, so the test must run AND succeed BEFORE the deploy stage. CodeBuild is a valid Test action provider that runs unit tests via a buildspec; CodeDeploy is a deploy provider and cannot run unit tests. Within a stage, runOrder controls sequencing: actions with the same runOrder run in parallel, while a higher runOrder runs serially after lower-numbered actions. Option B adds a CodeBuild test action to the build stage with runOrder 2, so it runs serially after the existing build action (runOrder 1); if the tests fail, the build stage fails and the deploy stage never executes, guaranteeing only tested code is deployed. The dump's suggested answer (B) is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是只有通過所有單元測試的程式碼才會被部署，因此測試必須在 deploy stage 之前執行並成功。CodeBuild 是有效的 Test action provider，能透過 buildspec 執行單元測試；CodeDeploy 是 deploy provider，無法執行單元測試。在同一個 stage 內，runOrder 控制執行順序：相同 runOrder 的 action 會平行執行，較大的 runOrder 會在較小編號的 action 之後序列執行。選項 B 在 build stage 加入 runOrder 為 2 的 CodeBuild 測試 action，使其在既有 build action（runOrder 1）之後序列執行；若測試失敗，build stage 失敗，deploy stage 便不會執行，確保只有通過測試的程式碼才會被部署。題庫建議答案（B）正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodeDeploy is a deploy action provider and cannot run unit tests, and runOrder 1 would run the test action in parallel with the existing build action rather than after it.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 是 deploy action provider，無法執行單元測試；且 runOrder 為 1 會讓測試 action 與既有 build action 平行執行，而非在其之後。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeDeploy cannot run unit tests, and runOrder 1 in the deploy stage runs the test in parallel with the deploy action, so it would not gate the deployment.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 無法執行單元測試；且 deploy stage 中 runOrder 為 1 會讓測試與 deploy action 平行執行，無法作為部署的把關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Placing a CodeBuild test action with runOrder 2 in the deploy stage runs the tests AFTER the deploy action (runOrder 1), so the code is deployed first and then tested, violating the requirement to deploy only code that passes unit tests.","why_zh":"在 deploy stage 放入 runOrder 為 2 的 CodeBuild 測試 action，會在 deploy action（runOrder 1）之後執行測試，等於先部署再測試，違反只部署通過單元測試之程式碼的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-requirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pipeline-add-test.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodeBuild.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":193,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage several AWS accounts that the company's developers use. The company requires all data to be encrypted in transit. Multiple Amazon S3 buckets that were created in developer accounts allow unencrypted connections. A DevOps engineer must enforce encryption of data in transit for all existing S3 buckets that are created in accounts in the organization. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织中的一个组织来管理其开发人员使用的多个 AWS 账户。该公司要求所有数 据在传输过程中都必须加密。 多个在开发者账户中创建的亚马逊 S3 存储桶允许未加密的连接。 DevOps 工程师必须为组织内所有现有账户中创建的 S3 存储桶强制实施传输中的数据加密。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy an AWS Network Firewall firewall to each account. Route all outbound requests from the AWS environment through the firewall. Deploy a policy to block access to all outbound requests on port 80.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy an AWS Network Firewall firewall to each account. Route all inbound requests to the AWS environment through the firewall. Deploy a policy to block access to all inbound requests on port 80.","C":"Turn on AWS Config for the organization. Deploy a conformance pack that uses the s3-bucket-ssl- requests-only managed rule and an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook. Use a runbook that adds a bucket policy statement to deny access to an S3 bucket when the value of the aws:SecureTransport condition key is false.","D":"Turn on AWS Config for the organization. Deploy a conformance pack that uses the s3-bucket-ssl- requests-only managed rule and an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook. Use a runbook that adds a bucket policy statement to deny access to an S3 bucket when the value of the s3:x-amz-server- side-encryption-aws-kms-key-id condition key is null."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 AWS Network Firewall 防火墙部署到每个账户。将来自 AWS 环境的所有出站请求通过防火墙进行路由。部署策略以阻止所有端口 80 上的出站请求访问。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 AWS Network Firewall 防火墙部署到每个账户。将所有入 站请求通过防火墙路由到 AWS 环境。部署策略以阻止对端口 80 上所有入站请求的访问。","C":"为组织启用 AWS Config。部署一个合规性包，该包使用 s3-bucket-sslrequests-only 管理规则和一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。使用一个运行手册，当 aws:SecureTransport 条件键的 值为 false 时，向 S3 存储桶添加一个策略语句以拒绝访问。","D":"为组织启用 AWS Config。部署一个合规性包，该包使用 s3-bucket-sslrequests-only 管理规则和一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。使用一个运行手册，当 s3:x-amz-serverside-encryption- aws-kms-key-id 条件键的值为空时，向 S3 存储桶添加一个策略语句以拒绝访问。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to enforce encryption of data in transit (HTTPS/TLS) for all existing S3 buckets across an AWS Organization. Option C uses AWS Config (turned on org-wide) with a conformance pack containing the s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only managed rule, which flags buckets NON_COMPLIANT when their policies allow HTTP (non-SSL) requests. The associated Systems Manager Automation runbook remediates by adding a bucket policy statement that denies access when aws:SecureTransport is false. The aws:SecureTransport global condition key is precisely the mechanism AWS documents to verify whether a request was sent over HTTPS (TLS), which is exactly enforcement of encryption in transit. Option D is incorrect because s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption-aws-kms-key-id governs server-side encryption at rest (SSE-KMS), not encryption in transit. Options A and B use AWS Network Firewall on outbound/inbound traffic, which does not enforce SSL on the S3 buckets themselves and does not remediate existing bucket policies.","explanation_zh":"需求是針對 AWS Organization 中所有現有 S3 buckets 強制執行傳輸中加密（HTTPS/TLS）。選項 C 在整個組織啟用 AWS Config，並部署包含 s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 受管規則的 conformance pack，該規則會在 bucket 政策允許 HTTP（非 SSL）請求時標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。搭配的 Systems Manager Automation runbook 透過新增一條 bucket 政策（當 aws:SecureTransport 為 false 時拒絕存取）來進行修復。aws:SecureTransport 全域條件鍵正是 AWS 文件中用來檢查請求是否經由 HTTPS（TLS）傳送的機制，正好就是傳輸中加密的強制執行方式。選項 D 不正確，因為 s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption-aws-kms-key-id 管控的是靜態的伺服器端加密（SSE-KMS），而非傳輸中加密。選項 A 和 B 使用 AWS Network Firewall 控管出/入流量，無法在 S3 bucket 層級強制 SSL，也無法修復現有的 bucket 政策。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Network Firewall filtering outbound port 80 does not enforce TLS on the S3 buckets themselves, does not remediate existing non-compliant bucket policies, and would not stop unencrypted connections originating outside the firewalled path. It addresses network egress, not S3 resource policy enforcement.","why_zh":"AWS Network Firewall 過濾出站 port 80 無法在 S3 bucket 本身強制 TLS，也無法修復現有不合規的 bucket 政策，且無法阻止來自防火牆路徑之外的未加密連線。它處理的是網路出站，而非 S3 資源政策的強制執行。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Blocking inbound port 80 via Network Firewall is irrelevant to S3, which is accessed over the AWS public/regional endpoints rather than through a customer-managed inbound firewall. It does not modify bucket policies or enforce aws:SecureTransport.","why_zh":"透過 Network Firewall 封鎖入站 port 80 與 S3 無關，因為 S3 是經由 AWS 公用/區域端點存取，而非透過客戶管理的入站防火牆。它不會修改 bucket 政策，也不會強制 aws:SecureTransport。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption-aws-kms-key-id condition key controls server-side encryption at rest with SSE-KMS, not encryption in transit. Denying when it is null would force KMS encryption at rest, which does not meet the stated requirement of encrypting data in transit (HTTPS/TLS).","why_zh":"s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption-aws-kms-key-id 條件鍵控制的是使用 SSE-KMS 的靜態伺服器端加密，而非傳輸中加密。當其為 null 時拒絕存取會強制靜態 KMS 加密，無法滿足題目要求的傳輸中（HTTPS/TLS）資料加密。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingEncryptionInTransit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/security-best-practices.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":194,"question_en":"A company is reviewing its IAM policies. One policy written by the DevOps engineer has been flagged as too permissive. The policy is used by an AWS Lambda function that issues a stop command to Amazon EC2 instances tagged with Environment: NonProduction over the weekend. The current policy is: What changes should the engineer make to achieve a policy of least permission? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在审查其身份和访问管理（IAM）策略。由 DevOps 工程师编写的一项策略被标记为过于宽 松。该策略被一个 AWS Lambda 函数使用，该函数会在周末向标记为“环境：非生产”的 Amazon EC2 实例发出停止命令。当前的策略是： 工程师应做出哪些更改才能实现最小权限策略？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add the following conditional expression:","B":"Change \"Resource\": \"*\"to \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/*\"","C":"Add the following conditional expression:","D":"Add the following conditional expression:","E":"Change \"Action\": \"ec2:*\"to \"Action\": \"ec2:StopInstances\"","F":"Add the following conditional expression:"},"options_zh":{"A":"添加以下条件表达式：","C":"添加以下条件表达式：","D":"添加以下条件表达式："},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is genuinely a 'Choose three' question, but the dump rendered the answer as a single letter and several options are garbled/embedded-as-images. The canonical AWS least-privilege pattern for a Lambda that stops only Environment:NonProduction EC2 instances requires three independent narrowings: (1) scope the Action from the wildcard ec2:* down to the single ec2:StopInstances (option E); (2) scope the Resource from '*' down to the instance ARN pattern arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/* (option B); and (3) add a Condition that restricts to the tag, e.g. StringEquals on ec2:ResourceTag/Environment (or aws:ResourceTag/Environment) equal to NonProduction (one of the unreadable 'Add the following conditional expression' options A/C/D/F). The AWS IAM example 'Allows starting or stopping EC2 instances a user has tagged' shows this exact structure: Action limited to StartInstances/StopInstances, Resource set to arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/*, and a Condition on a ResourceTag key. Of the readable options, B and E are both verifiably correct; B is the single letter the dump marked and it is a genuinely required change, so the verdict is set to B while noting E plus one tag-condition option complete the trio.","explanation_zh":"這實際上是「選三項」的題目，但題庫只渲染成單一答案，且部分選項以圖片嵌入而呈亂碼。針對只停止 Environment:NonProduction 標籤 EC2 的 Lambda，AWS 最小權限的標準寫法需要三個獨立的收斂：(1) 將 Action 由萬用字元 ec2:* 收斂為單一 ec2:StopInstances（選項 E）；(2) 將 Resource 由 '*' 收斂為實例 ARN 樣式 arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/*（選項 B）；(3) 加入限制標籤的 Condition，例如對 ec2:ResourceTag/Environment（或 aws:ResourceTag/Environment）做 StringEquals 等於 NonProduction（即無法閱讀的「Add the following conditional expression」選項之一 A/C/D/F）。AWS IAM 官方範例『Allows starting or stopping EC2 instances a user has tagged』正是此結構：Action 限定 StartInstances/StopInstances、Resource 設為 arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/*、並對 ResourceTag 加 Condition。可讀選項中 B 與 E 皆可驗證為正確；B 是題庫標記的單一字母且確為必要變更，故 verdict 設為 B，並註明還需 E 與一個標籤條件選項才湊齊三項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Garbled/image option. If it is a non-tag condition (e.g. region or time/date), it is not the change AWS docs require here; only the Environment:NonProduction tag condition belongs.","why_zh":"亂碼/圖片選項。若其為非標籤條件（例如區域或時間），則非 AWS 文件此處所需；只有 Environment:NonProduction 標籤條件才正確。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Contains injected vendor watermark text, confirming it is corrupted image OCR and not a legitimate distinct policy condition to select.","why_zh":"含注入的販售浮水印文字，確認為損毀的圖片 OCR，並非可選的合法條件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Garbled/image option; cannot be reliably identified. Only the conditional expression matching aws/ec2:ResourceTag/Environment = NonProduction would be correct.","why_zh":"亂碼/圖片選項，無法可靠辨識；只有符合 aws/ec2:ResourceTag/Environment = NonProduction 的條件式才正確。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Garbled/image option; cannot be reliably identified. The single correct tag condition belongs to whichever option literally encodes ResourceTag/Environment NonProduction.","why_zh":"亂碼/圖片選項，無法可靠辨識；正確的標籤條件屬於真正寫出 ResourceTag/Environment NonProduction 的那一個選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_ec2_tag-owner.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/service-authorization/latest/reference/list_amazonec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_condition.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_action.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":195,"question_en":"A company is developing an application that will generate log events. The log events consist of five distinct metrics every one tenth of a second and produce a large amount of data. The company needs to configure the application to write the logs to Amazon Timestream. The company will configure a daily query against the Timestream table. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the FASTEST query performance? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一款应用程序，该程序每十分之一秒会生成包含五项不同指标的日志事件，从而产生大量 数据。 该公司需要将应用程序配置为将日志写入亚马逊 Timestream。该公司将针对 Timestream 表配置每日查询。 哪种步骤组合能以最快的速度满足这些查询性能要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use batch writes to write multiple log events in a single write operation.","B":"Write each log event as a single write operation.","C":"Treat each log as a single-measure record.","D":"Treat each log as a multi-measure record.","E":"Configure the memory store retention period to be longer than the magnetic store retention period.","F":"Configure the memory store retention period to be shorter than the magnetic store retention period."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用批量写入在单次写入操作中写入多个日志事件。","B":"将每个日志事件作为一次单独的写入操作来写入。","C":"将每个日志条目视为单个度量记录。","D":"将每个日志条目视为多度量记录。","E":"将内存存储保留期设置为长于磁盘存储保留期。","F":"将内存存储保留期设置为短于磁盘存储保留期。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is FASTEST QUERY PERFORMANCE for a DAILY (analytical) query over a large volume of data where 5 distinct metrics share the same timestamp. (D) Multi-measure records are the documented choice when an application emits multiple measures at the same time instant: AWS states 'Multi-measure records results in lower query latency for most query types when compared to single-measure records' and that for queries referencing three or more measures multi-measure records also lower bytes scanned (the query references 5 measures). (F) The Configuring Timestream guide says the memory store is optimized for fast point-in-time queries on small amounts of recent data, while the magnetic store is 'optimized for fast analytical queries that process medium to large volumes of data'; for daily/weekly/monthly queries you should set a smaller memory store retention and let more data flow to the magnetic store, so memory retention should be SHORTER than magnetic retention. (A) The Writes best practices direct you to 'batch multiple records in a single request to optimize data ingestion performance' and to batch records from the same time series/measure name, which is the correct ingestion approach for a high-frequency producer (every 1/10 second). Thus A, D, F.","explanation_zh":"此題限定詞為「最快查詢效能 (FASTEST QUERY PERFORMANCE)」，情境是針對大量資料、每筆於同一時間戳記產生 5 個不同 metrics、且每日執行一次的分析型查詢。(D) 當應用程式在同一時間瞬間發出多個 measures 時，官方建議使用 multi-measure records：AWS 明確指出『multi-measure records 在大多數查詢類型下相較 single-measure records 可帶來更低的查詢延遲 (lower query latency)』，且查詢參考三個以上 measures 時 multi-measure 掃描的位元組更少（本題查詢涉及 5 個 measures）。(F) Configuring Timestream 文件說明 memory store 適合針對少量近期資料的快速 point-in-time 查詢，而 magnetic store『針對處理中大量資料的快速分析型查詢 (fast analytical queries) 進行最佳化』；對於每日/每週/每月查詢，應設定較短的 memory store 保留期，讓更多資料流入 magnetic store，因此 memory 保留期應「短於」magnetic 保留期。(A) Writes 最佳實務建議『在單一請求中批次寫入多筆記錄以最佳化資料寫入效能 (batch writes)』，並批次同一時間序列/measure name 的記錄，對於每 0.1 秒高頻產生資料的應用是正確做法。故選 A、D、F。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Writing each log event as a single write operation contradicts the Timestream Writes best practice to 'batch multiple records in a single request'; it adds overhead and is the opposite of recommended ingestion design.","why_zh":"將每筆 log event 以單獨寫入操作送出，違反 Timestream Writes 最佳實務『於單一請求中批次寫入多筆記錄』，會增加負擔，與建議的寫入設計相反。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Single-measure records are intended for devices emitting different metrics at different times. Here 5 metrics share the same timestamp, so single-measure modeling raises storage, bytes scanned, and query latency versus multi-measure.","why_zh":"single-measure records 適用於裝置在不同時間發出不同 metrics 的情況。本題 5 個 metrics 共用同一時間戳記，採 single-measure 反而提高儲存、掃描位元組與查詢延遲，劣於 multi-measure。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Setting memory store retention longer than magnetic store keeps large historical data in the memory store, which is optimized only for fast point-in-time queries on small recent data; daily analytical queries over large data perform best in the magnetic store, so this hurts query performance.","why_zh":"將 memory store 保留期設得比 magnetic store 長，會把大量歷史資料留在僅針對少量近期資料 point-in-time 查詢最佳化的 memory store；每日針對大量資料的分析型查詢在 magnetic store 表現最佳，故此設定反而損害查詢效能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/timestream/latest/developerguide/data-modeling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/timestream/latest/developerguide/configuration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/timestream/latest/developerguide/data-ingest.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/timestream/latest/developerguide/queries-bp.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":196,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer has created an AWS CloudFormation template that deploys an application on Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances run Amazon Linux. The application is deployed to the EC2 instances by using shell scripts that contain user data. The EC2 instances have an IAM instance profile that has an IAM role with the AmazonSSMManagedinstanceCore managed policy attached. The DevOps engineer has modified the user data in the CloudFormation template to install a new version of the application. The engineer has also applied the stack update. However, the application was not updated on the running EC2 instances. The engineer needs to ensure that the changes to the application are installed on the running EC2 instances. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于在亚马逊上部署应用程序。 EC2 实例。这些 EC2 实例运行的是 Amazon Linux 操作系统。应用程序通过包含用户数据的 shell 脚本部 署到 EC2 实例上。EC2 实例具有一个 IAM 实例配置文件，该配置文件包含一个附加了 AmazonSSMManagedinstanceCore 管理策略的 IAM 角色。 DevOps 工程师已在 CloudFormation 模板中修改了用户数据以安装应用程序的新版本，并已应用了堆栈 更新。然而，运行中的 EC2 实例上的应用程序并未更新。工程师需要确保将应用程序的更改安装到运 行中的 EC2 实例上。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure the user data content to use the Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) multipart format. Set the scripts-user parameter to always in the text/cloud-config section.","B":"Refactor the user data commands to use the cfn-init helper script. Update the user data to install and configure the cfn-hup and cfn-init helper scripts to monitor and apply the metadata changes.","C":"Configure an EC2 launch template for the EC2 instances. Create a new EC2 Auto Scaling group. Associate the Auto Scaling group with the EC2 launch template. Use the AutoScalingScheduledAction update policy for the Auto Scaling group.","D":"Refactor the user data commands to use an AWS Systems Manager document (SSM document). Add an AWS CLI command in the user data to use Systems Manager Run Command to apply the SSM document to the EC2 instances.","E":"Refactor the user data command to use an AWS Systems Manager document (SSM document). Use Systems Manager State Manager to create an association between the SSM document and the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"将用户数据内容配置为使用多用途互联网邮件扩展（MIME）多部分格式。在 text/cloud-config 部 分将 scripts-user 参数设置为 always 。","B":"重构用户数据命令以使用 cfn-init 辅助脚本。更新用户数据以安装和配置 cfn-hup 和 cfn-init 辅助脚本， 以监控并应用元数据更改。","C":"为 EC2 实例配置一个 EC2 启动模板。创建一个新的 EC2 自动缩放组。将自动缩放组与 EC2 启动模 板相关联。为自动缩放组使用 AutoScalingScheduledAction 更新策略。","D":"重构用户数据命令以使用 AWS 系统管理器文档（SSM 文档）。在用户数据中添加一个 AWS CLI 命 令，使用系统管理器运行命令将 SSM 文档应用于 EC2 实例。","E":"将用户数据命令重构为使用 AWS 系统管理器文档（SSM 文档）。使用系统管理器状态管理器在 SSM 文档和 EC2 实例之间创建关联。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"EC2 user data is executed by cloud-init only once at first launch by default. When the engineer modifies the user data property in the CloudFormation template and runs UpdateStack, CloudFormation updates the property but does not re-run user data on already-running instances (and a user-data-only change does not trigger replacement), so the application is never updated. Two distinct, complete, AWS-recommended patterns fix this. Option B refactors user data to use cfn-init (reads AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata) plus the cfn-hup daemon, which detects resource-metadata changes and runs cfn-init when UpdateStack changes the metadata; the cfn-hup docs explicitly state this 'allows you to make configuration updates on your running Amazon EC2 instances through the UpdateStack API action.' Option E moves the logic into an SSM document and uses State Manager to create an association that applies/enforces the desired state on the running instances on a schedule; the instances already have SSM Agent (Amazon Linux) and the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore policy, so the association can run immediately and on each cycle. Both run on the existing running instances, which is the requirement.","explanation_zh":"EC2 user data 預設只由 cloud-init 在首次啟動時執行一次。當工程師修改 CloudFormation 範本中的 user data 屬性並執行 UpdateStack 時，CloudFormation 雖更新了該屬性，但不會在已執行中的執行個體上重新執行 user data（且僅變更 user data 不會觸發替換），因此應用程式不會被更新。兩個各自完整且為 AWS 建議的做法可解決此問題。選項 B 將 user data 重構為使用 cfn-init（讀取 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata），並安裝設定 cfn-hup 常駐程式；cfn-hup 會偵測資源 metadata 的變更，並在 UpdateStack 改變 metadata 時執行 cfn-init。cfn-hup 文件明確指出此機制『可讓你透過 UpdateStack API 動作對執行中的 EC2 執行個體進行設定更新』。選項 E 將邏輯移入 SSM document，並使用 State Manager 建立 association，依排程在執行中的執行個體上套用並強制維持所需狀態；這些執行個體已具備 SSM Agent（Amazon Linux）與 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 政策，association 可立即且週期性地執行。兩者皆在現有執行中的執行個體上運作，符合需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Setting cloud-init's scripts-user to 'always' via MIME multipart makes user data run on every boot/reboot, not on a stack update. The instances are already running and a user-data property change does not reboot them, so the new version is still not applied to the running instances.","why_zh":"透過 MIME multipart 將 cloud-init 的 scripts-user 設為 'always' 只會讓 user data 在每次開機/重啟時執行，而非在堆疊更新時。執行個體已在執行中，且變更 user data 屬性不會重啟它們，因此新版本仍不會套用到執行中的執行個體。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating a brand-new launch template and a new Auto Scaling group does not touch the existing running instances. The AutoScalingScheduledAction update policy only governs scheduled scaling actions during a stack update; it does not roll or replace instances to pick up new user data (that would be AutoScalingRollingUpdate, and the instances aren't even in an ASG). It is a large refactor that still fails the requirement.","why_zh":"建立全新的 launch template 與新的 Auto Scaling group 並不會影響現有執行中的執行個體。AutoScalingScheduledAction 更新政策僅控管堆疊更新期間的排程擴縮動作，並不會輪替或替換執行個體以套用新 user data（那是 AutoScalingRollingUpdate，而這些執行個體甚至不在 ASG 中）。這是大幅重構卻仍無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Placing the AWS CLI Run Command call inside user data is self-defeating: user data only executes at launch, so on a stack update it will not run on the already-running instances. The Run Command would only fire on a fresh launch, leaving running instances un-updated.","why_zh":"把呼叫 Run Command 的 AWS CLI 放進 user data 是自相矛盾的：user data 只在啟動時執行，因此堆疊更新時不會在已執行中的執行個體上執行。Run Command 只會在全新啟動時觸發，執行中的執行個體仍不會被更新。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-hup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-init.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-init.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/user-data.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":197,"question_en":"A company is refactoring applications to use AWS. The company identifies an internal web application that needs to make Amazon S3 API calls in a specific AWS account. The company wants to use its existing identity provider (IdP) auth.company.com for authentication. The IdP supports only OpenID Connect (OIDC). A DevOps engineer needs to secure the web application's access to the AWS account. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在重构应用程序以使用 AWS。该公司确定了一个内部网络应用程序，需要在特定的 AWS 账 户中调用 Amazon S3 API。 该公司希望使用其现有的身份提供商 auth.company.com 进行身份验证。该身份提供商仅支持 OpenID Connect（OIDC）。一位 DevOps 工程师需要确保网络应用程序能够安全访问 AWS 账户。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). Configure an IdP. Upload the IdP metadata from the existing IdP.","B":"Create an IAM IdP by using the provider URL, audience, and signature from the existing IP.","C":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows the necessary S3 actions. Configure the role's trust policy to allow the OIDC IP to assume the role if the sts.amazon.com:aud context key is appid_from_idp.","D":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows the necessary S3 actions. Configure the role's trust policy to allow the OIDC IP to assume the role if the auth.company.com:aud context key is appid_from_idp.","E":"Configure the web application to use the AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity API operation to retrieve temporary credentials. Use the temporary credentials to make the S3 API calls.","F":"Configure the web application to use the GetFederationToken API operation to retrieve temporary credentials. Use the temporary credentials to make the S3 API calls."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）。配置身份提供方。上传现有身份提供方的元数据。","B":"使用现有 IP 的提供程序 URL、受众和签名创建一个 IAM 身份提供商。","C":"创建一个具有允许执行必要 S3 操作策略的 IAM 角色。配置该角色的信任策略，以便在 sts.amazon. com:aud 上下文键为 appid_from_idp 时允许 OIDC IP 假冒该角色。","D":"创建一个具有允许执行必要 S3 操作策略的 IAM 角色。配置该角色的信任策略，以便在 auth. company.com:aud 上下文键为 appid_from_idp 时，允许 OIDC IP 假冒该角色。","E":"配置网络应用程序使用 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity API 操作来获取临时凭证。使用临时凭证 来调用 S3 API。","F":"配置网络应用程序使用 GetFederationToken API 操作来获取临时凭证。使用临时凭证来调用 S3 API。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario requires an internal web application to make S3 API calls authenticated by an existing OIDC-only IdP (auth.company.com). The standard AWS pattern is OIDC web identity federation: (B) Create an IAM OIDC identity provider using the provider URL (issuer), audience (client/app ID), and the thumbprint/signature of the IdP's certificate - these are exactly the values AWS requires to register an IAM OIDC IdP. (D) Create an IAM role with an S3 permissions policy and a trust policy that allows sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity, restricting it with the aud context key prefixed by the IdP's fully qualified URL. The IAM docs explicitly state: 'For OIDC providers, use the fully qualified URL of the OIDC IdP with the aud context key, such as server.example.com:aud: appid_from_oidc_idp' - matching auth.company.com:aud = appid_from_idp. (E) The web application calls sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity, passing the OIDC token, to get temporary credentials for the S3 calls; this API does not require any long-term AWS credentials and validates the caller via the web identity token. B, D, and E together form the complete documented OIDC federation flow.","explanation_zh":"情境要求內部 web 應用程式透過既有的僅支援 OIDC 的 IdP (auth.company.com) 進行驗證後呼叫 S3 API。標準 AWS 做法是 OIDC web identity federation:(B) 使用 provider URL(issuer)、audience(client/app ID)以及 IdP 憑證的 thumbprint/signature 建立 IAM OIDC identity provider,這些正是 AWS 註冊 IAM OIDC IdP 所需的值。(D) 建立具備 S3 權限政策的 IAM role,其 trust policy 允許 sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity,並以 IdP 完整 URL 為前綴的 aud context key 限制。IAM 文件明確說明:'對於 OIDC providers,使用 OIDC IdP 的完整 URL 搭配 aud context key,例如 server.example.com:aud: appid_from_oidc_idp',正好對應 auth.company.com:aud = appid_from_idp。(E) Web 應用程式呼叫 sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity 並帶入 OIDC token 取得臨時憑證來呼叫 S3;此 API 不需任何長期 AWS 憑證,而是透過 web identity token 驗證呼叫者。B、D、E 共同構成完整的 OIDC federation 文件化流程。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS IAM Identity Center is for human user single sign-on into the AWS console/CLI (typically via SAML metadata), not for a web application making programmatic S3 API calls via OIDC. Uploading IdP metadata to Identity Center does not produce the role-assumption flow the application needs.","why_zh":"AWS IAM Identity Center 是給人類使用者 SSO 登入 AWS console/CLI(通常使用 SAML metadata),並非給 web 應用程式透過 OIDC 進行程式化 S3 API 呼叫。上傳 IdP metadata 到 Identity Center 無法產生應用程式所需的 role-assumption 流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The trust policy condition key is wrong. AWS docs require the aud key to be prefixed by the OIDC IdP's fully qualified URL (auth.company.com:aud), not sts.amazon.com:aud. The string sts.amazon.com is not a valid context-key prefix for OIDC federation (and is even misspelled vs sts.amazonaws.com).","why_zh":"trust policy 的 condition key 錯誤。AWS 文件要求 aud key 以 OIDC IdP 的完整 URL 為前綴(auth.company.com:aud),而非 sts.amazon.com:aud。sts.amazon.com 並非 OIDC federation 的有效 context-key 前綴(且拼字與 sts.amazonaws.com 不符)。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"GetFederationToken is for a custom identity broker and must be called using long-term IAM user credentials. It does not consume an OIDC web identity token, so it is not the correct API for federating an OIDC-authenticated web app, and it would require embedding long-term AWS credentials.","why_zh":"GetFederationToken 用於自訂 identity broker,且必須以長期 IAM user 憑證呼叫。它不接受 OIDC web identity token,因此不是 OIDC 驗證 web 應用程式的正確 API,且會需要嵌入長期 AWS 憑證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create_for-idp_oidc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_create_oidc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/API_AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_request.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_oidc.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":198,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon RDS for all databases in its AWS accounts. The company uses AWS Control Tower to build a landing zone that has an audit and logging account. All databases must be encrypted at rest for compliance reasons. The company's security engineer needs to receive notification about any noncompliant databases that are in the company’s accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"该公司在其所有 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon RDS 来管理数据库。该公司使用 AWS Control Tower 构建了一 个包含审计和日志记录账户的着陆区。出于合规性原因，所有数据库在静止状态下都必须进行加密。该公 司的安全工程师需要收到有关其账户中任何不符合规定的数据库的通知。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Control Tower to activate the optional detective control (guardrail) to determine whether the RDS storage is encrypted. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in the company's audit account. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to filter noncompliant events from the AWS Control Tower control (guardrail) to notify the SNS topic. Subscribe the security engineer's email address to the SNS topic.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy AWS Lambda functions to every account. Write the Lambda function code to determine whether the RDS storage is encrypted in the account the function is deployed to. Send the findings as an Amazon CloudWatch metric to the management account. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Create a CloudWatch alarm that notifies the SNS topic when metric thresholds are met. Subscribe the security engineer's email address to the SNS topic.","C":"Create a custom AWS Config rule in every account to determine whether the RDS storage is encrypted. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in the audit account. Create an Amazon EventBidge rule to filter noncompliant events from the AWS Control Tower control (guardrail) to notify the SNS topic. Subscribe the security engineer's email address to the SNS topic.","D":"Launch an Amazon C2 instance. Run an hourly cron job by using the AWS CLI to determine whether the RDS storage is encrypted in each AWS account. Store the results in an RDS database. Notify the security engineer by sending email messages from the EC2 instance when noncompliance is detected"},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 控制塔激活可选的检测控制（防护栏），以确定 RDS 存储是否已加密。在公司的审计账户中 创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，从 AWS 控制塔控制（防护栏）中筛选出不符合规定的事件，并通知 SNS 主题。将安全工程师的电子邮件地址 订阅到 SNS 主题。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 AWS Lambda 函数部署到每个账户。编写 Lambda 函数代码以确定 函数部署到的账户中的 RDS 存储是否已加密。将发现结果作为 Amazon CloudWatch 指标发送到管理账 户。创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，当 指标阈值达到时通知 SNS 主题。将安全工程师的电子邮件地址订阅到 SNS 主题。","C":"在每个账户中创建自定义的 AWS Config 规则，以确定 RDS 存储是否已加密。在审计账户中创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，从 AWS 控制塔控 制（防护栏）中筛选出不符合要求的事件，并通知 SNS 主题。将安全工程师的电子邮件地址订阅到 SNS 主题。","D":"启动一个 Amazon C2 实例。使用 AWS CLI 每小时运行一次 cron 任务，以确定每个 AWS 账户中的 RDS 存储是否已加密。将结果存储在 RDS 数据库中。当检测到不符合规定的情况时，从 EC2 实例发送电子 邮件通知安全工程师。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Control Tower already provides a built-in, fully managed detective control (guardrail) named 'Detect Whether Storage Encryption is Enabled for Amazon RDS Database Instances'. It is a strongly recommended detective control that is not enabled by default (the 'optional' control referenced in A) and is implemented behind the scenes with an AWS Config rule, so it produces compliance/noncompliance findings automatically across all enrolled accounts. Activating this managed control, then creating an SNS topic in the audit account (the account Control Tower designates for security and compliance aggregation, where Config compliance notifications already land) and an EventBridge rule that filters the noncompliant findings to publish to that topic, requires zero custom code and is the MOST operationally efficient solution. Options B (StackSets + custom Lambda in every account + cross-account CloudWatch metrics to the management account) and C (a custom AWS Config rule in every account, which is also self-contradictory because it then references filtering events from the Control Tower guardrail it never created) add significant build-and-maintain overhead and duplicate a capability that already exists natively. Option D (an EC2 instance running hourly cron jobs with the CLI, storing results in RDS, and emailing from the instance) is fragile, unscalable, and the highest operational burden.","explanation_zh":"AWS Control Tower 已內建一個完全託管的偵測型控制 (detective control/guardrail)，名為 'Detect Whether Storage Encryption is Enabled for Amazon RDS Database Instances'。它屬於強烈建議 (strongly recommended) 的偵測型控制，預設不啟用 (即選項 A 所稱的「optional 偵測型控制」)，背後以 AWS Config rule 實作，因此會自動在所有已納管帳戶中產生合規/不合規結果。啟用此託管控制後，於 audit 帳戶 (Control Tower 指定用來彙整安全與合規通知、Config 合規通知本來就會送達的帳戶) 建立 SNS topic，再以 EventBridge rule 過濾不合規結果並發布到該 topic，完全不需自訂程式碼，因此營運效率最高。選項 B (用 StackSets 在每個帳戶部署自訂 Lambda，並跨帳戶把 CloudWatch metric 送到 management 帳戶) 與選項 C (在每個帳戶建立自訂 AWS Config rule，且敘述自相矛盾，因為後面又去過濾從未建立的 Control Tower guardrail 事件) 都會增加大量建置與維運負擔，且重複了原生既有的功能。選項 D (用 EC2 跑每小時 cron 與 CLI、把結果存到 RDS、再由 EC2 寄信) 脆弱、無法擴展，營運負擔最高。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Deploying custom Lambda to every account via StackSets, writing custom encryption-check code, and piping cross-account CloudWatch metrics to the management account is high operational overhead and reinvents the managed RDS-encryption guardrail Control Tower already offers; security/compliance monitoring should target the audit account, not the management account.","why_zh":"用 StackSets 在每個帳戶部署自訂 Lambda、撰寫加密檢查程式碼、再跨帳戶把 CloudWatch metric 送到 management 帳戶，營運負擔極高，且重造 Control Tower 已提供的 RDS 加密託管 guardrail；安全/合規監控應導向 audit 帳戶而非 management 帳戶。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Authoring and deploying a custom AWS Config rule in every account is unnecessary because a native managed guardrail already detects RDS encryption; the option is also self-contradictory, claiming to filter noncompliant events from the Control Tower guardrail it never enabled, and it carries more overhead than activating the built-in control.","why_zh":"在每個帳戶撰寫並部署自訂 AWS Config rule 並無必要，因為原生託管 guardrail 已能偵測 RDS 加密；此選項亦自相矛盾，宣稱要過濾它從未啟用的 Control Tower guardrail 不合規事件，且比啟用內建控制負擔更大。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EC2 instance running an hourly cron job with the CLI, storing results in RDS, and sending email directly is the least efficient and most fragile approach: it requires building, securing, patching, and operating compute and cross-account access, with no native managed compliance detection.","why_zh":"用 EC2 每小時跑 cron 與 CLI、把結果存到 RDS、再直接寄信，是效率最低且最脆弱的做法：需自行建置、保護、修補與維運運算資源與跨帳戶存取，且完全沒有原生託管的合規偵測。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/strongly-recommended-detective-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/detective-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/receive-notifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-controltower.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":199,"question_en":"A company is migrating from its on-premises data center to AWS. The company currently uses a custom on-premises CI/CD pipeline solution to build and package software. The company wants its software packages and dependent public repositories to be available in AWS CodeArtifact to facilitate the creation of application-specific pipelines. Which combination of steps should the company take to update the CI/CD pipeline solution and to configure CodeArtifact with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在从其本地数据中心迁移到 AWS。该公司目前使用自定义的本地 CI/CD 管道解决方案来构建 和打包软件。 该公司希望其软件包及相关的公共存储库能在 AWS CodeArtifact 中获取，以方便创建特定于应用程序 的流水线。 公司应采取哪两种步骤的组合来更新 CI/CD 管道解决方案，并以最低的操作开销配置 CodeArtifact？ （选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the CI/CD pipeline to create a VM image that contains newly packaged software. Use AWS Import/Export to make the VM image available as an Amazon EC2 AMI. Launch the AMI with an attached IAM instance profile that allows CodeArtifact actions. Use AWS CLI commands to publish the packages to a CodeArtifact repository.","B":"Create an AWS Identity and Access Management Roles Anywhere trust anchor. Create an IAM role that allows CodeArtifact actions and that has a trust relationship on the trust anchor. Update the on- premises CI/CD pipeline to assume the new IAM role and to publish the packages to CodeArtifact.","C":"Create a new Amazon S3 bucket. Generate a presigned URL that allows the PutObject request. Update the on-premises CI/CD pipeline to use the presigned URL to publish the packages from the on- premises location to the S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function that runs when packages are created in the bucket through a put command. Configure the Lambda function to publish the packages to CodeArtifact.","D":"For each public repository, create a CodeArutact repository that is configured with an external connection. Configure the dependent repositories as upstream public repositories.","E":"Create a Codeartitact repository that is configured with a set of external connections to the public repositories. Configure the external connections to be downstream of the repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 CI/CD 管道以创建包含新打包软件的虚拟机映像。使用 AWS 导入/导出服务将虚拟机映像作为 Amazon EC2 AMI 提供。使用允许执行 CodeArtifact 操作的 IAM 实例配置文件启动 AMI。使用 AWS CLI 命令将软件包发布到 CodeArtifact 存储库。","B":"创建一个 AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）Roles Anywhere 信任锚。创建一个允许执行 CodeArtifact 操作 且与信任锚建立信任关系的 IAM 角色。更新本地 CI/CD 管道以承担新 IAM 角色，并将软件包发布 到 CodeArtifact。","C":"创建一个新的 Amazon S3 存储桶。生成一个预签名 URL，允许执行 PutObject 请求。更新本地的 CI/CD 管道，使其使用预签名 URL 将本地位置的软件包发布到 S3 存储桶。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，当 通过 put 命令在存储桶中创建软件包时运行。配置 Lambda 函数将软件包发布到 CodeArtifact。","D":"对于每个公共代码库，创建一个配置了外部连接的 CodeArutact 代码库。将依赖的代码库配置为 上游公共代码库。","E":"创建一个 Codeartitact 代码库，并将其配置为与公共代码库建立一组外部连接。将这些外部连接配置 为该代码库的下游。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The pipeline runs in the on-premises data center (outside AWS), so the lowest-overhead way to give it AWS credentials is IAM Roles Anywhere (B): create a trust anchor referencing the CA, create an IAM role with CodeArtifact permissions that trusts the trust anchor, and have the on-prem pipeline assume the role with its X.509 certificate to publish packages directly. This eliminates long-term credentials and needs no extra AWS infrastructure. For dependent public repositories (D), the documented design is one CodeArtifact repository per public repository, each with its own external connection, and other repositories configured to use those as upstream repositories. The CodeArtifact docs state explicitly that 'Each CodeArtifact repository can only have one external connection,' and recommend 'one repository per domain with an external connection to a given public repository... configure all the other repositories with an upstream to it.' This matches D and disqualifies E.","explanation_zh":"CI/CD pipeline 執行在地端資料中心（AWS 之外），因此以最少維運負擔提供 AWS 憑證的方式是 IAM Roles Anywhere（B）：建立指向 CA 的 trust anchor，建立具 CodeArtifact 權限且信任該 trust anchor 的 IAM role，地端 pipeline 以其 X.509 憑證取得臨時憑證並直接發佈套件。這免除長期憑證，且不需額外 AWS 基礎設施。對於相依的公開儲存庫（D），官方建議的設計是「每個公開儲存庫對應一個 CodeArtifact repository，各自設定自己的 external connection」，其他儲存庫再將其設為 upstream。CodeArtifact 文件明確指出『每個 CodeArtifact repository 只能有一個 external connection』，並建議『每個 domain 對單一公開儲存庫配置一個帶 external connection 的 repository，其餘 repository 以 upstream 連到它』。這正好對應 D，並否定 E。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Building a VM image, importing it as an EC2 AMI, and launching instances to run AWS CLI publish commands is enormous operational overhead and unnecessary. AWS Import/Export is a deprecated physical-disk shipping service (not VM image conversion). This violates the LEAST operational overhead requirement.","why_zh":"建立 VM 映像、匯入為 EC2 AMI 並啟動執行個體來跑 CLI 發佈指令，維運負擔極高且毫無必要。AWS Import/Export 是已淘汰的實體磁碟運送服務（並非 VM 映像轉換）。違反最少維運負擔要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Routing packages through an S3 bucket via a presigned URL and then a Lambda function to relay them into CodeArtifact adds multiple moving parts (bucket, URL generation, event trigger, Lambda code) when the pipeline could publish directly to CodeArtifact. Far more operational overhead than IAM Roles Anywhere.","why_zh":"透過 presigned URL 將套件送到 S3，再以 Lambda 轉發到 CodeArtifact，增加了多個元件（bucket、URL 產生、事件觸發、Lambda 程式碼），而 pipeline 其實可直接發佈到 CodeArtifact。維運負擔遠高於 IAM Roles Anywhere。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A single CodeArtifact repository cannot hold 'a set of external connections' — the docs state each repository can have only one external connection. Also, external connections are not configured 'downstream of the repository'; a repo with an external connection serves its downstream repositories. The correct pattern is one repo per public repo plus upstreams (D).","why_zh":"單一 CodeArtifact repository 無法擁有『一組 external connections』——文件指出每個 repository 只能有一個 external connection。且 external connection 並非設定為『repository 的下游』；帶有 external connection 的 repo 是供其下游 repo 使用。正確模式是每個公開 repo 一個 repository 加上 upstream（D）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/external-connection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdkref/latest/guide/access-rolesanywhere.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":200,"question_en":"A DevOps team uses AWS CodePipeline, AWS CodeBuild, and AWS CodeDeploy to deploy an application. The application is a REST API that uses AWS Lambda functions and Amazon API Gateway. Recent deployments have introduced errors that have affected many customers. The DevOps team needs a solution that reverts to the most recent stable version of the application when an error is detected. The solution must affect the fewest customers possible. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队使用 AWS CodePipeline、AWS CodeBuild 和 AWS CodeDeploy 来部署应用程序。该应用 程序是一个使用 AWS Lambda 函数和 Amazon API Gateway 的 REST API。最近的部署引入了错误，影响 了许多客户。 当检测到错误时，DevOps 团队需要一个解决方案，能够回退到应用程序的最新稳定版本。该解决方案对 客户的干扰应尽可能小。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set the deployment configuration in CodeDeploy to LambdaAllAtOnce. Configure automatic rollbacks on the deployment group. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that detects HTTP Bad Gateway errors on API Gateway. Configure the deployment group to roll back when the number of alarms meets the alarm threshold.","B":"Set the deployment configuration in CodeDeploy to LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes. Configure automatic rollbacks on the deployment group. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that detects HTTP Bad Gateway errors on API Gateway. Configure the deployment group to roll back when the number of alarms meets the alarm threshold.","C":"Set the deployment configuration in CodeDeploy to LambdaAllAtOnce. Configure manual rollbacks on the deployment group. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send notifications every time a deployment fails. Configure the SNS topic to invoke a new Lambda function that stops the current deployment and starts the most recent successful deployment.","D":"Set the deployment configuration in CodeDeploy to LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes. Configure manual rollbacks on the deployment group. Create a metric filter on an Amazon CloudWatch log group for API Gateway to monitor HTTP Bad Gateway errors. Configure the metric filter to invoke a new Lambda function that stops the current deployment and starts the most recent successful deployment."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CodeDeploy 中将部署配置设置为 LambdaAllAtOnce。在部署组上配置自动回滚。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，用于检测 API Gateway 上的 HTTP 错误网关错误。配置部署组，使其在警报数量达 到警报阈值时回滚。","B":"在 CodeDeploy 中将部署配置设置为 LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes。在部署组中配置自动回滚。创建 一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，用于检测 API Gateway 上的 HTTP 网关错误。配置部署组，使其在警报 数量达到警报阈值时回滚。","C":"在 CodeDeploy 中将部署配置设置为 LambdaAllAtOnce。在部署组上配置手动回滚。创建一个 Amazon 简 单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，以便每次部署失败时发送通知。配置 SNS 主题以调用一个新的 Lambda 函数，该函数会停止当前部署并启动最近一次成功的部署。","D":"在 CodeDeploy 中将部署配置设置为 LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes。在部署组上配置手动回滚。在 API Gateway 的 Amazon CloudWatch 日志组上创建一个指标过滤器，以监控 HTTP 网关错误。配置指标 过滤器以调用一个新的 Lambda 函数，该函数会停止当前部署并启动最近一次成功的部署。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: revert to the last stable version when an error is detected (automatic rollback), affect the fewest customers possible (canary traffic shifting so only a small slice of users hit the new version during validation), and do this with the MOST operational efficiency (use built-in CodeDeploy features, not custom code). Option B uses LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes, which per AWS docs shifts only 10 percent of traffic initially and the remaining 90 percent 10 minutes later, so at most 10 percent of customers are exposed to a faulty release before rollback. It pairs this with native automatic rollbacks triggered by a CloudWatch alarm on API Gateway errors, which CodeDeploy supports directly (roll back when a monitoring threshold/alarm is met). This is fully managed with no custom Lambda or wiring, so it is the most operationally efficient. The canary window also gives the alarm time to fire before full traffic shift, minimizing impact.","explanation_zh":"需求為:偵測到錯誤時回復到最近的穩定版本(自動 rollback)、影響最少的客戶(canary 流量切換,只讓少部分使用者在驗證期間命中新版本),並且要以最高的運維效率達成(使用 CodeDeploy 內建功能,而非自訂程式碼)。選項 B 使用 LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes,依 AWS 文件其初始只切換 10% 流量,剩餘 90% 在 10 分鐘後切換,因此在 rollback 前最多只有 10% 客戶接觸到有問題的版本。它搭配由 API Gateway 錯誤的 CloudWatch alarm 觸發的原生自動 rollback,CodeDeploy 直接支援此功能(當監控門檻/alarm 達標時 rollback)。整套為全託管、無需自訂 Lambda 或額外接線,因此運維效率最高。canary 視窗也讓 alarm 有時間在完整流量切換前觸發,將影響降到最低。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"LambdaAllAtOnce shifts 100 percent of traffic to the new version immediately, so all customers are affected before any rollback can occur. This violates the 'affect the fewest customers possible' requirement even though the automatic-rollback-on-alarm mechanism is correct.","why_zh":"LambdaAllAtOnce 立即將 100% 流量切到新版本,因此在任何 rollback 發生前所有客戶都會受影響,違反『影響最少客戶』的需求,即使其『以 alarm 觸發自動 rollback』的機制是正確的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses LambdaAllAtOnce (affects all customers) and manual rollbacks driven by a custom SNS topic invoking a custom Lambda that stops the current deployment and starts the prior one. That is high operational overhead and fails both the 'fewest customers' and 'most operational efficiency' requirements; CodeDeploy already provides native automatic rollback.","why_zh":"使用 LambdaAllAtOnce(影響所有客戶)並以自訂 SNS topic 觸發自訂 Lambda 停止當前部署並啟動前一版來進行手動 rollback。運維負擔高,同時違反『最少客戶』與『最高運維效率』需求;CodeDeploy 本身就提供原生自動 rollback。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Canary correctly limits customer impact, but it uses manual rollbacks plus a custom CloudWatch Logs metric filter that invokes a custom Lambda to stop and restart deployments. Building and maintaining that custom orchestration is far more operational overhead than CodeDeploy's built-in automatic rollback on a CloudWatch alarm, so it loses on the MOST operational efficiency qualifier.","why_zh":"Canary 正確地限制了客戶影響,但採用手動 rollback 加上自訂的 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 觸發自訂 Lambda 來停止並重啟部署。建置與維護這套自訂編排的運維負擔遠高於 CodeDeploy 內建的『以 CloudWatch alarm 觸發自動 rollback』,因此在『最高運維效率』這個限定條件上落敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-rollback-and-redeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-configure-advanced-options.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":201,"question_en":"A company recently deployed its web application on AWS. The company is preparing for a large-scale sales event and must ensure that the web application can scale to meet the demand. The application's frontend infrastructure includes an Amazon CloudFront distribution that has an Amazon S3 bucket as an origin. The backend infrastructure includes an Amazon API Gateway API, several AWS Lambda functions, and an Amazon Aurora DB cluster. The company's DevOps engineer conducts a load test and identifies that the Lambda functions can fulfil the peak number of requests. However, the DevOps engineer notices request latency during the initial burst of requests. Most of the requests to the Lambda functions produce queries to the database. A large portion of the invocation time is used to establish database connections. Which combination of steps will provide the application with the required scalability? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近将其网络应用程序部署在了亚马逊网络服务（AWS）上。该公司正在为一场大规模的促 销活动做准备，必须确保网络应用程序能够扩展以满足需求。 该应用程序的前端基础设施包括一个以 Amazon S3 存储桶作为源的 Amazon CloudFront 分发。后端基础设 施包括一个 Amazon API Gateway API、若干个 AWS Lambda 函数以及一个 Amazon Aurora 数据库集群。 该公司的 DevOps 工程师进行了负载测试，发现 Lambda 函数能够满足峰值请求数量。然而，DevOps 工程 师注意到在请求初始激增时存在请求延迟。大多数对 Lambda 函数的请求都会生成对数据库的查询。调用 时间的很大一部分用于建立数据库连接。 哪些步骤组合能为应用程序提供所需的可扩展性？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure a higher reserved concurrency for the Lambda functions.","B":"Configure a higher provisioned concurrency for the Lambda functions.","C":"Convert the DB cluster to an Aurora global database. Add additional Aurora Replicas in AWS Regions based on the locations of the company's customers.","D":"Refactor the Lambda functions. Move the code blocks that initialize database connections into the function handlers.","E":"Use Amazon RDS Proxy to create a proxy for the Aurora database. Update the Lambda functions to use the proxy endpoints for database connections."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 Lambda 函数配置更高的预留并发量。","B":"为 Lambda 函数配置更高的预置并发量。","C":"将数据库集群转换为 Aurora 全球数据库。根据公司客户所在的位置，在 AWS 区域中添加额外的 Aurora 副本。","D":"重构 Lambda 函数。将初始化数据库连接的代码块移至函数处理程序中。","E":"使用 Amazon RDS Proxy 为 Aurora 数据库创建代理。更新 Lambda 函数以使用代理端点进行数据库连 接。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario describes three scalability concerns. (1) 'Request latency during the initial burst of requests' is a cold-start problem; provisioned concurrency (B) pre-initializes execution environments so they respond immediately with low latency, which is exactly what AWS documents it for. (2) 'A large portion of the invocation time is used to establish database connections' is solved by Amazon RDS Proxy (E), which pools and reuses database connections, avoiding the memory/CPU overhead of opening a new connection on each invocation and absorbing connection surges. (3) For broad read scalability for a large-scale sales event with distributed customers, converting to an Aurora global database with cross-Region replicas (C) adds read capacity and geographic scaling, the only remaining option that legitimately improves scalability. Reserved concurrency (A) only reserves/caps capacity and does NOT pre-warm environments, so it does not reduce burst latency (and capacity was already proven adequate). Moving connection initialization INTO the handler (D) is the opposite of AWS best practice, which says to initialize database connections OUTSIDE the handler so they are reused across invocations; D would re-establish connections on every invocation and make the latency worse.","explanation_zh":"情境描述了三個擴展性問題。(1)『初始請求爆量時的延遲』是冷啟動問題；provisioned concurrency(B)會預先初始化執行環境，使其能以低延遲立即回應，正是 AWS 文件所述用途。(2)『大量呼叫時間用於建立資料庫連線』由 Amazon RDS Proxy(E)解決，它會建立連線池並重複使用連線，避免每次呼叫都開新連線的記憶體/CPU 開銷，並能吸收連線突增。(3)針對大型促銷活動、分散各地客戶的廣泛讀取擴展，轉換為 Aurora global database 並在各 Region 加入 read replica(C)可增加讀取容量與地理擴展，是唯一剩下能真正提升擴展性的選項。Reserved concurrency(A)僅保留/限制容量,並不會預熱環境,因此無法降低爆量延遲(且容量已證實足夠)。將連線初始化移入 handler(D)與 AWS 最佳實務相反——最佳實務是在 handler 之外初始化資料庫連線以跨呼叫重複使用;D 會在每次呼叫都重新建立連線,使延遲更糟。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Reserved concurrency only reserves and caps a function's concurrency; it does not pre-initialize (pre-warm) execution environments, so it does not reduce the cold-start latency seen during the initial burst. The DevOps engineer already confirmed the functions can fulfill the peak number of requests, so capacity is not the bottleneck.","why_zh":"Reserved concurrency 僅保留與限制函式的並行度,不會預先初始化(預熱)執行環境,因此無法降低初始爆量時的冷啟動延遲。工程師已確認函式能滿足尖峰請求數,容量並非瓶頸。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the inverse of AWS best practice. Lambda docs explicitly say to initialize database connections OUTSIDE the handler so subsequent invocations on the same environment reuse them. Moving connection setup INTO the handler forces a new connection on every invocation, worsening the exact latency problem described.","why_zh":"這與 AWS 最佳實務相反。Lambda 文件明確指出應在 handler 之外初始化資料庫連線,以便同一環境的後續呼叫重複使用。將連線建立移入 handler 會強迫每次呼叫都建立新連線,加劇所述的延遲問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/provisioned-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-proxy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.AuroraGlobalDatabase.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":202,"question_en":"A company runs a web application that extends across multiple Availability Zones. The company uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) for routing, AWS Fargate for the application, and Amazon Aurora for the application data. The company uses AWS CloudFormation templates to deploy the application. The company stores all Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository in the same AWS account and AWS Region. A DevOps engineer needs to establish a disaster recovery (DR) process in another Region. The solution must meet an RPO of 8 hours and an RTO of 2 hours. The company sometimes needs more than 2 hours to build the Docker images from the Dockerfile. Which solution will meet the RTO and RPO requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"该公司运行一个跨多个可用区的网络应用程序。该公司使用应用负载均衡器（ALB）进行路由，使用 AWS Fargate 运行应用程序，并使用 Amazon Aurora 存储应用程序数据。该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板 部署应用程序。该公司将所有 Docker 镜像存储在同一个 AWS 账户和 AWS 区域内的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库中。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要在另一个区域建立灾难恢复（DR）流程。该解决方案必须满足 8 小时的恢复点目 标（RPO）和 2 小时的恢复时间目标（RTO）。有时，该公司从 Dockerfile 构建 Docker 镜像需要超过 2 小 时。 哪种解决方案能以最经济的方式满足恢复时间目标（RTO）和恢复点目标（RPO）的要求？","options_en":{"A":"Copy the CloudFormation templates and the Dockerfile to an Amazon S3 bucket in the DR Region. Use AWS Backup to configure automated Aurora cross-Region hourly snapshots. In case of DR, build the most recent Docker image and upload the Docker image to an ECR repository in the DR Region. Use the CloudFormation template that has the most recent Aurora snapshot and the Docker image from the ECR repository to launch a new CloudFormation stack in the DR Region. Update the application DNS records to point to the new ALB.","B":"Copy the CloudFormation templates to an Amazon S3 bucket in the DR Region. Configure Aurora automated backup Cross-Region Replication. Configure ECR Cross-Region Replication. In case of DR, use the CloudFormation template with the most recent Aurora snapshot and the Docker image from the local ECR repository to launch a new CloudFormation stack in the DR Region. Update the application DNS records to point to the new ALB.","C":"Copy the CloudFormation templates to an Amazon S3 bucket in the DR Region. Use Amazon EventBridge to schedule an AWS Lambda function to take an hourly snapshot of the Aurora database and of the most recent Docker image in the ECR repository. Copy the snapshot and the Docker image to the DR Region. In case of DR, use the CloudFormation template with the most recent Aurora snapshot and the Docker image from the local ECR repository to launch a new CloudFormation stack in the DR Region.","D":"Copy the CloudFormation templates to an Amazon S3 bucket in the DR Region. Deploy a second application CloudFormation stack in the DR Region. Reconfigure Aurora to be a global database. Update both CloudFormation stacks when a new application release in the current Region is needed. In case of DR, update the application DNS records to point to the new ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CloudFormation 模板和 Dockerfile 复制到灾难恢复（DR）区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 AWS Backup 配置 Aurora 跨区域每小时自动快照。在发生灾难恢复时，构建最新的 Docker 镜像，并将其上 传到 DR 区域的 ECR 仓库。使用包含最新 Aurora 快照和来自 ECR 仓库的 Docker 镜像的 CloudFormation 模板，在 DR 区域启动新的 CloudFormation 堆栈。更新应用程序的 DNS 记录，使其指 向新的 ALB。","B":"将 CloudFormation 模板复制到灾难恢复区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。配置 Aurora 自动备份跨区域复制。 配置 ECR 跨区域复制。在发生灾难恢复时，使用包含最新 Aurora 快照和本地 ECR 存储库中的 Docker 镜像的 CloudFormation 模板在灾难恢复区域启动新的 CloudFormation 堆栈。更新应用程序的 DNS 记录 以指向新的 ALB。","C":"将 CloudFormation 模板复制到灾难恢复（DR）区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon EventBridge 安排 AWS Lambda 函数每小时对 Aurora 数据库和 ECR 存储库中的最新 Docker 镜像进行快照。将快照 和 Docker 镜像复制到 DR 区域。在发生灾难恢复时，使用包含最新 Aurora 快照和本地 ECR 存储库中 的 Docker 镜像的 CloudFormation 模板在 DR 区域启动新的 CloudFormation 堆栈。","D":"将 CloudFormation 模板复制到灾难恢复区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。在灾难恢复区域部署第二个应用 程序 CloudFormation 堆栈。将 Aurora 重新配置为全局数据库。当当前区域需要新的应用程序版本时， 更新两个 CloudFormation 堆栈。在发生灾难恢复时，更新应用程序的 DNS 记录以指向新的应用负载 均衡器（ALB）。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The deciding constraints are the 2-hour RTO combined with the fact that Docker image builds sometimes take more than 2 hours, plus the 'MOST cost-effective' qualifier. Because builds can exceed the RTO, the solution must pre-stage built images in the DR Region rather than building at failover time. Option B uses Amazon ECR cross-Region (private registry) replication, which automatically replicates pushed images to the DR Region, and Aurora cross-Region automated backup replication, which continuously replicates backups (easily meeting the 8-hour RPO). At DR time the CloudFormation stack is launched from the most recent replicated Aurora snapshot and the already-replicated image in the DR-Region ECR repository, so no build is needed and the 2-hour RTO is met. Both replication features are native, managed, pay-as-you-go, and require no idle standby infrastructure, making B the most cost-effective valid choice.","explanation_zh":"決定性條件是 2 小時的 RTO，加上 Docker image 建置有時會超過 2 小時，以及「MOST cost-effective」的限定詞。由於建置可能超出 RTO，解決方案必須在 DR Region 預先備妥已建置的 image，而非在故障切換時才建置。選項 B 使用 Amazon ECR 跨 Region（private registry）replication，會自動將推送的 image 複製到 DR Region；並使用 Aurora cross-Region automated backup replication 持續複製備份（輕鬆達成 8 小時 RPO）。DR 發生時，CloudFormation stack 直接以最新的已複製 Aurora snapshot 及 DR Region ECR repository 中已複製好的 image 啟動，無需建置，因此符合 2 小時 RTO。這兩項 replication 功能皆為原生、受管、依用量計費，且不需閒置的 standby 基礎設施，使 B 成為最具成本效益的有效選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"It copies the Dockerfile to S3 and builds the Docker image at DR time. Because builds sometimes take more than 2 hours, this violates the 2-hour RTO.","why_zh":"它將 Dockerfile 複製到 S3 並在 DR 時才建置 Docker image。由於建置有時超過 2 小時，違反了 2 小時 RTO。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Building a custom EventBridge + Lambda pipeline to snapshot Aurora and copy Docker images reinvents native ECR cross-Region replication and Aurora backup replication, adding operational overhead and cost, so it is not the most cost-effective option.","why_zh":"自建 EventBridge + Lambda 流程來對 Aurora 做 snapshot 並複製 Docker image，等於重造原生的 ECR 跨 Region replication 與 Aurora 備份複製，增加維運負擔與成本，並非最具成本效益的選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running a second full application stack continuously plus an Aurora global database (sub-second replication) is the most expensive, over-engineered approach and contradicts the MOST cost-effective requirement for an 8h RPO / 2h RTO.","why_zh":"持續運行第二套完整應用程式 stack 加上 Aurora global database（次秒級複製）是最昂貴、過度設計的方案，與 8 小時 RPO／2 小時 RTO 下的最具成本效益要求相違背。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/AutomatedBackups.Replicating.Enable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/registry-settings-configure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/Registries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-copy-snapshot.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":203,"question_en":"A company's application runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The application writes to a log file that records the username, date, time, and source IP address of the login. The log is published to a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The company is performing a root cause analysis for an event that occurred on the previous day. The company needs to know the number of logins for a specific user from the past 7 days. Which solution will provide this information?","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行。该应用程序会将用户名、日期、时间和登录源 IP 地址写 入日志文件。该日志会发布到亚马逊 CloudWatch Logs 中的一个日志组。 该公司正在对前一天发生的事件进行根本原因分析。公司需要了解特定用户在过去 7 天内的登录次数。 哪种解决方案能提供这些信息？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter on the log group. Use a filter pattern that matches the username. Publish a CloudWatch metric that sums the number of logins over the past 7 days.","B":"Create a CloudWatch Logs subscription on the log group. Use a filter pattern that matches the username. Publish a CloudWatch metric that sums the number of logins over the past 7 days.","C":"Create a CloudWatch Logs Insights query that uses an aggregation function to count the number of logins for the username over the past 7 days. Run the query against the log group.","D":"Create a CloudWatch dashboard. Add a number widget that has a filter pattern that counts the number of logins for the username over the past 7 days directly from the log group."},"options_zh":{"A":"在日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器。使用与用户名匹配的筛选模式。发布一个 CloudWatch 指标，该指标对过去 7 天内的登录次数进行求和。","B":"在日志组上创建 CloudWatch Logs 订阅。使用与用户名匹配的筛选模式。发布一个 CloudWatch 指标，该指标对过去 7 天内的登录次数进行求和。","C":"创建一个 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询，使用聚合函数来计算过去 7 天内该用户名的登录次数。针对 日志组运行该查询。","D":"创建一个 CloudWatch 控制面板。添加一个数字小部件，该小部件具有一个过滤模式，可直接从日志组中 计算过去 7 天内该用户名的登录次数。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The company needs to retroactively count logins for a specific user over the past 7 days of data that is ALREADY in the log group (the event occurred the previous day). CloudWatch Logs Insights queries operate against historical log data already ingested in a log group and let you set an arbitrary absolute/relative time range (e.g., the past 7 days). Using a query like 'fields @timestamp | filter username = \"...\" | stats count(*)' returns the exact retroactive count. This is the documented use case for an aggregation function query. In contrast, metric filters (options A and B) are forward-looking only: AWS docs explicitly state 'Filters do not retroactively filter data. Filters only publish the metric data points for events that happen after the filter was created.' So a metric filter created today could not count logins from the previous 7 days. A CloudWatch subscription (B) streams matching events to a downstream destination (Lambda/Kinesis/Firehose/OpenSearch) and does not itself publish a summing metric, and likewise only processes new events. A CloudWatch dashboard number widget (D) does not support a 'filter pattern that counts logins directly from the log group'; dashboard widgets graph metrics or run Logs Insights queries, not arbitrary log-group filter-pattern counts, so the construct described is not a valid native feature.","explanation_zh":"公司需要回溯統計過去 7 天內某特定使用者的登入次數，而這些資料已經存在於 log group 中（事件發生在前一天）。CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢針對已經攝取進 log group 的歷史日誌執行，並可設定任意的絕對／相對時間範圍（例如過去 7 天）。使用類似 'fields @timestamp | filter username = \"...\" | stats count(*)' 的查詢即可回溯得到精確計數，這正是聚合函數查詢的官方使用情境。相對地，metric filter（選項 A 和 B）只能向前生效：AWS 官方文件明確指出「Filters do not retroactively filter data. Filters only publish the metric data points for events that happen after the filter was created.」因此今天才建立的 metric filter 無法統計過去 7 天的登入。CloudWatch subscription（B）是將符合的事件串流到下游目的地（Lambda/Kinesis/Firehose/OpenSearch），本身不會發布加總的 metric，且同樣只處理新事件。CloudWatch dashboard 的 number widget（D）並不支援「直接用 filter pattern 從 log group 計算登入次數」；dashboard widget 是繪製 metric 或執行 Logs Insights 查詢，並非任意的 log-group filter-pattern 計數，所以該描述並非有效的原生功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Metric filters do not retroactively process existing log data. AWS docs state filters only publish metric data points for events that occur AFTER the filter is created, so a filter made today cannot count the previous 7 days of logins needed for the root cause analysis.","why_zh":"Metric filter 不會回溯處理既有的日誌資料。AWS 文件指出 filter 只會為建立之後發生的事件發布 metric 資料點，因此今天建立的 filter 無法統計根因分析所需的過去 7 天登入。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A subscription filter streams matching events to a downstream destination (Lambda/Kinesis/Firehose/OpenSearch); it does not itself publish a summing CloudWatch metric, and like metric filters it only acts on new events, not the historical 7 days already in the log group.","why_zh":"Subscription filter 是把符合的事件串流到下游目的地（Lambda/Kinesis/Firehose/OpenSearch），本身不會發布加總的 CloudWatch metric，且與 metric filter 一樣只處理新事件，無法處理 log group 中已存在的過去 7 天歷史資料。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A dashboard number widget cannot 'count logins with a filter pattern directly from the log group.' Dashboard widgets display metrics or Logs Insights query results, not arbitrary filter-pattern counts run directly against a log group, so the described capability is not a real native feature.","why_zh":"Dashboard 的 number widget 無法「用 filter pattern 直接從 log group 計算登入次數」。Dashboard widget 顯示的是 metric 或 Logs Insights 查詢結果，而非直接對 log group 執行任意 filter-pattern 計數，因此所述能力並非真正的原生功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_AggregationQuery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_QuerySyntax-Stats.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":204,"question_en":"A company has an AWS CodeDeploy application. The application has a deployment group that uses a single tag group to identify instances for the deployment of ApplicationA. The single tag group configuration identifies instances that have Environment=Production and Name=ApplicationA tags for the deployment of ApplicationA. The company launches an additional Amazon EC2 instance with Department=Marketing, Environment=Production, and Name=ApplicationB tags. On the next CodeDeploy deployment of Application, the additional instance has ApplicationA installed on it. A DevOps engineer needs to configure the existing deployment group to prevent ApplicationA from being installed on the additional instance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序。该应用程序有一个部署组，使用单个标签组来识别用于部 署 ApplicationA 的实例。单个标签组配置识别具有 Environment=Production 和 Name=ApplicationA 标签的 实例，以便部署 ApplicationA。 该公司启动了一个额外的 Amazon EC2 实例，其标签为 Department=Marketing、Environment=Production 和 Name=ApplicationB。在对 Application 进行下一次 CodeDeploy 部署时，该额外实例上安装了 ApplicationA。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要配置现有的部署组，以防止 ApplicationA 安装在该额外实例上。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Change the current single tag group to include only the Environment=Production tag. Add another single tag group that includes only the Name=ApplicationA tag.","B":"Change the current single tag group to include the Department=Marketing, Environment=production, and Name=ApplicationA tags.","C":"Add another single tag group that includes only the Department=Marketing tag. Keep the Environment=Production and Name=ApplicationA tags with the current single tag group.","D":"Change the current single tag group to include only the Environment=Production tag. Add another single tag group that includes only the Department=Marketing tag."},"options_zh":{"A":"将当前的单个标签组更改为仅包含“Environment=Production”标签。再添加一个仅包含“Name= ApplicationA”标签的单个标签组。","B":"将当前的单个标签组更改为包含“部门=市场部”、“环境=生产”和“名称=应用程序 A”这些标签。","C":"再添加一个仅包含“Department=Marketing”标签的单个标签组。将“Environment= Production”和“Name=ApplicationA”标签保留在当前的单个标签组中。","D":"将当前的单个标签组更改为仅包含“环境=生产”标签。再添加一个仅包含“部门=市场”标签的单 个标签组。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeDeploy tag matching follows two rules: within a SINGLE tag group, an instance is included if it matches AT LEAST ONE tag (OR logic); across MULTIPLE tag groups, an instance must match at least one tag in EACH group (AND logic). The current deployment group placed Environment=Production and Name=ApplicationA in ONE tag group, so OR logic applied: the new ApplicationB instance (Environment=Production) matched the Production tag alone and got ApplicationA installed. To require BOTH Environment=Production AND Name=ApplicationA, the two tags must be split into separate tag groups. Option A does exactly this: tag group 1 = Environment=Production, tag group 2 = Name=ApplicationA, producing AND logic. The ApplicationB instance has Name=ApplicationB (not ApplicationA), so it fails the second group and is correctly excluded, while genuine ApplicationA instances (which have both tags) still match.","explanation_zh":"CodeDeploy 的標籤比對遵循兩條規則：在「單一」標籤群組內，實例只要符合「至少一個」標籤即被納入（OR 邏輯）；而跨「多個」標籤群組時，實例必須在「每一個」群組中都符合至少一個標籤才被納入（AND 邏輯）。目前的 deployment group 把 Environment=Production 與 Name=ApplicationA 放在「同一個」標籤群組，因此套用 OR 邏輯：新的 ApplicationB 實例（Environment=Production）只憑 Production 標籤就符合條件，導致 ApplicationA 被誤裝。要求同時符合 Environment=Production「且」Name=ApplicationA，必須把兩個標籤拆到不同的標籤群組。選項 A 正是如此：標籤群組 1 = Environment=Production、標籤群組 2 = Name=ApplicationA，形成 AND 邏輯。ApplicationB 實例的 Name=ApplicationB（非 ApplicationA），無法通過第二個群組而被正確排除；真正的 ApplicationA 實例（兩個標籤都有）仍然符合。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"This keeps a single tag group (OR logic) and adds Department=Marketing and Environment=production. The new ApplicationB instance has both Marketing and Production tags, so it still matches via OR and ApplicationA is still installed on it. This makes the problem worse, not better.","why_zh":"這仍是單一標籤群組（OR 邏輯），又加入 Department=Marketing 與 Environment=production。新的 ApplicationB 實例同時有 Marketing 與 Production 標籤，仍會透過 OR 比對命中，ApplicationA 依舊會被安裝，反而讓問題更嚴重。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Keeping Environment=Production + Name=ApplicationA together in one group (OR) and adding a second group of Department=Marketing creates AND logic that requires Department=Marketing. Legitimate ApplicationA instances do not have a Marketing tag, so they would be wrongly excluded; meanwhile the ApplicationB instance (which DOES have Marketing and Production) could still match group 1 via Production and group 2 via Marketing, so it would still receive ApplicationA.","why_zh":"把 Environment=Production 與 Name=ApplicationA 留在同一群組（OR），再加上第二個 Department=Marketing 群組，形成要求 Department=Marketing 的 AND 邏輯。正常的 ApplicationA 實例沒有 Marketing 標籤，會被錯誤排除；而 ApplicationB 實例（確實有 Marketing 與 Production）仍可在群組 1 以 Production、群組 2 以 Marketing 命中，依舊會收到 ApplicationA。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Tag group 1 = Environment=Production and tag group 2 = Department=Marketing targets instances that have BOTH Production AND Marketing. That is precisely the unwanted ApplicationB instance, and it excludes the real ApplicationA instances (which have no Marketing tag). This is the exact opposite of the requirement.","why_zh":"標籤群組 1 = Environment=Production、群組 2 = Department=Marketing，會鎖定同時具有 Production 與 Marketing 的實例，正好就是不該部署的 ApplicationB 實例，並排除沒有 Marketing 標籤的真正 ApplicationA 實例，與需求完全相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/instances-tagging.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":205,"question_en":"A company is launching an application that stores raw data in an Amazon S3 bucket. Three applications need to access the data to generate reports. The data must be redacted differently for each application before the applications can access the data. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在推出一款应用程序，该程序将原始数据存储在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。有三个应用程序需要访 问这些数据以生成报告。在这些应用程序能够访问数据之前，必须针对每个应用程序对数据进行不同的脱 敏处理。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 bucket for each application. Configure S3 Same-Region Replication (SRR) from the raw data's S3 bucket to each application's S3 bucket. Configure each application to consume data from its own S3 bucket.","B":"Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by object creation events in the raw data’s S3 bucket. Program the Lambda function to redact data for each application. Publish the data on the Kinesis data stream. Configure each application to consume data from the Kinesis data stream.","C":"For each application, create an S3 access point that uses the raw data's S3 bucket as the destination. Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by object creation events in the raw data's S3 bucket. Program the Lambda function to redact data for each application. Store the data in each application's S3 access point. Configure each application to consume data from its own S3 access point.","D":"Create an S3 access point that uses the raw data’s S3 bucket as the destination. For each application, create an S3 Object Lambda access point that uses the S3 access point. Configure the AWS Lambda function for each S3 Object Lambda access point to redact data when objects are retrieved. Configure each application to consume data from its own S3 Object Lambda access point"},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个应用程序创建一个 S3 存储桶。将原始数据的 S3 存储桶配置为与每个应用程序的 S3 存储桶进行 同区域复制（SRR）。配置每个应用程序从其自身的 S3 存储桶中获取数据。","B":"创建一个 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。创建一个由原始数据 S3 存储桶中的对象创建事件触发的 AWS Lambda 函数。编写 Lambda 函数以针对每个应用程序对数据进行脱敏处理。将数据发布到 Kinesis 数 据流。配置每个应用程序从 Kinesis 数据流中获取数据。","C":"对于每个应用程序，创建一个使用原始数据的 S3 存储桶作为目标的 S3 访问点。创建一个由原始数据的 S3 存储桶中的对象创建事件触发的 AWS Lambda 函数。编写 Lambda 函数以对每个应用程序的数据进 行脱敏处理。将数据存储在每个应用程序的 S3 访问点中。配置每个应用程序从其自身的 S3 访问点获 取数据。","D":"创建一个使用原始数据 S3 存储桶作为目标的 S3 访问点。为每个应用程序创建一个使用该 S3 访问点的 S3 对象 Lambda 访问点。为每个 S3 对象 Lambda 访问点配置 AWS Lambda 函数，以便在检索对象时对 数据进行脱敏处理。配置每个应用程序从其自身的 S3 对象 Lambda 访问点获取数据。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"S3 Object Lambda Access Points are purpose-built for exactly this scenario: adding custom code to S3 GET requests to modify and process data as it is returned to an application, including redacting confidential/PII data. You create one supporting S3 access point on the raw data bucket, then create a separate S3 Object Lambda access point per application, each backed by its own Lambda function that redacts the data differently when objects are retrieved. AWS even publishes a dedicated tutorial 'Detecting and redacting PII data with S3 Object Lambda.' Crucially, this approach requires no derivative copies of the data and the raw data is redacted on-read for each consumer, so each of the three applications sees only its own redacted view. Option D directly maps to the documented architecture; the other options either store redundant copies, misuse plain access points, or insert an unnecessary streaming service.","explanation_zh":"S3 Object Lambda Access Points 正是為此情境設計：在 S3 GET 請求中加入自訂程式碼，於資料回傳給應用程式時即時修改與處理，包括遮蔽機密/PII 資料。做法是在原始資料 bucket 上建立一個 supporting S3 access point，再為每個應用程式各建立一個 S3 Object Lambda access point，各自由不同的 Lambda function 在物件被取回時以不同方式遮蔽資料。AWS 甚至提供專門教學「Detecting and redacting PII data with S3 Object Lambda」。關鍵在於此方法不需建立任何衍生副本，原始資料在讀取時針對每個消費端遮蔽，因此三個應用程式各自只看到屬於自己的遮蔽視圖。選項 D 直接對應官方文件架構；其他選項則分別產生冗餘副本、誤用一般 access point，或插入不必要的串流服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 Same-Region Replication only copies objects unchanged into each bucket; it provides no mechanism to redact or transform data differently per application. It also creates and stores three full derivative copies of the raw data, which Object Lambda avoids.","why_zh":"S3 Same-Region Replication 只會將物件原封不動複製到各 bucket，無法針對不同應用程式遮蔽或轉換資料，且會建立並儲存三份完整的原始資料副本，而 Object Lambda 可避免此情況。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Kinesis Data Streams is an event/streaming primitive, not a per-consumer redaction layer for objects in S3. This design is over-engineered, forces a streaming consumption model the reporting apps do not need, and a single Lambda publishing to one stream cannot cleanly give each application its own differently-redacted dataset.","why_zh":"Kinesis Data Streams 是事件/串流元件，並非針對 S3 物件做每個消費端遮蔽的機制。此設計過度複雜，強迫報表應用採用不必要的串流消費模式，且單一 Lambda 寫入單一 stream 無法清楚地讓每個應用程式取得各自不同遮蔽的資料集。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A plain S3 access point is only a named network/IAM entry point to the same underlying bucket; you cannot 'store data in an access point.' This option misunderstands access points and would require writing extra redacted copies into the bucket, which is what Object Lambda is designed to eliminate.","why_zh":"一般 S3 access point 只是指向同一底層 bucket 的具名網路/IAM 進入點，無法「將資料儲存到 access point 中」。此選項誤解了 access point 的作用，且需將額外的遮蔽副本寫回 bucket，而這正是 Object Lambda 旨在消除的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/transforming-objects.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/olap-writing-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/tutorial-s3-object-lambda-redact-pii.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/olap-create.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":206,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Control Tower and AWS CloudFormation to manage its AWS accounts and to create AWS resources. The company requires all Amazon S3 buckets to be encrypted with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) when the S3 buckets are created in a CloudFormation stack. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 控制塔和 AWS CloudFormation 来管理其 AWS 账户并创建 AWS 资源。该公司要求在 CloudFormation 堆栈中创建的所有 Amazon S3 存储桶都使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）进行加 密。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Organizations. Attach an SCP that denies the s3:PutObject permission if the request does not include an x-amz-server-side-encryption header that requests server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS).","B":"Use AWS Control Tower with a multi-account environment. Configure and enable proactive AWS Control Tower controls on all OUs with CloudFormation hooks.","C":"Use AWS Control Tower with a multi-account environment. Configure and enable detective AWS Control Tower controls on all OUs with CloudFormation hooks.","D":"Use AWS Organizations. Create an AWS Config organizational rule to check whether a KMS encryption key is enabled for all S3 buckets. Deploy the rule. Create and apply an SCP to prevent users from stopping and deleting AWS Config across all AWS accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 组织。附加一个服务控制策略（SCP），如果请求中不包含要求使用 AWS KMS 密钥进行服 务器端加密（SSE-KMS）的 x-amz-server-side-encryption 标头，则拒绝 s3:PutObject 权限。","B":"在多账户环境中使用 AWS 控制塔。通过 CloudFormation 挂钩在所有组织单元上配置并启用 AWS 控制塔的主动控制措施。","C":"在多账户环境中使用 AWS 控制塔。通过 CloudFormation 钩子在所有组织单元上配置并启用 AWS 控制塔的检测控制。","D":"使用 AWS 组织。创建一个 AWS Config 组织规则，检查所有 S3 存储桶是否启用了 KMS 加密密钥。 部署该规则。创建并应用一个服务控制策略（SCP），以防止用户在所有 AWS 账户中停止和删除 AWS Config。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to enforce KMS (SSE-KMS) encryption on S3 buckets at the moment they are created in a CloudFormation stack. AWS Control Tower proactive controls are purpose-built for this: they are implemented with CloudFormation hooks (preCreate/preUpdate handlers) and check resources before they are deployed, blocking non-compliant resources from being created. Enabling a proactive control (such as the S3 encryption control) on the OUs is the correct mechanism to prevent CloudFormation from provisioning a non-KMS-encrypted bucket. Option B matches both the 'proactive' nature (prevent before deployment) and the 'CloudFormation hooks' implementation detail exactly.","explanation_zh":"需求是在 CloudFormation 堆疊建立 S3 儲存貯體的當下，強制使用 KMS (SSE-KMS) 加密。AWS Control Tower 的 proactive controls 正是為此設計：它們以 CloudFormation hooks（preCreate/preUpdate handlers）實作，會在資源部署前進行檢查，阻止不合規的資源被建立。在 OU 上啟用 proactive control（例如 S3 加密控制）即可在 CloudFormation 佈建未使用 KMS 加密的貯體前加以阻擋。選項 B 同時符合「proactive（部署前預防）」特性以及「CloudFormation hooks」的實作方式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An SCP denying s3:PutObject governs object uploads into a bucket, not the creation or encryption configuration of the bucket itself, and is unrelated to enforcing encryption when a bucket is created in a CloudFormation stack.","why_zh":"拒絕 s3:PutObject 的 SCP 管控的是物件上傳行為，而非貯體本身的建立或加密設定，與在 CloudFormation 堆疊建立貯體時強制加密無關。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Detective controls use AWS Config rules to detect non-compliance only after resources exist; they do not prevent creation. They are also not implemented with CloudFormation hooks, so the description is technically inconsistent.","why_zh":"Detective controls 使用 AWS Config 規則，只能在資源建立後偵測不合規，無法阻止建立；且其並非以 CloudFormation hooks 實作，描述本身在技術上自相矛盾。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An AWS Config organizational rule is detective only; it reports unencrypted buckets after the fact but does not stop CloudFormation from creating a bucket without KMS encryption. The SCP to protect Config does not enforce encryption either.","why_zh":"AWS Config 組織規則僅為偵測性質，事後回報未加密貯體，但無法阻止 CloudFormation 建立未使用 KMS 加密的貯體；保護 Config 的 SCP 也無法強制加密。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/proactive-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudformation-cli/latest/hooks-userguide/proactive-controls-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/s3-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/how-controls-work.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":207,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer has developed an AWS Lambda function. The Lambda function starts an AWS CloudFormation drift detection operation on all supported resources for a specific CloudFormation stack. The Lambda function then exits its invocation. The DevOps engineer has created an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule that invokes the Lambda function every hour. An Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic already exists in the AWS account. The DevOps engineer has subscribed to the SNS topic to receive notifications. The DevOps engineer needs to receive a notification as soon as possible when drift is detected in this specific stack configuration. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师开发了一个 AWS Lambda 函数。该 Lambda 函数针对特定的 CloudFormation 堆栈对所 有受支持的资源启动 AWS CloudFormation 漂移检测操作，然后退出其调用。 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则，该规则每小时调用一次 Lambda 函数。AWS 账户中已存在一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。DevOps 工程师已订阅该 SNS 主题以接收通知。 当检测到此特定堆栈配置出现偏差时，DevOps 工程师需要尽快收到通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the existing EventBridge rule to also target the SNS topic. Configure an SNS subscription filter policy to match the CloudFormation stack. Attach the subscription filter policy to the SNS topic.","B":"Create a second Lambda function to query the CloudFormation API for the drift detection results for the stack. Configure the second Lambda function to publish a message to the SNS topic if drift is detected. Adjust the existing EventBridge rule to also target the second Lambda function.","C":"Configure Amazon GuardDuty in the account with drift detection for all CloudFormation stacks. Create a second EventBridge rule that reacts to the GuardDuty drift detection event finding for the specific CloudFormation stack. Configure the SNS topic as a target of the second EventBridge rule.","D":"Configure AWS Config in the account. Use the cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check managed rule. Create a second EventBridge rule that reacts to a compliance change event for the CloudFormation stack. Configure the SNS topic as a target of the second EventBridge rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"将现有的 EventBridge 规则配置为也指向 SNS 主题。配置一个 SNS 订阅过滤策略以匹配 CloudFormation 堆栈。将订阅过滤策略附加到 SNS 主题。","B":"创建第二个 Lambda 函数，用于查询 CloudFormation API 以获取堆栈的偏差检测结果。将第二个 Lambda 函数配置为在检测到偏差时向 SNS 主题发布消息。调整现有的 EventBridge 规则，使其也指向第二个 Lambda 函数。","C":"在账户中为所有 CloudFormation 堆栈配置带有漂移检测功能的 Amazon GuardDuty。创建第二个 EventBridge 规则，使其对特定 CloudFormation 堆栈的 GuardDuty 漂移检测事件做出反应。将 SNS 主 题配置为第二个 EventBridge 规则的目标。","D":"在账户中配置 AWS Config。使用 cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check 管理规则。创建第二个 EventBridge 规则，使其对 CloudFormation 堆栈的合规性变更事件做出反应。将 SNS 主题配置为第 二个 EventBridge 规则的目标。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Option D is the only solution that reliably delivers a drift notification. The AWS Config managed rule cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check performs DetectStackDrift on the stack and becomes NON_COMPLIANT when the stack drift status is DRIFTED (COMPLIANT when IN_SYNC). AWS Config emits a compliance change event to the EventBridge default event bus, so a second EventBridge rule scoped to the specific stack/rule can target the existing SNS topic, producing a notification exactly when drift is detected. The other options are technically broken: Option A targets the hourly SCHEDULED rule, whose event payload contains no drift status, so an SNS subscription filter policy cannot match 'drift detected' and it would fire every hour unconditionally. Option B triggers the second Lambda on the SAME hourly schedule as the first Lambda, but drift detection is asynchronous and takes minutes, so the API query runs while detection is still DETECTION_IN_PROGRESS (a race condition), returning stale or no results. Option C invents a feature: Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service and has no CloudFormation drift-detection capability or findings. Note: AWS even offers a native 'CloudFormation Drift Detection Status Change' EventBridge event (stack-drift-status DRIFTED) that would be the ideal trigger, but no option uses it; among the given choices only D works.","explanation_zh":"選項 D 是唯一能可靠送出 drift 通知的方案。AWS Config 受管規則 cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check 會對 stack 執行 DetectStackDrift，當 stack drift status 為 DRIFTED 時判定為 NON_COMPLIANT（IN_SYNC 時為 COMPLIANT）。AWS Config 會把 compliance change 事件送到 EventBridge 預設 event bus，因此第二條針對該特定 stack/規則的 EventBridge rule 可以將既有 SNS topic 設為 target，在偵測到 drift 時送出通知。其他選項在技術上不成立：選項 A 以每小時的 SCHEDULED rule 為 target，但排程事件的 payload 不含 drift 狀態，SNS subscription filter policy 無法比對「偵測到 drift」，且會無條件每小時觸發。選項 B 讓第二個 Lambda 與第一個 Lambda 共用同一條每小時排程觸發，但 drift detection 是非同步且需數分鐘，查詢 API 時偵測仍在 DETECTION_IN_PROGRESS（競態條件），會取得過時或無結果。選項 C 杜撰功能：Amazon GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務，並無 CloudFormation drift detection 能力或 findings。補充：AWS 其實有原生的 'CloudFormation Drift Detection Status Change' EventBridge 事件（stack-drift-status DRIFTED）才是最理想的觸發來源，但無選項採用；在給定選項中只有 D 可行。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The existing rule is a scheduled rule that fires every hour and its event payload carries no drift status, so an SNS subscription filter policy cannot match 'drift detected'; it would notify unconditionally every hour rather than only when drift occurs.","why_zh":"既有規則是每小時觸發的排程規則，事件 payload 不含 drift 狀態，SNS subscription filter policy 無法比對「偵測到 drift」；它會每小時無條件通知，而非僅在發生 drift 時通知。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The second Lambda is triggered by the same hourly schedule as the first Lambda, but drift detection is asynchronous and takes minutes; the query would run while detection is still DETECTION_IN_PROGRESS, a race condition returning stale or no results.","why_zh":"第二個 Lambda 與第一個 Lambda 共用同一每小時排程觸發，但 drift detection 為非同步且需數分鐘；查詢時偵測仍在 DETECTION_IN_PROGRESS，形成競態條件，回傳過時或無結果。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service analyzing CloudTrail/VPC/DNS logs; it has no CloudFormation drift-detection capability or drift findings, so this configuration does not exist.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是分析 CloudTrail/VPC/DNS 日誌的威脅偵測服務，並無 CloudFormation drift detection 能力或 drift findings，此設定並不存在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/eventbridge-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/event-detail-stack-drift-detection-change.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":208,"question_en":"A company has deployed a complex container-based workload on AWS. The workload uses Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus for monitoring. The workload runs in an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster in an AWS account. The company’s DevOps team wants to receive workload alerts by using the company’s Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. The SNS topic is in the same AWS account as the EKS cluster. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上部署了一个复杂的基于容器的工作负载。该工作负载使用 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 进行监控。工作负载在 Amazon 上运行。 AWS 账户中的弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群。 该公司的 DevOps 团队希望使用公司的亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题接收工作负载警报。该 SNS 主题与 EKS 集群位于同一个 AWS 账户中。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus remote write URL to send alerts to the SNS topic","B":"Create an alerting rule that checks the availability of each of the workload’s containers.","C":"Create an alert manager configuration for the SNS topic.","D":"Modify the access policy of the SNS topic. Grant the aps.amazonaws.com service principal the sns:Publish permission and the sns:GetTopicAttributes permission for the SNS topic.","E":"Modify the IAM role that Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus uses. Grant the role the sns:Publish permission and the sns:GetTopicAttributes permission for the SNS topic.","F":"Create an OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider for the EKS cluster. Create a cluster service account. Grant the account the sns:Publish permission and the sns:GetTopicAttributes permission by using an IAM role."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 的远程写入 URL 将警报发送到 SNS 主题","B":"创建一个警报规则，用于检查工作负载中每个容器的可用性。","C":"为 SNS 主题创建警报管理器配置。","D":"修改 SNS 主题的访问策略。授予 aps.amazonaws.com 服务主体 SNS 主题的 sns:Publish 权限和 sns: GetTopicAttributes 权限。","E":"修改 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 使用的 IAM 角色。为该角色授予 SNS 主题的 sns: Publish 权限和 sns:GetTopicAttributes 权限。","F":"为 EKS 集群创建一个 OpenID Connect （OIDC） 提供程序。创建一个集群服务账户。通过使用 IAM 角 色授予该账户 sns:Publish 权限和 sns:GetTopicAttributes 权限。"},"answer":["B","C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Sending workload alerts from Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP) to an SNS topic requires three pieces. First, you define alerting rules (a rules file) that evaluate metrics and fire alerts when a condition is met, such as a container becoming unavailable (B). Second, AMP's alert manager handles fired alerts and routes them to a receiver; AMP supports only Amazon SNS as a receiver and can route to SNS topics in the same account, so you must create an alert manager configuration pointing at the SNS topic (C). Third, you must grant AMP permission to publish by modifying the SNS topic's access (resource) policy to allow the aps.amazonaws.com service principal the sns:Publish and sns:GetTopicAttributes actions, ideally with aws:SourceArn (the workspace ARN) and aws:SourceAccount conditions to prevent the confused deputy problem (D). The AWS documentation explicitly shows this exact policy statement granting aps.amazonaws.com those two actions.","explanation_zh":"要將 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP) 的工作負載告警送到 SNS topic，需要三個元件。第一，定義 alerting rules（規則檔），用來評估指標並在符合條件時觸發告警，例如容器變為不可用 (B)。第二，AMP 的 alert manager 負責處理已觸發的告警並路由到 receiver；AMP 只支援 Amazon SNS 作為 receiver，且只能路由到同一帳號的 SNS topic，因此必須建立指向該 SNS topic 的 alert manager 設定 (C)。第三，必須透過修改 SNS topic 的存取（資源）政策，授予 aps.amazonaws.com 服務主體 sns:Publish 與 sns:GetTopicAttributes 權限，並建議搭配 aws:SourceArn（workspace ARN）與 aws:SourceAccount 條件以防止 confused deputy 問題 (D)。AWS 官方文件明確展示了授予 aps.amazonaws.com 這兩個動作的政策範例。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Remote write is the path for ingesting metrics INTO an AMP workspace, not for sending alerts out. There is no remote write URL that delivers alerts to SNS; alerts flow through alert manager to an SNS receiver.","why_zh":"Remote write 是把指標寫入 AMP workspace 的路徑，不是用來送出告警。並不存在把告警送到 SNS 的 remote write URL；告警是經由 alert manager 路由到 SNS receiver。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"AMP does not publish to SNS using a customer-managed IAM role with sns:Publish. Permission is granted via a resource-based policy on the SNS topic to the aps.amazonaws.com service principal, not by adding sns:Publish to an AMP IAM role.","why_zh":"AMP 不是透過帶有 sns:Publish 的客戶管理 IAM 角色來發佈到 SNS。權限是經由 SNS topic 的資源型政策授予 aps.amazonaws.com 服務主體，而非在 AMP 的 IAM 角色上加 sns:Publish。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"OIDC/IRSA (cluster service accounts) lets EKS pods call AWS APIs. But the alert publishing is performed by AMP's alert manager service, not by a pod in the cluster, so an EKS service account with sns:Publish is unnecessary and does not enable AMP to publish.","why_zh":"OIDC/IRSA（叢集 service account）讓 EKS pod 呼叫 AWS API。但發佈告警是由 AMP 的 alert manager 服務執行，而非叢集內的 pod，因此帶有 sns:Publish 的 EKS service account 既不必要，也無法讓 AMP 發佈告警。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-alert-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-alertmanager-receiver-AMPpermission.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-ruler-rulesfile.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-alertmanager-config.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":209,"question_en":"A company's organization in AWS Organizations has a single OU. The company runs Amazon EC2 instances in the OU accounts. The company needs to limit the use of each EC2 instance’s credentials to the specific EC2 instance that the credential is assigned to. A DevOps engineer must configure security for the EC2 instances. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中只有一个组织单元（OU）。该公司在该组织单元的账户中运行亚马逊 EC2 实例。 该公司需要限制每个 EC2 实例的凭证仅能用于分配该凭证的特定 EC2 实例。一位 DevOps 工程师必须为这 些 EC2 实例配置安全设置。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that specifies the VPC CIDR block. Configure the SCP to check whether the value of the aws:VpcSourcelp condition key is in the specified block. In the same SCP check, check whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivatelPv4 and aws:SourceVpc condition keys are the same. Deny access if either condition is false. Apply the SCP to the OU.","B":"Create an SCP that checks whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC and aws:SourceVpc condition keys are the same. Deny access if the values are not the same. In the same SCP check, check whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 and aws:VpcSourceIp condition keys are the same. Deny access if the values are not the same. Apply the SCP to the OU.","C":"Create an SCP that includes a list of acceptable VPC values and checks whether the value of the aws:SourceVpc condition key is in the list. In the same SCP check, define a list of acceptable IP address values and check whether the value of the aws:VpcSourceIp condition key is in the list. Deny access if either condition is false. Apply the SCP to each account in the organization.","D":"Create an SCP that checks whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC and aws:VpcSourceIp condition keys are the same. Deny access if the values are not the same. In the same SCP check, check whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 and aws:SourceVpc condition keys are the same. Deny access if the values are not the same. Apply the SCP to each account in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），指定 VPC 的 CIDR 块。将该 SCP 配置为检查 aws:VpcSourceIPv4 条 件键的值是否在指定的块内。在相同的 SCP 检查中，检查 aws:EC2InstanceSourceIPv4 和 aws: SourceVpc 条件键的值是否相同。如果任一条件为假，则拒绝访问。将该 SCP 应用于组织单位 （OU）。","B":"创建一个 SCP，检查 aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC 和 aws:SourceVpc 条件键的值是否相同。如果值不同， 则拒绝访问。在同一 SCP 检查中，检查 aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 和 aws:VpcSourceIp 条件键 的值是否相同。如果值不同，则拒绝访问。将该 SCP 应用于组织单位。","C":"创建一个 SCP，其中包含可接受的 VPC 值列表，并检查 aws:SourceVpc 条件键的值是否在该列表中。在 同一 SCP 检查中，定义可接受的 IP 地址值列表，并检查 aws:VpcSourceIp 条件键的值是否在该列表中。 如果任一条件为假，则拒绝访问。将该 SCP 应用于组织中的每个账户。","D":"创建一个 SCP，检查 `aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC`VpcSourceIp` 条件键的值是否相同。如果值不同，则 拒绝访问。在同一个 SCP 检查中，检查 `aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4` 和 `aws:SourceVpc` 条件 键的值是否相同。如果值不同，则拒绝访问。将该 SCP 应用于组织中的每个账户。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS provides two role-session condition keys specifically designed to bind EC2 instance role credentials to the instance they were delivered to: aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc (the VPC the credentials were delivered to) and aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 (the private IPv4 of the primary ENI the credentials were delivered to). The AWS documentation's exact SCP example denies access when aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc does NOT equal aws:SourceVpc, and (in a second statement) when aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 does NOT equal aws:VpcSourceIp. The docs explicitly state aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 'must be used with its companion key aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc to ensure a globally unique combination of VPC ID and source private IP.' Option B uses exactly these two correct pairings (EC2InstanceSourceVPC<->SourceVpc and EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4<->VpcSourceIp) and applies the SCP to the OU containing the accounts, which is the canonical solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS 提供兩個 role-session condition key，專門用來把 EC2 instance role 憑證綁定到其被傳遞到的特定執行個體：aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc（憑證被傳遞到的 VPC）與 aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4（憑證被傳遞到的主要 ENI 的私有 IPv4）。AWS 官方文件的 SCP 範例會在 aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc 不等於 aws:SourceVpc 時拒絕存取，並在第二個 statement 中於 aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 不等於 aws:VpcSourceIp 時拒絕存取。文件明確指出 aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4「必須與其搭配鍵 aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc 一起使用，以確保 VPC ID 與來源私有 IP 的組合具全域唯一性」。選項 B 使用了這兩組正確配對（EC2InstanceSourceVPC<->SourceVpc 與 EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4<->VpcSourceIp），並將 SCP 套用到包含這些帳戶的 OU，正是標準解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Pairs aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 with aws:SourceVpc, which is the wrong comparison (an IP address compared against a VPC ID). It also introduces an unnecessary static VPC CIDR/aws:VpcSourceIp range check that does not pin credentials to a specific instance.","why_zh":"把 aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 與 aws:SourceVpc 配對，比較錯誤（IP 位址對 VPC ID）。並引入不必要的靜態 VPC CIDR / aws:VpcSourceIp 範圍檢查，無法把憑證綁定到特定執行個體。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses lists of acceptable VPCs and IP addresses rather than comparing the credential-delivery context keys (aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc / aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4) against the request's source. This allows credentials to be used from any instance in the allowed list, so it does not limit a credential to its specific instance.","why_zh":"使用可接受的 VPC 與 IP 清單，而非比對憑證傳遞的 context key（aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc / aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4）與請求來源。憑證可被清單內任一執行個體使用，無法限制到特定執行個體。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Mismatches the condition keys: it compares aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC with aws:VpcSourceIp (VPC vs IP) and aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 with aws:SourceVpc (IP vs VPC). Both pairings are semantically wrong and would not enforce the intended binding.","why_zh":"condition key 配對錯誤：把 aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC 與 aws:VpcSourceIp 比較（VPC 對 IP），把 aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 與 aws:SourceVpc 比較（IP 對 VPC）。兩組配對在語意上都錯誤，無法強制執行預期的綁定。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":210,"question_en":"A company has a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances that run Linux in a single AWS account. The company is using an AWS Systems Manager Automation task across the EC2 instances. During the most recent patch cycle, several EC2 instances went into an error state because of insufficient available disk space. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that the EC2 instances have sufficient available disk space during the patching process in the future. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 AWS 账户中拥有一组运行 Linux 的 Amazon EC2 实例。该公司正在这些 EC2 实例上使 用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 任务。 在最近的补丁更新周期中，由于可用磁盘空间不足，有几台 EC2 实例进入了错误状态。DevOps 工程师需 要确保在未来的补丁更新过程中，EC2 实例拥有足够的可用磁盘空间。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that the Amazon CloudWatch agent is installed on all EC2 instances.","B":"Create a cron job that is installed on each EC2 instance to periodically delete temporary files.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch log group for the EC2 instances. Configure a cron job that is installed on each EC2 instance to write the available disk space to a CloudWatch log stream for the relevant EC2 instance.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to monitor available disk space on all EC2 instances. Add the alarm as a safety control to the Systems Manager Automation task.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function to periodically check for sufficient available disk space on all EC2 instances by evaluating each EC2 instance's respective Amazon CloudWatch log stream."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保在所有 EC2 实例上都安装了 Amazon CloudWatch 代理。","B":"在每个 EC2 实例上创建一个定期删除临时文件的 cron 任务。","C":"为 EC2 实例创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 日志组。在每个 EC2 实例上配置一个 cron 作业，将可用磁 盘空间写入相关 EC2 实例的 CloudWatch 日志流。","D":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控所有 EC2 实例的可用磁盘空间。将该警报作为安全控制添 加到 Systems Manager Automation 任务中。","E":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，定期检查所有 EC2 实例是否有足够的可用磁盘空间，方法是评估每 个 EC2 实例各自的 Amazon CloudWatch 日志流。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"EC2 instances do not emit OS-level filesystem free-space metrics by default; the default EC2 metrics are hypervisor-level (CPU, network, basic EBS) and do not include disk available space inside the OS. To monitor available disk space you must install the CloudWatch agent, which collects disk metrics such as disk_used_percent / disk_free (A). Systems Manager Automation has a native safety-control feature: when you start an automation you can attach a CloudWatch alarm, and per AWS docs 'if your alarm activates, the automation is stopped' (the start-automation-execution API exposes --alarm-configuration). So a CloudWatch alarm on available disk space, added as a safety control on the Automation task, stops the patching automation on low-disk conditions (D). Together A provides the disk metric and D enforces the guardrail during patching, directly preventing the insufficient-disk-space failures. The other options rely on per-instance cron scripts and log streams or custom Lambda, which are higher operational overhead, use the wrong mechanism (alarms operate on metrics, not log stream values), and are not wired into the Automation as a control that can stop patching.","explanation_zh":"EC2 執行個體預設並不會發出作業系統層級的檔案系統可用空間指標；EC2 預設指標屬於 hypervisor 層級（CPU、網路、基本 EBS），不包含 OS 內部的磁碟可用空間。要監控可用磁碟空間，必須安裝 CloudWatch agent，它會收集 disk_used_percent / disk_free 等磁碟指標（A）。Systems Manager Automation 內建安全控制功能：啟動 automation 時可附加一個 CloudWatch alarm，依 AWS 文件所述「若 alarm 觸發，automation 會被停止」（start-automation-execution API 提供 --alarm-configuration）。因此將監控可用磁碟空間的 CloudWatch alarm 作為 Automation 任務的安全控制，可在磁碟不足時停止修補 automation（D）。A 提供磁碟指標、D 在修補期間強制執行護欄，兩者結合可直接避免磁碟空間不足的失敗。其他選項依賴每台執行個體的 cron 腳本與 log stream 或自訂 Lambda，營運負擔較高、使用錯誤機制（alarm 是針對 metrics 而非 log stream 值運作），且未整合為能停止修補的控制。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A per-instance cron job that deletes temporary files is manual, high-overhead, not integrated with the Automation, and does not guarantee sufficient free space; it treats a symptom rather than ensuring the patching process verifies/guards disk space.","why_zh":"每台執行個體用 cron 刪除暫存檔屬於手動、高負擔、未與 Automation 整合的做法，且無法保證足夠可用空間；它只處理症狀，並未確保修補流程驗證或防護磁碟空間。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Writing available disk space into a CloudWatch Logs stream uses the wrong mechanism. Disk space monitoring belongs in metrics/alarms; the CloudWatch agent already collects disk metrics natively, and CloudWatch alarms act on metrics, not on arbitrary values buried in log streams.","why_zh":"把可用磁碟空間寫入 CloudWatch Logs stream 使用了錯誤的機制。磁碟空間監控應透過 metrics/alarms 處理；CloudWatch agent 本就能原生收集磁碟指標，且 CloudWatch alarm 是針對 metrics 運作，而非處理埋在 log stream 中的任意數值。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A Lambda function polling each instance's log stream reinvents native functionality with custom code, depends on the flawed log-stream approach from C, and is not attached to the Automation as a safety control, so it cannot actually stop the patching task when disk space is low.","why_zh":"用 Lambda 輪詢每台執行個體的 log stream，是用自訂程式重造原生功能，依賴 C 的有缺陷 log-stream 方式，且未作為安全控制附加到 Automation 上，因此在磁碟不足時無法真正停止修補任務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/running-automations-scale.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/metrics-collected-by-CloudWatch-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Agent-on-EC2-Instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-automation.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":211,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building an application that uses an AWS Lambda function to query an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster. The Lambda function performs only read queries. Amazon EventBridge events invoke the Lambda function. As more events invoke the Lambda function each second, the database's latency increases and the database's throughput decreases. The DevOps engineer needs to improve the performance of the application. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在构建一个应用程序，该程序使用 AWS Lambda 函数来查询 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库集群。Lambda 函数仅执行读取查询。Amazon EventBridge 事件会触发该 Lambda 函数。 随着每秒调用 Lambda 函数的事件增多，数据库的延迟增加，吞吐量降低。DevOps 工程师需要提 升应用程序的性能。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon RDS Proxy to create a proxy. Connect the proxy to the Aurora cluster reader endpoint. Set a maximum connections percentage on the proxy.","B":"Implement database connection pooling inside the Lambda code. Set a maximum number of connections on the database connection pool.","C":"Implement the database connection opening outside the Lambda event handler code.","D":"Implement the database connection opening and closing inside the Lambda event handler code.","E":"Connect to the proxy endpoint from the Lambda function.","F":"Connect to the Aurora cluster endpoint from the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon RDS Proxy 创建一个代理。将代理连接到 Aurora 集群的只读端点。在代理上设置最大 连接百分比。","B":"在 Lambda 代码内部实现数据库连接池。为数据库连接池设置最大连接数。","C":"在 Lambda 事件处理程序代码之外实现数据库连接的打开。","D":"在 Lambda 事件处理程序代码内部实现数据库连接的打开和关闭。","E":"从 Lambda 函数连接到代理端点。","F":"从 Lambda 函数连接到 Aurora 集群端点。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The problem is connection exhaustion: under high Lambda concurrency, each invocation opens its own Aurora connection, increasing latency and reducing throughput. (A) RDS Proxy pools and shares connections across many concurrent Lambda invocations and protects the database from oversubscription via a MaxConnectionsPercent setting; because the Lambda performs ONLY read queries, pointing the proxy at the Aurora reader endpoint also exploits Aurora read scalability (AWS docs: a read-only proxy endpoint 'passes connections to the reader endpoint of the cluster'). (E) The Lambda must connect to the proxy endpoint (not the cluster endpoint) so traffic actually flows through RDS Proxy. (C) Opening the database connection outside the handler (in the init phase) lets warm execution environments reuse the connection instead of creating a new one per invocation, since Lambda reuses execution environments. Together these three reduce the number of physical DB connections and balance reads, fixing the latency/throughput regression.","explanation_zh":"問題是連線耗盡：在 Lambda 高併發下，每次叫用都各自開啟一條 Aurora 連線，導致延遲上升、吞吐量下降。(A) RDS Proxy 會在大量併發的 Lambda 叫用之間建立連線池並共用連線，並透過 MaxConnectionsPercent 設定保護資料庫避免被超量訂閱；由於該 Lambda 只執行讀取查詢，將 proxy 指向 Aurora 的 reader endpoint 還能善用 Aurora 的讀取擴展能力(AWS 文件：唯讀 proxy endpoint「會將連線轉送到叢集的 reader endpoint」)。(E) Lambda 必須連到 proxy endpoint(而非 cluster endpoint)，流量才會真正經過 RDS Proxy。(C) 在 handler 之外(初始化階段)開啟資料庫連線，讓暖啟動的執行環境重複使用連線，而不是每次叫用都新建連線，因為 Lambda 會重用執行環境。這三項合在一起可減少實體 DB 連線數並分散讀取負載，修正延遲與吞吐量問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An in-Lambda connection pool with a max-connections cap is ineffective because each Lambda execution environment serves only one concurrent request, so a per-instance pool cannot share connections across the many concurrent invocations causing the exhaustion. Cross-invocation connection sharing is precisely what RDS Proxy provides; AWS recommends RDS Proxy instead of per-function pools for this pattern.","why_zh":"在 Lambda 內建連線池並設上限沒有效果，因為每個 Lambda 執行環境一次只服務一個併發請求，單實例連線池無法在造成耗盡的眾多併發叫用間共用連線。跨叫用的連線共用正是 RDS Proxy 的功能；AWS 在此情境建議使用 RDS Proxy 而非各函式自建連線池。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Opening AND closing the connection inside the handler is the anti-pattern that causes the problem: it creates and tears down a connection on every invocation, multiplying connection churn under high concurrency. It is the opposite of the recommended C.","why_zh":"在 handler 內開啟『並』關閉連線正是造成問題的反模式：每次叫用都新建並拆除連線，在高併發下使連線頻繁變動倍增。這與建議做法 C 正好相反。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Connecting to the Aurora cluster (writer) endpoint bypasses RDS Proxy entirely, negating options A and E, and routes read-only traffic to the writer instead of leveraging read scalability through the reader endpoint.","why_zh":"連到 Aurora cluster(writer)endpoint 會完全繞過 RDS Proxy，使 A 與 E 失效，且把唯讀流量導向 writer，而非透過 reader endpoint 善用讀取擴展能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/rds-proxy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/rds-proxy-connections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/rds-proxy-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/lambda-rds-connect.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-runtime-environment.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":212,"question_en":"A company has an AWS CloudFormation stack that is deployed in a single AWS account. The company has configured the stack to send event notifications to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. A DevOps engineer must implement an automated solution that applies a tag to the specific CloudFormation stack instance only after a successful stack update occurs. The DevOps engineer has created an AWS Lambda function that applies and updates this tag for the specific stack instance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个部署在单个 AWS 账户中的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈。该公司已将该堆栈配置为向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发送事件通知。 DevOps 工程师必须实现一个自动化解决方案，仅在特定的 CloudFormation 堆栈实例成功更新后为其 应用标签。该 DevOps 工程师已创建了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为特定的堆栈实例应用和更新此 标签。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Run the AWS-UpdateCloudFormationStack AWS Systems ManagerAutomation runbook when Systems Manager detects an UPDATE_COMPLETE event for the instance status of the CloudFormation stack. Configure the runbook to invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Create a custom AWS Config rule that produces a compliance change event if the CloudFormation stack has an UPDATE_COMPLETE instance status. Configure AWS Config to directly invoke the Lambda function to automatically remediate the change event.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches the UPDATE_COMPLETE event pattern for the instance status of the CloudFormation stack. Configure the rule to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Adjust the configuration of the CloudFormation stack to send notifications for only an UPDATE_COMPLETE instance status event to the SNS topic. Subscribe the Lambda function to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"当 AWS Systems Manager 检测到 CloudFormation 堆栈的实例状态出现 UPDATE_COMPLETE 事件时，运行 AWS-UpdateCloudFormationStack AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。 配置运行手册以调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"创建一个自定义的 AWS Config 规则，如果 CloudFormation 堆栈具有 UPDATE_COMPLETE 实例 状态，则生成合规性变更事件。配置 AWS Config 直接调用 Lambda 函数以自动修复变更事件。","C":"创建一个与 CloudFormation 堆栈实例状态的 UPDATE_COMPLETE 事件模式相匹配的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以调用 Lambda 函数。","D":"调整 CloudFormation 堆栈的配置，使其仅在实例状态事件为 UPDATE_COMPLETE 时向 SNS 主题 发送通知。将 Lambda 函数订阅到 SNS 主题。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudFormation automatically sends 'CloudFormation Stack Status Change' events to the EventBridge default event bus whenever a create, update, delete, or drift-detection operation occurs. Each event's detail contains status-details.status (for example UPDATE_COMPLETE) and the specific stack-id, so an EventBridge rule can match exactly the UPDATE_COMPLETE pattern for that stack and invoke a Lambda function directly as a target. The AWS docs even list this precise use case: 'Create stack or stack set specific tags on all resources provisioned through CloudFormation.' This is the native, fully event-driven, single-status, instance-scoped solution the question asks for, which is why C is correct.","explanation_zh":"CloudFormation 在發生 create、update、delete 或 drift-detection 操作時，會自動將 'CloudFormation Stack Status Change' 事件送到 EventBridge 預設事件匯流排。每個事件的 detail 內含 status-details.status（例如 UPDATE_COMPLETE）以及特定的 stack-id，因此可以建立 EventBridge rule 精確比對該堆疊的 UPDATE_COMPLETE 事件模式，並直接以 Lambda function 作為 target 觸發。AWS 文件甚至明確列出此使用情境：『為 CloudFormation 佈建的資源建立堆疊或堆疊集特定的標籤』。這正是題目要求的原生、完全事件驅動、針對單一狀態與特定執行個體的解法，因此 C 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no 'AWS-UpdateCloudFormationStack' Systems Manager Automation runbook that detects an UPDATE_COMPLETE event and invokes Lambda; SSM Automation does not natively watch for CloudFormation stack status events. The mechanism described is fabricated and would not trigger on stack update completion.","why_zh":"並不存在能偵測 UPDATE_COMPLETE 並呼叫 Lambda 的 'AWS-UpdateCloudFormationStack' Systems Manager Automation runbook；SSM Automation 不會原生監聽 CloudFormation 堆疊狀態事件。此機制屬虛構，無法在堆疊更新完成時觸發。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config evaluates resource configuration compliance; it does not emit a 'compliance change event' keyed to a transient UPDATE_COMPLETE stack status. UPDATE_COMPLETE is a momentary operational status, not a persistent configuration attribute, so a Config rule cannot reliably detect it, and Config remediation runs SSM documents rather than directly invoking Lambda for this scenario.","why_zh":"AWS Config 評估資源組態合規性，不會針對暫時性的 UPDATE_COMPLETE 堆疊狀態產生『合規變更事件』。UPDATE_COMPLETE 是瞬時的操作狀態而非持久組態屬性，因此 Config rule 無法可靠偵測，且 Config 補救是執行 SSM 文件而非直接呼叫 Lambda。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFormation stack notifications (NotificationARNs) cannot be configured to send only an UPDATE_COMPLETE event; CloudFormation publishes notifications for all stack and resource status changes to the SNS topic with no native filter to a single status. The described 'send notifications for only an UPDATE_COMPLETE' configuration does not exist, so this option misstates a capability.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 堆疊通知（NotificationARNs）無法設定為僅傳送 UPDATE_COMPLETE 事件；CloudFormation 會將所有堆疊與資源狀態變更通知都發佈到 SNS 主題，沒有原生過濾單一狀態的功能。所述『僅傳送 UPDATE_COMPLETE 通知』的設定並不存在，因此此選項錯誤描述了不存在的能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/eventbridge-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/events-detail-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/event-detail-stack-status-change.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/view-stack-events.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":213,"question_en":"A company deploys an application to two AWS Regions. The application creates and stores objects in an Amazon S3 bucket that is in the same Region as the application. Both deployments of the application need to have access to all the objects and their metadata from both Regions. The company has configured two- way replication between the S3 buckets and has enabled S3 Replication metrics on each S3 bucket. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution that retries the replication process if an object fails to replicate. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司将一个应用程序部署到了两个 AWS 区域。该应用程序会在与自身所在区域相同的区域内的一 个 Amazon S3 存储桶中创建并存储对象。应用程序的这两个部署都需要访问来自两个区域的所有对象及 其元数据。该公司已在两个 S3 存储桶之间配置了双向复制，并在每个 S3 存储桶上启用了 S3 复制指标。 一名 DevOps 工程师需要实现一个解决方案，如果对象复制失败，则重新尝试复制过程。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that listens to S3 event notifications for failed replication events. Create an AWS Lambda function that downloads the failed replication object and then runs a PutObject command for the object to the destination bucket. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function to handle the object that failed to replicate.","B":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Configure S3 event notifications to send failed replication notifications to the SQS queue. Create an AWS Lambda function that downloads the failed replication object and then runs a PutObject command for the object to the destination bucket. Configure the Lambda function to poll the queue for notifications to process.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that listens to S3 event notifications for failed replications. Create an AWS Lambda function that downloads the failed replication object and then runs a PutObject command for the object to the destination bucket.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that will use S3 batch operations to retry the replication on the existing object for a failed replication. Configure S3 event notifications to send failed replication notifications to the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于监听 S3 事件通知中的复制失败事件。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于下载复制失败的对象，然后对目标存储桶中的该对象运行 PutObject 命令。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用 Lambda 函数来处理复制失败的对象。","B":"创建一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列。配置 S3 事件通知，将失败的复制通知 发送到 SQS 队列。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于下载失败复制的对象，然后对目标存储桶中的 该对象运行 PutObject 命令。配置 Lambda 函数以轮询队列中的通知进行处理。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于监听 S3 失败复制事件通知。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数， 用于下载失败复制的对象，然后对目标存储桶运行 PutObject 命令。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数将使用 S3 批量操作对现有对象的复制失败情况进行重试。 配置 S3 事件通知，将复制失败通知发送到该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The genuinely correct retry mechanism is S3 Batch Replication, which is a Batch Operations job that AWS purpose-built to replicate objects that previously FAILED replication. The docs explicitly say you can filter a Batch Replication job by ObjectReplicationStatuses=\"FAILED\" to 'retry replicating only objects that previously failed to replicate.' Option D triggers this from S3 Event Notifications to Lambda (Lambda is a valid notification destination) and uses S3 Batch Operations to re-run the actual replication process, preserving replication semantics. Options A and C are eliminated because S3 does NOT send replication failure events to EventBridge: the EventBridge integration only emits Object Created/Deleted/Restore/StorageClassChanged/AccessTierChanged/ACL/Tag events, whereas s3:Replication:OperationFailedReplication is listed only under the 'Supported event types for SQS, SNS, and Lambda' destinations. Option B uses a valid SQS/Lambda path but does not retry the replication process at all; it bypasses replication by downloading the object and doing a manual cross-Region PutObject directly to the destination bucket, which loses replication metadata/status and is the wrong tool for a two-way replication setup.","explanation_zh":"真正正確的重試機制是 S3 Batch Replication，這是一個 Batch Operations 作業，AWS 專門設計用來重新複製先前 FAILED（複製失敗）的物件。官方文件明確指出可以用 ObjectReplicationStatuses=\"FAILED\" 篩選 Batch Replication 作業，以「只重試先前複製失敗的物件」。選項 D 透過 S3 Event Notifications 觸發 Lambda（Lambda 是合法的通知目的地），並使用 S3 Batch Operations 重新執行真正的複製流程，保留複製語意。選項 A 與 C 被排除，因為 S3 並不會把複製失敗事件送到 EventBridge：EventBridge 整合只發出 Object Created/Deleted/Restore/StorageClassChanged/AccessTierChanged/ACL/Tag 等事件，而 s3:Replication:OperationFailedReplication 只列在『SQS、SNS 和 Lambda 支援的事件類型』之下。選項 B 雖然使用了合法的 SQS/Lambda 路徑，但根本沒有重試複製流程；它是繞過複製，下載物件後手動跨區域 PutObject 直接寫入目的地儲存貯體，會遺失複製中繼資料/狀態，對於雙向複製設定來說是錯誤的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EventBridge does not receive S3 replication failure events; S3's EventBridge integration only emits Object Created/Deleted/Restore/StorageClass/AccessTier/ACL/Tag events, so a rule listening for failed-replication events will never fire. Also, PutObject directly to the destination bypasses the replication process and loses replication metadata.","why_zh":"EventBridge 不會收到 S3 複製失敗事件；S3 的 EventBridge 整合只發出 Object Created/Deleted/Restore/StorageClass/AccessTier/ACL/Tag 事件，因此監聽複製失敗事件的規則永遠不會觸發。此外，直接對目的地 PutObject 會繞過複製流程並遺失複製中繼資料。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Although SQS/Lambda is a valid notification destination for s3:Replication:OperationFailedReplication, this option does not retry the replication process: it bypasses replication with a manual download + cross-Region PutObject to the destination, losing replication metadata/status, and is problematic in a two-way replication topology. S3 can also invoke Lambda directly, making the SQS-poll construct unnecessary.","why_zh":"雖然 SQS/Lambda 是 s3:Replication:OperationFailedReplication 合法的通知目的地，但此選項並未重試複製流程：它以手動下載 + 跨區域 PutObject 寫入目的地來繞過複製，遺失複製中繼資料/狀態，且在雙向複製拓撲中會有問題。S3 亦可直接觸發 Lambda，使 SQS 輪詢結構成為多餘。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A: EventBridge does not emit S3 replication failure events, so the rule never triggers. The manual PutObject to the destination also bypasses the replication process rather than retrying it.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的致命缺陷：EventBridge 不會發出 S3 複製失敗事件，因此規則永遠不會觸發。對目的地的手動 PutObject 也是繞過而非重試複製流程。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-batch-replication-batch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-metrics-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/notification-how-to-event-types-and-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventBridge.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":214,"question_en":"A company needs to implement failover for its application. The application includes an Amazon CloudFront distribution and a public Application Load Balancer (ALB) in an AWS Region. The company has configured the ALB as the default origin for the distribution. After some recent application outages, the company wants a zero-second RTO. The company deploys the application to a secondary Region in a warm standby configuration. A DevOps engineer needs to automate the failover of the application to the secondary Region so that HTTP GET requests meet the desired RTO. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要为其应用程序实施故障转移。该应用程序包含一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发和一个位于 AWS 区域内的公共应用负载均衡器 （ALB）。该公司已将 ALB 配置为分发的默认源。 在最近出现了一些应用程序中断的情况后，该公司希望实现零秒恢复时间目标（RTO）。该公司将应用 程序部署到一个备用区域，采用热备配置。一位 DevOps 工程师需要实现应用程序自动切换到备用区域， 以确保 HTTP GET 请求满足期望的 RTO。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a second CloudFront distribution that has the secondary ALB as the default origin. Create Amazon Route 53 alias records that have a failover policy and Evaluate Target Health set to Yes for both CloudFront distributions. Update the application to use the new record set.","B":"Create a new origin on the distribution for the secondary ALB. Create a new origin group. Set the original ALB as the primary origin. Configure the origin group to fail over for HTTP 5xx status codes. Update the default behavior to use the origin group.","C":"Create Amazon Route 53 alias records that have a failover policy and Evaluate Target Health set to Yes for both ALBs. Set the TTL of both records to 0. Update the distribution's origin to use the new record set.","D":"Create a CloudFront function that detects HTTP 5xx status codes. Configure the function to return a 307 Temporary Redirect error response to the secondary ALB if the function detects 5xx status codes. Update the distribution's default behavior to send origin responses to the function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个将辅助 ALB 作为默认源的第二个 CloudFront 分发。为两个 CloudFront 分发创建具有故障转 移策略且“评估目标健康状况”设置为“是”的 Amazon Route 53 别名记录。更新应用程序以使用新 的记录集。","B":"在分发上为辅助 ALB 创建新的源。创建新的源组。将原始 ALB 设为主要源。配置源组以在出现 HTTP 5xx 状态码时进行故障转移。更新默认行为以使用源组。","C":"为两个应用负载均衡器（ALB）创建具有故障转移策略且“评估目标健康状况”设置为“是”的 Amazon Route 53 别名记录。将两个记录的生存时间（TTL）均设置为 0。更新分发的源以使用新的 记录集。","D":"创建一个 CloudFront 函数，用于检测 HTTP 5xx 状态码。将该函数配置为在检测到 5xx 状态码时向备用 ALB 返回 307 临时重定向错误响应。更新分发的默认行为，将源响应发送到该函数。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is a zero-second RTO for HTTP GET requests, while the architecture already uses a single CloudFront distribution with the primary ALB as the default origin. CloudFront origin failover (origin groups) is the AWS-documented mechanism that satisfies this: you add the secondary ALB as a second origin, create an origin group with the original ALB as primary, configure failover for HTTP 5xx status codes, and point the default behavior at the origin group. When the primary origin returns a configured failover status code (or fails to connect), CloudFront automatically re-routes the SAME viewer request to the secondary origin at the edge, so the GET still succeeds with effectively zero RTO - no DNS detection, propagation, or client re-resolution delay. AWS docs explicitly state CloudFront fails over only for GET, HEAD, and OPTIONS methods, which exactly matches the 'HTTP GET requests' requirement. This makes B correct.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是 HTTP GET 請求需達到 zero-second RTO，而架構已經使用單一 CloudFront distribution，並以主要 ALB 作為 default origin。CloudFront origin failover（origin groups）正是 AWS 文件記載能滿足此需求的機制：將次要 ALB 加為第二個 origin，建立 origin group 並把原 ALB 設為 primary，將 failover 條件設為 HTTP 5xx 狀態碼，再讓 default behavior 使用該 origin group。當 primary origin 回傳設定的 failover 狀態碼（或連線失敗）時，CloudFront 會在 edge 自動把同一筆 viewer 請求改送到 secondary origin，因此 GET 仍能成功，RTO 實質為零，毋須等待 DNS 偵測、傳播或用戶端重新解析。AWS 文件明確指出 CloudFront 只會對 GET、HEAD、OPTIONS 方法進行 failover，恰好對應題目的「HTTP GET requests」要求，故 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DNS-based failover between two CloudFront distributions via Route 53 cannot achieve zero-second RTO. Route 53 must first detect the failure via health checks and clients/resolvers must re-resolve DNS, both of which introduce delay. It also needlessly creates a second distribution and forces an application record-set change.","why_zh":"透過 Route 53 在兩個 CloudFront distribution 之間做 DNS failover 無法達成 zero-second RTO。Route 53 需先以 health check 偵測故障，用戶端／解析器也需重新解析 DNS，皆會產生延遲；此外還多建了一個 distribution 並強迫應用程式更換 record set。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Route 53 failover with TTL 0 is still DNS-based and cannot give zero RTO: health-check detection takes tens of seconds and resolvers/clients must re-query DNS. CloudFront also resolves and caches origin DNS rather than honoring a 0 TTL for instant per-request failover, so this does not meet the requirement.","why_zh":"即使 TTL 設為 0，Route 53 failover 仍屬 DNS 機制，無法達到 zero RTO：health check 偵測需數十秒，解析器／用戶端也須重新查詢 DNS。CloudFront 對 origin DNS 會解析並快取，並不會因 TTL 0 而做即時的逐請求 failover，故不符合需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFront Functions run only on viewer request/response events and cannot inspect origin responses; you cannot 'send origin responses to the function' (that is a Lambda@Edge origin-response capability). Returning a 307 redirect to the client also adds a round trip and surfaces an error first, so it is neither technically valid nor zero-RTO.","why_zh":"CloudFront Functions 只在 viewer request／response 事件執行，無法檢視 origin response；無法將 origin response 送給該 function（那是 Lambda@Edge 的 origin-response 能力）。回傳 307 redirect 給用戶端還會多一個來回並先暴露錯誤，因此既不技術可行也非 zero-RTO。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-cloudfront-distribution-origingroupfailovercriteria.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":215,"question_en":"A cloud team uses AWS Organizations and AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to manage a company's AWS accounts. The company recently established a research team. The research team requires the ability to fully manage the resources in its account. The research team must not be able to create IAM users. The cloud team creates a Research Administrator permission set in IAM Identity Center for the research team. The permission set has the AdministratorAccess AWS managed policy attached. The cloud team must ensure that no one on the research team can create IAM users. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个云团队使用 AWS 组织和 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）来管理公司的 AWS 账户。该公司最 近成立了一个研究团队。该研究团队需要能够完全管理其账户中的资源。该研究团队不得能够创建 IAM 用 户。 云团队在 IAM 身份中心为研究团队创建了一个“研究管理员”权限集。该权限集附加了“AdministratorA ccess”AWS 管理策略。云团队必须确保研究团队中的任何人都不能创建 IAM 用户。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM policy that denies the iam:CreateUser action. Attach the IAM policy to the Research Administrator permission set.","B":"Create an IAM policy that allows all actions except the iam:CreateUser action. Use the IAM policy to set the permissions boundary for the Research Administrator permission set.","C":"Create an SCP that denies the iam:CreateUser action. Attach the SCP to the research team's AWS account.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that deletes IAM users. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that detects the IAM CreateUser event. Configure the rule to invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个拒绝执行 iam:CreateUser 操作的 IAM 策略。将该 IAM 策略附加到“研究管理员”权限集。","B":"创建一个 IAM 策略，允许除 iam:CreateUser 操作之外的所有操作。使用该 IAM 策略为“研究管理员”权 限集设置权限边界。","C":"创建一个拒绝执行 iam:CreateUser 操作的 SCP（服务控制策略）。将该 SCP 附加到研究团队的 AWS 账户。","D":"创建一个用于删除 IAM 用户的 AWS Lambda 函数。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则来检测 IAM 的 CreateUser 事件。配置该规则以调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"An IAM Identity Center permission set provisions an IAM role in the target account; AdministratorAccess on that permission set grants full access. To remove a single action while keeping everything else, attach a customer managed (or inline) policy with an explicit Deny on iam:CreateUser to the Research Administrator permission set. Explicit deny always overrides any Allow (including AdministratorAccess) per IAM policy evaluation logic, so the research team keeps full management of resources but cannot create IAM users. This control is scoped precisely to the Research Administrator permission set, which is exactly the entity the question wants restricted, and it adds the least operational overhead (no extra account-wide guardrails or reactive automation). Option C (SCP) also blocks the action but applies the guardrail to every IAM principal in the entire account, not just the research team's role, which is broader than required; the question is built around restricting the permission set, so the targeted deny on the permission set is the better fit.","explanation_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的 permission set 會在目標帳號內佈建一個 IAM role；附加 AdministratorAccess 即授予完整權限。要在保留其他所有權限的同時移除單一動作，應在 Research Administrator permission set 上附加一個明確 Deny iam:CreateUser 的 customer managed（或 inline）policy。依 IAM policy 評估邏輯，explicit deny 永遠覆蓋任何 Allow（包含 AdministratorAccess），因此研究團隊仍可完整管理資源但無法建立 IAM users。此控制精確地限定在 Research Administrator permission set，正是題目要限制的對象，且營運負擔最低（不需額外的帳號層級 guardrail 或事後補救的自動化）。選項 C（SCP）雖也能封鎖該動作，但其 guardrail 會套用到整個帳號內所有 IAM principal，而非僅研究團隊的 role，範圍超出需求；題目以限制 permission set 為核心，故在 permission set 上做針對性 deny 更為合適。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A permissions boundary works by intersection and would technically block iam:CreateUser if written as Allow with NotAction, but a permissions boundary that 'allows all actions except iam:CreateUser' is the indirect, more convoluted way to do this. A simple explicit Deny on the action (option A) is the direct, standard mechanism; permissions boundaries are meant to delegate safe role/user creation, not to subtract one action from an admin.","why_zh":"permissions boundary 以交集運作，若以 Allow + NotAction 撰寫確實能封鎖 iam:CreateUser，但「允許除 iam:CreateUser 外的所有動作」是迂迴且較繁複的做法。直接對該動作做 explicit Deny（選項 A）才是標準直接的機制；permissions boundary 的用途是安全地委派 role/user 建立，而非從 admin 中扣除單一動作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP attached to the account applies to ALL IAM users and roles in that account (every principal, every permission set/role), not just the research team's Research Administrator permission set. The requirement is to restrict the research team specifically via their permission set, so an account-wide SCP is broader than needed and is not the targeted control the scenario calls for.","why_zh":"附加在帳號上的 SCP 會套用到該帳號內所有 IAM users 與 roles（每個 principal、每個 permission set/role），而非僅研究團隊的 Research Administrator permission set。需求是透過該 permission set 針對研究團隊做限制，因此帳號層級的 SCP 範圍過大，並非情境所需的針對性控制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Lambda + EventBridge to delete users is reactive, not preventive: the IAM user is actually created and exists for a window before deletion, so it does not 'ensure no one can create IAM users.' It is a security gap with high operational overhead compared to a simple deny policy.","why_zh":"以 Lambda + EventBridge 刪除使用者屬於事後補救而非預防：IAM user 實際上已被建立並存在一段時間才被刪除，無法達到「確保沒人能建立 IAM users」。相較簡單的 deny policy，這是有安全漏洞且營運負擔高的做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/howtocreatepermissionset.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":216,"question_en":"A company releases a new application in a new AWS account. The application includes an AWS Lambda function that processes messages from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue. The Lambda function stores the results in an Amazon S3 bucket for further downstream processing. The Lambda function needs to process the messages within a specific period of time after the messages are published. The Lambda function has a batch size of 10 messages and takes a few seconds to process a batch of messages. As load increases on the application's first day of service, messages in the queue accumulate at a greater rate than the Lambda function can process the messages. Some messages miss the required processing timelines. The logs show that many messages in the queue have data that is not valid. The company needs to meet the timeline requirements for messages that have valid data. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在新的 AWS 账户中发布了一个新的应用程序。该应用程序包含一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于处理 来自 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）标准队列的消息。Lambda 函数将处理结果存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，以便进行后续的下游处理。Lambda 函数需要在消息发布后的特定时间段内处理这些 消息。该 Lambda 函数的批处理大小为 10 条消息，处理一批消息需要几秒钟。 在应用程序投入使用的首日，随着负载的增加，队列中的消息积累速度超过了 Lambda 函数处理消息的速度。 一些消息未能在规定时间内完成处理。日志显示，队列中有许多消息的数据无效。该公司需要确保数据有 效的消息能够满足处理时间的要求。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the Lambda function's batch size. Change the SQS standard queue to an SQS FIFO queue. Request a Lambda concurrency increase in the AWS Region.","B":"Reduce the Lambda function's batch size. Increase the SQS message throughput quota. Request a Lambda concurrency increase in the AWS Region.","C":"Increase the Lambda function's batch size. Configure S3 Transfer Acceleration on the S3 bucket. Configure an SQS dead-letter queue.","D":"Keep the Lambda function's batch size the same. Configure the Lambda function to report failed batch items. Configure an SQS dead-letter queue."},"options_zh":{"A":"增加 Lambda 函数的批处理大小。将 SQS 标准队列更改为 SQS FIFO 队列。在 AWS 区域中请求增加 Lambda 并发量。","B":"减小 Lambda 函数的批处理大小。提高 SQS 消息吞吐量配额。在 AWS 区域内请求增加 Lambda 并发 量。","C":"增加 Lambda 函数的批处理大小。在 S3 存储桶上配置 S3 传输加速。配置一个 SQS 死信队列。","D":"保持 Lambda 函数的批处理大小不变。将 Lambda 函数配置为报告失败的批处理项。配置一个 SQS 死信 队列。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two compounding problems exist: insufficient throughput and many invalid-data messages causing batch failures. By default, when a Lambda function errors on any message in a batch, the entire batch (including valid messages) becomes visible again and is reprocessed, and Lambda backs off by scaling DOWN the concurrency allocated to the SQS event source mapping. AWS docs state that with ReportBatchItemFailures (partial batch response) enabled, 'Lambda doesn't scale down message polling when function invocations fail' and explicitly recommend it 'If you expect some messages to fail and you don't want those failures to impact the message processing rate.' This protects the valid messages' processing rate and prevents reprocessing of already-succeeded messages. Pairing this with a dead-letter queue (via redrive policy / maxReceiveCount) isolates the persistently-failing invalid messages so they stop being redelivered and consuming capacity. Option D keeps the batch size unchanged, which is correct because increasing batch size would only drag MORE valid messages into a batch that one invalid message could fail.","explanation_zh":"存在兩個相互加劇的問題：吞吐量不足，以及大量無效資料訊息導致批次處理失敗。預設情況下，當 Lambda 函式在批次中任一訊息上發生錯誤時，整個批次（包含有效訊息）會重新變為可見並被重新處理，且 Lambda 會以退避策略「縮減」分配給 SQS event source mapping 的並行度。AWS 文件指出，啟用 ReportBatchItemFailures（部分批次回應）後，「Lambda 在函式呼叫失敗時不會縮減訊息輪詢」，並明確建議「若您預期部分訊息會失敗，且不希望這些失敗影響訊息處理速率」時使用此功能。這可保護有效訊息的處理速率，並避免重新處理已成功的訊息。再搭配 dead-letter queue（透過 redrive policy / maxReceiveCount）可將反覆失敗的無效訊息隔離，使其不再被重新投遞並佔用處理容量。選項 D 維持批次大小不變是正確的，因為增大批次只會把「更多」有效訊息拖入可能因單一無效訊息而失敗的批次中。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing batch size pulls more valid messages into a batch that one invalid message can fail (causing full-batch reprocessing). Switching to FIFO reduces throughput (default 300 msg/s) and worsens the problem because a poison/invalid message blocks its entire message group.","why_zh":"增大批次會把更多有效訊息納入可能因單一無效訊息而失敗的批次（導致整批重新處理）。改用 FIFO 會降低吞吐量（預設 300 msg/s），且因毒訊息會阻塞整個 message group 而使問題惡化。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SQS standard queues already provide near-unlimited throughput; the bottleneck is Lambda, not an SQS throughput quota. Reducing batch size lowers efficiency, and nothing here stops invalid messages from failing batches and triggering Lambda concurrency back-off.","why_zh":"SQS 標準佇列本身已提供近乎無限的吞吐量；瓶頸在於 Lambda，而非 SQS 吞吐量配額。縮小批次降低效率，且此選項無法阻止無效訊息使批次失敗並觸發 Lambda 並行度退避。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Increasing batch size worsens the failed-batch problem. S3 Transfer Acceleration only speeds long-distance uploads and is irrelevant to the SQS/Lambda timeline. A DLQ alone (without ReportBatchItemFailures) still lets one invalid message fail the whole batch, reprocess valid messages, and trigger concurrency scale-down.","why_zh":"增大批次會加劇批次失敗問題。S3 Transfer Acceleration 僅加速長距離上傳，與 SQS/Lambda 時限無關。僅設定 DLQ（未啟用 ReportBatchItemFailures）仍會讓單一無效訊息使整批失敗、重新處理有效訊息並觸發並行度縮減。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-errorhandling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-sqs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-dead-letter-queues.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":217,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on AWS Lambda and sends logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. An Amazon Kinesis data stream is subscribed to the log groups in CloudWatch Logs. A single consumer Lambda function processes the logs from the data stream and stores the logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company’s DevOps team has noticed high latency during the processing and ingestion of some logs. Which combination of steps will reduce the latency? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在 AWS Lambda 上的应用程序，该应用程序将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。 一个 Amazon Kinesis 数据流订阅了 CloudWatch Logs 中的日志组。一个单独的消费者 Lambda 函数从数据 流中处理日志，并将日志存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 该公司的 DevOps 团队注意到在处理和摄取某些日志时存在高延迟。 哪些步骤的组合可以降低延迟？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a data stream consumer with enhanced fan-out. Set the Lambda function that processes the logs as the consumer.","B":"Increase the ParallelizationFactor setting in the Lambda event source mapping.","C":"Configure reserved concurrency for the Lambda function that processes the logs.","D":"Increase the batch size in the Kinesis data stream.","E":"Turn off the ReportBatchItemFailures setting in the Lambda event source mapping.","F":"Increase the number of shards in the Kinesis data stream."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有增强型扇出功能的数据流消费者。将处理日志的 Lambda 函数设置为该消费者。","B":"在 Lambda 事件源映射中增加 ParallelizationFactor 设置。","C":"为处理日志的 Lambda 函数配置预留并发量。","D":"增大 Kinesis 数据流中的批处理大小。","E":"在 Lambda 事件源映射中关闭 ReportBatchItemFailures 设置。","F":"增加 Kinesis 数据流中的分片数量。"},"answer":["A","B","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The pipeline is Kinesis Data Stream -> single consumer Lambda (via event source mapping) -> S3, and the symptom is high processing/ingestion latency (effectively a high IteratorAge). The official Lambda-with-Kinesis guidance lists exactly three levers to increase processing speed and reduce latency. (A) Enhanced fan-out creates a dedicated-throughput consumer that gives each shard a dedicated 2 MB/s connection and uses HTTP/2 to push records over a long-lived connection; AWS states this is done 'to minimize latency and maximize read throughput.' (F) Adding shards means 'there are more batches being processed at once,' increasing the speed at which the function processes records. (B) Increasing ParallelizationFactor lets Lambda process a single shard with up to 10 concurrent invocations; AWS explicitly recommends this 'when the data volume is volatile and the IteratorAge is high,' which matches the described latency symptom. These three are the canonical AWS-documented remedies, so the dump's suggested answer is correct.","explanation_zh":"此架構為 Kinesis Data Stream -> 單一 consumer Lambda (透過 event source mapping) -> S3，症狀是處理/擷取延遲過高 (實質上即 IteratorAge 偏高)。官方 Lambda with Kinesis 文件正好列出三個提升處理速度、降低延遲的手段。(A) Enhanced fan-out 建立專屬吞吐的 consumer，為每個 shard 提供專屬 2 MB/s 連線並以 HTTP/2 透過長連線推送記錄，AWS 明言此舉是為了「最小化延遲並最大化讀取吞吐」。(F) 增加 shard 數量代表「同時處理更多批次」，提升函式處理記錄的速度。(B) 提高 ParallelizationFactor 可讓 Lambda 以最多 10 個並行調用處理單一 shard，AWS 明確建議在「資料量波動且 IteratorAge 偏高」時採用，正符合本題的延遲症狀。這三項是 AWS 文件記載的標準解法，故 dump 建議答案正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Reserved concurrency sets a fixed maximum (cap) on concurrent executions for the function. It limits scaling rather than increasing throughput, and an overly low value would throttle the consumer and worsen latency. It does not by itself reduce processing latency.","why_zh":"Reserved concurrency 為函式設定並行執行數的固定上限 (cap)，是限制而非提升吞吐量；數值過低反而會節流 consumer、加劇延遲，本身無法降低處理延遲。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Increasing the batch size makes Lambda gather more records before each invocation, increasing buffering/wait time and the per-invocation processing duration. This tends to raise per-record latency, not reduce it.","why_zh":"增加 batch size 會讓 Lambda 在每次調用前累積更多記錄，增加緩衝等待時間與單次處理時長，通常會提高 (而非降低) 每筆記錄的延遲。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"ReportBatchItemFailures enables partial batch responses so only the failed records are retried instead of reprocessing the whole batch. Turning it OFF forces full-batch retries on any failure, which blocks the shard and increases latency rather than reducing it.","why_zh":"ReportBatchItemFailures 啟用部分批次回應，僅重試失敗的記錄而非整批重處理。將其關閉會在任何失敗時強制整批重試，阻塞該 shard 並增加 (而非降低) 延遲。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-kinesis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/enhanced-consumers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-eventsourcemapping.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_CreateEventSourceMapping.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":218,"question_en":"A company operates sensitive workloads across the AWS accounts that are in the company's organization in AWS Organizations. The company uses an IP address range to delegate IP addresses for Amazon VPC CIDR blocks and all non-cloud hardware. The company needs a solution that prevents principals that are outside the company’s IP address range from performing AWS actions in the organization's accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司在其 AWS 组织中的多个 AWS 账户中运行敏感工作负载。该公司使用一个 IP 地址范围来为 Amazon VPC CIDR 块和所有非云硬件分配 IP 地址。 该公司需要一个解决方案，以防止不在公司 IP 地址范围内的主体在组织的账户中执行 AWS 操作。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Firewall Manager for the organization. Create an AWS Network Firewall policy that allows only source traffic from the company's IP address range. Set the policy scope to all accounts in the organization.","B":"In Organizations, create an SCP that denies source IP addresses that are outside of the company’s IP address range. Attach the SCP to the organization's root.","C":"Configure Amazon GuardDuty for the organization. Create a GuardDuty trusted IP address list for the company's IP range. Activate the trusted IP list for the organization.","D":"In Organizations, create an SCP that allows source IP addresses that are inside of the company’s IP address range. Attach the SCP to the organization's root."},"options_zh":{"A":"为组织配置 AWS 防火墙管理器。创建一个仅允许来自公司 IP 地址范围的源流量的 AWS 网络防火墙策 略。将策略范围设置为组织中的所有账户。","B":"在组织中，创建一个安全策略配置文件（SCP），拒绝来自公司 IP 地址范围之外的源 IP 地址。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","C":"为组织配置 Amazon GuardDuty。为公司的 IP 范围创建一个 GuardDuty 可信 IP 地址列表。为组织激活 可信 IP 列表。","D":"在组织中，创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许公司 IP 地址范围内的源 IP 地址。将该 SCP 附加到 组织的根目录。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is an organization-wide guardrail that blocks any principal whose request originates outside the company IP range. A Deny SCP attached to the organization root applies to all member accounts and acts as a maximum-permission guardrail. The canonical AWS pattern for this is exactly option B: an SCP with Effect: Deny, Action: *, Resource: * and a NotIpAddress condition on aws:SourceIp, which explicitly denies all actions when the request comes from outside the listed CIDR ranges (the deny-list strategy). Because an explicit Deny always overrides any Allow, the request is blocked regardless of identity-based or other allow policies. Option D fails because SCPs NEVER grant permissions; an 'allow' SCP only sets a ceiling and, since the default FullAWSAccess (Allow *) policy remains attached, an additional allow SCP does not remove or deny anything outside the IP range, so out-of-range principals would still be permitted.","explanation_zh":"需求是建立組織層級的護欄 (guardrail)，阻擋任何來自公司 IP 範圍之外的 principal 發出的請求。將 Deny SCP 附加到組織 root 會套用到所有成員帳戶，並作為最大權限護欄。AWS 的標準做法正是選項 B：一條 Effect: Deny、Action: *、Resource: * 並對 aws:SourceIp 使用 NotIpAddress 條件的 SCP，當請求來自所列 CIDR 範圍以外時即明確拒絕所有動作 (deny-list 策略)。由於明確的 Deny 永遠覆蓋任何 Allow，無論 identity-based 或其他 allow 政策為何，該請求都會被封鎖。選項 D 不可行，因為 SCP 永遠不會授予權限；'allow' SCP 只是設定上限，而預設的 FullAWSAccess (Allow *) 政策仍然存在，額外的 allow SCP 並不會移除或拒絕 IP 範圍以外的任何動作，因此範圍外的 principal 仍會被允許。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Network Firewall / Firewall Manager filter network traffic flowing through VPCs (data-plane packet filtering); they do not control who can call AWS APIs (the control plane). They cannot deny AWS actions by principal source IP across all accounts, and require deployed firewall endpoints/VPCs, which is the wrong layer for this requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Network Firewall / Firewall Manager 過濾流經 VPC 的網路流量 (data-plane 封包過濾)，無法控制誰可以呼叫 AWS API (control plane)。它們無法依 principal 來源 IP 在所有帳戶層級拒絕 AWS 動作，且需部署防火牆端點/VPC，屬於錯誤的防護層。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that only generates findings/alerts. A trusted IP list merely suppresses findings for those IPs; it never blocks or denies any AWS API action. It cannot enforce a preventive permission guardrail.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務，只會產生 findings/警示。trusted IP list 只是抑制這些 IP 的 findings，從不封鎖或拒絕任何 AWS API 動作，無法作為預防性的權限護欄。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SCPs never grant permissions; they only cap them. With the default FullAWSAccess (Allow *) still attached, adding an SCP that 'allows' the company IP range does not deny anything outside that range, so out-of-range principals remain permitted. To restrict, you need an explicit Deny (option B). An allow-only SCP does not produce the intended block.","why_zh":"SCP 永遠不會授予權限，只會設上限。在預設 FullAWSAccess (Allow *) 仍附加的情況下，新增一條『允許』公司 IP 範圍的 SCP 並不會拒絕範圍外的任何動作，因此範圍外的 principal 仍被允許。要做到限制必須使用明確的 Deny (選項 B)，只有 allow 的 SCP 無法產生預期的封鎖效果。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_aws_deny-ip.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":219,"question_en":"A company deploys an application in two AWS Regions. The application currently uses an Amazon S3 bucket in the primary Region to store data. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that the application is highly available in both Regions. The DevOps engineer has created a new S3 bucket in the secondary Region. All existing and new objects must be in both S3 buckets. The application must fail over between the Regions with no data loss. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在两个 AWS 区域部署了一个应用程序。该应用程序目前使用主区域中的一个 Amazon S3 存 储桶来存储数据。 DevOps 工程师需要确保应用程序在两个区域都具有高可用性。该 DevOps 工程师已在辅助区域创建了 一个新的 S3 存储桶。所有现有和新的对象都必须同时存在于两个 S3 存储桶中。应用程序必须能够在两 个区域之间进行故障转移，且不能丢失任何数据。 哪种步骤组合能以最高的运营效率满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new IAM role that allows the Amazon S3 and S3 Batch Operations service principals to assume the role that has the necessary permissions for S3 replication.","B":"Create a new IAM role that allows the AWS Batch service principal to assume the role that has the necessary permissions for S3 replication.","C":"Create an S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) rule on the source S3 bucket. Configure the rule to use the IAM role for Amazon S3 to replicate to the target S3 bucket.","D":"Create a two-way replication rule on the source S3 bucket. Configure the rule to use the IAM role for Amazon S3 to replicate to the target S3 bucket.","E":"Create an AWS Batch job that has an AWS Fargate orchestration type. Configure the job to use the IAM role for AWS Batch. Specify a Bash command to use the AWS CLI to synchronize the contents of the source S3 bucket and the target S3 bucket","F":"Create an operation in S3 Batch Operations to replicate the contents of the source S3 bucket to the target S3 bucket. Configure the operation to use the IAM role for Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 IAM 角色，允许 Amazon S3 和 S3 批量操作服务主体承担具有 S3 复制所需权限的 角色。","B":"创建一个新的 IAM 角色，允许 AWS Batch 服务主体承担具有 S3 复制所需权限的角色。","C":"在源 S3 存储桶上创建一个 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）规则。配置该规则以使用 Amazon S3 的 IAM 角色 将数据复制到目标 S3 存储桶。","D":"在源 S3 存储桶上创建双向复制规则。配置该规则以使用 Amazon S3 的 IAM 角色将数据复制到目标 S3 存储桶。","E":"创建一个具有 AWS Fargate 调度类型的 AWS Batch 作业。将作业配置为使用 AWS Batch 的 IAM 角色。 指定一个 Bash 命令，使用 AWS CLI 同步源 S3 存储桶和目标 S3 存储桶的内容。","F":"在 S3 批量操作中创建一个操作，将源 S3 存储桶的内容复制到目标 S3 存储桶。配置该操作以使用 Amazon S3 的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario needs all EXISTING and NEW objects in both buckets, plus cross-Region failover with NO data loss, at MOST operational efficiency, so native S3 replication features are correct over custom scripts. (D) A two-way (bi-directional) replication rule with CRR is the documented way to make the application highly available and keep buckets in sync during failover: when the app fails over and writes to the secondary bucket, two-way replication copies that data back, preventing data loss. (F) Live replication only copies NEW objects after it is enabled, so to replicate the EXISTING objects you must use S3 Batch Operations (S3 Batch Replication), an on-demand job. (A) Because the single IAM role serves both live two-way replication AND a Batch Replication job, its trust policy must allow BOTH the Amazon S3 (s3.amazonaws.com) and S3 Batch Operations (batchoperations.s3.amazonaws.com) service principals to assume it; AWS docs show exactly this combined trust policy and say to use it when creating a Batch Replication job.","explanation_zh":"此情境要求所有「現有」與「新」物件都存在於兩個值區，並需跨 Region 故障轉移且「不遺失資料」，同時以「最高營運效率」達成，因此應使用 S3 原生複寫功能而非自訂腳本。(D) 使用 CRR 的雙向 (bi-directional) 複寫規則，是官方文件記載讓應用程式高可用並在故障轉移期間保持值區同步的方式：當應用程式故障轉移並寫入次要值區時，雙向複寫會把資料複寫回來，避免資料遺失。(F) Live replication 只會複寫啟用後的「新」物件，因此要複寫「現有」物件必須使用 S3 Batch Operations (S3 Batch Replication) 這種隨需作業。(A) 由於同一個 IAM 角色同時用於雙向 live replication 與 Batch Replication 作業，其信任政策必須同時允許 Amazon S3 (s3.amazonaws.com) 與 S3 Batch Operations (batchoperations.s3.amazonaws.com) 兩個服務主體擔任該角色；AWS 文件正是展示此合併信任政策，並說明建立 Batch Replication 作業時要使用它。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 Batch Operations / Batch Replication uses the batchoperations.s3.amazonaws.com service principal, not the AWS Batch (batch.amazonaws.com) compute service. AWS Batch is unrelated to S3 replication, so this trust policy would not work.","why_zh":"S3 Batch Operations / Batch Replication 使用的是 batchoperations.s3.amazonaws.com 服務主體，並非 AWS Batch (batch.amazonaws.com) 這個運算服務。AWS Batch 與 S3 複寫無關，此信任政策無法運作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"One-way Cross-Region Replication alone does not meet 'fail over with no data loss.' After failover, writes go to the secondary bucket; one-way CRR will not replicate those writes back to the primary, so data written during failover would be lost. Two-way replication (D) is required.","why_zh":"單向 Cross-Region Replication 無法滿足「故障轉移且不遺失資料」。故障轉移後寫入會進入次要值區；單向 CRR 不會把這些寫入複寫回主要值區，導致故障轉移期間寫入的資料遺失。必須使用雙向複寫 (D)。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Building a custom AWS Batch + Fargate job running a Bash 'aws s3 sync' script is a manual, self-managed solution with high operational overhead and is not continuous live replication. It is the opposite of MOST operational efficiency; native S3 two-way replication plus Batch Replication is the managed approach.","why_zh":"建立自訂的 AWS Batch + Fargate 作業執行 Bash 的『aws s3 sync』腳本，是需自行維護、營運負擔高的方案，且非持續性 live replication。這與「最高營運效率」背道而馳；原生 S3 雙向複寫加 Batch Replication 才是受管做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-batch-replication-batch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-batch-replication-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/setting-repl-config-perm-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mrap-create-two-way-replication-rules.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":220,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The company needs an automated process across all AWS accounts to isolate any compromised Amazon EC2 instances when the instances receive a specific tag. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司需要一个跨所有 AWS 账 户的自动化流程，在 Amazon EC2 实例收到特定标签时将其隔离。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy the CloudFormation stacks in all AWS accounts.","B":"Create an SCP that has a Deny statement for the ec2:* action with a condition of \"aws:RequestTag/ isolation\": false.","C":"Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","D":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that creates an EC2 instance role that has no IAM policies attached. Configure the template to have a security group that has an explicit Deny rule on all traffic. Use the CloudFormation template to create an AWS Lambda function that attaches the IAM role to instances. Configure the Lambda function to add a network ACL. Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function when a specific tag is applied to a compromised EC2 instance.","E":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that creates an EC2 instance role that has no IAM policies attached. Configure the template to have a security group that has no inbound rules or outbound rules. Use the CloudFormation template to create an AWS Lambda function that attaches the IAM role to instances. Configure the Lambda function to replace any existing security groups with the new security group. Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function when a specific tag is applied to a compromised EC2 instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在所有 AWS 账户中部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。","B":"创建一个 SCP，其中包含针对 ec2:* 操作的拒绝语句，并设置aws:RequestTag/isolation\": false 。","C":"将 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","D":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于创建一个未附加任何 IAM 策略的 EC2 实例角色。配置模 板以包含一个对所有流量都有明确拒绝规则的安全组。使用 CloudFormation 模板创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 IAM 角色附加到实例上。配置 Lambda 函数以添加网络访问控制列表（ACL）。 设置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，当特定标签应用于受攻击的 EC2 实例时调用 Lambda 函数。","E":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于创建一个未附加任何 IAM 策略的 EC2 实例角色。配置该模 板，使其包含一个既无入站规则也无出站规则的安全组。使用 CloudFormation 模板创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 IAM 角色附加到实例上。配置 Lambda 函数，使其用新安全组替换任何现有的安全 组。设置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在将特定标签应用于受攻击的 EC2 实例时调用 Lambda 函 数。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is an automated, organization-wide process that isolates a compromised EC2 instance when a specific tag is applied. A is correct because AWS CloudFormation StackSets is the documented mechanism to deploy the same stack (Lambda, EventBridge rule, isolation security group, IAM role) into all accounts in an AWS Organization in a single operation. E is correct because it implements the exact isolation procedure AWS prescribes for a compromised EC2 instance: create a dedicated isolation security group that has no inbound or outbound rules, then remove all existing security group associations and replace them with the isolation security group, attach a quarantine IAM role with no policies, and trigger the whole thing from an EventBridge rule that fires when the specific tag is applied. This matches the GuardDuty 'Remediating a potentially compromised Amazon EC2 instance' guidance step-for-step (isolation SG with no 0.0.0.0/0 rules, associate it, then remove all other SG associations). The decisive qualifier is 'automated process across all AWS accounts' triggered by a tag, which points to StackSets for fan-out (A) plus an event-driven Lambda that swaps the security group (E).","explanation_zh":"需求是一個跨整個組織的自動化流程：當套用特定標籤時隔離受感染的 EC2 執行個體。A 正確，因為 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 是官方文件記載的機制，可在單一操作中將同一個堆疊（Lambda、EventBridge 規則、隔離安全群組、IAM 角色）部署到 AWS Organizations 的所有帳戶。E 正確，因為它完全實作 AWS 對受感染 EC2 執行個體所規定的隔離程序：建立一個沒有任何輸入或輸出規則的專用隔離 security group，移除所有現有的 security group 關聯並以該隔離 security group 取代，附加一個沒有任何政策的隔離 IAM 角色，並由偵測到特定標籤時觸發的 EventBridge 規則啟動整個流程。這與 GuardDuty「Remediating a potentially compromised Amazon EC2 instance」指南逐步吻合（建立沒有 0.0.0.0/0 規則的隔離 SG、關聯它、然後移除所有其他 SG 關聯）。決定性的限定詞是『跨所有 AWS 帳戶的自動化流程』且由標籤觸發，這指向用 StackSets 做扇出（A）加上以事件驅動的 Lambda 替換 security group（E）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An SCP that denies ec2:* is a preventive guardrail evaluated at request time on principals; it does not perform or trigger automated isolation of an already-running compromised instance. The condition 'aws:RequestTag/isolation: false' is also malformed: aws:RequestTag/isolation only exists in the request context when that tag is being supplied in the request, and it is a string value, not a boolean - so this condition would not match the act of applying an isolation tag, and denying all ec2:* would break legitimate operations rather than isolate a host.","why_zh":"拒絕 ec2:* 的 SCP 是在請求時針對主體評估的預防性護欄，無法對已在執行中的受感染執行個體執行或觸發自動隔離。條件『aws:RequestTag/isolation: false』本身也有問題：aws:RequestTag/isolation 只有在請求中正在提供該標籤時才會存在於請求情境中，且其值為字串而非布林值，因此此條件不會匹配套用隔離標籤的動作；而拒絕所有 ec2:* 會破壞正常操作，並不能隔離主機。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This only matters if B were correct; it attaches the flawed SCP from B to the org root. Since B does not achieve automated tag-triggered isolation (and would broadly deny EC2 operations), attaching it does not meet the requirement.","why_zh":"只有在 B 正確時這才有意義；它將 B 中有缺陷的 SCP 附加到組織根。由於 B 無法達成由標籤觸發的自動隔離（且會廣泛拒絕 EC2 操作），附加它並不能滿足需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Two technical flaws. First, security groups support only allow rules - there is no 'explicit Deny rule on all traffic'; isolation is achieved with an empty (no-rule) security group, which E does correctly. Second, D only attaches the role and adds a NACL but never removes the instance's existing security groups, so the existing permissive SGs would still allow traffic; AWS's procedure requires removing/replacing all other SG associations, which only E does.","why_zh":"有兩處技術缺陷。第一，security group 只支援允許規則，不存在『對所有流量的明確 Deny 規則』；隔離是透過沒有任何規則的空 security group 達成，這正是 E 的做法。第二，D 只附加角色並新增 NACL，卻從未移除執行個體現有的 security group，因此既有的寬鬆 SG 仍會允許流量；AWS 的程序要求移除／取代所有其他 SG 關聯，只有 E 做到這點。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/what-is-cfnstacksets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/security-group-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/security-ir/latest/userguide/destination-containment.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":221,"question_en":"A company manages multiple AWS accounts by using AWS Organizations with OUs for the different business divisions. The company is updating their corporate network to use new IP address ranges. The company has 10 Amazon S3 buckets in different AWS accounts. The S3 buckets store reports for the different divisions. The S3 bucket configurations allow only private corporate network IP addresses to access the S3 buckets. A DevOps engineer needs to change the range of IP addresses that have permission to access the contents of the S3 buckets. The DevOps engineer also needs to revoke the permissions of two OUs in the company. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过使用 AWS 组织和组织单位（OU）来管理多个 AWS 账户，每个组织单位对应不同的 业务部门。该公司正在更新其企业网络以使用新的 IP 地址范围。该公司在不同的 AWS 账户中有 10 个 Amazon S3 存储桶，这些存储桶存储着不同部门的报告。S3 存储桶的配置仅允许来自公司内部私 有网络的 IP 地址访问这些存储桶。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要更改有权访问 S3 存储桶内容的 IP 地址范围。该 DevOps 工程师还需要撤销 公司内两个组织单位的权限。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new SCP that has two statements, one that allows access to the new range of IP addresses for all the S3 buckets and one that denies access to the old range of IP addresses for all the S3 buckets. Set a permissions boundary for the OrganizationAccountAccessRole role in the two OUs to deny access to the S3 buckets.","B":"Create a new SCP that has a statement that allows only the new range of IP addresses to access the S3 buckets. Create another SCP that denies access to the S3 buckets. Attach the second SCP to the two OUs.","C":"On all the S3 buckets, configure resource-based policies that allow only the new range of IP addresses to access the S3 buckets. Create a new SCP that denies access to the S3 buckets. Attach the SCP to the two OUs.","D":"On all the S3 buckets, configure resource-based policies that allow only the new range of IP addresses to access the S3 buckets. Set a permissions boundary for the OrganizationAccountAccessRole role in the two OUs to deny access to the S3 buckets."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 SCP，其中包含两条语句，一条允许所有 S3 存储桶对新范围的 IP 地址进行访问， 另一条拒绝所有 S3 存储桶对旧范围的 IP 地址进行访问。为两个组织单位中的 OrganizationAcco untAccessRole 角色设置权限边界，以拒绝访问 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建一个新的 SCP，其中包含仅允许新范围的 IP 地址访问 S3 存储桶的声明。创建另一个 SCP， 禁止访问 S3 存储桶。将第二个 SCP 附加到两个组织单位。","C":"在所有 S3 存储桶上配置基于资源的策略，仅允许新的 IP 地址范围访问这些 S3 存储桶。创建一个 新的服务控制策略（SCP），禁止访问 S3 存储桶。将该 SCP 附加到两个组织单位（OU）。","D":"在所有 S3 存储桶上配置基于资源的策略，仅允许新的 IP 地址范围访问这些 S3 存储桶。为两个组 织单位中的 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 角色设置权限边界，以拒绝访问 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two distinct requirements must each be met with the right mechanism. (1) Changing the IP range that may access the bucket contents must be done on the S3 bucket resource-based policies (bucket policies with an aws:SourceIp condition). SCPs never grant permissions and do not affect resource-based policies directly, so an SCP that 'allows the new IP range' cannot grant or define bucket access; only the bucket policies control IP-based access. (2) Revoking the permissions of two OUs is an Organizations-wide action: an SCP with a Deny statement attached to the two OUs blocks the affected actions for all IAM users and roles in every member account under those OUs. Option C does exactly this. A permissions boundary (options A and D) only sets the maximum permissions for a single named IAM entity (OrganizationAccountAccessRole, the per-account admin role) and is not an OU-level construct, so it does not revoke permissions across the OUs. Options A and B incorrectly rely on SCPs to allow/grant the new IP range, which SCPs cannot do.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個獨立需求,各自需用正確機制。(1) 變更可存取 bucket 內容的 IP 範圍,必須在 S3 bucket 的資源型政策 (bucket policy 搭配 aws:SourceIp 條件) 上修改。SCP 從不授予權限,也不會直接影響資源型政策,因此用 SCP 去『允許新 IP 範圍』無法授予或定義 bucket 存取;只有 bucket policy 才能控制以 IP 為基礎的存取。(2) 撤銷兩個 OU 的權限屬於組織層級動作:在兩個 OU 上掛載含 Deny 陳述式的 SCP,可對這些 OU 下所有成員帳戶中的 IAM 使用者與角色封鎖對應動作。選項 C 正是如此。權限邊界 (permissions boundary,選項 A 與 D) 只針對單一具名 IAM 實體 (OrganizationAccountAccessRole,即各帳戶的管理角色) 設定最大權限,並非 OU 層級構件,因此無法跨 OU 撤銷權限。選項 A 與 B 錯誤地依賴 SCP 去允許/授予新 IP 範圍,而這是 SCP 做不到的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SCPs never grant permissions and do not affect resource-based policies, so an SCP that 'allows the new IP range' cannot make the buckets accessible from the new IPs; the IP change must be made on the bucket policies. It also uses a permissions boundary on a single role rather than an SCP Deny on the OUs to revoke OU-wide permissions.","why_zh":"SCP 從不授予權限,也不影響資源型政策,因此用 SCP『允許新 IP 範圍』無法讓 bucket 從新 IP 存取;IP 變更必須在 bucket policy 上做。它還用單一角色的權限邊界,而非在 OU 上掛 Deny SCP 來跨 OU 撤銷權限。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An SCP that 'allows only the new IP range to access the S3 buckets' cannot grant access because SCPs only set guardrails and do not affect S3 bucket (resource-based) policies. The actual IP-range change must be applied to the bucket policies, which this option omits.","why_zh":"SCP『僅允許新 IP 範圍存取 S3 bucket』無法授予存取,因為 SCP 只設護欄且不影響 S3 bucket (資源型) 政策。真正的 IP 範圍變更必須套用在 bucket policy 上,而本選項並未這麼做。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It correctly edits bucket resource-based policies for the new IP range, but it uses a permissions boundary on the single OrganizationAccountAccessRole to revoke OU permissions. A permissions boundary limits only that one IAM entity, not all principals across the OUs, and is not an OU-level mechanism; an SCP Deny attached to the OUs is required.","why_zh":"它正確地修改 bucket 資源型政策以套用新 IP 範圍,但卻用單一 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 的權限邊界來撤銷 OU 權限。權限邊界只限制那一個 IAM 實體,而非 OU 下所有主體,且非 OU 層級機制;應在 OU 上掛 Deny SCP。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_identity-vs-resource.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access-cross-account-role.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":222,"question_en":"A company has started using AWS across several teams. Each team has multiple accounts and unique security profiles. The company manages the accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. Each account has its own configuration and security controls. The company's DevOps team wants to use preventive and detective controls to govern all accounts. The DevOps team needs to ensure the security of accounts now and in the future as the company creates new accounts in the organization. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已在多个团队中开始使用 AWS。每个团队拥有多个账户和独特的安全配置文件。该公司 在 AWS 组织中以组织形式管理这些账户。每个账户都有自己的配置和安全控制措施。 该公司的 DevOps 团队希望采用预防性和检测性控制措施来管理所有账户。随着公司不断在组织内创 建新账户，DevOps 团队需要确保现有及未来账户的安全。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Organizations to create OUs that have appropriate SCPs attached for each team. Place team accounts in the appropriate OUs to apply security controls. Create any new team accounts in the appropriate OUs.","B":"Create an AWS Control Tower landing zone. Configure OUs and appropriate controls in AWS Control Tower for the existing teams. Configure trusted access for AWS Control Tower. Enroll the existing accounts in the appropriate OUs that match the appropriate security policies for each team. Use AWS Control Tower to provision any new accounts.","C":"Create AWS CloudFormation stack sets in the organization's management account. Configure a stack set that deploys AWS Config with configuration rules and remediation actions for all controls to each account in the organization. Update the stack sets to deploy to new accounts as the accounts are created.","D":"Configure AWS Config to manage the AWS Config rules across all AWS accounts in the organization. Deploy conformance packs that provide AWS Config rules and remediation actions across the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"利用组织创建具有适合每个团队的适当 SCP（安全策略控制）的组织单位（OU）。将团队账 户置于适当的 OU 中以应用安全控制。在适当的 OU 中创建任何新的团队账户。","B":"创建一个 AWS Control Tower 落地区。为现有团队在 AWS Control Tower 中配置组织单元（OU） 和适当的控制措施。为 AWS Control Tower 配置受信任访问权限。将现有账户注册到与每个团队 相应的安全策略相匹配的适当组织单元中。使用 AWS Control Tower 配置任何新账户。","C":"在组织的管理账户中创建 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集。配置一个堆栈集，将 AWS Config 及其配 置规则和补救措施部署到组织中的每个账户。当新账户创建时，更新堆栈集以将其部署到新账户。","D":"配置 AWS Config 以管理组织内所有 AWS 账户的 AWS Config 规则。部署一致性包，以在整个组织中提 供 AWS Config 规则和修复操作。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is BOTH preventive AND detective controls governing all accounts now and as new accounts are created. AWS Control Tower is the only option that delivers all of this in one managed solution: it provides preventive controls (implemented via SCPs/RCPs in AWS Organizations), detective controls (implemented via AWS Config rules), and proactive controls. It organizes accounts into OUs with controls, enrolls existing accounts into the appropriate OUs to apply each team's security policies, and uses Account Factory to provision and govern any future accounts consistently. The other options each cover only one control type: AWS Config conformance packs (D) and StackSets deploying AWS Config (C) are detective-plus-remediation only and cannot prevent (block) noncompliant actions, while SCPs alone (A) are preventive only and provide no detection.","explanation_zh":"題目要求同時提供 preventive 與 detective 控制，並治理現有與未來新建的所有帳戶。AWS Control Tower 是唯一在單一受管解決方案中同時滿足這些需求的選項：它提供 preventive controls（以 AWS Organizations 的 SCPs/RCPs 實作）、detective controls（以 AWS Config rules 實作）以及 proactive controls。它將帳戶組織成 OUs 並套用控制，將現有帳戶 enroll 至符合各團隊安全政策的 OU，並透過 Account Factory 一致地佈建與治理未來新帳戶。其他選項僅涵蓋單一控制類型：AWS Config conformance packs（D）與以 StackSets 部署 AWS Config（C）僅為 detective 加 remediation，無法阻擋（prevent）不合規動作；而僅用 SCPs（A）只能 preventive，無偵測能力。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SCPs in Organizations provide only preventive controls (they disallow actions). They do not detect noncompliant resources, so this fails the detective-control requirement.","why_zh":"Organizations 的 SCPs 只提供 preventive 控制（禁止動作），無法偵測不合規資源，因此不符合 detective 控制需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudFormation StackSets deploying AWS Config rules and remediation give only detective controls plus remediation. AWS Config cannot block/prevent actions, so the preventive-control requirement is unmet, and this is far higher operational overhead than Control Tower.","why_zh":"以 CloudFormation StackSets 部署 AWS Config 規則與 remediation 只提供 detective 加修復，AWS Config 無法阻擋/預防動作，未滿足 preventive 控制需求，且維運負擔遠高於 Control Tower。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config conformance packs are a collection of Config rules and remediation actions deployed org-wide; they are detective-and-remediation only with no preventive capability, so they do not meet the preventive-control requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Config conformance packs 是跨組織部署的 Config 規則與 remediation 集合，僅有偵測與修復能力，沒有 preventive 能力，因此不符合 preventive 控制需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/what-is-control-tower.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/preventive-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/detective-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/how-controls-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-packs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":223,"question_en":"A company uses an AWS CodeCommit repository to store its source code and corresponding unit tests. The company has configured an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that includes an AWS CodeBuild project that runs when code is merged to the main branch of the repository. The company wants the CodeBuild project to run the unit tests. If the unit tests pass, the CodeBuild project must tag the most recent commit. How should the company configure the CodeBuild project to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodeCommit 存储库来存储其源代码及相应的单元测试。该公司已配置了一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，其中包含一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目，当代码合并到存储库的主分支时，该项目会运行。 该公司希望 CodeBuild 项目运行单元测试。如果单元测试通过，CodeBuild 项目必须为最近的一次提交添加 标签。 公司应如何配置 CodeBuild 项目以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the CodeBuild project to use native Git to done the CodeCommit repository. Configure the project to run the unit tests. Configure the project to use native Git to create a tag and to push the Git tag to the repository if the code passes the unit tests.","B":"Configure the CodeBuild projed to use native Git to done the CodeCommit repository. Configure the project to run the unit tests. Configure the project to use AWS CLI commands to create a new repository tag in the repository if the code passes the unit tests.","C":"Configure the CodeBuild project to use AWS CLI commands to copy the code from the CodeCommit repository. Configure the project to run the unit tests. Configure the project to use AWS CLI commands to create a new Git tag in the repository if the code passes the unit tests.","D":"Configure the CodeBuild project to use AWS CLI commands to copy the code from the CodeCommit repository. Configure the project to run the unit tests. Configure the project to use AWS CLI commands to create a new repository tag in the repository if the code passes the unit tests."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 CodeBuild 项目以使用原生 Git 访问 CodeCommit 代码库。配置项目运行单元测试。配置项目在代 码通过单元测试时使用原生 Git 创建标签，并将 Git 标签推送到代码库。","B":"配置 CodeBuild 项目以使用原生 Git 操作 CodeCommit 存储库。配置项目以运行单元测试。如果代码通 过单元测试，则配置项目使用 AWS CLI 命令在存储库中创建新的存储库标签。","C":"配置 CodeBuild 项目，使其使用 AWS CLI 命令从 CodeCommit 存储库复制代码。配置项目以运行单元测 试。如果代码通过单元测试，配置项目使用 AWS CLI 命令在存储库中创建新的 Git 标签。","D":"配置 CodeBuild 项目，使其使用 AWS CLI 命令从 CodeCommit 代码库复制代码。配置项目以运行单元测 试。如果代码通过单元测试，配置项目使用 AWS CLI 命令在代码库中创建新的代码库标签。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to tag the most recent commit, which means creating a Git tag (a label on a commit), not an AWS resource tag. Per the AWS CodeCommit documentation, Git tags in a CodeCommit repository are created from a local repo using native Git (git tag <name> <commit-id>) and pushed to the remote with git push --tags / git push origin <tag>. There is no AWS CLI or CodeCommit API operation that creates a Git tag on a commit; the codecommit tag-resource CLI command only applies AWS resource tags to the repository resource (for cost allocation/access control), not Git tags. Creating and pushing a Git tag requires an actual Git working copy with refs and history, which native git clone provides; merely copying files with AWS CLI (e.g., get-file) does not yield a Git repo capable of tagging/pushing. Therefore option A (native Git to clone, run tests, then native Git to create and push the tag) is the only technically valid approach.","explanation_zh":"需求是為最近的 commit 加標籤，意指建立 Git tag（標記某個 commit 的標籤），而非 AWS 資源標籤（resource tag）。根據 AWS CodeCommit 文件，CodeCommit 儲存庫中的 Git tag 是在本地端使用原生 Git 建立（git tag <name> <commit-id>），再以 git push --tags / git push origin <tag> 推送到遠端。並沒有任何 AWS CLI 或 CodeCommit API 操作能在 commit 上建立 Git tag；codecommit tag-resource CLI 指令只會對儲存庫資源套用 AWS 資源標籤（用於成本分攤/存取控制），並非 Git tag。建立並推送 Git tag 需要具備 refs 與歷史的實際 Git 工作副本，這由原生 git clone 提供；僅用 AWS CLI 複製檔案（如 get-file）無法產生可進行 tag/push 的 Git 儲存庫。因此選項 A（用原生 Git clone、執行測試、再用原生 Git 建立並推送 tag）是唯一在技術上可行的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Cloning with native Git is fine, but 'AWS CLI commands to create a new repository tag' creates an AWS resource tag on the repository (codecommit tag-resource), not a Git tag on the commit. There is no CLI command to create a Git tag, so this does not tag the commit.","why_zh":"用原生 Git clone 沒問題，但『用 AWS CLI 建立新的 repository tag』建立的是儲存庫的 AWS 資源標籤（codecommit tag-resource），而非 commit 上的 Git tag。沒有任何 CLI 指令能建立 Git tag，因此無法標記該 commit。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"'Copy the code' via AWS CLI (e.g., get-file) does not produce a real Git repository with history/refs, and there is no AWS CLI command that creates a Git tag in CodeCommit. Both halves are infeasible.","why_zh":"透過 AWS CLI『複製程式碼』（如 get-file）無法產生具有歷史/refs 的真正 Git 儲存庫，而且 CodeCommit 也沒有任何能建立 Git tag 的 AWS CLI 指令。前後兩部分皆不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same as C for the copy step, and 'create a new repository tag' via CLI is a resource tag, not a Git tag on the commit. It does not meet the requirement to tag the most recent commit.","why_zh":"複製步驟與 C 相同的問題，且用 CLI『建立新的 repository tag』是資源標籤，不是 commit 上的 Git tag，無法滿足為最近 commit 加標籤的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-create-tag.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-basic-git.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/v1/reference/codecommit/tag-resource.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/getting-started.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":224,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages a company's Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. The cluster runs on several Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The DevOps engineer must implement a solution that logs and reviews all stopped tasks for errors. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师负责管理公司的亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）集群。该集群在多个位于自动扩 展组中的亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行。这位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解决方案，用于记录和审查所有已停 止的任务以查找错误。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture task state changes. Send the event to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to investigate stopped tasks.","B":"Configure tasks to write log data in the embedded metric format. Store the logs in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Monitor the ContainerInstanceCount metric for changes.","C":"Configure the EC2 instances to store logs in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a CloudWatch Contributor Insights rule that uses the EC2 instance log data. Use the Contributor Insights rule to investigate stopped tasks.","D":"Configure an EC2 Auto Scaling lifecycle hook for the EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING scale-in event. Write the SystemEventLog file to Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena to query the log file for errors."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获任务状态更改。将事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 来调查已停止的任务。","B":"配置任务以嵌入式指标格式写入日志数据。将日志存储在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中。监控 ContainerInstanceCount 指标的变化。","C":"配置 EC2 实例将日志存储在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中。创建一个使用 EC2 实例日志数据的 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察规则。使用贡献者洞察规则来调查已停止的任务。","D":"为 EC2 实例终止（缩放）事件配置 EC2 自动缩放生命周期挂钩。将 SystemEventLog 文件写入 Amazon S3。使用 Amazon Athena 查询日志文件中的错误。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon ECS emits an 'ECS Task State Change' event to EventBridge whenever a task transitions to STOPPED (including stops caused by essential container exit, instance termination, or Spot interruption). For stopped tasks the event detail includes the stoppedReason and stopCode fields, which carry the error information needed to diagnose failures. CloudWatch Logs is a supported EventBridge target, so routing these events to a log group durably persists them (the ECS console only retains stopped tasks for one hour), and CloudWatch Logs Insights can then query the stored events to review all stopped tasks for errors. This is exactly the AWS-documented pattern, so option A meets the requirement end to end.","explanation_zh":"每當 Amazon ECS 的任務轉為 STOPPED 狀態（包括 essential container 退出、執行個體終止或 Spot 中斷導致的停止），ECS 都會向 EventBridge 發出 'ECS Task State Change' 事件。對於已停止的任務，事件的 detail 內含 stoppedReason 與 stopCode 欄位，提供診斷失敗所需的錯誤資訊。CloudWatch Logs 是 EventBridge 支援的目標，因此將這些事件送至 log group 可長期保存（ECS 主控台僅保留已停止任務一小時），再用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢所儲存的事件來檢視所有已停止任務的錯誤。這正是 AWS 文件記載的模式，故選項 A 完整符合需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Embedded Metric Format (EMF) is for emitting custom application metrics from logs, not for capturing a task's lifecycle or its stoppedReason/stopCode. ContainerInstanceCount is not a metric that surfaces why tasks stopped, so this neither logs nor lets you review stopped-task errors.","why_zh":"Embedded Metric Format (EMF) 用於從日誌發出自訂應用程式指標，並非用來擷取任務生命週期或其 stoppedReason/stopCode。ContainerInstanceCount 也無法呈現任務停止原因，因此既無法記錄也無法檢視已停止任務的錯誤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EC2 instance OS logs do not contain structured ECS task stop reasons, and CloudWatch Contributor Insights is designed to rank top contributors (e.g. top talkers) in high-cardinality log data, not to investigate individual stopped tasks and their error messages.","why_zh":"EC2 執行個體的作業系統日誌不含結構化的 ECS 任務停止原因，且 CloudWatch Contributor Insights 是用來在高基數日誌中排名主要貢獻者（例如流量最高者），而非調查個別已停止任務及其錯誤訊息。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING lifecycle hook only fires on instance scale-in, but tasks stop for many reasons unrelated to instance termination (OOM, failed health checks, image pull errors, essential container exit). It would miss most stopped tasks and the SystemEventLog does not capture ECS stopCode/stoppedReason.","why_zh":"EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING 生命週期掛鉤僅在執行個體縮減時觸發，但任務停止有許多與執行個體終止無關的原因（OOM、健康檢查失敗、映像拉取錯誤、essential container 退出）。此方案會遺漏大多數已停止的任務，且 SystemEventLog 也不會擷取 ECS 的 stopCode/stoppedReason。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/ecs_task_events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/resolve-stopped-errors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/stopped-task-errors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/viewing-state-events.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":225,"question_en":"A company wants to deploy a workload on several hundred Amazon EC2 instances. The company will provision the EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group by using a launch template. The workload will pull files from an Amazon S3 bucket, process the data, and put the results into a different S3 bucket. The EC2 instances must have least-privilege permissions and must use temporary security credentials. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望在数百台亚马逊 EC2 实例上部署工作负载。该公司将使用启动模板在自动扩展组 中配置 EC2 实例。 工作负载将从 Amazon S3 存储桶中提取文件，处理数据，并将结果放入另一个 S3 存储桶。EC2 实例 必须具有最低权限，并且必须使用临时安全凭证。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM role that has the appropriate permissions for S3 buckets. Add the IAM role to an instance profile.","B":"Update the launch template to include the IAM instance profile.","C":"Create an IAM user that has the appropriate permissions for Amazon S3. Generate a secret key and token.","D":"Create a trust anchor and profile. Attach the IAM role to the profile.","E":"Update the launch template. Modify the user data to use the new secret key and token."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有 S3 存储桶适当权限的 IAM 角色。将 IAM 角色添加到实例配置文件中。","B":"更新启动模板以包含 IAM 实例配置文件。","C":"创建一个具有适当权限访问 Amazon S3 的 IAM 用户。生成一个密钥和令牌。","D":"创建信任锚点和配置文件。将 IAM 角色附加到配置文件。","E":"更新启动模板。修改用户数据以使用新的密钥和令牌。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are least-privilege permissions and temporary security credentials for EC2 instances launched by an Auto Scaling group via a launch template. The canonical AWS pattern is: create an IAM role scoped with only the needed S3 permissions (read from source bucket, write to destination bucket) and place it in an instance profile (A), then reference that instance profile in the launch template so every instance the ASG launches assumes the role (B). When an EC2 instance assumes a role through its instance profile, the EC2 Instance Metadata Service supplies automatically rotated temporary STS credentials, satisfying both the least-privilege and temporary-credentials requirements. AWS IAM security best practices explicitly recommend requiring workloads to use temporary credentials with IAM roles rather than long-term access keys.","explanation_zh":"需求是 least-privilege 權限與 temporary security credentials，給由 Auto Scaling group 透過 launch template 啟動的 EC2 instances 使用。標準 AWS 做法是：建立一個只授予必要 S3 權限（從來源 bucket 讀取、寫入目的 bucket）的 IAM role，並放入 instance profile（A），再於 launch template 中參照該 instance profile，使 ASG 啟動的每個 instance 都承接此 role（B）。當 EC2 instance 透過 instance profile 承接 role 時，EC2 Instance Metadata Service 會提供自動輪替的 temporary STS credentials，同時滿足 least-privilege 與 temporary credentials 兩項要求。AWS IAM 安全最佳實務也明確建議 workloads 使用 IAM roles 的 temporary credentials，而非長期 access keys。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating an IAM user with a secret key (and token) uses long-term static credentials, which directly violates the temporary-security-credentials requirement and the IAM best practice of avoiding long-term access keys for workloads.","why_zh":"建立帶 secret key 的 IAM user 屬於長期靜態憑證，直接違反 temporary security credentials 的要求，也違反 IAM 不應在 workloads 使用長期 access keys 的最佳實務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Trust anchors and profiles are IAM Roles Anywhere constructs intended for workloads running OUTSIDE AWS (on-premises or other clouds) using X.509 certificates. EC2 instances inside AWS obtain temporary credentials through instance profiles, so this adds needless complexity and is the wrong mechanism here.","why_zh":"Trust anchor 與 profile 是 IAM Roles Anywhere 的概念，適用於 AWS 之外（on-premises 或其他雲）以 X.509 憑證執行的 workloads。AWS 內的 EC2 instances 透過 instance profile 取得 temporary credentials，因此此選項機制錯誤且增加不必要複雜度。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Injecting a secret key and token into user data hardcodes static long-term credentials onto instances, which is insecure and again fails the temporary-credentials requirement; instance profiles deliver auto-rotated temporary credentials with no user-data secrets.","why_zh":"將 secret key 與 token 寫入 user data 等於在 instances 上硬編碼長期靜態憑證，不安全且同樣不符 temporary credentials 要求；instance profile 可提供自動輪替的 temporary credentials，無需在 user data 中放憑證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_switch-role-ec2_instance-profiles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp_use-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-ec2-launchtemplate-iaminstanceprofile.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":226,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CodeDeploy to automate software deployment. The deployment must meet these requirements: • A number of instances must be available to serve traffic during the deployment. Traffic must be balanced across those instances, and the instances must automatically heal in the event of failure. • A new fleet of instances must be launched for deploying a new revision automatically, with no manual provisioning. • Traffic must be rerouted to the new environment to half of the new instances at a time. The deployment should succeed if traffic is rerouted to at least half of the instances: otherwise, it should fail. • Before routing traffic to the new fleet of instances, the temporary files generated during the deployment process must be deleted. • At the end of a successful deployment, the original instances in the deployment group must be deleted immediately to reduce costs. How can a DevOps engineer meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 来实现软件部署的自动化。该部署必须满足以下要求： •在部署期间必须有若干实例可用以承载流量。流量必须在这些实例之间均衡分配，并且在出现故 障时实例必须能够自动恢复。•必须能够自动为部署新版本启动新的实例群，无需人工配置。 • 流量必须每次重新定向到新环境中的半数新实例。如果流量重新定向到至少半数实例，则部署 应成功；否则，部署应失败。 在将流量路由到新的实例群组之前，必须删除部署过程中生成的临时文件。 在成功部署结束时，必须立即删除部署组中的原始实例以降低成本。 DevOps 工程师如何才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an Application Load Balancer and an in-place deployment. Associate the Auto Scaling group with the deployment group. Use the Automatically copy Auto Scaling group option, and use CodeDeployDefault.OneAtAtime as the deployment configuration. Instruct AWS CodeDeploy to terminate the original instances in the deployment group, and use the AllowTraffic hook within appspec.yml to delete the temporary files.","B":"Use an Application Load Balancer and a blue/green deployment. Associate the Auto Scaling group and Application Load Balancer target group with the deployment group. Use the Automatically copy Auto Scaling group option, create a custom deployment configuration with minimum healthy hosts defined as 50%, and assign the configuration to the deployment group. Instruct AWS CodeDeploy to terminate the original instances in the deployment group, and use the BeforeBlockTraffic hook within appspec.yml to delete the temporary files.","C":"Use an Application Load Balancer and a blue/green deployment. Associate the Auto Scaling group and the Application Load Balancer target group with the deployment group. Use the Automatically copy Auto Scaling group option, and use CodeDeployDefault.HalfAtAtime as the deployment configuration. Instruct AWS CodeDeploy to terminate the original instances in the deployment group, and use the BeforeAllowTraffic hook within appspec.yml to delete the temporary files.","D":"Use an Application Load Balancer and an in-place deployment. Associate the Auto Scaling group and Application Load Balancer target group with the deployment group. Use the Automatically copy Auto Scaling group option, and use CodeDeployDefault.AllatOnce as a deployment configuration. Instruct AWS CodeDeploy to terminate the original instances in the deployment group, and use the BlockTraffic hook within appspec.yml to delete the temporary files."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用应用负载均衡器和原地部署。将自动扩展组与部署组相关联。使用“自动复制自动扩展组” 选项，并使用 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtAtime 作为部署配置。指示 AWS CodeDeploy 终止部署 组中的原始实例，并在 appspec.yml 中使用 AllowTraffic 钩子来删除临时文件。","B":"使用应用负载均衡器和蓝/绿部署。将自动扩展组和应用负载均衡器目标组与部署组关联。使用 “自动复制自动扩展组”选项，创建一个自定义部署配置，将最小健康主机定义为 50%，并将 该配置分配给部署组。指示 AWS CodeDeploy 终止部署组中的原始实例，并在 appspec.yml 中使 用 BeforeBlockTraffic 钩子删除临时文件。","C":"使用应用负载均衡器和蓝/绿部署。将自动扩展组和应用负载均衡器目标组与部署组相关联。使用 “自动复制自动扩展组”选项，并使用 CodeDeployDefault.HalfAtAtime 作为部署配置。指示 AWS CodeDeploy 终止部署组中的原始实例，并在 appspec.yml 中使用 BeforeAllowTraffic 钩子删 除临时文件。","D":"使用应用负载均衡器和原地部署。将自动扩展组和应用负载均衡器目标组与部署组相关联。使用 “自动复制自动扩展组”选项，并使用 CodeDeployDefault.AllAtOnce 作为部署配置。指示 AWS CodeDeploy 终止部署组中的原始实例，并使用 在 appspec.yml 中使用 BlockTraffic 钩子删除临时文件。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements map precisely onto a blue/green deployment. A new fleet launched automatically with no manual provisioning requires blue/green plus the 'Automatically copy Auto Scaling group' option (in-place deployments reuse the existing instances, so options A and D fail this requirement). The traffic rule -- 'reroute to half of the new instances at a time, succeed if traffic is rerouted to at least half of the instances, otherwise fail' -- is the exact definition of CodeDeployDefault.HalfAtATime for blue/green: 'Routes traffic to up to half the instances in the replacement environment at a time. Succeeds if rerouting to at least half of the instances succeeds. Otherwise, fails.' A custom 50% minimumHealthyHosts (option B) controls how many hosts stay available during deployment, not the half-at-a-time traffic shift semantics, so it does not match. The hook must run on the NEW fleet 'before routing traffic to the new fleet,' which is BeforeAllowTraffic ('run tasks on instances before they are registered with a load balancer'); per the lifecycle hook availability table, BeforeAllowTraffic runs on blue/green replacement (new) instances, whereas BeforeBlockTraffic (option B) runs only on the ORIGINAL instances before deregistration -- the wrong fleet and wrong timing. Associating both the Auto Scaling group and the ALB target group with the deployment group plus instructing CodeDeploy to terminate the original instances satisfies the load balancing, healing, and cost-reduction requirements. Option C is the only choice that satisfies every requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求精確對應到 blue/green 部署。要自動啟動新一批執行個體且不需手動佈建，必須使用 blue/green 加上『Automatically copy Auto Scaling group』選項（in-place 部署會重用既有執行個體，因此選項 A 與 D 不符）。流量規則『一次將流量導向一半的新執行個體，若至少一半成功導流則部署成功，否則失敗』正是 blue/green 的 CodeDeployDefault.HalfAtATime 定義：『一次將流量導向最多一半的取代環境執行個體；若至少一半成功則成功，否則失敗。』自訂 50% minimumHealthyHosts（選項 B）控制的是部署期間需保持可用的主機數量，並非 half-at-a-time 的流量切換語意，故不符。Hook 必須在『將流量導向新一批執行個體之前』於新執行個體上執行，亦即 BeforeAllowTraffic（『在執行個體註冊到負載平衡器之前執行任務』）；依生命週期 hook 可用性表，BeforeAllowTraffic 於 blue/green 取代（新）執行個體上執行，而 BeforeBlockTraffic（選項 B）僅於原始執行個體取消註冊前執行——對象與時機皆錯誤。將 Auto Scaling group 與 ALB target group 同時關聯到部署群組，並指示 CodeDeploy 終止原始執行個體，可滿足負載平衡、自動修復與降低成本的需求。選項 C 是唯一滿足所有需求的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses an in-place deployment, which reuses existing instances and cannot launch a new fleet automatically; CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime does not match the half-at-a-time traffic rule; and 'AllowTraffic' is a CodeDeploy-reserved event that cannot run scripts.","why_zh":"使用 in-place 部署會重用既有執行個體，無法自動啟動新一批執行個體；CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime 不符合 half-at-a-time 流量規則；且 AllowTraffic 是 CodeDeploy 保留事件，無法執行腳本。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A custom config with 50% minimumHealthyHosts governs availability during deployment, not the 'half of new instances at a time / succeed at >=50%' traffic-shift semantics that HalfAtATime provides; and BeforeBlockTraffic runs on the ORIGINAL instances before deregistration, not on the new fleet before routing traffic to it.","why_zh":"自訂 50% minimumHealthyHosts 控制的是部署期間的可用性，而非 HalfAtATime 提供的『一次一半新執行個體／至少 50% 成功』流量切換語意；且 BeforeBlockTraffic 在原始執行個體取消註冊前執行，並非在新一批執行個體導流之前執行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"In-place deployment cannot auto-launch a new fleet; CodeDeployDefault.AllAtOnce routes traffic to all instances at once (not half at a time); 'BlockTraffic' is reserved and cannot run scripts; the option text is also corrupted with non-AWS watermark content.","why_zh":"In-place 部署無法自動啟動新一批執行個體；CodeDeployDefault.AllAtOnce 一次將流量導向所有執行個體（非一半）；BlockTraffic 為保留事件無法執行腳本；該選項文字亦含有非 AWS 的浮水印雜訊。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-create-blue-green.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":227,"question_en":"A company needs to adopt a multi-account strategy to deploy its applications and the associated CI/CD infrastructure. The company has created an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled. The company has configured AWS Control Tower and has set up a landing zone. The company needs to use AWS Control Tower controls (guardrails) in all AWS accounts in the organization. The company must create the accounts for a multi-environment application and must ensure that all accounts are configured to an initial baseline. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司需要采用多账户策略来部署其应用程序以及相关的持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）基础设施。 该公司已在 AWS 组织中创建了一个组织，并启用了所有功能。该公司已配置了 AWS 控制塔，并设 置了一个着陆区。 该公司需要在其组织内的所有 AWS 账户中使用 AWS 控制塔控制措施（防护栏）。公司必须为一个多 环境应用程序创建账户，并且必须确保所有账户都配置为初始基线。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Control Tower Account Factory Customization (AFC) blueprint that uses the baseline configuration. Use AWS Control Tower Account Factory to provision a dedicated AWS account for each environment and a CI/CD account by using the blueprint.","B":"Use AWS Control Tower Account Factory to provision a dedicated AWS account for each environment and a CI/CD account. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to apply the baseline configuration to the new accounts.","C":"Use Organizations to provision a multi-environment AWS account and a CI/CD account. In the Organizations management account, create an AWS Lambda function that assumes the Organizations access role to apply the baseline configuration to the new accounts.","D":"Use Organizations to provision a dedicated AWS account for each environment, an audit account, and a CI/CD account. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to apply the baseline configuration to the new accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个使用基准配置的 AWS 控制塔账户工厂自定义（AFC）蓝图。使用 AWS 控制塔账户工厂通 过该蓝图为每个环境配置一个专用的 AWS 账户，并配置一个持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）账户。","B":"使用 AWS 控制塔账户工厂为每个环境和持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）账户配置专用的 AWS 账户。 使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将基础配置应用于新账户。","C":"使用组织服务来配置一个多环境的 AWS 账户和一个 CI/CD 账户。在组织管理账户中，创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数通过承担组织访问角色来将基线配置应用于新账户。","D":"利用组织为每个环境、审计账户和 CI/CD 账户配置专用的 AWS 账户。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将基础配置应用于新账户。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The landing zone is already set up, so the lowest-overhead native path is AWS Control Tower Account Factory Customization (AFC). AFC lets you define a blueprint (a Service Catalog CloudFormation/Terraform product) that describes the resources and baseline configuration applied automatically whenever an account is provisioned. Per AWS docs, after a one-time setup, 'AWS Control Tower automates this process for future provisioning, so you don't have to maintain any pipelines,' and the customized accounts are ready immediately. Accounts created through Account Factory land in Control Tower-registered OUs, so Control Tower controls (guardrails) automatically apply. This satisfies all requirements (controls everywhere, per-environment + CI/CD accounts, an initial baseline applied to each) with the least operational overhead by using a single native mechanism rather than a separate StackSet or custom Lambda layer.","explanation_zh":"由於 landing zone 已建立，最省維運的原生做法是使用 AWS Control Tower Account Factory Customization (AFC)。AFC 讓你定義一個 blueprint（一個 Service Catalog 的 CloudFormation/Terraform 產品），描述每次佈建帳戶時自動套用的資源與 baseline 設定。根據 AWS 文件，完成一次性設定後，'AWS Control Tower 會自動化後續的佈建流程，因此你不需要維護任何 pipeline'，且客製化帳戶佈建後可立即使用。透過 Account Factory 建立的帳戶會放入 Control Tower 已註冊的 OU，因此 Control Tower controls（guardrails）會自動套用。這以單一原生機制（而非額外的 StackSet 或自訂 Lambda）滿足所有需求（所有帳戶皆有 controls、每個環境帳戶 + CI/CD 帳戶、每個帳戶套用初始 baseline），且維運負擔最低。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Provisioning via Account Factory is correct, but layering a separate CloudFormation StackSets mechanism to apply the baseline adds a second component to configure and maintain. A single AFC blueprint that bundles the baseline is lower operational overhead.","why_zh":"用 Account Factory 佈建是對的，但另外再用 CloudFormation StackSets 套用 baseline 會多出一個要設定與維護的元件。將 baseline 整合進單一 AFC blueprint 的維運負擔更低。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Provisioning accounts directly through AWS Organizations bypasses Control Tower Account Factory, so the accounts are not enrolled/governed by Control Tower controls automatically. Building a custom Lambda that assumes the Organizations access role is high operational overhead and does not satisfy the 'controls in all accounts' requirement.","why_zh":"直接透過 AWS Organizations 佈建帳戶會繞過 Control Tower Account Factory，帳戶不會自動受 Control Tower controls 治理。再自建一個假設 Organizations access role 的 Lambda 維運負擔很高，也無法滿足『所有帳戶都套用 controls』的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like C, accounts are provisioned directly via Organizations rather than Account Factory, so Control Tower controls do not automatically apply. It also introduces an unrequested audit account and relies on StackSets, adding overhead and failing the guardrails requirement.","why_zh":"與 C 類似，帳戶是直接透過 Organizations 佈建而非 Account Factory，因此 Control Tower controls 不會自動套用。它還多了一個非需求的 audit 帳戶並依賴 StackSets，增加負擔且不符合 guardrails 需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/af-customization-page.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/methods-of-provisioning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/account-factory.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/control-considerations.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":228,"question_en":"A DevOps team has created a Custom Lambda rule in AWS Config. The rule monitors Amazon Elastic Container Repository (Amazon ECR) policy statements for ecr:* actions. When a noncompliant repository is detected, Amazon EventBridge uses Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to route the notification to a security team. When the custom AWS Config rule is evaluated, the AWS Lambda function fails to run. Which solution will resolve the issue?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队在 AWS Config 中创建了一条自定义的 Lambda 规则。该规则会监控 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）策略语句中的 ecr:* 操作。一旦检测到不符合规定的存储库， Amazon EventBridge 就会使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）将通知转发给安全团 队。 当自定义的 AWS Config 规则被评估时，AWS Lambda 函数无法运行。 哪种解决方案能解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the Lambda function's resource policy to grant AWS Config permission to invoke the function.","B":"Modify the SNS topic policy to include configuration changes for EventBridge to publish to the SNS topic.","C":"Modify the Lambda function's execution role to include configuration changes for custom AWS Config rules.","D":"Modify all the ECR repository policies to grant AWS Config access to the necessary ECR API actions."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 Lambda 函数的资源策略，授予 AWS Config 调用该函数的权限。","B":"修改 SNS 主题策略，以包含针对 EventBridge 发布到 SNS 主题的配置更改。","C":"修改 Lambda 函数的执行角色，以包含自定义 AWS Config 规则的配置更改。","D":"修改所有 ECR 存储库策略，授予 AWS Config 对必要 ECR API 操作的访问权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For an AWS Config Custom Lambda rule, AWS Config (service principal config.amazonaws.com) invokes the associated Lambda function each time the rule is evaluated. For AWS Config to be allowed to call lambda:InvokeFunction, the function must have a resource-based (resource) policy that grants the AWS Config service principal invoke permission. When you create the rule through the AWS Config console this permission is added automatically, but when the rule/function is wired up via API, CLI, or CloudFormation the lambda:AddPermission / AWS::Lambda::Permission statement for config.amazonaws.com is easy to omit. If it is missing, AWS Config cannot invoke the function and the function 'fails to run' during evaluation, which is exactly the symptom described. Modifying the function's resource policy to grant AWS Config permission to invoke it resolves the failure.","explanation_zh":"對於 AWS Config Custom Lambda rule，每次規則被評估時，AWS Config（服務主體 config.amazonaws.com）會去呼叫所關聯的 Lambda function。要讓 AWS Config 能呼叫 lambda:InvokeFunction，該 function 必須有 resource-based（resource）policy 授予 AWS Config 服務主體 invoke 權限。透過 AWS Config 主控台建立規則時會自動加入此權限，但若透過 API、CLI 或 CloudFormation 設定，常會漏掉針對 config.amazonaws.com 的 lambda:AddPermission / AWS::Lambda::Permission 陳述式。一旦缺少，AWS Config 就無法呼叫該 function，評估時 function 便『無法執行』，正符合題目描述的現象。修改 function 的 resource policy 以授予 AWS Config 呼叫權限即可解決。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The SNS topic policy and EventBridge publishing only govern the downstream notification path AFTER a noncompliant repository is detected. It has no effect on whether AWS Config can invoke and run the Lambda function during rule evaluation.","why_zh":"SNS topic policy 與 EventBridge 發佈僅控制偵測到不合規 repository『之後』的下游通知流程，與 AWS Config 在規則評估時能否呼叫並執行 Lambda function 無關。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The Lambda execution role controls what the function can do once it is already running (e.g., config:PutEvaluations, reading ECR). An execution-role gap would cause a runtime error inside the function, not a failure to run/invoke. There is also no such permission as 'configuration changes for custom AWS Config rules' for an execution role.","why_zh":"Lambda execution role 控制 function『開始執行後』能做的事（例如 config:PutEvaluations、讀取 ECR）。execution role 不足會造成 function 內部執行時錯誤，而非無法被呼叫/執行。且 execution role 並不存在所謂『configuration changes for custom AWS Config rules』這種權限。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ECR repository policies do not control AWS Config's ability to invoke or run the Lambda function. AWS Config reads ECR configuration via its own recorder/service-linked role and the custom Lambda reads ECR via its execution role; changing repository policies does not fix an invocation failure.","why_zh":"ECR repository policy 不會控制 AWS Config 呼叫或執行 Lambda function 的能力。AWS Config 透過自身的 recorder/service-linked role 讀取 ECR 設定，custom Lambda 則透過其 execution role 讀取 ECR；修改 repository policy 無法修復呼叫失敗的問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules_lambda-functions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/access-control-resource-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/permissions-function-services.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-lambda-permission.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":229,"question_en":"A developer is creating a proof of concept for a new software as a service (SaaS) application. The application is in a shared development AWS account that is part of an organization in AWS Organizations. The developer needs to create service-linked IAM roles for the AWS services that are being considered for the proof of concept. The solution needs to give the developer the ability to create and configure the service-linked roles only. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位开发人员正在为一款新的软件即服务（SaaS）应用程序创建概念验证。该应用程序位于 AWS 组织 中一个组织所属的共享开发 AWS 账户内。 开发人员需要为正在考虑用于概念验证的 AWS 服务创建服务相关 IAM 角色。解决方案需要赋予开发人 员仅创建和配置服务相关角色的能力。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM user for the developer in the organization's management account. Configure a cross- account role in the development account for the developer to use. Limit the scope of the cross-account role to common services.","B":"Add the developer to an IAM group. Attach the PowerUserAccess managed policy to the IAM group. Enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) on the user account.","C":"Add an SCP to the development account in Organizations. Configure the SCP with a Deny rule for iam:* to limit the developer's access.","D":"Create an IAM role that has the necessary IAM access to allow the developer to create policies and roles. Create and attach a permissions boundary to the role. Grant the developer access to assume the role."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中为开发人员创建一个 IAM 用户。在开发账户中为开发人员配置一个跨账户角色 供其使用。将跨账户角色的权限范围限制在常见服务上。","B":"将开发人员添加到 IAM 组。将 PowerUserAccess 管理策略附加到 IAM 组。在用户账户上强制实施 多因素身份验证（MFA）。","C":"在“组织”中将一个 SCP 添加到开发账户。使用 Deny 规则配置该 SCP，限制对 iam:* 的访问权 限，从而限制开发人员的访问权限。","D":"创建一个具有必要 IAM 访问权限的 IAM 角色，以允许开发人员创建策略和角色。为该角色创建并附 加权限边界。授予开发人员承担该角色的权限。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to let the developer create and configure service-linked IAM roles ONLY, safely, in a shared dev account. The canonical AWS pattern for delegating the ability to create IAM roles/policies without enabling privilege escalation is to grant an entity the IAM permissions needed (e.g., iam:CreateServiceLinkedRole, iam:AttachRolePolicy/PutRolePolicy) and constrain it with a permissions boundary, which sets the maximum permissions any policy can grant. Option D does exactly this: an IAM role with the needed IAM access, a permissions boundary attached to cap its scope, and the developer assumes it. Per the IAM docs, a permissions boundary limits effective permissions to the intersection of identity policy and boundary, so the developer can create/configure service-linked roles but nothing beyond, satisfying 'only.' Options B and C cannot even enable service-linked role creation (PowerUserAccess excludes IAM role management; an SCP Deny iam:* blocks IAM entirely and SCPs grant no permissions), and A's management-account user with a 'common services' cross-account role neither scopes to service-linked roles nor follows least-privilege management-account practices.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓開發者「僅」能在共用開發帳戶中安全地建立與設定 service-linked IAM roles。AWS 官方建議用於委派建立 IAM roles/policies 同時防止權限提升的標準模式，就是授予所需 IAM 權限（例如 iam:CreateServiceLinkedRole、iam:AttachRolePolicy/PutRolePolicy），並以 permissions boundary 限制其最大可授予的權限。選項 D 正是如此：建立具備所需 IAM 權限的 role、附加 permissions boundary 以限縮範圍，並讓開發者去 assume 該 role。依 IAM 文件，permissions boundary 會將有效權限限制為 identity policy 與 boundary 的交集，因此開發者可建立/設定 service-linked roles 但無法越界，符合『僅』的要求。選項 B 與 C 連建立 service-linked role 的能力都無法提供（PowerUserAccess 不含 IAM role 管理；SCP Deny iam:* 會封鎖全部 IAM 且 SCP 不授予權限），而 A 在管理帳戶建立使用者並用『common services』的跨帳戶 role，既未限縮到 service-linked roles，也不符合管理帳戶最小使用的最佳實務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Placing an IAM user in the Organizations management account violates least-privilege management-account practice, and a cross-account role 'limited to common services' does not specifically scope to creating/configuring service-linked roles only.","why_zh":"在 Organizations 管理帳戶建立 IAM 使用者違反管理帳戶最小使用原則，且『限於 common services』的跨帳戶 role 並未專門限縮到僅建立/設定 service-linked roles。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"PowerUserAccess grants broad access to most services but explicitly excludes IAM and Organizations management actions, so the developer could not create service-linked roles; it is also far broader than 'service-linked roles only.' MFA does not address the scoping requirement.","why_zh":"PowerUserAccess 授予大多數服務的廣泛存取，但明確排除 IAM 與 Organizations 管理動作，因此無法建立 service-linked roles；範圍也遠超『僅 service-linked roles』。啟用 MFA 並未解決限縮範圍的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP with Deny iam:* blocks all IAM actions account-wide, preventing the developer from creating any service-linked role. SCPs are guardrails that never grant permissions, so this cannot enable the required capability.","why_zh":"以 SCP Deny iam:* 會在整個帳戶層級封鎖所有 IAM 動作，使開發者無法建立任何 service-linked role。SCP 為防護邊界且從不授予權限，故無法提供所需能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create-service-linked-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries_delegate.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":230,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company wants its monitoring system to receive an alert when a root user logs in. The company also needs a dashboard to display any log activity that the root user generates. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司希望其监控系统在根用户登录时收到警 报。该公司还需要一个仪表板来显示根用户生成的任何日志活动。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Config with a multi-account aggregator. Configure log forwarding to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","B":"Create an Amazon QuickSight dashboard that uses an Amazon CloudWatch Logs query.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs metric filter to match root user login events. Configure a CloudWatch alarm and an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send alerts to the company's monitoring system.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to match root user login events. Configure the filter to forward events to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Configure the SNS topic to send alerts to the company's monitoring system.","E":"Create an AWS CloudTrail organization trail. Configure the organization trail to send events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","F":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard that uses a CloudWatch Logs Insights query."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用多账户聚合器启用 AWS Config。配置日志转发至 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。","B":"创建一个使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 查询的 Amazon QuickSight 仪表板。","C":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器以匹配根用户登录事件。配置一个 CloudWatch 警报 和一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，以便向公司的监控系统发送警报。","D":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 订阅筛选器以匹配根用户登录事件。配置筛选器将事件转发到 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题。配置 SNS 主题以向公司的监控系统发 送警报。","E":"创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 组织跟踪。配置组织跟踪以将事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。","F":"创建一个使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询的 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板。"},"answer":["C","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has three parts solved by a chained pipeline. (E) Create a CloudTrail organization trail and send its events to CloudWatch Logs: an organization trail logs all events (including root console logins) for the management account and every member account, satisfying the AWS Organizations multi-account scope and providing the log source in CloudWatch Logs. (C) Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter to match root user login events (e.g., ConsoleLogin by Root credentials), then a CloudWatch alarm wired to an SNS topic that notifies the monitoring system; this is the exact pattern AWS documents for being notified when specific CloudTrail activity occurs. (F) Create a CloudWatch dashboard backed by a CloudWatch Logs Insights query to display the root user's log activity; Logs Insights query results can be added directly to a CloudWatch dashboard. The decisive distinction versus the trap option D is that a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter can only deliver to Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or OpenSearch Service, never directly to an SNS topic, so alerting must go through a metric filter plus alarm (C), not a subscription filter (D).","explanation_zh":"需求分三部分,以一條串接的管線解決。(E) 建立 CloudTrail organization trail 並將事件送到 CloudWatch Logs:organization trail 會記錄管理帳戶與所有成員帳戶的全部事件(含 root console 登入),滿足 AWS Organizations 多帳戶範圍,並把日誌來源放進 CloudWatch Logs。(C) 建立 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 比對 root 使用者登入事件(例如 Root 憑證的 ConsoleLogin),再以 CloudWatch alarm 連到 SNS topic 通知監控系統;這正是 AWS 文件記載「當特定 CloudTrail 活動發生時收到通知」的標準做法。(F) 建立以 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢為基礎的 CloudWatch dashboard 來顯示 root 使用者的日誌活動;Logs Insights 查詢結果可直接加入 CloudWatch dashboard。與陷阱選項 D 的關鍵區別在於:CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能將資料送到 Kinesis Data Streams、Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 OpenSearch Service,無法直接送到 SNS topic,因此告警必須透過 metric filter 加 alarm(C),而非 subscription filter(D)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config with a multi-account aggregator tracks resource configuration state and compliance, not API/authentication activity. It does not capture root user console login events, and Config does not forward records to CloudWatch Logs in the way described, so it cannot supply the login source data.","why_zh":"AWS Config 多帳戶 aggregator 追蹤資源組態狀態與合規,而非 API/驗證活動。它不會擷取 root 使用者 console 登入事件,也不會以所述方式把記錄轉送到 CloudWatch Logs,因此無法提供登入來源資料。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon QuickSight is a BI tool that does not natively query CloudWatch Logs; there is no 'CloudWatch Logs query' data source for QuickSight. The native, intended way to dashboard log activity is a CloudWatch dashboard fed by a Logs Insights query (option F).","why_zh":"Amazon QuickSight 是 BI 工具,並不原生查詢 CloudWatch Logs;QuickSight 沒有所謂的「CloudWatch Logs 查詢」資料來源。要把日誌活動做成儀表板,原生且正確的做法是用 Logs Insights 查詢驅動的 CloudWatch dashboard(選項 F)。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the primary trap. A CloudWatch Logs subscription filter can only forward log data to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service. It cannot send events directly to an SNS topic, so this configuration is technically impossible as written; alerting on a pattern requires a metric filter and alarm (option C).","why_zh":"這是主要陷阱。CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能將日誌資料轉送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service,無法直接把事件送到 SNS topic,因此如題所述的設定技術上不可行;對某模式發出告警需使用 metric filter 加 alarm(選項 C)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/monitor-cloudtrail-log-files-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/creating-trail-organization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/send-cloudtrail-events-to-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_ExportQueryResults.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":231,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. A DevOps engineer must ensure that all users who access the AWS Management Console are authenticated through the company’s corporate identity provider (IdP). Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。一位 DevOps 工程师必须确保所有访问 AWS 管 理控制台的用户都通过公司的企业身份提供商（IdP）进行身份验证。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon GuardDuty with a delegated administrator account. Use GuardDuty to enforce denial of IAM user logins.","B":"Use AWS IAM Identity Center to configure identity federation with SAML 2.0.","C":"Create a permissions boundary in AWS IAM Identity Center to deny password logins for IAM users.","D":"Create IAM groups in the Organizations management account to apply consistent permissions for all IAM users.","E":"Create an SCP in Organizations to deny password creation for IAM users."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用具有委托管理员权限的账户来使用 Amazon GuardDuty。利用 GuardDuty 来实施拒绝访问。 IAM 用户登录。","B":"使用 AWS IAM 身份中心通过 SAML 2.0 配置身份联合。","C":"在 AWS IAM 身份中心创建权限边界，以禁止 IAM 用户使用密码登录。","D":"在组织管理账户中创建 IAM 组，以便为所有 IAM 用户应用一致的权限。","E":"在组织中创建一个 SCP（服务控制策略），以禁止为 IAM 用户创建密码。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: provide an authentication path through the corporate IdP, and prevent users from bypassing it. B (IAM Identity Center configured for SAML 2.0 identity federation) is AWS's canonical way to authenticate workforce users to the Management Console through a corporate IdP. The IAM Identity Center docs describe it as 'one point of federation' using a 'SAML 2.0 identity provider' to give users access to AWS accounts. E (an SCP in Organizations that denies IAM-user password/login-profile creation) closes the backdoor: SCPs are the organization-wide guardrail that applies to all member accounts, and denying iam:CreateLoginProfile/iam:CreateUser password actions stops anyone from creating an IAM-user console password and bypassing the federated IdP. Together B and E ensure every console user authenticates through the IdP.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩個部分：提供透過企業 IdP 的驗證路徑，並阻止使用者繞過它。B（設定 IAM Identity Center 進行 SAML 2.0 身分聯合）是 AWS 讓員工使用者透過企業 IdP 驗證並存取 Management Console 的標準做法；IAM Identity Center 文件將其描述為使用 SAML 2.0 identity provider 的『單一聯合點』。E（在 Organizations 建立 SCP 拒絕 IAM 使用者建立密碼／login profile）則封住後門：SCP 是適用於所有成員帳戶的組織層級護欄，拒絕 iam:CreateLoginProfile／iam:CreateUser 密碼動作可防止任何人建立 IAM 使用者主控台密碼而繞過聯合的 IdP。B 與 E 結合即確保每位主控台使用者都透過 IdP 驗證。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that generates findings; it cannot enforce or deny IAM user logins. The described enforcement capability is fabricated.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務，只會產生 findings，無法強制或拒絕 IAM 使用者登入。所述的強制執行能力是虛構的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Permissions boundaries are an IAM construct (not created 'in IAM Identity Center') that cap the maximum API permissions of an IAM principal; they do not control or block console password authentication, so they cannot deny password logins.","why_zh":"Permissions boundary 是 IAM 的機制（並非在 IAM Identity Center 建立），用來限制 IAM principal 的最大 API 權限上限，並不控制或封鎖主控台密碼驗證，因此無法拒絕密碼登入。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"IAM groups only organize permissions for grouped users; they neither enforce IdP authentication nor prevent IAM-user password logins, and creating them in the management account does not apply a guardrail to member accounts.","why_zh":"IAM 群組僅用來組織使用者的權限，既不能強制 IdP 驗證，也無法阻止 IAM 使用者以密碼登入；在管理帳戶建立群組也不會對成員帳戶套用護欄。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/how-to-connect-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":232,"question_en":"A company has deployed a new platform that runs on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). The new platform hosts web applications that users frequently update. The application developers build the Docker images for the applications and deploy the Docker images manually to the platform. The platform usage has increased to more than 500 users every day. Frequent updates, building the updated Docker images for the applications, and deploying the Docker images on the platform manually have all become difficult to manage. The company needs to receive an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notification if Docker image scanning returns any HIGH or CRITICAL findings for operating system or programming language package vulnerabilities. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司部署了一个新的平台，该平台运行在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上。新平台承载 着用户经常更新的网络应用程序。应用程序开发人员为这些应用程序构建 Docker 镜像，并手动将 Docker 镜 像部署到该平台上。 该平台的每日使用用户已超过 500 人。频繁的更新、为应用程序构建更新后的 Docker 镜像以及手动在平 台上部署 Docker 镜像，这些都变得难以管理。 如果 Docker 镜像扫描发现操作系统或编程语言包存在任何高危或严重漏洞，公司需要收到亚马逊简单 通知服务（Amazon SNS）的通知。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository to store the Dockerfile and Kubernetes deployment files. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. Use an Amazon S3 event to invoke the pipeline when a newer version of the Dockerfile is committed. Add a step to the pipeline to initiate the AWS CodeBuild project.","B":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository to store the Dockerfile and Kubernetes deployment files. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. Use an Amazon EventBridge event to invoke the pipeline when a newer version of the Dockerfile is committed. Add a step to the pipeline to initiate the AWS CodeBuild project.","C":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project that builds the Docker images and stores the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Turn on basic scanning for the ECR repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that monitors Amazon GuardDuty events. Configure the EventBridge rule to send an event to an SNS topic when the finding-severity-counts parameter is more than 0 at a CRITICAL or HIGH level.","D":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project that builds the Docker images and stores the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Turn on enhanced scanning for the ECR repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that monitors ECR image scan events. Configure the EventBridge rule to send an event to an SNS topic when the finding-severity-counts parameter is more than 0 at a CRITICAL or HIGH level.","E":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project that scans the Dockerfile. Configure the project to build the Docker images and store the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository if the scan is successful. Configure an SNS topic to provide notification if the scan returns any vulnerabilities."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库来存储 Dockerfile 和 Kubernetes 部署文件。在 AWS CodePipeline 中创 建一个管道。使用 Amazon S3 事件在提交 Dockerfile 的新版本时调用该管道。在管道中添加一个步骤以 启动 AWS CodeBuild 项目。","B":"创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库来存储 Dockerfile 和 Kubernetes 部署文件。在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个管道。使用 Amazon EventBridge 事件在提交 Dockerfile 的新版本时调用该管道。在管道 中添加一个步骤以启动 AWS CodeBuild 项目。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目，用于构建 Docker 镜像并将这些镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。为 ECR 存储库开启基本扫描。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规 则来监控 Amazon GuardDuty 事件。配置 EventBridge 规则，当 CRITICAL 或 HIGH 级别的 finding- severity-counts 参数值大于 0 时，将事件发送到 SNS 主题。","D":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建 Docker 镜像，并将 Docker 镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。为 ECR 存储库开启增强扫描功能。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则来监控 ECR 镜像扫描事件。配置 EventBridge 规则，当 CRITICAL 或 HIGH 级别的 finding-severity- counts 参数值大于 0 时，将事件发送到 SNS 主题。","E":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来扫描 Dockerfile。如果扫描成功，配置该项目以构建 Docker 镜像并将 Docker 镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。配置一个 SNS 主题， 以便在扫描返回任何漏洞时提供通知。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements drive the answer: (1) automate the build/deploy pipeline triggered by Dockerfile changes, and (2) get an SNS notification when image scanning returns HIGH/CRITICAL findings for BOTH operating system AND programming language package vulnerabilities. For the pipeline trigger, AWS documents that a CodeCommit source action uses Amazon EventBridge as the recommended (and default console) change detection method; an 'Amazon S3 event' does not detect CodeCommit commits, so B is correct and A is wrong. For scanning, only ECR enhanced scanning (powered by Amazon Inspector) covers both OS and programming language package vulnerabilities, whereas basic scanning only performs OS-level CVE scans. Enhanced scanning has Amazon Inspector emit EventBridge events ('Inspector2 Scan'/'Inspector2 Finding') that include the finding-severity-counts parameter with CRITICAL and HIGH counts, which an EventBridge rule can route to an SNS topic. Therefore D is correct: enhanced scanning + an EventBridge rule monitoring ECR image scan events + SNS when finding-severity-counts for CRITICAL/HIGH is greater than 0.","explanation_zh":"兩個需求決定答案：(1) 由 Dockerfile 變更觸發的自動化 build/deploy pipeline；(2) 當映像掃描針對作業系統「以及」程式語言套件弱點回報 HIGH/CRITICAL 結果時，發出 SNS 通知。對於 pipeline 觸發，AWS 文件指出 CodeCommit source action 使用 Amazon EventBridge 作為建議（且為主控台預設）的變更偵測方法；'Amazon S3 event' 無法偵測 CodeCommit 的 commit，因此 B 正確、A 錯誤。對於掃描，只有 ECR enhanced scanning（由 Amazon Inspector 提供）同時涵蓋 OS 與程式語言套件弱點，而 basic scanning 僅執行 OS 層級的 CVE 掃描。Enhanced scanning 會讓 Amazon Inspector 發出 EventBridge 事件（'Inspector2 Scan'/'Inspector2 Finding'），其中包含帶有 CRITICAL 與 HIGH 計數的 finding-severity-counts 參數，EventBridge rule 可將其轉送至 SNS topic。因此 D 正確：enhanced scanning + 監控 ECR image scan 事件的 EventBridge rule + 當 CRITICAL/HIGH 的 finding-severity-counts 大於 0 時發送 SNS。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses an 'Amazon S3 event' to invoke the pipeline on a CodeCommit Dockerfile commit. CodeCommit commits do not generate S3 events; the documented (recommended/default) change detection method for a CodeCommit source action is Amazon EventBridge, not S3.","why_zh":"使用 'Amazon S3 event' 在 CodeCommit Dockerfile commit 時觸發 pipeline。CodeCommit 的 commit 不會產生 S3 事件；CodeCommit source action 文件記載的（建議/預設）變更偵測方法是 Amazon EventBridge，而非 S3。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Wrong on two points: basic scanning only covers operating system CVEs, not programming language package vulnerabilities; and it tells EventBridge to monitor 'Amazon GuardDuty events' for finding-severity-counts. ECR image scan findings come from Amazon Inspector/ECR, not GuardDuty.","why_zh":"兩處錯誤：basic scanning 僅涵蓋作業系統 CVE，不含程式語言套件弱點；且要 EventBridge 監控 'Amazon GuardDuty events' 取得 finding-severity-counts。ECR 映像掃描結果來自 Amazon Inspector/ECR，而非 GuardDuty。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Has CodeBuild 'scan the Dockerfile' and configure SNS for any vulnerabilities. Scanning a Dockerfile is not the same as scanning the built image for OS and programming-language CVE findings at HIGH/CRITICAL severity; this does not provide the Inspector-based finding-severity-counts notification the requirement needs.","why_zh":"讓 CodeBuild 「掃描 Dockerfile」並對任何弱點設定 SNS。掃描 Dockerfile 不等於針對建構後的映像掃描 OS 與程式語言 CVE 並以 HIGH/CRITICAL 嚴重性回報；無法提供需求所需、以 Inspector 為基礎的 finding-severity-counts 通知。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/change-detection-methods.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/triggering.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":233,"question_en":"A company groups its AWS accounts in OUs in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company has deployed a set of Amazon API Gateway APIs in one of the Organizations accounts. The APIs are bound to the account's VPC and have no existing authentication mechanism. Only principals in a specific OU can have permissions to invoke the APIs. The company applies the following policy to the API Gateway interface VPC endpoint: The company also updates the API Gateway resource policies to deny invocations that do not come through the interface VPC endpoint. After the updates, the following error message appears during attempts to use the interface VPC endpoint URL to invoke an API: \"User: anonymous is not authorized.\" Which combination of steps will solve this problem? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中的组织单元（OU）里对其 AWS 账户进行了分组。该公司在其中一个组织账户中部 署了一组 Amazon API Gateway API。这些 API 绑定到该账户的虚拟私有云（VPC），并且没有现有的身份 验证机制。只有特定 OU 中的主体才能获得调用这些 API 的权限。 该公司对 API 网关接口 VPC 终端节点采用以下策略： 该公司还更新了 API 网关资源策略，以拒绝未通过接口 VPC 端点的调用。更新后，在尝试使用接口 VPC 端点 URL 调用 API 时，会出现以下错误消息：“用户：匿名用户未获授权。” 哪两个步骤的组合能解决这个问题？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable IAM authentication on all API methods by setting AWS JAM as the authorization method.","B":"Create a token-based AWS Lambda authorizer that passes the caller's identity in a bearer token.","C":"Create a request parameter-based AWS Lambda authorizer that passes the caller's identity in a combination of headers, query string parameters, stage variables, and $cortext variables.","D":"Use Amazon Cognito user pools as the authorizer to control access to the API.","E":"Verify the identity of the requester by using Signature Version 4 to sign client requests by using AWS credentials."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过将 AWS JAM 设置为授权方法，在所有 API 方法上启用 IAM 身份验证。","B":"创建一个基于令牌的 AWS Lambda 授权程序，通过承载令牌传递调用方的身份。","C":"创建一个基于请求参数的 AWS Lambda 授权器，该授权器通过组合使用标头、查询字符串参数、 阶段变量和 $cortext 变量来传递调用者的身份。","D":"使用 Amazon Cognito 用户池作为授权方来控制对 API 的访问。","E":"使用 AWS 凭证通过 Signature Version 4 对客户端请求进行签名，以验证请求者的身份。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The error 'User: anonymous is not authorized to perform: execute-api:Invoke' is documented in API Gateway's resource policy troubleshooting guide. It occurs when a resource policy grants access to specific IAM principals/identities (or relies on IAM-based access) but the API methods are not configured with AWS_IAM authorization. AWS states explicitly: 'You must use AWS_IAM authorization for every method in your API, or else your API returns the previous error message.' Therefore step A (enable IAM authentication by setting AWS_IAM as the authorizationType on all methods) is required. However, enabling AWS_IAM alone is insufficient: with AWS_IAM the API expects an authenticated identity, and API Gateway authenticates the caller using Signature Version 4 (SigV4). If the client does not sign requests with AWS credentials, the caller is still treated as 'anonymous.' Thus step E (sign client requests with SigV4 using AWS credentials) is the second required step. Together, A establishes that an authenticated IAM identity is required, and E provides that identity, allowing only principals with appropriate IAM permissions (those in the specific OU) to invoke the API.","explanation_zh":"錯誤訊息 'User: anonymous is not authorized to perform: execute-api:Invoke' 在 API Gateway resource policy 的疑難排解文件中有明確記載。當 resource policy 將存取權授予特定 IAM principal/身分（或仰賴 IAM 型存取）但 API methods 並未設定 AWS_IAM 授權時，就會出現此錯誤。AWS 明確說明：'You must use AWS_IAM authorization for every method in your API, or else your API returns the previous error message.' 因此步驟 A（在所有 method 上將 authorizationType 設為 AWS_IAM 來啟用 IAM 驗證）是必要的。然而僅啟用 AWS_IAM 並不夠：啟用 AWS_IAM 後 API 會要求經過驗證的身分，而 API Gateway 透過 Signature Version 4 (SigV4) 驗證呼叫者。若用戶端未以 AWS 憑證簽署請求，呼叫者仍會被視為 'anonymous'。因此步驟 E（使用 AWS 憑證以 SigV4 簽署用戶端請求）是第二個必要步驟。A 確立需要經過驗證的 IAM 身分，E 提供該身分，使得只有具備適當 IAM 權限（特定 OU 中的 principal）才能呼叫 API。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A token-based (TOKEN) Lambda authorizer is an alternative auth mechanism using a bearer token, not the fix for an 'anonymous' error rooted in an IAM-principal resource policy. The requirement is to restrict to principals in a specific OU via IAM permissions, which maps to AWS_IAM authorization, not a custom Lambda authorizer. It also does nothing to provide the SigV4-signed identity the resource policy expects.","why_zh":"token 型（TOKEN）Lambda authorizer 是使用 bearer token 的替代驗證機制，並非修正源自 IAM-principal resource policy 之 'anonymous' 錯誤的方法。需求是透過 IAM 權限限制給特定 OU 中的 principal，對應的是 AWS_IAM 授權而非自訂 Lambda authorizer，且它無法提供 resource policy 所期望的 SigV4 簽署身分。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A request parameter-based (REQUEST) Lambda authorizer is again a custom authorization alternative based on headers/query strings/stage variables. It does not satisfy the IAM-based OU restriction and does not produce the SigV4-authenticated identity that resolves the 'anonymous' error.","why_zh":"request 參數型（REQUEST）Lambda authorizer 同樣是基於 headers/query string/stage variables 的自訂授權替代方案。它無法滿足以 IAM 為基礎的 OU 限制，也無法產生解決 'anonymous' 錯誤所需的 SigV4 驗證身分。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Cognito user pools (COGNITO_USER_POOLS authorizer) use JWT tokens for end-user authentication, not AWS IAM principals. It cannot enforce that only principals within a specific Organizations OU may invoke the API and does not address the SigV4/IAM signing needed to fix the 'anonymous' error.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito user pools（COGNITO_USER_POOLS authorizer）使用 JWT token 進行終端使用者驗證，而非 AWS IAM principal。它無法限制只有特定 Organizations OU 中的 principal 才能呼叫 API，也無法處理修正 'anonymous' 錯誤所需的 SigV4/IAM 簽署。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-resource-policies-create-attach.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-authorization-flow.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_sigv.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":234,"question_en":"A company wants to decrease the time it takes to develop new features. The company uses AWS CodeBuild and AWS CodeDeploy to build and deploy its applications. The company uses AWS CodePipeline to deploy each microservice with its own CI/CD pipeline. The company needs more visibility into the average time between the release of new features and the average time to recover after a failed deployment. Which solution will provide this visibility with the LEAST configuration effort?","question_zh":"一家公司希望缩短开发新功能所需的时间。该公司使用 AWS CodeBuild 和 AWS CodeDeploy 来 构建和部署其应用程序。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 为每个微服务部署其自身的 CI/CD 管道。 该公司需要更清楚地了解新功能发布之间的平均间隔时间以及部署失败后的平均恢复时间。 哪种解决方案能以最少的配置工作量提供这种可见性？","options_en":{"A":"Program an AWS Lambda function that creates Amazon CloudWatch custom metrics with information about successful runs and failed runs for each pipeline. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function every 5 minutes. Use the metrics to build a CloudWatch dashboard.","B":"Program an AWS Lambda function that creates Amazon CloudWatch custom metrics with information about successful runs and failed runs for each pipeline. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function after every successful run and after every failed run. Use the metrics to build a CloudWatch dashboard.","C":"Program an AWS Lambda function that writes information about successful runs and failed runs to Amazon DynamoDB. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function after every successful run and after every failed run. Build an Amazon QuickSight dashboard to show the information from DynamoDB.","D":"Program an AWS Lambda function that writes information about successful runs and failed runs to Amazon DynamoDB. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function every 5 minutes. Build an Amazon QuickSight dashboard to show the information from DynamoDB."},"options_zh":{"A":"编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为每个管道的成功运行和失败运行创建包含相关信息的 Amazon CloudWatch 自定义指标。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 5 分钟调用一次该 Lambda 函数。 利用这些指标构建一个 CloudWatch 仪表板。","B":"编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为每个管道的成功运行和失败运行创建包含相关信息的 Amazon CloudWatch 自定义指标。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在每次成功运行和每次失败运行后调 用该 Lambda 函数。使用这些指标构建一个 CloudWatch 仪表板。","C":"编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将成功运行和失败运行的信息写入 Amazon DynamoDB。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在每次运行后调用该 Lambda 函数。 在每次成功运行和每次失败运行之后。构建一个 Amazon QuickSight 仪表板来展示来自 DynamoDB 的信息。","D":"编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将成功运行和失败运行的信息写入 Amazon DynamoDB。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 5 分钟调用一次该 Lambda 函数。构建一个 Amazon QuickSight 仪表 板来展示 DynamoDB 中的信息。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The company needs visibility into lead time for changes (average time between new feature releases) and mean time to recovery (MTTR after a failed deployment). CodePipeline natively emits 'CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change' events to EventBridge, including SUCCEEDED and FAILED states, on a guaranteed at-least-once basis with the execution-id and timing in the payload. Therefore an EventBridge rule with an event pattern that invokes a Lambda function after every successful run and every failed run (B) captures the exact moments and data needed, with no polling, deduplication, or missed-window logic. The Lambda simply calls PutMetricData to create CloudWatch custom metrics, and a CloudWatch dashboard is built directly from those metrics within a single integrated monitoring service. This is the LEAST configuration effort. Options A and D use a 5-minute schedule that requires the function to poll pipeline execution history and reason about state changes, adding complexity and imprecision. Option C uses an event-driven trigger but adds DynamoDB plus QuickSight; QuickSight does not natively connect to DynamoDB (its supported sources are relational stores, SaaS, and files), so it needs an Athena federated query or export, plus dataset/analysis setup - more effort than CloudWatch metrics and a CloudWatch dashboard.","explanation_zh":"公司需要對 lead time for changes（新功能發布之間的平均時間）與 MTTR（部署失敗後的平均恢復時間）取得能見度。CodePipeline 原生會將 'CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change' 事件（包含 SUCCEEDED 與 FAILED 狀態）以保證至少一次的方式送至 EventBridge，且 payload 中含有 execution-id 與時間資訊。因此使用 event pattern 的 EventBridge rule，在每次成功與每次失敗執行後觸發 Lambda（選項 B），即可在精確時刻取得所需資料，無需輪詢、去重或處理時間窗遺漏。Lambda 只需呼叫 PutMetricData 建立 CloudWatch 自訂指標，並直接以這些指標建立 CloudWatch dashboard，全部在單一整合監控服務內完成，設定工作量最少。選項 A 與 D 採用每 5 分鐘排程，需自行輪詢 pipeline 執行歷史並判斷狀態變化，增加複雜度與不精確性。選項 C 雖為事件驅動，但加入 DynamoDB 與 QuickSight；QuickSight 並不原生連接 DynamoDB（其支援來源為關聯式資料庫、SaaS 與檔案），需透過 Athena 聯邦查詢或匯出，再加上 dataset/analysis 設定，工作量大於 CloudWatch 指標加 CloudWatch dashboard。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A 5-minute scheduled EventBridge rule forces the Lambda to poll CodePipeline execution history every 5 minutes, detect which runs newly succeeded or failed, and deduplicate - far more logic than reacting to native state-change events, and it can miss precise timing needed for MTTR.","why_zh":"每 5 分鐘的排程 rule 迫使 Lambda 每 5 分鐘輪詢 CodePipeline 執行歷史、判斷哪些執行新近成功或失敗並去重，遠比直接回應原生狀態變化事件複雜，且會遺失 MTTR 所需的精確時間點。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Although event-driven, it adds DynamoDB and QuickSight. QuickSight does not natively support DynamoDB as a data source, so it needs Athena federated queries or an export plus dataset and analysis configuration - more setup than CloudWatch custom metrics feeding a CloudWatch dashboard.","why_zh":"雖為事件驅動，但加入 DynamoDB 與 QuickSight。QuickSight 並不原生支援 DynamoDB 作為資料來源，需透過 Athena 聯邦查詢或匯出，再加上 dataset 與 analysis 設定，設定工作量大於以 CloudWatch 自訂指標驅動 CloudWatch dashboard。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines the two weakest choices: a 5-minute polling schedule (requiring history polling and deduplication) and the DynamoDB-to-QuickSight stack that QuickSight cannot natively query, maximizing configuration effort.","why_zh":"結合兩個最弱選擇：每 5 分鐘輪詢排程（需輪詢歷史並去重）與 QuickSight 無法原生查詢的 DynamoDB 至 QuickSight 架構，使設定工作量最大。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/detect-state-changes-cloudwatch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codepipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/publishingMetrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/quick/latest/userguide/supported-data-sources.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":235,"question_en":"A company has developed a static website hosted on an Amazon S3 bucket. The website is deployed using AWS CloudFormation. The CloudFormation template defines an S3 bucket and a custom resource that copies content into the bucket from a source location. The company has decided that it needs to move the website to a new location, so the existing CloudFormation stack must be deleted and re-created. However, CloudFormation reports that the stack could not be deleted cleanly. What is the MOST likely cause and how can the DevOps engineer mitigate this problem for this and future versions of the website?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一个托管在 Amazon S3 存储桶上的静态网站。该网站通过 AWS CloudFormation 进行部署。 CloudFormation 模板定义了一个 S3 存储桶以及一个自定义资源，该资源会将内容从源位置复制到该存储 桶中。 公司已决定将网站迁移到新位置，因此必须删除现有的 CloudFormation 堆栈并重新创建。然而， CloudFormation 报告称无法干净地删除该堆栈。 最有可能的原因是什么？DevOps 工程师应如何解决此问题以及未来版本网站中可能出现的类似问题？ 删除操作失败，原因是 S3 存储桶具有活动的网站配置。请修改 CloudFormation 模板，从 S3 存储桶 资源中移除 WebsiteConfiguration 属性。 删除操作失败，原因是 S3 存储桶未清空。请修改自定义资源的 AWS Lambda 函数代码，当请求类型为 “删除”时，递归清空存储桶。 删除操作失败，原因是自定义资源未定义删除策略。请在自定义资源定义中添加一个名为 DeletionPolicy 的属性，并将其值设为 RemoveOnDeletion。","options_en":{"A":"Deletion has failed because the S3 bucket has an active website configuration. Modify the CloudFormation template to remove the WebsiteConfiguration property from the S3 bucket resource.","B":"Deletion has failed because the S3 bucket is not empty. Modify the custom resource's AWS Lambda function code to recursively empty the bucket when RequestType is Delete.","C":"Deletion has failed because the custom resource does not define a deletion policy. Add a DeletionPolicy property to the custom resource definition with a value of RemoveOnDeletion.","D":"Deletion has failed because the S3 bucket is not empty. Modify the S3 bucket resource in the CloudFormation template to add a DeletionPolicy property with a value of Empty."},"options_zh":{"D":"删除失败，因为 S3 存储桶不为空。请在 CloudFormation 模板中修改 S3 存储桶资源，添加一个 值为“Empty”的 DeletionPolicy 属性。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudFormation can only delete an empty S3 bucket. The AWS::S3::Bucket reference states 'You can only delete empty buckets. Deletion fails for buckets that have contents,' and the DeletionPolicy reference confirms that for S3 buckets 'you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed.' Because the custom resource copies website content into the bucket, the bucket is not empty at delete time, so CloudFormation fails to delete it. The correct and forward-looking fix is to extend the existing custom resource's Lambda function so that when it receives a Delete RequestType (custom resources support Create, Update, and Delete operations) it recursively empties the bucket before responding SUCCESS, allowing CloudFormation to then delete the now-empty bucket. Since the custom resource is part of the template, this fix applies to the current stack and every future version of the website.","explanation_zh":"CloudFormation 只能刪除空的 S3 bucket。AWS::S3::Bucket 參考文件明確指出『You can only delete empty buckets. Deletion fails for buckets that have contents』,而 DeletionPolicy 文件也確認對 S3 bucket 而言『you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed』。由於 custom resource 把網站內容複製進 bucket,刪除堆疊時 bucket 並非空的,因此 CloudFormation 刪除失敗。正確且具前瞻性的修正方式是擴充現有 custom resource 的 Lambda 函式:當收到 Delete 的 RequestType 時(custom resource 支援 Create、Update、Delete 操作),先遞迴清空 bucket 再回傳 SUCCESS,讓 CloudFormation 接著刪除已清空的 bucket。由於 custom resource 屬於範本的一部分,此修正同時適用於目前堆疊及未來每個版本的網站。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An active WebsiteConfiguration does not block bucket deletion; only non-empty buckets cause delete failures. Removing WebsiteConfiguration would also break the static website hosting feature the company relies on.","why_zh":"啟用的 WebsiteConfiguration 不會阻擋 bucket 刪除;只有非空 bucket 才會導致刪除失敗。移除 WebsiteConfiguration 反而會破壞公司所依賴的靜態網站託管功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"'RemoveOnDeletion' is not a valid DeletionPolicy value (valid values are Delete, Retain, Snapshot, RetainExceptOnCreate). Custom resources are already deleted by default via the Lambda's Delete request; the missing deletion policy is not the cause and the proposed value is fabricated.","why_zh":"『RemoveOnDeletion』並非有效的 DeletionPolicy 值(有效值為 Delete、Retain、Snapshot、RetainExceptOnCreate)。custom resource 預設已透過 Lambda 的 Delete 請求被刪除;缺少刪除政策並非原因,且此提議的值是虛構的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"'Empty' is not a valid DeletionPolicy value. DeletionPolicy controls whether a resource is deleted/retained/snapshotted, not whether a bucket is emptied; it cannot delete objects from a bucket. The root cause is correctly identified but the proposed fix does not exist.","why_zh":"『Empty』並非有效的 DeletionPolicy 值。DeletionPolicy 控制資源是否被刪除/保留/快照,而非清空 bucket;它無法刪除 bucket 內的物件。雖然根本原因判斷正確,但提議的修正方式並不存在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-s3-bucket.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-attribute-deletionpolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":236,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon EC2 as its primary compute platform. A DevOps team wants to audit the company's EC2 instances to check whether any prohibited applications have been installed on the EC2 instances. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司将其主要计算平台定为亚马逊 EC2。一个 DevOps 团队想要审计该公司的 EC2 实例，以检查这 些实例上是否安装了任何被禁止的应用程序。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Systems Manager on each instance. Use AWS Systems Manager Inventory. Use Systems Manager resource data sync to synchronize and store findings in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function that runs when new objects are added to the S3 bucket. Configure the Lambda function to identify prohibited applications.","B":"Configure AWS Systems Manager on each instance. Use Systems Manager Inventory Create AWS Config rules that monitor changes from Systems Manager Inventory to identify prohibited applications.","C":"Configure AWS Systems Manager on each instance. Use Systems Manager Inventory. Filter a trail in AWS CloudTrail for Systems Manager Inventory events to identify prohibited applications.","D":"Designate Amazon CloudWatch Logs as the log destination for all application instances. Run an automated script across all instances to create an inventory of installed applications. Configure the script to forward the results to CloudWatch Logs. Create a CloudWatch alarm that uses filter patterns to search log data to identify prohibited applications."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个实例上配置 AWS 系统管理器。使用 AWS 系统管理器库存。使用系统管理器资源数据同步将发 现结果同步并存储到 Amazon S3 存储桶中。创建一个在向 S3 存储桶添加新对象时运行的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以识别被禁止的应用程序。","B":"在每个实例上配置 AWS 系统管理器。使用系统管理器库存创建 AWS 配置规则，以监控来自系统管理 器库存的更改，从而识别被禁止的应用程序。","C":"在每个实例上配置 AWS 系统管理器。使用系统管理器库存功能。在 AWS CloudTrail 中筛选系统管理器 库存事件的跟踪记录，以识别被禁止的应用程序。","D":"将 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 指定为所有应用程序实例的日志目标。在所有实例上运行自动化脚本以创建 已安装应用程序的清单。配置脚本将结果转发到 CloudWatch Logs。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，使用筛 选模式搜索日志数据以识别被禁止的应用程序。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Systems Manager Inventory collects 'Applications' metadata (names, publishers, versions) from managed nodes and stores it as configuration items of resource type AWS::SSM::ManagedInstanceInventory. AWS Config provides a purpose-built managed rule, ec2-managedinstance-applications-blacklisted (EC2_MANAGEDINSTANCE_APPLICATIONS_BLACKLISTED), whose resource type is AWS::SSM::ManagedInstanceInventory, whose trigger type is 'Configuration changes,' and which 'checks if none of the specified applications are installed on the instance,' taking a comma-separated applicationNames parameter. This is exactly Option B: enable Inventory, then create AWS Config rules that monitor changes from Systems Manager Inventory to identify prohibited applications. It is the most operationally efficient because it relies entirely on managed AWS services with no custom code to write, deploy, or maintain, and it evaluates automatically whenever inventory data changes.","explanation_zh":"Systems Manager Inventory 會從受管節點收集 'Applications' 中繼資料（名稱、發行者、版本），並以資源類型 AWS::SSM::ManagedInstanceInventory 的組態項目形式儲存。AWS Config 提供專用的受管規則 ec2-managedinstance-applications-blacklisted（EC2_MANAGEDINSTANCE_APPLICATIONS_BLACKLISTED），其資源類型為 AWS::SSM::ManagedInstanceInventory，觸發類型為 'Configuration changes'，並檢查實例上是否未安裝指定的應用程式，使用以逗號分隔的 applicationNames 參數。這正是選項 B：啟用 Inventory，然後建立 AWS Config 規則來監控來自 Systems Manager Inventory 的變更以識別違禁應用程式。這是最具營運效率的方案，因為完全依賴受管 AWS 服務，無需撰寫、部署或維護任何自訂程式碼，並會在 inventory 資料變更時自動評估。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Works technically but requires building and maintaining custom Lambda code to parse S3 objects and identify prohibited apps, which is more operational overhead than the out-of-the-box AWS Config managed rule.","why_zh":"技術上可行，但需要建立與維護自訂 Lambda 程式碼來解析 S3 物件並識別違禁應用程式，比現成的 AWS Config 受管規則有更高的營運負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically invalid. CloudTrail records AWS API management/data-plane activity, not the inventory contents of installed software. Filtering CloudTrail for 'Systems Manager Inventory events' will not surface which applications are installed on instances.","why_zh":"技術上不成立。CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API 管理/資料平面活動，而非已安裝軟體的 inventory 內容。為 'Systems Manager Inventory 事件' 過濾 CloudTrail 無法顯示實例上安裝了哪些應用程式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Reinvents inventory collection with a custom script and CloudWatch Logs filter patterns/alarms. This is high maintenance, error-prone, and duplicates capability already provided natively by SSM Inventory plus AWS Config; CloudWatch alarms are also not designed for software-compliance auditing.","why_zh":"用自訂腳本與 CloudWatch Logs 過濾模式/警示重新發明 inventory 收集，維護成本高、易出錯，且重複了 SSM Inventory 加 AWS Config 已原生提供的功能；CloudWatch 警示也並非為軟體合規稽核而設計。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/ec2-managedinstance-applications-blacklisted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-inventory.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/service-integrations.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":237,"question_en":"A company has an event-driven JavaScript application. The application uses decoupled AWS managed services that publish, consume, and route events. During application testing, events are not delivered to the target that is specified by an Amazon EventBridge rule. A DevOps team must provide application testers with additional functionality to view, troubleshoot, and prevent the loss of events without redeployment of the application. Which combination of steps should the DevOps team take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个事件驱动的 JavaScript 应用程序。该应用程序使用解耦的 AWS 管理服务来发布、 消费和路由事件。在应用程序测试期间，事件未被传递到由 Amazon EventBridge 规则指定的目标。 DevOps 团队必须为应用程序测试人员提供额外的功能，以便查看、排查和防止事件丢失，而无 需重新部署应用程序。 DevOps 团队应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Launch AWS Device Farm with a standard test environment and project to run a specific build of the application.","B":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Enable AWS CloudTrail. Create a CloudTrail trail that specifies the S3 bucket as the storage location.","C":"Configure the EventBridge rule to use an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue as a dead-letter queue.","D":"Configure the EventBridge rule to use an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) FIFO queue as a dead-letter queue.","E":"Create a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Specify the log group as an additional target of the EventBridge rule.","F":"Update the application code base to use the AWS X-Ray SDK tracing feature to instrument the code with support for the X-Amzn-Trace-Id header."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用标准测试环境和项目启动 AWS 设备农场，以运行应用程序的特定版本。","B":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。启用 AWS CloudTrail。创建一个 CloudTrail 跟踪，指定该 S3 存 储桶作为存储位置。","C":"配置 EventBridge 规则，使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）标准队列作为死 信队列。","D":"配置 EventBridge 规则，使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）FIFO 队列作为死信 队列。","E":"在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个日志组。将该日志组指定为 EventBridge 规则的附加目 标。","F":"更新应用程序代码库，以使用 AWS X-Ray SDK 跟踪功能，通过支持 X-Amzn-Trace-Id 标头来 对代码进行检测。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are to view, troubleshoot, and prevent loss of EventBridge events WITHOUT redeploying the application. (C) A standard SQS dead-letter queue is the documented mechanism to prevent event loss: EventBridge sends events with failed invocations to the DLQ for later inspection and resend, and it is configured at the rule/target level with no application redeployment. (E) CloudWatch Logs groups are a supported EventBridge target type; adding the log group as an additional target lets testers view the actual events flowing through the rule for troubleshooting, again a rule-level change with no redeployment. (B) Enabling AWS CloudTrail with a trail writing to an S3 bucket records the EventBridge (and related service) API activity, giving testers an additional auditable view to troubleshoot why events were not delivered, and it requires no application change. The decisive qualifiers eliminate the others: (D) is wrong because EventBridge DLQs explicitly support only standard SQS queues, never FIFO; (F) requires modifying and redeploying the application code (X-Ray SDK instrumentation), violating the no-redeployment constraint; (A) AWS Device Farm tests mobile/web app builds on devices and is irrelevant to EventBridge delivery troubleshooting.","explanation_zh":"需求是要在「不重新部署應用程式」的情況下，檢視 (view)、排錯 (troubleshoot) 並防止 EventBridge 事件遺失。(C) 標準 SQS dead-letter queue 是官方文件指定用來防止事件遺失的機制：EventBridge 會把投遞失敗的事件送到 DLQ 以便日後檢查與重送，且設定在 rule/target 層級，不需重新部署。(E) CloudWatch Logs group 是 EventBridge 支援的 target 類型；把 log group 加為額外 target 讓測試者可直接檢視通過該 rule 的實際事件以排錯，同樣是 rule 層級變更、無需重新部署。(B) 啟用 AWS CloudTrail 並建立寫入 S3 bucket 的 trail，可記錄 EventBridge 及相關服務的 API 活動，提供額外的可稽核檢視協助排查事件未投遞的原因，且不需更動應用程式。決定性的限定詞排除其他選項：(D) 錯誤，因為 EventBridge DLQ 明確只支援 standard SQS queue，不支援 FIFO；(F) 需要修改並重新部署應用程式程式碼 (X-Ray SDK 埋點)，違反「不重新部署」的限制；(A) AWS Device Farm 是在裝置上測試行動/網頁應用程式建置，與 EventBridge 投遞排錯無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Device Farm runs mobile/web app builds against real devices for app testing; it has nothing to do with viewing, troubleshooting, or preventing loss of EventBridge events.","why_zh":"AWS Device Farm 是在實體裝置上執行行動/網頁應用程式建置進行測試，與檢視、排錯或防止 EventBridge 事件遺失完全無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EventBridge dead-letter queues support ONLY standard SQS queues; FIFO queues cannot be used as an EventBridge DLQ, so this option is technically invalid.","why_zh":"EventBridge dead-letter queue 只支援 standard SQS queue；FIFO queue 不能作為 EventBridge DLQ，因此此選項技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Using the X-Ray SDK to instrument the code requires updating and redeploying the application code base, which directly violates the 'without redeployment of the application' requirement.","why_zh":"使用 X-Ray SDK 對程式碼埋點需要更新並重新部署應用程式程式碼，直接違反「不重新部署應用程式」的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-rule-dlq.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-targets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-monitoring-events-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-events-rule-deadletterconfig.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":238,"question_en":"A company is migrating its container-based workloads to an AWS Organizations multi-account environment. The environment consists of application workload accounts that the company uses to deploy and run the containerized workloads. The company has also provisioned a shared services account for shared workloads in the organization. The company must follow strict compliance regulations. All container images must receive security scanning before they are deployed to any environment. Images can be consumed by downstream deployment mechanisms after the images pass a scan with no critical vulnerabilities. Pre-scan and post- scan images must be isolated from one another so that a deployment can never use pre-scan images. A DevOps engineer needs to create a strategy to centralize this process. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST administrative overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其基于容器的工作负载迁移到 AWS 组织的多账户环境中。该环境由公司用于部署 和运行容器化工作负载的应用程序工作负载账户组成。该公司还为组织中的共享工作负载配置了一 个共享服务账户。 该公司必须遵循严格的合规规定。所有容器镜像在部署到任何环境之前都必须接受安全扫描。只 有在扫描未发现关键漏洞的情况下，镜像才能被下游部署机制使用。预扫描镜像和扫描后的镜像 必须相互隔离，以确保部署绝不会使用预扫描镜像。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要制定一项策略来将此流程集中化。 哪种步骤组合能以最低的管理开销满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories in the shared services account: one repository for each pre-scan image and one repository for each post-scan image. Configure Amazon ECR image scanning to run on new image pushes to the pre-scan repositories. Use resource- based policies to grant the organization write access to the pre-scan repositories and read access to the post-scan repositories.","B":"Create pre-scan Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories in each account that publishes container images. Create repositories for post-scan images in the shared services account. Configure Amazon ECR image scanning to run on new image pushes to the pre-scan repositories. Use resource-based policies to grant the organization read access to the post-scan repositories.","C":"Configure image replication for each image from the image's pre-scan repository to the image's post- scan repository.","D":"Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline for each pre-scan repository. Create a source stage that runs when new images are pushed to the pre-scan repositories. Create a stage that uses AWS CodeBuild as the action provider. Write a buildspec.yaml definition that determines the image scanning status and pushes images without critical vulnerabilities to the post-scan repositories.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to image scanning completed events and invokes the Lambda function. Write function code that determines the image scanning status and pushes images without critical vulnerabilities to the post-scan repositories."},"options_zh":{"A":"在共享服务账户中创建 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库：为每个预扫描 镜像创建一个存储库，为每个后扫描镜像创建一个存储库。配置 Amazon ECR 镜像扫描功能， 使其在向预扫描存储库推送新镜像时运行。使用基于资源的策略授予组织对预扫描存储库的写 入权限以及对后扫描存储库的读取权限。","B":"在每个发布容器镜像的账户中创建预扫描的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存 储库。在共享服务账户中为扫描后的镜像创建存储库。配置 Amazon ECR 镜像扫描功能，使其 在向预扫描存储库推送新镜像时运行。使用基于资源的策略授予组织对扫描后存储库的读取访 问权限。","C":"为每个镜像配置从镜像预扫描存储库到镜像后扫描存储库的镜像复制。","D":"为每个预扫描存储库在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个管道。创建一个源阶段，当有新镜像推送到 预扫描存储库时运行。创建一个使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序的阶段。编写一个 buildspec.yaml 定义，用于确定镜像扫描状态，并将没有关键漏洞的镜像推送到后扫描存储库。","E":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对图像扫描完成事件做 出反应并调用该 Lambda 函数。编写函数代码以确定图像扫描状态，并将没有关键漏洞的图 像推送到扫描后的存储库。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to CENTRALIZE the scan-and-promote workflow with isolation between pre-scan and post-scan images and LEAST administrative overhead. Option A centralizes all repositories in the single shared services account (one pre-scan and one post-scan repo per image), enables basic scan-on-push on the pre-scan repos, and uses resource-based (repository) policies to grant the organization write access to pre-scan repos and read-only access to post-scan repos. This gives strong isolation because workload accounts can only read post-scan images, and it is fully centralized in one account, minimizing overhead. Option E completes the promotion: ECR basic scanning emits an EventBridge event with detail-type 'ECR Image Scan', scan-status 'COMPLETE', and finding-severity-counts (including CRITICAL). A single EventBridge rule can react to scan-completion events and invoke one Lambda function that inspects the severity counts and copies (pushes) only images with no critical vulnerabilities into the post-scan repositories. One rule plus one function covers all repos and triggers AFTER the scan finishes, which is the lowest-overhead, technically correct promotion mechanism. Together A+E centralize the process, enforce the gate, and keep pre-scan images unreachable by deployments.","explanation_zh":"需求是以最少管理負擔集中化掃描與晉升流程，並讓掃描前(pre-scan)與掃描後(post-scan)映像彼此隔離。選項 A 將所有儲存庫集中在單一 shared services 帳戶（每個映像各有一個 pre-scan 與一個 post-scan repository），在 pre-scan repository 啟用 basic scan-on-push，並以 resource-based (repository) policy 授予組織對 pre-scan repository 寫入權、對 post-scan repository 唯讀權。由於工作負載帳戶只能讀取 post-scan 映像，隔離性強，且完全集中於單一帳戶，管理負擔最低。選項 E 完成晉升流程：ECR basic scanning 會發出 detail-type 為 'ECR Image Scan'、scan-status 'COMPLETE'、含 finding-severity-counts（包含 CRITICAL）的 EventBridge 事件。單一 EventBridge rule 即可在掃描完成時觸發一個 Lambda function，檢查嚴重性計數，只把沒有 critical 漏洞的映像推送到 post-scan repository。一條 rule 加一個 function 即可涵蓋所有 repository，且在掃描完成「之後」才觸發，是負擔最低且技術正確的晉升機制。A+E 共同達成集中化、強制把關，並確保部署無法使用 pre-scan 映像。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Placing pre-scan repositories in EACH publishing account is decentralized, which directly contradicts the goal to CENTRALIZE the process and increases administrative overhead (many repos/policies spread across accounts). It also fails to describe how images move into the shared post-scan repos and only grants org read to post-scan, leaving the write/promotion path undefined.","why_zh":"把 pre-scan repository 分散放在每個發佈帳戶屬於去中心化，直接違反「集中化」目標並增加管理負擔（眾多 repo/政策散落各帳戶）。它也未說明映像如何進入共用 post-scan repo，且只授予組織對 post-scan 唯讀，晉升/寫入路徑未定義。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ECR private image replication is unconditional: it copies every image pushed after the rule is configured and cannot gate on scan status or severity. It would replicate pre-scan (including vulnerable) images into post-scan repos, breaking the required isolation and the no-critical-vulnerabilities gate.","why_zh":"ECR 私有映像複製是無條件的：規則設定後推送的每個映像都會被複製，無法依掃描狀態或嚴重性把關。它會把 pre-scan（含含漏洞的）映像複製進 post-scan repo，破壞所需的隔離與「無 critical 漏洞」把關條件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a CodePipeline per pre-scan repository is high administrative overhead (one pipeline + CodeBuild project per repo). A CodePipeline ECR source triggers on image push, not on scan completion, so it can race the scan; EventBridge-on-scan-complete (E) is both lower overhead and correctly timed.","why_zh":"為每個 pre-scan repository 建立一條 CodePipeline 管理負擔高（每個 repo 都要一條 pipeline 加 CodeBuild 專案）。CodePipeline 的 ECR source 是在映像推送時觸發，而非掃描完成時，可能與掃描競態；以掃描完成事件觸發 EventBridge 的選項 E 負擔更低且時機正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/ecr-eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-basic-enabling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/repository-policy-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":239,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster to deploy its web applications on containers. The web applications contain confidential data that cannot be decrypted without specific credentials. A DevOps engineer has stored the credentials in AWS Secrets Manager. The secrets are encrypted by an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. A Kubernetes service account for a third-party tool makes the secrets available to the applications. The service account assumes an IAM role that the company created to access the secrets. The service account receives an Access Denied (403 Forbidden) error while trying to retrieve the secrets from Secrets Manager. What is the root cause of this issue?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群在其容器上部署其网络应用程 序。这些网络应用程序包含机密数据，没有特定凭证无法解密。 一位 DevOps 工程师已将凭证存储在 AWS 机密管理器中。这些机密由 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）的客户管理密钥进行加密。一个用于第三方工具的 Kubernetes 服务账户使应用程序能够获取 这些机密。该服务账户承担了公司为访问机密而创建的 IAM 角色。 服务账户在尝试从密钥管理器获取密钥时收到“访问被拒绝（403 禁止）”错误。 这个问题的根本原因是什么？","options_en":{"A":"The IAM role that is attached to the EKS cluster does not have access to retrieve the secrets from Secrets Manager.","B":"The key policy for the customer managed key does not allow the Kubernetes service account IAM role to use the key.","C":"The key policy for the customer managed key does not allow the EKS cluster IAM role to use the key.","D":"The IAM role that is assumed by the Kubernetes service account does not have permission to access the EKS cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"附加到 EKS 集群的 IAM 角色没有权限从 Secrets Manager 中检索机密信息。","B":"客户管理密钥的关键策略不允许 Kubernetes 服务账户 IAM 角色使用该密钥。","C":"客户管理密钥的关键策略不允许 EKS 集群的 IAM 角色使用该密钥。","D":"由 Kubernetes 服务账户所承担的 IAM 角色没有访问 EKS 集群的权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is an IRSA (IAM Roles for Service Accounts) scenario: the Kubernetes service account assumes an IAM role that is the calling principal for the Secrets Manager request. The role was 'created to access the secrets,' so it already holds secretsmanager:GetSecretValue. The secret is encrypted with a customer managed KMS key, and per the Secrets Manager docs, GetSecretValue causes Secrets Manager to call kms:Decrypt 'on behalf of the user who is accessing the secret value,' with that permission granted via an IAM policy OR the key policy. If neither the role's IAM policy nor the CMK key policy authorizes the service-account role to use the key, the Decrypt fails and the caller gets an Access Denied (403). Therefore the root cause is that the customer managed key's policy does not allow the Kubernetes service account IAM role to use the key.","explanation_zh":"這是 IRSA (IAM Roles for Service Accounts) 情境:Kubernetes service account 所承擔的 IAM role 才是呼叫 Secrets Manager 的 principal。題目說該 role 是『為了存取 secrets 而建立』,因此它已具備 secretsmanager:GetSecretValue 權限。Secret 以 customer managed KMS key 加密,依 Secrets Manager 文件,GetSecretValue 會讓 Secrets Manager『代表存取該 secret 的使用者』呼叫 kms:Decrypt,而該權限可透過 IAM policy 或 key policy 授予。若該 service account role 在 role 的 IAM policy 與 CMK 的 key policy 中都未被授權使用該金鑰,Decrypt 就會失敗並回傳 Access Denied (403)。因此根本原因是 customer managed key 的 key policy 未允許該 Kubernetes service account IAM role 使用該金鑰。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Under IRSA the pod assumes the service-account IAM role, not the EKS cluster/node role, to call Secrets Manager. The role here was explicitly created to access the secrets, so the missing piece is KMS key authorization, not the cluster role's Secrets Manager access.","why_zh":"在 IRSA 下,Pod 是以 service account 的 IAM role(非 EKS cluster/node role)呼叫 Secrets Manager。題中該 role 已明確為存取 secrets 而建立,因此缺的是 KMS 金鑰授權,而非 cluster role 的 Secrets Manager 存取權。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The calling principal for kms:Decrypt is the assumed service-account role, not the EKS cluster IAM role. KMS evaluates the assumed role, so granting/denying the cluster role on the key is irrelevant to this request.","why_zh":"kms:Decrypt 的呼叫 principal 是被承擔的 service account role,而非 EKS cluster IAM role。KMS 評估的是被承擔的 role,因此在金鑰上授予/拒絕 cluster role 與此請求無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"'Permission to access the EKS cluster' is not relevant to a Secrets Manager API call. The pod is already running in the cluster; a 403 from Secrets Manager is an AWS authorization error tied to Secrets Manager/KMS permissions, not Kubernetes cluster RBAC.","why_zh":"『存取 EKS cluster 的權限』與 Secrets Manager API 呼叫無關。Pod 已在 cluster 中運行;Secrets Manager 回傳的 403 是與 Secrets Manager/KMS 權限相關的 AWS 授權錯誤,而非 Kubernetes cluster RBAC。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/security-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/integrating_ascp_irsa.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/auth-and-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/iam-roles-for-service-accounts.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":240,"question_en":"A company is migrating its product development teams from an on-premises data center to a hybrid environment. The new environment will add four AWS Regions and will give the developers the ability to use the Region that is geographically closest to them. All the development teams use a shared set of Linux applications. The on-premises data center stores the applications on a NetApp ONTAP storage device. The storage volume is mounted read-only on the development on-premises VMs. The company updates the applications on the shared volume once a week. A DevOps engineer needs to replicate the data to all the new Regions. The DevOps engineer must ensure that the data is always up to date with deduplication. The data also must not be dependent on the availability of the on-premises storage device. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其产品开发团队从本地数据中心迁移到混合环境中。新环境将增加四个 AWS 区 域，并且能让开发人员使用距离他们最近的区域。 所有开发团队都使用一套共享的 Linux 应用程序。本地数据中心将这些应用程序存储在 NetApp ONTAP 存储设备上。该存储卷在本地开发虚拟机上以只读方式挂载。公司每周对共享卷上的应用 程序进行一次更新。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要将数据复制到所有新的区域。该工程师必须确保数据始终是最新的，并且 要进行重复数据删除。数据还不能依赖于本地存储设备的可用性。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 File Gateway in the on-premises data center. Create S3 buckets in each Region. Set up a cron job to copy the data from the storage device to the S3 File Gateway. Set up S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) to the S3 buckets in each Region.","B":"Create an Amazon FSx File Gateway in one Region. Create file servers in Amazon FSx for Windows File Server in each Region. Set up a cron job to copy the data from the storage device to the FSx File Gateway.","C":"Create Multi-AZ Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP instances and volumes in each Region. Configure a scheduled SnapMirror relationship between the on-premises storage device and the FSx for ONTAP instances.","D":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system in each Region. Deploy an AWS DataSync agent in the on-premises data center. Configure a schedule for DataSync to copy the data to Amazon EFS daily."},"options_zh":{"A":"在本地数据中心创建一个 Amazon S3 文件网关。在每个区域创建 S3 存储桶。设置一个 cron 作 业将数据从存储设备复制到 S3 文件网关。为每个区域的 S3 存储桶设置 S3 跨区域复制 （CRR）。","B":"在一个区域创建一个 Amazon FSx 文件网关。在每个区域的 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 中创 建文件服务器。设置一个 cron 作业，将数据从存储设备复制到 FSx 文件网关。","C":"在每个区域创建多可用区的 Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 实例和卷。在本地存储设备与 FSx for ONTAP 实例之间配置计划的 SnapMirror 关系。","D":"在每个区域创建一个 Amazon Elastic File System（Amazon EFS）文件系统。在本地数据中心部署一个 AWS DataSync 代理。为 DataSync 配置一个每日将数据复制到 Amazon EFS 的计划。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: replicate a NetApp ONTAP read-only Linux application volume to four Regions, keep it always up to date, preserve deduplication, and make the data independent of the on-premises device. FSx for NetApp ONTAP (Multi-AZ in each Region) plus a scheduled NetApp SnapMirror relationship from the on-premises ONTAP device is the only option that satisfies all of these. AWS explicitly documents using SnapMirror to replicate/migrate on-premises NetApp ONTAP file systems to FSx for ONTAP, and SnapMirror block-level replication keeps deduplicated and compressed data in those states, directly meeting the deduplication requirement. SnapMirror supports scheduled cross-Region replication (as frequent as every 5 minutes), so the data stays current, and once it resides in the Multi-AZ FSx for ONTAP file systems the Linux clients access AWS-resident NFS copies independent of the on-premises storage device's availability.","explanation_zh":"需求為：將 NetApp ONTAP 唯讀的 Linux 應用程式磁碟區複寫到四個 Region、保持資料隨時最新、保留去重 (deduplication)，並讓資料不依賴地端儲存裝置的可用性。只有在每個 Region 建立 Multi-AZ Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP，並設定從地端 ONTAP 裝置到 FSx for ONTAP 的排程 NetApp SnapMirror 關係，才能同時滿足所有條件。AWS 文件明確說明可使用 SnapMirror 將地端 NetApp ONTAP 檔案系統複寫/遷移到 FSx for ONTAP，且 SnapMirror 的區塊層級複寫會保留去重與壓縮狀態，直接符合去重需求。SnapMirror 支援跨 Region 排程複寫 (最頻繁可達每 5 分鐘)，因此資料保持最新；資料一旦存放於 Multi-AZ FSx for ONTAP，Linux 用戶端即可透過 NFS 存取 AWS 上的副本，不再依賴地端儲存裝置的可用性。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 File Gateway exposes data as S3 objects, not a POSIX/NFS file system that the Linux applications expect to mount read-only. S3 has no native deduplication, and a cron job copying from the device plus CRR is operationally heavy and does not satisfy the deduplication requirement.","why_zh":"S3 File Gateway 以 S3 物件形式呈現資料，而非 Linux 應用程式預期掛載的 POSIX/NFS 檔案系統。S3 無原生去重功能，且用 cron 複製再加上 CRR 操作繁重，無法滿足去重需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"FSx File Gateway and FSx for Windows File Server target Windows/SMB workloads, not the Linux applications and ONTAP NFS source described here. It also only provisions in one Region for the gateway, and a cron copy does not natively preserve the source ONTAP deduplication.","why_zh":"FSx File Gateway 與 FSx for Windows File Server 針對 Windows/SMB 工作負載，不符合本題的 Linux 應用程式與 ONTAP NFS 來源。它的閘道也只佈署於單一 Region，且 cron 複製無法原生保留來源 ONTAP 的去重。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon EFS does not provide data deduplication, so this fails the explicit deduplication requirement. DataSync transfers files but does not deliver block-level dedup, and a daily schedule is less 'always up to date' than scheduled SnapMirror.","why_zh":"Amazon EFS 不提供資料去重，因此無法滿足明確的去重需求。DataSync 雖能傳輸檔案，但不提供區塊層級去重，且每日排程相較於排程 SnapMirror 較難達到『隨時最新』。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/migrating-fsx-ontap-snapmirror.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/scheduled-replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/what-is-fsx-ontap.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":241,"question_en":"A company has an application that stores data that includes personally identifiable information (PII) in an Amazon S3 bucket. All data is encrypted with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed keys. All AWS resources are deployed from an AWS CloudFormation template. A DevOps engineer needs to set up a development environment for the application in a different AWS account. The data in the development environment's S3 bucket needs to be updated once a week from the production environment's S3 bucket. The company must not move PII from the production environment without anonymizing the PII first. The data in each environment must be encrypted with different KMS customer managed keys. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，其数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，这些数据包含个人身份信息（PII）。 所有数据均使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）客户管理密钥进行加密。所有 AWS 资源均通过 AWS CloudFormation 模板进行部署。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要在另一个 AWS 账户中为应用程序设置开发环境。开发环境的 S3 存储桶中的数 据需要每周从生产环境的 S3 存储桶中更新一次。 公司不得在未对个人身份信息（PII）进行匿名化处理的情况下将其从生产环境转移。每个环境中的数 据都必须使用不同的 KMS 客户管理密钥进行加密。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Activate Amazon Macie on the S3 bucket in the production account. Create an AWS Step Functions state machine to initiate a discovery job and redact all PII before copying files to the S3 bucket in the development account. Give the state machine tasks decrypt permissions on the KMS key in the production account. Give the state machine tasks encrypt permissions on the KMS key in the development account.","B":"Set up S3 replication between the production S3 bucket and the development S3 bucket. Activate Amazon Macie on the development S3 bucket. Create an AWS Step Functions state machine to initiate a discovery job and redact all PII as the files are copied to the development S3 bucket. Give the state machine tasks encrypt and decrypt permissions on the KMS key in the development account.","C":"Set up an S3 Batch Operations job to copy files from the production S3 bucket to the development S3 bucket. In the development account, configure an AWS Lambda function to redact ail PII. Configure S3 Object Lambda to use the Lambda function for S3 GET requests. Give the Lambda function's IAM role encrypt and decrypt permissions on the KMS key in the development account.","D":"Create a development environment from the CloudFormation template in the development account. Schedule an Amazon EventBridge rule to start the AWS Step Functions state machine once a week.","E":"Create a development environment from the CloudFormation template in the development account. Schedule a cron job on an Amazon EC2 instance to run once a week to start the S3 Batch Operations job."},"options_zh":{"A":"在生产账户的 S3 存储桶上激活 Amazon Macie。创建一个 AWS Step Functions 状态机，用于启动发 现任务，并在将文件复制到开发账户的 S3 存储桶之前对所有个人身份信息（PII）进行脱敏处理。 授予状态机任务在生产账户的 KMS 密钥上解密的权限。授予状态机任务在开发账户的 KMS 密钥 上加密的权限。","B":"在生产 S3 存储桶和开发 S3 存储桶之间设置 S3 复制。在开发 S3 存储桶上激活 Amazon Macie。创建一 个 AWS Step Functions 状态机，用于启动发现任务，并在文件复制到开发 S3 存储桶时对所有个人身 份信息（PII）进行脱敏处理。授予状态机任务在开发账户中的 KMS 密钥上进行加密和解密的权限。","C":"设置一个 S3 批量操作任务，将文件从生产 S3 存储桶复制到开发 S3 存储桶。在开发账户中，配置一 个 AWS Lambda 函数来删除所有 PII（个人身份信息）。配置 S3 对象 Lambda 使用该 Lambda 函数 处理 S3 GET 请求。授予 Lambda 函数的 IAM 角色在开发账户中的 KMS 密钥上进行加密和解密的权 限。","D":"在开发账户中根据 CloudFormation 模板创建开发环境。安排一条 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每周启 动一次 AWS Step Functions 状态机。","E":"在开发账户中根据 CloudFormation 模板创建开发环境。在 Amazon EC2 实例上安排一个每周运行一次 的 cron 作业来启动 S3 批量操作作业。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The decisive fact is that Amazon Macie only DISCOVERS sensitive data and generates findings/reports about where PII resides; it has no capability to redact, mask, or anonymize object content. The Macie docs describe it as creating findings to notify you, never modifying data. Therefore options A and B, which both claim a Step Functions state machine will 'initiate a discovery job and redact all PII,' describe a capability that does not exist and are technically invalid. The AWS-documented pattern for redacting PII on read is S3 Object Lambda with a Lambda redaction function (the S3 Object Lambda redact-PII tutorial). Option C uses S3 Batch Operations Copy (which officially supports copying to a destination bucket in a different account) to move data through the Object Lambda redaction path, writing redacted output to the dev bucket encrypted with the dev account's own KMS customer-managed key (Lambda role gets encrypt/decrypt on the dev key). That satisfies both 'anonymize PII before moving it' and 'different KMS keys per environment.' Option E is the correct orchestration partner for C: it creates the dev environment from the CloudFormation template and schedules a weekly job that starts the S3 Batch Operations job that C defined. Option D references 'the AWS Step Functions state machine,' which only exists in the broken A/B options, so it cannot pair with C. The genuinely correct, internally consistent pair is C + E.","explanation_zh":"決定性事實是 Amazon Macie 只能「探索 (discover)」敏感資料並產生 findings/報告，指出 PII 所在位置；它沒有任何能力可以 redact、遮罩或匿名化物件內容。Macie 文件一律描述它「建立 finding 來通知你」，從不修改資料。因此選項 A 與 B 都聲稱 Step Functions state machine 會「啟動 discovery job 並 redact 所有 PII」，描述的是不存在的能力，技術上無效。AWS 官方記載在讀取時 redact PII 的模式是 S3 Object Lambda 搭配 Lambda redaction function（即 S3 Object Lambda redact-PII 教學）。選項 C 使用 S3 Batch Operations Copy（官方支援複製到不同帳號的目的儲存貯體），讓資料經過 Object Lambda redaction 路徑，將 redact 後的輸出寫入 dev 貯體並以 dev 帳號自己的 KMS customer-managed key 加密（Lambda 角色取得 dev key 的 encrypt/decrypt 權限）。這同時滿足「移動前先匿名化 PII」與「各環境使用不同 KMS key」。選項 E 是 C 正確的編排搭配：它從 CloudFormation 範本建立 dev 環境，並排程每週啟動 C 所定義的 S3 Batch Operations job。選項 D 提到「the AWS Step Functions state machine」，那只存在於有缺陷的 A/B 選項中，因此無法與 C 搭配。真正正確且彼此一致的組合是 C + E。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Macie cannot redact or anonymize PII; it only discovers sensitive data and produces findings/reports. A Step Functions task cannot make a Macie discovery job 'redact all PII' because no such operation exists, so this is technically impossible.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 無法 redact 或匿名化 PII；它只會探索敏感資料並產生 findings/報告。Step Functions 任務無法讓 Macie discovery job「redact 所有 PII」，因為根本沒有這種操作，技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A: Macie does not redact data. Additionally, setting up S3 replication would copy PII into the development account before any redaction, violating the requirement not to move PII without anonymizing it first, and replication does not re-encrypt with a different per-environment KMS key by transforming content.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的致命缺陷：Macie 不會 redact 資料。此外，設定 S3 replication 會在任何 redaction 之前就把 PII 複製到開發帳號，違反「未先匿名化不得移動 PII」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"D schedules 'the AWS Step Functions state machine,' but that state machine only exists in options A and B, which are technically invalid (Macie cannot redact). C uses an S3 Batch Operations job, not a Step Functions state machine, so D is not a coherent partner for the only valid copy/redaction option.","why_zh":"D 排程「the AWS Step Functions state machine」，但該 state machine 只存在於技術上無效的 A、B 選項中（Macie 無法 redact）。C 使用的是 S3 Batch Operations job 而非 Step Functions state machine，因此 D 無法與唯一有效的複製/redaction 選項搭配。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/tutorial-s3-object-lambda-redact-pii.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/batch-ops-examples-copy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/olap-use.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/specify-batchjob-manifest-xaccount-inventory.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":242,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster to host its machine learning (ML) application. As the ML model and the container image size grow, the time that new pods take to start up has increased to several minutes. A DevOps engineer needs to reduce the startup time to seconds. The solution must also reduce the startup time to seconds when the pod runs on nodes that were recently added to the cluster. The DevOps engineer creates an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an automation in AWS Systems Manager. The automation prefetches the container images from an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository when new images are pushed to the repository. The DevOps engineer also configures tags to be applied to the cluster and the node groups. What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群来托管其机器学习（ML）应用程序。随 着 ML 模型和容器镜像大小的增加，新 Pod 启动所需的时间已增加到数分钟。 一名 DevOps 工程师需要将启动时间缩短至数秒。该解决方案还必须减少 启动时间至 当 Pod 在最近添加到集群的节点上运行时，可能会出现几秒钟的延迟。 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则会调用 AWS Systems Manager 中的自动化操 作。当有新的容器镜像被推送到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库时，该自动化操 作会预先获取这些容器镜像。DevOps 工程师还配置了要应用于集群和节点组的标签。 为了满足要求，开发运维工程师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows EventBridge to use Systems Manager to run commands in the EKS cluster's control plane nodes. Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that uses the control plane nodes' tags to prefetch corresponding container images.","B":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows EventBridge to use Systems Manager to run commands in the EKS cluster's nodes. Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that uses the nodes' machine size to prefetch corresponding container images.","C":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows EventBridge to use Systems Manager to run commands in the EKS cluster's nodes. Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that uses the nodes' tags to prefetch corresponding container images.","D":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows EventBridge to use Systems Manager to run commands in the EKS cluster's control plane nodes. Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that uses the nodes' tags to prefetch corresponding container images."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 EventBridge 使用 Systems Manager 在 EKS 集群的控 制平面节点上运行命令。创建一个 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联，该关联使用控制平面节点 的标签来预取相应的容器镜像。","B":"创建一个具有策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 EventBridge 使用 Systems Manager 在 EKS 集群的节点上 运行命令。创建一个 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联，该关联根据节点的机器大小预取相应的容 器镜像。","C":"创建一个具有策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 EventBridge 使用 Systems Manager 在 EKS 集群的节点上 运行命令。创建一个 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联，该关联使用节点的标签来预取相应的容器 镜像。","D":"创建一个具有策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 EventBridge 使用 Systems Manager 在 EKS 集群的控 制平面节点上运行命令。创建一个 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联，该关联使用节点的标签来 预取相应的容器镜像。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Container images must be prefetched onto the EKS worker nodes, because pods are scheduled and their container runtime (containerd) caches images on the worker EC2 instances, not on the control plane. In Amazon EKS the control plane is fully AWS-managed and customers cannot install SSM Agent on or run Run Command/Systems Manager commands against control plane nodes, so any option naming the control plane is invalid. State Manager associations target managed nodes by tags, node IDs, or AWS Resource Groups; the engineer already configured tags on the cluster and node groups, so the association should use the worker nodes' tags to prefetch the corresponding images. Option C is the only choice that both runs commands on the cluster's (worker) nodes and targets them by tags, which also covers newly added nodes since their tags match the association.","explanation_zh":"容器映像必須預先抓取（prefetch）到 EKS 的工作節點（worker nodes）上，因為 Pod 是被排程到工作節點的 EC2 執行個體上，容器執行階段（containerd）也是在這些工作節點上快取映像，而不是在控制平面上。在 Amazon EKS 中，控制平面完全由 AWS 託管，客戶無法在控制平面節點上安裝 SSM Agent 或執行 Run Command / Systems Manager 指令，因此任何指向控制平面（control plane nodes）的選項都不成立。State Manager 關聯（association）可透過標籤（tags）、節點 ID 或 AWS Resource Groups 來鎖定受管節點；題目中工程師已經在叢集與節點群組上設定了標籤，因此關聯應使用工作節點的標籤來預先抓取對應的映像。選項 C 是唯一同時在叢集（工作）節點上執行指令並以標籤鎖定它們的選項，且因新加入的節點標籤相符，也能涵蓋新節點的情境。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Targets the EKS control plane nodes, which are fully AWS-managed and cannot run SSM Run Command; images are also never cached there, so prefetching on control plane nodes is impossible and useless.","why_zh":"鎖定 EKS 控制平面節點，但控制平面由 AWS 完全託管，無法執行 SSM Run Command，且映像也不會快取在那裡，因此在控制平面上預抓映像既不可能也無意義。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Runs on the correct (worker) nodes but targets by 'machine size' instead of tags. State Manager associations target by tags, node IDs, or Resource Groups, not by instance size; this also ignores the tags the engineer already configured and would not reliably map images to nodes.","why_zh":"雖在正確的工作節點上執行，但以「機器大小（machine size）」而非標籤鎖定。State Manager 關聯是以標籤、節點 ID 或 Resource Groups 鎖定，而非執行個體大小；此選項也忽略了工程師已設定的標籤，無法可靠地將映像對應到節點。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Says to run commands on the control plane nodes (AWS-managed, inaccessible for Run Command and not where images are cached), even though it then mentions the nodes' tags. The execution target is wrong, so prefetching cannot occur.","why_zh":"指定在控制平面節點上執行指令（由 AWS 託管、無法使用 Run Command，也非映像快取所在），即使後面提到節點標籤，執行目標仍然錯誤，因此無法完成預抓映像。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-state.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/eks-compute.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/run-command.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":243,"question_en":"A company's application has an API that retrieves workload metrics. The company needs to audit, analyze, and visualize these metrics from the application to detect issues at scale. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序有一个 API，用于获取工作负载指标。该公司需要对这些指标进行审计、分析和可视化， 以便大规模地检测问题。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge schedule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls the API to retrieve workload metrics. Store the workload metric data in an Amazon S3 bucket.","B":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge schedule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls the API to retrieve workload metrics. Store the workload metric data in an Amazon DynamoDB table that has a DynamoDB stream enabled.","C":"Create an AWS Glue crawler to catalog the workload metric data in the Amazon S3 bucket. Create views in Amazon Athena for the cataloged data.","D":"Connect an AWS Glue crawler to the Amazon DynamoDB stream to catalog the workload metric data. Create views in Amazon Athena for the cataloged data.","E":"Create Amazon QuickSight datasets from the Amazon Athena views. Create a QuickSight analysis to visualize the workload metric data as a dashboard.","F":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard that has custom widgets that invoke AWS Lambda functions. Configure the Lambda functions to query the workload metrics data from the Amazon Athena views."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 计划，以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会调用 API 来获取工作负 载指标。将工作负载指标数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。","B":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 计划，以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会调用 API 来获取工作负 载指标。将工作负载指标数据存储在启用了 DynamoDB 流的 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。","C":"创建一个 AWS Glue 爬虫来对 Amazon S3 存储桶中的工作负载指标数据进行编目。在 Amazon Athena 中为编目的数据创建视图。","D":"将 AWS Glue 爬虫连接到 Amazon DynamoDB 流，以对工作负载指标数据进行编目。在 Amazon Athena 中为编目的数据创建视图。","E":"从 Amazon Athena 视图创建 Amazon QuickSight 数据集。创建一个 QuickSight 分析，将工作负载指标数 据可视化为仪表板。","F":"创建一个包含自定义小部件的 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板，这些小部件可调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配 置 Lambda 函数以从 Amazon Athena 视图中查询工作负载指标数据。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to audit, analyze, and visualize API workload metrics at scale, which maps to the canonical S3 data-lake analytics pattern: ingest -> catalog/query -> visualize. A handles ingestion: an EventBridge schedule invokes a Lambda function that calls the API and stores the metrics durably in Amazon S3. C handles cataloging and querying: an AWS Glue crawler catalogs the S3 data into the Glue Data Catalog, and Athena views are created over it. E handles visualization at scale: QuickSight creates datasets from the Athena views and a QuickSight analysis renders a dashboard. The decisive technical fact eliminating the DynamoDB-stream path (B + D) is that AWS Glue crawlers do not support data streams. The Glue documentation explicitly states 'Currently AWS Glue does not support crawlers for data streams,' so option D (connect a Glue crawler to a DynamoDB stream) is technically impossible, and B exists only to feed D.","explanation_zh":"需求是大規模地稽核、分析與視覺化 API 工作負載指標,對應到標準的 S3 資料湖分析模式:擷取 -> 編目/查詢 -> 視覺化。A 負責擷取:EventBridge 排程觸發 Lambda 呼叫 API,並將指標持久化存到 Amazon S3。C 負責編目與查詢:AWS Glue crawler 將 S3 資料編目到 Glue Data Catalog,並在其上建立 Athena views。E 負責大規模視覺化:QuickSight 從 Athena views 建立 dataset,並以 QuickSight analysis 呈現 dashboard。排除 DynamoDB stream 路徑(B + D)的關鍵技術事實是:AWS Glue crawler 不支援資料串流。Glue 文件明確指出 'Currently AWS Glue does not support crawlers for data streams',因此 D(將 Glue crawler 連到 DynamoDB stream)技術上不可行,而 B 僅是為了餵給 D 而存在。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Storing metrics in a DynamoDB table with a stream only makes sense as input to option D's stream crawling, which is impossible. DynamoDB streams capture item-level changes for event-driven processing, not for batch cataloging/analytics, and there is no Athena/Glue path from a stream.","why_zh":"將指標存入啟用 stream 的 DynamoDB table 只有在搭配 D 的 stream 編目時才合理,而 D 不可行。DynamoDB streams 用於捕捉項目層級變更以做事件驅動處理,並非用於批次編目/分析,且 stream 沒有通往 Athena/Glue 的路徑。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Glue crawlers cannot crawl data streams. The Glue docs explicitly state 'Currently AWS Glue does not support crawlers for data streams.' A crawler can crawl a DynamoDB table but not a DynamoDB stream, so this step is technically impossible.","why_zh":"AWS Glue crawler 無法編目資料串流。Glue 文件明確指出 'Currently AWS Glue does not support crawlers for data streams'。crawler 可以編目 DynamoDB table,但無法編目 DynamoDB stream,因此此步驟技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Using a CloudWatch dashboard with custom widgets that invoke Lambda functions to query Athena is a convoluted, high-overhead way to visualize query results and competes with the purpose-built option E. QuickSight is the documented, native tool for visualizing Athena data at scale, so F is the inferior/incorrect visualization choice.","why_zh":"使用 CloudWatch dashboard 的自訂 widget 觸發 Lambda 去查詢 Athena,是迂迴且高維運成本的視覺化方式,且與專為此設計的 E 競爭。QuickSight 才是用於大規模視覺化 Athena 資料的官方原生工具,因此 F 是較差/不正確的視覺化選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/crawler-data-stores.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/add-crawler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/data-sources-glue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/quick/latest/userguide/create-a-data-set-athena.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":244,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building the infrastructure for an application. The application needs to run on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster that includes Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances need to use an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system as a storage backend. The Amazon EFS Container Storage Interface (CSI) driver is installed on the EKS cluster. When the DevOps engineer starts the application, the EC2 instances do not mount the EFS file system. Which solutions will fix the problem? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一个应用程序构建基础设施。该应用程序需要在包含亚马逊 EC2 实例的亚马逊弹 性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群上运行。EC2 实例需要使用亚马逊弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS）文 件系统作为存储后端。Amazon EFS 容器存储接口（CSI）驱动程序已安装在 EKS 集群上。 当开发运维工程师启动应用程序时，EC2 实例未挂载 EFS 文件系统。 哪些解决方案能解决问题？（选择三个。）","options_en":{"A":"Switch the EKS nodes from Amazon EC2 to AWS Fargate.","B":"Add an inbound rule to the EFS file system’s security group to allow NFS traffic from the EKS cluster.","C":"Create an IAM role that allows the Amazon EFS CSI driver to interact with the file system","D":"Set up AWS DataSync to configure file transfer between the EFS file system and the EKS nodes.","E":"Create a mount target for the EFS file system in the subnet of the EKS nodes.","F":"Disable encryption or the EFS file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 EKS 节点从亚马逊 EC2 切换到 AWS Fargate。","B":"向 EFS 文件系统的安全组添加一条入站规则，以允许来自 EKS 集群的 NFS 流量。","C":"创建一个 IAM 角色，使 Amazon EFS CSI 驱动程序能够与文件系统进行交互","D":"设置 AWS DataSync 以配置 EFS 文件系统与 EKS 节点之间的文件传输。","E":"在 EKS 节点所在的子网中为 EFS 文件系统创建挂载目标。","F":"禁用加密或 EFS 文件系统。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Mounting Amazon EFS on EKS EC2 worker nodes via the EFS CSI driver requires three things, all confirmed by AWS docs. (E) An EFS mount target must exist in the node's VPC/Availability Zone subnet: 'To access an EFS file system in a VPC, you need to create mount targets,' and an NFSv4.1 client can only mount if it can reach the NFS port (TCP 2049) of one of the file system's mount targets. (B) The mount target's security group must have an inbound rule allowing NFS port 2049 from the EC2 instances; without this inbound rule the TCP 2049 connection is blocked and the mount fails. (C) The EFS CSI driver itself 'requires IAM permissions to interact with your file system' - you create an IAM role and attach the AmazonEFSCSIDriverPolicy managed policy (via Pod Identity or IRSA). Together these are the standard prerequisites whose absence causes the 'instances do not mount the EFS file system' symptom.","explanation_zh":"在 EKS 的 EC2 工作節點上透過 Amazon EFS CSI driver 掛載 EFS，需要三項條件，皆有 AWS 官方文件佐證。(E) 必須在節點所在 VPC/可用區的子網中建立 EFS mount target：'要在 VPC 中存取 EFS 檔案系統，必須建立 mount target'，且 NFSv4.1 用戶端唯有能連到某個 mount target 的 NFS port (TCP 2049) 才能掛載。(B) mount target 的 security group 必須有允許來自 EC2 instance 的 NFS port 2049 入站規則；若缺此規則，TCP 2049 連線會被擋而掛載失敗。(C) EFS CSI driver 本身 '需要 IAM 權限才能與檔案系統互動'，須建立 IAM role 並附加 AmazonEFSCSIDriverPolicy 受管政策（透過 Pod Identity 或 IRSA）。這些是標準先決條件，缺少任一項都會導致 'instance 無法掛載 EFS' 的症狀。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Switching EKS nodes from EC2 to Fargate is a major architecture change that contradicts the stated requirement to run on EC2 instances, and it does not fix the underlying mount misconfiguration (mount target, security group, IAM). It is not a remediation step.","why_zh":"把 EKS 節點從 EC2 改成 Fargate 是重大架構變更，與題目要求在 EC2 上執行相牴觸，也沒解決掛載設定問題（mount target、security group、IAM），並非修正方式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS DataSync is a data-transfer/migration service that copies files between storage systems; it does not mount a file system into pods and cannot replace the EFS CSI driver's mount mechanism.","why_zh":"AWS DataSync 是資料傳輸/遷移服務，用於在儲存系統間複製檔案；它不會把檔案系統掛載到 pod，也無法取代 EFS CSI driver 的掛載機制。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"EFS encryption at rest is transparent to NFS clients and has no effect on the ability to mount the file system; disabling it would not fix a mount failure (and can't be disabled after creation anyway).","why_zh":"EFS 靜態加密對 NFS 用戶端是透明的，不影響檔案系統掛載能力；停用它無法解決掛載失敗（且建立後也無法停用）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/efs-csi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/network-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/manage-fs-access-create-delete-mount-targets.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":245,"question_en":"A company deploys an application on on-premises devices in the company’s on-premises data center. The company uses an AWS Direct Connect connection between the data center and the company's AWS account. During initial setup of the on-premises devices and during application updates, the application needs to retrieve configuration files from an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. All traffic from the on-premises devices to Amazon EFS must remain private and encrypted. The on- premises devices must follow the principle of least privilege for AWS access. The company's DevOps team needs the ability to revoke access from a single device without affecting the access of the other devices. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在其本地数据中心的本地设备上部署了一个应用程序。该公司在本地数据中心和其 AWS 账户之间 使用了 AWS Direct Connect 连接。在本地设备的初始设置期间以及应用程序更新期间，该应用程序需要从 Amazon Elastic File System（Amazon EFS）文件系统中获取配置文件。 从本地设备到 Amazon EFS 的所有流量都必须保持私密并加密。本地设备访问 AWS 时必须遵循最小权限原 则。公司的 DevOps 团队需要能够撤销单个设备的访问权限，而不影响其他设备的访问权限。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM user that has an access key and a secret key for each device. Attach the AmazonElasticFileSystemFullAccess policy to all IAM users. Configure the AWS CLI on the on- premises devices to use the IAM user's access key and secret key.","B":"Generate certificates for each on-premises device in AWS Private Certificate Authority. Create a trust anchor in IAM Roles Anywhere that references an AWS Private CA. Create an IAM role that trust IAM Roles Anywhere. Attach the AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess to the role. Create an IAM Roles Anywhere profile for the IAM role. Configure the AWS CLI on the on-premises devices to use the aws_signing_helper command to obtain credentials.","C":"Create an IAM user that has an access key and a secret key for all devices. Attach the AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess policy to the IAM user. Configure the AWS CLI on the on-premises devices to use the IAM user's access key and secret key.","D":"Use the amazon-efs-utils package to mount the EFS file system.","E":"Use the native Linux NFS client to mount the EFS file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个设备创建一个具有访问密钥和秘密密钥的 IAM 用户。将 AmazonElasticFileSystemFullAcces s 策略附加到所有 IAM 用户。在本地设备上配置 AWS CLI 以使用 IAM 用户的访问密钥和秘密 密钥。","B":"在 AWS 私有证书颁发机构中为每个本地设备生成证书。在 IAM Roles Anywhere 中创建一个引用 AWS 私有 CA 的信任锚。创建一个信任 IAM Roles Anywhere 的 IAM 角色。将 AmazonElasticFileSystemClie ntReadWriteAccess 附加到该角色。为该 IAM 角色创建一个 IAM Roles Anywhere 配置文件。在本地设 备上配置 AWS CLI，使用 aws_signing_helper 命令获取凭证。","C":"创建一个具有访问密钥和秘密密钥的 IAM 用户，供所有设备使用。将 AmazonElasticFileSystemClientR eadWriteAccess 策略附加到该 IAM 用户。在本地设备上配置 AWS CLI，使其使用该 IAM 用户的访 问密钥和秘密密钥。","D":"使用 amazon-efs-utils 软件包挂载 EFS 文件系统。","E":"使用原生的 Linux NFS 客户端挂载 EFS 文件系统。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are private+encrypted EFS traffic, least-privilege AWS access, and the ability to revoke a single device without affecting others. Option B (IAM Roles Anywhere with an AWS Private CA trust anchor, a role trusting Roles Anywhere with the AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess managed policy, a profile, and aws_signing_helper) delivers per-device X.509 certificates that exchange for temporary credentials, satisfies least privilege via the scoped EFS client policy, and lets the team revoke one device's certificate (via a CRL) without touching the others. Option D (amazon-efs-utils) is required for encryption in transit: the EFS mount helper establishes a TLS connection via efs-proxy/stunnel so all NFS traffic is encrypted, while Direct Connect keeps it private. A plain native NFS mount (E) is unencrypted unless stunnel is configured manually, so it fails the encryption requirement. IAM user options (A, C) use long-term static keys; A also grants FullAccess (not least privilege), and C shares one credential across all devices, making single-device revocation impossible.","explanation_zh":"需求為：到 EFS 的流量必須私有且加密、AWS 存取需最小權限、且能在不影響其他裝置的情況下撤銷單一裝置。選項 B（以 AWS Private CA 作為 IAM Roles Anywhere 的 trust anchor、建立信任 Roles Anywhere 並附掛 AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess 的 IAM role、建立 profile、並用 aws_signing_helper 取得憑證）為每台裝置發放各自的 X.509 憑證以換取臨時憑證，透過範圍化的 EFS client 政策達成最小權限，並可藉由 CRL 撤銷單一裝置憑證而不影響其他裝置。選項 D（amazon-efs-utils）是傳輸加密所必需：EFS mount helper 透過 efs-proxy/stunnel 建立 TLS 連線使所有 NFS 流量加密，而 Direct Connect 維持私有性。原生 NFS 掛載（E）除非手動設定 stunnel 否則不加密，因此不符加密需求。IAM user 選項（A、C）使用長期靜態金鑰；A 還授予 FullAccess（非最小權限），C 則所有裝置共用同一組憑證，無法撤銷單一裝置。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses long-term static access/secret keys (not best practice for external workloads) and attaches AmazonElasticFileSystemFullAccess, which violates least privilege.","why_zh":"使用長期靜態存取金鑰（外部工作負載不建議），且附掛 AmazonElasticFileSystemFullAccess，違反最小權限原則。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A single shared IAM user/credential across all devices means revoking it would cut off every device at once, so you cannot revoke a single device without affecting others; also long-term keys.","why_zh":"所有裝置共用單一 IAM user/憑證，撤銷時會一次切斷所有裝置，無法只撤銷單一裝置而不影響其他裝置；且為長期金鑰。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"The native Linux NFS client mounts EFS without encryption in transit by default; encryption requires the EFS mount helper (amazon-efs-utils) or manual stunnel setup, so this alone fails the encrypted-traffic requirement.","why_zh":"原生 Linux NFS client 預設掛載 EFS 不提供傳輸加密；加密需透過 EFS mount helper（amazon-efs-utils）或手動設定 stunnel，因此單靠此選項不符加密需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/encryption-in-transit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/using-amazon-efs-utils.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-rolesanywhere-crl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/iam-roles-anywhere-private-ca.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":246,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is setting up an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) blue/green deployment for an application by using AWS CodeDeploy and AWS CloudFormation. During the deployment window, the application must be highly available and CodeDeploy must shift 10% of traffic to a new version of the application every minute until all traffic is shifted. Which configuration should the DevOps engineer add in the CloudFormation template to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 和 AWS CloudFormation 为一个应用程序设置 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）蓝/绿部署。在部署窗口期间，应用程序必须保持高可用性，并且 CodeDeploy 每分钟必须将 10% 的流量切换到应用程序的新版本，直到所有流量都切换完成。 DevOps 工程师应在 CloudFormation 模板中添加哪种配置才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add an AppSpec file with the CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEverylMinutes deployment configuration.","B":"Add the AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform and the AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook parameter with the CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery1Minutes deployment configuration.","C":"Add an AppSpec file with the ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes deployment configuration.","D":"Add the AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform and the AWS::CodeDepioy::BlueGreen hook parameter with the ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes deployment configuration."},"options_zh":{"A":"添加一个 AppSpec 文件，并使用 CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEverylMinutes 部署配置。 BCodeDeployBlueGreen 转换以及带有 CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery1Minutes 部署配置的 AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen 挂钩参数。","C":"添加一个包含 ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes 部署配置的 AppSpec 文件。 DCodeDeployBlueGreen 转换以及带有 ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes 部署CodeDeploy::BlueGreen 钩子参数。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application is deployed via AWS CloudFormation, so the CloudFormation-native mechanism for an ECS blue/green deployment through CodeDeploy must be used: add the AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform plus an AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook to the template. The requirement to shift 10% of traffic every minute until all traffic is shifted is a linear pattern, which matches CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery1Minutes ('Shifts 10 percent of traffic every minute until all traffic is shifted'). The canary option (ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes) shifts 10% and then the remaining 90% all at once five minutes later, which does not match. Therefore B is the only option that combines the correct CloudFormation transform/hook approach with the correct linear traffic-shifting behavior. (Note: in the hook the configuration is expressed via TrafficRoutingConfig/TimeBasedLinear, but among the four options B is the only one pairing the right CloudFormation method with the right 10%/1-minute linear behavior.)","explanation_zh":"本題應用程式是透過 AWS CloudFormation 部署，因此必須使用 CloudFormation 原生的 ECS blue/green (透過 CodeDeploy) 機制：在範本中加入 AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform 以及 AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook。需求是每分鐘轉移 10% 流量直到全部轉移完成，這是線性 (linear) 模式，對應 CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery1Minutes（每分鐘轉移 10% 流量直到全部轉移）。Canary 選項 (ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes) 是先轉移 10%，五分鐘後再一次轉移剩餘 90%，不符合需求。因此 B 是唯一同時具備正確 CloudFormation transform/hook 方法與正確線性流量轉移行為的選項。（註：hook 中實際是用 TrafficRoutingConfig/TimeBasedLinear 表達，但四個選項中只有 B 同時搭配正確的 CloudFormation 方法與 10%/每分鐘的線性行為。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The deployment config name is correct, but it specifies an AppSpec file rather than the CloudFormation transform + hook. The question states CloudFormation is used and asks what to add 'in the CloudFormation template'; CloudFormation-managed ECS blue/green deployments use the AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform and AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook, not a deployment config named inside an AppSpec file (an AppSpec references the task definition, not a CodeDeployDefault config string).","why_zh":"部署設定名稱正確，但它用的是 AppSpec 檔，而非 CloudFormation transform + hook。題目明確說使用 CloudFormation，並問要在 CloudFormation 範本中加入什麼；CloudFormation 管理的 ECS blue/green 部署使用 AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform 與 AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook，而非在 AppSpec 檔中指定部署設定名稱（AppSpec 參考的是 task definition，不是 CodeDeployDefault 設定字串）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses the canary configuration ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes, which shifts 10% then the remaining 90% all at once after 5 minutes - not 10% every minute. It also uses an AppSpec file rather than the CloudFormation transform/hook, and the name is missing the CodeDeployDefault prefix.","why_zh":"使用 canary 設定 ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes，先轉移 10%，5 分鐘後再一次轉移剩餘 90%，不是每分鐘 10%。且使用 AppSpec 檔而非 CloudFormation transform/hook，名稱也缺少 CodeDeployDefault 前綴。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses the correct CloudFormation transform + hook approach, but pairs it with the canary configuration ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes, which does not shift 10% every minute. The traffic-shifting behavior does not meet the stated requirement.","why_zh":"雖然使用了正確的 CloudFormation transform + hook 方法，但搭配的是 canary 設定 ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes，並非每分鐘轉移 10%，流量轉移行為不符合需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/about-blue-green-deployments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/blue-green-hook-syntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/transform-aws-codedeploybluegreen.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":247,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company's DevOps team has developed an AWS Lambda function that calls the Organizations API to create new AWS accounts. The Lambda function runs in the organization's management account. The DevOps team needs to move the Lambda function from the management account to a dedicated AWS account. The DevOps team must ensure that the Lambda function has the ability to create new AWS accounts only in Organizations before the team deploys the Lambda function to the new account. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司的 DevOps 团队开发了一个 AWS Lambda 函数， 该函数调用 Organizations API 来创建新的 AWS 账户。 Lambda 函数在组织的管理账户中运行。DevOps 团队需要将该 Lambda 函数从管理账户迁移到一个专用 的 AWS 账户。在团队将 Lambda 函数部署到新账户之前，DevOps 团队必须确保该 Lambda 函数仅能在 Organizations 中创建新的 AWS 账户。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the management account, create a new IAM role that has the necessary permission to create new accounts in Organizations. Allow the role to be assumed by the Lambda execution role in the new AWS account. Update the Lambda function code to assume the role when the Lambda function creates new AWS accounts. Update the Lambda execution role to ensure that it has permission to assume the new role.","B":"In the management account, turn on delegated administration for Organizations. Create a new delegation policy that grants the new AWS account permission to create new AWS accounts in Organizations. Ensure that the Lambda execution role has the organizations:CreateAccount permission.","C":"In the management account, create a new IAM role that has the necessary permission to create new accounts in Organizations. Allow the role to be assumed by the Lambda service principal. Update the Lambda function code to assume the role when the Lambda function creates new AWS accounts. Update the Lambda execution role to ensure that it has permission to assume the new role.","D":"In the management account, enable AWS Control Tower. Turn on delegated administration for AWS Control Tower. Create a resource policy that allows the new AWS account to create new AWS accounts in AWS Control Tower. Update the Lambda function code to use the AWS Control Tower API in the new AWS account. Ensure that the Lambda execution role has the controltower:CreateManagedAccount permission."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中，创建一个具有在 Organizations 中创建新账户所需权限的新 IAM 角色。允许该角色由新 AWS 账户中的 Lambda 执行角色进行承担。更新 Lambda 函数代码，使其在创建新 AWS 账户时承担 该角色。更新 Lambda 执行角色，确保其具有承担新角色的权限。","B":"在管理控制台中，为组织启用委托管理功能。创建一个新的委托策略，授予新的 AWS 账户在 组织中创建新 AWS 账户的权限。确保 Lambda 执行角色具有 organizations:CreateAccount 权 限。","C":"在管理账户中，创建一个具有在 Organizations 中创建新账户所需权限的新 IAM 角色。允许 Lambda 服务主体承担该角色。更新 Lambda 函数代码，使其在创建新的 AWS 账户时承担该角色。更新 Lambda 执行角色，确保其具有承担新角色的权限。","D":"在管理账户中启用 AWS Control Tower。为 AWS Control Tower 启用委托管理。创建一个资源策略， 允许新 AWS 账户在 AWS Control Tower 中创建新的 AWS 账户。更新 Lambda 函数代码，使其在新 AWS 账户中使用 AWS Control Tower API。确保 Lambda 执行角色具有 controltower: CreateManagedAccount 权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The organizations:CreateAccount action can be called ONLY from the organization's management account; AWS explicitly lists CreateAccount under 'Operations you can call from only the organization's management account.' Therefore a Lambda function that has been moved to a dedicated member account cannot call CreateAccount with its own local execution role. The correct pattern is to create an IAM role in the management account with the CreateAccount permission and a trust policy that names the assuming cross-account IAM principal (the Lambda execution role ARN in the new account), grant that execution role sts:AssumeRole, and have the function assume the management-account role before calling CreateAccount. Option A describes exactly this cross-account role-as-proxy delegation, where the trust policy allows the Lambda execution role in the new account to assume the role.","explanation_zh":"organizations:CreateAccount 動作只能從組織的 management account 呼叫；AWS 文件明確將 CreateAccount 列在「Operations you can call from only the organization's management account」之下。因此搬到專用 member account 的 Lambda 函式無法用自己本地的 execution role 直接呼叫 CreateAccount。正確做法是在 management account 建立一個具有 CreateAccount 權限的 IAM role,其 trust policy 指名跨帳號的 IAM principal(新帳號中 Lambda execution role 的 ARN),並賦予該 execution role sts:AssumeRole 權限,讓函式在呼叫 CreateAccount 前先 assume 此 management-account role。選項 A 正是描述這種跨帳號 role-as-proxy 委派,trust policy 允許新帳號中的 Lambda execution role 來 assume 該 role。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CreateAccount cannot be called by a delegated administrator. AWS lists CreateAccount only under management-account-only operations, and it is NOT among the operations a delegated administrator may call. There is also no 'delegation policy' construct that grants an account the CreateAccount permission; delegated administration is enabled per service via RegisterDelegatedAdministrator, not via a policy granting account creation.","why_zh":"CreateAccount 無法由 delegated administrator 呼叫。AWS 將 CreateAccount 只列在 management-account-only 的操作清單中,並不在 delegated administrator 可呼叫的操作之列。此外也沒有所謂的「delegation policy」可以授予某帳號 CreateAccount 權限;delegated administration 是透過 RegisterDelegatedAdministrator 依服務啟用,而非用一個授予建立帳號的 policy。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A cross-account trust policy must name the assuming IAM principal (the Lambda execution role / account ARN), not the Lambda service principal (lambda.amazonaws.com). The service principal trust is used for the execution role itself within the function's own account; at runtime the AssumeRole call is made with the execution role's credentials, so trusting only lambda.amazonaws.com does not authorize the cross-account function to assume the management-account role.","why_zh":"跨帳號 trust policy 必須指名執行 assume 的 IAM principal(Lambda execution role / 帳號 ARN),而非 Lambda service principal(lambda.amazonaws.com)。service principal 的信任是用在函式自身帳號內的 execution role;執行期的 AssumeRole 呼叫是用 execution role 的憑證發出,因此只信任 lambda.amazonaws.com 並無法授權跨帳號的函式去 assume management-account 的 role。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no controltower:CreateManagedAccount permission or resource policy that lets another account create accounts. Control Tower provisions accounts via Account Factory (Service Catalog product and the AWSControlTowerExecution role), not a CreateManagedAccount API. The requirement is also specifically to create accounts in Organizations (the Organizations API), so introducing Control Tower is both fabricated and off-scope.","why_zh":"並不存在 controltower:CreateManagedAccount 權限或可讓其他帳號建立帳號的 resource policy。Control Tower 透過 Account Factory(Service Catalog 產品與 AWSControlTowerExecution role)佈建帳號,而非 CreateManagedAccount API。需求也明確是要在 Organizations(Organizations API)建立帳號,因此引入 Control Tower 既屬虛構也超出範圍。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_reference_actions-by-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/APIReference/API_CreateAccount.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies-cross-account-resource-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/account-factory.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":248,"question_en":"A company has deployed an application in a single AWS Region. The application backend uses Amazon DynamoDB tables and Amazon S3 buckets. The company wants to deploy the application in a secondary Region. The company must ensure that the data in the DynamoDB tables and the S3 buckets persists across both Regions. The data must also immediately propagate across Regions. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司已在单个 AWS 区域部署了一个应用程序。该应用程序的后端使用了 Amazon DynamoDB 表和 Amazon S3 存储桶。 该公司希望在辅助区域部署应用程序。公司必须确保 DynamoDB 表和 S3 存储桶中的数据在两个区域都 能持久保存。数据还必须立即在两个区域之间同步传播。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Implement two-way S3 bucket replication between the primary Region's S3 buckets and the secondary Region’s S3 buckets. Convert the DynamoDB tables into global tables. Set the secondary Region as the additional Region.","B":"Implement S3 Batch Operations copy jobs between the primary Region and the secondary Region for all S3 buckets. Convert the DynamoDB tables into global tables. Set the secondary Region as the additional Region.","C":"Implement two-way S3 bucket replication between the primary Region's S3 buckets and the secondary Region's S3 buckets. Enable DynamoDB streams on the DynamoDB tables in both Regions. In each Region, create an AWS Lambda function that subscribes to the DynamoDB streams. Configure the Lambda function to copy new records to the DynamoDB tables in the other Region.","D":"Implement S3 Batch Operations copy jobs between the primary Region and the secondary Region for all S3 buckets. Enable DynamoDB streams on the DynamoDB tables in both Regions. In each Region, create an AWS Lambda function that subscribes to the DynamoDB streams. Configure the Lambda function to copy new records to the DynamoDB tables in the other Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在主区域的 S3 存储桶与辅助区域的 S3 存储桶之间实现双向复制。将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。将 辅助区域设置为 附加区域","B":"在主区域和辅助区域之间为所有 S3 存储桶实施 S3 批量操作复制任务。将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。 将辅助区域设置为附加区域。","C":"在主区域的 S3 存储桶与辅助区域的 S3 存储桶之间实现双向复制。在两个区域的 DynamoDB 表上启用 DynamoDB 流。在每个区域中，创建一个订阅 DynamoDB 流的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函 数，使其将新记录复制到另一个区域的 DynamoDB 表中。","D":"在主区域和辅助区域之间为所有 S3 存储桶实施 S3 批量操作复制任务。在两个区域的 DynamoDB 表上启 用 DynamoDB 流。在每个区域中，创建一个订阅 DynamoDB 流的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函 数将新记录复制到另一个区域的 DynamoDB 表中。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are bidirectional persistence across two Regions, immediate (near-real-time) propagation, and MOST operational efficiency. Option A uses two fully managed, AWS-native features: S3 two-way (bi-directional) Cross-Region Replication and DynamoDB global tables. S3 live replication (CRR) automatically and asynchronously copies new/updated objects as they are written, and DynamoDB global tables automatically replicate writes across Regions with multi-active, asynchronous, last-writer-wins replication and require no application changes. Both are managed services requiring no custom code, giving the highest operational efficiency while propagating data continuously. Converting tables to global tables and adding the secondary Region as an additional replica is the standard, supported approach.","explanation_zh":"需求是雙向跨兩個 Region 的資料持久化、近即時傳播，以及最高的運維效率。選項 A 使用兩個完全受管的 AWS 原生功能：S3 雙向（bi-directional）Cross-Region Replication 以及 DynamoDB global tables。S3 live replication (CRR) 會在物件寫入時自動且非同步地複製新增/更新的物件，而 DynamoDB global tables 會自動跨 Region 複製寫入，採用 multi-active、非同步、last-writer-wins 機制，且不需修改應用程式。兩者皆為受管服務，無需自訂程式碼，提供最高運維效率並持續傳播資料。將資料表轉為 global tables 並把次要 Region 加為 additional Region 是標準且受支援的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 Batch Operations / S3 Batch Replication is on-demand (batch) copying of existing objects, not live replication. It does not immediately/continuously propagate new objects as they are written, so it fails the 'immediately propagate' requirement and adds job-management overhead. (The DynamoDB global tables half is correct.)","why_zh":"S3 Batch Operations / S3 Batch Replication 是針對既有物件的隨選（批次）複製，並非 live replication。它不會在新物件寫入時即時/持續傳播，因此不符合『立即傳播』需求，且增加批次作業管理負擔。（DynamoDB global tables 的部分是正確的。）"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Building custom Lambda functions subscribed to DynamoDB Streams to copy records across Regions reinvents what DynamoDB global tables provide natively. It carries high operational overhead, conflict-resolution complexity, and risk of replication loops, so it is far less operationally efficient than global tables. (S3 two-way replication is correct.)","why_zh":"自行建立訂閱 DynamoDB Streams 的 Lambda 函式來跨 Region 複製記錄，是重新發明 DynamoDB global tables 原生提供的功能。需自行處理衝突、可能造成複製迴圈，運維負擔高，遠不如 global tables 有效率。（S3 雙向複製部分正確。）"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines both weakest choices: S3 Batch Operations (batch, not immediate) plus custom Lambda/Streams replication (high operational overhead and conflict risk). It fails the immediate-propagation requirement for S3 and is the least operationally efficient overall.","why_zh":"結合了兩個最差的做法：S3 Batch Operations（批次、非即時）加上自訂 Lambda/Streams 複製（運維負擔高且有衝突風險）。在 S3 不符合即時傳播需求，整體運維效率最低。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-walkthrough-5.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":249,"question_en":"A company has configured Amazon RDS storage autoscaling for its RDS DB instances. A DevOps team needs to visualize the autoscaling events on an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司已为其 RDS 数据库实例配置了 Amazon RDS 存储自动扩展功能。DevOps 团队需要在 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板上可视化这些自动扩展事件。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to RDS storage autoscaling events from RDS events. Create an AWS Lambda function that publishes a CloudWatch custom metric. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function. Visualize the custom metric by using the CloudWatch dashboard.","B":"Create a trail by using AWS CloudTrail with management events configured. Configure the trail to send the management events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a metric filter in CloudWatch Logs to match the RDS storage autoscaling events. Visualize the metric filter by using the CloudWatch dashboard.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to RDS storage autoscaling events from the RDS events. Create a CloudWatch alarm. Configure the EventBridge rule to change the status of the CloudWatch alarm. Visualize the alarm status by using the CloudWatch dashboard.","D":"Create a trail by using AWS CloudTrail with data events configured. Configure the trail to send the data events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a metric filter in CloudWatch Logs to match the RDS storage autoscaling events. Visualize the metric filter by using the CloudWatch dashboard."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对来自 RDS 事件的 RDS 存储自动扩展事件做出反应。创建一 个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于发布 CloudWatch 自定义指标。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用 Lambda 函数。 使用 CloudWatch 控制面板可视化自定义指标。","B":"使用配置了管理事件的 AWS CloudTrail 创建一条跟踪记录。将跟踪记录配置为将管理事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。在 CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个指标过滤器以匹配 RDS 存储自动扩展事件。 使用 CloudWatch 控制面板可视化该指标过滤器。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对来自 RDS 事件的 RDS 存储自动扩展事件做出反应。创 建一个 CloudWatch 警报。配置 EventBridge 规则以更改 CloudWatch 警报的状态。使用 CloudWatch 控制面板可视化警报状态。","D":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 并配置数据事件来创建一条跟踪。将跟踪配置为将数据事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。在 CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个指标过滤器以匹配 RDS 存储自动扩展事件。使用 CloudWatch 控制面板可视化该指标过滤器。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon RDS sends storage autoscaling actions as RDS service events (RDS DB Instance Event, source aws.rds) directly to Amazon EventBridge - for example RDS-EVENT-0018 (Applying modification to allocated storage) / RDS-EVENT-0017 (Finished applying modification to allocated storage) and the autoscaling-specific event. The correct, documented pattern is therefore: an EventBridge rule matches these RDS events and invokes an AWS Lambda function that calls CloudWatch PutMetricData to publish a custom metric, which can then be graphed on a CloudWatch dashboard. Option C fails because EventBridge rule targets cannot 'change the status of a CloudWatch alarm' - alarm state is derived from metric data, and the only manual override is the test-only SetAlarmState API, which is not an EventBridge target action and auto-reverts. Options B and D rely on AWS CloudTrail: storage autoscaling is an internal RDS service event, not a reliable user management-event API call, and it is definitely not a CloudTrail data event (data events cover resource-level ops like S3 objects, Lambda invokes, DynamoDB items - RDS storage autoscaling is not one of them).","explanation_zh":"Amazon RDS 會將儲存體自動擴展的動作以 RDS 服務事件 (RDS DB Instance Event, source 為 aws.rds) 直接送到 Amazon EventBridge,例如 RDS-EVENT-0018 (Applying modification to allocated storage) / RDS-EVENT-0017 (Finished applying modification to allocated storage) 以及自動擴展專屬事件。因此正確且有官方文件支持的做法是:建立 EventBridge 規則比對這些 RDS 事件,觸發 AWS Lambda 函式,函式呼叫 CloudWatch PutMetricData 發布自訂指標 (custom metric),再於 CloudWatch dashboard 以圖表呈現。選項 C 錯誤,因為 EventBridge 規則的 target 無法『變更 CloudWatch alarm 的狀態』 - 警示狀態是由指標資料推導出來的,唯一的手動覆寫是僅供測試的 SetAlarmState API,它不是 EventBridge target 動作且會自動還原。選項 B、D 依賴 AWS CloudTrail:儲存體自動擴展是 RDS 內部服務事件,並非可靠的使用者管理事件 (management event) API 呼叫,更絕對不是 CloudTrail data event (data event 涵蓋 S3 物件、Lambda invoke、DynamoDB 項目等資源層級操作,RDS 儲存體自動擴展不屬於此類)。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudTrail management events plus a CloudWatch Logs metric filter is the wrong source. RDS storage autoscaling is an internal RDS service event, not a reliable user-initiated management-event API call you can pattern-match in CloudTrail logs; the native source is RDS events via EventBridge.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 管理事件加 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 來源錯誤。RDS 儲存體自動擴展是 RDS 內部服務事件,並非可在 CloudTrail 紀錄中可靠比對的使用者發起管理事件 API 呼叫;原生來源應是透過 EventBridge 的 RDS 事件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EventBridge rule targets cannot 'change the status of a CloudWatch alarm'. Alarm state is derived from metric data; the only manual override is the test-only SetAlarmState API, which is not an EventBridge target and auto-reverts - so this does not visualize autoscaling events.","why_zh":"EventBridge 規則 target 無法『變更 CloudWatch alarm 狀態』。警示狀態由指標資料推導,唯一手動覆寫是僅供測試的 SetAlarmState API,它不是 EventBridge target 且會自動還原,故無法用來視覺化自動擴展事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail data events cover resource-level operations such as S3 object activity, Lambda Invoke, and DynamoDB item operations. RDS storage autoscaling is not a CloudTrail data event, so a metric filter on data events would never match it.","why_zh":"CloudTrail data event 涵蓋資源層級操作,如 S3 物件活動、Lambda Invoke、DynamoDB 項目操作。RDS 儲存體自動擴展並非 CloudTrail data event,因此針對 data event 的 metric filter 永遠不會比對到它。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-rds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_Events.Messages.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_PIOPS.Autoscaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/create_dashboard.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/publishingMetrics.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":250,"question_en":"A company uses containers for its applications. The company learns that some container images are missing required security configurations. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to create a standard base image. The solution must publish the base image weekly to the us-west-2 Region, us-east-2 Region, and eu-central-1 Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用容器来运行其应用程序。该公司发现一些容器镜像缺少必要的安全配置。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案来创建一个标准的基础镜像。该解决方案必须每周将基础镜 像发布到 us-west-2 区域、us-east-2 区域和 eu-central-1 区域。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an EC2 Image Builder pipeline that uses a container recipe to build the image. Configure the pipeline to distribute the image to an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository in us-west-2. Configure ECR replication from us-west-2 to us-east-2 and from us-east-2 to eu-central-1. Configure the pipeline to run weekly.","B":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses an AWS CodeBuild project to build the image. Use AWS CodeDeploy to publish the image to an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository in us-west-2. Configure ECR replication from us-west-2 to us-east-2 and from us-east-2 to eu-central-1. Configure the pipeline to run weekly.","C":"Create an EC2 Image Builder pipeline that uses a container recipe to build the image. Configure the pipeline to distribute the image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories in all three Regions. Configure the pipeline to run weekly.","D":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses an AWS CodeBuild project to build the image. Use AWS CodeDeploy to publish the image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories in all three Regions. Configure the pipeline to run weekly."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个使用容器配方来构建映像的 EC2 Image Builder 管道。将管道配置为将映像分发到 us-west-2 区 域的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库。配置 ECR 从 us-west-2 复制到 us- east-2，再从 us-east-2 复制到 eu-central-1。将管道配置为每周运行一次。","B":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道使用 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建镜像。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将镜像发布到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 。 在 us-west-2 区域设置存储库。配置从 us-west-2 到 us-east-2 以及从 us-east-2 到 eu-central-1 的 ECR 复 制。将管道配置为每周运行一次。","C":"创建一个使用容器配方来构建映像的 EC2 Image Builder 管道。将管道配置为将映像分发到所有三个区域 的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库。将管道配置为每周运行一次。","D":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道使用 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建镜像。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将镜像发布到所有三个区域的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储 库。将管道配置为每周运行一次。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"EC2 Image Builder container recipes are purpose-built to create a standardized, hardened base image and natively distribute it. The container pipeline produces a Docker image and distributes it directly to Amazon ECR repositories in multiple target Regions through its distribution settings, and pipelines support a built-in weekly build schedule. Option C therefore meets all requirements (us-west-2, us-east-2, eu-central-1) with a single, native mechanism. Option A is wrong because it relies on chained ECR replication (us-west-2 to us-east-2, then us-east-2 to eu-central-1): AWS docs explicitly state a replication action only occurs once per image push and replicated images are NOT re-replicated, so eu-central-1 would never receive the image. Options B and D are wrong because AWS CodeDeploy does not push or publish container images to Amazon ECR; CodeDeploy deploys applications to EC2/on-prem, Lambda, or ECS services, while image publishing is done via docker push (typically CodeBuild), not CodeDeploy.","explanation_zh":"EC2 Image Builder 的 container recipe 專為建立標準化、強化過的 base image 並原生散佈而設計。Container pipeline 會產生 Docker image，並透過其 distribution settings 直接散佈到多個目標 Region 的 Amazon ECR repositories，且 pipeline 內建支援每週 build 排程。因此選項 C 以單一原生機制即可滿足全部需求 (us-west-2、us-east-2、eu-central-1)。選項 A 錯誤，因為它依賴鏈式 ECR replication (us-west-2 到 us-east-2，再 us-east-2 到 eu-central-1)：AWS 文件明確說明每次 image push 只會觸發一次 replication 動作，已被複寫的 image 不會再次被複寫，因此 eu-central-1 永遠收不到 image。選項 B 與 D 錯誤，因為 AWS CodeDeploy 不會將 container image 推送或發布到 Amazon ECR；CodeDeploy 是把應用程式部署到 EC2/on-prem、Lambda 或 ECS 服務，而 image 發布是透過 docker push (通常是 CodeBuild) 完成，而非 CodeDeploy。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses chained ECR replication (us-west-2 to us-east-2, then us-east-2 to eu-central-1). AWS docs state a replication action only occurs once per image push and replicated images are not re-replicated, so eu-central-1 never receives the image. It also adds unnecessary complexity since Image Builder can distribute to all three Regions directly.","why_zh":"使用鏈式 ECR replication (us-west-2 到 us-east-2，再 us-east-2 到 eu-central-1)。AWS 文件指出每次 image push 只觸發一次 replication，已複寫的 image 不會再被複寫，故 eu-central-1 收不到 image。同時也多此一舉，因為 Image Builder 可直接散佈到全部三個 Region。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS CodeDeploy does not publish container images to Amazon ECR; that is done with docker push (e.g., CodeBuild). It also reuses the flawed chained ECR replication that fails to reach eu-central-1.","why_zh":"AWS CodeDeploy 不會把 container image 發布到 Amazon ECR；發布是用 docker push (例如 CodeBuild) 完成。它同樣使用無法抵達 eu-central-1 的鏈式 ECR replication，存在缺陷。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS CodeDeploy cannot push images to ECR repositories; image publishing is not a CodeDeploy capability. CodeDeploy targets EC2/on-prem, Lambda, and ECS service deployments, not registry image pushes across Regions.","why_zh":"AWS CodeDeploy 無法將 image 推送到 ECR repositories；發布 image 不是 CodeDeploy 的功能。CodeDeploy 針對的是 EC2/on-prem、Lambda 與 ECS 服務部署，而非跨 Region 的 registry image 推送。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/start-build-container-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/how-image-builder-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/registry-settings-configure.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":251,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to install antivirus software on all the Amazon EC2 instances in an AWS account. The EC2 instances run the most recent version of Amazon Linux. The solution must detect all instances and must use an AWS Systems Manager document to install the software if the software is not present. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，在 AWS 账户中的所有 Amazon EC2 实例上安装防病毒软 件。这些 EC2 实例运行的是最新版的 Amazon Linux。 该解决方案必须检测所有实例，并且如果软件不存在，必须使用 AWS 系统管理器文档来安装该软件。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an association in Systems Manager State Manager. Target all the managed nodes. Include the software in the association. Configure the association to use the Systems Manager document.","B":"Set up AWS Config to record all the resources in the account. Create an AWS Config custom rule to determine if the software is installed on all the EC2 instances. Configure an automatic remediation action that uses the Systems Manager document for noncompliant EC2 instances.","C":"Activate Amazon EC2 scanning on Amazon Inspector to determine if the software is installed on all the EC2 instances. Associate the findings with the Systems Manager document.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses AWS CloudTrail to detect the Runinstances API call. Configure inventory collection in Systems Manager Inventory to determine if the software is installed on the EC2 instances. Associate the Systems Manager inventory with the Systems Manager document."},"options_zh":{"A":"在系统管理器状态管理器中创建一个关联。将所有受管节点作为目标。在关联中包含该软件。配置该关 联以使用系统管理器文档。","B":"设置 AWS Config 以记录账户中的所有资源。创建一个 AWS Config 自定义规则，以确定软件是否已安 装在所有 EC2 实例上。配置一个自动修复操作，该操作使用 Systems Manager 文档来修复不符合要 求的 EC2 实例。","C":"在 Amazon Inspector 中激活 Amazon EC2 扫描，以确定该软件是否已安装在所有 EC2 实例上。将发现结 果与 Systems Manager 文档相关联。","D":"创建一个使用 AWS CloudTrail 检测 RunInstances API 调用的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。在 Systems Manager Inventory 中配置库存收集以确定软件是否已安装在 EC2 实例上。将 Systems Manager 库存与 Systems Manager 文档相关联。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Systems Manager State Manager is purpose-built for this exact scenario. The State Manager documentation literally uses antivirus software as its canonical example: an association can specify that antivirus software must be installed and running on a managed node, and if the software isn't installed on a node, the association instructs State Manager to install it. An association can target all managed nodes in the current AWS Region and account, which satisfies the 'detect all instances' requirement, and it runs the SSM document on a schedule to enforce the desired state, installing the software only if it is not present. This single-service, declarative solution detects all instances and uses an SSM document for installation, exactly as required.","explanation_zh":"AWS Systems Manager State Manager 正是為此情境而設計。State Manager 官方文件直接以防毒軟體作為標準範例：一個 association 可指定受管節點上必須安裝並執行防毒軟體，若節點上未安裝該軟體，association 會指示 State Manager 進行安裝。Association 可以鎖定目前 AWS 區域與帳戶中的所有受管節點，滿足『偵測所有執行個體』的需求，並依排程執行 SSM document 以維持期望狀態，僅在軟體不存在時才安裝。此單一服務、宣告式的方案能偵測所有執行個體並使用 SSM document 進行安裝，完全符合需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config with a custom rule plus auto-remediation could technically work, but it requires writing and maintaining a custom Config rule (typically a Lambda function) just to determine if the software is installed, and Config auto-remediation runs against a periodic compliance snapshot rather than continuously enforcing desired state. This is far more operationally complex than a State Manager association, which natively handles both detection-and-install via the SSM document. Config is also primarily a configuration-recording/compliance service, not a software-installation enforcement tool.","why_zh":"使用 AWS Config 自訂規則加上自動修復理論上可行，但需編寫並維護一個自訂 Config 規則（通常是 Lambda 函數）來判斷軟體是否已安裝，且 Config 的自動修復是依據週期性合規快照觸發，而非持續強制維持期望狀態。相較於原生即可同時處理偵測與安裝的 State Manager association，這在維運上複雜得多。Config 本質上是組態紀錄與合規服務，並非用於強制安裝軟體的工具。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability assessment service that scans for CVEs/software vulnerabilities and network exposure; it does not check whether an arbitrary application such as antivirus is installed, nor can it 'associate findings with an SSM document' to install software. There is no native mechanism in Inspector to trigger software installation, so this option does not meet the requirements.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是漏洞評估服務，掃描 CVE／軟體漏洞與網路暴露面；它不會檢查像防毒這類任意應用程式是否已安裝，也無法將『發現結果關聯到 SSM document』來安裝軟體。Inspector 沒有觸發軟體安裝的原生機制，因此無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This EventBridge + CloudTrail RunInstances approach only reacts to newly launched instances and would not detect existing instances already running in the account, failing the 'detect all instances' requirement. SSM Inventory collects software inventory data but cannot by itself install missing software or be 'associated with an SSM document' to perform installation. The architecture is convoluted and does not satisfy the enforcement requirement.","why_zh":"此 EventBridge 加 CloudTrail RunInstances 的方法只會對新啟動的執行個體做出反應，無法偵測帳戶中已在執行的既有執行個體，未滿足『偵測所有執行個體』的需求。SSM Inventory 會收集軟體清單資料，但本身無法安裝缺少的軟體，也無法『關聯到 SSM document』來執行安裝。此架構繞圈且無法滿足強制安裝需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-state.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/what-is-inspector.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":252,"question_en":"A company needs to increase the security of the container images that run in its production environment. The company wants to integrate operating system scanning and programming language package vulnerability scanning for the containers in its CI/CD pipeline. The CI/CD pipeline is an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that includes an AWS CodeBuild build project, AWS CodeDeploy actions, and an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. A DevOps engineer needs to add an image scan to the CI/CD pipeline. The CI/CD pipeline must deploy only images without CRITICAL and HIGH findings into production. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司需要提高其生产环境中运行的容器镜像的安全性。该公司希望在其持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD） 流水线中集成操作系统扫描和编程语言包漏洞扫描功能，以针对容器进行操作。该 CI/CD 流水线是一个 AWS CodePipeline 流水线，其中包括一个 AWS CodeBuild 构建项目、AWS CodeDeploy 操作以及一个亚马 逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）存储库。 DevOps 工程师需要在持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流水线中添加镜像扫描功能。该 CI/CD 流水线必须仅 将没有“严重”和“高危”漏洞的镜像部署到生产环境。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon ECR basic scanning.","B":"Use Amazon ECR enhanced scanning.","C":"Configure Amazon ECR to submit a Rejected status to the CI/CD pipeline when the image scan returns CRITICAL or HIGH findings.","D":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function when the image scan is completed. Configure the Lambda function to consume the Amazon Inspector scan status and to submit an Approved or Rejected status to the CI/CD pipeline.","E":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function when the image scan is completed. Configure the Lambda function to consume the Clair scan status and to submit an Approved or Rejected status to the CI/CD pipeline."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon ECR 基本扫描。","B":"使用亚马逊 ECR 增强扫描功能。","C":"配置 Amazon ECR，使其在镜像扫描结果返回“严重”或“高”风险时，向 CI/CD 管道提交“已拒绝”状 态。","D":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在图像扫描完成后调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数以获取 Amazon Inspector 扫描状态，并向 CI/CD 管道提交“已批准”或“已拒绝”状态。","E":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在图像扫描完成后调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数以获取 Clair 扫描状态，并向 CI/CD 管道提交“已批准”或“已拒绝”状态。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to scan for BOTH operating system vulnerabilities AND programming language package vulnerabilities, and to gate deployment so only images with no CRITICAL/HIGH findings reach production. Only Amazon ECR enhanced scanning (B) covers both categories: it integrates with Amazon Inspector to scan container images for OS and programming language package vulnerabilities. Amazon ECR basic scanning (A) only performs OS-level CVE scans and cannot detect language package vulnerabilities, so it fails the requirement. For gating, Amazon Inspector emits an event to EventBridge when an image scan completes (detail-type 'Inspector2 Scan', source 'aws.inspector2'), and that event includes finding-severity-counts (CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM). Option D correctly uses an EventBridge rule to invoke a Lambda function that consumes the Amazon Inspector scan status and submits an Approved or Rejected result back to CodePipeline (via PutJobSuccessResult/PutJobFailureResult on an invoke/Lambda action). Therefore B and D together meet the requirements.","explanation_zh":"需求是同時掃描作業系統 (OS) 弱點與程式語言套件弱點，並把關部署，讓只有沒有 CRITICAL/HIGH 發現的映像檔才能進入正式環境。只有 Amazon ECR enhanced scanning (B) 同時涵蓋這兩類：它整合 Amazon Inspector，對容器映像進行 OS 與程式語言套件弱點掃描。Amazon ECR basic scanning (A) 只做 OS 層級的 CVE 掃描，無法偵測語言套件弱點，因此不符合需求。在把關方面，當映像掃描完成時 Amazon Inspector 會向 EventBridge 發出事件（detail-type 為 'Inspector2 Scan'，source 為 'aws.inspector2'），事件中包含 finding-severity-counts（CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM）。選項 D 正確地使用 EventBridge 規則觸發 Lambda 函式，由該函式讀取 Amazon Inspector 掃描狀態，並向 CodePipeline 回報 Approved 或 Rejected 結果（透過 invoke/Lambda action 的 PutJobSuccessResult/PutJobFailureResult）。因此 B 與 D 一起滿足所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"ECR basic scanning uses the CVE database to scan only for operating system vulnerabilities; it does not scan programming language package vulnerabilities, so it fails the explicit dual-scanning requirement.","why_zh":"ECR basic scanning 使用 CVE 資料庫只掃描作業系統弱點，不會掃描程式語言套件弱點，因此無法滿足明確要求的雙重掃描需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon ECR has no native feature to submit an Approved/Rejected status to CodePipeline based on scan findings. Gating the pipeline requires the EventBridge + Lambda pattern to consume Inspector results and call the CodePipeline job result APIs; ECR cannot do this directly.","why_zh":"Amazon ECR 沒有原生功能可根據掃描發現向 CodePipeline 提交 Approved/Rejected 狀態。要把關管線必須使用 EventBridge + Lambda 模式來讀取 Inspector 結果並呼叫 CodePipeline 的 job result API；ECR 無法直接做到。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Clair is a third-party open-source scanner and is not used by ECR enhanced scanning. ECR enhanced scanning uses Amazon Inspector (event source aws.inspector2), so a Lambda consuming a 'Clair scan status' would not receive the relevant ECR/Inspector scan events.","why_zh":"Clair 是第三方開源掃描器，並非 ECR enhanced scanning 所使用的元件。ECR enhanced scanning 使用 Amazon Inspector（事件來源為 aws.inspector2），因此讀取『Clair 掃描狀態』的 Lambda 不會收到相關的 ECR/Inspector 掃描事件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-invoke-lambda-function.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":253,"question_en":"A company's DevOps team manages a set of AWS accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company needs a solution that ensures that all Amazon EC2 instances use approved AM Is that the DevOps team manages. The solution also must remediate the usage of AMIs that are not approved. The individual account administrators must not be able to remove the restriction to use approved AMIs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 团队管理着一组位于 AWS 组织中的 AWS 账户。 该公司需要一个解决方案，确保所有亚马逊 EC2 实例都使用由 DevOps 团队管理的已获批准的 AMI。 该解决方案还必须纠正使用未获批准的 AMI 的情况。各个账户管理员不得解除使用已获批准的 AMI 的限制。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy an Amazon EventBridge rule to each account. Configure the rule to react to AWS CloudTrail events for Amazon EC2 and to send a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the DevOps team to the SNS topic.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy the approved-amis-by-id AWS Config managed rule to each account. Configure the rule with the list of approved AMIs. Configure the rule to run the AWS- StopEC2Instance AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook for the noncompliant EC2 instances.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that processes AWS CloudTrail events for Amazon EC2. Configure the Lambda function to send a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the DevOps team to the SNS topic. Deploy the Lambda function in each account in the organization. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule in each account. Configure the EventBridge rules to react to AWS CloudTrail events for Amazon EC2 and to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Enable AWS Config across the organization. Create a conformance pack that uses the approved-amis- by-id AWS Config managed rule with the list of approved AMIs. Deploy the conformance pack across the organization. Configure the rule to run the AWS-StopEC2lnstance AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook for the noncompliant EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 Amazon EventBridge 规则部署到每个账户。配置该规则以响 应 Amazon EC2 的 AWS CloudTrail 事件，并向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS） 主题发送通知。让 DevOps 团队订阅该 SNS 主题。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 approved-amis-by-id AWS Config 管理规则部署到 每个账户。使用已批准的 AMI 列表配置规则。配置规则以运行 AWS- 用于不符合规定的 EC2 实例的 StopEC2Instance AWS 系统管理器自动化运行记录。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来处理 Amazon EC2 的 AWS CloudTrail 事件。配置该 Lambda 函数向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题发送通知。让 DevOps 团队订阅该 SNS 主题。 在组织中的每个账户中部署该 Lambda 函数。在每个账户中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配 置 EventBridge 规则以响应 Amazon EC2 的 AWS CloudTrail 事件并调用 Lambda 函数。","D":"在整个组织内启用 AWS Config。创建一个一致性包，使用带有已批准 AMI 列表的 approved-amisby- id AWS Config 管理规则。在整个组织内部署一致性包。配置规则，对不符合要求的 EC2 实例运行 AWS-StopEC2lnstance AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are threefold: (1) enforce approved AMIs across all org accounts, (2) automatically remediate noncompliant EC2 instances, and (3) prevent individual account admins from removing the restriction. Both B and D use the correct approved-amis-by-id managed rule plus the AWS-StopEC2Instance SSM Automation runbook for remediation, so the deciding qualifier is requirement (3). The AWS Config docs state that an organization conformance pack lets you 'use the management account in AWS Organizations to enforce governance by ensuring that the underlying AWS Config rules and remediation actions are not modifiable by your organization's member accounts.' That directly satisfies the non-removable restriction. Option B deploys the rule via CloudFormation StackSets as ordinary resources INTO each member account, where the local account administrator can modify or delete the Config rule/remediation, so it fails requirement (3). Options A and C only send SNS notifications and never remediate, failing requirement (2). Therefore D is correct.","explanation_zh":"本題有三項要求：(1) 在組織所有帳戶強制使用核准的 AMI、(2) 自動修復不合規的 EC2 執行個體、(3) 個別帳戶管理員不得移除該限制。B 與 D 都使用正確的 approved-amis-by-id 受管規則搭配 AWS-StopEC2Instance SSM Automation runbook 進行修復，因此關鍵判別點是第 (3) 項要求。AWS Config 文件明確指出組織型 conformance pack 可『使用 AWS Organizations 管理帳戶強制治理，確保底層的 AWS Config 規則與修復動作無法被組織成員帳戶修改』，這正好滿足無法移除限制的需求。選項 B 透過 CloudFormation StackSets 將規則當作一般資源部署『進入』各成員帳戶，本地帳戶管理員可以修改或刪除該 Config 規則/修復，因此不符合第 (3) 項要求。選項 A 與 C 僅發送 SNS 通知、完全不做修復，不符合第 (2) 項要求。因此 D 為正解。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An EventBridge rule on CloudTrail events only sends an SNS notification to the DevOps team. It does not enforce approved AMIs nor automatically remediate noncompliant instances, so it fails the core remediation requirement.","why_zh":"基於 CloudTrail 事件的 EventBridge 規則只會發 SNS 通知給 DevOps 團隊，既不強制核准 AMI 也不自動修復不合規執行個體，未達修復要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses the correct rule and runbook but deploys them via StackSets as resources inside each member account, where the local account administrator can edit or delete the Config rule and remediation. It does not prevent admins from removing the restriction, failing that requirement.","why_zh":"雖使用正確規則與 runbook，但透過 StackSets 將其當作資源部署在各成員帳戶內，本地帳戶管理員可修改或刪除該 Config 規則與修復，無法阻止管理員移除限制，故不符合要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Lambda function triggered by EventBridge that only publishes to SNS provides notification, not remediation, and does not enforce approved AMIs in a non-removable way. It fails the remediation requirement.","why_zh":"由 EventBridge 觸發、僅發布到 SNS 的 Lambda 只提供通知而非修復，也無法以不可移除的方式強制核准 AMI，未達修復要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-pack-organization-apis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-packs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/approved-amis-by-id.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":254,"question_en":"A company gives its employees limited rights to AWS. DevOps engineers have the ability to assume an administrator role. For tracking purposes, the security team wants to receive a near-real-time notification when the administrator role is assumed. How should this be accomplished?","question_zh":"一家公司赋予其员工有限的 AWS 权限。DevOps 工程师能够承担管理员角色。出于追踪目的，安全团 队希望在管理员角色被承担时能收到近乎实时的通知。 这该如何实现呢？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Config to publish logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to query the logs and send a notification to the security team when the administrator role is assumed.","B":"Configure Amazon GuardDuty to monitor when the administrator role is assumed and send a notification to the security team.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge event rule using an AWS Management Console sign-in events event pattern that publishes a message to an Amazon SNS topic if the administrator role is assumed.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge events rule using an AWS API call that uses an AWS CloudTrail event pattern to invoke an AWS Lambda function that publishes a message to an Amazon SNS topic if the administrator role is assumed."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Config 将日志发布到 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon Athena 查询日志，并在管理员角色 被使用时向安全团队发送通知。","B":"配置 Amazon GuardDuty 来监控管理员角色何时被使用，并向安全团队发送通知。","C":"使用 AWS 管理控制台登录事件模式创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则，如果管理员角色被承 担，则向 Amazon SNS 主题发布一条消息。","D":"使用 AWS API 调用创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则，该规则使用 AWS CloudTrail 事件模式， 如果管理员角色被使用，则调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数向 Amazon SNS 主题发布一条消息。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Assuming an IAM role is an sts:AssumeRole API call. STS delivers these events to the default EventBridge bus via CloudTrail with detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' (source aws.sts, eventSource sts.amazonaws.com, eventName AssumeRole), provided a CloudTrail trail is enabled. Option D creates an EventBridge rule on that AWS-API-call-via-CloudTrail pattern, invokes a Lambda that publishes to SNS, giving near-real-time notification. This is the documented mechanism for matching STS API activity. Option C is wrong because it uses an 'AWS Management Console sign-in events' pattern (detail-type 'AWS Console Signin via CloudTrail'), which captures console sign-ins, not role assumption via the STS API.","explanation_zh":"假設(assume)IAM 角色實際上是一個 sts:AssumeRole 的 API 呼叫。只要啟用 CloudTrail trail，STS 會透過 CloudTrail 將事件以 detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail'(source 為 aws.sts、eventSource 為 sts.amazonaws.com、eventName 為 AssumeRole)送到預設的 EventBridge event bus。選項 D 在此 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' 模式上建立 EventBridge 規則,觸發 Lambda 將訊息發布到 SNS,達成近即時通知,這正是比對 STS API 活動的官方文件做法。選項 C 錯誤,因為它使用 'AWS Management Console sign-in events'(detail-type 'AWS Console Signin via CloudTrail')模式,只能捕捉主控台登入,無法捕捉透過 STS API 進行的角色假設。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config records resource configuration changes, not IAM/STS API activity like role assumption. Querying logs with Athena is batch/on-demand, not near-real-time, so it fails the near-real-time requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Config 記錄資源組態變更,而非像角色假設這種 IAM/STS API 活動。用 Athena 查詢日誌是批次/隨選方式,並非近即時,因此不符合近即時的需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that surfaces anomalous or malicious findings. It does not emit a notification simply because a legitimate, known administrator role is assumed; there is no rule to alert on every assumption of a specific role.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務,僅針對異常或惡意行為產生 findings。它不會因為合法且已知的管理員角色被假設就發出通知,也無法針對每次假設特定角色發出警示。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses an 'AWS Management Console sign-in events' (AWS Console Signin via CloudTrail) event pattern, which detects console sign-ins by IAM users/root, not the sts:AssumeRole API call used when a role is assumed. The pattern matches the wrong event type and would not fire on role assumption.","why_zh":"使用 'AWS Management Console sign-in events'(AWS Console Signin via CloudTrail)事件模式,只能偵測 IAM 使用者/root 的主控台登入,無法偵測假設角色時所用的 sts:AssumeRole API 呼叫。此模式比對的是錯誤的事件類型,角色被假設時並不會觸發。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-sts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-event-reference-aws-console-sign-in-events.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":255,"question_en":"A company needs a strategy for failover and disaster recovery of its data and application. The application uses a MySQL database and Amazon EC2 instances. The company requires a maximum RPO of 2 hours and a maximum RTO of 10 minutes for its data and application at all times. Which combination of deployment strategies will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司需要为其数据和应用程序制定故障转移和灾难恢复策略。该应用程序使用 MySQL 数据库和亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司要求其数据和应用程序在任何时候的最大恢复点目标（RPO）为 2 小时，最大恢复时间 目标（RTO）为 10 分钟。 哪种部署策略组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Aurora Single-AZ cluster in multiple AWS Regions as the data store. Use Aurora's automatic recovery capabilities in the event of a disaster.","B":"Create an Amazon Aurora global database in two AWS Regions as the data store. In the event of a failure, promote the secondary Region to the primary for the application. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster endpoint in the secondary Region.","C":"Create an Amazon Aurora cluster in multiple AWS Regions as the data store. Use a Network Load Balancer to balance the database traffic in different Regions.","D":"Set up the application in two AWS Regions. Use Amazon Route 53 failover routing that points to Application Load Balancers in both Regions. Use health checks and Auto Scaling groups in each Region.","E":"Set up the application in two AWS Regions. Configure AWS Global Accelerator to point to Application Load Balancers (ALBs) in both Regions. Add both ALBs to a single endpoint group. Use health checks and Auto Scaling groups in each Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在多个 AWS 区域创建 Amazon Aurora 单可用区集群作为数据存储。在发生灾难时利用 Aurora 的自动恢 复功能。","B":"在两个 AWS 区域创建一个 Amazon Aurora 全球数据库作为数据存储。若发生故障，将备用区域提升为 主区域以供应用程序使用。更新应用程序以使用备用区域中的 Aurora 集群端点。","C":"在多个 AWS 区域创建 Amazon Aurora 集群作为数据存储。使用网络负载均衡器来平衡不同区域的数 据库流量。","D":"在两个 AWS 区域中设置应用程序。使用 Amazon Route 53 故障转移路由，该路由指向两个区域中 的应用负载均衡器。在每个区域中使用健康检查和自动扩展组。","E":"在两个 AWS 区域中设置应用程序。配置 AWS 全球加速器以指向两个区域中的应用负载均衡器（ALB）。 将两个 ALB 添加到单个终端节点组。在每个区域中使用健康检查和自动扩展组。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement needs one data-tier strategy and one application-tier strategy that together meet RPO of 2 hours and RTO of 10 minutes. For the data tier, B (Aurora global database across two Regions) is correct: AWS docs state RPO is typically measured in seconds and RTO can be in the order of minutes, easily within the 2-hour RPO and 10-minute RTO; on failure you promote the secondary Region to primary and point the app at that Region's cluster endpoint. For the application tier, both D (Route 53 failover) and E (Global Accelerator) provide multi-Region failover with health checks and Auto Scaling. The decisive qualifier is the strict 10-minute RTO that must hold 'at all times'. AWS Global Accelerator uses static anycast IPs and fails over to a healthy endpoint in another endpoint group within about 30 seconds, independent of DNS TTL and resolver caching, giving deterministic, fast failover. Route 53 failover depends on DNS health-check intervals plus client/resolver TTL caching, which adds variable propagation delay and is less reliable for a guaranteed tight RTO. Therefore B and E are the most robust pair. (Note: D is also technically defensible and is the dump's suggested answer, which is why confidence is medium; but E is the stronger application-failover choice for a strict RTO and matches the canonical answer for this question.)","explanation_zh":"需求需要一個資料層策略加一個應用層策略，共同達成 RPO 2 小時與 RTO 10 分鐘。資料層方面，B（跨兩個 Region 的 Aurora global database）正確：AWS 文件指出其 RPO 通常以秒計、RTO 約為分鐘級，遠在 2 小時 RPO 與 10 分鐘 RTO 之內；故障時將次要 Region 提升為主要並讓應用指向該 Region 的 cluster endpoint。應用層方面，D（Route 53 failover）與 E（Global Accelerator）皆能提供搭配 health checks 與 Auto Scaling 的多 Region 故障切換。決定性條件是必須「隨時」維持嚴格的 10 分鐘 RTO。AWS Global Accelerator 使用靜態 anycast IP，可在約 30 秒內切換到另一 endpoint group 中的健康端點，不受 DNS TTL 與解析器快取影響，提供確定且快速的切換。Route 53 failover 取決於 DNS health check 間隔以及客戶端/解析器的 TTL 快取，增加不確定的傳播延遲，對於保證嚴格 RTO 較不可靠。因此 B 與 E 是最穩健的組合。（註：D 在技術上亦可成立，也是題庫建議答案，故信心為中等；但 E 對嚴格 RTO 是更強的應用切換選擇，並符合此題的權威答案。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An Aurora 'Single-AZ cluster in multiple Regions' is not a coordinated DR construct; Aurora automatic recovery operates within a Region, not across Regions, and there is no cross-Region replication described, so it cannot meet a 10-minute RTO or guaranteed 2-hour RPO across Regions.","why_zh":"Aurora 在多個 Region 各自建立 Single-AZ cluster 並非協調式 DR 設計；Aurora 自動復原作用於單一 Region 之內而非跨 Region，且未描述跨 Region 複寫，無法保證跨 Region 的 10 分鐘 RTO 或 2 小時 RPO。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot place a relational database behind a Network Load Balancer to 'balance database traffic in different Regions'. Aurora writes go to a single primary; an NLB does not replicate data, maintain write consistency, or perform cross-Region promotion, so this does not provide valid DR.","why_zh":"無法將關聯式資料庫置於 Network Load Balancer 之後以「平衡不同 Region 的資料庫流量」。Aurora 寫入僅送往單一主要節點；NLB 不會複寫資料、維持寫入一致性或執行跨 Region 提升，因此無法構成有效 DR。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Route 53 failover routing does provide multi-Region failover, but it relies on DNS health-check intervals plus client/resolver TTL caching, which introduces variable propagation delay. For a strict 10-minute RTO that must hold at all times, Global Accelerator's ~30-second anycast failover (E) is the more reliable application-tier choice, so E is preferred over D.","why_zh":"Route 53 failover routing 確實提供多 Region 切換，但需依賴 DNS health check 間隔加上客戶端/解析器 TTL 快取，產生不確定的傳播延遲。對於必須隨時維持的嚴格 10 分鐘 RTO，Global Accelerator 的約 30 秒 anycast 切換（E）為更可靠的應用層選擇，故 E 優於 D。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/about-endpoints-endpoint-weights.unhealthy-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":256,"question_en":"A developer is using the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) to create a prototype for an AWS Lambda function. The AWS SAM template contains an AWS::Serverless::Function resource that has the CodeUri property that points to an Amazon S3 location. The developer wants to identify the correct commands for deployment before creating a CI/CD pipeline. The developer creates an archive of the Lambda function code named package.zip. The developer uploads the .zip file archive to the S3 location specified in the CodeUri property. The developer runs the sam deploy command and deploys the Lambda function. The developer updates the Lambda function code and uses the same steps to deploy the new version of the Lambda function. The sam deploy command fails and returns an error of no changes to deploy. Which solutions will deploy the new version? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位开发人员正在使用 AWS 无服务器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）为一个 AWS Lambda 函数创建原型。 AWS SAM 模板Serverless::Function 资源，该资源具有指向 Amazon S3 位置的 CodeUri 属性。开发人员希望 在创建持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）管道之前确定正确的部署命令。 开发人员创建了一个名为 package.zip 的 Lambda 函数代码归档文件。开发人员将 .zip 文件归档上传到 CodeUri 属性中指定的 S3 位置。开发人员运行 sam deploy 命令并部署 Lambda 函数。开发人员更新 Lambda 函数代码，并使用相同的步骤部署 Lambda 函数的新版本。sam deploy 命令失败并返回错误信息， 提示没有可部署的更改。 哪些解决方案将部署新版本？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use the aws cloudformation update-stack command instead of the sam deploy command.","B":"Use the aws cloudformation update-stack-instances command instead of the sam deploy command.","C":"Update the CodeUri property to reference the local application code folder. Use the sam deploy command.","D":"Update the CodeUri property to reference the local application code folder. Use the aws cloudformation create-change-set command and the aws cloudformation execute-change-set command.","E":"Update the CodeUri property to reference the local application code folder. Use the aws cloudformation package command and the aws cloudformation deploy command."},"options_zh":{"A":"请使用 aws cloudformation update-stack 命令，而非 sam deploy 命令。","B":"请使用 aws cloudformation update-stack-instances 命令，而非 sam deploy 命令。","C":"将 CodeUri 属性更新为引用本地应用程序代码文件夹。使用 sam deploy 命令。","D":"将 CodeUri 属性更新为引用本地应用程序代码文件夹。使用 aws cloudformation create-change-set 命令和 aws cloudformation execute-change-set 命令。","E":"将 CodeUri 属性更新为引用本地应用程序代码文件夹。使用 aws cloudformation package 命令和 aws cloudformation deploy 命令。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The deployment fails because the developer re-uploads new code to the SAME S3 key/location referenced by a static CodeUri. AWS docs (AWS::Lambda::Function Code) state: 'Changes to a deployment package in Amazon S3 or a container image in ECR are not detected automatically during stack updates. To update the function code, change the object key or version in the template.' Since the template's CodeUri still points to the same unchanged S3 location, CloudFormation/SAM sees an identical template and reports 'no changes to deploy.' Both C and E fix this by pointing CodeUri at a LOCAL folder so that an automatic packaging step uploads the code with a content-hash-based S3 key. C: sam deploy implicitly packages local files, uploads them to S3 under a new content-hash key, and rewrites the template, so changed code yields a new key that CloudFormation detects. E: aws cloudformation package zips the local folder, names the .zip using the MD5 checksum of the folder contents, uploads it, and emits a processed template; aws cloudformation deploy then applies it. New code -> new checksum -> new key -> change detected. This is exactly the mechanism SAM wraps.","explanation_zh":"部署失敗的原因是開發者把新程式碼重新上傳到 CodeUri 所指向的「相同」S3 key/位置。AWS 文件 (AWS::Lambda::Function Code) 明確指出：在 stack 更新期間，Amazon S3 中部署套件或 ECR 容器映像的變更不會被自動偵測；若要更新函式程式碼，必須變更 template 中的物件 key 或版本。由於 template 的 CodeUri 仍指向相同且未變更的 S3 位置，CloudFormation/SAM 看到的是完全相同的 template，因此回報「no changes to deploy」。C 與 E 都把 CodeUri 改為指向「本機資料夾」，藉由自動 packaging 步驟以內容雜湊 (content-hash) 作為 S3 key 上傳程式碼來修正問題。C：sam deploy 會隱含執行 packaging，將本機檔案以新的內容雜湊 key 上傳到 S3 並改寫 template，程式碼變更便產生新的 key，CloudFormation 即可偵測到變更。E：aws cloudformation package 會把本機資料夾打包成 .zip，並以資料夾內容的 MD5 checksum 命名 .zip 後上傳，再產生處理後的 template；接著 aws cloudformation deploy 套用該 template。新程式碼 -> 新 checksum -> 新 key -> 偵測到變更。這正是 SAM 所封裝的底層機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"aws cloudformation update-stack still uses the same template referencing the same static S3 key. The CodeUri is unchanged, so the template is identical and CloudFormation detects no change. It also does not perform any local-artifact packaging, so it cannot pick up the newly uploaded code under the same key.","why_zh":"aws cloudformation update-stack 仍使用指向相同靜態 S3 key 的相同 template。CodeUri 未變更，template 完全相同，CloudFormation 偵測不到變更；它也不會執行任何本機檔案 packaging，因此無法擷取上傳到相同 key 的新程式碼。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"aws cloudformation update-stack-instances is a StackSets command used to update stack instances across multiple accounts/Regions in a stack set. It is the wrong tool entirely for a single SAM/CloudFormation stack and does not address the no-changes-detected root cause.","why_zh":"aws cloudformation update-stack-instances 是 StackSets 指令，用於更新跨多個帳戶/區域的 stack 集合中的 stack 執行個體。對於單一 SAM/CloudFormation stack 而言完全是錯誤的工具，也無法解決偵測不到變更的根本原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Even after changing CodeUri to a local folder, aws cloudformation create-change-set / execute-change-set do NOT perform local-artifact packaging. They cannot resolve a local-folder CodeUri (that is the job of sam package / aws cloudformation package). Without a packaging step to upload the new code and rewrite the template to a new S3 key, the new code is never uploaded and the change is not deployed. A package step is missing from this workflow.","why_zh":"即使把 CodeUri 改為本機資料夾，aws cloudformation create-change-set / execute-change-set 也「不會」執行本機檔案 packaging，無法解析指向本機資料夾的 CodeUri（那是 sam package / aws cloudformation package 的工作）。缺少 packaging 步驟來上傳新程式碼並把 template 改寫為新的 S3 key，新程式碼永遠不會被上傳，變更也不會被部署。此流程缺少 package 步驟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-lambda-function-code.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/deploy-upload-local-files.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-cli-package.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/sam-cli-command-reference-sam-deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/sam-cli-command-reference-sam-package.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":257,"question_en":"A company runs its container workloads in AWS App Runner. A DevOps engineer manages the company's container repository in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). The DevOps engineer must implement a solution that continuously monitors the container repository. The solution must create a new container image when the solution detects an operating system vulnerability or language package vulnerability. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS App Runner 上运行其容器工作负载。一位 DevOps 工程师负责管理公司位于亚马逊弹 性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中的容器仓库。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个持续监控容器仓库的解决方案。该解决方案在检测到操作系统漏洞或语言 包漏洞时，必须创建一个新的容器镜像。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use EC2 Image Builder to create a container image pipeline. Use Amazon ECR as the target repository. Turn on enhanced scanning on the ECR repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture an Inspector2 finding event. Use the event to invoke the image pipeline. Re-upload the container to the repository.","B":"Use EC2 Image Builder to create a container image pipeline. Use Amazon ECR as the target repository. Enable Amazon GuardDuty Malware Protection on the container workload. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture a GuardDuty finding event. Use the event to invoke the image pipeline.","C":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project to create a container image. Use Amazon ECR as the target repository. Turn on basic scanning on the repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture an ECR image action event. Use the event to invoke the CodeBuild project. Re-upload the container to the repository.","D":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project to create a container image. Use Amazon ECR as the target repository. Configure AWS Systems Manager Compliance to scan all managed nodes. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture a configuration compliance state change event. Use the event to invoke the CodeBuild project."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建一个容器镜像流水线。将 Amazon ECR 用作目标存储库。在 ECR 存储 库上启用增强扫描。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获 Inspector2 发现事件。使用该事件调 用镜像流水线。将容器重新上传到存储库。","B":"使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建一个容器镜像流水线。将 Amazon ECR 用作目标存储库。在容器工 作负载上启用 Amazon GuardDuty 恶意软件防护。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获 GuardDuty 发现事件。使用该事件调用镜像流水线。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目以生成容器镜像。将 Amazon ECR 用作目标存储库。在该存储库上启 用基本扫描。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获 ECR 镜像操作事件。使用该事件调用 CodeBuild 项目。将容器重新上传到存储库。","D":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目以生成容器镜像。将 Amazon ECR 用作目标存储库。配置 AWS Systems Manager Compliance 以扫描所有托管节点。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获配置 合规性状态更改事件。使用该事件调用 CodeBuild 项目。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: continuously monitor the ECR repository, detect BOTH operating system AND programming language package vulnerabilities, and trigger a new container image build. Amazon ECR enhanced scanning integrates with Amazon Inspector and is the only ECR scan type that provides continuous (continuous scan) coverage of both OS and programming-language package vulnerabilities. AWS docs state that with enhanced scanning, 'As new vulnerabilities appear, the scan results are updated and Amazon Inspector emits an event to EventBridge to notify you.' Option A captures that Inspector2 finding event with an EventBridge rule and uses it to invoke an EC2 Image Builder container image pipeline (which can build Docker container images and distribute them to ECR), rebuilding and re-uploading a patched image. This satisfies every requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求為:持續監控 ECR 儲存庫、同時偵測作業系統(OS)與程式語言套件(language package)漏洞,並在偵測到漏洞時建立新的容器映像。Amazon ECR enhanced scanning 整合 Amazon Inspector,是唯一能對 OS 與語言套件漏洞提供持續(continuous scan)掃描的 ECR 掃描類型。AWS 文件指出:在 enhanced scanning 下,『當新漏洞出現時,掃描結果會更新,Amazon Inspector 會向 EventBridge 發出事件通知您』。選項 A 以 EventBridge 規則捕捉該 Inspector2 finding 事件,並用它觸發 EC2 Image Builder 容器映像 pipeline(可建置 Docker 容器映像並發佈到 ECR),重新建置並上傳修補後的映像,完全符合所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"GuardDuty Malware Protection detects malware in container/EC2/EBS volumes, not operating-system or programming-language package CVE vulnerabilities. It is the wrong detection mechanism for the stated requirement.","why_zh":"GuardDuty Malware Protection 偵測的是惡意軟體(malware),而非作業系統或程式語言套件的 CVE 漏洞,偵測機制與需求不符。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ECR basic scanning only performs OS scans (no programming-language package vulnerabilities) and only on manual/scan-on-push frequency, so it is not continuous monitoring. Also an 'ECR image action event' relates to push/delete actions, not vulnerability findings.","why_zh":"ECR basic scanning 只做 OS 掃描(無程式語言套件漏洞),且僅支援 manual / scan-on-push,並非持續監控;且『ECR image action event』是 push/delete 等動作事件,而非漏洞 finding 事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager Compliance scans managed nodes (EC2/on-prem instances), not container images stored in ECR. A Config compliance state-change event is unrelated to container image vulnerabilities, so it does not monitor the repository.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Compliance 掃描的是受管節點(EC2/地端執行個體),而非儲存在 ECR 的容器映像;Config 合規狀態變更事件與容器映像漏洞無關,無法監控該儲存庫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/ecr-eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/start-build-container-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/enable-disable-scanning-ecr.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":258,"question_en":"A company wants to use AWS Systems Manager documents to bootstrap physical laptops for developers. The bootstrap code is stored in GitHub. A DevOps engineer has already created a Systems Manager activation, installed the Systems Manager agent with the registration code, and installed an activation ID on all the laptops. Which set of steps should be taken next?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用 AWS 系统管理器文档为开发人员的物理笔记本电脑进行初始设置。初始设置代码存 储在 GitHub 上。一位 DevOps 工程师已经创建了一个系统管理器激活码，使用注册码安装了系统管理 器代理，并在所有笔记本电脑上安装了激活 ID。 接下来应该采取哪一系列步骤？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Systems Manager document to use the AWS-RunShellScript command to copy the files from GitHub to Amazon S3, then use the aws-downloadContent plugin with a sourceType of S3.","B":"Configure the Systems Manager document to use the aws-configurePackage plugin with an install action and point to the Git repository.","C":"Configure the Systems Manager document to use the aws-downloadContent plugin with a sourceType of GitHub and sourceInfo with the repository details.","D":"Configure the Systems Manager document to use the aws:softwareInventory plugin and run the script from the Git repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 Systems Manager 文档以使用 AWS-RunShellScript 命令将文件从 GitHub 复制到 Amazon S3，然 后使用源类型为 S3 的 aws-downloadContent 插件。","B":"配置 Systems Manager 文档以使用带有安装操作的 aws-configurePackage 插件，并指向 Git 代码库。","C":"配置 Systems Manager 文档以使用 aws-downloadContent 插件，将 sourceType 设置为 GitHub，并在 sourceInfo 中提供存储库详细信息。","D":"配置 Systems Manager 文档以使用 aws:softwareInventory 插件，并从 Git 存储库运行脚本。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The aws:downloadContent SSM command plugin natively downloads SSM documents and scripts from remote locations, and its sourceType input explicitly supports the values GitHub, Git, HTTP, S3, and SSMDocument. For sourceType GitHub, the sourceInfo StringMap takes the repository details (owner, repository, path, and getOptions for branch/commit). Since the bootstrap code lives in GitHub and the laptops are already registered as hybrid managed instances (activation created, agent installed with registration code and activation ID), the next step is simply to author an SSM document that uses aws:downloadContent with sourceType GitHub and sourceInfo pointing at the repo. This is the direct, AWS-documented mechanism and requires no intermediary S3 copy or custom packaging. Option C matches this exactly.","explanation_zh":"aws:downloadContent SSM 命令外掛程式原生支援從遠端位置下載 SSM 文件與指令碼，其 sourceType 輸入明確支援 GitHub、Git、HTTP、S3 與 SSMDocument 等值。當 sourceType 為 GitHub 時，sourceInfo StringMap 需提供存放庫詳細資訊（owner、repository、path，以及用於指定分支或 commit 的 getOptions）。由於 bootstrap 程式碼存放在 GitHub，且筆電已透過 hybrid activation 註冊為受管執行個體（已建立 activation、安裝 agent 並帶入 registration code 與 activation ID），下一步只需撰寫一份使用 aws:downloadContent、sourceType 設為 GitHub、sourceInfo 指向該存放庫的 SSM 文件即可。這是 AWS 文件記載的直接做法，不需先複製到 S3 或自訂封裝。選項 C 完全符合。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using AWS-RunShellScript to copy files from GitHub to S3 first and then aws:downloadContent with sourceType S3 is an unnecessary multi-step detour; AWS-RunShellScript has no native GitHub fetch and would require custom git/curl logic, when aws:downloadContent already supports sourceType GitHub directly.","why_zh":"先用 AWS-RunShellScript 把檔案從 GitHub 複製到 S3，再用 aws:downloadContent 的 S3 sourceType，是不必要的多步繞路；AWS-RunShellScript 並無原生 GitHub 擷取能力，需自寫 git/curl 邏輯，而 aws:downloadContent 本就直接支援 GitHub sourceType。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"aws:configurePackage installs or uninstalls AWS Systems Manager Distributor packages identified by name (e.g., AWSPVDriver, AmazonCloudWatchAgent, CodeDeployAgent). It cannot point to a Git repository and is not a mechanism for fetching arbitrary GitHub bootstrap code.","why_zh":"aws:configurePackage 用於依名稱安裝或解除安裝 AWS Systems Manager Distributor 套件（如 AWSPVDriver、AmazonCloudWatchAgent、CodeDeployAgent），無法指向 Git 存放庫，並非擷取任意 GitHub bootstrap 程式碼的機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"aws:softwareInventory collects inventory metadata about installed applications, files, network config, and so on; it is a data-gathering plugin and cannot run a script pulled from a Git repository.","why_zh":"aws:softwareInventory 用於收集已安裝應用程式、檔案、網路設定等的盤點中繼資料，屬於資料蒐集外掛程式，無法執行從 Git 存放庫取得的指令碼。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/documents-command-ssm-plugin-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/documents-running-remote-github-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":259,"question_en":"A company's development team uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy its application resources. The team must use CloudFormation for all changes to the environment. The team cannot use the AWS Management Console or the AWS CLI to make manual changes directly. The team uses a developer IAM role to access the environment. The role is configured with the AdministratorAccess managed IAM policy. The company has created a new CloudFormationDeployment IAM role that has the following policy attached: The company wants to ensure that only CloudFormation can use the new role. The development team cannot make any manual changes to the deployed resources. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"该公司的发展团队使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署其应用程序资源。团队必须对环境的所有变更都使用 CloudFormation，不能直接使用 AWS 管理控制台或 AWS CLI 进行手动更改。 该团队使用开发人员 IAM 角色来访问环境。该角色配置了“管理员访问”托管 IAM 策略。该公司创建了 一个新的 CloudFormationDeployment IAM 角色，并为其附加了以下策略： 该公司希望确保只有 CloudFormation 能够使用新角色。开发团队不得对已部署的资源进行任何手动更改。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Remove the AdministratorAccess policy. Assign the ReadOnlyAccess managed IAM policy to the developer role. Instruct the developers to use the CloudFormationDeployment role as a CloudFormation service role when the developers deploy new stacks.","B":"Update the trust policy of the CloudFormationDeployment role to allow the developer IAM role to assume the CloudFormationDeployment role.","C":"Configure the developer IAM role to be able to get and pass the CloudFormationDeployment role if iam:PassedToService equals cloudformation.amazonaws.com. Configure the CloudFormationDeployment role to allow all cloudformation actions for all resources.","D":"Update the trust policy of the CloudFormationDeployment role to allow the cloudformation.amazonaws.com AWS principal to perform the iam:AssumeRole action.","E":"Remove the AdministratorAccess policy. Assign the ReadOnlyAccess managed IAM policy to the developer role. Instruct the developers to assume the CloudFormationDeployment role when the developers deploy new stacks.","F":"Add an IAM policy to the CloudFormationDeployment role to allow cloudformation:* on all resources. Add a policy that allows the iam:PassRole action for the ARN of the CloudFormationDeployment role if iam:PassedToService equals cloudformation.amazonaws.com."},"options_zh":{"A":"移除“管理员访问”策略。将“只读访问”托管 IAM 策略分配给开发人员角色。指示开发人员在 部署新堆栈时使用“CloudFormation 部署”角色作为 CloudFormation 服务角色。","B":"更新 CloudFormationDeployment 角色的信任策略，允许开发人员 IAM 角色承担 CloudFormationDeployment 角色。","C":"配置开发人员 IAM 角色，使其能够在 iam:PassedToService 等于 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 时获 取并传递 CloudFormationDeployment 角色。配置 CloudFormationDeployment 角色，使其允许对所有 资源执行所有 CloudFormation 操作。","D":"更新 CloudFormationDeployment 角色的信任策略，允许 cloudformation.amazonaws.com AWS 主体执行 iam:AssumeRole 操作。","E":"移除“管理员访问”策略。将“只读访问”托管 IAM 策略分配给开发人员角色。指示开发人员在 部署新堆栈时承担“CloudFormation 部署”角色。","F":"向 CloudFormationDeployment 角色添加一个 IAM 策略，以允许对所有资源执行 cloudformation:* 操作。 添加一个策略，如果 iam:PassedToService 等于 cloudformation.amazonaws.com，则允许对 CloudFormationDeployment 角色的 ARN 执行 iam:PassRole 操作。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the AWS-documented 'CloudFormation service role' pattern for forcing all changes through CloudFormation while applying least privilege. (A) Removing AdministratorAccess and assigning ReadOnlyAccess stops developers from making manual changes through the console/CLI, while instructing them to pass the CloudFormationDeployment role as the CloudFormation service role lets CloudFormation provision resources on their behalf. (D) The service role's trust policy must allow the cloudformation.amazonaws.com service principal to perform sts:AssumeRole (the docs phrase this as iam:AssumeRole/sts:AssumeRole), which guarantees that only CloudFormation, not the developers or other services, can use the role. (F) The developer role needs an identity-based policy granting cloudformation:* plus iam:PassRole on the CloudFormationDeployment role ARN with the iam:PassedToService = cloudformation.amazonaws.com condition; per the CloudFormation service role docs, a principal must have iam:PassRole to specify a service role, and the PassedToService condition restricts the pass target to CloudFormation. Together these three steps deliver least privilege: developers can only read and deploy via CloudFormation, the deployment role's broad permissions are usable only by CloudFormation, and manual changes are blocked.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS 官方文件中的 CloudFormation service role 模式，用於強制所有變更都透過 CloudFormation 進行並落實最小權限。(A) 移除 AdministratorAccess 並改用 ReadOnlyAccess，可阻止開發人員透過主控台或 CLI 手動變更資源；同時指示開發人員在部署時把 CloudFormationDeployment role 當成 CloudFormation service role 傳入，讓 CloudFormation 代為佈建資源。(D) 該 service role 的信任政策必須允許 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 服務 principal 執行 sts:AssumeRole（文件以 iam:AssumeRole/sts:AssumeRole 表示），確保只有 CloudFormation 能使用此角色，開發人員或其他服務都不能。(F) 開發人員 role 需要一個身分政策授予 cloudformation:* 以及針對 CloudFormationDeployment role ARN 的 iam:PassRole，並加上 iam:PassedToService = cloudformation.amazonaws.com 的條件；依文件，principal 必須具備 iam:PassRole 才能指定 service role，而 PassedToService 條件把傳遞目標限制在 CloudFormation。這三步驟共同實現最小權限：開發人員只能讀取並透過 CloudFormation 部署，部署角色的高權限只有 CloudFormation 能使用，手動變更被阻擋。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Allowing the developer IAM role to assume the CloudFormationDeployment role gives developers the role's broad provisioning permissions directly, enabling manual changes and violating the requirement that only CloudFormation can use the role. The service-role pattern uses the cloudformation.amazonaws.com service principal in the trust policy, not the developer role.","why_zh":"讓開發人員 IAM role 能 assume CloudFormationDeployment role，等於把該角色的廣泛佈建權限直接交給開發人員，使其能做手動變更，違反『只有 CloudFormation 能使用此角色』的需求。Service role 模式的信任政策應指定 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 服務 principal，而非開發人員 role。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The PassRole portion is partly right, but configuring the CloudFormationDeployment (service) role to allow 'all cloudformation actions for all resources' is wrong: the service role needs permissions for the underlying stack resources (EC2, S3, etc.), not cloudformation:*. The cloudformation:* actions belong on the developer principal, not the service role.","why_zh":"PassRole 部分大致正確，但將 CloudFormationDeployment（service）role 設為允許『所有 cloudformation 動作、所有資源』是錯的：service role 需要的是佈建底層堆疊資源（EC2、S3 等）的權限，而非 cloudformation:*。cloudformation:* 動作應放在開發人員 principal 上，而非 service role。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Instructing developers to assume the CloudFormationDeployment role grants them the role's provisioning permissions directly, allowing manual changes and breaking the 'only CloudFormation can use the role' rule. The correct flow is to pass the role to CloudFormation as a service role (option A), not to assume it.","why_zh":"指示開發人員去 assume CloudFormationDeployment role，會把該角色的佈建權限直接給開發人員，使其能手動變更，破壞『只有 CloudFormation 能使用此角色』的規則。正確流程是把角色當作 service role 傳給 CloudFormation（選項 A），而非 assume 它。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-iam-servicerole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/least-privilege-cloudformation/service-roles-for-cloudformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_passrole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_iam-passrole-service.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":260,"question_en":"A company is developing a web application's infrastructure using AWS CloudFormation. The database engineering team maintains the database resources in a CloudFormation template, and the software development team maintains the web application resources in a separate CloudFormation template. As the scope of the application grows, the software development team needs to use resources maintained by the database engineering team. However, both teams have their own review and lifecycle management processes that they want to keep. Both teams also require resource-level change-set reviews. The software development team would like to deploy changes to this template using their CI/CD pipeline. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CloudFormation 开发一个网络应用程序的基础设施。数据库工程团队在一个 CloudFormation 模板中维护数据库资源，而软件开发团队则在另一个单独的 CloudFormation 模板中维护网络 应用程序资源。随着 随着应用程序的范围不断扩大，软件开发团队需要使用由数据库工程团队维护的资源。然而，两个团 队都有各自想要保留的审查和生命周期管理流程。两个团队也都需要进行资源级别的变更集审查。软 件开发团队希望使用其 CI/CD 管道来部署对此模板的更改。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a stack export from the database CloudFormation template and import those references into the web application CloudFormation template.","B":"Create a CloudFormation nested stack to make cross-stack resource references and parameters available in both stacks.","C":"Create a CloudFormation stack set to make cross-stack resource references and parameters available in both stacks.","D":"Create input parameters in the web application CloudFormation template and pass resource names and IDs from the database stack."},"options_zh":{"A":"从数据库 CloudFormation 模板创建一个堆栈导出，并将这些引用导入到 Web 应用程序 CloudFormation 模板中。","B":"创建一个 CloudFormation 嵌套堆栈，以便在两个堆栈中都能使用跨堆栈资源引用和参数。","C":"创建一个 CloudFormation 堆栈集，以便在两个堆栈中都能使用跨堆栈资源引用和参数。","D":"在 Web 应用程序的 CloudFormation 模板中创建输入参数，并从数据库堆栈传递资源名称和 ID。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario maps almost verbatim to the AWS CloudFormation best practice 'Organize your stacks by lifecycle and ownership' plus 'Use cross-stack references to share values between stacks': a web/application team and a separate database team each own a stack with their own review and lifecycle/release process, and the application stack needs to consume resources owned by the database stack. AWS prescribes cross-stack references for exactly this case: the database (exporting) stack declares values in its Outputs section with the Export field, and the web application (importing) stack consumes them with Fn::ImportValue. This keeps each template separately owned and independently deployable (the software team can deploy the importing template through their own CI/CD pipeline), preserves each team's lifecycle and review processes, and still gives resource-level change-set reviews because each stack is updated via its own change set. Option A is the only choice that describes exporting from the database template and importing those references into the web application template, which is the documented mechanism.","explanation_zh":"此情境幾乎逐字對應到 AWS CloudFormation 最佳實務中的「依生命週期與擁有者組織 stacks」以及「使用 cross-stack references 在 stacks 之間共享值」：一個 web/application 團隊與另一個獨立的 database 團隊各自擁有自己的 stack 與審查、生命週期/發布流程，而 application stack 需要使用 database stack 所擁有的資源。AWS 對此情境明確建議使用 cross-stack references：由 database（匯出端）stack 在 Outputs 區段以 Export 欄位宣告值，web application（匯入端）stack 則以 Fn::ImportValue 取用。如此可讓兩個範本各自獨立擁有與部署（software 團隊可透過自家 CI/CD pipeline 部署匯入端範本），保留各團隊的生命週期與審查流程，且因每個 stack 各自以自己的 change set 更新，仍能提供 resource-level change-set review。選項 A 是唯一描述從 database 範本匯出並將參考匯入 web application 範本的選項，正是文件所載的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A nested stack uses the AWS::CloudFormation::Stack resource to deploy and manage all child stacks as a single unit from one root stack. AWS docs explicitly say nested stacks are for isolating information sharing WITHIN a single nested-stack group managed together; they collapse the two teams into one combined lifecycle and ownership, which directly violates the requirement that each team keep its own separate review and lifecycle processes.","why_zh":"Nested stack 使用 AWS::CloudFormation::Stack 資源，從單一 root stack 將所有子 stack 當成一個整體部署與管理。AWS 文件明言 nested stacks 適用於在同一個共同管理的 nested-stack 群組「內部」共享資訊；它會把兩個團隊併入單一生命週期與擁有權，直接違反各團隊各自保留獨立審查與生命週期流程的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"StackSets are for deploying the same stack across multiple AWS accounts and Regions with one operation. They do not provide a mechanism for one stack to reference another stack's resources, and the scenario is about two different teams' templates in (presumably) one account, not multi-account/multi-Region replication. StackSets do not 'make cross-stack resource references available' as the option claims.","why_zh":"StackSets 用於以單一操作將同一個 stack 部署到多個 AWS 帳戶與區域。它並未提供讓一個 stack 參考另一個 stack 資源的機制，而本情境是兩個不同團隊的範本（推測在同一帳戶內），並非多帳戶/多區域複寫。StackSets 並不會如該選項所稱「讓 cross-stack 資源參考可用」。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Passing resource names and IDs as input parameters technically works, but AWS best practices explicitly call this out as inferior: hardcoding values or passing them as input parameters 'can make templates difficult to reuse or can increase the overhead to get a stack running,' and instead recommends cross-stack references. It also creates no enforced dependency, so the database team could delete or change a referenced resource and break the application stack, whereas Export/ImportValue prevents that. Therefore A is the prescribed, more robust solution.","why_zh":"將資源名稱與 ID 以 input parameters 傳入在技術上可行，但 AWS 最佳實務明確指出此法較差：硬編碼或以 input parameters 傳值「會使範本難以重用或增加啟動 stack 的額外成本」，並建議改用 cross-stack references。此法也不會建立強制相依，database 團隊可能刪除或變更被參考資源而破壞 application stack，而 Export/ImportValue 會阻止此情況。因此 A 才是文件所建議且更穩健的解法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-stack-exports.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/walkthrough-crossstackref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/intrinsic-function-reference-importvalue.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":261,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations. A DevOps engineer needs to maintain multiple AWS accounts that belong to different OUs in the organization. All resources, including IAM policies and Amazon S3 policies within an account, are deployed through AWS CloudFormation. All templates and code are maintained in an AWS CodeCommit repository. Recently, some developers have not been able to access an S3 bucket from some accounts in the organization. The following policy is attached to the S3 bucket: What should the DevOps engineer do to resolve this access issue?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有一个组织架构。一位 DevOps 工程师需要维护该组织中不同组织单位 （OU）所属的多个 AWS 账户。所有资源，包括账户内的 IAM 策略和 Amazon S3 策略，均通过 AWS CloudFormation 进行部署。所有模板和代码都保存在 AWS CodeCommit 代码库中。最近，一些 开发人员无法从组织中的某些账户访问 S3 存储桶。 以下策略已附加到 S3 存储桶： 开发运维工程师应该采取什么措施来解决这个访问问题？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the S3 bucket policy. Turn off the S3 Block Public Access setting on the S3 bucket. In the S3 policy, add the aws:SourceAccount condition. Add the AWS account IDs of all developers who are experiencing the issue.","B":"Verify that no IAM permissions boundaries are denying developers access to the S3 bucket. Make the necessary changes to IAM permissions boundaries. Use an AWS Config recorder in the individual developer accounts that are experiencing the issue to revert any changes that are blocking access. Commit the fix back into the CodeCommit repository. Invoke deployment through CloudFormation to apply the changes.","C":"Configure an SCP that stops anyone from modifying IAM resources in developer OUs. In the S3 policy, add the aws:SourceAccount condition. Add the AWS account IDs of all developers who are experiencing the issue. Commit the fix back into the CodeCommit repository. Invoke deployment through CloudFormation to apply the changes.","D":"Ensure that no SCP is blocking access for developers to the S3 bucket. Ensure that no IAM policy permissions boundaries are denying access to developer IAM users. Make the necessary changes to the SCP and IAM policy permissions boundaries in the CodeCommit repository. Invoke deployment through CloudFormation to apply the changes."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 S3 存储桶策略。关闭 S3 存储桶上的“阻止公共访问”设置。在 S3 策略中添加 aws: SourceAccount 条件。添加所有遇到此问题的开发人员的 AWS 账户 ID。","B":"确认没有 IAM 权限边界阻止开发人员访问 S3 存储桶。对 IAM 权限边界进行必要的更改。在遇到 问题的各个开发人员账户中使用 AWS Config 记录器撤销任何阻止访问的更改。将修复内容提交 回 CodeCommit 存储库。通过 CloudFormation 调用部署以应用更改。","C":"配置一个安全策略（SCP），禁止任何人修改开发人员组织单位（OU）中的 IAM 资源。在 S3 策略 中添加 aws:SourceAccount 条件。添加所有开发人员的 AWS 账户 ID。 遇到此问题。将修复内容提交回 CodeCommit 代码库。通过 CloudFormation 调用部署以应用 更改。","D":"确保没有 SCP 阻止开发人员访问 S3 存储桶。确保没有 IAM 策略权限边界拒绝开发人员 IAM 用 户的访问权限。在 CodeCommit 存储库中对 SCP 和 IAM 策略权限边界进行必要的更改。通过 CloudFormation 调用部署以应用这些更改。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"In AWS Organizations, a principal's effective S3 permissions are the intersection of identity-based policies, SCPs, and (for the IAM user) permissions boundaries, with any explicit Deny in the bucket policy, an SCP, or a permissions boundary overriding an Allow. Because developers in only some accounts/OUs are blocked, the likely culprits are organization-level guardrails (SCPs attached at OU/account level) and/or IAM permissions boundaries that deny access. Option D correctly checks both of these guardrail policy types, then makes the corrective changes in the CodeCommit repository and redeploys them through CloudFormation, which matches the company's established infrastructure-as-code workflow (all IAM and S3 policies are deployed via CloudFormation from CodeCommit). The S3 'Troubleshoot 403' guide lists AWS Organizations policies (SCPs) and IAM/bucket policies among the common causes, and the IAM policy evaluation logic confirms SCP and permissions-boundary denies override allows.","explanation_zh":"在 AWS Organizations 中，主體對 S3 的有效權限是 identity-based policy、SCP 以及（對 IAM user 而言）permissions boundary 三者的交集，且 bucket policy、SCP 或 permissions boundary 中任何一個明確的 Deny 都會覆蓋 Allow。由於只有部分帳戶/OU 的開發者被擋下，最可能的原因是組織層級的護欄（附加在 OU 或帳戶層級的 SCP）和/或 IAM permissions boundary 拒絕了存取。選項 D 正確地同時檢查這兩種護欄政策，然後在 CodeCommit repository 中進行修正並透過 CloudFormation 重新部署，這符合公司既有的 IaC 工作流程（所有 IAM 與 S3 政策皆由 CodeCommit 透過 CloudFormation 部署）。S3 的 403 疑難排解文件將 AWS Organizations policies（SCP）與 IAM/bucket policies 列為常見原因，IAM policy evaluation logic 也確認 SCP 與 permissions boundary 的 Deny 會覆蓋 Allow。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Disabling S3 Block Public Access and adding aws:SourceAccount treats the bucket as needing public access, which is a security anti-pattern and not the root cause. Internal organization developers needing access does not require making the bucket public, and this also bypasses the CodeCommit/CloudFormation workflow.","why_zh":"關閉 S3 Block Public Access 並加入 aws:SourceAccount 等於把 bucket 當成需要公開存取，這是安全反模式，也非根本原因。組織內部開發者需要存取並不代表要把 bucket 設為公開，且此做法繞過了 CodeCommit/CloudFormation 工作流程。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It ignores SCPs entirely and misuses AWS Config: an AWS Config recorder records and evaluates resource configurations but does not by itself revert changes that block access. Remediation is not what a Config recorder does, and the answer omits the SCP guardrail that commonly causes cross-account/OU denials.","why_zh":"完全忽略 SCP 並誤用 AWS Config：AWS Config recorder 只記錄與評估資源組態，本身並不會還原阻擋存取的變更。還原並非 Config recorder 的功能，且此選項遺漏了常造成跨帳戶/OU 拒絕的 SCP 護欄。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP that stops anyone from modifying IAM resources further restricts permissions rather than granting developers S3 access, and adding aws:SourceAccount does not resolve a guardrail-based denial. This makes the access problem worse, not better.","why_zh":"一個阻止任何人修改 IAM 資源的 SCP 只會進一步限制權限，而非授予開發者 S3 存取權；加入 aws:SourceAccount 也無法解決護欄造成的拒絕。此做法只會讓存取問題更嚴重。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/troubleshoot-403-errors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":262,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations for its multi-account environment. A DevOps engineer is developing an AWS CodeArtifact based strategy for application package management across the organization. Each application team at the company has its own account in the organization. Each application team also has limited access to a centralized shared services account. Each application team needs full access to download, publish, and grant access to its own packages. Some common library packages that the application teams use must also be shared with the entire organization. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST administrative overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中为其多账户环境建立了一个组织架构。一位 DevOps 工程师正在为 整个组织开发基于 AWS CodeArtifact 的应用包管理策略。该公司每个应用团队在组织中都有自己的 账户。每个应用团队还对一个集中的共享服务账户拥有有限的访问权限。 每个应用程序团队都需要完全访问权限来下载、发布和授予其自身软件包的访问权限。应用程序 团队使用的某些常见库软件包也必须与整个组织共享。 哪种步骤组合能以最低的管理开销满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a domain in each application team's account. Grant each application team's account full read access and write access to the application team's domain.","B":"Create a domain in the shared services account. Grant the organization read access and CreateRepository access.","C":"Create a repository in each application team’s account. Grant each application team’s account full read access and write access to its own repository.","D":"Create a repository in the shared services account. Grant the organization read access to the repository in the shared services account Set the repository as the upstream repository in each application team's repository.","E":"For teams that require shared packages, create resource-based policies that allow read access to the repository from other application teams' accounts.","F":"Set the other application teams' repositories as upstream repositories."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个应用团队的账户中创建一个域。授予每个应用团队的账户对其所属域的完全读取访问权限 和写入访问权限。","B":"在共享服务账户中创建一个域。授予该组织读取权限和创建存储库权限。","C":"在每个应用团队的账户中创建一个代码库。授予每个应用团队的账户对其自身代码库的完全读取权 限和写入权限。","D":"在共享服务账户中创建一个代码库。授予组织对该共享服务账户中代码库的读取权限。将 该代码库设置为每个应用团队代码库的上游代码库。","E":"对于需要共享包的团队，请创建基于资源的策略，允许其他应用程序团队的账户从存储库读取内 容。","F":"将其他应用程序团队的代码库设置为上游代码库。"},"answer":["B","C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeArtifact recommends a single production domain for the whole organization so packages can be discovered and shared, and upstream relationships only work between repositories that are members of the SAME domain. (B) Create one domain in the shared services account and attach a domain policy that uses the aws:PrincipalOrgID condition to grant the entire organization GetAuthorizationToken (read) and CreateRepository access; this is the documented, lowest-overhead pattern for letting all org accounts use a shared domain. (C) Each team uses its CreateRepository grant to create and own a repository in that shared domain; by default the repository owner has full access to download, publish, and manage the repository's resource policy (grant access) to its own packages, with no extra configuration. (D) For the common library packages, create one repository in the shared services account, grant the organization read access, and set it as an upstream repository on each team's repository. Because upstream package versions are exposed through the downstream repository's single endpoint, all teams consume the shared libraries automatically with minimal ongoing administration. A (a domain per team) breaks the single-domain recommendation and the cross-domain upstream sharing while multiplying admin work; E (per-team resource-based read policies) and F (cross-meshing every team's repo as upstream of every other) both create O(N^2) manual sharing instead of the single centralized upstream, so they add far more administrative overhead.","explanation_zh":"CodeArtifact 建議整個組織使用單一 production domain，讓套件能跨團隊被發現與共享，而 upstream 關係只能在「同一個 domain」內的 repository 之間建立。(B) 在 shared services 帳號建立一個 domain，並使用 aws:PrincipalOrgID 條件鍵的 domain policy 授予整個 organization GetAuthorizationToken（讀取）與 CreateRepository 權限；這正是官方文件記載、管理負擔最低的做法，讓組織內所有帳號都能使用共享 domain。(C) 各應用團隊利用 CreateRepository 權限在該共享 domain 內建立並擁有自己的 repository；預設情況下 repository 擁有者即擁有下載、發布及管理該 repository resource policy（授權他人存取）的完整權限，毋須額外設定。(D) 對於共用函式庫套件，在 shared services 帳號建立一個 repository，授予 organization 讀取權限，並將其設定為每個團隊 repository 的 upstream repository。由於 upstream 的套件版本會透過下游 repository 的單一 endpoint 自動暴露，所有團隊即可自動取得共用函式庫，後續管理成本極低。A（每個團隊各建一個 domain）違反單一 domain 建議，破壞跨 domain 的 upstream 共享並大幅增加管理工作；E（為每個團隊建立資源型讀取政策）與 F（讓每個團隊互設彼此 repository 為 upstream）都會造成 O(N^2) 的手動共享，而非單一集中式 upstream，管理負擔遠高於正確選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a domain in every team account violates the recommended single-production-domain model, fragments storage/KMS encryption, and breaks upstream sharing because upstream repositories must be in the same domain. It maximizes, not minimizes, administrative overhead.","why_zh":"在每個團隊帳號建立 domain 違反建議的單一 production domain 模型，造成儲存與 KMS 加密分散，且因 upstream repository 必須位於同一 domain 而破壞 upstream 共享，反而使管理負擔最大化。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Per-team resource-based policies that grant read access from each other team's account is manual, pairwise sharing. For org-wide common libraries this is far more administrative overhead than a single centralized upstream repository granted org read access (option D).","why_zh":"為每個團隊建立彼此互相讀取的資源型政策屬於手動、成對的共享方式；對於需要全組織共用的函式庫，這比單一集中式 upstream repository 授予 organization 讀取（選項 D）的管理負擔大得多。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Setting every other team's repositories as upstreams creates an O(N^2) mesh and does not implement the centralized common-library sharing the scenario needs; it greatly increases ongoing administration versus a single shared-services upstream.","why_zh":"將其他所有團隊的 repository 互設為 upstream 會形成 O(N^2) 的網狀結構，且無法實現情境所需的集中式共用函式庫共享，與單一 shared services upstream 相比會大幅增加持續管理成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/codeartifact-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/domain-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repo-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repos-upstream.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/welcome.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":263,"question_en":"A company deploys an application to Amazon EC2 instances. The application runs Amazon Linux 2 and uses AWS CodeDeploy. The application has the following file structure for its code repository: The appspec.yml file has the following contents in the files section: What will the result be for the deployment of the config.txt file?","question_zh":"一家公司将一个应用程序部署到 Amazon EC2 实例上。该应用程序运行 Amazon Linux 2 操作系统， 并使用 AWS CodeDeploy。该应用程序的代码库具有以下文件结构： appspec.yml 文件在 files 部分包含以下内容： 部署 config.txt 文件的结果会怎样？","options_en":{"A":"The config.txt file will be deployed to only /var/www/html/config/config.txt.","B":"The config.txt file will be deployed to /usr/local/src/config.txt and to /var/www/html/config/config.txt.","C":"The config.txt file will be deployed to only /usr/local/src/config.txt.","D":"The config.txt file will be deployed to /usr/local/src/config.txt and to /var/www/html/application/web/ config.txt."},"options_zh":{"A":"config.txt 文件将仅部署到 /var/www/html/config/config.txt 这个位置。","B":"config.txt 文件将被部署到 /usr/local/src/config.txt 以及 /var/www/html/config/config.txt 。","C":"config.txt 文件将仅部署到 /usr/local/src/config.txt 。","D":"config.txt 文件将被部署到 /usr/local/src/config.txt 以及 /var/www/html/application/web/config.txt 。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question text is corrupted by vendor watermark text that mangled the appspec.yml files section and the option path strings. This is a known DOP-C02 question whose canonical files section is: (1) source: config/config.txt -> destination: /usr/local/src, and (2) source: / -> destination: /var/www/html/application/web. Per the AppSpec 'files' section reference, when source points to a file and destination is a directory, the file is copied as destination/<filename>, so entry 1 places it at /usr/local/src/config.txt (exactly mirroring the doc's own example source: Config/config.txt -> destination: /webapps/Config => /webapps/Config/config.txt). Entry 2 uses source: / (single slash), which copies ALL files in the revision to the destination while preserving their relative paths, so config/config.txt lands at /var/www/html/application/web/config/config.txt. Thus config.txt is deployed to TWO locations, which matches the intent of option B (the two-destination option whose first path is /usr/local/src/config.txt). The dump-suggested answer B is correct.","explanation_zh":"題目文字被販售浮水印污染,破壞了 appspec.yml files 區段與選項中的路徑字串。這是已知的 DOP-C02 題,其原始 files 區段為:(1) source: config/config.txt -> destination: /usr/local/src,(2) source: / -> destination: /var/www/html/application/web。依 AppSpec 'files' section 文件,當 source 指向單一檔案而 destination 為目錄時,檔案會被複製為 destination/<檔名>,因此第一筆會放到 /usr/local/src/config.txt(完全對應文件自身範例 source: Config/config.txt -> destination: /webapps/Config => /webapps/Config/config.txt)。第二筆使用 source: /(單一斜線),會將 revision 中所有檔案複製到 destination 並保留其相對路徑,所以 config/config.txt 會落在 /var/www/html/application/web/config/config.txt。因此 config.txt 被部署到兩個位置,符合選項 B(兩個目的地、且第一個路徑為 /usr/local/src/config.txt 的選項)。dump 建議答案 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Claims the file is deployed to only ONE location. Both files entries copy config.txt (the explicit file mapping and the '/' whole-revision copy), so it lands in two places, not one.","why_zh":"宣稱只部署到一個位置。兩筆 files 設定都會複製 config.txt(明確檔案對應與「/」整份 revision 複製),因此會落在兩個位置而非一個。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Lists only /usr/local/src/config.txt and ignores the second files entry (source: /) that also copies the file under /var/www/html/application/web, so it understates the result to a single location.","why_zh":"只列出 /usr/local/src/config.txt,忽略第二筆 files 設定(source: /)也會把該檔複製到 /var/www/html/application/web 之下,因此低估為單一位置。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Correctly identifies two locations but gets the second path wrong: a source of '/' preserves relative paths, so config/config.txt copies to /var/www/html/application/web/config/config.txt, NOT /var/www/html/application/web/config.txt (it does not flatten away the config/ subdirectory).","why_zh":"正確指出兩個位置,但第二個路徑錯誤:source 為「/」會保留相對路徑,因此 config/config.txt 會複製到 /var/www/html/application/web/config/config.txt,而非 /var/www/html/application/web/config.txt(不會把 config/ 子目錄壓平移除)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-files.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/application-revisions-plan.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":264,"question_en":"A company has set up AWS CodeArtifact repositories with public upstream repositories. The company's development team consumes open source dependencies from the repositories in the company's internal network. The company's security team recently discovered a critical vulnerability in the most recent version of a package that the development team consumes. The security team has produced a patched version to fix the vulnerability. The company needs to prevent the vulnerable version from being downloaded. The company also needs to allow the security team to publish the patched version. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司已设置了带有公共上游存储库的 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。该公司的开发团队从公司内部网 络中的这些存储库获取开源依赖项。 该公司安全团队最近在开发团队使用的最新版本的一个软件包中发现了一个严重漏洞。安全团队已制 作出修复该漏洞的补丁版本。公司需要阻止易受攻击的版本被下载。公司还需要允许安全团队发布补 丁版本。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the status of the affected CodeArtifact package version to unlisted.","B":"Update the status of the affected CodeArtifact package version to deleted.","C":"Update the status of the affected CodeArtifact package version to archived.","D":"Update the CodeArtifact package origin control settings to allow direct publishing and to block upstream operations.","E":"Update the CodeArtifact package origin control settings to block direct publishing and to allow upstream operations."},"options_zh":{"A":"将受影响的 CodeArtifact 包版本的状态更新为“未列出”。","B":"将受影响的 CodeArtifact 包版本的状态更新为已删除。","C":"将受影响的 CodeArtifact 包版本的状态更新为已归档。","D":"更新 CodeArtifact 包源代码控制设置，以允许直接发布并阻止上游操作。","E":"更新 CodeArtifact 包源代码控制设置，以阻止直接发布并允许上游操作。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":265,"question_en":"A company is running a custom-built application that processes records. All the components run on Amazon EC2 instances that run in an Auto Scaling group. Each record's processing is a multistep sequential action that is compute-intensive. Each step is always completed in 5 minutes or less. A limitation of the current system is that if any steps fail, the application has to reprocess the record from the beginning. The company wants to update the architecture so that the application must reprocess only the failed steps. What is the MOST operationally efficient solution that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在运行一个定制开发的应用程序来处理记录。所有组件都在一个自动扩展组中的亚马 逊 EC2 实例上运行。每条记录的处理是一个多步骤的顺序操作，计算密集型。每个步骤总是能在 5 分钟或更短时间内完成。 当前系统的一个局限性在于，如果任何步骤失败，应用程序就必须从头开始重新处理该记录。公司希 望更新架构，使应用程序只需重新处理失败的步骤。 满足这些要求的最高效的操作解决方案是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create a web application to write records to Amazon S3. Use S3 Event Notifications to publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Use an EC2 instance to poll Amazon SNS and start processing. Save intermediate results to Amazon S3 to pass on to the next step.","B":"Perform the processing steps by using logic in the application. Convert the application code to run in a container. Use AWS Fargate to manage the container instances. Configure the container to invoke itself to pass the state from one step to the next.","C":"Create a web application to pass records to an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Decouple the processing by using the Kinesis data stream and AWS Lambda functions.","D":"Create a web application to pass records to AWS Step Functions. Decouple the processing into Step Functions tasks and AWS Lambda functions."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个网络应用程序，将记录写入亚马逊 S3。使用 S3 事件通知发布到亚马逊简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题。使用 EC2 实例轮询亚马逊 SNS 然后开始处理。将中间结果保存到亚马逊 S3，以便传递给下一步。","B":"在应用程序中使用逻辑执行处理步骤。将应用程序代码转换为在容器中运行。使用 AWS Fargate 来管理 容器实例。配置容器使其能够调用自身，以便将状态从一个步骤传递到下一个步骤。","C":"创建一个网络应用程序，将记录传递到 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。通过使用 Kinesis 数据流和 AWS Lambda 函数来解耦处理过程。","D":"创建一个网络应用程序，将记录传递给 AWS Step Functions。将处理过程分解为 Step Functions 任务和 AWS Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are a multistep, sequential, compute-intensive process where each step finishes in 5 minutes or less, and on failure only the failed step (not the whole record) should be reprocessed, with the MOST operationally efficient solution. AWS Step Functions is purpose-built for exactly this: it orchestrates a series of Task states in sequence, persists the state/output between steps, and provides built-in Retry and Catch error handling so a failed step can be retried (with exponential backoff) without re-running the steps that already succeeded. Decoupling each compute step into its own Lambda function (max 15-minute timeout, comfortably above the 5-minute step duration) and wiring them as Step Functions tasks gives a fully managed, serverless orchestration with per-step failure recovery and no servers to operate. AWS documentation explicitly lists 'sequential processing' and 'complex error handling' (per-step retries, Catch to fallback) as the canonical reasons to orchestrate Lambda with Step Functions, making D both technically correct and the most operationally efficient choice.","explanation_zh":"需求是多步驟、循序、運算密集的處理流程，每個步驟在 5 分鐘以內完成，且失敗時只需重新處理失敗的步驟（而非整筆記錄），並要求最具營運效率的方案。AWS Step Functions 正是為此設計：它以 Task state 循序編排各步驟，於步驟之間保存狀態與輸出，並內建 Retry 與 Catch 錯誤處理，因此失敗的步驟可單獨重試（含指數退避），無須重跑已成功的步驟。將每個運算步驟拆成獨立的 Lambda function（最長 15 分鐘逾時，遠高於 5 分鐘步驟時長），再串成 Step Functions tasks，即可得到完全託管、無伺服器的編排，具備逐步失敗復原能力且無需維運伺服器。AWS 官方文件明確將「sequential processing」與「complex error handling」（逐步重試、Catch 轉至 fallback）列為用 Step Functions 編排 Lambda 的典型理由，因此 D 在技術上正確且最具營運效率。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon SNS is a push pub/sub service and cannot be polled (you poll SQS, not SNS), so 'poll Amazon SNS' is not a valid pattern. Building sequential step orchestration and per-step checkpointing manually on EC2 with S3 intermediate files is brittle and carries high operational overhead, not the most efficient option.","why_zh":"Amazon SNS 是推送式 pub/sub 服務，無法被輪詢（要輪詢的是 SQS 而非 SNS），因此「poll Amazon SNS」並非有效模式。在 EC2 上以 S3 中介檔案手動實作循序步驟編排與逐步檢查點既脆弱又營運負擔高，並非最有效率的方案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Fargate container 'invoking itself to pass state from one step to the next' is not a real orchestration or recovery pattern; there is no managed mechanism to checkpoint progress or retry only the failed step, so a failure still forces reprocessing from the start. It requires substantial custom code and operational effort.","why_zh":"Fargate 容器「呼叫自己以在步驟間傳遞狀態」並非真正的編排或復原模式；沒有任何託管機制可保存進度或只重試失敗步驟，失敗時仍須從頭重跑。此作法需大量自訂程式碼與營運投入。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is for high-throughput, ordered streaming ingestion, not for orchestrating a sequential multistep workflow with per-step failure recovery. Kinesis + Lambda has no native concept of 'reprocess only the failed step'; a failure in step N would not cleanly resume mid-workflow, and you would have to build state tracking yourself.","why_zh":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 用於高吞吐、有序的串流擷取，而非用來編排具逐步失敗復原的循序多步驟工作流。Kinesis + Lambda 沒有「只重新處理失敗步驟」的原生概念；第 N 步失敗無法乾淨地在工作流中途續行，必須自行建構狀態追蹤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-step-functions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/concepts-error-handling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/tutorial-handling-error-conditions.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":266,"question_en":"A company is migrating its on-premises Windows applications and Linux applications to AWS. The company will use automation to launch Amazon EC2 instances to mirror the on-premises configurations. The migrated applications require access to shared storage that uses SMB for Windows and NFS for Linux. The company is also creating a pilot light disaster recovery (DR) environment in another AWS Region. The company will use automation to launch and configure the EC2 instances in the DR Region. The company needs to replicate the storage to the DR Region. Which storage solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其本地的 Windows 应用程序和 Linux 应用程序迁移到 AWS。该公司将使用自动化来启动 Amazon EC2 实例以复制本地配置。迁移后的应用程序需要访问共享存储，其中 Windows 使用 SMB 协议， Linux 使用 NFS 协议。 该公司还在另一个 AWS 区域创建了一个试点的轻量级灾难恢复（DR）环境。该公司将使用自动化来在 DR 区域启动和配置 EC2 实例。该公司需要将存储复制到 DR 区域。 哪种存储方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon S3 for the application storage. Create an S3 bucket in the primary Region and an S3 bucket in the DR Region. Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the primary Region to the DR Region.","B":"Use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) for the application storage. Create a backup plan in AWS Backup that creates snapshots of the EBS volumes that are in the primary Region and replicates the snapshots to the DR Region.","C":"Use a Volume Gateway in AWS Storage Gateway for the application storage. Configure Cross-Region Replication (CRR) of the Volume Gateway from the primary Region to the DR Region.","D":"Use Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP for the application storage. Create an FSx for ONTAP instance in the DR Region. Configure NetApp SnapMirror replication from the primary Region to the DR Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"为应用程序存储使用亚马逊 S3。在主区域创建一个 S3 存储桶，在灾难恢复区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。 配置从主区域到灾难恢复区域的 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。","B":"为应用程序存储使用亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）。在 AWS 备份中创建一个备份计划，该计划对 主区域中的 EBS 卷创建快照，并将快照复制到灾难恢复区域。","C":"在 AWS 存储网关中使用卷网关作为应用程序存储。配置卷网关从主区域到灾难恢复区域的跨区域复制 （CRR）。","D":"使用 Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 作为应用程序存储。在灾难恢复区域创建一个 FSx for ONTAP 实例。 从主区域配置 NetApp SnapMirror 复制到灾难恢复区域。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive requirement is shared storage that simultaneously serves SMB for Windows applications and NFS for Linux applications, plus replication to a DR Region for a pilot light setup. Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP is the only listed option that natively provides multiprotocol file access (NFS, SMB, iSCSI, NVMe) from a single file system, so both Windows and Linux EC2 instances can mount the same shared storage. FSx for ONTAP also supports NetApp SnapMirror replication for cross-Region deployments, replicating to a second FSx for ONTAP file system in the DR Region to meet RPO/RTO targets. This directly satisfies both the multiprotocol shared-storage and cross-Region DR replication requirements, making D correct.","explanation_zh":"決定性需求是共享儲存必須同時提供給 Windows 應用程式使用的 SMB 以及給 Linux 應用程式使用的 NFS，並且要複寫到 DR Region 以建立 pilot light 環境。Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 是唯一原生支援多協定檔案存取（NFS、SMB、iSCSI、NVMe）的選項，單一檔案系統即可讓 Windows 與 Linux EC2 執行個體掛載同一份共享儲存。FSx for ONTAP 也支援 NetApp SnapMirror 跨 Region 複寫，將資料複寫到 DR Region 的第二個 FSx for ONTAP 檔案系統以滿足 RPO/RTO。因此 D 同時滿足多協定共享儲存與跨 Region DR 複寫需求，為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon S3 is object storage accessed via API/HTTPS, not a file share. It does not present SMB or NFS mounts that on-premises-style Windows and Linux applications can use as shared storage without re-architecting the applications. CRR replicates objects but the protocol requirement fails.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 是透過 API/HTTPS 存取的物件儲存，並非檔案共享，無法提供 SMB 或 NFS 掛載供 Windows 與 Linux 應用程式直接當共享儲存使用，除非重寫應用程式。CRR 雖能複寫物件，但不符合協定需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon EBS volumes are block storage attached to a single EC2 instance and do not provide SMB or NFS shared file access across Windows and Linux clients. AWS Backup can copy EBS snapshots cross-Region, but the core shared-storage multiprotocol requirement is not met.","why_zh":"Amazon EBS 是掛載到單一 EC2 執行個體的區塊儲存，無法跨 Windows 與 Linux 用戶端提供 SMB 或 NFS 共享檔案存取。AWS Backup 雖能跨 Region 複製 EBS 快照，但無法滿足核心的多協定共享儲存需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Storage Gateway Volume Gateway presents iSCSI block volumes, not SMB/NFS file shares (that is the File Gateway type, and even File Gateway does not offer simultaneous SMB+NFS the way ONTAP does). There is also no native Volume Gateway 'Cross-Region Replication' feature as described, so it does not meet either requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Storage Gateway 的 Volume Gateway 提供的是 iSCSI 區塊磁碟區，而非 SMB/NFS 檔案共享（檔案共享是 File Gateway 類型，且 File Gateway 也無法像 ONTAP 那樣同時提供 SMB+NFS）。同時也沒有題目所述的 Volume Gateway 原生跨 Region 複寫功能，因此兩項需求皆不符合。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/what-is-fsx-ontap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/scheduled-replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/how-it-works-fsx-ontap.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":267,"question_en":"A company's application uses a fleet of Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances to analyze and process data. The EC2 instances are in an Auto Scaling group. The Auto Scaling group is a target group for an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The application analyzes critical data that cannot tolerate interruption. The application also analyzes noncritical data that can withstand interruption. The critical data analysis requires quick scalability in response to real-time application demand. The noncritical data analysis involves memory consumption. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that reduces scale-out latency for the critical data. The solution also must process the noncritical data. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序使用一组亚马逊 EC2 按需实例来分析和处理数据。这些 EC2 实例位于一个自动扩展组 中。该自动扩展组是应用负载均衡器（ALB）的目标组。该应用程序分析关键数据，这些数据不能容忍中 断。该应用程序还分析非关键数据，这些数据可以承受中断。 关键数据的分析需要能够快速扩展以响应实时应用需求。非关键数据的分析涉及内存消耗。开发运维工 程师必须实施一种解决方案，以降低关键数据的横向扩展延迟。该解决方案还必须处理非关键数据。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"For the critical data, modify the existing Auto Scaling group. Create a warm pool instance in the stopped state. Define the warm pool size. Create a new version of the launch template that has detailed monitoring enabled. Use Spot Instances.","B":"For the critical data, modify the existing Auto Scaling group. Create a warm pool instance in the stopped state. Define the warm pool size. Create a new version of the launch template that has detailed monitoring enabled. Use On-Demand Instances.","C":"For the critical data, modify the existing Auto Scaling group. Create a lifecycle hook to ensure that bootstrap scripts are completed successfully. Ensure that the application on the instances is ready to accept traffic before the instances are registered. Create a new version of the launch template that has detailed monitoring enabled.","D":"For the noncritical data, create a second Auto Scaling group that uses a launch template. Configure the launch template to install the unified Amazon CloudWatch agent and to configure the CloudWatch agent with a custom memory utilization metric. Use Spot Instances. Add the new Auto Scaling group as the target group for the ALB. Modify the application to use two target groups for critical data and noncritical data.","E":"For the noncritical data, create a second Auto Scaling group. Choose the predefined memory utilization metric type for the target tracking scaling policy. Use Spot Instances. Add the new Auto Scaling group as the target group for the ALB. Modify the application to use two target groups for critical data and noncritical data."},"options_zh":{"A":"对于关键数据，请修改现有的自动扩展组。创建处于停止状态的预热池实例。定义预热池大小。 创建启用详细监控的新版本启动模板。使用竞价型实例。","B":"对于关键数据，请修改现有的自动扩展组。创建处于停止状态的预热池实例。定义预热池的大小。 创建新的启动模板版本，该版本具有 详细监控已启用。使用按需实例。","C":"对于关键数据，请修改现有的自动扩展组。创建一个生命周期挂钩，以确保引导脚本成功完成。在 实例注册之前，请确保实例上的应用程序已准备好接受流量。创建一个新版本的启动模板，启用 详细监控。","D":"对于非关键数据，创建一个使用启动模板的第二个自动扩展组。配置启动模板以安装统一的 Amazon CloudWatch 代理，并使用自定义内存利用率指标配置 CloudWatch 代理。使用竞价型实例。 将新的自动扩展组添加为 ALB 的目标组。修改应用程序以针对关键数据和非关键数据使用两个目 标组。","E":"对于非关键数据，创建第二个自动扩展组。为目标跟踪扩展策略选择预定义的内存利用率指标类型。 使用竞价型实例。将新的自动扩展组添加为 ALB 的目标组。修改应用程序以使用两个目标组分别 处理关键数据和非关键数据。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question has two independent requirements. (1) Critical data cannot tolerate interruption and needs reduced scale-out latency: a warm pool of pre-initialized instances in the Stopped state accelerates scale-out for long-boot applications, and because the data cannot be interrupted the instances must be On-Demand (Spot can be reclaimed). That is exactly option B; option A is identical except it uses Spot, which violates the no-interruption requirement (and warm pools don't even support Spot in mixed instance groups). Option C uses a lifecycle hook, which makes instances wait until bootstrap completes before serving traffic and actually adds delay rather than reducing scale-out latency. (2) Noncritical data tolerates interruption (so Spot is appropriate) and must scale on memory consumption. EC2 Auto Scaling target tracking supports only four predefined metrics (ASGAverageCPUUtilization, ASGAverageNetworkIn, ASGAverageNetworkOut, ALBRequestCountPerTarget) - there is no predefined memory metric - so memory must be collected by the unified CloudWatch agent as a custom metric. That is option D; option E is wrong because no predefined memory utilization metric exists for EC2 Auto Scaling.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個獨立需求。(1) Critical data 不能中斷且需要降低 scale-out 延遲：使用處於 Stopped 狀態的 warm pool 預先初始化執行個體可加速長開機時間應用的擴展，而由於資料不可中斷，執行個體必須使用 On-Demand（Spot 可能被回收）。這正是選項 B；選項 A 唯一差別是使用 Spot，違反不可中斷的需求（且 warm pool 在 mixed instance group 中根本不支援 Spot）。選項 C 使用 lifecycle hook，會讓執行個體等到 bootstrap 完成才接收流量，實際上增加而非降低 scale-out 延遲。(2) Noncritical data 可容忍中斷（適合 Spot）且須依記憶體使用量擴展。EC2 Auto Scaling target tracking 只支援四個 predefined metric（ASGAverageCPUUtilization、ASGAverageNetworkIn、ASGAverageNetworkOut、ALBRequestCountPerTarget），沒有記憶體 predefined metric，因此記憶體必須由 unified CloudWatch agent 以 custom metric 收集，即選項 D；選項 E 錯誤，因為 EC2 Auto Scaling 並不存在 predefined memory utilization metric。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Critical data cannot tolerate interruption, but Spot Instances can be reclaimed by AWS at any time, breaking the requirement. Warm pools also do not support Spot Instances in mixed instance groups.","why_zh":"Critical data 不可中斷，但 Spot Instances 隨時可能被 AWS 回收，違反需求。Warm pool 在 mixed instance group 中也不支援 Spot Instances。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A lifecycle hook holds instances in a pending state until bootstrap completes before registering them, which adds latency. It does not pre-initialize a pool of ready instances, so it does not reduce scale-out latency the way a warm pool does.","why_zh":"Lifecycle hook 會讓執行個體在註冊前停留於 pending 狀態直到 bootstrap 完成，反而增加延遲。它不會預先初始化一批就緒的執行個體，因此無法像 warm pool 那樣降低 scale-out 延遲。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"EC2 Auto Scaling target tracking has no predefined memory utilization metric; only CPU, NetworkIn, NetworkOut, and ALBRequestCountPerTarget are predefined. Memory must be supplied as a custom metric via the CloudWatch agent.","why_zh":"EC2 Auto Scaling target tracking 沒有 predefined memory utilization metric；只有 CPU、NetworkIn、NetworkOut 與 ALBRequestCountPerTarget 為 predefined。記憶體必須透過 CloudWatch agent 以 custom metric 提供。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-warm-pools.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-scaling-target-tracking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/mon-scripts.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":268,"question_en":"A company recently migrated its application to an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster that uses Amazon EC2 instances. The company configured the application to automatically scale based on CPU utilization. The application produces memory errors when it experiences heavy loads. The application also does not scale out enough to handle the increased load. The company needs to collect and analyze memory metrics for the application over time. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近将其应用程序迁移到了一个使用亚马逊 EC2 实例的亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务 （Amazon EKS）集群。该公司配置了应用程序，使其能够根据 CPU 利用率自动扩展。 该应用程序在负载过重时会出现内存错误。此外，该应用程序的横向扩展能力不足，无法应对不断 增加的负载。公司需要收集并分析该应用程序一段时间内的内存指标。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Attach the CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy managed IAM policy to the IAM instance profile that the cluster uses.","B":"Attach the CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy managed IAM policy to a service account role for the cluster.","C":"Collect performance metrics by deploying the unified Amazon CloudWatch agent to the existing EC2 instances in the cluster. Add the agent to the AMI for any new EC2 instances that are added to the cluster.","D":"Collect performance logs by deploying the AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry collector as a DaemonSet.","E":"Analyze the pod_memory_utilization Amazon CloudWatch metric in the ContainerInsights namespace by using the Service dimension.","F":"Analyze the node_memory_utilization Amazon CloudWatch metric in the ContainerInsights namespace by using the ClusterName dimension."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy 管理的 IAM 策略附加到集群使用的 IAM 实例配置文件上。","B":"将 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy 管理的 IAM 策略附加到集群的服务账户角色。","C":"通过在集群中的现有 EC2 实例上部署统一的 Amazon CloudWatch 代理来收集性能指标。对于添 加到集群中的任何新 EC2 实例，将代理添加到 AMI 中。","D":"通过将 AWS OpenTelemetry 分发版收集器部署为守护集来收集性能日志。","E":"使用“服务”维度在 ContainerInsights 命名空间中分析 pod_memory_utilization Amazon CloudWatch 指标。","F":"使用“ClusterName”维度在“ContainerInsights”命名空间中分析 Amazon CloudWatch 的“node_ memory_utilization”指标。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":269,"question_en":"A company's video streaming platform usage has increased from 10,000 users each day to 50,000 users each day in multiple countries. The company deploys the streaming platform on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). The EKS workload scales up to thousands of nodes during peak viewing time. The company's users report occurrences of unauthorized logins. Users also report sudden interruptions and logouts from the platform. The company wants additional security measures for the entire platform. The company also needs a summarized view of the resource behaviors and interactions across the company's entire AWS environment. The summarized view must show login attempts, API calls, and network traffic. The solution must permit network traffic analysis while minimizing the overhead of managing logs. The solution must also quickly investigate any potential malicious behavior that is associated with the EKS workload. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的视频流媒体平台的日活跃用户数已从 10,000 人增加到在多个国家的 50,000 人。该公司将 流媒体平台部署在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上。在观看高峰期，EKS 工作负载会 扩展到数千个节点。 该公司用户报告称出现了未经授权的登录情况。用户还报告称平台会突然中断连接并强制退出。 该公司希望为其整个平台采取更多的安全措施。此外，该公司还需要一个概览，以了解其整个 AWS 资源的行为和交互情况。 环境。汇总视图必须显示登录尝试、 API 调用和网络流量。该解决方案必须允许进行网络流量分析，同 时尽量减少管理日志的开销。该解决方案还必须能够快速调查与 EKS 工作负载相关的任何潜在恶意行 为。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty for EKS Audit Log Monitoring. Enable AWS CloudTrail logs. Store the EKS audit logs and CloudTrail log files in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to create an external table. Use Amazon QuickSight to create a dashboard.","B":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty for EKS Audit Log Monitoring. Enable Amazon Detective in the company's AWS account. Enable EKS audit logs from optional source packages in Detective.","C":"Enable Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights. Enable AWS CloudTrail logs. Store the EKS audit logs and CloudTrail log files in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to create an external table. Use Amazon QuickSight to create a dashboard.","D":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty for EKS Audit Log Monitoring. Enable Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights and VPC Flow Logs. Enable AWS CloudTrail logs."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 以对 EKS 审计日志进行监控。启用 AWS CloudTrail 日志。将 EKS 审计日志 和 CloudTrail 日志文件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon Athena 创建外部表。使用 Amazon QuickSight 创建仪表板。","B":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 对 EKS 审计日志进行监控。在公司的 AWS 账户中启用 Amazon Detective。 在 Detective 中启用来自可选源包的 EKS 审计日志。","C":"启用 Amazon CloudWatch 容器洞察功能。启用 AWS CloudTrail 日志。将 EKS 审计日志和 CloudTrail 日志文件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon Athena 创建外部表。使用 Amazon QuickSight 创 建仪表板。","D":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 对 EKS 审计日志进行监控。启用 Amazon CloudWatch 容器洞察和 VPC 流日志。启用 AWS CloudTrail 日志。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":270,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage hundreds of AWS accounts. The company has a team that is responsible for AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). The IAM team wants to implement AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). The IAM team must have only the minimum needed permissions to manage IAM Identity Center. The IAM team must not be able to gain unneeded access to the Organizations management account. The IAM team must be able to provision new IAM Identity Center permission sets and assignments for existing and new member accounts. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织来管理数百个 AWS 账户。该公司有一个团队负责 AWS 身份和访问管理 （IAM）。 IAM 团队希望实施 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）。IAM 团队必须仅拥有管理 IAM 身份中心 所需的最低权限。IAM 团队不得能够获得对组织管理账户的不必要的访问权限。IAM 团队必须能够为 现有和新成员账户配置新的 IAM 身份中心权限集和分配。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account for the IAM team. In the new account, enable IAM Identity Center. In the Organizations management account, register the new account as a delegated administrator for IAM Identity Center.","B":"Create a new AWS account for the IAM team. In the Organizations management account, enable IAM Identity Center. In the Organizations management account, register the new account as a delegated administrator for IAM Identity Center.","C":"In IAM Identity Center, create users and a group for the IAM team. Add the users to the group. Create a new permission set. Attach the AWSSSODirectoryAdministrator managed IAM policy to the group.","D":"In IAM Identity Center, create users and a group for the IAM team. Add the users to the group. Create a new permission set. Attach the AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator managed IAM policy to the group.","E":"Assign the permission set to the Organizations management account. Allow the IAM team group to use the permission set.","F":"Assign the permission set to the new AWS account. Allow the IAM team group to use the permission set."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 IAM 团队创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在新账户中启用 IAM 身份中心。在组织管理账户中，将新 账户注册为 IAM 身份中心的委托管理员。","B":"为 IAM 团队创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在组织管理账户中，启用 IAM 身份中心。在组织管理账户中， 将新账户注册为 IAM 身份中心的委托管理员。","C":"在 IAM 身份中心，为 IAM 团队创建用户和一个组。将用户添加到该组。创建一个新的权限集。将 AWSSSODirectoryAdministrator 管理的 IAM 策略附加到该组。","D":"在 IAM 身份中心，为 IAM 团队创建用户和一个组。将用户添加到该组。创建一个新的权限集。将 AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator 管理的 IAM 策略附加到该组。","E":"将权限集分配给组织管理账户。允许 IAM 团队组使用该权限集。","F":"将权限集分配给新的 AWS 账户。允许 IAM 团队组使用该权限集。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":271,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled. The company uses AWS Backup in a primary account and uses an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key to encrypt the backups. The company needs to automate a cross-account backup of the resources that AWS Backup backs up in the primary account. The company configures cross-account backup in the Organizations management account. The company creates a new AWS account in the organization and configures an AWS Backup backup vault in the new account. The company creates a KMS key in the new account to encrypt the backups. Finally, the company configures a new backup plan in the primary account. The destination for the new backup plan is the backup vault in the new account. When the AWS Backup job in the primary account is invoked, the job creates backups in the primary account. However, the backups are not copied to the new account's backup vault. Which combination of steps must the company take so that backups can be copied to the new account's backup vault? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用了 AWS 组织中的一个组织单元，该组织单元启用了所有功能。该公司在一个主账户中使 用 AWS 备份服务，并使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥对备份进行加密。 该公司需要对 AWS Backup 在主账户中备份的资源实现跨账户备份。该公司在组织管理账户中配置跨 账户备份。该公司在组织中创建了一个新的 AWS 账户，并在新账户中配置了一个 AWS Backup 备份 存储库。该公司在新账户中创建了一个 KMS 密钥来加密备份。最后，该公司在主账户中配置了一个新 的备份计划。新备份计划的目标是新账户中的备份存储库。 当主账户中的 AWS 备份作业被调用时，该作业会在主账户中创建备份。然而，这些备份不会被复 制到新账户的备份库中。 公司必须采取哪两种步骤组合才能将备份复制到新账户的备份库中？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Edit the backup vault access policy in the new account to allow access to the primary account.","B":"Edit the backup vault access policy in the primary account to allow access to the new account.","C":"Edit the backup vault access policy in the primary account to allow access to the KMS key in the new account.","D":"Edit the key policy of the KMS key in the primary account to share the key with the new account.","E":"Edit the key policy of the KMS key in the new account to share the key with the primary account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在新账户中编辑备份库访问策略，以允许访问主账户。","B":"在主账户中编辑备份库访问策略，以允许新账户访问。","C":"在主账户中编辑备份库访问策略，以允许访问新账户中的 KMS 密钥。","D":"在主账户中编辑 KMS 密钥的关键策略，以与新账户共享该密钥。","E":"在新账户中编辑 KMS 密钥的关键策略，以与主账户共享该密钥。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":272,"question_en":"A company runs an application that uses an Amazon S3 bucket to store images. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a multi-Region strategy for the objects that are stored in the S3 bucket. The company needs to be able to fail over to an S3 bucket in another AWS Region. When an image is added to either S3 bucket, the image must be replicated to the other S3 bucket within 15 minutes. The DevOps engineer enables two-way replication between the S3 buckets. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take next to meet the requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司运行的应用程序使用 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储图像。一位 DevOps 工程师需要为存储在 S3 存储 桶中的对象实施多区域策略。该公司需要能够故障转移到另一个 AWS 区域的 S3 存储桶。当图像被添加 到任一 S3 存储桶时，必须在 15 分钟内将该图像复制到另一个 S3 存储桶。 DevOps 工程师在两个 S3 存储桶之间实现了双向复制。 为了满足要求，DevOps 工程师接下来应采取哪三种步骤的组合？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable S3 Replication Time Control (S3 RTC) on each replication rule.","B":"Create an S3 Multi-Region Access Point in an active-passive configuration.","C":"Call the SubmitMultiRegionAccessPointRoutes operation in the AWS API when the company needs to fail over to the S3 bucket in the other Region.","D":"Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration on both S3 buckets.","E":"Configure a routing control in Amazon Route 53 Recovery Controller. Add the S3 buckets in an active- passive configuration.","F":"Call the UpdateRoutingControlStates operation in the AWS API when the company needs to fail over to the S3 bucket in the other Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个复制规则上启用 S3 复制时间控制（S3 RTC）。","B":"创建一个处于主备配置的 S3 多区域访问点。","C":"当公司需要故障转移到另一个区域的 S3 存储桶时，请调用 AWS API 中的 SubmitMultiRegionAccessP ointRoutes 操作。","D":"在两个 S3 存储桶上启用 S3 传输加速功能。","E":"在 Amazon Route 53 恢复控制器中配置路由控制。以主备配置添加 S3 存储桶。","F":"当公司需要故障转移到另一个区域的 S3 存储桶时，在 AWS API 中调用 UpdateRoutingControlStates 操 作。"},"answer":["A","B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":273,"question_en":"A company uses the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) to define its application. The company uses a pipeline that consists of AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild to deploy the CDK application. The company wants to introduce unit tests to the pipeline to test various infrastructure components. The company wants to ensure that a deployment proceeds if no unit tests result in a failure. Which combination of steps will enforce the testing requirement in the pipeline? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）来定义其应用程序。该公司使用由 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 组成的管道来部署 CDK 应用程序。 该公司希望在流水线中引入单元测试来测试各种基础设施组件。该公司希望确保在没有单元测试失败 的情况下进行部署。 在管道中，哪两种步骤组合可以强制执行测试要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the CodeBuild build phase commands to run the tests then to deploy the application. Set the OnFailure phase property to ABORT.","B":"Update the CodeBuild build phase commands to run the tests then to deploy the application. Add the -- rollback true flag to the cdk deploy command.","C":"Update the CodeBuild build phase commands to run the tests then to deploy the application. Add the -- require-approval any-change flag to the cdk deploy command.","D":"Create a test that uses the AWS CDK assertions module. Use the template.hasResourceProperties assertion to test that resources have the expected properties.","E":"Create a test that uses the cdk diff command. Configure the test to fail if any resources have changed."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 CodeBuild 构建阶段的命令，使其先运行测试，然后部署应用程序。将 OnFailure 阶段属性设置为 ABORT。","B":"更新 CodeBuild 构建阶段的命令，使其先运行测试，然后部署应用程序。在 cdk deploy 命令中添加 -- rollback true 标志。","C":"更新 CodeBuild 构建阶段的命令，使其先运行测试，然后部署应用程序。在 cdk deploy 命令中添加 -- require-approval any-change 标志。","D":"创建一个使用 AWS CDK 断言模块的测试。使用 template.hasResourceProperties 断言来测试资源是否 具有预期的属性。","E":"创建一个使用 `cdk diff` 命令的测试。将测试配置为在任何资源发生变化时失败。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":274,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The EC2 instances are in multiple Availability Zones. The application was misconfigured in a single Availability Zone, which caused a partial outage of the application. A DevOps engineer made changes to ensure that the unhealthy EC2 instances in one Availability Zone do not affect the healthy EC2 instances in the other Availability Zones. The DevOps engineer needs to test the application's failover and shift where the ALB sends traffic. During failover, the ALB must avoid sending traffic to the Availability Zone where the failure has occurred. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序在多个可用区的亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行，并由应用负载均衡器（ALB）提供支持。由 于单个可用区中的应用程序配置错误，导致该应用程序出现部分中断。 一位 DevOps 工程师进行了更改，以确保一个可用区中不健康的 EC2 实例不会影响其他可用区中的健康 EC2 实例。该 DevOps 工程师需要测试应用程序的故障转移，并改变 ALB 发送流量的位置。在故障转移期间， ALB 必须避免将流量发送到发生故障的可用区。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn off cross-zone load balancing on the ALB. Use Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller to start a zonal shift away from the Availability Zone.","B":"Turn off cross-zone load balancing on the ALB’s target group. Use Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller to start a zonal shift away from the Availability Zone.","C":"Create an Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller resource set that uses the DNS hostname of the ALB. Start a zonal shift for the resource set away from the Availability Zone.","D":"Create an Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller resource set that uses the ARN of the ALB’s target group. Create a readiness check that uses the ElbV2TargetGroupsCanServeTraffic rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"关闭应用负载均衡器（ALB）上的跨区负载均衡。使用亚马逊 Route 53 应用程序恢复控制器启动从该可 用区的区域迁移。","B":"关闭应用负载均衡器（ALB）目标组的跨区域负载均衡。使用 Amazon Route 53 应用程序恢复控制 器开始将流量从该可用区转移出去。","C":"创建一个使用 ALB 的 DNS 主机名的 Amazon Route 53 应用程序恢复控制器资源集。启动该资 源集从可用区的区域切换。","D":"创建一个使用 ALB 目标组的 ARN 的 Amazon Route 53 应用程序恢复控制器资源集。创建一个使用 ElbV2TargetGroupsCanServeTraffic 规则的就绪检查。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":275,"question_en":"A company sends its AWS Network Firewall flow logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company then analyzes the flow logs by using Amazon Athena. The company needs to transform the flow logs and add additional data before the flow logs are delivered to the existing S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司将其 AWS 网络防火墙的流量日志发送到一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。然后，该公司使用 Amazon Athena 对流量日志进行分析。 在将流量日志交付到现有的 S3 存储桶之前，公司需要对流量日志进行转换并添加额外的数据。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to transform the data and to write a new object to the existing S3 bucket. Configure the Lambda function with an S3 trigger for the existing S3 bucket. Specify all object create events for the event type. Acknowledge the recursive invocation.","B":"Enable Amazon EventBridge notifications on the existing S3 bucket. Create a custom EventBridge event bus. Create an EventBridge rule that is associated with the custom event bus. Configure the rule to react to all object create events for the existing S3 bucket and to invoke an AWS Step Functions workflow. Configure a Step Functions task to transform the data and to write the data into a new S3 bucket.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is associated with the default EventBridge event bus. Configure the rule to react to all object create events for the existing S3 bucket. Define a new S3 bucket as the target for the rule. Create an EventBridge input transformation to customize the event before passing the event to the rule target.","D":"Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that is configured with an AWS Lambda transformer. Specify the existing S3 bucket as the destination. Change the Network Firewall logging destination from Amazon S3 to Kinesis Data Firehose."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来转换数据，并将新对象写入现有的 S3 存储桶。为现有的 S3 存储桶配置 Lambda 函数的 S3 触发器。指定事件类型为所有对象创建事件。确认递归调用。","B":"在现有的 S3 存储桶上启用 Amazon EventBridge 通知。创建一个自定义的 EventBridge 事件总线。创建一 个与自定义事件总线关联的 EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以响应现有 S3 存储桶中的所有对象创建事 件，并调用 AWS Step Functions 工作流。配置一个 Step Functions 任务以转换数据并将数据写入新的 S3 存储桶。 桶","C":"创建一个与默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线相关联的规则。配置该规则以响应现有 S3 存储桶 中的所有对象创建事件。定义一个新的 S3 存储桶作为规则的目标。创建一个 EventBridge 输入转 换，以便在将事件传递给规则目标之前对其进行自定义。","D":"创建一个配置了 AWS Lambda 转换器的 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流。将现有的 S3 存储桶 指定为目的地。将网络防火墙的日志记录目的地从 Amazon S3 更改为 Kinesis Data Firehose。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":276,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to implement integration tests into an existing AWS CodePipeline CI/CD workflow for an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) service. The CI/CD workflow retrieves new application code from an AWS CodeCommit repository and builds a container image. The CI/CD workflow then uploads the container image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) with a new image tag version. The integration tests must ensure that new versions of the service endpoint are reachable and that various API methods return successful response data. The DevOps engineer has already created an ECS cluster to test the service. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST management overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要将集成测试纳入现有的 AWS CodePipeline 持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）工作 流中，该工作流用于 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）服务。该 CI/CD 工作流从 AWS CodeCommit 代码库中获取新的应用程序代码，并构建容器镜像。然后，该 CI/CD 工作流将容器镜像上 传到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR），并使用新的镜像标签版本。 集成测试必须确保服务端点的新版本可访问，并且各种 API 方法都能返回成功的响应数据。DevOps 工程 师已经创建了一个 ECS 集群来测试该服务。 哪种步骤组合能以最小的管理开销满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add a deploy stage to the pipeline. Configure Amazon ECS as the action provider.","B":"Add a deploy stage to the pipeline. Configure AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider.","C":"Add an appspec.yml file to the CodeCommit repository.","D":"Update the image build pipeline stage to output an imagedefinitions.json file that references the new image tag.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function that runs connectivity checks and API calls against the service. Integrate the Lambda function with CodePipeline by using a Lambda action stage.","F":"Write a script that runs integration tests against the service. Upload the script to an Amazon S3 bucket. Integrate the script in the S3 bucket with CodePipeline by using an S3 action stage."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管道中添加一个部署阶段。将 Amazon ECS 配置为操作提供程序。","B":"在管道中添加一个部署阶段。将 AWS CodeDeploy 配置为操作提供程序。","C":"在 CodeCommit 存储库中添加一个 appspec.yml 文件。","D":"更新镜像构建流水线阶段，使其输出一个引用新镜像标签的 imagedefinitions.json 文件。","E":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于对服务执行连接性检查和 API 调用。通过使用 Lambda 操作 阶段将 Lambda 函数与 CodePipeline 集成。","F":"编写一个针对服务运行集成测试的脚本。将该脚本上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。通过使用 S3 操作阶段 将 S3 存储桶中的脚本与 CodePipeline 集成。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":277,"question_en":"A company runs applications on Windows and Linux Amazon EC2 instances. The instances run across multiple Availability Zones in an AWS Region. The company uses Auto Scaling groups for each application. The company needs a durable storage solution for the instances. The solution must use SMB for Windows and must use NFS for Linux. The solution must also have sub-millisecond latencies. All instances will read and write the data. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"该公司在 Windows 和 Linux 的亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行应用程序。这些实例分布在 AWS 区域内的多个 可用区。该公司为每个应用程序使用了自动扩展组。 该公司需要一种持久的存储方案来满足实例的需求。该方案必须为 Windows 系统使用 SMB 协议，为 Linux 系统使用 NFS 协议。此外，该方案还必须具备亚毫秒级的延迟。所有实例都将读取和写入数据。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system that has targets in multiple Availability Zones.","B":"Create an Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP Multi-AZ file system.","C":"Create a General Purpose SSD (gp3) Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume to use for shared storage.","D":"Update the user data for each application’s launch template to mount the file system.","E":"Perform an instance refresh on each Auto Scaling group.","F":"Update the EC2 instances for each application to mount the file system when new instances are launched."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个在多个可用区都有目标的 Amazon 弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS）文件系统。","B":"创建一个适用于 NetApp ONTAP 的 Amazon FSx 多可用区文件系统。","C":"创建一个通用型 SSD（gp3）Amazon Elastic Block Store（Amazon EBS）卷用于 共享存储。","D":"更新每个应用程序启动模板的用户数据以挂载文件系统。","E":"对每个自动扩展组执行实例刷新操作。","F":"更新每个应用程序的 EC2 实例，以便在启动新实例时挂载文件系统。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":278,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations that a security team and a DevOps team manage. Both teams access the accounts by using AWS IAM Identity Center. A dedicated group has been created for each team. The DevOps team's group has been assigned a permission set named DevOps. The permission set has the AdministratorAccess managed IAM policy attached. The permission set has been applied to all accounts in the organization. The security team wants to ensure that the DevOps team does not have access to IAM Identity Center in the organization's management account. The security team has attached the following SCP to the organization root: After implementing the policy, the security team discovers that the DevOps team can still access IAM Identity Center. Which solution will fix the problem?","question_zh":"一家公司使用由安全团队和 DevOps 团队管理的 AWS 组织。两个团队均通过 AWS IAM 身份中心访问 账户。 为每个团队都创建了一个专用组。DevOps 团队的组已分配了一个名为 DevOps 的权限集。该权限 集附加了 AdministratorAccess 管理的 IAM 策略。该权限集已应用于组织中的所有账户。 安全团队希望确保 DevOps 团队无法访问组织管理账户中的 IAM 身份中心。安全团队已在组织根目 录附加了以下服务控制策略（SCP）： 在实施该政策后，安全团队发现 DevOps 团队仍能访问 IAM 身份中心。 哪种解决方案能解决问题？","options_en":{"A":"In the organization's management account, create a new OU. Move the organization's management account to the new OU. Detach the SCP from the organization root. Attach the SCP to the new OU.","B":"In the organization's management account, update the SCP condition reference to the ARN of the DevOps team's group role to include the AWS account ID of the organization's management account.","C":"In IAM Identity Center, create a new permission set. Ensure that the assigned policy has full access but explicitly denies permission for the sso:* action and the sso-directory:* action. Update the assigned permission set for the DevOps team's group role in the organization's management account. Delete the SCP.","D":"In IAM Identity Center, update the DevOps permission set. Ensure that the assigned policy has full access but explicitly denies permission for the sso:* action and the sso-directory:* action. In the Deny statement, add a StringEquals condition that compares the aws:SourceAccount global condition context key with the organization's management account ID. Delete the SCP."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个新的组织单位（OU）。将组织的管理账户移动到新的 OU 中。 从组织根目录分离安全策略配置文件（SCP）。将 SCP 附加到新的 OU。","B":"在组织的管理账户中，将 SCP 条件引用更新为 DevOps 团队组角色的 ARN，以包含组织管理账户 的 AWS 账户 ID。","C":"在 IAM 身份中心，创建一个新的权限集。确保所分配的策略具有完全访问权限，但明确拒绝 sso:* 操作和 sso-directory:* 操作的权限。更新组织管理账户中 DevOps 团队组角色所分配的权限集。删除 SCP.","D":"在 IAM 身份中心，更新 DevOps 权限集。确保分配的策略具有完全访问权限，但明确拒绝 sso:* 操 作和 sso-directory:* 操作的权限。在拒绝语句中，添加一个 StringEquals 条件，将 aws: SourceAccount 全局条件上下文键与组织的管理账户 ID 进行比较。删除 SCP。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":279,"question_en":"An Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group manages EC2 instances that were created from an AMI. The AMI has the AWS Systems Manager Agent installed. When an EC2 instance is launched into the Auto Scaling group, tags are applied to the EC2 instance. EC2 instances that are launched by the Auto Scaling group must have the correct operating system configuration. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"亚马逊 EC2 自动扩展组管理从 AMI 创建的 EC2 实例。该 AMI 安装了 AWS 系统管理器代理。当 EC2 实 例启动到自动扩展组中时，会将标签应用于该 EC2 实例。 由自动扩展组启动的 EC2 实例必须具有正确的操作系统配置。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a Systems Manager Run Command document that configures the desired instance configuration. Set up Systems Manager Compliance to invoke the Run Command document when the EC2 instances are not in compliance with the most recent patches.","B":"Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that links to the Systems Manager command document. Create a tag query that runs immediately.","C":"Create a Systems Manager Run Command task that specifies the desired instance configuration. Create a maintenance window in Systems Manager Maintenance Windows that runs daily. Register the Run Command task against the maintenance window. Designate the targets.","D":"Create a Systems Manager Patch Manager patch baseline and a patch group that use the same tags that the Auto Scaling group applies. Register the patch group with the patch baseline. Define a Systems Manager command document to patch the instances Invoke the document by using Systems Manager Run Command."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Systems Manager Run Command 文档，用于配置所需的实例配置。设置 Systems Manager Compliance，以便在 EC2 实例不符合最新补丁要求时调用 Run Command 文档。","B":"创建一个与 Systems Manager 命令文档相关联的 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联。创建一个立即 运行的标签查询。","C":"创建一个指定所需实例配置的 Systems Manager 运行命令任务。在 Systems Manager 维护窗口中创建一 个每日运行的维护窗口。将运行命令任务与维护窗口相关联。指定目标。","D":"创建一个与自动扩展组应用的标签相同的系统管理器补丁管理器补丁基准和补丁组。将补丁组注册 到补丁基准。定义一个用于修补实例的系统管理器命令文档。使用系统管理器运行命令来调用该文 档。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":280,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The organization root has a child OU that is named Department. The Department OU has a child OU that is named Engineering. The default FullAWSAccess policy is attached to the root, the Department OU, and the Engineering OU. The company has many AWS accounts in the Engineering OU. Each account has an administrative IAM role with the AdministratorAccess IAM policy attached. The default FullAWSAccessPolicy is also attached to each account. A DevOps engineer plans to remove the FullAWSAccess policy from the Department OU. The DevOps engineer will replace the policy with a policy that contains an Allow statement for all Amazon EC2 API operations. What will happen to the permissions of the administrative IAM roles as a result of this change?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。组织根目录有一个名为“部门”的子组织单元 （OU）。该“部门”OU 有一个名为“工程”的子 OU。默认的“FullAWSAccess”策略已附加到根目 录、“部门”OU 和“工程”OU。 该公司在工程组织单元（OU）中有许多 AWS 账户。每个账户都具有一个附有 AdministratorAccess IAM 策略的管理 IAM 角色。每个账户还附有默认的 FullAWSAccessPolicy 策略。 一位 DevOps 工程师计划从部门组织单元中移除“FullAWSAccess”策略。该工程师将用一个包含对 所有亚马逊 EC2 API 操作的允许语句的策略来替换它。 此次变更会对管理 IAM 角色的权限产生什么影响？","options_en":{"A":"All API actions on all resources will be allowed.","B":"All API actions on EC2 resources will be allowed. All other API actions will be denied.","C":"All API actions on all resources will be denied.","D":"All API actions on EC2 resources will be denied. All other API actions will be allowed."},"options_zh":{"A":"所有资源上的所有 API 操作都将被允许。","B":"对于 EC2 资源的所有 API 操作都将被允许。所有其他 API 操作都将被拒绝。","C":"对所有资源的所有 API 操作都将被拒绝。","D":"对所有 EC2 资源的 API 操作都将被拒绝。其他所有 API 操作都将被允许。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":281,"question_en":"A company manages AWS accounts in AWS Organizations. The company needs a solution to send Amazon CloudWatch Logs data to an Amazon S3 bucket in a dedicated AWS account. The solution must support all existing and future CloudWatch Logs log groups. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司需要一个解决方案，将 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 数 据发送到一个专用 AWS 账户中的 Amazon S3 存储桶。该解决方案必须支持所有现有的和未来的 CloudWatch Logs 日志组。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Organizations backup policies to back up all log groups to a dedicated S3 bucket. Add an S3 bucket policy that allows access from all accounts that belong to the company.","B":"Create a backup plan in AWS Backup. Specify a dedicated S3 bucket as a backup vault. Assign all CloudWatch Logs log group resources to the backup plan. Create resource assignments in the backup plan for all accounts that belong to the company.","C":"Create a backup plan in AWS Backup. Specify a dedicated S3 bucket as a backup vault. Assign all existing log groups to the backup plan. Create resource assignments in the backup plan for all accounts that belong to the company. Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to assign log groups to a backup plan. Create an AWS Config rule that has an automatic remediation action for all noncompliant log groups. Specify the runbook as the rule's target.","D":"Create a CloudWatch Logs destination and an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream in the dedicated AWS account. Specify the S3 bucket as the destination of the delivery stream. Create subscription filters for all existing log groups in all accounts. Create an AWS Lambda function to call the CloudWatch Logs PutSubscriptionFilter API operation. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function when a CreateLogGroup event occurs."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用组织备份策略，将所有日志组备份到专用的 S3 存储桶。添加一个 S3 存储桶策略，允许公司所属 的所有账户访问。","B":"在 AWS 备份中创建一个备份计划。指定一个专用的 S3 存储桶作为备份金库。将所有 CloudWatch Logs 日志组资源分配给该备份计划。在备份计划中为公司所属的所有账户创建资源分配。","C":"在 AWS Backup 中创建备份计划。指定一个专用的 S3 存储桶作为备份金库。将所有现有的日志组分配给 备份计划。在备份计划中为公司所属的所有账户创建资源分配。创建一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，用于将日志组分配给备份计划。创建一个具有自动修复操作的 AWS Config 规则， 针对所有不符合要求的日志组。将运行手册指定为规则的目标。","D":"在专用的 AWS 账户中创建 CloudWatch Logs 目标和 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流。将 S3 存储桶指 定为交付流的目的地。为所有账户中的所有现有日志组创建订阅筛选器。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来 调用 CloudWatch Logs PutSubscriptionFilter API 操作。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在发生 CreateLogGroup 事件时调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":282,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages a Java-based application that runs in an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster on AWS Fargate. Auto scaling has not been configured for the application. The DevOps engineer has determined that the Java Virtual Machine (JVM) thread count is a good indicator of when to scale the application. The application serves customer traffic on port 8080 and makes JVM metrics available on port 9404. Application use has recently increased. The DevOps engineer needs to configure auto scaling for the application. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师管理着一个基于 Java 的应用程序，该程序在 AWS Fargate 上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）集群中运行。该应用程序尚未配置自动扩展功能。 DevOps 工程师已确定 Java 虚拟机（JVM）线程数是决定何时扩展应用程序的一个良好指标。该应用程序在 8080 端口为客户提供服务，并在 9404 端口提供 JVM 指标。 应用程序的使用量近来有所增加。开发运维工程师需要为该应用程序配置自动扩展功能。 哪种解决方案能在运营开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the Amazon CloudWatch agent as a container sidecar. Configure the CloudWatch agent to retrieve JVM metrics from port 9404. Create CloudWatch alarms on the JVM thread count metric to scale the application. Add a step scaling policy in Fargate to scale up and scale down based on the CloudWatch alarms.","B":"Deploy the Amazon CloudWatch agent as a container sidecar. Configure a metric filter for the JVM thread count metric on the CloudWatch log group for the CloudWatch agent. Add a target tracking policy in Fargate. Select the metric from the metric filter as a scale target.","C":"Create an Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace. Deploy AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry as a container sidecar to publish the JVM metrics from port 9404 to the Prometheus workspace. Configure rules for the workspace to use the JVM thread count metric to scale the application. Add a step scaling policy in Fargate. Select the Prometheus rules to scale up and scaling down.","D":"Create an Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace. Deploy AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry as a container sidecar to retrieve JVM metrics from port 9404 to publish the JVM metrics from port 9404 to the Prometheus workspace. Add a target tracking policy in Fargate. Select the Prometheus metric as a scale target."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Amazon CloudWatch 代理部署为容器的侧边车。配置 CloudWatch 代理从 9404 端口获取 JVM 指标。 根据 JVM 线程数指标创建 CloudWatch 警报以对应用程序进行扩展。在 Fargate 中添加一个步进扩 展策略，根据 CloudWatch 警报进行扩展和缩减。","B":"将 Amazon CloudWatch 代理部署为容器的边车。在 CloudWatch 代理的 CloudWatch 日志组上为 JVM 线程计数指标配置一个指标筛选器。在 Fargate 中添加一个目标跟踪策略。从指标筛选器中选择该 指标作为缩放目标。","C":"创建一个 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 工作区。将 AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry 作为容器边 车部署，将来自 9404 端口的 JVM 指标发布到 Prometheus 工作区。为工作区配置规则，使用 JVM 线 程数指标来扩展应用程序。在 Fargate 中添加一个步进扩展策略。选择用于扩展和缩减的 Prometheus 规则。","D":"创建一个 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 工作区。部署 AWS Distro for Prometheus。 将 OpenTelemetry 作为容器的侧车，从 9404 端口获取 JVM 指标，并将这些 JVM 指标从 9404 端 口发布到 Prometheus 工作区。在 Fargate 中添加一个目标跟踪策略。选择 Prometheus 指标作为缩 放目标。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":283,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs in a single AWS Region. The application runs on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster and connects to an Amazon Aurora MySQL cluster. The application is built in an AWS CodeBuild project. The container images are published to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). The company needs to replicate the state of the application for the container images and the database to a second Region. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个在单个 AWS 区域运行的应用程序。该应用程序在 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service （Amazon EKS）集群上运行，并连接到 Amazon Aurora MySQL 集群。应用程序是在 AWS CodeBuild 项目中构建的。容器镜像发布到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）。 该公司需要将容器镜像和数据库的应用状态复制到第二个区域。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on Amazon S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) on the bucket that holds the ECR container images. Deploy the application to an EKS cluster in the second Region by referencing the new S3 bucket object URL for the container image in a Kubernetes deployment file. Configure a cross-Region Aurora Replica in the second Region. Configure the new application deployment to use the endpoints for the cross-Region Aurora Replica.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to image pushes to the ECR repository. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to replicate the image to a new ECR repository in the second Region. Deploy the application to an EKS cluster in the second Region by referencing the new ECR repository in a Kubernetes deployment file. Configure a cross-Region Aurora Replica in the second Region. Configure the new application deployment to use the endpoints for the cross-Region Aurora Replica.","C":"Turn on Cross-Region Replication to replicate the ECR repository to the second Region. Deploy the application to an EKS cluster in the second Region by referencing the new ECR repository in a Kubernetes deployment file. Configure an Aurora global database with clusters in the initial Region and the second Region. Configure the new application deployment to use the endpoints for the second Region's cluster in the Aurora global database.","D":"Configure the CodeBuild project to also push the container image to an ECR repository in the second Region. Deploy the application to an EKS cluster in the second Region by referencing the new ECR repository in a Kubernetes deployment file. Configure an Aurora MySQL cluster in the second Region as the target for binary log replication from the Aurora MySQL cluster in the initial Region. Configure the new application deployment to use the endpoints for the second Region's cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在保存 ECR 容器镜像的存储桶上启用 Amazon S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。通过在 Kubernetes 部署文 件中引用新 S3 存储桶对象 URL 来将应用程序部署到第二个区域的 EKS 集群。在第二个区域配置 跨区域 Aurora 副本。将新的应用程序部署配置为使用跨区域 Aurora 副本的端点。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对推送到 ECR 存储库的镜像作出反应。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数，将镜像复制到第二个区域的新 ECR 存储库。通过在 Kubernetes 部 署文件中引用新的 ECR 存储库，将应用程序部署到第二个区域的 EKS 集群。在第二个区域配置跨 区域 Aurora 副本。配置新的应用程序部署以使用跨区域 Aurora 副本的端点。","C":"启用跨区域复制功能，将 ECR 仓库复制到第二个区域。通过在 Kubernetes 部署文件中引用新的 ECR 仓库，将应用程序部署到第二个区域的 EKS 集群。配置一个包含初始区域和第二个区域集群的 Aurora 全球数据库。将新的应用程序部署配置为使用 Aurora 全球数据库中第二个区域集群的端点。","D":"将 CodeBuild 项目配置为还将容器镜像推送到第二个区域的 ECR 存储库。通过在 Kubernetes 部署 文件中引用新的 ECR 存储库，将应用程序部署到第二个区域的 EKS 集群。在第二个区域配置一 个 Aurora MySQL 集群 将初始区域中的 Aurora MySQL 集群的二进制日志复制目标设置为该新应用部署。配置新应用部署 以使用第二个区域集群的端点。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":284,"question_en":"A company is building a serverless application that uses AWS Lambda functions to process data. A BeginResponse Lambda function initializes data in response to specific application events. The company needs to ensure that a large number of Lambda functions are invoked after the BeginResponse Lambda function runs. Each Lambda function must be invoked in parallel and depends on only the outputs of the BeginResponse Lambda function. Each Lambda function has retry logic for invocation and must be able to fine-tune concurrency without losing data. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司正在构建一个无服务器应用程序，该程序使用 AWS Lambda 函数来处理数据。 一个名为 BeginResponse 的 Lambda 函数会在特定的应用程序事件发生时初始化数据。该公司需要确保在 BeginResponse Lambda 函数运行之后能够并行调用大量其他 Lambda 函数。每个 Lambda 函数仅依赖于 BeginResponse Lambda 函数的输出结果，并且必须能够并行调用。每个 Lambda 函数都具有调用重试逻辑， 并且必须能够在不丢失数据的情况下对并发进行微调。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Modify the BeginResponse Lambda function to publish to the SNS topic before the BeginResponse Lambda function finishes running. Subscribe all Lambda functions that need to invoke after the BeginResponse Lambda function runs to the SNS topic. Subscribe any new Lambda functions to the SNS topic.","B":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue for each Lambda function that needs to run after the BeginResponse Lambda function runs. Subscribe each Lambda function to its own SQS queue. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe each SQS queue to the SNS topic. Modify the BeginResponse function to publish to the SNS topic when it finishes running.","C":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue for each Lambda function that needs to run after the BeginResponse Lambda function runs. Subscribe the Lambda function to the SQS queue. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic for each SQS queue. Subscribe the SQS queues to the SNS topics. Modify the BeginResponse function to publish to the SNS topics when the function finishes running.","D":"Create an AWS Step Functions Standard Workflow. Configure states in the workflow to invoke the Lambda functions sequentially. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Modify the BeginResponse Lambda function to publish to the SNS topic before the Lambda function finishes running. Create a new Lambda function that is subscribed to the SNS topic and that invokes the Step Functions workflow."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。修改 BeginResponse Lambda 函数，使其在运行结 束前向 SNS 主题发布消息。将所有需要在 BeginResponse Lambda 函数运行后调用的 Lambda 函数订 阅到 SNS 主题。将任何新的 Lambda 函数订阅到 SNS 主题。","B":"为每个需要在 BeginResponse Lambda 函数运行之后运行的 Lambda 函数创建一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列。将每个 Lambda 函数订阅到其自身的 SQS 队列。创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。将每个 SQS 队列订阅到 SNS 主题。修改 BeginResponse 函数，使其在运行结束时发布到 SNS 主题。","C":"为每个需要在 BeginResponse Lambda 函数运行之后运行的 Lambda 函数创建一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列。将该 Lambda 函数订阅到 SQS 队列。为每个 SQS 队列创建一 个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。将 SQS 队列订阅到 SNS 主题。修改 BeginResponse 函数，使其在运行结束时发布到 SNS 主题。","D":"创建一个 AWS Step Functions 标准工作流。在工作流中配置状态以按顺序调用 Lambda 函数。创建 一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。修改 BeginResponse Lambda 函数，使其在函数 运行结束前向 SNS 主题发布消息。创建一个新的 Lambda 函数，使其订阅 SNS 主题并调用 Step Functions 工作流。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":285,"question_en":"A company operates a globally deployed product out of multiple AWS Regions. The company's DevOps team needs to use Amazon API Gateway to deploy an API to support the product. The API must be deployed redundantly. The deployment must provide independent availability from each company location. The deployment also must respond to a custom domain URL and must optimize performance for the API user requests. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过多个 AWS 区域运营一款全球部署的产品。该公司的 DevOps 团队需要使用亚马逊 API 网 关来部署一个 API 以支持该产品。 该 API 必须冗余部署。部署必须为每个公司地点提供独立的可用性。部署还必须响应自定义域名 URL， 并且必须优化 API 用户请求的性能。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an API Gateway edge-optimized API endpoint in the us-east-1 Region. Create an API Gateway custom domain for the API. Create an Amazon Route 53 record set with a geoproximity routing policy for the API's custom domain. Increase the geographic bias to the maximum allowed value.","B":"Deploy an API Gateway regional API endpoint in the us-east-1 Region. Integrate the API Gateway API with a public Application Load Balancer (ALB). Create an AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator. Associate the endpoint with the ALB. Create an Amazon Route 53 alias record set that points the custom domain name to the DNS name that is assigned to the accelerator.","C":"Deploy an API Gateway regional API endpoint in every AWS Region where the company's product is deployed. Create an API Gateway custom domain in each Region for the deployed API Gateway API. Create an Amazon Route 53 record set that has a latency routing policy for every deployed API Gateway custom domain.","D":"Deploy an API Gateway edge-optimized API endpoint in the us-east-1 Region. Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Configure the CloudFront distribution with an alternate domain name. Specify the API Gateway Invoke URL as the origin domain. Create an Amazon Route 53 alias record set with a simple routing policy. Point the routing policy to the CloudFront distribution domain name."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 us-east-1 区域部署一个 API 网关边缘优化的 API 端点。为该 API 创建一个 API 网关自定义域名。为 该 API 的自定义域名创建一个具有地理邻近性路由策略的 Amazon Route 53 记录集。将地理偏差增加 到允许的最大值。","B":"在 us-east-1 区域部署 API 网关的区域 API 端点。将 API 网关 API 与公共应用负载均衡器（ALB）集 成。创建一个 AWS 全球加速器标准加速器。将端点与 ALB 关联。创建一个指向分配给加速器的 DNS 名称的自定义域名的 Amazon Route 53 别名记录集。","C":"在公司产品部署的每个 AWS 区域中部署一个 API 网关区域 API 端点。在每个区域为部署的 API 网 关 API 创建一个自定义域名。为每个部署的 API 网关自定义域名创建一个具有延迟路由策略的 Amazon Route 53 记录集。","D":"在 us-east-1 区域部署一个 API 网关边缘优化的 API 端点。创建一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发。使用备 用域名配置 CloudFront 分发。将 API 网关调用 URL 指定为源域名。使用简单路由策略创建一个 Amazon Route 53 别名记录集。将路由策略指向 CloudFront 分发的域名。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":286,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer uses AWS CodeBuild to frequently produce software packages. The CodeBuild project builds large Docker images that the DevOps engineer can use across multiple builds. The DevOps engineer wants to improve build performance and minimize costs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS CodeBuild 定期生成软件包。CodeBuild 项目构建大型 Docker 镜像，该 DevOps 工程师可在多 个构建中使用这些镜像。 这位 DevOps 工程师想要提升构建性能并降低费用。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Store the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Implement a local Docker layer cache for CodeBuild.","B":"Cache the Docker images in an Amazon S3 bucket that is available across multiple build hosts. Expire the cache by using an S3 Lifecycle policy.","C":"Store the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Modify the CodeBuild project runtime configuration to always use the most recent image version.","D":"Create custom AMIs that contain the cached Docker images. In the CodeBuild build, launch Amazon EC2 instances from the custom AMIs."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Docker 镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库中。为 CodeBuild 实现本地 Docker 层 缓存。","B":"将 Docker 镜像缓存在一个可在多个构建主机间访问的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 S3 生命周期策略使缓存过期。","C":"将 Docker 镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库中。修改 CodeBuild 项目的运行时配置，使其始 终使用最新版本的镜像。","D":"创建包含缓存 Docker 镜像的自定义 AMI。在 CodeBuild 构建过程中，从自定义 AMI 启动 Amazon EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":287,"question_en":"A large company recently acquired a small company. The large company invited the small company to join the large company's existing organization in AWS Organizations as a new OU. A DevOps engineer determines that the small company needs to launch t3.small Amazon EC2 instance types for the company's application workloads. The small company needs to deploy the instances only within US-based AWS Regions. The DevOps engineer needs to use an SCP in the small company's new OU to ensure that the small company can launch only the required instance types. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大型公司最近收购了一家小型公司。大型公司邀请小型公司加入其在 AWS 组织中现有的组织结构，作为新的组织单元（OU）。 一位 DevOps 工程师确定，这家小公司需要为其应用程序工作负载启动 t3.small 类型的亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司仅需在美国境内 的 AWS 区域内部署这些实例。 DevOps 工程师需要在这家小公司的新组织单位（OU）中使用安全组策略（SCP），以确保该公司只能启动所需的实例类型。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a statement to deny the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the ec2:InstanceType condition is not equal to t3.small. Configure another statement to deny the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the aws:RequestedRegion condition is not equal to us-*.","B":"Configure a statement to allow the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the ec2:InstanceType condition is not equal to t3.small. Configure another statement to allow the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the aws:RequestedRegion condition is not equal to us-*.","C":"Configure a statement to deny the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the ec2:InstanceType condition is equal to t3.small. Configure another statement to deny the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the aws:RequestedRegion condition is equal to us-*.","D":"Configure a statement to allow the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the ec2:InstanceType condition is equal to t3.small. Configure another statement to allow the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the aws:RequestedRegion condition is equal to us-*."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一条语句，当 ec2:InstanceType 条件不等于 t3.small 时，拒绝所有 EC2 实例资源的 ec2:RunInstances 操作。 配置另一条语句，当 `aws:RequestedRegion` 条件不等于 `us-*` 时，拒绝所有 EC2 实例资源的 `ec2：RunInstances` 操作。","B":"配置一条语句，允许对所有 EC2 实例资源执行 ec2:RunInstances 操作，条件是 ec2:InstanceType 不等于 t3.small。 配置另一条语句，允许在 aws:RequestedRegion 条件不等于 us-* 时对所有 EC2 实例资源执行 ec2:RunInstances 操作。","C":"配置一条语句，当 ec2:InstanceType 条件等于 t3.small 时，拒绝所有 EC2 实例资源的 ec2:RunInstances 操作。 配置另一条语句，当条件 aws:RequestedRegion 等于 us-* 时，拒绝所有 EC2 实例资源的 ec2:RunInstances 操作。","D":"配置一条语句，允许在 ec2:InstanceType 条件等于 t3.small 时对所有 EC2 实例资源执行 ec2:RunInstances 操作。 配置另一条语句，当 aws:RequestedRegion 条件等于 us-* 时，允许对所有 EC2 实例资源执行 ec2:RunInstances 操作。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":288,"question_en":"A DevOps team manages infrastructure for an application. The application uses long-running processes to process items from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. The application is deployed to an Auto Scaling group. The application recently experienced an issue where items were taking significantly longer to process. The queue exceeded the expected size, which prevented various business processes from functioning properly. The application records all logs to a third-party tool. The team is currently subscribed to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that the team uses for alerts. The team needs to be alerted if the queue exceeds the expected size. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队负责管理应用程序的基础设施。该应用程序使用长期运行的进程来处理来自亚马逊简 单队列服务（Amazon SQS）队列中的项目。该应用程序部署在自动扩展组中。 该应用程序最近出现了一个问题，即处理项目所需的时间大幅增加。队列的规模超出了预期，导致各种 业务流程无法正常运行。该应用程序会将所有日志记录到第三方工具中。 该团队当前订阅了一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，用于接收警报。如果队列超出预期 大小，团队需要收到警报。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric alarm with a period of 1 hour and a static threshold to alarm if the average of the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed metric is greater than the expected value. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric alarm with a period of 1 hour and a static threshold to alarm if the sum of the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible metric is greater than the expected value. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that retrieves the ApproximateNumberOfMessages SQS queue attribute value and publishes the value as a new CloudWatch custom metric. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is scheduled to run every 5 minutes and that invokes the Lambda function. Configure a CloudWatch metrics alarm with a period of 1 hour and a static threshold to alarm if the sum of the new custom metric is greater than the expected value.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that checks the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed SQS queue attribute and compares the value to a defined expected size in the function. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is scheduled to run every 5 minutes and that invokes the Lambda function. When the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed SQS queue attribute exceeds the expected size, send a notification the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 指标报警，设置周期为 1 小时，并设定静态阈值，当 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed 指标的平均值大于预期值时触发报警。将该报警配置为通知 SNS 主题。","B":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 指标报警，设置周期为 1 小时，并设定静态阈值，当 “ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible”指标的总和大于预期值时触发报警。将该报警配置为通 知 SNS 主题。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于获取 SQS 队列的“ApproximateNumberOfMessages”属性值，并将 该值作为新的 CloudWatch 自定义指标发布。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则每 5 分钟运 行一次并调用 Lambda 函数。配置一个 CloudWatch 指标警报，周期为 1 小时，设置静态阈值，如果 新自定义指标的总和大于预期值则发出警报。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数检查 SQS 队列的“ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed”（延 迟消息近似数量）属性，并将该值与函数中定义的预期大小进行比较。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则每 5 分钟运行一次，并调用该 Lambda 函数。当“ApproximateNumberOfM essagesDelayed”SQS 队列属性超过预期大小时，向 SNS 主题发送通知。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":289,"question_en":"A large company runs critical workloads in multiple AWS accounts. The AWS accounts are managed under AWS Organizations with all features enabled. The company stores confidential customer data in an Amazon S3 bucket. Access to the S3 bucket requires multiple levels of approval. The company wants to monitor when the S3 bucket is accessed by using the AWS CLI. The company also wants insights into the various activities performed by other users on all other S3 buckets in the AWS accounts to detect any issues. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大型公司在多个 AWS 账户中运行关键工作负载。这些 AWS 账户在 AWS 组织中进行管理，并启用 了所有功能。该公司将机密客户数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。访问该 S3 存储桶需要经过多级审批。 该公司希望使用 AWS 命令行界面（AWS CLI）来监控 S3 存储桶的访问时间。该公司还希望了解 AWS 账户中所有其他 S3 存储桶上其他用户执行的各种活动，以检测任何问题。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail that is delivered to Amazon CloudWatch in each AWS account. Enable data events logs for all S3 buckets. Use Amazon GuardDuty for anomaly detection in all the AWS accounts. Use Amazon Athena to perform SQL queries on the custom metrics created from the CloudTrail logs.","B":"Create an AWS CloudTrail organization trail that is delivered to Amazon CloudWatch in the Organizations management account. Enable data events logs for all S3 buckets. Use Amazon CloudWatch anomaly detection in all the AWS accounts. Use Amazon Athena to perform SQL queries on the custom metrics created from the CloudTrail logs.","C":"Create an AWS CloudTrail organization trail that is delivered to Amazon CloudWatch in the Organizations management account. Enable data events logs for all S3 buckets. Use Amazon CloudWatch anomaly detection in all the AWS accounts. Use Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights to perform SQL queries on the custom metrics created from the CloudTrail logs.","D":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail that is delivered to Amazon CloudWatch in each AWS account. Enable data events logs for all S3 buckets. Use a custom solution for anomaly detection in all the AWS accounts. Use Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights to perform SQL queries on the custom metrics created from the CloudTrail logs."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建一条交付至 Amazon CloudWatch 的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。为所有 S3 存储桶 启用数据事件日志记录。在所有 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon GuardDuty 进行异常检测。使用 Amazon Athena 对从 CloudTrail 日志创建的自定义指标执行 SQL 查询。","B":"在组织管理账户中创建一个交付至 Amazon CloudWatch 的 AWS CloudTrail 组织跟踪。为所有 S3 存 储桶启用数据事件日志记录。在所有 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon CloudWatch 异常检测功能。使用 Amazon Athena 对从 CloudTrail 日志创建的自定义指标执行 SQL 查询。","C":"在组织管理账户中创建一个交付至 Amazon CloudWatch 的 AWS CloudTrail 组织跟踪。为所有 S3 存 储桶启用数据事件日志记录。在所有 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon CloudWatch 异常检测功能。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights 对从 CloudTrail 日志创建的自定义指标执行 SQL 查询。","D":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建一条交付至 Amazon CloudWatch 的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。为所有 S3 存储桶 启用数据事件日志记录。在所有 AWS 账户中使用自定义解决方案进行异常检测。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights 对从 CloudTrail 日志创建的自定义指标执行 SQL 查询。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":290,"question_en":"A DevOps team is deploying microservices for an application on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. The cluster uses managed node groups. The DevOps team wants to enable auto scaling for the microservice Pods based on a specific CPU utilization percentage. The DevOps team has already installed the Kubernetes Metrics Server on the cluster. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队正在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群上为一个应用程序部署微服务。 该集群使用托管节点组。DevOps 团队希望启用自动 根据特定的 CPU 利用率百分比对微服务 Pod 进行缩放。开发运维团队已经在集群上安装了 Kubernetes 指标服务器。 哪种解决方案 将以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Edit the Auto Scaling group that is associated with the worker nodes of the EKS cluster. Configure the Auto Scaling group to use a target tracking scaling policy to scale when the average CPU utilization of the Auto Scaling group reaches a specific percentage.","B":"Deploy the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) and the Kubernetes Vertical Pod Autoscaler (VPA) in the cluster. Configure the HPA to scale based on the target CPU utilization percentage. Configure the VPA to use the recommender mode setting.","C":"Run the AWS Systems Manager AWS-UpdateEKSManagedNodeGroup Automation document. Modify the values for NodeGroupDesiredSize, NodeGroupMaxSize, and NodeGroupMinSize to be based on an estimate for the required node size.","D":"Deploy the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) and the Kubernetes Cluster Autoscaler in the cluster. Configure the HPA to scale based on the target CPU utilization percentage. Configure the Cluster Autoscaler to use the auto-discovery setting."},"options_zh":{"A":"编辑与 EKS 集群工作节点相关联的自动扩展组。将自动扩展组配置为使用目标跟踪扩展策略，在自 动扩展组的平均 CPU 利用率达到特定百分比时进行扩展。","B":"在集群中部署 Kubernetes 水平 Pod 自动扩缩器（HPA）和 Kubernetes 垂直 Pod 自动扩缩器（VPA）。 将 HPA 配置为根据目标 CPU 利用率百分比进行扩缩。将 VPA 配置为使用推荐模式设置。","C":"运行 AWS Systems Manager 的 AWS-UpdateEKSManagedNodeGroup 自动化文档。将 NodeGroupDesiredSize、NodeGroupMaxSize 和 NodeGroupMinSize 的值修改为基于对所需节点大小 的估计。","D":"在集群中部署 Kubernetes 水平 Pod 自动伸缩器（HPA）和 Kubernetes 集群自动伸缩器。将 HPA 配置 为根据目标 CPU 利用率百分比进行扩展。将集群自动伸缩器配置为使用自动发现设置。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":291,"question_en":"A company has multiple AWS accounts. The company uses AWS IAM Identity Center that is integrated with a third-party SAML 2.0 identity provider (IdP). The attributes for access control feature is enabled in IAM Identity Center. The attribute mapping list maps the department key from the IdP to the ${path:enterprise.department} attribute. All existing Amazon EC2 instances have a d1, d2, d3 department tag that corresponds to three company’s departments. A DevOps engineer must create policies based on the matching attributes. The policies must grant each user access to only the EC2 instances that are tagged with the user’s respective department name. Which condition key should the DevOps engineer include in the custom permissions policies to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有多个 AWS 账户。该公司使用与第三方 SAML 2.0 身份提供商（IdP）集成的 AWS IAM 身份中心。 IAM 身份中心已启用访问控制功能的属性。属性映射列表将身份提供方中的部门键映射到 ${path: enterprise.department} 属性。所有现有的 Amazon EC2 实例都有 d1、d2、d3 部门标签，分别对应公司的 三个部门。 DevOps 工程师必须根据匹配的属性创建策略。这些策略必须仅授予每个用户访问其所在部门名称已作 为标签添加到的 EC2 实例的权限。 DevOps 工程师应在自定义权限策略中包含哪个条件键才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"","B":"","C":"","D":""},"options_zh":{},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":292,"question_en":"A security team wants to use AWS CloudTrail to monitor all actions and API calls in multiple accounts that are in the same organization in AWS Organizations. The security team needs to ensure that account users cannot turn off CloudTrail in the accounts. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一个安全团队希望使用 AWS CloudTrail 来监控同一 AWS 组织中多个账户的所有操作和 API 调用。该安全团 队需要确保账户用户无法在这些账户中关闭 CloudTrail。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Apply an SCP to all OUs to deny the cloudtrail:StopLogging action and the cloudtrail:DeleteTrail action.","B":"Create IAM policies in each account to deny the cloudtrail:StopLogging action and the cloudtrail:DeleteTrail action.","C":"Set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms to notify the security team when a user disables CloudTrail in an account.","D":"Use AWS Config to automatically re-enable CloudTrail if a user disables CloudTrail in an account."},"options_zh":{"A":"对所有组织单位应用安全策略控制（SCP），以拒绝执行“cloudtrail:StopLogging”操作和“cloudtrail: DeleteTrail”操作。","B":"在每个账户中创建 IAM 策略，以拒绝 cloudtrail:StopLogging 操作和 cloudtrail:DeleteTrail 操作。","C":"在用户在一个账户中禁用 CloudTrail 时，设置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报以通知安全团队。","D":"使用 AWS Config 自动重新启用 CloudTrail，以防用户在账户中禁用 CloudTrail。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":293,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to configure a blue/green deployment for an existing three-tier application. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances and uses an Amazon RDS database. The EC2 instances run behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and are in an Auto Scaling group. The DevOps engineer has created launch templates, Auto Scaling groups, and ALB target groups for the blue environment and the green environment. Each target group specifies which application version, blue or green, will be loaded on the EC2 instances. An Amazon Route 53 record for www.example.com points to the ALB. The deployment must shift traffic all at once from the blue environment to the green environment. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要为现有的三层应用程序配置蓝/绿部署。该应用程序在 Amazon EC2 实例上运 行，并使用 Amazon RDS 数据库。EC2 实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后，并处于自动扩展组中。 DevOps 工程师为蓝色环境和绿色环境创建了启动模板、自动扩展组和 ALB 目标组。每个目标组都指 定了将在 EC2 实例上加载的应用程序版本，即蓝色版本或绿色版本。Amazon Route 53 中的 www. example.com 记录指向 ALB。 部署必须一次性将所有流量从蓝色环境切换到绿色环境。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Starta rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new application version to the green environment's EC2 instances. When the rolling restart is complete, use an AWS CLI command to update the ALB to send traffic to the green environment's target group.","B":"Use an AWS CLI command to update the ALB to send traffic to the green environments target group. Start a rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new application version to the green environment's EC2 instances.","C":"Update the launch template to deploy the green environment's application version to the blue environment's EC2 instances. Do not change the target groups or the Auto Scaling groups in either environment. Perform a rolling restart of the blue environments EC2 instances.","D":"Starta rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new application version to the green environment's EC2 instances. When the rolling restart is complete, update Route 53 to point to the green environment's endpoint on the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"对绿色环境的自动扩展组启动滚动重启，以将新应用版本部署到绿色环境的 EC2 实例。滚动重启完 成后，使用 AWS CLI 命令更新应用负载均衡器，使其将流量发送到绿色环境的目标组。","B":"使用 AWS CLI 命令将应用负载均衡器（ALB）更新为将流量发送到绿色环境的目标组。启动绿色环 境的自动扩展组的滚动重启，以将新应用版本部署到绿色环境的 EC2 实例上。","C":"更新启动模板，将绿色环境的应用程序版本部署到蓝色环境的 EC2 实例上。不要更改任一环境 中的目标组或自动扩展组。对蓝色环境的 EC2 实例执行滚动重启。","D":"对绿色环境的自动扩展组启动滚动重启，以将新应用版本部署到绿色环境的 EC2 实例上。滚动重启 完成后，更新 Route 53 使其指向绿色环境在 ALB 上的端点。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":294,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. The application processes a high volume of messages from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. A DevOps engineer noticed that the application took several hours to process a group of messages from the SQS queue. The average CPU utilization of the Auto Scaling group did not cross the threshold of a target tracking scaling policy when processing the messages. The application that processes the SQS queue publishes logs to ‘Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The DevOps engineer needs to ensure that the queue is processed quickly. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的应用程序，这些实例位于一个自动扩展组中。该应用程序 处理来自亚马逊简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）队列的大量消息。 一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，应用程序处理来自 SQS 队列的一组消息需要数小时。在处理这些消息时， 自动扩展组的平均 CPU 利用率未超过目标跟踪扩展策略的阈值。处理 SQS 队列的应用程序将日志发 布到“Amazon CloudWatch Logs”。 DevOps 工程师需要确保队列能够快速处理。 哪种解决方案在满足这些要求的同时，运营开销最小？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to publish a custom metric by using the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible SQS queue attribute and the GroupInServiceInstances Auto Scaling group attribute to publish the queue messages for each instance. Schedule an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Lambda function every hour. Create a target tracking scaling policy for the Auto Scaling group that uses the custom metric to scale in and out.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to publish a custom metric by using the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible SQS queue attribute and the GroupInServiceInstances Auto Scaling group attribute to publish the queue messages for each instance. Create a CloudWatch subscription filter for the application logs with the Lambda function as the target. Create a target tracking scaling policy for the Auto Scaling group that uses the custom metric to scale in and out.","C":"Create a target tracking scaling policy for the Auto Scaling group. In the target tracking policy, use the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible SQS queue attribute and the GroupInServiceInstances Auto Scaling group attribute to calculate how many messages are in the queue for each number of instances by using metric math. Use the calculated attribute to scale in and out.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that logs the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible attribute of the SQS queue to a CloudWatch Logs log group. Schedule an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Lambda function every 5 minutes. Create a metric filer to count the number of log events from a CloudWatch logs group. Create a target tracking scaling policy for the Auto Scaling group that uses the custom metric to scale in and out."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数，通过使用 SQS 队列的 ApproximateNumberOfM essagesVisible 属性和 Auto Scaling 组的 GroupInServiceInstances 属性来发布每个实例的队列消息的 自定义指标。安排一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每小时运行一次该 Lambda 函数。为 Auto Scaling 组创建一个目标跟踪扩展策略，使用该自定义指标进行扩展和收缩。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数，通过使用 SQS 队列的 ApproximateNumberOfM essagesVisible 属性和 Auto Scaling 组的 GroupInServiceInstances 属性来发布每个实例的队列消息 的自定义指标。为应用程序日志创建一个 CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，将 Lambda 函数作为目标。为 Auto Scaling 组创建一个目标跟踪扩展策略，使用自定义指标进行扩展和收缩。","C":"为自动扩展组创建目标跟踪扩展策略。在目标跟踪策略中，使用 通过使用指标数学，结合 SQS 队列的“ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible”属性和 Auto Scaling 组的“GroupInServiceInstances”属性，计算出在不同实例数量下队列中的消息数量。利用计算得出 的属性进行缩放操作。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 SQS 队列的 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible 属性记录到 CloudWatch Logs 日志组中。安排一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 5 分钟运行一次该 Lambda 函 数。创建一个指标过滤器，用于计算来自 CloudWatch 日志组的日志事件数量。为 Auto Scaling 组 创建一个目标跟踪扩展策略，使用自定义指标进行扩展和收缩。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":295,"question_en":"A company has a single AWS account that runs hundreds of Amazon EC2 instances in a single AWS Region. The company launches and terminates new EC2 instances every hour. The account includes existing EC2 instances that have been running for longer than a week. The company's security policy requires all running EC2 instances to have an EC2 instance profile attached. The company has created a default EC2 instance profile. The default EC2 instance profile must be attached to any EC2 instances that do not have a profile attached. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个 AWS 账户，在单个 AWS 区域运行着数百台亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司每小时 都会启动和终止新的 EC2 实例。该账户中还包括运行时间超过一周的现有 EC2 实例。 公司的安全策略要求所有正在运行的 EC2 实例都必须附加一个 EC2 实例配置文件。公司已创建了一 个默认的 EC2 实例配置文件。对于未附加配置文件的任何 EC2 实例，都必须附加默认的 EC2 实例配 置文件。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches the Amazon EC2 RunInstances API calls. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","B":"Configure AWS Config. Deploy an AWS Config ec2-instance-profile-attached managed rule. Configure an automatic remediation action that invokes an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","C":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches the Amazon EC2 StartInstances API calls. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","D":"Configure AWS Config. Deploy an AWS Config iam-role-managed-policy-check managed rule. Configure an automatic remediation action that invokes an AWS Lambda function to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个与 Amazon EC2 的 RunInstances API 调用相匹配的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将该规则配 置为调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例。","B":"配置 AWS Config。部署一个与 EC2 实例配置文件关联的 AWS Config 管理规则。配置一个自动修 复操作，调用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例。","C":"配置一个与 Amazon EC2 的 StartInstances API 调用相匹配的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将该 规则配置为调用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，以将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例。","D":"配置 AWS Config。部署一个名为“iam-role-managed-policy-check”的 AWS Config 管理规则。配置 一个自动修复操作，调用 AWS Lambda 函数将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例上。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":296,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage hundreds of AWS accounts. The company has a team that is responsible for AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). The IAM team wants to implement AWS IAM Identity Center. The IAM team must have only the minimum required permissions to manage IAM Identity Center. The IAM team must not be able to gain unnecessary access to the Organizations management account. The IAM team must be able to provision new IAM Identity Center permission sets and assignments for new and existing member accounts. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织来管理数百个 AWS 账户。该公司有一个团队负责 AWS 身份和访问管理 （IAM）。 IAM 团队希望实施 AWS IAM 身份中心。IAM 团队必须仅拥有管理 IAM 身份中心所需的最低权限。 IAM 团队不得能够获得对组织管理账户的不必要的访问权限。IAM 团队必须能够为新成员账户和现有 成员账户配置新的 IAM 身份中心权限集和分配。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account for the IAM team. Enable IAM Identity Center in the new account. In the Organizations management account, register the new account as a delegated administrator for IAM Identity Center.","B":"Create a new AWS account for the IAM team. Enable IAM Identity Center in the Organizations management account. In the Organizations management account, register the new account as a delegated administrator for IAM Identity Center.","C":"Create an SCP in Organizations. Create a new OU for the Organizations management account, and link the new SCP to the OU. Configure the SCP to deny all access to IAM Identity Center.","D":"Create IAM users and an IAM group for the IAM team in IAM Identity Center. Add the users to the group. Create a new permission set. Attach the AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator managed IAM policy to the group.","E":"Assign the new permission set to the Organizations management account. Allow the IAM team's group to use the permission set.","F":"Assign the new permission set to the new AWS account. Allow the IAM team's group to use the permission set."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 IAM 团队创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在新账户中启用 IAM 身份中心。在组织管理账户中，将 新账户注册为 IAM 身份中心的委托管理员。","B":"为 IAM 团队创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在组织管理账户中启用 IAM 身份中心。在组织管理账 户中，将新账户注册为 IAM 身份中心的委托管理员。","C":"在组织中创建服务控制策略（SCP）。为组织管理账户创建一个新的组织单位（OU），并将新的 SCP 链接到该 OU。配置 SCP 以拒绝对 IAM 身份中心的所有访问。","D":"在 IAM 身份中心为 IAM 团队创建 IAM 用户和一个 IAM 组。将用户添加到该组。创建一个新的权 限集。将 AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator 管理的 IAM 策略附加到该组。","E":"将新的权限集分配给组织管理账户。允许 IAM 团队的组使用该权限集。","F":"将新的权限集分配给新的 AWS 账户。允许 IAM 团队的组使用该权限集。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":297,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL global database that has two secondary AWS Regions. A DevOps engineer has configured the database parameter group to guarantee an RPO of 60 seconds. Write operations on the primary cluster are occasionally blocked because of the RPO setting. The DevOps engineer needs to reduce the frequency of blocked write operations. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用了一个亚马逊 Aurora PostgreSQL 全球数据库，该数据库在两个辅助 AWS 区域设有副本。一 位 DevOps 工程师将数据库参数组配置为保证 60 秒的恢复点目标（RPO）。由于 RPO 设置的原因，主集 群上的写入操作偶尔会被阻塞。 DevOps 工程师需要降低写入操作被阻塞的频率。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add an additional secondary cluster to the global database.","B":"Enable write forwarding for the global database.","C":"Remove one of the secondary clusters from the global database.","D":"Configure synchronous replication for the global database."},"options_zh":{"A":"在全局数据库中添加一个额外的辅助集群。","B":"为全局数据库启用写转发。","C":"从全局数据库中移除一个辅助集群。","D":"为全局数据库配置同步复制。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":298,"question_en":"A company has a web application that is hosted on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. The EKS cluster runs on AWS Fargate that is available through an internet-facing Application Load Balancer. The application is experiencing stability issues that lead to longer response times. A DevOps engineer needs to configure observability in Amazon CloudWatch to troubleshoot the issue. The solution must provide only the minimum necessary permissions. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个托管在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群上的网络应用程序。该 EKS 集群 通过面向互联网的应用程序负载均衡器在 AWS Fargate 上运行。 该应用程序出现稳定性问题，导致响应时间延长。一位 DevOps 工程师需要在 Amazon CloudWatch 中配 置可观测性以排查问题。解决方案必须仅提供必要的最小权限。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the CloudWatch agent as a Kubernetes StatefulSet to the EKS cluster.","B":"Deploy the AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry Collector as a Kubernetes DaemonSet to the EKS cluster.","C":"Associate a Kubernetes service account with an IAM role by using IAM roles for service accounts in Amazon EKS. Use the CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy AWS managed policy.","D":"Associate a Kubernetes service account with an IAM role by using IAM roles for service accounts in Amazon EKS. Use the CloudWatchAgentAdminPolicy AWS managed policy.","E":"Configure an IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider for the EKS cluster.","F":"Enable EKS control plane logging for the EKS cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 EKS 集群中将 CloudWatch 代理部署为 Kubernetes 有状态集。","B":"在 EKS 集群中以 Kubernetes 守护集的形式部署 AWS 版 OpenTelemetry 收集器。","C":"使用 Amazon EKS 中的服务账户的 IAM 角色功能将 Kubernetes 服务账户与 IAM 角色相关联。使用 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy AWS 管理策略。","D":"使用 Amazon EKS 中的服务账户 IAM 角色功能将 Kubernetes 服务账户与 IAM 角色相关联。使用 CloudWatchAgentAdminPolicy AWS 管理策略。","E":"为 EKS 集群配置一个 IAM OpenID Connect （OIDC） 提供程序。","F":"为 EKS 集群启用 EKS 控制平面日志记录。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":299,"question_en":"A company stores its Python-based application code in AWS CodeCommit. The company uses AWS CodePipeline to deploy the application. The CodeCommit repository and the CodePipeline pipeline are deployed to the same AWS account. The company's security team requires all code to be scanned for vulnerabilities before the code is deployed to production. If any vulnerabilities are found, the deployment must stop. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司将其基于 Python 的应用程序代码存储在 AWS CodeCommit 中。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 来 部署应用程序。CodeCommit 存储库和 CodePipeline 管道部署在同一个 AWS 账户中。 公司的安全团队要求所有代码在部署到生产环境之前都要进行漏洞扫描。如果发现任何漏洞，部署 必须停止。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new CodeBuild project. Configure the project to run a security scan on the code by using Amazon CodeGuru Security. Configure the CodeBuild project to raise an error if CodeGuru Security finds vulnerabilities. Create a new IAM role that has sufficient permissions to run CodeGuru Security scans. Assign the role to the CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, add a new stage before the deployment stage. Select AWS CodeBuild as the action provider for the new stage. Use the source artifact from the CodeCommit repository. Configure the action to use the CodeBuild project.","B":"Create a new CodeBuild project. Configure the project to run a security scan on the code by using Amazon Inspector. Configure the CodeBuild project to raise an error if Amazon Inspector finds vulnerabilities. Create a new IAM role that has sufficient permissions to run Amazon Inspector scans. Assign the role to the CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, add a new stage before the deployment stage. Select AWS CodeBuild as the action provider for the new stage. Use the source artifact from the CodeCommit repository. Configure the action to use the CodeBuild project.","C":"Update the IAM role that is attached to CodePipeline to include sufficient permissions to invoke Amazon DevOps Guru. In the CodePipeline pipeline, add a new stage before the deployment stage. Select DevOps Guru as the action provider for the new stage. Use the source artifact from the CodeCommit repository.","D":"Update the IAM role that is attached to CodePipeline to include sufficient permissions to invoke Amazon DevOps Guru. In the CodePipeline pipeline, add a new stage before the deployment stage. Select CodeGuru Security as the action provider for the new stage. Use the source artifact from the CodeCommit repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 CodeBuild 项目。配置该项目，使其使用 Amazon CodeGuru Security 对代码进行安全扫描。 配置 CodeBuild 项目，若 CodeGuru Security 发现漏洞则触发错误。创建一个新的 IAM 角色，赋予其运 行 CodeGuru Security 扫描的足够权限。将该角色分配给 CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中，在部 署阶段之前添加一个新阶段。选择 AWS CodeBuild 作为新阶段的操作提供程序。使用来自 CodeCommit 存储库的源工件。配置操作以使用 CodeBuild 项目。","B":"创建一个新的 CodeBuild 项目。配置该项目，使其使用 Amazon Inspector 对代码进行安全扫描。配置 CodeBuild 项目，如果 Amazon Inspector 发现漏洞则引发错误。创建一个新的 IAM 角色，该角色具有 运行 Amazon Inspector 扫描的足够权限。将该角色分配给 CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中， 在部署阶段之前添加一个新阶段。选择 AWS CodeBuild 作为新阶段的操作提供程序。使用来自 CodeCommit 存储库的源工件。配置操作以使用 CodeBuild 项目。","C":"更新附加到 CodePipeline 的 IAM 角色，使其包含调用 Amazon DevOps Guru 的足够权限。在 CodePipeline 管道中，在部署阶段之前添加一个新阶段。选择 DevOps Guru 作为新阶段的操作提供程 序。使用来自 CodeCommit 存储库的源工件。","D":"更新附加到 CodePipeline 的 IAM 角色，使其包含调用 Amazon DevOps Guru 的足够权限。在 CodePipeline 管道中，在部署阶段之前添加一个新阶段。为新阶段选择 CodeGuru Security 作为操作 提供程序。使用来自 CodeCommit 存储库的源工件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":300,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer deploys an application to a fleet of Amazon Linux EC2 instances. The DevOps engineer needs to monitor system metrics across the fleet. The DevOps engineer wants to monitor the relationship between network traffic and memory utilization for the application code. The DevOps engineer wants to track the data on a 60 second interval. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师将一个应用程序部署到一组亚马逊 Linux EC2 实例上。该 DevOps 工程师需要监控整个 实例群组的系统指标。该 DevOps 工程师希望监控应用程序代码的网络流量与内存利用率之间的关系。该 DevOps 工程师希望以 60 秒为间隔跟踪数据。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon CloudWatch basic monitoring to collect the NetworkIn metric and the MemoryBytesUsed metric. Graph the metrics in CloudWatch.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch detailed monitoring to collect the NetworkIn metric and the MemoryBytesUsed metric. Graph the metrics in CloudWatch.","C":"Use Amazon CloudWatch detailed monitoring to collect the NetworkIn metric. Install the CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances to collect the mem_used metric. Graph the metrics in CloudWatch.","D":"Use Amazon CloudWatch basic monitoring to collect the built-in NetworkIn metric. Install the CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances to collect the mem_used metric. Graph the metrics in CloudWatch."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 基本监控来收集 NetworkIn 指标和 MemoryBytesUsed 指标。在 CloudWatch 中 绘制这些指标的图表。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 详细监控来收集 NetworkIn 指标和 MemoryBytesUsed 指标。 在 CloudWatch 中绘制这些指标的图表。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 详细监控来收集 NetworkIn 指标。在 EC2 实例上安装 CloudWatch 代理以收 集 mem_used 指标。在 CloudWatch 中绘制这些指标的图表。","D":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 基本监控来收集内置的 NetworkIn 指标。在 EC2 实例上安装 CloudWatch 代理以收集 mem_used 指标。在 CloudWatch 中绘制这些指标的图表。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":301,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Systems Manager to manage a fleet of Amazon Linux EC2 instances that have SSM Agent installed. All EC2 instances are configured to use Instance Metadata Service Version 2 (IMDSv2) and are running in the same AWS account and AWS Region. Company policy requires developers to use only Amazon Linux. The company wants to ensure that all new EC2 instances are automatically managed by Systems Manager after creation. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Systems Manager 来管理一批安装了 SSM 代理的 Amazon Linux EC2 实例。所有 EC2 实例均配置为使用实例元数据服务版本 2（IMDSv2），并且都在同一个 AWS 账户和 AWS 区域中运行。 公司政策要求开发人员只能使用 Amazon Linux。 该公司希望确保所有新创建的 EC2 实例在创建后都能自动由系统管理器进行管理。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM role that has a trust policy that allows Systems Manager to assume the role. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedEC2InstanceDefaultPolicy policy to the role. Configure the default-ec2-instance- management-role SSM service setting to use the role.","B":"Ensure that AWS Config is set up. Create an AWS Config rule that validates if an EC2 instance has SSM Agent installed. Configure the rule to run on EC2 configuration changes. Configure automatic remediation for the rule to run the AWS-InstallSSMAgent SSM document to install SSM Agent.","C":"Configure Systems Manager Patch Manager. Create a patch baseline that automatically installs SSM Agent on all new EC2 instances. Create a patch group for all EC2 instances. Attach the patch baseline to the patch group. Create a maintenance window and maintenance window task to start installing SSM Agent daily.","D":"Create an EC2 instance role that has a trust policy that allows Amazon EC2 to assume the role. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore policy to the role. Ensure that AWS Config is set up. Use the ec2-instance-profile-attached managed AWS Config rule to validate if an EC2 instance has the role attached. Configure the rule to run on EC2 configuration changes. Configure automatic remediation for the rule to run the AWS-SetupManagedRoleOnEc2Instance SSM document to attach the role to the EC2 instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有信任策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 Systems Manager 假定该角色。将 AmazonSSMManagedEC2InstanceDefaultPolicy 策略附加到该角色。将默认的 ec2 实例管理角色 SSM 服 务设置配置为使用该角色。","B":"确保已设置 AWS Config。创建一条 AWS Config 规则，用于验证 EC2 实例是否已安装 SSM 代理。将 规则配置为在 EC2 配置更改时运行。为该规则配置自动修复，以运行 AWS-InstallSSMAgent SSM 文 档来安装 SSM 代理。","C":"配置系统管理器补丁管理器。创建一个补丁基准，自动在所有新的 EC2 实例上安装 SSM 代理。为所有 EC2 实例创建一个补丁组。将补丁基准附加到补丁组。创建一个维护窗口和维护窗口任务，每天开始安 装 SSM 代理。","D":"创建一个 EC2 实例角色，该角色的信任策略允许 Amazon EC2 假定该角色。将 AmazonSSMManaged InstanceCore 策略附加到该角色。确保已设置 AWS Config。使用 ec2-instance-profile-attached 管理 的 AWS Config 规则来验证 EC2 实例是否附加了该角色。配置规则在 EC2 配置更改时运行。为该 规则配置自动修复，以运行 AWS-SetupManagedRoleOnEc2Instance SSM 文档将角色附加到 EC2 实 例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":302,"question_en":"A company configured an Amazon S3 event source for an AWS Lambda function. The company needs the Lambda function to run when a new object is created or an existing object is modified in a specific S3 bucket. The Lambda function will use the S3 bucket name and the S3 object key of the incoming event to read the contents of the new or modified S3 object. The Lambda function will parse the contents and save the parsed contents to an Amazon DynamoDB table. The Lambda function's execution role has permissions to read from the S3 bucket and to write to the DynamoDB table. During testing, a DevOps engineer discovers that the Lambda function does not run when objects are added to the S3 bucket or when existing objects are modified. Which solution will resolve these problems?","question_zh":"一家公司为 AWS Lambda 函数配置了一个 Amazon S3 事件源。该公司需要在特定的 S3 存储桶中创建新 对象或修改现有对象时运行该 Lambda 函数。该 Lambda 函数将使用传入事件的 S3 存储桶名称和 S3 对 象键来读取新创建或已修改的 S3 对象的内容。该 Lambda 函数将解析内容，并将解析后的内容保存到 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。 Lambda 函数的执行角色具有从 S3 存储桶读取以及向 DynamoDB 表写入的权限。在测试期间，一 位 DevOps 工程师发现，当向 S3 存储桶添加对象或修改现有对象时，Lambda 函数不会运行。 哪种解决方案能解决这些问题？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 bucket policy for the S3 bucket that grants the S3 bucket permission to invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Create a resource policy for the Lambda function to grant Amazon S3 permission to invoke the Lambda function on the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as an OnFailure destination for the Lambda function. Update the Lambda function to process messages from the SQS queue and the S3 event notifications.","D":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as the destination for the S3 bucket event notifications. Update the Lambda function's execution role to have permission to read from the SQS queue. Update the Lambda function to consume messages from the SQS queue."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 S3 存储桶创建一个 S3 存储桶策略，授予该 S3 存储桶调用 Lambda 函数的权限。","B":"为 Lambda 函数创建资源策略，授予 Amazon S3 在 S3 存储桶上调用 Lambda 函数的权限。","C":"将 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列配置为 Lambda 函数的 OnFailure 目的地。更新 Lambda 函数以处理来自 SQS 队列和 S3 事件通知的消息。","D":"将 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列配置为 S3 存储桶事件通知的目的地。更新 Lambda 函数的执行角色，使其具有从 SQS 队列读取的权限。更新 Lambda 函数以从 SQS 队列 中消费消息。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":303,"question_en":"A company recently configured AWS Control Tower in its organization in AWS Organizations. The company enrolled all existing AWS accounts in AWS Control Tower. The company wants to ensure that all new AWS accounts are automatically enrolled in AWS Control Tower. The company has an existing AWS Step Functions workflow that creates new AWS accounts and performs any actions required as part of account creation. The Step Functions workflow is defined in the same AWS account as AWS Control Tower. Which combination of steps should the company add to the Step Functions workflow to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近在其 AWS 组织中配置了 AWS Control Tower。该公司已将所有现有的 AWS 账户纳入 AWS Control Tower。该公司希望确保所有新的 AWS 账户都能自动纳入 AWS Control Tower。 该公司现有的 AWS Step Functions 工作流会创建新的 AWS 账户，并执行账户创建过程中所需的任何 操作。此 Step Functions 工作流定义在与 AWS Control Tower 相同的 AWS 账户中。 公司应向 Step Functions 工作流添加哪些步骤组合才能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge event that has an aws.controltower source and a CreateManagedAccount detail-type. Add the details of the new AWS account to the detail field of the event.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge event that has an aws.controltower source and a SetupLandingZone detail-type. Add the details of the new AWS account to the detail field of the event.","C":"Create an AWSControlTowerExecution role in the new AWS account. Configure the role to allow the AWS Control Tower administrator account to assume the role.","D":"Call the AWS Service Catalog ProvisionProduct API operation with the details of the new AWS account.","E":"Call the Organizations EnableAWSServiceAccess API operation with the controltower.amazonaws.com service name and the details of the new AWS account."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有 aws.controltower 源和 CreateManagedAccount 详细类型（detail-type）的 Amazon EventBridge 事件。将新 AWS 账户的详细信息添加到事件的 detail 字段中。","B":"创建一个具有 aws.controltower 源和 SetupLandingZone 详细类型属性的 Amazon EventBridge 事件。 将新 AWS 账户的详细信息添加到事件的 detail 字段中。","C":"在新创建的 AWS 账户中创建一个 AWSControlTowerExecution 角色。配置该角色，使其允许 AWS 控制塔管理员账户承担此角色。","D":"使用新 AWS 账户的详细信息调用 AWS 服务目录的 ProvisionProduct API 操作。","E":"调用组织的 EnableAWSServiceAccess API 操作，使用 controltower.amazonaws.com 服务名称以及新 AWS 账户的详细信息。"},"answer":["D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":304,"question_en":"A company's web application uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) to direct traffic to Amazon EC2 instances across three Availability Zones. The company has deployed a newer version of the application to one Availability Zone for testing. If a problem is detected with the application, the company wants to direct traffic away from the affected Availability Zone until the deployment has been rolled back. The application must remain available and maintain static stability during the rollback. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司的网络应用程序使用应用负载均衡器（ALB）将流量分配到三个可用区中的亚马逊 EC2 实例。 该公司已在其中一个可用区部署了应用程序的新版本以进行测试。如果出现 检测到应用程序出现问题，公司希望在回滚部署期间将流量从受影响的可用区转移出去。在此期间，应 用程序必须保持可用并维持静态稳定。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Disable cross-zone load balancing on the ALB's target group. Initiate a zonal shift on the ALB to direct traffic away from the affected Availability Zone.","B":"Disable cross-zone load balancing on the ALB's target group. Manually remove instances in the target group that belong to the affected Availability Zone.","C":"Configure cross-zone load balancing on the ALB's target group to inherit settings from the ALB. Initiate a zonal shift on the ALB to direct traffic away from the affected Availability Zone.","D":"Configure cross-zone load balancing on the ALB's target group to inherit settings from the ALB. Remove the subnet that is associated with the affected Availability Zone."},"options_zh":{"A":"禁用应用负载均衡器（ALB）目标组的跨区负载均衡。在 ALB 上启动区域转移，将流量从受影响的可 用区转移出去。","B":"禁用应用负载均衡器（ALB）目标组的跨区域负载均衡。手动从目标组中移除属于受影响可用区的实例。","C":"在 ALB 的目标组上配置跨区域负载均衡，以继承 ALB 的设置。在 ALB 上启动区域转移，将流量从受影 响的可用区转移出去。","D":"在 ALB 的目标组上配置跨区域负载均衡以继承 ALB 的设置。移除与受影响的可用区相关联的子 网。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":305,"question_en":"A company has several AWS accounts. An Amazon Connect instance runs in each account. The company uses an Amazon EventBridge default event bus in each account for event handling. A DevOps team needs to receive all the Amazon Connect events in a single DevOps account. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有多个 AWS 账户。每个账户中都运行着一个 Amazon Connect 实例。该公司在每个账户中使用 Amazon EventBridge 默认事件总线来处理事件。 一个 DevOps 团队需要在一个 DevOps 账户中接收所有的 Amazon Connect 事件。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the resource-based policy of the default event bus in each account to allow the DevOps account to replay events. Configure an EventBridge rule in the DevOps account that matches Amazon Connect events and has a target of the default event bus in the other accounts.","B":"Update the resource-based policy of the default event bus in each account to allow the DevOps account to receive events. Configure an EventBridge rule in the DevOps account that matches Amazon Connect events and has a target of the default event bus in the other accounts.","C":"Update the resource-based policy of the default event bus in the DevOps account. Update the policy to allow events to be received from the accounts. Configure an EventBridge rule in each account that matches Amazon Connect events and has a target of the DevOps account's default event bus.","D":"Update the resource-based policy of the default event bus in the DevOps account. Update the policy to allow events to be replayed by the accounts. Configure an EventBridge rule in each account that matches Amazon Connect events and has a target of the DevOps account's default event bus."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个账户中更新默认事件总线的基于资源的策略，以允许 DevOps 账户重放事件。在 DevOps 账户中 配置一个 EventBridge 规则，使其匹配 Amazon Connect 事件，并将目标设置为其他账户中的默认事件 总线。","B":"在每个账户中更新默认事件总线的基于资源的策略，以允许 DevOps 账户接收事件。在 DevOps 账户中配 置一个 EventBridge 规则，使其匹配 Amazon Connect 事件，并将目标设置为其他账户中的默认事件总线。","C":"更新 DevOps 账户中默认事件总线的基于资源的策略。将策略更新为允许从这些账户接收事件。在每个账 户中配置一个 EventBridge 规则，使其匹配 Amazon Connect 事件，并将目标设置为 DevOps 账户的默认 事件总线。","D":"更新 DevOps 账户中默认事件总线的基于资源的策略。将策略更新为允许账户重放事件。在每个账户中配 置一个 EventBridge 规则，该规则匹配 Amazon Connect 事件，并将目标设置为 DevOps 账户的默认事件 总线。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":306,"question_en":"A company has deployed an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster with Amazon EC2 node groups. The company's DevOps team uses the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler and recently installed a supported EKS cluster Autoscaler. The DevOps team needs to implement a solution to collect metrics and logs of the EKS cluster to establish a baseline for performance. The DevOps team will create an initial set of thresholds for specific metrics and will update the thresholds over time as the cluster is used. The DevOps team must receive an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) email notification if the initial set of thresholds is exceeded or if the EKS cluster Autoscaler is not functioning properly. The solution must collect cluster, node, and pod metrics. The solution also must capture logs in Amazon CloudWatch. Which combination of steps should the DevOps team take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司部署了一个带有 Amazon EC2 节点组的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service（Amazon EKS）集群。 该公司的 DevOps 团队使用了 Kubernetes 水平 Pod 自动扩展器，并且最近安装了一个受支持的 EKS 集群 自动扩展器。 DevOps 团队需要实施一个解决方案来收集 EKS 集群的指标和日志，以建立性能基准。DevOps 团队将为 特定指标创建初始阈值集，并随着集群的使用情况适时更新这些阈值。如果初始阈值集被超出，或者 EKS 集群的自动扩展器运行不正常，DevOps 团队必须收到亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）的电子 邮件通知。 该解决方案必须收集集群、节点和 Pod 的指标。该解决方案还必须在 Amazon CloudWatch 中捕获日志。 DevOps 团队应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the CloudWatch agent and Fluent Bit to the cluster. Ensure that the EKS cluster has appropriate permissions to send metrics and logs to CloudWatch.","B":"Deploy AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry to the cluster. Ensure that the EKS cluster has appropriate permissions to send metrics and logs to CloudWatch.","C":"Create CloudWatch alarms to monitor the CPU, memory, and node failure metrics of the cluster. Configure the alarms to send an SNS email notification to the DevOps team if thresholds are exceeded.","D":"Create a CloudWatch composite alarm to monitor a metric log filter of the CPU, memory, and node metrics of the cluster. Configure the alarm to send an SNS email notification to the DevOps team when anomalies are detected.","E":"Create a CloudWatch alarm to monitor the logs of the Autoscaler deployments for errors. Configure the alarm to send an SNS email notification to the DevOps team if thresholds are exceeded.","F":"Create a CloudWatch alarm to monitor a metric log filter of the Autoscaler deployments for errors. Configure the alarm to send an SNS email notification to the DevOps team if thresholds are exceeded."},"options_zh":{"A":"在集群中部署 CloudWatch 代理和 Fluent Bit。确保 EKS 集群具有向 CloudWatch 发送指标 和日志的适当权限。","B":"将 AWS OpenTelemetry 发行版部署到集群。确保 EKS 集群具有向 CloudWatch 发送指标和日志的 适当权限。","C":"创建 CloudWatch 警报以监控集群的 CPU、内存和节点故障指标。将警报配置为在阈值超出时向 DevOps 团队发送 SNS 电子邮件通知。","D":"创建一个 CloudWatch 复合警报，用于监控集群的 CPU、内存和节点指标的日志筛选器。配置警报， 以便在检测到异常时向 DevOps 团队发送 SNS 电子邮件通知。","E":"创建一个 CloudWatch 警报来监控自动缩放器部署的日志中的错误。如果超出阈值，配置警报向 DevOps 团队发送 SNS 电子邮件通知。","F":"创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，用于监控 Autoscaler 部署的指标日志筛选器中的错误。如果超出阈值，配 置警报向 DevOps 团队发送 SNS 电子邮件通知。"},"answer":["A","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":307,"question_en":"A company discovers that its production environment and disaster recovery (DR) environment are deployed to the same AWS Region. All the production applications run on Amazon EC2 instances and are deployed by AWS CloudFormation. The applications use an Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP volume for application storage. No application data resides on the EC2 instances. A DevOps engineer copies the required AMIs to a new DR Region. The DevOps engineer also updates the CloudFormation code to accept a Region as a parameter. The storage needs to have an RPO of 10 minutes in the DR Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司发现其生产环境和灾难恢复（DR）环境部署在同一个 AWS 区域。所有生产应用程序均在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行，并通过 AWS CloudFormation 进行部署。这些应用程序使用 Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 卷进行应用存储。没有应用程序数据驻留在 EC2 实例上。 一位 DevOps 工程师将所需的 AMI 复制到新的灾难恢复区域。该 DevOps 工程师还更新了 CloudFormation 代码，使其能够接受区域作为参数。在灾难恢复区域，存储需要具有 10 分钟的恢复点目标（RPO）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket in both Regions. Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) for the S3 buckets. Create a scheduled AWS Lambda function to copy any new content from the FSx for ONTAP volume to the S3 bucket in the production Region.","B":"Use AWS Backup to create a backup vault and a custom backup plan that has a 10-minute frequency. Specify the DR Region as the target Region. Assign the EC2 instances in the production Region to the backup plan.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to create snapshots of the instance store volumes that are attached to the EC2 instances. Configure the Lambda function to copy the snapshots to the DR Region and to remove the previous copies. Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule that invokes the Lambda function every 10 minutes.","D":"Create an FSx for ONTAP instance in the DR Region. Configure a 5-minute schedule for a volume- level NetApp SnapMirror to replicate the volume from the production Region to the DR Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在两个区域分别创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。为这两个 S3 存储桶配置 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。创 建一个计划的 AWS Lambda 函数，用于将 FSx for ONTAP 卷中的任何新内容复制到生产区域的 S3 存储桶中。","B":"使用 AWS Backup 创建一个备份存储库和一个自定义备份计划，该计划的频率为 10 分钟。指定灾难 恢复区域作为目标区域。将生产区域中的 EC2 实例分配给该备份计划。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为附加到 EC2 实例的实例存储卷创建快照。配置该 Lambda 函数， 使其将快照复制到灾难恢复区域，并删除之前的副本。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则， 每 10 分钟调用一次该 Lambda 函数。","D":"在灾难恢复区域创建一个 FSx for ONTAP 实例。为卷级 NetApp SnapMirror 配置 5 分钟的计划，将 生产区域的卷复制到灾难恢复区域。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":308,"question_en":"During a security audit, a company discovered that some security groups allow SSH traffic from 0.0.0.0/0. A security team must implement a solution to detect and remediate this issue as soon as possible. The company uses one organization in AWS Organizations to manage all the company's AWS accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"在一次安全审计中，一家公司发现某些安全组允许从 0.0.0.0/0 进行 SSH 通信。安全团队必须尽快实施 解决方案来检测并修复此问题。该公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理其所有的 AWS 账 户。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Config for all AWS accounts. Use a periodic trigger to activate the vpe-sg-port-restriction- check AWS Config rule. Create an AWS Lambda function to remediate any noncompliant rules.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function in each AWS account to delete all the security group rules. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match security group update events or creation events. Set the Lambda function in each account as a target for the rule.","C":"Enable AWS Config for all AWS accounts. Create a custom AWS Config rule to run on the restricted- ssh configuration change trigger. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to remediate any noncompliant resources.","D":"Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation document in each account to inspect all security groups and to delete noncompliant rules. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Automation document every hour."},"options_zh":{"A":"为所有 AWS 账户启用 AWS Config。使用定期触发器激活 vpe-sg-port-restrictioncheck AWS Config 规 则。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来修复任何不符合规则的情况。","B":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来删除所有安全组规则。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以匹配安全组更新事件或创建事件。将每个账户中的 Lambda 函数设置为该规则的 目标。","C":"为所有 AWS 账户启用 AWS Config。创建一个自定义的 AWS Config 规则，在受限的账户上运行。 SSH 配置更改触发器。配置规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来修复任何不符合要求的资源。","D":"在每个账户中创建一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 文档，用于检查所有安全组并删除不符合 规定的规则。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则每小时运行一次该 Automation 文档。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":309,"question_en":"A company's DevOps engineer must install a software package on 30 on-premises VMs and 15 Amazon EC2 instances. The DevOps engineer needs to ensure that all VMs receive the package in a process that is auditable and that any configuration drift on the VMs is automatically identified and alerted on. The company uses AWS Direct Connect to connect its on-premises data center to AWS. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师必须在 30 台本地虚拟机和 15 台亚马逊 EC2 实例上安装一个软件包。 DevOps 工程师需要确保所有虚拟机都能接收到该软件包，并且整个过程可审计，同时自动识别虚拟机 上的任何配置偏差。 并发出警报。该公司使用 AWS Direct Connect 将其本地数据中心连接到 AWS。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Write a script that iterates through the list of VMs once a week. Configure the script to check for the package and install the package if the package is not found. Configure the script to send an email message notification to the system administrator if the package is not found.","B":"Install the AWS Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent) on all VMs. Use the SSM Agent to install the package. Use AWS Config to monitor for configuration drift. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to notify the system administrator if any drift is found.","C":"Write a script that checks if the package is installed across the environment. Configure the script to create a list of all VMs that are noncompliant. Configure the script to send the list to the system administrator, who will install the package on the noncompliant VMs.","D":"Log in to each VM. Use a local package manager to install the package. Use AWS Config to monitor the AWS resources for configuration changes. Write a script to monitor the on-premises resources."},"options_zh":{"A":"编写一个每周运行一次的脚本，遍历虚拟机列表。配置该脚本检查指定软件包，如果未找到该软 件包则进行安装。如果未找到该软件包，配置脚本向系统管理员发送电子邮件通知。","B":"在所有虚拟机上安装 AWS 系统管理器代理（SSM 代理）。使用 SSM 代理来安装软件包。使用 AWS 配置来监控配置漂移。如果发现任何漂移，使用亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）通知 系统管理员。","C":"编写一个脚本，用于检查整个环境中是否已安装该软件包。配置该脚本，使其生成所有未安装该 软件包的虚拟机列表。配置该脚本，使其将该列表发送给系统管理员，由系统管理员在未安装 该软件包的虚拟机上进行安装。","D":"登录到每台虚拟机。使用本地包管理器安装软件包。使用 AWS Config 监控 AWS 资源的配置更改。 编写一个脚本以监控本地资源。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":310,"question_en":"A company has an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in the eu-west-1 Region. The pipeline stores the build artifacts in an Amazon S3 bucket. The pipeline builds and deploys an AWS Lambda function by using an AWS CloudFormation deploy action. A DevOps engineer needs to update the existing pipeline to also deploy the Lambda function to the us- east-1 Region. The pipeline has already been updated to create an additional artifact to deploy to us-east- 1. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 eu-west-1 区域拥有一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。该管道将构建工件存储在 Amazon S3 存储 桶中。该管道通过使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署操作来构建和部署一个 AWS Lambda 函数。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要更新现有的流水线，以便将 Lambda 函数也部署到 useast-1 区域。该流水线已更 新为创建一个额外的工件以部署到 us-east-1 区域。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Modify the CloudFormation template to include a parameter for the Lambda function code's .zip file location. Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to pass in the us-east-1 artifact location as a parameter override.","B":"Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to use the CloudFormation template from the additional artifact that was created for us-east-1.","C":"Create an S3 bucket in us-east-1. Configure the S3 bucket policy to allow CodePipeline to have read and write access.","D":"Create an S3 bucket in us-east-1. Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the S3 bucket in eu-west-1 to the S3 bucket in us-east-1.","E":"Modify the pipeline to include the S3 bucket for us-east-1 as an artifact store. Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to use the CloudFormation template from the us-east-1 artifact."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 CloudFormation 模板，添加一个用于 Lambda 函数代码的 .zip 文件位置的参数。在管道中为 us- east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。配置新的部署操作，将 us-east-1 的工件位置作为参 数覆盖传入。","B":"在管道中为 us-east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。将新部署操作配置为使用为 us-east-1 创建的附加工件中的 CloudFormation 模板。","C":"在 us-east-1 区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。配置 S3 存储桶策略，允许 CodePipeline 具有读写访问权限。","D":"在 us-east-1 区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。配置从 eu-west-1 区域的 S3 存储桶到 us-east-1 区域的 S3 存储桶 的 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。","E":"修改管道，将 us-east-1 区域的 S3 存储桶作为工件存储包含进来。在管道中为 us-east-1 区域创建一个 新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。配置新的部署操作，使其使用来自 us-east-1 区域的工件中的 CloudFormation 模板。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":311,"question_en":"A company uses an AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) application for its infrastructure. The AWS CDK application creates AWS Lambda functions and the IAM roles that are attached to the functions. The company also uses AWS Organizations. The company's developers can assume the AWS CDK application deployment role. The company's security team discovered that the developers and the role used to deploy the AWS CDK application have more permissions than necessary. The security team also discovered that the roles attached to the Lambda functions that the CDK application creates have more permissions than necessary. The developers must not have the ability to grant additional permissions. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）应用程序来构建其基础设施。该 AWS CDK 应用程序会创 建 AWS Lambda 函数以及与这些函数关联的 IAM 角色。该公司还使用 AWS 组织。公司的开发人员可以 承担 AWS CDK 应用程序部署角色。 该公司安全团队发现，开发人员以及用于部署 AWS CDK 应用程序的角色所拥有的权限超出了必要范 围。安全团队还发现，CDK 应用程序创建的 Lambda 函数所关联的角色所拥有的权限也超出了必要范 围。开发人员不得拥有授予额外权限的能力。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that denies the iam:CreateRole action and the iam:UpdateRole action for the developer role and the AWS CDK application deployment role. Centrally create new IAM roles to attach to the Lambda functions for the developers to use to provision Lambda functions.","B":"Create an IAM permission boundary policy. Define the maximum actions that the AWS CDK application requires in the policy. Update the account's AWS CDK bootstrapping to use the permission boundary. Update the configuration in the AWS CDK application for the default permissions boundary to use the policy.","C":"Create an IAM permission boundary policy. Define the maximum actions that the AWS CDK application requires in the policy. Instruct the developers to use the permission boundary policy name when they create a role in the AWS CDK application code.","D":"Create an SCP that denies the iam:CreateRole action and the iam:UpdateRole action for the developer role. Give the AWS CDK deployment role access to create roles associated with Lambda functions. Run AWS Identity and Access Management Access Analyzer to verify that the Lambda functions role does not have permissions."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 SCP，拒绝开发人员角色和 AWS CDK 应用程序部署角色的 iam:CreateRole 操作和 iam: UpdateRole 操作。集中创建新的 IAM 角色，将其附加到 Lambda 函数，供开发人员用于配置 Lambda 函数。","B":"创建一个 IAM 权限边界策略。在策略中定义 AWS CDK 应用程序所需的最大操作权限。更新账户的 AWS CDK 启动配置以使用该权限边界。在 AWS CDK 应用程序的默认权限边界配置中使用该策略。","C":"创建一个 IAM 权限边界策略。在策略中定义 AWS CDK 应用程序所需的最大操作权限。指示开发人 员在 AWS CDK 应用程序代码中创建角色时使用权限边界策略名称。","D":"创建一个 SCP，拒绝开发人员角色的 iam:CreateRole 操作和 iam:UpdateRole 操作。授予 AWS CDK 部 署角色创建与 Lambda 函数相关联的角色的权限。运行 AWS 身份和访问管理访问分析器以验证 Lambda 函数角色没有权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":312,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) private registries to store container images. A DevOps team needs to ensure that the container images are regularly scanned for software package vulnerabilities. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）的私有注册表来存储容器镜像。 DevOps 团队需要确保定期扫描容器镜像中的软件包漏洞。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable enhanced scanning for private registries in Amazon ECR.","B":"Enable basic continuous scanning for private registries in Amazon ECR.","C":"Create an AWS System Manager Automation document to scan images by using the AWS SDK. Configure the Automation document to run when a new image is pushed to an ECR registry.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that scans all images in Amazon ECR by using the AWS SDK. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function each day."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用对 Amazon ECR 中的私有注册表的增强扫描功能。","B":"启用对 Amazon ECR 中私有注册表的基本持续扫描。","C":"使用 AWS SDK 创建一个 AWS 系统管理器自动化文档来扫描镜像。配置该自动化文档，使其 在新镜像推送到 ECR 注册表时运行。","D":"使用 AWS SDK 创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于扫描 Amazon ECR 中的所有镜像。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每天调用该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":313,"question_en":"A security team sets up a workflow that invokes an AWS Step Functions workflow when Amazon EventBridge matches specific events. The events can be generated by several AWS services. AWS CloudTrail records user activities. The security team notices that some important events do not invoke the workflow as expected. The CloudTrail logs do not indicate any direct errors related to the missing events. Which combination of steps will identify the root cause of the missing event invocations? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一个安全团队设置了一个工作流，当 Amazon EventBridge 匹配到特定事件时，该工作流会调用 AWS Step Functions 工作流。这些事件可以由多个 AWS 服务生成。AWS CloudTrail 记录用户活动。 安全团队注意到一些重要事件并未如预期那样触发工作流。CloudTrail 日志中也没有显示与这些 缺失事件直接相关的任何错误。 哪些步骤组合能够找出事件调用丢失的根本原因？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable EventBridge schema discovery on the event bus to determine whether the event patterns match the expected schema.","B":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch to monitor EventBridge metrics and Step Functions metrics. Set up alerts for anomalies in event patterns and workflow invocations.","C":"Configure an AWS Lambda logging function to monitor and log events from EventBridge to provide more details about the processed events.","D":"Review the Step Functions execution history for patterns of failures or timeouts that could correlate to the missing event invocations.","E":"Review metrics for the EventBridge failed invocations to ensure that the IAM execution role that is attached to the rule has sufficient permissions.","F":"Verify that the Step Functions workflow has the correct permissions to be invoked by EventBridge."},"options_zh":{"A":"在事件总线上启用 EventBridge 架构发现功能，以确定事件模式是否与预期架构匹配。","B":"配置 Amazon CloudWatch 来监控 EventBridge 指标和 Step Functions 指标。为事件模式和工作流调 用中的异常情况设置警报。","C":"配置一个 AWS Lambda 日志记录函数，以监控并记录来自 EventBridge 的事件，从而提供有关已 处理事件的更多详细信息。","D":"查看步骤函数的执行历史记录，寻找可能与缺失事件调用相关的故障或超时模式。","E":"检查 EventBridge 失败调用的指标，以确保附加到规则的 IAM 执行角色具有足够的权限。","F":"确认 Step Functions 工作流具有被 EventBridge 调用的正确权限。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":314,"question_en":"A company's DevOps engineer uses AWS Systems Manager to perform maintenance tasks. The company has a few Amazon EC2 instances that require a restart after notifications from AWS Health. The DevOps engineer must implement an automated solution that uses Amazon EventBridge to remediate the notifications during the company's scheduled maintenance windows. How should the DevOps engineer configure an EventBridge rule to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS 系统管理器来执行维护任务。该公司有几台亚马逊 EC2 实例，在 收到 AWS 健康状况的通知后需要重启。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个自动化解决方案，该方案使用亚马逊事件总线（Amazon EventBridge）来进行修复。 公司在计划维护期间的通知。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置 EventBridge 规则以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an event source of AWS Health. Configure event types that indicate scheduled instance termination and retirement. Target the AWS-RestartEC2Instance Systems Manager Automation runbook to restart the EC2 instances.","B":"Configure an event source of Systems Manager. Configure an event type that indicates a maintenance window. Target the AWS-RestartEC2Instance Systems Manager Automation runbook to restart the EC2 instances.","C":"Configure an event source of AWS Health. Configure event types that indicate scheduled instance termination and retirement. Target a newly created AWS Lambda function that registers a Systems Manager maintenance window task to restart the EC2 instances.","D":"Configure an event source of EC2. Configure an event type that indicates instance state notification. Target a newly created AWS Lambda function that registers a Systems Manager maintenance window task to restart the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Health 的事件源。配置指示计划内实例终止和退役的事件类型。将目标指向 AWS- RestartEC2Instance 系统管理器自动化运行手册以重启 EC2 实例。","B":"配置 Systems Manager 的事件源。配置一种表明维护窗口的事件类型。将 AWS-RestartEC2Instance Systems Manager 自动化运行手册作为目标，以重启 EC2 实例。","C":"配置 AWS Health 的事件源。配置指示计划内实例终止和退役的事件类型。将目标指向新创建的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会注册一个 Systems Manager 维护窗口任务以重启 EC2 实例。","D":"配置一个 EC2 事件源。配置一种表示实例状态通知的事件类型。将目标指向新创建的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数用于注册 Systems Manager 维护窗口任务以重启 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":315,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that builds and deploys a web application on AWS. The pipeline has a source stage, a build stage, and a deploy stage. When deployed properly, the web application responds with a 200 OK HTTP response code when the URL of the home page is requested. The home page recently returned a 503 HTTP response code after CodePipeline deployed the application. The DevOps engineer needs to add an automated test into the pipeline. The automated test must ensure that the application returns a 200 OK HTTP response code after the application is deployed. The pipeline must fail if the response code is not present during the test. The DevOps engineer has added a CheckURL stage after the deploy stage in the pipeline. What should the DevOps engineer do next to implement the automated test?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师管理着一条 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道用于在 AWS 上构建和部署一个网络应 用程序。此管道包含源代码阶段、构建阶段和部署阶段。如果部署得当，当请求主页的 URL 时，该网 络应用程序会返回 200 OK 的 HTTP 响应代码。 最近在 CodePipeline 部署应用程序后，主页返回了 503 HTTP 响应代码。开发运维工程师需要在管道中添 加一个自动化测试。该自动化测试必须确保应用程序在部署后返回 200 OK HTTP 响应代码。如果在测试 期间未出现该响应代码，管道必须失败。开发运维工程师已在管道的部署阶段之后添加了一个 CheckURL 阶段。 接下来，DevOps 工程师应该做什么来实现自动化测试？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the CheckURL stage to use an Amazon CloudWatch action. Configure the action to use a canary synthetic monitoring check on the application URL and to report a success or failure to CodePipeline.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function to check the response code status of the URL and to report a success or failure to CodePipeline. Configure an action in the CheckURL stage to invoke the Lambda function.","C":"Configure the CheckURL stage to use an AWS CodeDeploy action. Configure the action with an input artifact that is the URL of the application and to report a success or failure to CodePipeline.","D":"Deploy an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API that checks the response code status of the URL and that reports success or failure to CodePipeline. Configure the CheckURL stage to use the AWS Device Farm test action and to provide the API Gateway HTTP API as an input artifact."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CheckURL 阶段配置为使用 Amazon CloudWatch 操作。配置该操作以对应用程序 URL 进行金丝 雀合成监控检查，并向 CodePipeline 报告成功或失败。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来检查 URL 的响应代码状态，并向 CodePipeline 报告成功或失败。在 CheckURL 阶段配置一个操作以调用该 Lambda 函数。","C":"将 CheckURL 阶段配置为使用 AWS CodeDeploy 操作。配置该操作，使其输入工件为应用程序的 URL，并向 CodePipeline 报告成功或失败。","D":"部署一个 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API，用于检查 URL 的响应代码状态，并向 CodePipeline 报告 成功或失败。配置 CheckURL 阶段以使用 AWS 设备农场测试操作，并将 API Gateway HTTP API 作为输入工件提供。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":316,"question_en":"A company has an application that uploads access logs to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. The fields in the log lines include the response code and the application name. The company wants to create a CloudWatch metric to track the number of requests by response code in a specific range and with a specific application name. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，会将访问日志上传到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。日志行中的字段 包括响应代码和应用程序名称。 该公司希望创建一个 CloudWatch 指标，用于跟踪特定范围内且具有特定应用程序名称的请求数量（按 响应代码划分）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Logs log event filter on the CloudWatch Logs log stream to match the response code range. Configure the log event filter to increment a metric. Set the response code and application name as dimensions.","B":"Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter on the CloudWatch Logs log group to match the response code range. Configure the metric filter to increment a metric. Set the response code and application name as dimensions.","C":"Create a CloudWatch Contributor Insights rule on the CloudWatch Logs log stream with a filter to match the response code range. Configure the Contributor Insights rule to increment a CloudWatch metric with the response code and application name as dimensions.","D":"Create a CloudWatch Logs Insights query on the CloudWatch Logs log group to match the response code range. Configure the Logs Insights query to increment a CloudWatch metric with the response code and application name as dimensions."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudWatch Logs 日志流上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 日志事件筛选器，以匹配响应代码范围。配 置日志事件筛选器以递增一个指标。将响应代码和应用程序名称设置为维度。","B":"在 CloudWatch Logs 日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，以匹配响应代码范围。配置指 标筛选器以递增一个指标。将响应代码和应用程序名称设置为维度。","C":"在 CloudWatch Logs 日志流上创建一个 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察规则，并设置一个过滤器以匹配响 应代码范围。配置贡献者洞察规则，以响应代码和应用程序名称作为维度来递增 CloudWatch 指 标。","D":"在 CloudWatch Logs 日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询以匹配响应代码范围。配置 Logs Insights 查询，以响应代码和应用程序名称作为维度来递增一个 CloudWatch 指标。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":317,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer provisioned an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster with managed node groups. The DevOps engineer associated an OpenID Connect (OIDC) issuer with the cluster. The DevOps engineer is configuring Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) General Purpose SSD (gp3) volumes for the cluster. The DevOps engineer attempts to initiate a PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) request but is unable to provision a volume. To troubleshoot the issue, the DevOps engineer runs the kubectl describe pyc command. The DevOps engineer receives a failed to provision volume with StorageClass error and a could not create volume in EC2:UnauthorizedOperation error. Which solution will resolve these errors?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师配置了一个亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群，其中 托管节点组。DevOps 工程师将一个 OpenID Connect（OIDC）颁发者与集群相关联。 DevOps 工程师正在为集群配置 Amazon Elastic Block Store（Amazon EBS）通用型 SSD（gp3）卷。 DevOps 工程师尝试发起 PersistentVolumeClaim（PVC）请求，但无法分配卷。为了排查问题， DevOps 工程师运行了 kubectl describe pyc 命令。DevOps 工程师收到“无法使用 StorageClass 分配卷” 错误和“无法在 EC2 中创建卷：未经授权的操作”错误。 哪种解决方案能解决这些错误？","options_en":{"A":"Create a Kubernetes cluster role that allows the persistent volumes to perform get, list, watch, create, and delete operations. Configure the cluster role to allow get, list, and watch operations for storage in the cluster.","B":"Create an Amazon EBS Container Storage Interface (CSI) driver IAM role that has the required permissions and trust relationships. Attach the IAM role to the Amazon EBS CSI driver add-on in the cluster.","C":"Add the ebs.csi.aws.com/volumeType:gp3 annotation to the PersistentVolumeClaim object in the cluster.","D":"Create a Kubernetes storage class object. Set the provisioner value to ebs.csi.aws.com. Set the volumeBindingMode value to WaitForFirstConsumer in the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Kubernetes 集群角色，允许持久卷执行获取、列表、监视、创建和删除操作。配置该集群 角色，使其允许在集群中对存储执行获取、列表和监视操作。","B":"创建一个具有所需权限和信任关系的 Amazon EBS 容器存储接口 （CSI） 驱动程序 IAM 角色。将 IAM 角色附加到集群中的 Amazon EBS CSI 驱动程序附加组件。","C":"在集群中的 PersistentVolumeClaim 对象上添加 ebs.csi.aws.com/volumeType:gp3 注解。","D":"创建一个 Kubernetes 存储类对象。将 provisioner 值设置为 ebs.csi.aws.com。在集群中将 volumeBindingMode 值设置为 WaitForFirstConsumer。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":318,"question_en":"A company runs a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances in a VPC. The company's employees remotely access the EC2 instances by using the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP). The company wants to collect metrics about how many RDP sessions the employees initiate every day. Which combination of steps will meet this requirement? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在虚拟私有云（VPC）中运行着一组亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司的员工通过使用远程桌面协议 （RDP）远程访问这些 EC2 实例。 该公司希望收集有关员工每天发起多少次远程桌面协议（RDP）会话的指标。 哪三种步骤的组合能满足这一要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EC2 Instance State-change Notification events.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Specify the log group as a target for the EventBridge rule.","C":"Create a flow log in VPC Flow Logs.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Specify the log group as a destination for the flow log.","E":"Create a log group metric filter.","F":"Create a log group subscription filter. Use EventBridge as the destination."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个亚马逊账 户 对 EC2 实例状态更改通知事件作出反应的 EventBridge 规则。","B":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。将该日志组指定为 EventBridge 规则的目标。","C":"在 VPC 流日志中创建一个流日志。","D":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。将该日志组指定为流日志的目标。","E":"创建日志组指标筛选器。","F":"创建一个日志组订阅筛选器。将 EventBridge 用作目标。"},"answer":["C","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":319,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) to run its applications. The EKS cluster is successfully running multiple pods. The company stores the pod images in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). The company needs to configure Pod Identity access for the EKS cluster. The company has already updated the node IAM role by using the permissions for Pod Identity access. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）来运行其应用程序。EKS 集群成功运 行了多个容器组（Pod）。该公司将容器组镜像存储在亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中。 该公司需要为 EKS 集群配置 Pod 身份访问权限。该公司已通过使用 Pod 身份访问权限更新了节点 IAM 角色。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider for the EKS cluster.","B":"Ensure that the nodes can reach the EKS Auth API. Add and configure the EKS Pod Identity Agent add-on for the EKS cluster.","C":"Create an EKS access entry that uses the API_AND-CONFIG_MAP cluster authentication mode.","D":"Configure the AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) endpoint for the Kubernetes service account that the pods in the EKS cluster use."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 EKS 集群创建一个 IAM OpenID 连接（OIDC）提供程序。","B":"确保节点能够访问 EKS 认证 API。为 EKS 集群添加并配置 EKS Pod 身份代理插件。","C":"创建一个使用 API_AND-CONFIG_MAP 集群身份验证模式的 EKS 访问条目。","D":"为 EKS 集群中 Pod 使用的 Kubernetes 服务账户配置 AWS 安全令牌服务（AWS STS）端点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":320,"question_en":"A company has multiple AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled. The company’s DevOps administrator needs to improve security across all the company's AWS accounts. The administrator needs to identify the top users and roles in use across all accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有多个 AWS 账户，该组织启用了所有功能。该公司的 DevOps 管理员需要 提高公司所有 AWS 账户的安全性。管理员需要确定所有账户中使用频率最高的用户和角色。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new organization trail in AWS CloudTrail. Configure the trail to send log events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a CloudWatch Contributor Insights rule for the userIdentity.arn log field. View the results in CloudWatch Contributor Insights.","B":"Create an unused access analysis for the organization by using AWS Identity and Access Management Access Analyzer. Review the analyzer results and determine if each finding has the intended level of permissions required for the workload.","C":"Create a new organization trail in AWS CloudTrail. Create a table in Amazon Athena that uses partition projection. Load the Athena table with CloudTrail data. Query the Athena table to find the top users and roles.","D":"Generate a Service access report for each account by using Organizations. From the results, pull the last accessed date and last accessed by account fields to find the top users and roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CloudTrail 中创建一个新的组织跟踪。配置该跟踪以将日志事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。为 userIdentity.arn 日志字段创建 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察规则。在 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察中 查看结果。","B":"使用 AWS 身份和访问管理访问分析器为组织创建未使用的访问分析。查看分析器结果，并确定每个 发现是否具有工作负载所需的预期权限级别。","C":"在 AWS CloudTrail 中创建一个新的组织跟踪。在 Amazon Athena 中创建一个使用分区投影的表。使 用 CloudTrail 数据加载 Athena 表。查询 Athena 表以找出使用最多的用户和角色。","D":"使用 Organizations 为每个账户生成服务访问报告。从结果中提取“最后访问日期”和“最后访问账 户”字段，以找出主要的用户和角色。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":321,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations with many OUs that contain many AWS accounts. The organization has a dedicated delegated administrator AWS account. The company needs the accounts in one OU to have server-side encryption enforced for all Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes and Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queues that are created or updated on an AWS CloudFormation stack. Which solution will enforce this policy before a CloudFormation stack operation in the accounts of this OU?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有多个组织单元（OU），每个组织单元包含多个 AWS 账户。该组织有一个 专门的委托管理员 AWS 账户。 该公司需要在某个组织单元 （OU） 中的账户对通过 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈创建或更新的所有 Amazon 弹性块存储 （Amazon EBS） 卷和 Amazon 简单队列服务 （Amazon SQS） 队列强制实施服务 器端加密。 在该组织单位（OU）的账户中，哪种解决方案会在执行 CloudFormation 堆栈操作之前强制实施此策略？","options_en":{"A":"Activate trusted access to CloudFormation StackSets. Create a CloudFormation Hook that enforces server-side encryption on EBS volumes and SQS queues. Deploy the Hook across the accounts in the OU by using StackSets.","B":"Set up AWS Config in all the accounts in the OU. Use AWS Systems Manager to deploy AWS Config rules that enforce server-side encryption for EBS volumes and SQS queues across the accounts in the OU.","C":"Write an SCP to deny the creation of EBS volumes and SQS queues unless the EBS volumes and SQS queues have server-side encryption. Attach the SCP to the OU.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function in the delegated administrator account that checks whether server- side encryption is enforced for EBS volumes and SQS queues. Create an IAM role to provide the Lambda function access to the accounts in the OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"激活 CloudFormation StackSets 的可信访问。创建一个 CloudFormation Hook，强制对 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列进行服务器端加密。通过使用 StackSets 在组织单元中的各个账户中部署该 Hook。","B":"在组织单位（OU）中的所有账户中设置 AWS Config。使用 AWS Systems Manager 部署 AWS Config 规则，以强制要求组织单位（OU）中所有账户的 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列启用服务器端加密。","C":"编写一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止创建未启用服务器端加密的 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列，除非这些 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列已启用服务器端加密。将该 SCP 附加到组织单位（OU）。","D":"在委托管理员账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于检查 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列是否强制执行服务 器端加密。创建一个 IAM 角色，以使 Lambda 函数能够访问组织单位中的账户。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":322,"question_en":"A company is running an internal application in an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster on Amazon EC2. The ECS cluster instances can connect to the public internet. The ECS tasks that run on the cluster instances are configured to use images from both private Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories and a public ECR registry repository. A new security policy requires the company to remove the ECS cluster's direct access to the internet. The company must remove any NAT gateways and internet gateways from the VPC that hosts the cluster. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure the ECS cluster can still download images from both the public ECR registry and the private ECR repositories. Images from the public ECR registry must remain up-to-date. New versions of the images must be available to the ECS cluster within 24 hours of publication. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在亚马逊 EC2 上的亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）集群中运行内部应用程序。ECS 集 群实例可以连接到公共互联网。在集群实例上运行的 ECS 任务配置为使用来自私有亚马逊弹性容器注册 表（Amazon ECR）存储库和公共 ECR 注册表存储库的镜像。 一项新的安全策略要求公司取消 ECS 集群直接访问互联网的权限。公司必须从承载该集群的 VPC 中移 除任何 NAT 网关和互联网网关。一位 DevOps 工程师需要确保 ECS 集群仍能从公共 ECR 注册表和私有 ECR 仓库下载镜像。公共 ECR 注册表中的镜像必须保持最新。新发布的镜像版本必须在发布后的 24 小 时内可供 ECS 集群使用。 哪种步骤组合能在满足这些要求的同时，将操作开销降至最低？（选择） 三。","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project and a new private ECR repository for each image that is downloaded from the public ECR registry. Configure each project to pull the image from the public ECR repository and push the image to the new private ECR repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes the CodeBuild project once every 24 hours. Update each task definition in the ECS cluster to refer to the new private ECR repository.","B":"Create a new Amazon ECR pull through cache rule for each image that is downloaded from the public ECR registry. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes each pull through cache rule. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes the Lambda function once every 24 hours. Update each task definition in the ECS cluster to refer to the image from the pull through cache.","C":"Create a new Amazon ECR pull through cache rule for the public ECR registry. Update each task definition in the ECS cluster to refer to the image from the pull through cache. Ensure each public image has been downloaded through the pull through cache at least once before removing internet access from the VPC.","D":"Create an Amazon ECR interface VPC endpoint for the public ECR repositories that are in the VPC.","E":"Create an Amazon ECR interface VPC endpoint for the private ECR repositories that are in the VPC.","F":"Create an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint in the VPC."},"options_zh":{"A":"为从公共 ECR 注册表下载的每个镜像创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目和一个新的私有 ECR 仓库。将每 个项目配置为从公共 ECR 仓库拉取镜像并将其推送到新的私有 ECR 仓库。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 24 小时调用一次 CodeBuild 项目。更新 ECS 集群中的每个任务定义，使其指向 新的私有 ECR 仓库。","B":"为从公共 ECR 注册表下载的每个镜像创建一个新的 Amazon ECR 拉取缓存规则。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于调用每个拉取缓存规则。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 24 小时调用一 次该 Lambda 函数。更新 ECS 集群中的每个任务定义，使其引用来自拉取缓存的镜像。","C":"为公共 ECR 注册表创建一个新的 Amazon ECR 拉取缓存规则。更新 ECS 集群中的每个任务定义， 使其引用来自拉取缓存的镜像。在从 VPC 中移除互联网访问权限之前，确保每个公共镜像至少 已通过拉取缓存下载过一次。","D":"为 VPC 中的公共 ECR 存储库创建一个 Amazon ECR 接口 VPC 端点。","E":"为 VPC 内的私有 ECR 存储库创建一个 Amazon ECR 接口 VPC 端点。","F":"在 VPC 中创建一个 Amazon S3 网关端点。"},"answer":["C","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":323,"question_en":"A company has a continuous integration pipeline where the company creates container images by using AWS CodeBuild. The created images are stored in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Checking for and fixing the vulnerabilities in the images takes the company too much time. The company wants to identify the image vulnerabilities quickly and notify the security team of the vulnerabilities. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司拥有一个持续集成流水线，通过使用 AWS CodeBuild 创建容器镜像。创建的镜像存储在亚马逊 弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中。 检查并修复镜像中的漏洞耗费了公司太多时间。公司希望快速识别出镜像中的漏洞，并将漏洞情况通知 给安全团队。 哪种步骤组合能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Activate Amazon Inspector enhanced scanning for Amazon ECR. Configure the enhanced scanning to use continuous scanning. Set up a topic in Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for Amazon Inspector findings. Set an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the rule target.","C":"Activate AWS Lambda enhanced scanning for Amazon ECR. Configure the enhanced scanning to use continuous scanning. Set up a topic in Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES).","D":"Create a new AWS Lambda function. Invoke the new Lambda function when scan findings are detected.","E":"Activate default basic scanning for Amazon ECR for all container images. Configure the default basic scanning to use continuous scanning. Set up a topic in Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS)."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 Amazon ECR 激活 Amazon Inspector 增强扫描功能。将增强扫描配置为使用持续扫描。在 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）中设置一个主题。","B":"为 Amazon Inspector 发现结果创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题设置为规则目标。","C":"启用 AWS Lambda 对 Amazon ECR 的增强扫描功能。将增强扫描配置为使用持续扫描。在 Amazon 简 单电子邮件服务（Amazon SES）中设置一个主题。","D":"创建一个新的 AWS Lambda 函数。在检测到扫描结果时调用新的 Lambda 函数。","E":"为所有容器镜像激活 Amazon ECR 的默认基本扫描。将默认基本扫描配置为使用持续扫描。在 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）中设置一个主题。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":324,"question_en":"A DevOps administrator is configuring a repository to store a company's container images. The administrator needs to configure a lifecycle rule that automatically deletes container images that have a specific tag and that are older than 15 days. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 管理员正在配置一个存储库来存放公司的容器镜像。该管理员需要配置一个生命周期规则， 自动删除具有特定标签且超过 15 天的容器镜像。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a repository in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Add a lifecycle policy to the repository to expire images that have the matching tag after 15 days.","B":"Create a repository in AWS CodeArtifact. Add a repository policy to the CodeArtifact repository to expire old assets that have the matching tag after 15 days.","C":"Create a bucket in Amazon S3. Add a bucket lifecycle policy to expire old objects that have the matching tag after 15 days","D":"Create an EC2 Image Builder container recipe. Add a build component to expire the container that has the matching tag after 15 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）中创建一个存储库。向该存储库添加一个生命周期 策略，使具有匹配标签的镜像在 15 天后过期。","B":"在 AWS CodeArtifact 中创建一个存储库。向 CodeArtifact 存储库添加存储库策略，以便在 15 天后 过期具有匹配标签的旧资产。","C":"在亚马逊 S3 中创建一个存储桶。添加一个存储桶生命周期策略，在 15 天后自动删除具有匹配标 签的旧对象。","D":"创建一个 EC2 Image Builder 容器配方。添加一个构建组件，在 15 天后过期具有匹配标签的容器。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":325,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Redshift as its data warehouse solution. The company wants to create a dashboard to view changes to the Redshift users and the queries the users perform. Which combination of steps will meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 Redshift 作为其数据仓库解决方案。该公司希望创建一个仪表板，以查看 Redshift 用户的变更情况以及这些用户执行的查询。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这一要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch log group. Create an AWS CloudTrail trail that writes to the CloudWatch log group.","B":"Create a new Amazon S3 bucket. Configure default audit logging on the Redshift cluster. Configure the S3 bucket as the target.","C":"Configure the Redshift cluster database audit logging to include user activity logs. Configure Amazon CloudWatch as the target.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard that has a log widget. Configure the widget to display user details from the Redshift logs.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function that uses Amazon Athena to query the Redshift logs. Create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard that has a custom widget type that uses the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 日志组。创建一个将日志写入 CloudWatch 日志组的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。","B":"创建一个新的 Amazon S3 存储桶。在 Redshift 集群上配置默认的审计日志记录。将 S3 存储桶配置为目标。","C":"配置 Redshift 集群数据库审计日志记录以包含用户活动日志。将 Amazon CloudWatch 配置为日志目标。","D":"创建一个包含日志小部件的 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板。配置该小部件以显示来自 Redshift 日志的用 户详细信息。","E":"创建一个使用 Amazon Athena 查询 Redshift 日志的 AWS Lambda 函数。创建一个包含自定义小部件 类型的 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板，该小部件使用该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":326,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage its 500 AWS accounts. The organization has all features enabled. The AWS accounts are in a single OU. The developers need to use the CostCenter tag key for all resources in the organization's member accounts. Some teams do not use the CostCenter tag key to tag their Amazon EC2 instances. The cloud team wrote a script that scans all EC2 instances in the organization's member accounts. If the EC2 instances do not have a CostCenter tag key, the script will notify AWS account administrators. To avoid this notification, some developers use the CostCenter tag key with an arbitrary string in the tag value. The cloud team needs to ensure that all EC2 instances in the organization use a CostCenter tag key with the appropriate cost center value. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理其 500 个 AWS 账户。该组织启用了所有功能。 这些 AWS 账户位于单个组织单元（OU）中。开发人员需要在该组织成员账户中的所有资源上使用 “CostCenter”标签键。但有些团队在标记其 Amazon EC2 实例时并未使用“CostCenter”标签键。 云团队编写了一个脚本，用于扫描组织成员账户中的所有 EC2 实例。如果 EC2 实例没有“CostCenter” 标签键，该脚本将通知 AWS 账户管理员。为了避免收到此类通知，一些开发人员在标签值中使用任意 字符串来设置“CostCenter”标签键。 云团队需要确保组织内的所有 EC2 实例都使用带有适当成本中心值的“CostCenter”标签键。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that prevents the creation of EC2 instances without the CostCenter tag key. Create a tag policy that requires the CostCenter tag to be values from a known list of cost centers for all EC2 instances. Attach the policy to the OU. Update the script to scan the tag keys and tag values. Modify the script to update noncompliant resources with a default approved tag value for the CostCenter tag key.","B":"Create an SCP that prevents the creation of EC2 instances without the CostCenter tag key. Attach the policy to the OU. Update the script to scan the tag keys and tag values and notify the administrators when the tag values are not valid.","C":"Create an SCP that prevents the creation of EC2 instances without the CostCenter tag key. Attach the policy to the OU. Create an IAM permission boundary in the organization's member accounts that restricts the CostCenter tag values to a list of valid cost centers.","D":"Create a tag policy that requires the CostCenter tag to be values from a known list of cost centers for all EC2 instances. Attach the policy to the OU. Configure an AWS Lambda function that adds an empty CostCenter tag key to an EC2 instance. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches events to the RunInstances API action with the Lambda function as the target."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 SCP，禁止创建未带有“CostCenter”标签键的 EC2 实例。创建一个标签策略，要求所有 EC2 实例的“CostCenter”标签值必须来自已知的成本中心列表。将该策略附加到组织单位。更 新脚本以扫描标签键和标签值。修改脚本，为不符合要求的资源更新“CostCenter”标签键的默 认批准标签值。","B":"创建一个 SCP，禁止创建未带有“CostCenter”标签键的 EC2 实例。将该策略附加到组织单元。更 新脚本以扫描标签键和标签值，并在标签值无效时通知管理员。","C":"创建一个 SCP，禁止创建未设置“CostCenter”标签键的 EC2 实例。将该策略附加到组织单元。在 组织成员账户中创建一个 IAM 权限边界，将“CostCenter”标签值限制为有效成本中心列表。","D":"创建一个标签策略，要求所有 EC2 实例的“CostCenter”标签值必须来自已知的成本中心列表。将该 策略附加到组织单元。配置一个 AWS Lambda 函数，为 EC2 实例添加一个空的“CostCenter”标签 键。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，将与 RunInstances API 操作匹配的事件定向到该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":327,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer uses a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. The pipeline has a build action and a deploy action for a single-page web application that is delivered to an Amazon S3 bucket. Amazon CloudFront serves the web application. The build action creates an artifact for the web application. The DevOps engineer has created an AWS CloudFormation template that defines the S3 bucket and configures the S3 bucket to host the application. The DevOps engineer has configured a CloudFormation deploy action before the S3 action. The CloudFormation deploy action creates the S3 bucket. The DevOps engineer needs to configure the S3 deploy action to use the S3 bucket from the CloudFormation template. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师在 AWS CodePipeline 中使用了一条管道。该管道针对一个单页网络应用程序， 包含构建操作和部署操作，该应用程序会被交付到一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。Amazon CloudFront 为该 网络应用程序提供服务。构建操作会为网络应用程序创建一个工件。 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，该模板定义了 S3 存储桶，并配置了该 S3 存储 桶以托管应用程序。DevOps 工程师还配置了一个 CloudFormation 在 S3 操作之前部署操作。CloudFormation 部署操作会创建 S3 存储桶。DevOps 工程师需要将 S3 部署操 作配置为使用 CloudFormation 模板中的 S3 存储桶。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add an output named BucketName to the CloudFormation template. Set the output's value to refer to the S3 bucket from the CloudFormation template. Configure the output value to export to an AWS::SSM::Parameter resource named Stackvariables.","B":"Add an output named BucketName to the CloudFormation template. Set the output's value to refer to the S3 bucket from the CloudFormation template. Set the CloudFormation action's namespace to StackVariables in the pipeline.","C":"Configure the output artifacts of the CloudFormation action in the pipeline to be an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store parameter named StackVariables. Name the artifact BucketName.","D":"Configure the build artifact from the build action as the input to the CodePipeline S3 deploy action. Configure the deploy action to deploy to the S3 bucket by using the StackVariables.BucketName variable.","E":"Configure the build artifact from the build action and the AWS Systems Manager parameter as the inputs to the deploy action. Configure the deploy action to deploy to the S3 bucket by using the StackVariables.BucketName variable."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFormation 模板中添加一个名为 BucketName 的输出。将该输出的值设置为引用 CloudFormation 模板中的 S3 存储桶。配置输出值以导出到名为 Stackvariables 的 AWS::SSM:: Parameter 资源。","B":"在 CloudFormation 模板中添加一个名为 BucketName 的输出。将该输出的值设置为引用 CloudFormation 模板中的 S3 存储桶。在管道中将 CloudFormation 操作的命名空间设置为 StackVariables。","C":"在管道中配置 CloudFormation 操作的输出工件，使其成为名为 StackVariables 的 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储参数。将该工件命名为 BucketName。","D":"将构建操作生成的构建工件配置为 CodePipeline S3 部署操作的输入。配置部署操作，使用 StackVariables.BucketName 变量将内容部署到 S3 存储桶。","E":"将构建操作生成的构建工件和 AWS Systems Manager 参数配置为部署操作的输入。配置部署操作， 使用 StackVariables.BucketName 变量将内容部署到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":328,"question_en":"A company used a lift and shift strategy to migrate a workload to AWS. The company has an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances. Each EC2 instance runs a web application, a database, and a Redis cache. Users are experiencing large variations in the web application's response times. Requests to the web application go to a single EC2 instance that is under significant load. The company wants to separate the application components to improve availability and performance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司采用“平移”策略将工作负载迁移到了 AWS。该公司有一个由亚马逊 EC2 实例组成的自动扩 展组。每个 EC2 实例都运行着一个网络应用程序、一个数据库和一个 Redis 缓存。 用户在使用网络应用程序时，发现其响应时间存在较大差异。向该网络应用程序发出的请求都发送到 了一台负载过重的 EC2 实例上。该公司希望将应用程序的各个组件分离，以提高可用性和性能。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a Network Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the web application. Migrate the database to an Amazon Aurora Serverless database. Create an Application Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the Redis cache.","B":"Create an Application Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the web application. Migrate the database to an Amazon Aurora database that has a Multi-AZ deployment. Create a Network Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group in a single Availability Zone for the Redis cache.","C":"Create a Network Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the web application. Migrate the database to an Amazon Aurora Serverless database. Create an Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster for the cache. Create a target group that has a DNS target type that contains the ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster hostname.","D":"Create an Application Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the web application. Migrate the database to an Amazon Aurora database that has a Multi-AZ deployment. Create an Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster for the cache."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 Web 应用程序创建一个网络负载均衡器和一个自动扩展组。将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora Serverless 数据库。为 Redis 缓存创建一个应用负载均衡器和一个自动扩展组。","B":"为 Web 应用程序创建一个应用负载均衡器和一个自动扩展组。将数据库迁移到具有多可用区部署 的 Amazon Aurora 数据库。在单个可用区中为 Redis 缓存创建一个网络负载均衡器和一个自动扩 展组。","C":"为网络应用创建一个网络负载均衡器和一个自动扩展组。将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora 无服务 器数据库。创建一个 Amazon ElastiCache（Redis 开源软件） 为缓存创建一个集群。创建一个具有 DNS 目标类型的靶向组，其中包含 ElastiCache（Redis OSS） 集群的主机名。","D":"为 Web 应用程序创建应用负载均衡器和自动扩展组。将数据库迁移到具有多可用区部署的 Amazon Aurora 数据库。创建一个 Amazon ElastiCache（Redis OSS）集群用于缓存。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":329,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations and wants to implement a governance strategy with the following requirements: • AWS resource access is restricted to the same two Regions for all accounts. • AWS services are limited to a specific group of authorized services for all accounts. • Authentication is provided by Active Directory. • Access permissions are organized by job function and are identical in each account. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 组织，并希望实施一项具有以下要求的治理策略： • 所有账户对 AWS 资源的访问权限均仅限于相同的两个区域。 • 对于所有账户，AWS 服务仅限于特定的一组授权服务。 身份验证由 Active Directory 提供。 访问权限按工作职能进行组织，并且每个账户中的权限都相同。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Establish an organizational unit (OU) with group policies in the management account to restrict Regions and authorized services. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to provision roles with permissions for each job function, including an IAM trust policy for IAM identity provider authentication in each account.","B":"Establish a permission boundary in the management account to restrict Regions and authorized services. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to provision roles with permissions for each job function, including an IAM trust policy for IAM identity provider authentication in each account.","C":"Establish a service control policy in the management account to restrict Regions and authorized services. Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share management account roles with permissions for each job function, including AWS IAM Identity Center for authentication in each account.","D":"Establish a service control policy in the management account to restrict Regions and authorized services. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to provision roles with permissions for each job function, including an IAM trust policy for IAM identity provider authentication in each account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中创建一个具有组策略的组织单位（OU），以限制区域和授权服务。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 为每个工作职能配置具有相应权限的角色，包括每个账户中用于 IAM 身份 提供商身份验证的 IAM 信任策略。","B":"在管理账户中设置权限边界，以限制区域和授权服务。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 为 每个工作职能配置具有相应权限的角色，包括为每个账户中的 IAM 身份提供商身份验证配置 IAM 信任策略。","C":"在管理账户中建立服务控制策略，以限制区域和授权服务。使用 AWS 资源访问管理器（AWS RAM） 与每个工作职能的权限共享管理账户角色，包括在每个账户中使用 AWS IAM 身份中心进行身份验 证。","D":"在管理账户中建立服务控制策略，以限制区域和授权服务。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 为每个工作职能配置具有相应权限的角色，包括为每个账户中的 IAM 身份提供商身份验证配 置 IAM 信任策略。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":330,"question_en":"A company detects unusual login attempts in many of its AWS accounts. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that sends a notification to the company's security team when multiple failed login attempts occur. The DevOps engineer has already created an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and has subscribed the security team to the SNS topic. Which solution will provide the notification with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司发现其多个 AWS 账户出现了异常登录尝试。一位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解决方案，当多 次登录尝试失败时向公司的安全团队发送通知。该 DevOps 工程师已经创建了一个亚马逊简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题，并已将安全团队订阅到该 SNS 主题。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力提供通知？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send management events to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter to match failed ConsoleLogin events. Create a CloudWatch alarm that is based on the metric filter. Configure an alarm action to send messages to the SNS topic.","B":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send management events to an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an Amazon Athena query that returns a failure if the query finds failed logins in the logs in the S3 bucket. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to periodically run the query. Create a second EventBridge rule to detect when the query fails and to send a message to the SNS topic.","C":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send data events to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Create a CloudWatch logs metric filter to match failed ConsoleLogin events. Create a CloudWatch alarm that is based on the metric filter. Configure an alarm action to send messages to the SNS topic.","D":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send data events to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure an Amazon S3 event notification for the s3:ObjectCreated event type. Filter the event type by ConsoleLogin failed events. Configure the event notification to forward to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将管理事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器以匹配失败的控制台登录事件。基于该指标筛选器创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。配置警报 操作以向 SNS 主题发送消息。","B":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将管理事件发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。创建一个 Amazon Athena 查询，如果在 S3 存储桶中的日志中发现登录失败，则该查询返回失败。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以定期运行 该查询。创建第二个 EventBridge 规则以检测查询失败并向 SNS 主题发送消息。","C":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将数据事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。创建一个 CloudWatch 日志指 标过滤器以匹配失败的控制台登录事件。基于该指标过滤器创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。配置警报操作 以向 SNS 主题发送消息。","D":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将数据事件发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。为 s3:ObjectCreated 事件类型配置 Amazon S3 事件通知。通过控制台登录失败事件筛选事件类型。配置事件通知将其转发到 SNS 主 题。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":331,"question_en":"A company has deployed a new REST API by using Amazon API Gateway. The company uses the API to access confidential data. The API must be accessed from only specific VPCs in the company. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过使用亚马逊 API 网关部署了一个新的 REST API。该公司使用此 API 访问机密数据。该 API 必须仅能从公司内部的特定虚拟私有云（VPC）进行访问。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create and attach a resource policy to the API Gateway API. Configure the resource policy to allow only the specific VPC IDs.","B":"Add a security group to the API Gateway API. Configure the inbound rules to allow only the specific VPC IP address ranges.","C":"Create and attach an IAM role to the API Gateway API. Configure the IAM role to allow only the specific VPC IDs.","D":"Add an ACL to the API Gateway API. Configure the outbound rules to allow only the specific VPC IP address ranges."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建并附加一个资源策略到 API 网关 API 上。配置该资源策略，使其仅允许特定的 VPC ID。","B":"将安全组添加到 API 网关 API 中。配置入站规则，仅允许特定的 VPC IP 地址范围。","C":"创建并向 API 网关 API 挂载一个 IAM 角色。将该 IAM 角色配置为仅允许特定的 VPC ID。","D":"在 API 网关 API 上添加访问控制列表（ACL）。配置出站规则，仅允许特定的 VPC IP 地址范围。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":332,"question_en":"A company runs a website by using an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) service that is connected to an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The service was in a steady state with tasks responding to requests successfully. A DevOps engineer updated the task definition with a new container image and deployed the new task definition to the service. The DevOps engineer noticed that the service is frequently stopping and starting new tasks because the ALB health checks are failing. What should the DevOps engineer do to troubleshoot the failed deployment?","question_zh":"一家公司通过使用与应用负载均衡器（ALB）相连接的亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）来运营其 网站。该服务一直保持稳定状态，任务能够成功响应请求。 一位 DevOps 工程师使用新的容器镜像更新了任务定义，并将新的任务定义部署到服务中。该 DevOps 工程师注意到，由于应用负载均衡器（ALB）的健康检查失败，服务频繁停止并启动新任务。 DevOps 工程师应该采取什么措施来排查部署失败的问题？","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that a security group associated with the service allows traffic from the ALB.","B":"Increase the ALB health check grace period for the service.","C":"Increase the service minimum healthy percent setting.","D":"Decrease the ALB health check interval."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保与服务相关联的安全组允许来自应用负载均衡器（ALB）的流量。","B":"延长该服务的 ALB 健康检查宽限期。","C":"提高服务最低健康百分比设置。","D":"减少 ALB 健康检查的间隔时间。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":333,"question_en":"A company that uses electronic patient health records runs a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances with an Amazon Linux operating system. The company must continuously ensure that the EC2 instances are running operating system patches and application patches that are in compliance with current privacy regulations. The company uses a custom repository to store application patches. A DevOps engineer needs to automate the deployment of operating system patches and application patches. The DevOps engineer wants to use both the default operating system patch repository and the custom patch repository. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家使用电子患者健康记录的公司运行着一批搭载亚马逊 Linux 操作系统的亚马逊 EC2 实例。该 公司必须持续确保这些 EC2 实例运行的操作系统补丁和应用程序补丁符合当前的隐私法规。该 公司使用一个自定义的存储库来存储应用程序补丁。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要实现操作系统补丁和应用程序补丁的自动化部署。该工程师希望同时使用 默认的操作系统补丁库和自定义补丁库。 哪种解决方案能以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager to create a new custom patch baseline that includes the default operating system repository and the custom repository. Run the AWS-RunPatchBaseline document by using the Run command to verify and install patches. Use the BaselineOverride API to configure the new custom patch baseline.","B":"Use AWS Direct Connect to integrate the custom repository with the EC2 instances. Use Amazon EventBridge events to deploy the patches.","C":"Use the yum-config-manager command to add the custom repository to the /etc/yum.repos.d configuration. Run the yum-config-manager-enable command to activate the new repository.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager to create a patch baseline for the default operating system repository and a second patch baseline for the custom repository. Run the AWS-RunPatchBaseline document by using the Run command to verify and install patches. Use the BaselineOverride API to configure the default patch baseline and the custom patch baseline."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 创建一个新的自定义补丁基准，该基准包含默认的操作系统存储库和自 定义存储库。使用“运行”命令运行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline 文档以验证并安装补丁。使用 BaselineOverride API 配置新的自定义补丁基准。","B":"使用 AWS Direct Connect 将自定义存储库与 EC2 实例集成。使用 Amazon EventBridge 事件部 署补丁。","C":"使用 yum-config-manager 命令将自定义存储库添加到 /etc/yum.repos.d 配置中。运行 yum- config-manager-enable 命令以激活新的存储库。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 为默认操作系统存储库创建一个补丁基准，为自定义存储库创建另一 个补丁基准。使用 Run 命令运行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline 文档以验证并安装补丁。使用 BaselineOverride API 配置默认补丁基准和自定义补丁基准。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":334,"question_en":"A company use an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The company has enabled all features enabled for the organization. The company configured the organization as a hierarchy of OUs under the root OU. The company recently registered all its OUs and enrolled all its AWS accounts in AWS Control Tower. The company needs to customize the AWS Control Tower managed AWS Config configuration recorder in each of the company's AWS accounts. The company needs to apply the customizations to both the existing AWS accounts and to any new AWS accounts that the company enrolls in AWS Control Tower in the future. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司已启用该组织的所有 功能。该公司将组织配置为在根组织单元（OU）下分层的多个 OU。该公司最近已注册其所有 OU， 并将所有 AWS 账户纳入 AWS Control Tower。 该公司需要在每个 AWS 账户中自定义 AWS Control Tower 管理的 AWS Config 配置记录器。该公司 需要将这些自定义设置应用于现有的 AWS 账户以及未来在 AWS Control Tower 中注册的任何新账户。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account. Create an AWS Lambda function in the new account to apply the customizations to the AWS Config configuration recorder in each AWS account in the organization.","B":"Create a new AWS account as an AWS Config delegated administrator. Create an AWS Lambda function in the delegated administrator account to apply the customizations to the AWS Config configuration recorder in the delegated administrator account.","C":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule in the AWS Control Tower management account to invoke an AWS Lambda function when the Organizations OU is registered or reregistered. Re-register the root Organizations OU.","D":"Configure the AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role in each AWS account in the organization to be assumable by an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to assume the AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role.","E":"Create an IAM role in the AWS Control Tower management account that an AWS Lambda function can assume. Grant the IAM role permission to assume the AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role in any account in the organization. Configure the Lambda function to use the new IAM role.","F":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule in the AWS Control Tower management account to invoke an AWS Lambda function when an AWS account is updated or enrolled in AWS Control Tower or when the landing zone is updated. Re-register each Organizations OU in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在新账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于对组织中每个 AWS 账户的 AWS Config 配置记录器应用自定义设置。","B":"以 AWS Config 委托管理员的身份创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在委托管理员账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以对委托管理员账户中的 AWS Config 配置记录器应用自定义设置。","C":"在 AWS 控制塔管理账户中配置 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在组织单位（OU）注册或重新注 册时调用 AWS Lambda 函数。重新注册根组织单位（OU）。","D":"在组织中的每个 AWS 账户中配置可由 AWS Lambda 函数承担的 AWSControlTowerExecution IAM 角色。配置 Lambda 函数以承担 AWSControlTowerExecution IAM 角色。","E":"在 AWS 控制塔管理账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数可以承担的 IAM 角色。授予该 IAM 角色在组织内 任何账户中承担 AWSControlTowerExecution IAM 角色的权限。配置 Lambda 函数使用新创建的 IAM 角 色。","F":"在 AWS 控制塔管理账户中配置 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在 AWS 账户更新或注册到 AWS 控制 塔时，或者在着陆区更新时调用 AWS Lambda 函数。重新注册组织中的每个 Organizations 组织单元。"},"answer":["C","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":335,"question_en":"A company runs an application in an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The EC2 instances run Docker containers that make requests to a MySQL database that runs on separate EC2 instances. A DevOps engineer needs to update the application to use a serverless architecture. Which solution will meet this requirement with the FEWEST changes?","question_zh":"一家公司在应用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的亚马逊 EC2 实例的自动扩展组中运行一个应用程序。这些 EC2 实例运行的 Docker 容器会向运行在单独的 EC2 实例上的 MySQL 数据库发出请求。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要更新应用程序以采用无服务器架构。 哪种解决方案只需做最少的改动就能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Replace the containers that run on EC2 instances and the ALB with AWS Lambda functions. Replace the MySQL database with an Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 database that is compatible with MySQL.","B":"Replace the containers that run on EC2 instances with AWS Fargate. Replace the MySQL database with an Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 database that is compatible with MySQL.","C":"Replace the containers that run on EC2 instances and the ALB with AWS Lambda functions. Replace the MySQL database with Amazon DynamoDB tables.","D":"Replace the containers that run on EC2 instances with AWS Fargate. Replace the MySQL database with Amazon DynamoDB tables."},"options_zh":{"A":"用 AWS Lambda 函数替换在 EC2 实例上运行的容器和应用负载均衡器（ALB）。用与 MySQL 兼容的 Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 数据库替换 MySQL 数据库。","B":"将在 EC2 实例上运行的容器替换为 AWS Fargate。将 MySQL 数据库替换为与 MySQL 兼容的 Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 数据库。","C":"用 AWS Lambda 函数替换在 EC2 实例上运行的容器和应用负载均衡器（ALB）。用 Amazon DynamoDB 表替换 MySQL 数据库。","D":"将在 EC2 实例上运行的容器替换为 AWS Fargate。将 MySQL 数据库替换为 Amazon DynamoDB 表。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":336,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage 10 AWS accounts. All features are enabled, and trusted access for AWS CloudFormation is enabled. A DevOps engineer needs to use CloudFormation to deploy an IAM role to the Organizations management account and all member accounts in the organization. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织中的一个组织来管理 10 个 AWS 账户。所有功能均已启用，并且已为 AWS CloudFormation 启用受信任访问。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要使用 CloudFormation 将一个 IAM 角色部署到组织管理账户以及该组织中的所有成 员账户。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudFormation StackSet that has service-managed permissions. Set the root OU as a deployment target.","B":"Create a CloudFormation StackSet that has service-managed permissions. Set the root OU as a deployment target. Deploy a separate CloudFormation stack in the Organizations management account.","C":"Create a CloudFormation StackSet that has self-managed permissions. Set the root OU as a deployment target.","D":"Create a CloudFormation StackSet that has self-managed permissions. Set the root OU as a deployment target. Deploy a separate CloudFormation stack in the Organizations management account."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有服务管理权限的 CloudFormation 栈集。将根组织单位设置为部署目标。","B":"创建一个具有服务管理权限的 CloudFormation 栈集。将根组织单元设置为部署目标。在 Organizations 管理账户中部署单独的 CloudFormation 栈。","C":"创建一个具有自管理权限的 CloudFormation 栈集。将根组织单位设置为部署目标。","D":"创建一个具有自管理权限的 CloudFormation 栈集。将根组织单位设置为部署目标。在 Organizations 管理账户中部署单独的 CloudFormation 栈。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":337,"question_en":"A company runs an application that stores artifacts in an Amazon S3 bucket. The application has a large user base. The application writes a high volume of objects to the S3 bucket. The company has enabled event notifications for the S3 bucket. When the application writes an object to the S3 bucket, several processing tasks need to be performed simultaneously. The company's DevOps team needs to create an AWS Step Functions workflow to orchestrate the processing tasks. Which combination of steps should the DevOps team take to meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司运行着一个应用程序，该程序将工件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。该应用程序拥有庞大的 用户群。该应用程序向 S3 存储桶写入大量对象。该公司已为该 S3 存储桶启用了事件通知功能。 当应用程序将对象写入 S3 存储桶时，需要同时执行多个处理任务。公司的 DevOps 团队需要创建 一个 AWS Step Functions 工作流来协调这些处理任务。 DevOps 团队应采取哪两种步骤组合才能以最低的运营开销满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a Standard workflow that contains a parallel state that defines the processing tasks. Create an Asynchronous Express workflow that contains a parallel state that defines the processing tasks.","B":"Create a Synchronous Express workflow that contains a map state that defines the processing tasks.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match when a new S3 object is created. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to start the processing workflow.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match when a new S3 object is created. Configure the EventBridge rule to start the processing workflow."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个标准工作流，其中包含一个并行状态，用于定义处理任务。创建一个异步快速工作流， 其中包含一个并行状态，用于定义处理任务。","B":"创建一个包含定义处理任务的映射状态的同步 Express 工作流。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于匹配新 S3 对象创建的事件。配置 EventBridge 规则 以调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以启动处理工作流。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于匹配新 S3 对象创建的事件。配置 EventBridge 规则以启动处理工作流。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":338,"question_en":"A DevOps team supports an application that runs in an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Currently, the DevOps team uses AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the application by using a blue/green all-at-once strategy. Recently, the DevOps team had to roll back a deployment when a new version of the application dramatically increased response times for requests. The DevOps team needs use to a deployment strategy that will allow the team to monitor a new version of the application before the team shifts all traffic to the new version. If a new version of the application increases response times, the deployment should be rolled back as quickly as possible. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队支持一个在 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）集群中运行的应用程 序，该集群位于一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。目前，该 DevOps 团队使用 AWS CodeDeploy 通过蓝绿全量部署策略来部署应用程序。最近，由于应用程序的新版本大幅增加了请求的响应时间， DevOps 团队不得不回滚部署。 DevOps 团队需要采用一种部署策略，以便在将所有流量切换到新版本之前，能够对新版本的应用 程序进行监控。如果新版本的应用程序增加了响应时间，应尽快回滚部署。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Modify the CodeDeploy deployment to use the CodeDeployDefault.ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes configuration.","B":"Modify the CodeDeploy deployment to use the CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes configuration.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to monitor the UnHealthyHostCount metric for the ALB. Set the alarm to activate if the metric is higher than the desired value. Associate the alarm with the CodeDeploy deployment group. Modify the deployment group to roll back when a deployment fails.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to monitor the TargetResponseTime metric for the ALB. Set the alarm to activate if the metric is higher than the desired value. Associate the alarm with the CodeDeploy deployment group. Modify the deployment group to roll back when alarm thresholds are met.","E":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to monitor the TargetConnectionErrorCount metric for the ALB. Set the alarm to activate if the metric is higher than the desired value. Associate the alarm with the CodeDeploy deployment group. Modify the deployment group to roll back when alarm thresholds are met."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CodeDeploy 部署修改为使用 CodeDeployDefault.ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes 配置。","B":"将 CodeDeploy 部署修改为使用 CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes 配置。","C":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控 ALB 的 UnHealthyHostCount 指标。将警报设置为在该 指标高于期望值时触发。将警报与 CodeDeploy 部署组关联。修改部署组，使其在部署失败时 回滚。","D":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控 ALB 的 TargetResponseTime 指标。将警报设置为在该 指标高于期望值时触发。将警报与 CodeDeploy 部署组相关联。修改部署组，使其在达到警报 阈值时回滚。","E":"为应用负载均衡器（ALB）的 TargetConnectionErrorCount 指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警 报。将警报设置为当该指标高于期望值时触发。将警报与 CodeDeploy 部署组关联。修改部署 组，使其在达到警报阈值时回滚。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":339,"question_en":"A security team must record the configuration of AWS resources, detect issues, and send notifications for findings. The main workload in the AWS account consists of an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group that scales in and out several times during the day. The team wants to be notified within 2 days if any Amazon EC2 security group allows traffic on port 22 for 0.0.0.0/0. The team also needs a snapshot of the configuration of the AWS resources to be taken routinely. The security team has already created and subscribed to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"安全团队必须记录 AWS 资源的配置，检测问题，并为发现的情况发送通知。AWS 账户中的主要工 作负载由一个 Amazon EC2 自动扩展组构成，该组在一天内会进行多次扩展和收缩。 如果任何亚马逊 EC2 安全组允许 0.0.0.0/0 在 22 端口进行通信，团队希望在 2 天内得到通知。团队还 需要定期对 AWS 资源的配置进行快照。 安全团队已经创建并订阅了一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Config to use periodic recording for the AWS account. Deploy the vpc-sg-port- restriction-check AWS Config managed rule. Configure AWS Config to use the SNS topic as the target for notifications.","B":"Configure AWS Config to use configuration change recording for the AWS account. Deploy the vpc-sg- open-only-to-authorized-ports AWS Config managed rule. Configure AWS Config to use the SNS topic as the target for notifications.","C":"Configure AWS Config to use configuration change recording for the AWS account. Deploy the ssh- restricted AWS Config managed rule. Configure AWS Config to use the SNS topic as the target for notifications.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function to evaluate security groups and publish a message to the SNS topic. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to schedule the Lambda function to run once a day."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Config 以使用周期性记录方式记录 AWS 账户。部署 vpc-sg-portrestriction-check AWS Config 管理规则。配置 AWS Config 以使用 SNS 主题作为通知目标。","B":"配置 AWS Config 以使用配置更改记录功能记录 AWS 账户的配置更改。部署 vpc-sgopen-only-to- authorized-ports AWS Config 管理规则。配置 AWS Config 以将 SNS 主题用作通知的目标。","C":"配置 AWS Config 以对 AWS 账户使用配置更改记录功能。部署 sshrestricted AWS Config 管理规则。 配置 AWS Config 以将 SNS 主题用作通知目标。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来评估安全组并向 SNS 主题发布消息。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则安 排该 Lambda 函数每天运行一次。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":340,"question_en":"A company has proprietary data available by using an Amazon CloudFront distribution. The company needs to ensure that the distribution is accessible by only users from the corporate office that have a known set of IP address ranges. An AWS WAF web ACL is associated with the distribution and has a default action set to Count. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司通过使用亚马逊 CloudFront 分发服务可获取专有数据。该公司需要确保只有来自公司办公 室且具有已知 IP 地址范围的用户才能访问该分发服务。已将 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）与该分发服务相关联，并将默认操作设置为计数。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new regex pattern set. Add the regex pattern set to a new rule group. Create a new web ACL that has a default action set to Block. Associate the web ACL with the CloudFront distribution. Add a rule that allows traffic based on the new rule group.","B":"Create an AWS WAF IP address set that matches the corporate office IP address range. Create a new web ACL that has a default action set to Allow. Associate the web ACL with the CloudFront distribution. Add a rule that allows traffic from the IP address set.","C":"Create a new regex pattern set. Add the regex pattern set to a new rule group. Set the default action on the existing web ACL to Allow. Add a rule that has priority 0 that allows traffic based on the regex pattern set.","D":"Create a WAF IP address set that matches the corporate office IP address range. Set the default action on the existing web ACL to Block. Add a rule that has priority 0 that allows traffic from the IP address set."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的正则表达式模式集。将该正则表达式模式集添加到新的规则组中。创建一个新的 Web ACL 并将其默认操作设置为“阻止”。将 Web ACL 与 CloudFront 分发关联。添加一条基于新规则 组允许流量的规则。","B":"创建一个与公司办公室 IP 地址范围匹配的 AWS WAF IP 地址集。创建一个新的 Web ACL 并将其默认 操作设置为允许。将 Web ACL 与 CloudFront 分发关联。添加一条允许来自该 IP 地址集的流量的规 则。","C":"创建一个新的正则表达式模式集。将该正则表达式模式集添加到新的规则组。将现有 Web ACL 的默认 操作设置为允许。添加一个优先级为 0 的规则，该规则基于正则表达式模式集允许流量。","D":"创建一个与公司办公室 IP 地址范围匹配的 WAF IP 地址集。将现有 Web ACL 的默认操作设置为阻止。 添加一个优先级为 0 的规则，允许来自该 IP 地址集的流量。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":341,"question_en":"A company runs several applications in the same AWS account. The applications send logs to Amazon CloudWatch. A data analytics team needs to collect performance metrics and custom metrics from the applications. The analytics team needs to transform the metrics data before storing the data in an Amazon S3 bucket. The analytics team must automatically collect any new metrics that are added to the CloudWatch namespace. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在同一个 AWS 账户中运行多个应用程序。这些应用程序将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch。 一个数据分析团队需要从应用程序中收集性能指标和自定义指标。该团队需要在将数据存储到 Amazon S3 存储桶之前对指标数据进行转换。该团队必须自动收集添加到 CloudWatch 命名空间中的任何新指标。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a CloudWatch metric stream to include metrics from the application and the CloudWatch namespace. Configure the metric stream to deliver the metrics to an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream. Configure the Firehose delivery stream to invoke an AWS Lambda function to transform the data. Configure the delivery stream to send the transformed data to the S3 bucket.","B":"Configure a CloudWatch metrics stream to include all the metrics and to deliver the metrics to an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream. Configure the Firehose delivery stream to invoke an AWS Lambda function to transform the data. Configure the delivery stream to send the transformed data to the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure metric filters for the CloudWatch logs to create custom metrics. Configure a CloudWatch metric stream to deliver the application metrics to the S3 bucket.","D":"Configure subscription filters on the application log groups to target an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream. Configure the Firehose delivery stream to invoke an AWS Lambda function to transform the data. Configure the delivery stream to send the transformed data to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 CloudWatch 指标流，使其包含来自应用程序和 CloudWatch 命名空间的指标。将指标流配 置为将指标传递到 Amazon Data Firehose 交付流。将 Firehose 交付流配置为调用 AWS Lambda 函 数来转换数据。将交付流配置为将转换后的数据发送到 S3 存储桶。","B":"配置一个 CloudWatch 指标流，使其包含所有指标，并将这些指标传递给 Amazon Data Firehose 交付 流。配置 Firehose 交付流以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数来转换数据。配置交付流以将转换后的数 据发送到 S3 存储桶。","C":"为 CloudWatch 日志配置指标筛选器以创建自定义指标。配置 CloudWatch 指标流将应用程序指标 传递到 S3 存储桶。","D":"在应用程序日志组上配置订阅筛选器，以指向 Amazon Data Firehose 交付流。配置 Firehose 交付流以 调用 AWS Lambda 函数来转换数据。配置交付流将转换后的数据发送到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":342,"question_en":"A company uses an HPC platform to run analysis jobs for data. The company uses AWS CodeBuild to create container images and store the images on Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). The images are then deployed on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). To maintain compliance, the company needs to ensure that the images are signed before the images are deployed on Amazon EKS. The signing keys must be rotated periodically and must be managed automatically. The company needs to track who generates the signatures. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司使用高性能计算（HPC）平台来运行数据的分析任务。该公司使用 AWS CodeBuild 来创建容器 镜像，并将这些镜像存储在亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中。随后，这些镜像会被部署到亚 马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上。 为保持合规性，公司需要确保在将图像部署到亚马逊 EKS 之前对其进行签名。签名密钥必须定期轮换， 并且必须自动管理。公司需要追踪谁生成了签名。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use CodeBuild to retrieve the image that was previously pushed to Amazon ECR. Use AWS Signer to sign the image. Use AWS CloudTrail to track who generates the signatures.","B":"Use AWS Lambda to retrieve the image that was previously pushed to Amazon ECR. Use a Lambda function to sign the image. Use Amazon CloudWatch to track who generates the signatures.","C":"Use AWS Lambda to retrieve the image that was previously pushed to Amazon ECR. Use AWS Signer to sign the image. Use Amazon CloudWatch to track who generates the signatures.","D":"Use CodeBuild to build the image. Sign the image by using AWS Signer before pushing the image to Amazon ECR. Use AWS CloudTrail to track who generates the signatures."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 CodeBuild 检索先前推送到 Amazon ECR 的镜像。使用 AWS Signer 对镜像进行签名。使用 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪谁生成了签名。","B":"使用 AWS Lambda 检索先前推送到 Amazon ECR 的镜像。使用 Lambda 函数对镜像进行签名。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 跟踪生成签名的人员。","C":"使用 AWS Lambda 检索先前推送到 Amazon ECR 的镜像。使用 AWS Signer 对镜像进行签名。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 跟踪生成签名的人员。","D":"使用 CodeBuild 构建镜像。在将镜像推送到 Amazon ECR 之前，使用 AWS Signer 对其进行签名。使 用 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪谁生成了签名。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":343,"question_en":"A company uses an AWS CodeArtifact repository to store Python packages that the company developed internally. A DevOps engineer needs to use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy an application to an Amazon EC2 instance. The application uses a Python package that is stored in the CodeArtifact repository. A BeforeInstall lifecycle event hook will install the package. The DevOps engineer needs to grant the EC2 instance access to the CodeArtifact repository. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库来存储其内部开发的 Python 包。一位 DevOps 工程师需要使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序部署到 Amazon EC2 实例上。该应用程序使用存储在 CodeArtifact 存储库中 的 Python 包。在部署过程中，BeforeInstall 生命周期事件钩子将安装该包。 DevOps 工程师需要授予 EC2 实例访问 CodeArtifact 存储库的权限。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a service-linked role for CodeArtifact. Associate the role with the EC2 instance. Use the aws codeartifact get-authorization-token CLI command on the instance.","B":"Configure a resource-based policy for the CodeArtifact repository that allows the ReadFromRepository action for the EC2 instance principal.","C":"Configure ACLs on the CodeArtifact repository to allow the EC2 instance to access the Python package.","D":"Create an instance profile that contains an IAM role that has access to CodeArtifact. Associate the instance profile with the EC2 instance. Use the aws codeartifact login CLI command on the instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 CodeArtifact 创建一个服务关联角色。将该角色与 EC2 实例相关联。在实例上使用 aws codeartifact get-authorization-token CLI 命令。","B":"为 CodeArtifact 存储库配置基于资源的策略，允许 EC2 实例主体执行“从存储库读取”操作。","C":"在 CodeArtifact 存储库上配置访问控制列表（ACL），以允许 EC2 实例访问 Python 包。","D":"创建一个包含有权访问 CodeArtifact 的 IAM 角色的实例配置文件。将实例配置文件与 EC2 实例相 关联。在实例上使用 aws codeartifact login CLI 命令。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":344,"question_en":"A company has a file-reading application that saves files to a database that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. Regulations require the company to delete files from EC2 instances every day at a specific time. The company must delete database records that are older than 60 days. The database record deletion must occur after the file deletions. The company has created scripts to delete files and database records. The company needs to receive an email notification for any failure of the deletion scripts. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款文件读取应用程序，该程序会将文件保存到运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的数据库中。法 规要求该公司每天在特定时间从 EC2 实例中删除文件。公司必须删除超过 60 天的数据库记录。 数据库记录的删除必须在文件删除之后进行。该公司已创建了用于删除文件和数据库记录的脚本。公司 需要在删除脚本出现任何故障时收到电子邮件通知。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager State Manager to automatically invoke a Systems Manager Automation document at the specified time each day. Configure the Automation document to use a run command to run the deletion scripts in sequential order. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to send failure notifications to the company.","B":"Use AWS Systems Manager State Manager to automatically invoke a Systems Manager Automation document at the specified time each day. Configure the Automation document to use a run command to run the deletion scripts in sequential order. Create a conditional statement inside the Automation document as the last step to check for errors. Use Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to send failure notifications as email messages to the company.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function at the specified time. Add the necessary permissions for the invocation to the Lambda function's resource-based policy. Configure the Lambda function to run the deletion scripts in sequential order. Configure the Lambda function to use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to send failure notifications to the company.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function at the specified time. Add the necessary permissions for the invocation to the Lambda function's resource-based policy. Configure the Lambda function to run the deletion scripts in sequential order. Configure the Lambda function to use Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to send failure notifications as email messages to the company."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager State Manager 每天在指定时间自动调用 Systems Manager Automation 文 档。配置 Automation 文档以使用运行命令按顺序运行删除脚本。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规 则，使用 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）向公司发送失败通知。","B":"使用 AWS Systems Manager State Manager 每天在指定时间自动调用 Systems Manager Automation 文 档。配置 Automation 文档以使用运行命令按顺序运行删除脚本。在 Automation 文档的最后一步创 建一个条件语句来检查错误。使用 Amazon Simple Email Service （Amazon SES） 将失败通知作为 电子邮件发送给公司。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在指定时间调用 AWS Lambda 函数。向 Lambda 函数的基于资 源的策略添加必要的调用权限。配置 Lambda 函数按顺序运行删除脚本。配置 Lambda 函数使用 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）向公司发送失败通知。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在指定时间调用 AWS Lambda 函数。向 Lambda 函数的基于资 源的策略添加必要的调用权限。配置 Lambda 函数按顺序运行删除脚本。配置 Lambda 函数使用 Amazon 简单电子邮件服务（Amazon SES）将失败通知以电子邮件形式发送给公司。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":345,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled to manage its AWS accounts. Amazon EQ instances run in the AWS accounts. The company requires that all current EC2 instances must use Instance Metadata Service Version 2 (IMDSv2). The company needs to block AWS API calls that originate from EC2 instances that do not use IMDSv2. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织中的一个启用了所有功能的组织来管理其 AWS 资源。 账户。Amazon EQ 实例在 AWS 账户中运行。 公司要求所有当前的 EC2 实例必须使用实例元数据服务版本 2（IMDSv2）。公司需要阻止源自未使 用 IMDSv2 的 EC2 实例的 AWS API 调用。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new SCP statement that denies the ec2:RunInstances action when the ec2:MetadataHttpTokens condition key is not equal to the value of required. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","B":"Create a new SCP statement that denies the ec2:RunInstances action when the ec2:MetadataHttpPutResponseHopLimit condition key value is greater than two. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","C":"Create a new SCP statement that denies \"*\" when the ec2:RoleDelivery condition key value is less than two. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","D":"Create a new SCP statement that denies when the ec2:MetadataHttpTokens condition key value is not equal to required. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 SCP 语句，MetadataHttpTokens 条件键不等于 required 值时，拒绝 ec2:RunInstances 操 作。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","B":"创建一个新的 SCP 语句，当 ec2:MetadataHttpPutResponseHopLimit 条件键值大于 2 时，拒绝 ec2: RunInstances 操作。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","C":"创建一个新的 SCP 语句，当 ec2:RoleDelivery 条件键值小于 2 时拒绝“*”。将该 SCP 附加到组织的 根目录。","D":"创建一个新的 SCP 语句，当 ec2:MetadataHttpTokens 条件键值不等于 required 时拒绝。将该 SCP 附 加到组织的根目录。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":346,"question_en":"A DevOps team supports an application that runs on a large number of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. The DevOps team uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy the EC2 instances. The application recently experienced an issue. A single instance returned errors to a large percentage of requests. The EC2 instance responded as healthy to both Amazon EC2 and Elastic Load Balancing health checks. The DevOps team collects application logs in Amazon CloudWatch by using the embedded metric format. The DevOps team needs to receive an alert if any EC2 instance is responsible for more than half of all errors. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队支持的应用程序在 Auto Scaling 组中的大量 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。该团队使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 EC2 实例。最近，该应用程序出现了一个问题。单个实例对大量请求返回错 误。该 EC2 实例对 Amazon EC2 和 Elastic Load Balancing 的健康检查均显示为正常。 DevOps 团队通过使用嵌入式指标格式在 Amazon CloudWatch 中收集应用程序日志。如果任何 EC2 实 例导致的错误超过所有错误的一半，DevOps 团队需要收到警报。 哪种步骤组合能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Contributor Insights rule that groups logs from the CloudWatch application logs based on instance ID and errors.","B":"Create a resource group in AWS Resource Groups. Use the CloudFormation stack to group the resources for the application. Add the application to CloudWatch Application Insights. Use the resource group to identify the application.","C":"Create a metric filter for the application logs to count the occurrence of the term \"Error.'' Create a CloudWatch alarm that uses the METRIC_COUNT function to determine whether errors have occurred. Configure the CloudWatch alarm to send a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the DevOps team.","D":"Create a CloudWatch alarm that uses the INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC function to determine whether a specific instance is responsible for more than half of all errors reported by EC2 instances. Configure the CloudWatch alarm to send a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the DevOps team.","E":"Create a CloudWatch subscription filter for the application logs that filters for errors and invokes an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to send the instance ID and error and in a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the DevOps team."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察规则，根据实例 ID 和错误对 CloudWatch 应用程序日志进行分组。","B":"在 AWS 资源组中创建一个资源组。使用 CloudFormation 堆栈对应用程序的资源进行分组。将应用程 序添加到 CloudWatch 应用程序洞察中。使用资源组来标识应用程序。","C":"为应用程序日志创建一个度量筛选器，用于计算“Error”（错误）一词出现的次数。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，该警报使用 METRIC_COUNT 函数来确定是否发生了错误。配置 CloudWatch 警 报，使其向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发送通知，以告知 DevOps 团队。","D":"创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，该警报使用 INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC 函数来确定特定实例是否导致 了由 EC2 实例报告的所有错误中的超过一半。配置 CloudWatch 警报，使其向 Amazon 简单通知 服务（Amazon SNS）主题发送通知，以告知 DevOps 团队。","E":"为应用程序日志创建一个 CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，用于筛选错误并调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数。 配置该 Lambda 函数，使其将实例 ID 和错误信息发送到 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS）主题，以通知 DevOps 团队。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":347,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CloudFormation to perform deployments of its application environment. A deployment failed during a recent update to the existing CloudFormation stack. A DevOps engineer discovered that some resources in the stack were manually modified. The DevOps engineer needs a solution that detects manual modification of resources and sends an alert to the DevOps lead. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CloudFormation 来部署其应用程序环境。在最近对现有 CloudFormation 堆栈进行更新时，部署失败了。一位 DevOps 工程师发现堆栈中的某些资源被手动修改了。 DevOps 工程师需要一个解决方案，能够检测到对资源的手动修改，并向 DevOps 负责人发送警报。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the DevOps lead to the topic by using an email address. Create an AWS Config managed rule that has the CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK identifier. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is invoked on the NON_COMPLIANT resources status. Set the SNS topic as the rule target.","B":"Tag all CloudFormation resources with a specific tag. Create an AWS Config custom rule by using the AWS Config Rules Development Kit Library (RDKlib) that checks all resource changes that have the specific tag. Configure the custom rule to mark all the tagged resource changes as NON_COMPLIANT when the change is not performed by CloudFormation. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is invoked on the NON_COMPUANT resources status. Create an AWS Lambda function that sends an email message to the DevOps lead. Set the Lambda function as the rule target.","C":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the DevOps lead to the topic by using an email address. Create an AWS Config managed rule that has the CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK identifier. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is invoked on the COMPLIANT resources status. Set the SNS topic as the rule target.","D":"Create an AWS Config managed rule that has the CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK identifier. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is invoked on the NON_COMPLIANT resources status. Create an AWS Lambda function that sends an email message to the DevOps lead. Set the Lambda function as the rule target."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。使用电子邮件地址将 DevOps 负责人订阅到该 主题。创建一个具有 CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK 标识符的 AWS Config 管理规则。创建一个在资源状态为 NON_COMPLIANT 时被触发的 Amazon EventBridge 规 则。将 SNS 主题设置为规则目标。","B":"使用特定标签标记所有 CloudFormation 资源。通过使用 AWS Config 规则开发工具包库（RDKlib） 创建一个自定义规则，该规则检查所有带有特定标签的资源更改。配置自定义规则，当更改不是由 CloudFormation 执行时，将所有带有标签的资源更改标记为“不符合”。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在“不符合”资源状态时触发。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，向 DevOps 领导 发送电子邮件消息。将 Lambda 函数设置为规则目标。","C":"创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。使用电子邮件地址将 DevOps 负责人订阅到 该主题。创建一个具有 CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK 标识符的 AWS Config 管理规则。创建一个在资源状态为 COMPLIANT 时被调用的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。 将 SNS 主题设置为规则目标。","D":"创建一个具有以下特性的 AWS Config 管理规则： CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK 标识符。创建一个在资源状态为“不 合规”时被调用的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。创建一个向 DevOps 领导发送电子邮件消息的 AWS Lambda 函数。将 Lambda 函数设置为规则的目标。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":348,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer deployed multiple AWS accounts by using AWS Control Tower to support different business, technical, and administrative units in a company. A security team needs the DevOps engineer to automate AWS Control Tower guardrails for the company. The guardrails must be applied to all accounts in an OU of the company's organization in AWS Organizations. The security team needs a solution that has version control and can be reviewed and rolled back if necessary. The security team will maintain the management of the solution in its OU. The security team wants to limit the type of guardrails that are allowed and allow only new guardrails that are approved by the security team. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师通过使用 AWS 控制塔部署了多个 AWS 账户，以支持公司内的不同业务、技术和 行政部门。安全团队要求该 DevOps 工程师为公司自动化 AWS 控制塔的防护措施。这些防护措施必须 应用于公司 AWS 组织中某个组织单元（OU）内的所有账户。 安全团队需要一个具备版本控制功能的解决方案，并且在必要时能够进行审查和回滚。安全团队将在其 组织单位中负责该解决方案的管理。安全团队希望限制允许的防护措施类型，并且只允许经过安全团队 批准的新防护措施。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create individual AWS CloudFormation templates that align to a guardrail. Store the templates in an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl logical resource in the template for each OU in the organization. Configure an AWS Code Build project that an Amazon EventBridge rule will invoke for the security team's AWS CodeCommit changes.","B":"Create individual AWS CloudFormation templates that align to a guardrail. Store the templates in an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl logical resource in the template for each account in the organization. Configure an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in the security team's account. Advise the security team to invoke the pipeline and provide these parameters when starting the pipeline.","C":"Create individual AWS CloudFormation templates that align to a guardrail. Store the templates in an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl logical resource in the template for each OU in the organization. Configure an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in the security team's account that an Amazon EventBridge rule will invoke for the security team's CodeCommit changes.","D":"Configure an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in the security team's account that an Amazon EventBridge rule will invoke for PutObject events to an Amazon S3 bucket. Create individual AWS CloudFormation templates that align to a guardrail. Store the templates in the S3 bucket. Create an AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl logical resource in the template for each OU in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建与防护栏对齐的单独的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将模板存储在 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中。 为组织中的每个组织单元（OU）在模板中ControlTower::EnableControl 逻辑资源。配置一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目，该项目将由 Amazon EventBridge 规则在安全团队对 AWS CodeCommit 进行更改时 调用。","B":"为每个防护栏创建单独的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将模板存储在 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中。在组 织中的每个账户的模板中创建一个 AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl 逻辑资源。在安全团队的账户中 配置一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。建议安全团队启动管道时调用该管道，并提供以下参数。","C":"创建与防护栏对齐的单独的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将模板存储在 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中。 为组织中的每个组织单元（OU）在模板中ControlTower::EnableControl 逻辑资源。在安全团队的账 户中配置一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道将由 Amazon EventBridge 规则在安全团队的 CodeCommit 更改时调用。","D":"在安全团队的账户中配置一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道将由 Amazon EventBridge 规则在向 Amazon S3 存储桶写入对象时触发。为每条防护栏创建单独的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将模板存储 在 S3 存储桶中。在模板中为组织中的每个组织单元（OU）创建一个 AWS::ControlTower:: EnableControl 逻辑资源。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":349,"question_en":"A company runs a web application on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). The company uses Amazon CloudFront to distribute the application. The company recently enabled AWS WAF. The company set up Amazon CloudWatch Logs to send logs to an aws-waf-logs log group. The company wants a DevOps engineer to receive alerts if there are sudden changes in blocked traffic. The company does not want to receive alerts for other changes in AWS WAF log behavior. The company will tune AWS WAF rules over time. The DevOps engineer is currently subscribed to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in the environment. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上运行一个网络应用程序。该公司使用亚马逊云 分发服务（Amazon CloudFront）来分发该应用程序。该公司最近启用了 AWS WAF。该公司设置了亚马逊 云监控日志服务（Amazon CloudWatch Logs）将日志发送到一个名为“aws-waf-logs”的日志组。 该公司希望有一位 DevOps 工程师在出现突发的被阻断流量变化时收到警报。该公司不希望收到 AWS WAF 日志行为其他变化的警报。该公司会随着时间的推移调整 AWS WAF 规则。 该 DevOps 工程师当前已订阅了环境中的亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Logs metrics filter for blocked requests on the AWS WAF log group to create a custom metric. Create a CloudWatch alarm by using CloudWatch anomaly detection and the published custom metric. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic to alert the DevOps engineer.","B":"Create a CloudWatch anomaly detector for the log group. Create a CloudWatch alarm by using metrics that the CloudWatch anomaly detector publishes. Use the high setting for the LogAnomalyPriority metric. Configure the alarm to go into alarm state if a static threshold of one anomaly is detected. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic to alert the DevOps engineer.","C":"Create a CloudWatch metrics filter for counted requests on the AWS WAF log group to create a custom metric. Create a CloudWatch alarm that activates when the sum of blocked requests in the custom metric during a period of 1 hour is greater than a static estimate for the acceptable number of blocked requests in 1 hour. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic to alert the DevOps engineer.","D":"Create a CloudWatch anomaly detector for the log group. Create a CloudWatch alarm by using metrics that the CloudWatch anomaly detector publishes. Use the medium setting for the LogAnomalyPriority metric. Configure the alarm to go into alarm state if a sum of anomalies over 1 hour is greater than an expected value. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic to alert the DevOps engineer."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS WAF 日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，用于被阻止的请求，以创建自定义指标。 使用 CloudWatch 异常检测和发布的自定义指标创建 CloudWatch 警报。将警报配置为通知 SNS 主题， 以提醒 DevOps 工程师。","B":"为日志组创建一个 CloudWatch 异常检测器。使用 CloudWatch 异常检测器发布的指标创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。将 LogAnomalyPriority 指标设置为高。配置警报，使其在检测到一个异常的静态阈 值时进入警报状态。配置警报以通知 SNS 主题，从而提醒 DevOps 工程师。","C":"在 AWS WAF 日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch 指标筛选器，用于对计数请求创建自定义指标。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，当自定义指标中 1 小时内被阻止的请求数量之和超过 1 小时内可接受的被阻止请求 数量的静态估计值时激活该警报。将警报配置为通知 SNS 主题以提醒 DevOps 工程师。","D":"为日志组创建一个 CloudWatch 异常检测器。使用 CloudWatch 异常检测器发布的指标创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。将 LogAnomalyPriority 指标设置为中等。配置警报，使其在 1 小时内的异常总 和大于预期值时进入警报状态。配置警报以通知 SNS 主题，从而提醒 DevOps 工程师。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":350,"question_en":"A video platform company is migrating its video catalog to AWS. The company will host MP4 videos files in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company will use Amazon CloudFront and Amazon EC2 instances to serve the video files. Users first connect to a frontend application that redirects to a video URL. The video URL contains an authorization token in CloudFront. The cache is activated on the CloudFront distribution. Authorization token check activity needs to be logged in Amazon CloudWatch. The company wants to prevent direct access to video files on CloudFront and Amazon S3 and wants to implement checks of the authorization token that the frontend application provides. The company also wants to perform regular rolling updates of the code that checks the authorization token signature. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家视频平台公司正在将其视频目录迁移到 AWS。该公司将在 Amazon S3 存储桶中托管 MP4 视频文件， 并使用 Amazon CloudFront 和 Amazon EC2 实例来提供视频文件。 用户首先连接到前端应用程序，该程序会重定向到视频 URL。视频 URL 中包含 CloudFront 中的授 权令牌。CloudFront 分发中的缓存已激活。授权令牌检查活动需要在 Amazon CloudWatch 中进行 记录。 该公司希望阻止对 CloudFront 和 Amazon S3 上视频文件的直接访问，并希望对前端应用程序提供的 授权令牌进行检查。该公司还希望定期滚动更新用于检查授权令牌签名的代码。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Implement an authorization token check in Lambda@Edge as a trigger on the CloudFront distribution. Enable CloudWatch logging for the Lambda@Edge function. Attach the Lambda@Edge function to the CloudFront distribution. Implement CloudFront continuous deployment to perform updates.","B":"Implement an authorization token check in CloudFront Functions. Enable CloudWatch logging for the CloudFront function. Attach the CloudFront function to the CloudFront distribution. Implement CloudFront continuous deployment to perform updates.","C":"Implement an authorization token check in the application code that is installed on the EC2 instances. Install the CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances. Configure the application to log to the CloudWatch agent. Implement a second CloudFront distribution. Migrate the traffic from the first CloudFront distribution by using Amazon Route 53 weighted routing.","D":"Implement an authorization token check in CloudFront Functions. Enable CloudWatch logging for the CloudFront function. Attach the CloudFront function to the CloudFront distribution. Implement a second CloudFront distribution. Migrate the traffic from the first CloudFront distribution by using Amazon Route 53 weighted routing."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFront 分发上作为触发器在 Lambda@Edge 中实现授权令牌检查。为 Lambda@Edge 函数启 用 CloudWatch 日志记录。将 Lambda@Edge 函数附加到 CloudFront 分发。实现 CloudFront 持续部 署以执行更新。","B":"在 CloudFront 函数中实现授权令牌检查。为 CloudFront 函数启用 CloudWatch 日志记录。将 CloudFront 函数附加到 CloudFront 分发。实现 CloudFront 持续部署以执行更新。","C":"在安装于 EC2 实例上的应用程序代码中实现授权令牌检查。在 EC2 实例上安装 CloudWatch 代理。 将应用程序配置为向 CloudWatch 代理进行日志记录。实现第二个 CloudFront 分发。使用 Amazon Route 53 加权路由将流量从第一个 CloudFront 分发迁移到第二个。","D":"在 CloudFront 函数中实现授权令牌检查。为 CloudFront 函数启用 CloudWatch 日志记录。将 CloudFront 函数附加到 CloudFront 分发。实现第二个 CloudFront 分发。使用 Amazon Route 53 加权 路由将流量从第一个 CloudFront 分发迁移到第二个。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":351,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts in a hierarchical structure. An SCP that is associated with the organization root allows IAM users to be created. A DevOps team must be able to create IAM users with any level of permissions. Developers must also be able to create IAM users. However, developers must not be able to grant new IAM users excessive permissions. The developers have the CreateAndManageUsers role in each account. The DevOps team must be able to prevent other users from creating IAM users. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来以分层结构管理多个 AWS 账户。与组织根关联的一个 服务控制策略（SCP）允许创建 IAM 用户。 DevOps 团队必须能够创建具有任何权限级别的 IAM 用户。开发人员也必须能够创建 IAM 用户。然而， 开发人员不得向新创建的 IAM 用户授予过多权限。开发人员在每个账户中都具有“创建和管理用户” 角色。DevOps 团队必须能够阻止其他用户创建 IAM 用户。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP in the organization to deny users the ability to create and modify IAM users. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization. Attach the CreateAndManageUsers role to developers.","B":"Create an SCP in the organization to grant users that have the DeveloperBoundary policy attached the ability to create new IAM users and to modify IAM users. Configure the SCP to require users to attach the PermissionBoundaries policy to any new IAM user. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","C":"Create an IAM permissions policy named PermissionBoundaries within each account. Configure the PermissionBoundaries policy to specify the maximum permissions that a developer can grant to a new IAM user.","D":"Create an IAM permissions policy named PermissionBoundaries within each account. Configure PermissionsBoundaries to allow users who have the PermissionBoundaries policy to create new IAM users.","E":"Create an IAM permissions policy named DeveloperBoundary within each account. Configure the DeveloperBoundary policy to allow developers to create IAM users and to assign policies to IAM users of only if the developer includes the PermissionBoundaries policy as the permissions boundary. Attach the DeveloperBoundary policy to the CreateAndManageUsers role within each account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织中创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止用户创建和修改 IAM 用户。将该 SCP 附加到组织的 根目录。将 CreateAndManageUsers 角色附加到开发人员。","B":"在组织内创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），授予附加了“DeveloperBoundary”策略的用户创建新 IAM 用户以及修改 IAM 用户的权限。配置该 SCP，要求用户在创建任何新 IAM 用户时附加 “PermissionBoundaries”策略。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","C":"在每个账户中创建一个名为“PermissionBoundaries”的 IAM 权限策略。配置“PermissionBoundaries” 策略以指定开发人员可以授予新 IAM 用户的最大权限。","D":"在每个账户中创建一个名为“PermissionBoundaries”的 IAM 权限策略。配置“PermissionBoundarie s”，允许拥有“PermissionBoundaries”策略的用户创建新的 IAM 用户。","E":"在每个账户中创建一个名为“DeveloperBoundary”的 IAM 权限策略。将 DeveloperBoundary 策略配置 为仅当开发人员将“PermissionBoundaries”策略作为权限边界包含在内时，才允许开发人员创建 IAM 用户并向 IAM 用户分配策略。在每个账户中将 DeveloperBoundary 策略附加到 “CreateAndManageUsers”角色。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":352,"question_en":"A company has deployed a landing zone that has a well-defined AWS Organizations structure and an SCP. The company's development team can create their AWS resources only by using AWS CloudFormation and the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK). A DevOps engineer notices that Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queues that are deployed in different CloudFormation stacks have different configurations. The DevOps engineer also notices that the application cost allocation tag is not always set. The DevOps engineer needs a solution that will enforce tagging and promote the reuse of code. The DevOps engineer needs to avoid different configurations for the deployed SQS queues. What should the DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司已部署了一个着陆区，该着陆区具有明确的 AWS 组织结构和 SCP。该公司的开发团队只能 通过使用 AWS CloudFormation 和 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）来创建其 AWS 资源。 一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，部署在不同 CloudFormation 堆栈中的 Amazon Simple Queue Service （Amazon SQS）队列具有不同的配置。该 DevOps 工程师还发现，应用程序成本分配标签并非总是设置。 DevOps 工程师需要一个解决方案来强制执行标签使用并促进代码复用。DevOps 工程师需要避免为 部署的 SQS 队列设置不同的配置。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Organizations tag policy to enforce the cost allocation tag in CloudFormation stacks. Instruct the development team to use CloudFormation to define SQS queues. Instruct the development team to deploy the SQS queues by using CloudFormation StackSets.","B":"Update the SCP to enforce the cost allocation tag in CloudFormation stacks. Instruct the development team to use CloudFormation modules to define SQS queues. Instruct the development team to deploy the SQS queues by using CloudFormation stacks.","C":"Use AWS CDK tagging to enforce the cost allocation tag in CloudFormation StackSets. Instruct the development team to use the AWS CDK to define SQS queues. Instruct the development team to deploy the SQS queues by using CDK stacks.","D":"Use AWS CDK tagging to enforce the cost allocation tag in CloudFormation stacks. Instruct the development team to use the AWS CDK to define SQS queues. Instruct the development team to deploy the SQS queues by using CDK feature flags."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个组织标签策略，以强制在 CloudFormation 堆栈中使用成本分配标签。指示开发团队使用 CloudFormation 来定义 SQS 队列。指示开发团队通过使用 CloudFormation 堆栈集来部署 SQS 队列。","B":"更新 SCP 以强制在 CloudFormation 堆栈中使用成本分配标签。指示开发团队使用 CloudFormation 模 块来定义 SQS 队列。指示开发团队通过使用 CloudFormation 堆栈来部署 SQS 队列。","C":"使用 AWS CDK 标签在 CloudFormation StackSets 中强制执行成本分配标签。指示开发团队使用 AWS CDK 定义 SQS 队列。指示开发团队通过使用 CDK 堆栈部署 SQS 队列。","D":"使用 AWS CDK 标签在 CloudFormation 堆栈中强制执行成本分配标签。指示开发团队使用 AWS CDK 定义 SQS 队列。指示开发团队通过使用 CDK 功能标志来部署 SQS 队列。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":353,"question_en":"A DevOps team manages a company's AWS account. The company wants to ensure that specific AWS resource configuration changes are automatically reverted. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队管理着一家公司的 AWS 账户。该公司希望确保特定的 AWS 资源配置更改能够自 动回滚。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Config rules to detect changes in resource configurations. Configure remediation action that uses AWS Systems Manager Automation documents to revert the configuration changes.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor resource metrics. When an alarm is activated, use an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify an administrator to manually reverts the configuration changes.","C":"Use AWS CloudFormation to create a stack that deploys the necessary configuration changes. Update the stack when configuration changes need to be reverted.","D":"Use AWS Trusted Advisor to check for noncompliant configurations. Manually apply necessary changes based on Trusted Advisor recommendations."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Config 规则检测资源配置的变化。配置使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 文档来还 原配置更改的修复操作。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控资源指标。当警报被触发时，使用 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题通知管理员手动还原配置更改。","C":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 创建一个堆栈来部署必要的配置更改。当需要撤销配置更改时，更新该堆 栈。","D":"使用 AWS 可信顾问检查不符合规定的配置。根据可信顾问的建议手动应用必要的更改。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":354,"question_en":"A company hosts an application in its AWS account. The application uses an Amazon S3 bucket to store objects that contain sensitive information. The company needs to capture object-level S3 API calls, including calls that are rejected because the calls were made by using credentials that are not valid. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在其 AWS 账户中托管了一个应用程序。该应用程序使用一个 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储包含 敏感信息的对象。 该公司需要捕获对象级别的 S3 API 调用，包括因使用无效凭证而被拒绝的调用。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail in the account. Enable S3 data events logging. Configure the trail to log to Amazon CloudWatch.","B":"Create a new S3 bucket. Configure access logging on the application's S3 bucket. Deliver the access logs to the new S3 bucket.","C":"Configure Amazon GuardDuty with S3 protection enabled for the account. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches findings that are associated with the S3 bucket. Configure the rule to use an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as the target.","D":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail and a new S3 bucket in the account. Configure the trail to log to the S3 new bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"在账户中创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。启用 S3 数据事件日志记录。将跟踪配置为记录到 Amazon CloudWatch。","B":"创建一个新的 S3 存储桶。在应用程序的 S3 存储桶上配置访问日志记录。将访问日志传递到新的 S3 存储桶。","C":"为账户配置启用 S3 保护功能的 Amazon GuardDuty。创建一个与 S3 存储桶相关联的发现相匹配的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将规则配置为使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队 列作为目标。","D":"在账户中创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪和一个新的 S3 存储桶。将跟踪配置为记录到新的 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":355,"question_en":"A DevOps administrator is responsible for managing the security of a company's Amazon CloudWatch Logs log groups. The company's security policy states that employee IDs must not be visible in logs except by authorized personnel. Employee IDs follow the pattern of Emp-XXXXXX, where each X is a digit. An audit discovered that employee IDs are found in a single log file. The log file is available to engineers, but the engineers are not authorized to view employee IDs. Engineers currently have an AWS IAM Identity Center permission that allows logs:* on all resources in the account. The administrator must mask the employee ID so that new log entries that contain the employee ID are not visible to unauthorized personnel. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"DevOps 管理员负责管理公司 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组的安全。公司的安全政策规定，员工 ID 除 授权人员外不得在日志中显示。员工 ID 的格式为 Emp-XXXXXX，其中每个 X 代表一位数字。 一次审计发现员工 ID 出现在一个单独的日志文件中。该日志文件可供工程师访问，但工程师无权查看 员工 ID。目前，工程师拥有一个 AWS IAM 身份中心权限，允许其对账户中的所有资源执行日志操作。 管理员必须对员工 ID 进行屏蔽，以确保包含员工 ID 的新日志条目不会被未经授权的人员看到。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new data protection policy on the log group. Add an Emp-\\d{6} custom data identifier configuration. Create an IAM policy that has a Deny action for the Action\":\"logs:Unmask\" permission on the resource. Attach the policy to the engineering accounts.","B":"Create a new data protection policy on the log group. Add managed data identifiers for the personal data category. Create an IAM policy that has a Deny action for the \"NotAction\":\"logs:Unmask\" permission on the resource. Attach the policy to the engineering accounts.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to parse a log file entry, remove the employee ID, and write the results to a new log file. Create a Lambda subscription filter on the log group and select the Lambda function. Grant the lambda:InvokeFunction permission to the log group.","D":"Create an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream that has an Amazon S3 bucket as the destination. Create a Firehose subscription filter on the log group that uses the Firehose delivery stream. Remove the \"logs:*\" permission on the engineering accounts. Create an Amazon Macie job on the S3 bucket that has an Emp-\\d{6} custom identifier."},"options_zh":{"A":"在日志组上创建新的数据保护策略。添加一个 Emp-\\d{6} 自定义数据标识符配置。创建一个 IAM 策 略，该策略对资源上的“Action\":\"logs:Unmask\" 权限具有拒绝操作。将该策略附加到工程账户。","B":"在日志组上创建新的数据保护策略。为个人数据类别添加托管数据标识符。创建一个 IAM 策略， 该策略对资源具有“NotAction”为“logs:Unmask”的拒绝操作。将该策略附加到工程账户。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来解析日志文件条目，移除员工 ID，并将结果写入新的日志文件。在 日志组上创建一个 Lambda 订阅筛选器，并选择该 Lambda 函数。向日志组授予 lambda: InvokeFunction 权限。","D":"创建一个将 Amazon S3 存储桶作为目标的 Amazon Data Firehose 传输流。在日志组上创建一个使用 该 Firehose 传输流的订阅筛选器。移除工程账户上的“logs:*”权限。在具有 Emp-\\d{6} 自定义标 识符的 S3 存储桶上创建一个 Amazon Macie 任务。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":356,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage many AWS accounts. The company has enabled all features for the organization. The company uses AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy configurations to the accounts. The company uses AWS Config to monitor an Amazon S3 bucket. The company needs to ensure that all object uploads to the S3 bucket use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) encryption. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司已为该组织启用所有功 能。该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将配置部署到这些账户。该公司使用 AWS Config 来监 控一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。 该公司需要确保所有上传至 S3 存储桶的对象都使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）进行加密。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Config conformance pack that includes the s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled rule. Deploy the conformance pack to the accounts. Configure the rule to target an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","B":"Create an SCP that includes a deny statement for the s3:createBucket action and a condition statement where s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption is not aws:kms. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","C":"Create an AWS CloudFormation stack set to enable an AWS CloudTrail trail to capture S3 data events for the organization. In the stack set, create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match S3 PutObject events that do not use AWS KMS encryption. Configure the rule to target an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","D":"Create an SCP that includes a deny statement for the s3:putObject action and a condition where s3:x- amz-server-side-encryption is not aws:kms. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个包含 s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled 规则的 AWS Config 合规性包。将合规性包部署 到各个账户。配置该规则以针对 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。","B":"创建一个 SCP，其中包含对 s3:createBucket 操作的拒绝声明以及一个条件声明，即 s3:x-amz-server- side-encryption 不为 aws:kms。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","C":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 栈集，以启用 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪来捕获组织的 S3 数据事件。在该栈 集中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以匹配未使用 AWS KMS 加密的 S3 PutObject 事件。配 置该规则以指向一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。","D":"创建一个 SCP，其中包含针对 s3:putObject 操作的拒绝语句以及一个条件，即 s3:xamz-server-side- encryption 不为 aws:kms。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":357,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster and loads transactional data into the database every 5 hours. Data analysts use the Aurora PostgreSQL database to run short-running queries, create complex aggregated queries, and create simple reports that use the data. The data analysts also manually update the data, including deleting and inserting data. The data analysts have reported performance issues. The database team recently identified a long-running idle transaction connection that affected performance by blocking other queries and preventing VACUUM operations. The team wants to be proactively notified about these potential operational issues and about the recommended actions to fix the issues. The company's AWS account uses Amazon DevOps Guru to monitor all the applications in the account. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群，每 5 小时将事务数据加载到数据库中。数据分析师 使用 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库运行短时间查询、创建复杂的聚合查询，并生成使用这些数据的简单报告。 数据分析师还会手动更新数据，包括删除和插入数据。 数据分析师报告了性能问题。数据库团队最近发现了一个长时间空闲的事务连接，该连接阻塞了其他查 询并妨碍了 VACUUM 操作，从而影响了性能。团队希望在出现此类潜在运营问题时能主动收到通知，并 了解解决这些问题的建议措施。 该公司的 AWS 账户使用亚马逊 DevOps Guru 来监控账户中的所有应用程序。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on Performance Insights and DevOps Guru in the existing Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster. Configure DevOps Guru to send notifications to the database team by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","B":"Turn on Performance Insights in the existing Aurora PostrgreSQL DB cluster. Configure Amazon EventBridge to receive events from the existing Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster. Configure the Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster to send notifications to the database team by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","C":"Turn on Performance Insights and DevOps Guru in the existing Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster. Configure the Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster to send notifications to the database team by using Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES).","D":"Turn on Performance Insights in the existing Aurora PostrgreSQL DB cluster. Configure Amazon EventBridge to receive events from the existing Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster. Configure DevOps Guru to send notifications to the database team by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS)."},"options_zh":{"A":"在现有的 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群中启用性能洞察和 DevOps 专家。配置 DevOps 专家通 过使用亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）向数据库团队发送通知。","B":"在现有的 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群中启用性能洞察功能。配置 Amazon EventBridge 以接收来自现 有 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群的事件。配置 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群，通过使用 Amazon 简 单通知服务（Amazon SNS）向数据库团队发送通知。","C":"在现有的 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群中启用性能洞察和 DevOps 专家功能。配置 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群，通过使用亚马逊简单电子邮件服务（Amazon SES）向数据库团队发 送通知。","D":"在现有的 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群中启用性能洞察功能。配置 Amazon EventBridge 以接收来自 现有 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群的事件。配置 DevOps Guru 使用 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）向数据库团队发送通知。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":358,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is implementing governance controls for a company that requires its infrastructure to be housed within the United States. The company has many AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled. The engineer must restrict which AWS Regions the company can use. The engineer must also ensure that an alert is sent as soon as possible if any activity outside the governance policy occurs. The controls must be automatically enabled on any new Region outside the United States. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一家要求其基础设施必须部署在美国境内的公司实施治理控制措施。该公司 在 AWS 组织中拥有多个 AWS 账户，该组织已启用所有功能。 工程师必须限制公司可以使用的 AWS 区域。工程师还必须确保一旦出现任何违反治理策略的活动，能尽 快发送警报。对于美国以外的任何新区域，这些控制措施必须自动启用。 哪种步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Organizations SCP deny policy that has a condition that the aws:RequestedRegion property does not match a list of all US Regions. Include an exception in the policy for global services. Attach the policy to the root of the organization.","B":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Enable CloudTrail for all Regions. Use a CloudWatch Logs metric filter to create a metric in non-US Regions. Configure a CloudWatch alarm to send an alert if the metric is greater than 0.","C":"Use an AWS Lambda function that checks for AWS service activity. Deploy the Lambda function to all Regions. Write an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs the Lambda function every hour. Configure the rule to send an alert if the Lambda function finds any activity in a non-US Region.","D":"Use an AWS Lambda function to query Amazon Inspector to look for service activity in non-US Regions. Configure the Lambda function to send alerts if Amazon Inspector finds any activity.","E":"Create an Organizations SCP allow policy that has a condition that the aws:RequestedRegion property matches a list of all US Regions. Include an exception in the policy for global services. Attach the policy to the root of the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个组织 SCP 拒绝策略，该策略包含一个条件，即 aws:RequestedRegion 属性与所有美国区域列 表不匹配。在策略中为全球服务添加一个例外。将该策略附加到组织的根目录。","B":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。为所有区域启用 CloudTrail。在 非美国区域使用 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器创建一个指标。配置 CloudWatch 警报，如果该 指标大于 0 则发送警报。","C":"使用一个检查 AWS 服务活动的 AWS Lambda 函数。将该 Lambda 函数部署到所有区域。编写一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每小时运行一次该 Lambda 函数。配置该规则，如果 Lambda 函数在非 美国区域发现任何活动，则发送警报。","D":"使用 AWS Lambda 函数查询 Amazon Inspector 以查找非美国区域的服务活动。配置 Lambda 函 数，以便在 Amazon Inspector 发现任何活动时发送警报。","E":"创建一个组织 SCP 允许策略，该策略包含一个条件，即 aws:RequestedRegion 属性与所有美国区域的列 表相匹配。在策略中为全球服务添加一个例外。将该策略附加到组织的根目录。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":359,"question_en":"A company runs applications on Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group. The EC2 instances are behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Users recently began to experience errors when traffic was directed to some of the EC2 instances. A DevOps engineer discovers that the Auto Scaling group reports the problematic instances are healthy despite the application errors. User experience returns to normal after the DevOps engineer resolves the application errors on the problematic instances. The company wants to ensure that traffic is routed only to healthy instances that are not experiencing application errors. The company also wants a support team to receive a notification if the traffic routing configuration changes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行应用程序，这些实例位于一个亚马逊 EC2 自动扩展组中。 EC2 实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。最近，用户在流量被定向到某些 EC2 实例时开始遇到 错误。 一位 DevOps 工程师发现，尽管应用程序出现错误，但自动扩展组报告有问题的实例是健康的。在 DevOps 工程师解决了有问题的实例上的应用程序错误后，用户体验恢复正常。 该公司希望确保流量仅被路由到运行正常且未出现应用程序错误的实例。该公司还希望在流量路 由配置发生更改时，支持团队能够收到通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to use ELB health checks. Enable AWS Config. Create an AWS Config rule to ensure that any new Auto Scaling group will use ELB health checks. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the support team if the traffic routing configuration changes. Configure the AWS Config rule to send a notification to the topic.","B":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to use EC2 health checks. Enable AWS Config. Create an AWS Config rule to ensure that any new Auto Scaling group will use EC2 health checks. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the support team if the traffic routing configuration changes. Configure the AWS Config rule to send a notification to the topic.","C":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to use EC2 health checks. Create an Amazon CloudWatch synthetic canary to monitor the application. Create a CloudWatch alarm that is triggered when the CloudWatch canary fails. Configure the alarm to notify the support team when the alarm state is in alarm.","D":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to use ELB health checks. Create an Amazon CloudWatch synthetic canary to monitor the application. Create a CloudWatch alarm that is triggered when the CloudWatch canary fails. Configure the alarm to notify the support team when the alarm state is in alarm."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置自动扩展组以使用 ELB 健康检查。启用 AWS 配置。创建一个 AWS 配置规则，以确保任何新 的自动扩展组都将使用 ELB 健康检查。创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题， 以便在流量路由配置更改时通知支持团队。配置 AWS 配置规则，使其向该主题发送通知。","B":"将自动扩展组配置为使用 EC2 健康检查。启用 AWS 配置。创建一个 AWS 配置规则，以确保任何 新的自动扩展组都将使用 EC2 健康检查。创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题， 以便在流量路由配置更改时通知支持团队。将 AWS 配置规则配置为向该主题发送通知。","C":"将自动扩展组配置为使用 EC2 健康检查。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 合成金丝雀来监控应用程 序。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，当 CloudWatch 金丝雀出现故障时触发该警报。将警报配置为在 警报状态处于警报时通知支持团队。","D":"配置自动扩展组以使用 ELB 健康检查。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 合成金丝雀来监控应用程序。 创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，当 CloudWatch 金丝雀出现故障时触发该警报。配置警报，当警报状 态处于警报状态时通知支持团队。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":360,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to troubleshoot a pipeline that uses a GitHub code repository. The pipeline contains a source stage, a build stage, and a deploy stage. The pipeline also has an AWS CodeStar connection to the GitHub code repository. The build stage uses an AWS CodeBuild build project. The build project needs to perform a git clone of the repository as part of the build process. The DevOps engineer validates that the source stage is working properly. However, the build stage fails each time the pipeline runs. What is the reason that the build stage fails in the pipeline?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要排查使用 GitHub 代码库的流水线故障。该流水线包含源代码阶段、构建 阶段和部署阶段。该流水线还与 GitHub 代码库建立了 AWS CodeStar 连接。 构建阶段使用 AWS CodeBuild 构建项目。构建项目需要在构建过程中执行对存储库的 git 克隆操作。 开发运维工程师确认源代码阶段运行正常。然而，每次运行流水线时，构建阶段都会失败。 管道中的构建阶段失败的原因是什么？","options_en":{"A":"The build stage within the pipeline needs to use the AWS CodeStar connection action.","B":"The AWS CodeStar connection to GitHub contains incorrect credentials.","C":"The AWS CodePipeline service role does not have permission to use the AWS CodeStar connection.","D":"The AWS CodeBuild service role does not have permission to use the AWS CodeStar connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管道中的构建阶段需要使用 AWS CodeStar 连接操作。","B":"AWS CodeStar 与 GitHub 的连接包含错误的凭证。","C":"AWS CodePipeline 服务角色没有使用 AWS CodeStar 连接的权限。","D":"AWS CodeBuild 服务角色没有使用 AWS CodeStar 连接的权限。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":361,"question_en":"A company's DevOps team uses Node Package Manager (NPM) open source libraries to build applications. The DevOps team runs its application build process in an AWS CodeBuild project that downloads the NPM libraries from public NPM repositories. The company wants to host the NPM libraries in private NPM repositories. The company also needs to be able to run checks on new versions of the libraries before the DevOps team uses the libraries. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 团队使用 Node 包管理器（NPM）开源库来构建应用程序。该 DevOps 团队在其 AWS CodeBuild 项目中运行应用程序构建流程，从公共 NPM 存储库下载 NPM 库。 该公司希望将 NPM 库托管在私有 NPM 仓库中。此外，公司还需要能够在 DevOps 团队使用这些库之前对 新版本的库进行检查。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeArtifact repository with an upstream repository named npm-store. Configure the application build process to use the CodeArtifact repository as the default source for NPM. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline to perform the required checks on package versions in the CodeArtifact repository. Set the package status to unlisted if a failure occurs.","B":"Enable Amazon S3 caching in the CodeBuild project configuration. Add a step in the buildspec.yaml config file to perform the required checks on the package versions in the cache.","C":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository for each library. Clone the required NPM libraries to the appropriate CodeCommit repository. Modify the CodeBuild appspec.yaml config file to use the private CodeCommit repositories. Add a step to perform the required checks on the package versions.","D":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository for each library. Clone the required NPM libraries to the appropriate CodeCommit repository. Modify the CodeBuild buildspec.yaml config file so that NPM uses the private CodeCommit repositories. Add an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that performs the required checks on the package versions for each new commit to the repositories. Configure the pipeline to revert to the most recent commit in the event of a failure."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个名为 npm-store 的上游仓库的 AWS CodeArtifact 仓库。配置应用程序构建过程，将 CodeArtifact 仓库设置为 NPM 的默认源。创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，对 CodeArtifact 仓库中 的软件包版本执行所需的检查。如果出现故障，则将软件包状态设置为未列出。","B":"在 CodeBuild 项目配置中启用 Amazon S3 缓存。在 buildspec.yaml 配置文件中添加一个步骤，对缓存中 的软件包版本执行所需的检查。","C":"为每个库创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库。将所需的 NPM 库克隆到相应的 CodeCommit 存储库。修 改 CodeBuild 的 appspec.yaml 配置文件以使用私有 CodeCommit 存储库。添加一个步骤来执行所需的包 版本检查。","D":"为每个库创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库。将所需的 NPM 库克隆到相应的 CodeCommit 存储库中。 修改 CodeBuild 的 buildspec.yaml 配置文件，以便 NPM 使用私有 CodeCommit 存储库。添加一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，对每个存储库的新提交执行所需的包版本检查。配置管道在出现故障时回滚到最近 的提交。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":362,"question_en":"A company has a search application that has a web interface. The company uses Amazon CloudFront, Application Load Balancers (ALBs), and Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 3. The company uses prebaked AMIs. The application starts in 1 minute. The application queries an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster. The application is deployed to multiple Availability Zones. Because of compliance requirements, the application needs to have a disaster recovery (DR) environment in a separate AWS Region. The company wants to minimize the ongoing cost of the DR environment and requires an RTO and an RPO of under 30 minutes. The company has created an ALB in the DR Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款具备网络界面的搜索应用程序。该公司使用了亚马逊 CloudFront、应用负载均衡器 （ALB）以及处于自动扩展组中的 3 台亚马逊 EC2 实例，该组的期望容量为 3。该公司使用预配置的 AMI。该应用程序在 1 分钟内启动。该应用程序会查询亚马逊 OpenSearch 服务集群。 该应用程序已部署到多个可用区。由于合规性要求，该应用程序需要在单独的 AWS 区域中拥有一个灾 难恢复（DR）环境。该公司希望将 DR 环境的持续成本降至最低，并要求恢复时间目标（RTO）和恢 复点目标（RPO）均低于 30 分钟。该公司已在 DR 区域创建了一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add the new ALB as an origin in the CloudFront distribution. Configure origin failover functionality. Copy the AMI to the DR Region. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 0 in the DR Region. Create a new OpenSearch Service cluster in the DR Region. Set up cross-cluster replication for the cluster.","B":"Create a new CloudFront distribution in the DR Region and add the new ALB as an origin. Use Amazon Route 53 DNS for Regional failover. Copy the AMI to the DR Region. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 0 in the DR Region. Reconfigure the OpenSearch Service cluster as a Multi-AZ with Standby deployment. Ensure that the standby nodes are in the DR Region.","C":"Create a new CloudFront distribution in the DR Region and add the new ALB as an origin. Use Amazon Route 53 DNS for Regional failover. Copy the AMI to the DR Region. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 3 in the DR Region. Reconfigure the OpenSearch Service cluster as a Multi-AZ with Standby deployment. Ensure that the standby nodes are in the DR Region.","D":"Add the new ALB as an origin in the CloudFront distribution. Configure origin failover functionality. Copy the AMI to the DR Region. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 3 in the DR Region. Create a new OpenSearch Service cluster in the DR Region. Set up cross-cluster replication for the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFront 分发中将新的 ALB 添加为源站。配置源站故障转移功能。将 AMI 复制到灾难恢复 区域。在灾难恢复区域创建一个启动模板和一个期望容量为 0 的自动扩展组。在灾难恢复区域创 建一个新的 OpenSearch 服务集群。为该集群设置跨集群复制。","B":"在灾难恢复区域创建一个新的 CloudFront 分发，并将新的应用负载均衡器（ALB）添加为源。使 用 Amazon Route 53 DNS 实现区域故障转移。将 AMI 复制到灾难恢复区域。在灾难恢复区域创 建一个启动模板和一个期望容量为 0 的自动扩展组。将 OpenSearch Service 集群重新配置为具有 备用节点的多可用区部署。确保备用节点位于灾难恢复区域。","C":"在灾难恢复区域创建一个新的 CloudFront 分发，并将新的 ALB 添加为源。使用 Amazon Route 53 DNS 实现区域故障转移。将 AMI 复制到灾难恢复区域。在灾难恢复区域创建一个启动模板和一 个期望容量为 3 的自动扩展组。将 OpenSearch Service 集群重新配置为多可用区带备用节点部署。 确保备用节点位于灾难恢复区域。","D":"在 CloudFront 分发中将新的 ALB 添加为源站。配置源站故障转移功能。将 AMI 复制到灾难恢复 区域。在灾难恢复区域创建一个启动模板和一个期望容量为 3 的自动扩展组。在灾难恢复区域创 建一个新的 OpenSearch 服务集群。为该集群设置跨集群复制。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":363,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer uses AWS WAF to manage web ACLs across an AWS account. The DevOps engineer must ensure that AWS WAF is enabled for all Application Load Balancers (ALBs) in the account. The DevOps engineer uses an AWS CloudFormation template to deploy an individual ALB and AWS WAF as part of each application stack's deployment process. If AWS WAF is removed from the ALB after the ALB is deployed, AWS WAF must be added to the ALB automatically. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS WAF 来管理整个 AWS 账户中的网络访问控制列表（ACL）。该 DevOps 工程师必须确保账户中的所有应用负载均衡器（ALB）都启用了 AWS WAF。DevOps 工程师使 用 AWS CloudFormation 模板在每个应用堆栈的部署过程中部署单个 ALB 和 AWS WAF。如果在部署 ALB 后从 ALB 中移除了 AWS WAF，则必须自动将 AWS WAF 添加回 ALB。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Config. Add the alb-waf-enabled managed rule. Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation document to add AWS WAF to an ALB. Edit the rule to automatically remediate. Select the Systems Manager Automation document as the remediation action.","B":"Enable AWS Config. Add the alb-waf-enabled managed rule. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to send all AWS Config ConfigurationItemChangeNotification notification types to an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to call the AWS Config start-resource-evaluation API in detective mode.","C":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to periodically call an AWS Lambda function that calls the detect-stack-drift API on the CloudFormation template. Configure the Lambda function to modify the ALB attributes with waf.fail_open.enabled set to true if the AWS::WAFv2::WebACLAssociation resource shows a status of drifted.","D":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to periodically call an AWS Lambda function that calls the detect-stack-drift API on the CloudFormation template. Configure the Lambda function to delete and redeploy the CloudFormation stack if the AWS::WAFv2::WebACLAssociation resource shows a status of drifted."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 AWS Config。添加 alb-waf-enabled 管理规则。创建一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 文档 以将 AWS WAF 添加到 ALB。编辑规则以自动修复。选择 Systems Manager Automation 文档作为修 复操作。","B":"启用 AWS Config。添加 alb-waf-enabled 管理规则。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，将所有 AWS Config 的 ConfigurationItemChangeNotification 通知类型发送到一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配 置该 Lambda 函数以在检测模式下调用 AWS Config 的 start-resource-evaluation API。","C":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，定期调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 CloudFormation 模 板上的 detect-stack-drift API。如果 AWS::WAFv2::WebACLAssociation 资源的状态显示为“已偏离”， 则配置该 Lambda 函数将 ALB 属性修改为 waf.fail_open.enabled 设置为 true。","D":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，定期调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 CloudFormation 模板上的 detect-stack-drift API。如果 AWS::WAFv2::WebACLAssociation 资源的状态显示为“已偏 离”，则配置该 Lambda 函数删除并重新部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":364,"question_en":"A company is developing an ecommerce application on AWS. The company wants to make sure that the application can handle sudden increases in traffic. The company uses AWS CodePipeline for its CI/CD process. The company must implement a solution to integrate automated load testing into the CI/CD pipeline to validate the application's performance. The solution must perform production deployment only if the performance exceeds a threshold. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上开发一个电子商务应用程序。该公司希望确保该应用程序能够应对流量的突然增 加。 该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 来执行其持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流程。该公司必须实施一个解决 方案，将自动化负载测试集成到 CI/CD 管道中，以验证应用程序的性能。只有在性能超过阈值的情况 下，该解决方案才能执行生产部署。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application by using AWS Elastic Beanstalk. Enable load balancing. Use Elastic Beanstalk to deploy tools for load tests. Run the tests during each deployment, and roll back the deployment if performance thresholds are unmet. Create an AWS Lambda function to monitor test metrics. Set up alarms for performance thresholds. Configure Amazon EventBridge to return an error if a test fails and to proceed with production deployment if a test passes.","B":"Implement AWS Fargate tasks to run tools for load tests. Use Amazon Elastic container Service (Amazon ECS) to manage the test containers. Create AWS Lambda functions to analyze the test results. Integrate the functions with CodePipeline by using custom actions to initiate and evaluate the tests. Program the functions to return an error if a test fails and to proceed with production deployment if a test passes.","C":"Launch Amazon EC2 instances to run tools for load tests. Store test scripts in a GitHub repository. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate the tests and result analysis in the CodePipeline workflow. Use Amazon EventBridge to invoke an AWS Lambda function based on the test results. Program the function to return an error if a test fails and to proceed with production deployment if a test passes.","D":"Use AWS CodeBuild to run tools for load tests, store the test artifacts in Amazon S3, and configure a CodePipeline stage to invoke the CodeBuild project. Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor the test metrics and to set up alarms for performance thresholds. Integrate an AWS Lambda function into the pipeline by using a custom action. Program the function to return an error if a test fails and to proceed with production deployment if a test passes."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 部署应用程序。启用负载均衡。使用 Elastic Beanstalk 部署负载测试工具。 在每次部署期间运行测试，如果未达到性能阈值则回滚部署。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来监控测 试指标。为性能阈值设置警报。配置 Amazon EventBridge，如果测试失败则返回错误，如果测试通 过则继续进行生产部署。","B":"实施 AWS Fargate 任务以运行负载测试工具。使用亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）管理测试容 器。创建 AWS Lambda 函数来分析测试结果。通过使用自定义操作将这些函数与 CodePipeline 集成， 以启动和评估测试。编写函数，使其在测试失败时返回错误，并在测试通过时继续进行生产部署。","C":"启动 Amazon EC2 实例以运行负载测试工具。将测试脚本存储在 GitHub 代码库中。使用 AWS Step Functions 在 CodePipeline 工作流中编排测试和结果分析。使用 Amazon EventBridge 根据测试结果调 用 AWS Lambda 函数。编写该函数，使其在测试失败时返回错误，在测试通过时继续进行生产部署。","D":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 运行负载测试工具，将测试工件存储在 Amazon S3 中，并配置 CodePipeline 阶 段以调用 CodeBuild 项目。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 监控测试指标，并为性能阈值设置警报。通过 自定义操作将 AWS Lambda 函数集成到管道中。编写函数，使其在测试失败时返回错误，并在测 试通过时继续进行生产部署。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":365,"question_en":"A company needs to update its order processing application to improve resilience and availability. The application requires a stateful database and uses a single-node Amazon RDS DB instance to store customer orders and transaction history. A DevOps engineer must make the database highly available. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司需要更新其订单处理应用程序以提高其弹性和可用性。该应用程序需要一个有状态的数据库， 并使用单节点的 Amazon RDS 数据库实例来存储客户订单和交易历史记录。一位 DevOps 工程师必须 使该数据库具备高可用性。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the database to Amazon DynamoDB global tables. Configure automatic failover between AWS Regions by using Amazon Route 53 health checks.","B":"Migrate the database to Amazon EC2 instances in multiple Availability Zones. Use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) Multi-Attach to connect all the instances to a single EBS volume.","C":"Use the RDS DB instance as the source instance to create read replicas in multiple Availability Zones. Deploy an Application Load Balancer to distribute read traffic across the read replicas.","D":"Modify the RDS DB instance to be a Multi-AZ deployment. Verify automatic failover to the standby instance if the primary instance becomes unavailable."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon DynamoDB 全球表。通过使用 Amazon Route 53 健康检查在 AWS 区域之间配 置自动故障转移。","B":"将数据库迁移到多个可用区的 Amazon EC2 实例上。使用 Amazon Elastic Block Store（Amazon EBS）多挂载功能将所有实例连接到单个 EBS 卷。","C":"使用 RDS 数据库实例作为源实例，在多个可用区创建只读副本。部署应用负载均衡器以将读取流量 分配到各个只读副本。","D":"将 RDS 数据库实例修改为多可用区部署。如果主实例不可用，验证是否能自动故障转移到备用实 例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":366,"question_en":"A company has application code in an AWS CodeConnections compatible Git repository. The company wants to configure unit tests to run when pull requests are opened. The company wants to ensure that the test status is visible in pull requests when the tests are completed. The company wants to save output data files that the tests generate to an Amazon S3 bucket after the tests are finished. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司将其应用程序代码存放在与 AWS CodeCommit 兼容的 Git 代码库中。该公司希望在打开拉取请 求时运行单元测试，并确保测试完成后在拉取请求中显示测试状态。该公司还希望在测试结束后将测试生 成的输出数据文件保存到 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 哪种解决方案的组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM service role to allow access to the resources that are required to run the tests. B Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline that has a test stage. Create a trigger to run the pipeline when pull requests are created or updated. Add a source action to report test results.","B":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project to run the tests. Enable webhook triggers to run the tests when pull requests are created or updated. Enable build status reporting to report test results.","C":"Create a buildspec.yml file that has a reports section to upload output files when the tests have finished running.","D":"Create a buildspec.yml file that has an artifacts section to upload artifacts when the tests have finished running.","E":"Create an appspec.yml file that has a files section to upload output files when the tests have finished running."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 IAM 服务角色，以允许访问运行测试所需的资源。B. 在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个 具有测试阶段的管道。创建一个触发器，以便在创建或更新拉取请求时运行管道。添加一个源 操作以报告测试结果。","B":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来运行测试。启用网络钩子触发器，以便在创建或更新拉取请求时运 行测试。启用构建状态报告以报告测试结果。","C":"创建一个包含“reports”部分的 buildspec.yml 文件，以便在测试运行结束后上传输出文件。","D":"创建一个包含 artifacts（工件）部分的 buildspec.yml 文件，以便在测试完成后上传工件。","E":"创建一个 appspec.yml 文件，其中包含一个 files 部分，以便在测试运行结束后上传输出文件。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":367,"question_en":"A software development team is implementing a CI/CD pipeline for its web application. The team is using AWS CodeBuild to compile Java-based source code and to run unit tests. The team needs to store the artifacts that are created by the CodeBuild project. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一个软件开发团队正在为其网络应用程序实施持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流水线。该团队使用 AWS CodeBuild 来编译基于 Java 的源代码并运行单元测试。 团队需要存储由 CodeBuild 项目创建的工件。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the S3 bucket as an artifact output location in the project. Add the artifact locations to the project's buildspec file. Configure an S3 bucket policy that allows the CodeBuild project's resource access role to access the S3 bucket.","B":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the S3 bucket as an artifact output location in the project's buildspec file. Add the artifact locations to the project's buildspec file. Configure an S3 bucket policy that allows the CodeBuild service role to access the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system as a file system location for the project. Configure the EFS file system as the artifact output location in the project's buildspec file. Configure a file system policy that allows CodeBuild to access the file system.","D":"Create an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume. Configure the EBS volume as the artifact output location in the project's buildspec file. Configure an IAM role that allows CodeBuild to access the volume."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。在项目中将 S3 存储桶配置为工件输出位置。将工件位置添加到项目的 buildspec 文件中。配置一个 S3 存储桶策略，允许 CodeBuild 项目的资源访问角色访问该 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。在项目的 buildspec 文件中将 S3 存储桶配置为工件输出位置。将工件位 置添加到项目的 buildspec 文件中。 配置一个 S3 存储桶策略，允许 CodeBuild 服务角色访问该 S3 存储桶。","C":"为项目配置一个 Amazon 弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS）文件系统作为文件系统位置。在项目的 buildspec 文件中将 EFS 文件系统配置为构建输出位置。配置一个文件系统策略，允许 CodeBuild 访 问该文件系统。","D":"创建一个亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷。在项目的 buildspec 文件中将 EBS 卷配置为工件输出 位置。配置一个 IAM 角色，允许 CodeBuild 访问该卷。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":368,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The accounts are in an OU that has a policy attached to allow all actions. The company is migrating several Git repositories to a specified AWS CodeConnections supported Git provider. The Git repositories manage AWS CloudFormation stacks for application infrastructure that the company deploys across multiple AWS Regions. The company wants a DevOps team to integrate CodeConnections into the CloudFormation stacks. The DevOps team must ensure that company staff members can integrate only with the specified Git provider. The deployment process must be highly available across Regions. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理多个 AWS 账户。这些账户位于一个组织单元（OU）中，该组织单 元附有一个允许执行所有操作的策略。该公司正在将多个 Git 代码库迁移到指定的 AWS CodeCommit 支持 的 Git 提供商。这些 Git 代码库管理着公司跨多个 AWS 区域部署的应用程序基础设施的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈。 该公司希望组建一个 DevOps 团队将 CodeConnections 集成到 CloudFormation 堆栈中。DevOps 团队必须确 保公司员工只能与指定的 Git 提供商进行集成。部署过程必须在各区域都具备高可用性。 哪种步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add a new SCP statement to the OU that denies the CodeConnections CreatingConnections action where the provider type is not the specified Git provider.","B":"Add a new SCP statement to the OU that allows the CodeConnections CreatingConnections action where the provider type is the specified Git provider.","C":"Use CodeConnectlons to configure a single CodeConnections connection to each Git repository.","D":"Use CodeConnections to create a CodeConnections connection from each Region where the company operates to each Git repository.","E":"Use CodeConnections to create a CodeConnections repository link. Update each CfoudFormation stack to sync from the Git repository.","F":"For each Git repository, create a pipeline in AWS CodePipefine that has the Git repository set as the source and a CloudFormation deployment stage."},"options_zh":{"A":"向组织单位添加一个新的 SCP 语句，拒绝提供程序类型不是指定的 Git 提供程序的 CodeConnections CreatingConnections 操作。","B":"向该组织单位添加一个新的 SCP 语句，允许在提供程序类型为指定的 Git 提供程序时执行 CodeConnections 的 CreatingConnections 操作。","C":"使用 CodeConnectlons 为每个 Git 代码库配置一个 CodeConnections 连接。","D":"使用 CodeConnections 从公司运营的每个区域到每个 Git 代码库创建一个 CodeConnections 连接。","E":"使用 CodeConnections 创建一个 CodeConnections 代码库链接。更新每个 CloudFormation 堆栈以从 Git 代码库同步。","F":"对于每个 Git 代码库，在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个管道，将该 Git 代码库设置为源，并添加一 个 CloudFormation 部署阶段。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":369,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer updates an AWS CloudFormation stack to add a nested stack that includes several Amazon EC2 instances. When the DevOps engineer attempts to deploy the updated stack, the nested stack fails to deploy. What should the DevOps engineer do to determine the cause of the failure?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师更新了一个 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈，以添加一个包含多个 Amazon EC2 实例的 嵌套堆栈。当该 DevOps 工程师尝试部署更新后的堆栈时，嵌套堆栈部署失败。 DevOps 工程师应该怎么做才能确定故障的原因？","options_en":{"A":"Use the CloudFormation detect root cause capability for the failed stack to analyze the failure and return the event that is the most likely cause for the failure.","B":"Query failed stacks by specifying the root stack as the ParentId property. Examine the StackStatusReason property for all returned stacks to determine the reason the nested stack failed to deploy.","C":"Activate AWS Systems Manager for the AWS account where the application runs. Use the AWS Systems Manager Automation AWS-SupportTroubleshootCFNCustomResource runbook to determine the reason the nested stack failed to deploy.","D":"Configure the CloudFormation template to publish logs to Amazon CloudWatch. View the CloudFormation logs for the failed stack in the CloudWatch console to determine the reason the nested stack failed to deploy."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 CloudFormation 的检测根本原因功能来分析失败的堆栈，并返回最有可能导致失败的事件。","B":"通过将根堆栈指定为 ParentId 属性来查询失败的堆栈。检查所有返回堆栈的 StackStatusReason 属性， 以确定嵌套堆栈部署失败的原因。","C":"为运行应用程序的 AWS 账户激活 AWS Systems Manager。使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 中 的 AWS-SupportTroubleshootCFNCustomResource 运行手册来确定嵌套堆栈部署失败的原因。","D":"配置 CloudFormation 模板以将日志发布到 Amazon CloudWatch。在 CloudWatch 控制台中查看失败堆 栈的 CloudFormation 日志，以确定嵌套堆栈部署失败的原因。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":370,"question_en":"A DevOps team operates an integration service that runs on an Amazon EC2 instance. The DevOps team uses Amazon Route 53 to manage the integration service's domain name by using a simple routing record. The integration service is stateful and uses Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) for data storage and state storage. The integration service does not support load balancing between multiple nodes. The DevOps team deploys the integration service on a new EC2 instance as a warm standby to reduce the mean time to recovery. The DevOps team wants the integration service to automatically fail over to the standby EC2 instance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队运营着一个在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行的集成服务。该团队使用亚马逊 Route 53 通过简 单的路由记录来管理集成服务的域名。集成服务是有状态的，并使用亚马逊弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS） 进行数据存储和状态存储。该集成服务不支持在多个节点之间进行负载均衡。 DevOps 团队在新的 EC2 实例上部署集成服务作为热备，以减少平均恢复时间。DevOps 团队希望集成服 务能自动切换到备用的 EC2 实例。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the existing Route 53 DNS record's routing policy to weighted. Set the existing DNS record's weighting to 100. For the same domain, add a new DNS record that points to the standby EC2 instance. Set the new DNS record's weighting to 0. Associate an application health check with each record.","B":"Update the existing Route 53 DNS record's routing policy to weighted. Set the existing DNS record's weighting to 99. For the same domain, add a new DNS record that points to the standby EC2 instance. Set the new DNS record's weighting to 1. Associate an application health check with each record.","C":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Update the existing Route 53 record to point to the ALB. Create a target group for each EC2 instance. Configure an application health check on each target group. Associate both target groups with the same ALB listener. Set the primary target group's weighting to 100. Set the standby target group's weighting to 0.","D":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Update the existing Route 53 record to point to the ALB. Create a target group for each EC2 instance. Configure an application health check on each target group. Associate both target groups with the same ALB listener. Set the primary target group's weighting to 99. Set the standby target group's weighting to 1."},"options_zh":{"A":"将现有的 Route 53 DNS 记录的路由策略更新为加权策略。设置现有 DNS 记录的权重。 将权重设置为 100。对于相同的域，添加一个新的 DNS 记录，指向备用的 EC2 实例。将新 DNS 记 录的权重设置为 0。为每个记录关联一个应用程序健康检查。","B":"将现有的 Route 53 DNS 记录的路由策略更新为加权策略。将现有 DNS 记录的权重设置为 99。对于相同 的域名，添加一个新的 DNS 记录，指向备用的 EC2 实例。将新 DNS 记录的权重设置为 1。为每个记 录关联一个应用程序健康检查。","C":"创建一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。更新现有的 Route 53 记录以指向该 ALB。为每个 EC2 实例创建一 个目标组。在每个目标组上配置应用健康检查。将两个目标组都与同一个 ALB 监听器相关联。将主 目标组的权重设置为 100。将备用目标组的权重设置为 0。","D":"创建一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。更新现有的 Route 53 记录以指向该 ALB。为每个 EC2 实例创建一 个目标组。在每个目标组上配置应用健康检查。将两个目标组都与同一个 ALB 监听器相关联。将主 目标组的权重设置为 99。将备用目标组的权重设置为 1。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":371,"question_en":"A company hosts several applications in an AWS account. Each application sends logs to its own log group in Amazon CloudWatch. The company's CloudWatch costs for ingestion are increasing. A DevOps engineer needs to identify which applications are the source of the increased logging costs. Which solution will meet this requirement in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 账户中托管了多个应用程序。每个应用程序都将日志发送到其在 Amazon CloudWatch 中自己的日志组。该公司在 CloudWatch 日志摄取方面的成本正在增加。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要确定哪些应用程序是导致日志记录成本增加的原因。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use CloudWatch metrics to create a custom expression that identifies the CloudWatch log groups that receive the most data.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to create a query for the application log groups to identify the number of log groups that received data during a specific time period.","C":"Use AWS Cost Explorer to generate a cost report that details costs for CloudWatch usage.","D":"Use AWS CloudTrail to filter for CreateLogStream events for each application."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 CloudWatch 指标创建自定义表达式，以识别接收数据量最大的 CloudWatch 日志组。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights 为应用程序日志组创建查询，以确定在特定时间段内收到数据的 日志组数量。","C":"使用 AWS 成本管理器生成一份成本报告，详细列出 CloudWatch 使用的成本。","D":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 过滤每个应用程序的 CreateLogStream 事件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":372,"question_en":"A company has an AWS account named PipelineAccount. The account manages a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. The account uses an IAM role named CodePipeline_Service_Role and produces an artifact that is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company uses a customer managed AWS KMS key to encrypt objects in the S3 bucket. A DevOps engineer wants to configure the pipeline to use an AWS CodeDeploy application in an AWS account named CodeDeployAccount to deploy the produced artifact. The DevOps engineer updates the KMS key policy to grant the CodeDeployAccount account permission to use the key. The DevOps engineer configures an IAM role named DevOps_Role in the CodeDeployAccount account that has access to the CodeDeploy resources that the pipeline requires. The DevOps engineer updates an Amazon EC2 instance role that operates within the CodeDeployAccount account to allow access to the S3 bucket and the KMS key that is in the PipelineAccount account. Which additional steps will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个名为 PipelineAccount 的 AWS 账户。该账户在 AWS CodePipeline 中管理一条流水线。该 账户使用名为 CodePipeline_Service_Role 的 IAM 角色，并生成一个存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中的工件。该 公司使用客户管理的 AWS KMS 密钥对 S3 存储桶中的对象进行加密。 一位 DevOps 工程师希望配置流水线，以便在名为 CodeDeployAccount 的 AWS 账户中使用 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序来部署生成的工件。 DevOps 工程师更新 KMS 密钥策略，授予 CodeDeployAccount 账户权限以 使用该密钥。DevOps 工程师在 CodeDeployAccount 账户中配置了一个名为 DevOps_Role 的 IAM 角色，该 角色有权访问管道所需的 CodeDeploy 资源。DevOps 工程师更新了在 CodeDeployAccount 账户中运行的 Amazon EC2 实例角色，以允许其访问 PipelineAccount 账户中的 S3 存储桶和 KMS 密钥。 哪些额外的步骤能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the S3 bucket policy to grant the CodeDeployAccount account access to the S3 bucket. Configure the DevOps_Role IAM role to have an IAM trust policy that allows the PipelineAccount account to assume the role. Update the CodePipeline_Service_Role IAM role to grant permission to assume the DevOps_Role role.","B":"Update the S3 bucket policy to grant the CodeDeployAccount account access to the S3 bucket. Configure the DevOps_Role IAM role to have an IAM trust policy that allows the PipelineAccount account to assume the role. Update the DevOps_Role IAM role to grant permission to assume CodePipelfne_Service_Role role.","C":"Update the S3 bucket policy to grant the PipelineAccount account access to the S3 bucket. Configure the DevOps_Role IAM role to have an IAM trust policy that allows the PipelineAccount account to assume the role. Update the CodePipeline_Service_Role IAM to grant permission to assume the DevOps_Role role.","D":"Update the S3 bucket policy to grant the CodeDeployAccount account access to the S3 bucket. Configure the DevOps_Role IAM role to have an IAM trust policy that allows the CodeDeployAccount account to assume the role. Update the CodePipeline_Service_Role IAM role to grant permission to assume the DevOps_Role role."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 S3 存储桶策略，授予 CodeDeployAccount 账户对 S3 存储桶的访问权限。配置 DevOps_Role IAM 角色，使其具有允许 PipelineAccount 账户承担该角色的 IAM 信任策略。更新 CodePipeline_Service_ Role IAM 角色，授予其承担 DevOps_Role 角色的权限。","B":"更新 S3 存储桶策略，授予 CodeDeployAccount 账户对 S3 存储桶的访问权限。配置 DevOps_Role IAM 角色，使其具有允许 PipelineAccount 账户承担该角色的 IAM 信任策略。更新 DevOps_Role IAM 角色，授予其承担 CodePipelfne_Service_Role 角色的权限。","C":"更新 S3 存储桶策略，授予 PipelineAccount 账户访问该 S3 存储桶的权限。配置 DevOps_Role IAM 角色， 使其具有允许 PipelineAccount 账户承担该角色的 IAM 信任策略。更新 CodePipeline_Service_Role IAM 角色，授予其承担 DevOps_Role 角色的权限。","D":"更新 S3 存储桶策略，授予 CodeDeployAccount 账户访问该 S3 存储桶的权限。配置 DevOps_Role IAM 角色，使其具有允许 CodeDeployAccount 账户承担该角色的 IAM 信任策略。更新 CodePipeline_ Service_Role IAM 角色，授予其承担 DevOps_Role 角色的权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":373,"question_en":"A company has multiple development teams in separate business units that work in a single shared AWS account. All Amazon EC2 resources that users create in the account must include tags that specify which user created the resources. The tagging must occur within the first hour of resource creation. A DevOps engineer needs to add tags to new resources that include the ID of the user that created the resource and the appropriate cost center ID. The DevOps engineer configures an AWS Lambda function to use the cost center mappings to tag the resources. The DevOps engineer also sets up AWS CloudTrail in the shared AWS account. An Amazon S3 bucket stores the CloudTrail event logs. Which solution will meet the tagging requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有多个开发团队分布在不同的业务部门，这些团队在一个共享的 AWS 账户中工作。用户在该账 户中创建的所有 Amazon EC2 资源都必须包含指定创建资源的用户的标签。这些标签必须在资源创建后的 第一个小时内添加。 DevOps 工程师需要为新资源添加标签，标签中应包含创建资源的用户 ID 以及相应的成本中心 ID。DevOps 工程师配置了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，利用成本中心映射来为资源添加标签。DevOps 工程师还在共享的 AWS 账户中设置了 AWS CloudTrail。Amazon S3 存储桶用于存储 CloudTrail 事件日志。 哪种解决方案能满足标签要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 event notification on the S3 bucket to invoke the Lambda function for s3:ObjectTagging:Put events. Enable bucket versioning on the S3 bucket.","B":"Enable server access logging on the S3 bucket. Create an S3 event notification on the S3 bucket for s3:ObjectTagging:* events.","C":"Enable AWS Config in the account. Configure the required-tags AWS managed rule to check and update the required tags. D Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses Amazon EC2 as the event source. Configure the rule to match events that CloudTrail delivers. Configure the rule to target the Lambda function.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses Amazon EC2 as the event source. Configure the rule to match events that CloudTrail delivers. Configure the rule to target the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 S3 存储桶上创建 S3 事件通知，以便在发生 s3:ObjectTagging:Put 事件时调用 Lambda 函数。在 S3 存储桶上启用版本控制。","B":"在 S3 存储桶上启用服务器访问日志记录。在 S3 存储桶上为 s3:ObjectTagging:* 事件创建 S3 事件通知。","C":"在账户中启用 AWS Config。配置“所需标签”AWS 管理规则以检查并更新所需的标签。 D 创建一个使用 Amazon EC2 作为事件源的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以匹配 CloudTrail 传 递的事件。配置该规则以将目标指向 Lambda 函数。","D":"创建一个使用 Amazon EC2 作为事件源的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以匹配 CloudTrail 传递 的事件。将该规则配置为指向 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":374,"question_en":"A company is developing code and wants to use semantic versioning. The company's DevOps team needs to create a pipeline for compiling the code. The team also needs to manage versions of the compiled code. If the code uses any open source libraries, the libraries must also be cached in the build process. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发代码，并希望采用语义化版本控制。该公司的 DevOps 团队需要创建一个用于编译代码的 流水线。团队还需要管理编译代码的版本。如果代码使用了任何开源库，这些库也必须在构建过程中进行缓 存。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeArtifact repository and associate the upstream repositories. Create an AWS CodeBuild project that builds the semantic version of the code artifacts. Configure the project to authenticate and connect to the CodeArtifact repository and publish the artifact to the repository.","B":"Use AWS CodeDeploy to upload the generated semantic version of the artifact to an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system.","C":"Use an AWS CodeBuild project to build the code and to publish the generated semantic version of the artifact to AWS Artifact. Configure build caching in the CodeBuild project.","D":"Create a new AWS CodeArtifact repository. Create an AWS Lambda function that pulls open source packages from the internet and publishes the packages to the repository. Configure AWS CodeDeploy to build semantic versions of the code and publish the versions to the repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库并关联上游存储库。创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建代码 工件的语义版本。配置该项目以进行身份验证并连接到 CodeArtifact 存储库，并将工件发布到该 存储库。","B":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将生成的语义版本的工件上传到 Amazon Elastic File System（Amazon EFS）文 件系统。","C":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建代码，并将生成的语义版本的工件发布到 AWS Artifact。在 CodeBuild 项目中配置构建缓存。","D":"创建一个新的 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，从互联网上拉取开源软件包并将 其发布到该存储库。配置 AWS CodeDeploy 以构建代码的语义版本，并将这些版本发布到存储库。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":375,"question_en":"A company uses a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline to deploy an application. The company created an AWS Fault Injection Service (AWS FIS) experiment template to test the resiliency of the application. A DevOps engineer needs to integrate the experiment into the pipeline. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 中的管道来部署应用程序。该公司创建了一个 AWS 故障注入服务（AWS FIS）实验模板来测试应用程序的弹性。一位 DevOps 工程师需要将该实验集成到管道中。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a new stage in the pipeline that includes an AWS FIS action. Configure the action to reference the AWS FIS experiment template. Grant the pipeline access to start the experiment.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduler. Grant the scheduler permission to start the AWS FIS experiment. Configure a new stage in the pipeline that includes an action to invoke the EventBridge scheduler.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to start the AWS FIS experiment. Grant the Lambda function permission to start the experiment. Create a new stage in the pipeline that has a Lambda action. Set the action to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Export the AWS FIS experiment template to an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an AWS CodeBuild unit test project that has a buildspec that starts the AWS FIS experiment. Grant the CodeBuild project access to start the experiment. Configure a new stage in the pipeline that includes an action to run the CodeBuild unit test project."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管道中配置一个新的阶段，其中包含一个 AWS FIS 操作。配置该操作以引用 AWS FIS 实验模 板。授予管道启动实验的权限。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 调度器。授予该调度器启动 AWS FIS 实验的权限。在管道中配置一个 新阶段，其中包括调用 EventBridge 调度器的操作。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来启动 AWS FIS 实验。授予该 Lambda 函数启动实验的权限。在管道中创 建一个新阶段，该阶段包含一个 Lambda 操作。将操作设置为调用该 Lambda 函数。","D":"将 AWS FIS 实验模板导出到 Amazon S3 存储桶。创建一个具有启动 AWS FIS 实验的构建规范的 AWS CodeBuild 单元测试项目。授予 CodeBuild 项目启动实验的权限。在管道中配置一个新阶段，其中包括 运行 CodeBuild 单元测试项目的操作。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":376,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is creating a CI/CD pipeline to build container images. The engineer needs to store container images in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) and scan the images for common vulnerabilities. The CI/CD pipeline must be resilient to outages in upstream source container image repositories. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在创建一个 CI/CD 管道来构建容器镜像。该工程师需要将容器镜像存储在亚马逊弹 性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中，并对这些镜像进行常见漏洞扫描。CI/CD 管道必须能够抵御上游源容 器镜像仓库中断的影响。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an ECR private repository in the private registry to store the container images and scan images when images are pushed to the repository. Configure a replication rule in the private registry to replicate images from upstream repositories.","B":"Create an ECR public repository in the public registry to cache images from upstream source repositories. Create an ECR private repository to store images. Configure the private repository to scan images when images are pushed to the repository.","C":"Create an ECR public repository in the public registry. Configure a pull through cache rule for the repository. Create an ECR private repository to store images. Configure the ECR private registry to perform basic scanning.","D":"Create an ECR private repository in the private registry to store the container images. Enable basic scanning for the private registry, and create a pull through cache rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"在私有注册表中创建一个 ECR 私有存储库来存储容器镜像，并在将镜像推送到该存储库时扫描镜像。在 私有注册表中配置一个复制规则，以从上游存储库复制镜像。","B":"在公共注册表中创建一个 ECR 公共存储库以缓存来自上游源存储库的镜像。创建一个 ECR 私有存储库来 存储镜像。配置私有存储库，使其在将镜像推送到存储库时扫描镜像。","C":"在公共注册表中创建一个 ECR 公共存储库。为该存储库配置一个拉取缓存规则。创建一个 ECR 私有 存储库来存储镜像。配置 ECR 私有注册表执行基本扫描。","D":"在私有注册表中创建一个 ECR 私有存储库以存储容器镜像。为私有注册表启用基本扫描，并创建一 个拉取缓存规则。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":377,"question_en":"A company is running its ecommerce website on AWS. The website is currently hosted on a single Amazon EC2 instance in one Availability Zone. A MySQL database runs on the same EC2 instance. The company needs to eliminate single points of failure in the architecture to improve the website's availability and resilience. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST configuration changes to the website?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上运行其电子商务网站。该网站目前托管在单个可用区的一个 Amazon EC2 实例 上。MySQL 数据库也运行在同一个 EC2 实例上。 该公司需要消除架构中的单点故障，以提高网站的可用性和弹性。 哪种解决方案会 以对网站进行最少的配置更改来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application by using AWS Fargate containers. Migrate the database to Amazon DynamoDB. Use Amazon API Gateway to route requests.","B":"Deploy the application on EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones. Put the EC2 instances into an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer. Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora Multi-AZ. Use Amazon CloudFront for content delivery.","C":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to deploy the application across multiple AWS Regions. Migrate the database to Amazon Redshift. Use Amazon ElastiCache for session management.","D":"Migrate the application to AWS Lambda functions. Use Amazon S3 for static content hosting. Migrate the database to Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility)."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Fargate 容器部署应用程序。将数据库迁移到 Amazon DynamoDB。使用 Amazon API Gateway 路由请求。","B":"在多个可用区的 EC2 实例上部署应用程序。将 EC2 实例置于应用负载均衡器后面的自动扩展组中。将数 据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora 多可用区。使用 Amazon CloudFront 进行内容分发。","C":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 在多个 AWS 区域部署应用程序。将数据库迁移到 Amazon Redshift。 使用 Amazon ElastiCache 进行会话管理。","D":"将应用程序迁移到 AWS Lambda 函数。使用 Amazon S3 来托管静态内容。将数据库迁移到具有 MongoDB 兼容性的 Amazon DocumentDB。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":378,"question_en":"A company is developing a microservices-based application on AWS. The application consists of AWS Lambda functions and Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) services that need to be deployed frequently. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a consistent deployment solution across all components of the application. The solution must automate the deployments, minimize downtime during updates, and manage configuration data for the application. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上开发一个基于微服务的应用程序。该应用程序由 AWS Lambda 函数和需要频 繁部署的 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）服务组成。 一名 DevOps 工程师需要在应用程序的所有组件中实施一致的部署方案。该方案必须实现部署自动化， 将更新期间的停机时间降至最低，并管理应用程序的配置数据。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation to define and provision the Lambda functions and ECS services. Implement stack updates with resource replacement for all components. Use AWS Secrets Manager to manage the configuration data.","B":"Use AWS CodeDeploy to manage deployments for the Lambda functions and ECS services. Implement canary deployments for the Lambda functions. Implement blue/green deployments for the ECS services. Use AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to manage the configuration data.","C":"Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate deployments for the Lambda functions and ECS services. Use canary deployments for the Lambda functions and ECS services in a different AWS Region. Use AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to manage the configuration data.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager to manage deployments for the Lambda functions and ECS services. Implement all-at-once deployments for the Lambda functions. Implement rolling updates for the ECS services. Use AWS Secrets Manager to manage the configuration data."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 来定义和配置 Lambda 函数以及 ECS 服务。对所有组件实施堆栈更新时采 用资源替换的方式。使用 AWS Secrets Manager 来管理配置数据。","B":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 来管理 Lambda 函数和 ECS 服务的部署。为 Lambda 函数实施金丝雀部署。 为 ECS 服务实施蓝/绿部署。使用 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储来管理配置数据。","C":"使用 AWS Step Functions 来编排 Lambda 函数和 ECS 服务的部署。在不同的 AWS 区域对 Lambda 函 数和 ECS 服务使用金丝雀部署。使用 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储来管理配置数据。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 来管理 Lambda 函数和 ECS 服务的部署。对 Lambda 函数实施一次性部 署。对 ECS 服务实施滚动更新。使用 AWS Secrets Manager 来管理配置数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":379,"question_en":"A company is implementing a CI/CD pipeline for an application by using AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild. The company needs a solution to run unit tests and automatically generate code coverage reports before any code is deployed to production. The CI/CD pipeline execution must fail if the code coverage is less than 80%. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 为一个应用程序实施持续集成/持续部署 （CI/CD）流水线。该公司需要一个解决方案，在任何代码部署到生产环境之前运行单元测试并自 动生成代码覆盖率报告。如果代码覆盖率低于 80%，CI/CD 流水线的执行必须失败。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to run unit tests and generate code coverage reports. Add a Lambda invoke action to a stage in the CodePipeline pipeline. Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to run hourly to monitor the Lambda function's output. Configure the rule to fail the pipeline if coverage is less than 80%.","B":"Create an AWS Step Functions workflow to run unit tests and generate code coverage reports. Add a Step Functions test action to a stage in the CodePipeline pipeline to invoke the workflow. Configure the workflow to fail if the code coverage is less than 80%.","C":"Create a CodeBuild project with a buildspec.yml file that includes commands to run unit tests and generate code coverage reports. Add a CodeBuild test action to a stage in the CodePipeline pipeline. Configure the CodeBuild test action to use the source artifacts from the source action as input. Modify the buildspec.yml file to fail the build if coverage is less than 80%.","D":"Create a CodeBuild project with Jenkins installed. Configure Jenkins to run unit tests and generate code coverage reports. Add a Jenkins test action to a stage in the CodePipeline pipeline. Configure the Jenkins test action to output the coverage report as an output artifact. Configure an approval action to fail the pipeline if code coverage is less than 80%."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来运行单元测试并生成代码覆盖率报告。在 CodePipeline 管道的某个阶段 添加一个 Lambda 调用操作。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则，每小时运行一次以监控 Lambda 函数的输出。配置该规则，如果覆盖率低于 80%，则使管道失败。","B":"创建一个 AWS Step Functions 工作流来运行单元测试并生成代码覆盖率报告。在 CodePipeline 管道的 某个阶段添加一个 Step Functions 测试操作以调用该工作流。配置工作流，使其在代码覆盖率低于 80% 时失败。","C":"创建一个带有 buildspec.yml 文件的 CodeBuild 项目，该文件包含运行单元测试和生成代码覆盖率报 告的命令。在 CodePipeline 管道的某个阶段添加一个 CodeBuild 测试操作。配置 CodeBuild 测试操 作，使其将源操作的源工件作为输入。修改 如果覆盖率低于 80%，则让 buildspec.yml 文件使构建失败。","D":"创建一个安装了 Jenkins 的 CodeBuild 项目。配置 Jenkins 运行单元测试并生成代码覆盖率报告。在 CodePipeline 管道的某个阶段添加一个 Jenkins 测试操作。配置 Jenkins 测试操作将覆盖率报告输出为输 出工件。配置一个审批操作，如果代码覆盖率低于 80%，则使管道失败。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":380,"question_en":"A company has a web application that publishes logs that contain metadata for transactions, with a status of success or failure for each log. The logs are in JSON format. The application publishes the logs to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. The company wants to create a dashboard that displays the number of successful transactions. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个网络应用程序，该程序会发布包含交易元数据的日志，每个日志都有成功或失败的状态。 这些日志采用 JSON 格式。该应用程序将日志发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。 该公司希望创建一个仪表板来显示成功交易的数量。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster and an OpenSearch Service subscription filter to send the log group data to the cluster. Create a dashboard within the Dashboards feature in the OpenSearch Service cluster by using a search query for transactions that have a status of success.","B":"Create a CloudWatch subscription filter for the log group that uses an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to parse the JSON logs and publish a custom metric to CloudWatch for transactions that have a status of success. Create a CloudWatch dashboard by using a metric graph that displays the custom metric.","C":"Create a CloudWatch metric filter for the log groups with a filter pattern that matches the transaction status property and a value of success. Create a CloudWatch dashboard by using a metric graph that displays the new metric.","D":"Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream that is subscribed to the log group. Configure the data stream to filter incoming log data based on a status of success and to send the filtered logs to an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to publish a custom metric to CloudWatch. Create a CloudWatch dashboard by using a metric graph that displays the custom metric."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群和一个 OpenSearch Service 订阅筛选器，将日志组数据发送到该 集群。在 OpenSearch Service 集群的“仪表板”功能中，使用搜索查询创建一个仪表板，该查询针对状 态为“成功”的交易。","B":"为日志组创建一个使用 AWS Lambda 函数的 CloudWatch 订阅筛选器。配置 Lambda 函数以解析 JSON 日 志，并为状态为成功的交易向 CloudWatch 发布自定义指标。使用显示自定义指标的指标图创建 CloudWatch 仪表板。","C":"为日志组创建一个 CloudWatch 指标筛选器，筛选模式匹配事务状态属性且值为“成功”。使用显示新 指标的指标图表创建一个 CloudWatch 仪表板。","D":"创建一个订阅了日志组的 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。配置数据流，使其根据成功状态过滤传入的日志数据， 并将过滤后的日志发送到一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数，使其向 CloudWatch 发布自定 义指标。使用显示自定义指标的指标图创建一个 CloudWatch 仪表板。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":381,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda functions to implement an API. The company uses a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline to build and deploy the API. The pipeline contains a source stage, build stage, and deployment stage. The company deploys the API without performing smoke tests. Soon after the deployment, the company observes multiple issues with the API. A security audit finds security vulnerabilities in the production code. The company wants to prevent these issues from happening in the future. Which combination of steps will meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 API 网关和 AWS Lambda 函数来实现一个 API。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 中的 管道来构建和部署该 API。该管道包含源代码阶段、构建阶段和部署阶段。 该公司在未进行冒烟测试的情况下就部署了 API。部署后不久，该公司就发现 API 存在多个问题。一次安 全审计发现生产代码中存在安全漏洞。 该公司希望防止此类问题在未来再次发生。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这一要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a smoke test script that returns an error code if the API code fails the test. Add an action in the deployment stage to run the smoke test script after deployment. Configure the deployment stage for automatic rollback.","B":"Create a smoke test script that returns an error code if the API code fails the test. Add an action in the deployment stage to run the smoke test script after deployment. Configure the deployment stage to fail if the smoke test script returns an error code.","C":"Add an action in the build stage that uses Amazon Inspector to scan the Lambda function code after the code is built. Configure the build stage to fail if the scan returns any security findings.","D":"Add an action in the build stage to run an Amazon CodeGuru code scan after the code is built. Configure the build stage to fail if the scan returns any security findings.","E":"Add an action in the deployment stage to run an Amazon CodeGuru code scan after deployment. Configure the deployment stage to fail if the scan returns any security findings."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个冒烟测试脚本，如果 API 代码未通过测试则返回错误代码。在部署阶段添加一个操作，在 部署完成后运行冒烟测试脚本。为部署阶段配置自动回滚功能。","B":"创建一个冒烟测试脚本，如果 API 代码未通过测试则返回错误代码。在部署阶段添加一个操作，在部 署完成后运行该冒烟测试脚本。配置部署阶段，如果冒烟测试脚本返回错误代码则部署失败。","C":"在构建阶段添加一个操作，在代码构建完成后使用 Amazon Inspector 扫描 Lambda 函数代码。如果 扫描返回任何安全问题，则配置构建阶段失败。","D":"在构建阶段添加一个操作，在代码构建完成后运行 Amazon CodeGuru 代码扫描。配置构建阶 段，如果扫描返回任何安全问题则构建失败。","E":"在部署阶段添加一个操作，在部署完成后运行 Amazon CodeGuru 代码扫描。配置部署阶段，如 果扫描返回任何安全问题则部署失败。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":382,"question_en":"A company is implementing a standardized security baseline across its AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company must deploy consistent IAM roles and policies across all existing and future accounts in the organization. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司正在其所有的 AWS 账户中实施标准化的安全基线。这些账户都属于 AWS 组织中的一个组织。 该公司必须在其组织内所有现有及未来的账户中部署一致的身份和访问管理（IAM）角色及策略。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Control Tower in the management account. Configure AWS Control Tower Account Factory customization to deploy the required IAM roles and policies to all accounts.","B":"Activate trusted access for AWS CloudFormation StackSets in Organizations. In the management account, create a stack set that has service-managed permissions to deploy the required IAM roles and policies to all accounts. Enable automatic deployment for the stack set.","C":"In each member account, create IAM roles that have permissions to create and manage resources. In the management account, create an AWS CloudFormation stack set that has self-managed permissions to deploy the required IAM roles and policies to all accounts. Enable automatic deployment for the stack set.","D":"In the management account, create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline. Configure the pipeline to use AWS CloudFormation to automate the deployment of the required IAM roles and policies. Set up cross- account IAM roles to allow CodePipeline to deploy resources in the member accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中启用 AWS Control Tower。配置 AWS Control Tower 账户工厂自定义设置，以便将 所需的 IAM 角色和策略部署到所有账户。","B":"在组织中为 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 启用受信任访问。在管理账户中创建一个具有服务管理权 限的堆栈集，以便将所需的 IAM 角色和策略部署到所有账户。启用堆栈集的自动部署。","C":"在每个成员账户中，创建具有创建和管理资源权限的 IAM 角色。在管理账户中，创建一个具有自我 管理权限的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集，以便将所需的 IAM 角色和策略部署到所有账户。启用 堆栈集的自动部署。","D":"在管理账户中，创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。配置该管道以使用 AWS CloudFormation 自动部署 所需的 IAM 角色和策略。设置跨账户 IAM 角色，以允许 CodePipeline 在成员账户中部署资源。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":383,"question_en":"A company is migrating its web application to AWS. The application uses WebSocket connections for real- time updates and requires sticky sessions. A DevOps engineer must implement a highly available architecture for the application. The application must be accessible to users worldwide with the least possible latency. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其网络应用程序迁移到 AWS。该应用程序使用 WebSocket 连接来实现实时通信。 时间更新并需要保持会话持久。 DevOps 工程师必须为应用程序实现高可用性架构。该应用程序必须能以尽可能低的延迟为全球用户 提供访问服务。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Deploy another ALB in a different AWS Region. Enable cross-zone load balancing and sticky sessions on the ALBs. Integrate the ALBs with Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing.","B":"Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Deploy another NLB in a different AWS Region. Enable cross- zone load balancing and sticky sessions on the NLBs. Integrate the NLBs with Amazon Route 53 geolocation routing.","C":"Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB) with cross-zone load balancing enabled. Configure the NLB with IP-based targets in multiple Availability Zones. Use Amazon CloudFront for global content delivery. Implement sticky sessions by using source IP address preservation on the NLB.","D":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) for HTTP traffic. Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each of the company’s AWS Regions for WebSocket connections. Enable sticky sessions on the ALB. Configure the ALB to forward requests to the NLB."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。在另一个 AWS 区域部署另一个 ALB。在 ALB 上启用跨区负载 均衡和粘性会话。将 ALB 与基于延迟的 Amazon Route 53 路由集成。","B":"部署一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）。在不同的 AWS 区域部署另一个 NLB。在 NLB 上启用跨区负载均 衡和粘性会话。将 NLB 与 Amazon Route 53 地理位置路由集成。","C":"部署一个启用了跨区域负载均衡的网络负载均衡器（NLB）。在多个可用区中使用基于 IP 的目标配置 NLB。使用 Amazon CloudFront 进行全球内容分发。通过在 NLB 上保留源 IP 地址来实现粘性会话。","D":"部署一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）来处理 HTTP 流量。在公司的每个 AWS 区域部署一个网络负载均 衡器（NLB）来处理 WebSocket 连接。在 ALB 上启用粘性会话。配置 ALB 将请求转发到 NLB。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":384,"question_en":"A company has a workflow that generates a file for each of the company's products and stores the files in a production environment Amazon S3 bucket. The company's users can access the S3 bucket. Each file contains a product ID. Product IDs for products that have not been publicly announced are prefixed with a specific UUID. Product IDs are 12 characters long. IDs for products that have not been publicly announces begin with the letter P. The company does not want information about products that have not been publicly announced to be available in the production environment S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个工作流程，为公司的每种产品生成一个文件，并将这些文件存储在生产环境的亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。该公司的用户可以访问此 S3 存储桶。 每个文件都包含一个产品 ID。尚未公开宣布的产品的产品 ID 以特定的 UUID 作为前缀。产品 ID 长 度为 12 个字符。尚未公开宣布的产品的 ID 以字母 P 开头。 该公司不希望尚未公开发布的产品信息出现在生产环境的 S3 存储桶中。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new staging S3 bucket. Generate all files in the new staging bucket. Create an Amazon Macie custom data identifier to identify product IDs in the new bucket that begin with the specific UUID. Launch an Amazon Macie sensitive data discovery job with the custom data identifier. Copy all files that do not have a Macie finding to the production S3 bucket.","B":"Create an Amazon Macie custom data identifier to identify product IDs in the production bucket that begin with the specific UUID. Launch an Amazon Macie sensitive data discovery job with the custom data identifier. Remove all files that have a Macie finding from the production S3 bucket.","C":"Create a new staging S3 bucket. Generate all files in the new staging bucket. Launch an Amazon Macie sensitive data discovery job with a managed data identifier. Copy all files that do not have a Macie finding to the production S3 bucket.","D":"Create an Amazon Macie sensitive data discovery job with a managed data identifier. Remove all files that have a Macie finding from the production S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的暂存 S3 存储桶。在新的暂存存储桶中生成所有文件。创建一个 Amazon Macie 自定义数 据标识符，用于识别新存储桶中以特定 UUID 开头的产品 ID。使用自定义数据标识符启动 Amazon Macie 敏感数据发现任务。将所有没有 Macie 发现结果的文件复制到生产 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建一个 Amazon Macie 自定义数据标识符，用于识别生产存储桶中以特定 UUID 开头的产品 ID。 使用该自定义数据标识符启动 Amazon Macie 敏感数据发现任务。从生产 S3 存储桶中删除所有被 Macie 发现存在问题的文件。","C":"创建一个新的暂存 S3 存储桶。在新的暂存存储桶中生成所有文件。使用托管数据标识符启动 Amazon Macie 敏感数据发现任务。将所有没有 Macie 发现结果的文件复制到生产 S3 存储桶。","D":"使用托管数据标识符创建一个 Amazon Macie 敏感数据发现任务。从生产 S3 存储桶中移除所有被 Macie 标记出问题的文件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":385,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server as its primary database for applications. The company needs to ensure high availability within and across AWS Regions. An Amazon Route 53 CNAME record is configured for the database endpoint. The applications connect to the database endpoint. The company must redirect application traffic to a standby database during a failover event. The company must maintain an RPO of less than 1 minute and an RTO of less than 10 minutes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司将其应用程序的主要数据库托管在 Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server 上。该公司需要确 保在 AWS 区域内部以及跨区域的高可用性。 亚马逊 Route 53 的 CNAME 记录已针对数据库端点进行配置。应用程序连接到数据库端点。在故障转移 事件期间，公司必须将应用程序流量重定向到备用数据库。公司必须保持小于 1 分钟的恢复点目标 （RPO）和小于 10 分钟的恢复时间目标（RTO）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Amazon RDS for SQL Server Multi-AZ DB cluster deployment that uses cross-Region read replicas. Use automation to promote the read replica to a standalone instance and to update the Route 53 record.","B":"Deploy an Amazon RDS for SQL Server Multi-AZ DB cluster deployment. Set up automated snapshots to be copied to another Region every 5 minutes. Use AWS Lambda to restore the latest snapshot in the secondary Region during failover.","C":"Deploy an Amazon RDS for SQL Server Single-AZ DB instance. Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to replicate data continuously to an RDS DB instance in another Region. Use Amazon CloudWatch alarms to notify the company about failover events.","D":"Deploy an Amazon RDS for SQL Server Single-AZ DB instance. Configure AWS Backup to create cross-Region backups every 30 seconds. Use automation to restore the latest backup and to update the Route 53 record during failover."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署一个使用跨区域读取副本的 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 多可用区数据库集群。使用自动化将读 取副本提升为独立实例，并更新 Route 53 记录。","B":"部署一个 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 多可用区数据库集群。设置每 5 分钟将自动快照复制到另一个区 域。使用 AWS Lambda 在故障转移期间在辅助区域恢复最新的快照。","C":"部署一个 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 单可用区数据库实例。使用 AWS 数据库迁移服务（AWS DMS） 将数据持续复制到另一个区域的 RDS 数据库实例。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警报在发生故障转移事 件时通知公司。","D":"部署一个 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 单可用区数据库实例。配置 AWS Backup 每 30 秒创建一次跨 区域备份。使用自动化在故障转移期间恢复最新备份并更新 Route 53 记录。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":386,"question_en":"A company wants to build a pipeline to update the standard AMI monthly. The AMI must be updated to use the most recent patches to ensure that launched Amazon EC2 instances are up to date. Each new AMI must be available to all AWS accounts in the company's organization in AWS Organizations. The company needs to configure an automated pipeline to build the AMI. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司希望构建一条管道，每月更新标准的 AMI。AMI 必须更新为使用最新的补丁，以确保所启动的 Amazon EC2 实例保持最新状态。每个新的 AMI 都必须可供公司组织中 AWS 组织内的所有 AWS 账户使 用。 该公司需要配置一个自动化流水线来构建 AMI。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses AWS CodeBuild. Create an AWS Lambda function to run the pipeline every month. Create an AWS CloudFormation template. Share the template with all AWS accounts in the organization.","B":"Create an AMI pipeline by using EC2 Image Builder. Configure the pipeline to distribute the AMI to the AWS accounts in the organization. Configure the pipeline to run monthly.","C":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that runs an AWS Lambda function to build the AMI. Configure the pipeline to share the AMI with the AWS accounts in the organization. Configure Amazon EventBridge Scheduler to invoke the pipeline every month.","D":"Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook. Configure the automation to run in all AWS accounts in the organization. Create an AWS Lambda function to run the automation every month."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个使用 AWS CodeBuild 的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，每月运行一 次该管道。创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将该模板与组织中的所有 AWS 账户共享。","B":"使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建 AMI 管道。配置管道将 AMI 分发到组织中的 AWS 账户。配置管道每月 运行一次。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，运行一个 AWS Lambda 函数来构建 AMI。配置管道与组织中的 AWS 账户共享 AMI。配置 Amazon EventBridge 调度程序每月调用一次该管道。","D":"创建一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。配置自动化以在组织中的所有 AWS 账户中 运行。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，每月运行一次该自动化。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":387,"question_en":"A company has an application that uses an Amazon API Gateway REST API, AWS Lambda functions, and an Amazon DynamoDB table. The application currently runs in a single AWS Region. The company wants to make the application highly available across two Regions. User traffic must be routed to the Region that provides the least latency. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款应用程序，该程序使用了亚马逊 API 网关 REST API、AWS Lambda 函数以及亚马逊 DynamoDB 表。目前该应用程序仅在一个 AWS 区域运行。该公司希望使应用程序在两个区域都具备高可 用性。用户流量必须被路由到延迟最小的区域。 哪种步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a replica of the DynamoDB table in a second Region.","B":"Create a global secondary index for the DynamoDB table.","C":"Create copies of the REST API and the Lambda functions in a second Region.","D":"Create health checks in Amazon Route 53. Create DNS records that include a failover routing policy.","E":"Create health checks in Amazon Route 53. Create DNS records that include a latency routing policy.","F":"Create DNS records in Amazon Route 53 that include a multivalue answer routing policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"在第二个区域创建 DynamoDB 表的副本。","B":"为 DynamoDB 表创建一个全局二级索引。","C":"在第二个区域创建 REST API 和 Lambda 函数的副本。","D":"在 Amazon Route 53 中创建健康检查。创建包含故障转移路由策略的 DNS 记录。","E":"在 Amazon Route 53 中创建健康检查。创建包含延迟路由策略的 DNS 记录。","F":"在 Amazon Route 53 中创建包含多值答案路由策略的 DNS 记录。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":388,"question_en":"A company has a web application that is hosted on Amazon EC2 instances. The company is deploying the application into multiple AWS Regions. The application consists of dynamic content such as WebSocket-based real-time product updates. The company uses Amazon Route 53 to manage all DNS records. Which solution will provide multi-Region access to the application with the LEAST latency?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个托管在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的网络应用程序。该公司正在将该应用程序部署到多个 AWS 区域。 该应用程序包含诸如基于 WebSocket 的实时产品更新之类的动态内容。该公司使用亚马逊 Route 53 来管理所有 DNS 记录。 哪种解决方案能以最低的延迟为应用程序提供多区域访问？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of the EC2 instances in each Region. Create a Route 53 A record with a latency-based routing policy. Add IP addresses of the ALBs as the value of the record.","B":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of the EC2 instances in each Region. Deploy an Amazon CloudFront distribution with an origin group that contains the ALBs as origins. Create a Route 53 alias record that points to the CloudFront distribution's DNS address.","C":"Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in front of the EC2 instances in each Region. Create a Route 53 A record with a multivalue answer routing policy. Add IP addresses of the NLBs as the value of the record.","D":"Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in front of the EC2 instances in each Region. Deploy an AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator with an endpoint group for each NLB. Create a Route 53 alias record that points to the accelerator's DNS address."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个区域的 EC2 实例前部署一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。创建一个具有基于延迟的路由策略的 Route 53 A 记录。将 ALB 的 IP 地址作为该记录的值。","B":"在每个区域的 EC2 实例前部署一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。部署一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发，其 源组包含这些 ALB 作为源。创建一个指向 CloudFront 分发的 DNS 地址的 Route 53 别名记录。","C":"在每个区域的 EC2 实例前部署网络负载均衡器（NLB）。创建一个具有多值响应路由策略的 Route 53 A 记录。将 NLB 的 IP 地址作为该记录的值添加进去。","D":"在每个区域的 EC2 实例前部署网络负载均衡器（NLB）。为每个 NLB 部署一个 AWS 全球加速器标 准加速器及一个端点组。创建一个指向加速器 DNS 地址的 Route 53 别名记录。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":389,"question_en":"A company manages its multi-account environment by using AWS Organizations and AWS Control Tower. The company must deploy standardized security controls and compliance policies across all of its AWS accounts and AWS Regions. Any changes to these controls must be automatically applied to all accounts simultaneously. The company has the required security controls and compliance policies defined in AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) as a security controls construct. Which solution will deploy these controls across all accounts and Regions with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"该公司通过使用 AWS 组织和 AWS 控制塔来管理其多账户环境。该公司必须在其所有的 AWS 账户和 AWS 区域中部署标准化的安全控制措施和合规性策略。对这些控制措施所做的任何更改都必须同时自 动应用于所有账户。 该公司已在 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）中定义了所需的安全部署和合规策略，作为 安全控制结构的一部分。 哪种解决方案能在所有账户和地区部署这些控制措施，且操作开销最小？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CDK app that includes an AWS CloudFormation StackSets construct. Configure the StackSets construct to use the security controls construct as its template. Specify the target accounts and Regions. Create automation to deploy the CDK app to create and manage the CloudFormation stack set.","B":"Create an AWS CDK app that synthesizes an AWS CloudFormation template from the security controls construct. Use Amazon EventBridge to invoke an AWS Lambda function to update a CloudFormation stack set when changes are made to the security controls construct.","C":"Convert the security controls construct to an AWS CloudFormation macro. Create a CloudFormation stack set that references the macro and deploys the macro to all target accounts. Use Organizations to automatically add new accounts to the stack set’s list of target accounts.","D":"Use AWS Control Tower to create a customized landing zone that includes configurations from the security controls construct. Configure AWS Control Tower to automatically enroll new accounts and to apply the landing zone template."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个包含 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 构造的 AWS CDK 应用程序。将 StackSets 构造配置 为使用安全控制构造作为其模板。指定目标账户和区域。创建自动化流程以部署 CDK 应用程序 来创建和管理 CloudFormation 堆栈集。","B":"创建一个 AWS CDK 应用程序，该程序从安全控制构造中合成一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板。使用 Amazon EventBridge 调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，在对安全控制构造进行更改时更新 CloudFormation 堆栈集。","C":"将安全控制结构转换为 AWS CloudFormation 宏。创建一个引用该宏的 CloudFormation 堆栈集，并 将该宏部署到所有目标账户。使用 Organizations 自动将新账户添加到堆栈集的目标账户列表中。","D":"使用 AWS Control Tower 创建一个包含安全控制结构配置的自定义着陆区。配置 AWS Control Tower 以自动注册新账户并应用着陆区模板。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":390,"question_en":"A company needs to manage shared libraries for various projects across its development AWS account and production AWS account. The company has configured IAM roles for developers and has defined an AWS CodePipeline pipeline by using the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK). A DevOps engineer must implement a solution to ensure that only developers can access the latest versions of the libraries. The solution must test shared packages independently before the shared packages are consumed by other applications and before they go to production. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要在其开发 AWS 账户和生产 AWS 账户之间管理多个项目的共享库。该公司已为开发人 员配置了 IAM 角色，并使用 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）定义了一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一项解决方案，以确保只有开发人员能够访问库的最新版本。该解决方 案必须在其他应用程序使用这些共享包以及这些包投入生产之前，对共享包进行独立测试。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a single AWS CodeArtifact repository for development and production in a central account. Use IAM policies for the developer roles to allow only developers to access the shared libraries. Create an Amazon EventBridge role to start an AWS CodeBuild project and to test each package before the package is copied to the production repository.","B":"Create an AWS CodeArtifact repository in the development account. Create another CodeArtifact repository in the production account. For the development repository, add a repository policy that allows only developers to access the shared libraries. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to start the CodePipeline pipeline and to test each package before the package is copied to the production repository.","C":"Create a single Amazon S3 bucket with versioning enabled for development and production in a central account. Use IAM policies for the developer roles to allow only the developers to access the shared libraries. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to start an AWS CodeBuild project and to test each package before the package is copied to production.","D":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket with versioning enabled in the development account. Create another S3 bucket with versioning enabled in the production account. For the development S3 bucket, add a bucket policy that allows only developers to access the shared libraries. Create an Amazon EventBridge role to start the CodePipeline pipeline. Configure the role to test each package when the package is copied to production and to revert the changes if the tests fail."},"options_zh":{"A":"在中央账户中为开发和生产创建一个单一的 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。使用 IAM 策略为开发人员 角色设置权限，仅允许开发人员访问共享库。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 角色，用于启动 AWS CodeBuild 项目，并在将每个软件包复制到生产存储库之前对其进行测试。","B":"在开发账户中创建一个 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。在生产账户中创建另一个 CodeArtifact 存储库。 对于开发存储库，添加一个存储库策略，仅允许开发人员访问共享库。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以启动 CodePipeline 管道，并在将软件包复制到生产存储库之前对每个软件包 进行测试。","C":"在一个中央账户中创建一个启用版本控制功能的单一 Amazon S3 存储桶，用于开发和生产环境。使 用 IAM 策略为开发人员角色授权，仅允许开发人员访问共享的存储桶。 创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在将每个软件包复制到生产环境之前启动 AWS CodeBuild 项目并对其进行测试。","D":"在开发账户中创建一个启用了版本控制的 Amazon S3 存储桶。在生产账户中创建另一个启用了版本 控制的 S3 存储桶。对于开发 S3 存储桶，添加一个仅允许开发人员访问共享库的存储桶策略。创建 一个 Amazon EventBridge 角色以启动 CodePipeline 管道。配置该角色，以便在将软件包复制到生产 环境时对其进行测试，并在测试失败时回滚更改。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":391,"question_en":"A company manages environments for its application in multiple AWS accounts. Each environment account is in a different OU in AWS Organizations. A DevOps team is responsible for the application deployment process across the environments. The deployment process uses an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in a Shared Services account. The DevOps team members are in the same user group. The team members have administrative access to all accounts through AWS IAM Identity Center. A recent deployment problem in the development environment required the DevOps team to perform manual steps. The deployment to the production environment then resulted in an incident that caused the pipeline to fail, which blocked new deployments for several hours. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that only the pipeline can perform deployments in the production environment. The DevOps engineer must have access to the environment in case of an emergency. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司在多个 AWS 账户中为其应用程序管理环境。每个环境账户都在 AWS 组织中的不同组织 单元（OU）中。 DevOps 团队负责跨环境的应用程序部署流程。部署流程使用共享服务账户中的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。 DevOps 团队成员处于同一用户组。团队成员通过 AWS IAM 身份中心对所有账户拥有管理权限。 最近开发环境出现了一个部署问题，导致 DevOps 团队不得不执行手动操作。随后在生产环境的部署又 引发了一起事故，致使流水线中断，新部署也因此停滞了数小时。 DevOps 工程师需要确保只有流水线能够在生产环境中执行部署操作。在紧急情况下，DevOps 工程 师必须能够访问该环境。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the DevOps group to have the ReadOnlyAccess permission set for the production accounts. Configure the DevOps engineer user with a new permission set that has AdministratorAccess permissions and that allows the user to assume the pipeline role. Add an SCP that denies modification of resources by any entity other than the pipeline role.","B":"Create an SCP that denies all write actions for the DevOps team members on the production OU. Configure a new user in IAM Identity Center for the DevOps engineer with a new permission set that has AdministratorAccess permissions. Add an SCP that denies modification of resources by any entity other than the pipeline role.","C":"Update the DevOps group to be able to assume the pipeline role for the production accounts. Configure a new user in IAM Identity Center for the DevOps engineer with a new permission set that has AdministratorAccess permissions. Add an SCP that denies modification of resources by any entity other than the DevOps engineer.","D":"Create an SCP that denies all write actions for the DevOps team members on the production OU. Use a specific tag to tag the resources that CodePipeline provisions. Add an SCP that denies modification of tagged resources by any entity other than the DevOps engineer."},"options_zh":{"A":"将开发运维团队的权限集更新为对生产账户具有只读访问权限。为开发运维工程师用户配置一个新的 权限集，该权限集具有管理员访问权限，并允许该用户承担管道角色。添加一个服务控制策略 （SCP），禁止除管道角色之外的任何实体修改资源。","B":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止开发运维团队成员对生产组织单位（OU）执行所有写入操作。 在 IAM 身份中心为开发运维工程师配置一个新用户，并为其分配一个具有管理员访问权限的新权限 集。添加一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止除管道角色之外的任何实体修改资源。","C":"更新 DevOps 团队，使其能够承担生产账户的管道角色。在 IAM 身份中心为 DevOps 工程师配置一个 新用户，并为其分配一个具有管理员访问权限的新权限集。添加一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止 除 DevOps 工程师之外的任何实体修改资源。","D":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止 DevOps 团队成员对生产组织单位（OU）执行所有写入操作。 使用特定标签标记 CodePipeline 部署的资源。添加一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止除 DevOps 工程 师以外的任何实体修改已标记的资源。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":392,"question_en":"A company builds container images and stores them on Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) in the company's primary AWS Region. A DevOps engineer wants to replicate all the company's ECR repository images to a secondary Region. The DevOps engineer creates a new ECR repository in the secondary Region and configures permission on the new repository to allow replication. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司构建容器镜像，并将其存储在公司主要 AWS 区域的亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中。 一位 DevOps 工程师想要将公司所有的 ECR 仓库镜像复制到一个备用区域。该 DevOps 工程师在备用 区域创建了一个新的 ECR 仓库，并在新仓库上配置了权限以允许复制。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Pull the existing primary ECR images and then push the images to the secondary ECR repository. Create a replication rule on the primary ECR registry to replicate the images to the secondary ECR registry.","B":"Pull the existing primary ECR images and then push the images to the secondary ECR repository. Configure permission on the primary ECR registry to allow access from the secondary Region.","C":"Configure permission on the primary ECR registry to allow access from the secondary Region. Create a replication rule on the primary ECR registry to replicate the images to the secondary ECR registry.","D":"Configure an AWS Lambda function to automatically save the ECR images to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure cross-Region replication for the S3 bucket. Configure a second Lambda function to push the images to ECR repositories in the replication destination Region when images are replicated to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"拉取现有的主 ECR 镜像，然后将这些镜像推送到辅助 ECR 存储库。在主 ECR 注册表上创建一 个复制规则，将镜像复制到辅助 ECR 注册表。","B":"拉取现有的主 ECR 镜像，然后将这些镜像推送到辅助 ECR 仓库。在主 ECR 注册表上配置权限， 以允许从辅助区域访问。","C":"在主 ECR 注册表上配置权限，允许从辅助区域访问。在主 ECR 注册表上创建复制规则，将镜像复 制到辅助 ECR 注册表。","D":"配置一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以自动将 ECR 镜像保存到 Amazon S3 存储桶。为该 S3 存储桶配置跨 区域复制。配置第二个 Lambda 函数，在镜像复制到 S3 存储桶时将镜像推送到复制目标区域的 ECR 仓库。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":393,"question_en":"A company is experiencing failures in its AWS CodeDeploy deployments for a critical application. The application is deployed on Amazon EC2 instances. A DevOps engineer must analyze the failed deployments to identify the root cause of the failures. Which solution will provide the appropriate information to troubleshoot the deployment issues?","question_zh":"一家公司发现其关键应用程序在 AWS CodeDeploy 上的部署出现故障，该应用程序部署在 Amazon EC2 实例上。一位 DevOps 工程师必须分析这些失败的部署，以找出故障的根本原因。 哪种解决方案能提供适当的信息来排查部署问题？","options_en":{"A":"Configure VPC Flow Logs to monitor network traffic. Use Amazon Inspector to detect non-network deployment issues. Use Amazon Detective to analyze the findings.","B":"Enable detailed monitoring on the EC2 instances. Use AWS Systems Manager Run Command to run troubleshooting scripts on all the EC2 instances simultaneously. Analyze the results in AWS CloudTrail logs.","C":"Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to review application logs. Analyze CodeDeploy deployment logs in the /opt/codedeploy-agent/deployment-root/ directory on the EC2 instances. Use AWS X-Ray to trace requests through the application components.","D":"Examine AWS Trusted Advisor checks for the CodeDeploy deployments. Use the AWS Health Dashboard to monitor application health. Analyze performance metrics in Amazon CloudWatch dashboards."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 VPC 流日志以监控网络流量。使用 Amazon Inspector 检测非网络部署问题。使用 Amazon Detective 分析发现的结果。","B":"在所有 EC2 实例上启用详细监控。使用 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 同时在所有 EC2 实例 上运行故障排除脚本。在 AWS CloudTrail 日志中分析结果。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 查看应用程序日志。分析 EC2 实例上 /opt/codedeploy-agent/deployment- root/ 目录中的 CodeDeploy 部署日志。使用 AWS X-Ray 跟踪请求在应用程序组件中的路径。","D":"检查 AWS 可信顾问针对 CodeDeploy 部署的检查结果。使用 AWS 健康控制面板来监控应用 程序的运行状况。在 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板中分析性能指标。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":394,"question_en":"A company has developed a web application that conducts seasonal sales on public holidays. The web application is deployed on AWS and uses AWS services for storage, database, computing, and encryption. During seasonal sales, the company expects high network traffic from a large number of users. The company must receive insights regarding any unexpected behavior during the sale. A DevOps team wants to review the insights upon detecting anomalous behaviors during the sale. The DevOps team wants to receive recommended actions to resolve the anomalous behaviors. The recommendations must be provided on the provisioned infrastructure to address the issues that might occur in the future. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一个在公共假日进行季节性促销的网络应用程序。该应用程序部署在 AWS 上，并使用 AWS 的服务进行存储、数据库、计算和加密。在季节性促销期间，公司预计会有大量用户访问，从而 产生高网络流量。公司必须获取有关促销期间任何意外行为的洞察信息。 DevOps 团队希望在销售期间检测到异常行为时审查相关见解。该团队希望收到解决异常行为的建 议措施。这些建议必须在已配置的基础设施上提供，以解决未来可能出现的问题。 哪种步骤组合能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon DevOps Guru in the AWS account. Determine the coverage for DevOps Guru for all supported AWS resources in the account. Use the DevOps Guru dashboard to find the analysis, recommendations, and related metrics.","B":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Configure Amazon DevOps Guru to send notifications about important events to the company when anomalies are identified.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Store Amazon CloudWatch logs, AWS CloudTrail data, and AWS Config data in the S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to generate insights on the data. Create a dashboard by using Amazon QuickSight.","D":"Configure email message reports for an Amazon QuickSight dashboard. Schedule and send the email reports to the company.","E":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Configure Amazon Athena to send query results about important events to the company when anomalies are identified."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS 账户中启用 Amazon DevOps Guru。确定 DevOps Guru 对账户中所有受支持的 AWS 资源 的覆盖范围。使用 DevOps Guru 控制面板查找分析结果、建议及相关指标。","B":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。配置亚马逊 DevOps Guru，在检测到异常时向 公司发送有关重要事件的通知。","C":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。将 Amazon CloudWatch 日志、AWS CloudTrail 数据和 AWS Config 数 据存储在该 S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon Athena 对数据进行分析。通过 Amazon QuickSight 创建一个 仪表板。","D":"为 Amazon QuickSight 控制面板配置电子邮件消息报告。安排并发送电子邮件报告给公司。","E":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。配置 Amazon Athena，在发现异常情况时向公司 发送有关重要事件的查询结果。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":395,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to design a cloud-based solution to standardize deployment artifacts for AWS Cloud deployments and on-premises deployments. There is currently no routing traffic between the on- premises data center and the AWS environment. The solution must be able to consume downstream packages from public repositories and must be highly available. Data must be encrypted in transit and at rest. The solution must store the deployment artifacts in object storage and deploy the deployment artifacts into Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). The deployment artifacts must be encrypted in transit if the deployment artifacts travel across the public internet. The DevOps engineer needs to deploy this solution in less than two weeks. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要设计一个基于云的解决方案，以统一 AWS 云部署和本地部署的部署工件。 目前，本地数据中心与 AWS 环境之间没有路由流量。 该解决方案必须能够从公共存储库中获取下游软件包，并且必须具有高可用性。数据在传输过程中和静 止时都必须进行加密。该解决方案必须将部署工件存储在对象存储中，并将部署工件部署到亚马逊弹性 容器服务（Amazon ECS）。如果部署工件通过公共互联网传输，则必须对其进行加密。 这位 DevOps 工程师需要在不到两周的时间内部署此解决方案。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a third-party software VPN appliance to connect the on-premises data center and AWS. Use AWS CodeArtifact to store the deployment artifacts.","B":"Use an AWS Direct Connect connection and a VPN connection to connect the on-premises data center to AWS. Deploy third-party artifact management software on Amazon EC2 instances.","C":"Use two AWS VPN connections to connect the on-premises data center to AWS. Use AWS CodeArtifact to store the deployment artifacts.","D":"Use parallel AWS Direct Connect connections to connect the on-premises data center to AWS. Deploy third-party artifact management software on Amazon EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用第三方软件 VPN 设备将本地数据中心与 AWS 连接起来。使用 AWS CodeArtifact 来存储部署工 件。","B":"使用 AWS Direct Connect 连接和 VPN 连接将本地数据中心连接到 AWS。在 Amazon EC2 实例上部署 第三方工件管理软件。","C":"使用两个 AWS VPN 连接将本地数据中心连接到 AWS。使用 AWS CodeArtifact 存储部署 工件。","D":"使用多个并行的 AWS Direct Connect 连接将本地数据中心连接到 AWS。在 Amazon EC2 实例上部署 第三方工件管理软件。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":396,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer successfully creates an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster that includes managed node groups. When the DevOps engineer tries to add node groups to the cluster, the cluster returns an error that states, \"NodeCreationFailure: Instances failed to join the Kubernetes cluster.\" The DevOps engineer confirms that the EC2 worker nodes are running and that the EKS cluster is in an active state. How should the DevOps engineer troubleshoot this issue?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师成功创建了一个包含托管节点组的亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集 群。当该 DevOps 工程师尝试向集群添加节点组时，集群返回一个错误，内容为：“NodeCreationFailu re：实例未能加入 Kubernetes 集群。” DevOps 工程师确认 EC2 工作节点正在运行，并且 EKS 集群处于活动状态。 DevOps 工程师应如何排查此问题？","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that the EKS cluster's VPC subnets do not overlap with the 172.17.0.0/16 CIDR range.","B":"Use kubectl to update the kubeconfig file to use the credentials that created the cluster.","C":"Run the AWSSupport-TroubleshootEKSWorkerNode runbook.","D":"Create an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider for the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保 EKS 集群的 VPC 子网不与 172.17.0.0/16 的 CIDR 范围重叠。","B":"使用 kubectl 更新 kubeconfig 文件以使用创建集群时的凭证。","C":"运行 AWSSupport-TroubleshootEKSWorkerNode 运行手册。","D":"为集群创建一个 AWS 身份和访问管理 （IAM） 开放身份连接 （OIDC） 提供程序。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":397,"question_en":"A company is developing an ecommerce application that has a backend that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The application has a static frontend website that is hosted in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company uses a GitHub repository for version control and must automate builds and deployments whenever code is pushed to the main branch. The company must deploy changes to the frontend and backend independently of each other. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一个电子商务应用程序，其后端运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上。该应用程序有一 个静态的前端网站，托管在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。 该公司使用 GitHub 代码库进行版本控制，并且每当代码被推送到主分支时，必须自动执行构建和部 署操作。公司还必须将前端的更改部署到位。 后端彼此独立。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline to use for the frontend and the backend. Specify the GitHub repository as the source. Configure two build stages that use AWS CodeBuild as the action provider to build the frontend components and backend components, respectively. Configure two deployment stages that use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to deploy the frontend and backend, respectively.","B":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline to use for the frontend and the backend. Specify the GitHub repository as the source. Configure two build stages that use AWS CodeBuild as the action provider to build the frontend components and backend components, respectively. Configure two deployment stages. For the backend stage, use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to deploy the backend to the EC2 instances. For the frontend stage, use Amazon S3 as the action provider to deploy the frontend to the S3 bucket.","C":"Create two AWS CodePipeline pipelines: one for the frontend and one for the backend. Specify the GitHub repository as the source. Configure a build stage that uses AWS CodeBuild as the action provider for each pipeline to build the frontend and the backend. Configure a deployment stage that uses AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider for each pipeline to deploy the frontend and the backend.","D":"Create two AWS CodePipeline pipelines: one for the frontend and one for the backend. Specify the GitHub repository as the source. Configure a build stage that uses AWS CodeBuild as the action provider for each pipeline to build the frontend and the backend. For the backend pipeline, use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to deploy the backend to the EC2 instances. For the frontend pipeline, use Amazon S3 as the action provider to deploy the frontend to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个用于前端和后端的单一 AWS CodePipeline 管道。将 GitHub 代码库指定为源。配置两个构建 阶段，分别使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来构建前端组件和后端组件。配置两个部署阶 段，分别使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序来部署前端和后端。","B":"创建一个用于前端和后端的单一 AWS CodePipeline 管道。将 GitHub 代码库指定为源。配置两个构建阶段， 分别使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来构建前端组件和后端组件。配置两个部署阶段。对于后 端阶段，使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序将后端部署到 EC2 实例。对于前端阶段，使用 Amazon S3 作为操作提供程序将前端部署到 S3 存储桶。","C":"创建两个 AWS CodePipeline 管道：一个用于前端，一个用于后端。将 GitHub 代码库指定为源。为每 个管道配置一个构建阶段，使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来构建前端和后端。为每个管道 配置一个部署阶段，使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序来部署前端和后端。","D":"创建两个 AWS CodePipeline 管道：一个用于前端，一个用于后端。将 GitHub 代码库指定为源。为每 个管道配置一个构建阶段，使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来构建前端和后端。对于后端管 道，使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序将后端部署到 EC2 实例。对于前端管道，使用 Amazon S3 作为操作提供程序将前端部署到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":398,"question_en":"A company has an RPO of 24 hours and an RTO of 10 minutes for a critical web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS account. The company wants to set up AWS Backup for its AWS environment. A DevOps engineer configures AWS Organizations for AWS Backup. The DevOps engineer creates a new centralized AWS account to store the backups. Each EC2 instance has four Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes attached. Which solution will meet this requirement MOST securely?","question_zh":"一家公司对其运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的关键网络应用程序设定了 24 小时的恢复点目标（RPO）和 10 分钟的恢复时间目标（RTO）。该公司使用 AWS 组织来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司希望为其 AWS 环境设 置 AWS 备份服务。 一位 DevOps 工程师为 AWS 备份配置了 AWS 组织。该 DevOps 工程师创建了一个新的集中式 AWS 账户来 存储备份。每个 EC2 实例都附加了四个亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷。 哪种解决方案能最安全地满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create encrypted backup vaults and customer managed AWS KMS keys in both accounts. Configure AWS Backup to create full EC2 backups as AMIs. Copy the backups to the centralized vault.","B":"Create encrypted vaults in both accounts by using the source account's AWS KMS key. Configure AWS Backup to create EC2 AMIs. Copy the AMIs to the centralized vault.","C":"Create backup vaults in both accounts. Use AWS managed keys for encryption. Configure AWS Backup to create EC2 AMIs. Copy the AMIs to the centralized vault.","D":"Create encrypted vaults in both accounts. Use a customer managed KMS key in the source account. Use an AWS managed key in the centralized account. Configure AWS Backup to create EC2 AMIs. Copy the AMIs to the centralized vault."},"options_zh":{"A":"在两个账户中创建加密备份库和客户管理的 AWS KMS 密钥。配置 AWS 备份以创建完整的 EC2 备份 作为 AMI。将备份复制到集中式备份库。","B":"使用源账户的 AWS KMS 密钥在两个账户中创建加密存储库。配置 AWS Backup 以创建 EC2 AMI。 将 AMI 复制到集中式存储库。","C":"在两个账户中创建备份库。使用 AWS 管理的密钥进行加密。配置 AWS 备份以创建 EC2 AMI。将 AMI 复制到集中式备份库。","D":"在两个账户中创建加密存储库。在源账户中使用客户管理的 KMS 密钥。在集中账户中使用 AWS 管理 的密钥。配置 AWS 备份以创建 EC2 AMI。将 AMI 复制到集中存储库。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":399,"question_en":"A company wants to proactively monitor and respond to AWS service issues that might affect an application. The company must correlate AWS Health events with application performance metrics and must set up automated alerts. The solution must give the company the ability to archive events, test the application's latency in different scenarios, and create custom metrics. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望主动监控并响应可能影响应用程序的 AWS 服务问题。该公司必须将 AWS Health 事件 与应用程序性能指标相关联，并且必须设置自动警报。该解决方案必须使公司能够存档事件、测试 应用程序在不同场景下的延迟，并创建自定义指标。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudTrail to log all AWS Health events. Use Amazon Athena to query the logs and to correlate the logs with application metrics stored in Amazon Timestream for LiveAnalytics. Set up AWS Chatbot for real-time notifications.","B":"Use Amazon EventBridge to route AWS Health events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a metric filter for AWS Health events. Create custom metrics in CloudWatch that are based on application performance data. Set up CloudWatch alarms that correlate AWS Health events with the custom metrics.","C":"Configure the AWS Health Dashboard to send notifications to Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). Use AWS Lambda to correlate the notifications with metrics and to update custom metrics in Amazon CloudWatch. Set up CloudWatch alarms for the custom metrics. Use AWS Systems Manager for automated remediation.","D":"Configure AWS X-Ray to trace AWS Health events and application performance. Use Amazon QuickSight to visualize the correlations between events and metrics. Use Amazon GuardDuty to detect anomalies in the application's behavior and to provide alerts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 记录所有 AWS Health 事件。使用 Amazon Athena 查询日志，并将日志与存储 在 Amazon Timestream 中的 LiveAnalytics 应用程序指标相关联。设置 AWS Chatbot 以实现实时通 知。","B":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 将 AWS Health 事件路由到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。为 AWS Health 事 件创建指标过滤器。在 CloudWatch 中基于应用程序性能数据创建自定义指标。设置 CloudWatch 警报，将 AWS Health 事件与自定义指标相关联。","C":"配置 AWS 健康仪表板，使其向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）发送通知。使用 AWS Lambda 将通知与指标相关联，并更新 Amazon CloudWatch 中的自定义指标。为自定义指标设置 CloudWatch 警报。使用 AWS 系统管理器进行自动修复。","D":"配置 AWS X-Ray 来追踪 AWS 健康事件和应用程序性能。使用 Amazon QuickSight 来可视化事件与 指标之间的关联。使用 Amazon GuardDuty 来检测应用程序行为中的异常情况并提供警报。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":400,"question_en":"A company uses a CI/CD pipeline to deploy its workload in the ap-southeast-2 Region. The company receives images through a Network Load Balancer (NLB) and processes the images in AWS Fargate tasks on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. An Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository stores the images as Docker images. The company uses Amazon Route 53 to configure DNS. The company saves the images in an Amazon S3 bucket and saves the metadata from the images in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The company wants to expand the workload to a second Region. A DevOps engineer needs to build a highly available and resilient design to expand the workload to the eu-west-2 Region. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the FEWEST configuration changes? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 CI/CD 管道在 ap-southeast-2 区域部署其工作负载。该公司通过网络负载均衡器（NLB） 接收图像，并在 Amazon ECS 集群上的 AWS Fargate 任务中处理这些图像。 亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）存储库将镜像存储为 Docker 镜像。该公司使用亚马逊路由 53 来配置 DNS。该公司将镜像保存在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并将镜像的元数据保存在 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。 该公司希望将工作负载扩展到第二个区域。一名 DevOps 工程师需要构建一个高可用且具有弹性的 设计，以将工作负载扩展到 eu-west-2 区域。 哪种组合的 哪些步骤能以最少的配置更改满足这些要求？ （选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure ECR replication to eu-west-2 on the repository. Configure an NLB in eu-west-2 that resolves to Fargate tasks in an ECS cluster in eu-west-2. Configure a latency routing policy in Route 53 for the two workloads.","B":"Configure the DynamoDB table as a global table with a replica in eu-west-2. Configure the Fargate tasks to interact with the DynamoDB table in ap-southeast-2.","C":"Configure the DynamoDB table as a global table with a replica in eu-west-2. Configure the Fargate tasks to interact with the DynamoDB table in the same Region that the tasks run in.","D":"Configure a new S3 bucket in eu-west-2. Configure data replication between the S3 bucket in ap- southeast-2 and the S3 bucket in eu-west-2. Configure the Fargate tasks to use the S3 bucket in the same Region that the tasks run in to perform S3 PUT operations and GET operations.","E":"Configure an S3 Multi-Region Access Point for the S3 bucket in ap-southeast-2 and a new S3 bucket in eu-west-2. Configure two-way replication on the S3 buckets. Configure the workloads to use the Multi- Region Access Point for S3 PUT operations and GET operations.","F":"Configure the CI/CD pipeline to deploy ECR images to both Regions. Configure an NLB in eu-west-2 that resolves to Fargate tasks in an ECS cluster in eu-west-2. Configure a failover routing policy in Route 53 for the two workloads."},"options_zh":{"A":"在该存储库中配置 ECR 复制到 eu-west-2 区域。在 eu-west-2 区域配置一个网络负载均衡器（NLB），使 其解析到 eu-west-2 区域中 ECS 集群内的 Fargate 任务。在 Route 53 中为这两个工作负载配置延迟路由 策略。","B":"将 DynamoDB 表配置为全局表，并在 eu-west-2 区域设置一个副本。将 Fargate 任务配置为与 ap- southeast-2 区域的 DynamoDB 表进行交互。","C":"将 DynamoDB 表配置为全局表，并在 eu-west-2 区域设置一个副本。将 Fargate 任务配置为与任务运 行所在区域的 DynamoDB 表进行交互。","D":"在 eu-west-2 区域配置一个新的 S3 存储桶。在 apsoutheast-2 区域的 S3 存储桶与 eu-west-2 区域的 S3 存 储桶之间配置数据复制。配置 Fargate 任务使用其所在区域的 S3 存储桶来执行 S3 的 PUT 操作和 GET 操作。","E":"为位于 ap-southeast-2 区域的 S3 存储桶和位于 eu-west-2 区域的新 S3 存储桶配置 S3 多区域访问点。在两 个 S3 存储桶上配置双向复制。配置工作负载使用 S3 多区域访问点执行 S3 PUT 操作和 GET 操作。","F":"配置 CI/CD 管道以将 ECR 镜像部署到两个区域。在 eu-west-2 区域配置一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）， 使其解析到 eu-west-2 区域中 ECS 集群内的 Fargate 任务。在 Route 53 中为这两个工作负载配置故障 转移路由策略。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":401,"question_en":"A company has deployed a microservices-based application on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). The application is experiencing performance issues. The company needs to identify which microservices are causing the issues. Which solution will provide this information?","question_zh":"一家公司已在亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）上部署了一个基于微服务的应用程序。该应用程序正遭 遇性能问题。该公司需要确定是哪些微服务导致了这些问题。 哪种解决方案能提供这些信息？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS X-Ray for each ECS task. Create an X-Ray group for each microservice. Implement custom X-Ray subsegments in each microservice to capture detailed timing information. Use an X-Ray service map to visualize and identify slow microservices and requests.","B":"Configure AWS X-Ray for each ECS task. Use an X-Ray service map to visualize the application's architecture and request flow. Filter the X-Ray traces by response time and error rate. Identify the microservices that have high latency or high error rates. Analyze individual traces to identify slow microservices and requests.","C":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights for each ECS task. Analyze Container Insights metrics to identify slow microservices. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to filter the Container Insights log data by response time and error rate. Analyze the log data to identify slow requests.","D":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights for each ECS task. Use the CloudWatch automatic dashboard for Amazon ECS to identify slow microservices. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to analyze the Container Insights performance logs for each ECS task to identify slow requests."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个 ECS 任务配置 AWS X-Ray。为每个微服务创建一个 X-Ray 组。在每个微服务中实现自定义 X- Ray 子段以捕获详细的计时信息。使用 X-Ray 服务映射来可视化并识别运行缓慢的微服务和请求。","B":"为每个 ECS 任务配置 AWS X-Ray。使用 X-Ray 服务映射来可视化应用程序的架构和请求流程。按 响应时间和错误率筛选 X-Ray 跟踪。识别出延迟高或错误率高的微服务。分析单个跟踪以找出运 行缓慢的微服务和请求。","C":"为每个 ECS 任务配置 Amazon CloudWatch 容器洞察功能。分析容器洞察指标以识别运行缓慢的微服务。 使用 CloudWatch 日志洞察功能按响应时间和错误率筛选容器洞察日志数据。分析日志数据以识别运行 缓慢的请求。","D":"为每个 ECS 任务配置 Amazon CloudWatch 容器洞察功能。使用 Amazon ECS 的 CloudWatch 自动仪表板 来识别运行缓慢的微服务。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 分析每个 ECS 任务的容器洞察性能日志，以 识别运行缓慢的请求。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"}];
